ExxonMobil,,,,Syracuse,Petrobras Profit Tops Estimates on Iran War-Driven Oil Rally,Bloomberg,2026-08-07T13:44:34.728000Z,2026-08-07 13:44:34.728000+00:00,FinancialsActivityMarketingActivity,https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-08-06/petrobras-profit-tops-estimates-on-iran-war-driven-oil-rally,"Petroleo Brasileiro SA, as the company is formally known, joins major companies including ExxonMobil Holdings Corp. , Chevron Corp. and Shell Plc in reaping bumper profits amid the energy-market disarray wrought by wars in the Persian Gulf region and Russia. Read More: Exxon, Chevron Steer Windfall Profits Into Paying Down Debt. The Rio de Janeiro - based oil giant defied the trend among its biggest rivals that plowed windfall profits into debt reduction, signaling caution over the durability of war-driven gains. For its part, Petrobras focused on rewarding investors with $ 3.4 billion in shareholder payouts. Analysts had forecast $ 3.1 billion in such outlays."
ExxonMobil,,,,Syracuse,"Grupo Plastilene, ExxonMobil Set New Packaging Benchmark",plasticstoday,2026-08-04T11:18:14Z,2026-08-04 11:18:14+00:00,PartnershipActivity,https://www.plasticstoday.com/packaging/grupo-plastilene-exxonmobil-set-new-packaging-benchmark,"Grupo Plastilene, ExxonMobil Set New Packaging Benchmark. Grupo Plastilene has achieved a breakthrough in Colombia's flexible packaging sector by implementing Tube Water Quench (TWQ) blown film technology in partnership with ExxonMobil Signature Polymers, enabling the company to produce high-performance thermoforming films that match and replace imported structures. The longtime regional leader in thermoforming films strengthened its technology platform by integrating TWQ extrusion equipment from Windmöller & Hölscher (W & H) in 2021, marking what the company describes as a transformative leap in optical, mechanical, and thermoforming capability. According to an ExxonMobil Signature Polymers case study, the collaboration addresses a critical challenge: elevating locally produced thermoforming film performance while delivering premium optics, mechanical strength, barrier performance, and strong shelf impact. "" TWQ expands the design space for barrier thermoforming films - cast-like optics, stable gauge, and a wider sealing window that enables deeper draws with less scrap."
ExxonMobil,,,,Syracuse,Exxon posts slight miss as repairs dogged refining results,Transport Topics,2026-07-31T15:19:28Z,2026-07-31 15:19:28+00:00,FinancialsActivity,https://www.ttnews.com/articles/exxon-earnings-q2-2026,"ExxonMobil Holdings Corp. narrowly missed profit forecasts despite soaring crude prices and widening fuel-making margins as the U.S.-Iran conflict enters its sixth month. Adjusted second-quarter earnings of $ 3.52 a share were 2 cents below the average estimate in a Bloomberg survey. Exxon's miss was due in part to refinery maintenance that meant it was n't able to fully capture high prices for gasoline, diesel and jet fuel. READ MORE: Shell profit surges as oil trading and refining margins boom. That said, overall profit of $ 14.7 billion was the largest since Russia's 2022 invasion of Ukraine that upended global markets."
ExxonMobil,,,,Syracuse,ExxonMobil reveals how much profits have surged amid Iran war,TAG24,2026-07-31T11:58:24.302000Z,2026-07-31 11:58:24.302000+00:00,FinancialsActivity,https://www.tag24.com/en/topic/iran-war/exxonmobil-reveals-how-much-profits-have-surged-amid-iran-war-3520647,"Spring, Texas - ExxonMobil's second-quarter profits more than doubled to $ 14.5 billion on surging oil prices and refining margins due to the Middle East war, the company reported on Friday. Vehicles pass an ExxonMobil gas station in Rosemead, California. © FREDERIC J. BROWN / AFP. The results come on the heels of massive profits reported by other petroleum giants in the aftermath of Iran's virtual shutdown of the Strait of Hormuz, a key waterway for crude oil and liquefied natural gas shipments."
ExxonMobil,,,,Syracuse,Exxon made $160 million per day last quarter as oil prices surged,CNN,2026-07-31T11:09:24.761000Z,2026-07-31 11:09:24.761000+00:00,FinancialsActivity,https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/31/business/big-oil-earnings-q2-2026,"ExxonMobil and Chevron, the two biggest US oil companies, reported gangbusters profits on Friday driven by the spike in global oil prices unleashed by the US-Iran war. Exxon raked in $ 14.5 billion in profit during the second quarter, more than doubling its year-earlier earnings and its highest haul since 2022 during the onset of the Russia-Ukraine war. Broken down, Exxon made about $ 160 million per day last quarter. Chevron, the No."
ExxonMobil,,,,Syracuse,Exxon Is Bullish on Mideast Despite Half-Million-Barrel War Hit,Bloomberg,2026-07-31T11:00:11.417000Z,2026-07-31 11:00:11.417000+00:00,MarketingActivity,https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-31/exxon-is-bullish-on-mideast-despite-half-million-barrel-war-hit,"ExxonMobil Holdings Corp. is standing by Mideast growth plans despite the Iran conflict that knocked half-a-million barrels of the company's daily production offline. "" We 're not going to make broad investment decisions based on today's headlines ,"" Chief Financial Officer Neil Hansen said during an interview. "" We thrive in these types of environments, and we remain committed to the current and future investments in the region ."" Before the war began in late February, ExxonMobil was pumping the equivalent of 900,000 barrels of crude a day in the United Arab Emirates and Qatar, or roughly one-fifth of its global output. Both nations have seen oil output and exports choked as the conflict effectively shut the Strait of Hormuz."
