Borouge,,,,Perplexity,Borouge International and Lanxess Advance Circular Acetone with Borvida B-acetone,ChemXplore,2026-06-01T00:00:00Z,2026-06-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.chemxplore.com/news/borouge-international-lanxess-acetone-sustainability,"Borouge International was reported to be supplying Lanxess with Borvida™ B-acetone, an ISCC PLUS-certified product derived from non-food waste and residue biomass. The development is relevant to procurement and supplier negotiations because it shows Borouge expanding certified circular raw-material offerings that may command premium pricing or support sustainability requirements."
Borouge,,,,Syracuse,Borouge revenue rises as it finds Hormuz workaround,AGBI,2026-08-03T09:23:04Z,2026-08-03 09:23:04+00:00,FinancialsActivity,https://www.agbi.com/petrochemicals/2026/08/borouge-revenue-rises-as-it-finds-hormuz-workaround/,"Abu Dhabi petrochemical company Borouge reported increased revenue in the second quarter. The top line increased 8 percent year on year to $ 1.4 billion in the quarter ending in June, as the company used alternative logistics routes to cut its dependence on the Strait of Hormuz. The company said the rise was driven by higher average selling prices in a tight polyolefins market with stable customer demand. Production volumes fell 24 percent year on year, due to the impact of asset damage sustained at the Ruwais complex on April 5 and the closure of the Strait of Hormuz, which restricted exports and led upstream suppliers to temporarily reduce output. Repair activities were accelerated throughout the quarter, enabling a return to full production at the Ruwais complex by the end of June, the company said in a statement to the Abu Dhabi Securities Exchange."
Borouge,,,,Syracuse,Borouge reports 23% rise in Q2 net profit as Ruwais operations recover,Energy Connects,2026-07-31T07:26:30.597000Z,2026-07-31 07:26:30.597000+00:00,FinancialsActivity,https://www.energyconnects.com/news/utilities/2026/july/borouge-reports-23-rise-in-q2-net-profit-as-ruwais-operations-recover/,Borouge reports 23 % rise in Q2 net profit as Ruwais operations recover.
Borouge,,,,Syracuse,"Borouge International launch a new recycled PP compound, Borcycle GE2331SY",Interplas Insights,2026-06-11T16:00:49.747847Z,2026-06-11 16:00:49.747847+00:00,ProductActivity,https://interplasinsights.com/plastics-materials/automotive-plastics-materials-news/borouge-international-recycled-pp-compound-borcycle-ge2331sy/,"Borouge International unveils its new high-performance, recycled polypropylene (PP) compound, Borcycle GE2331SY. Designed for demanding structural automotive components, the material is a finalist in the Plastics Recycling Awards Europe (PRAE) 2026. × Expand Borouge International Borcycle GE2331SY is designed for high-end structural automotive components, including center console carriers and dashboard carriers. Borcycle GE2331SY demonstrates Borouge International's commitment to delivering materials offering greater efficiency, durability, and circularity across critical applications. The glass-fibre reinforced compound combines 40 % post-consumer recycled material with 20 % glass fibres to provide the strength required for interior structural parts."
Borouge,,,,Syracuse,AD Ports' Safeen Drydocks signs Dh1.3bn local and international shipbuilding deals,The National,2026-06-04T00:00:00Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,PartnershipActivity,https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/economy/2026/06/04/ad-ports-safeen-drydocks-signs-dh13bn-local-and-international-shipbuilding-deals/,"The company did not break down the individual costs of the projects or provide a time frame for their delivery. "" These contract awards demonstrate Safeen Drydocks' ability to deliver complex vessel construction programmes for both local and international customers ,"" said Ammar Al Shaiba, chief executive of AD Ports' maritime and shipping cluster. Play 39:50 DP World's top executive on why trade never stops. "" Expanding in-country capacity remains strategically important, supporting industrial growth, strengthening resilience across the maritime sector and reinforcing the UAE's position as an emerging regional shipbuilding hub ."" AD Ports Group, which posted a 43 per cent profit increase in the first quarter of this year, also recently signed an agreement with Abu Dhabi chemicals group Borouge to study the concept of an alternative export hub at Fujairah on the country's east coast."
Borouge,,,,Syracuse,AD Ports Group and Borouge sign pact for potential Fujairah export terminal,The National,2026-05-19T00:00:00Z,2026-05-19 00:00:00+00:00,PartnershipActivity,https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/05/19/ad-ports-group-and-borouge-sign-pact-for-potential-fujairah-export-terminal/,"Abu Dhabi chemicals maker Borouge and AD Ports Group have made an agreement to study the concept of an alternative export hub on the country's east coast. The move is aimed at boosting the export resilience of Borouge, allowing the company to bypass the Strait of Hormuz, where months-long blockades by Iran and the US have disrupted maritime operations. The agreement is ""an essential element of Borouge's long-term export strategy"" which will ensure continuity of delivery for its global client and add ""resilience by design"" across its logistics network, the companies said in a joint statement on Tuesday. AD Ports Group, the biggest ports and free zones operator in Abu Dhabi, is evaluating ways to cut reliance on ""constrained maritime passages"". The collaboration will involve AD Ports' strong marine connectivity and access to its comprehensive services of Fujairah Terminals and Eastern ports facilities in the UAE, ""while assessing the development of dedicated polyolefins infrastructure on the east coast"", the companies said."
Borouge,,,,Syracuse,Al Ain Farms and Borouge expand UAE packaging resin deal,Packaging Gateway,2026-05-11T13:31:13Z,2026-05-11 13:31:13+00:00,PartnershipActivity,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/al-ain-farms-borouge-packaging-resin/,"Credit: Yudi Herdadi / Shutterstock.com. Al Ain Farms Group and petrochemicals company Borouge have signed a memorandum of understanding (MoU) to expand supplies of locally made resin used in the food producer's packaging operations, according to a press release posted on Zawya. Signed during the Make it in the Emirates event, the MoU states that Borouge will supply 3,50tpa of high-density polyethylene resin for Al Ain Farms Group's caps and closures unit. The petrochemicals company will also support the group's planned move into in-house blow moulding. Borouge CEO Hazeem Sultan Al Suwaidi said: ""Borouge is proud to support the UAE's leading food producers with locally manufactured resin solutions to help them grow reliably and sustainably."
