Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund (TSE:CHE.UN) Shares Cross Above 200 Day Moving Average – Here’s What Happened - American Market News,www.americanbankingnews.com (ABMN Staff),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.americanbankingnews.com/2026/08/05/chemtrade-logistics-income-fund-tseche-un-shares-cross-above-200-day-moving-average-heres-what-happened.html,"# Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund (TSE:CHE.UN) Shares Cross Above 200 Day Moving Average – Here’s What Happened ... Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund (TSE:CHE.UN – Get Free Report) passed above its two hundred day moving average during trading on Tuesday . The stock has a two hundred day moving average of C$16.11 and traded as high as C$ 16.30. Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund shares last traded at C$16.28, with a volume of 229,516 shares traded. ... Several brokerages recently issued reports on CHE.UN. Scotia boosted their price target on shares of Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund from C$17.00 to C$ 19.00 and gave the company a “sector perform” rating in a research report on Thursday, May 14th. Raymond James Financial upgraded shares of Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund from a “market perform” rating to an “outperform” rating and raised their price objective for the stock from C$15.00 to C$ 21.00 in a report on Tuesday, April 28th. National Bank Financial lifted their price objective on Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund from C$18.00 to C$ 23.50 and gave the company an “outperform” rating in a research report on Monday, April 13th. BMO Capital Markets upgraded Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund from a “market perform” rating to an “outperform” rating and set a C$18.50 target price on the stock in a report on Thursday, April 23rd. Finally, Royal Bank Of Canada increased their target price on Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund from C$ 18.00 to C$20.00 and gave the stock an “outperform” rating in a research report on Wednesday, May 13th. Five analysts have rated the stock with a Buy rating and two have assigned a Hold rating to the stock. According to data from MarketBeat, the company presently has an average rating of “Moderate Buy” and a consensus target price of C$ 19.25. ... ## Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund Trading Down 0.5% ... The company has a debt-to-equity ratio of 128.02, a current ratio of 0.40 and a quick ratio of 0.47. The stock’s 50-day moving average is C$16.33 and its two-hundred day moving average is C$ 16.11. The company has a market cap of C$1.83 billion, a P/E ratio of 15.81 and a beta of 0.88. ... Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund (TSE:CHE.UN – Get Free Report) last posted its earnings results on Monday, May 11th. The company reported C$0.23 EPS for the quarter. The business had revenue of C$ 503.00 million during the quarter. Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund had a net margin of 7.85% and a return on equity of 19.73%. As a group, equities research analysts predict that Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund will post 0.9919929 earnings per share for the current fiscal year. ... Chemtrade operates a diversified business providing industrial chemicals and services to customers in North America and around the world. Chemtrade is one of North America’s largest suppliers of sulphuric acid, spent acid processing services, inorganic coagulants for water treatment, sodium chlorate, sodium nitrite and sodium hydrosulphite. Chemtrade is also one of the largest producers of high purity sulphuric acid for the semiconductor industry in North America. Chemtrade is a leading regional supplier of sulphur, chlor-alkali products, and zinc oxide."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,"Ascent Industries (ACNT) Q2 2026 Results: Net Sales Surge 37.6%, Adjusted EBITDA Up $1.8M, Midwest Acquisition Boosts Growth – Minichart",www.minichart.com.sg,2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.minichart.com.sg/2026/08/05/ascent-industries-acnt-q2-2026-results-net-sales-surge-37-6-adjusted-ebitda-up-1-8m-midwest-acquisition-boosts-growth/,"Ascent Industries (ACNT) Q2 2026 Results: Net Sales Surge 37.6%, Adjusted EBITDA Up $1.8M, Midwest Acquisition Boosts Growth – Minichart ... # Ascent Industries (ACNT) Q2 2026 Results: Net Sales Surge 37.6%, Adjusted EBITDA Up $1.8M, Midwest Acquisition Boosts Growth ... # Ascent Industries Co. (Nasdaq: ACNT) Reports Strong Q2 2026 Results: Sales Surge, Profitability Returns, and Strategic Acquisition Delivers Immediate Benefits ... - Net Sales Jump 37.6% YoY: Q2 2026 net sales reached \$25.7 million, up from \$18.7 million in Q2 2025. ... - Adjusted EBITDA Significantly Improves: Adjusted EBITDA was \$1.5 million, a \$1.8 million improvement over Q2 2025, with margin rising to 5.7% from -1.8%. ... - Acquisition of Midwest Graphic Sales and Sigma Coatings: Immediately accretive, the acquisition added \$1.9 million in net sales and \$0.3 million in Adjusted EBITDA in the quarter. ... President and CEO J. Bryan Kitchen described Q2 2026 as one of the strongest quarters in Ascent’s recent history, emphasizing sequential and year-over-year improvements across all key financial metrics. Kitchen credited the company’s ongoing optimization initiatives for the significant increase in gross margin and Adjusted EBITDA, despite a specialty chemicals market that remains soft. ... Management highlighted that the successful integration of the Midwest Graphic Sales and Sigma Coatings acquisition was completed ahead of schedule, with the business performing in line with expectations and contributing positively to both gross profit and Adjusted EBITDA. The operational integration was completed a full quarter early, and manufacturing transition is proceeding as planned. The acquisition is already generating opportunities beyond the original underwriting case. ... Kitchen reiterated that Ascent’s platform-wide optimization initiative is on track to deliver a run-rate improvement of \$3 million to \$5 million in annualized gross profit by year-end 2026. The company has focused on standardizing, simplifying, and optimizing its operations, and management believes these efforts will further enhance earnings power and long-term shareholder returns. ... The company has also executed disciplined capital allocation, including strategic share repurchases, strengthening the balance sheet, and focusing on higher-return investments. ... - Immediate Accretion from Acquisition: The Midwest Graphic Sales and Sigma Coatings acquisition delivered immediate positive contributions, de-risking the transaction and supporting future growth and margin expansion. ... for a material ... could lead to further upside if achieved. ... Ascent Industries Co. (Nasdaq: ACNT) is a specialty chemicals platform delivering differentiated, performance-driven chemical solutions for a range of industries."
