ers; BMS and AstraZeneca reportedly in merger talks"
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,"Univar Solutions Acquires H.M. Royal, Expanding Reach in",www.globenewswire.com (Univar Solutions LLC),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/08/03/3337722/0/en/Univar-Solutions-Acquires-H-M-Royal-Expanding-Reach-in-Rubber-Plastics-and-Adhesive-Additives-in-the-United-States.html,"Univar Solutions Acquires H.M. Royal, Expanding Reach in ... # Univar Solutions Acquires H.M. Royal, Expanding Reach in Rubber, Plastics, and Adhesive Additives in the United States ... August 03, 2026 11:04 ET | Source: Univar Solutions LLC Univar Solutions LLC ... Strengthens service and supply across key U. ... . markets by bringing together a century of technical expertise and trusted customers relationships ... DOWNERS GROVE, Ill., Aug. 03, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Univar Solutions LLC (“Univar Solutions” or “the Company”), a leading global solutions provider to users of specialty ingredients and chemicals, today announced it has acquired H.M. Royal, a highly respected 101-year-old specialty distributor of rubber, plastics, and adhesive additives. The addition of H.M. Royal strengthens the Performance Materials business within the Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions division, expanding access to specialized products, technical knowledge, and long-standing customer relationships, particularly on the East and West Coasts, where H.M. Royal has a strong presence. As the organizations come together, H.M. Royal customers will gain access to Univar Solutions’ broader scale, logistics network, and digital tools, while continuing to benefit from the technical expertise and trusted relationships that have been central to H.M. Royal’s success. ... ""We’re proud to welcome H.M. Royal into the Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions family,” said Nick Powell, CEO of Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions. “They bring deep technical expertise in rubber, plastics, and adhesives, along with long-standing customer and supplier partnerships, and together we offer an enhanced portfolio and team of professionals to better support customers in the U.S. Underscored by a shared commitment to service and excellence, this strategic partnership builds on both companies’ legacy of values-first and customer-centric business.” ... “H.M. Royal has long been a trusted partner in the rubber, plastics adhesives, sealants, and protective coatings spaces, and this marks an important step forward for our Performance Materials business,” said Matthew Oliver, Senior Vice President of Performance Materials for Univar Solutions. “This combination allows us to create a more connected platform in rubber and plastics, strengthen collaboration, and open new opportunities for growth across the value chain. We are committed to preserving and building on the technical knowledge, supplier relationships, and market focus that have made H.M. Royal successful, especially in applications where consistency, processing performance, and reliable supply matter most.” ... The combined organization is expected to deliver broader product access, extended technical support, and greater supply continuity for customers and supplier partners, building on both companies’ century-plus legacy of service and expertise. ... “For more than 100 years, H.M. Royal has built its reputation on strong relationships, integrity, technical expertise, and an unwavering commitment to our customers and suppliers,” said Joseph Royal, President of H.M. Royal. “We are excited to join Univar Solutions, a company that shares these core values. Together, we look forward to building on H.M. Royal’s proud legacy and creating new opportunities for our employees, customers, and supply partners.” ... About Univar SolutionsUnivar Solutions is a leading global specialty chemical and ingredient distributor representing a premier portfolio from the world’s leading producers. With one of the industry’s largest private transportation fleets and technical sales force, unparalleled logistics know-how, deep market and regulatory knowledge, formulation and recipe development, and leading digital tools, the Company is well-positioned to offer tailored solutions and value-added services to a wide range of markets, industries, and applications. While fulfilling its purpose to help keep communities healthy, fed, clean, and safe, Univar Solutions is committed to helping customers and suppliers innovate and focus on Growing Together. Learn more at univarsolutions.com. ... About H.M. Royal H.M. Royal is a long-established distributor of specialty raw materials and chemicals, backed by decades of supplier relationships and 101 years of industry experience. The company offers over 1,000 chemical grades and supports customers with reliable supply, repackaging, and inventory management capabilities tailored to their needs. With 10 strategically located warehouses across the United States, H.M. Royal is positioned to provide timely delivery in quantities ranging from small bags to full truckloads. Its product portfolio serves a wide range of industries, including transportation, electronics, medical, construction, agriculture, mining, and industrial markets. As a family-owned business with third-generation leadership, H.M. Royal emphasizes personal service, dependable support, and cost-effective solutions for North American customers. ... August 04, 2026 12:17 ET | Source: Univar Solutions LLC ... Univar Solutions 收购 H.M. Royal，扩大在美国橡胶、塑料及胶粘剂助剂领域的布局 ... 融合百年技术积淀与值得信赖的客户关系，强化在美国关键市场的服务与供应能力 伊利诺伊州唐纳斯格罗夫, Aug. 05, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- 全球领先的特种原料和化学品解决方案提供商 Univar Solutions LLC（简称“Univar Solutions”或“公司”）今日宣布已收购 H.M. Royal——一家拥有 101... ... July 3 ... 026 ... :27 ET ... Source: Univar Solutions LLC ... Univar Solutions ... 年度承运商颁奖礼表 ... 顶尖运输合作伙伴 ... 伊利诺伊州唐纳斯格罗夫, Aug. 01, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- 全球领先的特种原料与化学品解决方案提供商 Univar Solutions LLC (“Univar Solutions” 或“公司”)，周四公布年度承运商奖获奖名单，表彰在北美地区表现卓越、合作紧密、并致力于提供安全可靠服务的运输合作伙伴。 ..."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,"SK Pharmteco Completes Obesity-Drug API Plant, Sets Up Peptide CDMO Clash With Samsung - Seoul Economic Daily",en.sedaily.com (Tae-heui Han),2026-08-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/08/02/sk-pharmteco-completes-obesity-drug-api-plant-sets-up,"Pharmteco Completes Obesity-Drug API ... SK Biotek, the domestic subsidiary of SK Pharmteco, has completed a new plant in Sejong to produce active pharmaceutical ingredients (API) for obesity treatments. As demand for peptide ingredients surges amid the growth of the global obesity-drug market, competition for orders with Samsung Biologics (207940.KS), which recently acquired a peptide CDMO company, is also expected to intensify. ... According to industry sources on the 2nd, SK Biotek received approval to use its new Sejong facility, the ""M5 plant,"" at the end of June this year. The facility is a peptide API plant newly built to meet demand for glucagon-like peptide (GLP)-1 class obesity treatments. Spanning 12,634 square meters, it can produce dozens of tons of small-molecule and peptide drugs annually across eight production trains. SK Pharmteco decided in 2024 to invest $260 million to build the plant. It was completed about a year after construction began last year. SK Inc. established SK Pharmteco in Sacramento, in the United States, in 2019 to operate its global pharmaceutical contract development and manufacturing organization (CDMO) business structure. SK Biotek is SK Pharmteco's Korean subsidiary. ... Once the new plant begins full operation next year, it is expected to generate about 400 billion won in annual revenue. That is equivalent to 43% of SK Pharmteco's revenue last year (932 billion won). SK Pharmteco secured orders for obesity-drug API in advance of the new plant's completion. After signing a supply contract with Eli Lilly in 2024 worth up to 2 trillion won over five years, it has been producing API for clinical use since this year. Kim Soo-hyun, head of the research center at DS Investment & Securities, explained, ""This API is used to develop a long-acting formulation that extends the dosing cycle from once a week to once a month."" SK Pharmteco is expected to move into commercial API production following the plant's completion. ... SK Pharmteco's push to expand peptide production capacity comes as demand for peptide API is rising rapidly with the growth of the GLP-1 class treatment market. A peptide is a substance made of two or more amino acids, the basic units of protein, linked together. Representative drugs developed by artificially synthesizing these to mimic the action of hormones in the body are GLP-1 class obesity treatments such as Wegovy and Mounjaro. According to market research firm Fortune Business Insights, the global GLP-1 receptor agonist market is projected to grow from $73.4 billion (about 107 trillion won) in 2026 to $254.2 billion (about 372 trillion won) in 2034. ... SK Pharmteco plans to expand additional orders based on the production track record accumulated at the new Sejong plant. It plans to build peptide production capacity at the California plant of AMPAC in the United States going forward. SK Pharmteco holds contract manufacturing (CMO) affiliates based in the United States and Europe, including SK Biotek, SK Biotek Ireland, AMPAC, Yposkesi, and CBM. ... Samsung Biologics also decided on the 20th of last month to acquire a 100% stake in PolyPeptide, a peptide CDMO company, for 2.7 trillion won. Unlike building production facilities in-house through new plant construction, the strategy is to secure a production base in a short period through mergers and acquisitions (M&A). PolyPeptide currently holds six production sites across five countries, including Europe, the United States, and India, and posted revenue of 389.3 million euros (about 656.4 billion won) last year. If the acquisition process is completed by year-end, the acquired company's performance is expected to be reflected in consolidated financial statements for a full year starting next year. ... Along with the entry of the two conglomerates, competition in the CDMO business surrounding the peptide market is also heating up. Major competitors such as Switzerland's Lonza and China's WuXi are supporting peptide CDMO services in addition to existing biopharmaceuticals. Domestic companies such as HLB Pep and Hanmi Fine Chemical are also broadening their business base by expanding peptide production facilities. An industry official stressed, ""The scope of peptide drug applications is expanding to cancer, immune and rare diseases, and brain disorders,"" adding, ""Competition among CDMO companies to secure production capacity will become even fiercer going forward."""
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Investment firm acquires majority stake in Indianapolis-based ShipSigma – Indianapolis Business Journal,www.ibj.com (Susan Orr),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ibj.com/articles/investment-firm-acquires-majority-stake-in-indianapolis-based-shipsigma,Investment firm acquires majority stake in Indianapolis-based ShipSigma – Indianapolis Business Journal
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Clean Science To Incorporate 100% Wholly Owned Subsidiary In The Netherlands For Global Expansion,www.sahi.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sahi.com/news/clean-science-to-incorporate-100-wholly-owned-subsidiary-in-the-netherlands-for-global-expansion-4407-PE1_COR,"Clean Science is establishing a 100% step-down wholly-owned subsidiary in the Netherlands under Clean-Fino Chem Limited. The new Dutch entity will spearhead European sales, distribution, and trading of specialty chemicals. An initial capital of EUR 50,000 will be infused in tranches, keeping the upfront risk structure highly capital-efficient. This international push follows the company's recent exclusive global HALS manufacturing partnership with Swiss-based Geneus Chem AG. ... Market snapshot: Clean Science and Technology Limited's Board has approved the incorporation of a wholly-owned step-down subsidiary in the Netherlands under its existing subsidiary, Clean-Fino Chem Limited. This strategic move, backed by an initial capital infusion of EUR 50,000, aims to scale the company’s global specialty chemical sales, trading, and distribution footprint. ... - The proposed subsidiary in the Netherlands is approved with an initial capital of EUR 50,000 (equivalent to approximately ₹45.3 L) to be infused in tranches. - Clean Science's wholly-owned subsidiary Clean-Fino Chem Limited entered into a long-term strategic partnership with Swiss-based Geneus Chem AG, securing exclusive manufacturing rights with warrants to acquire a 25% stake in GC within 4 years. - Clean Science recorded a standalone FY26 revenue of ₹815 crore, declining from ₹922 crore in FY25. - Standalone FY26 Profit After Tax (PAT) stood at ₹251 crore, reflecting a decline of 14% from ₹292 crore in FY25, though stand-alone EBITDA margins remained resilient at 44.3%. ... - Standalone operating revenues for FY26 contracted by 11.6% YoY to ₹815 crore (derived: ₹815 cr vs ₹922 cr in FY25), primarily owing to global pricing headwinds and the loss of a key FMCG customer segment. - Net standalone profit after tax fell 14% to ₹251 crore in FY26 compared to ₹292 crore in the prior fiscal year, signaling near-term pressure in the base performance chemical segments. - Clean Science has significantly ramped up subsidiary funding, executing a ₹50 cr rights issue subscription in Clean-Fino Chem Limited in June 2026, positioning the subsidiary to lead global manufacturing and distribution operations. ... - Direct European Footprint: Establishing a physical Dutch entity allows Clean Science to engage directly with European chemical consumers, bypassing distributor networks and capturing higher margins. - Structured Growth Mechanism: Placing the Dutch wing as a step-down unit under Clean-Fino Chem unifies the company's international business strategy, linking European sales directly to their primary HALS manufacturing subsidiary. - Capital-Light Initial Risk: An initial equity setup of EUR 50,000 (~₹45.3 L) demonstrates a phased, low-risk approach to expanding geographical operations before deploying substantial capital. - Strategic Synergy with Swiss Deal: The Dutch distribution channel is uniquely positioned to handle marketing and logistics for the advanced grades of Hindered Amine Light Stabilizers (HALS) that Clean-Fino Chem will exclusively manufacture for Swiss partner Geneus Chem AG. ... The incorporation of a Dutch subsidiary is a calculated move to transition Clean Science from a domestic exporter to an internationally integrated specialty chemical player. In FY26, the company's standalone business suffered due to aggressive Chinese competition in products like MEHQ and anisole. By shifting its growth core to its subsidiary, Clean-Fino Chem, and building localized marketing wings in key global chemical hubs like the Netherlands, the management is aiming to capture high-margin global market share. This step-down structure, integrated with the recent Swiss HALS alliance, is a clear long-term play to offset localized pricing pressures and revive volume growth. ... The specialty chemicals industry is slowly emerging from a cycle of aggressive destocking and severe pricing competition. Clean Science's active expansion in Europe indicates that it expects international market gains to provide a strong buffer against domestic margin compression. With its HALS export mix already reaching 50%, setting up localized trading and job-work divisions in the Netherlands will likely optimize logistic chains and enhance competitive delivery timelines in Western markets. ... While the international expansion and the strategic HALS alliance are structurally positive for the medium-to-long term, Clean Science continue to navigate challenging near-term margins and volume contractions in its core standalone business, as evidenced by the 14% decline in standalone FY26 PAT. ... - Timely incorporation and operational scaling of the Netherlands subsidiary. - Volume ramp-up and EBITDA margin expansion at the Clean-Fino Chem subsidiary in coming quarters. - Stabilization of Chinese pricing pressure on core chemical product categories. ... Indian specialty chemical manufacturers are increasingly establishing international marketing arms to compete effectively on the global stage. Shifting from indirect exports to a localized step-down subsidiary structure is a growing industry trend designed to capture higher realizations from end-users, particularly in highly regulated Western markets where sustainability and green chemistry standards are premium differentiators. ... - Geopolitical uncertainty and logistical disruptions in European shipping lanes could affect delivery timelines. - Slower-than-expected commercialization of premium product categories like Performance Chemical 2 (delayed to September 2026). - Sustained crude price volatility impacting raw material cost structures. ... On July 16, 2026, wholly owned subsidiary Clean-Fino Chem Limited executed a long-term strategic partnership with Switzerland-based startup Geneus Chem AG, securing exclusive worldwide manufacturing rights for advanced HALS grades and an option to buy up to 25% equity in the Swiss company within 4 years. On June 24, 2026, Clean Science also subscribed to a ₹50 cr rights issue of Clean-Fino Chem to support its working capital and capex needs. ... Clean Science’s expansion into the Netherlands shows strategic agility. By placing its international distribution wing directly under Clean-Fino Chem, the group is establishing a robust commercial pipeline to handle advanced products as the chemical market cycle recovers."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,"Sigma Advanced Systems bags Rs 1,013 crore export order for 155mm artillery shell bodies - The Economic Times",economictimes.indiatimes.com (Shilpa Ranipeta),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/defence/sigma-advanced-systems-bags-rs-1013-crore-export-order-for-155mm-artillery-shell-bodies/articleshow/132653393.cms,"Sigma Advanced Systems bags Rs 1,013 crore export order for 155mm artillery shell bodies - The Economic Times ... Defence›Sigma Advanced Systems bags Rs 1,013 crore export order for 155mm artillery shell bodies ... # Sigma Advanced Systems bags Rs 1,013 crore export order for 155mm artillery shell bodies ... Sigma Advanced Systems bags Rs 1,013 crore export order for 155mm artillery shell bodies ... Sigma Advanced Systems secured a significant export order valued at over one thousand crore rupees. This contract involves manufacturing and supplying 147,000 units of 155mm base bleed artillery shell bodies. The Hyderabad-based firm will execute this substantial order over the next six to twelve months. This marks an expansion into more advanced artillery shell manufacturing for the company. ... The Hyderabad-based company said the contract marks its entry into the production of advanced base bleed artillery shells, following earlier export orders for 155mm fuzes and M107 artillery shell bodies. (Representational Image) ... Hyderabad: Defence manufacturer Sigma Advanced Systems Ltd has secured an export order worth $104.9 million (around Rs 1,013 crore) from a North American customer to manufacture and supply 147,000 units of 155mm base bleed artillery shell bodies, the company said on Monday. The order is scheduled to be executed over the next six to 12 months.The Hyderabad-based company said the contract marks its entry into manufacturing more advanced base bleed artillery shells, after previously securing export orders for 155mm fuzes and M107 artillery shell bodies. Base bleed shells are designed to extend the range of artillery systems by reducing aerodynamic drag during flight through a gas-generating unit at the rear of the projectile, while remaining compatible with existing 155mm artillery platforms. ... Read More: DRDO partners with AIESL, Adani Defence for new surveillance aircraft The company said the order comes amid rising global demand for extended-range artillery ammunition as countries increase investments in defence modernisation and ammunition stockpiling. ... Sigma said the contract is expected to improve its profitability and strengthen its position in the global defence manufacturing supply chain by adding a reference programme for future export opportunities."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Sigma Advanced System secures USD 104.9M export order from North America | Capital Market News - Business Standard,www.business-standard.com (Business Standard),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.business-standard.com/markets/capital-market-news/sigma-advanced-system-secures-usd-104-9m-export-order-from-north-america-126072700150_1.html,"Sigma Advanced System secures USD 104.9M export order from North America | Capital Market News - Business Standard ... Home/ Markets/ Capital Market News/ Sigma Advanced System secures USD 104.9M export order from North America ... # Sigma Advanced System secures USD 104.9M export order from North America ... Last Updated : Jul 27 2026 | 3:50 PM IST ... To supply 147,000 units of 155mm base bleed artillery shell bodies ... Sigma Advanced System has secured a USD 104.9 million (roughly Rs 1,013 crore) export order from a North American customer for the manufacture and supply of 147,000 units of 155mm base bleed artillery shell bodies which are in massive demand worldwide. The order will be executed in the next 6 to 12 months. ... As Sigma continues to invest in R&D and further advance its technological capabilities, it is adapting to the latest global requirements. Having previously secured contracts for 155mm fuzes and M107 artillery shell bodies, the company is now manufacturing more technologically advanced blase bleed shells that integrate aerodynamics, energetics, propulsion-related technologies, and systems engineering into the projectile. The progression reflects Sigma's deliberate strategy to move up the value chain in artillery ammunition, building the engineering capability and programme credentials expected by global customers from their long-term strategic suppliers. ... The programme involves manufacturing of precision-engineered artillery projectile casings designed for integration into extended-range ammunition systems. Unlike conventional artillery shells, which experience aerodynamic drag and turbulence at the base of the projectile during flight, base bleed shells incorporate a gas-generating unit at the rear that reduces this drag, significantly extending the effective range of the system while maintaining full compatibility with existing 155mm artillery platforms in service worldwide."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Site visit: Sigma’s lithium mine operating after restructuring,source.benchmarkminerals.com (Benchmark Team),2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://source.benchmarkminerals.com/article/site-visit-sigma-s-grota-do-cirilo-lithium-mine-operating-at-capacity-following-restructuring,"Site visit: Sigma’s lithium mine operating after restructuring ... Spodumene concentrate 5% stockpile. The visit showed active trucking activity both at the mine site and transport to port. ... Benchmark’s July visit to Sigma Lithium's Grota do Cirilo operation in Minas Gerais, Brazil, came just before the company reported its strongest operating quarter in over a year. Sigma Lithium had paused operation at the mine in October 2025 for upgrades, though the restart was complicated by three waste piles at the site being shut down following a, now-resolved, government inspection at the start of 2026. Federico Gay, Benchmark’s principal lithium analyst, visited the site mid-July to “establish whether the mining restart had genuinely taken hold”. The visit also offered a chance to see on the ground how the self-imposed restructuring of its mine, following a period of operational bottlenecks, resulted in a significant operational turnaround “On the evidence in front of us,” Gay said, “the mine is operating at full capacity, with active blasting, continuous load and haul operations on both pits, supported by a fully functioning DMS plant, with a clear path of growth ahead."""
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Sigma Advanced Systems Completes Full Acquisition of UK's Bromford Precision Solutions,www.sahi.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sahi.com/news/sigma-advanced-systems-completes-full-acquisition-of-uk-s-bromford-precision-solutions-2800-PE1_COR,"Sigma Advanced Systems Completes Full Acquisition of UK's Bromford Precision Solutions ... Sigma Advanced Systems Completes Full Acquisition of UK's Bromford Precision Solutions ... Sigma Advanced Systems has closed its acquisition of UK's Bromford Precision Solutions for £11.89 million (approx. ₹153 crore). This 100% equity buyout integrates Bromford's high-precision aeroengine component manufacturing into Sigma's global aerospace and defense platform, enhancing capabilities in UK and European markets. ... Market snapshot: Sigma Advanced Systems Limited has successfully completed its 100% acquisition of UK-based aerospace manufacturer Bromford Precision Solutions Limited. The transaction, initially announced on July 14, 2026, was finalized on July 22, 2026, following the satisfaction of all condition precedents. This move expands Sigma's international aerospace manufacturing footprint, especially within key global supply chains like Rolls-Royce. ... - The acquisition of 100% equity share capital of Bromford Precision Solutions is valued at approximately £11.89 million (approximately ₹153 crore). - Bromford's turnover for the twelve-month period ending April 30, 2026, stood at £1.782 crore (approximately ₹228.04 crore). - The transaction was executed at an enterprise value to CY2026 estimated adjusted EBITDA multiple of approximately 4.6x. ... - Sigma Advanced Systems transitions from an India-centric precision player into a globally integrated aerospace manufacturer with dual manufacturing bases in India and the UK. - The acquisition integrates Bromford's specialized precision rings and engine structures manufacturing capability, broadening product offerings for key aerospace original equipment manufacturers (OEMs). ... - Full ownership: Sigma has completed 100% acquisition of Bromford Precision Solutions following the satisfaction of conditions precedent on July 22, 2026. - Strategic value: The acquisition expands Sigma's existing UK footprint alongside its subsidiary, Nasmyth Group, and deepens integration within the Rolls-Royce and Siemens aerospace supply chains. - Financial viability: Acquired at a multiple of approximately 4.6x estimated CY2026 adjusted EBITDA, demonstrating capital discipline. - Growth playbook: Sigma aims to optimize margins by implementing capital investment, automation, and transferring select manufacturing activities to India. ... The completion of Bromford's acquisition marks a crucial milestone in Sigma's inorganic expansion. By bringing Bromford's high-precision aerospace component capability and long-term OEM contracts under its fold, Sigma not only gains specialized manufacturing assets in Leicestershire but also cements its position as a global Tier-1 partner. This synergistic combination will likely yield cost-efficiency benefits through selective offshoring of manufacturing to India, while retaining advanced engineering expertise in the UK. ... The consolidation reflects the growing prowess of Indian defense and aerospace companies acquiring international aerospace assets to capture a larger share of the global supply chain. Positive investor sentiment is likely as the acquisition adds an established revenue-generating business with certified OEM approvals to Sigma's portfolio, reinforcing its long-term growth outlook. ... The successful completion of this ₹153 crore UK acquisition reinforces Sigma's global aerospace capabilities and revenue diversification. It follows closely after raising ₹459.99 crore via share allotment, indicating strong capital backing and execution capability. ... - Integration progress and realization of cost synergies through manufacturing shift to India. - Contribution of Bromford's revenue and margins to Sigma's consolidated financials. - Securing of new high-value aerospace contracts through the combined global platform. ... Global aerospace and defense supply chains are experiencing intense modernization and shifting toward integrated, multi-location platforms. By combining Bromford's precision rings manufacturing in the UK with Sigma's domestic facilities in India, the enlarged group positions itself as a highly competitive and resilient global supplier. ... - Integration challenges across cross-border manufacturing locations and regulatory environments. - Slower-than-expected margin improvement or delays in transferring component manufacturing to India. - Dependence on key global aerospace OEMs like Rolls-Royce for sustained order inflows. ... Sigma has made several strategic strides in recent months: (1) In June 2026, it bagged a ₹208 crore export order to supply 155 mm artillery shell bodies to a North American customer. (2) In February 2026, it acquired Delhi-based AS Strategic for ₹30 crore to expand into European markets. (3) In July 2026, it raised ₹459.99 crore by allotting 1.33 crore shares at ₹347 each. ... Sigma's successful buyout of Bromford is a strong signal of its global ambition. Coupled with recent massive order wins and successful capital raising, the company is well-positioned to scale its operations and transition into a formidable global aerospace and defense player."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Sigma Lithium rises after moving to settle dispute with Minas Gerais government (SGML:NASDAQ) | Seeking Alpha,seekingalpha.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://seekingalpha.com/news/4617376-sigma-lithium-rises-after-moving-to-settle-dispute-with-minas-gerais-government,"Sigma Lithium rises after moving to settle dispute with Minas Gerais government (SGML:NASDAQ) | Seeking Alpha ... # Sigma Lithium rises after moving to settle dispute with Minas Gerais government ... Jul 23, 2026, 8:52 AM ET[Sigma Lithium Corporation (SGML) Stock](https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SGML#source=section:main_content|section_asset:meta|first_level_url:news|symbol:SGML)By: [Carl Surran](https://seekingalpha.com/author/sa-editor-carl-surran#source=section:main_content|section_asset:meta|button:author_name|first_level_url:news), SA News Editor ... Sigma Lithium ([SGML](https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SGML)) up 3.8% pre-market Thursday after saying it has started [negotiating](https://seekingalpha.com/pr/20592281-sigma-lithium-negotiating-agreement-with-minas-gerais-state-government-to-settle-notification) a ""terms for adjustment of procedures"" agreement with Brazil's Minas Gerais state government following the issuance of fines totaling \~US$540K related to environmental issues that occurred during 2013-22."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Should Chemtrade’s Extended North Vancouver Chlorine Operations and Safety Covenant Reshape the (TSX:CHE.UN) Investment Thesis? - Simply Wall St News,simplywall.st,2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://simplywall.st/stocks/ca/materials/tsx-che.un/chemtrade-logistics-income-fund-shares/news/should-chemtrades-extended-north-vancouver-chlorine-operatio,"Should Chemtrade’s Extended North Vancouver Chlorine Operations and Safety Covenant Reshape the (TSX:CHE.UN) Investment Thesis? - Simply Wall St News ... - Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund recently secured final approval for the rezoning of its North Vancouver chlor-alkali facility, allowing liquid chlorine production to continue until the earlier of its Vancouver Fraser Port Authority lease expiry or 2046 and enabling planned safety upgrades under a new restrictive covenant with the District. - This agreement not only extends operational certainty for a key asset, but also formalizes community oversight and safety reporting, potentially reducing regulatory overhang and reputational risk. - We’ll now explore how this extended North Vancouver operating horizon and associated safety commitments may influence Chemtrade’s existing investment narrative. ... Chemtrade’s story still rests on a simple thesis: a cash generative chemicals platform gradually tilting toward more resilient water treatment and specialty acid, while managing debt and input cost volatility. The North Vancouver rezoning strengthens the durability of a key chlor alkali asset, but it does not materially alter the near term focus on earnings execution and sulfur related cost risk that could pressure margins if pricing lags. ... Against that backdrop, Chemtrade’s ongoing share buyback program stands out as the most relevant recent development. By May 2026 the fund had repurchased roughly 4.6 percent of its units for about CA$70.3 million, alongside steady monthly distributions of CA$0.06 per unit. Together with the longer operating horizon at North Vancouver, these capital returns frame how management is currently balancing balance sheet priorities with shareholder payouts. ... Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund's narrative projects CA$2.4 billion revenue and CA$216.2 million earnings by 2029. This requires 6.4% yearly revenue growth and a CA$100.5 million earnings increase from CA$115.7 million today. ... Before the rezoning news, the most optimistic analysts were assuming revenue could reach about CA$2.5 billion with earnings near CA$203 million, a far more upbeat view than consensus, especially if safety focused capital at sites like North Vancouver really does help underpin uptime and margins over time. ... - A great starting point for your Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund research is ... analysis highlighting 2 key rewards and ... important warning signs that could impact your investment decision. - Our ... Logistics Income Fund research ... provides a comprehensive fundamental ... summarized in a single visual - the Snowflake - making it easy to evaluate Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund's overall financial health at a glance. ... #### Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund ... Offers industrial chemicals and services in Canada, the United States, and Brazil."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Sigma Lithium Corporation Negotiates Agreement With Minas Gerais State Government To Settle Notification By Regional Environmental State Body | MarketScreener UK,uk.marketscreener.com (S&P Capital IQ),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uk.marketscreener.com/news/sigma-lithium-corporation-negotiates-agreement-with-minas-gerais-state-government-to-settle-notifica-ce7f51ded881ff24,"Sigma Lithium Corporation Negotiates Agreement With Minas Gerais State Government To Settle Notification By Regional Environmental State Body | MarketScreener UK ... | 07-22 | Sigma Lithium Corporation Negotiates Agreement With Minas Gerais State Government To Settle Notification By Regional Environmental State Body | CI | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-10 | Sigma Lithium Shares Rise After Q2 Lithium Production Guidance Exceeded | MT | ... # Sigma Lithium Corporation Negotiates Agreement With Minas Gerais State Government To Settle Notification By Regional Environmental State Body Published on 07/22/2026 at 09:51 pm BST ... S&P Capital IQ ... Sigma Lithium Corporation started negotiating a TAC or terms for adjustment of procedures (""Termo de Ajuste de Conduta"" or ""TAC Agreement""), with the Minas Gerais State Government. The negotiations follow a notification by the Vale do Jequitinhonha branch of SUPRAM, the Minas Gerais environmental state body, which is based in Diamantina, issuing fines totaling approximately USD 540,000. Several fines were related to environmental issues that occurred from 2013 to 2022. ... Sigma Lithium Corporation started negotiating a TAC Agreement directly with the State Government of Minas Gerais in Belo Horizonte, which has regulatory authority in the matter. Sigma Lithium Corporation has agreed to a settlement to be established by the TAC Agreement, in addition to the payment of up to USD 540,000 for the abovementioned fines. The fines are not due for at least 120 days. ... Sigma Lithium Corporation estimates that the execution of the proposed adjustments of environmental procedures under the TAC Agreement will require an estimated capex of approximately USD 1,000,000 to enable the resumption of the activities that have been partially and temporarily suspended by the auditors of SUPRAM Jequitinhonha."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Private equity drives surge in transformative chemicals mergers amid sustainability push | Noah Intelligence,noah-news.com,2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://noah-news.com/private-equity-drives-surge-in-transformative-chemicals-mergers-amid-sustainabil-2/,"Private equity drives surge in transformative chemicals mergers amid sustainability push | Noah Intelligence ... # Private equity drives surge in transformative chemicals mergers amid sustainability push ... Private equity-backed deals continued to dominate the chemicals and materials sector in Q2, with major mergers, acquisitions in niche markets, and a rising focus on circular economy initiatives shaping a resilient and... ... Private equity-backed deals continued to dominate the chemicals and materials sector in Q2, with major mergers, acquisitions in niche markets, and a rising focus on circular economy initiatives shaping a resilient and sustainable industry landscape. ... Private equity continued to loom large over chemicals and materials deal-making in the second quarter, even as strategic buyers used the period to reshape portfolios and deepen positions in faster-growing niches. ... The most prominent transaction was Olin Corporation and Huntsman Corporation’s agreed all-stock merger of equals, a deal valued at $4.8 billion that would create OlinHuntsman and combine upstream scale with downstream formulations. The companies said they expect more than $300 million in cost synergies, plus further raw-material integration benefits later in the decade. ... The quarter also featured several sizeable portfolio moves in ingredients and speciality chemicals. Ingredion’s recommended cash offer for Tate & Lyle, valued at $5.1 billion, underlined the appeal of nutrition, texture and sugar-reduction technologies, while CVC Capital Partners agreed to take a 90% stake in International Flavours & Fragrances’ Food Ingredients business for $4.2 billion. In another major transaction, H.B. Fuller agreed to buy UK medical products maker Advanced Medical Solutions for $943 million, signalling continued investor interest in healthcare-adjacent adhesives and wound-care applications. ... Beyond the headline transactions, the period was crowded with smaller but strategically important acquisitions. K+S moved to strengthen its salt business with the purchase of Qemetica’s sites in Poland and Germany, while Westlake expanded its chlorovinyls footprint by agreeing to buy a PVC and vinyl chloride monomer plant in Wilhelmshaven. There was also a clear recycling and circularity theme: Agilyx-backed GreenDot Global acquired Anviplas Spain, and GreenDot separately increased its stake in GreenDot Global earlier in the spring, as platforms built around waste sorting and recycled plastics continued to attract capital. ... Private equity remained especially active in niche industrial businesses. Mutares agreed to buy Synthomer’s Czech acrylics unit, Valiant Energy Management acquired VanDeMark Chemical, and Parcom took a majority stake in Plastchem, a PVC compounder that recently added a dedicated recycling line. At the same time, sponsor-backed buyers pursued growth in speciality segments ranging from flavours and fragrances to water treatment, with deals such as Ambienta’s investment in GFF, Döhler’s move for Treatt and Rochester Midland’s purchase of ClarityChem. ... The mix of transactions suggests a market that is still rewarding businesses with technical differentiation, recurring demand and local manufacturing strength. It also shows how chemicals M&A is increasingly being shaped by regulatory pressure, sustainability targets and the search for resilient supply chains. Noah Intelligence can help dealmakers and advisers follow how individual announcements, mandates and acquisitions fit into the wider flow of chemicals and banking developments, and what they signal about strategic intent and competitive positioning."
Sigma Chemtrade,,,,Exa,Chemtrade Logistics Announces Successful Final Adoption of Rezoning Application for the North Vancouver Chlor-Alkali Facility,www.bnnbloomberg.ca,2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/press-releases/2026/07/21/chemtrade-logistics-announces-successful-final-adoption-of-rezoning-application-for-the-north-vancouver-chlor-alkali-facility/,"Successful Final Adoption of ... Application for the North ... # Chemtrade Logistics Announces Successful Final Adoption of Rezoning Application for the North Vancouver Chlor-Alkali Facility ... NORTH VANCOUVER, British Columbia--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Chemtrade Logistics Income Fund (TSX: CHE.UN; OTCQX®: CGIFF) (“Chemtrade” or the “Fund”) announced today that the rezoning application for its chlor-alkali facility, located in North Vancouver (the “Facility”), received final adoption at last night’s District of North Vancouver (the “District”) Council meeting. This marks the final step in the rezoning application process. ... Subject to the terms outlined in a restrictive covenant entered into between Chemtrade and the District (the “Restrictive Covenant”), the final adoption of the rezoning bylaw enables Chemtrade to continue to produce liquid chlorine until the earlier of the expiry of Chemtrade’s prospective lease with the Vancouver Fraser Port Authority (the “Port”) or 2046. This certainty of long term continued liquid chlorine operations will allow Chemtrade to advance planned safety upgrades at the Facility. ... The Facility has been operating safely since 1957 and is a key producer of liquid chlorine, which is used in the treatment of municipal drinking water in Canada. The Facility also produces caustic soda and hydrochloric acid - both products play important roles in industries with significant positions in Canada’s economic strategy including the energy sector, pulp and paper, technology, water treatment, and mining. ... “Our facility represents 40 per cent of the available production capacity of liquid chlorine in Canada and plays a critical role supporting both safe drinking water for millions and the supply chains of major industries that are key economic generators for Canada. In total, over 60 per cent of the facility’s production stays in Canada, supporting Canadian businesses and industry,” said Scott Rook, President and CEO of Chemtrade. “We would like to thank the members of the District Council who supported our application, securing critical Canadian production of liquid chlorine, caustic soda and hydrochloric acid. We can now move forward with our plans for additional investments in capital safety projects aimed at improving reliability and safety.” ... In response to concerns voiced by the District Council, Chemtrade made additional commitments secured by the Restrictive Covenant, including regular reporting and opportunity for oversight from the District, timebound liquid chlorine production aligned with the earlier of the termination of the proposed lease with the Port or 2046, and a commitment to ongoing community education and safety and technology reviews. ... Chemtrade will continue to engage with the Port to finalize its land lease for a portion of the Facility situated on Port lands. In 2025, Chemtrade and the Port entered into a non-binding letter of intent outlining terms of a new 20-year agreement. ... Chemtrade operates a diversified business providing industrial chemicals and services to customers in North America and around the world. Chemtrade is one of North America’s largest suppliers of sulphuric acid, spent acid processing services, inorganic coagulants for water treatment, sodium chlorate, sodium nitrite and sodium hydrosulphite. Chemtrade is also one of the largest producers of high purity sulphuric acid for the semiconductor industry in North America. Chemtrade is a leading regional supplier of sulphur, chlor-alkali products, and zinc oxide. Additionally, Chemtrade provides value-added water solutions, as well as industrial services such as processing by-products and waste streams. ... statements can be ... identified by the use of words such as ... anticipate”, “continue”, “estimate”, “expect”, “expected”, “intend”, “may”, “will”, “project”, “plan”, “should”, “believe” and similar expressions. Specifically, forward-looking statements in this news release include statements regarding: Chemtrade’s belief that the adoption of the bylaw amendment secures the long term operational certainty and continued liquid chlorine production until the earlier of expiry of the prospective Port lease or 2046; Chemtrade’s ability to advance planned safety upgrades and the timing thereof; its intention to ensure the continued production of liquid chlorine and long term operations at the Facility; Chemtrade’s intention to move forward with plans for additional investment in capital safety projects; Chemtrade’s expectation that such projects will improve safety and reliability; and Chemtrade’s intention that it will continue engagement with the Port to finalize its land lease for a portion of the Facility situated on Port lands; and Chemtrade’s expectation that a new land lease would result in a 20-year agreement. ... forward-looking statements ... trade’s expectation ... such projects will improve safety and reliability; ... belief that the adoption of the bylaw ... long-term operational certainty and ... liquid chlorine production until the earlier of expiry of the prospective Port lease or 2046; ... expectation that the ... lease with the Port ... be finalized on terms outlined in ... including a lease term of 20 years."
