ferent channels and occasions, including an octagonal seven mini-can pack, a basket-style pack, and an e-commerce solution. ... Throughout the project, the teams worked closely to balance creativity with efficiency through optimising materials, refining structures, and aligning production across multiple sites. ... Chris Zhong, Retail Customer Marketing Manager, Coca-Cola China added: “The World Cup is a key moment for connecting with consumers, and packaging plays an important role in that. Working with Smurfit Westrock, we’ve created solutions that not only stand out on shelf but also deliver a unique experience for consumers wherever they shop.” ... Smurfit Westrock is a leading global provider of paper-based packaging solutions, with approximately 97,000 employees across 40 countries. ... ## Smurfit Westrock partners with Coca-Cola on World Cup packaging ... Smurfit Westrock partnered with Coca-Cola China to launch a series of innovative paper-based packaging solutions... ... ## Smurfit Westrock’s Longview mill under inspection ... The Washington State Department of Labor & Industries (L&I) has opened two new inspections into..."
Westrock,,,,Exa,Illycaffè Faucets Westrock for North American Manufacturing Push - Street Food Spectacle,streetfoodspectacle.com (Street Food Spectacle),2026-07-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://streetfoodspectacle.com/illycaffe-faucets-westrock-for-north-american-manufacturing-push/,"Illycaffè Faucets Westrock for North American Manufacturing Push - Street Food Spectacle ... Illycaffè Faucets Westrock for North American Manufacturing ... Italian espresso large Illycaffè has signed a multi-year strategic manufacturing settlement with Arkansas-based Westrock Espresso Firm for improvement and packaging of particular merchandise for the North American market, in line with the Italian information company Ansa and different Italian information retailers. ... The businesses haven’t publicly introduced the settlement via their very own pressrooms or investor-relations channels. ... The Italian studies describe Westrock as offering a multi-site manufacturing platform that can permit Illy to double the share of merchandise for the North American market which might be packaged domestically, primarily within the ready-to-drink class. ... In a press release to Every day Espresso Information, Westrock Espresso Firm stated, “We’re proud to be a trusted accomplice to most of the world’s most iconic manufacturers, and we’re excited to proceed rising our roster of world companions on our platform, together with as a ready-to-drink (RTD) accomplice, as we broaden our footprint throughout Europe and Asia. We’re excited to welcome Illycaffè as the latest member of our platform.” ... Illycaffè CEO Cristina Scocchia has described america as a precedence marketplace for the Trieste, Italy-based firm, saying Illy has posted double-digit development within the U.S. over the previous 4 years. ... The Italian studies state that Illy’s espresso roasting will stay fully on the firm’s most important manufacturing facility in Trieste, the place the corporate has been increasing manufacturing. ... For Westrock, the settlement aligns with the corporate’s positioning as a large-scale beverage options supplier serving international manufacturers in packaged espresso, tea, ready-to-drink espresso, vitality and purposeful drinks. The publicly traded firm says its platform consists of beverage formulation, manufacturing and packaging in cans, glass, multi-serve bottles, single-serve capsules, bulk extract and concentrates. ... what product varieties it’ll deal with ... what particular manufacturing roles it’ll carry out on behalf of Illy. ... In 2024, Westrock opened a 570,000-square-foot,$315 million roasting and ready-to-drink beverage manufacturing facility in Conway, Arkansas. Upon its opening, the power included inexperienced espresso storage, two automated 360-kilogram-per-batch Scolari roasters, beverage processing tanks, packaging strains and a improvement lab. ... The next yr, Westrock opened a 525,000-square-foot facility in Conway dedicated to single-serve espresso pod manufacturing, additional increasing the corporate’s contract manufacturing and packaging capabilities."
Westrock,,,,Exa,Illycaffè Taps Westrock for North American Production Push,dailycoffeenews.com (Nick Brown),2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://dailycoffeenews.com/2026/07/03/illycaffe-taps-westrock-for-north-american-production-push/,"Illycaffè Taps Westrock for North American Production Push ... # Illycaffè Taps Westrock for North American Production Push ... Italian coffee giant Illycaffè has signed a multi-year strategic production agreement with Arkansas-based Westrock Coffee Company for development and packaging of specific products for the North American market, according to the Italian news agency Ansa and other Italian news outlets. ... or investor- ... The Italian reports describe Westrock as providing a multi-site production platform that will allow Illy to double the share of products for the North American market that are packaged locally, primarily in the ready-to-drink category. ... In a statement to Daily Coffee News, Westrock Coffee Company said, “We’re proud to be a trusted partner to many of the world’s most iconic brands, and we’re excited to continue growing our roster of global partners on our platform, including as a ready-to-drink (RTD) partner, as we expand our footprint across Europe and Asia. We are excited to welcome Illycaffè as the newest member of our platform.” ... Illycaffè CEO Cristina Scocchia has described the United States as a priority market for the Trieste, Italy-based company, saying Illy has posted double-digit growth in the U.S. over the past four years. ... The Italian reports state that Illy’s coffee roasting will remain entirely at the company’s main production facility in Trieste, where the company has been expanding production. ... For Westrock, the agreement aligns with the company’s positioning as a large-scale beverage solutions provider serving global brands in packaged coffee, tea, ready-to-drink coffee, energy and functional beverages. The publicly traded company says its platform includes beverage formulation, manufacturing and packaging in cans, glass, multi-serve bottles, single-serve capsules, bulk extract and concentrates. ... In 2024, Westrock opened a 570,000-square-foot,$315 million roasting and ready-to-drink beverage factory in Conway, Arkansas. Upon its opening, the facility included green coffee storage, two automated 360-kilogram-per-batch Scolari roasters, beverage processing tanks, packaging lines and a development lab. ... The following year, Westrock opened a 525,000-square-foot facility in Conway devoted to single-serve coffee pod production, further expanding the company’s contract manufacturing and packaging capabilities."
Westrock,,,,Exa,"Westrock Coffee Extends Credit Facility Maturity to 2028, Adds Texas Capital Bank - WEST News - EveryTicker",everyticker.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://everyticker.com/quote/WEST/news/westrock-coffee-extends-credit-facility-maturity-to-2028-adds-texas-capital-bank,"Westrock Coffee Extends Credit Facility Maturity to 2028, Adds Texas Capital Bank - WEST News - EveryTicker ... # Westrock Coffee Extends Credit Facility Maturity to 2028, Adds Texas Capital Bank ... Westrock Coffee closed an amendment to its credit agreement on June 30 2026 that extends the maturity of approximately $361 million of its credit facilities from August 29 2027 to November 29 2028 and adds Texas Capital Bank as a new lender in the syndicate. ... The amendment also ends the covenant relief period early, tightening the secured net leverage ratio to 4.00× for the June 30 and September 30 2026 test periods. The change reflects the company’s confidence in improving free cash flow as it moves beyond the peak investment phase of its Conway, Arkansas facility. ... Westrock’s CFO Chris Pledger said the extension “provides Westrock Coffee with meaningful financial flexibility as we move beyond the peak investment phase of our Conway facility and into a period of declining capital intensity and improving free cash flow. Given the continued strength of our business performance, we also elected to terminate the covenant relief period ahead of schedule, which lowers our borrowing costs and reflects the underlying momentum across our platform.” ... The company’s recent financial results show a 29% to 44% growth in consolidated adjusted EBITDA for 2026 versus 2025, driven by strong demand in packaged coffee and ready‑to‑drink segments. Westrock continues to invest in its Conway facility, which created 800 jobs and invested over $300 million. ... By extending the debt maturity and tightening leverage ratios, Westrock reduces maturity risk and improves liquidity as it completes the peak investment phase of its flagship facility. The move signals confidence in its ability to maintain financial discipline while pursuing growth opportunities in its core beverage categories. ... The addition of Texas Capital Bank diversifies Westrock’s banking relationships and may provide more favorable terms in future refinancing, further strengthening the company’s balance sheet as it transitions to a lower‑capital‑intensity phase."
Westrock,,,,Exa,illycaffè signs manufacturing deal with Westrock Coffee Company,www.comunicaffe.com (Desk3),2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.comunicaffe.com/illycaffe-signs-a-multi-product-manufacturing-agreement-with-westrock-coffee-company-to-strengthen-its-strategic-presence-in-the-states/,"illycaffè signs manufacturing deal with Westrock Coffee Company ... # illycaffè signs a multi-product manufacturing agreement with Westrock Coffee Company to strengthen its strategic presence in the U.S. ... Westrock will provide a multi-site platform that will enable the company to double the proportion of products destined for the US market that are packaged on-site, primarily within the ready-to-drink category ... July 1, 2026 ... MILAN — illycaffè has signed a multi-year strategic production agreement with Westrock Coffee Company, a US-based company operating in the beverage sector and specialising in coffee, tea and ready-to-drink products, with a view to developing and packaging a number of products for the North American market. ... “The United States is a priority market for us, where we have achieved double-digit growth over the last four years. ... “The launch of our partnership with Westrock marks a key milestone in our growth plan: it will help to strengthen our operations in North America, support the development of new products tailored to the local market and further improve our service levels in this strategic region,” commented Cristina Scocchia, Chief Executive Officer of illycaffè. ... Westrock will provide a multi-site platform that will enable the company to double the proportion of products destined for the US market that are packaged on-site, primarily within the ready-to-drink category. ... The coffee roasting process will continue to be carried out entirely at the main production facility in Trieste, where the expansion plan is ongoing; key initiatives include increasing production of the iconic 250-gram tin and the forthcoming commissioning of a new roasting plant. ... The development plan for the Trieste plant has already led to the permanent recruitment of around 100 new staff members in 2025."
Westrock,,,,Exa,Westrock Coffee Company Announces Maturity Extension of its,www.globenewswire.com (Westrock Coffee Company),2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/06/30/3320148/0/en/Westrock-Coffee-Company-Announces-Maturity-Extension-of-its-Credit-Facilities.html,"Westrock Coffee Company Announces Maturity Extension of its ... # Westrock Coffee Company Announces Maturity Extension of its Credit Facilities ... LITTLE ROCK, Ark., June 30, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Westrock Coffee Company (NASDAQ: WEST) (“Westrock Coffee” or the “Company”), an integrated beverage solutions platform serving the world’s largest brands across packaged coffee, tea, ready-to-drink coffee, energy, and functional beverage categories, today announced the closing of an amendment to the Company’s existing credit agreement that extends the maturity date of approximately $361 million of the loans and commitments under its credit facilities from August 29, 2027 to November 29, 2028, with the remaining approximately $26 million continuing to mature on August 29, 2027. Texas Capital Bank has also become a lender in connection with the amendment. ... Chris Pledger, Chief Financial Officer of Westrock Coffee, commented, “Extending the maturity of our credit facility to November 2028 provides Westrock Coffee with meaningful financial flexibility as we move beyond the peak investment phase of our Conway facility and into a period of declining capital intensity and improving free cash flow. Given the continued strength of our business performance, we also elected to terminate the covenant relief period ahead of schedule, which lowers our borrowing costs and reflects the underlying momentum across our platform. I want to thank the banks in our syndicate – Wells Fargo, Bank of America, Truist, Rabobank, First Horizon, Stifel and SMBC – as well as the members of the Farm Credit System, for their continued support and partnership, and we are pleased to welcome Texas Capital Bank as we continue to build a truly exceptional business.” ... As a result of the Company’s early termination of the covenant relief period under the credit agreement prior to its scheduled expiration on October 1, 2026, the applicable margin on any loans will decrease, certain restrictions limited to the covenant relief period will no longer apply, and the maximum permitted secured net leverage ratio under the secured net leverage ratio financial covenant will decrease from 5.00x to 4.00x for the test period ending June 30, 2026, and from 4.50x to 4.00x for the test period ending September 30, 2026. ... Westrock Coffee is an integrated beverage solutions platform serving the world's largest brands across packaged coffee, tea, ready-to-drink coffee, energy, and functional beverage categories. With our global manufacturing and sourcing footprint, the Company formulates, manufactures, and packages beverages in cans, glass, multi-serve bottles, single-serve capsules, bulk extract, and concentrates, backed by a digitally traceable supply chain. With operations spanning 10 countries, Westrock Coffee partners with brands across retail, foodservice, convenience, CPG, and hospitality to bring beverage programs to market at scale. ... ,"" ""continue,"" ""anticipate,"" ""intend,"" ""expect,"" ""should,"" ""would,"" ""plan,"" ""predict,"" ""potential,"" ""seem,"" ""seek,"" ""future,"" ""outlook,"" and similar expressions that predict or indicate future events or trends or that are not statements of historical matters, but the absence of these words does not mean that a statement is not forward-looking. These forward-looking statements include, but are not limited to, our future capital intensity, cash flows, long term financing, growth opportunities, and other statements that are not historical facts. These statements are based on information available to Westrock Coffee as of the date hereof and Westrock Coffee is not under any duty to update any of the forward-looking statements after the date of this press release to conform these statements to actual results. These statements are based on various assumptions, whether or not identified in this press release, and on the current expectations of the management of Westrock Coffee as of the date hereof and are not predictions of actual performance. These forward-looking statements are provided for illustrative purposes only and are not intended to serve as and should not be relied on by an investor, or others, as a guarantee, an assurance, a prediction, or a definitive statement of fact or probability. Actual events and circumstances are difficult or impossible to predict and will differ from assumptions. Many actual events and circumstances are beyond the control of Westrock Coffee. These forward-looking statements are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties, including, but not limited to, changes in domestic and foreign business, market, financial, political, and legal conditions; our inability to secure an adequate supply of key raw materials, including green coffee and tea, or a disruption in our supply chain, including from tariffs or trade restrictions or global conflicts (including the ongoing conflicts in Europe, the Middle East and Latin America); risks relating to the uncertainty of the projected financial information with respect to Westrock Coffee; risks related to the rollout of Westrock Coffee's business and the timing of expected business milestones; our inability to successfully commercialize customers at our Conway, Arkansas facility, and generate positive operating cash flows within the anticipated time frame; the effects of competition and industry consolidation on Westrock Coffee's business; the ability ... agreement; the risk that Westrock Coffee fails to attract, motivate or retain qualified personnel; the risk that Westrock Coffee fails to fully realize the potential benefits of acquisitions or joint ventures or has difficulty successfully integrating acquired companies; the loss of significant customers or delays in bringing their products to market; litigation or legal disputes, which could lead us to incur significant liabilities and costs or harm our reputation; the risk of incurring additional costs when Westrock Coffee no longer qualifies as an emerging growth company (as defined in the JOBS Act); and those factors discussed in Westrock Coffee’s Annual Report on Form 10-K, which was filed with the United States Securities and Exchange Commission (the “SEC”) on March 10, 2026, in Part I, Item 1A “Risk Factors” and other documents Westrock Coffee has filed, or will file, with the SEC. If any of these risks ... results implied by these forward-looking statements. There may be additional risks that Westrock Coffee does not presently know, or that Westrock Coffee currently believes are immaterial, that could also cause actual results to differ from those contained in the forward-looking statements. In addition, the forward-looking statements reflect Westrock Coffee's expectations, plans, or forecasts of future events and views as of the date of this press release. Westrock Coffee anticipates that subsequent events and developments will cause Westrock Coffee's assessments to change. However, while Westrock Coffee may elect to update these forward-looking statements at some point in ... future, Westrock Coffee specifically disclaims any obligation to do so unless required by applicable law. These forward-looking statements should not be relied upon as a representation of Westrock Coffee's assessments as of any date subsequent to the date of this press release. Accordingly, undue reliance should not be placed upon the forward ... looking statements. ... Company ProfileWestrock Coffee CompanyIndustry: Food & Beverage & Tobacco ... July 20, 2026 16:05 ET | Source: Westrock Coffee Company ... Westrock Coffee Company to Report Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results on August 6th, 2026 ... Westrock Coffee Company to Report Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results on August 6th, 2026 ... May 07, 2026 16:05 ET | Source: Westrock Coffee Company ... Westrock Coffee Company Reports First Quarter 2026 Results and Reaffirms 2026 Outlook ... Westrock Coffee Company Reports First Quarter 2026 Results and Reaffirms 2026 Outlook"
Westrock,,,,Exa,Beyond the Balance Sheet: Westrock Coffee's Conway Bet Is Paying Off - BriefGlance.com,briefglance.com,2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://briefglance.com/articles/beyond-the-balance-sheet-westrock-coffees-conway-bet-is-paying-off,"On the surface, Westrock Coffee Company’s announcement today looks like standard corporate financial housekeeping. The beverage solutions provider extended the maturity on the bulk of its debt, shuffled its banking syndicate, and tweaked some loan covenants. These are moves that typically excite accountants and credit analysts but rarely capture broader attention. Yet, to dismiss this as mere balance sheet maintenance is to miss the real story: this is the financial echo of a massive operational victory, a signal that Westrock's audacious, multi-hundred-million-dollar bet on its Conway, Arkansas facility is beginning to pay off. ... In a strategic maneuver, the company extended the maturity date for approximately $361 million of its credit facilities to November 2028, providing a longer runway for its long-term plans. More tellingly, it terminated its covenant relief period well ahead of schedule. As CFO Chris Pledger noted, this provides “meaningful financial flexibility as we move beyond the peak investment phase of our Conway facility.” That single phrase, “peak investment phase,” is the key that unlocks the entire narrative. This isn't just about managing debt; it's about entering a new era of declining capital intensity and, crucially, improving free cash flow. ... To understand the significance of today’s financial news, one must first appreciate the sheer scale of the Conway project. Since 2021, Westrock has poured over $300 million into transforming a 524,000-square-foot facility into what is now the largest of its kind in the United States. This wasn't just an expansion; it was a fundamental reinvention of the company’s operational core, designed to shift its focus from traditional coffee roasting toward the higher-margin, high-growth world of ready-to-drink (RTD) beverages, extracts, and complex ingredients. ... The term “peak investment phase” is a stark understatement. Company filings show capital expenditures ballooning to approximately $160 million in 2024 as the facility was built out. That number fell to $89 million in 2025, and by the first quarter of 2026, it had plummeted to just $7 million. This dramatic drop is the clearest evidence that the heavy lifting is done. The massive capital sink that was Conway is now a fully commercialized, cash-flow-positive asset. With all five of its advanced production lines now operational, the facility that once consumed capital is now primed to generate it. ... This operational milestone is the direct enabler of the financial restructuring. The company’s lenders, a syndicate that now includes Texas Capital Bank, are not extending terms out of charity; they are responding to a fundamentally de-risked business profile. The proven performance of the Conway plant, which has effectively doubled Westrock's operational footprint, provides the confidence needed to offer more favorable terms. ... The details of the amended credit agreement read like a report card of a company that has earned its lenders' trust. By exiting the covenant relief period early, Westrock has voluntarily accepted a tighter leash. The maximum permitted secured net leverage ratio, a key measure of debt relative to earnings, will now be capped at 4.00x, down from a temporary ceiling of 5.00x. In corporate finance, offering to abide by stricter rules is a power move. It signals profound confidence from management that future earnings will comfortably support the debt load. ... The reward for this confidence is immediate and tangible: lower borrowing costs. The early termination triggers a decrease in the applicable interest margin on its loans, which will directly reduce interest expenses and bolster the bottom line. According to one credit analyst, this move effectively trades temporary covenant flexibility for longer-term stability and lower costs—a trade any healthy, growing company would make. ... This confidence is backed by tangible results. After a rocky period post-SPAC, Westrock's performance is showing a sharp upward trajectory. In the first quarter of 2026, the company more than tripled its consolidated adjusted EBITDA year-over-year to $26 million and swung from a $13.1 million operating loss to a $3.2 million operating income. Its secured net leverage ratio had already improved to 3.45x, well within the new, stricter covenant. The company isn’t just hoping for future performance; it’s already delivering it. ... This newfound financial flexibility isn't an end in itself; it's fuel for Westrock's strategic ambitions. The company is positioning itself as the essential behind-the-scenes partner for the world's largest brands, capitalizing on the biggest trends shaping the $5 trillion global beverage market. The “cold coffee revolution,” the explosive growth in functional beverages promising everything from energy to focus, and the unwavering consumer demand for convenience are all squarely in Conway’s wheelhouse. ... The plant's capabilities in canning, bottling, and producing complex extracts allow Westrock to move beyond being a private-label supplier and become an integrated solutions platform. It is already developing high-protein beverages for leading CPG brands and expanding its capabilities for milk-based RTD products and energy drinks. This aligns perfectly with a market where RTD beverages are projected to grow from $732 billion to over $1.2 trillion by 2032. ... Furthermore, this operational and financial stability reinforces the company's competitive advantage in sustainability. Westrock recently announced it had achieved 100% responsibly sourced green coffee and tea purchases, a powerful differentiator in a market of increasingly conscious consumers. Financial strength allows the company to maintain and expand these ethical sourcing programs, which are not just good for the world but are also good for business, attracting premium partners who value a transparent and traceable supply chain. ... For investors who have watched Westrock since its public debut, this moment feels like a turning point. The narrative is shifting from one of potential and investment to one of execution and monetization. The company has successfully navigated the most difficult and capital-intensive part of its transformation. The operational engine in Conway is running, the financial structure has been fortified, and the market trends are blowing squarely at its back. ... The road ahead will require continued discipline. Management has acknowledged the loss of a large single-serve customer due to M&A activity but projects it will backfill that capacity by 2027, driven by a strong sales pipeline for the new capabilities at Conway. Today’s announcement demonstrates that Westrock has secured the financial stability and runway necessary to see that strategy through. The focus now shifts from building the factory to filling it, proving that the massive bet on Conway can deliver the sustained profitability and growth the company has long promised."
Westrock,,,,Exa,"Smurfit Westrock to permanently close Lebanon folding carton plant in Tennessee, 52 affected",www.lesprom.com (Lesprom Network),2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lesprom.com/en/news/Smurfit_Westrock_to_permanently_close_Lebanon_folding_carton_plant_in_Tennessee_52_affected_123768/,"Smurfit Westrock to permanently close Lebanon folding carton plant in Tennessee, 52 affected ... Smurfit Westrock has filed an official WARN Notice with the Tennessee Department of Labor and Workforce Development, notifying the agency of a permanent closure effective August 14, 2026. ... The affected facility is located in Lebanon, Tennessee, with a total of 52 workers affected, and the company notified the department's Dislocated Worker Unit on June 15, 2026. ... The employees at the facility are not represented by a collective bargaining agreement and do not have bumping rights, with the Northern Middle Local Workforce Development Area rapid response team notified to coordinate services with the employer and affected employees. ... The Lebanon plant produces folding cartons and printed paperboard packaging used for retail, food, and specialty packaging needs."
Westrock,,,,Exa,Smurfit Westrock Earns Roca Five-Star Supplier Rating,www.paperadvance.com (Paper Advance Editorial Team),2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-18 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.paperadvance.com/news/industry-news/smurfit-westrock-earns-roca-five-star-supplier-rating.html,"Smurfit Westrock Earns Roca Five-Star Supplier Rating ... Smurfit Westrock earned Roca’s five-star supplier rating, achieving the highest score among all evaluated suppliers. Photo: Smurfit Westrock. ... ## Smurfit Westrock has been awarded a five-star supplier rating by Roca, one of Europe’s leading bathroom manufacturers, after achieving the highest overall score in the company’s supplier evaluation process. ... The assessment measured supplier performance across several criteria, including product quality, delivery reliability, relationship management and sustainability. Smurfit Westrock received top marks across all categories and ranked first among all suppliers evaluated. ... Roca, known for its portfolio of bathroom furniture, sanitary fittings, ceramics, bathtubs and shower solutions, works with suppliers across Europe and beyond. The recognition reflects Smurfit Westrock’s support for Roca operations in Germany, Portugal, Poland, Spain, Switzerland, the United Kingdom, Morocco and Austria. ... “We are proud to be recognised by Roca with this five-star rating, particularly as it reflects excellence across such a broad range of performance criteria,” said Nobert Faunie, Key Account Manager at Smurfit Westrock. ... According to the company, the award highlights the efforts of both local and central account management teams in delivering consistent packaging performance, innovation and sustainability across multiple markets. ... Roca also praised Smurfit Westrock’s overall performance during the evaluation process. ... “Smurfit Westrock has demonstrated exceptional performance across all aspects of our supplier evaluation,” said Roman Köhler, Corporate Category Manager at Roca Group. “From product quality and reliable delivery to strong relationship management and sustainability leadership, they have set a benchmark for excellence.” ... The recognition underscores the growing importance of quality, service performance and sustainability in supplier relationships and strengthens Smurfit Westrock’s position as a packaging partner for major manufacturers across Europe. ... Smurfit Westrock is a global provider of paper-based packaging solutions, serving customers across consumer and industrial markets through an extensive network of paper mills and packaging operations worldwide. ... ### Smurfit Westrock to Close Tennessee Packaging Plant ... smurfit ... westrock-to-close-tennessee-packaging-plant.html ... ### Smurfit Westrock Earns Roca Five-Star Supplier Rating"
Westrock,,,,Exa,"Two years on, how is the company behind Ireland’s biggest-ever merger performing?",www.thejournal.ie (Paul O'Donoghue),2026-06-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thejournal.ie/smurfit-westrock-merger-stock-market-analysis-7069926-Jun2026/,"It was formed in 2024 following a merger between Ireland-based Smurfit Kappa and its US rival, Westrock. Alamy Stock Photo ... # Two years on, how is the company behind Ireland’s biggest-ever merger performing? ... This has been boosted by the fact that Smurfit Westrock is a relatively new corporate entity. It was formed in 2024 following a merger between Ireland-based Smurfit Kappa and its US rival, Westrock. The new entity has its headquarters in Dublin. ... The deal was worth an estimated $25 billion (€21.61 billion) or so, which is likely the largest ever merger involving an indigenous Irish company. ... For the fact-checkers among you – there have been some transactions which rival it, such as the 2015 acquisition of Covidien by Medtronic. But both of those firms began life as US businesses, and the deal was about Medtronic shifting its headquarters to Ireland for tax reasons. ... So, like we said – the Smurfit Westrock merger is the largest merger involving an indigenous Irish company. ... Before we dive in, it’s worth reiterating what Smurfit Westrock actually does. Its business mainly consists of: ... - Corrugated packaging, including shipping cartons. It also makes packaging for e-commerce, such as boxes for online shopping orders - Paper goods and cardboard boxes - Packaging for other business areas, like retail and point-of-sale - Forestry (ie, growing paper) and recycling ... Westrock traditionally had more of a focus on North America, while Smurfit Kappa was the big boy in Europe. ... The picture is a bit mixed, but broadly speaking, the company has avoided many of the typical merger traps. ... The most obvious area to look ... Does the new business bring in more money as a single entity ... , yes. ... In the 12 months to the end of 2024, Smurfit Westrock recorded sales of $21 billion (€18.16 billion). ... In 2025, the first full year of operating as a single unit, the firm’s sales rose significantly to $31 billion (€26.8 billion). ... This is one of the clearest signs that the merger has gone fairly well. Smurfit Westrock now has a much bigger global platform. ... Of course, expenses also jumped alongside that. But still, the company’s net profit more than doubled, rising from $319 million to $699 million (€604.31 million). ... This was helped by the fact that the two businesses were able to realise combined savings of over $400 million (€345.81 million), due to complimentary parts of their operations. ... This wasn’t good news for everyone – Smurfit Westrock said it let go 3,000 employees during 2025 (it currently employs about 97,000 people). ... Well if that’s the case, why has the firm’s stock been largely stagnant? Its opening price on its first day of trading on the New York Stock Exchange was a touch over $43 (€37). ... That was back in July 2024. Two years later, and the firm’s share price stands at… just over $43. ... A key one is whether containerboard prices will drop in the near term, with signs across the sector that this may be a risk. It led one bank to cut its price target. ... Another worry is that earnings in the final three months of 2025 dropped compared to the same period in 2024. Net income fell pretty significantly, from $146 million (€126.22 million) to $98 million (€84.72 million). ... Management cited“difficult market conditions” during the quarter, with talk of ‘downtime to balance our system’. ... This goes back to the concern that the Dublin-based company could be facing a weaker economic environment, leading to softer demand and lower prices. ... However, other commentators have said that the company is trading ... its fair market ... For example, one analyst said that based on its current performance, its ... (€46) compared to its actual ... of $43. ... It said this is because the company is due to finish several loss-making contracts in North America soon, and can then move onto more profitable ventures. ... Smurfit Westrock itself seems confident. In a recent update, it pledged to increase earnings by 40% by 2030 and deliver a “significant and growing return to shareholders”. ... Most analysts have a positive view of the business and rate its stock a ‘buy’. ... The view overall is that Smurfit Kappa and Westrock have integrated pretty well and managed to take a bigger slice of the pie in their market. ... The European side of the business has typically had strong margins, but most think that North America is the biggest growth opportunity. The hope is that Smurfit management can lift profitability over time. ... But there are still concerns over a possible slowdown in the company’s market. ... It’s probably fair to say that while the jury is still out to some degree, the merger is going reasonably well. ... Shareholders who have seen essentially no return in two years may be unimpressed. But strong revenue growth and the possibility of further earnings boosts means the deal certainly isn’t one to throw on the ‘70% failure rate’ scrapheap. ... Smurfit Westrock may not be Ireland’s sexiest company. But it is one which has proven to be solid – and has come a long way from its humble beginnings as a small box-maker in 1930s Rathmines."
Westrock,,,,Exa,"Westrock Coffee Company now ""100 per cent"" responsibly sourced - Global Coffee Report",www.gcrmag.com (Meg Kennedy),2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gcrmag.com/westrock-coffee-company-now-100-per-cent-responsibly-sourced/,"Westrock Coffee Company now ""100 per cent"" responsibly sourced - Global Coffee Report ... # Westrock Coffee Company now “100 per cent” responsibly sourced ... June 12, 2026 ... Westrock Coffee Company has announced it has officially achieved its goal of becoming “100 per cent responsibly sourced”, fulfilling a commitment set by the company in 2021. ... Westrock says that as of 2025, 100 per cent of Westrock Coffee’s tea, green coffee, and soluble purchases are verified through second- or third-party programs, confirming responsible growing and processing environments across its global supply chain. ... In addition, all direct suppliers are third-party audited for compliance with Westrock Coffee’s Responsible Sourcing Policy. ... “This milestone reflects years of intentional investment, collaboration and accountability across our business,” says Brooke Cantrell, Vice President of Sustainability. ... “Responsible sourcing is not a box we check – it is a commitment to the people, environments and communities that make our products possible. Reaching 100 per cent responsibly sourced is an important moment for our company and our partners around the world.” ... Westrock says meeting the goal required “close collaboration” across the company’s commodities, sourcing, and sustainability teams to expand responsible supply chain partnerships capable of supporting increased volume. ... The effort was then further tested by “unprecedented market volatility” over the past several years. ... Westrock says its responsible sourcing framework was designed to remain resilient amid shifting market dynamics, ensuring continuity without compromising standards. ... “This work directly supports our mission to deliver competitive, innovative beverage solutions for leading global brands, while creating meaningful economic opportunity at origin,” says Chief Operating Officer Will Ford. ... “By building resilient, responsibly sourced supply chains, we’re strengthening long-term value for our customers and supporting smallholder farmers and their families in developing countries.”"
Westrock,,,,Exa,Smurfit Westrock to invest €600m in French operation – ThePackagingPortal.com,www.thepackagingportal.com,2026-06-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thepackagingportal.com/industry-news/smurfit-westrock-to-invest-e600m-in-french-operation/,"Smurfit Westrock to invest €600m in French operation – ThePackagingPortal.com ... # Smurfit Westrock to invest €600m in French operation ... Smurfit Westrock has confirmed plans to invest approximately €600m across its operations in France, reinforcing its long-term commitment to French manufacturing, innovation, and sustainability ahead of the Choose France initiative. ... The investment will take place over the next three to five years and will support the modernisation and decarbonisation of its operations; enhancing manufacturing efficiency, customer innovation, and sustainable packaging capabilities. ... Established in France for over 40 years, the company employs approximately 6,000 people at 50 sites across the country, underscoring France’s strategic importance to the company’s European operations and its attractiveness as a destination for industrial investment. ... “With this continuous programme of investment in France, our commitment to innovation, quality, and decarbonisation efforts is clear,” said Saverio Mayer, CEO Europe, MEA and APAC, Smurfit Westrock. “France continues to provide a strong environment for this to take place; through long-term industrial investment, supported by skilled talent, innovation, and a clear commitment to sustainability.” ... This next phase of investment builds on a solid foundation: the company has already spent more than €500m in France over the past five years to modernise operations, improve service, and expand capabilities. Smurfit Westrock operates four net zero plants in France and an almost fully decarbonised paper mill, underscoring its leadership in sustainable packaging production. ... “It only makes sense that sites creating sustainable packaging are sustainable in their own right,” said Andrew Coffey, CEO, Smurfit Westrock France. “Achieving net zero at these plants was a significant milestone, and one which has given us an excellent platform to go even further. That’s why strategic investments in key sites are important to continue this momentum. These include a €40m expansion and modernisation of our Épernay facility, €20m to continue progress at our advanced corrugated facility in Vernon, and over €100m to support multiple projects at our Facture paper mill, including the installation of an evaporation plant. These investments will further elevate our capabilities and reduce our environmental impact.”"
Westrock,,,,Exa,Westrock Coffee Company reports strong Q1 results - Global Coffee Report,www.gcrmag.com (Meg Kennedy),2026-05-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gcrmag.com/westrock-coffee-company-reports-strong-q1-results/,"Westrock Coffee Company reports strong Q1 results - Global Coffee Report # Westrock Coffee Company reports strong Q1 results by Meg Kennedy May 12, 2026 Image: Westrock Coffee ... Westrock Coffee Company has reported a steady start to the 2026 fiscal year, following the release of its Q1 2026 results. ... For the period ending 31 March 2026, the company posted consolidated net sales of US$308.8 million, reflecting continued demand across its diverse beverage platforms, despite a complex global economic environment. ... “I am pleased to report that our first quarter delivered strong results across every dimension of our business, and that this is the fourth consecutive quarter of year-over-year Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA growth,” says Westrock Coffee CEO and Co-Founder Scott T. Ford. ... “However, the real story of the quarter is that the platform we spent three years building is now attracting the demand we envisioned, with brands coming to us not for a single SKU, but for the full spectrum of beverage partnerships across all categories.” ... The standout performer for the quarter was the company’s Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA, which rose to US$26 million, a notable increase from the US$8.2 million reported in the first quarter of 2025. The company notes all five of its production lines at the Conway, Arkansas extract and ready-to-drink facility have been fully commercialised. ... Looking ahead, Westrock Coffee reaffirmed its full-year 2026 outlook, signaling confidence in its ability to meet previous financial targets. ... The company expects Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA for the full year to fall between US$90 million and $100 million."
Westrock,,,,Exa,Westrock Coffee Company Reports First Quarter 2026 Results and Reaffirms 2026 Outlook | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Acquiremedia),2026-05-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/westrock-coffee-company-reports-first-quarter-2026-results-and-reaffirms-2026-outlook-ce7f5bd9da88f02d,"| Jun. 30 | Westrock Coffee Extends Maturity of $361 Million Credit Facilities | MT | | --- | --- | --- | | Jun. 30 | Westrock Coffee Company Announces Maturity Extension Of Its Credit Facilities | CI | ... # Westrock Coffee Company Reports First Quarter 2026 Results and Reaffirms 2026 Outlook ... LITTLE ROCK, Ark-- Westrock Coffee Company (Nasdaq: WEST) ('Westrock Coffee' or the 'Company') today reported financial results for the first quarter ended March 31, 2026. ... Net sales were $308.8 million, an increase of 44.4% ... Gross profit was $45.8 million, an increase of 57.4% ... Net loss was $8.5 million, compared to a net loss of $27.2 million in the prior year period ... Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA2 was $26.0 million, more than tripling the Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA of $8.2 million in the prior year period, as all five production lines at the Conway, Arkansas extract and ready-to-drink facility have been fully commercialized ... Capital expenditures of $7.1 million, down from $41.3 million in the first quarter of 2025, reflecting a structural shift in the Company's capital intensity ... Commenting on our results, Scott T. Ford, CEO and Co-founder stated, 'I am pleased to report that our first quarter delivered strong results across every dimension of our business, and that this is the fourth consecutive quarter of year-over-year Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA growth. However, the real story of the quarter is that the platform we spent three years building is now attracting the demand we envisioned, with brands coming to us not for a single SKU, but for the full spectrum of beverage partnerships across all categories.' ... The Company is reaffirming its 2026 guidance for Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA of $90.0 million to $100.0 million, which was provided in its earnings release dated March 10, 2026. ... Westrock Coffee is an integrated beverage solutions platform serving the world's largest brands across packaged coffee, tea, ready-to-drink coffee, energy, and functional beverage categories. With our global manufacturing and sourcing footprint, the Company formulates, manufactures, and packages beverages in cans, glass, multi-serve bottles, single-serve capsules, bulk extract, and concentrates, backed by a digitally traceable supply chain. With operations spanning 10 countries, Westrock partners with brands across retail, foodservice, convenience, CPG, and hospitality to bring beverage programs to market at scale. ... to serve as and should not be relied on by an investor, or others, as a guarantee, an assurance, a prediction, or a definitive statement of fact or probability. Actual events and circumstances are difficult or impossible to predict and will differ from assumptions. Many actual events and circumstances are beyond the control of Westrock Coffee. These forward-looking statements are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties, including, but not limited to, changes in domestic and foreign business, market, financial, political, and legal conditions; our inability to secure an adequate supply of key raw materials, including green coffee and tea, or a disruption in our supply chain, including from tariffs or trade restrictions or global conflicts (including the ongoing conflicts in Europe, the Middle East and Latin America); risks relating to the uncertainty of the projected financial information with respect to Westrock Coffee; risks related to the rollout of Westrock Coffee's business and the timing of expected business milestones; our inability to successfully commercialize customers at our Conway, Arkansas facility, and generate positive operating cash flows within the anticipated time frame; the effects of competition and industry consolidation on Westrock Coffee's business; the ability of Westrock Coffee to issue equity or equity-linked securities or obtain, refinance or extend the maturities of debt financing in the future; Westrock Coffee's future level of indebtedness, which may reduce funds available for other business purposes and reduce the Company's operational flexibility; Westrock Coffee's inability to comply with the financial covenants in our credit agreement; the risk that Westrock Coffee fails to attract, motivate or retain qualified personnel; the risk that Westrock Coffee fails to fully realize the potential benefits of acquisitions or joint ventures or has difficulty successfully integrating acquired companies; the loss of significant customers or delays in bringing their products to market; litigation or legal disputes, which could lead us to incur significant liabilities and costs or harm our reputation; the risk of incurring additional costs if Westrock Coffee no longer qualifies as an emerging growth company (as defined in the JOBS Act); and those factors discussed in Westrock Coffee's Annual Report on Form 10-K, which was filed with the United States Securities and Exchange Commission (the 'SEC') on March 10, 2026, in Part I, Item 1A 'Risk Factors' and other documents Westrock Coffee has filed, or will file, with the SEC. If any of these risks materialize or our assumptions prove incorrect, actual results could differ materially from the results implied by these forward-looking statements. There may be additional risks that Westrock Coffee does not presently know, or that Westrock Coffee currently believes are immaterial, that could also cause actual results to differ from those contained in the forward-looking statements. In addition, the forward-looking statements reflect Westrock Coffee's ... | Jun. 30 | Westrock Coffee Extends Maturity of $361 Million Credit Facilities | MT | | --- | --- | --- | | Jun. 30 | Westrock Coffee Company Announces Maturity Extension Of Its Credit Facilities | CI | | Jun. 29 | Westrock Coffee Company(NasdaqGM:WEST) added to Russell 2000 Value Benchmark | CI | | Jun. 28 | Westrock Coffee Company(NasdaqGM:WEST) added to Russell 3000E Value Benchmark | CI | | Jun. 28 | Westrock Coffee Company(NasdaqGM:WEST) added to Russell 3000 Value Benchmark | CI | | Jun. 28 | Westrock Coffee Company(NasdaqGM:WEST) added to Russell Small Cap Comp Value Benchmark | CI | | Jun. 28 | Westrock Coffee Company(NasdaqGM:WEST) added to Russell 2500 Value Benchmark | CI | | May. 08 | Westrock Coffee Company, Q1 2026 Earnings Call, May 07, 2026 | | | May. 07 | Westrock Coffee Company Reports Earnings Results for the First Quarter Ended March 31, 2026 | CI | | Apr. 20 | Westrock Coffee Company Announces Board and Committee Changes, Effective April 20, 2026 | CI | | Mar. 10 | Westrock Coffee Company, Q4 2025 Earnings Call, Mar 10, 2026 | | | Mar. 10 | Westrock Coffee Fiscal Q4 Loss Narrows, Revenue Rises | MT | | Mar. 10 | Westrock Coffee Company Reports Earnings Results for the Fourth Quarter and Full Year Ended December 31, 2025 | CI | | Dec. 11 | Westrock Coffee Insider Bought Shares Worth $414,000, According to a Recent SEC Filing | MT | | Nov. 07 | Westrock Coffee Company, Q3 2025 Earnings Call, Nov 06, 2025 | | ... Westrock Coffee Company is an integrated coffee, tea, flavors, extracts, and ingredients solutions provider in the United States. It provides coffee sourcing, supply chain management, product development, roasting, packaging and distribution services to the retail, food service and restaurant, store and travel center, non-commercial account, consumer packaged goods, and hospitality industries around the world. It has two segments: Beverage Solutions and Sustainable Sourcing & Traceability (SS&T). Beverage Solutions segment provides products in a variety of packaging, including branded and private label coffee in bags, fractional packs, and single-serve cups, as well as extract solutions to be used in products, such as cold brew and ready-to-drink offerings. SS&T segment utilizes its technology and digitally traceable supply chain to impact and improve the lives of its farming partners, tangible economic empowerment and an emphasis on environmental accountability and farmer literacy."
