ion for the segment’s operating income and adjusted EBITDA was $169.7 million and $385.7 million, respectively. ... EMEA Business Remains Under Pressure ... Packaging Solutions EMEA sales were $2.29 billion, nearly flat with the prior-year quarter. Our expectation for the segment’s sales was $2.36 billion. ... The segment reported an operating loss of $80 million compared with a loss of $1 million a year ago. Adjusted EBITDA decreased 6.2% to $182 million, and the adjusted EBITDA margin narrowed to 8% from 8.5%. Higher paper costs within packaging, distribution expenses and weaker volumes offset energy-cost benefits and cost-reduction actions. ... Our projection for the segment’s operating income and adjusted EBITDA was a loss of $90.1 million and $158.9 million, respectively. ... ## International Paper's Free Cash ... Cash provided by operating activities increased to $526 million from $476 million in the year-ago quarter. However, capital expenditures rose to $533 million from $422 million. This led to a free cash flow of a negative $7 million against positive $54 million a year earlier. ... ## IP Sets Third-Quarter EBITDA Target ... International Paper expects third-quarter adjusted EBITDA from continuing operations between $780 million and $830 million. The outlook includes an estimated $85 million negative impact from the temporary suspension of operations at the Pine Hill mill for roof repairs.Packaging Solutions North America adjusted EBITDA is projected between $555 million and $585 million, including the Pine Hill impact. Packaging Solutions EMEA adjusted EBITDA is expected between $230 million and $250 million. ... ## International Paper Maintains 2026 Targets ... For 2026, management targets adjusted EBITDA from continuing operations of $3.20-$3.40 billion. The company expects Packaging Solutions North America adjusted EBITDA of $2.35-$2.45 billion and Packaging Solutions EMEA adjusted EBITDA of $900 million-$1 billion. ... International Paper projects full-year net sales of $24.5-$25.1 billion and free cash flow of $300-$500 million. Capital expenditures are targeted between $2 billion and $2.1 billion, while maintenance outage expenses are forecast at $431 million. ... ## IP Advances Strategic Investments and Separation ... The company completed the NORPAC acquisition in June and the acquisition of a converting facility from Delmarva Corrugated Packaging in Dover, DE, in May. It also finished the Riverdale machine conversion, with the ramp-up progressing as expected. Operations at the Waterloo greenfield packaging plant are scheduled to begin in the fourth quarter. ... In EMEA, International Paper has announced more than $210 million of run-rate savings tied to footprint and headcount actions. The planned separation of the North American and EMEA packaging operations remains on track with the previously announced timeline. ... IP currently carries a Zacks Rank #3 (Hold)."
International Paper,,,,Exa,"More producers announce price hikes for containerboard, boxboard | Packaging Dive",www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/international-paper-containerboard-price-hike-boxboard-sbs-smurfit-westrock/826355/,"Cascades, Smurfit Westrock and International Paper announced containerboard price increases days after PCA’s, which is being called unprecedented ... July 28: Smurfit Westrock and International Paper both announced price increases for containerboard to take effect Sept. 1, according to Tuesday memos to investors from Michael Roxland, Truist Securities senior paper and packaging analyst, citing containerboard industry contacts and Fastmarkets RISI. ... IP’s hike is for $80 per ton. SW’s is for $100 per ton, as is its increase for kraft paper prices. The latter company reportedly cited reasons such as sustained demand, tight supply across its mill network and ongoing cost pressures. ... This follows Packaging Corporation of America’s Friday announcement of a$140 per ton price hike for containerboard. That amount is double the typical increases, and industry observers widely have called it unprecendented. The announcement kicked off containerboard producers’ third wave of price increases in 2026 so far. PCA, IP and SW are the three largest North American containerboard producers. ... Analysts believe that similar to PCA’s, IP’s increase is driven by rising costs for inputs including recycled fiber, freight and electricity. Other factors include improving demand and tight supply following announced facility closures in 2025 totaling nearly 10% of the North American industry’s production capacity. ... IP has also announced closures this year, most recently disclosing on July 16 that it plans to shut a box plant in Carrollton, Texas. Days earlier, the company announced that it would temporarily idle its containerboard mill in Pine Hill, Alabama, due to roof damage from storms. In February, IP announced it would close a Georgetown, South Carolina, container plant, and in January, the company filed a notice with the state of Washington about closing a facility in Union Gap. ... SBS remains in oversupply and producers have taken actions in recent months to rationalize production capacity. In April, Clearwater Paper announced that it’s restructuring an SBS mill in Cypress Bend, Arkansas, and will halve production there while reducing employee count by about 20%. In February, Smurfit Westrock announced that it would permanently close down one of the machines at its SBS mill in La Tuque, Quebec."
International Paper,,,,Exa,JPMorgan upgrades International Paper as linerboard pricing cycle gains momentum,"ca.finance.yahoo.com (Jaiveer Shekhawat Tue, July 28, 2026 at 5:18 p.m. EDT 2 min read)",2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/jpmorgan-upgrades-international-paper-linerboard-211810248.html,"JPMorgan upgrades International Paper as linerboard pricing cycle gains momentum ... # JPMorgan upgrades International Paper as linerboard pricing cycle gains momentum ... Investing.com -- JPMorgan upgraded International Paper to ""Overweight"" from ""Neutral,"" arguing that an improving U.S. linerboard pricing cycle and tightening supply-demand dynamics are likely to lift earnings across the corrugated packaging sector, with International Paper offering the most attractive risk-reward profile. ... The brokerage raised its price target on International Paper to $61 from $51, while increasing its London-listed target to 4,600 pence from 3,200 pence. It maintained Overweight ratings on Smurfit WestRock and Packaging Corp. of America, lifting their price targets to $71 from $65 and $312 from $271, respectively. ... The upgrade follows reports that Packaging Corp. of America plans to implement a $140-per-ton U.S. kraftliner price increase from Sept. 1. JPMorgan expects only $50 per ton to be realized in its base case but said even that would represent the strongest quarterly price-cost progression in a decade, with further upside possible if supply remains tight. ... JPMorgan said the latest price increases are being driven by favorable supply-demand fundamentals rather than rising production costs. It argued linerboard prices remain below levels needed to justify investment in new capacity, estimating prices would need to exceed $1,200 per ton to generate acceptable returns on a new mill, versus current spot prices of about $1,045 per ton. ... Assuming a $50-per-ton price increase, the brokerage raised its 2027 EBITDA forecasts by 5% for Smurfit WestRock, 11% for Packaging Corp. of America and 12% for International Paper. It said Packaging Corp. and International Paper remain the most leveraged to higher linerboard pricing, while International Paper stands to benefit the most from a valuation perspective given its currently depressed earnings base and higher financial leverage. ... Despite the upgrade, JPMorgan said it continues to prefer Packaging Corp. of America and Smurfit WestRock due to their stronger execution, higher returns on invested capital and lower operational risk, while noting International Paper offers roughly 43% upside to its current share price under its revised assumptions. ... JPMorgan upgrades International Paper as linerboard pricing cycle gains momentum"
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper raised at J.P. Morgan on improving U.S. linerboard pricing cycle (IP:NYSE) | Seeking Alpha,seekingalpha.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://seekingalpha.com/news/4619754-international-paper-raised-at-j-p-morgan-on-improving-u-s-linerboard-pricing-cycle,"International Paper raised at J.P. Morgan on improving U.S. linerboard pricing cycle (IP:NYSE) | Seeking Alpha ... International Paper (IP) up 3.6% in Tuesday's trading as J.P. Morgan upgrades to Overweight from Neutral with a $61 price target, raised from $51, saying the U.S. linerboard pricing cycle is starting to pick up the pace, raising earnings expectations for corrugators."
International Paper,,,,Exa,JPMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential By Investing.com,za.investing.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://za.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/jpmorgan-upgrades-international-paper-stock-rating-on-upside-potential-93CH-4388885,"JPMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential By Investing.com ... # JPMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential ... PMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential ... PMorgan upgrades International Paper ... Investing.com - JPMorgan upgraded International Paper (NYSE:IP) from Neutral to Overweight and raised its price target to $61.00 from $51.00. The stock currently trades at $42.41 and has surged 16.67% over the past week, reflecting growing investor confidence. ... Analyst Detlef Winckelmann said the firm’s valuation incorporating a further $50 per ton suggests approximately 43% upside for International Paper versus the current share price. Even assuming no further cost reductions or operational improvements, the firm could justify upside of approximately 34%. ... The analyst noted this level of upside is sufficient to account for the potential risk of guidance downgrades, which consensus already assumes, and near-term earnings risk. According to InvestingPro Tips, analysts predict the company will be profitable this year, supporting the upgrade thesis. The platform offers 8 additional exclusive tips for IP investors, along with comprehensive Pro Research Reports available for over 1,400 US equities. JPMorgan said International Paper still trades at a premium to Smurfit WestRock, which the firm does not view as fair. ... JPMorgan maintains its preference for Packaging Corporation of America and Smurfit WestRock. The firm said Packaging Corporation of America trades at a 30% premium to peers for a return on invested capital twice as high, regardless of the scenario. ... For Smurfit WestRock, JPMorgan expects approximately $800 million in operational improvements beyond any cyclical tailwinds, which will materially improve the return on invested capital profile and are not yet fully incorporated in consensus estimates for later years. ... In other recent news, International Paper has completed its acquisition of North Pacific Paper Company (NORPAC) for $360 million. This acquisition adds a Longview, Washington-based producer of recycled packaging papers to International Paper’s portfolio. Additionally, International Paper announced the temporary suspension of operations at its Pine Hill, Alabama mill due to weather-related damage. The company expects to resume manufacturing in August after assessing the necessary repairs. ... On the corporate governance front, International Paper has appointed Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to its Board of Directors, effective October 1, 2026. Meanwhile, BofA Securities downgraded International Paper from Buy to Neutral, citing European market softness and preferring shares of Packaging Corporation of America and Smurfit Westrock. BofA had previously upgraded the company following an optimistic containerboard price forecast. ... Furthermore, Hamburger Containerboard’s recent price increase on recycled containerboard in European markets is seen as beneficial for International Paper, according to Truist Securities. These developments provide a snapshot of the company’s recent activities and market positioning."
International Paper,,,,Exa,JPMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential - Info-Today,info-today.eu,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://info-today.eu/2026/07/jpmorgan-upgrades-international-paper-stock-rating-on-upside-potential/,"Home Economy Finance JPMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential # JPMorgan upgrades International Paper stock rating on upside potential July 28, 2026 ... Investing.com – JPMorgan upgraded International Paper () from Neutral to Overweight and raised its price target to $61.00 from $51.00. The stock currently trades at $42.41 and has surged 16.67% over the past week, reflecting growing investor confidence. ... Analyst Detlef Winckelmann said the firm’s valuation incorporating a further $50 per ton suggests approximately 43% upside for International Paper versus the current share price. Even assuming no further cost reductions or operational improvements, the firm could justify upside of approximately 34%. ... The analyst noted this level of upside is sufficient to account for the potential risk of guidance downgrades, which consensus already assumes, and near-term earnings risk. According to InvestingPro Tips, analysts predict the company will be profitable this year, supporting the upgrade thesis. The platform offers 8 additional exclusive tips for IP investors, along with comprehensive Pro Research Reports available for over 1,400 US equities. JPMorgan said International Paper still trades at a premium to , which the firm does not view as fair. ... JPMorgan maintains its preference for and Smurfit WestRock. The firm said Packaging Corporation of America trades at a 30% premium to peers for a return on invested capital twice as high, regardless of the scenario. ... For Smurfit WestRock, JPMorgan expects approximately $800 million in operational improvements beyond any cyclical tailwinds, which will materially improve the return on invested capital profile and are not yet fully incorporated in consensus estimates for later years. ... In other recent news, International Paper has completed its acquisition of North Pacific Paper Company (NORPAC) for $360 million. This acquisition adds a Longview, Washington-based producer of recycled packaging papers to International Paper’s portfolio. Additionally, International Paper announced the temporary suspension of operations at its Pine Hill, Alabama mill due to weather-related damage. The company expects to resume manufacturing in August after assessing the necessary repairs. ... On the corporate governance front, International Paper has appointed Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to its Board of Directors, effective October 1, 2026. Meanwhile, BofA Securities downgraded International Paper from Buy to Neutral, citing European market softness and preferring shares of Packaging Corporation of America and Smurfit Westrock. BofA had previously upgraded the company following an optimistic containerboard price forecast. ... Furthermore, Hamburger Containerboard’s recent price increase on recycled containerboard in European markets is seen as beneficial for International Paper, according to Truist Securities. These developments provide a snapshot of the company’s recent activities and market positioning."
International Paper,,,,Exa,PCA’s $140/ton containerboard price increase considered unprecedented | Packaging Dive,www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/packaging-corporation-america-containerboard-price-hike-third-2026-unprecedented/826179/,"For instance, an analyst on International Paper’s April earnings call suggested the containerboard market at that time had not yet shown the anticipated tightness from the industry’s 10% capacity cuts that would warrant price hikes. Some observers have noted that OCC’s steady upward price movement came after producers announced their first containerboard hikes, and others note that OCC costs aren’t that high by historic norms. ... Wall Street watchers noted PCA’s stock surged to a record high Friday after Truist broke the price increase news. The movement appears to have also helped pull up stocks for competitors including International Paper and Smurfit Westrock, which along with PCA round out the top three North American containerboard producers. Barron’s reported that PCA’s price hike drove paper stocks to be the “biggest gainers in the S&P 500 on Friday.” ... Some observers believe this stock movement will put additional pressure on competitors to join a third round of containerboard price hikes. Truist Securities anticipates “other producers are likely to follow suit in ... coming weeks.” However, it’s still unclear whether competitors would attempt to align with PCA’s eye-popping $140 per ton or a more traditional level of increase."
International Paper,,,,Exa,Electric Bidet Seats Market to Reach USD 394.2 Million by 2032 (9.2% CAGR) – Big News,www.bignews.uk,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bignews.uk/business/electric-bidet-seats-market-to-reach-usd-394-2-million-by-2032-9-2-cagr,"to Reach USD ... .2 Million ... ) – Big News ... As PW Consulting’s Senior Strategic Advisor and Lead Industry Analyst, I present a focused preview of our latest market study on electric bidet seats. The market is entering a decisive growth phase: our base year is 2025, the forecast window runs from 2026–2032, and the industry is projected to expand at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 9.2% through the forecast period. By the end of the horizon the market is expected to approach the high hundreds of millions (USD), demonstrating clear runway for product innovation, channel expansion, and institutional adoption. This briefing highlights the strategic implications for corporations planning investments, partnerships, or go-to-market moves in 2026—while intentionally withholding granular segment tables to preserve the “preview” purpose and to encourage access to the full report for transaction‑level detail. Electric Bidet Seats Market ... Regulatory and reimbursement tailwinds: Recent policy moves—most notably Medicaid waiver programs increasingly recognizing electric bidet seats as durable medical equipment—create a runway into healthcare procurement channels (notably long‑term care and assisted living). Early institutional adopters report reductions in infection rates, driving evidence-based procurement decisions. Electric Bidet Seats Market ... Growth profile: The market posted steady expansion through the 2020–2025 period and is forecast to continue expanding at ~9.2% annually over 2026–2032. That pace implies meaningful scale opportunities for players that can execute on product differentiation, cost control, and distribution reach by 2026. ... Regulatory compliance and product positioning: GFCI outlet requirements and hygiene performance standards (e.g., UV/nozzle sterilization) are now market norms. Compliance is table stakes; differentiation will depend on user experience, integrated services (warranty, subscription maintenance), and demonstrable clinical outcomes for institutional buyers. ... benchmarks (instant ... , self‑ ... nozzles, app control ... strategic planners, TOTO’s ... emphasizes premium product engineering, global brand leverage, and deep ... partnerships—particularly in regions where ... name carries strong ... Kohler Co. — The January 2026 launch of the PureWash E930 with dual-wand, app connectivity, and voice control underscores Kohler’s strategy to blend design-led premium positioning with smart-home integration. Expect Kohler to push through both retail and specification channels (high-end residential and boutique commercial projects). ... Brondell Inc. — Recent distribution expansions indicate a channel-driven growth strategy. By broadening retailer availability and offering a range of Swash models, Brondell is pursuing volume growth through mainstream shelf presence and competitive product breadth. ... New product introductions and refreshed model lineups (early 2026) indicate that incumbents are accelerating product roadmaps to capture share among smart-home consumers and commercial specifiers alike. ... Distribution expansions suggest retailers and online marketplaces see sufficient demand elasticity to justify broader assortments—this will intensify pricing competition but also help normalize install costs through bundled promotions with plumbing and renovation services. ... Policy/coverage updates that explicitly recognize bidet seats as necessary medical equipment for certain populations can catalyze institutional procurement contracts and third-party reimbursement pathways—an attractive growth lever for vendors that can demonstrate clinical evidence and compliance. ... and reimbursement impact assessments, with a prioritized checklist for product compliance and clinical evidence generation. ... Actionable M&A and partnership screening criteria for bolt-on acquisitions, OEM relationships, and white‑label opportunities. ... Prioritize platform modularity: Design product platforms that ... configuration for residential, commercial, and clinical settings without wholesale re-engineering—leveraging common back‑ ... electronics while varying user ... facing features and service packages. ... Invest in compliance and clinical evidence: Vendors that can demonstrate reduced infection rates, validated safety compliance (GFCI and sterilization standards), and cost-savings in care settings will unlock institutional contracts and reimbursement channels. ... Manage cost-to-serve aggressively: Material sourcing strategies, installation partnerships, and bundled service offers (installation + extended warranty) will be decisive in protecting margins as competition intensifies. ... Choose channel strategy by cohort: Premium brands should double down on specification channels and design partnerships; value brands should expand big-box and e-commerce presence; D2C players should prioritize subscription and recurring-revenue services for aftermarket filters/wash cycles. ... Explore partnerships with healthcare integrators and O&P providers: Integration into durable medical equipment catalogs and hospital procurement frameworks requires both product certification and care pathway alignment. ... Fragmented standards: Divergent regional safety and hygiene regulations could raise compliance costs for global players. ... and distribution expansion ... The electric bidet seat market in 2026 represents a compelling blend of growth and strategic complexity. With a clear CAGR trajectory and visible institutional adoption pathways, firms that act now to align product architectures, compliance programs, and go-to-market channels will secure advantaged positions for the rest of the decade. Our study provides the operational playbooks, financial models, and competitive maps to inform M&A diligence, product roadmaps, and channel investments."
International Paper,,,,Exa,"International Paper adds two directors; Sullivan, Dorduncu retire - Memphis Business Journal",www.bizjournals.com,2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bizjournals.com/memphis/news/2026/07/20/international-paper-appoints-two-new-board-members.html,"International Paper adds two directors; Sullivan, Dorduncu retire - Memphis Business Journal ... The appointments bring the board to 13 members. Two longtime directors of the board are retiring at the end of the year."
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper expands board with two new appointments,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/international-paper-expands-board/,"International Paper expands board with two new appointments ... International Paper has appointed Katherine Collins and Lori J Ryerkerk to its board, with the additions taking effect on 1 October 2026. ... She was most recently Putnam Investments’ first head of sustainable investing. The role saw her establish the company’s sustainable investment business, which managed more than $10bn in assets. ... Ryerkerk has more than 40 years of experience in the energy, chemicals and specialty materials industries. ... She most recently served as chairman, president and CEO of Celanese Corporation, where she oversaw a period of change that included the $11bn purchase of DuPont’s Mobility & Materials business, as well as sustainability-related programmes. ... International Paper CEO and board chairman Andy Silvernail said: “Lori and Katherine each bring exceptional leadership experience and a proven ability to help guide organisations through complexity and change. ... “The strategic insight and experience they each offer will strengthen our Board and support the company’s continued transformation.” ... International Paper’s two current directors intend to step down at the end of 2026: Dr Kathryn Sullivan, who joined the board in 2017; and Ahmet Dorduncu, who has been a director since 2011. ... The leadership change comes amid a restructuring at International Paper, which offers sustainable packaging solutions. ... This has seen the company downsize operations, most recently through the closure of Carrollton South packaging plant in Texas."
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper adds two directors to its BoD effective 1 October 2026,www.lesprom.com (Lesprom Network),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lesprom.com/en/news/International_Paper_adds_two_directors_to_its_BoD_effective_1_October_2026_123944/,"International Paper adds two directors to its BoD effective 1 October 2026 # International Paper adds two directors to its BoD effective 1 October 2026 ... Lori Ryerkerk brings energy and chemicals experience; Katherine Collins contributes investment and governance perspective. ... - International Paper named Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to its board effective October 1, 2026. - International Paper named Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to its board effective October 1, 2026. - Dr. Kathryn Sullivan and Ahmet Dorduncu plan to retire from International Paper's board at the end of 2026. - Collins brings over three decades in sustainable investing and asset management, while Ryerkerk brings four decades in energy and chemicals. ... International Paper has appointed Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to the company's Board of Directors, effective October 1, 2026, according to International Paper. ... Collins brings more than three decades of experience in asset management and sustainable investing, having most recently served as the first Head of Sustainable Investing at Putnam Investments, where she built the firm's sustainable investment platform into a top 10 U.S. sustainable asset manager with more than $10 billion in assets, while earlier holding senior investment roles at Fidelity including leading equity research for more than $500 billion in U.S. equity mutual fund assets. ... Ryerkerk brings more than four decades of experience across the global energy, chemicals, and specialty materials sectors, most recently serving as Chairman, President and CEO of Celanese Corporation, where she led the company through significant transformation including the $11 billion acquisition of DuPont's Mobility & Materials business. ... The company also announced that two directors, Dr. Kathryn Sullivan, who has served on the board since 2017, and Ahmet Dorduncu, who has served since 2011, plan to retire from the board at the end of 2026. ... International Paper creates sustainable packaging solutions that enable our customers, teammates and shareowners to thrive in an ever-changing world."
International Paper,,,,Exa,"International Paper to shut packaging site in Carrollton, Texas",www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/international-paper-shut-texas-packaging-site/,"International Paper to shut packaging site in Carrollton, Texas ... International Paper is further downsizing its US network by shutting down its Carrollton South packaging plant in Texas. ... The site is slated for closure by the end of the third quarter of 2026. ... According to the company, the move forms part of a broader effort to match production capacity with customer requirements and support the long-term position of its North American packaging operations. ... International Paper said it regularly reviews its industrial network to decide how best to deploy resources for customers. ... It added that the Texas closure fits with that longer-term approach. ... Staff affected by the shutdown will get severance, ongoing benefits and outplacement assistance. ... International Paper North America Packaging East group vice-president Keith Townsend said: “Decisions that affect our people and our communities are never made lightly. We’re committed to supporting our Carrollton South team members throughout this transition. ... “Customers will be serviced at other International Paper facilities in the region.” ... In June, the company said it would close its sheet plant in Aurora, Illinois; preprint operations at Richwood, Kentucky; and converting facilities in Elk Grove, California, and Barrington, New Jersey. ... Earlier in the year, packaging plants in Compton, California, and Louisville, Kentucky, stopped operating. Those closures affected 125 workers in Compton and 93 in Louisville. ... Last year, International Paper closed the Red River containerboard mill in Campti, Louisiana; a recycling facility in Phoenix, Arizona; a box plant in Hazleton, Pennsylvania; and a sheet feeder site in St Louis, Missouri. ... Meanwhile, in May, the company began construction of a new $225m packaging plant in Rankin County, Mississippi."
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper Announces Changes to Its Board of Directors,www.prnewswire.com (International Paper),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/international-paper-announces-changes-to-its-board-of-directors-302828759.html,"International Paper Announces Changes to Its Board of Directors Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to Join as Newest Board Members ... Directors Dr. Kathryn Sullivan and ... C. Dorduncu to Retire from Board at Year-End ... MEMPHIS, Tenn., July 17, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- International Paper (NYSE: IP; LSE: IPC) is pleased to announce that Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk have been appointed to the company's Board of Directors, effective October 1, 2026. ... IP CEO and Chairman of the Board Andy Silvernail said, ""Lori and Katherine each bring exceptional leadership experience and a proven ability to help guide organizations through complexity and change. Lori brings deep operational expertise and public company leadership experience, while Katherine brings a distinguished investment background and thoughtful governance perspective. The strategic insight and experience they each offer will strengthen our Board and support the company's continued transformation."" ... In addition, two directors plan to retire from serving on IP's board of directors at the end of 2026: Dr. Kathryn Sullivan, who has served on the IP board since 2017, and Ahmet Dorduncu, who has served on the IP board since 2011. ... About International Paper (NYSE: IP; LSE: IPC)International Paper creates sustainable packaging solutions that enable our customers, teammates and shareowners to thrive in an ever-changing world. We are a leader in corrugated packaging, partnering with customers across industries to protect what matters most, strengthen supply chains and create lasting value. Learn more at internationalpaper.com. ... ### International Paper CEO to Speak at Jefferies 2026 Industrials Conference ... International Paper Chief Executive Officer Andy Silvernail will speak at Jefferies 2026 Industrials Conference on September 10, 2026. The... ... ### International Paper to Close Carrollton South, Texas Packaging Facility ... International Paper (NYSE: IP; LSE: IPC), a leader in sustainable packaging, today announced it will close its Carrollton South packaging facility..."
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper Announces Changes to Its Board of Directors | AP News,apnews.com,2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://apnews.com/press-release/pr-newswire/press-release-ea582c9f349e63e11935b56e25d4dc75,"International Paper Announces Changes to Its Board of Directors | AP News ... Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk to Join as Newest Board Members ... Directors Dr. Kathryn Sullivan and Ahmet C. Dorduncu to Retire from Board at Year-End ... MEMPHIS, Tenn., July 17, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- International Paper (NYSE: IP; LSE: IPC) is pleased to announce that Katherine Collins and Lori J. Ryerkerk have been appointed to the company’s Board of Directors, effective October 1, 2026. ... IP CEO and Chairman of the Board Andy Silvernail said, “Lori and Katherine each bring exceptional leadership experience and a proven ability to help guide organizations through complexity and change. Lori brings deep operational expertise and public company leadership experience, while Katherine brings a distinguished investment background and thoughtful governance perspective. The strategic insight and experience they each offer will strengthen our Board and support the company’s continued"
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper to close Texas box plant | Packaging Dive,www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/international-paper-close-box-plant-container-carrollton-texas/825424/,"# International Paper to close Texas box plant ... This closure announcement builds on a string of others from the company, the most recent coming less than three weeks ago. ... International Paper CEO Andy Silvernail spoke at the Jefferies Industrials Conference on Sept. 4, 2025, detailing moves the company has made as part of its optimization strategy. ... International Paper announced Thursday it will permanently close its box plant in the Dallas suburb of Carrollton, Texas, as part of the company’s ongoing string of shutdowns impacting thousands of employees. ... The facility is scheduled to close by the end of the third quarter, according to the company. Nearly all of the 45 hourly and 19 salaried employees will be affected, and they’re eligible to apply for posted jobs at another IP facilities, said Amy Simpson, IP’s head of communications for North America, via email. The company intends to assist affected employees will severance, benefits and outplacement support. ... Customers will be serviced by other IP facilities in the region, according to a news release. IP has another box plant about 2.5 miles away that produces similar products to the South Carrollton site. It also has a recycling center about 1.5 miles away. The South Carrollton box plant closure will not affect the recycling center, Simpson said. ... This shutdown is part of IP's “ongoing work to align its manufacturing footprint with customer demand and strengthen the long-term competitiveness of its North America packaging business,” the news release said. ... When Andy Silvernail became CEO two years ago, he introduced an optimization strategy to turn around the company’s results and operations. That has involved a plethora of global facility closures and layoffs. ... Including this new announcement, more than 5,864 employees have been affected by IP’s closures since October 2024. The company's most recent announcement came less than three weeks ago, for four closures across the United States slated to occur by the end of Q3. In total, 330 employees will be affected. ... In January, executives said they expect to close at least seven facilities and cut 700 jobs in Europe, the Middle East and Africa. The company also filed a notice that month with the state of Washington about closing a facility in Union Gap with 102 employees. In February, IP announced it would close a container plant in Georgetown, South Carolina, affecting 126 employees. And during an April earnings call, executives said they were considering additional cuts in EMEA ahead of the company’s planned split into two companies next year. ... In addition, IP disclosed on July 9 that it would temporarily suspend operations at its containerboard mill in Pine Hill, Alabama, due to rain damage to the roof. The company aims to resume operations in August. ... International Paper executives have discussed geopolitical and macroeconomic conditions that have challenged the business during the last several quarters, prompting them in April to lower guidance for the year. Still, the packaging firm brought in$5.97 billion in revenue last quarter, up 13.4% compared with Q1 2025. IP next reports earnings on July 30. ... International Paper, Niagara Bottling announced closures in July"
International Paper,,,,Exa,DS Smith and Verdi conclude talks on German site closures,"www.euwid-paper.com (EUWID, Gernsbach, Germany)",2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.euwid-paper.com/news/companies/ds-smith-and-verdi-conclude-talks-on-german-site-closures-150726/,"DS Smith and Verdi conclude talks on German site closures ... DS Smith and the German trade union Verdi have confirmed that negotiations over the planned restructuring measures in Germany have been concluded. DS Smith said that an agreement had been reached with employee representatives and that the negotiations had been successfully completed, but declined to comment further."
International Paper,,,,Exa,IP temporarily closes Alabama containerboard mill following storm | Packaging Dive,www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/international-paper-temporary-closure-pine-hill-mill-storm-damage/825166/,"# IP temporarily closes Alabama containerboard mill following storm ... While the company doesn’t “have a full timeline” for repairs needed on the rain-damaged roof, it hopes to resume operations in August, according to an IP spokesperson. ... International Paper announced it’s temporarily suspending operations at its containerboard mill in Pine Hill, Alabama, due to storm damage to the building. ... The company identified roof damage after excessive rain in the area, said Amy Simpson, IP’s head of communications for North America, via email. The company is assessing the damage and the repairs needed. ... “While we don't have a full timeline, our current thinking is that we can resume manufacturing in August,” Simpson said. ... The company is working with customers served by the Pine Hill mill to manage impacts. “Thankfully, IP has a strong network of mills and can shift work orders where possible to minimize impact,” Simpson said. ... The Pine Hill mill is about 60 miles from IP’s Riverdale mill in Selma, Alabama. The company had been converting the No. 16 machine at Riverdale to produce containerboard instead of uncoated free sheet. Company executives had expected project completion by the end of the second quarter, with about$80 million in non-repeating costs this year from the project. ... The unplanned downtime at Pine Hill comes as IP has been reworking its footprint and closing facilities. Most recently, the company announced in June that it would close four sites across the United States by the end of the third quarter, which will affect 330 employees. ... This followed other such announcements this year. In February, IP announced it would close a Georgetown, South Carolina, container plant, affecting 126 employees. In January, the company filed a notice with the state of Washington about closing a facility in Union Gap with 102 employees. And during a January earnings call, executives said they expected to close at least seven facilities and cut 700 jobs in Europe, the Middle East and Africa. ... IP also was one of numerous fiber companies to report unplanned downtime due to a winter storm in January. That storm caused a roughly$53 million hit to IP’s earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, executives said during an April earnings call. ... - International Paper announces shutdowns, layoffs at 4 US facilities By Katie Pyzyk• June 29, 2026 ... International Paper, Niagara Bottling announced closures in July ... Containerboard production healthier in Q2, but still in decline"
International Paper,,,,Exa,International Paper Declares Quarterly Dividend,www.prnewswire.com (International Paper),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/international-paper-declares-quarterly-dividend-302825464.html,"MEMPHIS, Tenn., July 14, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- International Paper (NYSE: IP; LSE: IPC), today declared a quarterly dividend of $0.4625 per share for the period from July 1, 2026, to September 30, 2026, inclusive, on the common stock, par value $1.00, of the Company, payable on September 15, 2026, to holders of record at the close of business on August 14, 2026. ... Today, the Company also declared a quarterly dividend of $1.00 per share for the period from July 1, 2026, to September 30, 2026, inclusive, on the cumulative $4.00 preferred stock of the Company, payable on September 15, 2026, to holders of record at the close of business on August 14, 2026. ... About International Paper (NYSE: IP; LSE: IPC)International Paper creates sustainable packaging solutions that enable our customers, teammates and shareowners to thrive in an ever-changing world. We are a leader in corrugated packaging, partnering with customers across industries to protect what matters most, strengthen supply chains and create lasting value. Learn more at internationalpaper.com. ... ### International Paper Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results ... International Paper (NYSE: IP) (LSE: IPC) (the ""Company"") today announced results for the quarter ended June 30, 2026. ""Our teams delivered strong... ... ### International Paper CEO to Speak at Jefferies 2026 Industrials Conference ... International Paper Chief Executive Officer Andy Silvernail will speak at Jefferies 2026 Industrials Conference on September 10, 2026. The..."
