International Paper,,,,Tavily,Japan’s Wobbling Yen Could Trigger A Global Financial Crisis,,,,,https://www.google.com/goto?url=CAESqAEB7keqTeWeebCkbM6gkCCynBQpMPHvbtPb6arnvCVvjOptc5MNP7iQcZkyKYGblImRNjN5AaPR2c2DR3rtDVKcR6NplwlYGJfsjmAzUIuhRLysMwf2DW3uamqeHh1IYzOvdVAKM0ZzVC3yqlgJLhpBCIGoCh0-gc5dca_l40zD6LVTKkMHOB5_5jOukUwaI2C_DP36SiSx3dUZ-mWoQ8IeiBTOEsV43Jo%3D,"The immediate worry for U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent is that in an effort to save the yen from collapse, Japan will start liquidating its $1.1 trillion portfolio of Treasury bonds and bills, not to mention its holdings of German and British bonds. Such sales would put pressure on interest rates. After all, financing our immense budget deficits and refinancing some $7 trillion of our existing debt that’s coming up for renewal are already worrying the markets. This anxiety, for instance, is why the interest rate on our 30-year Treasury bond has reached its highest level in almost 20 years. [...] ## Download The Forbes App Mini Crossword Frase Pinpoint Queens Crossclimb # Japan’s Wobbling Yen Could Trigger A Global Financial Crisis BySteve Forbes, Forbes Staff. The wobbling Japanese yen could trigger a global financial crisis, but effectively dealing with it is surprisingly straightforward. The yen recently reached a 40-year low against the dollar. The fear is that a furthe"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Print vendor serving restaurant brands expanding nationwide after acquisition | Fast Casual,www.fastcasual.com,2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.fastcasual.com/news/print-vendor-serving-restaurant-brands-expanding-nationwide-after-acquisition/,"Print vendor serving restaurant brands expanding nationwide after acquisition | Fast Casual ... # Print vendor serving restaurant brands expanding nationwide after acquisition ... Sandy Alexander, a commercial printing and marketing services company that counts restaurant chains among its clients, has been acquired by the Marth Group, giving the printer a coast-to-coast production network, according to a company press release. ... Sandy Alexander produces printed menus, in-store signage, direct mail campaigns and other marketing materials for dining brands, along with clients in the automotive, beauty, healthcare and retail sectors. The Marth Group is the parent company of ENPOINTE, based in Minneapolis, and Digital Lizard, which operates in New Jersey and Idaho. The deal brings the three businesses together under a single ownership structure while preserving the Sandy Alexander name. ... The combined company will operate six facilities giving s clients production capability spanning the East Coast, West Coast and Midwest — a scale that could appeal to multiunit restaurant brands looking to standardize menu boards, packaging inserts and promotional materials across regions from a single vendor. ... The company also holds Woman-Owned and Minority-Owned Business certifications, along with HITRUST and SOC 2 compliance designations carried over from ENPOINTE. Company officials said those credentials give Sandy Alexander clients — including those in healthcare, life sciences and financial services — expanded procurement options and stronger data security assurances. ... ""Sandy Alexander is stronger than ever, and as part of the Marth Group, it's about to reach more clients, in more markets, than at any point in its 60-year history,"" Mark Marth said in the release. ... Luke Westlake, a Sandy Alexander representative, said the acquisition builds on the company's reputation while adding resources. ... ""Joining the Marth Group amplifies everything we've built — giving our clients coast-to-coast production capability, expanded certifications and a team that's larger and stronger than ever,"" Westlake said. ... The newly combined organization will draw on Sandy Alexander's experience in commercial printing, brand environments, direct mail, and kitting and fulfillment; ENPOINTE's large-format and data-driven variable print production; and Digital Lizard's digital print platform and West Coast operations. ... Founded in Clifton more than 60 years ago, Sandy Alexander serves clients in the dining, automotive, beauty, healthcare, life sciences, retail and travel industries. The Marth Group, a privately held holding company, employs more than 500 people across five states."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Packaging M&A activity dips in 2026 | Packaging Dive,www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/capstone-partners-packaging-acquisitions-muted-2026/826759/,"Packaging M&A activity dips in 2026 | Packaging Dive ... # Packaging M&A activity dips in 2026 Economic uncertainty has contributed to “cautious buyer behavior” resulting in a more than 21% decrease in packaging M&A activity through the second quarter, according to a Capstone Partners report. Published Aug. 6, 2026 Katie Pyzyk Lead Reporter Getty Images If you’ve felt like packaging industry M&A activity has been muted so far in 2026, your instincts are correct. Various economic and geopolitical factors mean activity has “skewed selective,” according to a newly released report from investment banking and financial advisory firm Capstone Partners. ... Through the second quarter of this year, the paper and packaging industry has charted a 21.3% decrease in the number of M&A deals, compared with the same time last year, according to the Capstone report. Comparatively, the broader industrials sector has experienced a 12.1% increase. ... The muted M&A environment underscored a broader trend of companies being cautious with their capital allocations. They’re focusing on navigating uncertain conditions and preserving financial flexibility until growth visibility improves, the report says. “[O] verall growth visibility remains ... , reinforcing cautious buyer behavior and a defensive posture in packaging M&A.” ... Despite subdued transaction volumes, average deal values have “remained robust” this year so far, showing that “buyers have continued to target high-quality assets and resilient business models even amid challenging macroeconomic conditions.” The enterprise value paid in 2026 has averaged $164.4 million, up from $60.4 million during the same period in 2025. ... Strategic buyers remain the most interested in pursuing deals, as has been the case since the COVID-19 pandemic, according to the report. Private, public and hybrid buyers are dominant, representing 83.1% of all M&A activity. ... However, these groups also have seen the largest pullback in transaction volumes this year. The number of private strategic transactions in 2026 are down 29.7% from last year, and hybrid deals dropped 26.6% year over year. Public strategic volumes grew by one deal, and private equity decreased by one deal. ... Performance across the paper and packaging industry has diverged, with many companies lagging while “a subset of companies have achieved above-market growth” via strategies such as technology differentiation or targeting niche end markets, the report says. That’s contributing to uneven interest in M&A across the packaging industry. ... Scale, in this context, functions as both a strategic enabler ... and a defensive mechanism, allowing leading operators to consolidate weaker ... and emerge stronger as ... Challenges within the corrugated market have made the sector particularly sensitive to uncertainty that plays into depressed M&A activity. North American box shipments dropped 1.9% year over year in Q1, according to Fibre Box Association data, and containerboard production fell 8% year over year in Q1, according to American Forest & Paper Association data. These conditions follow the industry’s historic, nearly 10% cut in production capacity during 2025. And input costs are up notably in 2026, prompting fiber producers to announce numerous price increases. ... Glimmers of improving market health have emerged as 2026 progresses, and during recent earnings calls some company executives cited signs of improving demand in Q2. But containerboard production still declined 2% year over year in Q2, according to AF&PA. ... Even so, Capstone points to some notable deals that have occurred in corrugated this year. For one, International Paper acquired North Pacific Paper Co. in June for $360 million. And private equity firm Kingswood Capital Management acquired Coveris’ paper business unit."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Rondocarton investeşte 7 mil. euro ca să înlocuiască stivuitoarele cu roboţi de manipulare mărfuri - Produs in Ardeal,produsinardeal.ro (Produs in Ardeal),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://produsinardeal.ro/2026/08/06/rondocarton-investeste-7-mil-euro-ca-sa-inlocuiasca-stivuitoarele-cu-roboti-de-manipulare-marfuri/,"Rondocarton investeşte 7 mil. euro ca să înlocuiască stivuitoarele cu roboţi de manipulare mărfuri - Produs in Ardeal ... # Rondocarton investeşte 7 mil. euro ca să înlocuiască stivuitoarele cu roboţi de manipulare mărfuri ... 6 august 2026 Rondocarton, parte a gru­pului austriac Rondo Ganahl, unul dintre cei mai mari producători de carton ondulat, investeşte în automatizarea transpor­tului intern în cadrul fabricii din Târgovişte, potrivit Ziarului Financiar. ... ”Renunţăm la stivuitoare şi trecem la roboţi de manipulare mărfuri. Investim la Târgovişte în automatizare. Roboţii de manipulare reprezintă un sistem integrat, ce se va implementa în mai mulţi paşi. În trei ani succesiv va fi implementată auto­matizarea transportului intern din fabrică. Primul pas înseamnă o in­vestiţie de 7 mil. euro”, a declarat Mihnea Bâldea, directorul gene­ral al companiei Rondocarton, citat de ZF. ... Rondocarton vinde 90% din ambalaje pe piaţa locală, sectorul alimentar fiind unul strategic pentru Rondocarton. Compania mai are clienţi şi din automotive, din electro­nice, producători de echipa­mente electronice şi electrice, industria mobilei. Producătorii de ambalaje sunt un barometru al comenzilor din piaţă şi al economiei, în condiţiile în care livrează pentru jucători din toate sectoarele."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Mondi introduces laser-marked flexible packaging,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/mondi-laser-marked-flexible-packaging/,"Mondi introduces laser-marked flexible packaging ... # Mondi introduces laser-marked flexible packaging ... The design is aimed at e-commerce and bag-in-box uses and can be applied to several flexible packaging formats. Vidhya Edwards Munnangi August 5, 2026 Artwork is added directly to the flexible packaging during converting through laser marking technology. Credit: Mondi. Mondi has introduced a packaging format that pairs a corrugated outer carton with recyclable flexible packaging marked by laser. ... The design is aimed at e-commerce and bag-in-box uses and can be applied to several flexible packaging formats to support circularity and form supply chains. ... Mondi is working with customers and partners to examine wider commercial use of the format in pet food, home and personal care products, and e-commerce packaging. ... In the first half of 2026 (H1 2026), Mondi reported loss, hit by asset impairment charges, reduced average selling prices, and rising input costs. ... The packaging company’s net loss for the period attributable to shareholders stood at €255m ($293.95m) in H1 2026, compared with a profit of €63m in the prior year."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Paranova supplies paper-based punnets for Tomalina tomatoes in Asda,www.packagingnews.co.uk (Waqas Qureshi),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingnews.co.uk/news/markets/food/paranova-supplies-paper-based-punnets-for-tomalina-tomatoes-in-asda-04-08-2026,"Paranova has partnered with British grower Flavourfresh to launch a limited-edition premium Tomalina tomato range in Asda stores, using its FibreFresh paper-based punnets. ... Supported by half a million-pound investment in Boix punnet-forming technology, the launch marks the beginning of Paranova’s expansion into heat-sealed paper-based punnet packaging. ... Michael Conway, chief commercial officer, Paranova, said: “Following our recent investment and development in leading punnet technology, we are proud to have launched this new format for Flavourfresh. Delivering a significant reduction in plastic, it demonstrates how paper-based punnets can offer on-shelf differentiation, operational efficiency, and support sustainability ambitions.” ... Paranova also confirmed it is preparing to launch FastFlex, a new tray and lidding system designed for fresh produce and convenience applications. ... The system will offer lead times of less than seven days for lidding supply, significantly reducing turnaround times compared with traditional 2-4 week print cycles. ... According to Paranova, the platform has been developed to provide greater agility for retailers and growers managing short production windows, promotional launches, seasonal demand fluctuations and reduced stock holdings. ... Produced using a newly commissioned press designed specifically for filmic paper-based tray applications, the FastFlex system will combine reduced origination costs with no minimum order quantity requirements."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Vandemoortele buys US baker Banneton outright,www.just-food.com (Satarupa Bhowmik),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.just-food.com/news/vandemoortele-buys-us-baker-banneton/,"Vandemoortele buys US baker Banneton outright ... Belgium-based Vandemoortele has taken full ownership of US bakery peer Banneton by acquiring the remaining stake in the business. ... Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed as the Belgian baker added to its 80% interest in Banneton purchased in 2024. ... In a statement yesterday (3 August), Vandemoortele said the acquisition “marks a major milestone” for its North American strategy by “establishing a domestic US manufacturing footprint”. ... The family-owned company said: “Combining Vandemoortele’s European import infrastructure with Banneton’s domestic production plant provides a flexible, hybrid model that streamlines logistics and quickly meets customer demands.” ... The Banneton brand will be retained. ... After the deal’s completion, Alexandre Bloch, previously with Vandemoortele’s unit in France, will take over as operations manager. ... Founded in 2008, Banneton produces croissants and pastries at its facility in Swedesboro, New Jersey. ... Its products are sold across retail, foodservice and bakery channels throughout the US. ... Before the 2024 transaction with Vandemoortele, Banneton was owned by private-equity firm Encore Consumer Capital and founders Victor and Alex Litinetsky. ... Curt Coolidge, the general manager of Vandemoortele North America, said: “We are excited to fully integrate the Swedesboro facility into our operations, allowing us to deliver the ultimate one-stop-shop experience for authentic, premium freezer-to-oven croissants and pastries.” ... The company operates production sites across 12 European countries and markets its products in more than 95 countries, including the US and Canada. ... Meanwhile, Vandemoortele announced its purchase of Délifrance early last year, creating a bakery business with an estimated combined turnover of €2.4bn (then $2.6bn). ... However, the deal encountered competition concerns in the UK and Europe. ... The transaction then received conditional approval from the European Commission last year amid Vandemoortele’s pledge to sell two French plants in Avignon and Béthune but it was unable to secure a buyer for the sites.Consequently, the UK’s Competition and Markets Authority (CMA) launched a Phase 2 investigation into the deal in April. ... Then in June, Vandemoortele offered to sell its factory in Worcester in the UK to address those concerns. The company is now awaiting the next step from the CMA."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Made in Benin WAPACK lance la production locale de sacs en papier - Matin Libre,matinlibre.com (Matin Libre),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://matinlibre.com/2026/07/31/made-in-benin-wapack-lance-la-production-locale-de-sacs-en-papier/,"Made in Benin WAPACK lance la production locale de sacs en papier - Matin Libre ... WAPACK lance la production locale de sacs en papier ... SEME-KPODJI, 17 juillet 2026, Trois ans après son installation au Bénin, WAPACK INDUSTRIES, entreprise spécialisée dans la production d’emballages en carton, a franchi un nouveau cap. La société a inauguré ce vendredi 17 juillet 2026, à son siège dans la zone industrielle de SEME-KPODJI, une nouvelle ligne de production dédiée aux sacs en papier. ... Le Directeur général de WAPACK, Monsieur Rohan GARG à l’entame des discours, a présenté aux invités, le leitmotiv qui guide les actions de l’entreprise. A l’en croire, WAPACK INDUSTRIES croit fermement que la véritable croissance réside dans la résolution des problèmes et la satisfaction des besoins du pays. ... Dans leurs interventions, les officiels ont unanimement salué cette initiative industrielle. Ils ont souligné qu’elle s’inscrit parfaitement dans la vision du gouvernement béninois qui vise à préserver l’environnement à travers l’interdiction progressive de l’utilisation des sachets en plastique. ... « Cette nouvelle ligne de production est une réponse concrète aux défis de la pollution plastique. WAPACK INDUSTRIES contribue à offrir aux consommateurs et aux entreprises une alternative durable, made in Bénin », a déclaré le Maire de la commune de SEME-KPODJI. ... Le DG de l’ APIEX a pour sa part mis en avant l’impact de cet investissement sur l’emploi local et la compétitivité de l’industrie béninoise. La coordonnatrice du PAEB a insisté sur l’importance des partenariats public-privés pour atteindre les objectifs de développement durable. ... Après les discours officiels, les invités ont effectué une visite guidée des installations de la nouvelle ligne. Ils ont pu constater de près le processus de fabrication des sacs en papier, de la matière première au produit fini. ... Cette extension de capacité marque pour WAPACK INDUSTRIES la volonté de diversifier son offre et de devenir un acteur clé de l’emballage écologique en Afrique de l’Ouest. ... Trois ans après son démarrage, l’entreprise confirme ainsi son ancrage au Bénin et son ambition : allier performance industrielle et responsabilité environnementale. WAPACK INDUSTRIES, certifiée ISO 9001 : 2015, leader dans la fabrication d’emballages en carton au Bénin et dans la sous-région, vise, avec cette nouvelle ligne, une capacité de fabrication de 4 millions de sacs en papier par mois, pour atteindre un objectif global de 10 millions."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Axjo, Balcan, Detpak among international packaging companies expanding in US | Packaging Dive",www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/packaging-manufacturing-expansions-axjo-balcan-detpak-graham-sonoco-quad/825658/,"# Axjo, Balcan, Detpak among international packaging companies expanding in US ... Recent announcements of new facilities and expansions also come from U.S.-based companies including Graham Packaging, Packaging Corporation of America, Quad and Sonoco. ... Detpak, an Australia-based Detmold Group company, opened its first U.S. manufacturing site, in Spartanburg, South Carolina, in 2026. Courtesy of Detpak ... Plastic packaging producers led a round of announcements in recent weeks about facility openings and expansions. Several international companies are among those opening or upgrading packaging facilities in the United States. ... - Axium Packaging is expanding its Midwest presence with a new facility in the St. Louis area. The 202,000-square-foot facility is the company’s third in Missouri. It will initially launch with extrusion blow molding capabilities and will expand into injection stretch blow molding. ... - Axjo Group, a Sweden-based recycled plastic packaging specialist whose U.S. headquarters is in Conover, North Carolina, opened a new 160,600-square-foot plant in Haltom City, Texas. The company has begun production there for large reels to serve customers in the wire and cable sector. The company says it’s seeing strong demand for these products, and the new location will bring it closer to customers. ... - Balcan Packaging, a Quebec-based manufacturer of plastic technical films and flexible packaging, launched a new extrusion line at its plant in Pleasant Prairie, Wisconsin. The five-layer wide web line will enable the company to produce industrial sheeting up to 50 feet wide, meeting growing demand for the products that are largely used to wrap boats, scaffolding, modular homes and other construction projects. The Pleasant Prairie plant opened in 2022, marking Balcan’s entry into production in the U.S. ... - Detpak, an Australia-based Detmold Group company, opened a new manufacturing site in Spartanburg, South Carolina — its first plant in North America. While the company has supplied foodservice packaging into this market for 20 years, the local plant will improve responsiveness and supply chain reliability, a spokesperson said via email. Detpak chose Spartanburg because of the area’s “strong manufacturing environment, skilled workforce, strategic logistics network and proximity to key customer markets,” according to the spokesperson. ... - Graham Packaging signed a lease for a 216,000-square-foot industrial space in Lee’s Summit, Missouri, according to CoStar. The rigid plastic container manufacturer proposed to the city council in May that it would begin operations this year and that all lines would be open by 2028. The company said the project would bring 82 jobs, and it sought property tax abatement. ... - Packaging Corporation of America announced during a July 23 earnings call that it had started up a new corrugated converting plant in Ohio. The 550,000-square-foot facility is “in a very strategic area for us while improving our operational efficiency over the long term,” said President Tom Hassfurther during the call. ... - Quad is expanding its packaging manufacturing with a new facility in Salt Lake City. Operations are expected to launch at the 100,000-square-foot facility during the fourth quarter. The company says box-making equipment at the site will include a sheeter, die cutters, folding gluers and a Heidelberg XL 106 press with UV capabilities. ... - Sonoco announced during a July 23 earnings call that it had completed a$20 million expansion at its wire and cable reels production and assembly facility in Hartselle, Alabama. The additional 15% production capacity for wood reels is intended to meet surging demand amid the data center construction boom and power grid upgrades. “We have been essentially sold out and needed this additional capacity to meet market demand,” said CEO Howard Coker during the call. ... Axjo, Balcan, Detpak among international packaging companies expanding in US"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,EMBALLAGES ET BOUCHONS COURONNES – Multiprint investit 3 milliards FCFA pour conquérir la sous-région - Télé'Asu,teleasu.tv (Armel Mouanjo),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://teleasu.tv/emballages-et-bouchons-couronnes-multiprint-investit-3-milliards-fcfa-pour-conquerir-la-sous-region/,"EMBALLAGES ET BOUCHONS COURONNES – Multiprint investit 3 milliards FCFA pour conquérir la sous-région - Télé'Asu ... # EMBALLAGES ET BOUCHONS COURONNES – Multiprint investit 3 milliards FCFA pour conquérir la sous-région ... Les investissements effectués en 2026 par cet industriel visent à capter un marché d’import-substitution de 24 milliards FCFA sur les emballages premium et de 23,7 milliards FCFA sur les bouchons couronnes. ... Multiprint Labels & Packaging, acteur majeur de l’industrie de l’emballage en Afrique centrale, vient d’effectuer trois investissements industriels majeurs déployés sur son site de Douala. Les investissements effectués au cours de l’exercice 2026 en cours concernent notamment la mise en service de la presse offset Heidelberg Speedmaster CX 104 (2 milliards FCFA), l’acquisition d’une ligne SACMI PMC300C dédiée à la production locale de bouchons couronnes (600 millions FCFA), et l’installation d’une centrale solaire photovoltaïque (400 millions FCFA). ... Ces investissements traduisent la volonté de Multiprint de renforcer durablement son outil industriel afin d’accompagner les besoins croissants de ses clients et de contribuer au développement de l’industrie locale. Représentant un engagement total de 3 milliards FCFA, ces opérations permettront à Multiprint de capter deux marchés d’import-substitution stratégiques, évalués à 24 milliards FCFA pour les emballages premium et 23,7 milliards FCFA pour les bouchons couronnes. Ils s’inscrivent par ailleurs dans un plan global de 25 milliards FCFA à l’horizon 2030, porté par l’ambition de hisser le chiffre d’affaires du groupe à 70 milliards FCFA. ... L’acquisition de la Heidelberg Speedmaster CX104 a été rendue possible grâce au directeur général de la Société anonyme des Boissons du Cameroun, par qui Multiprint a pu obtenir la lettre de confort qui a permis à cette entreprise de réunir le financement auprès de la banque. Une marque de confiance que le DG de Multiprint entend capitaliser. «Le tiers des billets de banque est imprimé sur une Heidelberg comme celle que nous venons d’acquérir. C’est un saut qualitatif important. Dans la sous-région, c’est le plus gros investissement dans une machine comme celle-là. Cela renforce notre compétitivité ; pour nos clients, ça améliore la qualité et le délai, et pour l’économie nationale, nous allons soutenir l’import-substitution. Les professionnels qui ont besoin d’emballages qui répondent aux standards internationaux peuvent se référer à nous», note le DG de Multiprint, Ibrahima Ousmanou. ... À cet effet, l’entreprise bénéficie, une fois de plus, de l’accompagnement de la SABC. Au cours de la présentation de ces acquisitions, le mardi 28 juillet 2026, le DG de la SABC, Stéphane Descazeaud, a indiqué avoir instruit ses équipes de réduire une part des commandes faites à l’étranger pour les adresser à Multiprint. « Cet équipement va permettre de capter une partie importante de ce que nous importons de l’étranger. C’est une grande avancée pour Multiprint. Mais il n’y a pas encore de capacité suffisante pour imprimer tous nos besoins actuels au Cameroun », fait-il observer. Néanmoins, le marché est vaste. «Le marché du packaging est volumineux et important.; actuellement, on n’arrive pas à satisfaire 30 % de ce marché. Cet investissement apporte plus de rapidité, de fiabilité, de qualité et un volume plus important en termes de capacité. Cela va nous permettre de répondre en temps et en heure aux commandes de nos clients», précise la directrice marketing et commercial de Multiprint, Félicité Ndjetehe. ... L’acquisition de la machine d’impression va booster le tissu national en termes de qualité d’emballage, d’étiquettes et de cartons. «La machine a une capacité de production de 15 000 feuilles par heure sur le carton ; et sur le papier métallisé, nous produisons 12 000 feuilles par heure», précise le chef de projet, Firmin Athis. Elle permettra également de satisfaire les clients, de livrer un travail de qualité et dans les délais. Mais les responsables de Multiprint comptent, en plus, à court terme, réduire le déficit criard sur l’emballage métallique. L’entreprise entend proposer une solution d’emballage en boîte métallique pour faire des conserves pour les produits issus de notre agriculture."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Reno De Medici Secures €100 Million Funding to Strengthen Cartonboard Supply,www.procurementresource.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.procurementresource.com/news-and-articles/reno-de-medici-cartonboard-debt-restructuring-capital,"Reno De Medici Secures €100 Million Funding to Strengthen Cartonboard Supply ... ## Cardboard Buyers Monitor Supply After Producer Recapitalisation ... - The producer is set to receive €100 million in new capital. - The agreement includes a reduction in outstanding bond debt. - Ownership control is expected to change. - Completion is planned for the fourth quarter of 2026. - Buyers should retain approved alternate cartonboard suppliers. ... A financing agreement for one of Europe’s recycled cartonboard producers has reduced immediate concern about supplier stability. Reno De Medici is set to receive €100 million in fresh capital under a transaction that also includes a large reduction in bond debt. Control of the business is expected to move away from the existing owner as part of the agreement. ... The transaction is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2026. Until completion, customers buying recycled cartonboard should continue monitoring the supplier’s financial position, payment terms and operating performance. A binding agreement provides more certainty than an unfinished negotiation, but closing conditions and approvals can still affect the timetable. ... Recycled cartonboard is widely used for folding cartons in food, household products, pharmaceuticals and other consumer markets. A disruption at a large producer could affect board availability, lead times and prices across several packaging grades. The planned capital injection gives the company more financial room to support production, maintenance and customer deliveries. ... The agreement could also influence negotiations. A better-funded producer may have less need to accept heavily discounted orders solely to generate cash. At the same time, the company will need to retain customers during its turnaround, giving established buyers room to negotiate service commitments, lead times and volume flexibility. ... The financing plan improves the supplier’s position, but customers should continue tracking progress through the fourth quarter. Procurement decisions should be based on delivery performance, credit conditions and available alternate capacity."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Dunapack to acquire El Pack corrugated packaging operations in Greece,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/dunapack-acquire-el-pack-greece-corrugated-packaging/,"Dunapack to acquire El Pack corrugated packaging operations in Greece ... Prinzhorn Group company Dunapack Packaging Hellas has agreed to purchase El Pack’s corrugated packaging business in Greece. ... The deal covers facilities in Patras, Kapandriti and Thiva. ... Financial terms of the deal remain undisclosed. ... The transaction is pending regulatory clearance and is due to be completed in the second half of 2026. ... Dunapack Packaging managing director and board member Stanislav Razpopov said: “The acquisition represents an important step in our regional growth strategy. By bringing together local expertise and the capabilities of the Dunapack Packaging network, we are well positioned to create added value for existing and future customers in Greece and neighbouring markets.” ... El Pack’s corrugated packaging activities in Greece employ approximately 250 people and posted turnover of €43m ($48.9m) in 2025. ... Prinzhorn Group CEO Gerald Prinzhorn said:“This acquisition represents another important milestone in strengthening Dunapack Packaging’s presence in Southeast Europe. Greece is an attractive market with significant growth potential, and we are pleased to welcome a strong local partner into the Prinzhorn Group.” ... In April, Dunapack Packaging agreed to acquire Stora Enso’s corrugated packaging businesses in Germany. ... That transaction includes Gaster Wellpappe, Wellpappe Sausenheim and PTI, along with their sites in south-west Germany. ... The German operations employ 350 people and generated €74m in revenue in 2025."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Dunapack to acquire El Pack corrugated packaging operations in Greece,"finance.yahoo.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi Tue, July 28, 2026 at 5:10 AM EDT 1 min read)",2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.yahoo.com/small-business/articles/dunapack-acquire-el-pack-corrugated-091004630.html,"Dunapack to acquire El Pack corrugated packaging operations in Greece ... # Dunapack to acquire El Pack corrugated packaging operations in Greece ... Prinzhorn Group company Dunapack Packaging Hellas has agreed to purchase El Pack's corrugated packaging business in Greece. ... The deal covers facilities in Patras, Kapandriti and Thiva. ... Financial terms of the deal remain undisclosed. ... The transaction is pending regulatory clearance and is due to be completed in the second half of 2026. ... Dunapack Packaging managing director and board member Stanislav Razpopov said: ""The acquisition represents an important step in our regional growth strategy. By bringing together local expertise and the capabilities of the Dunapack Packaging network, we are well positioned to create added value for existing and future customers in Greece and neighbouring markets."" ... El Pack's corrugated packaging activities in Greece employ approximately 250 people and posted turnover of €43m ($48.9m) in 2025. ... Prinzhorn Group CEO Gerald Prinzhorn said:""This acquisition represents another important milestone in strengthening Dunapack Packaging's presence in Southeast Europe. Greece is an attractive market with significant growth potential, and we are pleased to welcome a strong local partner into the Prinzhorn Group."" ... In April, Dunapack Packaging agreed to acquire Stora Enso's corrugated packaging businesses in Germany. ... That transaction includes Gaster Wellpappe, Wellpappe Sausenheim and PTI, along with their sites in south-west Germany. ... The German operations employ 350 people and generated €74m in revenue in 2025."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Vosges. À Arches, NaturNes adapte sa stratégie face à la baisse de la natalité et au recul du marché des aliments pour bébés",www.vosgesmatin.fr (Philippe Nicolle),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.vosgesmatin.fr/economie/2026/07/22/a-arches-naturnes-adapte-sa-strategie-face-a-la-baisse-de-la-natalite-et-au-recul-du-marche-des-aliments-pour-bebes,"Vosges. À Arches, NaturNes adapte sa stratégie face à la baisse de la natalité et au recul du marché des aliments pour bébés ... # Vosges À Arches, NaturNes adapte sa stratégie face à la baisse de la natalité et au recul du marché des aliments pour bébés ... Devenue autonome depuis son rachat par le fonds FNB, l’usine Sitpa NaturNes d’aliments pour bébés, basée à Arches, doit faire preuve d’innovation pour contrer un marché qui se réduit en raison de la baisse de la natalité et du pouvoir d’achat des familles, lesquelles se tournent vers l’alimentation traditionnelle. ... Les nouveaux dirigeants de l’usine Sitpa NaturNes ont diversifié leur gamme de produits pour bébés en lançant notamment des repas conditionnés sous forme d’assiettes pour les enfants de plus de 15 mois. Photo Ph.N. ... On pourrait trouver ça paradoxal, mais les nouveaux propriétaires de l’usine Sitpa NaturNes d’Arches y voient au contraire une source de motivation. Alors qu’ils viennent d’acheter à Nestlé le site vosgien qui fabrique les produits destinés à l’alimentation des bébés, hors lait infantile, ils sont contraints de constater que le marché français des aliments pour les plus jeunes est en..."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Hinojosa regroupe ses activités françaises de carton plat - RIA - L'actualité de l'industrie agroalimentaire,www.ria.fr (Alexandre Couto),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ria.fr/innover/emballages/hinojosa-regroupe-ses-activites-francaises-de-carton-plat/,"Hinojosa regroupe ses activités françaises de carton plat - RIA - L'actualité de l'industrie agroalimentaire ... © Hinojosa Folding Packaging France ; Depuis le 1er juillet 2026, Hinojosa regroupe ses trois sites français de carton plat sous l’identité Hinojosa Folding Packaging France. ... Quelques mois après l’acquisition d’ASV Packaging, le fabricant d’emballages espagnol Hinojosa consolide ses activités françaises dans une nouvelle entité. ... Hinojosa poursuit l’intégration d’ASV Packaging. Depuis le 1er juillet 2026, le groupe espagnol spécialisé dans les solutions d’emballages a réuni sous une même identité ses activités françaises de carton plat, sous le nom de Hinojosa Folding Packaging France. L’ensemble est dirigé par Xavier Freyermuth et réunit les sites CEC Packaging du Mans (Sarthe) et de Valence (Drôme), ainsi que Covepa-Michels à Châteauroux (Indre). Ces unités conçoivent et fabriquent des boîtes pliantes en carton compact imprimé pour les produits agroalimentaires et …"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Duni Group Q2 Profit Falls as Logistics Transition Disrupts Deliveries, Food Packaging Business Posts Growth | Pulp and Paper Chronicle: Daily Pulp and Paper News & Insights",pulpandpaperchronicle.com,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pulpandpaperchronicle.com/duni-group-q2-profit-falls-as-logistics-transition-disrupts-deliveries-food-packaging-business-posts-growth,"Duni Group reported lower sales and earnings for the second quarter of 2026 as the ramp-up of a new external logistics operation in Germany disrupted deliveries, increased costs and weighed on profitability, although its Food Packaging Solutions business continued to grow. ... Net sales for the April–June period declined 3.2% year-on-year to SEK ... 1.823 billion from SEK 1.884 billion. At constant exchange rates, sales were down 2.0%, primarily due to temporarily limited delivery capacity during the transition to the Group's external logistics setup. Operating income fell to SEK 65 million from SEK 121 million, while operating margin narrowed to 3.6% from 6.4%. EBIT decreased to SEK ... 17 million from SEK 103 million, and earnings per share attributable to shareholders fell to SEK -0.44 from SEK ... 1.25. For the first six months of 2026, net sales totaled SEK 3.587 billion, down from SEK 3.747 billion a year earlier, while ... to SEK ... The company said the main factor behind the weaker performance was temporary delivery disruptions during the transition to a new external warehouse in Meppen, Germany. Limited outbound delivery capacity prevented Duni from fully meeting customer demand and led to higher warehousing and transport costs. The quarter was also affected by weaker demand in the Middle East as geopolitical tensions reduced travel and tourism activity. Additional pressure came from higher IT investments, increased energy costs and restructuring expenses related to a new efficiency programme and unused warehouse capacity. ... President and CEO Robert Dackeskog said the logistics transition is a key step toward building a more scalable logistics network but acknowledged that implementation had been more challenging than expected. To stabilize operations, Duni postponed the planned transfer of German market distribution to the new logistics setup. The company said delivery performance improved toward the end of the quarter and during the first days of July, with the financial impact expected to be significantly lower in the third quarter. ... Within the Dining Solutions business area, net sales declined 6.2% at constant exchange rates to SEK 1.045 billion, while operating income dropped to SEK 31 million from SEK 99 million. The business was affected by logistics disruptions across Europe, a weaker product mix with increased sales of lower-margin products, and a sharp decline in Middle East sales. Germany performed comparatively better because distribution there had not yet been transferred to the new logistics network. During the quarter, Duni Lighting Solutions introduced its d.ls brand globally at Milan Design Week and showcased its modular lighting platform at 3daysofdesign in Copenhagen. The company also launched a Carbon Trust-verified carbon calculator for napkins and table covers and received supplier awards from Transgourmet/Prodega. ... The Food Packaging Solutions business delivered stronger performance, with net sales increasing 4.3% at constant exchange rates to SEK 779 million, while operating income rose to SEK 34 million from SEK 22 million. Growth was supported by BioPak Group, recently acquired businesses and improved margins, despite logistics-related challenges in Europe. During the quarter, Duni consolidated newly acquired Solserv Solutions & Services Europe AB, expanded its industrial packaging and service offering, completed the rollout of its packaging portfolio without added PFAS to meet upcoming EU regulatory requirements, launched new recyclable paper-based packaging for sushi, deli and bakery applications, and introduced local composting solutions and reusable packaging at Sweden Rock Festival. ... Financially, Duni reported operating cash flow of SEK -19 million for the first half of the year. The Group entered into a new 15-year lease for its logistics facility in Meppen, increasing interest-bearing net debt to SEK 2.567 billion at the end of June from SEK 1.591 billion at the end of 2025. During the period, the company also secured a new EUR 200 million long-term revolving credit facility and converted an existing SEK 200 million loan into a three-year EUR 25 million facility. ... Duni continued to advance strategic initiatives alongside operational improvements. The company highlighted progress in integrating Solserv, the completion of its transition to packaging without added PFAS, continued expansion of Duni Lighting Solutions, and improvements in sustainability metrics, including a higher share of circular input materials and increased supplier adoption of its Code of Business Conduct. Management said its priorities remain restoring stable delivery performance, improving profitability and cash flow, strengthening competitiveness and continuing long-term growth initiatives."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Cartwright & Butler's Post Box Tin gains momentum in UK travel retail,www.dfnionline.com (Sheena Adesilu),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.dfnionline.com/brand-news/confectionery-fine-foods/cartwright-butlers-post-box-tin-drives-uk-travel-retail-growth-at-avolta-14-07-2026/,"Cartwright & Butler's Post Box Tin gains momentum in UK travel retail # Cartwright & Butler’s Post Box Tin gains momentum in UK travel retail ... By Sheena Adesilu in Airports, Food & Confectionery, Latest News, Retail News July 14, 2026 Comments Off on Cartwright & Butler’s Post Box Tin gains momentum in UK travel retail Destination-inspired biscuit tin becomes brand’s second best-selling 200g product in World Duty Free The Cartwright & Butler Post Box Tin has become the company’s second best-selling 200g biscuit product at Avolta‘s UK World Duty Free stores, one year after its travel retail debut. ... Launched exclusively with Avolta in July 2025, the destination-inspired biscuit tin has helped drive growth for Cartwright & Butler‘s biscuit category while increasing the brand’s visibility and market share across the retailer’s UK estate. ... The launch has been supported by prominent merchandising, including a High-Profile Promotion (HPP) at Heathrow Airport Terminal 3. According to Cartwright & Butler, the activation ranked among the airport’s best-performing HPP sites in 2025 in terms of uplift in the brand’s sales. ... While the Post Box Tin has rolled out across Cartwright & Butler‘s wider retail channels since January 2026, it remains exclusive to Avolta within the global travel retail channel. ... The product is available as a 200g clip-top tin and in a new twin-pack format paired with the brand’s Great Britain Triple Chocolate Chunk Tin. ... Building on the product’s performance, Cartwright & Butler has confirmed six High-Profile Promotions for 2026 across Heathrow Terminals 3 and 5, London Gatwick North and London Stansted."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Canpac acquires Krishna Creation, plans new Ahmedabad plant - THE PACKMAN",thepackman.in,2026-07-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thepackman.in/canpac-acquires-krishna-creation-plans-new-ahmedabad-plant/,"Canpac acquires Krishna Creation, plans new Ahmedabad plant - THE PACKMAN ... Monocartons Canpac acquires Krishna Creation, plans new Ahmedabad plant # Canpac acquires Krishna Creation, plans new Ahmedabad plant - July 11, 2026 # Canpac acquires Krishna Creation, plans new Ahmedabad plant ... - July 11, 2026 ... Canpac has acquired Krishna Creation, an Ahmedabad-based folding carton and rigid box packaging manufacturer, expanding its presence in India’s premium packaging segment. Krishna Creation’s clients include Welspun, Renee Cosmetics, Indocount, Damson, and Trident. ... As part of the transaction, Canpac and Krishna Creation will jointly set up a greenfield plant in Ahmedabad, the company’s 3rd unit in the city and 10th overall in India. The plant, arriving in September 2026, will house a new KBA 106-7 color coater with UV, alongside an existing Komori 6 color UV press and a range of post-press equipment for rigid paper packaging, folding cartons, and gift bags. ... The acquisition extends Canpac’s presence in the specialty, gift, and premium packaging segment. It follows what the company describes as a 15-year expansion from a single plant to ten, and from a regional folding carton player to a diversified packaging platform serving Indian consumer brands. ... This is Canpac’s 5th acquisition. The company states it has grown at a 25% CAGR over the last 15 years, scaling from a single regional operation into one of India’s diversified paper packaging platforms. ... “This partnership brings together Canpac’s operational scale with Krishna Creation’s design and finishing expertise. This is a step towards the premium and luxury segment of packaging in India,” said Sagar Makhija, M&A head, Canpac Trends. ... The two teams will now work together to grow the business, combining Canpac’s scale and process discipline with Krishna Creation’s boutique craftsmanship."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Lordos United agrees €8.16m deal for majority stake in P&S Carton | Cyprus Mail,cyprus-mail.com,2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://cyprus-mail.com/2026/07/10/lordos-united-agrees-e8-16m-deal-for-majority-stake-in-ps-carton,"Lordos United agrees €8.16m deal for majority stake in P&S Carton | Cyprus Mail ... Lordos United Public Ltd announced on Friday that it has signed an agreement to acquire a 51 per cent controlling stake in P&S Carton Industries Ltd for €8.16 million in cash, marking its entry into Cyprus’ corrugated packaging sector. ... The company said the acquisition agreement was signed with the existing shareholders of P&S Carton Industries Ltd, with the transaction subject to regulatory approval from the Commission for the Protection of Competition. ... Lordos United, a Cyprus-registered public company listed on the Cyprus Stock Exchange, said the acquisition aligns with its long-term strategy of sustainable growth, operational excellence and shareholder value creation. ... The company currently operates in the plastics manufacturing and packaging industry, while the acquisition will expand its activities into the corrugated cardboard packaging market. ... The company manufactures and sells corrugated cardboard boxes and packaging solutions, serving customers across a broad range of industries in Cyprus, including the beverage, agriculture, pharmaceutical and consumer goods sectors. ... According to the announcement, P&S Carton Industries is the only domestic manufacturer of corrugated cardboard boxes in Cyprus, supplying approximately 60 per cent of domestic packaging demand, with the remaining demand met through imports. ... has developed over ... past three decades into the ... ’s leading packaging supplier. ... Under the share purchase agreement, Lordos United will acquire 35,700 shares, representing 51 per cent of the company’s share capital, at a price of €228.57 per share. ... Following completion of the transaction, the existing vendors will retain the ... 49 per cent minority stake in ... The board said it considers the acquisition strategically and financially attractive following an internal assessment and advice from an external expert. ... It explained that P&S Carton’s dominant market position was one of the principal reasons behind the acquisition, pointing out that the company operates in a structurally protected market without any significant domestic competition. ... The board also said the transaction would diversify Lordos United’s product portfolio beyond plastics manufacturing by adding corrugated cardboard packaging, thereby reducing concentration risk. ... It added that the cardboard packaging sector is expected to benefit from long-term structural growth, driven by increasing European Union regulatory pressure against single-use plastics. ... The company further stated that P&S Carton’s customer base complements Lordos United’s existing commercial relationships, creating opportunities for cross-selling and the delivery of integrated packaging solutions across the food, agriculture, pharmaceutical and consumer goods sectors. ... In addition, the board pointed to planned investment in new machinery during 2027 and 2028, which is expected to significantly increase production capacity and improve the target company’s cost competitiveness. ... Once completed, the acquisition will see P&S Carton consolidated as a 51 per cent-owned subsidiary in Lordos United’s consolidated financial statements under IFRS 10 Consolidated Financial Statements. ... Based on P&S Carton’s 2025 financial results, the company expects approximately €11,399,764 in annual turnover to be consolidated into the group’s results from the acquisition date, increasing overall revenue. ... Lordos United also estimated that its 51 per cent share of P&S Carton’s EBITDA would amount to approximately €869,248, based on the target company’s 2025 financial performance. ... The company said the final purchase price allocation will be completed within 12 months of the acquisition date. ... It added that P&S Carton’s net assets, estimated at approximately €8,744,749 based on pro forma accounts prepared in April 2026, will also be consolidated into the group’s balance sheet from the acquisition date. ... Completion of the acquisition remains conditional upon approval by the Commission for the Protection of Competition. ... Looking ahead, Lordos United said it expects the transaction to have a positive impact on profitability, reflecting its participation in the target company’s share capital and the anticipated distribution of profits. ... The company added that the investment also marks its entry into a new business segment, creating opportunities for further expansion into related activities. ... and reasonable for ... announcement was approved by the company’s board of directors ... Finally, Lordos United said it will issue a further announcement once the acquisition has been completed."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Woodberry Packaging buys Medica and Curtis,"www.euwid-paper.com (Frauke Schmidt, EUWID)",2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.euwid-paper.com/news/companies/woodberry-packaging-buys-medica-and-curtis-100726/,"Woodberry Packaging buys Medica and Curtis ... Woodberry Packaging Group has acquired UK folding carton manufacturers Medica Packaging and F.G. Curtis, significantly expanding its presence in pharmaceutical, healthcare and personal care packaging. ... The transactions will almost double the size of the group, which will now employ around 650 people compared with roughly 350 staff before the transaction. Combined turnover of the combined businesses will exceed €120m, according to the company. Financial details were not disclosed. ... Medica, based in Crewe, is described as the UK’s largest independent manufacturer of folding cartons for the pharmaceutical industry. The company produces folding cartons and patient information leaflets for pharmaceutical, healthcare and medical technology customers. ... F.G. Curtis, which trades as Curtis Packaging, manufactures folding cartons mainly for the cosmetics and personal care sectors, with additional activities in healthcare packaging. The company has been part of Medica since 2022. ... Dublin-based Woodberry said both businesses would continue to operate under their existing brands and management teams. The company also stressed that existing staff, customer relationships and supplier links would be retained. ... Reelvision, Woodberry’s existing UK business, produces folding cartons, sleeves, wallets and shelf-ready packaging for customers in sectors including pharmaceuticals, healthcare, cosmetics and veterinary products. ... Woodberry Packaging is backed by Dublin-based Woodberry Capital and has expanded through acquisitions in Ireland and the UK in recent years. ... Hinojosa takes full control of French company ASV Packaging Hinojosa takes full control of French company ASV Packaging ... Spanish Hinojosa Packaging Group is continuing its growth path. The company announced it had now taken full control of French folding carton manufacturer ASV Packaging.... ... Mailway acquires Derwent Displays out of administration Mailway acquires Derwent Displays out of administration ... UK packaging and fulfilment company Mailway Packaging Group has acquired the business of point-of-sale display manufacturer Derwent Displays out of administration. The transaction was completed on 9 July, according to Derwent’s joint administrators Ben Fallon and Louise Longley of restructuring firm BTG. Financial..."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Quillan : Ça cartonne, une entreprise qui détonne ! - lindependant.fr",www.lindependant.fr,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lindependant.fr/2026/07/09/quillan-ca-cartonne-une-entreprise-qui-detonne-13462135.php,"entreprise qui dé ... 21 ... Ce mercredi 8 juillet au matin, les adjoints au maire de Quillan, Malika Gimenez et Éric Breton, ont été accueillis au sein de l’entreprise locale Ça Cartonne dans la zone industrielle de la Plaine. Une visite riche en échanges, qui leur a permis d’appréhender le dynamisme et l’innovation de cette structure ancrée dans le territoire. Catherine Brechignac, dirigeante de l’entreprise, a personnellement guidé les élus à travers les ateliers et les espaces de production. Avec passion, elle a présenté l’entreprise qui allie savoir-faire artisanal et engagement local. Spécialisée dans la fabrication de produits scolaires en cartonnage, l’entreprise propose également une large gamme de Publicité sur Lieu de Vente (PLV), de calendriers, et d’autres supports sur mesure. ... Ce qui distingue Ça Cartonne, c’est sa volonté de collaborer avec tous les acteurs du territoire : associations, entreprises, collectivités, particuliers. Une approche inclusive qui renforce les liens entre l’économie locale et les habitants de Quillan et ses alentours. ... Pour Malika Gimenez et Éric Breton, cette immersion était l’occasion de comprendre les enjeux de l’entreprise et de soutenir son développement. ""C’est toujours inspirant de voir des entrepreneurs comme Catherine Brechignac. Leur travail contribue à la vitalité économique de Quillan"", a souligné Éric Breton. ... De son côté, Catherine Brechignac a exprimé sa fierté d’accueillir les élus : ""Nous sommes ravis de partager notre univers avec eux. Leur intérêt pour notre activité est une belle reconnaissance de notre engagement au quotidien"". ... Cette visite pourrait bien marquer le début de nouvelles collaborations entre la mairie et l’entreprise, notamment pour des projets éducatifs ou événementiels. Une chose est sûre, Ça Cartonne a su séduire par la qualité de ses produits et son ancrage territorial."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,TotalEnergies Corbion launches PLA foam grade - IN Food,in-food.co.uk (IN Food Team),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://in-food.co.uk/totalenergies-corbion-launches-pla-foam-grade/,"TotalEnergies Corbion launches PLA foam grade - IN Food ... # TotalEnergies Corbion launches PLA foam grade ... July 9, 2026 ... Foamed food packaging is gaining another lower-carbon material route globally. Luminy FOAM 50F targets fresh food trays, clamshells, bowls, and food service formats. ... - Luminy FOAM 50F is a high melt strength PLA grade for extrusion foamed packaging. - The material is intended to run on existing XPS extrusion lines with limited modification. - Target applications include fresh meat and fish trays, clamshells, bowls, and food service packaging. ... TotalEnergies Corbion has launched Luminy FOAM 50F, a high melt strength PLA grade for extrusion foamed packaging applications including fresh food trays, clamshells, and bowls. ... The sugarcane-based material is being introduced as a lower carbon alternative to conventional extruded polystyrene foam. It is intended to run on existing XPS extrusion lines with comparable throughput and limited modification, giving converters a potential transition route without wholesale replacement of installed equipment. ... Target applications include trays for fresh products such as meat and fish, as well as food service formats where stiffness, cushioning, low density, moisture handling, and forming consistency are important. The company describes the material as biobased, industrially compostable, recyclable, and free from styrene, PFAS, and persistent microplastics. ... Foam packaging is under increasing scrutiny as polystyrene restrictions expand across multiple markets. Food processors and packaging converters have been looking for materials that can match the practicality of XPS while reducing regulatory exposure. Fresh food trays are not passive containers; they protect product presentation, support absorbent pads where required, maintain rigidity, resist cracking, and run through packing systems without excessive rejects. ... The launch sits alongside wider work to find circular or lower impact alternatives for difficult food packaging formats. Tray materials have been pulled in several directions at once, with circular food grade polystyrene development showing how incumbent materials are also being redesigned while newer biobased options move towards production trials. ... Converters also need the economics to work on installed assets. Extrusion lines represent major capital investment, and few packaging producers can justify new equipment for every emerging material. If a PLA foam grade can use current machinery with practical output rates, the barrier to adoption is lower. If it requires slower throughput, tighter process control, or higher scrap rates, the commercial case weakens. ... Food contact status will shape market rollout. Luminy FOAM 50F is available for commercial orders globally and has food contact approvals for the US and South Korea. Use in other markets will depend on the relevant regulatory route and application, with European users needing to consider food contact status, compostability claims, end-of-life infrastructure, and customer requirements around recyclability. ... The strongest opportunity for PLA foam will be in applications where processors and converters need a lower impact alternative without compromising forming and handling. Fresh protein and food service packaging are obvious test areas because they combine regulatory exposure, high material volumes, and demanding performance requirements. ... TotalEnergies Corbion’s launch adds another technical option as polystyrene alternatives move from niche discussion into operational decision-making. The material will now be judged on commercial line performance, food contact compliance, customer acceptance, and whether recovery systems can support the environmental claims attached to the pack."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Wraps et sandwiches, le Gembloutois Nonna va fournir Shell aux Pays-Bas, avec à la clé 25% d'activité en plus - L'Avenir",www.lavenir.net (Vincent Desguin),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lavenir.net/regions/namur/2026/07/09/wraps-et-sandwiches-le-gembloutois-nonna-va-fournir-shell-aux-pays-bas-avec-a-la-cle-25-dactivite-en-plus-AKMLSACWYVAJNGGY5BFTMPU6SE/,"Wraps et sandwiches, le Gembloutois Nonna va fournir Shell aux Pays-Bas, avec à la clé 25% d'activité en plus - L'Avenir ... Wraps et sandwiches, le Gembloutois Nonna va fournir Shell aux Pays-Bas, avec à la clé 25% d'activité en plus ... ## Au bord de la faillite durant le Covid, l'entreprise Nonna, spécialisée dans les sandwichs et autres plats ultrafrais préemballés, s'apprête à signer un contrat d'ampleur. Pendant trois ans, elle fournira ses produits à plus de 200 stations-service Shell aux Pays-Bas. Un contrat qui devrait amener une hausse de 25% des activités. ... Après avoir évité la sortie de route il y a quelques années, Nonna va signer un contrat qui marque une nouvelle étape de son développement. ... Le fabricant gembloutois de snackings ultrafrais préemballés fournira pendant trois ans ses produits aux stations-service Shell aux Pays-Bas. ""Dans un premier temps, nous approvisionnerons quelque 200 stations avant une extension, à terme, à la quasi-totalité du réseau"", souligne Philippe Bodart, CEO de Nonna. ©EDA ... Selon les projections, ce partenariat devrait amener une hausse de 25% du volume d'activités. ... Si Nonna propose une large gamme de produits allant de la salade, aux plats chauds en passant par les baguettes préparées, c'est principalement avec des sandwiches mous, des wraps et des triangles qu'elle va partir à la conquête des estomacs bataves.""Nous sommes en test depuis le début de l'année et les chiffres de vente pour les wraps et triangles sont en augmentation. Nous venons avec une gamme différente, un bon rapport qualité-prix"", se félicite Philippe Bodart qui situe Nonna dans le haut de gamme du préemballé. ... Pour la société namuroise, déjà bien implantée au nord et au sud de la Belgique, cette opération est une belle revanche. Dirigée depuis 2008 par Philippe Bodart, elle a frôlé de peu la faillite il y a quelques années. ""Le Covid a durement touché l'entreprise alors que nous étions en croissance. Nous pouvons considérer que nous avons perdu 60% de notre activité"", rappelle le CEO. Entre 2019 et 2020, le chiffre d'affaires a été divisé par deux, s'établissant à 5,3 millions€, tandis que la trésorerie s'est retrouvée sous extrême tension.""Sans l'intervention de Namur Invest, je ne serais probablement plus là pour en parler. Grâce à leur soutien, à la conversion de prêts en actions, nous avons pu traverser cette période extrêmement compliquée."" ... Depuis sa première intervention en 2010, l'invest namurois est intervenu à une quinzaine de reprises dans le développement de l'entreprise, pour un montant total de 4,8 millions€. ... Si les soutiens financiers ont permis à Nonna de traverser la crise, un contrat d'envergure signé avec Monoprix, enseigne du groupe Casino, a véritablement relancé sa croissance à partir de 2023. ""C'est l'un des rares clients qui nous avons démarché par nous-mêmes, indique Philippe Bodart. Monoprix recherchait une offre premium correspondant à sa stratégie. Nous partageons la même vision d'un produit de qualité. Les volumes réalisés ont été trois fois supérieurs aux prévisions initiales."" ... En quelques années, Monoprix est devenu l'un des principaux clients de Nonna, au même titre que des acteurs tels que Carrefour, Trendy Foods ou encore Delhaize, avec qui la relation commerciale en est à ses débuts. ... En 2025, l'entreprise a réalisé un chiffre d'affaires de 17,5 millions€ et renoué avec les bénéfices. Son site de Gembloux est désormais en mesure de produire entre 30 000 et 50 000 références par jour, selon les saisons. Le contrat conclu avec Shell devrait lui permettre de franchir cette année le cap des 20 millions€ de chiffre d'affaires. ... de qualité… ... Un peu plus de six mois après l'aveu de faillite, c'en est définitivement terminé de Gembl ... .Beer. Faute de reprise, le matériel de la brasserie universitaire va être mis en vente. ... Ces dernières années, le biscuitier-conf ... Clarembeau a multiplié les références au point, dit-il, ""de s'être perdu."" Pour relancer l'activité, il va opérer dans les prochains mois un recentrage stratégique."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Woodberry Packaging acquires two UK packaging businesses,www.packaging-gateway.com (Satarupa Bhowmik),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/woodberry-packaging-acquires-two-uk-packaging-businesses/,"Woodberry Packaging acquires two UK packaging businesses ... The move strengthens Woodberry’s foothold in Europe, expanding its capabilities in pharmaceutical, healthcare and personal care packaging. Credit: SNeG17 / Shutterstock.com. ... Woodberry Packaging has acquired UK packaging manufacturers Medica Packaging and FG Curtis, which trades as Curtis Packaging. ... Financial terms of the deal were not revealed. ... The move strengthens Woodberry’s foothold in Europe, expanding its capabilities in pharmaceutical, healthcare and personal care packaging. ... Both companies will continue trading under their existing brands and management, preserving continuity for staff, customers and suppliers. ... The expanded group employs 650 people across the UK and Ireland and generates combined turnover of more than €120m ($137m). ... Backed by Dublin-based Woodberry Capital, Woodberry Packaging has grown through acquisitions across Ireland and the UK. ... Medica specialises in pharmaceutical and healthcare cartons while Curtis adds expertise in cosmetics and personal care packaging. ... Medica Packaging’s owner Medication Packaging acquired FG Curtis in 2022. ... Alongside Woodberry Packaging’s existing Reelvision site, the deal gives the group three PS 9000-accredited carton sites in the UK, meeting the pharmaceutical industry’s quality standard. Its Irish business, Colorman, is working toward the same accreditation. ... Woodberry Packaging said the enlarged group can act as a single accredited partner for customers while providing the security of supply increasingly required in regulated markets. ... Curtis managing director James Williams said: “Joining the wider Woodberry group gives us the scale and investment to build on that while keeping the service and standards our customers value.”"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,TotalEnergies Corbion commercializes bio-based polystyrene alternative,www.packaginginsights.com (08 Jul 2026),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaginginsights.com/news/bio-based-polystyrene-alternative.html,"# TotalEnergies Corbion commercializes bio-based polystyrene alternative ... - TotalEnergies Corbion has commercialized Luminy Foam 50F, a high melt strength PLA material designed for extrusion foamed packaging applications. - The bio-based material is positioned as a drop-in alternative to XPS for fresh food trays, clamshells, and bowls, with minimal changes needed on existing lines. - The company says the sugarcane-based PLA can reduce carbon footprint by at least 70% compared to XPS foam. ... TotalEnergies Corbion has launched Luminy Foam 50F, a high melt strength polylactic acid (PLA) solution for extrusion foamed packaging applications. The material is developed for use in trays for fresh food products, including fish and meat, as well as for foodservice packaging formats, such as clamshells and bowls. ... Luminy Foam 50F is available for commercial orders globally. The material is approved for food contact applications by the US Food and Drug Administration and in South Korea. While in other countries it can be used for non-food applications, says TotalEnergies Corbion. ... “With polystyrene (PS) bans accelerating, this is one of the first solutions positioned as an industrial-scale replacement, not a niche material,” says Laurent Daligault, global packaging segment leader at TotalEnergies Corbion. ... “Luminy Foam 50F enables converters and brand owners to adopt a drop-in [alternative] to XPS, in terms of processing and product functionality. The sugarcane-based PLA delivers at least a 70% reduction in carbon footprint compared to XPS foam parts. We look forward to supporting our customers globally, commercially, and technically, as they advance their sustainability ambitions.” ... TotalEnergies ... ion says that its Luminy Foam 5 ... F’s high melt strength facilitates stable foam production without requiring additives, chain extenders, or reactive processing. ... TotalEnergies Corbion describes Luminy Foam 50F as engineered to be a drop-in replacement of PS to allow converters to run it on existing XPS extrusion lines with a similar throughput and minimal modification. ... -free material, according to the ... Previously, TotalEnergies Corbion introduced Luminy PLA bags featuring 30% post-industrial recycled content in the outer layer. Last year, it reached a strategic agreement to distribute its Luminy PLA in the Middle East, including in the United Arab Emirates and Saudi Arabia. ... During last year’s UN Global Plastic Treaty negotiations, Thomas Philipon, CEO of TotalEnergies Corbion, spoke to us live from the talks about the company’s objectives, the need to promote bioplastics, and greenwashing."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,French packaging association CAP expects marked business downturn in second half of 2026,"www.euwid-packaging.com (EUWID, Gernsbach, Germany)",2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.euwid-packaging.com/news/markets/french-packaging-association-cap-expects-marked-business-downturn-in-second-half-of-2026-070726/,"French packaging association CAP expects marked business downturn in second half of 2026 ... French manufacturers of cartonboard packaging, cores and paper products anticipate that business conditions will worsen significantly in the second half of 2026. This is one finding of a business survey by the French industry federation Fédération du Cartonnage et des Articles de Papeterie (CAP) that was conducted i... ... UK: solid demand but no turnaround on the cartonboard market UK: solid demand but no turnaround on the cartonboard market ... economic environment and subdued consumer sentiment ... Recovered paper market Poland: moderate price hikes in second half Higher transport costs and periods of stronger demand shaping the market"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Rainmatter leads Rs 40 crore funding in sustainable packaging startup Econovus - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (ET),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/funding/rainmatter-leads-rs-40-crore-funding-in-sustainable-packaging-startup-econovus/articleshow/132236803.cms,"Rainmatter leads Rs 40 crore funding in sustainable packaging startup Econovus - The Economic Times ... Rainmatter leads Rs 40 crore funding in ... Econovus Packaging has secured Rs 40 crore in a funding round led by Rainmatter. This capital will establish a manufacturing facility and a design centre in Pune. The company designs and manufactures sustainable industrial packaging solutions for various sectors. Econovus aims to reduce waste and lower logistics costs for its clients. This funding will also support expansion into Indian and global export markets. ... Sustainable industrial packaging startup Econovus Packaging has raised Rs 40 crore in a funding round led by Rainmatter by Zerodha, with participation from Rockstud Capital. Econovus designs and manufactures industrial packaging solutions for sectors such as automotive, lithium-ion batteries, solar, steel and defence. Its products include UN-certified lithium-ion battery packaging, export packaging and returnable packaging systems that aim to"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Duniform Shifts to Single-Material Packaging to Improve Recyclability - NUFFOODS Spectrum ASIA,nuffoodsspectrum.asia (Shraddha Warde),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://nuffoodsspectrum.asia/2026/07/07/duniform-shifts-to-single-material-packaging-to-improve-recyclability.html,"Duniform Shifts to Single-Material Packaging to Improve Recyclability - NUFFOODS Spectrum ASIA ... #### Duniform Shifts to Single-Material Packaging to Improve Recyclability ... July 7, 2026 | Company News ... The launch is in line with Duni Group’s ambition to contribute to future sustainable and inspiring dining experiences Large parts of the Duniform range for takeaway, ready meals and catering are now… ... The launch is in line with Duni Group’s ambition to contribute to future sustainable and inspiring dining experiences ... Large parts of the Duniform range for takeaway, ready meals and catering are now transitioning to new material solutions that improve recyclability without affecting functionality or use. This marks an important step in Duni Group’s work towards more circular solutions. ... Duni Group, via its brand Duniform, is now implementing mono-material solutions, i.e. products made of one single material across its key product families: Take Away, HMR (ready meals) and Cater Line. By reducing the use of additives and fillers, the material now consists of only pure polypropylene (PP), making the products more compatible with existing recycling systems. ... This transition is part of Duni Group’s long-term efforts to develop packaging designed for recycling and to meet increasing regulatory requirements, including the EU’s upcoming Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR). ... “This is an important step where we significantly improve recyclability at scale, while maintaining the same functionality and quality for our customers. It makes it easy to choose more sustainable alternatives without requiring any changes to operations”, says Marie Davies, Category Manager Trays and Films Duniform. ... The transition does not entail any changes for customers in terms of product design, functionality or article numbers. The products retain the same performance and areas of use, without affecting the customer’s way of working. ... The new solution has now been implemented across all new production, following long-term development focused on combining high functional requirements with improved environmental performance, and is being gradually rolled out to customers. ... By evolving the range towards products made from a single material, Duniform is creating better conditions for efficient sorting and recycling, while also aligning its offering with increasing demands for circular material solutions. ... The launch is in line with Duni Group’s ambition to contribute to future sustainable and inspiring dining experiences. ... #### Duniform Shifts to Single-Material Packaging to Improve Recyclability ... #### Duniform Shifts to Single-Material Packaging to Improve Recyclability ... Jul 07, 2026 | Company News ... 07,"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Le fabricant d'étiquettes et d'étuis haut de gamme Inessens se sécurise - Les Echos,www.lesechos.fr,2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lesechos.fr/pme-regions/occitanie/le-fabricant-detiquettes-et-detuis-haut-de-gamme-inessens-se-securise-2239863,"Le fabricant d'étiquettes et d'étuis haut de gamme Inessens se sécurise - Les Echos ... Les étiquettes pèsent 80 % de l'activité d'Inessens. (Photo Sofilaro x Inessens) ... Publié le 30 juin 2026 à 11:00Mis à jour le 30 juin 2026 à 11:01 ... Le fabricant français d'étiquettes et étuis haut de gamme Inessens, présent sur les marchés des vins et spiritueux, de la cosmétique, de l'agroalimentaire et de la santé, ouvre son capital à hauteur de 20 % au Groupe Crédit Agricole. L'opération, dont le montant n'est pas communiqué, est menée par Sofilaro, IDIA Capital Investissement, Socadif et Sofipaca. Les huit actionnaires historiques, dont certains ont cédé des parts au nouvel entrant, conservent 80 % du capital. L'opération vise à sécuriser les huit dirigeants actionnaires et assurer la pérennité de cette PME audoise de 300 salariés. ... « La valorisation d'Inessens se renforce d'année en année. Il peut arriver malheur à l'un d'entre nous. Dans cette perspective, une trésorerie importante était mise en réserve, pour que les actionnaires puissent racheter les parts de la personne qui viendrait à disparaître, explique Eric Groshens, son président. Immobiliser une grosse somme pour ce motif est un peu ridicule : il est plus utile de la déployer pour acquérir ou se rapprocher de partenaires industriels, investir, innover… »."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Carve-out of MR Cartonnage Numérique’s MR Factory business, a subsidiary of the Diam Group, to Nortier Emballages - Largilliere Finance",largilliere-finance.com,2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://largilliere-finance.com/en/transaction/carve-out-of-mr-cartonnage-numeriques-mr-factory-business-a-subsidiary-of-the-diam-group-to-nortier-emballages/,"Carve-out of MR Cartonnage Numérique’s MR Factory business, a subsidiary of the Diam Group, to Nortier Emballages - Largilliere Finance ... # Carve-out of MR Cartonnage Numérique’s MR Factory business, a subsidiary of the Diam Group, to Nortier Emballages ... ## Advised by Largillière Finance, the sale of MR Factory to Nortier Emballages gives rise to a leading premium packaging company combining digital and offset printing ... Nortier Emballages, a subsidiary of the Firopa Group, has announced the acquisition of MR Factory, the short-run folding carton production business of MR Cartonnage Numérique, a subsidiary of the Diam Group. Advised by Largillière Finance, this transaction brings together two complementary players in the premium packaging market, enabling MR Factory to leverage the expertise of an offset printing specialist to support its clients’ growth, while accelerating Nortier Emballages’ expansion in digital printing. ... Established in 2019, MR Factory is the short-run folding carton production business (runs of fewer than 30,000 units) of MR Cartonnage Numérique, a pioneer in digital printing and a specialist in niche solutions, short production runs and carton mock-ups. Agile and highly responsive, the business has established itself as a leading player in the beauty, luxury and lifestyle markets, serving a client portfolio that includes several Maisons of the LVMH Group, as well as L’Oréal, PUIG and Estée Lauder. ... Nortier Emballages is a leading manufacturer of premium folding cartons for the fragrance, cosmetics, skincare and luxury goods industries. A subsidiary of the Firopa Group, a century-old French family-owned industrial group, Nortier supports brands throughout their product lifecycle through its dual expertise in offset printing for medium and large production runs, and digital printing for short runs. ... This transaction is driven by a shared strategic vision: for the Diam Group, to partner MR Factory with an offset printing specialist capable of supporting its clients’ growth and adapting to evolving market needs; and for Nortier Emballages, to accelerate its expansion in digital printing while broadening its value proposition for its entire client base. The acquisition is further supported by the close proximity of the two production sites, both located in Saint-Ouen-l’Aumône. MR Factory’s operations will be integrated into Nortier’s facility by the end of October 2026, bringing together all of the combined expertise under a single roof. ... This transaction was a natural choice for us. With its digital expertise and complementary industrial capabilities, Nortier Emballages is ideally positioned to support MR Factory's continued growth and drive its development in synergy with its existing operations. We would like to thank Largillière Finance for identifying the best buyer for our employees—one whose profile is perfectly aligned with our values and our commitment to securing their future under the best possible conditions. ... This acquisition is a perfect fit with our strategy to expand our digital printing capabilities, enabling us to serve our clients even better with an even stronger offering. We are also delighted to welcome MR Factory's 24 employees to the Nortier family. ... We are proud to have advised on this strategic transaction for MR Factory and all of its stakeholders. Our deep understanding of the packaging ecosystem serving the beauty and luxury industries enabled us to identify Nortier Emballages as a highly relevant partner, perfectly aligned with the sellers' objectives: complementary technologies, business continuity, and the ability to provide the teams with sustainable long-term growth opportunities."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Carve-out de l'activité MR Factory de MR Cartonnage Numérique, filiale du Groupe Diam, à Nortier Emballages - Largillière Finance",largilliere-finance.com,2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://largilliere-finance.com/transaction/cession-de-mr-factory-a-nortier-emballages/,"Carve-out de l'activité MR Factory de MR Cartonnage Numérique, filiale du Groupe Diam, à Nortier Emballages - Largillière Finance ... # Carve-out de l'activité MR Factory de MR Cartonnage Numérique, filiale du Groupe Diam, à Nortier Emballages ... ## Conseillée par Largillière Finance, la cession de MR Factory à Nortier Emballages donne naissance à un acteur de référence du packaging premium alliant impression numérique et offset ... Nortier Emballages, filiale du Groupe Firopa, a annoncé l’acquisition de MR Factory, site de production d’étuis cartons en petites séries de MR Cartonnage Numérique, filiale du Groupe Diam. Accompagnée par Largillière Finance, cette opération unit deux acteurs complémentaires du packaging premium et permet à MR Factory de s’adosser à un spécialiste de l’offset pour accompagner la croissance de ses clients, tout en accélérant le développement de Nortier dans l’impression numérique. ... Lancée en 2019, MR Factory est l’unité de production d’étuis cartons en petites séries (moins de 30 000 exemplaires) de MR Cartonnage Numérique – pionnière en impression numérique et spécialiste des solutions de niche, des petites séries et maquettes cartons. L’activité, agile et rapide, s’est imposée comme la référence pour les marchés de la beauté, du luxe et du lifestyle, avec un portefeuille clients comprenant notamment plusieurs Maisons des Groupes LVMH, L’Oréal, PUIG, Estée Lauder. ... Nortier Emballages est un acteur majeur de l’étui carton pliant haut-de-gamme pour les secteurs de la parfumerie, de la cosmétique, des soins et des objets de luxe. Filiale du Groupe Firopa, groupe industriel familial français centenaire, Nortier accompagne les marques tout au long de leur cycle de vie, grâce à sa double expertise en impression offset, pour les moyennes et grandes séries, et en impression numérique, pour les petites séries. ... Ce rapprochement repose sur une double volonté : celle du Groupe Diam d’adosser MR Factory à un spécialiste de l’offset pour pouvoir accompagner la croissance de ses clients ainsi que les évolutions du marché, et celle de Nortier d’accélérer son développement dans le numérique et d’élargir sa proposition de valeur pour l’ensemble de ses clients. Cette acquisition est également facilitée par la proximité géographique des deux sites industriels, situés à Saint-Ouen-l’Aumône. L’activité MR Factory sera intégrée au site de Nortier d’ici fin octobre 2026, afin de regrouper l’ensemble des expertises sur un même site. ... Cette transmission nous apparaît comme une évidence : grâce à ses expertises digitales et à ses capacités industrielles complémentaires, Nortier Emballages pourra accompagner le développement de MR Factory et poursuivre son évolution en synergie avec ses activités existantes. Nous tenons à remercier Largillière Finance, qui a su trouver le meilleur repreneur pour nos collaborateurs, en parfaite adéquation avec nos valeurs et notre volonté d’assurer leur avenir dans les meilleures conditions. ... Cette acquisition concrétise idéalement notre stratégie de développement dans le numérique, pour toujours mieux servir nos clients avec une offre encore plus robuste. Nous nous réjouissons également d’accueillir les 24 collaborateurs de MR Factory, qui vont agrandir la famille Nortier. ... Nous sommes fiers d’avoir accompagné cette opération stratégique pour MR Factory et l’ensemble de ses parties prenantes. Notre connaissance fine de l’écosystème du packaging pour les secteurs de la beauté et du luxe nous a permis d’identifier en Nortier Emballages un partenaire particulièrement pertinent, en parfaite adéquation avec les objectifs des cédants : complémentarité des technologies, continuité de l’activité et offrir des perspectives de développement durables aux équipes."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Jealsa And Tetra Pak Introduce Paper-Based Alternative To Traditional Tuna Cans | Packaging Reporter,packagingreporter.com (Packaging Reporter),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://packagingreporter.com/food-beverage/jealsa-and-tetra-pak-introduce-paper-based-alternative-to-traditional-tuna-cans/,"Tetra Pak has introduced what it describes as the industry’s first carton packaging solution for shelf-stable tuna, marking a new development in the transition towards paper-based alternatives in the canned seafood sector. ... The launch was achieved in collaboration with Spanish seafood producer Jealsa, which served as the industrial partner throughout the development, validation and commercialisation process. Jealsa supplied the tuna product, contributed to packaging development and conducted testing under real production and market conditions. ... The product is packaged in Tetra Pak’s Tetra Recart® format and was launched in Sweden last month through retailer Axfood in a 200 ml mini pack format. ... According to Tetra Pak, the new packaging offers a substantially lower environmental footprint compared with traditional packaging formats. The company states that Tetra Recart has an 85% lower carbon footprint than steel cans and an 83% lower carbon footprint than glass jars. The package also contains up to 71% FSC™-certified paper. ... “With the industry’s first carton packaging for shelf-stable tuna in Tetra Recart, we are giving producers and brands a new way to stand out on the shelf, protect and grow their market share, modernize with a paper-based alternative to cans, and contribute to more sustainable food systems,” said Tatiana Liceti, Executive Vice President of Packaging Solutions at Tetra Pak. ... project combines new packaging technology with its expertise in seafood processing. ... “Thanks to our collaboration with Tetra Pak, we have brought to market an innovative solution that combines modern packaging formats with our long-standing expertise in seafood products,” said Jesús M. Alonso Escurís, President of Jealsa. ... Beyond sustainability considerations, Tetra Pak highlighted operational advantages associated with the carton format. The rectangular shape of Tetra Recart is designed to improve storage efficiency and simplify pick-and-pack operations, making it particularly suitable for e-commerce fulfilment, home delivery services and meal kit applications. ... The launch represents another step in the expansion of carton-based packaging into food categories traditionally dominated by metal cans and glass containers, as packaging suppliers and food manufacturers seek alternatives that combine product protection, logistics efficiency and reduced environmental impact."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Sealed Air and Yangi: Fiber trays & flexibles reshape protein packs amid regulatory pressures,www.packaginginsights.com (24 Jun 2026 | By Libby Davis),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaginginsights.com/news/protein-packaging-sustainable-redesign.html,"# Sealed Air and Yangi: Fiber trays & flexibles reshape protein packs amid regulatory pressures ... - Sealed Air and Yangi say protein packaging innovation is shifting toward formats that combine sustainability, barrier performance, affordability, and industrial scalability. - Fiber-based trays, including Yangi’s dry-formed Cellera range, are gaining momentum as brands seek alternatives that can perform in fresh protein applications. - Flexible high-barrier formats and stand-up pouches are reshaping meat and plant-based protein packaging. ... Innova Market Insights’ data reveals a 2% increase in meat and dairy launches globally between April 2021 and March 2026, with Europe leading the launches. Regulatory requirements and high raw material costs are shaping protein packaging decisions. ... Samantha Murphy, strategic marketing manager EMEA, at Sealed Air, says: “Regulatory requirements, like the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR), and consumer demand for more eco-conscious products, are driving strong interest in sustainable protein packaging innovations.” ... “However, demand is being held back by rising operating costs and tighter margins. The challenge when it comes to changing packaging is managing the impact on retail selling prices, especially in price-sensitive markets where raw material prices are high and volatile.” ... Yangi and Sealed Air say they aim to strike a balance between affordability, shelf life, sustainability, and consumer convenience. This can often involve trade-offs, with 69% of consumers globally saying that packaging is important when they buy meat products, according to Innova Market Insights. ... For Yangi, protein packaging innovation is linked to the rise of fiber-based packaging. Rüdel says that fiber-based options have been discussed for years, with early iterations featuring laminated paperboard. ... Yangi’s Cellera range features dry-formed fiber and combines airlaid fiber technology with 3D thermoforming, eliminating the wet pulp stage.According to Innova Market Insights, there was a 139% CAGR growth in molded fiber packaging launches for meat, meat and dairy, and their alternatives globally from April 2021 to March 2026. ... Rüdel explains that the emergence of fiber-based tray solutions compatible with modified atmospheric packaging for fresh protein products highlights how the industry has “moved beyond” material substitution toward “formats that can carry the full performance burden of the plastic tray.” ... Innova Market Insights data says that plastic was the most used material in protein packaging launches globally from April 2025 to March 2026, with 55%, followed by carton at 20% and cardboard at 6%. ... Sealed Air’s Murphy says that a “quite monumentous” shift in the protein packaging category at the moment is the move away from the tray-and-lid system. ... Murphy says a “monumentous” shift in protein packaging is the move away from tray-and-lid systems.“We’re increasingly working with retailers and processors to replace this long-standing packaging system with Cryovac brand MonoPP Flowpack, a range of flexible, high-barrier rollstock and films, which are certified as recyclable by Cyclos-HTP Institute.” ... Innova Market Insights’ data explores protein packaging formats, finding that standard trays lead protein product launches globally between April 2025 and March 2026, with flat pouches coming in second. ... Murphy continues: “Tray-and-lid systems in fresh meat have been around for about four to five decades, and have stood the test of time because of their structural integrity. We’re now seeing growing demand to eliminate trays to support regulatory compliance, reduce costs, and use less packaging.” ... She gives the example of the UK’s packaging EPR, which applies fees according to material type and weight. In this case, “it can make huge commercial sense to remove rigid plastic trays from fresh meat packaging.” ... “Similarly, reducing overall pack size by replacing a tray with a flexible, high-barrier film may support future compliance with the PPWR in the EU.” ... Innova Market Insights’ data corroborates this, revealing that between April 2021 and March 2026, there was a 43% CAGR growth in cup packaging for F&B launches globally. ... segment that is also ... is the rise of plant-based protein products, which often require different protection, design, and branding requirements. ... Murphy says that in plant-based protein, there is “strong usage” of stand-up pouches.Murphy says that in plant-based protein, there is “strong usage” of stand-up pouches. She observes that adoption of this form is “more advanced” in the plant-based category than in fresh meat or dairy protein products. ... “The versatility of stand-up pouches suits a lot of the ‘ready to cook’ formats seen across plant-based proteins, while clear windows in pouches can also enable brands to showcase product quality.” ... “Cutting-edge digital printing enables the easy, high-quality branding of pouches, which helps capture consumer attention. This can deliver a competitive edge in the plant-based proteins category, which is busy with pioneering new entrants and established brands that are prioritizing innovation to win market share.” ... Meanwhile, she highlights how animal protein brands have also built their branding around these requirements, but with cost efficiency and high barrier performance as the primary commercial drivers. ... Rüdel points toward plant-based protein packagings’ emphasis on design and brand storytelling, noting a convergence of animal and plant-based protein packaging.“Both of those positions are under pressure today, from opposite directions. Plant-based brands are grappling with the commercial realities of mainstream distribution; packaging economics, barrier performance, and supply chain compatibility need to match the demands of high-volume retail without requiring consumers to make trade-offs.” ... The result, Rüdel argues, is a convergence. “The distinction that is emerging is less about protein source and more about where a product sits on the premium-to-value spectrum, and whether it is fresh, chilled, or shelf-stable.” ... “Those variables drive packaging requirements more meaningfully than plant-based versus animal-based at this"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Pontarlier. Des dosettes Ricoré solidaires produites chez Nestlé à Pontarlier,www.estrepublicain.fr (Benoît Caurette),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.estrepublicain.fr/economie/2026/06/23/des-dosettes-ricore-solidaires-produites-chez-nestle-a-pontarlier,"L’usine Nestlé de Pontarlier produit depuis lundi 22 juin, en partenariat avec Café Joyeux, une nouvelle gamme de dosettes. 35 tonnes de « Sticks Ricoré Joyeux » doivent en sortir d’ici à la fin de l’année prochaine. Pendant un an et demi, l’entreprise solidaire, qui veut les mettre à la carte de ses restaurants, en tirera 100 % des bénéfices. ... L’ami du petit-déjeuner « servi avec le cœur ». Voici l’ambition du nouveau produit qui sort depuis lundi 22 juin de l’une des quatre lignes de l’usine Nestlé de Pontarlier. Au rythme possible de vingt palettes par jour, l’iconique Ricoré se décline désormais en stick estampillé « Café Joyeux ». ... Le géant agroalimentaire renforce son partenariat avec la marque solidaire née à Rennes en 2017 et spécialisée dans l’inclusion durable des personnes souffrant de handicap (elle en emploie plus de deux cents en CDI). ... « L’an dernier, nous avions expérimenté pendant six mois une première édition spéciale : la poudre dans son contenant traditionnel, qui nous encourage à poursuivre sur notre lancée », savoure Alisée Hauss, responsable marketing Ricoré. Diffusée exclusivement chez Carrefour, la boîte produite à Dieppe (Normandie), sans alors l’intervention de l’entité pontissalienne, s’était écoulée à 225 000 exemplaires, soit 24 tonnes de produit, dont l’intégralité des profits avait été reversée à Café Joyeux. ... Virage stratégique avec la version dosettes, qui répond d’autant mieux aux attentes du partenaire. En plus d’en récolter 100 % des bénéfices jusqu’en fin d’année prochaine, l’entreprise profite de l’aubaine pour mettre facilement - et avec une identité forte - la Ricoré à la carte de ses trente-cinq cafés-restaurants. ... « Une demande de nos clients », glisse Claire Faure-Miller, directrice générale de Café Joyeux. Le mélange de café et de chicorée est de nouveau en vogue, y compris auprès des jeunes publics, qui le réclament dans les coffee-shops. « Même s’il accompagne encore 250 millions de petits-déjeuners par an, contextualise Patrice Grèze, directeur général de la catégorie « café » chez Nestlé. Les amateurs en boivent en moyenne trois tasses par jour. ... L’entreprise rennaise a beau connaître une forte popularité et un chiffre d’affaires honorable sur l’ensemble de ses activités (25 millions d’euros), « les bars-restaurants sont en perte, admet Claire Faure-Miller. Chez nous, la masse salariale représente 65 % quand elle n’est que de 25 % chez Starbucks. L’entreprise est tout juste à l’équilibre. Nous y parvenons grâce à la vente de notre marque de café et à des partenariats comme celui-ci. » ... Nestlé travaille ici son engagement sociétal et pose des billes. « Nous visons une production de 35 tonnes l’année prochaine, détaille Alisée Hauss. Un élargissement de notre distribution à cinq enseignes à partir de juillet et peut-être un renforcement sur le marché des restaurants, où nous sommes peu présents. » ... Connue pour sa fabrication de Nesquik, l’usine de Pontarlier (260 salariés) est parée pour le défi de ce conditionnement amené à se pérenniser : « Depuis 1998, c’est aussi notre savoir-faire », rappelle Céline Coste, la directrice. Tous produits confondus, elle fabrique 3,3 millions de sticks par jour."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Altago acquiert la société L'Hexagone | Food Process & Packaging Automation | France,foodpackautomation.fr,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,"https://foodpackautomation.fr/news/112103-altago-acquiert-la-soci%C3%A9t%C3%A9-l-hexagone-%0D%0Agroupe-altago-a-annonc%C3%A9-l-acquisition-de-l-entreprise-l-hexagone,-sp%C3%A9cialis%C3%A9e-dans-la-fabrication-de-carton-alv%C3%A9olaire","Altago acquiert la société L'Hexagone | Food Process & Packaging Automation | France 22 {{ ""2026-06-22T00:00:00+00:00"" | date ""MMM"" }} '26 # Altago acquiert la société L'Hexagone ... ## Groupe Altago a annoncé l'acquisition de l'entreprise L'Hexagone, spécialisée dans la fabrication de carton alvéolaire. ##### groupealtago.com ... Site de production de carton de la société L'Hexagone. Cette opération de croissance externe intervient après le changement de dénomination du groupe survenu en octobre 2025 et l'intégration de CPL-OP Emballages au cours de la même année. Extension de l'infrastructure industrielle Fondée en 1975 et implantée à La Guerche-de-Bretagne (Ille-et-Vilaine), L'Hexagone emploie 59 collaborateurs et enregistre un chiffre d'affaires de 13,6 millions d'euros, dont 29 % sont réalisés à l'exportation. Son directeur, Gilles Latil, en fonction depuis 2016 et membre du comité exécutif de l'EMPHA depuis 2017, a notamment encadré la construction d'une nouvelle usine de production en 2021. La transaction englobe également l'entité L'Hexagone 64 (anciennement Corint Sud), située à proximité de la frontière espagnole. Ce double ancrage géographique permet au repreneur d'étendre son réseau de distribution en Europe de l'Ouest, sur une zone couvrant le Benelux et la péninsule ibérique. Le portefeuille de clients de l'entreprise acquise comprend des acteurs industriels et commerciaux tels que BSH, Danfoss, la DGA, Ikea et Saint-Gobain. Positionnement et structure d'Altago Le Groupe Altago, fondé par Bertrand Bulteau, est une structure à l'actionnariat 100 % familial affichant un chiffre d'affaires de 242 millions d'euros pour un effectif de 800 collaborateurs. Son modèle économique intègre l'ensemble de la chaîne de valeur de l'emballage en tant que fabricant, transformateur et distributeur. L'organisation repose sur un réseau de 18 entités réparties en quatre pôles d'activité : le carton, le papier, l'extrusion de films techniques et la distribution. Les implantations industrielles et commerciales du groupe sont situées en France (métropole et Dom-Tom), en Belgique ainsi qu'en Espagne. L'intégration de L'Hexagone vise à développer les capacités de production et les synergies techniques au sein de son pôle carton, sur un marché de l'emballage industriel marqué par le remplacement des matériaux synthétiques de calage en réponse aux évolutions réglementaires sur le plastique. Publié par Youssef Belgnaoui, rédacteur pour Induportals. www.groupealtago.com"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Emballages : le groupe Altago se renforce dans le carton alvéolaire - Les Echos,www.lesechos.fr,2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lesechos.fr/pme-regions/hauts-de-france/emballages-le-groupe-altago-se-renforce-dans-le-carton-alveolaire-2237229,"Emballages : le groupe Altago se renforce dans le carton alvéolaire - Les Echos ... L'entreprise L'Hexagone, avec ses 59 salariés et un chiffre d'affaires de 13,6 millions d'euros, vient compléter les activités d'Altago, qui a réalisé 242 millions d'euros en 2022. (Photo Altago) ... Avec l'acquisition en décembre dernier - mais révélée seulement aujourd'hui - de L'Hexagone, basé à La Guerche-de-Bretagne, en Ille-et-Vilaine, le spécialiste de l'emballage Altago (ex-Bulteau Développement) renforce son pôle carton alvéolaire. Celui-ci comptait déjà la société Corint Sud, spécialiste du carton nid d'abeille, installé à Orthez (Pyrénées-Atlantiques), rebaptisé depuis L'Hexagone 64. ... Installé à Wambrechies (Nord), près de Lille, et organisé en quatre pôles complémentaires - carton, papier, extrusion de films techniques et distribution -, Altago a réalisé l'an dernier un chiffre d'affaires de 242 millions d'euros, en hausse de 11 %, avec 800 salariés. Avec 59 salariés, L'Hexagone renforce le groupe de 13,6 millions d'euros, dont 29 % à l'export. ... ### Emballages : le groupe Altago se renforce dans le carton alvéolaire ... Emballages : le groupe Altago se renforce dans le carton alvéolaire"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Lagarde becomes President of Carton Ondulé de France - packaging journal,packaging-journal.de,2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://packaging-journal.de/en/lagarde-becomes-the-president-of-corrugated-cardboard-of-france/,"Lagarde becomes President of Carton Ondulé de France - packaging journal ... # Lagarde becomes President of Carton Ondulé de France The former Smurfit Kappa manager succeeds Philippe Durand. ... The French industry association Carton Ondulé de France (COF) has elected Dominique Lagarde as its new president. He will take office for a two-year term, succeeding Philippe Durand, who has led the association since 2020. According to the association, Durand particularly strengthened the political visibility of the corrugated board industry and represented its interests in national and European regulatory debates. ... With the election of Lagarde, Carton Ondulé de France intends to further expand its activities in an environment of regulatory changes. The association announced that it will continue to advocate for reliable framework conditions for the industry, highlight the environmental benefits of corrugated cardboard, and underscore the sector's importance to the French economy. ... Lagarde has over 35 years of experience in the corrugated board industry. After roles at Socar, he moved to Smurfit Kappa in 1998. There, he held various management positions, including head of the French carton division from 2016 to 2022. Subsequently, until 2025, he was responsible for the industrial activities of Smurfit Westrock in France. ... > „It is with pride that I take over the presidency of Carton Ondulé de France. I would like to acknowledge the remarkable work of Philippe Durand, who has significantly strengthened the association's political visibility. Our sector possesses considerable strengths: a high-performing industry, recognised expertise, and a material that fully meets today's environmental requirements. However, like all industrial sectors, we wish for greater recognition from political decision-makers, with whom we must work together to create a more favourable regulatory environment for growth and employment. My aim is to strengthen our collective influence so that our companies can combine environmental requirements with industrial performance.“ ... Carton Ondulé de France states it represents more than 70 percent of the French corrugated board industry. The sector employs around 14,955 staff at more than 80 production sites and achieved revenues of 3.4 billion euros in 2025. Production stood at approximately 2.5 million tonnes of corrugated board. Furthermore, the association highlights a recycling rate of 97 percent and a proportion of 90 percent recycled fibres in material usage."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Green light for Dunapack’s takeover of Stora Enso plants,"www.euwid-paper.com (EUWID, Gernsbach, Germany)",2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.euwid-paper.com/news/companies/green-light-for-dunapacks-takeover-of-stora-enso-plants-100626/,"Green light for Dunapack’s takeover of Stora Enso plants ... On 2 June 2026, the German cartel office has given green light to Dunapack Packaging’s proposed acquisition of Stora Enso’s German corrugated packaging plants. The transaction comprises Gaster Wellpappe, Wellpappe Sausenheim and PTI, with around 350 employees and sales of €74m. Duna... ... Altago acquires honeycomb board specialist ... French packaging group Altago has acquired L’Hexagone, a leading French manufacturer of honeycomb cardboard packaging solutions, as part of its external growth strategy. The transaction strengthens Altago’s position in industrial packaging and creates what the company describes as the first multi-site honeycomb board... ... JH Holding GmbH, owner of Germany’s corrugated case material and corrugated board manufacturer Progroup AG, is taking minority stakes in two corrugated packaging firms as part of its efforts to provide financial support for independent family-owned companies in the packaging industry. As of January, the holding became... ... Antalis expands packaging offer, buys Hein Verpackungen Antalis expands packaging offer, buys Hein Verpackungen ... Packaging and paper merchant Antalis has acquired Hein Verpackungen, a German producer of corrugated packaging and point-of-sale solutions. This move is aimed at strengthening the company’s footprint in the European packaging market. Hein Verpackungen employs 50 people and generated sales of €8m in 2025. The company..."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,MR Factory (MR Cartonnage Numérique) rejoint Nortier Emballages - Caractère,caractere.net,2026-06-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://caractere.net/breve/mr-factory-mr-cartonnage-numerique-rejoint-nortier-emballages/,"MR Factory (MR Cartonnage Numérique) rejoint Nortier Emballages - Caractère ... # MR Factory (MR Cartonnage Numérique) rejoint Nortier Emballages ... - Publié le 8 juin 2026 - Emballage & étiquette ... Nortier Emballages (groupe Firopa) a finalisé, le 1er juin 2026, l’acquisition MR Factory, branche de MR Cartonnage numérique, spécialisée dans les petites séries d’étuis pliants haut de gamme imprimés en numérique. Basé à Saint-Ouen-l’Aumône (95), tout comme MR Cartonnage Numérique, Nortier Emballages est un acteur historique de l’étui carton pliant destiné aux secteurs de la […]"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Technicarton acquires Cartec – ThePackagingPortal.com,www.thepackagingportal.com,2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thepackagingportal.com/industry-news/technicarton-acquires-cartec/,"Technicarton acquires Cartec – ThePackagingPortal.com ... # Technicarton acquires Cartec ... France-based Technicarton has confirmed it has recently completed the acquisition of Cartec, the French manufacturer of corrugated converting and peripheral equipment, based in Chasse-sur-Rhône. ... “With this move, we continued the strong trajectory that reflects the ongoing evolution of a growing family business, which is strengthening and adapting without losing its DNA,” explains Thomas Poncet, Managing Director, Technicarton. “As a business, Technicarton is now enhancing its presence, expanding the scope of operations and confirming our ongoing commitment to long-term investment in tools, skills and production capacity.” ... The strategic acquisition also helps ensure continuity of service for customers of Cartec. This is achieved by way of: ... - Ongoing availability of spare parts; - Mechanical, electronic and automation maintenance, provided by industry-specific mechanics and automation engineer. ... Poncet concludes, “By joining a well-structured and high-performing group, Cartec’s customers now benefit from a significantly stronger industrial base, which affords increased production capacity and greater access to innovative technical solutions. We are excited by the opportunities ahead!”"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,CAP survey: confidence among cardboard industry leaders falls sharply in 2026,www.printindustry.news (Faustine Loison),2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.printindustry.news/story/52042/cap-survey-confidence-among-cardboard-industry-leaders-falls-sharply-in-2026,"cardboard industry leaders ... # CAP survey: confidence among cardboard industry leaders falls sharply in 2026 ... ## Concern is spreading among cardboard and stationery manufacturers. A survey carried out by CAP shows a clear drop in confidence among managers, faced with rising costs, logistical tensions and an unfavorable outlook for the second half of 2026. ... Faustine Loison Published on June 5, 2026 ... Managers in the cardboard and stationery industry are anticipating a difficult second half-year. This is the main finding of a survey conducted by the Fédération française du cartonnage et des articles de papeterie (CAP) among 30 managers of member companies between May 5 and 22, 2026, with the support of the Confédération des petites et moyennes entreprises (CPME). ... The first sign of this deterioration is the sharp drop in manufacturers' confidence levels. In the first half of the year, 40% of managers surveyed indicated that their company's overall situation had deteriorated. ... ""The outlook for the second half of the year shows no sign of improvement: sales remain on a downward trend, cash flow is coming under severe pressure and the workforce continues to erode"" says CAP. ... The crisis in the Middle East is one of the main warning signs identified by the survey. According to the survey, 97% of respondents feel that their business has already suffered its consequences. ... Tensions are having a direct impact on purchasing. Seven out of ten executives report an increase in raw materials procurement costs of between 5% and 20%. Fuel prices are also affected. One company manager in two reports a price increase of over 20%. ... For the federation, which represents 300 companies including 120 members, ""rising raw material supply costs and volatile energy prices are weighing heavily on the economic equilibrium of companies in the sector"" . ... Logistical disruptions also remain a source of fragility. One manager in two says he has experienced supply difficulties that have had a concrete impact on his site's operations. ... In the most severe cases, 3% of respondents said they had experienced supply disruptions leading to partial or total shutdown of their business. ... Faced with these difficulties, manufacturers are seeking to strengthen their resilience. According to the survey, 70% of companies have already initiated or are planning corrective measures. ... The responses envisaged combine short-term actions, such as postponing investments or renegotiating supplier contracts, with more structural measures such as diversifying sources of supply or prospecting for new markets."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Nortier Emballages takes over MR Factory,www.printindustry.news (Faustine Loison),2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.printindustry.news/story/52032/nortier-emballages-takes-over-mr-factory,"Nortier Em ... takes over MR Factory ... # Nortier Emballages takes over MR Factory ... ## With the announced transfer of MR Factory to the Nortier site by the end of October, the operation reorganizes the activities of the two companies: Nortier expands its offer in small digital series, and MR Cartonnage Numérique returns to its historic businesses. ... A new chapter begins for MR Factory. As of June 1, the digital production of small series has been taken over by Nortier Emballages, headed by Benoit Boulet. ... MR Factory was launched in 2019 by Jonathan Mihy as part of MR Cartonnage Numérique, a subsidiary of the Diam International group. Based in Saint-Ouen-l'Aumône with its 24 employees, MR Factory produces high-end digital boxes. ... With this acquisition, Nortier Emballages, which specializes in folding cartons for the perfume, cosmetics, skincare and luxury goods markets, aims to ""accelerate its development in the digital sector and ""expand its value proposition for all its customers"" . ... MR Factory's operations will be relocated to the Nortier site by the end of October. The move is facilitated by the geographical proximity of Nortier and MR Factory, both located in the Val-d'Oise, less than three kilometers away. ... The sale also marks a change of direction for MR Cartonnage Numérique. In a message addressed to its customers, the company explains that it intends to concentrate its resources on its core business of industrial models and artworks. ... It is also strengthening its presence in the United States in these activities. MR Factory's current projects are to be gradually transferred between May and July to ensure continuity of production and commercial relations."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Altago strengthens its cardboard division with the acquisition of L'Hexagone,www.printindustry.news (Faustine Loison),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.printindustry.news/story/51996/altago-strengthens-its-cardboard-division-with-the-acquisition-of-lhexagone,"Altago strengthens its cardboard division with the acquisition of L'Hexagone ... # Altago strengthens its cardboard division with the acquisition of L'Hexagone ... ## The acquisition gives the group an additional industrial presence between Brittany and the Spanish border, as well as a portfolio of customers including Ikea, Saint-Gobain, BSH and Danfoss. ... Altago continues to make acquisitions. After CPL-OP Emballages in 2025 the packaging manufacturer takes over L'Hexagone, specialized in honeycomb cardboard. This operation strengthens the cartonboard business of the group, which is managed from Wambrechies in the Nord region of France, and which now comprises 18 companies and 800 employees, with sales of 242 million euros by 2025 in four business segments. ... L'Hexagone, a manufacturer of honeycomb cardboard based in La Guerche-de-Bretagne in Ille-et-Vilaine, employs 59 people at two production sites: Ille-et-Vilaine and L'Hexagone 64, formerly Corint Sud, located near the Spanish border. The company generated sales of 13.6 million euros, 29% of which were exported. It works for some 380 industrial and logistics customers, including BSH, Danfoss, Ikea, Saint-Gobain and the French Defence Procurement Agency. ... Since 2016, L'Hexagone has been headed by Gilles Latil. The CEO, who is also a member of the executive committee of the European Manufacturers Paper Honeycomb Association (EMPHA), the European association of honeycomb paperboard manufacturers, notably steered the construction of the new Breton plant due to come on stream in 2021. ... ""Joining the Altago group means having the resources to take a new European step forward in a market we know intimately and whose considerable growth potential we measure every day"", says Gilles Latil. ... Alveolar board is one of the most active markets in industrial packaging, driven in particular by the reduction in the use of plastic and the replacement of synthetic cushioning materials, according to the Group. ... ""Hexagone embodies our vision"" adds Altago CEO Hervé Marchand. ""The Altago Group is not just a new banner. It's an industrial and societal project: consolidating a growing group, developing our synergies and supporting our customers in the transition to high-performance, sustainable packaging."" ... In October 2025, the family group founded by Bertrand Bulteau, Bulteau Développement, opted for the name Altago""asserts an identity that matches its ambitions"" and ""embodies a unique model in France: manufacturer, converter and distributor of packaging"", he reminds ."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Emballage Digest,www.emballagedigest.fr (Karine Duval),2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.emballagedigest.fr/en/latelier-des-producteurs-securise-lapprovisionnement-de-ses-legumes-avec-ipp/,"# L’Atelier des Producteurs sécurise l’approvisionnement de ses légumes avec IPP ... posted Tuesday 26 May 2026 ... Basée à Liposthey, dans le Sud-Ouest, l’usine de conditionnement de légumes landaise – filiale des Fermes Larrère – confie la gestion de ses palettes bois à l’acteur européen IPP. Chaque année, 115 000 mouvements de palettes sont réalisés depuis la station de lavage et de conditionnement semi-automatisée vers les enseignes de la grande distribution. ... Selon les prévisions d’IPP, la palette locative pourrait encore gagner 20 à 30 % de parts de marché supplémentaires d’ici 2030 sur le parc européen de palettes Europe et de palettes perdues en circulation. Porté par cette croissance à deux chiffres, le spécialiste du pooling ambitionne de doubler son chiffre d’affaires en Europe à cet horizon, pour atteindre 500 millions d’euros. ... Parmi les utilisateurs emblématiques du Sud-Ouest figure L’Atelier des Producteurs, filiale des Fermes Larrère, entreprise familiale implantée dans les Landes depuis 1958. Spécialisée dans la production de légumes – historiquement la carotte – et désormais diversifiée (chou, patate douce, asperge…), l’exploitation cultive 1 960 hectares, dont 50 % en agriculture biologique. Dans une logique de maîtrise de la chaîne de valeur, les Fermes Larrère assurent l’ensemble du cycle, de la production à la commercialisation, auprès de la grande distribution, des grossistes et des transformateurs. À Liposthey, L’Atelier des Producteurs réceptionne les récoltes, les lave, les trie et les calibre avant expédition. Le site, qui emploie une centaine de personnes, fonctionne avec une station semi-automatisée équipée de trieurs optiques et d’ensacheuses automatisées. ... Pour accompagner des volumes soumis à la saisonnalité et à des pics d’activité, L’Atelier des Producteurs a choisi de confier la gestion de ses flux de palettes à IPP. Depuis le site de Liposthey, IPP livre ses palettes, qui sont chargées en légumes puis expédiées vers les grandes surfaces alimentaires. Une fois les produits arrivés en rayon, les palettes sont récupérées par le loueur, triées, réparées si nécessaire, puis remises en circulation. « Grâce aux contrôles qualité, nos palettes bénéficient d’une durée de vie moyenne d’environ dix ans, conformes aux exigences », souligne Michael Karadjinov, directeur commercial France d’IPP. « La qualité des palettes IPP nous donne entière satisfaction. Nous n’avons jamais eu de réclamation de nos clients. Elles sont plus résistantes que les palettes Europe ou perdues », ajoute Anthony Lafargue. ... Au-delà de l’aspect circulaire, L’Atelier des Producteurs met en avant la simplicité du dispositif. « Chaque semaine, nous estimons nos besoins en palettes via la plateforme IPP. Le vendredi, nous déclarons les mouvements effectués. Nous ne réalisons ensuite que deux inventaires par an », détaille Anthony Lafargue. « C’est un système simple, souple et très efficace ». Le site utilise des palettes aux formats 80×120 et 60×80 type Düsseldorf, pour un total de 115 000 mouvements annuels."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"Avec l’acquisition d’Hexagone, le groupe Altago se positionne sur le carton alvéolaire",www.processalimentaire.com,2026-05-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.processalimentaire.com/emballage/avec-l-acquisition-d-hexagone-le-groupe-altago-se-positionne-sur-le-carton-alveolaire,"Avec l’acquisition d’Hexagone, le groupe Altago se positionne sur le carton alvéolaire ... # Avec l’acquisition d’Hexagone, le groupe Altago se positionne sur le carton alvéolaire ... Fort d’un chiffre d’affaires de 242 millions d’euros en 2025, le groupe Altago (ex-Bulteau) continue sa stratégie de croissance externe avec le rachat de l’Hexagone. Ensemble, les deux entités construisent le premier dispositif multisite européen de carton en « nid d’abeille »."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Altago acquires L'Hexagone – ThePackagingPortal.com,www.thepackagingportal.com,2026-05-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thepackagingportal.com/industry-news/altago-acquires-lhexagone/,"Altago acquires L'Hexagone – ThePackagingPortal.com ... # Altago acquires L’Hexagone ... French packaging group Altago has completed the acquisition of L’Hexagone, a Breton-based company and manufacturer of honeycomb cardboard located in La Guerche-de-Bretagne. L’Hexagone generates €13.6m in revenue, 29% of which comes from exports."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,"En Ille-et-Vilaine, cette entreprise spécialiste du carton « nid d’abeille » passe sous pavillon nordiste | Le Télégramme",www.letelegramme.fr,2026-05-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.letelegramme.fr/ille-et-vilaine/rennes-35000/en-ille-et-vilaine-cette-entreprise-specialiste-du-carton-nid-dabeille-passe-sous-pavillon-nordiste-7047826.php,"L’Hexagone, spécialiste de l’emballage en carton alvéolaire installé à La Guerche-de-Bretagne (35), change de mains. Le groupe nordiste Altago, déjà actif dans l’Ouest, annonce son rachat. ... Spécialiste de l’emballage en carton alvéolaire (ou « nid d’abeille »), l’entreprise L’Hexagone, à La Guerche-de-Bretagne (35), au sud de Vitré, a un nouveau propriétaire. Dans un communiqué, le groupe nordiste Altago annonce l’acquisition de l’entreprise bretonne, qui emploie 59 salariés pour un chiffre d’affaires annuel de 13,6 M€. Le montant de la transaction n’a pas été dévoilé. ... Fondée en 1975, L’Hexagone conçoit et fabrique des solutions d’emballage en carton alvéolaire pour de nombreux secteurs : industrie, bâtiment, agroalimentaire, logistique, automobile… Elle réalise 29 % de son chiffre d’affaires à l’international et compte près de 380 clients européens (dont des grands noms comme Saint-Gobain ou Ikea). Pilotée par Gilles Latil depuis 2016, l’entreprise s’est dotée en 2021 d’une nouvelle usine à La Guerche-de-Bretagne. ... Altago, de son côté, réunit 18 entreprises spécialisées dans le carton, comme L’Hexagone, mais aussi dans le papier, l’extrusion de films techniques et la distribution. Le groupe, 100 % familiale, revendique un chiffre d’affaires de 242 M€ et 800 salariés. Il était déjà présent dans l’Ouest depuis 2015 avec le rachat de CPL-OP Emballages, un spécialiste du carton implanté à dans la Sarthe et en Loire-Atlantique."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Emballage Digest,www.emballagedigest.fr (Karine Duval),2026-05-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.emballagedigest.fr/en/diam-bouchage-reprend-la-societe-altasur-en-amerique-du-sud/,"Emballage Digest Diam Bouchage reprend la société Altasur en Amérique du Sud - Emballage Digest ... age reprend la société Altasur en Amérique du Sud ... Diam Bouchage, numéro deux mondial du bouchage en liège, a annoncé l’acquisition stratégique de la société Altasur, distributeur historique de ses produits en Argentine, au Brésil et au Chili, après 20 ans de collaboration fructueuse. ... Cette acquisition traduit la volonté de Diam Bouchage de consolider son ancrage local sur des marchés clés. L’entreprise capitalise ainsi deux décennies de travail en commun, alliant la haute technologie française à l’expertise de terrain sud-américaine. Elle permettra aussi de soutenir la forte croissance du marché brésilien en progression de 34% en 2025. ... « Cette acquisition renforce notre maîtrise de la chaîne de valeur, une stratégie qui a démontré son efficacité en France et en Espagne, » explique Eric Feunteun, directeur général de Diam Bouchage. « Dans un contexte de marché plus contraint, cette opération renforce nos activités en Amérique du Sud Nous investissons aujourd’hui pour garantir notre résilience et notre compétitivité de demain ». ... Avec près de 170 Millions bouchons vendus par an, Altasur distribue un large panel de solutions oenologiques en Amérique du Sud et compte 55 salariés. L’entreprise dispose de deux installations situées à Mendoza en Argentine et à Quilicura au Chili, depuis lesquelles elle opère vers plusieurs pays de la région. La structure continuera d’être pilotée par Alejandro Karnincic, garant de l’identité d’Altasur. ... « Ce rapprochement est une suite logique pour Altasur après 20 ans d’engagement aux côtés de Diam Bouchage », souligne Alejandro Karnincic. « Notre priorité absolue reste la continuité du fonctionnement local et cette proximité qui fait notre force. Nos clients bénéficieront toujours de notre qualité de service et du suivi personnalisé qui ont fait le succès d’Altasur, désormais complétés par la puissance d’innovation et les ressources mondiales de Diam Bouchage ». ... Cette acquisition renforce la capacité de l’entreprise à répondre aux besoins des marchés sudaméricains, une région de plus en plus exigeante en matière de qualité des vins. L’Argentine y reste un marché central, grâce au volume qu’elle représente et à la maturité de son industrie viticole. Le Brésil, lui, connaît une expansion rapide et voit émerger de nouveaux segments haut de gamme. Le Chili, de son côté, progresse régulièrement vers une offre plus premium. ... Inventeur du bouchon « sans goût de bouchon » grâce au CO2 supercritique, Diam Bouchage, filiale du groupe Oeneo, compte 750 collaborateurs répartis sur trois sites de production, en France, en Espagne et au Portugal. Elle conçoit, produit et commercialise des solutions de bouchage pour vins tranquilles et effervescents et spiritueux dans 80 pays. Diam Bouchage réalise un chiffre d’affaires de 210 millions d’euros au 31 mars 2026 et produit près de 2 milliards de bouchons par an."
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Le Brétillien l’Hexagone racheté par le groupe Altago,www.7jours.fr,2026-05-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.7jours.fr/actualites/altago-rachete-lhexagone/,"Le Brétillien l’Hexagone racheté par le groupe Altago ... # Le Brétillien l’Hexagone racheté par le groupe Altago ... 20/05/2026 Rédaction Cet article est réservé aux abonnés Le groupe Altago vient d’annoncer l’acquisition de L’Hexagone, leader français du carton alvéolaire, situé à La Guerche-de-Bretagne (35). Cette acquisition permet au groupe de créer un dispositif industriel inédit en Europe de l’Ouest. ... L’Hexagone est considéré comme leader français du carton alvéolaire avec un chiffre d'affaires de 13,6 millions d'euros. © Altago ... Alors que le carton alvéolaire s’est imposé comme emballage industriel de choix dans un contexte de réglementation anti-plastique et de remplacement des matériaux synthétique de calage, le groupe Altago vient d’annoncer l’acquisition de L’Hexagone. Fondé en ... 1975 à La Guerche-de-Bretagne, L’Hexagone est considéré comme leader français du carton alvéolaire avec un chiffr…"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Corrugated board: grammage down 16% despite industrial crisis,www.printindustry.news (Faustine Loison),2026-05-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.printindustry.news/story/51907/corrugated-board-grammage-down-16-despite-industrial-crisis,"## Corrugated packaging manufacturers are confirming a steady decline in the grammage of their packaging, and are multiplying their adaptations to meet future European regulations. ... Corrugated board continues to become lighter. Carton Ondulé de France reports that the average grammage of packaging has increased from 580 g/m 2 in 1995 to 487 g/m 2 in 2025, a 16% drop. After several years of continuous reduction, the level is now stabilizing around this threshold. ... The trade organization, which represents over 80% of the French corrugated board industry, links this development to long-term work on packaging eco-design. The industry explains that, over the past ten years, it has invested more than 100âeuros000Â euros in research and filed 500Â patents to improve packaging design and reduce volumes. ... And this strategy is being pursued at a time when paper and packaging manufacturers are going through tense times. The sector is facing insufficient demand in several customer markets, high energy and raw material costs, and reduced economic visibility. ... By 2025, the industry had filed around 19 patents, focusing in particular on reducing empty space and adapting formats to new uses such as e-commerce. ... Carton Ondulé de France emphasizes that these developments anticipate future European requirements. In particular, the regulations provide for a 50% void limit in transport and distribution packaging by 2030. ... Manufacturers are also working on single-material packaging, water-based inks and glue reduction to improve product recyclability. ... The industry points out that corrugated board is manufactured on average with over 90% recycled fiber. According to Ademe, the recycling rate for paper and cardboard packaging will reach 94.8% in 2023. ... Philippe Durand, President of Carton Ondulé de France, believes that "" the corrugated board industry demonstrates every day that it is possible to combine innovation, eco-design and environmental performance"". However, it calls for a regulatory framework "" adapted to our industrial realities"" in a difficult economic climate. ""Steering an industrial sector like ours with a theoretical, even dogmatic, approach is no longer conceivable, nor possible, if we wish to preserve our national economic fabric."" ... France's corrugated board industry threatened by energy and regulatory risks"
Dine Cartonnages,,,,Exa,Driving the Shift towards Low-Carbon Food Packaging Solutions - NUFFOODS Spectrum ASIA,nuffoodsspectrum.asia (Shraddha Warde),2026-05-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://nuffoodsspectrum.asia/2026/05/15/driving-the-shift-towards-low-carbon-food-packaging-solutions.html,"May 15, 2026 | Interaction ... Marie Davies, Category Manager, Trays and Films at Duni Group As the global ... packaging industry accelerates its transition toward low-carbon and resource-efficient solutions, balancing sustainability with food safety and… ... As the global food packaging industry accelerates its transition toward low-carbon and resource-efficient solutions, balancing sustainability with food safety and shelf-life performance remains a critical challenge. Against this backdrop, the Duni Group is advancing innovative packaging technologies designed to reduce environmental impact without compromising operational efficiency or product protection. One such development is Sealable Ronda, a paper-based packaging solution engineered to support hermetic sealing and Modified Atmosphere Packaging (MAP) while significantly lowering plastic usage and carbon emissions. ... In this interaction with NUFFOODS Spectrum, Marie Davies, Category Manager Trays and Films at Duni Group, discusses the technological complexities behind developing low-plastic barrier packaging, the role of integrated packaging ecosystems, and how sustainable materials can help address food waste and evolving regulatory demands. She also shares insights into market adoption trends and the company’s future innovation roadmap for environmentally responsible food packaging. ... of similar size within ... . The calculations are generated using ... Footprint Calculator, which is assured by the Carbon Trust. ... food packaging, material choice has ... ₂ emissions. By substantially reducing ... amount of plastic— ... carbon footprint—and replacing it with paper from ... and what barriers ... large-scale adoption? ... We see strong interest from both food producers and retailers. This is driven by evolving regulations such as PPWR, companies’ own sustainability targets, and growing consumer expectations to reduce the climate impact of packaged meals. While interest is high, large‑scale adoption naturally requires adjustments in production processes and supply chains. ... Duniform is a full‑solution provider offering an integrated portfolio of packaging, films, machines, and service. This is critical because even small disruptions in sealing operations can quickly become very costly for our customers. Sealable packaging requires a precise match between tray, film, and machine performance. By also providing service support, we give our customers additional operational security and confidence that they cannot achieve by sourcing each of these items separately. ... Duniform has a dedicated and experienced innovation team working on future projects focused on materials and solutions that further reduce climate impact. At the same time, we ensure that food protection, operational efficiency, and performance remain uncompromised, as food safety and waste reduction are equally important sustainability factors. ... and IIM ... India’s Clean Food Framework ... Kosterina Expands ... Shots Into Mainstream Retail With Launch in Whole Foods Market and Sprouts"
