Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Jones Healthcare Group Acquires Ontario Thermoforming Facility | Contract Pharma,www.contractpharma.com,2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.contractpharma.com/breaking-news/jones-healthcare-group-acquires-ontario-thermoforming-facility/,"Jones Healthcare Group Acquires Ontario Thermoforming Facility | Contract Pharma ... # Jones Healthcare Group Acquires Ontario Thermoforming Facility ... Jones Healthcare Group acquired an operational thermoforming facility, and its related business assets, in Brampton, Ontario as of Aug. 1. Site operations, run by an experienced team, will continue under the Jones Healthcare name. ... For Jones Healthcare, this adds in-house production of custom-formed packaging components to its integrated offering. ... The company says thermoforming is crucial to its medication adherence packaging—with formed blisters organizing medications by dose and time. Thermoforming also supports blister-and-backer-card formats. These secure small, cylindrical convenience or travel vials, used for products such as solid-dose medications. ... Not only will bringing these capabilities in-house strengthen production control and coordination, Jones Healthcare says, it also supports continued development. Materials innovation and design enhancements improving handling and ease of use will be made easier. ... Moreover, the company says, thermoforming creates opportunities to support customers, either current or prospective, with specialized formats. These include custom blisters, trays and inserts for kitting and assembly, retail-ready packaging, and certain other components. ... Jones Healthcare President and CEO Ron Harris said customers want packaging partners managing more of the process, with fewer handoffs. ... “Bringing thermoforming in-house strengthens important areas of our existing business,” Harris said. “[It] gives our teams greater opportunity to innovate and creates new possibilities for customers across health, wellness and nutrition. It is a complementary capability that makes our broader portfolio more connected and more valuable.” ... Specifically concerning convenience-vial packaging, the acquisition complements Jones Healthcare’s planned installation of an additional bottle and vial line this year. ... Overall, the acquisition adds to Jones Healthcare’s existing expertise in printed packaging components, contract packaging services, and medication dispensing solutions."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,China Bakery Manufacturers Turn to Sustainable Packaging Solutions - Asia Pacific Food Industry,www.apfoodonline.com (Asia Pacific Food Industry),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.apfoodonline.com/industry/china-bakery-manufacturers-turn-to-sustainable-packaging-solutions/,"As bakery manufacturers across ASEAN face increasing pressure to reduce plastic waste while extending product shelf life, Chinese packaging manufacturer Minghefa Group is emerging as a company to watch. ... Founded in 2001, the company has evolved from a corrugated box supplier into a packaging solutions provider offering paper-based bakery packaging, cold-chain packaging and customised food packaging for commercial food manufacturers. In recent years, it has expanded its focus beyond conventional cartons to recyclable, fibre-based packaging designed to support circular economy initiatives and reduce dependence on petroleum-derived plastics. ... Minghefa’s manufacturing network incorporates automated production lines and in-house packaging design capabilities, enabling it to develop solutions tailored to bakery products ranging from bread and pastries to frozen dough. Its sustainable packaging portfolio includes recyclable paper materials, foldable transport packaging and lightweight designs aimed at reducing logistics costs and carbon emissions. ... The development comes as demand for environmentally responsible food packaging accelerates across Asia. Rising regulatory scrutiny, retailer sustainability targets and growing consumer expectations are prompting bakery chains to replace conventional plastic packaging with recyclable paper-based alternatives where technically feasible. Reuters also reported that higher plastic costs have accelerated interest in paper packaging across Asian food manufacturers, reinforcing the momentum towards fibre-based solutions. ... For ASEAN bakery producers, packaging is increasingly viewed as a competitive differentiator rather than merely a transport medium. Companies investing in sustainable materials, improved barrier performance and cost-efficient manufacturing are likely to be better positioned as regional food exports continue to expand. Suppliers such as Minghefa demonstrate how packaging innovation is becoming an integral part of bakery product development, shelf-life optimisation and brand sustainability strategies."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"Driving Packaging Safety Upgrades With Professional Testing, Making Chengde Technology’s Packaging Trusted By Brands - News - Joyful Printing",www.joyful-printing.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.joyful-printing.com/news/driving-packaging-safety-upgrades-with-profess-85604384.html,"## Driving Packaging Safety Upgrades with Professional Testing, Making Chengde Technology's Packaging Trusted by Brands From July 23 to 24, 2026, the 'Open Day at the China Packaging Federation Packaging User Experience Center and CNAS Packaging Materials Testing Center' was successfully held at Zhejiang Longgang Chengde Technology Co., Ltd. The event was hosted by the Packaging User Professional Committee of the China Packaging Federation, Chengde Technology, and NewMeishu Media Group, bringing together R&D, quality, and packaging leaders from dozens of well-known brands including Guobao Pet, Asic Bio, BiRuiji, Yanjin Shop, Jinsi Monkey, Bowelry, Want Want Foods, Master Kong, Bufan Difan Meile, and Yiming Foods. Through lab visits, special seminars, and factory tours, the event fully showcased Chengde Technology's technical strength and service capabilities. Driving packaging safety upgrades with professional testing ... For 34 years, we've focused on just one thing-making Chengde's flexible packaging trusted by brands. In his opening speech, Wang Daode, Chairman of Chengde Technology, shared his 34-year dedication to the flexible packaging industry. He said, ""Packaging isn't just an accessory to products; it's the first line of defense for food safety. Quality isn't a cost, it's trust. CNAS isn't just a certificate; it's a 'passport of credibility'-recognized in 116 countries and regions. For Chinese packaging to go global, it's not about price, it's about data."" ... Wang Daode officially launched the innovative service 'Packaging Health Check Card' and introduced a strategic framework of '1 goal, 2 centers, 3 points': aiming for 'data-driven quality,' and promoting the simultaneous launch of the User Experience Center and CNAS Testing Center, connecting three key stages-raw materials, manufacturing, and brand usage-to achieve a full-chain closed-loop safeguard. Testing is not a cost, it's insurance. Fang Jingping, Deputy General Manager of Production Quality Management at Chengde Technology, gave an authoritative presentation on '80 testing capabilities · full-chain quality closed loop.' He explained the strategic reasoning behind building a CNAS laboratory: 'Testing is not a cost, it's insurance-catch risks before products leave the factory.' ... Fang Jingping introduced Chengde Technology's full-chain quality control system, based on ISO9001, BRCGS, BSCI certifications, which can achieve complete process traceability within two hours. He deeply analyzed three main driving forces: the systematic upgrade of food safety standards - aromatic primary amines changing from 'optional' to 'mandatory' (detection limit 0.01mg/kg), with microbial indicators included in mandatory requirements; the upgrade in brand customer demand - going from 'usable' to 'verifiable'; and the tightening of export compliance - with the EU PPWR fully implemented on August 12, 2026. Regarding testing capabilities, Fang Jingping focused on four core safety indicators: aromatic primary amines, plasticizer migration, heavy metal limits, and total migration, emphasizing: 'Chengde invested heavily in building this lab so that every brand customer who trusts Chengde can get a reliable test report for every batch of packaging they receive.' Compliance isn't an open-book test; it's a closed-book test. Xu Chao, Deputy Director of the Packaging Division at Shandong Product Quality Inspection Research Institute, provided expert insights on 'Food Packaging Compliance Policy Analysis and Countermeasures.' He systematically compared domestic and international regulatory frameworks and delved into high-risk substances such as aromatic primary amines, chloropropanol, organophosphate flame retardants, and phthalate plasticizers. ... Regarding the EU PPWR, Xu Chao gave a detailed breakdown of the core requirements: full implementation by August 12, 2026; total heavy metals ≤100mg/kg; strict limits on PFAS; from 2030, all packaging must meet recyclable standards. He suggested that companies prepare in three areas: rethink product design logic, expect some increase in compliance costs, and shift from 'packaging products' to a 'packaging data chain'. Packaging is going through a silent revolution. Li Li, Chairperson of the Packaging Users Professional Committee of the China Packaging Federation, gave a talk titled 'Empowering Innovation-Brand and Market Insights Under Packaging Value Reconstruction.' She pointed out that by 2026, China's packaging market is expected to exceed $229 billion, and 76% of brand CMOs will list packaging as the fastest-growing area for marketing investment over the next three years. ... Li Li analyzed the four core challenges for brand users: differentiated innovation, quality and safety certification, compliance risk management, and cost reduction efficiency. She pointed out that companies spend about five times more budget on flavor development but neglect packaging innovation, and that homogeneity leads over 40% of consumers to have blurred brand perception - 'just imitating won't help you; it actually makes consumers think you're not capable.' Packaging innovation starts with creativity and ends with safety. Chengde Technology's R&D Technical Director, Feng Zhiwei, systematically presented a full-chain packaging empowerment solution. He proposed four main pillars: rapid digital packaging implementation - samples in 4 hours, finished products delivered in 24 hours; intelligent compliance forecasting - using big data to drive global regulatory alerts; material-equipment adaptation - solving 'machine compatibility issues' from the R&D stage; Packaging User Experience Center platform - building a 'machine-service-brand' collaborative ecosystem. ... Feng Zhiwei emphasized: 'Packaging innovation starts with creativity and ends with safety. During the innovative design phase, compliance work is pushed forward, strengthening control over packaging safety risks based on quality risk assessment.' On green packaging, Feng Zhiwei introduced Chengde Technology's progress in bringing in Germany's MDO single recyclable film production line, as well as their layout in MDOPE films and recyclable packaging. Comprehensive hardcore testing, compliance ensures peace of mind Cheng Xujun, Quality System Director at Chengde Technology, systematically explained the full CNAS verification process. He compared the value differences among three types of test reports: routine reports only check basic indicators and lack authoritative endorsement; CNAS reports are internationally recognized by ILAC and valid in 100 countries worldwide; full reports add special tests for food contact safety, fully meeting national standard requirements. ... Cheng Xujun announced the Phase II expansion plan, which will add high-priority items like phthalates, BPA, and PFAS. By introducing advanced equipment such as LC-MS/MS and ICP-MS, testing accuracy will be improved to the ppb level. He officially unveiled five free testing services for attending brands during this event and emphasized: 'Testing is not just about compliance; it's also a brand's ""safety insurance""-a long-term safeguard for avoiding risks, protecting trust, and boosting credibility.' At the end of the seminar, the attendees had an in-depth Q&A session with the on-site expert team, covering key issues like single materials, overseas compliance, and testing cycles, with lively interaction all around."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"Gerresheimer Tubular Glass Plant, China",www.packaging-gateway.com (Raghavi Joshi),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/projects/gerresheimer-tubular-glass-plant-china/,"Gerresheimer’s new pharmaceutical glass packaging plant in Zhenjiang Dagang, China, began operations in July 2026. Credit: Gerresheimer. ... The new plant doubles Gerresheimer’s production capacity of primary packaging for injectable pharmaceuticals in China. Credit: Gerresheimer. ... Gerresheimer, the German manufacturer of drug delivery systems and pharmaceutical packaging, established a new tubular glass plant in Zhenjiang Dagang, China, to produce glass primary packaging for medicines. ... The plant is owned and managed by Gerresheimer Shuangfeng Pharmaceutical Glass Co., a joint venture between Gerresheimer Group and China’s Shuangfeng Glass. ... Construction of the facility commenced in 2022 and operations started in July 2026. The Zhenjiang Dagang plant is the company’s fourth tubular glass facility in China. ... The site currently manufactures pharmaceutical vials and ampoules mainly for the Chinese market. It doubled Gerresheimer’s capacity for primary packaging for injectable medicines in China. ... The company employs around 250 people at the facility and anticipates creating approximately 50 further positions over the next few years. ... Zhenjiang Economic and Technological Development Zone ( ... ETDZ) in Jiangsu Province. ... Gerresheimer’s tubular glass plant spans approximately 40,000m² (430,556ft2). The site also reserves an additional 33,000m² for potential future expansion. ... The facility is equipped with advanced glass-forming lines and highly automated, intelligent production and logistics systems. It manufactures borosilicate glass vials and ampoules in multiple sizes and specifications, meeting China’s Good Manufacturing Practice requirements for injectable pharmaceutical packaging. ... Gerresheimer manufactures ampoules in flint and amber glass with filling capacities from 1ml to 50ml. The range covers straight-stem, funnel-type and closed formats conforming to ISO types B, C and D, with break options including One Point Cut, Colour Break Ring and Score Ring. ... In addition, Gerresheimer’s portfolio includes vials marketed under the Gx Vials Platform, prefillable syringes under the Gx Syringes Platform and the Gx Cap smart closure for prescription vials. ... Gerresheimer supplies a broad range of primary pharmaceutical packaging, closures and accessories, alongside drug delivery systems, medical devices and healthcare solutions. ... Its portfolio spans infusion, dropper and syrup bottles, tablet containers, vials, syringes and pens, as well as auto-injectors, inhalers, ampoules, cartridges and on-body devices. The portfolio also includes digital tools that support therapy. ... The company operates 39 manufacturing sites across Europe, the Americas and Asia, producing close to end markets. Including Bormioli Pharma, the Group reported revenues of around €2.3bn ($2.61bn) in 2025 and employs more than 13,000 people."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"동양당, 50년 원료 배합 노하우 담아 ‘동양녹용진액’ 출시 | 서울신문",www.seoul.co.kr (양승현 리포터),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.seoul.co.kr/news/economy/2026/08/03/20260803500046,"동양당, 50년 원료 배합 노하우 담아 ‘동양녹용진액’ 출시 | 서울신문 ... # 동양당, 50년 원료 배합 노하우 담아 ‘동양녹용진액’ 출시 # 동양당, 50년 원료 배합 노하우 담아 ‘동양녹용진액’ 출시 ... 입력 2026-08-03 10:17 수정 2026-08-03 10:25 동양당이 50년 원료 배합 노하우를 담아 러시아 알타이산 녹용과 국내산 한방 원료를 조합한 액상차 ‘동양녹용진액’을 출시했다. 초미립 온체식 추출과 효소분해 공정을 적용해 원료 본연의 성분과 흡수율을 높였고, 김도경 대표가 기획부터 생산까지 직접 관리했다. ... (사진=동양당 제공) 한방건강식품 전문기업 동양당(대표 김도경)이 러시아 알타이산 녹용과 국내산 한방 원료를 배합한 액상차 신제품 ‘동양녹용진액’을 출시했다고 밝혔다. 이번 신제품은 러시아 알타이산 녹용 중에서도 상대 부위를 주요 원료로 사용했다. 여기에 원료별 성질과 향, 맛, 농도를 고려해 선정한 국내산 한방 원료를 최적 비율로 배합했다. 제조 과정에는 원료를 미세하게 분쇄해 추출하는 ‘초미립 온체식 추출 공정’을 적용했다. 원료 잔여물(추출박)을 제거하는 일반적인 방식과 달리 원료 본래의 성분을 고스란히 담아내기 위한 가공 기술이다. 이와 함께 유효 성분을 미세한 단위로 분해해 체내 흡수율을 높이는 효소 분해 공정을 도입해 영양 성분의 전달력을 다졌다. (사진=동양당 제공) 이번 제품은 한약사이자 한약학 박사인 김도경 대표가 제품 기획부터 원료 선별, 배합, 생산 공정 설계까지 전 과정에 직접 관여했다. 동양당은 외부 위탁 생산(OEM)을 배제하고 자사 제조 시설에서 원료 입고부터 추출, 포장, 품질 관리, 출고에 이르는 모든 과정을 직접 운영·관리하고 있다. 김도경 대표는 “50년 동안 동양당을 믿고 찾아준 고객의 신뢰에 보답한다는 마음으로 원료 선정부터 생산과 출고까지 직접 관리하겠다”고 말했다. 그러면서 녹용은 원산지 못지않게 어떤 부위를 사용하고 어떤 원료와 배합하며 어떻게 가공하느냐가 중요하다며, 원료 선택을 넘어 유효 성분을 온전히 담아내기 위한 제조 공정까지 고심해 개발한 제품이라고 설명했다. 동양녹용진액은 80mL 파우치 제형으로 15포와 30포 두 가지 세트로 구성됐다. 동양당 공식 온라인 몰과 스마트스토어, 전국 주요 약국 매장에서 판매된다. 동양당은 향후 한방 원료 연구와 제조 기술 고도화를 바탕으로 건강식품 라인업을 지속 확대할 계획이다. 한편, 동양당은 1976년 경남 산청의 작은 한약방에서 출발했다. 1대가 쌓은 원료 선별과 배합 노하우는 2대인 김도경 대표에게 이어졌고, 현재는 식품 제조 기술과 품질 관리 체계가 더해진 제품으로 발전하고 있다. 그 결실 중 하나가 최근 출시된 신제품 ‘동양녹용진액’이다."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"What Multi-Scenario Tunable Bio-Based Plastics Help Brands Pass Global Plastic Regulatory Audits? - News - Jiangsu Jinhe High-tech Co., Ltd.",www.bio-based.cn,2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bio-based.cn/news/what-multi-scenario-tunable-bio-based-plastics-help-brands-pass-global-plastic-regulatory-audits.html,"What Multi-Scenario Tunable Bio-Based Plastics Help Brands Pass Global Plastic Regulatory Audits? - News - Jiangsu Jinhe High-tech Co., Ltd. ... # What Multi-Scenario Tunable Bio-Based Plastics Help Brands Pass Global Plastic Regulatory Audits? 2026-07-31 0 Leave me a message FMCG packaging enterprises, agricultural material manufacturers and automotive component suppliers are facing severe cross-border compliance pressure under EU PPWR and global plastic tax policies. Most single-formula bio-based resins have fixed degradation cycles and poor mechanical balance; some cannot adapt injection & extrusion dual production lines, while others fail food chemical resistance standards, forcing brands to source multiple material suppliers and bear extra testing costs. Jiangsu Jinhe eco-friendly bio-based plastic raw materials adopt modified biomass composite formulas with adjustable degradation speed, balanced toughness and multi-process compatibility, solving material switching costs and export detention risks for enterprises transitioning to fully sustainable product lines. ### 1. Customizable degradation cycle matches regional waste treatment infrastructure differences European, Southeast Asian and North American regions have distinct composting and landfill disposal systems. Fixed-standard bio-plastics either degrade too fast during storage and transportation or cannot fully decompose under local natural conditions, leading to product disqualification in third-party sustainability audits. Jinhe’s modified bio-based matrix allows technicians to adjust microbial decomposition speed according to customer target markets. Short-cycle formulas suit catering disposable goods for industrial compost facilities; long-stable versions adapt agricultural mulch requiring multi-month soil coverage without premature breakage. Brands no longer need to develop separate material formulas for different export regions, cutting raw material R&D and batch testing expenses. ... ### 3. Universal multi-process compatibility simplifies factory equipment transformation costs Most bio-resins only support single molding technology, forcing manufacturers to reconstruct production lines or purchase dedicated equipment when expanding product categories, bringing high fixed asset investment pressure. Jinhe bio-based plastic adapts all mainstream plastic processing workflows including injection molding, extrusion, blow molding and vacuum thermoforming. Factories can replace traditional fossil plastic raw materials on existing machines without modifying heating, feeding and mold structures. One single bio-based raw material stock covers packaging tableware, agricultural supplies and industrial accessories, reducing multi-type raw material warehousing capital occupation for mixed-production manufacturers. ... ### 4. Stable chemical resistance meets food & pharmaceutical contact safety thresholds Unmodified biomass plastics easily swell and dissolve under weak acid, grease and organic solvent erosion, which cannot pass food contact migration testing and cannot be used for food containers and drug packaging. The finished bio-based material adds special barrier modifiers during synthesis to form a dense stable molecular structure, resisting corrosion from edible oil, fruit acid and mild pharmaceutical reagents. Every batch completes heavy metal and volatile substance inspection before delivery, fully complying with EU food packaging safety standards, helping food and medical brands avoid cargo seizure caused by unqualified packaging materials during customs clearance. ... ### 5. Diversified functional customization builds differentiated brand product competitiveness Homogeneous generic bio-plastics fall into vicious price competition, unable to match brand personalized positioning demands such as high transparency, matte texture or anti-UV agricultural use. The factory supports targeted formula adjustment: transparent grade for high-end retail food boxes, anti-UV modified formula for outdoor agricultural mulch, matte low-gloss version for electronic housing shells. Color, gloss and auxiliary functional additives can be freely matched per customer design requirements, enabling brands to launch exclusive eco product lines that differ from mass market competitors and raise retail product premium space. ... ### 6. Full R&D testing system provides complete LCA & compliance certification documents Overseas brand buyers require complete life cycle assessment (LCA) data and material test reports for plastic tax and circular economy audits, while small bio-material factories lack standardized inspection archives. Jinhe equips professional material laboratories with thermogravimetric analyzers and universal tensile testing machines, conducting full physical, chemical and degradability testing for each production batch. Cooperated university research institutions support authoritative sustainability certification application, providing full traceability raw material files for cross-border enterprises to smoothly pass EU PPWR and local plastic tax supervision audits without compliance delays. Jiangsu Jinhe specializes in modified eco-friendly bio-based plastic raw materials with adjustable degradation performance, multi-molding compatibility and food-safe chemical stability. Our customizable biomass composite resins serve catering packaging, agriculture, auto parts and electronics manufacturers worldwide, helping enterprises complete sustainable material replacement and eliminate cross-border plastic regulation audit risks with stable large-batch supply and full testing document support."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,The China Packaging Federation's Packaging User Experience Center And CNAS Packaging Material Testing Center Open Day Event Was Successfully Held - News - Joyful Printing,www.joyful-printing.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.joyful-printing.com/news/the-china-packaging-federation-s-packaging-use-85602462.html,"From July 23 to 24, 2026, the ""Open Day Event of the China Packaging Federation Packaging User Experience Center and CNAS Packaging Material Testing Center"" was successfully held at Chengde Technology Co., Ltd. in Longgang, Zhejiang. The event was hosted by the Packaging User Professional Committee of the China Packaging Federation, Chengde Technology, and New Media Group, bringing together R&D, quality, and packaging leaders from dozens of well-known brands including Guai Bao Pets, Aixike Bio, BRIDGE, Yanjin Shop, Golden Monkey, Powery, Want Want Foods, Master Kong, Bufan Di Fan Meile, and Yiming Foods. Through lab tours, thematic seminars, and factory visits, the event fully showcased Chengde Technology's technical strength and service capabilities. ... On-site Visit: Packaging User Experience Center and CNAS Testing Laboratory On the morning of July 23, the attendees visited the Packaging User Experience Center (Zhejiang) of the China Packaging Federation and the CNAS Packaging Material Testing Center. The Experience Center was officially established at Chengde Technology in December 2025, and it is the first packaging user experience center set up by the China Packaging Federation nationwide, aiming to provide brands with quick-to-implement packaging innovation solutions. ... Chengde Technology's CNAS Packaging Materials Testing Center, built on over 20 years of experience in flexible packaging technology, has officially obtained CNAS accreditation. This internationally recognized qualification ensures that test reports are accepted worldwide, providing strong credibility for product exports. The center has more than 80 advanced testing capabilities, meeting comprehensive quality control needs for flexible packaging in food, pharmaceuticals, daily chemicals, pet products, and more. It establishes a complete quality chain from raw material inspection to finished product release. The CNAS Packaging Materials Testing Center spans about 1,000 square meters and covers multiple aspects such as physical performance, chemical properties, barrier performance, and microbiology, with testing capabilities at the industry-leading level. The attendees not only toured over 50 top international testing devices, including those from Shimadzu, Agilent, and Mocon, but also got hands-on experience with several rapid sample testing projects on site. ... A Walk into the Factory: MDO Single-Material Production Base On the morning of July 24th, the attendees visited Zhejiang Xiangpeng New Materials Co., Ltd., a wholly-owned subsidiary of Chengde Technology Co., Ltd. Xiangpeng focuses on the research and application innovation of high-performance packaging materials. Its core product, MDOPE (HMDOPE) eco-friendly recyclable film, is widely used in soft packaging for food, daily chemicals, and pharmaceuticals due to its technical advantages such as lightweight, easy recycling as a single material, excellent printing and heat-sealing performance, and high barrier properties. ... As a tech-driven company, Xiangpeng New Materials is equipped with industry-leading multi-layer co-extrusion film production lines and professional R&D labs. We stick to independent innovation and have accumulated several technical patents. In 2022, our company was the first in the industry to introduce Germany's Reifenhäuser MDOPE and online coating production lines for material barriers. Leveraging two core invention patents, we successfully developed the MDOPE and HMDOPE product series on our own, and the related packaging applications have received authoritative certifications like 'China Green Product' and 'Double Easy Certification.' At the same time, we actively participated in drafting two group standards related to single-material products, continuously promoting industry standardization and high-quality development. ... The open day event fully showcased the technical strength of the Packaging User Experience Center of the China Packaging Federation and the CNAS Packaging Material Testing Center. As Chairman Wang Daode said, the simultaneous launch of the two centers marks a solid step forward in 'data-driven quality.' Chengde Technology is committed to providing brands with full-chain support, from packaging innovation and quality testing to compliance verification, living up to its mission of 'offering users more valuable products and services.' The event concluded successfully in a lively atmosphere, and attendees gained a more systematic and in-depth understanding of packaging compliance, testing capabilities, and innovation empowerment. Everyone looks forward to leveraging the value of the Experience Center and the Testing Center in the future to drive packaging innovation and compliance development for their own products."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,The sector is heating up! Multiple listed companies are intensively investing in PEEK projects. - ChemNet,news.chemnet.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.chemnet.com/news-8124.html,"Following the announcement by domestic PEEK leader Zhongyan Shares that it would invest 100 million yuan to establish a subsidiary, Zhongyan Tuopu, to advance the implementation of an integrated project with an annual output of 10,000 tons of polyether ether ketone (PEEK) polymer materials and 2,000 tons of raw materials, three other domestic companies have recently seen significant progress in their PEEK-related projects, and the industry expansion boom continues to heat up. ... On July 27, DFBP (4,4'-difluorobenzophenone) leader Xinhan New Materials replied to the second round of inquiry from the Shenzhen Stock Exchange regarding its private placement and simultaneously disclosed the revised prospectus for the 2026 fixed-raise. The company's non-public issuance is expected to raise a total of no more than 1 billion yuan. The funds will be invested in three major projects, focusing on building an integrated system of ""core raw materials—resins—composite materials"" for specialty engineering plastics. ... Among the fundraising sectors, the annual output of 8,100 tons of high-performance resins and composite materials supporting project plans to form a capacity of 3,000 tons of PAEK resins and 5,100 tons of thermoplastic composite materials. The products cover modified materials such as PAEK, polyetherimide, polyphenylene sulfide, and PTFE. The project is scheduled to start in 2026 with a construction period of 36 months and will be completed and put into operation in 2029. ... The annual output of 5,000 tons of monomers project is an expansion of the existing main business, with the goal of adding 5,000 tons of DFBP capacity. DFBP is a key upstream raw material for synthesizing PEEK and directly affects the quality of the resin. This project can stabilize the supply of PEEK raw materials and strengthen cost competitiveness. In addition, the company is simultaneously building a high-performance composite material innovation center to improve R&D and testing support. ... Xinhan New Materials analyzes that the specialty engineering plastics industry continues to receive policy support, and downstream demand is steadily expanding. Although new supply in the industry continues to be released, overall supply and demand remain tight, and the new capacity after the completion of the new projects has room for market absorption. ... On July 27, the Tai'an Ecological Environment Bureau accepted the environmental impact assessment documents for Shandong Xiangyue New Materials' specialty engineering plastic polyether ether ketone polymer and supporting raw materials project. ... Shandong Xiangyue New Materials was established in July 2025 and is 80% held by Shandong Zhuotai Grease. Zhuotai Grease, which mainly deals with waste mineral oil recovery and lubricating oil processing, has officially crossed the border into the PEEK new materials track through its subsidiary. ... The total project investment is 184.486 million yuan, constructed in two phases, located within the Zhuotai Grease factory area in Ningyang Chemical Industrial Park. ... The first phase investment is 119.486 million yuan, building DFBP, polyaluminum chloride, and PEEK resin production lines. After completion, it will produce 1,000 tons of DFBP, 500 tons of PEEK resin annually, and co-produce 6,000 tons of polyaluminum chloride; ... The second phase adds a PEEK resin production line, forming another 500 tons of PEEK capacity. ... After the full completion of the project, the simultaneous production of PEEK and its core raw materials will be realized, further expanding the domestic supply map of PEEK and DFBP. ... Baihua Group Acquires Project Land, Promoting the Implementation of the Annual 1,000-Ton PEEK Project ... On July 21, organic pigment listed company Baihua Group secured the Hang Qiantang Gong Chu [2026] No. 12 plot, with a land area of 29.499 mu. The plot will be used to build the PEEK material project. This plot is integrated with the 132.067 mu of land previously acquired by the company, forming a total land scale of approximately 162 mu, for the coordinated layout of high-performance organic pigments, electronic chemicals, and high-end new material industries. ... As early as January 30 this year, Baihua Group announced a plan to invest no more than 100 million yuan to build an annual output of 1,000 tons of PEEK material project, located in the Linjiang High-tech Park, Qiantang District, Hangzhou. The project is implemented in two phases. The first phase has an investment cap of 50 million yuan (including land purchase) and a construction period of 12 months. After completion, it will form a capacity of 200 tons of PEEK; the second phase capacity will be launched based on market conditions. ... Currently, the company has formed a professional PEEK technical team and laid out the PEEK track to seize opportunities in high-end material demand in the fields of aerospace, medical, new energy, electronics and electrical, and industrial manufacturing, achieving an extension from traditional pigments to the high-performance engineering plastics field."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"The Output Value Of Enterprises Above Designated Size Has Surpassed 2 Billion Yuan, Highlighting The Cluster Effect Of The Printing And Packaging Industry in Yuhuangmiao Town, Shanghe, Jinan. - News - Joyful Printing",www.joyful-printing.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.joyful-printing.com/news/the-output-value-of-enterprises-above-designat-85599292.html,"## The output value of enterprises above designated size has surpassed 2 billion yuan, highlighting the cluster effect of the printing and packaging industry in Yuhuangmiao Town, Shanghe, Jinan. ... On July 24th, Shanghe County in Jinan held a press conference for the printing and packaging industry in Yuhuangmiao Town. So far, Yuhuangmiao Town has 43 printing and packaging companies, covering a total area of over 1,000 acres. Among them, 14 are large-scale industrial enterprises, and 3 of them have a production value exceeding 100 million yuan. ... Yu Jindong, deputy party secretary and mayor of Yuhuangmiao Town, introduced that Yuhuangmiao Town has a complete range of industries and well-established supporting facilities. Its products cover multiple categories including glass packaging, paper-plastic packaging, carton packaging, and plastic packaging. All kinds of processes such as dyeing and printing, hot stamping, gravure printing, and screen printing are available, forming a complete industry chain from raw material supply, design and plate making, printing and processing, to finished product inspection and logistics distribution. By 2025, the town aims to achieve an output value of 2.042 billion yuan for enterprises above a designated size. Standing at a new starting point for development, Yuhuangmiao Town will continue to use the printing and packaging industry as a key driver for upgrading the town's featured industries, focusing particularly on three main initiatives. ... Create solid market expansion content to strengthen the foundation for industry development Based on core surrounding markets like Jiyang Taiwan Food Industrial Park and Qihe Tmall JD Logistics Park, continue to deepen within the province and expand nationally, steadily increasing our share in the traditional packaging market. At the same time, keep up with consumer upgrades and industry transformation trends, accelerate the layout in new areas like medical beauty product packaging, ready-to-eat meal packaging, smart agricultural packaging, and eco-friendly degradable and reusable packaging. Push for both high-end custom orders and mass-market orders, building a multi-level, diversified market structure. ... Create strong brand-building articles to boost the core recognition of the industry. Focus on developing 'two business cards': one is the corporate business card, guiding key companies to strengthen quality management, expand market development, and enhance brand promotion, continuously polishing the industry brands of companies like Chengxiang Printing, Yehua Paper Products, and Zhongtuo Packaging, while nurturing more 'single champions' in niche areas; the other is the industry business card, continuously amplifying the cluster and track advantages of the Yuhuangmiao printing and packaging industry. Through industry exhibitions, special promotions, media coverage, and other means, make the Yuhuangmiao printing and packaging industry a well-known professional brand nationwide, boosting its visibility and influence in the sector. ... Do a good job in attracting and nurturing businesses and improving the industrial chain ecosystem. Focus on sectors that are still blank, like listed packaging companies, high-tech specialized packaging, and tinplate packaging. Accurately attract well-known high-end printing and packaging companies, as well as their upstream and downstream partners, to settle here, filling gaps in the industrial chain and strengthening the high-end of the value chain. At the same time, make full use of entrepreneurs' role in attracting business, leveraging the resources of existing leading companies to draw in more upstream raw materials, supporting equipment, and design and R&D companies. This will further boost the collaboration and support in the industrial chain, creating a more resilient and competitive industrial ecosystem."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Gerresheimer doubles China injectable packaging capacity with new plant,www.packaginginsights.com (28 Jul 2026),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaginginsights.com/news/gerresheimer-china-injectable-packaging-plant.html,"# Gerresheimer doubles China injectable packaging capacity with new plant ... - Gerresheimer has opened a 40,000 square meter pharmaceutical glass packaging plant in Zhenjiang, China. - The facility produces borosilicate glass vials and ampoules, and includes ISO-classified cleanrooms, laboratories, and silicone-coating areas. - The plant features rooftop solar power, water recycling, and heat recovery in line with green building standards. ... Gerresheimer, a drug and healthcare packaging supplier headquartered in Düsseldorf, Germany, has started operations at a new plant in Zhenjiang Dagang, China, dedicated to the production of glass primary pharmaceutical packaging. ... The facility covers around 40,000 square meters in the Zhenjiang Economic Development Zone in Jiangsu Province. According to the company, an additional 33,000 square meters of land is available for future expansion. The building is said to be energy-efficient and the facility produces glass packaging that meets the regulatory requirements of the pharmaceutical and biotech industries. ... The facility doubles Gerresheimer’s Chinese production capacity for injectable pharmaceutical packaging, according to the company. Gerresheimer currently produces pharmaceutical vials and ampoules at the site, primarily for the local market. ... Mehran Nilchian, global senior VP of Tubular Glass at Gerresheimer, says: “With our new plant in Zhenjiang Dagang, we are responding to the dynamic market growth in China, particularly in the field of injectable biologics.” ... “We are pleased that we can provide our pharma and biotech customers in China and the Asia-Pacific region with the best possible support through our expanded production capacity, excellent quality, and comprehensive service.” ... The plant is built with glass forming lines along with intelligent production and logistics systems featuring a high degree of automation. The borosilicate glass vials and ampoules are produced in different sizes and designs in accordance with China’s Good Manufacturing Practices for pharmaceutical packaging. ... Controlled areas include over 2,700 square meters of ISO Class 8 cleanroom space, an ISO Class 7 microbiological laboratory, and an area of over 700 square meters of ISO Class 8 space for the silicone coating of ampoules and vials. The company further states that the plant has a comprehensive ISO-certified quality and environmental management system. ... The plant was designed and constructed in accordance with China’s “Green Factory” guidelines and the Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design Gold certification requirements of the US Green Building Council. ... Gerresheimer outlines that a 2 MWp rooftop photovoltaic system generates electricity that is used on-site, and water is systematically collected and recycled, including rainwater and condensation from the air conditioning systems. The exhaust heat generated during production is used to heat other areas, the company adds. ... Previously, a delegation from the Zhenjiang municipal government, led by Ma Minglong, Secretary, Municipal Committee of the Communist Party of China, and Vice Mayor Yin Min, paid a visit to Gerresheimer’s headquarters. Gerresheimer said that it would continue to develop locally tailored capabilities and provide high-quality packaging solutions and services for China’s pharmaceutical industry. ... Gerresheimer is also strengthening its European footprint. Earlier, Gerresheimer Glas, an indirect subsidiary of the company, signed a purchase agreement to acquire Blitz LuxCo Sarl, the holding company of Bormioli Pharma Group."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Jiamei Packaging Control Shifts to Dreame-Linked Investor,en.shuziqushi.com,2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.shuziqushi.com/new405732.html,"Jiamei Packaging Control Shifts to Dreame-Linked Investor ... Jiamei Packaging completed a control transfer to a Dreame-linked investor after the buyer raised its stake to 45.01%. ... Jiamei Packaging said a takeover by an investor linked to Dreame Technology founder Yu Hao has completed, with Suzhou Zhuyue Hongzhi Technology Development Partnership raising its stake to 45.01% and becoming the company's controlling shareholder.The investor completed the transfer and settlement of shares from a partial tender offer launched by Suzhou Zhuyue Hongzhi, according to a June 4 company announcement. The partnership was established in 2025 and is controlled by Yu Hao, founder and CEO of Dreame Technology.A July 9 company announcement listed several new board members with backgrounds at Dreame Technology (Suzhou), including Jiang Ming, who serves as a director and finance chief at Dreame Technology (Suzhou); Li Fei, a former business group general manager; Wang Zehao, who serves as finance director; and Guo Wanghui, a former investment director.Jiamei Packaging's shares closed at 10.42 yuan per share on July 24, down from the year's high of 33.54 yuan per share, according to the source. The company said its main business remains packaging container research, design, production and sales, along with beverage filling services.Jiamei Packaging reported net profit attributable to shareholders of 87 million yuan in 2025, down 52.75% year over year, while first-quarter 2026 revenue reached 857 million yuan, up 42.31%, and net profit was 67 million yuan, up 432.41%, according to the source.The company has said it is not involved in Dreame-related robot or robot vacuum businesses and that its main operations remain focused on food and beverage packaging."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Jiamei Packaging Control Shifts to Dreame-Linked Investor,www.newsglobenow.com,2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newsglobenow.com/new405732.html,"Jiamei Packaging Control Shifts to Dreame-Linked Investor ... # Jiamei Packaging Control Shifts to Dreame-Linked Investor ... Jiamei Packaging completed a control transfer to a Dreame-linked investor after the buyer raised its stake to 45.01%. ... Jiamei Packaging said a takeover by an investor linked to Dreame Technology founder Yu Hao has completed, with Suzhou Zhuyue Hongzhi Technology Development Partnership raising its stake to 45.01% and becoming the company's controlling shareholder.The investor completed the transfer and settlement of shares from a partial tender offer launched by Suzhou Zhuyue Hongzhi, according to a June 4 company announcement. The partnership was established in 2025 and is controlled by Yu Hao, founder and CEO of Dreame Technology.A July 9 company announcement listed several new board members with backgrounds at Dreame Technology (Suzhou), including Jiang Ming, who serves as a director and finance chief at Dreame Technology (Suzhou); Li Fei, a former business group general manager; Wang Zehao, who serves as finance director; and Guo Wanghui, a former investment director.Jiamei Packaging's shares closed at 10.42 yuan per share on July 24, down from the year's high of 33.54 yuan per share, according to the source. The company said its main business remains packaging container research, design, production and sales, along with beverage filling services.Jiamei Packaging reported net profit attributable to shareholders of 87 million yuan in 2025, down 52.75% year over year, while first-quarter 2026 revenue reached 857 million yuan, up 42.31%, and net profit was 67 million yuan, up 432.41%, according to the source.The company has said it is not involved in Dreame-related robot or robot vacuum businesses and that its main operations remain focused on food and beverage packaging."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"Perkuat Rantai Pasok Industri, Bea Cukai Beri Izin Gudang Berikat ke Perusahaan Ini",www.jpnn.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.jpnn.com/news/perkuat-rantai-pasok-industri-bea-cukai-beri-izin-gudang-berikat-ke-perusahaan-ini,"Kamis, 23 Juli 2026 – 15:57 WIB ... Kepala Kanwil Bea Cukai Jawa Tengah dan D.I. Yogyakarta Agus Yulianto (kiri) secara simbolis menyerahkan izin fasilitas Gudang Berikat kepada perwakilan PT Yong Sheng Packaging pada Kamis (16/7). Foto: Dokumentasi Bea Cukai ... jpnn.com, SEMARANG - Kantor Wilayah Bea Cukai Jawa Tengah dan D.I. Yogyakarta kembali menunjukkan komitmennya dalam mendukung pertumbuhan industri nasional. ... Komitmen tersebut ditunjukkan melalui pemberian persetujuan fasilitas Gudang Berikat kepada PT Yong Sheng Packaging. ... Surat keputusan pemberian izin fasilitas tersebut diserahkan langsung Kepala Kanwil Bea Cukai Jawa Tengah dan D.I. Yogyakarta Agus Yulianto kepada perwakilan PT Yong Sheng Packaging pada Kamis (16/7). ... “Pemberian fasilitas ini diharapkan mampu meningkatkan efisiensi rantai pasok, memperkuat daya saing industri, serta memberikan dampak positif terhadap perekonomian daerah,” kata Agus dalam keterangannya, Kamis (23/7). ... ikat merupakan fasilitas kepabeanan yang memberikan kemudahan bagi pelaku usaha untuk menimbun barang impor sebelum didistribusikan atau digunakan oleh industri tertentu ... memperoleh berbagai kemudahan, seperti penangguhan bea masuk dan pajak dalam rangka impor, ... dan biaya logistik dapat ditekan. ... Bagi PT Yong Sheng Packaging, fasilitas Gudang Berikat akan memberikan fleksibilitas yang lebih besar dalam mengelola persediaan bahan baku asal impor sesuai kebutuhan kliennya. ... Efisiensi tersebut memungkinkan perusahaan merespons kebutuhan klien dengan lebih cepat, menjaga kelancaran pasokan bahan baku untuk menjamin kelancaran proses produksi, sehingga diharapkan dapat meningkatkan daya saing produk di tengah dinamika perdagangan global. ... #### Kanwil bea Cukai Jateng dan DIY memberikan izin fasilitas gudang berikat kepada PT Yong Sheng Packaging untuk memperkuat rantai pasok industri"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,New Heidelberg CX104 Fitted with Yaguang UV System to Boost Product Qu - Yaguang,www.yaguanguv.com,2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.yaguanguv.com/news/new-heidelberg-cx104-fitted-with-yaguang-uv-system-to-boost-product-quality/,"Heidelberg CX104 Fitted with ... aguang UV System to Boost ... ### Yaguang Empowers the Upgrading of Beiren 9-Color 850 Gravure Printing Press ... ### New Heidelberg CX104 Fitted with Yaguang UV System to Boost Product Quality ... ### Yaguang UV successfully concluded the Hanoi Printing and Packaging Exhibition ... 10 ... ang UV C ... ### Yaguang UV System Integrated into Brand New KBA Rapida 105-9 — Now Fully Operational ... # New Heidelberg CX104 Fitted with Yaguang UV System to Boost Product Quality ... Recently, the brand-new Heidelberg CX104-8+1 machine was successfully delivered to the site, and the installation and commissioning of the Yaguang UV curing system were simultaneously initiated. To enhance product quality and upgrade customer service, the customer purchased brand-new high-end production equipment and steadily expanded production capacity. ... Choosing to upgrade hardware against the trend and finalizing the entire solution provided by Yaguang is not only a far-sighted long-term plan of the enterprise, but also a high level of trust in Yaguang's technical strength and customized modification services. This mutual choice stems from the shared original aspiration of years of deep engagement in the printing and packaging field, and it is also the solid confidence for both parties to grow together. ... Relying on Heidelberg's high-quality printing machines and paired with Yaguang's mature UV curing system, it will comprehensively empower high-end printing businesses such as cigarette packs, wine packs, and beauty premium packaging, further optimize the production process, create more outstanding printing products, and bring a better delivery experience to end customers. ... At present, the installation of the new machine is advancing in an orderly manner. From the customization of the plan, equipment installation to on-site commissioning, Yaguang provides one-stop technical support throughout the process. Looking forward to the smooth commissioning of the equipment, Yaguang will walk hand in hand with printing enterprises, with hardcore equipment and stable processes, embarking on a new journey of high-quality development together."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Jinghe Integration Clears Hong Kong Listing Hearing,www.newsglobenow.com,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newsglobenow.com/new398416.html,"Integration Clears Hong Kong Listing Hearing ... Integration Clears Hong Kong Listing Hearing ... NewsGlobeNow Editorial Team ... 026 ... 7-14 ... 4:13 EDT ... Jinghe Integration passed a Hong Kong listing hearing as it expands from DDIC foundry work into CIS, PMIC and 40nm/28nm platforms. ... Jinghe Integration, a Hefei-based wafer foundry already listed on Shanghai's STAR Market, passed a Hong Kong Stock Exchange listing hearing in July 2026, according to the source. The planned second listing comes as the company tries to move beyond display-driver chip manufacturing and fund a much broader foundry platform. The company was founded in 2015 to support Hefei's display-panel supply chain, especially demand tied to BOE and other panel makers with local capacity. Its core business has been DDIC foundry work, the chips used to drive screens. The source said domestic DDIC demand grew from 2.2 billion units in 2016 and is expected to reach about 5.8 billion units in 2026, with China accounting for 60% of global demand. By DDIC foundry revenue, Jinghe Integration had a 26.6% global market share in 2024. The source said that figure moved to 23.3% in 2025 after a change in statistical scope, but the company remained the world's largest DDIC wafer foundry. The problem is that the market it dominates is slow-moving: global DDIC foundry revenue is described as having a compound annual growth rate of only about 0.3% from 2021 to 2025, reaching about $3.8 billion in 2025. Jinghe is now expanding into image sensors and power-management chips. In CIS, it has built process coverage from 90 nanometers to 55 nanometers and has mass-produced 55-nanometer stacked CIS products with resolution of up to 50 megapixels, according to the source. CIS accounted for 23% of main business revenue in 2025, up nearly 17 percentage points from 2023. The source also said the company ranked third in mainland China and fifth globally among CIS foundries by prospectus metrics, with about 7.1% global share. In PMIC, the company has put 150-nanometer and 110-nanometer platforms into mass production, is verifying 90-nanometer BCD products, and has started research and development for PMIC products related to AI servers, the source said. PMIC revenue accounted for more than 12% of company revenue in 2025, with target markets including consumer electronics, industrial uses and vehicles. The shift has not yet produced stronger profits. The company's capacity utilization rose from 72.5% in 2023 to 94% in 2024 and 100.8% in 2025, but its gross and net profit structure stayed thin at 20.3% and 1.7% in 2023, 25.2% and 5.3% in 2024, and 22.7% and 4.5% in 2025. In the first quarter of 2026, revenue rose 13.41% year over year to 2.912 billion yuan, while gross margin fell to 21.3% from 27.3% a year earlier and net profit dropped 62.6% to 51 million yuan. A major pressure point is depreciation. The source said depreciation rose from 1.18 billion yuan in 2021 to 3.75 billion yuan in 2025, increasing from 21.8% of revenue to 34.5% over that period. Jinghe is also planning a fourth-phase project with total investment of 35.5 billion yuan, including a 12-inch wafer line with monthly capacity of 55,000 wafers. The project is expected to target 40-nanometer and 28-nanometer CIS, OLED and logic platforms, with equipment move-in planned for the fourth quarter of 2026 and full production expected by the end of 2028."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Anhui Jinhe Industrial profit falls 37.66% in difficult 2025,www.newsglobenow.com,2026-07-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newsglobenow.com/new396896.html,"Anhui Jinhe Industrial profit ... 37.66% in difficult 2025 ... # Anhui Jinhe Industrial profit falls 37.66% in difficult 2025 ... Global sweetener giant Anhui Jinhe Industrial reported a 37.66% drop in net profit for 2025, prompting its chairman to buy shares to boost investor confidence. ... Anhui Jinhe Industrial Co., Ltd., a dominant global supplier of artificial sweeteners used by major beverage companies like Coca-Cola and PepsiCo, reported significant declines in both revenue and profit for 2025. The company attributed the downturn to weak downstream demand and falling product prices in a cyclical market. According to its 2025 annual report, Jinhe Industrial generated 4.911 billion CNY in revenue, a 7.39% decrease year-on-year. Net profit attributable to shareholders plummeted by 37.66% to 347 million CNY. Amidst the challenging performance, Chairman Yang Le, who also serves as the company's actual controller, recently completed a purchase of approximately 30 million CNY worth of company shares. This move was explicitly stated as being aimed at boosting investor confidence and reflecting a firm belief in Jinhe's long-term strategic development and value. Headquartered in Chuzhou, Anhui Province, Jinhe Industrial is recognized as a global leader in the sweetener market. As of 2025, it holds commanding global market shares of 60% for acesulfame K and 65% for sucralose. However, the cyclical nature of the industry impacted results; sucralose prices, for instance, have fallen from historical highs over the past two years due to significant capacity expansion across the sector. Under the leadership of Yang Le, who took over as chairman from his father Yang Yingchun in 2019, Jinhe is actively seeking a ""second growth curve."" The company is shifting its strategic focus from traditional chemical production toward emerging sectors such as new energy materials, electronic chemicals, and synthetic biology. In 2025, Jinhe invested 233 million CNY, or 4.75% of revenue, in research and development. The company is leveraging regional industrial strengths in Anhui, specifically its proximity to major display panel and semiconductor hubs in Hefei and Chuzhou, to develop its electronic chemicals business. To counter changes in the international trade environment, Jinhe also finalized plans for a new production base in Malaysia in 2025."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Yangi's dry-formed trays enter live food service,indifoodbev.com (IFB Desk),2026-07-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://indifoodbev.com/technology-innovation/yangis-dry-formed-trays/,"Yangi's dry-formed trays enter live food service ... # Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter live food service ... Industrial demo line to food truck By ... IFB Desk - July 11, 2026 ... The collaboration marks the first public introduction of Yangi's quick-serve and takeaway packaging range, a growing offering that includes lids for hot and cold beverages, bowls, and plates, amongst other items, designed to replace single-use plastic in food service settings. ... Yangi, a global sustainable packaging solutions company specializing in fiber-based technologies and materials, has reached a significant milestone: takeaway trays produced on its industrial demo line in Varberg are now being used to serve real customers, through a collaboration with Flavor Boss, a multi-award-winning food truck and catering business operating across Sweden, providing direct feedback on handling, functionality, and everyday usability under real operating conditions. ... Yangi’s dry-forming technology produces fiber-based packaging without the water-intensive processes required by conventional fiber forming, significantly reducing resource consumption and CO₂ emissions compared with plastic alternatives, with end products compatible with existing paper recycling streams. Barrier performance sits at the heart of Yangi’s material recipe development and is what enabled their takeaway range to be a viable option in real food service applications. A tray or bowl needs to handle oil and moisture for the duration of a meal, not for days. Yangi’s tailored material recipe with integrated barrier chemistry is matched exactly to that requirement without the plastic or multilayer materials that add complexity well beyond what the product’s lifespan or end-of-life management warrants. ... The collaboration marks the first public introduction of Yangi’s quick-serve and takeaway packaging range, a growing offering that includes lids for hot and cold beverages, bowls, and plates, amongst other items, designed to replace single-use plastic in food service settings. Yangi’s industrial demo line in Varberg provides brands and retailers with a practical route to market-test dry-formed fiber packaging in real operating conditions before committing to high-volume production. ... “Seeing Yangi trays being used to serve real customers is a proud moment for our team,” said Anna Altner, Founder of Yangi. “Years of research, engineering, product development, and controlled production have led to this point. It is a powerful demonstration that dry-formed packaging is entering the world in a real way.”"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Leads Intelligent & Dust-Free Packaging Equipment Innovation,www.cxpacktech.com,2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cxpacktech.com/news/jiangsu-innovation-packaging-technology-leads-intelligent-dust-free-packaging-equipment-innovation-375195.html,"# Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Leads Intelligent & Dust-Free Packaging Equipment Innovation ... GAOYOU, JIANGSU, China – July 11, 2026 — Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Co., Ltd., formerly Yangzhou Innovation Packaging Co., Ltd., is a national high-tech enterprise and Jiangsu provincial innovative enterprise located at No.10 Tongxin East Road, Gaoyou City, Jiangsu Province. Specializing in R&D, manufacturing and sales of intelligent Packaging Equipment and professional Packaging Bags, the company has become one of China’s leading manufacturers of high-end automatic packaging machines and valve port packaging bags. ... The company’s core product lineup fully covers Powder Packing Machine, Bulk Bag Packing Machine, Automatic Packing Line, Dust Free Packing Machine and Ultralight Powder Packing Machine, delivering full-set packaging solutions for powder, granular and ultralight fine powder materials. Its diversified equipment series and supporting packaging bags serve multiple Industrial Packaging scenarios with high precision and high efficiency. ... Innovation Packaging has obtained ISO9001 quality management system certification, national measuring instrument manufacturing license and export dangerous goods packaging production license. It has been awarded AAA credit enterprise, contract-abiding and trustworthy enterprise, and outstanding packaging enterprise in Jiangsu Province. The company has built multiple provincial and municipal R&D platforms, including Jiangsu Provincial Engineering Technology Research Center for Powder and Granule Automatic Packaging, enterprise academician workstation and municipal enterprise technology center, holding more than 20 national patents. ... Over the years, the company has undertaken 11 key national and provincial scientific research projects, including national torch plan projects, technological innovation fund projects for technology-based enterprises, and special industrial upgrading projects. More than 10 products have been recognized as national key new products and provincial high-tech products, and its core packaging machines have won the title of Jiangsu Famous Brand Product. ... The enterprise boasts strong independent R&D capabilities with a series of industry-leading patented equipment. The LCS-50-FB valve port powder packing machine solves long-standing packaging difficulties in the titanium dioxide industry, featuring stable quality, compact structure, high precision, dust-free operation and low gas content. Optimized into LCS-50-FBC dual-purpose open and valve port automatic packing machine, it supports flexible switching of packaging modes. The LCS-1000-T bulk bag packing machine with two national patents achieves precise metering and completely dust-free operation, widely applied for high-value materials such as molybdenum iron powder and molybdenum dioxide powder. The LCS-50-Z gravity automatic packing machine features fast speed, high precision and low failure rate for granular and powder materials. Specially developed for ultra-fine materials, the LCS-50-C ultralight powder packing machine adopts unique vacuum air extraction technology, realizing dust-free packaging and saving over 30% packaging materials, filling the technical gap in ultralight fine powder packaging. ... Through in-depth industry-university cooperation with Southeast University and Hunan University, the company has successfully developed intelligent automatic packing and palletizing production lines. The advanced production line has won numerous authoritative honors, including Jiangsu Provincial First Set of Major Equipment, China Light Industry Federation Science and Technology Progress Award, and China Packaging Science and Technology Innovation Award, obtaining support from national high-tech R&D funds. ... In addition to intelligent packaging equipment, the company provides high-quality supporting packaging bags, including paper-plastic composite bags, all-paper bags and all-plastic bags in open and valve port types. Its high-performance paper-plastic and all-paper valve bags feature high strength, excellent sealing, colorfast surface and superior printing quality, with neat stacking and environmental advantages, ranking at the leading level in the domestic industry. ... Adhering to the development philosophy of technological innovation, management innovation and conceptual innovation, and the tenet of “Innovation, Quality, Integrity and Win-Win”, Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology continuously enhances comprehensive competitiveness. Committed to delivering high-efficiency, dust-free and cost-effective industrial packaging solutions, the company strives to build a nationally renowned technology-driven packaging enterprise and create greater value for global customers. ... Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Leads Industrial Packaging Upgrade with High-Precision and Dust-Free Automatic Packing Solutions ... July 25, 2026 ... Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Leads High-Precision Packaging Machinery Innovation with Full-Spectrum Powder and Bulk Packing Solutions ... July 18, 2026 ... Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Leads Industrial Packaging Upgrade with High-Precision and Dust-Free Automatic Packing Solutions ... July 25, 2026 ... Jiangsu Innovation Packaging Technology Leads High-Precision Packaging Machinery Innovation with Full-Spectrum Powder and Bulk Packing Solutions ... July 18, 2026"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Green Transformation Takes Over Disposable Paper Packaging: 2026 Core - Judin,www.judin-packing.com,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.judin-packing.com/news/green-transformation-takes-over-disposable-paper-packaging-2026-core-industry-hotspots-supplier-innovation-from-ningbo-judin-pack/,"# Green Transformation Takes Over Disposable Paper Packaging: 2026 Core Industry Hotspots & Supplier Innovation from Ningbo Judin Pack ... 2026-07-09 ... The global disposable paper Food Packaging sector is undergoing unprecedented structural reshuffling in 2026, fueled by worldwide single-use plastic bans, rising consumer eco-awareness, and breakthroughs in biodegradable coating technology. Compostable kraft paper containers, plastic-free paper cups and customized takeaway packaging have become three defining industry hotspots, reshaping procurement standards for coffee chains, quick-service restaurants and catering distributors across continents. As a verified Chinese professional paper packaging manufacturer with over 13 years of production experience, Ningbo Haishu Judin Packing Products Co., Ltd. (JUDIN PACK) stands at the forefront of this green revolution, delivering compliant, cost-effective eco paper packaging solutions to global buyers via its two official platforms: the corporate independent site www.judin-packing.com and Made-in-China flagship store https://papercupfactory.en.made-in-china.com/. ... Regulatory policies including EU PPWR, regional plastic prohibition orders in the Middle East and North America have eliminated traditional PE-lined paper products with microplastic residues from mainstream supply chains. The market now prioritizes PLA-coated, water-based coated kraft paper goods that support industrial and home composting, with zero PFAS chemical additives as a non-negotiable entry threshold. ... Industry data shows the global compostable foodservice packaging market will hit USD 9.058 billion in 2026, maintaining a 6.77% compound annual growth rate through 2034. Catering brands are willing to pay a 5%-10% premium for fully biodegradable packaging, pushing manufacturers to upgrade material lines rapidly. ... JUDIN PACK has fully iterated its product portfolio to match this trend. On its Made-in-China store https://papercupfactory.en.made-in-china.com/, buyers can browse full ranges of biodegradable kraft paper soup cups, hamburger clamshell boxes, noodle bowls and ripple wall coffee cups, all adopting food-grade compostable coatings without harmful plastic components. All products pass third-party factory audits, with flexible MOQ support: 30,000 pieces for most paper cup and box items, and a lower 10,000-piece threshold for window pastry boxes and noodle containers to serve small and medium brand clients. ... Personalized packaging has evolved from a marketing bonus to a core competitive advantage for foodservice brands. Flexo custom logo printing, special structural designs (4-cup carriers, octagonal sushi boxes, window bakery trays) and multi-size matched packaging sets (500ml–1300ml salad bowls, 8oz–32oz noodle boxes) dominate global purchasing inquiries in 2026. ... The food delivery economy remains the core demand engine: global annual takeaway orders exceed 28 billion, generating massive consumption of paper cups, fries boxes and portable food containers. Buyers now prefer one-stop suppliers covering all disposable food packaging categories instead of sourcing cups, meal boxes and trays separately. ... As an integrated manufacturer and trading firm established on January 10, 2013, JUDIN PACK operates a complete product matrix covering single/double wall paper coffee cups, ice cream paper cups, kraft takeaway food boxes, paper food boats and chip containers. Clients can submit OEM & ODM customization requests via email judinpack@judinpacking.com or through the online inquiry channel on www.judin-packing.com. ... The company guarantees an average response time within 2.89 hours, enabling fast communication for artwork confirmation, sample development and bulk order arrangement. Located in Ningbo, a world-famous seaport city in Zhejiang Province, the factory at Fengshuigang Village, Gulin Town enjoys seamless logistics for FOB shipments to all global ports. ... A long-standing industry pain point is the cost gap between biodegradable materials and traditional plastic packaging. In 2026, structural lightweight optimization and large-scale mass production have significantly narrowed this price difference, making green paper packaging economically viable for mass market adoption. ... Leading manufacturers optimize paper gram weight and ripple wall structures to cut raw material consumption while retaining waterproof and oil-resistant performance. JUDIN PACK leverages stable large-batch production capacity to offer competitive FOB prices: ... The enterprise holds a 5.0/5 buyer rating and has maintained Diamond Member status on Made-in-China since 2021, with verified business licenses and regular factory audits to eliminate supply chain risks for overseas importers. Video product displays on https://papercupfactory.en.made-in-china.com/ allow buyers to inspect production craft, packaging texture and printing effects remotely before placing orders. ... ### Industry Outlook & Supplier Value ... Market analysts forecast that over 80% of mainstream disposable foodservice packaging will achieve plastic-free standards by 2028, and paper-based packaging will capture more than 65% of global takeaway packaging market share by 2030. For global importers, selecting experienced, fully certified Chinese manufacturers with complete eco product lines is the key to seizing sustainable packaging business opportunities. ... JUDIN PACK combines 13 years of manufacturing experience, professional design teams, flexible customization services and stable ocean transportation advantages in Ningbo. Global buyers can access full product catalogs, request free samples and negotiate bulk cooperation terms through two official channels: the independent corporate website www.judin-packing.com and the Made-in-China flagship store https://papercupfactory.en.made-in-china.com/, or send detailed procurement demands to the dedicated business email: judinpack@judinpacking.com. ... Ningbo Haishu Judin Packing Products Co., Ltd. is a professional manufacturer and trading company specializing in eco disposable paper packaging, founded in 2013 with a 24-person on-site production team. The factory focuses on single wall & double wall paper cups, noodle boxes, kraft takeaway food containers and biodegradable food packaging, providing one-stop OEM/ODM customization, sample service and global FOB delivery for coffee shops, fast food chains, catering distributors and retail brands worldwide. All products comply with international food contact safety and compostable environmental standards."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter real-world foodservice use with Flavor Boss - THE PACKMAN,thepackman.in,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thepackman.in/yangis-dry-formed-trays-enter-real-world-foodservice-use-with-flavor-boss/,"Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter real-world foodservice use with Flavor Boss - THE PACKMAN ... # Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter real-world foodservice use with Flavor Boss ... s dry-formed trays enter real- ... Yangi has reached a milestone as takeaway trays produced on its industrial demo line in Varberg are now being used to serve customers, through a collaboration with Flavor Boss, a food truck and catering business operating across Sweden. The collaboration is providing direct feedback on handling, functionality, and everyday usability under real operating conditions. ... Yangi’s dry-forming technology produces fiber-based packaging without the water-intensive processes required by conventional fiber forming, reducing resource consumption and CO2 emissions compared with plastic alternatives, according to the company, with end products said to be compatible with existing paper recycling streams. ... Barrier performance is central to Yangi’s material recipe development and, according to the company, is what enabled its takeaway range to become viable for food service applications. A tray or bowl needs to handle oil and moisture for the duration of a meal, not for days. Yangi’s material recipe, with integrated barrier chemistry, is matched to that requirement without the plastic or multilayer materials that the company says add complexity beyond what the product’s lifespan or end-of-life management warrants. ... The collaboration marks the first public introduction of Yangi’s quick-serve and takeaway packaging range, an offering that includes lids for hot and cold beverages, bowls, and plates, among other items, designed to replace single-use plastic in food service settings. Yangi’s industrial demo line in Varberg provides brands and retailers with a route to market-test dry-formed fiber packaging in real operating conditions before committing to high-volume production. ... “Seeing Yangi trays being used to serve real customers is a proud moment for our team,” said Anna Altner, founder of Yangi. “Years of research, engineering, product development, and controlled production have led to this point. It is a powerful demonstration that dry-formed packaging is entering the world in a real way.”"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter live foodservice | Packaging Strategies,www.packagingstrategies.com (Packaging Strategies Editorial Team),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingstrategies.com/articles/106554-yangis-dry-formed-trays-enter-live-foodservice,"Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter live foodservice | Packaging Strategies ... # Yangi’s dry-formed trays enter live foodservice ... Global sustainable packaging solutions company Yangi has reached a new milestone: takeaway trays produced on its industrial demo line in Varberg, Sweden, are now being used to serve real customers. Through a collaboration with award-winning Afro-Caribbean food truck Flavor Boss, Yangi will receive direct feedback on handling, functionality and everyday usability under operating conditions. ... The dry-forming technology from ... produces fiber-based packaging without ... water-intensive processes often required by conventional fiber forming. This significantly reduces both resource consumption and CO2 emissions compared with plastic alternatives. End products are compatible with existing ... recycling streams, the company notes. ... This collaboration is the first introduction of the company’s quick-serve and takeaway packaging range. This growing portfolio includes lids for hot and cold beverages, plates and bowls all designed to replace single-use plastic in foodservice settings. Yangi’s industrial demo line in Varberg offers brands and retailers a practical route to market-test dry-formed fiber packaging in real operating conditions before committing to high-volume production, it adds. ... “Seeing Yangi trays being used to serve real customers is a proud moment for our team,” said Anna Altner, founder of Yangi, in a statement. “Years of research, engineering, product development and controlled production have led to this point. It is a powerful demonstration that dry-formed packaging is entering the world in a real way.” ... Yangi specializes in fiber-based technologies and materials, offering dry-forming technology that allows for the production of high-quality, cost-competitive and recyclable packaging. Compared to traditional methods, the company’s approach significantly reduces CO2 emissions, water usage, and energy consumption. Through strategic collaborations such as this, the company aims to reshape the packaging industry with its sustainable alternatives."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Wintipak expands aseptic packaging capacity in Halle - IN Food,in-food.co.uk (IN Food Team),2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://in-food.co.uk/wintipak-expands-aseptic-packaging-capacity-in-halle/,"Wintipak expands aseptic packaging capacity in Halle - IN Food ... # Wintipak expands aseptic packaging capacity in Halle ... 2026 ... Wintipak is expanding aseptic packaging print capacity in Germany’s Halle. The Heidelberg Boardmaster investment supports faster job changes, lower start-up waste, and higher-volume liquid food packaging. #### IN Brief: ... - Wintipak is investing in a Heidelberg Boardmaster inline flexo press at its Halle/Saale operation in Germany. - The press is designed for speeds of up to 600 metres per minute and rapid job changes across aseptic packaging production. - The project supports rising demand for carton-based liquid food packaging with tighter cost, waste, and sustainability requirements. ... Wintipak is expanding its printing capacity for aseptic liquid food packaging with an investment in a Heidelberg Boardmaster inline flexo press at its Halle/Saale site in Germany. ... The investment will increase productivity, add operational flexibility, and support higher production volumes for carton-based aseptic packaging used in liquid food applications. Wintipak supplies aseptic packaging materials for categories including milk, juice, and plant-based drinks, with both blank-fed and roll-fed systems in its wider portfolio. ... Heidelberg’s Boardmaster platform is designed for high-volume folding carton and cartonboard production, with production speeds of up to 600 metres per minute. The system also supports rapid job changes and reduced start-up waste, allowing converters to handle multiple orders per day while limiting material losses at the beginning of each production run. ... The Halle investment also reflects the changing economics of waste. Start-up losses, misregistration, colour adjustment, and ... over inefficiency become material issues when cartonboard volumes are high and input costs remain exposed. Reducing start-up waste can improve production cost while supporting ... reporting at a point when ... under closer scrutiny ... Packaging regulation is adding pressure to that operating environment. Retailer concern over the PPWR transition has already shown how stock, conformity declarations, PFAS restrictions, and packaging already in circulation can create production and compliance risk. Wintipak’s capacity investment sits on the manufacturing side of the same transition: more sustainable packaging formats still have to be printed, converted, supplied, and filled at industrial speed. ... The project also fits Wintipak’s broader expansion in Halle, where additional capacity is being developed for next-generation aseptic carton packaging. Adding high-speed print capability is a logical part of that build-out, particularly as liquid food manufacturers seek suppliers able to handle volume without losing flexibility. ... Wintipak’s Halle investment shows how packaging sustainability is becoming a factory issue as much as a material issue. The strongest carton concept still needs converting capacity, print reliability, line compatibility, and predictable supply. In aseptic liquid foods, that operational layer will decide how quickly lower-waste packaging ambitions can be translated into filled packs."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Yangi Cellera dry forming platform operational at European converter,packagingsouthasia.com (PSA Desk),2026-07-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://packagingsouthasia.com/type-of-article/industry-news/yangi-cellera-european-converter/,"Yangi Cellera dry forming platform operational at European converter ... Yangi has commissioned its serial Cellera machine platform at the production site of a European converter, marking its deployment in a commercial manufacturing environment and a key step in the industrialization of its dry forming technology. ... During operation under industrial production conditions, Cellera demonstrated robust performance, including continuous operation, high uptime, fast production cycles, and repeatable product quality, based on operational feedback from the customer site. Dry-formed products are expected to enter the market this year. ... “Having the first serial Cellera platform operating at a customer site is a major milestone for Yangi and the industry,” says Johann Kaiser, CEO of Yangi. “It reflects years of development in dry forming technology and validates key aspects of our technology’s performance, stability, and readiness for high-volume packaging production.” ... The Cellera platform is powered by FiberIQ, Yangi’s patented fiber-formation system, which provides precise control of fiber distribution throughout the forming process, giving packaging converters a high degree of process control. By optimizing material architecture within each product, FiberIQ enables consistent product quality, structural performance, and efficient material utilization. ... Combined with the dry forming process, which eliminates water-based molding, this significantly reduces resource consumption and CO₂ emissions by 70–80% compared with conventional plastic alternatives. The resulting fiber-based products are compatible with existing paper recycling streams, supporting circular end-of-life pathways. ... The Cellera platform was industrialized in collaboration with GDM, a Coesia company, and AP&T, leveraging proven industrial machine execution to ensure reliable production and repeatable performance. ... This establishes Cellera as a complete industrial dry forming system enabling high-performance, resource-efficient, and circular fiber-based packaging production while maintaining long-term competitiveness. ... “Converters and brands are seeking solutions that combine high operational performance with improved resource efficiency,” says Hanna Rüdel, chief commercial officer of Yangi. “The performance achieved at the customer site demonstrates that dry forming can be deployed for high-volume industrial food packaging production in a real manufacturing environment, enabling a new category of fiber-based packaging that can be produced at scale.” ... Yangi is a global sustainable packaging solutions company specializing in fiber-based technologies and materials. By leveraging a decade of research and development, Yangi offers innovative dry-forming technology that enables the production of high-quality, cost-competitive, and recyclable packaging."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Packaging firm WINTIPAK picks Heidelberger inline flexo press,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/wintipak-heidelberger-inline-flexo-press/,"Packaging firm WINTIPAK picks Heidelberger inline flexo press ... WINTIPAK, a Switzerland-based supplier of aseptic packaging materials for liquid food, has chosen Heidelberger Druckmaschinen’s Boardmaster inline flexo press. ... The move is aimed at increasing capacity and operational flexibility at its production site in Halle, Germany. ... The press allows job changes and can run at speeds of up to 600 metres per minute and start-up waste can be cut by up to 90% with the new system. ... The equipment will support the production of several orders a day while keeping quality standards consistent. ... The expansion of the Halle site is part of WINTIPAK’s broader growth plans. ... In summer 2025, the company held a groundbreaking ceremony for a new production hall at the German facility. ... WINTIPAK CEO Markku Vauhkonen said: “HEIDELBERG’s extensive experience together with their latest innovation for drastic production-cost reduction at highest quality level have been decisive factors for WINTIPAK’s investment in the Boardmaster platform.” ... WINTIPAK said extra printing capacity will be needed to handle higher output and future demand. ... Before making its choice, the company said it carried out a review of several technology providers. The final selection included the Intellimatch scanner system. ... The Boardmaster is designed for the folding carton segment. ... The company works with partners as a system integrator to enter additional market areas. ... HEIDELBERG CSO David Schmedding said: “The high international demand from customers for the Boardmaster underscores that we are operating in attractive growth markets with our solutions. The global trend toward more sustainable packaging solutions made of paper or cardboard will continue to rise worldwide and we deliver state-of-the-art technology as well as reliable service to optimise our customers’ production and reduce their costs.”"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,China’s Xinjiang region to get its first two-piece beverage can line - The Canmaker,canmaker.com (Beth Wright),2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://canmaker.com/chinas-xinjiang-region-to-get-first-two-piece-can-production-line/,"China’s Xinjiang region to get its first two-piece beverage can line - The Canmaker ... # China’s Xinjiang region to get its first two-piece beverage can line ... July 2, ... 026 ... China’s Lanzhou Zhongshihe Packaging Co is investing in the first two-piece beverage can line in Xinjiang, in addition to a digital printing line with a view to further increasing capacity."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Yonghe Shares invests 1.914 billion yuan to build high-end fluorine materials and pilot base - ChemNet,news.chemnet.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.chemnet.com/news-6983.html,"Yonghe Shares invests 1.914 billion yuan to build high-end fluorine materials and pilot base - ChemNet ... # Yonghe Shares invests 1.914 billion yuan to build high-end fluorine materials and pilot base ... 2026-07-01 10:38:01 Source:ChemNet中文 ... On June 30, 2026, Yonghe Shares (605020) released an announcement regarding adjustments to its two major industries. Centered on the core strategy of ""expanding high-end, easing low-end,"" the company is promoting capacity expansion for high-end fluorine materials while optimizing the construction pace of ongoing low-end projects. This aims to precisely adapt to the current cyclical landscape of the fluorine chemical industry, further improve the company's industrial chain layout, and enhance core profitability. ... Implementation of new high-end projects, increasing investment in the high value-added fluorine new materials sector. The company's wholly-owned subsidiary, Shaowu Yonghe Jintang New Materials Co., Ltd., plans to invest 1.914 billion yuan to build a high-end fluorine material and R&D pilot base project. The project covers a planned area of 400 mu with a total construction cycle of 60 months. This project focuses on high-end fluorine chemical products for the electronics and new energy fields. The core construction content includes a series of high value-added products such as electronic fluorinated liquids, perfluoropentanone, fluororubber, PTFE resin, ETFE, and perfluorosulfonic acid resin, along with the establishment of a supporting professional R&D pilot platform. ... This project is a key layout for the company to extend its refrigerant and fluoropolymer industrial chains. It can effectively fill the gap in domestic market supply for electronic-grade and new energy high-end fluorine materials, addressing the shortage in high-end product supply. In terms of return expectations, the project's Internal Rate of Return (IRR) reaches 18.17%, indicating good investment value and profitability, which will inject new momentum into the company's long-term performance growth. ... Optimizing the pace of ongoing projects, increasing investment and delaying production to avoid low-end involution. Regarding the ongoing projects at the Shaowu Fluorine Chemical Production Base, the company simultaneously released an adjustment scheme: the total project investment was increased from 2.388 billion yuan to 2.654 billion yuan, with an additional investment of 266 million yuan. This is mainly used for production process upgrades, iteration of core equipment, and offsetting cost increases in engineering materials and labor. ... At the same time, to cope with changes in the industry supply and demand pattern, the company proactively adjusted the production schedule. Among them, the 10,000 tons/year PVDF expansion project and the remaining works of the Shaowu Fluorine Chemical Production Base have had their expected available dates delayed from June 2026 to December 2027. Currently, domestic low-end PVDF capacity is being released intensively, leading to industry supply-demand mismatches and intensified homogeneous low-price competition. The company's proactive delay in putting low-end projects into production shifts the focus to optimizing existing production line processes and increasing capacity for lithium battery-grade high-end products. This effectively avoids profit pressure caused by low-end overcapacity and focuses on developing high-margin sectors. ... Funding sources are clear, and projects face phased approval risks. The funding for this new high-end project comes from self-owned funds and bank loans, while the additional investment for ongoing projects is resolved through the company's self-owned or self-raised funds. It does not involve changes to raised funds, ensuring capital investment remains robust and controllable. Meanwhile, the company flagged risks: the new project needs to complete preliminary approval processes such as project initiation and environmental assessment in sequence, so there is a possibility of delays in the construction cycle; if the subsequent market demand expansion for high-end fluorine materials falls short of expectations, it may have a certain impact on the project's investment return. ... Overall, in July 2026, the company officially enters a critical cycle of iteration between new and old capacity. Although short-term capital expenditure pressure has increased, through the structural adjustment of ""expanding high-end capacity, controlling low-end volume,"" the company will thoroughly optimize its product profitability structure, break away from homogeneous competition in the low-end sector, significantly enhance the enterprise's ability to withstand industry cyclical fluctuations, and consolidate its long-term core competitiveness."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,京漾生技「THE ONE」核心精神迎接美好想像雙GMP認證與全面PIF合規精準定義唯一解方 | 天天上新聞,mknews.com.tw (天天上新聞),2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mknews.com.tw/2026/07/971001/,專注高功效配方研發保養品的OBM/ODM/OEM領導大廠京漾生技事業股份有限公司（JING YOUNG BIOTECH），於2026亞洲美容保養・生技保健大展盛大亮相，京漾生技以「THE ONE」為核心主題，高調展示其同時符合CNS 22716及ISO 22716的「化粧品雙GMP」優良製造規範，並宣布全線製程與配方已100%對接國家最新PIF（產品資訊檔案，Product Information File）嚴格標準，為海內外美妝品牌主提供最安全、合規且具市場爆發力的唯一解方。 ... 在台灣化粧品安全衛生管理新制全面上路的關鍵時刻，京漾生技以領先姿態，成為台灣美妝產業轉型升級的標竿企業，面對PIF成為美妝市場上架強制門檻的嚴峻挑戰，京漾生技不僅廠區榮獲雙國際GMP認證，更從源頭將PIF要求內建於每一道製程，為全球美妝品牌夥伴打造零風險、高信賴的市場防火牆，精準卡位高端生技美容市場。 ... 長期專注於高功效 ... 研發與製造，累積豐沛的OBM/ODM/OEM經驗，已成為眾多國內外知名品牌的重要策略夥伴， ... 公司堅持「 ... 能感官」的研發哲學，將最前沿 ... 使用體驗完美 ... ，打造兼具 ... 與愉悅觸感的 ... 在全球美妝產業面臨法規嚴格化的浪潮下，京漾生技提前布局，全面升級品質管理體系，廠區同時通過CNS 22716國家標準與ISO 22716國際標準的雙GMP認證，這意味著從原料進料、生產製造、品質檢驗到成品出貨，每一個環節皆符合最高國際規範，確保產品微生物安全、穩定性與一致性達到頂尖水準。 ... 更重要的是，京漾生技已將PIF標準全面融入日常營運，PIF要求品牌必須備妥完整的原料來源 traceability、毒理學評估、安全性證明、功效驗證報告以及不良事件監測機制，對許多中小美妝品牌而言，這是極大的挑戰；但對京漾生技而言，卻是早已內化的核心能力。每一款配方從研發初期即同步建置完整的科學數據鏈，包含微生物檢測、穩定性測試、功效臨床數據等，能讓合作品牌在最短時間內完成產品登錄，無後顧之憂地推向美妝市場。 ... 本次展會，京漾生技以「THE ONE」為精神核心，象徵「唯一解方」——唯一能同時滿足美妝法規合規、高效保養與市場競爭力的完美方案，展位上將展示完整的雙GMP生產流程介紹、PIF文件建置示範，以及多項已通過嚴格驗證的明星配方，邀請美妝品牌商與通路夥伴現場體驗京漾生技的專業實力。 ... 「THE ONE」不僅是生技展會主題，更是京漾生技對產業的鄭重承諾：在複雜多變的美妝法規環境中，提供美妝品牌主最可靠的單一合作窗口，讓他們專注於品牌故事與市場行銷，而將繁瑣的法規與品質管理交給最專業的夥伴。 ... 京漾生技本次打破傳統保養界線，將「浪漫愛情與陪伴」的語彙巧妙融入經雙GMP與PIF嚴格把關的頂級高效製程，推出十款兼具感官享受與卓越科學功效的全方位護理選品。每一款產品皆承載品牌對「唯一摯愛」的美好想像，同時具備美妝法規級安全保障。 ... 面對全球美妝市場激烈競爭與法規持續演進，京漾生技以「THE ONE」精神持續精進，未來，京漾生技公司將加大生技成分研發投入，深化與學研機構合作，開發更多搭載外泌體、胜肽、植物萃取等前沿技術的創新配方，同時擴大國際市場布局，協助更多海外品牌進入台灣及亞洲美妝市場。 ... 京漾生技深信，在台灣美妝產業邁向80週年轉型升級的歷史時刻，唯有真正具備雙GMP硬實力與PIF全面合規能力的企業，才能成為美妝品牌主最值得信賴的長期夥伴，「THE ONE」不僅是對產品的承諾，更是對合作關係的唯一選擇。 ... 透過本次亞洲美容保養・生技保健大展，京漾生技期待與台灣美妝產業攜手共創，共同迎接台灣生技美妝產業的下一個黃金十年，無論您是尋求穩定美妝供應鏈的品牌商、追求高毛利差異化美妝產品的通路商，或是渴望優質合作機會的美妝行銷夥伴，京漾生技都是您最專業的「THE ONE」。 ... 新聞來源： https://news.586.com.tw/2026/07/644858/
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Zhejiang Yonghe Stock Hits Record High on Rising Refrigerant Price...,en.shuziqushi.com,2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.shuziqushi.com/new387675.html,"Zhejiang Yonghe Stock Hits Record High on Rising Refrigerant Price... ... Zhejiang Yonghe (605020.SH) stock hit a record high of 42 CNY on June 26, driven by soaring R32 and R134a refrigerant prices and its large 2026 HFC production quota. ... Zhejiang Yonghe Refrigerant Co., Ltd. (605020.SH) saw its stock price hit an all-time high of 42 CNY per share during trading on June 26. The surge reflects investor confidence driven by record-high prices for third-generation (HFC) refrigerants and the company's strong position under China's strict quota management system. The stock has rallied over 81% since early April. Prices for key refrigerants R32 and R134a, widely used in household and automotive air conditioning, have reached ten-year highs for this period. As of mid-June, the market average price for R32 was approximately 62,500 CNY per ton, a year-on-year increase of over 34%. Similarly, R134a averaged nearly 59,700 CNY per ton, up more than 30% from the previous year. Prices have remained high even during the traditional off-season. The sustained price increase stems from tight supply following China's implementation of strict HFC production quotas beginning in 2024, aligned with the Kigali Amendment to phase down these greenhouse gases. The total production quota for third-generation refrigerants in 2026 is set at 797,844 tons, representing dynamic zero growth in capacity. While supply is frozen, demand continues to rise with the growing inventory of air conditioners and vehicles. Yonghe, recognized as a leader in the fluorochemical sector, holds a 2026 production quota of 60,300 tons, among the highest in the industry. The company operates a fully integrated supply chain, from upstream fluorite mines to downstream high-value polymer materials, allowing it to internalize profits during price upswings. Yonghe reported record net profit of 180 million CNY for Q1 2026, an 85% increase year-on-year, solidifying its financial foundation amid the market rally."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,欣泛亞勇奪2026綠色願景獎金葉獎 打造rPET閉環循環經濟新典範 - 商情 - 工商時報,www.ctee.com.tw (工商時報),2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ctee.com.tw/news/20260626700615-431202,# 欣泛亞勇奪2026綠色願景獎金葉獎 打造rPET閉環循環經濟新典範 ... ## 攜手7-ELEVEN、統奕推動智慧回收，循環包材、高階電子及醫療應用三箭齊發 ... - 2026.06.26 - 16:36 - 工商時 ... 王妙琴 ... 新光合纖（1409）關係企業欣泛亞聚酯工業，憑藉多年深耕循環經濟與永續包材創新成果，榮獲「2026綠色願景獎」金葉獎肯定。欣泛亞總經理莊振斌表示，該公司持續推動塑膠資源循環再利用，透過集團上下游整合優勢，打造從回收、再生到再利用的閉環循環經濟模式，為台灣綠色包裝產業建立新標竿。 ... 莊振斌指出，欣泛亞的永續發展策略採取「向上整合原料供應、向下串聯消費與回收端」雙軸布局。其中，與統奕包裝及7-ELEVEN合作推動「iCIRCLE」智慧回收系統，並攜手和全豐光電建置「碳足雞」AI智慧回收機，讓民眾使用後的寶特瓶及塑膠容器能夠有效回收，再透過集團供應鏈完成再生循環。 ... 在循環經濟實務運作方面，智慧回收機所回收的塑膠容器，首先由鼎浩公司進行專業清洗與分類處理，再交由新光合纖製成符合TFDA及國際食品接觸材料規範的高品質rPET再生粒料，最後由欣泛亞轉化為「鈕開樂（NEW CARRY）」專利防破壞環保餐盒、蛋盒及rPET寶特瓶等產品，並取得GRS 認證，在兼顧食品安全與包裝性能的同時，大幅提升再生材料使用比例，落實減碳與資源循環目標。 ... 除食品包材市場外，欣泛亞近年亦積極布局高階電子產業包材領域，成果顯著。莊振斌指出，公司已與全球前三大半導體處理器及AI晶片領導品牌供應鏈建立長期合作關係，合作時間超過20年。憑藉新光合纖集團在高分子材料配方研發、客製化設計及製程技術上的深厚實力，可依客戶需求進行快速調整與產品優化，通過相關認證要求，成為高階電子產業重要合作夥伴。 ... 隨著AI伺服器、高效能運算（HPC）及先進半導體產業需求持續成長，相關高階電子包材業務近年快速擴大，目前營收占比已提升至約三成，成為公司重要成長動能之一。 ... 此外，醫療級包材市場亦呈現穩定成長趨勢。欣泛亞持續投入高潔淨、高規格醫療包材產品開發，提供醫療器材及相關產業客戶更完整的包裝解決方案，拓展多元應用市場。 ... 欣泛亞此次也參與2026台北國際食品系列展（Food Taipei Mega Shows），於南港展覽館一館4樓永續包材專區（攤位編號L0006）展示最新循環包裝與再生材料應用成果。 ... 莊振斌表示，未來將持續攜手便利商店、量販通路及品牌業者，共同擴大閉環循環經濟生態圈，推動塑膠資源高值化再利用，朝向淨零碳排與永續發展目標邁進。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"용기(容器)에 신뢰를 담다, 한양패키지 < CEO < 기사본문 - 경제인뉴스",www.newseconomy.kr (정재경 기자),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newseconomy.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=20404,"- 입력 ... 026. ... 배달과 온라인 쇼핑이 일상으로 자리 잡으면서 상품을 안전하게 담고 보관하는 포장의 중요성이 어느 때보다 커졌다. 식품부터 화장품, 생활용품에 이르기까지 다양한 제품이 소비자에게 전달되는 과정에서 플라스틱 용기는 품질을 보호하고 유통 효율을 높이는 필수 요소로 활용된다. 제품은 달라도 내용물을 안전하게 담아야 한다는 공통된 과제 속, 플라스틱 용기 시장의 역할 역시 더욱 확대되고 있는 요즘이다. ... 이러한 변화 속 플라스틱 용기 유통 전문 기업 한양패키지는 신뢰, 신용 중심의 경영을 이어가며 업계의 경쟁력을 발휘하고 있다. 플라스틱 용기 설계와 생산, 유통을 아우르는 원스톱 시스템을 구축하여 식품 제조업체와 유통업체를 대상으로 잡곡, 견과류, 젓갈 등 다양한 제품에 활용되는 플라스틱 용기를 공급하였고, 고객의 용도에 맞춘 OEM 생산과 안정적인 납품 체계를 구축했다. ‘사람을 남기는 유통, 환경을 생각하는 혁신’이라는 가치를 바탕으로 고객과 파트너가 함께 성장하는 유통 생태계를 만들어가고 있는 한양패키지 노고웅 대표를 만나 이야기를 나눴다. ... 한양패키지는 생활용부터 산업용까지 폭넓게 활용되는 플라스틱(PET) 용기를 기반으로 설계, 생산, 유통 전 과정을 아우르는 원스톱 시스템을 구축한 유통 전문 기업이다. 식품용·가정용·기업용 용기의 제조·유통을 주력으로 하며, 프리미엄 펫푸드 브랜드 ‘펫츠비통’과 다양한 브랜드 유통 사업으로 영역을 확장하며 시장 경쟁력을 강화하고 있다. ... 한양패키지는 3가지 사업부를 통해 사업을 전개해 나가고 있다. 플라스틱 용기 사업부는 식품 제조업체와 유통업체를 대상으로 잡곡, 견과류, 젓갈 등 다양한 식품을 보관할 수 있는 플라스틱 용기를 공급하며 고객의 용도와 요구에 맞춘 OEM 생산 서비스를 제공한다. 설계부터 생산·유통까지 연계된 시스템을 바탕으로 안정적인 공급과 맞춤형 패키징 솔루션을 지원하고 있다. ... 자사는 글로벌 환경 규제와 재활용 정책 변화에 발맞춰 용기 구조 개선과 친환경 소재 연구를 지속하며 환경 친화적인 제품 개발에도 힘쓰고 있다. 단순히 제품을 공급하는 데 그치지 않고 지속 가능한 포장 솔루션을 제공하기 위해 사업 영역을 꾸준히 확대 중이다. ... 한양패키지의 경쟁력은 고객층의 다변화에 있다. 기존 플라스틱 용기 시장은 제조사가 대기업이나 대량 구매 고객 중심으로 제품을 공급하는 구조로 소량 구매를 원하는 개인이나 소규모 사업자를 위한 유통 채널은 사실상 부족한 상황이었다. 여기에 주목해 누구나 손쉽게 제품을 구매할 수 있는 유통 환경을 구축했으며 온라인 판매를 선도적으로 도입하며 기존 B2B 중심 시장을 B2C 영역까지 확장했다. 이를 통해 보다 다양한 고객층을 확보하며 새로운 비즈니스 흐름을 만들어가고 있다. ... 이렇게 구축한 유통 기반과 업계 네트워크를 바탕으로 사업 영역을 확장해 펫푸드 브랜드 ‘펫츠비통’을 출시했다. 펫츠비통은 반려동물 간식 시장에서 차별화된 프리미엄 브랜드를 지향한다. 브랜드명은 반려동물을 의미하는 ‘펫(Pet)’과 용기를 뜻하는 ‘통’을 결합해 만들었으며, 한양패키지가 보유한 용기 사업의 강점을 브랜드 아이덴티티에 담았다. 프리미엄 시장을 겨냥해 고급스러운 패키지 디자인과 차별화된 제품 구성으로 브랜드 가치를 높이고 있다. ... 현재 반려동물 호텔과 프리미엄 전문 채널을 중심으로 공급되며, 희소성과 고급 이미지를 바탕으로 브랜드 경쟁력을 확보하고 있다. 프리미엄 소비층과 충성 고객층을 중심으로 시장을 확대하고 있으며, 실제로 국내에서도 꾸준한 매니아층을 형성하고 있다. 인도네시아 박람회에 출품되는 등 해외 시장 진출에도 나서며 브랜드 인지도를 넓혀가고 있다. ... 이와 함께 브랜드 유통 사업부는 다양한 유통 경로를 확보하고 트렌드에 맞는 제품 라인업을 지속적으로 발굴하며 사업 영역을 확장 중이다. 변화하는 시장 수요에 유연하게 대응하면서 브랜드 영향력과 시장 점유율을 높이고 유통 전문 플랫폼으로 도약하고자 한다. ... 한양패키지는 유통업에서 가장 중요한 가치를 신용으로 보고 있다. 납기 준수와 투명한 정산, 약속 이행은 단순한 업무 절차를 넘어 기업의 신뢰와 직결되는 요소이며, 때로는 손해를 감수하더라도 시장에서 쌓아온 평판을 지키는 것이 더 큰 자산이라고 판단하고 있다. ... 이러한 신뢰를 바탕으로 단순히 제품을 판매하는 회사를 넘어, 고객이 필요할 때 가장 먼저 떠올리는 기업으로 자리매김하는 것을 목표로 한다. 정확한 업무 프로세스와 일관된 서비스, 약속을 지키는 운영을 통해 일회성 거래가 아닌 지속적으로 찾게 되는 관계를 구축하고, 뚜렷한 정체성을 가진 기업으로 성장하고자 한다. ... 또한 변화하는 시장 환경에 유연하게 대응하며 새로운 기회를 적극적으로 발굴하고 있다. 환경을 고려한 제품 개발과 함께 취급 품목과 사업 영역을 확장하며 성장 가능성을 넓혀가고 있으며, 고정된 방식에 머무르지 않고 변화와 혁신을 수용하는 기업을 지향한다. 앞으로도 ‘사람을 남기는 유통, 환경을 생각하는 혁신’이라는 가치를 바탕으로 고객과 파트너의 신뢰를 축적하며 시장의 기준이 되는 기업으로 성장해 나갈 것이다."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,The Story Of A Homegrown Supply Chain Breakthrough Behind A Milk Carton Top - News - Joyful Printing,www.joyful-printing.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.joyful-printing.com/news/the-story-of-a-homegrown-supply-chain-breakthr-85569300.html,"## The Story of a Homegrown Supply Chain Breakthrough Behind a Milk Carton Top High-barrier aluminum foil tops have long relied on imports, with long shipping times and unstable supply, which has been a major headache for domestic liquid food packaging companies. Asia Pulp & Paper (Shandong) dug deep into customer needs and teamed up with leading top carton manufacturer QuanHua Packaging. After a year of technical research, they developed their own top carton base paper compatible with aluminum foil, completely breaking free from overseas supply constraints. This win-win approach for both upstream and downstream players offers a great example of localizing the food packaging supply chain. ... Quanhua Roof Pack Samples In the liquid milk packaging field, roof packs with an aluminum foil layer can achieve long-term storage of drinks at room temperature thanks to their strong barrier properties, and market demand keeps rising. But previously, there was a lack of supporting specialized cardboard in China, so the raw materials had to be imported from overseas, leaving many packaging factories struggling with supply issues for a long time. Jinan Quanhua Packaging, a leading manufacturing company in the province and a top domestic roof pack enterprise, has been cooperating on base paper with Asia Pacific SM (Shandong) since 2019. Relying on SM's stable quality, ready stock, and technical support, they've been purchasing standard coated base paper long-term. However, the company always faced a core problem: for roof packs requiring aluminum foil, there's no mature domestic supply of cardboard, so everything had to be imported. Long sea shipping times, combined with port congestion, international situations, typhoons, and other uncontrollable factors, often delayed shipments for months, constantly tying up production schedules. ... Quanhua Factory The customer's needs directly guide our R&D direction. After receiving Quanhua's feedback on pain points, Asia Pulp & Paper immediately coordinated multiple departments-R&D, production, and sales-to launch a special technical campaign. With no mature processes to refer to domestically, the team had to start from scratch. Balancing multiple indicators like pulp ratios, machine compatibility, light transmission, and cardboard stiffness was tricky; adjusting one parameter could easily cause another performance metric to fall short. After countless trials, tweaks, and reworks, the R&D team never stopped pushing forward. ... Asia Pulp & Paper (Shandong) Liquid Packaging Workshop To match the client's on-machine testing, APP proactively adjusted capacity, materials, manpower, and even the overall production schedule, fully cooperating with the sample testing. Quanhua also went the extra mile, voluntarily handling test samples that didn't meet standards under controlled quality conditions to reduce paper company losses, jointly promoting process optimization. After a whole year of repeated refining, both sides finally found the optimal balance for various performance aspects and successfully developed a dedicated cardboard for roof packaging compatible with high-barrier aluminum foil processes. Mutual Benefits of Cooperation For Quanhua Packaging: Saves on import tariffs and long-distance shipping costs, no need to stock up months in advance, completely eliminates the risk of production halts due to overseas supply delays, greatly enhances production autonomy; For Asia Pulp & Paper: Becomes one of the few domestic paper companies capable of mass-producing this technology, opens up a new niche market, and creates a new growth point for performance; For the industry: Achieves a breakthrough in domestic production of aluminum-foil roof-pack cardboard, providing local liquid food packaging companies with a stable, low-cost, and fast local supply chain solution. ... Aluminum Foil Craft Roof Packaging From sourcing a single type of base paper to joint technological innovation, deep collaboration between upstream and downstream partners allows everyone to achieve success together, truly embodying the packaging industry's idea of 'customer first, win-win cooperation.' In the future, continued collaboration and innovation between domestic paper companies and packaging factories will further break down the import barriers for various high-end packaging materials."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,New Tampon Line: Premium Care Expansion | AIMISIN,www.newclears.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newclears.com/news/new-tampon-production-line-launched-expanding-premium-feminine-care-capacity-aimisin/,"New Tampon Line: Premium Care Expansion | AIMISIN ... # New Tampon Production Line Launched: Expanding Premium Feminine Care Capacity | AIMISIN 2026-06-24 To meet the fast-growing global demand for high-quality, safe, and eco-friendly feminine hygiene products, our company has officially put a new professional tampon production line into operation. This capacity expansion marks a key strategic upgrade in our feminine care product portfolio, enabling us to deliver more standardized, comfortable, and trustworthy menstrual care solutions for global distributors, retailers, and brand partners. With upgraded automated production equipment and optimized manufacturing workflows, the new line greatly improves production efficiency, product consistency, and product safety standards, laying a solid foundation for large-scale order fulfillment and high-end customized cooperation. As a professional FDA certificated tampon manufacturer, we have always adhered to strict international health and safety standards throughout product research and development, production, and quality inspection. All products produced by the new production line fully comply with FDA regulatory requirements, with rigorous testing implemented for raw material safety, production hygiene, finished product sterilization, and physical performance. Every batch of tampons undergoes systematic quality screening to eliminate potential safety risks such as harmful residues and unqualified materials. This strict compliance system ensures that our feminine care products can stably serve global mainstream markets and meet the stringent access standards of North America, Europe, and other regions. ... Equipped with advanced flexible production systems, the new line focuses on upgrading high-end feminine care products, especially the development and mass production of organic tampon for feminine daily care. Different from ordinary synthetic material tampons, our organic series adopts pure natural organic cotton as the core raw material, free of fluorescent agents, fragrances, chlorine bleaching, and synthetic additives. The ultra-soft and breathable material effectively reduces skin friction and sensitivity, bringing gentler and more comfortable protection for women with sensitive skin. The launch of the new production line solves the capacity bottleneck of organic tampon mass production, enabling stable and continuous supply of high-quality organic feminine care products for global users. ... The completion of the new production line also comprehensively strengthens our service capability for tampon wholesale business. In the past, high-end organic tampon products were restricted by production capacity, making it difficult to meet the growing bulk order demands of cross-border distributors, supermarket chains, and maternal and child stores. The newly launched automated line achieves high-speed, standardized, and large-scale production, greatly shortening order delivery cycles while maintaining stable product quality. Whether customers need conventional standard tampons or customized organic tampons with exclusive packaging and specifications, we can efficiently complete bulk production and timely delivery. ... In addition to capacity improvement, this expansion further enriches our product matrix and market competitiveness. We can now provide diversified product combinations covering daily conventional tampons, high-absorption night-use tampons, and pure organic skin-friendly tampons, fully meeting the differentiated needs of different age groups, usage scenarios, and market positioning. Meanwhile, we continue to support OEM and ODM customized services, helping global partners create personalized feminine hygiene product lines and quickly occupy the high-end feminine care market. Looking ahead, we will continue to invest in production technology upgrading and product innovation, always focusing on women’s healthy and dignified care. By virtue of standardized FDA certification, reliable large-scale production capacity, and professional wholesale and customized service systems, we will further expand global market layout, provide more cost-effective and high-quality feminine hygiene products for global partners and end users, and consolidate our position as a trustworthy supplier in the global feminine care industry."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Yangi scales dry-formed fiber packaging with Cellera platform,www.packaginginsights.com (23 Jun 2026),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaginginsights.com/news/yangi-dry-forming-cellera-packaging.html,"# Yangi scales dry-formed fiber packaging with Cellera platform ... - Yangi has commissioned its first serial Cellera machine platform at a European converter’s site to scale its dry-formed fiber technology. - The Sweden-based company says its dry forming process can reduce resource consumption and CO2 emissions compared to conventional plastics. - Dry-formed products are expected to enter the European market later this year, targeting high-volume food packaging applications. ... Yangi, a Sweden-based packaging provider, has commissioned its first Cellera machine platform at a European converter’s production site to scale the commercial manufacturing of its dry forming technology. ... Dry-formed products, like fiber-based trays, are expected to enter the European market later this year. ... “Having the first serial Cellera platform operating at a customer site is a milestone for Yangi and the industry,” says Johann Kaiser, CEO at Yangi. ... “It reflects years of development in dry forming technology and validates key aspects of our technology’s performance, stability, and readiness for high-volume packaging production.” ... The Cellera platform is powered by FiberIQ, Yangi’s patented fiber-formation system, which is said to provide precise control in the forming process. “FiberIQ enables consistent product quality, structural performance, and efficient material utilization,” says Yangi. ... According to Yangi, the dry forming process eliminates water-based molding, which reduces consumption of resources and CO2 emissions by 70-80% compared to conventional plastic. ... Hanna Rüdel, chief commercial officer of Yangi, says: “Converters and brands are seeking solutions that combine high operational performance with improved resource efficiency.” ... “The performance achieved at the customer site demonstrates that dry forming can be deployed for high-volume industrial food packaging production in a real manufacturing environment, enabling a new category of fiber-based packaging that can be produced at scale.” ... Fiber-based ... The Cellera platform was industrialized in collaboration with GDM, a Coesia company, and AP&T, an industrial machinery company. ... In 2024, Yangi unveiled its fiber-based food tray designed to replace conventional plastic trays in the food sector. It then went on to explore lamination, sealing, lids, embossing, debossing, and labeling options — evaluating how all these elements work together to meet current market needs. ... In September 2025, it raised€10 million(US$11.8 million) in an oversubscribed Series A funding round for its packaging solution, which it says helps customers switch from plastics to renewable fiber. ... Earlier this year, Yangi launched a production-ready dry-formed fiber tray for meat, fish, deli, and ready meals. Cellera, according to Yangi, offers cost-competitive and high-volume output with repeatable precision."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,First Serial Yangi Cellera® Dry Forming Platform Operational at Customer Production Site | Yangi®,www.mynewsdesk.com,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mynewsdesk.com/se/yangi/pressreleases/first-serial-yangi-cellera-r-dry-forming-platform-operational-at-customer-production-site-3454229,"First Serial Yangi Cellera® Dry Forming Platform Operational at Customer Production Site | Yangi® ... # First Serial Yangi Cellera® Dry Forming Platform Operational at Customer Production Site ... Yangi has commissioned its serial Cellera®machine platform at the production site of a European converter, marking its deployment in a commercial manufacturing environment and a key step in the industrialization of its dry forming technology. ... During operation under industrial production conditions, Cellera demonstrated robust performance, including continuous operation, high uptime, fast production cycles, and repeatable product quality, based on operational feedback from the customer site. Dry-formed products are expected to enter the market this year. ... “Having the first serial Cellera platform operating at a customer site is a major milestone for Yangi and the industry,” says Johann Kaiser, CEO of Yangi. “It reflects years of development in dry forming technology and validates key aspects of our technology’s performance, stability, and readiness for high-volume packaging production.” ... The Cellera platform was industrialized in collaboration with GDM, a Coesia company, and AP&T, leveraging proven industrial machine execution to ensure reliable production and repeatable performance. ... This establishes Cellera as a complete industrial dry forming system enabling high-performance, resource-efficient, and circular fiber-based packaging production while maintaining long-term competitiveness. ... “Converters and brands are seeking solutions that combine high operational performance with improved resource efficiency,” says Hanna Rüdel, Chief Commercial Officer of Yangi. “The performance achieved at the customer site demonstrates that dry forming can be deployed for high-volume industrial food packaging production in a real manufacturing environment, enabling a new category of fiber-based packaging that can be produced at scale.” ... Yangi is a global sustainable packaging solutions company specializing in fiber-based technologies and materials. By leveraging a decade of research and development, Yangi offers innovative dry-forming technology that enables the production of high-quality, cost-competitive, and recyclable packaging. Their approach significantly reduces CO₂ emissions, water usage, and energy consumption compared to traditional methods. Through strategic collaborations across the packaging value chain, Yangi aims to reshape the packaging industry by providing sustainable alternatives to conventional plastic packaging. To learn more, please visit www.yangi.se"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,嘉亨家化“新东家”拟6月24日起向全体股东发起要约收购，收购价仍为33.21元/股_新浪财经_新浪网,finance.sina.com.cn,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.sina.com.cn/roll/2026-06-22/doc-iniehwmp6970838.shtml,6月22日，嘉亨家化（300955.SZ，股价38.42元，市值38.73亿元）披露，新控股股东杭州拼便宜网络科技有限公司（以下简称杭州拼便宜）及其一致行动人公布了面向嘉亨家化全体股东的要约收购报告书。 ... 这次以33.21元/股的价格发起主动要约收购，拟收购2126.88万股，占公司总股本的21.10%。本次要约收购期限为2026年6月24日至7月23日，共计30个自然日。值得注意的是，此次要约收购系主动要约，并非履行法定收购义务，不以终止嘉亨家化上市地位为目的。 ... 嘉亨家化是国内日化产品OEM/ODM（均为代工生产模式）及塑料包装容器的知名供应商。2025年，嘉亨家化实现营业收入11.38亿元，同比增长23.28%，业务规模持续扩张。 ... 本次要约收购的收购人为杭州拼便宜，一致行动人为温州苍霄企业管理合伙企业（有限合伙）（以下简称温州苍霄）和杭州润宜企业管理咨询合伙企业（有限合伙）（以下简称杭州润宜），上述三方已签署《一致行动协议》。在2026年5月26日完成的协议转让中，杭州拼便宜及其一致行动人已合计受让嘉亨家化29.70%的股份，成为公司新控股股东。 ... 收盘价3 ... 元/股计算 ... 基于要约价格33.21元/股、预定收购股份数量2126.88万股的前提，本次要约收购所需最高资金总额为7.06亿元。 ... 收购人表示，基于对上市公司长期价值的认可，拟通过本次要约收购进一步增持上市公司股份，巩固对上市公司的控制权。收购完成后，收购人将结合自身在消费品领域的产业资源、渠道资源等方面的优势，提高上市公司的持续经营能力和盈利能力，助力上市公司长远发展。 ... 2026年5月27日，嘉亨家化披露，控股股东、实际控制人协议转让股份已完成过户登记，公司控制权发生变更。 ... 原控股股东、实际控制人曾本生通过协议转让方式，将其持有的嘉亨家化合计2993.76万股（占公司总股本的29.70%）转让给杭州拼便宜及其一致行动人。随着股份转让完成，嘉亨家化控股股东变更为杭州拼便宜，徐意成为公司实际控制人。 ... 公告显示，截至报告书签署日，除这次要约收购外，杭州拼便宜及其一致行动人暂无在未来12个月内继续增持或处置上市公司股份的安排。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,发展“YUAN”动力 | 破解mRNA储运难题！宜诺生物推出研究级LNP冻干技术,www.yixing.gov.cn (yxhky),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,http://www.yixing.gov.cn/doc/2026/06/22/1400536.shtml,！宜诺生物推出研究级LNP冻干技术 ... 发展“YUAN”动力 | 破解mRNA储运难题！宜诺生物推出研究级LNP冻干技术 ... 来源：环科园 发布时间：2026-06-22 14:49:12 [ 大 中 小 ] 浏览次数： ... 从环保科技起步，到如今在生物医药、新能源、高端制造等赛道上全面开花，环科园正经历一场深刻的产业“蝶变”，成为硬核科技的“孵化器”和新兴产业的“策源地”。 ... 即日起，“宜兴环科园”推出系列报道《发展“YUAN”动力》，深入园区各个角落，挖掘那些隐藏在产业链深处、手握核心技术的“宝藏企业”，呈现环科园的创新韧性与产业厚度。一起解锁这座“不止环保”的园区里更多硬核故事。 ... 破解mRNA储运难题！ ... 宜诺生物推出研究级LNP冻干技术 ... 近日，环科园企业 ... 江苏宜诺生物科技有限公司 ... 正式推出研究级LNP冻干技术 ... 可实现产品在2℃-8℃稳定储存 ... 宜诺生物是一家以AI技术与专利平台驱动的mRNA CRDMO企业，为mRNA药物和疫苗提供从早期研发、工艺开发到商业化生产的一站式服务，核心团队拥有十年以上RNA及生物药开发经验。近年来，企业凭借从质粒DNA、RNA到LNP（脂质纳米粒）的全链条服务，从新药研发、工艺开发到生产制造的全流程数字化解决方案，迅速抢占市场、赢得行业地位。 ... 当前，mRNA技术正迎来高速发展时期，而在第三代疫苗mRNA疫苗与药物的产业化进程中，储存与运输始终是绕不开的核心痛点。“传统mRNA-LNP制剂需在-20℃甚至-80℃超低温环境下储运，限制了其在全球范围内的可及性。”企业相关负责人介绍，冻干技术在制药行业已经很常见，而在mRNA领域，冻干的应用也正在逐步增加。 ... 宜诺生物紧抓机遇，此次推出的研究级LNP冻干技术，就是通过真空冷冻干燥去除制剂中的水分，使mRNA药物在2℃-8℃的普通冷藏条件下长期稳定保存，不再需要超低温冷链。这一突破，为mRNA疫苗和药物走进更多地区、拓宽市场扫清了关键障碍。 ... 据介绍，宜诺生物在厂房布局阶段就规划了冻干产线。目前，研究级冻干技术可灵活匹配早期小批量需求，单批次处理20至300瓶，最快7个工作日完成制备与检测。在GMP级冻干生产层面，宜诺生物搭建了全封闭无菌一体化产线，已完成多种经典脂质配方工艺确定，单批最高可生产产品6400瓶。据悉，目前企业已有多个客户就冻干服务达成合作意向或进入实质协作阶段。 ... 冻干技术并非宜诺生物技术布局的全部。企业相关负责人表示，宜诺生物真正的创新开发和专利布局围绕mRNA和LNP两大核心进行，全力打造了从序列设计到冻干成品的完整技术链条，提供涵盖序列设计与优化、质粒构建与制备、mRNA体外转录与纯化、LNP/tLNP制剂开发以及冻干服务的全链条服务，构建自主可控的知识产权体系，为企业高质量发展打造“硬核”武器。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,聚汇包装：赶订单忙生产 奏响生产“奋进曲”-宁化在线,www.zgnhzx.com,2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-18 00:00:00+00:00,,http://www.zgnhzx.com/sitehtml/news/xwlm/2026/06/18/200337223374.html,# 聚汇包装：赶订单忙生产 奏响生产“奋进曲” ... 连日来，三明聚汇包装材料有限公司开足马力忙生产、赶订单，一派热火朝天的景象。当前，企业订单持续充盈，全线开启满负荷生产模式，全力抢抓产销窗口期。 ... 6月15日，走进三明聚汇包装材料有限公司生产车间，各条生产线有序运转。裁剪、缝制、质检、折叠装箱等工序衔接紧密，工人们各司其职赶制订单，确保按时交付。据了解，该企业是城南镇2025年招商引资落地项目，是一家从事包装制品的研发生产企业，主要设计、生产和销售集装袋，产品大多用于新能源、化工等企业。 ... “我们主打各类集装袋的生产与销售，采取的是订单模式，根据客户需求安排生产，基本做到零库存。产品销往三明、江西及周边地区。目前日均产量在1000个左右，上半年总产量达到18万个，实现产值约700万元，整体保持了平稳向上的发展态势。”公司总经理谢鸿胜介绍。 ... 该项目总投资1.8亿元，总建筑面积4.1万平方米，现阶段企业依托租赁厂房完成一期投产，满足初期市场订单需求，后续二期建设生产厂房、仓库、综合楼、产品研发中心等，配套建设相关设施设备，新增多条新型包装袋生产线，项目全面建成后，将实现新型包装袋集约化、自动化量产。 ... “目前我们已经吸纳了不少本地劳动力就业，随着二期投产，用工需求还会进一步扩大。接下来，我们也将在保证品质的前提下，逐步优化工艺、拓大生产线，争取把业务覆盖到更多周边的省市，进一步提升品牌影响力。”谢鸿胜说。近年来，城南镇紧扣工业强镇发展思路，持续优化营商环境，构建全链条保姆式服务体系。一方面聚焦轻工配套、绿色包装等低耗高效产业精准开展以商招商、产业链招商，补齐镇域工业产业短板；另一方面落实项目挂包制度，安排专人对接企业手续办理、用工招工、场地协调、能耗报备等痛点问题，打通项目落地堵点。同时，常态化开展本地劳动力摸排，搭建企业用工供需对接平台，以优质营商环境激活镇域实体经济发展活力。 ... ### 聚汇包装：赶订单忙生产 奏响生产“奋进曲” ... 连日来，三明聚汇包装材料有限公司开足马力忙生产、赶订单，一派热火朝天的景象。当前，企业订单持续充盈，全线开启满负荷生产模式，全力抢抓产销窗口期。 6月15日，走进三明聚汇包装材料有…
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,嘉美包装市值蒸发190亿，俞浩持股浮盈56亿|市值_新浪财经_新浪网,finance.sina.com.cn,2026-06-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.sina.com.cn/roll/2026-06-09/doc-iniavfsn6430576.shtml,到今年2 ... 全部股权收购计划刚刚完成，追觅创始人俞浩控制的企业，就将 ... 包装（002969.SZ）股份 ... 质押给了银行。 ... 嘉美包装6月8日晚间披露，近日收到告知函，控股股东苏州逐越鸿智科技发展合伙企业（下称“逐越鸿智”）已将所持该公司约2.47亿股、占其持股比例50%的股份，在兴业银行苏州分行办理了股票质押业务。质押的主要原因，是逐越鸿智为履行此前受让、要约收购该公司股权时的相关融资安排，也是应兴业银行并购贷款风控要求而实施的合规担保。 ... 根据披露，逐越鸿智质押的起始时间，是在6月5日。就在前一天，嘉美包装才披露，要约收购的2.15亿股，已过户到逐越鸿智名下。按照最新收盘价计算，逐越鸿智收嘉美包装股份的成本，约为22亿元，质押市值接近40亿元。 ... 逐越智能收购计划披露后，嘉美包装股价一飞冲天，从去年12月中下旬，到今年2月中旬，累计上涨超过6倍以上，随后又剧烈下跌，目前累计跌幅超过50%，近190亿元市值已经蒸发。但相较于收购成本，逐越鸿智及其实际控制人俞浩，浮盈仍达56亿元左右。 ... 上市六年以来，嘉美包装业绩增长几乎停滞，2025年净利润仅有上市当年的一半左右。在经营未有显著改善，又无资产注入的情况下，如何维持现有估值和股价，将是摆在逐越鸿智和俞浩面前的现实考验。 ... 嘉美包装6月8日披露，近日，逐越鸿智已将持有的该公司约2.47亿股、占总股本22.51%的股份，质押给了兴业银行，质押开始时间为6月5日，到期时间则为办理解押登记为止。 ... 逐越鸿智由追觅科技创始人俞浩控制。此次质押的嘉美包装股份，占该公司全部持股的50%。过去半年左右，该公司共计收购了嘉美包装4.94亿股股份，成为持股45.01%的控股股东，俞浩则为实际控制人。 ... 逐越鸿智收购嘉美包装控制权，分为两个部分。2025 年 12 月16日，逐越鸿智与中国食品包装有限公司（下称“中包香港”）签订协议，约定该公司通过协议转让，从后者手上受让嘉美包装2.79亿股。以此为前提，逐越鸿智还将通过要约收购，增持上市公司约2.33亿股。 ... 随后，逐越鸿智又在今年4月底启动要约收购。根据嘉美包装6月4日披露，截至5月29日，预受要约的股东总计为36 户，对应股份2.15亿股，分占该公司总股本、约定要约收购股份数的 19.59%。截至披露日，要约收购清算过户手续已办理完毕。至此，收购计划全部完成。 ... 按照上述时间计算，收购全部完成并披露的第二天，逐越鸿智就质押了其中一半的股份。而之所以在收购后迅速质押，是因为该公司的部分收购资金，来自银行并购贷款。 ... 嘉美包装也在最新公告中称，逐越鸿智曾承诺，此次收购的股份中，用于自筹资金支付收购款所质押股份的数量，不超过收购数量的 50%。因此，逐越鸿智须以持有的嘉美包装50%股份，为并购贷款提供质押担保，以保障并购贷款合同的履行。 ... 公告还称，逐越鸿智此番股权质押，为了履行股权收购的相关融资安排，也是应兴业银行并购贷款风控要求而实施的合规担保，并非逐越鸿智或公司实际控制人出于自身融资需求进行的股份质押，不涉及第三方个人借贷、资金拆借或其他非经营性融资行为，质押股份不存在负担重大资产重组等业绩补偿义务的情况。 ... 根据披露，逐越鸿智受让、要约收购嘉美包装的成本，合计约为22亿元。而并购贷款的金额，相关公告均未提及。按照6月5日收盘价计算，逐越鸿智质押的嘉美包装2.47亿股，对应市值高达41亿元以上。按最新价格计算，质押市值也接近40亿元。 ... 6月9日，嘉美包装小幅低开后，随即快速拉升，盘中最高一度冲到16.6元，距离涨停只有0.02元的差距。到收盘时，最新股价为15.87元，全天上涨5.03%，总市值174.3亿元。 ... 尽管有所反弹，但相较于前期高点，嘉美包装目前股价已经腰斩。逐越鸿智收购控制权披露后，该股一飞冲天，从去年12月9日收盘时的4.56元，一路猛涨到今年2月12日盘中的33.54元，达到上市以来最高点，短短两个月的时间，累计上涨28.98元，区间涨幅高达630%以上。 ... 登上巅峰后，该股又猛烈回撤。从2月13日到6月8日，累计下跌18.43元，跌幅亦接近55%。9日虽有反弹，但累计跌幅仍在50%以上，近190亿元市值已经折损。 ... 虽然跌幅巨大，逐越鸿智及其实际控制人俞浩，目前仍有可观浮盈。 ... 公开披露显示，逐越鸿智受让、要约收购嘉美包装股权的价格，均为4.45 元/股。其中，受让部分总对价约为12.4亿元，要约成本则在9.6亿元左右，总计在22亿元左右。 ... 而按照嘉美包装最新收盘价计算，逐越鸿智持有的4.94亿股，对应市值高达78亿元左右。在不考虑融资成本的情况下，该公司及俞浩目前的浮盈金额，依旧高达56亿元，收益率则达250%以上。 ... 截至6月9日收盘，嘉美包装静态市盈率达到201.3倍，动态市盈率虽然稍低，亦达65.1倍，市盈率（TTM）则达123.6倍，市净率5.35倍。 ... 公开信息显示，嘉美包装2019年12月在深交所上市，主营业务包括食品饮料包装容器的研发、设计、生销，以及饮料灌装服务，食品饮料金属罐市场的占有份额，在同行中具有一定优势。 ... 上市以来，该公司业绩增长缓慢，最近几年还处于波动下滑之中。年报显示，2019年，该公司营业收入26.2亿元，净利润1.72亿元，第二年即分别降至19.9亿元、3453万元，降幅达到24.07%、79.91%。 ... 2021年是该公司上市后营收规模最大的一年，达到34.5亿元，但净利润仍然只有1.63亿元。 ... 到了2025年，该公司营业收入只有28.14亿元，同比下降12.03%；净利润8660万元，同比大幅下降56.32%，只有上市当年的一半左右。 ... 今年一季度，该公司经营有所起色，实现营收8.57亿元，净利润6693万元，同比分别增长42.31%、432.4%。 ... 该公司解释称，这主要是因为今年一季度是饮料行业“大年”，即旺季订单落在2026年的天数较多，且财务费用大幅下降，显著提升了一季度业绩。虽然一季度业绩同比大增，但仍稳定在“大年”正常的平均水平。 ... 在这种情况下，嘉美包装的股价，长期在发行价附近低位震荡。2021年初跌破5元后，便一路下行，在2.8元至4.5元之间横盘震荡。直到此次逐越鸿智收购，才带动其股价出现从未有过的腾飞。 ... 尽管股价已经腰斩，但仍处于历史高位，在主营业务波动向下，新增长点又未出现的情况下，如何将嘉美包装的高估值维持下去，是摆在逐越鸿智和俞浩面前的现实考验。 ... 根据嘉美包装此前多次披露，未来12 个月内，逐越鸿智没有改变上市公司主营业务，或对上市公司主营业务进行重大调整的计划。取得上市公司控制权后的 36 个月内，俞浩及其关联方不会对上市公司进行资产注入，且目前不存在任何资产注入计划。 ... 嘉美包装原实际控制人陈民、中包香港，转让股权时曾给出业绩承诺，上市公司原有的业务在2026 年至 2030 年间，每年实现的净利润不低于1.2亿元，这一目标仅略高于2025年的实际水平。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,包材商機越喝越大！宏全、福貞、吉源卡位戰 海內外布局一次看懂 - 產業 - 工商時報,www.ctee.com.tw (工商時報),2026-06-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ctee.com.tw/news/20260606700385-430503,一次看懂 ... 三大飲料包材廠今年忙著海、內外市場卡位部署，宏全（9939）除固守台灣飲料包材市場，也布局海外市場。宏全表示，旗下越南廠與國外營養品大廠合作，提供PET阻隔包材，1年產量9千萬支的PET阻隔瓶，預定2027年量產交貨。 ... 至於宏全大陸區廣東清新廠，新增無菌線，2月2日與三得利進行無菌線量產剪綵儀式，此合作案為三得利邀請宏全投資合作，並包下六成的產量，雙方簽訂10年合約。 ... 無獨有偶，宏全在大陸浙江常山廠駐廠生產（In-house）新增鋁蓋產線，今年初放量。旗下廣東中山廠In-house，預計於2026年第二季商業量產，並與達能公司簽訂10年駐廠生產合約，將供應其所需包材產品。 ... 至於東南亞區，宏全的印尼KIIC廠-熱充填產線，於2025年第四季投產、無菌產線於2026年第二季商業量產；印尼板底蘭水廠（In-house），於2026年第二季商業量產。泰國宏信廠，2026年第二季完工，第三季試車、第四季商業量產。越南VSIP 2A廠，於2026年第二季完工，2027年第二季商業量產。 ... 至於非洲區，為宏全營運第四支柱，公司在非洲投資持股，已提升為100％，將持續卡位具潛力的賣方市場，去年底於莫三比克，成立宏正廠，已進行整建廠房及設備移入作業，預計今年第四季正式投產，產能快速擴充，將積極拓展莫三比克市場布局與訂單爭取。 ... 福貞-KY表示，中國大陸啤酒市場金屬罐包裝滲透率，近年呈提升趨勢，主要受到消費習慣變化、即飲場景增加，及包裝輕量化需求帶動。此趨勢有助於擴大金屬包裝市場規模，福貞將持續強化產品競爭力及客戶服務能力，以掌握市場發展機會。 ... 福貞-KY2025年合併營收已達91.87億元，今年在永定廠新產線投產，加上第二季起調漲產品售價助力下，法人估福貞2026年度合併營收可望超過100億元，躍居大陸台資金屬空罐製造第一大廠。 ... 吉源表示，旗下工廠，包括湖北漢川、安徽滁州、福建廈門，及廣東清遠等工廠。吉源的主力瓶罐產品，包括三片式馬口鐵罐，客戶包括泰山仙草蜜、椰子汁、銀鷺的桂圓蓮子、好粥道及雀巢咖啡等多種罐型，公司將持續優化馬口鐵罐產線，以提升產能與效率。 ... 兩片罐方面，吉源的新產能建置完成，布局客戶需求，包括多元罐型滿足市場250/330/500毫升等空罐，持續研發產品減薄，提升產品價值。 ... | 公司 | 布局市場 | 重點進度 | | --- | --- | --- | | 宏全（9939） | 台灣、大陸、東南亞、非洲 | 越南PET阻隔瓶年產9千萬支，預計2027年量產；大陸與三得利、達能簽10年合約；印尼、泰國、莫三比克新產能陸續投產。 | | 福貞-KY | 中國大陸 | 永定廠新產線投產，第二季起調漲售價，法人估2026年營收有望突破100億元。 | | 吉源 | 中國大陸 | 兩片罐新產能建置完成，布局250／330／500毫升等多元空罐，並持續推動產品減薄。 | | 資料來源:資料整理：劉朱松 |
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"Jiahe Technology's annual dividend is 7.67 million yuan, with the equity registration on June 15 | Longbridge",longbridge.com,2026-06-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://longbridge.com/news/288864084,"Jiahe Technology's annual dividend is 7.67 million yuan, with the equity registration on June 15 | Longbridge ... Jiahe Technology disclosed its annual equity distribution plan for 2025, proposing to distribute a cash dividend of 1.00 yuan for every 10 shares to all shareholders, totaling 7.6675 million yuan. The equity registration date is June 15, 2026, and the ex-dividend date is June 16. The company's revenue for 2025 is 738 million yuan, a year-on-year increase of 13.74%, while the net profit attributable to the parent company is 20.5824 million yuan, a year-on-year decrease of 39.17% ... According to Tongbi Finance, Kunshan Jiahe Paper Products Technology Co., Ltd. (stock abbreviation: Jiahe Technology, stock code: 920392) disclosed an announcement on June 5, 2026. The company's annual equity distribution plan for 2025 has been approved by the shareholders' meeting held on May 25, 2026. Based on the existing total share capital of 76.6749 million shares, a cash dividend of RMB 1.00 will be distributed for every 10 shares to all shareholders, totaling a cash dividend of RMB 7.6675 million. The record date for this equity distribution is June 15, 2026, and the ex-dividend date is June 16, 2026. ... According to Tongbi Finance, Jiahe Technology was established in 2001 and is registered in Kunshan, Jiangsu Province. Its main business includes the research, production, and sales of packaging materials such as watermark cartons, color printed cartons, and cardboard. The company's products are widely used in consumer electronics, home appliances, food and beverage, and other fields, with production bases in Changshu, Guangde, and Vietnam Lisheng, possessing collaborative supply capabilities both domestically and internationally. Financial data shows that in 2025, the company achieved operating revenue of RMB 738 million, a year-on-year increase of 13.74%; net profit attributable to the parent company was RMB 20.5824 million, a year-on-year decrease of 39.17%, while the net profit attributable to the parent company after deducting non-recurring gains and losses was RMB 19.9541 million, a year-on-year increase of 2.00%. The revenue growth in 2025 was mainly due to the increase in the revenue period of the consolidated Vietnam Lisheng from 8 months in the previous period to 12 months in the current period. ... As of the equity distribution benchmark date, the undistributed profits in the consolidated financial statements amounted to RMB 152 million, while the undistributed profits of the parent company were RMB 157 million. The cash dividends will be directly credited to the shareholders' fund accounts through the securities companies that manage the shareholders' holdings on June 16, 2026, with 6 shareholders including Dong Hongjiang, Chen Yuchuan, Zhang Yi, and Duan Xiaoyong receiving their distributions directly from the company. The company also stated that it will adjust the repurchase price of restricted stocks according to the adjustment methods specified in the draft of the 2026 equity incentive plan. This dividend plan is consistent with the preliminary plan approved by the shareholders' meeting and its adjustment principles"
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,要约收购落地！嘉美包装6月5日复牌 逐越鸿智持股45%巩固控制权|复牌_新浪财经_新浪网,finance.sina.com.cn,2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.sina.com.cn/roll/2026-06-04/doc-iniahaiq9231911.shtml,要约收购落地！嘉美包装6月5日复牌 逐越鸿智持股45%巩固控制权|复牌_新浪财经_新浪网 ... # 要约收购落地！嘉美包装6月5日复牌 逐越鸿智持股45%巩固控制权 ... 要约收购落地！嘉美包装6月5日复牌 逐越鸿智持股45%巩固控制权 ... 嘉美包装(002969)6月4日公告，截至5月29日，苏州逐越鸿智科技发展合伙企业（有限合伙）（简称“逐越鸿智”）要约收购期限届满，预受要约的股东账户总数为36户，预受要约股份数量合计为2.15亿股，占公司总股本的19.59%，占预定要约收购股份数量的92.17%。本次要约收购完成后，逐越鸿智持有公司股份4.94亿股，占公司总股本的45.01%，公司股票自6月5日开市起复牌。 ... 公司于4月29日披露了要约收购报告书，逐越鸿智或其指定关联方向除其自身外的公司全体股东发出部分要约，要约收购股份数量为2.33亿股，要约收购价格为4.45元/股。本次要约收购期限为4月30日至5月29日。截至2026年5月29日，本次要约收购期限已届满。 ... 根据中国食品包装有限公司（以下简称“中包香港”）与逐越鸿智签署的股份转让协议有关约定，中包香港已通过要约收购方式将其所持上市公司1.03亿股无限售条件流通股份（占上市公司总股本的9.37%）出售给逐越鸿智。 ... 根据富新投资有限公司（以下简称“富新投资”）、中凯投资发展有限公司（以下简称“中凯投资”）与逐越鸿智签署的预先接受要约收购的协议，富新投资已通过要约收购方式将其所持上市公司8899.19万股无限售条件流通股份（占上市公司总股本的8.10%）出售给逐越鸿智；中凯投资已通过要约收购方式将其所持上市公司2327.91万股无限售条件流通股份（占上市公司总股本的2.12%）出售给逐越鸿智。 ... 本次要约收购完成后，收购人持有公司股份4.94亿股，占公司总股本的45.01%，社会公众股东持有的股份不低于公司股份总数的10%，公司股权分布仍符合上市条件，上市地位不受影响。 ... 逐越鸿智表示，本次要约收购旨在进一步增持上市公司股份，助力公司长远发展，同时巩固上市公司控制权，优化股权结构。本次要约收购完成后，收购人将本着勤勉尽责的原则，按照相关法律法规及内部制度的要求，履行作为股东的权利及义务，规范管理运作上市公司。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,周五复牌！002969易主，追觅科技俞浩成实控人|股份收购协议_新浪财经_新浪网,finance.sina.com.cn,2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.sina.com.cn/stock/relnews/cn/2026-06-05/doc-iniahxpc2026202.shtml,今日，嘉美包装（002969）发布公告称，苏州逐越鸿智科技发展合伙企业（有限合伙）（以下简称“逐越鸿智”）发起的部分要约收购已完成全部股份清算过户手续。收购方持股比例升至45.01%，正式成为公司控股股东，公司股票将于6月5日开市起复牌。逐越鸿智于2025年9月注册设立，实际控制人为追觅科技创始人俞浩。 ... 本次部分要约收购方案于今年4月29日披露，逐越鸿智以4.45元/股的现金对价，向除自身外的全体嘉美包装股东发起收购。本次计划收购2.3349亿股股份，对应要约报告书摘要披露日剔除回购专户股份后总股本的25%、报告书签署日总股本的21.26%，要约申报时间为4月30日至5月29日。 ... 此次收购为逐越鸿智主动发起，不触发法定要约收购义务，核心目的为夯实上市公司控制权、优化股权结构，全程无终止公司上市地位的相关安排。截至5月29日要约期限届满，据中国结算深圳分公司数据，本次收购共36户股东提交预受要约申请，累计预受股份2.1521亿股，占公司总股本的19.59%，完成原定收购规模的92.17%。 ... 本次预受股份主要来自公司三大老牌股东，其中中包香港出让1.0291亿股，占总股本9.37%；富新投资转让8899.19万股，占总股本8.10%；中凯投资出让2327.91万股，占总股本2.12%，三方股份转让构成本次收购核心标的。过户完成后，逐越鸿智合计持有嘉美包装4.9445亿股，持股比例45.01%，成为公司控股股东。同时公司确认，本次股权变更后社会公众股东持股比例满足上市规则要求，公司上市地位不受影响。 ... 资料显示，逐越鸿智2025年9月注册设立，实际控制人为追觅科技创始人俞浩。2025年12月，收购方先行通过协议转让，从中包香港受让对应总股本25.42%（原协议约定29.90%口径为剔除回购股份后占比）股权，该笔协议转让已于2026年3月27日完成过户登记。协议转让叠加本次要约收购后，逐越鸿智实际持股45.01%；此前交易预案规划两笔交易落地后合计持股54.90%，整体交易预案对应总对价约22.82亿元。 ... 本次交易附带业绩约束条款，原股东承诺2026至2030年，嘉美包装原有主业每年归母净利润底线不低于1.2亿元。据悉，嘉美包装主营食品饮料包装容器研发、生产及饮料灌装配套业务，合作客户涵盖王老吉、养元饮品、银鹭等行业头部企业。 ... 公司2025年经营承压，全年实现营收28.15亿元，同比下滑12.03%；归母净利润8660万元，同比下降52.75%，业绩下滑主要受饮料行业小年、春节旺季较短、礼品消费疲软影响。2026年一季度行业景气度回升，公司业绩大幅回暖，当期营收8.57亿元，同比增长42.31%；归母净利润6693.96万元，同比大增432.41%，增长得益于行业旺季订单扩容及可转债转股后财务费用下降。截至5月29日收盘，嘉美包装报18.65元/股，跌幅2.71%，成交额10.49亿元，主力资金净流出203.29万元。 ... 自2025年末俞浩敲定入主意向以来，二级市场始终预期追觅科技与嘉美包装落地产业协同，但截至当前，两家主体尚未落地任何实质性业务合作。在2026年5月12日的业绩说明会上，针对投资者关切的产线改造、资产注入、订单导入等事项，上市公司全部予以否认；俞浩同步出具书面承诺：取得上市公司控制权后36个月内不向嘉美包装注入任何资产，短期上市公司持续聚焦食品饮料包装主业，不切入追觅科技主营扫地机器人、智能家电赛道。 ... 资本端，追觅科技自2025年9月启动IPO筹备工作，尚未敲定A股或港股上市路径，若其上市进程延后，资产注入上市公司仅为远期备选方案。二级市场层面，本次4.45元/股要约收购价，对比5月29日18.65元的二级市场现价，价差超3倍，成为市场关注焦点。 ... 此前二级市场投资者普遍博弈追觅科技入主带来的资产整合红利，但公司一季度业绩高增完全依托行业周期回暖与财务优化，和追觅科技产业赋能无关，市场炒作预期逐步回归理性，同步扰动盘面。较大的价格差距使得中小股东预受要约意愿偏弱，本次要约预受筹码高度集中在三大原始股东，普通投资者普遍观望。 ... 业内分析认为，本次要约顺利完成过户，打消了市场关于公司股权结构不达标、存在退市风险的疑虑；后续上市公司基本面改善进度、实控人中长期产业落地规划，将成为左右股价的关键变量，投资者应审慎参与交易。 ... 复牌：嘉美包装（002969）、艾德生物（ ... 0068
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,不再“迷恋”六个核桃、王老吉，嘉美包装为何选择“牵手”俞浩？ - 今日头条,www.toutiao.com,2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.toutiao.com/article/7644861243429356038/,在构建追觅生态的过程中，俞浩肯定不会放弃万亿规模的饮品产业圈——这个宗庆后口中“永远的朝阳行业”。5月24日，嘉美食品包装（滁州）股份有限公司（简称“嘉美包装”）发布《关于苏州逐越鸿智科技发展合伙企业（有限合伙）要约收购公司股份的第三次提示性公告》。 ... 虽然该要约期限还剩5月29日一天，但在2025年末至2026年初，俞浩通过苏州逐越鸿智以22.82亿元对价，已完成对嘉美包装的控制权收购，嘉美包装事实已步入“俞浩时代”。 ... 嘉美包装作为国内食品饮料包装龙头企业之一，也是养元饮品、王老吉、银鹭、达利等饮料巨头的长期战略合作供应商，为何能成为“追觅生态”中的一环？以清洁智能家电起家的俞浩，能给嘉美包装，甚至整个饮品产业链带来怎样的“鲶鱼效应”？ ... 公开信息显示，嘉美包装是一家全产业链服务于饮料品牌的平台企业，旗下拥有17家企业，业务涵盖印铁、三片罐、两片罐、ABC罐、TBC罐、SBC罐、无菌纸包、各包材配套的饮料灌装OEM等多个板块。嘉美包装主要客户包括养元饮品、王老吉、银鹭集团、达利集团、承德露露、喜多多等主流饮料品牌。 ... 同时，基于公司“全产业链的中国饮料服务平台”理念，嘉美包装既能为轻资产成熟品牌提供策略性的配套代工服务，也能为新进入饮料市场的新品牌提供一站式服务和整体解决方案，客户包括山姆会员店、盒马、朴朴、柠檬共和国、可可满分、菲诺、好望水、永璞、锋味派等。 ... 直到如今，养元饮品也一直是嘉美包装的第一大客户。有消息透露，双方曾签署战略合作框架协议，约定养元年度用罐总量的60%以上由嘉美供应。 ... 这种长期协议虽然保障了订单稳定性，但也让嘉 ... 业绩与六个 ... 桃的终端动销深度挂钩 ... ，当六个核 ... 2025年，养元饮品旗下主力单品六个核桃营收仅44.30亿元，同比下滑17.55%；而嘉美包装也遭遇了营利双跌，2025年营业收入约28.15亿元，同比下滑12.03%；实现归母净利润约8660.02万元，同比下滑52.75%。 ... 业内普遍认为，近年来，随着养元自身面临增长瓶颈（礼品市场萎缩），其采购订单的收缩成为嘉美业绩下滑（如2025年净利润腰斩）的重要原因之一。如嘉美在财报中多次提及“受主要客户产品终端销量下滑影响”，所指的主要就是养元饮品。 ... 事实上，嘉美管理层早已意识到“把鸡蛋放在一个篮子里”的危险。在俞浩入主前的几年，嘉美已开始向“全产业链饮料服务平台”转型，试图通过拓展气泡水、燕麦奶等新品类客户来稀释养元的影响。 ... 2026年5月24日，可可满分与嘉美包装联合打造的滁州嘉可饮料有限公司正式启动投产，双方合作的第一条无菌冷灌24000产线同步亮相；时间倒退一年，新锐品牌柠檬共和国已与嘉美包装成立合资企业鹰潭嘉柠饮料有限公司，共同研发、生产、推广新品…… ... 由此可见，嘉美包装一直在推动与新锐品牌的合作层次从单一的供应链协同，提升至全产业链的深度整合，共同探索从产品设计到市场推广的一体化创新路径。 ... 经过多年转型调整，尽管当前养元饮品的占比已降至30%左右，王老吉等第二梯队客户占比约19%，但前五大客户合计仍有66%的集中度，仍然被外界视作未来发展隐患。 ... 另外，在嘉美包装的财报中还看到，其二片罐业务正面临“全面失血”的状态——营收暴跌38%，毛利率跌至-5.93%，陷入实质性亏损。 ... 财报显示，嘉美在鹰潭的二片罐项目投产后，2023年至2024年，其高峰期产能利用率仅在 74%–80%徘徊。而二片罐生产线设备昂贵，折旧和摊销是刚性支出。当订单填不满产能，单位产品分摊的固定成本飙升，直接击穿了微薄的毛利。 ... 另一方面，二片罐是高度标准化的“红海”市场。下游啤酒和碳酸饮料巨头（如华润、百威等）拥有极强的议价能力，导致加工费被压到极致。嘉美在财报中坦言，行业经过前几年的价格战，整体利润率仍处于修复期，难以覆盖原材料和运费成本。 ... 可以说，在行业龙头奥瑞金并购中粮包装、CR3集中度超75%的背景下，嘉美在规模与议价权上已处于劣势，也是最需要外部资本与智能化改造的“谷底时刻”。 ... 嘉美的选择，是饮品包材行业从“依附大品牌”走向“独立平台化”的一个缩影，也是饮品产业步入高质量发展周期、企业进入精细化运营阶段的证明。 ... 过去，包材商以绑定可口可乐、农夫山泉等巨头为荣；现在，这种绑定意味着议价权丧失与业绩波动风险。因此，头部包材商如奥瑞金、嘉美，都在主动降低单一大客户占比，转向服务分散化的新消费品牌集群，这已成为新的产业趋势。 ... 而未来的包材巨头，不再是简单的供应商，而是提供从配方研发、包材设计到灌装代工的一站式解决方案商。俞浩的跨界资源，也许是打通嘉美包装这“最后一公里”的关键催化剂。 ... 其次，追觅在智能化、数字化制造领域的技术积累，也恰好能匹配嘉美降本增效的改造需求。如前文所述，当前嘉美二片罐业务亏损的核心原因之一就是产能利用率不足，而通过智能化生产调度优化，俞浩可以帮助嘉美打通上下游订单数据，提升排产效率，减少产能闲置浪费，同时精准控制原材料成本，慢慢修复二片罐业务的盈利能力。 ... 更关键的是，俞浩手握追觅的流量与用户资源，本身又有打造消费品牌的野心，嘉美包装的全产业链代工能力，刚好可以成为追觅切入饮品赛道的跳板——依托嘉美包装给新消费品牌做代工积累的经验，俞浩可以快速推出自有饮品品牌，接入追觅的用户生态，给嘉美包装带来稳定的新增产能需求。 ... 对站在谷底的嘉美包装来说，绑定俞浩和追觅生态，远比继续依附传统饮料巨头更有想象空间，这也是嘉美包装选择这场“牵手”的核心原因。 ... 而对于行业而言，这场“牵手”已释放出一个明确信号：供应链正在被重新定义。若赋能成功，饮品产业链平台价值将被彻底重塑；若失败，这或许只是资本市场的又一次短暂狂欢。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,俞浩收购一家A股上市公司：3年内不进行资产注入丨消费参考 - 21经济网,www.21jingji.com,2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.21jingji.com/article/20260527/herald/1c782b17722bbc302bcf61a85641274b.html,A股上市公司 ... 进行资产注入 ... 1经济网 ... 俞浩收购一家A股上市公司：3年内不进行资产注入丨消费参考 ... 在资本市场 ... 5月24日，嘉美包装发布《关于苏州逐越鸿智科技发展合伙企业（有限合伙）要约收购公司股份的第三次提示性公告》。 ... 此次要约收购始于2025年年末。当年12月16日，逐越鸿智通过协议转让方式受让嘉美包装控股股东中包香港持有的上市公司约2.79亿股股份（占协议签署日剔除回购专用账户中股份数量后上市公司股份总数的29.90%）。 ... 仅过去一天，嘉美包装便披露公告称，逐越鸿智或其指定关联方向除其自身外的公司全体股东发出部分要约收购。本次要约收购上市公司的股份数量约为2.33亿股（占剔除回购专用账户中股份数量后上市公司股份总数的25.00%），要约收购价格为每股4.45元。同时，公告还披露，本次要约收购所需资金总额预计不超过10.39亿元。 ... 而此次的收购人逐越鸿智成立于2025年9月26日，其实际控制人为追觅科技创始人兼CEO俞浩。此后，嘉美包装的股票价格从2025年12月的3.93元/股涨到最高33.54元/股。 ... 需要注意的是，虽然俞浩正处于流量高位，但嘉美包装多次对外强调不涉及俞浩关联企业经营的机器人、扫地机器人等相关业务，主营业务仍为食品饮料包装容器的研发、设计、生产和销售及提供饮料灌装服务。“公司生产经营未发生重大变化，市场环境或行业政策未发生重大调整；生产成本和销售等情况未出现重大变化。”嘉美包装称。 ... 在2026年5月12日举行的业绩说明会上，嘉美包装提到，逐越鸿智不存在未来12个月内改变上市公司主营业务或对上市公司主营业务进行重大调整的计划；不存在未来12个月内对上市公司或其子公司的资产和业务进行出售、合并、与他人合资或合作、或上市公司拟购买或置换资产的资产重组计划。 ... “为进一步明确后续发展安排，俞浩及其关联方经梳理现有资产，考虑到其战略规划及业务发展情况尚存在较大不确定性，同时基于对上市公司主营业务发展的充分信心和坚定看好，为支持上市公司主营业务的持续稳定发展，在前期逐越鸿智承诺基础上，逐越鸿智实际控制人俞浩进一步承诺，取得上市公司控制权后的36个月内，俞浩及其关联方不会对上市公司进行资产注入，且目前不存在任何资产注入计划。”嘉美包装称。 ... 在一季度，嘉美包装营收同比增长42.31%至8.57亿元；归母净利润同比增长432.41%至6693.96万元。 ... 5月26日，嘉美包装报收20.38元/股，涨幅6.81%。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Flexible Packaging In Focus As W&H And GARANT Shine At Interpack | Modern Business Germany,modernbusinessgermany.com,2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://modernbusinessgermany.com/2026/05/27/flexible-packaging-in-focus-as-wh-and-garant-shine-at-interpack/,"Home Flexible Packaging Flexible Packaging In Focus As W&H And GARANT Shine At Interpack ... # Flexible Packaging In Focus As W&H And GARANT Shine At Interpack ... Discussions around the future direction of packaging were at the center of W&H’s booth. In addition to a collection of MDO-PE packaging produced worldwide, W&H also presented further sustainable sample packaging in a supermarket shelf display. ... ### Flexible Packaging In Focus As W&H And GARANT Shine At Interpack ... Interpack has once again confirmed its role as a key platform for international exchange in the packaging industry, concluding successfully for Windmöller & Hölscher (W&H) and its subsidiary GARANT Maschinenhandel (GARANT). ... The international trade fair for packaging, dosing, processing, and logistics took place in Düsseldorf from May 7-13, 2026. The booth was very well attended on almost all days, providing ideal conditions for in-depth discussions with customers and partners from around the world. The focus was clearly on personal interactions and direct dialogue: existing relationships were further strengthened, and new contacts were established. ... “interpack was, above all, a place for exchange and personal encounters this year,” summarizes Nicolai Bisgaard, Sales Director Asia Pacific at Windmöller & Hölscher. “Our discussions with customers once again highlighted how important close partnerships are to successfully address the challenges facing the industry together.” A particular added value for international visitor groups was the proximity to the W&H and GARANT headquarters. Many took the opportunity to gain a comprehensive impression of the companies’ capabilities and offerings on site. ... Sustainability played a central role in many conversations. A large proportion of customers showed strong interest in solutions that enable more sustainable packaging production. Efficiency, design for recycling (mono-material solutions),and the use of recycled materials were key topics in making packaging future-proof, especially in the context of European and global legislation. ... A common starting point for these discussions was the W&H“supermarket shelf,” which showcased a collection of international MDO-PE packaging solutions. Efficiently and industrially produced by W&H customers worldwide. In addition to these proven mono-material packaging solutions, the display featured a wide range of sample packaging for various applications, including paper-based solutions with and without barriers, mono-material packaging with and without barriers, and packaging solutions incorporating PCR. ... Solutions for paper-based packaging, as offered by the W&H subsidiary GARANT Maschinen, also attracted strong interest among visitors. In particular, applications in e-commerce, such as padded paper shipping and return mailers were identified as a growing market. In connection with the trade show, visitors also had the opportunity to take a closer look at automation solutions during the GARANT Open House in Lengerich. The focus here was on integrated processes, from bag making to end-of-line automation and palletizing. ... With many new impulses and strengthened partnerships, W&H and GARANT now look ahead to the coming months, continuing to rely on innovation, collaboration, and close customer relationships as key success factors."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,【关注】裕同科技新项目一期在昆山开业！年产值剑指8亿元|昆山市_新浪财经_新浪网,finance.sina.com.cn,2026-05-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.sina.com.cn/roll/2026-05-25/doc-inhzafpt5253416.shtml,【关注】裕同科技新项目一期在昆山开业！年产值剑指8亿元|昆山市_新浪财经_新浪网 ... # 【关注】裕同科技新项目一期在昆山开业！年产值剑指8亿元 ... 关注】裕同科技新项目一期在昆山开业！年产值剑指8亿元 ... 5月22日，裕同科技高端环保包装智能化产业基地项目一期正式开业。该项目是上市公司裕同科技深耕千灯、加码昆山的又一关键布局，深圳市裕同包装科技股份有限公司高级副总裁刘中庆，副总裁邓琴，副市长王昊，市农业农村局局长朱天舒，镇党委副书记、镇长朱飞波，各相关单位负责人出席活动。 ... 苏州裕同印刷有限公司是上市公司深圳裕同科技的全资子公司，于2004年落户千灯，主要生产精品彩盒、礼盒、纸箱等环保包装产品，配套国内外知名企业，先后获评江苏省企业技术中心、江苏省服务型制造示范企业、江苏省智能智造车间等荣誉。2025年，公司实现产值29亿元。 ... 裕同科技高端环保包装智能化产业基地项目总投资5亿元，规划总建筑面积8.5万平方米，于2024年8月签约，分两期推进。 ... 一期项目建筑面积约7.43万平方米，涵盖厂房、办公楼、仓库等，可满足生产、办公、仓储等全需求，已于今年1月交付入驻，计划于今年8月全面投产，达产后年产值可达8亿元，有望推动苏州裕同年产值突破35亿元。 ... 二期项目预留的约1.1万平方米厂房空间，也为后续招商及扩产提供弹性空间。同时，该项目对完善全市“1+2345”产业体系、壮大绿色低碳产业、带动群众增收具有重要示范作用。 ... 该项目是“政府引导、市场运作、村村参与、企业定制”新型集体经济发展模式的生动实践，在“抱团+定建”双轮驱动下，由14个村集体联合出资7800万元成立合资公司，收购盘活闲置土地，定向建设后租赁，实现载体建成即投用、竣工即收益。 ... 由金千灯乡村建设公司统一负责载体运营，联结政企村三方实行市场化运营管理，项目仅一年便建成投用，大幅降低企业建厂成本与周期，实现村级产业载体快速投产见效。 ... 项目租期10年，年租金超2200万元，可持续为14个参股村带来每年200-300万元的稳定收益分红，为激活村集体经济发展活力、促进共同富裕提供坚强保障。 ... 裕同新项目的正式开业，不仅为全镇产业升级注入了新动能，也为全市村集体经济发展提供了可复制推广的经验。接下来，千灯镇将持续深化政企村三方联动机制，同步加大招商引资力度，吸引更多优质项目入驻，共同推动村集体经济持续壮大与全镇经济高质量发展。
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,"Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million. | MarketScreener",www.marketscreener.com (S&P Capital IQ),2026-05-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/beijing-anjing-licheng-health-technology-partnership-enterprise-limited-partnership-signed-a-share-ce7f5adddc8afe22,"Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million. | MarketScreener ... | May. 23 | Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million. | CI | | --- | --- | --- | | Apr. 26 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd announces Annual dividend, payable on May 28, 2026 | CI | ... # Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million. ... Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd (SHSE:603976) from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million on May 22, 2026. A cash consideration of CNY 269.45 million will be paid by Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership). Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) will pay deferred payment of CNY 29.94 million cash. ... As part of consideration, CNY 299.38 million is paid towards common equity of ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd. Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) will pay 50% of the transfer price within five working days of receiving the Shanghai Stock Exchange confirmation document, 40% within five working days of transfer completion, and the remaining 10% within 300 working days of transfer completion. ... ### Latest news about ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd ... | May. 23 | Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million. | CI | | --- | --- | --- | | Apr. 26 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd announces Annual dividend, payable on May 28, 2026 | CI | | Apr. 24 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the First Quarter Ended March 31, 2026 | CI | | Apr. 23 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd announced that it expects to receive CNY 300 million in funding | CI | | Nov. 14 | Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Completes Business Registration of Hong Kong Unit | MT | | 25-10-24 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the Nine Months Ended September 30, 2025 | CI | | 25-08-22 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the Half Year Ended June 30, 2025 | CI | | 25-06-20 | Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Starts Optional Bond Redemption | MT | | 25-06-05 | Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging to Set Up Hong Kong Subsidiary | MT | | 25-04-29 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the First Quarter Ended March 31, 2025 | CI | | 25-04-09 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the Full Year Ended December 31, 2024 | CI | | 24-10-24 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the Nine Months Ended September 30, 2024 | CI | | 24-08-23 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the Half Year Ended June 30, 2024 | CI | | 24-04-26 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the Full Year Ended December 31, 2023 | CI | | 24-04-26 | ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd Reports Earnings Results for the First Quarter Ended March 31, 2024 | CI | ... ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co Ltd is a China-based company mainly engaged in the research and development, production and sales of pharmaceutical packaging materials such as pharmaceutical glass tube bottles. The Company's main products include borosilicate glass tube bottles and soda-lime glass tube bottles of different types and specifications, and it also produces various types of aluminum caps, aluminum-plastic combination caps and other pharmaceutical bottle caps. The Company's products are mainly used for the inner packaging of biological preparations, traditional Chinese medicine preparations, chemical medicine injections, powder injections, oral liquids and other medicines as well as health products. The Company mainly distributes its products in the domestic and overseas markets. ... Non-Paper Containers & Packaging ... News 3. Beijing Anjing Licheng Health Technology Partnership Enterprise (Limited Partnership) signed a Share Transfer Agreement to acquire 10% stake in ChongQing Zhengchuan Pharmaceutical Packaging Co.,Ltd from Chongqing Zhengchuan Investment Management Co., Ltd. for approximately CNY 270 million."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,NewJF-Greatview Deal Strains Profit and Hong Kong Listing,en.shuziqushi.com,2026-05-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.shuziqushi.com/new360576.html,"NewJF-Greatview Deal St ... Profit and Hong Kong Listing ... # NewJF-Greatview Deal Strains Profit and Hong Kong Listing ... Summarize: NewJF's Greatview takeover left the Hong Kong unit suspended, profit down sharply and liabilities above 3.2 billion yuan by 2025. ... NewJF Packaging's takeover of Greatview Aseptic Packaging has turned into a costly integration test, with the China-listed buyer facing weaker profit, higher debt costs and unresolved Hong Kong listing issues after gaining control of the company. NewJF listed on the A-share market in September 2022, announced in January 2023 that it would buy a 28.22% stake in Greatview, and completed a tender offer in early 2025.After the offer, NewJF held 97.76% of Greatview, leaving public shareholders with only 2.24%, below the Hong Kong Stock Exchange's usual 25% public float requirement. Greatview has been suspended from trading since February 18, 2025, while NewJF said on May 15 that it wants to keep Greatview as a Hong Kong-listed subsidiary.The financial pressure is now visible in NewJF's results. Its 2025 report showed revenue of 2.928 billion yuan and net profit attributable to shareholders of 43.7 million yuan, while recurring net profit fell 80.13% to 31.23 million yuan. Financial expenses rose from 19.46 million yuan in 2024 to 64.74 million yuan in 2025, and the article links that jump to acquisition-related borrowing and integration costs.Greatview's own numbers also moved sharply lower. The source says Greatview reported 2024 revenue of 2.24 billion yuan and net profit of 278 million yuan, but in 2025 revenue fell to 1.857 billion yuan and net profit dropped to 52.748 million yuan. NewJF's total liabilities exceeded 3.2 billion yuan by the end of 2025, while operating cash flow fell more than 46% year over year to 342 million yuan.The deal has also produced governance and disclosure questions. Greatview changed auditors, delayed financial reports and faced disputes tied to Wintipak, described in the article as a key vehicle for the former international business. The source says a December 2025 Hong Kong High Court-related emergency arbitration order required Greatview to stop contacting Wintipak customers and stop employee poaching, but the article claims the litigation was not disclosed for a long period on the Hong Kong exchange disclosure platform.For investors, the central issue is whether NewJF can restore Greatview's public float, publish reliable financial information and prove the acquisition can still create value without full support from the international business that once helped Greatview's earnings. The source frames the transaction as a failed 'snake swallowing an elephant' deal, arguing that debt, customer uncertainty, founder-team exits and industry competition from companies such as ORG Technology, COFCO Packaging and Tetra Pak have weakened the expected benefits."
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,沪江材料参展2026德国杜塞尔多夫包装展圆满收官！|沪江材料_新浪财经_新浪网,finance.sina.com.cn,2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.sina.com.cn/wm/2026-05-13/doc-inhxtqxn9388475.shtml,沪江材料参展2 ... 26德国杜塞尔多夫 ... 展圆满收官！ ... 材料参展2 ... 26德国杜塞尔多 ... 2026 年 5月7日-13日，为期七天的2026 德国杜塞尔多夫国际包装展览会（Interpack） 顺利落下帷幕。作为包装行业极具行业声望的专业盛会，本次展会集结了全球百余个国家的行业企业、技术大咖以及优质采购商，围绕绿色低碳、智能智造、轻量化包装三大主流发展方向，为全球包装产业搭建了交流互通、携手共赢的优质对接平台。 ... 南京沪江复合材料股份有限公司（证券代码：920204）也圆满完成了本次德国参展之行。此次远赴海外，沪江团队带着多款高阻隔创新包装产品登陆国际舞台，依靠扎实稳定的产品品质、成熟专业的定制技术方案，赢得了众多海外客商的青睐与认可，顺利实现了行业交流、商务对接、开拓国际市场的参展初衷。 ... 作为引领全球包装行业发展趋势的标杆展会，本次盛会涵盖包装材料、生产设备、包装成品等全产业链环节，拥有扎实的行业专业度与广泛的国际口碑。参展期间，沪江材料精准贴合国际中高端市场需求，通过实物陈列、现场技术解读、个性化方案定制等多种形式，全面展现企业深耕复合包装领域多年积累的技术实力，也让观展客户直观感受到产品在材质升级、结构优化、低碳环保、安全阻隔等维度的突出优势，为海内外客户输出专业度高、适配性强的工业包装定制方案。 ... 深耕复合包装领域三十余年，沪江材料一直专注深耕高阻隔工业软包装细分赛道。目前企业已布局南京江宁、溧水、广东惠州三大现代化生产基地，完成华东、华南核心产能布局，具备批量量产、快速响应供货的综合配套实力。 ... 此次德国展会圆满落幕，不仅是一场收获满满的行业交流之旅，更是沪江材料稳健布局、深耕国际市场的重要里程碑。借助本次参展契机，公司进一步拓展了海外合作渠道，提升了品牌国际影响力，同时深入了解欧美包装市场发展走向，为后续稳步开拓海外市场夯实了扎实根基。 ... 展望未来，沪江材料将继续以技术创新为发展内核，精研产品实力、升级服务体系、稳步拓展海外布局。坚守匠心专注主业，参照国际化严苛标准严控产品品质，持续为全球客户提供高适配度的工业包装解决方案，用心打造拥有强劲国际竞争力的中国包装民族品牌！
Jiangin Yonghe Packaging Products,,,,Exa,Jollibee Q1 2026 Earnings Report Highlights Challenges | radar,radar.ph (radar Business),2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://radar.ph/jollibee-q1-earnings-nearly-halved/,"Jollibee Foods Corp. saw its first-quarter net income plummet by 43.6% to ₱1.41 billion, despite a robust 9% rise in revenue to ₱76.55 billion. The conglomerate continues an aggressive international push, opening 181 new stores in Q1 alone—including a significant franchise expansion in China and its growing coffee and tea segment. ... Jollibee Foods Corp. posted a sharp drop in first-quarter earnings, with net income falling 43.6% to ₱1.41 billion from ₱2.5 billion a year earlier. This came as higher input costs weighed on profitability, even as the group continued to scale its operations. ... Revenue rose 9% to ₱76.55 billion, while systemwide sales increased 10.3% to ₱113.86 billion, supported by steady growth across both domestic and international markets. The Philippines expanded 8%, while overseas operations grew 13.5%, driven by continued demand across key regions. ... Expansion remained active during the quarter, with the group opening 181 gross new stores, including 149 abroad. China added 29 outlets under Yonghe King’s franchise-led model, while the coffee and tea business contributed 103 new stores, reinforcing its role in international growth. ... Management said underlying demand stayed firm despite cost pressures, supported by productivity initiatives, cost controls, and targeted actions to protect margins. ... The company is also rolling out price adjustments in the second quarter alongside efficiency measures. Portfolio adjustments continue, including early improvements in Smashburger and a strategic shift in China toward a higher-return franchising model. ... Executives said the group remains focused on managing near-term cost volatility while sustaining long-term growth and shareholder value. ... Revenue is up, but profits are down. Jollibee’s Q1 earnings nearly halved as the fast-food giant battles soaring input costs and a massive 181-store global expansion. ... The shift toward franchising in China and other regions is a capital-light move. It reduces the risk for JFC while allowing them to continue collecting royalty fees—a safer strategy in a volatile global economy. ... ### Jollibee scales coffee expansion as Compose Coffee gains traction in Taiwan ... Tags: Fast food industry inflation Philippines 2026 Jollibee net income drop 2026 Jollibee price adjustments Q2 Jollibee Q1 2026 earnings report Jollibee store expansion China Coffee & Tea Jollibee systemwide sales growth Smashburger profitability update 2026"
