Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"Germany's newest unicorn: Moss bags €30M to hit €1B valuation, aims for profitability by 2027 — TFN",techfundingnews.com (Sofia Chesnokova),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://techfundingnews.com/moss-germany-newest-unicorn-30m-series-c/,"# Germany’s newest unicorn: Moss bags €30M to hit €1B valuation, aims for profitability by 2027 ... - Berlin-based Moss has raised €30 million, bringing its valuation to €1 billion and making it Germany’s newest unicorn. - Portage and Cherry Ventures led the round, which is Moss’s first fundraising since its Series B in 2022. - Moss now serves over 5,000 businesses and generates more than €70 million in annual revenue. ... Moss has completed a €30 million Series C round, reaching unicorn status, according to a LinkedIn post by co-founder and CEO Ante Spittler. The fintech now joins Germany’s unicorn list alongside Finn and Neura Robotics, both of which passed the billion-euro mark earlier this year. ... Spittler founded Moss in 2019 with Anton Rummel, Ferdinand Meyer, and Stephan Haslebacher. It launched in mid-2020 as one of the first corporate credit cards for German startups. The company is based in Berlin, with offices in Tallinn and Amsterdam, and has about 339 employees. ... The company brings together corporate cards, invoice management, reimbursements, real-time budgets, and automated accounting on a single platform. For example, a mid-sized manufacturer can give department heads virtual cards with preset spending limits. ... Moss’s AI agents then automatically categorise and reconcile transactions, so there is no need to export spreadsheets for month-end accounting. The company says its agents process over two million transactions each month. ... Moss competes with US-based Ramp, which reached a $22.5 billion valuation in 2025, as well as Bulgaria’s Payhawk and Denmark’s Pleo. Unlike rivals, Moss offers AI that prepares work but always needs human approval before taking action. ... Portage, the fintech arm of Canadian investment firm Sagard, led the round. Cherry Ventures, one of Moss’s earliest backers, also participated along with other existing investors. Moss’ total funding is now about €160 million, up from €130 million at its Series B in 2022. ... says that control, rather than autonomy, shapes its product roadmap. In a survey of 471 finance leaders commissioned by the company, 48% said control was their top priority for AI tools, while only 6% preferred full autonomy. ... The new funding will help Moss develop more AI agents to automate financial processes for mid-sized companies. Its previous round was a €75 million Series B in 2022, led by Tiger Global Management, at a valuation exceeding €500 million. ... Moss serves more than 5,000 businesses across Germany, the UK, the Netherlands, and Austria, generating over €70 million in annual recurring revenue and achieving 65% revenue growth despite a challenging funding environment for European fintech. ... The global spend-management software market will be worth about $29 billion in 2026 and could reach nearly $46 billion by 2030, growing at a 12% annual rate. The main drivers are AI-powered automation and more adoption by small and mid-sized businesses. ... Whether ‘Finance AI’ will set companies apart in spend management or simply become another marketing term remains unclear and will likely be revealed in the next round of industry funding."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Berlin’s Moss becomes a unicorn betting on ‘controllable’ finance AI,thenextweb.com (Ana-Maria Stanciuc),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thenextweb.com/news/moss-berlin-unicorn-30m-series-c-finance-ai,"Berlin’s Moss becomes a unicorn betting on ‘controllable’ finance AI ... Another European fintech has joined the unicorn ranks. Berlin-based Moss has raised €30m in a Series C round that values the spend-management company at more than €1bn. ... The round was led by Portage. The specialist fintech investor headlined the raise, with existing backer Cherry Ventures also taking part, extending its bet on a company it has supported for years. ... The business has real scale behind the valuation. Moss serves more than 5,000 companies across Germany, the UK, the Netherlands and Austria, and reports annual recurring revenue above €70m. ... already run at volume. ... company says it processes more than two million transactions a month through AI agents, a sign that automation is not a roadmap item but a live part of ... That is where Moss is planting its flag. It is building a suite of configurable AI agents for financial tasks, pitching automation that a finance team can shape and supervise rather than simply switch on and trust. ... The positioning is deliberate. Moss cites its own research finding that 48% of finance leaders prioritise control over full autonomy, a nod to how nervous money managers are about handing decisions to a black box. ... Compliance is central to the story. Moss is a BaFin-regulated institution operating under Europe’s payment rules, holds security certifications and meets the bloc’s new digital-resilience regime, credentials that matter to cautious corporate buyers. ... The raise also reads as a signal about the funding climate. A fresh unicorn round in European fintech, a sector that has been through a bruising correction, suggests investors are again willing to write large cheques for the right growth story. ... Moss’s pitch leans on that revenue base. With ARR above €70m and thousands of paying customers, it can argue it is funding expansion from a real business rather than a speculative one, a distinction investors now prize. ... The competitive field is crowded, though. Denmark’s Pleo has pushed into the same territory, recently pairing a finance AI agent launch with layoffs, a reminder that automation cuts both ways for the companies building it. ... American rivals are circling too. Ramp has been expanding into Europe, buying the Stockholm fintech Billhop to gain a foothold, which raises the stakes for home-grown players like Moss. ... The control-first framing is also a hedge. If regulators tighten the rules on autonomous financial software, a product built around human oversight is better placed than one that hands decisions entirely to a model. ... For Moss, the raise is validation and a warning. A €1bn tag confirms European fintech still mints unicorns, but with consolidation looming, scale and a defensible AI pitch are now the price of survival."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Cover Genius Acquires Friendsurance: EU Bancassurance Deal - InsuraBeat,insurabeat.com,2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://insurabeat.com/cover-genius-friendsurance-bancassurance-eu/,"Cover Genius Acquires Friendsurance: EU Bancassurance Deal - InsuraBeat ... Cover Genius has acquired Friendsurance, wagering that Europe’s banks would rather buy a compliance-ready insurance layer than build one themselves. The Berlin-based insurtech, which spent more than a decade building the technology, bank networks and institutional compliance needed to sell insurance through banks, now becomes the bancassurance engine inside a global protection platform active in more than 60 countries and all 50 US states. Financial terms were not disclosed, and neither company has said what Cover Genius paid. ... Friendsurance describes itself as the Berlin-based insurtech powering digital bancassurance for the European market, and what it sells a bank is infrastructure, not a product line: a technology stack that lets a lender plug insurance directly into its existing banking app rather than negotiate a bespoke tie-up with an insurer from scratch. Cover Genius says the platform runs on PSD2 open banking rails and a compliance framework built for GDPR (DSGVO) requirements — the two pieces of regulatory plumbing that decide whether a bank can legally pull account data into an insurance quote and pass a customer’s information to a third party at all. That combination, assembled over more than ten years of bank integrations, is what Cover Genius is buying rather than replicating, as Tim Kunde, Friendsurance’s co-founder and chief executive, framed it in the deal announcement distributed by Business Wire. The Friendsurance team is joining Cover Genius, giving existing and prospective partners access to an expanded suite of protection products, according to Angus McDonald, Cover Genius’s chief executive and co-founder, who is quoted in the same release. ... A platform selling embedded cover through banks in Germany, Austria and Switzerland answers to three separate regulators at once — Germany’s BaFin, Austria’s FMA and Switzerland’s FINMA — and none of them treat bank-sold insurance as a footnote. The EU’s Insurance Distribution Directive explicitly names “bancassurance” operators, alongside agents and brokers, as a distribution channel subject to the same consumer-protection rules that apply to a traditional broker, per the directive’s text in the EU’s Official Journal. Switzerland, Friendsurance’s most idiosyncratic market in this deal, sits outside the EU and runs its own regime: a new insurance-intermediary supervision framework took effect on 1 January 2024, and every untied insurance intermediary must now register or file follow-up documentation through FINMA’s EHP platform, according to FINMA’s own description of the regime. Cover Genius frames the acquisition as accelerating a market-wide shift toward what it calls “Bancassurance 2.0,” equipping banks across the DACH region with an intelligent, compliant protection infrastructure — language that only holds up if the underlying paperwork, not just the software, is the asset actually changing hands. French regulators have already shown how seriously they police bank-sold insurance, fining Societe Generale over bancassurance IDD compliance failures, a reminder that owning three supervisors’ worth of clean compliance history is worth more to an acquirer than another country’s user base alone. ... EIOPA’s own survey work explains the logic without needing Cover Genius’s press office to spell it out. Around 40% of surveyed European insurance undertakings already have commercial relationships with insurtech start-ups and expect to deepen them, and insurers rank bancassurance among the top areas for cross-selling activity, alongside e-commerce and the mobility sector, according to EIOPA’s digitalisation survey of the sector. The regulator’s own term for what Cover Genius is now selling into DACH banks is “embedded insurance” — the cross-selling of insurance products bundled with other products to retail customers. None of that demand is manufactured by acquirers with something to sell: it sits against a backdrop of real premium growth that gives banks a reason to want a cut of it. Non-life premiums across OECD-monitored jurisdictions grew 7.4% in nominal terms in 2024, while life premiums grew 11% nominally across 44 reporting jurisdictions, per the OECD’s preliminary market dataset, which covers 47 OECD and non-OECD jurisdictions. A bank that already owns the customer relationship and the payment rail has an obvious incentive to capture a slice of that growth rather than watch an insurer or broker take it — provided the compliance layer is somebody else’s problem to have already solved. National Bank of Greece’s own move into an Allianz bancassurance partnership and Admiral’s acquisition of the commercial-fleet insurtech Flock both point to the same pattern: buy the distribution or the technology rather than build it against a live regulatory deadline. ... The uncomfortable number behind this deal is how little of European insurance actually moves through digital channels today. Digital channels generate on average just 19% of non-life gross written premiums and 9% of life GWP across the European insurance sector, and European consumers still overwhelmingly prefer physical channels — 34% buy directly from an insurer in person or by phone, 15% via an intermediary and 11% via a bank, according to the same EIOPA digitalisation survey. That is a thin base to build what Cover Genius calls “Bancassurance 2.0” on, but it is also the argument for buying rather than waiting: the number of EU intermediaries operating cross-border under an IDD passport grew 12% between 2020 and 2024, even as the total count of nationally registered intermediaries kept falling over the same two years, per EIOPA’s third report on the Insurance Distribution Directive. Domestic broker and agent ranks are thinning while cross-border, platform-based distribution expands — exactly the gap a bank-embedded insurtech is designed to fill before a traditional intermediary network can catch up. Cover Genius is not a niche buyer making that bet: it says it has already protected more than 70 million customers across 240 million policies, worth $3.2 billion in gross written sales, through partners including Klarna, Revolut, Stripe, Booking.com, eBay and Uber. Folding a decade of German, Austrian and Swiss bank relationships into that distribution machine is a bet that the thin digital slice of European insurance premiums grows fastest where a bank, not an insurer, owns the customer’s screen. ... The companies have not disclosed a purchase price. The acquisition is effective immediately, and financial terms of the transaction have not been disclosed. ... A digital bancassurance platform built over more than a decade for German, Austrian and Swiss banks, running on PSD2 open banking rails and a GDPR-oriented compliance framework. ... Cover Genius says it has protected more than 70 million customers across 240 million policies, worth $3.2 billion in gross written sales, operating in more than 60 countries and all 50 US states."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,FNZ divests banking business in Germany,www.fintechfutures.com,2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.fintechfutures.com/m-a/fnz-sells-german-banking-unit-fnz-bank,"FNZ divests banking business in Germany ... # FNZ sells German banking unit FNZ Bank ... The deal enables FNZ to focus entirely on its core wealth management technology business under the leadership of group CEO Blythe Masters. ... Wealth management technology provider FNZ has agreed to sell its banking business in Germany, FNZ Bank, for an undisclosed sum to private equity firm Advent International and a consortium of investors featuring HarbourVest Partners. ... FNZ says it expects to close the deal in H2 2027, subject to regulatory approval. ... assets under management ... FNZ has historically supported FNZ Bank with Platform-as-a-Service and Banking-as-a-Service solutions. The London-headquartered company states that this partnership will continue once the sale closes. ... FNZ originally acquired the business from German bank Commerzbank in 2019 for €154 million. ... Blythe Masters, who succeeded founder Adrian Durham as FNZ group CEO in 2024, says the deal ""supports FNZ's sharper focus on its core platform"". ... This strategy is backed financially by the $2.15 billion raised by FNZ under Masters' leadership. Her August appointment came with a $1 billion capital injection from existing institutional investors. ... Following that initial raise, more recent rounds include $500 million raised in April 2025 and a $650 million client-backed round closed the following November."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Inside DLC’s $58.5-million Filogix deal and what it means for brokers - CMT News,"www.canadianmortgagetrends.com (Jared Lindzon, Senior CMT writer •)",2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.canadianmortgagetrends.com/2026/08/inside-dlcs-58-5-million-filogix-deal-and-what-it-means-for-brokers/,"Inside DLC’s $58.5-million Filogix deal and what it means for brokers - CMT News ... # Inside DLC’s $58.5-million Filogix deal and what it means for brokers ... DLC Group CEO Gary Mauris explains how the acquisition came together and responds to concerns about competition after two major mortgage submission platforms came under common ownership. ... Dominion Lending Centres’ $58.5-million acquisition of mortgage technology provider Filogix has put two of Canada’s most widely used mortgage submission platforms under common ownership. ... DLC Group founder and CEO Gary Mauris told Canadian Mortgage Trends that Filogix will remain separate from Velocity and continue serving brokers across competing networks. However, others in the mortgage technology sector say the deal’s longer-term impact on competition will be worth monitoring. ... According to Mauris, Filogix parent Finastra Holdings began an auction process late last year, but initial talks between the two companies were called off soon after they began in February. ... “We disengaged with them, and then recently re-engaged with them over the last three weeks and brought the deal together very quickly,” he says. “We knew it was for sale, and we thought that we could be very good stewards of that asset.” ... Mauris adds that Finastra Holdings is owned by Vista Equity Partners and that the Texas-headquartered enterprise software investment firm has been selling off its Canadian assets recently. ... “They divested like six assets in the last 12 to 15 months, and we had done a really good job at Velocity in being a competitor, so they thought the timing was right to put the asset up for sale,” he says. ... Despite taking ownership of the platform, Mauris says DLC has no plans to shut it down or integrate it with Velocity. ... “We’re keeping the existing management team in place and there isn’t going to be any commingling of the DLCG broker group and the technology-utility group of Filogix,” he says. ... Mauris emphasizes that both platforms will continue to operate independently, though they will share some back-end services, such as human resources, payroll and compliance. ... “We’re never going to cross-sell, we’re not going to sell your data, it’s business as usual,” he says. “I don’t care who you are, whether you’re with DLC or a competitor, nothing is going to change day-to-day, and now you have a completely redundant system, which is good to have.” ... Mauris explains that the redundancy gives users an alternative that can help them avoid costly delays in the event of a system update or outage. He also assures customers that DLC intends to invest in the Filogix platform moving forward, particularly in its artificial intelligence capabilities. ... “They were owned by a company that wasn’t making much investment into the space, and now they’re owned by a company that is all about improvement and making investments,” Mauris says. “If you like Filogix today, it’s only going to get better.” ... Though Mauris is adamant that the DLC-owned platforms will remain operationally separate, the deal ultimately puts two of the country’s most popular mortgage submission tools under the same ownership. ... “I’m just wrapping my head around it, like everybody else,” says Tom Hall, co-founder and co-CEO of CRM provider BluMortgage. “It’s an exciting deal, and I think the overall sentiment brokers should have is an optimistic one, but it’s also a situation worth monitoring.” ... For much of its 34-year history, Filogix was the dominant submission platform used by Canadian brokers, with its Expert tool once used for more than 90% of all deals. That started to change in 2016 when DLC purchased Marlborough Stirling Canada Limited (MSC), which later became Newton. Today, brokers have a variety of options, including M3 Group’s BOSS, Lendesk’s Finmo and TMG’s Hurricane. ... “The competition was great; it was great for brokers, and it was really great for technology providers,” Hall tells CMT. “Better features for the brokers, better connectivity for tech partners, and it was a really dynamic environment, so I guess the question is, are we going back that way?” ... hough Hall says DLC’s acquisition could mark the start of further consolidation in the industry, he says the company has earned a certain degree of credibility in that regard. “They could have many times forced things on people, but they chose not to, and I think that should give people some comfort,” he says. ... Mauris, meanwhile, argues that platforms like Filogix don’t come up for sale often, and that the industry has little reason to fear that it will lead to further consolidation in the future. ... “If we were consolidating it, closing it down and moving everyone over to Velocity, you would have that argument, but we’re not taking choice away,” Mauris says. “We’ve got a proven track record of investing in Canadian mortgage technology and the Canadian mortgage industry, so we think we’re preserving choice.”"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Insurtech Cover Genius acquires Friendsurance for Europe bancassurance,beinsure.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://beinsure.com/news/cover-genius-acquires-friendsurance/,"Insurtech Cover Genius acquires Friendsurance for Europe bancassurance ... # Insurtech Cover Genius acquires Friendsurance for Europe bancassurance ... Cover Genius, the global infrastructure for embedded protection, acquired Friendsurance, the Berlin-based insurtech and digital bancassurance platform serving banks and insurers. ... The deal strengthens Cover Genius’s position in European digital insurance distribution by combining its global embedded protection infrastructure with Friendsurance’s local regulatory knowledge and banking technology. ... Financial terms were not disclosed. The acquisition takes effect immediately. ... Cover Genius said the deal creates a stronger distribution platform for banks across the DACH region, where financial institutions are under pressure to move beyond older cross-selling models. The target: insurance products embedded into everyday banking interactions, rather than sold as disconnected add-ons. ... Angus McDonald, CEO and co-founder of Cover Genius, said European banking represents one of the company’s strongest growth opportunities in embedded protection. He said banks across Germany, Austria and Switzerland need protection products that fit into customers’ daily financial lives. Friendsurance, he said, spent more than a decade building the technology, bank relationships and compliance framework needed for that shift. ... said the combined ... Friendsurance brings a European technology hub with experience in digital bancassurance. Cover Genius adds global reach, embedded insurance infrastructure and broader protection products. The companies are positioning the acquisition around Bancassurance 2.0, a model built on digital distribution, regulatory readiness and non-interest revenue for banks. ... The Friendsurance team will join Cover Genius. Existing and prospective partners will gain access to a wider suite ... protection products through ... combined platform. ... One part of the deal centers on Friendsurance’s architecture for PSD2 open banking rails and regional GDPR, or DSGVO, compliance. Cover Genius said this local structure helps reduce regulatory friction that often slows digital insurance launches for banks and fintechs in Europe. ... Tim Kunde, ... -founder and CEO ... Friendsurance, said the company was built to solve a specific problem for banks. Financial institutions want to offer modern customer-focused protection, but older infrastructure and compliance requirements make rollout difficult. ... said joining Cover Genius gives ... ’s team and technology the scale and resources needed to push the ... For Cover Genius, the acquisition adds regional depth in Europe at a time when banks seek fee income outside lending. For Friendsurance, it brings broader distribution and capital behind a platform already built for bank-grade compliance. ... Insurance Services acquires ... , adding farm, ag and business ... Mapfre will acquire ... 38.9 ... of Tuio as the Spanish insurtech prepares to expand across Europe and Latin America next year ... Mapfre USA agrees to ... Safety Insurance for $1 ... 54 bn, expanding ... Massachusetts and Northeast P ... Asia-Pacific insurance M&A slows despite India and Malaysia deals ... India and Malaysia posted large insurance M&A deals in Q2, though Asia-Pacific activity fell to its lowest level in five quarters"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Dominion Lending Centres acquires Filogix for $58.5 million - CMT News,www.canadianmortgagetrends.com (CMT Team •),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.canadianmortgagetrends.com/2026/08/dominion-lending-centres-acquires-filogix-for-58-5-million/,"Dominion Lending Centres acquires Filogix for $58.5 million - CMT News ... # Dominion Lending Centres acquires Filogix for $58.5 million ... The mortgage network says Filogix will remain operationally independent from its Velocity platform following the acquisition from Finastra. ... Dominion Lending Centres has acquired mortgage technology provider Filogix from Finastra Holdings for $58.5 million in cash, significantly expanding its technology and data presence across Canada’s mortgage industry. ... Filogix operates the Expert, Expert Plus and FXLink platforms, which connect more than 8,000 mortgage brokers with approximately 350 lenders and other industry participants. Its technology supports the mortgage application process from submission through underwriting, along with workflow, compliance and data functions. ... DLC said Filogix will operate as an independent, wholly owned subsidiary and remain operationally separate from Newton Connectivity Systems, which operates the competing Velocity platform. ... The company said the structure is intended to ensure uninterrupted service for Filogix customers and partners. DLC also committed to continued investment in Filogix’s technology, infrastructure, customer service and data security. ... “This is a highly strategic acquisition for the DLC Group,” said co-founder and CEO Gary Mauris. ... “By bringing both Filogix and Velocity under the DLC Group banner, we significantly enhance our access to real-time market data and insights, while adding important redundancy across our critical connectivity infrastructure to ensure reliable and operational resilience for our customers.” ... ### Filogix expected to add up to $18 million in adjusted EBITDA ... Filogix processed approximately $60 billion in funded mortgage volume during the 12 months ended May 31, according to DLC. The company expects the business to contribute between $15 million and $18 million in adjusted EBITDA during its first 12 months under DLC ownership. ... The acquisition is expected to immediately add to DLC’s adjusted earnings per share. ... DLC financed the purchase through existing liquidity and its credit facilities. As part of the transaction, it entered into an amended credit agreement with TD Bank that includes a new $65-million term facility. Its revolving facility was reduced from $40 million to $30 million. ... The company expects its ratio of total debt to pro forma trailing 12-month adjusted EBITDA to be approximately 1.65 as of June 30. ... “Over its 30-year history, Filogix has become a trusted partner to brokers, lenders and suppliers,” Mauris said. “Filogix will continue to operate as a standalone business within DLC Group, ensuring a seamless transition for customers and partners and a dedicated team focused on supporting all its partners.”"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Fossil spikes over the last week as investors eye turnaround potential (FOSL:NASDAQ) | Seeking Alpha,seekingalpha.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://seekingalpha.com/news/4623818-fossil-spikes-over-the-last-week-as-investor-eye-turnaround-potential,"Fossil spikes over the last week as investors eye turnaround potential (FOSL:NASDAQ) | Seeking Alpha ... # Fossil spikes over the last week as investors eye turnaround potential ... Aug 03, 2026, 1:54 PM ET Fossil Group, Inc. (FOSL) Stock By: Clark Schultz, SA News Editor Fossil Group (FOSL) jumped 19% in Monday afternoon trading in a move that was not tied to the release of any corporate news or SEC filing. Shares carved out a new 52-week high of $6.15 earlier in the session."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Why Cover Genius snapped up Berlin's Friendsurance,insurtechanalyst.com (Molly Snaylam),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://insurtechanalyst.com/2026/08/03/why-cover-genius-snapped-up-berlins-friendsurance/,"Cover Genius, the embedded protection infrastructure firm, has bought Berlin-based InsurTech Friendsurance, deepening its footprint in European bancassurance and reinforcing its reach across Germany, Austria and Switzerland (DACH). ... The transaction unites Cover Genius’ embedded insurance platform with Friendsurance’s digital bancassurance technology and local regulatory know-how. According to the companies, the tie-up will enable banks and insurers across the DACH region to weave insurance products into digital banking journeys while managing regional compliance demands. ... Friendsurance’s technology is built on PSD2 open banking infrastructure and includes a framework designed for regional GDPR (DSGVO) compliance. Its work has centred on helping financial institutions embed cover into customer journeys while streamlining implementation and regulatory processes. ... As part of the deal, Friendsurance’s team joins Cover Genius, bolstering the enlarged group’s capabilities in European banking and insurance distribution. The companies said current and prospective partners will be able to access an expanded suite of embedded protection products. ... Cover Genius is active in over 60 countries and all 50 US states, delivering embedded protection through partners such as Klarna, Revolut, Stripe, Booking.com, Uber and eBay. The firm said it has protected upwards of 70 million customers worldwide across more than 240 million policies, with over $3.2bn in gross written sales. ... Cover Genius CEO and co-founder Angus McDonald said, “European banking represents one of the highest-conviction growth opportunities in embedded protection.” ... Friendsurance co-founder and CEO Tim Kunde added, “Banks want to offer modern, customer-centric protection, but legacy infrastructure and compliance make it incredibly difficult.” ... The move underlines the ongoing momentum behind embedded insurance in Europe, with insurers and banks seeking fresh revenue streams by building protection products directly into digital banking platforms."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Cover Genius acquires Friendsurance to expand DACH banking,fintech.global (Molly Snaylam),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fintech.global/2026/08/03/cover-genius-acquires-friendsurance-to-expand-dach-banking/,"Cover Genius acquires Friendsurance to expand DACH banking ... Cover Genius, the embedded protection technology provider, has acquired Berlin-based InsurTech Friendsurance, expanding its presence in the European bancassurance market and strengthening its position across Germany, Austria and Switzerland (DACH). ... The acquisition combines Cover Genius’ embedded insurance platform with Friendsurance’s digital bancassurance technology and regulatory expertise. The companies said the deal will help banks and insurers in the DACH region integrate insurance products into digital banking experiences while navigating local regulatory requirements. ... Friendsurance’s platform uses PSD2 open banking infrastructure alongside technology designed to support regional GDPR (DSGVO) compliance. The company has focused on helping financial institutions embed insurance products into customer journeys while simplifying implementation and regulatory processes. ... Cover Genius operates in more than 60 countries and every US state, providing embedded protection through partners including Klarna, Revolut, Stripe, Booking.com, Uber and eBay. The company said it has protected more than 70 million customers globally through over 240 million policies, generating more than $3.2bn in gross written sales. ... Cover Genius CEO and co-founder Angus McDonald said, “European banking represents one of the highest-conviction growth opportunities in embedded protection. ... “Banks across the DACH region are under pressure to move beyond legacy cross-selling and deliver protection that integrates into their customers’ daily financial lives. Friendsurance has spent over a decade building the technology, the deep bank networks, and the institutional compliance required to make that possible. Together, we can offer European banking partners a clear advantage: a protection layer that is already compliant, highly optimized, and proven to drive platform yield.” ... Friendsurance co-founder and CEO Tim Kunde added, “Banks want to offer modern, customer-centric protection, but legacy infrastructure and compliance make it incredibly difficult. By joining the Cover Genius team, our people and our technology gain the global scale and resources needed to truly transform the market. We are incredibly excited to deliver a unified, world-class experience to European financial institutions.” ... The acquisition reflects continued investment in embedded insurance across Europe, as insurers and financial institutions look to generate new revenue streams by integrating protection products directly into digital banking platforms."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,FIC Partners Acquires Texas Battery Storage Developer Perfect Power · Big Energy,bigenergynews.com (Raeylee Barefield),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bigenergynews.com/2026/08/fic-partners-acquires-texas-battery-storage-developer-perfect-power/,"FIC Partners Acquires Texas Battery Storage Developer Perfect Power · Big Energy ... FIC Partners Management has acquired Perfect Power, the developer of Jaguar Energy Center in Texas, positioning the company to expand one of ERCOT's largest planned battery storage and solar platforms. ... FIC Partners Management announced it has acquired Perfect Power LLC, the developer, owner, and operator of the Jaguar Energy Center, a large-scale battery energy storage and solar platform serving one of the fastest-growing regions in the Texas electric grid. ... The acquisition positions FIC to continue expanding the project while pursuing additional energy infrastructure opportunities to meet growing electricity demand. ... The Jaguar Energy Center is a grid-connected battery storage and solar development with plans for up to 1.15 gigawatts (GW) of generating capacity across approximately 4,500 acres. ... The facility delivers power into the Electric Reliability Council of Texas(ERCOT) grid, which continues to experience rapid demand growth driven by population increases, industrial development, and new data centers. ... FIC Partners said the acquisition aligns with its strategy of investing in infrastructure assets that have both existing operations and future expansion potential. ... Co-Managing Partner Cay Freihofer: ""Perfect Power is exactly the type of opportunity we created FIC to pursue—a contracted, in-service infrastructure asset paired with a clear, accretive growth pipeline in one of the most attractive power markets in the country."" ... Co-Managing Partner Cyrus Aghili said Texas remains one of the nation's strongest long-term energy markets. ... Co-Managing Partner Cyrus Aghili: ""The Texas Triangle is at the center of multi-decade demand growth driven by population demographics, industrial expansion, and data center development."" ... Perfect Power CEO Tony Maselli said the partnership will help accelerate the company's next phase of growth. ... CEO Tony Maselli: ""Perfect Power has been looking forward to partnering with FIC to pursue this renewed growth chapter for our experienced team given our shared vision of scaling a best-in-class power platform."" ... FIC Partners has acquired Texas-based Perfect Power and plans to expand the Jaguar Energy Center, a battery storage and solar project expected to deliver up to 1.15 GW of capacity into the rapidly growing ERCOT power market."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"Frazier and Deeter acquires Gray, Gray and Gray in New England push - Boston Business Journal",www.bizjournals.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bizjournals.com/boston/news/2026/08/03/gray-gray-gray-acquired-by-frazier-deeter.html,"Frazier and Deeter acquires Gray, Gray and Gray in NE expansion - Boston Business Journal ... Frazier and Deeter has been acquiring firms nationwide over the past year."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Quantios announces strategic growth investment from Vista Equity Partners - IFA Magazine,ifamagazine.com,2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ifamagazine.com/quantios-announces-strategic/,"Quantios announces strategic growth investment from Vista Equity Partners - IFA Magazine ... As artificial intelligence continues to reshape financial services, investment in the technology firms supporting regulated businesses is gathering pace. Quantios, a leading provider of SaaS solutions to the global trust and corporate services industry, has been acquired by Vista Equity Partners(“Vista”), a global technology investor that specialises in enterprise software. Current investors HG and EQT will exit their investment upon completion of the transaction. ... The investment comes at a time when trust and corporate services firms are under pressure to do more with less. Regulatory demands continue to increase, entity volumes are growing, and clients increasingly expect faster, more AI-enabled services. ... Quantios has been at the forefront of that shift, helping close to 700 firms across six continents modernise key workflows, move away from legacy on-prem systems and build the foundations for the next generation of AI-enabled services. ... Adoption of Quantios Core, the company’s cloud-native platform, continues to gather pace as firms look for technology that can scale with them, reduce operational complexity and unlock the benefits of automation. ... Building on that foundation, Quantios has significantly expanded its investment in generative and agentic AI. More than 20 firms are already participating in its early adopter programme, with specialised agents now live in customer environments helping automate repeatable, process-heavy workflows across the front, middle and back office. ... Vista’s investment will bring more than just capital. As one of the world’s leading software investors, Vista offers deep operational expertise, a proven track record of scaling software businesses and access to a global technology ecosystem. ... This partnership will help Quantios accelerate product innovation, expand its AI capabilities and raise the bar for customer experience, support and delivery across its global customer base. ... “Quantios delivers mission-critical software that sits at the heart of how trust and corporate services firms manage and automate their most complex workflows,” said Patrick Severson, Senior Managing Director and Co-Head of the Foundation Fund at Vista Equity Partners. “As the industry faces rising regulatory demands and growing client expectations, we believe Quantios is strongly positioned to help firms operate with greater speed, clarity and scale. ... “Quantios has built a market-leading platform and real momentum in bringing agentic AI into live customer environments,” said Jake Hodgman, Managing Director at Vista Equity Partners. “We share the team’s commitment to modernising operations across the industry and are thrilled to support them in this next chapter of growth.”"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,FritzOS 8.50: Exciting New Features Coming to Your FritzBox! - World News | TakeToNews,taketonews.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://taketonews.com/fritzos-8-50-exciting-new-features-coming-to-your-fritzbox/,"FritzOS 8.50: Exciting New Features Coming to Your FritzBox! - World News | TakeToNews ... # FritzOS 8.50: Exciting New Features Coming to Your FritzBox! ... ### FritzOS 8.50: Exciting New Features and Enhancements for FritzBox Users ... The FritzBox has long been admired for its versatility, thanks in large part to regular firmware updates that continuously refine and enhance its capabilities. The upcoming FritzOS 8.50 represents a significant leap in features, promising robust new functionalities and improvements for users. ... While FritzOS 8.50 is still in development, users can already test a preliminary version (build number 8.40-xyz) through beta versions. This latest update includes a broad array of new features, solidifying the FritzBox’s position as a top choice for home networking. ... 8. Customizable FritzFon Softkeys: The FritzFon softkeys can now be programmed as quick-dial buttons for phone numbers or specific functions. ... 10. Device Prioritization: An automatic prioritization feature ensures that specific devices maintain the best possible internet connection. ... #### Notable Improvements in FritzOS 8.50 ... The update is not only about adding new features; it also enhances existing functionalities: ... WireGuard VPN Enhancements: Users can now manually set up WireGuard VPN connections, complete with customizable port forwarding options. A killswitch feature prevents data transmission during connection failures. ... Improved Parental Controls: The updated parental control system allows users to extend online time by 45 minutes, now applicable across shared budgets. ... Robust TLS Certificate Management: The automatic renewal of TLS certificates is now more reliable, ensuring long-term security for encrypted connections without user intervention. ... Additional Local Hostnames: Users can access the FritzBox via new local hostnames such as fritzbox.local, gateway.local, and router.local. ... Risk Warnings for Port Forwarding: New alerts inform users of potential security risks when setting up port forwarding, thus safeguarding the home network. ... Mesh Setup Without Button Press: Users can now integrate multiple Fritz products into a Mesh network directly from the router interface, eliminating the need for physical button pressing. ... Expanded DECT Compatibility: The update enhances support for DECT phones and smart home devices, ensuring stable connections and improved interoperability. ... Increased NAS Share Capacity: The maximum number of NAS shares has increased from 20 to 250, a boon for demanding home networks or small businesses. ... Expanded Internet Radio: Sender lists for internet radio stations will now include more countries, broadening listening options. ... FritzBox users eager to experience the new features can opt for beta testing. To do this, ensure your device is running the latest stable FritzOS version before proceeding with the installation of the test version. ... In conclusion, FritzOS 8.50 is shaping up to be a monumental update for FritzBox users, bringing a wealth of new functionalities and enhancements. Whether you’re a tech enthusiast or simply looking to improve your home network experience, there’s something valuable in this upcoming release."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Frenos Closes on $1.5M to Build OT Security's AI-Powered Simulated Pentesting Platform | citybiz,www.citybiz.co (Win Warfield),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.citybiz.co/article/880741/frenos-closes-on-1-5m-to-build-ot-securitys-ai-powered-simulated-pentesting-platform/,"Frenos Closes on $1.5M to Build OT Security's AI-Powered Simulated Pentesting Platform | citybiz ... Fulton, Md.-based Frenos, a cybersecurity firm specializing in operational technology (OT), has announced raising $1.52 million via a seed extension round led by Momenta and Exposition Ventures, joined by Riptide Ventures. It has so far raised $6.4 million. ... Founded in 2023 by cybersecurity veterans Brian Proctor and Harry Thomas, Frenos has built AI-native technology and enlisted infrastructure security firm Dragos’ co-founder and CEO Robert M. Lee as an adviser. ... Frenos is launching SAIRA Co-Work — a reasoning engine that has evolved into a persistent OT security co-worker that reasons over “live digital twin data” and guides users. It also runs fully simulated penetration tests that mimic real adversary behavior. ... Frenos claims growth momentum. Its annual recurring revenue (ARR) reportedly is up more than 10x since the start of 2025, and grew 215% in the first half of 2026. Pipeline is up 2.7x year over year, average deal size is up 5x. Bookings this year have quadrupled full-year 2025 level with five months remaining, the company said. ... The OT security market is projected to grow from $27.4 billion in 2026 to $58.9 billion by 2031, according to MarketsandMarkets, as ransomware and cyber-physical threats accelerate alongside IT/OT convergence."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Cover Genius targets DACH bancassurance with Friendsurance deal | Insurance Business,www.insurancebusinessmag.com (Mark Rosanes),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.insurancebusinessmag.com/uk/news/mergers-acquisitions/cover-genius-targets-dach-bancassurance-with-friendsurance-deal-583949.aspx,"Cover Genius targets DACH bancassurance with Friendsurance deal | Insurance Business ... # Cover Genius targets DACH bancassurance with Friendsurance deal ... ### The deal brings Cover Genius the compliance infrastructure needed to embed insurance into German, Austrian and Swiss banking platforms ... Cover Genius, the embedded insurance infrastructure provider, has acquired Berlin-based insurtech Friendsurance. The deal gives the San Francisco company direct access to the regulatory and distribution infrastructure required to operate in the DACH bancassurance market. Financial terms were not disclosed, and neither company has stated whether Friendsurance's founders retain any ongoing equity stake or earn-out in the combined business. ... The transaction, effective immediately, brings together Cover Genius' global platform with Friendsurance's bank-facing technology. Founded in Berlin in 2010, Friendsurance has spent more than 15 years building digital bancassurance tools for European banks and insurers, growing to around 100 employees and a network of more than 175 insurance company partnerships serving close to 150,000 customers. Its bank-facing brand, Friendsurance Business, has previously partnered with Deutsche Bank and cooperative insurer R+V Versicherung to embed digital insurance products into their platforms - exactly the kind of institutional banking relationship that underpins the compliance infrastructure Cover Genius is acquiring. Its architecture is built around PSD2 open banking rails and a framework to meet regional GDPR requirements, including the German adaptation known as DSGVO. ... Angus McDonald, chief executive and co-founder of Cover Genius, said banks across the region faced a specific distribution problem. ""Banks across the DACH region are under pressure to move beyond legacy cross-selling and deliver protection that integrates into their customers' daily financial lives,"" McDonald said. He said Friendsurance had spent over a decade building the bank networks and institutional compliance required to make that shift viable. ... The DACH region, covering Germany, Austria and Switzerland, has been one of the more persistent barriers to embedded insurance rollouts in continental Europe. Distinct licensing requirements, data protection frameworks, and the DSGVO have complicated product launches for firms without established local compliance infrastructure. That is the specific gap Friendsurance's existing bank relationships and regulatory groundwork are being acquired to close - infrastructure built over 15 years of operating inside German and Austrian banking compliance regimes is not something a foreign entrant could easily replicate through a licensing partnership alone. ... Tim Kunde, co-founder and chief executive of Friendsurance, said the deal was aimed at resolving that barrier directly. ""Banks want to offer modern, customer-centric protection, but legacy infrastructure and compliance make it incredibly difficult,"" Kunde said. ... For UK-based insurers and brokers with European distribution ambitions, compliance friction of this kind is a familiar obstacle. Embedded insurance can reach customers that traditional channels miss, but the regulatory complexity of each jurisdiction has slowed adoption well below its potential. ... Cover Genius operates in more than 60 countries and all 50 US states. The company has protected more than 70 million customers across 240 million policies, with US$3.2 billion in gross written sales. Its existing partners include Klarna, Revolut, Stripe, Booking.com, and Uber. ... The acquisition follows a US$100 million capital raise completed on July 14, backed by Vista Credit Partners, which valued the company at US$1.9 billion. The raise was partly earmarked for strategic acquisitions, and the Friendsurance deal is the first major transaction under that mandate. ... The European embedded insurance market is forecast to grow from US$3.05 billion in 2025 to US$18.29 billion by 2031, according to Mordor Intelligence. The UK holds the largest national share within Europe at 17.3%. The DACH region's banking infrastructure has made it a priority target for bancassurance deployment. ... The Friendsurance team is joining Cover Genius in full. The company said existing and prospective partners would be able to access an expanded product suite through the combined platform."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"Friendsurance sold for its paperwork, not its big idea",thenextweb.com (Cristian Dina),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thenextweb.com/news/cover-genius-friendsurance-acquisition-bancassurance-berlin,"Cover Genius has acquired Friendsurance, the Berlin company that invented peer-to-peer insurance. The deal took effect immediately, and neither side disclosed a price. ... “Friendsurance has spent over a decade building the technology, the deep bank networks, and the institutional compliance required to make that possible,” said Angus McDonald, chief executive and co-founder of Cover Genius, in the company announcement. ... The specifics sit lower in the text. Cover Genius cites an architecture built on PSD2 open banking rails, and a framework designed for regional GDPR requirements, known in Germany as DSGVO. ... That combination, it says, “helps neutralize the complex regional regulatory landscapes that typically stall digital product rollouts”. ... Friendsurance’s own site lists the other asset. Its platform connects to more than 175 insurers and processes unstructured data using machine learning. ... Both firms are chasing ... the fees as non ... Tim Kunde, co-founder and chief executive of Friendsurance, framed the sale as a scale problem solved. ... “We built Friendsurance to solve a clear friction point. Banks want to offer modern, customer-centric protection, but legacy infrastructure and compliance make it incredibly difficult,” he said. ... Demand looks real. A YouGov survey commissioned by Friendsurance found 52% of Germans interested in managing insurance contracts through online banking. Interest peaked at 67% among 35 to 44 year olds, and dropped to 42% among the over 55s. ... The timing repays attention. On 14 July, Cover Genius announced $100m backed by Vista Credit Partners, at a $1.9bn valuation. ... Fourteen days later it bought a company. Vista Credit Partners supplies credit rather than equity, so that was financing rather than a fresh round of ownership. ... Cover Genius is not a small buyer. It operates in more than 60 countries and all 50 US states, and counts Klarna, Revolut, Stripe, Booking.com, eBay and Uber among its partners. ... Both Klarna and Revolut have been pushing into regulated banking themselves, which makes them natural customers for an insurance layer. ... Genius sells insurance that appears inside somebody else’s checkout. Its XCover platform carries ... policies, XClaim pays approved claims in more than 90 currencies, ... BrightWrite prices the ... in real time. ... The company has protected more than 73 million customers across 240 million policies, on $3.2bn of gross written sales. ... Banks are a harder sell than airlines. Selling ... policy beside a current account triggers rules that ... apply at a travel checkout, which is the ... Friendsurance is ... Friendsurance had a harder run than its early coverage suggested. It raised $15.3m in March 2016, in a round led by Horizons Ventures, EU-Startups reported. ... By 2020 it was reaching for debt instead. Carrier Management reported that June that the company had secured close to $1.7m through the lending platform creditshelf. ... European fintech has been bracing for consolidation for some time. Valuations keep climbing at the top of insurtech, with Ominimo reaching $1.4bn and Alan passing $5bn, while smaller platforms look for a buyer. ... Undisclosed terms usually signal a price nobody wants framed. The peer-to-peer idea made Friendsurance famous. The compliance stack is what made it sellable."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Cover Genius Acquires Friendsurance to Accelerate Embedded Protection Across European Banking | AP News,apnews.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://apnews.com/press-release/business-wire/press-release-33ec61381ea24c0fa69d6b4b2b91611c,"Cover Genius Acquires Friendsurance to Accelerate Embedded Protection Across European Banking | AP News ... Cover Genius Acquires Friendsurance to Accelerate Embedded Protection Across European Banking ... & BERLIN ... )--Jul ... Cover Genius, the global infrastructure for embedded protection, today announced its acquisition of Friendsurance, the Berlin-based insurtech and digital bancassurance platform for banks and insurers. The transaction establishes a powerhouse in European digital insurance distribution, combining Cover Genius’s market-leading global infrastructure with Friendsurance’s deep local regulatory expertise and bank-grade technology. ... “European banking represents one of the highest-conviction growth opportunities in embedded protection,” said Angus McDonald, CEO and Co-founder of Cover Genius. “Banks across the DACH region are under pressure to move beyond legacy cross-selling and deliver protection that integrates into their customers’ daily financial lives."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Frenos Raises $1.52M in Seed Extension Funding,www.finsmes.com (FinSMEs),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.finsmes.com/2026/07/frenos-raises-1-52m-in-seed-extension-funding.html,"Frenos Raises $1.52M in Seed Extension Funding ... Home USA Frenos Raises $1.52M in Seed Extension Funding ... # Frenos Raises $1.52M in Seed Extension Funding ... July 28, 2026 ... Frenos, a Charlotte, NC-based provider of an AI-native operational technology (OT) security posture management platform, raised $1.52M in Seed extension financing. ... The round was led by Momenta and Exposition Ventures with participation from Riptide Ventures. ... The raise brought the total amount to $6.4M. ... The company intends to use the funds to grow its customer success team supporting its expansion across critical infrastructure and defense, and expand its AI R&D team. ... Led by CEO Brian Proctor, Frenos provides a simulated AI penetration testing platform that combines digital twin technology with an AI reasoning agent to continuously validate OT security posture. The solution runs fully simulated penetration tests that mimic real adversary behavior to identify and prioritize exploitable risks with zero impact on operations, hardware, or scanning downtime."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Frenos Raises $1.52M for AI-Powered OT Security | Frenos,frenos.io,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://frenos.io/resource/frenos-closes-usd1-52-million-to-advance-ot-security-s-first-ai-powered-simulated-penetration,"Frenos Raises $1.52M for AI-Powered OT Security | Frenos ... FULTON, Md., July 28, 2026 – AI-native OT security pioneer Frenos today announced a $1.52 million seed extension round led by leading industrial investors Momenta, Exposition Ventures, and joined by Riptide Ventures, bringing the company's total funding to $6.4 million. Frenos will use the capital to grow its customer success team, supporting a rapidly expanding customer base across critical infrastructure enterprises and defense, and to expand its AI R&D team. ... That investment is already producing results: alongside the round, Frenos is launching SAIRA Co-Work, evolving its reasoning engine into a persistent OT security co-worker that reasons over live digital twin data and guides users through complex investigations with evidence-based insights. Research will continue toward a next-generation foundation model for long-context reasoning and autonomous engineering workflows, a core component of the company's future AI-powered simulated penetration testing platform. ... for the operators ... The round follows a year of significant momentum. Annual recurring revenue is up more than 10x since the start of 2025, growing 215 percent in the first half of 2026. Pipeline is up 2.7x year over year, average deal size is up 5x as Frenos moves upmarket, and 2026 bookings have already quadrupled full-year 2025 with five months remaining. In one customer environment, SAIRA analyzed more than 12,000 OT vulnerability findings and surfaced the eight that were actually exploitable, cutting remediation noise by 99.9 percent. ... Industrial leaders know that OT cyber resilience is essential for protecting revenue and uptime, particularly as AI accelerates both automation and attack sophistication,” said Carlos Furlotti ... Traditional IT security tools fail in industrial settings ... Frenos delivers the precise, safe visibility operators ... to manage risk without threatening production. The team ... are proud to back them ... Frenos is the industry’s first fully simulated AI penetration testing platform, combining digital twin technology with an AI reasoning agent that thinks like an adversary to reveal every attack path in your OT environment, risk-free. Frenos transforms how operational technology (OT) cybersecurity teams assess the cybersecurity posture of mission-critical sites and environments, reducing assessment time from months to minutes with zero impact on operations. Follow our blog, connect with us on LinkedIn, or visit our website at www.frenos.io. ... ### Frenos and Tecplix Partner to Deliver Continuous, Simulated OT Penetration Testing to Critical Infrastructure Operators ... Press-Critical Infrastructure-JUN 18, 2026Frenos and Tecplix partner to deliver continuous, simulated OT penetration testing. Safely reveal attack paths in critical infrastructure without downtime. ... ### Frenos Debuts First-Ever Free Assessment to Defend Against ‘Mythos-Class’ Autonomous Threats in Critical Infrastructure ... Press-Critical Infrastructure-APR 30, 2026Frenos offers a free one-day Mythos Readiness Assessment, utilizing AI and digital twins to identify critical infrastructure vulnerabilities without impacting production. ... ### Frenos Launches Industry’s First IT/OT Cybersecurity Intelligence Catalog to Power Transparent AI-Driven Defense ... Press-Critical Infrastructure-FEB 18, 2026New “Adversary Intelligence Engine” Community Edition Gives Defenders Visibility Into How AI Analyzes Attack Paths in Operational Technology Environments"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Danfoss Looks to Grow Fluid Conveyance Division with Alfagomma Acquisition | Power & Motion Tech,www.powermotiontech.com (Sara Jensen),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.powermotiontech.com/hydraulics/article/55393146/danfoss-power-solutions-danfoss-looks-to-grow-fluid-conveyance-division-with-alfagomma-acquisition,"Danfoss Looks to Grow Fluid Conveyance Division with Alfagomma Acquisition | Power & Motion Tech ... Danfoss Looks to Grow Fluid Conveyance Division with Alfagomma Acquisition ... Danfoss Power Solutions’ Daniel Winter discusses how the acquisition of Alfagomma will aid the company’s ability to further grow its Fluid Conveyance division where it sees numerous market opportunities. ... - Daniel Winter, President of Danfoss Power Solutions, provides his insights on how the acquisition of hose and fittings manufacturer Alfagomma will benefit the company's long-term growth strategies. - Winter offers his perspectives on the increased product offerings, production capacity and technological capabilities that will now be possible to help drive growth for the Fluid Conveyance division. ... Danfoss recently signed an agreement to acquire hose and fittings manufacturer Alfagomma to help further grow its Fluid Conveyance division. ... On July 9, Danfoss announced the signing of an agreement to acquire Italy-based Alfagomma, a manufacturer of hoses and fittings. Through this acquisition, the company aims to further grow its Fluid Conveyance division. ... This is the second acquisition the company has made in the past year to aid growth for its fluid conveyance business. In December 2025, Danfoss closed its acquisition of Hydro Holding which develops hose fittings. ... To learn more about the opportunities Danfoss sees for its Fluid Conveyance division and how they fit in with the company’s overall growth strategy, I spoke with Daniel Winter, President of Danfoss Power Solutions. He offered his insights on how the acquisition of Alfagomma will help increase localized production capacity in more customer markets, potential technological benefits it will bring and more. ... Daniel Winter: Acquiring Alfagomma aligns with Danfoss' long-term strategy, part of which is to accelerate profitable growth. Combining the Alfagomma business with the Fluid Conveyance division — a core business within Danfoss Power Solutions — will create a leading global player in hydraulic and industrial hose manufacturing and distribution. ... The acquisition brings together two highly complementary businesses that, together, offer a more complete and competitive fluid conveyance offering. This positions us to gain market share and accelerate long-term growth. ... Through its acquisition of Alfagomma, Danfoss will be able to enhance its fluid conveyance technology offering to help drive long-term growth for this segment of its business. ... Daniel Winter: Fluid conveyance is a strategic growth engine for Danfoss Power Solutions and one of the fastest-growing divisions in the Danfoss Group. We are growing not only through acquisition, but also organically. ... Fluid conveyance is a large, highly diverse industry with significant potential. Since entering the market through the Eaton Hydraulics acquisition, Danfoss has identified opportunities across a wide range of sectors, and we continue to uncover applications where the movement of fluids is essential. ... With demand spanning nearly every industry, we are only beginning to capture the market’s full potential. ... Daniel Winter: In the fluid conveyance industry, success depends on being able to provide hoses and fittings — sometimes complete assemblies — as well as local service and supply. Danfoss has strong hose manufacturing and fitting production capabilities globally, but those capabilities are not always located in the same regions. Alfagomma closes those gaps. ... Daniel Winter, President of Danfoss Power Solutions, said the acquisition of Alfagomma will help strengthen Danfoss' service and supply to customers in various markets. ... For example, Danfoss produces hoses in Brazil, whereas Alfagomma manufactures fittings there. Danfoss currently serves Asia Pacific customers with hoses produced in Turkey, while one of Alfagomma’s primary hose manufacturing sites is in Malaysia. South America and Asia are key regions for the Fluid Conveyance division due to their expected growth potential. ... With Alfagomma, we will strengthen our service and supply to customers in those markets, which will improve our local market position and enable us to capitalize on that growth. ... Beyond local production, the acquisition enhances our portfolio and expertise in markets where Alfagomma has established leadership. Alfagomma is particularly strong in oil and gas, with a dedicated manufacturing footprint, deep technical knowledge, and a comprehensive product range. ... The company also has extensive experience serving the mining industry, which requires a different go-to-market strategy and specialized customer support. We will learn from Alfagomma’s success and invest in what works. By combining our strengths, we can offer broader market coverage, uncover new opportunities, and grow in these segments and others. ... Daniel Winter: By bringing together our engineering expertise, application knowledge, and product portfolios, we will accelerate innovation, expand solution offerings, and create more value for customers than either company could achieve independently. ... Industrial hose is one of the clearest areas where we see technology benefits. Alfagomma's strong expertise in industrial hose complements our existing capabilities, enabling us to expand our offering, bring new solutions to market more quickly, and better address the evolving needs of industrial hose customers."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Presto strengthens its market position in Germany through acquisition of F&H Feuerschutz GmbH & Co. KG | Presto,www.mynewsdesk.com,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mynewsdesk.com/se/presto/pressreleases/presto-strengthens-its-market-position-in-germany-through-acquisition-of-f-och-h-feuerschutz-gmbh-och-co-kg-3459251,"Presto strengthens its market position in Germany through acquisition of F&H Feuerschutz GmbH & Co. KG | Presto ... # Presto strengthens its market position in Germany through acquisition of F&H Feuerschutz GmbH & Co. KG ... Jockel Brandschutz, part of Presto Group (""Presto""), Europe’s leading provider of fire protection, first aid, and safety training, has successfully completed the acquisition of F&H Feuerschutz GmbH & Co. KG. ... With this acquisition, Jockel Brandschutz continues to expand its regional presence, with a particular focus on strengthening its service operations in southern Germany and the greater Karlsruhe area. ... F&H Feuerschutz, headquartered in Walzbachtal, Baden-Württemberg, is an established provider of preventive fire protection with a broad service portfolio. Its offering spans the full spectrum of fire safety maintenance, including fire extinguisher servicing, inspection and maintenance of smoke-heat-exhaust systems, fire safety doors and hydrants, as well as the development of evacuation and emergency plans. ... Dirk Hoffmann, Managing Director of F&H Feuerschutz, will continue to lead the company, ensuring continuity for customers, employees, and partners. ... “F&H Feuerschutz stands for high technical competence, strong customer loyalty, and a clear regional foothold. It is precisely this combination that makes the company an ideal addition for us. With this acquisition, we are strengthening our presence in southern Germany and creating the foundation to serve our customers even more closely,” says Laura Peters, CEO of Jockel Brandschutztechnik-Service GmbH. ... “It was important to me to find a solution that puts our company in a strong position for the long term, both for our customers and for our employees. In Jockel, we have found a partner that shares our values and brings the right conditions to lead the company reliably into the future. This creates new opportunities to further develop our service offering and sustainably expand our market position,” adds Dirk Hoffmann. ... With this acquisition, Jockel Brandschutztechnik-Service GmbH continues its consistent growth trajectory in Germany, reinforcing its ambition to serve customers nationwide even more closely, quickly, and comprehensively with high technical expertise, reliable service, and a clear focus on long-term partnerships. ... Presto is Europe’s leading player with a comprehensive offer in fire protection, first aid, and safety training. Presto was founded in 1959 in Katrineholm, Sweden, and has since grown into a group with a turnover of SEK 3.5 billion and 2,200 employees in 135 locations. The company serves more than 145,000 customers across Europe, providing complete safety solutions that protect businesses and save lives. The head office is in Stockholm, Sweden. More information: www.presto.se ... F&H Feuerschutz GmbH & Co. KG, headquartered in Walzbachtal, has been active in preventive fire protection for over 31 years. The company offers a comprehensive range of services, from the maintenance and servicing of fire protection systems to training and consulting. With strong technical expertise, long-standing customer relationships and a solid regional presence, F&H Feuerschutz serves customers across the region and southern Germany. More information: www.fh-feuerschutz.de"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Maryland microgrid lands US$30 million in tax equity - Energy-Storage.News,www.energy-storage.news (April Bonner),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.energy-storage.news/growing-interest-in-us-microgrids-attracts-tax-equity-investor-foss-company-to-us30-million-maryland-deal/,"Maryland microgrid lands US$30 million in tax equity - Energy-Storage.News ... # ‘Growing interest’ in US microgrids attracts tax equity investor Foss & Company to US$30 million Maryland deal ... Foss & Company, a tax equity investor that has deployed over US$11 billion since 1983, recently closed financing for a microgrid project combining solar and energy storage—one of the first such deals to secure institutional tax equity backing. Image: Foss & Company via LinkedIn ... Energy-Storage.news Premium speaks with Bryen Alperin and Sophie Brkovic of tax equity investor Foss & Company about the company’s entrance into microgrids. ... Around the same time, the Paskenta Band of Nomlaki Indians partnered with Open Access Technology International (OATI) to integrate advanced microgrid controls into a two-part solar and battery energy storage system (BESS) project in Northern California, to enable the tribal community to operate independently of the local utility grid during outages or periods of grid instability. ... Microgrids are attracting institutional tax equity investment as project sizes reach viable thresholds and developers gain operational experience. ... Foss & Company, a tax equity investor that has deployed over US$11 billion since 1983, recently closed financing for a microgrid project combining solar and energy storage—one of the first such deals to secure institutional tax equity backing. ... Announced 8 July, Foss & Company closed a US$30 million Section 48 tax equity investment in a microgrid system from energy as a service (EaaS) provider AlphaStruxure, located in Montgomery County, Maryland, US, designed to integrate solar PV and battery storage to power a public transit facility and its transitioning electric bus fleet. ... The microgrid is expected to achieve commercial operations in August 2026 and “is projected to generate more than 6,000MWh of clean energy annually.” ... The transaction marks Foss & Company’s first partnership with AlphaStruxure and represents the firm’s entry into the microgrid sector. ... Alperin, managing director, and Brkovic, vice president of energy & infrastructure project finance at Foss & Company, discuss the factors that made this investment possible, how they approached valuation of the energy storage component, and the outlook for distributed energy resources (DERs) in tax equity markets. ... Foss & Company claims that it has historically moved into emerging technologies as they mature. After the Inflation Reduction Act (IRA) passed, the firm quickly entered standalone battery storage. ... Alperin and Brkovic highlight three factors made this microgrid project viable: a creditworthy developer with operational experience, sufficient project size, and proven technology components. ... “Some of the earlier microgrid opportunities we saw were just a bit too small for a lot of our investors who tend to be large banks, insurance companies, and Fortune 500 corporates,” Alperin says. “Generally, we’re typically transacting in the US$20 million and above tax credits range, but really ideally closer to US$50 or US$100 million.” ... ## Distributed energy portfolio expansion ... Foss & Company established its renewables platform approximately nine years ago with distributed generation solar. The firm is now expanding into other distributed energy or distributed generation (DG) technologies, particularly energy storage. ... “The DG space has continued to be one of our primary business areas,” Alperin says. “We’re looking now at expanding that beyond what was primarily solar into other technologies. Obviously, there’s a lot of energy storage that’s going to get built in this country.” ... If the solar tax credit expires as scheduled, Foss expects energy storage, both utility-scale and distributed, to represent a larger share of its investment volume. The firm is also monitoring geothermal, fuel cells, and potentially small or micro nuclear projects. ... “We might see more distributed battery portfolios popping up,” Alperin highlights. “A lot of the solar developers we’ve worked with over the years are starting to diversify their business and develop more batteries as well.” ... ## Market adoption varies by investor type ... Microgrids are gaining traction but remain less common than utility-scale projects among the largest tax equity investors. ... “The big banks—the top four or five in the country—may still prefer to do utility-scale projects because they can get more scale with fewer projects,” Alperin says. “But for groups like Foss that are syndicators able to navigate the complexities of these DG projects more efficiently, there is growing interest in microgrids.” ... Alperin adds, “I wouldn’t say that (microgrids are) as popular as the utility-scale solar projects, but we’re probably seeing some increased competition from other investors over time on these kinds of assets. But it’s a very opaque market, so it’s hard to say.” ... Foss & Company’s microgrid financing demonstrates that distributed energy systems can attract institutional tax equity when they meet requirements for project size, developer quality, and technology maturity. As energy storage deployment accelerates and developers build operational track records, microgrids may become more common in tax equity portfolios. ... “We’d love to continue to transact in this space,” Brkovic says. ... and optimisation specialists ... with the decision ... Central Eastern Europe is set to return in September 2025 for its third edition, focusing on regional markets and the unique opportunities they present. This ... will bring together key stakeholders from across the ... to explore the latest trends in energy storage, with a focus on the increasing integration of energy storage into regional grids, evolving ... policies, and the ... need for energy security."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,‘Growing interest’ in US microgrids attracts tax equity investor Foss & Company to US$30 million Maryland deal – GreenTV,greentv.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://greentv.com/growing-interest-in-us-microgrids-attracts-tax-equity-investor-foss-company-to-us30-million-maryland-deal/,"‘Growing interest’ in US microgrids attracts tax equity investor Foss & Company to US$30 million Maryland deal – GreenTV ... # ‘Growing interest’ in US microgrids attracts tax equity investor Foss & Company to US$30 million Maryland deal ... 🌍✨ ‘Growing interest’ in US microgrids attracts tax equity investor Foss & Company to US$30 million Maryland deal ... Why we’re watching: ESN Premium speaks with Bryen Alperin and Sophie Brkovic of Foss & Company about the tax equity investor's entrance into microgrids. ... - 📌 Key signal: ESN Premium speaks with Bryen Alperin and Sophie Brkovic of Foss & Company about the tax equity investor's entrance into microgrids. - ✅ Watch for measurable follow-through, not just announcements. - 🔎 Share the most practical takeaway with your community."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,A recent The New York Times article spotlights the revival of the Jacob Riis Park Bathhouse in the Rockaways and the role historic rehabilitation is playing in bringing landmark public spaces back … | Foss & Company,www.linkedin.com (Foss & Company),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/foss-and-company_a-private-club-plans-a-grand-debut-on-the-activity-7486118014824644609-pwSQ,"# A recent The New York Times article spotlights the revival of the Jacob Riis Park Bathhouse in the Rockaways and the role historic rehabilitation is playing in bringing landmark public spaces back … | Foss & Company · LinkedIn · 2026-07-23 ... **Foss & Company**: Foss & Company is a tax credit investment partner that specializes in unlocking the potential of tax credits to drive sustainable investments and maximize returns. They offer transferable tax credits, community revitalization, and environmental transformation. Foss & Company has 40-50 employees (+5-6% YoY) and has annual revenue in the $10M-$20M range, founded in 1983. Headquartered in San Francisco, California, United States. Has $250M in total funding, with 1 prior funding round. ... A recent [The New York Times](https://linkedin.com/company/the-new-york-times) article spotlights the revival of the Jacob Riis Park Bathhouse in the Rockaways and the role historic rehabilitation is playing in bringing landmark public spaces back to life. ... Foss & Company is proud to have supported that work by providing capital through federal and state historic tax equity and a bridge loan for a project that helps restore one of New York's most iconic Art Deco destinations. ... The feature highlights the $88 million transformation of the 1930s bathhouse, long known as the ""People's Beach,"" into the Rockaway Ocean Club, with restored Art Deco windows, original glazed tiles brought back after Hurricane Sandy and a new hotel, restaurants and members club inside the National Register landmark."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Advent Said in Talks to Buy German Bank Arm of Wealth Firm FNZ,news.bloomberglaw.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.bloomberglaw.com/bankruptcy-law/advent-said-in-talks-to-buy-german-bank-arm-of-wealth-firm-fnz,"Advent Said in Talks to Buy German Bank Arm of Wealth Firm FNZ ... Advent is in talks to buy the German custody banking arm of digital wealth management platform FNZ Group Ltd., people familiar with the matter said. ... The private equity firm is negotiating a deal that could value FNZ Bank at more than €400 million ($455 million), according to the people, who asked not to be identified discussing confidential information. ... While discussions are advanced, they could still be delayed or falter, the people said. Other suitors may also emerge, they said. Representatives for FNZ and Advent declined to comment. ... London-headquartered FNZ is led by former JPMorgan Chase & Co. executive Blythe ..."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Passionfroot raises $15M to expand its B2B creator marketplace to the US | TechCrunch,techcrunch.com (Ivan Mehta),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/22/passionfroot-raises-15m-to-expand-its-b2b-creator-marketplace-to-the-us/,"Passionfroot raises $15M to expand its B2B creator marketplace to the US | TechCrunch ... # Passionfroot raises $15M to expand its B2B creator marketplace to the US ... Passionfroot, a German startup building a marketplace connecting B2B creators with brands, said on Wednesday it has raised $15 million in a Series A funding round led by Insight Partners. ... With the funding, the Berlin-based startup’s co-founder and CEO, Jen Phan, is moving to New York, where Passionfroot is opening an office to expand its U.S. operations. The company is also opening an office in São Paulo, and expanding its current headcount of 15 employees. ... Phan said over the last year, the company increased its revenue by 13 times, and onboarded clients such as ElevenLabs, Figma, Replit, Framer, and Gamma. ... Since its last fundraise in 2024, the company has released an AI agent called Zest, which helps brands create, execute and monitor the performance of campaigns. Passionfruit claims Zest can also help companies find suitable creators both inside and outside the platform that are suited to its marketing strategy. ... Passionfroot claims it has paid at least $10 million to creators on its platform in the last 18 months. ... The company says it is working on helping its clients measure how a campaign is impacting AI citations, and how their brand appears in AI-powered answers. The startup is also planning to build AI features for creators, such as helping them with monetization tips and content ideas. ... The funding comes as creator platforms like Substack and Beehiiv move to help creators find better monetization opportunities. Beehiiv launched a new community and ad marketplace last week, and Substack has introduced subscriber-only perks within newsletters. ... Passionfroot’s Series A also saw participation from existing investors Creandum, Supernode Global, and s16vc. The company has raised more than $21 million so far."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Intersnack Acquires Utz in $2.9 Billion Deal; Salty Snack Maker Will Go Private - Food Trade News & Food World,foodtradenews.com (Bryce Graham),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://foodtradenews.com/2026/07/21/intersnack-acquires-utz-in-2-9-billion-deal-salty-snack-maker-will-go-private/,"Intersnack Acquires Utz in $2.9 Billion Deal; Salty Snack Maker Will Go Private - Food Trade News & Food World ... Utz Brands Inc. has agreed to be acquired by Germany-based Intersnack Group in a transaction valued at approximately $2.9 billion that will take the Hanover, Pa.-based snack manufacturer private while keeping the founding Rice and Lissette family as a 50% owner. ... Under the definitive agreement announced July 21, Intersnack will acquire all outstanding Class A common shares of Utz for $14.25 per share in cash, representing a 91% premium over the company’s July 20 closing price. Following the transaction, Intersnack and the Rice and Lissette family will each own 50% of the privately held company. ... The acquisition is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2026, subject to shareholder approval, regulatory clearance and customary closing conditions. The Rice and Lissette family and certain affiliates, which control approximately 42% of Utz’s voting shares, have agreed to support the transaction. ... Following the closing, Chairman Dylan Lissette will become executive chairman, and Utz shares will be delisted from the New York Stock Exchange. Howard Friedman, Utz’s president and chief executive officer, said Intersnack’s marketing, manufacturing, technology and innovation capabilities will help accelerate the company’s long-term growth strategy. ... The deal marks another major transition for Utz, which became a publicly traded company in 2020 through a merger with a special purpose acquisition company (SPAC). When Food Trade News interviewed Lissette following that announcement, he shared this perspective: “If you think about it, we are really the only stand-alone pure-play snacking platform in the United States of scale. As a public company we will be well poised to be the potential consolidator of choice.” ... The firm bought a selection of pretzel brands from Conagra Brands, and assets of the C.J. Vitner salty snack business in 2021. He added that the company had developed expertise integrating acquisitions across financial, cultural and brand dimensions. Friedman succeeded Lissette as chief executive in December 2022, while Lissette remained chairman. ... Intersn ... -private transaction ... all-cash ... The transaction will be financed through approximately $920 million in cash from Intersnack, new debt facilities totaling $1.35 billion, rollover equity from the Rice and Lissette family and the family’s reinvestment of a portion of proceeds from the settlement of the company’s tax receivable agreement. ... Founded more than a century ago in Hanover, Utz has grown into a national snack manufacturer with brands including Utz, Zapp’s, On The Border Chips & Dips, Boulder Canyon, Golden Flake, Hawaiian Brand, Dirty Potato Chips, Bachman, and Tim’s Cascade Snacks. The company reported fiscal 2025 net sales of approximately $1.44 billion. ... For Düsseldorf-based Intersnack, the acquisition provides its first operating presence in the U.S. snack market. The privately held company operates in 31 countries across Europe, Asia, and Oceania, employs approximately 14,500 people and generated about $5 billion in sales in 2025. ... Utz said it will maintain its headquarters in Hanover and continue its commitment to the local community following the transaction."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Blackstone buys Busan-based actuator maker Futronic | Aju Press,www.ajupress.com,2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ajupress.com/view/20260720133103705,"Blackstone buys Busan-based actuator maker Futronic | Aju Press ... # Blackstone buys Busan-based actuator maker Futronic ... SEOUL, July 20 (AJP) -Blackstone has bought a majority stake in South Korean actuator and motion-control technology company Futronic in a deal that values the Busan-based company at about 1 trillion won ($720 million), according to multiple local media outlets. The two companies are yet to announce the deal or disclose the financial terms. The investment is being made in partnership with Futronic founder and Chairman Ko Jin-ho, who will remain chairman and chief executive officer to lead the company's next phase of global expansion alongside Blackstone. ... Founded in 1993, Futronic has grown into a key supplier of actuators and motion-control systems for the global automotive industry, working with leading original equipment manufacturers from the early engineering and development stages. The company has broadened its business beyond traditional automotive applications into next-generation mobility, including humanoid and general-purpose robotics, reflecting rising demand for precision motion-control technologies.Futronic operates primarily from South Korea and the United States while continuing to expand its global manufacturing and customer base. Its client roster includes major global automakers such as General Motors, Ford, Volvo, Mercedes-Benz, Volkswagen, Nissan and Hyundai Motor, as well as several leading Chinese vehicle manufacturers. The company employed 216 people as of April 2026."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Shipeezi launches dedicated operating system for moving industry – FIDI Focus,www.fidifocus.org (Dominic Weaver),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.fidifocus.org/news/shipeezi-launches-dedicated-operating-system-for-moving-industry/,"Shipeezi launches dedicated operating system for moving industry – FIDI Focus ... The founders of supply chain tracking platform Shipeezi have launched a new system built exclusively for moving, relocation and storage companies. ... Moveezi has been launched by Dumont, a new parent company of the two businesses. While Shipeezi will continue to focus on global supply chain movements, Moveezi is dedicated to the moving industry. The platform includes sales and quoting, video surveys, dispatch and crew scheduling, warehousing, shipment tracking, invoicing, and per-move profit and loss. ... In a forthcoming white paper, The moving industry the way I see, company founder and CEO Carlos Ferri says three developments have reshaped the sector over the past 18 months. These are consolidation among major players, last year’s collapse of the US military’s US$17.9bn Global Household Goods Contract, and the first AI-native workflows going live. The paper identifies five trends that will impact the future of international mobility, including greater transparency, AI-driven operations and stronger long-term customer relationships. ... ‘Movers do not need another demo of the future; they need software that their crews open on moving day and their office trusts for the invoice,’ said Ferri. ‘The next decade rewards real-time visibility, genuine compliance, AI built into the architecture, rather than bolted on, and relationships that outlast a single move. Moveezi is built for that, and only that.’ ... Ferri added that the Moveezi platform has been designed for high-trust sectors – including corporate relocation, and government and military mobility – and is compliant with standards including FAIM 3.4, ISO 9001, ISO 27001 and NIST SP 800-171."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Foss & Company Q2 2026 Report: Market Conditions and Capital Deployment - Foss & Co,fossandco.com (smarathe),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fossandco.com/uncategorized/foss-company-q2-2026-report/,"Foss & Company Q2 2026 Report: Market Conditions and Capital Deployment - Foss & Co ... # Foss & Company Q2 2026 Report: Market Conditions and Capital Deployment Q2 2026 was a busy one for Foss & Company and for the tax credit market as a whole. We kicked things off in April by convening an investor roundtable in Atlanta, where we dug into market dynamics, regulatory developments and capital deployment strategies across energy, infrastructure and historic tax credit investments. From there, the quarter kept moving: our team crisscrossed the country for conferences, met with current and prospective investors, and hosted social events to keep those relationships warm. Meanwhile, our Investments, Historic Tax Credit and Energy & Infrastructure teams stayed close to every piece of new industry guidance, sharing their perspective through blog posts, Insights papers, panel discussions and media commentary. ... A year out from the One Big Beautiful Bill (OB3), we’re still finding value-added investment solutions for our clients across markets that continue to adapt to evolving guidance. As we move into Q3, our focus stays where it’s always been: underwriting, due diligence and compliance. ... We published two white papers this quarter. Practical Application Guide: Transferable Tax Credit Carrybacks walks through the mechanics of carrying back transferred clean energy tax credits under Section 6418, covering filing procedures, NOL interaction and Section 38(c) limitations. Partner and Managing Director Eric Brubaker also authored Historic Tax Credits in 2026: Durable Incentives, Institutional Discipline and a Market That Scales, an in-depth look at the federal and state HTC landscape. ... Kevin Haley added two blog posts to the mix this quarter, tackling six big questions facing energy and infrastructure investors and breaking down what corporate directors need to know about carrybacks on transferred tax credits. We also published a piece on how tax equity is helping fund the rehabilitation of historic landmarks in Cleveland, Ohio. ... It was a productive quarter on the deal front. Foss & Company closed 2 energy and infrastructure projects and 12 historic preservation projects across the country in Q2. ... On the historic tax credit and redevelopment side, our closed deals included: ... - Elanco Animal Health HQ 2.0 (Indianapolis, IN) — Foss served as the Indiana Redevelopment Tax Credit investor - Central Park Phase II (Heath, OH) — Foss served as the Ohio Transformational Mixed-Use Development (TMUD) Tax Credit investor - DalPark (Dallas, TX) — Foss arranged the purchaser for Texas Historic Preservation Tax Credits - 1401 Cary St (Richmond, VA) — Foss served as the Virginia State Historic Tax Credit investor - Harry Hake (Richmond, VA) — Foss served as the Virginia State Historic Preservation Tax Credit investor ... We also closed additional historic tax credit investments in Syracuse, NY; Cincinnati, OH; Buffalo, NY; Newport News, VA; and Fort Wayne, IN. Altogether, our energy & infrastructure and historic tax credit teams closed approximately $160 million in projects this quarter. ... Our team stayed active on the conference circuit this quarter, attending 13 industry conferences and speaking on panels at 7 of them, covering topics like FEOC regulations, tax credit structuring and energy storage financing. ... Highlights included Bryen Alperin’s panel on FEOC regulations at the Infocast Tax Credits & Transferability Conference in Houston, where Foss also sponsored a downtown dinner with Novogradac. In San Diego, Sophie Brkovic and Harry Hegeman each spoke at the Novogradac Spring RETC Conference, and Trent Douglass led a sunrise beach walk for 107 attendees on Day 2. In May, Kevin Haley and Adam Rutherford represented our Investments team at Regional TEI Conferences in Sandusky, OH and Monterey, CA, respectively. ... This level of engagement reflects our commitment to helping the market navigate policy uncertainty through a full-service approach across legal, origination, underwriting, compliance and asset management. ... The tax credit market continues to evolve, and we’re built to move with it. Foss & Company has raised more than $11 billion in project equity since our founding and currently manages nearly $3 billion in active assets. As a vertically integrated firm, we’re a one-stop shop for tax credit solutions at both the federal and state level, ready to support investors from early-stage education all the way through to comprehensive investment management across the full deal cycle. ... Questions about tax credit acquisition, FEOC regulations or market positioning? Contact Foss & Company today."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"DEUTZ accelerates transformation with billion-euro transaction in the defense sector : News, DEUTZ AG",www.deutz.com,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.deutz.com/en/news/press-releases/news-detail/deutz-accelerates-transformation-with-billion-euro-transaction-in-the-defense-sector/,"DEUTZ accelerates transformation with billion-euro transaction in the defense sector : News, DEUTZ AG ... # DEUTZ accelerates transformation with billion-euro transaction in the defense sector ... 2026 / 09 / 07 Press Release Investor News ... - Agreement signed for the full acquisition of FFG Flensburger Fahrzeugbau Gesellschaft mbH for around €1.6 billion - The combination creates a new leading systems provider for military vehicles, propulsion systems, and energy solutions in Europe - FFG will remain operationally independent and, going forward, will form the core of DEUTZ’s defense activities - Milestone for the transformation into a broad-based industrial company: Defense business to become a further cornerstone of DEUTZ - Transaction to accelerate profitable growth: strategic 2030 revenue and margin targets (€4 billion, 10% EBIT margin) expected to be reached ahead of schedule - Families that currently own FFG to become new, long-term anchor shareholders of DEUTZ ... Cologne, July 9, 2026 – DEUTZ has entered into an agreement to acquire 100% of the shares in FFG Flensburger Fahrzeugbau Gesellschaft mbH (FFG). Headquartered in Flensburg, Germany, FFG is one of Europe's leading providers of military land and special-purpose vehicles and an established partner of the Bundeswehr and armed forces in NATO and Ukraine.The purchase price is €1.6 billion and is to be paid partly in cash and partly in the form of newly issued DEUTZ shares. The families that currently own FFG are thus to become new, long-term anchor shareholders of DEUTZ, with a stake of up to 29.9%.DEUTZ CEO Dr. Sebastian Schulte says: “Technological sovereignty, innovative capability, speed of execution: Joining forces with FFG, DEUTZ will become a leading national systems provider for military vehicles, propulsion systems, and energy solutions. Together, we will fulfill our responsibilities for security and future resilience in Europe, while securing value creation and high-quality jobs in Germany.”Employing over 1,100 people, FFG produces, maintains, and modernizes wheeled and tracked military vehicles. These include armored recovery vehicles, infantry fighting vehicles, armored personnel carriers, and special-purpose vehicles. FFG also develops proprietary platforms and is a manufacturing partner for NATO multinational armaments programs.The combination is based on a clear industrial logic: FFG will contribute the areas of expertise that will make DEUTZ a systems provider for European defense programs. DEUTZ complements this with its propulsion portfolio – ranging from conventional combustion engines and hybrid drivetrains to solutions for decentralized power supply in the field – as well as its expertise in industrialization and scaling and its global service network. FFG will form the new core of the DEUTZ Defense business unit, remaining independent from an operational perspective. The Group will provide the framework for technological, financial, and strategic scaling. Norbert Erichsen, spokesman for FFG’s shareholders, says: “With this strategic combination with DEUTZ, we are setting the course for the next generations. At the same time, it will create a German industrial group in the defense sector that combines the strengths of the two companies and provides impetus for their shared long-term development.”Rapidly scalable production capacity will enable DEUTZ and FFG to make a key contribution to the defense capabilities of Germany and Europe. This move will also strengthen German industry because strategically relevant defense technologies remain in German hands, and defense programs – with their long lifecycles of ten to 30 years – secure high-quality jobs. In terms of corporate culture, DEUTZ’s acquisition of FFG brings together two long-established German industrial companies that have strong engineering skills, reliable products, and short decision-making lines.The transaction will accelerate the DEUTZ Group’s profitable growth and is expected to bring the 2030 strategic targets (€4 billion in revenue, EBIT margin of 10%) within reach ahead of schedule. FFG is currently in a phase of strong growth and, based on its financial reporting in accordance with the German Commercial Code (HGB), generated revenue of around €760 million in 2025. The value of its orders on hand is many times higher than its current revenue. The acquisition of FFG marks an important milestone in DEUTZ’s transformation into a diversified industrial company in line with the Next DEUTZ strategy. Going forward, the Defense business unit – with FFG as the new core element – will become a further cornerstone of the DEUTZ Group alongside the established Energy, Engines and New Tech business units and the service business, which is a key driver of growth across all segments.DEUTZ expects the combination to generate significant revenue synergies – particularly in the Engines and Service business units – as well as further opportunities through targeted cost synergies. The transaction is expected to have a significantly positive impact on the combined company’s EBIT margin.With a stake of up to 29.9%, the families that own FFG at present will become new anchor shareholders of DEUTZ and will constructively support DEUTZ over the long term as it continues with its transformation. In line with their intended investment, the families that currently own FFG are aiming to take two seats on the DEUTZ Supervisory Board once the transaction has been completed.The parity-based composition of the Supervisory Board will be maintained; DEUTZ reaffirms its clear commitment to co-determination. Approval for the planned capital increase against contribution in kind is to be obtained from DEUTZ’s shareholders at an Extraordinary General Meeting to be held as a virtual event on August 24, 2026. Completion of the transaction is dependent on a number of conditions, including the agreement of the shareholders at the Extraordinary General Meeting as well as the necessary approvals being granted by the relevant authorities. Once all conditions have been met, completion is expected in late 2026 or in the first quarter of 2027. Download press release"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,FFG shapes its next phase of growth – strategic combination with DEUTZ - European Security & Defence,euro-sd.com (Thomas Liebe),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://euro-sd.com/2026/07/news/land/52206/ffg-shapes-its-next-phase-of-growth-strategic-combination-with-deutz/,"FFG shapes its next phase of growth – strategic combination with DEUTZ - European Security & Defence ... Security & Defence ... Start News Land FFG shapes its next phase of growth – strategic combination with DEUTZ ... ##### The family shareholders of FFG have chosen a strategic combination with DEUTZ to unlock the company’s next phase of long-term growth. As part of the DEUTZ Group, FFG will strengthen its ability to invest, innovate and execute at scale while continuing the successful growth trajectory that has characterised the company in recent years. ... The family shareholders will become a long-term anchor shareholder in DEUTZ. Through their representation on the Supervisory Board, they will actively shape the Group’s long-term strategic direction and continue to play a key role in its future development. ... Norbert Erichsen, Chair of the Family Shareholders, said: “Joining the DEUTZ Group is a strategic decision for the long-term development of FFG. By combining the complementary strengths of both companies, we are creating the conditions to accelerate our development for many years to come.” ... The operational management of FFG remains unchanged under Managing Directors Max Heimann and Jörg Kamper. Together with their teams, they are responsible for leading FFG’s continued development as part of the DEUTZ Group and driving the company’s successful growth trajectory. ... FFG-Defense will become the DEUTZ Group’s dedicated defence platform, combining FFG’s decades of expertise in military land systems with DEUTZ’s industrial capabilities, international footprint and global sales and service network. ... ### FFG showcases Armored Innovations in Paris ... ### FFG invests in the future ... ### Norway Orders New Armoured Recovery Vehicles ... ### FFG Presents Recovery Module for the Boxer"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,DEUTZ to acquire FFG for €1.6 billion to expand into military vehicle and defence systems market,defence-industry.eu,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://defence-industry.eu/deutz-to-acquire-ffg-for-e1-6-billion-to-expand-into-military-vehicle-and-defence-systems-market/,"DEUTZ to acquire FFG for €1.6 billion to expand into military vehicle and defence systems market ... # DEUTZ to acquire FFG for €1.6 billion to expand into military vehicle and defence systems market ... DEUTZ Group AG has agreed to acquire 100% of FFG Flensburger Fahrzeugbau Gesellschaft mbH for around €1.6 billion. The German industrial company said the deal would create a leading European systems provider for military vehicles, propulsion systems and energy solutions. ... FFG, based in Flensburg, is one of Europe’s leading providers of military land and special-purpose vehicles. The company is an established partner of the Bundeswehr, NATO armed forces and Ukraine. ... The purchase price will be paid partly in cash and partly through newly issued DEUTZ shares. The families that currently own FFG are expected to become long-term anchor shareholders of DEUTZ, with a stake of up to 29.9%. ... DEUTZ said FFG will remain operationally independent and become the core of its new defence business unit. The group said the transaction is a milestone in its transformation into a broader industrial company under the Next DEUTZ strategy. ... DEUTZ CEO Dr. Sebastian Schulte says: “Technological sovereignty, innovative capability, speed of execution: Joining forces with FFG, DEUTZ will become a leading national systems provider for military vehicles, propulsion systems, and energy solutions. Together, we will fulfill our responsibilities for security and future resilience in Europe, while securing value creation and high-quality jobs in Germany.” ... The company also develops proprietary platforms and acts as a manufacturing partner for NATO multinational armaments programmes. DEUTZ said FFG will provide expertise that will help make the group a systems provider for European defence programmes. ... DEUTZ will add its propulsion portfolio, including combustion engines, hybrid drivetrains and decentralised field power supply solutions. The group will also contribute industrialisation, scaling expertise and its global service network. ... Norbert Erichsen, spokesman for FFG’s shareholders, says: “With this strategic combination with DEUTZ, we are setting the course for the next generations. At the same time, it will create a German industrial group in the defense sector that combines the strengths of the two companies and provides impetus for their shared long-term development.” ... DEUTZ said rapidly scalable production capacity will allow the combined group to contribute to the defence capabilities of Germany and Europe. It said the transaction would also keep strategically relevant defence technologies in German hands and secure high-quality jobs through long-cycle defence programmes. ... The company said the acquisition is expected to accelerate profitable growth and bring its 2030 strategic targets within reach ahead of schedule. These targets include €4 billion in revenue and an EBIT margin of 10%. ... FFG generated revenue of around €760 million in 2025 under German Commercial Code reporting and is currently in a phase of strong growth. DEUTZ said FFG’s order backlog is many times higher than its current revenue. ... The new defence unit will sit alongside DEUTZ’s established Energy, Engines and New Tech business units. The group also said its service business remains a key growth driver across all segments. ... DEUTZ expects the combination to generate significant revenue synergies, particularly in the Engines and Service business units. It also sees further opportunities through targeted cost synergies and expects the deal to have a significantly positive impact on the combined company’s EBIT margin. ... The current FFG owners plan to support DEUTZ’s transformation as new anchor shareholders and aim to take two seats on the DEUTZ Supervisory Board after completion. DEUTZ said the parity-based composition of the Supervisory Board will be maintained and reaffirmed its commitment to co-determination. ... DEUTZ will seek shareholder approval for a planned capital increase against contribution in kind at an extraordinary general meeting on 24 August 2026. Completion remains subject to several conditions, including shareholder approval and regulatory clearances, and is expected in late 2026 or the first quarter of 2027. ... ### Royal Navy launches Uncrewed Systems ... in Swindon to accelerate use of drones, autonomous boats and minehunting systems ... U.S. military ... ### NATO launches Front Door and Engine initiatives to connect industry with procurement needs and expand Allied production capacity ... NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte has launched two new initiatives intended to strengthen transatlantic defence industrial cooperation and speed up the delivery of military capabilities. ... ### NATO Allies to invest more ... billion in counter-drone systems and expand drone operator"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Foss & Company Enters Microgrid Sector with ~$30 Million Tax Equity Investment in Montgomery County Transit Project,www.prnewswire.com (Foss & Company),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/foss--company-enters-microgrid-sector-with-30-million-tax-equity-investment-in-montgomery-county-transit-project-302817123.html,"Foss & Company Enters Microgrid Sector with ~$30 Million Tax Equity Investment in Montgomery County Transit Project Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... DENVER, July 8, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Foss & Company, an established tax credit syndicator, today announced the closing of an approximately $30 million Section 48 tax equity investment, a state-of-the-art microgrid system located in Montgomery County, MD. The transaction marks Foss & Company's first partnership with AlphaStruxure and represents the firm's entry into the microgrid sector. ... This project will finance an advanced energy system integrating solar photovoltaic (PV) generation with battery energy storage, purpose-built to power a transit facility and support an electric bus fleet. It is expected to achieve commercial operations in August 2026 and is projected to generate more than 6,000 megawatt-hours (MWh) of clean energy annually, enough to meaningfully reduce the facility's reliance on the traditional grid while lowering its carbon footprint. ... ""We are thrilled to close this investment alongside AlphaStruxure and to expand Foss & Company's portfolio into microgrid technology,"" said Bryen Alperin, partner and managing director, Foss & Company. ""Project Orchid exemplifies the kind of innovative, high-impact clean energy infrastructure we seek to support, delivering resilient, sustainable power to critical public transit operations while aiming to generate strong returns for our investors."" ... AlphaStruxure, a leading developer of microgrid solutions, brings deep expertise in designing and delivering integrated energy systems for complex facilities. This inaugural transaction establishes a strong foundation for a continued partnership between AlphaStruxure and Foss & Company. ... ""We're excited to close this transaction with Foss & Company,"" said Troy Patton, general manager, AlphaStruxure. "" We look forward to delivering a best-in-class microgrid solution that will serve Montgomery County's transit operations for decades to come."" ... The Section 48 Investment Tax Credit (ITC) supports the deployment of clean energy technologies including solar and energy storage, providing a critical financing mechanism for projects like this that advance the decarbonization of public infrastructure. ... Founded in 1983, Foss & Company is a national tax equity investor and fund sponsor that, since its inception, has deployed over $11 billion in tax equity on behalf of insurance, banking, and other large corporate clients into historic rehabilitation projects, renewable energy, and advanced energy production facilities. Foss & Company is a full-service advisor with proven expertise in helping its partners navigate the world of tax equity investments. For more information about Foss & Company, please visit www.FossandCo.com. ... This press release contains forward-looking statements based on current expectations and projections, subject to risks including changes in tax law, construction/completion risks, energy production variability, and market conditions that could cause actual results to differ materially. Foss & Company undertakes no obligation to update these statements. ... ### From Office Tower to Urban Living: Foss & Company Backs Historic Financial Center Transformation ... Foss & Company, an established tax credit syndicator, today announced the successful closing of financing for the Financial Center, a landmark... ... ### Foss & Company Closes Tax Equity Investment in Altus Power Distributed Solar-Plus-Storage Portfolio ... Foss & Company, an established tax equity syndicator, today announced the closing of Project London II, a Section 48 ITC tax equity investment..."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Foss & Company Ventures Into Microgrid Investment with $30 Million Partnership in Maryland - Third News,third-news.com,2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://third-news.com/article/cc14324a-7ad0-11f1-a3e1-9ca3ba08e13f,"Foss & Company Ventures Into Microgrid Investment with $30 Million Partnership in Maryland - Third News ... # Foss & Company Ventures Into Microgrid Investment with $30 Million Partnership in Maryland ... ## Foss & Company Steps into the Microgrid Sector ... Foss & Company, a well-established tax credit syndicator, recently made a significant leap into the microgrid sector by securing an investment of approximately $30 million under Section 48 tax equity. This milestone was reached through a collaboration with AlphaStruxure, a prominent developer specializing in microgrid solutions. The investment will fund an advanced energy system in Montgomery County, Maryland, integrating solar photovoltaic (PV) generation with state-of-the-art battery energy storage. This particular project aims to power a transit facility that supports an electric bus fleet. Its commercial operations are expected to commence by August 2026, with projections indicating that it will generate over 6,000 megawatt-hours (MWh) of clean energy annually. Such a significant output will substantially lessen the transit facility’s dependence on the traditional power grid while also helping to shrink its carbon footprint. Bryen Alperin, a partner and managing director at Foss & Company, expressed enthusiasm for this new venture, stating, ""We are thrilled to close this investment alongside AlphaStruxure, which signifies an expansion of our portfolio into microgrid technology. Project Orchid epitomizes the innovative, high-impact clean energy infrastructure we strive to support. Ultimately, we aim to deliver resilient, sustainable power to public transit while generating strong returns for our investors."" Unveiling a New Era for Clean Energy AlphaStruxure, known for its expertise in developing integrated energy systems tailored for complex facilities, is poised to play a crucial role in the success of this project. Troy Patton, the general manager of AlphaStruxure, echoed the excitement surrounding the partnership, emphasizing the potential benefits that the microgrid solution will bring to Montgomery County's transit operations. He said, ""We look forward to delivering a best-in-class microgrid solution that will serve Montgomery County's transit operations for decades to come."" The project benefits greatly from the Section 48 Investment Tax Credit (ITC), which encourages the deployment of clean energy technologies such as solar and energy storage. This funding mechanism is vital in advancing the decarbonization of public infrastructure, making projects like this financially feasible and environmentally beneficial. A Commitment to Sustainability With a history dating back to 1983, Foss & Company has deployed more than $11 billion in tax equity across various sectors, including renewable energy and historic rehabilitation projects. Their extensive experience makes them a key player in the transition to sustainable energy solutions. Furthermore, their new partnership with AlphaStruxure is set to yield not just financial returns, but also a marked contribution toward environmentally responsible public transit. As Foss & Company delves deeper into clean energy through this innovative microgrid initiative, they position themselves not just as investors but as vital contributors to a sustainable future. The organization aims to lead by example, showcasing how private investments can facilitate significant advancements in public infrastructure while addressing climate change. The anticipation surrounding this project showcases a growing recognition of the importance of clean energy solutions in urban settings and sets a precedent for future investments in sustainable infrastructure across the country. The push toward microgrids is a significant move away from conventional energy models, paving the way for more resilient, responsive, and, importantly, environmentally friendly energy practices. In closing, the Foss & Company and AlphaStruxure partnership signifies a crucial step in reshaping public transit infrastructure. By integrating cutting-edge energy systems, they are setting the stage for future developments that embrace sustainability and environmental stewardship."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"Foss & Company is proud to have served as the Texas State Historic Tax Credit investor for the Gunter Hotel restoration in downtown San Antonio, TX. | Foss & Company",www.linkedin.com (Foss & Company),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/foss-and-company_tax-taxcredits-historictaxcredits-activity-7480289716064514050-CXgK,"Foss & Company Serves as Texas State Historic Tax Credit Investor for Gunter Hotel | Foss & Company posted on the topic | LinkedIn ... # Foss & Company Serves as Texas State Historic Tax Credit Investor for Gunter Hotel ... Foss & Company is proud to have served as the Texas State Historic Tax Credit investor for the Gunter Hotel restoration in downtown San Antonio, TX. Built in 1909 and listed on the National Register of Historic Places, the Gunter Hotel was redeveloped by Axle Capital Group through a $57 million project that restored the lobby, ballroom and guest rooms. Foss & Company contributed $9.94 million in Texas state HTC equity to support the rehabilitation. The project was featured in the June 2026 issue of the Novogradac Journal of Tax Credits as a Historic Tax Credit Tool Box case study. Read the full article from Novogradac: https://bit.ly/4uYZh3v#tax#taxcredits#historictaxcredits#HTC#historicpreservation#adaptivereuse#SanAntonio#Texas For informational purposes only. Not tax advice."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Bayou Best Foods reels in BettaF!sh | Food Business News,www.foodbusinessnews.net (Brooke Just),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.foodbusinessnews.net/articles/30629-bayou-best-foods-reels-in-bettafsh,"NEW YORK — Bayou Best Foods has acquired BettaF!sh, a brand of Wunderfish GMbH. Financial terms of the acquisition were not disclosed. ... Founded and led by Deniz Ficicioglu, BettaF!sh is a Berlin-based company that manufactures such fish alternatives as Tu-Nah and Sal-Mon that are formulated with seaweed for retailers, foodservice operators and consumers. ... The acquisition of BettaF!sh grows Bayou Best Foods portfolio beyond plant-based shrimp and soon will be introduced to BettaF!sh’s foodservice partners across Europe. ... “Our goal has always been to bring great-tasting, ocean-friendly seafood to more people, and BettaF!sh is exactly the kind of partner that makes that possible,” said Kelli Wilson, chief executive officer of Bayou Best Foods. “We share the same belief that seafood should be delicious, accessible, and sustainable, and we see enormous potential in what we can build together.” ... In turn, BettaF!sh’s plant-based tuna and salmon also will be introduced to Bayou Best Foods’ US network. ... “This is a natural next chapter for BettaF!sh,” Ficicioglu said. “Both of our companies were built on the belief that protecting the ocean and creating exceptional food should go hand-in-hand. By joining forces, we can move faster, reach more customers, and help shape the future of seafood together.”"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"Kenyan startups Fuzu, Kyosk secure funding from Jobtech Alliance - Disrupt Africa",disruptafrica.com (Tom Jackson),2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://disruptafrica.com/2026/07/06/kenyan-startups-fuzu-kyosk-secure-funding-from-jobtech-alliance/,"Kenyan startups Fuzu, Kyosk secure funding from Jobtech Alliance - Disrupt Africa ... Kenyan startups Fuzu and Kyosk are the latest to secure an undisclosed amount of funding from the Jobtech Alliance. ... Disrupt Africa reported in October 2022 on the launch of the Jobtech Alliance, an ecosystem-building initiative around inclusive jobtech in Africa steered by Mercy Corps and BFA Global, which aims to create an enabling environment for entrepreneurs to build platforms that deliver quality livelihoods, are inclusive, and enable users to engage in decent work. ... It has run several cohorts, but is now also making direct investments in relevant ventures, most recently Nigeria’s Bumpa and Kenya’s Flowcart, both e-commerce ventures, and Kenyan social commerce startup Twiva. ... It has now made two further investments, in Fuzu and Kyosk. ... Fuzu has spent more than a decade building talent infrastructure across Africa, and has now pivoted from running a marketplace to managing global teams for AI data operations, evaluation, and QA work. The investment came out of the Jobtech Alliance’s Digital Work Sector Scan, which mapped how AI is reshaping African digital work. ... Over the next six months, the alliance will work with Fuzu on direct international client growth, refining the positioning around Fuzu Atlas, and moving up the value chain into higher-quality AI-adjacent work. ... “Most African talent platforms still operate as marketplaces, competing on volume and cheaper sourcing. Fuzu has already moved past that. They’ve built the infrastructure layer underneath the marketplace, and Fuzu Atlas is now using it to deliver managed teams that global clients can actually build with. It’s one of the more credible answers we’ve seen to where good digital jobs in Africa come from next,” said Nick Markham, investment lead at the Jobtech Alliance. ... The second new portfolio company is Kyosk, a B2B commerce platform that serves over 200,000 informal retailers across Kenya, Nigeria, Uganda, and Tanzania. Kyosk sits inside the alliance’s microenterprise investment thesis– platforms that operate inside the daily workflow challenges of informal retailers, from inventory access to delivery consistency to repeat purchasing behaviour. ... “African B2B commerce is maturing, and the platforms that win from here will be the ones that learn to bridge the fragmented workflows of informal retailers: inventory access, delivery reliability, repeat ordering. Kyosk’s shift from 25 warehouses in Kenya to one per country, with a sharper focus on route-level economics, is exactly the kind of operational discipline this market needs,” said Mide Alonge, senior venture builder at the Jobtech Alliance."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Tech Talk: Jack Henry’s David Foss reflects on career and company in Q&A | Springfield Business Journal,sbj.net,2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,"https://sbj.net/stories/tech-talk,104830","Tech Talk: Jack Henry’s David Foss reflects on career and company in Q&A | Springfield Business Journal ... David Foss, who previously served for nearly a decade as CEO at Jack Henry & Associates Inc. (Nasdaq: JKHY), is nearing the end of his time with the Monett-based financial software company."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Foss & Company Enters Microgrid Sector with ~$30 Million Tax Equity Investment in Montgomery County Transit Project - Mining Stock Education,www.miningstockeducation.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.miningstockeducation.com/2026/07/foss-company-enters-microgrid-sector-with-30-million-tax-equity-investment-in-montgomery-county-transit-project/,"Foss & Company Enters Microgrid Sector with ~$30 Million Tax Equity Investment in Montgomery County Transit Project - Mining Stock Education ... # Foss & Company Enters Microgrid Sector with ~$30 Million Tax Equity Investment in Montgomery County Transit Project Posted on July 8th, 2026 | Filed under Press Releases First Transaction with AlphaStruxure Brings Resilient Clean Energy to Maryland Public Transit ... DENVER, July 8, 2026 /PRNewswire/ — Foss & Company, an established tax credit syndicator, today announced the closing of an approximately $30 million Section 48 tax equity investment, a state-of-the-art microgrid system located in Montgomery County, MD. The transaction marks Foss & Company’s first partnership with AlphaStruxure and represents the firm’s entry into the microgrid sector. This project will finance an advanced energy system integrating solar photovoltaic (PV) generation with battery energy storage, purpose-built to power a transit facility and support an electric bus fleet. It is expected to achieve commercial operations in August 2026 and is projected to generate more than 6,000 megawatt-hours (MWh) of clean energy annually, enough to meaningfully reduce the facility’s reliance on the traditional grid while lowering its carbon footprint. ... “We are thrilled to close this investment alongside AlphaStruxure and to expand Foss & Company’s portfolio into microgrid technology,” said Bryen Alperin, partner and managing director, Foss & Company. “Project Orchid exemplifies the kind of innovative, high-impact clean energy infrastructure we seek to support, delivering resilient, sustainable power to critical public transit operations while aiming to generate strong returns for our investors.” ... AlphaStruxure, a leading developer of microgrid solutions, brings deep expertise in designing and delivering integrated energy systems for complex facilities. This inaugural transaction establishes a strong foundation for a continued partnership between AlphaStruxure and Foss & Company. ... “We’re excited to close this transaction with Foss & Company,” said Troy Patton, general manager, AlphaStruxure. ” We look forward to delivering a best-in-class microgrid solution that will serve Montgomery County’s transit operations for decades to come.” ... The Section 48 Investment Tax Credit (ITC) supports the deployment of clean energy technologies including solar and energy storage, providing a critical financing mechanism for projects like this that advance the decarbonization of public infrastructure. ... ABOUT FOSS & COMPANY Founded in 1983, Foss & Company is a national tax equity investor and fund sponsor that, since its inception, has deployed over $11 billion in tax equity on behalf of insurance, banking, and other large corporate clients into historic rehabilitation projects, renewable energy, and advanced energy production facilities. Foss & Company is a full-service advisor with proven expertise in helping its partners navigate the world of tax equity investments. For more information about Foss & Company, please visit www.FossandCo.com. ... This press release contains forward-looking statements based on current expectations and projections, subject to risks including changes in tax law, construction/completion risks, energy production variability, and market conditions that could cause actual results to differ materially. Foss & Company undertakes no obligation to update these statements."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,"250 Years of America, and the Tax Code That Helped Build It - Foss & Co",fossandco.com (smarathe),2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fossandco.com/uncategorized/250-years-of-america-and-the-tax-code-that-helped-build-it/,"250 Years of America, and the Tax Code That Helped Build It - Foss & Co Skip to content ... Foss & Company has been part of this history since Joe Foss founded the firm in 1983, just seven years after the first historic tax incentives became law. Over four decades and more than$11 billion in tax equity deployed, Foss has helped preserve historic buildings and finance clean energy infrastructure from coast to coast. As America marks 250 years, that work continues. ... ← What Corporate Tax Directors Need to Know About Carrybacks on Transferred Energy Credits Foss & Company Q2 2026 Report: Market Conditions and Capital Deployment →"
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Aquaponics and food security: Horizon Farms acquires Fësch Haff in agritech expansion - RTL Today,today.rtl.lu,2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://today.rtl.lu/news/luxembourg/horizon-farms-acquires-fesch-haff-in-agritech-expansion-1574277182,"Aquaponics and food security: Horizon Farms acquires Fësch Haff in agritech expansion - RTL Today ... # Aquaponics and food security Horizon Farms acquires Fësch Haff in agritech expansion ... Luxembourg start-up Horizon Farms has acquired aquaponics company Fësch Haff and raised seven-figure funding to expand production and develop the country’s first commercial-scale agritech greenhouse. ... Luxembourg start-up Horizon Farms has acquired Greiveldange-based company Fësch Haff, with plans to bring innovative agricultural production in the country to a commercial scale. ... Horizon Farms said it had also raised seven-figure seed funding, primarily from Luxembourg investors, to support further innovation in agriculture. ... Horizon Farms plans to use the investment to expand Fësch Haff's capacity and finance what it describes as Luxembourg's first commercial-scale agritech greenhouse. ... The company sees the project as a way of strengthening Luxembourg's food supply. According to its press release, the country currently imports around 95% of its fruit and vegetables. ... During his visit to the pilot facility, Hansen praised the company's innovative approach. He said aquaponics demonstrated that more sustainable food production using less water and no pesticides was not merely a ""vision for the future"", but was already being put into practice in Luxembourg. ... Innovations of this kind could help make food systems more sustainable while creating new opportunities for agriculture, Hansen concluded."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Sovereign Space Expansion: Spain’s FOSSA Systems Secures €9.25M to Scale Defense Constellation and SIGINT Infrastructure – SatNews,satnews.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://satnews.com/2026/06/24/sovereign-space-expansion-spains-fossa-systems-secures-e9-25m-to-scale-defense-constellation-and-sigint-infrastructure/,"Sovereign Space Expansion: Spain’s FOSSA Systems Secures €9.25M to Scale Defense Constellation and SIGINT Infrastructure – SatNews ... MADRID, SPAIN — June 24, 2026 — FOSSA Systems, a prominent player in the European space and defense ecosystem, has officially closed a €9.25 million funding round to accelerate its international expansion and aggressively deploy its sovereign low-Earth orbit (LEO) satellite constellation. ... The investment round was led by Kibo Ventures and features heavy institutional backing from the newly established Spanish Society for Technological Transformation (SETT)—an entity attached to Spain’s Ministry for Digital Transformation and Civil Service. Additional participants in the syndicate include the Space Frontiers Fund II (managed by Japan’s SPARX Asset Management), Indico Capital Partners, and WISeSAT. The capital injection brings FOSSA’s total funding since inception to nearly €20 million. ... Founded in 2020 by Julián Fernández and Vicente González, FOSSA Systems has scaled rapidly to become Spain’s most active satellite operator, having successfully orbited 25 satellites to date. The company’s upcoming launch in the consecutive weeks will place its 26th satellite into orbit as part of a broader blueprint to field a 140-satellite global Internet of Things (IoT) network. ... The capital injection coincides with a profound strategic shifts across the European Union toward strategic autonomy and resilient localized space architecture. As space assets cement themselves as vital defense infrastructure, European nations are heavily prioritizing space operators capable of deploying payload capacity without outside technological dependencies. ... “Thanks to FOSSA, small nations, Ministries of Defence, and global corporations can define and execute their own space strategy in just a few months, while the vertical integration of the entire technology chain has allowed us to reduce costs by an order of magnitude,” stated Julián Fernández, CEO and co-founder of FOSSA. “In just a few years, we have gone from being a startup to an internationally present company with 25 satellites launched and technology that responds to real needs of industrial, institutional, and governmental clients. Our goal is to establish FOSSA as a European benchmark in sovereign space infrastructure.” ... “Europe needs technological champions capable of reducing dependencies in strategic sectors,” Santamaría noted. “FOSSA has demonstrated that it can develop and operate sovereign space infrastructure with exceptional speed and efficiency.” Following the close of the transaction, Santamaría will formally join FOSSA’s board of directors. ... FOSSA’s defense credentials have steadily gained momentum across allied networks. The company was recently selected to participate in NATO’s Defence Innovation Accelerator for the North Atlantic (DIANA) program, selected for its advanced low-Earth orbit electromagnetic and signals intelligence capabilities. ... Concurrently, FOSSA is accelerating its international commercial push. With existing offices operating in Madrid and Lisbon, the company has established its third international corporate presence in Tokyo, Japan. The expansion is backed by a major strategic agreement with Japanese industrial powerhouse Kanematsu Corporation to formally introduce and deploy FOSSA’s space intelligence and dual-use technologies directly into the Japanese Ministry of Defense market."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Spanish IoT Startup FOSSA Secures $10M in Funding - Via Satellite,www.satellitetoday.com (Mark Holmes),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.satellitetoday.com/finance/2026/06/24/spanish-iot-startup-fossa-secures-10m-in-funding/,"Spanish IoT Startup FOSSA Secures $10M in Funding - Via Satellite ... FOSSA, a Spanish IoT satellite company, has closed a new funding round worth 9.25 million euros ($10.5 million) to fund international expansion and global deployment of its sovereign satellite capabilities. The funds will be used to strengthen the team, boost the commercial expansion launched in 2024, advance new capabilities focused on security and defense, and continue deploying its constellation of Low-Earth Orbit (LEO) satellites. ... Kibo Ventures led the funding round with participation from the Spanish Society for Technological Transformation (SETT, entity affiliated with the Ministry for Digital Transformation and the Civil Service), Space Frontiers Fund II (with SPARX Asset Management Co., Ltd. As Manager), Indico Capital and WISeSAT. ... The company has launched over 25 satellites and is targeting a constellation of 140 satellites. Its next launch in the coming weeks, will be the 26th satellite in its constellation. FOSSA develops its own technological infrastructure for satellite IoT connectivity, secure communications, and space-based intelligence solutions (SIGINT), with applications in energy, logistics, agriculture, critical infrastructure, and national security. ... “In just a few years, we have gone from being a startup to an internationally present company with 25 satellites launched and technology that responds to real needs of industrial, institutional, and governmental clients. Our goal is to establish FOSSA as a European benchmark in sovereign space infrastructure,” Julián Fernández, CEO and co-founder of FOSSA, said in a statement."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo delivers 6.6% sales growth in first quarter of 2026 - GlobalPETS,globalpetindustry.com (David Palacios Rubio),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://globalpetindustry.com/news/fressnapf-maxi-zoo-delivers-6-6-sales-growth-in-first-quarter-of-2026/,"Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo delivers 6.6% sales growth in first quarter of 2026 - GlobalPETS ... # Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo delivers 6.6% sales growth in first quarter of 2026 ... The European pet retailer expanded its store network in France, Italy and Poland, and opened a new e-commerce fulfillment center. ... Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo generated revenue of €928 million ($1.07B) in the first quarter of 2026, up from €871 million ($998M) during the same period last year. ... The European pet retail group says the 6.6% year-over-year (YoY) increase was accompanied by continued operational efficiency. Adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization (EBITDA) reached €82 million ($94M), representing a 15.6% increase. ... The Germany-based company recorded positive like-for-like sales growth of 4% across all regions in which it operates. According to the retailer, this performance was driven by value-focused initiatives, including price guarantees on exclusive brands and more affordable everyday options, which helped attract more pet owners to its stores. ... Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo opened 33 new stores between January and March 2026, bringing its network to 2,919 locations. Expansion efforts focused on high-potential markets, particularly France, Italy and Poland. In 2025, the retailer opened 195 new stores. ... “In a challenging market environment, characterized by an overall deteriorating consumer sentiment, we gained market share across key regions,” says Fressnapf CFO Florian Wieser. ... According to the company, Fressnapf Germany outperformed the market, driven by strong sales of snacks and cat litter. Meanwhile, Arcaplanet in Italy exceeded market growth by more than 5 percentage points, while Maxi Zoo France outperformed its market by double digits, driven by strong sales in core food and litter categories. ... In 2025, the pet retail group generated €3.7 billion ($4.2B) in sales and increased operating profit by 11% to €380 million ($435.4M), reflecting the impact of its internal restructuring efforts and disciplined cost management. Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo recorded a slight 0.8% decline in like-for-like sales last year while reducing operating costs by €80 million ($91.7M). ... To support its market expansion, the group recently opened a new e-commerce fulfillment center in Nörvenich, 35 kilometers from Cologne. ... Representing an €80 million ($91.7M) investment over 3 years, the 72,000-square-meter facility is one of Europe’s most modern logistics hubs, acting as the central e-commerce headquarters for Germany, France and the Benelux region. ... “It’s not just about fulfillment. Nörvenich also enables us to deliver better value through click-and-collect. Customers can pick up products at stores when it suits them, leveraging both our distribution and store networks,” says Fressnapf | Maxi Zoo CEO Matt Simister in a recent interview with PETS International. ... The new site boasts a system comprising 260 robots and 120,000 containers, capable of processing up to 40,000 parcels per day, with room to expand to 60,000. ... Online sales currently account for around 12% of the business and are expected to grow in the coming years. “Our online business is solid, particularly in Germany and Italy, but across other countries there are clear opportunities to improve things like assortment, pricing and delivery promise,” adds Simister. ... Fressnapf also recently celebrated the opening of the 2.0 central warehouse in Krefeld, where the group is headquartered. Serving as a central inbound hub, the facility is designed to manage full pallets efficiently and supply the main warehouse on a just-in-time basis. ... A key feature of the project is a planned service bridge equipped with automated conveyor systems that will connect the new building to the existing infrastructure, enabling a seamless automated pallet flow. ... The facility is expected to become fully operational later this year and is intended to strengthen the company’s supply chain across European markets."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Familiefirma i Hillerød i rekordregnskab: Ny topchef satser på vækstøkonomier,borsen.dk (Peter B. Rasmussen),2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://borsen.dk/nyheder/virksomheder/familiefirma-i-hillerod-i-rekordregnskab-ny-topchef-satser-pa-vaekstokonomier,"Familiefirma i Hillerød i rekordregnskab: Ny topchef satser på vækstøkonomier ... # Familiefirma i Hillerød i rekordregnskab: Ny topchef satser på vækstøkonomier ... Foss’ nye topchef, Christian Rosenkrantz de Lasson, vil investere massivt i teknologi og produktion for at fastholde væksten ... Christian Rosenkrantz de Lasson er ny adm. direktør i Foss, hvor han har været ansat i de seneste ti år. Foto: Simon Fals ... . 2 ... Gem til senere ... Den danske analysekoncern Foss leverer det bedste regnskab i selskabets 70-årige historie. Omsætningen steg i 2025 til 2,7 mia. kr., mens driftsindtjeningen nåede rekordhøje 700 mio. kr. ... Resultatet kommer i en tid præget af geopolitisk uro og handelsspændinger, men ifølge den nye topchef, Christian Rosenkrantz de Lasson, står selskabet solidt i markedet."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Jack Henry & Associates Announces Retirement of David Foss as Board Chair,"www.prnewswire.com (Jack Henry & Associates, Inc.)",2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/jack-henry--associates-announces-retirement-of-david-foss-as-board-chair-302791126.html,"Jack Henry & Associates Announces Retirement of David Foss as Board Chair Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... Flanigan to ... MONETT, Mo., June 4, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Jack Henry & Associates, Inc.® (Nasdaq: JKHY) announced today that Board Chair, David Foss, will retire effective July 15, 2026. As part of the planned transition, Matt Flanigan, current Vice Chair and Lead Independent Director, will become Board Chair upon Foss's retirement. ... Foss joined Jack Henry in 1999 and served as President from 2014 to 2022 and as Chief Executive Officer from 2016 to 2024. He was appointed to the Board in 2017 and named Chair in 2021. Throughout his tenure, he played a pivotal role in shaping the company's long-term strategy, expanding its technology capabilities, and strengthening its position as a leading provider of solutions for banks and credit unions. ... ""It has been a privilege to serve this company and our clients over the years,"" Foss said. ""I'm incredibly proud of what we've accomplished together – from strengthening our culture to advancing our technology modernization strategy. Most importantly, I am proud of the management team we've built and have great confidence in Matt's ability to serve the Board as its Chair."" ... Board in 2007 and ... served as Lead Director since 2012 ... retired in 2019 as Executive Vice President, Chief Financial Officer, and Board Member of Leggett & Platt, Inc. Prior to joining Leggett in 1997, ... spent 13 years in the banking industry in Dallas, Texas. ... ""We will continue to build upon the strong foundation that Dave established,"" Flanigan said. ""The Board remains focused on supporting the company's long-term strategy and disciplined growth, and we will work closely with management to deliver high value for all stakeholders."" ... Greg Adelson, President and CEO, added, ""Dave's leadership has had a lasting impact on Jack Henry and on me personally – including the strategy and innovation that drive our business, as well as the values and culture that define who we are. Dave is an exceptional leader and mentor, and we are all deeply grateful for his many contributions. We have been prepared to have Matt step into this role as part of our succession plan, given his extensive leadership experience, financial expertise, banking background, and long-standing service on our Board."" ... Jack Henry® (Nasdaq: JKHY) is a well-rounded financial technology company that strengthens connections between financial institutions and the people and businesses they serve. We are an S&P 500 company that prioritizes openness, collaboration, and user centricity – offering banks and credit unions a vibrant ecosystem of internally developed modern capabilities as well as the ability to integrate with leading fintechs. For 50 years, Jack Henry has provided technology solutions to enable clients to innovate faster, strategically differentiate, and successfully compete while serving the evolving needs of their accountholders. We empower approximately 7,400 clients with people-inspired innovation, personal service, and insight-driven solutions that help reduce the barriers to financial health. Additional information is available at www.jackhenry.com. ... Jack Henry® (Nasdaq: JKHY) announced today that MCBANK has selected Jack Henry to support its long-term growth strategy, build its commercial banking ..."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Ny dansk topmoderne fabrik skal styrke kvaliteten af fødevarer - TekniskFOKUS,www.tekniskfokus.dk (Helle Friemann Nielsen),2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tekniskfokus.dk/ny-dansk-topmoderne-fabrik-skal-styrke-kvaliteten-af-foedevarer/,"Automatisering Navnenyt Procesteknologi Robotter Top 01. 06. 2026 By Helle Friemann Nielsen Dansk teknologi spiller en afgørende rolle i den globale fødevarekvalitet: Omkring 80 procent af al mælk og korn i verden analyseres i dag med løsninger fra FOSS. Torsdag den 28. maj åbnede det familieejede selskab sin nye fabrik, FOSS Production & Logistics, der fremover skal producere de innovative analyseinstrumenter, som bliver brugt verden over. ... Med lyset strømmende ind gennem store panoramavinduer, lyden af klirrende glas og omkring 200 særligt inviterede gæster samlet, blev fabrikken officielt indviet i den højloftede hjørnekantine, der har uforstyrret udsigt over marker og skov. Snoren blev klippet af Frederikssunds borgmester Anne Sofie Uhrskov, DI-direktør Lars Sandahl Sørensen og FOSS-bestyrelsesformand Peter Foss. -Åbningen er en milepæl i FOSS’ nu 70-årige historie. Vi tager et stort skridt ind i fremtiden med vores nye topmoderne fabrik, der vil styrke fundamentet under vores vækstrejse. Samtidig med at vi er en meget global virksomhed, sætter vi streg under vores forankring i Danmark, hvor vi er tæt på vores innovationscenter i Hillerød og har adgang til kompetent arbejdskraft, siger adm. direktør i FOSS, Christian Rosenkrantz de Lasson. ... En fabrik i verdensklasse Den nye fabrik omfatter 18.000 kvadratmeter og er opført på en 15 hektar stor grund i naturskønne omgivelser. Investeringen beløber sig til ca. en halv mia. kr. og afspejler FOSS’ filosofi om at træffe langsigtede og bæredygtige løsninger. Hjertet i bygningen og produktionsprocessen er en automatiseret lagerløsning. AutoStore-løsningen leveret i samarbejde med Element Logic A/S. Læs mere om lagerløsningen i Teknisk Nyt. ... Fabrikken er baseret på jordvarme og solenergi, og vil efter planen blive suppleret med en vindmølle på grunden i 2027. Samlet set vil den producere mere strøm, end FOSS forbruger globalt. Samtidig sætter FOSS nye standarder for rammerne omkring moderne produktion. Fabrikken rummer blandt andet fitnessfaciliteter, massagerum, indbydende fællesområder og storslået udsigter til det omkringliggende landskab. -FOSS er et unikt og inspirerende eksempel på et dansk familieejet selskab, der tør tænke langsigtet og investere i fremtiden. Med den nye fabrik i Vinge viser de, at global vækst sagtens kan gå hånd i hånd med en stærk lokal forankring og fastholdelse af produktion i Danmark, siger Lars Sandahl Sørensen, adm. direktør i DI. ... FOSS Production & Logistics • Investering: 500 mio. kr. • Størrelse: 18.000 kvm • Lokation: Vinge, Frederikssund • Arkitekt: Henning Larsen Architects, Totalentreprenør: 5E • Bygningen har opnået guld præcertificering i den internationale DGNB-certificering. • Medarbejderne flytter ind i løbet af 2026. • Bonusinfo: Fabrikken er beklædt med italiensk skifer, og bygningen har en unik tagkonstruktion med limtræsbjælker som det bærende element og ovenlysvinduer i otte m. højde."
Fritz Foss,,,,Exa,Official opening of FOSS Production & Logistics ✂️ | FOSS,www.linkedin.com (FOSS),2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/foss_official-opening-of-foss-production-logistics-activity-7466066259592396800-sUje,"# Official opening of FOSS Production & Logistics ✂️ | FOSS · LinkedIn · 2026-05-29 ... **FOSS**: FOSS creates end-to-end solutions that secure and improve food quality. From raw material to finished product. Our analysis instruments refine measurements into information management that enables businesses to run intelligent data-driven productions with less waste and bigger yields. FOSS has 800-900 employees (+2-3% YoY) and has annual revenue in the $300M-$400M range, founded in 1956. Headquartered in Hillerød, Capital Region, Denmark, operates in 22 countries (including United States, China, Poland, Japan, and New Zealand). Its workforce is distributed across 37 countries (including Denmark, Poland, United States, Sweden, and China). ... Official opening of [FOSS](https://linkedin.com/company/foss) Production & Logistics ✂️ ... With our new global facility in Vinge, Denmark, we are scaling our ability to deliver what the world depends on and carry out our tasks with an even greater reach. ... We play our part by partnering with the global food and agriculture industry. And we do so all across the globe. ... 95% of the world’s wine, and 80% of the world’s milk and grain are analyzed with a [ ... ](https://linkedin.com/company/foss) solution. ... With our new future proof production facility, we’ve taken a major step to further strengthen our role. ... Our mission hasn’t changed: We contribute to the sustainable use of our planet's agricultural resources, and thus to the nutrition and health of the people of the world. ... We couldn’t be more excited about what our new site enables. ... > Congratulations on this impressive milestone. 👏 > > Having worked across food, pharma, and other regulated industries, I have seen firsthand that sustainable growth depends on much more than new facilities and technology. It requires strong capabilities, clear processes, and a culture that enables people to deliver quality and compliance every day. > > Wishing the FOSS Team every success in this exciting new chapter. 🌱"
