Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,"Automatic Lawn Mower Market to Reach USD 5,906.8M by 2032 (11.5% CAGR) - News Release",www.prnewsreleaser.com (PW Consulting),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewsreleaser.com/news/342306,"Automatic Lawn Mower Market to Reach USD 5,906.8M by 2032 (11.5% CAGR) - News Release # Automatic Lawn Mower Market to Reach USD 5,906.8M by 2032 (11.5% CAGR) 2026-07-09 by PW Consulting ... As PW Consulting’s Senior Strategy Advisor and Chief Industry Analyst, I present a strategic preview of our latest market study on the Automatic Lawn Mower market. This briefing is designed specifically for executives, corporate development teams, product leaders, and investors who must make high‑stakes decisions in 2026. It synthesizes the essential macro trends, competitive dynamics, regulatory inflections, and prioritized plays that our full report unpacks in operational detail. Consider this a premium trailer: we reveal the directional intelligence and strategic implications while reserving the granular segment matrices and proprietary valuations for the full report. Automatic ... Mower Market ... Investment and product decisions made in 2026 will determine competitive positions through the next technology cycle. Our base-year alignment (2025) and the forecast horizon (2026–2032) show a robust structural expansion driven by electrification, sensor‑fusion navigation, and the consumerization of commercial autonomy. The market’s compound annual growth rate (CAGR) is 11.5% over the forecast horizon, reflecting accelerating adoption across both residential and commercial use cases. From a strategic perspective, that growth curve creates three interlocking imperatives: (1) capture early share in high-growth subsegments enabled by wire‑free navigation and LiDAR/AI stacks, (2) de‑risk supply chain exposure to battery and sensor cost swings, and (3) define profitable service and fleet models before commoditization intensifies. Automatic Lawn Mower Market ... Our topline study anchors on 2025 as the base year and models a sustained climb through 2032. In practical terms, the market approximately doubles over the forecast window, a signal of both expanding unit demand and rising average selling prices for advanced, boundary‑free systems. For strategy teams, this implies that product roadmaps aligned with premium sensor suites and connectivity can command margin expansion even as lower‑cost models retain broad penetration. Importantly, the market concentration metrics indicate a concentrated competitive set: the top three players collectively hold a significant share of revenue, and the top five add only marginally beyond that, underscoring the scale advantages enjoyed by incumbents. Automatic Lawn Mower Market ... - Sensor fusion becomes the table stakes. LiDAR, NetRTK/RTK‑grade positioning, dual‑camera AI vision, and complementary inertial systems are migrating from high‑end commercial units to premium residential products. The strategic implication: R&D investments must prioritize integrated stack development, not just component procurement. ... - Wire‑free navigation is a growth catalyst. The transition from boundary‑wire models to wire‑free solutions (visual SLAM, LiDAR mapping, RTK enhancement) opens new installation pathways and subscription models, but also raises customer support and safety requirements. ... - Battery economics and supply constraints. Lithium‑ion cost dynamics materially influence price positioning across the portfolio. Product teams must model battery pack options and lifecycle‑based service bundles to defend margins. ... - Regulatory tightening affects time‑to‑market. Emerging safety standards for AI vision in consumer robotics, updated federal blade‑stop mechanisms, and enhanced CE marking/ISO expectations require proactive compliance engineering. Noncompliance is a commercial risk; early certification planning is now a competitive advantage. ... of high‑value residential and professional segments ... - Robotics‑native challengers (e.g., Segway Navimow, Mammotion, Ambrogio, Positec’s Greenworks). These firms push innovation in LiDAR, NetRTK and wireless fleet orchestration. Recent product launches — including Segway Navimow’s early‑2026 LiDAR models and Mammotion’s LUBA 3 AWD series — demonstrate how challenger innovations compress incumbent response windows. ... - Scale challengers from China (e.g., Mammotion, Positec Group investments). Aggressive capital deployment and vertically integrated manufacturing enable rapid price‑performance gains. Strategic responses from Western OEMs include deeper IP, service differentiation, and channel exclusivity. ... Recent market actions give additional clues about near‑term trajectories: Husqvarna’s late‑2025 introduction of AI‑enhanced Automower variants with infrared night vision underscores the migration of advanced sensing into mainstream product lines. Segway Navimow’s January 2026 LiDAR launches accelerate the pace at which wire‑free, high‑precision navigation becomes ubiquitous. And material investments from players like Positec signal that M&A and capacity expansion will remain active themes. ... - A regulatory compliance checklist mapped to product release timelines, including recommended test plans and certification milestones for CE, ISO, and U ... federal safety standards. ... - M&A heatmaps, strategic partnership frameworks, and due‑diligence checklists tailored to acquiring robotics IP or channel footprint. ... - Prioritize wire‑free, mapped navigation for premium segments. Plan product introductions and channel pilots in 2026 that showcase wire‑free installation and simplified user setup; differentiate on night‑time operation and AI obstacle handling. ... - Architect for lifecycle value, not just unit sale. Introduce connectivity tiers and predictive maintenance subscriptions to monetize battery replacements and sensor upgrades. ... - Lock in supply for critical sensors and battery cells. Secure long‑lead contracts and dual‑sourcing plans to mitigate price volatility and capacity constraints. ... - Invest in compliance and safety engineering early. Embed certification gates in product roadmaps to avoid costly rework and market launch delays as standards evolve. ... - Use focused partnerships to accelerate fleet and commercial capabilities. For firms lacking enterprise experience, partner with telematics or grounds‑maintenance platforms rather than building end‑to‑end systems internally. ... - Be acquisition‑ready. Maintain an M&A scout list of robotics IP, fleet‑management startups, and sensor integrators to rapidly fill capability gaps. ... This preview was designed to surface the strategic signals that will matter most for 2026 planning cycles: robust market growth at an 11.5% CAGR, a near‑doubling of market size across the 2026–2032 horizon, and a competitive set dominated by a small number of scale players. If you are evaluating product investments, preparing for regulatory certification, modeling channel transitions, or building M&A mandates, the full PW Consulting report provides the executable data, scenario models, and playbooks you need to act with conviction. ... For 2026, the competitive window is both wide and narrow: market growth creates many opportunities, but the pace of technological adoption and regulatory change compresses timing. Executives who combine targeted product investments, supply‑chain resilience, and monetized connectivity will capture disproportionate value. Our full report is organized to get your team from strategy to execution in 90 days — with clear milestones for R&D, certification, channel rollout, and M&A. Use this preview to prioritize, and let the full intelligence de‑risk your next moves."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI,www.brazilbusinessinsights.com,2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.brazilbusinessinsights.com/news/moomoo-engine-launch-futu-xp-nubank-brazil,"Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI ... # Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil ... Moomoo is launching 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified trading toolkit designed to capture active retail and professional traders in Brazil, challenging incumbents. ... - ▸ Global user base: Over 22 million users - ▸ Launch date: July 2, 2026 - ▸ Target market: Active retail & pro traders - ▸ Primary region: Brazil expansion ... The Bottom Line: - Moomoo, the digital brokerage subsidiary of Futu Holdings ($FUTU), is set to launch 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified suite of advanced trading tools designed to consolidate market analysis, charting, and execution. - The rollout represents a strategic push to capture high-value retail and professional traders in emerging markets, particularly Brazil, where digital brokerage competition is intensifying. - While the launch enhances $FUTU's technological moat, it poses direct competitive pressure on local incumbents such as XP Inc. ($XP) and Nubank ($NU). Strategic Expansion in Latin America: Futu Holdings ($FUTU), through its international trading platform Moomoo, is accelerating its expansion into Latin America with the exclusive announcement of 'Moomoo Engine.' This unified toolkit is designed to streamline the trading lifecycle for retail and professional investors. By integrating advanced charting, real-time data analytics, and algorithmic execution into a single, cohesive interface, Moomoo aims to address the fragmentation that has historically plagued active traders in emerging markets. The Brazilian market, characterized by a highly sophisticated retail investor base and a rapidly growing interest in global equities, serves as the primary launchpad for this technological deployment. Technological Disruption and the 'Moomoo Engine': The 'Moomoo Engine' represents a significant upgrade to the platform's existing infrastructure. Historically, active traders in Brazil have had to rely on multiple third-party platforms for technical analysis, order routing, and portfolio tracking. This fragmentation often leads to latency issues, higher subscription costs, and execution inefficiencies. Moomoo's unified toolkit addresses these pain points by offering proprietary, low-latency charting algorithms and institutional-grade data feeds directly within the trading application. This integration is expected to lower the barrier to entry for advanced trading strategies, enabling retail investors to execute complex multi-leg options strategies and automated technical trades with greater precision. Competitive Dynamics in the Brazilian Brokerage Sector: The introduction of the 'Moomoo Engine' comes at a time of intense competition within the Brazilian financial services sector. Incumbents like XP Inc. ($XP) and BTG Pactual have traditionally dominated the affluent and active trader segments through extensive advisory networks and proprietary platforms. Concurrently, digital-first platforms like Nubank ($NU) and Inter have successfully democratized access to basic investment products for the mass market. Moomoo's strategy bypasses the traditional advisory model, focusing instead on self-directed, tech-savvy traders who prioritize execution speed, analytical depth, and low transaction costs. By offering institutional-grade tools without the premium price tag, Moomoo is positioning itself to capture market share from both high-end incumbents and mass-market digital banks looking to upsell their user bases. Regulatory and Operational Considerations: Operating a foreign-backed digital brokerage in Brazil requires navigating a complex regulatory framework overseen by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Brazil (CVM) and the Central Bank of Brazil (BCB). Moomoo's expansion strategy relies heavily on seamless integration with local clearing systems and compliance with strict foreign exchange (FX) regulations. For Brazilian investors trading international assets, tax compliance—specifically the calculation of capital gains and the monthly 'Carnê-Leão' tax filing—has historically been a major friction point. To gain widespread adoption, the 'Moomoo Engine' must integrate localized tax reporting tools that simplify these compliance obligations for domestic users. Furthermore, fluctuations in the USD/BRL exchange rate remain a critical variable, as currency volatility can significantly impact the net returns of Brazilian investors trading on US exchanges through the platform. Implications for Futu Holdings ($FUTU): For Futu Holdings ($FUTU), the successful rollout of the 'Moomoo Engine' in Brazil is vital for its broader international diversification strategy. Facing mature markets and regulatory headwinds in mainland China and Hong Kong, Futu has increasingly looked to Southeast Asia and Latin America to drive its next phase of growth. Brazil represents one of the largest retail investment markets in the developing world, making it a high-stakes testing ground for Moomoo's global scalability. If the 'Moomoo Engine' succeeds in capturing a meaningful share of Brazil's active trading volume, it could serve as a blueprint for further expansion into other Latin American markets, such as Mexico and Colombia, thereby bolstering Futu's long-term revenue growth and reducing its geographic concentration risk. ... Market Impact: The launch of the 'Moomoo Engine' has distinct implications for the key players in the digital brokerage space: - Futu Holdings ($FUTU): Bullish. The successful deployment of advanced trading tools in Brazil accelerates Futu's international diversification, reducing its reliance on Asian markets and opening a high-margin revenue stream from active Latin American traders. - XP Inc. ($XP): Bearish. XP faces direct technological competition in its high-value active trader segment. While its advisory network remains a strong moat, Moomoo's low-cost, high-tech offering could pressure XP's commission margins and active client retention. - Nu Holdings ($NU): Neutral. Nubank's primary investment audience consists of mass-market retail investors rather than sophisticated active traders. However, as Nubank seeks to upsell its client base into more complex financial products, Moomoo's advanced platform represents a long-term competitive hurdle. ... > analyst consensus: Bullish on Futu Holdings ($FUTU) international expansion; bearish on XP Inc. ($XP) active trader retention; neutral on Nu Holdings ($NU). > asset_class: Equities"
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,"HIVE Digital Technologies’ Buzz HPC joins Bell and Cohere for Canadian AI factory - ICYMI | TSX:HIVE, NASDAQ:HIVE, BVC:HIVECO",www.proactiveinvestors.com (Emily Jarvie),2026-06-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1094602/hive-digital-technologies-buzz-hpc-joins-bell-and-cohere-for-canadian-ai-factory-icymi-1094602.html,"HIVE Digital Technologies’ Buzz HPC joins Bell and Cohere for Canadian AI factory - ICYMI ... , BVC:HIVECO ... # HIVE Digital Technologies’ Buzz HPC joins Bell and Cohere for Canadian AI factory - ICYMI ... HIVE Digital Technologies Ltd (TSX:HIVE, NASDAQ:HIVE, FRA:YO0, BVC:HIVECO) subsidiary Buzz HPC earlier this week discussed its role in a newly announced Canadian sovereign AI infrastructure initiative involving Bell Canada, Cohere and Hypertec, with CEO Craig Tavares outlining how the partnership aims to create a fully domestic AI ecosystem capable of supporting enterprise, government and research applications across the country. ... Speaking with Proactive, Tavares said the collaboration grew out of Bell Canada's Bell AI Fabric initiative, which was launched to bring together leading Canadian companies capable of delivering sovereign AI infrastructure. He explained that the addition of Cohere completed what he described as a fully Canadian AI stack, extending from data centres and networking through to AI models and compute infrastructure. ... Tavares said Bell AI Fabric contributes data centre capacity, connectivity, professional services and cybersecurity, while Cohere provides enterprise-grade AI models and applications. Hypertec supplies and integrates Canadian-built AI hardware, creating an end-to-end platform designed to keep sensitive data within Canadian-operated systems. ... According to Tavares, the initiative addresses a growing demand for sovereign AI infrastructure among organizations seeking to meet regulatory, compliance and security requirements. He said the platform is intended for a broad range of users, including governments, researchers, healthcare providers and financial institutions. ... Tavares also outlined Buzz HPC's role in delivering the AI-native GPU cloud layer that connects infrastructure, networking, compute and AI applications into what the company refers to as an ""AI factory."" He said the company is positioning the combined offering as production-grade sovereign AI infrastructure located and operated entirely within Canada. ... The interview also highlighted Buzz HPC's ongoing expansion strategy. Tavares noted that the company has established a presence in British Columbia through the Bell partnership and recently announced developments in Manitoba and the Greater Toronto Area. ... One potential catalyst for investors is the planned AI gigafactory project in the GTA, which Tavares said is expected to host more than 100,000 GPUs. Additional growth opportunities may emerge through the company's edge infrastructure developments in Toronto and upgrades to facilities in New Brunswick. ... Tavares said Buzz HPC's growing footprint across multiple provinces demonstrates the scale of the company's ambitions and strengthens its ability to serve organizations seeking Canadian sovereign AI infrastructure. ... ### HIVE Digital upsizes note to $115m to fuel AI and GPU cloud expansion ... HIVE Digital Technologies Ltd (TSX:HIVE, NASDAQ:HIVE, FRA:YO0, BVC:HIVECO) CEO Aydin Kilic joined Proactive's Stephen Gunnion to discuss the company's upsized US$115 million zero-coupon exchangeable note offering and how it will accelerate HIVE's AI infrastructure, GPU cloud and HPC... ... BUZZ HPC joins Bell Canada and Cohere to build Canada’s sovereign... ... HIVE Digital secures $220 Million AI deal and expands data center... ... 2/2026 ... HIVE Digital delivers record revenue growth as Bitcoin and AI... ... Buzz AI acquisition strengthens Hive’s Canadian AI infrastructure..."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,Husky HyCAP 4.0 Tooling for Beverage Closures,www.packagingworldinsights.com (API PWI),2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingworldinsights.com/trends/husky-hycap-4-0-tooling-advancing-injection-molding-performance-for-beverage-closures/,"Husky HyCAP 4.0 Tooling for Beverage Closures ... # Husky HyCAP® 4.0 Tooling: Advancing Injection Molding Performance for Beverage Closures As the beverage packaging industry continues to evolve, manufacturers face increasing pressure to deliver lighter, more sustainable, and regulation compliant closures without sacrificing performance or cost efficiency. ... Husky Technologies addresses these challenges with HyCAP® 4.0 tooling, a next-generation solution engineered to maximize injection molding performance for beverage closures. ... The introduction of tethered closure requirements under EU regulations has increased the need for flexible manufacturing solutions. ... ® 4.0 tooling offers enhanced design flexibility, allowing ... - Switch between tethered and non-tethered closures with minimal changes - Respond quickly to evolving regulatory requirements - Support a wider range of closure applications ... With HyCAP® 4.0 tooling, Husky Technologies delivers a solution designed to meet both current and future demands in beverage closure production. ... From improved precision and durability to enhanced flexibility and lower operating costs, HyCAP® 4.0 enables manufacturers to optimize performance while supporting long-term sustainability goals. ... As the industry continues to evolve, advanced tooling solutions like HyCAP® 4.0 will be essential to achieving efficient, reliable, and future-ready beverage packaging operations."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,Husky HyCap 4.0 Targets Closure Manufacturers,www.plasticstoday.com,2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.plasticstoday.com/packaging/husky-technologies-launches-hycap-40-tooling-platform-for-beverage-closure-manufacturing-efficiency,"ky HyCap 4.0 Targets Closure Manufacturers ... # Husky Launches HyCap 4.0 Tooling for Beverage Closure Manufacturing ... The injection molding solution targets lightweight, sustainable packaging production while addressing tethered cap mandates and regulatory pressures. ... May 29, 2026 ... - Platform enables ultra-lightweight ... production with enhanced precision and repeatability capabilities. ... - Advanced polymer bushings reduce steel-to-steel contact to minimize wear and extend mold life significantly. ... - Tooling supports both tethered and non-tethered ... designs with minimal changeover requirements. ... Husky Technologies is targeting beverage closure manufacturers with its newly launched HyCap 4.0 tooling platform, an injection molding solution engineered to meet rising demands for lightweight, sustainable packaging while navigating increasingly complex regulatory requirements. ... The timing addresses critical industry pressures. Beverage packaging producers face mounting challenges from tethered cap mandates in the European Union, accelerating lightweighting trends, and the need for faster production cycles with lower operating costs. For plastics processors, the company said this platform represents an advancement in precision tooling designed specifically for high-volume closure production environments. ... According to Husky, HyCap 4.0 tooling enables ultra-lightweight beverage closure production with enhanced precision and repeatability. The system supports accurate molding of increasingly complex closure designs while maintaining consistent, high-quality output across fast production cycles — a critical capability as closure designs become more intricate to meet sustainability and functionality requirements. ... Enhanced durability stands as a cornerstone feature. Husky said the tooling incorporates advanced material selection and precision-guided stack design to improve long-term reliability in demanding production environments. A notable innovation includes polymer bushings that reduce steel-to-steel contact between core components, helping minimize wear, extend mold life, and lower the risk of mechanical failure during millions of production cycles. ... These durability improvements translate directly to operational benefits. With fewer wear-prone components and extended maintenance intervals, manufacturers can reduce downtime and improve production consistency. The result: improved overall equipment effectiveness (OEE) through faster cycle times, higher uptime, and simplified servicing. ... Flexibility represents another key advantage. Husky highlighted the tooling's capability to support both tethered and non-tethered closure production, allowing manufacturers to switch between designs with minimal tooling changes. Husky said this adaptability enables quicker responses to changing regulatory and market requirements without major capital investments — particularly valuable as regulations continue evolving across global markets. ... Beyond operational efficiency, Husky said the new tooling solution helps reduce total cost of ownership by lowering maintenance expenses, minimizing spare parts consumption, and reducing production disruptions. These economic benefits complement the platform's technical capabilities, addressing the full spectrum of manufacturer concerns from production floor performance to financial impact. ... As beverage brands continue prioritizing sustainability and lightweight packaging, Husky believes advanced tooling technologies such as HyCap 4.0 will play an increasingly important role in delivering efficient, reliable, and future-ready beverage closure manufacturing. The company concluded its platform positions manufacturers to meet current demands while adapting to future regulatory and market shifts in the evolving beverage packaging landscape."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,"Husky Technologies has appointed Karen Stone as its chief human resources officer, effective June 22, 2026. | HR News Canada",www.linkedin.com (HR News Canada),2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/hr-news-canada_husky-technologies-names-karen-stone-as-chief-activity-7466132168637853696-_y85,"Husky Technologies names Karen Stone as chief human resources officer | HR News Canada | 42 comments ... Husky Technologies has appointed Karen Stone as its chief human resources officer, effective June 22, 2026. Stone joins the Bolton, Ontario-based company from WESCO International, a Fortune 200 distributor, where she served as vice-president, human resources. She has more than 20 years of experience leading global organizations through mergers, leadership redesign, and operating model changes. “I look forward to partnering with Karen to build the world-class team and high-performance culture that will power our next phase of growth,"" said Robert Domodossola, president and chief executive officer of Husky. Full story here: https://lnkd.in/efdKeCAj#HR#CHRO#PeopleontheMove#HRNews ... Husky Technologies names Karen Stone as chief human resources officer https://hrnewscanada.com"
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,GPGI | Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as Chief Financial Officer and Karen Stone as Chief Human Resources Officer,gpgi.com (Ben),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://gpgi.com/husky-technologies-appoints-mohammad-kanaan-as-chief-financial-officer-and-karen-stone-as-chief-human-resources-officer/,"GPGI | Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as Chief Financial Officer and Karen Stone as Chief Human Resources Officer ... ### Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as Chief Financial Officer and Karen Stone as Chief Human Resources Officer ... BOLTON, Ontario, May 28, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) — GPGI, Inc.(NYSE: GPGI) today announced the appointments of Mohammad Kanaan as Chief Financial Officer and Karen Stone as Chief Human Resources Officer of Husky Technologies™ (“Husky” or the “Company”), a GPGI business. Mr. Kanaan and Ms. Stone will join the Company effective June 8 and June 22, 2026, respectively. The appointments add significant financial and human resources expertise to Husky’s leadership team, reinforcing GPGI’s commitment to building a world-class management team at the Husky business and accelerating the Company’s growth strategy through the Resolute Operating System. ... Dave Cote, GPGI’s Executive Chairman, said, “We are thrilled to welcome Mohammad and Karen to Husky. Both are proven leaders with significant global experience that will accelerate the cultural transformation Rob is leading across the business. We remain focused on doing the things necessary to position Husky to achieve its full potential as a high-performing company – and the addition of Mohammad and Karen represent a big step in that process.” ... Robert Domodossola, President and CEO of Husky, continued, “Bringing Mohammad and Karen onto our leadership team is a significant milestone for Husky. I look forward to partnering with Mohammad to instill a culture of financial rigor and operational discipline, and with Karen to build the world-class team and high-performance culture that will power our next phase of growth. These are exactly the right leaders for this moment.” ... a senior finance executive with more than 20 years of international experience across global manufacturing, energy services, and management consulting. He joins Husky from Carrier Global Corporation, where he most recently served as Chief Financial Officer of the Replacement Components (Aftermarket) division, overseeing complex supply chain operations and a global P&L of over $1 billion. He has held progressively senior leadership roles at Schlumberger and Deloitte Canada, where he spearheaded major finance transformations and margin expansion initiatives in complex, multinational environments. Mr. Kanaan holds an Executive MBA from Ivey Business School at the University of Western Ontario and is a Certified Management Accountant (CMA). ... Karen Stone is a senior human resources executive with more than 20 years of experience leading global organizations through transformation, complex integrations, and leadership and operating model redesign. She joins from Fortune 200 company WESCO International, where she served as Vice President, Human Resources. There, Ms. Stone was instrumental in the successful $4.5 billion merger with Anixter, where her leadership contributed to delivering more than $300 million in cost synergies ahead of schedule. Ms. Stone holds CHRO Certificate and Executive Compensation Strategies credentials from the Wharton School at the University of Pennsylvania, and an Honours BA in Labour Relations and Economics from McMaster University. ... GPGI, Inc. (NYSE: GPGI) is a diversified, multi-industry platform for companies with great positions in good industries. The platform is managed by Resolute Holdings Management, Inc. (NYSE: RHLD) and is purpose-built to acquire, own, and scale high-quality businesses led by great operators, benefiting from a permanent capital base and the systematic deployment of the Resolute Operating System. GPGI currently consists of CompoSecure and Husky – two market leaders with best-in-class financials and durable opportunities for growth. For more information, please visit GPGI.com. ... Founded in 1953, Husky is a technology pioneer that enables the delivery of essential needs to the global community with industry-leading expertise and service. Husky is a leader in highly engineered equipment and aftermarket services. Husky’s products are used to manufacture a wide range of plastic products, including beverage and food containers, medical devices, and consumer electronic parts. Husky provides comprehensive and integrated systems solutions that are comprised of injection molding machines, molds, hot runners, controllers, and auxiliaries. For more information, please visit Husky.co."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,"Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as CFO and Karen Stone as CHRO on May 28, 2026 - GeneOnline News",www.geneonline.com (GOAI),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.geneonline.com/husky-technologies-appoints-mohammad-kanaan-as-cfo-and-karen-stone-as-chro-on-may-28-2026/,"Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as CFO and Karen Stone as CHRO on May 28, 2026 - GeneOnline News ... ### Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as CFO and Karen Stone as CHRO on May 28, 2026 ... Husky Technologies Appoints Mohammad Kanaan as CFO and Karen Stone as CHRO on May 28, 2026 ... Husky Technologies recently announced the appointment of Mohammad Kanaan as Chief Financial Officer and Karen Stone as Chief Human Resources Officer. These appointments mark a strategic shift in the company’s leadership structure. ... Mohammad Kanaan assumes the role of CFO, bringing his expertise in financial management to Husky Technologies. Karen Stone steps in as CHRO, where she will oversee the company’s human resources strategies and employee relations. The company made the announcement on Thursday, May 28, 2026."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,Husky Technologies strengthens India presence with Chennai expansion initiatives,www.foodtechbiz.com (FoodTechBiz Desk),2026-05-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-18 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.foodtechbiz.com/business-updates/husky-technologies-strengthens-india-presence-with-chennai-expansion-initiatives,"Husky Technologies strengthens India presence with Chennai expansion initiatives ... # Husky Technologies strengthens India presence with Chennai expansion initiatives ... Husky Technologies has announced major expansion initiatives in Chennai, reinforcing the company’s long-term commitment to India and its continued focus on advancing digital innovation, engineering excellence, and regional manufacturing capabilities. ... As part of its ongoing IT and R&D strategy, Husky has opened a new shared office in Chennai to further strengthen its digital and engineering operations. The new facility is expected to play a key role in supporting the development of future-ready technologies while enhancing collaboration and technical expertise across global teams. ... The expansion reflects Husky’s broader vision of driving innovation and building stronger internal capabilities to support customers and partners worldwide. ... In another significant milestone, the company also marked the ceremonial beginning of a factory expansion project at its Chennai campus. The initiative highlights Husky’s continued investment in India and its commitment to strengthening its local footprint to better serve producers across the region. ... According to the company, the expansion comes at a time when India is increasingly emerging as a global hub for sustainable manufacturing, creating growing demand for advanced production solutions and localized support. ... The Chennai expansion represents the next chapter in Husky’s 25-year journey in India and underscores the company’s long-term growth strategy for the region. ... Husky stated that it looks forward to sharing further progress as the project advances."
Husky Technologies,,,,Exa,"Webinar Alert: Husky Technologies to spotlight all-PET closures as beverage industry pushes for circular packaging | Food Business Middle East & Africa - No.1 Food & Beverage Formulation, Processing & Packaging Publication",www.foodbusinessmea.com,2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.foodbusinessmea.com/webinar-alert-husky-technologies-to-spotlight-all-pet-closures-as-beverage-industry-pushes-for-circular-packaging/,"Webinar Alert: Husky Technologies to spotlight all-PET closures as beverage industry pushes for circular packaging | Food Business Middle East & Africa - No.1 Food & Beverage Formulation, Processing & Packaging Publication ... # Webinar Alert: Husky Technologies to spotlight all-PET closures as beverage industry pushes for circular packaging ... GLOBAL – Husky Technologies has announced yet another webinar to explore the growing shift toward mono-material beverage packaging solutions designed to improve recyclability and circularity. ... The webinar, titled “One Material, One Package: Advancing Sustainability with All-PET Closures and Bottle,” will be held in June 23, 2026, with the official date yet to be confirmed. ... The session comes at a time when the global beverage packaging industry is accelerating efforts to reduce material complexity, improve recycling rates, and tightening environmental regulations. ... During the webinar, Husky will showcase its HyCAP™ SecuRE+ solution, an innovation that combines PET closures with PET bottles in a single-material packaging approach aimed at simplifying recycling streams and supporting a more circular packaging model. ... The webinar will also examine several trends transforming the sector, including lightweight packaging, tethered closures, improved tamper-evidence technologies, and system-level optimization aimed at reducing material usage and operational costs. ... Growing consumer demand for sustainable packaging, coupled with stricter regulations on plastic waste and recycled content targets, is pushing beverage companies to rethink packaging design and material choices. ... Participants attending the session will gain insights into how an all-PET bottle-and-closure system can help brands achieve sustainability targets without compromising performance. ... The webinar will further explore how HyCAP™ SecuRE+ enhances consumer security through advanced tamper-evidence capabilities while improving capping efficiency and production line performance. ... Attendees are also expected to learn how lightweighting strategies can reduce resin consumption, lower transportation costs, and improve environmental outcomes across the packaging value chain. ... In addition, the discussion will highlight how integrated packaging system optimization can support both environmental compliance and long-term business profitability. ... The webinar will be led by Michael White, Director of Business Development for Closures at Husky Technologies. ... White is responsible for the global market introduction of new beverage closure injection molding technologies and Husky’s portfolio of beverage closures. ... With more than two decades of experience in product management and marketing across Husky’s operations in the United States and Canada, White is expected to provide valuable insights into the evolving demands facing beverage packaging manufacturers and brand owners worldwide. ... Packaging professionals, sustainability managers, converters, bottlers, recyclers, and equipment specialists are encouraged to attend the webinar to better understand how next-generation mono-material solutions could shape the future of circular beverage packaging."
Husky Technologies,,,,Linkup,"Husky exhibits at Propak Asia 2026, deepening commitment to Southeast Asian packaging producers",Husky Technologies official news,2026-06-10T00:00:00Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.husky.co/en/about-us/news/husky-exhibits-at-propak-asia-2026-deepening-commitment-to-southeast-asian-packaging-producers/,"Husky Technologies showcased its solutions at Propak Asia 2026, emphasizing that rising conversion costs and sustainability mandates are parallel goals for regional packaging producers. The event highlights Husky's regional relevance and commitment to Southeast Asia."
