 is intended to facilitate correct sorting after use and support participation in recycling systems. ... Klöckner Pentaplast also reports that kp Infinity fruit trays have a lower carbon footprint and require less water and energy in production compared with alternative packaging materials. According to the company, this is intended to help customers meet broader sustainability goals. For customers seeking a complete packaging solution, the trays can be combined with a kp FlexiStretch overwrap or kp FlexiFlow films. In this configuration, the solutions are intended to provide appropriate product presentation and protection, while also helping to maintain the quality of fresh fruit from the packing line to the retail shelf. ... Austin Schwarz, Sales Director for the UK and Ireland in the kp Food Packaging division, said: “Following the success of kp Infinity in food-to-go applications, we identified growing demand for recyclable packaging solutions in the fresh produce sector. The new fruit tray range combines the durability, presentation and recyclability customers expect in a format designed specifically for whole fruit such as apples and pears.” ... He added: “When combined with a kp FlexiStretch overwrap or our kp FlexiFlow films, customers can obtain a complete packaging solution from a single supplier, benefiting from simplified procurement, technical expertise and consistent packaging performance across the supply chain.” ... The launch of the new range strengthens the company’s portfolio in fresh produce packaging and confirms its development direction focused on solutions intended to support customers in achieving environmental and operational objectives. ... ## Klöckner Pentaplast ... Manufacturer of plastic films specializing in high‑barrier films and recycled-content packaging solutions for the pharmaceutical, food and consumer industries."
