Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Romania's TeraPlast completes acquisition of Spain plant | Romania Investments News | SeeNews,seenews.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://seenews.com/news/romanias-teraplast-completes-acquisition-of-spain-plant-1297397,"# Romania's TeraPlast completes acquisition of Spain plant ... July 1 (SeeNews) - Romanian construction materials producer TeraPlast Group said on Wednesday that it has completed the acquisition of the MASA polyethylene pipe manufacturing facility in Spain from Belgian peer Aliaxis. ... ###### Romania's TeraPlast inaugurates pipe plant in Spain ... ###### Latest in Teraplast SA ... ###### Bucharest stocks fall further, TeraPlast leads blue-chip decliners ... ###### Romania's Teraplast enters Spain through plant acquisition ... ###### Romania's TeraPlast swings to net loss in Q1"
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Klöckner Pentaplast event discusses food packaging trends,www.packagingnews.co.uk (Waqas Qureshi),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingnews.co.uk/news/markets/food/klockner-pentaplast-event-discusses-food-packaging-trends-25-06-2026,"# Klöckner Pent ... last event discusses food packaging trends ... Klöckner Pentaplast (KP) has recently hosted an event covering trends within the food packaging sector, attended by retailers, recyclers, technology providers and manufacturers. ... The ‘Inside the Future of Food Packaging’ event was held at Silverstone motor racing circuit, with conversations on how the industry can adapt to evolving sustainability regulations while maintaining performance, shelf appeal and commercial viability. ... Discussions ranged from extended producer responsibility (EPR) and the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR) to consumer recycling behaviour, soft plastics, and the growing role of AI on the factory floor and in packaging design. ... PPWR and EPR reforms were a key topic of discussion. Denise Mathieson, head of packaging innovation & programme delivery, Waitrose & Partners, suggested that the raft of new compliance standards created a balancing act that many businesses are still unprepared for. While the focus on EPR is welcome, Mathieson argued that the same focus should be applied to PPWR, given its far-reaching impact on issues like PET recycling. ... The event covered many case studies that demonstrated how this kind of collaboration can drive real progress. ... For example, Tesco’s ‘Bring Back’ trial; partnerships with Plastic Energy and SABIC; customer-returned soft plastics being used in cheese wrap, and later moved towards mono-material solutions when chemical recycling proved too costly and complex. The best case studies always focus on the practical, rather than the theoretical, and events like this present an opportunity to learn from them. ... Thomas Jakobsen, president, Food Packaging, KP, said: “Packaging today is no longer simply about containment or protection. It is about balancing increasingly complex demands, performance, sustainability, compliance and cost, often under tighter timelines and greater scrutiny than ever before. In a world where volatility is increasingly the new constant, working in isolation is not an option.”"
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Klöckner Pentaplast expands kp Infinity® range with recyclable trays designed to help reduce food and packaging waste,www.kpfilms.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.kpfilms.com/en/news-events/_news?qlId=5564,"24 June 2026 ... ## Klöckner Pentaplast expands kp Infinity® range with recyclable trays designed to help reduce food and packaging waste ... Klöckner Pentaplast (kp), a global leader in rigid and flexible packaging and specialty film solutions, has expanded its kp Infinity® portfolio with the launch of a new fruit tray range designed specifically for packed fresh fruit. Building on the success of kp Infinity® in food-to-go packaging, the new range introduces dedicated tray formats for fresh fruit, bringing the proven benefits of lightweight, durable and fully recyclable mono-material packaging to the fresh produce market. As retailers, producers and consumers increasingly focus on packaging sustainability, fresh produce businesses are looking for solutions that help reduce food waste and improve recyclability while maintaining shelf appeal. The new kp Infinity® Fruit Tray Range has been developed to meet these evolving requirements. ... Manufactured from expanded polypropylene (EPP), kp Infinity® fruit trays are fully recyclable and feature a lightweight yet durable design that helps protect packed fruit throughout the supply chain, supporting efforts to reduce product damage and waste. Their traditional artisan appearance enhances product presentation, while their stackable format supports efficient handling, transportation and storage. The trays also feature clear consumer-facing recycling messaging, helping to simplify disposal and support recycling participation. In addition to their recyclability benefits, kp Infinity® fruit trays offer a lower carbon footprint and require less water and energy to manufacture compared with alternative packaging materials, helping customers meet their broader sustainability objectives. ... For customers seeking a complete packaging solution, kp Infinity® fruit trays can be combined with kp FlexiStretch® overwrap or kp FlexiFlow® films. Together, the solutions provide excellent product presentation and protection while helping fresh produce businesses maintain product quality from packing line to retail shelf. Austin Schwarz, Sales Director UK&I at kp Food Packaging, said: ""Following the success of kp Infinity® in food-to-go applications, we identified a growing need for recyclable packaging solutions in the fresh produce sector. The new fruit tray range brings together the durability, presentation and recyclability customers are looking for in a format specifically designed for whole fruit such as apples and pears.” “Combined with kp FlexiStretch® overwrap or our kp FlexiFlow® films, customers can source a complete packaging solution from one supplier, benefiting from streamlined procurement, technical expertise and consistent packaging performance across the supply chain.” The launch further strengthens kp's fresh produce packaging portfolio and reinforces the company's commitment to delivering innovative packaging solutions that help customers achieve their sustainability and operational goals. To learn more about the kp Infinity® fruit tray range, click here. About Klöckner Pentaplast Focused on delivering its vision: The Sustainable Protection of Everyday Needs, kp is a global leader in rigid and flexible packaging and specialty film solutions, serving the pharmaceutical, medical device, food, beverage and card markets, amongst others. With a broad and innovative portfolio of packaging and product films and services, kp plays an integral role in the customer value chain by safeguarding product integrity, assuring safety and consumer health, improving sustainability, and protecting brand reputation. kp’s “Investing in Better” sustainability strategy solidifies its commitment to achieving ten clear targets for long-term improvement by increasing the recycling and recyclability of products, cutting carbon emissions and continuous improvement in employee engagement, safety, and diversity, equity and inclusion. For five consecutive years, kp has held a gold rating from EcoVadis, the leading platform for environmental, social and ethical performance ratings. This ranks kp in the top 1% of companies rated in the manufacturing of plastics products sector. Founded in 1965, kp has 27 plants in 16 countries and employs over 5,000 people committed to serving customers worldwide in over 60 locations. kp is proud to have celebrated its 60th anniversary in 2025."
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition,www.prnewswire.com (Klöckner Pentaplast),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/klockner-pentaplast-announces-leadership-transition-302805933.html,"Appoints industry veteran Michael Zacka as Interim Chief Executive Officer, Robert Villaquiran retiring after 42 years in packaging industry ... LONDON, June 22, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Klöckner Pentaplast (""kp"" or the ""Company"") today announced that Michael Zacka, a current member of the Company's Board of Directors, has been appointed Interim Chief Executive Officer, effective June 22, 2026. He succeeds Roberto Villaquiran, who has decided to retire from the Company after 42 years in the packaging industry. The Board has initiated a search to identify the next CEO. ... ""Over the past year, kp has transformed its balance sheet, establishing a strong financial foundation and enhancing its ability to better meet the evolving needs of its customers,"" said Andrew Berlin, Chairman of the Board. ""The Company's next CEO will be responsible for building on our momentum and leveraging our competitive advantages to drive continued innovation for customers worldwide. As this search proceeds, we are fortunate to be able to tap into Michael's strong record of leadership and driving meaningful value creation. Looking ahead, our team remains fully focused on deepening collaboration with customers and partners across the value chain to advance a differentiated portfolio of sustainable, high-performance packaging and film solutions and reinforce our leadership position in the industry."" ... Mr. Zacka has a proven track record of driving transformation and shareholder value through operational excellence, innovation, and disciplined capital allocation, including leading major restructurings, M&A integrations, and divestitures. Previously, as Amcor's Chief Commercial Officer, he led global commercial and sustainability strategies, helping position the company as an industry leader in recyclable and reusable packaging. ... Focused on delivering its vision: The Sustainable Protection of Everyday Needs, kp is a global leader in rigid and flexible packaging and specialty film solutions, serving the pharmaceutical, medical device, food, beverage and card markets, amongst others. With a broad and innovative portfolio of packaging and product films and services, kp plays an integral role in the customer value chain by safeguarding product integrity, assuring safety and consumer health, improving sustainability, and protecting brand reputation. kp's ""Investing in Better"" sustainability strategy solidifies its commitment to achieving ten clear targets for long-term improvement by increasing the recycling and recyclability of products, cutting carbon emissions and continuous improvement in employee engagement, safety, and diversity, equity and inclusion. ... For five consecutive years, kp has held a gold rating from EcoVadis, the leading platform for environmental, social and ethical performance ratings. This ranks kp in the top 1% of companies rated in the manufacturing of plastics products sector. ... Founded in 1965, kp has 27 plants in 16 countries and employs over 5,000 people committed to serving customers worldwide in over 60 locations. kp is proud to have celebrated its 60th anniversary in 2025. ... ### Klöckner Pentaplast successfully completes financial restructuring ... Klöckner Pentaplast (""kp"" or the ""Company"") today announced that it has successfully completed its financial restructuring and emerged from the US... ... ### Klöckner Pentaplast receives court approval for financial restructuring plan ... Klöckner Pentaplast (""kp"" or the ""Company"") today announced that the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Southern District of Texas (the ""Court"")..."
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition - AOL,www.aol.com (AOL),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.aol.com/articles/kl-ckner-pentaplast-announces-leadership-120000000.html,"Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition - AOL ... Appoints industry veteran Michael Zacka as Interim Chief Executive Officer, Robert Villaquiran retiring after 42 years in packaging industry ... LONDON, June 22, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Klöckner Pentaplast (""kp"" or the ""Company"") today announced that Michael Zacka, a current member of the Company's Board of Directors, has been appointed Interim Chief Executive Officer, effective June 22, 2026. He succeeds Roberto Villaquiran, who has decided to retire from the Company after 42 years in the packaging industry. The Board has initiated a search to identify the next CEO. ... ""Over the past year, kp has transformed its balance sheet, establishing a strong financial foundation and enhancing its ability to better meet the evolving needs of its customers,"" said Andrew Berlin, Chairman of the Board. ""The Company's next CEO will be responsible for building on our momentum and leveraging our competitive advantages to drive continued innovation for customers worldwide. As this search proceeds, we are fortunate to be able to tap into Michael's strong record of leadership and driving meaningful value creation. Looking ahead, our team remains fully focused on deepening collaboration with customers and partners across the value chain to advance a differentiated portfolio of sustainable, high-performance packaging and film solutions and reinforce our leadership position in the industry."" ... ""I am honoured to serve as Interim CEO and appreciate the Board's confidence and support at this critical time for kp,"" said Mr. Zacka. ""As we continue to move the Company ... and unlock its full potential, I am eager to roll up my sleeves alongside the leadership team to execute our value creation strategy rooted in operational excellence and differentiated customer service and innovation."" ... Mr. Zacka has a proven track record of driving transformation and shareholder value through operational excellence, innovation, and disciplined capital allocation, including leading major restructurings, M&A integrations, and divestitures. Previously, as Amcor's Chief Commercial Officer, he led global commercial and sustainability strategies, helping position the company as an industry leader in recyclable and reusable packaging. ... Focused on delivering its vision: The Sustainable Protection of Everyday Needs, kp is a global leader in rigid and flexible packaging and specialty film solutions, serving the pharmaceutical, medical device, food, beverage and card markets, amongst others. With a broad and innovative portfolio of packaging and product films and services, kp plays an integral role in the customer value chain by safeguarding product integrity, assuring safety and consumer health, improving sustainability, and protecting brand reputation. kp's ""Investing in Better"" sustainability strategy solidifies its commitment to achieving ten clear targets for long-term improvement by increasing the recycling and recyclability of products, cutting carbon emissions and continuous improvement in employee engagement, safety, and diversity, equity and inclusion. ... For five consecutive years, kp has held a gold rating from EcoVadis, the leading platform for environmental, social and ethical performance ratings. This ranks kp in the top 1% of companies rated in the manufacturing of plastics products sector. ... Founded in 1965, kp has 27 plants in 16 countries and employs over 5,000 people committed to serving customers worldwide in over 60 locations. kp is proud to have celebrated its 60th anniversary in 2025."
