Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Leadership Transition at Klöckner Pentaplast: Michael Zacka Steps in as Interim CEO - Third News,third-news.com,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://third-news.com/article/63864144-6e34-11f1-9c60-9ca3ba08e13f,"Leadership Transition at Klöckner Pentaplast: Michael Zacka Steps in as Interim CEO - Third News ... # Leadership Transition at Klöckner Pentaplast: Michael Zacka Steps in as Interim CEO ... Klöckner Pentaplast, a prominent name in the packaging industry, has recently made significant changes at the top of its leadership structure. On June 22, 2026, the company appointed Michael Zacka as the Interim Chief Executive Officer, taking over from Roberto Villaquiran, who has decided to retire after an impressive 42-year career in the packaging sector. This strategic shift comes as the company initiates a search for a permanent CEO to guide it through its next chapter. Michael Zacka, currently a member of Klöckner Pentaplast’s Board of Directors, is a seasoned executive with rich experience spanning over three decades in global leadership roles across consumer goods, packaging, and industrial sectors. He has a proven history of enhancing value through operational excellence, innovation, and effective commercial strategies. Andrew Berlin, Chairman of the Board, praised Zacka’s appointment, highlighting his strong leadership qualities and indicating that Zacka will be instrumental in maintaining the momentum of the company during this transition period. Berlin noted, ""Our next CEO will need to build on our momentum and leverage our competitive advantages to drive continuous innovation across our customer base worldwide. Until then, we are fortunate to have someone like Michael at the helm, given his extensive track record in driving meaningful transformation."" In his new role, Zacka expressed his enthusiasm and commitment to steering Klöckner Pentaplast towards unlocking its full potential. He emphasized the importance of operational excellence and superior customer service as key components of the company’s strategy moving forward. Prior to this appointment, Zacka served as President of EMEA and Asia Pacific at Amcor plc, where he led a substantial business with over €5 billion in revenue. His previous experience also includes significant leadership positions at Tetra Pak, showcasing his ability to manage large operations effectively. Known for his hands-on approach, Zacka is looking forward to collaborating closely with the leadership team to execute the company’s value creation strategy. Robert Villaquiran, the outgoing CEO, has been a pivotal figure at Klöckner Pentaplast, particularly during the company's recent restructuring efforts that have laid a solid foundation for future growth. Berlin took the opportunity to thank Villaquiran for his contributions, noting his role in steering the company through transformative transitions and preparing it for future challenges. Klöckner Pentaplast, dedicated to ‘The Sustainable Protection of Everyday Needs,’ is recognized globally for its customizable and high-quality rigid and flexible packaging solutions, fulfilling essential functions across various markets including pharmaceuticals, medical devices, food, beverages, and more. The company is also deeply invested in sustainability, striving to increase recycling efforts while minimizing its carbon footprint. Having celebrated its 60th anniversary in 2025, Klöckner Pentaplast continues to innovate and enhance its offerings, reinforced by initiatives such as its 'Investing in Better' sustainability strategy. With 27 manufacturing plants across 16 countries and a commitment to operational excellence, the company is poised to maintain its leadership position in the packaging industry while meeting the evolving needs of its customers globally. As Klöckner Pentaplast embarks on this new chapter under Michael Zacka’s interim leadership, the industry watches closely, eager to see how the company will adapt and thrive in the competitive packaging landscape."
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition - Worldnews.com,article.wn.com (system),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://article.wn.com/view/2026/06/22/Klockner_Pentaplast_announces_leadership_transition/,"Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition - Worldnews.com ... öckner ... aplast announces leadership transition ... Appoints industry veteran Michael Zacka as Interim Chief Executive Officer, Robert Villaquiran retiring after 42 years in packaging industry Initiates search process to identify next CEO LONDON, June 22, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Klöckner Pentaplast (""kp"" or the ""Company"") today announced that Michael Zacka, a... read full story ... ""Over the past year, kp has transformed its balance sheet, establishing a strong financial foundation and enhancing its ability to better meet the evolving needs of its customers,"" ... ### Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition (KP Holding GmbH & Co KG) ... ### Klöckner narrows Q1 losses, expects Worthington deal to close by year’s end ... https://article.wn.com/view/2026/05/07/Klockner_narrows_Q1_losses_expects_Worthington_deal_to_close/ Steel Market Update 2026-05-07, 04:25 ... ### Klöckner & Co expects higher European sales volumes ... ### Klöckner steps up sale of SSC Becker ... ### Worthington Steel completes acquisition of majority stake in Klöckner & Co ... https://article.wn.com/view/2026/06/08/Worthington_Steel_completes_acquisition_of_majority_stake_in/ Eurometal 2026-06-08, 12:32 ... ### Klöckner Pentaplast expands kp Infinity® range with recyclable trays designed to help reduce food and packaging waste (KP Holding GmbH & Co KG) ... https://article.wn.com/view/2026/06/25/Klockner_Pentaplast_expands_kp_Infinity_range_with_recyclabl/ Public Technologies 2026-06-25, 12:01"
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,kp delves Inside the Future of Food Packaging with industry leaders - FRY Magazine,frymagazine.com (Helen Edmonds),2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://frymagazine.com/news/kp-delves-inside-the-future-of-food-packaging-with-industry-leaders/,"Packaging manufacturer Klöckner Pentaplast (kp) hosted its ‘Inside the Future of Food Packaging’ event earlier this month, bringing together retailers, recyclers, technology providers and manufacturers to discuss how the industry can adapt to evolving sustainability regulations while maintaining performance, shelf appeal and commercial viability. ... Held at held at the iconic Silverstone motor racing circuit, discussions ranged from extended producer responsibility (EPR) and the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR) to consumer recycling behaviour, soft plastics, and the growing role of AI on the factory floor and in packaging design. While each topic considered a different challenge, a consistent theme emerged: the need for greater clarity, collaboration, and data-driven decision-making across the entire packaging ecosystem. ... Speaking at the event, Thomas Jakobsen, president of food packaging for kp, said: “Packaging today is no longer simply about containment or protection. It is about balancing increasingly complex demands, performance, sustainability, compliance and cost, often under tighter timelines and greater scrutiny than ever before. In a world where volatility is increasingly the new constant, working in isolation is not an option.” ... The strongest overarching theme of the day is one that kp says it encounters every day: food packaging is being pulled in multiple directions at once. Performance, sustainability, compliance, cost, recyclability, recovery infrastructure, and consumer trust are all essential considerations. During the kp event, speaker after speaker reinforced how the role of packaging has evolved into something that helps food businesses make confident decisions under greater scrutiny and tighter timelines. ... That is precisely the challenge that kp’s portfolio is built around. Whether it’s kp Elite, its mono-material MAP trays made from up to 100% rPET, kp Infinity. fully recyclable EPP-based alternative to banned single serve EPS food packaging, or any other innovation throughout the range, kp says customers can rest assured that its solutions are designed not just for market needs today, but tomorrow too."
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,Capstone Advised CTL Aerospace on its Sale in Chapter 11 | Capstone Partners,www.capstonepartners.com (Scott Crislip),2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.capstonepartners.com/transactions/capstone-partners-advised-ctl-aerospace-inc-on-its-sale-to-davidson-kempner-in-chapter-11-bankruptcy/,"Capstone Advised CTL Aerospace on its Sale in Chapter 11 | Capstone Partners ... # Capstone Partners Advised CTL Aerospace, Inc. on its Sale to Davidson Kempner in Chapter 11 Bankruptcy ... Capstone Partners’ Special Situations Investment Banking group advised CTL Aerospace, Inc. (CTL)—a manufacturer of composite parts serving aerospace and defense end markets—in its Chapter 11 Bankruptcy case and sale to an affiliate of Davidson Kempner Capital Management (DK). The transaction closed in March 2026. ... CTL operates as a Tier 2 & 3 build-to-print manufacturer for large, blue-chip aerospace and defense customers. CTL has been a supplier to both the U.S. Government and major aerospace companies since 1946. CTL also provides maintenance, repair, and overhaul services for jet engine components and other aerospace parts. For more information, visit CTL here. ... In 2024 and early 2025, CTL experienced significant manufacturing quality disruptions, which were resolved, but the resulting financial strain led to defaults under the Company’s credit agreement with its senior lender. With no viable alternatives to sustain operations and a rapidly deteriorating relationship with its lender, CTL filed for Chapter 11 in September 2025. ... CTL retained Capstone shortly after its bankruptcy filing. Capstone’s services in this engagement included two separate teams: Capstone’s Special Situations Investment Banking team sourced debtor in possession financing and executed a sale of the business through the Chapter 11 process and Capstone’s Financial Advisory Services (FAS) team delivered comprehensive managerial, operation and financial and advisory services to support the company’s daily operating functions. Capstone’s Special Situations Investment Banking and FAS teams worked seamlessly together through the Chapter 11 bankruptcy process. ... to our selection. Important factors in our selection included confidence, competence, honesty, accessibility, sincerity, and a proven track record. They listened as we told our story. Capstone realized we had a business worth saving and were up for ... fight. We made ... right choice. Cap ... provided professionals in two work streams needed by the business. Cap ... ’s Special Situations Investment Banking team developed a go-to-market strategy both for our debtor in possession financing needs as well as a sale of business, and the Financial Advisory Services team created endless requested budgets, forecasts and regularly communicated with counsel. They did an excellent job in both camps. Our legal team and ... worked as a seamless ... which enabled CTL to fight a good fight even against daunting odds of ... “It was a great privilege to fight for a business with such dedicated management and employees. We’re proud to have supported CTL’s efforts to secure financing to operate “business as usual” in the Chapter 11 case and, ultimately, to sell the business to a well-capitalized and capable buyer,” said Geoffrey Frankel, Capstone’s head of Special Situation Investment Banking. ... Davidson Kempner Capital Management (DK) is a global investment firm with approximately ~$38 billion in assets under management across multiple funds and strategies. Backed by over 40 years of investment experience, DK invest across the capital structure in both public and private markets, including middle market aerospace and defense companies in the United States. DK applies their research-driven investment process to evaluate and execute a diverse range of transactions across asset classes, geographies and market cycles. In addition to CTL, DK’s A&D investments include The Atlas Group. For more information, visit DK here. ... The investment banking professionals on Capstone’s Special Situations Investment Banking team offers a full range of services to companies and stakeholders facing capital structure challenges, including distressed M&A advisory, special situation/bankruptcy capital solutions, balance sheet restructurings, corporate divestitures and carve-outs, and evaluation of strategic alternatives. To learn more about this transaction, or about the benefits of starting a relationship with this team at Capstone, please contact our Special Situations Investment Banking team. ... Previous Capstone Partners Provided Restructuring Services to CTL Aerospace, Inc. During its Chapter 11 Bankruptcy ... Next Capstone Partners Advised Titanium Payments on its Sale to an Undisclosed Strategic Buyer ... ENGAGED CAPSTONE PARTNERS TO PROVIDE FINANCIAL ADVISORY AND RESTRUCTURING SERVICES DURING CHAPTER 11 ... HAS RECEIVED A GROWTH EQUITY INVESTMENT FROM ... - Business Process Outsourcing ... - Business Services ... - Public Safety & Physical Security ... has been acquired by ... - Aerospace, Defense, Government & Security - Air, Land, Sea & Space - C4ISR, Unmanned Systems & Robotics"
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Exa,"Compactor Rentals of America Completes $385 Million Securitization, the First in the Waste Compactor & Baler Leasing Sector - Kinderhook Industries",www.kinderhook.com,2026-06-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.kinderhook.com/press-release/compactor-rentals-of-america-completes-385-million-securitization-the-first-in-the-waste-compactor-baler-leasing-sector/,"Compactor Rentals of America Completes $385 Million Securitization, the First in the Waste Compactor & Baler Leasing Sector - Kinderhook Industries ... New York, NY – Kinderhook Industries (“Kinderhook”) today announced that its portfolio company, Compactor Rentals of America (“CRA” or the “Company”), a leading provider of waste compaction solutions, specializing in compactor and baler leasing programs across the U.S., has completed a securitization (“Securitization”), with over $300 million funded at closing. The Securitization recapitalizes CRA’s balance sheet and establishes a scalable, long-term source of capital to support the Company’s continued growth. ... The Securitization refinances CRA’s existing indebtedness and introduces a dedicated, lower-cost source of long-term capital. In addition to amounts funded at closing, the facility includes incremental committed delayed-draw and variable funding capacity that the Company can access to fund fleet expansion and future acquisitions, providing CRA with significant flexibility to continue executing its growth strategy. ... “This financing is an important milestone for CRA and a strong endorsement of the platform our team has built,” said Kelly Williams, Chief Executive Officer of CRA. “Access to a scalable, long-term source of capital gives us the flexibility to invest in our fleet, expand our national footprint, and pursue accretive acquisitions as we continue to grow.” ... “We are excited to put this investment grade capital structure in place for CRA,” said Rob Michalik, Managing Director at Kinderhook. “A securitization is a natural fit for a business with CRA’s high-quality, recurring rental cash flows, and it provides a flexible and efficient source of capital to support the Company’s continued organic growth and acquisition strategy.”"
Klöckner Pentaplast,,,,Linkup,Klöckner Pentaplast announces leadership transition,PR Newswire,2026-06-22T00:00:00Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/klockner-pentaplast-announces-leadership-transition-302805933.html,"Klöckner Pentaplast appointed Michael Zacka as Interim CEO, succeeding Roberto Villaquiran who retired after 42 years in the packaging industry. Zacka brings over 30 years of leadership experience, most recently as President of EMEA and Asia Pacific at Amcor plc."
