Universal McCann,,,,Exa,"Universal Music Group generated $3.83bn in Q2, up 13.3% YoY – driven by Noah Kahan, BTS, Olivia Rodrigo, Drake, and Olivia Dean - Music Business Worldwide",www.musicbusinessworldwide.com (Murray Stassen),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/universal-music-group-generated-3-83bn-in-q2-up-13-3-yoy-driven-by-noah-kahan-bts-olivia-rodrigo-drake-and-olivia-dean/,"Universal Music Group generated $3.83B in Q2, up 13.3% YoY – driven by Noah Kahan, BTS, Olivia Rodrigo, Drake, and Olivia Dean - Music Business Worldwide ... Universal Music Group generated revenues of EUR €3.294 billion (USD $3.83bn) across all of its divisions (including recorded music, publishing, and more) in Q2 (the three months ending June 30, 2026). ... They reveal that UMG’s overall Q2 revenue grew 13.3% YoY at constant currency, driven by the consolidation of Downtown Music Holdings, pricing benefits of Streaming 2.0 agreements, strong physical and licensing and other sales, and healthy performance revenue, contributing to growth in Recorded Music and Music Publishing. ... Excluding Downtown, whose results are consolidated from its acquisition date of February 20, revenue grew 6.4% YoY at constant currency. ... Adjusted EBITDA came in at €674 million ($783.8m), a margin of 20.5%, down from 22.7% in the second quarter of 2025. ... One highlight from UMG’s latest results was the company’s recorded music subscription revenue, which grew 16.6% YoY at constant currency to €1.368 billion ($1.59bn) in Q2, benefiting from the consolidation of Downtown and pricing benefits of Streaming 2.0 agreements. ... Commenting on the Q2 earnings announcement, UMG’s Chairman and CEO, Sir Lucian Grainge, said: “We’re delivering on our strategic plan, and working to further sharpen our execution, while capitalizing on the opportunities presented by new technologies and the ever-evolving music ecosystem. ... “Our unique combination of global reach, local expertise, artist development, vast audio and visual IP and entrepreneurial culture positions UMG to deliver long-term growth, sustained value creation, and creative and commercial success for our artists and songwriters.” ... Universal’s overall Recorded Music revenue for the second quarter of 2026 was €2.516 billion ($2.93bn), up 16.2% YoY at constant currency. Excluding Downtown, Recorded Music revenue grew 8.7% YoY at constant currency. ... Within the Recorded Music segment, UMG’s ‘Subscription and streaming revenues’ (including ad-supported and subscription streaming revenues) grew 15.4% YoY at constant currency to €1.757 billion ($2.04bn). ... Breaking UMG’s recorded music streaming figure down further reveals that the company’s subscription streaming revenues grew 16.6% YoY at constant currency to reach €1.368 billion ($1.59bn). Excluding Downtown, subscription revenue grew 6.7% YoY at constant currency. ... Universal’s ad-supported recorded music streaming revenue grew 11.5% YoY at constant currency to €389 million ($452.4m), as consumers “continue to shift consumption from better monetized video platforms to short-form platforms”, according to UMG. ... Within Universal’s recorded music business, Physical revenue grew 15.9% YoY at constant currency to €342 million ($397.7m), with “particular strength in the U.S. and Europe, partially offset by declines in Japan due to the timing of releases”, UMG said. ... ‘License and other’ revenue increased 34.9% YoY at constant currency to €379 million ($440.7m), with “outsized contributions from audiovisual and live and related income, along with healthy licensing revenue growth”, according to UMG. ... Downloads and other digital revenue fell 43.3% YoY at constant currency to €38 million ($44.2m), which UMG attributed to a previously disclosed settlement with an internet service provider in Q2 2025 and the “ongoing industry-wide format shift”. ... Top sellers for the quarter included Noah Kahan, BTS, Olivia Rodrigo, Drake, and Olivia Dean. ... Universal’s overall Music Publishing revenue for the second quarter of 2026 was €616 million ($716.3m), up 9.8% YoY at constant currency. Excluding Downtown, Music Publishing revenue grew 2.7% YoY at constant currency. ... Digital revenue grew 13.6% YoY at constant currency to €392 million ($455.9m), “reflecting strength in subscription, partially offset by softer ad-supported streaming”, UMG said. ... Performance revenue increased 12.8% YoY at constant currency to €123 million ($143m), which UMG attributed to “continued industry growth”. ... 9.4% YoY at constant currency to €5 ... “related to the timing of deals ... Mechanical revenue grew 3.6% YoY at constant currency to €29 million ($ ... 3.7m), “driven by release schedules ... ’s ‘Merchandising and Other’ revenue in the second quarter of 2026 was €167 ... ), down 1 ... YoY at constant currency ... The division posted an Adjusted EBITDA loss of €5 million ($5.8m) in Q2, compared with a €1 million profit a year earlier. ... Downtown Music Holdings contributed €202 million ($234.9m) in total revenue in Q2 2026, its first full quarter under UMG ownership. ... That was up from the€86 million Downtown added in Q1 2026, when it was consolidated for only around five-and-a-half weeks following the deal’s completion on February 20. ... The bulk of Downtown’s Q2 contribution came from Recorded Music, at €162 million ($188.4m), with Music Publishing accounting for a further €40 million ($46.5m). ... Downtown’s Adjusted EBITDA was €10 million ($11.6m), an Adjusted EBITDA margin of 5.0%. ... In Q2 2026, UMG’s EBITDA (earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization) was €610 million ($709.4m), down 0.2% YoY but up 1.5% at constant currency. ... EBITDA margin was 18 ... quarter of ... 025. ... Adjusted EBITDA for Q2 was €674 million ($783.8m), down 0.3% YoY but up 1.5% at constant currency. ... Adjusted EBITDA margin was 20.5%, compared to 22.7% in Q2 2025, with the decline “due to the consolidation of Downtown, pressure from revenue and repertoire mix in Recorded Music, and a loss in Merchandising”, according to UMG. ... UMG’s Board of Directors declared an interim dividend for the first half of 2026 of €432 million, or €0.24 per share, in line with the 2025 interim dividend. ... UMG’s financial net debt stood at €4.131 billion ($4.80bn) at the end of June, up 72.8% from €2.390 billion at the end of 2025. ... The increase reflected €806 million of cash used for investing activities, including the Downtown acquisition, alongside €734 million of stock repurchases and €514 million of dividend payments. ... That was partially offset by €379 million ($440.7m) in proceeds from the sale of Spotify shares, after UMG confirmed in April that it would monetize half of its equity stake in the streaming company. ... “Our focus is on building our market leadership, while driving top and bottom-line growth, improving efficiency, and continuing to invest where we see the greatest returns.” ... “This quarter demonstrated both the strong fundamentals of our business and the opportunities we see to improve,” said Matt Ellis, UMG’s CFO. “Our focus is on building our market leadership, while driving top and bottom-line growth, improving efficiency, and continuing to invest where we see the greatest returns.” ... #### Suno muscles into vinyl market, plans to let users press their AI songs onto 12-inch records ... #### Sony Music Group and Universal Music Group take legal action against 'parasitic' streaming app Musi in Canada ... #### Spotify says it doesn't need deals with all the majors to launch its AI covers and remixes tool ... #### Universal has sold a chunk of Spotify stock for around $467M. Artists will likely be paid over $100M of it."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Principal trading is ‘part of the value equation’ as Omnicom media arm hits US$3.1b - Mumbrella,mumbrella.com.au (Eleanor Dickinson),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mumbrella.com.au/principal-trading-is-part-of-the-value-equation-as-omnicom-media-arm-hits-us3-1b-931254,"Omnicom Media global CEO Florian Adamski says principal media is now &quot;part of the modern marketplace"" ... Principal media is now “part of the value equation” for Omnicom’s clients, as the newly merged group’s media business generated US$3.1 billion revenue in its latest quarterly results. ... The newly combined Omnicom-Interpublic group posted US$6 billion in second-quarter revenue, with organic growth of 6.1% measured against the pre-merger Omnicom and Interpublic businesses. Omnicom named the healthcare sector as a major driver of growth. ... The results reveal Omnicom’s “integrated media” division now encompasses over half of overall revenue, US$3.1 billion, with “more than 10%” organic growth. Omnicom did not disclose the comparable combined media revenue figure for Q2 2025, but the numbers indicate it would have been around US$2.8 billion. ... Adamski described it as “part of the value equation. This is what the modern marketplace looks like.” ... “It gives clients what they need and what they want in terms of value extraction, so it becomes part of a very integrated go-to-market approach.” ... Adamski did not address whether IPG Mediabrands had previously lagged in principal media capabilities, instead pointing to the broader role the practice now plays in the market. ... ’s where we ... will say the ... The dominance of media within Omnicom’s new structure comes as other disciplines make ... a significantly smaller share of ... Advertising contributed US$9 ... 2.6 ... , or 15. ... , followed by public relations at US$6 ... and experiential & other at US$ ... 69. ... million (1 ... During the earnings call, it was noted that Omnicom’s advertising revenue declined by high single digits during the quarter. Addressing this, CFO Philip Angelastro reiterated that “creativity is and continues to be a key part of our DNA”. ... “It’s certainly a core in what we deliver throughout all our businesses and to our clients,” he said. “The advertising group continues to roll out our implementation of a more connected and centrally driven Omnicom Advertising Group.” ... Despite the advertising business’ decline, Omnicom reported a significant uplift in profitability following its US$13 billion acquisition of IPG, with adjusted EBITDA increasing US$581 million to US$1.04 billion in the second quarter of 2026 on a like-for-like basis. ... For the first half, the combined group also reported revenue of US$12.8 billion, up from US$12.5 billion year on year. ... Echoing recent comments from WPP CEO Cindy Rose that the business is [“no longer a holding company”](https://mumbrella.com.au/we-are-no-longer-a-holding-company-wpp-unveils-a949m-global-restructure-as-profit-plunge-916174), Omnicom CEO John Wren positioned the newly expanded group in similar terms. ... “We’re now more of an operating company than a holding company. And we’re selling as a team with multiple capabilities and crafts because clients are asking for that, because they’re asking for simplification in a complicated environment,” he said. ... Omnicom’s results follow those of rival French holding companies Publicis Groupe and Havas, which last week reported Q2 organic growth of 4.8% and 2.5% respectively. ... Publicis posted Q2 net revenue of €3.7 billion (US$4.2b), with its connected media operation now accounting for 62% of the group’s net revenue. ... Havas, meanwhile, posted €724 million (US$824m) for the quarter, with its first-half results showing Havas Media accounted for 38% of revenue, behind Havas Creative at 42% and ahead of Havas Health at 20%. ... Notably, both Omnicom and Publicis pointed to healthcare and pharmaceutical clients as major growth drivers, with the sector now forming the largest client category for each. Health accounted for 18% of Omnicom’s revenue and 15% of Publicis’ net revenue in the first half. ... Meanwhile, a regional breakdown showed a mixed picture across Asia-Pacific. Omnicom reported revenue of US$537.6m in the region during Q2, representing 9% of global revenue, but noted that the region declined slightly during the period. ... Publicis reported a stronger regional performance, with APAC representing 9% of net revenue and delivering organic growth of 2.6% in the first half. Havas recorded a decline across APAC — which is grouped with Africa — with the region down 3.5% in Q2."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,NEW REPORT RECOGNIZES OMNICOM MEDIA AS THE LEADING MEDIA MANAGEMENT NETWORK BY BILLINGS AND INDUSTRY SHARE,www.prnewswire.com (Omnicom Media Group),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/in/news-releases/new-report-recognizes-omnicom-media-as-the-leading-media-management-network-by-billings-and-industry-share-302837630.html,"NEW YORK, July 29, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- A new report from the Research Company Evaluating the Media Industry (RECMA) reinforces Omnicom Media's leadership position following the integration of Omnicom and IPG's media operations in November 2025. ... According to the recently published RECMA 2025 Overall Activity Volume (OAV) report, the Omnicom Media - an Omnicom (NYSE: OMC) Connected Capability - is now the largest global media management network, with $107.3 billion in billings ($20 billion + ahead of its nearest competitor), representing 30.1% of the global media agency market. ... The report also reveals Omnicom Media leads in overall activity volume across North America, EMEA and LATAM. ... Describing the combination of Omnicom and IPG as a ""historic event"" that has reshaped the global media agency landscape, RECMA looks beyond scale alone in offering proof points for Omnicom Media's leadership, highlighting the enhanced capabilities of the AI-enable Omni Intelligence Platform through the integration of Acxiom's identity and data assets and Flywheel's commerce expertise. Together, these capabilities enable clients to connect planning, activation, measurement, and optimization across channels while benefiting from the scale, intelligence, and specialist expertise of the industry's largest media organization. ... Commenting on the report, Omnicom Media CEO Florian Adamski said, ""Scale matters only to the extent that it creates better outcomes for our clients. Beyond billings, our leadership position reflects the investments we've made in bringing together the industry's strongest talent, technology, data and commerce capabilities into a single connected organization that can translate unprecedented scale into disproportionate growth for the world's leading brands - helping them make smarter decisions, move faster and unlock opportunities others can't."" ... The report also reaffirmed the strength of Omnicom Media's agency portfolio, with OMD retaining its position as the world's largest individual media network with $35.1 billion in activity volume and a 9.9% global market share. OMD also secured the #1 ranking across North America and EMEA, as well as in the top five European advertising markets (UK, Germany, France, Spain, and Italy), the Nordics and Central & Eastern Europe. ... RECMA also highlighted the continued momentum of PHD, which delivered strong growth and gained share in both APAC and LATAM; while Hearts & Science has increased its billings by +27% over the three-year period covered in the report, making it one of the fastest growing brands among the 16 global agency networks included in the ranking - momentum that will be an asset to the new enterprise that will launch next month when Hearts & Science and Omnicom Media agency Mediahub come together to create a new agency brand. ... The RECMA report arrives as Omnicom Media also leads all Big Five global media management groups in new business performance, with more than $3 billion in year-to-date billings awarded from major wins and retentions including Adidas, Delta Air Lines, Dyson, IBM, Subway and Uber - a performance that further underscores how the new network's unique advantages in scale, data &technology, identity, commerce, and talent are translating into sustained client confidence and marketplace growth. ... Omnicom Media, an Omnicom (NYSE: OMC) Connected Capability, is the world's largest global media management network. Powered by the Omni Intelligence Platform, Omnicom Media agencies leverage $75.6 billion in billings, 40,000+ specialists across 70+ markets, and the industry's most powerful portfolio identity, commerce, and intelligence assets to design dynamic Growth Ecosystems that enable the world's most ambitious businesses to grow faster and smarter. The Omnicom Media portfolio includes global media agency brands OMD, Initiative, PHD, UM, Hearts & Science, and Mediahub; core Omnicom Integrated Media offerings Acxiom, the world's premier identity solution, and the Flywheel digital commerce practice; and specialty services across the cloud consulting, creator, financial, healthcare, and sports & entertainment categories. For more information visit omnicommedia.com ... ### NEW REPORT CONFIRMS OMNICOM MEDIA AS LARGEST GLOBAL MEDIA MANAGEMENT NETWORK FOLLOWING THE INTEGRATION OF OMG AND MEDIABRANDS ... Omnicom Media, an Omnicom (NYSE: OMC) Connected Capability, has been recognized in the COMvergence Final 2025 Global & Regional Billings Rankings as... ... ### OMNICOM MEDIA NAMED BEST PERFORMING GLOBAL MEDIA GROUP, EARNS #1 RANKING ACROSS ALL FOUR REGIONS ... In the latest edition of the Network Diagnostics report from RECMA (Research Company Evaluating the Media Agency Industry), Omnicom Media, an Omnicom ..."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,"Ogilvy, WPP Top Latest World Creative Rankings - Brand Communicator",brandcom.ng (Sherifat Tijani),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://brandcom.ng/2026/07/29/ogilvy-wpp-top-latest-world-creative-rankings/,"TBWA moved up from seventh to fifth place, led by Hornbach’s No Project Without Drama and Apple’s A Critter Carol. McCann held steady in sixth, thanks in part to L’Oréal Paris’ The Final Copy of Ilon Specht. ... Things look more settled at the top of the Holding Company rankings. WPP keeps hold of first place, and Omnicom stays in second. WPP’s strength comes from its two leading networks, Ogilvy and VML, continuing to perform well. Standout campaigns across its portfolio include Vaseline Verified, Ziploc’s Preserved Promos, Coca-Cola’s Thanks for Coke Creating, KitKat’s The KitKat Heist, Dove’s Dove R/Eal Reviews, and Oreo’s Name This Oreo. ... Omnicom’s strong position comes down to its high profile purchase of IPG and a wide range of award winning work, including Chicago Hearing Society’s Caption with Intention, Hornbach’s No Project Without Drama, Columbia Sportswear’s Expedition Impossible, L’Oréal Paris’ The Final Copy of Ilon Specht, SickKids Foundation’s The Count, and Apple’s A Critter Carol. ... Publicis Groupe moved up one spot to third, though part of that shift is simply due to changes in how the holding companies are now organized. IPG, which sat in third place last year, is no longer listed on its own after being bought by Omnicom. Even so, Publicis had a genuinely strong year, helped along by the rise of Leo Constellation and LePub, plus campaigns like Tecate’s Gulf of Mexico (Bar), AXA, Three Words, and Heineken’s Pub Succession and Could Have Been a Heineken. ... This mid year update covered 1,059 campaigns from 691 advertisers across 606 agencies. For the first time, organizers also plan to publish the full annual World Creative Rankings before the year wraps up, coming out at the end of 2026 rather than the usual February date, in an effort to keep the rankings closer to real time."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Omnicom Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results - Omnicom,www.omc.com (Eliecer Valerio),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.omc.com/newsroom/omnicom-reports-second-quarter-2026-results/,"Omnicom Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results - Omnicom ... Omnicom Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results ... # Omnicom Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results ... Revenue of $6.0 billion, 6.1% organic growth ... Non-GAAP Adjusted EBITA of $1.1 billion, 17.8% margin ... Operating Income of $922.5 million; $1.1 billion Non-GAAP Adjusted EBITA, 17.2% margin ... NEW YORK, July 28, 2026 – Omnicom (NYSE: OMC) today announced results for the quarter ended June 30, 2026. ... “Our second quarter results reflect the momentum of the new Omnicom. Revenue in our Core Operations grew 6.1% organically and we had strong margin expansion,” said John Wren, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Omnicom. “We are built for an era where speed, integration, and scale matter most. Our wins this quarter demonstrate that. Clients are consolidating more work with us because they see the competitive advantage our connected capabilities deliver. Looking ahead, we will strengthen our position as an integrated growth partner by focusing on three key areas: leading in agentic marketing transformation, expanding and deepening our partnerships with existing and new clients, and helping clients win across the new consumer engagement models in sports & entertainment, social & creator, connected commerce, and AI-driven discovery.”"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,UM Wins Mark Anthony Brands Global Media Account - B&T,www.bandt.com.au (Staff Writers),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bandt.com.au/um-wins-mark-anthony-brands-global-media-account/,"UM Wins Mark Anthony Brands Global Media Account - B&T ... White Claw parent company Mark Anthony Brands International has appointed Omnicom Media agency UM as its global media agency of record following a competitive global agency review. ... Under the new partnership, UM will be responsible for global media strategy, planning and buying, analytics and measurement, growth frameworks, cross-market governance and global-to-local coordination across the company’s international business. ... Building on UM’s existing relationship with Mark Anthony in Australia and Canada, the expanded remit now includes the United States and the United Kingdom, covering the company’s portfolio of category-leading RTD brands. ... The review, managed by MediaSense, began in March and included participation from holding companies and independent agencies. ... Mark Anthony selected UM based on the agency’s strategic media vision, measurement capabilities, commercial stewardship, scalable global buying model, and ability to build culturally relevant, social-first communications. ... “As our portfolio continues to grow globally, we were looking for a media partner that could bring strategic consistency across markets while helping our brands connect with consumers through culture locally. UM demonstrated a clear understanding of the evolving RTD landscape, as well as the strategic leadership, measurement capabilities and global scale needed to support the next phase of growth for our portfolio,” said Mark Anthony Brands International chief marketing and innovation officer Sam Reader. ... “We are incredibly grateful to Haworth for their strong partnership and the impact they’ve had on our growth journey. With our strategy increasingly requiring global scale, we are moving to a model that better matches those evolving needs.” ... “Mark Anthony has built its culturally influential portfolio by consistently challenging convention and staying close to changing consumer behavior,” said UM global brand president Susan Kingston Brown. ... “That mindset aligns closely with UM’s Full Color Media approach, which helps brands grow through a deeper understanding of people, culture and connection. We’re excited to partner with the team as they continue expanding some of the world’s most dynamic beverage brands.” ... The partnership is effective immediately."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,McCann Studio Indonesia picks up Unilever Foods Division Social Media Account – Campaign Brief Asia,campaignbriefasia.com (Adam Shaw),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://campaignbriefasia.com/2026/07/27/mccann-studio-indonesia-picks-up-unilever-foods-division-social-media-account/,"McCann Studio Indonesia picks up Unilever Foods Division Social Media Account – Campaign Brief Asia ... # McCann Studio Indonesia picks up Unilever Foods Division Social Media Account ... ### McCann Studio Indonesia has been appointed as the social media agency for Unilever’s Foods Division in Indonesia, effective July 2026. The appointment covers social media content strategy, production, and creator management across Unilever’s Foods portfolio – including flagship brands Bango and Royco. ... The win marks a significant expansion of McCann Studio Indonesia’s relationship with Unilever, adding the Foods Division to its growing portfolio of Unilever brand partnerships in the market. ... What sets this engagement apart is the working model agreed upon by both parties. Rather than operating from a traditional agency setup, the McCann Studio team will be embedded directly within Unilever’s office – working alongside the Foods brand teams on a day-to-day basis to ensure greater speed, responsiveness, and creative alignment. ... The model integrates a dedicated team of social managers, content creators, and multimedia designers, supported by an external creator network and AI-powered content production tools. The setup is designed to function as a true extension of the Unilever Foods brand team – from brief to delivery. ... Bellamia Agustina, General Manager of McCann Studio Indonesia, said: “Winning the Unilever Foods account is something we’re genuinely proud of – not just as a business milestone, but because of what it represents in terms of how we work. We’ve always believed that the best creative partnerships are built on proximity and trust. The embedded model we’ve agreed on with the Foods team reflects exactly that. We’re not just an agency they brief remotely – we’re sitting alongside them, thinking alongside them, and moving at the speed their brands demand.” ... Dinoy Alamsyah, Media Lead for Unilever Foods Indonesia, said: “Our consumers decide what’s for dinner while scrolling – every day, across every brand we run. Meeting that means being genuinely social-first: an audience-first content supply chain with insight at the front, and the pace and craft to turn it into content people choose to watch in the feed. We needed a partner who could operate at that speed and complexity as an extension of our team. McCann Studio built their model around that. We’re excited for what we start building in July”"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Havas shows acquisitions are the new agency playbook,www.emarketer.com,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.emarketer.com/content/havas-shows-acquisitions-new-agency-playbook,"# Havas shows acquisitions are the new agency playbook ... The news: Havas expanded its agency portfolio in H1 2026 through a series of marketing acquisitions across sports, experiential marketing, social media, and other sectors. Three of those deals closed in Q2, helping drive a 3.8% YoY increase in net revenues alongside organic growth. ... - Q2 acquisitions included French agency Format, which specializes in media relations, social media, and content creators; Archival, a US sports marketing agency with a specialization in youth culture and experiential activation; and MUT, a Spanish agency focused on experiential marketing and events. - Havas also acquired Dutch sports marketing agency SportsVibes in July after its closing date. ... The trend: Advertising consolidation is accelerating, making strategic acquisitions increasingly important as more market power concentrates among a smaller group of major players. ... - Omnicom’s 2025 acquisition of IPG created the largest ad agency group globally, surpassing WPP’s 2024 revenues. - Publicis has made several acquisitions centered on enhancing its AI and data capabilities, including content intelligence and measurement company AdgeAI and data management company Lotame. - WPP acquired data collaboration and clean room company InfoSum last year as it doubled down on AI and data ownership. ... Why consolidation? Agency consolidation boils down to a few factors: ... - Holdcos are increasingly seeking enterprise-grade AI capabilities, often by acquiring AI- and data-first agencies. As tech platforms expand their advertising offerings and brands bring more work in-house, advanced AI is becoming essential for agencies to remain competitive. ... - That competition from tech platforms and in-housing adds margin pressure. Competition is squeezing agency profitability, and consolidation is an attractive cost reduction option. ... - Acquisitions can help holdcos address client demand for integrated solutions. Rather than managing multiple agency relationships, advertisers want a single partner that can connect creative, data, media, and commerce. ... Implications for marketers: Expect the agency landscape to consolidate further around a smaller group of holdcos that use acquisitions to build more unified offerings across creative, media, data, and commerce. ... The result of this consolidation could make agency relationships more streamlined, but could also give marketers fewer independent partners to choose from."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,"Digest: Omnicom Merges Hearts & Science, Mediahub; Judge Approves Anthropic’s $1.5bn Settlement - ExchangeWire.com",www.exchangewire.com (Sheila Obeng-King),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.exchangewire.com/blog/2026/07/23/digest-omnicom-merges-hearts-science-mediahub-judge-approves-anthropics-1-5bn-settlement/,"Digest: Omnicom Merges Hearts & Science, Mediahub; Judge Approves Anthropic’s $1.5bn Settlement - ... In today’s Digest, we cover Omnicom Media merging Hearts & Science and Mediahub into a new global network, a judge approving Anthropic’s $1.5bn settlement, and M+C Saatchi ANZ heading for a management buyout amid steep local losses. ... ##### Omnicom merges Hearts & Science and Mediahub ... Omnicom Media is combining Hearts & Science and Mediahub into a single global agency network spanning 40 markets, in a move expected to launch next month under a new name and brand identity. The merged business will oversee roughly USD$9.1bn (£7.19bn) in annual billings. An Omnicom Media spokesperson confirmed both agencies will continue operating independently there, describing it as a reflection of the market's ""unique"" operating model. ... Hearts & Science Australia will still adopt the new global brand identity once unveiled, but clients and staff locally won't see any operational changes. Leadership for the new global entity is also beginning to take shape, with Nicole Estebanell, currently CEO of Mediahub US, expected to lead the combined agency in the United States, and Ross Jenkins, who oversees Mediahub across EMEA, set to become regional CEO there. ... ##### M+C Saatchi ANZ heads for management buyout ... M+C Saatchi has signed heads of terms for a management buyout of its Australia and New Zealand business, with completion expected in October and backing from growth investment firm Parc. The buyout is led by chief executive Dani Bassil, alongside chief strategy officer Simon Wassef, executive creative director Jeremy Hogg, chief client officer Anita Zanesco, Re managing director Remi Couzelas, and head of sport and entertainment Jack Playfair. ... Clients are expected to see no disruption, with the business continuing to operate under its existing brands and leadership structure. Bassil said the deal would let the locally-led management team focus entirely on the opportunities ahead, pointing to strong client relationships and creative talent across the region."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,M&C Saatchi ANZ breaks from London in management buyout - Mumbrella,mumbrella.com.au (Eleanor Dickinson),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mumbrella.com.au/mc-saatchi-anz-breaks-from-london-in-management-buyout-930451,"Saatchi ANZ breaks from London in management buyout ... M&C Saatchi’s Australia and New Zealand business is set to return to local ownership after its management team agreed a deal to acquire the agency from its London-listed parent company, backed by investment firm Parc. ... The buyout is being led by M&C Saatchi ANZ chief executive Dani Bassil, alongside chief strategy officer Simon Wassef, executive creative director Jeremy Hogg, chief client officer [Anita Zanesco](https://mumbrella.com.au/anita-zanesco-reunites-with-dani-bassil-at-mc-saatchi-886671), managing director of its design agency Re, Remi Couzelas and head of sport and entertainment Jack Playfair. ... Under the deal, the Australian and New Zealand operations will continue to trade under the M&C Saatchi name, but will become independent of the London-based parent company by 1 October. ... Bassil said the deal would allow the agency to focus on local growth opportunities. ... “We have outstanding client relationships and a team of exceptional creative talent across Australia and New Zealand,” Bass ... said in a statement. ... “The transaction will allow the locally led management team to focus entirely on the opportunities in front of us and to shape our future with speed and ambition.” ... The buyout is being backed by equity growth investor Parc Capital, which said it saw “significant opportunity to support their growth ambitions, both organically and through further investment”. ... Dame Heather Rabbatts, executive chair of M&C Saatchi globally, said she was delighted that the Australia and New Zealand business would “begin a new chapter” as the group continued to simplify its operational structure. ... “This proposed transaction is intended to provide the best platform for our clients in the region, while enabling the M&C Saatchi brand to remain present in the market. ... “I would like to thank our teams across Australia and New Zealand and wish them every success for the future.” ... The deal follows a challenging period for M&C Saatchi globally and locally, which saw the departure of global chief executive Zaid Al-Qassab, who left the role earlier this year. ... In its most recent financial results, [Australia’s revenue fell 31.9% in the 2025 calendar year](https://mumbrella.com.au/how-mc-saatchi-australia-went-from-glory-to-basket-case-921025), impacted by the closure of its Bohemia media unit and the loss of several major accounts, including Optus and Tourism Australia. ... The decline was significant enough that M&C Saatchi separated Australia’s performance in its financial reporting. Excluding Australia, group net revenue declined 3.1%, compared with a 7.3% fall when the Australian business was included. ... The group’s financial report, released in April, stated the Australian business would undergo “remedial action”, with the agency subsequently [making at least 20 roles redundant. ](https://mumbrella.com.au/mc-saatchi-makes-major-cuts-to-australian-staff-925876) ... Recently, Commonwealth Bank and M&C Saatchi ended their 14-year partnership as the bank appointed [Howatson and Company as its new creative agency of record. ](https://mumbrella.com.au/howatsoncompany-wins-commonwealth-bank-924864) ... Another major client, Woolworths, also moved its [creative account to Droga5 ANZ](https://mumbrella.com.au/droga5-lands-woolworths-creative-account-930413), although M&C Saatchi did not contest the pitch. ... M&C Saatchi ... ](https://mumbrella.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/StaticBentoBox_MCSAATCHI_GROUP-scaled.jpg?w=260&h=150&crop=1) ](https://mumbrella.com.au/ ... -saatchi-unveils-new- ... -of- ... -in-the- ... -858726 ... M&C Saatchi unveils new strategic proposition ahead of rebrand in the new year ... .com.au/mc-saatchi-unveils-new-strategic- ... -ahead-of-re ... -in-the-new-year-8587"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Omnicom Media Retains Uber’s $800M Account and Expands Brazil Remit,www.adweek.com (SUBSCRIPTION ONLY),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.adweek.com/agencies/omnicom-media-retains-ubers-800m-account-and-expands-brazil-remit/,"Omnicom Media Retains Uber’s $800M Account and Expands Brazil Remit ... Rideshare giant Uber has retained Omnicom Media as its global agency of record in most major markets, according to a press release."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,WPP Media’s EssenceMediacom retains Uber’s media mandate across APAC,bestmediainfo.com (BestMediaInfo Bureau),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bestmediainfo.com/mediainfo/advertising/wpp-medias-essencemediacom-retains-ubers-media-mandate-across-apac-12183008,"# WPP Media’s EssenceMediacom retains Uber’s media mandate across APAC ## The account spans seven markets, including India, and will continue to be led from Australia. EssenceMediacom has handled the mandate since 2017 ... New Delhi: WPP Media's EssenceMediacom has retained Uber&rsquo;s media account across Asia-Pacific following a competitive regional pitch. ... The agency has handled Uber’s media mandate in the region since 2017. ... The partnership will continue through a connected regional model covering Australia and New Zealand, Hong Kong, India, Japan, South Korea and Taiwan. ... The account will remain led from Australia, with Maddison Keogh, Client Managing Partner, overseeing teams across the seven markets. ... “This approach blends deep local expertise with a unified APAC strategy—ensuring work is culturally relevant in-market while delivering consistency, governance and scale through an integrated regional hub,” EssenceMediacom said. ... “We’re incredibly proud to continue our partnership with Uber across APAC,” said EssenceMediacom’s Pippa Berlocher. “Working together across such diverse and fast-moving markets has shaped a strong, trusted partnership. By bringing together data, technology, creativity and human ingenuity, and by consistently showing up for each other as a connected team, we’re unlocking new opportunities to ignite what’s next for Uber.” ... Lee Walsh, Global Head of Media at Uber, said, “Following a thorough RFP process, we're delighted to continue our partnership with EssenceMediacom.” ... Walsh added, “Their team demonstrated they are the best fit to support our ambitions across APAC. Their deep local market expertise, strong strategic thinking, and clear understanding of our business stood out throughout the process. We were particularly impressed by their vision for how data, technology and AI can help accelerate our next phase of growth.”"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,EssenceMediacom Australia retains $214m Uber media account - Mumbrella,mumbrella.com.au (Eleanor Dickinson),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mumbrella.com.au/essencemediacom-australia-retains-214m-uber-media-account-930220,"EssenceMediacom Australia retains $214m Uber media account - Mumbrella ... EssenceMediacom has retained Uber’s US$150m Asia Pacific media account after a competitive global pitch, with Australia continuing to lead the regional business. ... The account, worth around A$214m at current exchange rates, has been with EssenceMediacom since 2017, but was again put to a global review that began in April, Mumbrella understands. ... The WPP-owned agency retained the APAC account in 2023, when PHD was appointed to handle Uber’s remaining global media business. ... Led from Sydney, the account covers Australia, New Zealand, Hong Kong, India, Japan, South Korea and Taiwan, with client managing partner Maddison Keogh overseeing teams across the seven markets. ... “We’re incredibly proud to continue our partnership with Uber across APAC,” said EssenceMediacom’s Pippa Berlocher. ... “Working together across such diverse and fast-moving markets has shaped a strong, trusted partnership. ... “By bringing together data, technology, creativity and human ingenuity, and by consistently showing up for each other as a connected team, we’re unlocking new opportunities to ignite what’s next for Uber.” ... Meanwhile, Uber global head of media Lee Walsh said the local EssenceMediacom “team demonstrated they are the best fit to support our ambitions across APAC.” ... “Their deep local market expertise, strong strategic thinking, and clear understanding of our business stood out throughout the process,” Walsh added. ... “We were particularly impressed by their vision for how data, technology and AI can help accelerate our next phase of growth.” ... The retention follows a string of recent client wins for WPP Media Australia, including Michael Hill and BYD. ... News Michael Hill hands $25m media account to Essencemediacom ... News EssenceMediacom Sydney appoints Marcelle Hoyek client managing director"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,EssenceMediacom Retains Uber's APAC Media Account - B&T,www.bandt.com.au (Arvind Hickman),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bandt.com.au/essencemediacom-retains-ubers-apac-media-account/,"EssenceMediacom Retains Uber's APAC Media Account - B&T ... EssenceMediacom has retained Uber across Asia-Pacific, following a competitive regional pitch. ... The regional account is led by Sydney-based client managing partner Maddison Keogh, who joined the agency last year. ... EssenceMediacom handles more than $200 million in media billings for Uber across the APAC region in a relationship that began in 2017. ... The regional model spans Australia and New Zealand, Hong Kong, India, Japan, South Korea and Taiwan. ... EssenceMediacom last defended the account in 2023, which led to Uber’s APAC media being hubbed from Sydney. ... “We’re incredibly proud to continue our partnership with Uber across APAC,” EssenceMediacom’s CEO Pippa Berlocher said. ... “Working together across such diverse and fast-moving markets has shaped a strong, trusted partnership. By bringing together data, technology, creativity and human ingenuity, and by consistently showing up for each other as a connected team, we’re unlocking new opportunities to ignite what’s next for Uber.” ... Lee Walsh, global head of media at Uber, added: “Following a thorough RFP process, we’re delighted to continue our partnership with EssenceMediacom. Their team demonstrated they are the best fit to support our ambitions across APAC. ... “Their deep local market expertise, strong strategic thinking, and clear understanding of our business stood out throughout the process. We were particularly impressed by their vision for how data, technology and AI can help accelerate our next phase of growth.” ... The win follows a strong run of awards success for Uber, with its ‘Backseat Arcade’ campaign recognised across Festival of Media APAC, Festival of Media Global, Cairns Crocodiles and the MFAs, where it secured multiple shortlists and wins in 2026. ... For EssenceMediacom, the Uber retention follows a run of new business success. Recently the agency won the Michael Hill and NRL accounts, while last year it picked up beer brewer Lion, the Australian Retirement Trust, Mastercard and HBO Max. ... EssenceMediacom ... ’s B&T Agency Scorecards, scoring a mark of 9.2."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,McCann and Omnicom Canada on moving past merger mode » Strategy,strategyonline.ca (Laurie Wilson),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://strategyonline.ca/2026/07/17/mccann-omnicom-roundtable/,"McCann and Omnicom Canada on moving past merger mode » Strategy ... ## McCann and Omnicom Canada on moving past merger mode ... In a conversation with strategy, McCann global CEO Tyler Turnbull, Omnicom Advertising Canada CEO Bryan Kane, McCann Canada CSO Joshua Hansen and CCO Jordan Doucette discussed how the agency is leaning on AI expertise, global talent and specialist resources to reshape client relationships."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Omnicom Media Retires Kinesso & Annalect: Here’s What It Means To Aussie Market - B&T,www.bandt.com.au (Arvind Hickman),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bandt.com.au/omnicom-media-retires-kinesso-annalect-heres-what-it-means-to-aussie-market/,"Omnicom Media Retires Kinesso & Annalect: Here’s What It Means To Aussie Market - B&T ... Omnicom has sunsetted the Kinesso and Annalect brands as part of a broader restructure to simplify how the business operates. ... Kinesso has been absorbed into Omnicom’s commercial discipline, while Annalect has been absorbed by the network’s data, technology and analytics division. ... B&T understands the capability will be folded into the business and the ... is about making it easier for clients to access Omnicom’s connected expertise across media, data, technology, commerce and analytics. ... Omnicom inherited IPG’s performance marketing Kinesso as part of its takeover of IPG Mediabrands. ... , the business is led by Jessica ... B&T understands that there are no planned redundancies as a result of the integration and that Kinesso and Annalect clients will continue to work with ... existing teams and leadership, who will continue to support client work and contractual commitments. ... Kinesso and Analect are the latest Omnicom brands to retire after Omnicom’s takeover of IPG Mediabrands. ... When the takeover process concluded late last year, Omnicom retired the DDB, FCB and Mullen Lowe brands globally, which led to DDB Australia’ team merging with Clemenger BBDO, while DDB Group Aotearoa and FCB merged under the McCann brand. ... On the media side, none of the agencies have yet been retired, leaving OMD, PHD, Hearts & Science, UM and Initiative to continue operating, although there has been industry conjecture Omnicom may cut some media brands in the future. ... roles since. ... Omnicom has previously state=d it would consolidate brands across the group and remove duplicated roles as it aims to save $US1.5 billion (A$2.25 billion) in costs as a result of the takeover. ... Omnicom Oceania boss Nick Garrett ... told B&T that agency brands “matter deeply” but “culture eats strategy for ... ” and clients ... increasingly looking for a solution delivered by talent and tools, rather than just looking to work for a specific agency brand. ... “Clients are looking for big solutions. Do I believe, having spoken to more than 200 clients over the past three months, that they care about brands? I think clients deeply care about ... people that they’re working with,” he said. ... “When those people are living a philosophy and delivering work relative to that unique and differentiated position for that brand, they care and then it really matters. That’s why they selected a TBWA, a PHD or anyone else.”"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,EXCLUSIVE: Zenith Retains Reckitt’s $400M US Media Business Following WPP's Europe Win,www.adweek.com (SUBSCRIPTION ONLY),2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.adweek.com/agencies/exclusive-zenith-retains-reckitts-400m-us-media-business-following-wpps-europe-win/,"EXCLUSIVE: Zenith Retains Reckitt’s $400M US Media Business Following WPP's Europe Win ... Zenith defended the business in a competitive pitch.Reckitt ... Publicis Media agency Zenith has retained Reckitt’s U.S. media business in a final shootout with WPP Media, ADWEEK has learned."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,UM: B&T's Agency Scorecard 2026 - B&T,www.bandt.com.au (Arvind Hickman),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bandt.com.au/um-bts-agency-scorecard-2026/,"#### Omnicom Media ... When UM describes 2025, the words “reset”, “resilience” and “repositioning” all appear. The choice of those words is notable and describe what has been a challenging year for the Omnicom agency. ... It lost three of its largest clients in Optus (to Accenture Song), Lion (to EssenceMediacom) and HBF Health (to Starcom). Zurich and Emirates also headed for the departure lounge. ... UM managed to win six clients, including Australian luxury furniture retailer King Living, Village Roadshow and Bayer, but overall media billings took a hit. ... Of course, UM’s 2025 was dominated by Omnicom’s takeover of IPG which concluded in November. It’s important to assess the agency’s performance within that context. ... The agency said that rather than standing still, it set about building stronger and more resilient foundations for future growth. ... This included sharpening its ‘Full Colour Media’ market proposition by upskilling its media specialists into “end-to-end business partners” who are grounded with “commercial acumen” and focused on “measurable business impact”. ... It’s not quite clear how this focus differentiates UM from the rest of the pack—surely this is table stakes for a media agency—but it is clear that a reset and cultural change is in motion. ... In spite of the upheaval, UM won MFA Awards for the Queensland beer XXXX and the National Office for Child Safety, as well as two APAC Effies for ‘A Masterclass in Government Sex Talks’, a campaign that targeted 20-to-34-year-old Australians to increase awareness and destigmatiae regular STI testing. ... of strategy chief Raj Gupta, investment lead Brittany Crowley, planning lead Michael Mellington ... has a strong and experienced leadership bench. ... EssenceMedicom ... Advisory Panel admired ... a reset year, ... ## Chery: New Energy Launch ... Chery Motor Australia, a new auto entrant to Australia, was introducing its new innovative hybrid technology, Chery Super Hybrid, during a time when consumer sentiment around EVs had shifted from hype to hesitation. ... UM needed “emotional proof” through credible, culture-led experiences to make the new Chery Super Hybrid brand feel safe, quality, and right for families, driving consideration and sales. ... UM adopted a “blockbuster” approach ... and literally by partnering with a brand universally associated with quality, excitement, and family experiences, Disney’s Marvel. ... We aimed for instant credibility, cultural relevance, and effective education utilising their tent-pole movie launch in July 2025 – The Fantastic Four: First Steps. ... Rather than competing on media spend, we leveraged borrowed equity through Disney/Marvel to create instantaneous brand credibility through a media strategy that challenges traditional automotive marketing. ... By selecting cultural moment and media partner strategically, Chery achieved 9 per cent sales growth whilst the category declined 21 per cent, proving that media strategy, not just creative or product, drives brand impact. ... ## UM's take on 2025 ... 2025 was a defining reset for UM Australia. ... We faced challenges, including the loss of major clients, but used that moment to refocus the business – sharpening our proposition, simplifying how we operate and redefining the consistency of what we call “the UM way”. ... 2025 has been about substance over noise. We’ve strengthened our commercial thinking, evolved how we partner with clients and ensured we are delivering against business outcomes – not just media metrics. ... At the same time, we’ve rebuilt belief across our people, creating the cultural momentum that underpins high performance. Importantly, we’ve laid the foundations for what comes next. With new leadership, clearer direction and a stronger operating rhythm, 2026 is about acceleration – turning clarity into growth and momentum into meaningful impact. ... The merger with Omnicom will further strengthen this, unlocking greater capability, scale and opportunity for our clients."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Influencer marketing's next battleground: Why ad holdcos are racing to build creator infrastructure - Storyboard18,www.storyboard18.com,2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.storyboard18.com/how-it-works/influencer-marketings-next-battleground-why-ad-holdcos-are-racing-to-build-creator-infrastructure-103434.htm,"The latest signal came this week from Dentsu, which partnered with Meta to build the operational plumbing required for large-scale creator activation, allowing brands to move from working with dozens of creators to managing hundreds or even thousands through integrated discovery, activation and measurement workflows. ... The move underscores a broader shift underway at Dentsu, Publicis, WPP, Omnicom and Havas. Holding companies are no longer positioning influencer marketing as a specialist service. They are rebuilding their media, commerce and data stacks around creators. ... Among the latest developments in the sector, Dentsu's new Meta partnership is perhaps the clearest indication of where influencer marketing is headed. The agency is integrating Meta's Creator Marketplace and Partnership Ads APIs into its Creator & Trends Studio (CATS), creating a system that combines trend discovery, creator identification and paid amplification in a single workflow. ... The ambition is bigger than campaign management. Dentsu is attempting to connect creator content with performance media, making influencer marketing part of what it calls ... Social"" model rather than a standalone discipline. Early deployments reportedly cut creator discovery timelines from hours to minutes and significantly speed up activation workflows. ... The company has also expanded its ecosystem through a partnership with CreatorIQ, integrating creator intelligence directly into dentsu's audience planning infrastructure. ... Publicis bought Influential in 2024 and Captiv8 in 2025, bolstering its ambitions in the creator economy. The deal added a platform with a reported network of more than 15 million creators across 120 countries and extensive social commerce capabilities. ... More importantly, Publicis is integrating creator data into Epsilon's identity graph and CoreID infrastructure. That enables it to position influencer marketing not as awareness media but as a measurable commerce channel, linking creator activity to audience identity, transaction data and business outcomes. ... In 2025, Omnicom Media Group took an audacious step by consolidating all influencer capabilities globally under the Creo brand. The move was not merely organisational—it formalised a philosophy that influencers should be planned and measured like any other media channel. ... Omni, Omnicom's operating system, powers the model by connecting creator discovery, planning, measurement and optimisation. Through partnerships with Amazon, Google, Instacart, Snap and TikTok, Creo is increasingly linking creator activity with commerce signals and search behaviour. ... The group has also launched AI-powered creator briefing, selection and measurement capabilities that utilise Omni data to improve campaign performance and predict outcomes more accurately. ... Goat and INCA anchor the group's influencer capabilities, which today operate within WPP's broader media and AI ecosystem. Goat's global footprint spans more than 40 markets, providing WPP with large-scale creator activation capabilities tied directly to media planning and performance outcomes. ... What is changing now is the degree to which WPP Open and WPP Media's AI-driven infrastructure is embedding influencer marketing. The company's latest India Influencer Marketing Report shows brands increasingly prioritising creator relevance, engagement quality and long-term partnerships while demanding stronger measurement and discovery tools. ... This aligns closely with WPP's broader strategy of integrating creator marketing into unified data, commerce and media operations, rather ... The group is also investing in culture-led and social-first capabilities through Havas Play, rather than just competing on scale. Its acquisition of social-first agency Wilderness expanded expertise in branded content, social storytelling, entertainment marketing and shoppable experiences. ... Combined with capabilities such as PivotRoots in India and the growing Havas Play network, the company is positioning influencer marketing alongside sports, entertainment, gaming, events and fan communities. ... The implications are significant for India, where creator marketing is increasingly becoming a core line item in media planning. ... Global holding companies are bringing sophisticated creator-tech stacks into the market at a time when brands are demanding stronger ROI, better measurement and commerce-linked outcomes. Simultaneously, Indian advertisers continue to rely on vernacular creators, regional communities and long-term ambassador models to drive relevance. ... The winners in influencer marketing may no longer be the agencies with the ... Instead, they will likely be those that own the infrastructure connecting ... , audiences, media, commerce ... In that race, Publicis is buying scale, Omnicom is standardising influence as media, WPP is embedding creators into AI-powered planning systems, Havas is building culture-first ecosystems, and Dentsu's latest Meta partnership shows the industry's newest obsession: building the plumbing that can turn influencer marketing into a repeatable, measurable growth engine."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Publicis wins Samsung Australia media account - Mumbrella,mumbrella.com.au (Eleanor Dickinson),2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mumbrella.com.au/publicis-wins-samsung-australia-media-account-928261,"Publicis wins Samsung Australia media account - ... Australia media account ... Samsung is to consolidate its Australian media account with its global agency, Publicis Groupe, returning the business to the network after a six-year hiatus. ... The electronics giant confirmed it has awarded its Australian media portfolio to the local holding company under its global “connected capabilities” model rather than a single-agency structure, [following a five-month pitch. ](https://mumbrella.com.au/samsung-calls-creative-and-media-pitch-914154)The account was previously held by Omnicom’s CHEP ... The elecgtronics manufacturer also confirmed Mumbrella’s earlier reporting that Samsung-owned creative agency [Cheil Australia will assume responsibility for creative.](https://mumbrella.com.au/samsung-australia-set-to-move-creative-in-house-927798) ... “Samsung Australia recognises the efforts of every participating agency in its recent roster review, and can confirm the process has now concluded,” an agency spokesperson said. ... “We welcome Samsung’s global media agency of record, Publicis Groupe, to the local agency village; and can confirm Cheil will continue creative work alongside our existing roster that spans a number of disciplines. We would also like to extend our gratitude to the incumbent, Clemenger Group, for a successful seven years of partnership, and wish the entire team every future success.” ... Cheil already handles a portion of Samsung’s creative work and execution locally, while Clemenger had the creative work since 2020, after taken over from Publicis agency Leo Burnett. Before CHEP, the Publicis agency Starcom previously handled media duties. ... The decision follows Clemenger’s recent losses of major creative accounts, including Asahi and Bupa, although [the agency announced it had picked up Stan today](https://mumbrella.com.au/clemenger-bbdo-bags-stan-creative-account-928244). Leo Burnett, Ogilvy and M&C Saatchi were also on Samsung’s final creative pitch list."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,McCann New Zealand cements its launch into the NZ market with strong first showing at Cannes Lions – Campaign Brief NZ,campaignbrief.co.nz (Ricki Green),2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://campaignbrief.co.nz/2026/07/01/mccann-new-zealand-cements-its-launch-into-the-nz-market-with-strong-first-showing-at-cannes-lions/,"McCann New Zealand cements its launch into the NZ market with strong first showing at Cannes Lions – Campaign Brief NZ ... # McCann New Zealand cements its launch into the NZ market with strong first showing at Cannes Lions ... ### McCann New Zealand has marked its debut year at Cannes Lions with a strong first showing at the festival, earning 1 Gold, 1 Silver, 4 Bronzes and 20 shortlists across its newly merged creative offering. ... The results showcase the creative impact of the newly launched agency, demonstrating that the combination of FCB Aotearoa, DDB Group Aotearoa and Clemenger Wellington has formed a formidable creative force in the New Zealand market. ... Says Leisa Wall, CCO of McCann New Zealand: “The best introductions don’t come from what you say about yourself, they come from what the industry says about your work. As McCann New Zealand launches in Auckland and Wellington, it’s great to see both markets’ work recognised on a world stage. That’s a debut we’re bloody proud of!” ... Says Gary Steele, CCO of McCann New Zealand: “This is more than a great Cannes result for us; it’s a statement of our intent. It shows what’s possible when outstanding talent comes together with a shared ambition to create work that earns attention, delivers impact for our clients, and competes with the very best in the world. At McCann, we believe in creating stories that live on, and this is just the beginning.” ... Says Brigid Alkema, CCO of McCann Wellington: “This epic showing is testament to the diverse talent of our new team, with recognition across an enviable set of categories – including the rare honour of Glass. While the global acknowledgement of our work is worth celebrating, we’re full of energy for what the next year will bring.” ... Now New Zealand’s largest integrated marketing services business, McCann Group NZ is accelerating its transition to a fully connected operating model — bringing creative, media, data, martech, commerce and earned capabilities together under one roof, backed by the global scale of Omnicom."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,What will Comcast/NBCU’s conscious uncoupling mean for brands?,digiday.com (Sam Bradley),2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://digiday.com/media-buying/what-will-nbcus-conscious-uncoupling-from-comcast-mean-for-brands/,"To quickly recap, Comcast CEO Brian Roberts announced Monday (June 29th) that the two businesses, which were merged following a 2009 deal, would separate as part of a tax-free spinoff. Comcast spun out its cable TV business Versant back in January. ... Roberts said the newly unshackled NBCU, which will span NBC, several cable networks, Telemundo, Peacock and Sky, would function as a “unique, independent, focused company that will be home to some of the industry’s most valuable brands and assets across theme parks, film, television, streaming, sports and news.” Mike Cavanagh, the current co-chief exec of Comcast, is set to become CEO at NBCU. ... The spinning-out plan was a surprise from Roberts, but has been received well by the markets; Comcast’s share price has risen 6.5% since Monday, at the time of writing. Quite what it means for advertisers is less clear. ... Three media buyers told Digiday they’d had no information from contacts within NBCU or Comcast regarding how the split might affect their clients, or how elements of the Comcast/NBCU ad stack will get divvied up – though ad server and DSP provider Freewheel and Universal Ads are expected to remain with Comcast. ... Despite the absence of detail, agency experts told Digiday that the move might impact CPMs once the dust has settled. ... Some expect NBCU to attempt to raise the pricing floor on its streaming and linear TV inventory, particularly as it looks to fund expensive sports rights deals amid competition from streaming platforms. ... “Once the spinoff is complete (maybe 12 months), there will be pressure for NBCUniversal to grow advertising and subscription revenue without the support of Comcast,” said Luke Moore, vp and managing director, media partner at full service agency FUSE Create, in an email. “This will likely push available inventory towards higher CPM media purchases, like addressable or data-heavy media products and reduce focus on traditional, linear TV.” ... With this year’s TV upfronts firmly in play, few buyers expect the split to upset negotiations. “I definitely don’t see it affecting this year’s upfront and I don’t really see it impacting next year’s either,” said Horizon Media’s evp and head of investment Samantha Rose. ... That might change by 2027, with an unbundled NBCU under pressure to establish a solid footing. “Next year could be a different story, as that will be the first year they go into the upfronts as a standalone entity,” said Abby McNally, group director, connections strategy at Collective Measures. ... “NBC has historically been a place where it’s been hard to push for better rates. With this unbundling, I’d hope they would be more amenable to conversations with advertisers. I’m looking at it as a pro,” said McInnis. ... Advertisers with existing long-term deals, such as presenting sponsor slots, are also unlikely to see changes, added Keynes’ Larkman. “Companies like NBC [will] protect advertisers at all costs,” he said. ... Buyers looking farther down the line sense trouble, however. NBCU without its Comcast pairing could become an acquisition target for deep-pocketed streamers (Netflix, for example, might consider another run at a major media acquisition). ... One media buyer, who exchanged candor for anonymity, shared their “catastrophe” scenario, in which NBCU’s custodianship of Olympic broadcasting rights was compromised by a carve up or merger with a larger entity. ... “If they cut back on [coverage], that would ultimately impact what we’re planning or the reasons why clients come on board [for Olympic media buyers],” said the buyer."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,"Agentic ad buying, retail media unity, and the AI trust gap",notes.ppc.land (Luís Rijo),2026-06-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://notes.ppc.land/p/agentic-ad-buying-retail-media-unity,"The week that closed Cannes Lions 2026 ended with a cluster of announcements that, read together, point toward a single underlying pressure on the advertising industry: automation is arriving faster than governance frameworks, consumer trust norms, or even platform infrastructure is prepared to absorb it. On June 27, 2026, PPC Land published four stories that sit at the intersection of those tensions - an autonomous AI ad buy completed in Prague, a retail media unification deal announced on the Croisette, a Google API update racing to meet EU AI Act deadlines, and a consumer trust study whose numbers are sharp enough to demand attention from any brand running AI-powered campaigns. ... The friction between digital advertising and physical retail has been a documented structural problem in retail media for years. On June 24, 2026, at Cannes Lions, Broadsign and Mirakl Ads announced a strategic partnership designed to address it at the point of campaign activation, with a Q3 2026 launch planned. ... The two companies occupy distinct positions in the technology stack. Mirakl Ads is the retail media arm of Mirakl, a company founded in 2012 with dual headquarters in Boston and Paris. Broadsign is a Montreal-based platform that manages and monetizes out-of-home media globally; the company says more than 2.8 million static and digital signs - across airports, shopping malls, grocery stores, transit systems, and health clinics - run on its platform. It currently powers more than 35 in-store retail media networks worldwide. ... What the partnership enables, in structural terms, is a unified buying surface. A retailer already running a retail media network on Mirakl Ads gains the ability to offer advertisers a single campaign brief and a single point of contact that covers both e-commerce placements and in-store digital screens. Mirakl Ads handles the commerce logic, the marketplace monetization functions, and the online placements. Broadsign handles the technical delivery of content to the physical screens. Neither company absorbs the other’s function. Retailers retain ownership of their inventory, pricing, and shopper data decisions. ... The commercial pressure that created demand for this kind of solution is measurable. Retail media spending is projected to exceed $300 billion globally by 2030, representing approximately 20 percent of total worldwide advertising revenue, a figure Omdia research from September 2025 placed as the projected ceiling. At that scale, the cost of maintaining separate workflows for e-commerce placements and in-store screens becomes significant. It falls on retailers managing vendor relationships, on advertisers reconciling fragmented performance reports, and on agencies trying to attribute sales outcomes that cross the physical-digital boundary. ... That boundary has proven persistently difficult to account for. Forrester research, cited in Amazon documentation, places 72 percent of US retail sales in physical stores. Most digital retail media investment, however, is built around online conversion events. The Broadsign-Mirakl integration is not the first attempt to bridge that gap, but the specific combination - Mirakl’s marketplace infrastructure alongside Broadsign’s scale in physical screen delivery - gives it a broader reach at launch than most previous efforts. ... On June 24, 2026, Google published version 24.2 of the Google Ads API. The release note, authored by Anash P. Oommen of the Google Ads API Team and published on the Google Ads Developer Blog, describes it as a drop-in upgrade for v24.1. The changes it introduces are, however, more consequential than a minor version number implies. ... PPC Land covered the release in detail on June 27, 2026. Four headline changes define it: synthetic content labeling aligned with the EU AI Act, multi-party approval infrastructure for sensitive account actions, granular network segmentation for Performance Max placement reporting, and two new campaign experiment types that allow advertisers to test campaign mix strategies. ... The EU AI Act context is direct. Article 50 of the Act requires transparency labeling for AI-generated content, with obligations taking effect August 2, 2026 - fewer than six weeks after the v24.2 release date. Google’s new synthetic content labeling structures give developers the programmatic infrastructure needed to flag AI-generated ad assets in compliance with that requirement. The timing is tight enough to make the regulatory connection unambiguous. ... Google also, notably, moved its Dynamic Search Ads compliance deadline to 2027, a change documented in AI Max for Search reporting updates published on June 23, 2026. The same update introduced four new search term report views and a Search Campaigns for Travel guide. These changes were made without a corresponding announcement, a pattern that PPC Land has flagged in its coverage of how Google communicates documentation changes to practitioners. ... The Performance Max segmentation changes in v24.2 are the feature practitioners have been waiting for longest. Performance Max campaigns have, since their introduction, allocated spend across Google’s ad networks - Search, Display, YouTube, Gmail, Discover, Maps - without giving advertisers programmatic access to a breakdown of where impressions and spend were distributed at the network level. The v24.2 release adds placement report segmentation by ad network for PMax, enabling that breakdown via the API for the first time. For any advertiser or agency trying to audit whether Performance Max budget allocation aligns with their actual channel strategy, this is a materially useful addition. ... Taken together, the v24.2 changes reflect two simultaneous pressures on platform API design: regulatory compliance timelines that do not move, and practitioner demand for accountability features that have been requested for years. Both arrived in the same release. ... The most commercially urgent story published on June 27, 2026 is also the one least framed as ad tech news. Usercentrics released the State of Digital Trust 2026, a study of 11,000 consumers across seven markets - Germany, the United States, the United Kingdom, Spain, Italy, the Netherlands, and Sweden - conducted by Sapio Research in March 2026. PPC Land’s coverage of the report surfaced numbers that are, for any brand running AI-powered advertising, structurally important. ... The headline figure: 47 percent of consumers globally took at least one action with a direct revenue consequence in the six months before fieldwork closed, because of concerns about how a brand handled their data in the context of AI. These are not expressions of concern or stated intentions. They are completed commercial decisions. ... The breakdown matters. Twenty-four percent canceled a subscription or stopped purchasing from a brand entirely. Twenty percent switched to a competitor they believed handled AI data more responsibly. A further 20 percent reduced spending. Thirty-one percent warned others or complained publicly. And 35 percent took two or more of these actions against the same brand. For a brand with one million customers, the Usercentrics figures imply that as many as 240,000 purchase-affecting decisions may have been driven by AI data concerns alone within a six-month window. ... June 27, 2026. VIOOH’s agentic Seller Agent automated more than 100 curated DOOH private marketplace deal packages in H1 2026, with a global self-serve platform expansion planned for Q3 2026. PPC Land ... June 27, 2026. IAB Ukraine’s 2026 Digital Media Market Overview recorded 22% growth in the digital advertising market in 2025 and forecast a further 18% expansion in 2026, with video, CTV, and retail media identified as primary drivers. PPC Land ... June 27, 2026. Almedia, ranked Europe’s third fastest-growing company, opened a London office at King’s Cross to recruit data scientists and machine learning engineers,"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,The partnership aims to lift viewers relevance for NBCU CTV.,digiday.com (Michael Bürgi),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://digiday.com/media-buying/at-cannes-omnicom-media-and-nbcu-say-theyre-crafting-dynamic-contextual-ads-for-content/,"# At Cannes, Omnicom Media and NBCU say they’re crafting dynamic contextual ads for content ... The last of a series of partnerships and collaborations Omnicom Media rolled out during Cannes Lions 2026 has the media agency network co-developing a dynamic contextual content solution with NBCUniversal that aims to boost creative relevance to viewers watching the media company’s CTV shows. ... The partnership pairs audience and performance data from Omnicom’s Acxiom unit with contextual metadata on NBCUniversal’s shows in order to optimize in-flight creative from Omnicom clients, who can dynamically align their ad messages with specific shows, down to the episode level and even moments in the episodes. The goal is to enable a more adaptive and self-optimizing CTV advertising system that helps those clients improve creative performance and relevance throughout their campaigns. ... The partnership, according to Omnicom Media, is currently beta testing and should be available in the U.S. by end of 2026. ... “We created this semantic layer over premium video,” she said. “We see this as the evolution of dynamic creative optimization. Now we’re introducing DCC, (dynamic contextual content), and it really is extending the capability by using those contextual signals to manipulate creative expression based on scenes to get right down to that really authentic relevancy for the creative ads we’re serving within those placements.” ... “Marketers are navigating a fragmented, highly competitive ecosystem while being held to performance metrics,” said Ryan McConville, chief product officer and evp of ad products & solutions, NBCUniversal. “By pairing NBCUniversal’s content metadata with Omnicom’s audience and performance data, we can make creative optimization actionable and open up more relevant, effective ways for brands to engage their customers.” ... The motivation for the joint effort comes from Omnicom Media research out of its intelligence unit, which found, among other things, that 76% of people say they connect with ads relevant to the content that is being watched. ... The ultimate goal here: better outcomes, said Keagan McDonnell, head of partner innovation and strategic initiatives at OM North America. “Being able to connect all this to business outcomes really means that we’ll be able to audit if one or another of the given contextual tags are outperforming from a business perspective,” said McDonnell. ... He added that although Omnicom has offered the opportunity to several clients across CPG, financial services and telecoms, the experimental nature of this hasn’t landed a real-market example yet. ... “We’ve talked to quite a few brands that are really excited, but it’s not something that we can just turn on, like ‘Oh, test this in this upcoming campaign that’s launching next week’,” said McDonnell. “We’re really having to have proactive, meaningful conversations, both on the creative and production side with stakeholders at brands, as well as the media side, to really deliver that synchronicity.”"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Tourism Australia ditches UM for Zenith - Mumbrella,mumbrella.com.au (Zac Nikolovski),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-ditches-um-for-zenith-927550,"Tourism Australia ditches UM for Zenith - Mumbrella ... Tourism Australia ditches UM for Zenith - Mumbrella ... Tourism Australia ditches UM for Zenith ... Tourism Australia has ended its 10-year relationship with UM, as it hands its global media account to Zenith. ... The Publicis-owned agency will take over the global media buying from UM from 1 September under a three-year contract with a maximum value of $189 million and two one-year extensions. ... The incumbent UM [first won the account from OMD in 2016](https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-parts-ways-omd-appoints-newagency-369557) under a five-year contract worth $120 million. The agency was reappointed in [2021 on a new five-year deal valued at $300 million](https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-keeps-with-um-for-media-account-700399), almost triple the size of the original contract. ... The win for Zenith comes nine months after Tourism Australia [went to pitch for media planning and buying services,](https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-takes-media-account-to-pitch-889831) which span 16 major overseas markets. ... In an official announcement, Zenith’s chief executive Jason Tonelli said there was “no greater brief in our market than Australia itself”. ... Tourism Australia’s chief marketing officer Susan Coghill said the partnership with Publicis marks the beginning of a new chapter in the agency’s marketing. ... “What distinguished Publicis through this process was a genuine understanding of where travel discovery is heading, and a clear, demonstrated capability to help Tourism Australia be present and chosen wherever that moment happens,” she added. ... Zenith will now inherit the media strategy for Tourism Australia’s “Come and Say G’day” platform, with the latest campaign [chapter having launched last August.](https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-goes-for-tailored-local-creative-in-latest-gday-campaign-883871) ... Tourism Australia first launched the “Come and say G’day” platform in October 2022 via UM and creative agency M&amp;C Saatchi, a[ launch that marked its first global campaign in six years. ](https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-hops-to-it-with-first-global-campaign-in-six-years-via-mc-saatchi-760839) ... Less than two years later, the body parted ways with M&C Saatchi after six years, handing creative duties to [Accenture Song.](https://mumbrella.com.au/tourism-australia-goes-for-tailored-local-creative-in-latest-gday-campaign-883871)"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,TV broadcasters unite to compete with big tech - MediaCat UK,"mediacat.uk (Elliot Wright, James Swift, India Stronach)",2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mediacat.uk/tv-broadcasters-unite-to-compete-with-big-tech/,"Channel 4, ITV and Sky say that buying ad space on premium TV is now ‘as simple as social’. By India Stronach 25.06.2026 UK broadcasters have joined Universal Ads for the first time, with several touting it as a new platform allowing small brands to reach premium TV. ... Channel 4, ITV, Sky and Comcast have launched a new self-service platform for ‘premium’ TV advertising in the UK. ... Universal Ads is pitched as ‘as simple as social’, promising SMEs no minimum spend, access to over 35m UK households and less than 24 hours from sign-up to the ad appearing. Brands can buy ads with a credit card in minutes, mimicking the convenience of Google Ads or Meta. ... Channel 4’s chief commercial officer, Rak Patel, said that this lowering of the barriers to premium media will be a ‘gamechanger’ for small brands, praising the collaboration and simplicity of the new service. He added that it will ‘help ensure premium TV remains innovative and competitive alongside global social and digital platforms’. ... Universal Ads could offer traditional TV stations an opportunity to compete with social platforms for advertising spend by offering more flexible terms for smaller brands. Kelly Williams, managing director of commercial for ITV, described it as a ‘future-proofing’ measure which would ‘deliver real value for small-to-medium advertisers’. ... Interestingly, some platforms appear to be pitching the service as a standalone alternative more than a continuation of Comcast’s existing services. Channel 4’s release stated: ‘Channel 4 is launching a new self-service platform for premium TV advertising alongside ITV, Sky and Comcast’. This could be an indication that Universal Ads is planned to provide an alternative not just to the walled gardens of Google Ads and Meta, but also to the growing strength of Netflix and Disney+ as they continue to aggressively pursue advertising spend. ... The level of collaboration between Channel 4, ITV and Sky is unprecedented, indeed this is the first time ITVX audiences can be bought programmatically outside of ITV’s own platform, Planet V. The show of unity from these competitors shows a real push to achieve that ‘future-proof’ system for traditional broadcasters, though how much the lower barrier to entry will change the face of TV advertising remains to be seen."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Comcast works with British broadcasters on Universal Ads product,thedesk.net,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thedesk.net/2026/06/comcast-channel-4-itv-sky-ads-product/,"Comcast works with British broadcasters on Universal Ads product # Comcast works with British broadcasters on Universal Ads product ... - Comcast has rolled out its Universal Ads product through a partnership with ITV, Sky and Channel 4. - The platform allows advertisers to buy premium TV inventory across all three broadcasters through a single self-service interface; the initiative primarily targets small- and medium-sized businesses that have typically found traditional TV advertising difficult to access. - Separately, Channel 4 unveiled Enhance, a new dynamic creative optimization platform for streaming campaigns. ... Three of Britain’s largest broadcasters are taking new steps to modernize television advertising, launching platforms designed to make premium TV inventory easier to buy while offering advertisers more sophisticated creative and targeting capabilities. ... Comcast’s Universal Ads platform officially launched in the United Kingdom this week through a partnership with Channel 4, ITV and the company’s own Sky, creating a self-service marketplace that allows advertisers to purchase inventory across all three broadcasters through a single interface. ... The platform is aimed primarily at small and medium-sized businesses that have traditionally viewed television advertising as too complex or expensive to access. Advertisers can launch campaigns by setting a budget, selecting target audiences, uploading creative assets and activating campaigns through a workflow designed to resemble social media advertising platforms. ... The launch marks Universal Ads’ first major international expansion and follows more than a year of collaboration among Comcast and the three broadcasters. The partnership was originally announced last June. ... “Together with Channel 4, ITV and Sky, we’ve built a platform that changes how TV advertising works in the U.K. today,” David Shaw, the Head of Global Expansion at Universal Ads, said in a statement this week. ... At the same time, Channel 4 announced the launch of Enhance, a new creative optimization platform developed with Brightline’s ScreenSense technology that allows advertisers to dynamically modify television creative for streaming audiences. ... Omnicom Media UK is serving as an early partner for the Enhance platform and has supported efforts to expand addressable and performance-driven advertising across premium video environments."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,"Universal Ads goes live in UK, providing TV with ‘easy button’ – The Media Leader",uk.themedialeader.com (John Moulding),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uk.themedialeader.com/universal-ads-goes-live-in-uk-providing-tv-with-easy-button/,"Universal Ads goes live in UK, providing TV with ‘easy button’ – The Media Leader ... # Universal Ads goes live in UK, providing TV with ‘easy button’ ... From today, SME advertisers in the UK can buy streaming TV audiences from ITV, Sky and Channel 4 through the same self-service advertising platform, allowing these broadcasters to compete harder for budget that has historically gone to global tech platforms like Meta and Google. ... The Universal Ads platform – harnessing Comcast Advertising technology with some customisation for the UK – is designed to make TV as easy to buy as social. ... Universal Ads becomes the first place anyone can buy ITVX audiences programmatically outside of Planet V – the broadcaster’s owned-and-operated planning, buying and selling platform (albeit limited to SMEs). ... Universal Ads is a notable broadcaster collaboration, described by the companies involved as a ‘groundbreaking move’ for the UK advertising industry. ... This is also an important step in the hoped-for international expansion of Universal Ads, which has been live in the US for over a year (and today offers inventory from 20+ TV providers). ... The UK broadcasters hope Universal Ads will attract new-to-TV advertisers including digital-native and direct-to-consumer brands who previously thought TV advertising was out of reach. ... The UK version of Universal Ads was first unveiled at last year’s Cannes Lions, and its stakeholders are using this year’s festival to hail the live deployment. ... 4, ... Shaw says Universal Ads is working closely with Clearcast to ensure copy approval does not become a bottleneck if, as expected, there is a proliferation of advertisers on TV with new creatives. ... Meanwhile, Universal Ads is collaborating with Clearcast to see how the approval workflow can be streamlined at a technical level. ... To ensure smooth take-off, Universal Ads has opened to an initial base of advertisers. The advertiser pool will be broadened in the months ahead. ... The Universal Ads platform also integrates with third-party measurement partners. One of those is Lantern, the measurement and reporting solution that will demonstrate online responses and actions generated by TV advertising. ... This is another UK collaboration between Channel 4, ITV and Sky, powered by Thinkbox, and is due to go live next year. ... Shaw has worked previously at Twitter and TikTok, where his focus was to expand their advertising businesses beyond Top 250 enterprise brands to a broader group of largely performance-focused advertisers. ... “This mirrors what we are trying to do with Universal Ads,” he notes. “We want to change the perception that for those advertisers, TV is inaccessible and expensive.” ... Sky, Channel 4, ... convinced the small-medium business ... will respond to the ... safety and proven effectiveness of TV. ... Universal Ads is part of Comcast Advertising but operates under its own brand. ... The media owners using Universal Ads in the US (to open the TV market to smaller advertisers) include NBCUniversal, Paramount, Fox, Scripps, AMC Networks, Roku, Vizio, Samsung, DirecTV, Cox, Xumo and Vevo. ... Comcast Advertising’s president James Rooke is a long-time champion of the need for TV to develop an ‘easy button’ – removing buying hurdles to compete harder with social and search. ... Universal Ads is a practical example of that vision."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,"Universal Ads UK Launch: TV Advertising for SMEs on ITV, Sky & C4",bmmagazine.co.uk (Amy Ingham),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bmmagazine.co.uk/in-business/universal-ads-uk-launch-sme-tv-advertising/,"Universal Ads UK Launch: TV Advertising for SMEs on ITV, Sky & C4 ... # Small firms can buy ITV, Sky and Channel 4 airtime in minutes as Universal Ads launches in the UK ... been the preserve of brands with deep pockets and a media agency on retainer. ... From today that changes. Comcast’s Universal Ads, the self-service platform built for the premium TV industry, has launched in the UK in partnership with Channel 4, ITV and Sky, opening the medium to the small and medium-sized businesses that have long watched from the sidelines. ... “This milestone represents the next phase of Universal Ads as we expand onto the global stage,” said David Shaw, Head of Global Expansion at Universal Ads. “Together with Channel 4, ITV and Sky, we’ve built a platform that changes how TV advertising works in the UK today, bringing an experience that feels as simple as social, while preserving everything that makes broadcaster TV trusted, effective and impactful.” ... The launch, first unveiled at Cannes Lions in 2025, follows a year of work between Comcast and the three broadcasters’ product, operations and commercial teams to turn a statement of intent into a market-ready product. It is a notable show of collective will from rivals who, in a fragmenting media market, increasingly see the changing media landscape as a shared challenge rather than a zero-sum fight for spend. ... past decade turning ... low entry costs ... Available to US advertisers for more than a year, where it has reported encouraging early results, the platform is built on an API-first foundation, giving brands and technology partners room to integrate, customise and scale. It is aimed squarely at firms that have found TV out of reach, yet it retains the targeting depth and performance reporting that larger advertisers and agencies expect. The broader announcement, set out by Channel 4, ITV and Sky, positions the marketplace as a way to widen the pool of brands on screen while protecting the standards that define premium TV. ... For the UK’s army of smaller advertisers, the proposition is straightforward: more brands on screen, more choice for viewers and, for the first time, a national TV campaign that can be live before lunch. It is a development that sits comfortably alongside other moves to put broadcast within reach of growing firms, including ITV’s £500,000 TV advertising prize for SMEs. Whether it shifts budgets at scale will become clear over the coming year, but the direction of travel is unmistakable. Premium TV is no longer just for the big players."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Comcast’s Universal Ads launches in UK - CSI Magazine,www.csimagazine.com (CSI),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.csimagazine.com/csi/Comcast-Universal-Ads-launches-in-UK.php,"Comcast’s Universal Ads launches in UK - CSI Magazine ... ## Comcast’s Universal Ads launches in UK ... 23/06/202 ... Comcast’s Universal Ads platform has launched in the UK through a partnership with Channel 4, ITV and Sky, allowing small and medium-sized businesses to buy premium TV advertising across all three broadcasters from a single self-service platform for the first time. The launch, first announced at Cannes Lions 2025, is designed to make TV advertising easier to access for brands that have traditionally relied on digital and social channels. Advertisers can set budgets, target audiences, upload creative and launch campaigns within minutes through one interface. David Shaw, head of global expansion at Universal Ads, said the platform “changes how TV advertising works in the UK today” and offers an experience that feels “as simple as social”. The initiative follows a year of collaboration between Comcast, Channel 4, ITV and Sky and forms part of Universal Ads’ wider international expansion after operating in the US for more than a year, where it has shown ""compelling results"", according to Comcast. “This milestone represents the next phase of Universal Ads as we expand onto the global stage”, said David Shaw, Head of Global Expansion at Universal Ads. “Together with Channel 4, ITV and Sky, we’ve built a platform that changes how TV advertising works in the UK today, bringing an experience that feels as simple as social, while preserving everything that makes broadcaster TV trusted, effective and impactful.” Universal Ads also includes built-in campaign measurement tools, enabling advertisers to track outcomes such as website visits, sign-ups and purchases. Built on an API-first foundation, the platform is designed for growth-focused brands, whether digital-native, DTC, or scaling beyond social, that have historically found TV out of reach, but it retains the performance depth and targeting sophistication that larger advertisers and agencies expect. Advertisers can track campaign impact through first-party pixel measurement, placing a Universal Ads pixel on their site to connect TV impressions directly to web visits, sign-ups, and purchases. For brands that require independent verification, Universal Ads Manager Marketing API integrates with leading third-party measurement partners (including Lantern due to go live in 2027), giving advertisers the same accountability infrastructure they rely on across their digital and social channels. ... ### Comcast’s Universal Ads launches in UK"
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Omnicom Media’s Lodestar UM wins AMFI’s integrated media mandate to drive next phase of ‘Mutual Funds Sahi Hai’,www.medianews4u.com,2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.medianews4u.com/omnicom-medias-lodestar-um-wins-amfis-integrated-media-mandate-to-drive-next-phase-of-mutual-funds-sahi-hai/,"Omnicom Media’s Lodestar UM wins AMFI’s integrated media mandate to drive next phase of ‘Mutual Funds Sahi Hai’ ... # Omnicom Media’s Lodestar UM wins AMFI’s integrated media mandate to drive next phase of ‘Mutual Funds Sahi Hai’ ... Mumbai: Omnicom Media’s Lodestar UM has been awarded the integrated media mandate for the Association of Mutual Funds in India (AMFI), following a closely contested multi-agency pitch. The account is among the largest mandates in India’s financial services sector. ... Under the mandate, Lodestar UM will lead AMFI’s end-to-end media strategy, planning and buying responsibilities, while further strengthening the media ecosystem and strategic direction behind the widely recognised ‘Mutual Funds Sahi Hai’ campaign. ... Through the partnership, the agency will support AMFI’s efforts to deepen investor awareness, expand participation beyond traditional markets and accelerate the next stage of growth for India’s mutual fund industry. ... The appointment comes at a significant phase for the category, as India’s mutual fund industry continues to record strong growth driven by rising financial awareness, expanding digital access and increasing investor participation from emerging markets. The industry is witnessing structural changes that are reshaping how Indian consumers approach long-term wealth creation. ... As the representative body of India’s mutual fund industry, AMFI has played an important role in encouraging investor participation and strengthening financial inclusion. With evolving investor expectations and a growing base of new-age investors entering financial markets, the association is focusing on enhancing engagement, reinforcing trust and increasing the relevance of mutual funds for future investors. ... As part of the mandate, Lodestar UM will deploy its strategic planning expertise, audience-first media approach, data capabilities and integrated media solutions to support AMFI’s objective of encouraging informed participation and sustained category growth. ... Commenting on the win, Aditi Mishra, CEO of Lodestar UM, said, “AMFI has played an instrumental role in transforming the investment landscape in India and creating one of the country’s most successful financial inclusion movements. We are excited to partner with them at this important juncture and help shape the next chapter of its growth journey.” ... The mandate further strengthens Omnicom Media’s position in the financial services and investment category and reinforces its focus on delivering integrated media strategies designed to drive both brand impact and business outcomes."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Omnicom Media's Lodestar UM Wins AMFI's Integrated Media Mandate; To Steward Iconic 'Mutual Funds Sahi Hai' Campaign,adtechtoday.com (News Bureau),2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://adtechtoday.com/omnicom-medias-wins-amfis-integrated-media-mandate-to-steward-iconic-mutual-funds-sahi-hai-campaign/,"# Omnicom Media’s Lodestar UM Wins AMFI’s Integrated Media Mandate; To Steward Iconic ‘Mutual Funds Sahi Hai’ Campaign Published on: June 19, 2026 Mumbai, India, 19 th June 2026: Omnicom Media’s Lodestar UM has been awarded the integrated media mandate for the Association of Mutual Funds in India (AMFI) – one of the largest mandates in the financial services sector – following a closely contested multi-agency pitch. ... The mandate will see Lodestar UM lead AMFI’s end-to-end media strategy, planning and buying responsibilities, while strengthening the media ecosystem and strategic thinking underpinning the iconic ‘Mutual Funds Sahi Hai’ campaign. Through the partnership, the agency will support AMFI’s efforts to deepen investor awareness, broaden participation beyond traditional markets and drive the next phase of growth for India’s mutual fund ecosystem. ... Under the partnership, Lodestar UM will leverage its strategic planning capabilities, data intelligence, audience-first approach and integrated media expertise to support AMFI’s goal of driving informed participation and sustained category growth. ... Commenting on the win, Aditi Mishra, CEO of Lodestar UM, said, “AMFI has played an instrumental role in transforming the investment landscape in India and creating one of the country’s most successful financial inclusion movements. We are excited to partner with them at this important juncture and help shape the next chapter of its growth journey.” ... The win further strengthens Omnicom Media’s momentum in the financial services and investment category, reinforcing its reputation for delivering integrated media solutions that drive both brand growth and business outcomes."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Just Eat dials up WPP’s EssenceMediacom - More About Advertising,www.moreaboutadvertising.com (Staff),2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,http://www.moreaboutadvertising.com/2026/06/just-eat-dials-up-wpps-essencemediacom/,"Just Eat dials up WPP’s EssenceMediacom - More About Advertising ... It’s all change at Just Eat Takeaway.com with the EMEA media account moving to WPP’s EssenceMediacom from Omnicom’s UM, hard on the heels of the food delivery’s firm’s creative business abandoning Omnicom’s McCann for independent VCCP. ... EssenceMediacom beat Publicis Media’s Spark Foundry and UM to the business which includes major market the UK. Just Eat, now owned by tech investor Prosus, is one of those businesses that has found profits hard to come by despite being a big factor in people’s lives. ... McCanc and UM were both long-serving agencies for Just Eat before the merger with Omnicom. McCann in particular might feel aggrieved. Just Eat is scheduled to spend just under £200m in 2026 so, while hardly a major global account, it’s a useful addition to some recent wins by latterly embattled WPP Media. A win over previously all-conquering Publicis is particularly welcome. ... Just Eat head of global media Celine Francois says WPP Media’s “advanced data and technology capabilities” will be critical as the brand “accelerates its growth and drives relevance across food and delivery”."
Universal McCann,,,,Exa,Universal Ads’ Adam Royle: Koddi Partnership Brings CTV to Commerce Buyers ‘Where They are Working Today’ – Beet.TV,www.beet.tv (12 May 2026 / David Kaplan),2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.beet.tv/2026/05/universal-ads-adam-royle-koddi-partnership-brings-ctv-to-commerce-buyers-where-they-are-working-today.html,"Universal Ads’ Adam Royle: Koddi Partnership Brings CTV to Commerce Buyers ‘Where They are Working Today’ – Beet.TV ... # Universal Ads’ Adam Royle: Koddi Partnership Brings CTV to Commerce Buyers ‘Where They are Working Today’ 12 May 2026 / David Kaplan Connected TV buying, planning, and measurement integration into commerce platforms eliminates traditional barriers that prevented retail media advertisers from accessing television inventory through familiar workflows. ... “This week, Universal Ads and ad tech company Koddi announced a strategic partnership that brings CTV buying, planning, and measurement into the Koddi platform,” Adam Royle, head of Strategic Partnerships at Comcast’s Universal Ads, told Beet.TV editorial director Lisa Granatstein at POSSIBLE. “This means that CTV is now accessible to commerce buyers in Koddi and it meets them where they are working today.” ... The partnership allows brands and retail media networks to treat television as performance channel through native commerce ecosystem integration, expanding both advertiser access and publisher inventory reach. ... This creates broader industry expansion where publishers gain access to advertisers who never used television while enabling advertisers to reach previously inaccessible TV audiences. ... Universal Ads solves these challenges through integrated solutions delivered natively within commerce advertising environments. ... CTV convergence leverages shopper data to improve premium video targeting accuracy, enabling commerce advertisers to apply familiar data assets to television inventory. ... Universal Ads was founded specifically to remove television friction and expand category participation through simplified access that maintains targeting precision and measurement capabilities. ... “A winning TV strategy for brands is not a one size fits all, but this partnership allows these brands to test and prove TV as a performance channel at scale,” Royle said. ... Connected TV buying, planning, and measurement integration into commerce platforms eliminates traditional barriers that prevented retail media advertisers from accessing television inventory through familiar workflows. ... “This week, Universal Ads and ad tech company Koddi announced a strategic partnership that brings CTV buying, planning, and measurement into the Koddi platform,” Adam Royle, head of Strategic Partnerships at Comcast’s Universal Ads, told Beet.TV editorial director Lisa Granatstein at POSSIBLE. “This means that CTV is now accessible to commerce buyers in Koddi and it meets them where they are working today.” ... The integration enables precision targeting, buying, and measurement within existing commerce advertising workflows rather ... The partnership allows brands and retail media networks to treat television as performance channel through native commerce ecosystem integration, expanding both advertiser access and publisher inventory reach. ... “There is an opportunity for brands and retail media networks on a tactical level to now use TV as a performance channel at scale and test it and see how it fits into their objectives,” Royle said. ... This creates broader industry expansion where publishers gain access to advertisers who never used television while enabling advertisers to reach previously inaccessible TV audiences. ... Universal Ads solves these challenges through integrated solutions delivered natively within commerce advertising environments. ... Retail media and CTV convergence leverages shopper data to improve premium video targeting accuracy, enabling commerce advertisers to apply familiar data assets to television inventory. ... Universal Ads was founded specifically to remove television friction and expand category participation through simplified access that maintains targeting precision and measurement capabilities. ... “A winning TV strategy for brands is not a one size fits all, but this partnership allows these brands to test and prove TV as a performance channel at scale,” Royle said."
