Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Fred Boothby Purchases Little River Marina - WEIS | Local & Area News, Sports, & Weather",weisradio.com (Tony Hathcock),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://weisradio.com/2026/07/31/fred-boothby-purchases-little-river-marina/,"Fred Boothby Purchases Little River Marina - WEIS | Local & Area News, Sports, & Weather ... ### Fred Boothby Purchases Little River Marina ... Little River Marina has been sold. ... Fred Boothby, CEO of Enjoy Unique Stays, was in Cedar Bluff this week to finalize a purchase of Little River Marina from Gary and Tina Gordon. Boothby and his team manage around 250 vacation rental properties. Many of these are in the tri-state area of Tennessee, Alabama, and Georgia. ... “It’s wonderful when you can find wonderful properties, but it’s really hard to find wonderful properties that are owned by great people,” said Boothby. “Our goal is to continue that legacy of investment in the property in the community, to work to make this a really special place. We don’t want to just highlight Little River Marina, but also Cedar Bluff, the surrounding areas, and all the wonderful things that are here.” ... Boothby and his team manage Paradise Point in Bryant, Alabama, and Treetop Escapes in Wildwood, Georgia. “We now have an opportunity to take it from mountains to lakes with the purchase of Little River Marina,” said Boothby. “Some of the things that we’ve found to work at Paradise Point, we plan to incorporate here. I think a nice pool is very important. We’ll look to put in the nicest pool we can afford and probably a nicer one than we can afford. We’re also looking to do some pickleball courts. We’re definitely looking to celebrate outdoor water recreation activities. We’re hoping to expand the marina and rentals and sales with that to celebrate all the wonderful water recreation and the fishing and different activities that are here…As people come in, we’ll probably bring in some more experiential stay lodging units. We could be hosting up to 1,000 plus guests a year on this end of the lake.” ... The Gordons and Boothby worked through logistics with Bill Warren, the mayor of Cedar Bluff, who was in attendance at the sale announcement. Gary and Tina weren’t necessarily looking to sell, but Boothby’s vision helped convince them. “They’re going to do so much to this property,” said Mrs. Gordon. “I think everybody here will be extremely proud of it when he gets done with it.”"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Little Island kicks off 6-week slate of performances,ny1.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/the-rush-hour/2026/07/30/little-island-kicks-off-6-week-slate-of-performances-and-culinary-events,"Little Island kicks off 6-week slate of performances ... Zack Winokur, the producing artistic director of Little Island, joined ""The Rush Hour."" (Spectrum News NY1) ... Little Island kicked off its schedule of summer programming Wednesday night. ... The public park on the Hudson River has become a performance space, theater hall and dance party venue for the next six weeks. While many of the shows are already sold out, remaining tickets are priced at $25 or free, as organizers aim to make performing arts accessible to all New Yorkers. ... Zack Winokur, the producing artistic director of Little Island, joined ""The Rush Hour"" on Thursday to talk more about the performances and culinary events."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Locarno-Bound 'In All My Journeys I Am Returning' Boarded by Lights On,variety.com (Anna Marie de la Fuente),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/tv/markets-festivals/lights-on-colombia-all-my-journeys-i-am-returning-locarno-1236823773/,"Boutique Italian sales agency Lights On has picked up international sales rights to the debut feature of Colombian Manuel Ponce de León’s “In All My Journeys I Am Returning” (“Todos mis viajes son viajes de regreso”) ahead of its world premiere at the Locarno Film Festival. ... “It’s an exceptionally bold and distinctive first feature film that we’re confident will resonate with audiences around the world,” said Flavio Armone, co-founder & managing director at Lights On, who expressed the company’s delight at returning to Locarno’s Filmmakers of the Present competition for the fifth consecutive year. ... “In All My Journeys I Am Returning” is produced by Ponce de León’s Los Niños Films with Daniela Rocha Giraldo, Ana Winograd and Héctor Ulloque producing alongside him. ... The 79th Locarno Film Festival runs over August 5-15."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Italy-Based Lights On Snags Colombia’s ‘In All My Journeys I Am Returning’ Ahead of Its Locarno Bow (EXCLUSIVE) — CitrixNews,citrixnews.cz,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://citrixnews.cz/article/italy-based-lights-on-snags-colombia-s-in-all-my-journeys-i-am-returning-ahead-of-its-locarno-bow-exclusive,"Italy-Based Lights On Snags Colombia’s ‘In All My Journeys I Am Returning’ Ahead of Its Locarno Bow (EXCLUSIVE) — CitrixNews ... # Italy-Based Lights On Snags Colombia’s ‘In All My Journeys I Am Returning’ Ahead of Its Locarno Bow (EXCLUSIVE) · July 30, 2026 at 12:37 PM Jul 30, 2026 5:37am PT Italy-Based Lights On Snags Colombia’s ‘In All My Journeys I Am Returning’ Ahead of Its Locarno Bow (EXCLUSIVE) Courtesy of Lights On Boutique Italian sales agency Lights On has picked up international sales rights to the debut feature of Colombian Manuel Ponce de León’s “In All My Journeys I Am Returning” (“Todos mis viajes son viajes de regreso”) ahead of its world premiere at the Locarno Film Festival. ... “It’s an exceptionally bold and distinctive first feature film that we’re confident will resonate with audiences around the world,” said Flavio Armone, co-founder & managing director at Lights On, who expressed the company’s delight at returning to Locarno’s Filmmakers of the Present competition for the fifth consecutive year."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Island Peži prepares to open Mankato dispensary | Local News | mankatofreepress.com,www.mankatofreepress.com (Leah Call lcall@mankato freepress.com),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mankatofreepress.com/news/local_news/island-pe-i-prepares-to-open-mankato-dispensary/article_6bddb03c-a8d4-402e-ad73-a18df76793e9.html,"Island Peži prepares to open Mankato dispensary | Local News | mankatofreepress.com ... MANKATO — A new cannabis dispensary is preparing to open in Mankato this fall, marking the Prairie Island Indian Community’s first off-reservation retail location and the latest expansion of its tribally owned cannabis enterprise. ... Island Peži is targeting an opening sometime in August or early fall, pending final regulatory approvals and completion of licensing requirements, according to the location’s general manager, Erik Arvidson. ... At 1809 Adams Street, the dispensary will offer adult-use cannabis products including flower, pre-rolls, vape cartridges, disposable vape products and edibles. Cannabis-infused beverages will be offered once it’s on the Minnesota market, and hemp-derived products, including CBD and other cannabinoid offerings, will also be available. ... The Mankato location extends the Prairie Island Indian Community’s cannabis operation beyond its flagship dispensary on the reservation near Welch. According to tribal officials, Prairie Island CBH Inc. is the ecosystem in which everything operates under, overseeing every stage of production from cultivation to distribution and retail sales — all under tribal governance. ... Every product is tracked through a “seed to sale” inventory system and the operation includes Tokáhe Distribution, which Arvidson said supplies products to over 80 dispensaries throughout Minnesota. ... Cannabis inventory is separated into secured storage areas that meet state requirements, including climate-controlled vaults for flower and refrigerated storage for concentrates. Separate hemp storage areas were incorporated into the existing building, which previously operated as the Mankato Clinic Occupational Medicine campus. Rather than constructing a new facility, Island Peži adapted the former clinic, allowing much of the existing layout to remain the same, Arvidson said. ... Surveillance, controlled access and multiple inventory verification steps are incorporated throughout the operation. According to Arvidson and tribal public relations representative Eric Pehle, those safeguards must satisfy both state standards and tribal regulations through the Prairie Island Cannabis Regulatory Commission. ... The dispensary is expected to open with about 20 employees, most hired locally from Mankato and surrounding communities. With an emphasis on customer education alongside sales, Arvidson said budtenders will be trained to explain product types and responsible use so customers leave with information. ... The tribe intends to continue expanding its retail footprint under Minnesota’s tribal-state compact which maintains off-reservation Island Peži dispensaries are subject to the same Office of Cannabis Management requirements as non-tribal retailers, though tribal dispensaries operating under compacts are not necessarily counted toward municipal caps on the number of adult-use cannabis stores. Mankato has limited adult-use cannabis retail licenses to four, the minimum allowed under state law based on population. ... “The history here is very near and dear to all Native people’s hearts in this area. So I think that this is a great place to start,” said brand ambassador and tribe member Demetria Buck on the decision to expand in Mankato. ... Buck said the expansion represents continued growth and community fostering for both the Prairie Island Indian Community and its cannabis business. She said the operation has strengthened connections within the tribal community while creating employment opportunities and increasing public awareness of Prairie Island. ... Pehle said the decision to expand into Mankato followed extensive planning and conversations with local officials before development began. According to Pehle, the tribe has prioritized deliberate growth, emphasizing intentionality, community relationships and quality control over rapid expansion."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Experience The Playmill Theatre at a new location in Island Park - AOL,www.aol.com (AOL),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.aol.com/articles/experience-playmill-theatre-location-island-150047000.html,"Experience The Playmill Theatre at a new location in Island Park - AOL ... ISLAND PARK — After many years of dreaming and planning, it has now become a reality: The Playmill has opened its state-of-the-art theater in a brand-new building for audiences. Now, the owners want you to visit and check out what they have in store. ... Roger and Heidi Merrill have been the owners of The Playmill Theatre since 2005. It started in 1964. Roger explained that they had outgrown the previous building in West Yellowstone. ... “The only alternative was to relocate, and so we determined Island Park at Mack’s Inn was in close enough proximity,” he said. ... They moved to Island Park at 4111 South Big Springs Loop Road and the new theater space just opened to the community and tourists on July 1. ... The previous theater could only seat 265. Merrill said they were constantly selling out, and people tried to buy tickets but couldn’t because of it. ... The new theater space can seat 475 people and has been successful. ... “It’s been good to move into a bigger venue. We’re still doing 13 shows, but we can seat many more people, and it’s been great,” he said. ... Not only that, but the new location will have a steakhouse, ice cream parlor, and a gift shop, all under the same roof, which is projected to open in the Fall. ... “Our new facility is actually 23,000 square feet, and it also incorporates housing. There’s a dormitory that will sleep 32 people in the basement under the stage so that we can have all of our employees there,” Merrill said. ... As for the new eatery, Steakhouse 64 will be an American-fusion restaurant featuring locally sourced ingredients. Merrill said it will focus on steaks, burgers, and home cooking. ... We are excited ... The “Ice Cream Parlour” is called Heidi Ann’s, named after Roger’s wife. It will be designed like an 1890s soda fountain and ice cream parlor with counter service. It’s “the perfect spot for a timeless treat,” the website says. It will also offer Heidi’s famous fudge. ... has made fudge for the theater for about ... 40 years. We sell it at intermission. One reason a ... the theater is ... the fudge because it has ... s all handmade by my ... Heidi,” Merrill said. ... Then, there’s the Mill Creek Mercantile. “From home decor to old-fashioned candy, children’s toys, Playmill merch, and everything in between, we’ve carefully curated our gift shop to be filled with unique finds that feel special to take home,” the website said. ... Right now for the summer season, The Playmill has three shows: Disney’s Frozen, Les Misérables, and Disney’s Newsies. ... Merrill added that they will be a year-round theater, which wasn’t what they did before. ... Coming in the fall will be The Foreigner. Then, during Christmas, it will be A Very Playmill Christmas. ... positive environmental experience ... The Playmill Theatre is in its 63rd season. Click here to check out tickets and dates. Audience members have responded positively to the new space. ... “It’s been great. It’s beautiful. It’s very aesthetically pleasing,” Merrill said. “Every show we’ve done, we’ve sold more tickets than we could have in West Yellowstone.” ... The post Experience The Playmill Theatre at a new location in Island Park appeared first on East Idaho News."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Deep Com Roots Sells Strongly 'Summer Days,' Rolls on Amor de Dios",variety.com (John Hopewell),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/film/news/isii-group-deep-com-roots-taz-skylar-belen-rueda-1236821688/,"Flexing its muscles as one of the biggest new kids on its film industry block, Spain’s ISII Group has gone into production on “Amor de Dios” headlined by “The Orphanage” star Belén Rueda and produced by ISII banner label Inefable Productions. ... The news comes as ISII Group distribution-sales house Deep Com Roots has sold “Summer Days” to half the world’s major markets and cameras have rolled on “La Cathédrale,” Inefable’s first fully English production starring “One Piece” icon Taz Skylar. ... As a mark of its step-up in scale, ISII Group now has four films in production in 2026 and another quartet released or awaiting release, including Spanish Western “Trinidad,” an ambitious Wild West-set Spanish family saga led by “Your Fault’s” Gabriela Andrada, Paz Vega and Karla Sofía Gascón. All ISII Group titles are sold and distributed in Spain by Deep Com Roots, a strategic partner. ... Headed by Maggie Civantos, star of “Locked Up,” “Money Heist” creator Alex Pina’s first international breakout, “Summer Days” has closed Latin America, bought by Brazil’s Sofa Digital, plus Germany, Austria and Switzerland (Busch Media Group) and CIS (Kinologistika). Tokyo’s Aya Pro has licensed Japan, Mumbai’s PictureWorks India, distributor of Anatomy of a Fall and Flow, has acquired rights to India, and Scene & Sound those to South Korea. ... “Deep Com Roots attended Cannes Market for the first time and was met with strong interest from the international market. Among our slate, Summer Days was one of the films that attracted the most attention from the buyers,” Emir Duzel, Deep Com Roots head of international sales, told Variety. “We believe its powerful story and the strong sense of tension made the film especially appealing. We are currently continuing negotiations for distribution deals for several more territories.” ... Inspired in its origins by an original idea by Spanish cinema great Carlos Saura, “Amor de Dios” is also produced by Inefable Productions ... Scheduled for release in 2027, “Amor de Dios” marks the awaited fiction feature debut of Paula Palacios, winner of the IDA Netflix 2022 Global Emerging Filmmaker Award and a double Goya best doc feature nominee for two stirring and affecting films, set against the context of African immigration to Europe: “Drowning Letters” (“Cartas Mojadas,” 2020) and “My Brother Ali,” (2024). ... “At ISII Group, we conceive each project not only from its creative ambition, but also the commercial career it can have inside and outside Spain,” said ISII Group President Silvia Carvalho. ... “So we have developed a structure which integrates development, financing, production, services, distribution and sales, with Deep Com Roots as the sales agent on all of our catalog,” she added. “‘Summer Days’ pre-sales and the interest generated by ‘La Cathédrale,’ ‘Amor de Dios’ and ‘Trinidad’ confirm that this model allows us to create value and market opportunities from the first stages of every film.”"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Social services nonprofit aims to diversify funding via acquisitions,mainebiz.biz (Laurie Schreiber),2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mainebiz.biz/article/social-services-nonprofit-aims-to-diversify-funding-via-acquisitions/,"# Social services nonprofit aims to diversify funding via acquisitions ... July 24, 2026 ... Waypoint Maine Inc., a nonprofit serving children and adults with intellectual disabilities and autism headquartered at 5 Dunaway Drive in Sanford, acquired the Little Dolphin School, an early childhood education provider with locations in Westbrook and Scarborough, as well as Little Dolphin Marketplace, a retail plaza in Scarborough. ... Terms of the deal were not disclosed. ... families with continuity ... The partnership expands access to Waypoint’s services while retaining Little Dolphin’s caregivers, classrooms and day-to-day operations. ... Waypoint’s broader strategy aims to strengthen long-term financial sustainability while expanding its mission impact. Integrating a mix of payers is expected to support the financial sustainability of both entities. ... As a nonprofit with significant program funding tied to Medicaid reimbursement, where rates and policy priorities can shift over time, Waypoint said it will invest in business and real estate assets that can generate diversified, unrestricted income and reduce dependence on any single funding stream. ... The strategy allows Waypoint to test new service models, explore technologies and build on its strategy to develop pioneering housing and workforce solutions, the organization said. ... Little Dolphin’s Westbrook campus is at 101 County Road. Its Scarborough campus is at 183 U.S. Route 1 and is part of the Little Dolphin Marketplace, which Waypoint also purchased. ... , Little Dolphin Marketplace is a commercial shopping plaza and is separate from the operations of the ... Dolphin School, which is one of the tenants in ... Waypoint funded the acquisition through a combination of funds, including a private loan, an investment draw and cash reserved for capital expenditures. ... The acquisition came about when Waypoint was seeking to expand its services in Greater Portland in order to provide more young children and families with access to special education services. ... Steven Brier, Little Dolphin School’s executive director, was seeking to ensure that Little Dolphin School continued to provide high-quality child care when he moved on to other ventures, a spokesperson told Mainebiz. ... Negotiations took a year. ... Waypoint has over 1,000 clients and 350 employees. Little Dolphin in Westbrook has 102 clients and 30 employees. Little Dolphin in Scarborough enrolls 80 infants and children and has 20 employees. ... The acquisition brings Waypoint’s total employee count to 400. Little Dolphin will keep its name. ... “Waypoint’s experience, resources and mission alignment will strengthen our ability to recruit and retain exceptional early childhood educators, support our staff at a new level and continue delivering the high-quality learning environment families have come to know and trust,” said Brier. ... ## Training investment ... The acquisition will not disrupt Little Dolphin’s day-to-day operations, according to a news release. It positions Waypoint to invest in staff training, strengthen program support and maximize the collective experience of both organizations. Waypoint will be able to expand children’s access to special education services in Greater Portland and support Little Dolphin staff with additional training."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"STIM Opens Canary Islands Animation Hub, Plans More Than 100 Jobs",variety.com (Emiliano de Pablos),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/film/markets-festivals/stim-canary-islands-animation-studio-tenerife-zec-1236817891/,"STIM Opens Canary Islands Animation Hub, Plans More Than 100 Jobs STIM Opens Canary Islands Animation Hub, Plans More Than 100 Jobs ... French animation and visual effects company STIM – the studio behind “The Girl in the Clouds,” which also contributed to “ The Wild Robot,” “Garfield,” and “Coyote vs. Acme,” – is opening a production center in Spain’s Canary Islands, with plans to create more than 100 jobs as it expands its European operations. ... STIM Tenerife is set to begin operating in August and expects to employ 60 people by the end of 2026. Recruitment is already underway for character modelers, set and prop modelers, look-development artists and supervisors, among other high-skilled positions. ... The company has chosen to establish the operation within the Canary Islands Special Zone, or ZEC, a low-tax regime for qualifying companies operating in the Spanish archipelago. ... “The opening of STIM Tenerife in the Canary Islands marks a strategic stage in STIM’s evolution,” said STIM Tenerife CEO Amélie Houpline. “We have found an environment here that brings together talent, strong development potential and a dynamic creative community.” ... The new base, she added, will allow STIM to increase its production capacity “without compromising the artistic and technical excellence that defines our identity.” ... Founded by Félix Ferrand, Jordan Soler and Benoit Gielly, STIM specializes in 3D animation, VFX and digital production for film, TV and advertising. With operations in France and Belgium, it has evolved from a character-focused studio into a company capable of handling projects from design and pre-production through to final delivery. ... The Tenerife operation will expand the company’s production capacity while supporting financing structures spanning France, Belgium and the Canary Islands. STIM said that footprint could give producers additional options for assembling European animation and VFX financing. ... “Our ambition is not limited to producing international projects from the islands,” Houpline said. “We want to build a studio with a long-term future, generate highly qualified employment and contribute to the development of the Canary Islands ecosystem.” ... STIM’s arrival comes as the archipelago continues to build its animation, VFX and digital-arts sector. According to figures provided by the ZEC, the Canary Islands now host more than 30 specialist companies and close to 2,000 professionals, up from a comparatively small industry less than a decade ago. ... Companies operating in the islands include Fortiche, the studio behind “Arcane,” as well as Atlantis Animation, 3 Doubles Producciones, Tomavision, Gigglebug, Amuse Studios and Ánima Kitchent. ... Recent expansion has also included Surfing Giant Studios’ Tenerife operation and DNEG’s investment in Ánima Kitchent, backed by the Spanish government’s SETT, as part of a broader effort to scale the sector. ... “A few years ago, there was practically no animation industry in the Canary Islands,” said ZEC President Pablo Hernández. “Today, we have dozens of studios, close to 2,000 professionals and projects for some of the world’s largest entertainment companies.” ... STIM’s arrival, he added, shows that the archipelago “has ceased to be a promise and has become an established reality within the international animation industry.” ... Hernández said the significance of the latest investments goes beyond attracting individual companies or productions. ... “We are seeing the creation of a genuine industrial ecosystem, with local talent, specialist training and companies capable of leading global productions,” he said. “We have moved from attracting specific projects to attracting permanent centers for decision-making, production and creative development.” ... The next phase, according to Hernández, will involve strengthening local intellectual property, developing original content and attracting larger-scale international investment. ... Industry projections suggest the Canary Islands could reach between 3,000 and 4,000 specialized animation and digital-arts jobs over the coming years."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Fresh Films shines light on QC’s movie future,quadcitiesbusiness.com (Jennifer DeWitt),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://quadcitiesbusiness.com/fresh-films-shines-light-on-qcs-movie-future/,"For the past several weeks, a small cast and a Fresh Films’ production crew from near and far have been busy filming a new ghostly streaming series known as “Dearly Departed.” On location at First Lutheran Church and its pastor’s house and surrounding grounds, located atop Rock Island’s 20th Street hill, Fresh Films is in full production mode. The stately church house with architecture of yesteryear and other Quad Cities sites are serving as backdrops in the filming of the six-episode “Dearly Departed.” A co-production between Fresh Films and Rock Media, it is planned for release later this year on the YouTube channel Rock Squad. CREDIT JENNIFER DEWITT ... In some ways, the work Fresh Films is performing in Rock Island this summer may be a prequel to what many believe will become a thriving Quad Cities industry – the production of film, television and other media."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Alon Shtruzman & Scott Einbinder Debut Vertical Video Studio New Short,deadline.com (Jesse Whittock),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://deadline.com/2026/07/new-short-media-vertical-video-studio-1237000005/,"Shtruzman & Scott Einbinder ... Vertical Video Studio New ... 5X Media‘s Alon Shtruzman and Scott Einbinder are getting into the microdrama game. ... The veteran producers have tapped a “consortium of investors” to launch New Short Media, which they claim will bring “bring brand-name content creators, actors and creative talent to vertical storytelling with premium, innovative micro-series.” ... The microdrama biz will sit alongside 5X, but operate separately to the existing company. ... New Short is latest vertical video player on the market, with the likes of RoseBerry Media’s Epis, Jason Strickman and Kumbáli Satori’s HighFive and Kelly Luegenbiehl, Jon Koa and Onur Güvenatam’s Shorties Studios among others that have launched in the past year as the microdrama trend keeps a tight grip of online audiences and industry execs. ... Among the first three projects coming out of New Short are Speeding Towards You, which is billed as “a Mr. and Mrs. Smith-style action romance thriller about two competing car thieves who find themselves in the middle of a covert operation to take down one of the top crime syndicates.” The Offer and Long Bright River writer Russell Rothberg is attached to pen the series. ... The 5X bosses say the shift that’s seen vertical videos move away from editorial strategies almost entirely based around “serialized romance and melodrama” is attracting more Hollywood producers, studios and investors. ... Shtruzman, who was the founding CEO of Keshet International and producer of shows such as La Brea and Our Boys, said there is a “blue sky” opportunity for producers to craft niches in the emerging space. ... “Social media distribution and creator-led marketing are one of the most significant shifts in filmed entertainment since the emergence of streaming,” he said. “By combining that with mobile-first premium storytelling, New Short Media is aimed at reaching new and larger audiences. We believe the next generation of Hollywood franchises won’t necessarily begin on television or in theaters but on the phone. ... “Vertical storytelling is evolving incredibly fast, but much of the market still revolves around the same types of romance stories. We see an opportunity to bring broader genres, premium production values and recognizable talent into the space while harnessing the enormous reach of today’s creator economy.” ... Einbinder added: “Hollywood is discovering that vertical isn’t simply another distribution format – it’s becoming an entirely new storytelling medium. With New Short Studios combining experienced filmmakers with creators who already command enthusiastic global audiences, we’re creating projects designed to break through culturally, commercially and move beyond posts and clips into character-driven worlds that can live across multiple formats.” ... New Short isn’t planning on launching its own distribution platform and will instead develop IP for platforms that can be developed into longer-form TV, feature films, games and consumer products. ... Einbinder, the former co-CEO of Cristal Pictures, launched 5X in 2023 as a management and production business, with Shtruzman and Gil Goldschein joining as partners a year later and became co-CEOs. Einbinder is now Executive Chairman. Goldschein exited last year to pursue his own projects, a spokesman said today. ... New Short isn’t the only Hollywood-led microdrama house launching today. As we revealed a few moments ago, veteran producers Jeffrey Schenck, Barry Barnholtz and Peter Sullivan have teamed up to launch VertTV."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,LI drugmaker Country Life acquires competitor Aura Cachia,www.longislandpress.com (James Bernstein),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.longislandpress.com/2026/07/22/country-lifie-drugmaker-aura/,"LI drugmaker Country Life acquires competitor Aura Cachia ... Hauppauge-based Country Life LLC bought Aura Cachia. ... Long Island’s rapidly expanding pharmaceutical-nutraceutical industry has grown larger with Hauppauge-based Country Life LLC, one of the oldest of the companies, recently acquiring a Midwestern competitor. ... So, a number of local economy-watchers took note in early July when Country Life, a company founded in 1971, announced that it had acquired Aura Cachia from Frontier Distribution LLC, described as a member-owned cooperative, based in Norway, Iowa, and established in 1976. ... Country Life is privately held, and no terms of the deal were announced. The company has about 150 employees. Once the acquisition is completed, Country Life’s sales will be over $100 million. The company declined to state what sales are currently. ... Growth in the pharma and neutral industry has been rapid. Suffolk economic development officials say the industry employs about 10,000 people — a 64% jump since 2004. The officials said in a report that the sector in Suffolk employs more people than any other county in New York State. Salaries in key executive or technical positions can pay over $100,000 annually, state officials say. ... much fanfare or ... role it plays ... “Without a concerted effort or strategic planning to foster its growth, and absent a Grumman-like behemoth to drive the sector, pharma-neutra has nonetheless grown into a critical component of Long Island’s economy,” the county report said. ... Stacey Sikes, acting president and CEO of the Long Island Association, the Island’s largest business and civic organization, told the Press the acquisition was a positive for the region. ... this industry, ... ikes said. ... State economic development officials say Country Life is “a significant regional manufacturer in the industry.” ... Country Life describes itself as a “holistic wellness company” that makes health supplements and personal care products. The company said that the acquisition will expand its portfolio. Frontier Co-Op’s products include culinary herbs, spices, oils and aroma therapies. ... “Aura Cacia is a strong fit within the Country Life family,” Rob Robillard, CEO of Country Life, said in a statement. “Together, we bring more than a century of combined experience helping consumers live healthier, more balanced lives.” ... said, “We believe this decision allows both organizations to focus, scale and thrive.” ... Country Life said that effective immediately, Aura Cacia will operate as a brand within Country Life’s portfolio. Country Life said that the organization will “maintain manufacturing operations” in Urbana, Iowa, and corporate headquarters in Hauppauge. ... A company spokesman said no jobs will be eliminated as a result of the acquisition. ... Tom Mariner, executive director of LIBO, an organization that supports the biotechnology industry on Long Island, said the pharmaceutical and nutraceutical business has been expanding here because of available space for warehouses and the available pool of talent from the State University at Stony Brook and support from other institutions, such as Cold Spring Harbor Lab and the Feinstein Institute, the research arm of Northwell Health. ... “New York City is trying to invest” in pharma and neutral, “but the costs of property there are prohibitive,” Mariner said. ... “It depends on what we do,” Mariner said. “It depends on how much we want to invest, and it depends on what we want Long Island to look like.”"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Little Dot Studios unveils HyperLaunch to supercharge YouTube revenue and scale channel growth - SportsPro,www.sportspro.com (SportsPro),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sportspro.com/announcements/little-dot-studios-unveils-hyperlaunch-to-supercharge-youtube-revenue-and-scale-channel-growth/,"Little Dot Studios unveils HyperLaunch to supercharge YouTube revenue and scale channel growth - SportsPro ... # Little Dot Studios unveils HyperLaunch to supercharge YouTube revenue and scale channel growth ... ##### The new tool marks the formal introduction of ‘Little Dot OS’ (Optimisation Sidekicks), the company's proprietary technology suite designed to maximise returns. 21 July 2026 SportsPro Little Dot Studios, the social media agency, digital media network and multi-platform production company, today unveils HyperLaunch, the latest addition to the Little Dot OS (Optimisation Sidekicks), its growing suite of proprietary optimisation technologies. HyperLaunch helps broadcasters, distributors, sports rights holders, brands and content owners rapidly scale their YouTube output, significantly increasing revenue while maintaining premium channel management standards. ... Developed entirely in-house, Little Dot OS leverages over 13 years of expertise managing 1,000+ YouTube channels for more than 600 global partners. Over the past decade, the company has delivered more than half a billion US dollars in revenue for its partners. With HyperLaunch, partners now stand to, on average, triple their historical returns by efficiently monetising vast content archives that were previously too complex or costly to exploit. ... Already deployed across Little Dot Studios’ owned-and-operated network of 135+ channels, HyperLaunch has distributed more than 21,500 hours of content to YouTube in 2026 alone. The platform uses operational AI and automated workflows to ingest, analyse and distribute large volumes of video content, drastically reducing prep time while integrating complex rights management and maintaining human oversight throughout. By increasing upload speeds by 90%, HyperLaunch solves one of the biggest commercial challenges facing media companies today: how to rapidly turn deep video archives into highly profitable digital inventory. ... Dan Jones, CEO, Little Dot Studios, said: “For many partners, the challenge isn’t a lack of content, it’s the complexity and speed required to effectively monetise archives across YouTube. HyperLaunch dramatically reduces time to market, allowing partners to average tripling what they used to make by unlocking long-term value from their IP that simply wasn’t commercially viable before. By automating the heavy operational lifting, we increase inventory and returns faster, while freeing up our teams to focus on the human side of audience growth – building communities and driving fandoms.” ... The launch comes as YouTube becomes the fastest-growing platform in the media and marketing mix, with content owners increasingly prioritising direct audience relationships and long-term IP monetisation. Little Dot OS fills a critical market gap, combining high-yield commercial technology with the proven expertise of one of the world’s largest YouTube specialists. The broader toolkit includes EchoScope, for advanced audience intelligence; ReLaunch, which maximises value from existing content libraries; and Seismo (formerly ChIP), for ongoing performance analysis and optimisation. Together with HyperLaunch, these tools enable Little Dot Studios (part of media and entertainment group, Banijay Entertainment) to deliver smarter strategies, faster execution and significantly stronger financial outcomes for its partners. ... Little Dot Studios is a social media agency, digital media network and multi-platform production company. As the world’s leading YouTube specialist, it partners with top entertainment, sports and consumer brands to deliver strategy, audience growth, content production, monetisation and digital rights management. ... Its multi-format production studio creates everything from premium TV and film to award-winning podcasts, live streams, and short-form social content that build communities and drive performance. Through its owned network, Little Dot Channels, the company operates 135+ social channels and seven FAST brands streaming across 130+ channels, reaching over 125 million unique viewers monthly and offering one of the largest premium ad inventories across YouTube and CTV. ... Little Dot Studios also includes specialist sports and branded content agency WING and owns broadcaster Dan Snow’s History Hit network. A certified B Corp™ and Carbon Negative, growing on being verified carbon neutral since launch, it is committed to reaching Net Zero by 2030. Founded in 2013, Little Dot Studios has offices in the UK, US, Germany and ANZ, and is part of media and entertainment group, Banijay Entertainment."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Sister, Producer Of 'Black Doves' Turns Profit For First Time",deadline.com (Max Goldbart),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://deadline.com/2026/07/sister-turns-profit-first-time-black-doves-liz-murdoch-1236998333/,"EXCLUSIVE: Sister Group is entering its “next phase” after turning a profit for the first time in six years. ... Chris Fry, CFO at the Black Doves and The Woman in Cabin 10 producer, told Deadline Sister “refocused on our strengths” in 2025 after shutting down its U.S. hub, and is now looking to the future. The “next phase” will be driven by “delivering best-in-class storytelling from a UK base to a global audience” while potential acquisitions in the vein of docs indie Dorothy Street and digital-first label After Party Studios could be incoming, he added. ... Deadline has seen Sister Group’s financial filing for 2025 and it showed adjusted EBITDA in the black for the first time since the group launched in 2019, rising by around £7M ($9.4M) to £3.8M. Overall profit for the year was £3.3M. Net assets rose sharply to £12.4M. ... Launched in 2019 by Jane Featherstone and Liz Murdoch, Sister Group incorporates the likes of drama indie Sister Pictures, which launched in 2015, New York-based independent publisher Zando, Richard Bacon’s Yes Yes Media and live music venue Koko. Its constituent parts including Sister Pictures have turned a profit in the past but this year is the first time the overall Sister Group hasn’t been in the red. ... Revenue in 2025 did slip, however, by 22% to £56.6M, which the filing said “reflects smaller budgets on the productions completed in 2025, with a larger proportion being sold to public sector broadcasters versus the prior year.” ... Sister has made numerous shows and movies for streamers down the years including the likes of Black Doves and Eric for Netflix, but last year saw well-regarded series for public broadcasters like the BBC’s Waiting for the Out and ITV’s Coldwater starring Andrew Lincoln. These lower-budget shows generate less revenue upfront but Sister holds the IP, which is beneficial further down the road. Revenue in the TV division dipped, according to the filing, while it rose in movies, mainly due to Netflix’s hit The Woman in Cabin 10. Big streamer projects are to come in the shape of Black Doves Season 2 and Apple TV’s Prodigies starring Will Sharpe and Ayo Edebiri. ... Sister’s “next phase” is seeing the rapid continuation of the closure of the U.S. office, which was run by ex-Netflix TV boss Cynthia Holland but shuttered in late 2024 after a review amid tough market conditions. Holland and fellow high-profile execs like Jane Wiseman and Efrain Miron exited. Sister Group’s results revealed that the U.S. wind-down is now “substantially complete” and will be fully done by 2027, with a loss of just £2.5M taken last year compared to £34.5M the prior one. Sister executives have always stressed they will continue to seek work from American buyers and have a footprint there in the shape of Zando and podcast maker Campside Media. ... “We’ve refocused on our strengths – delivering best-in-class storytelling from a UK base to a global audience – and it’s great to see this strategy validated by the numbers,” said Fry. ... The results indicated a number of potential bumps in the road going forwards including “the costs of production having risen to a point whereby UK public sector broadcasters… are funding smaller proportions of budgets” and the “continued shift in consumer viewing habits towards content on social platforms.” “Rapid advancement of AI capabilities combined with uncertainty around audience appetite, legal and ethical guardrails” was also cited. ... Many of Sister’s scripted rivals are now part of the enormous combined Banijay-All3Media operation but there is no suggestion the group is looking for a buyer or to become part of a larger group."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,What Merging Two Completion Bond Guarantors Means for Indie Films,www.indiewire.com (Brian Welk),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.indiewire.com/news/business/what-merging-completion-bond-guarandots-means-indie-films-1235206476/,"Leading completion bond guarantors Film Finances and Media Guarantors are combining under the STX Entertainment family of companies. By Brian Welk ... Completion bonds are a little-discussed but essential part of the independent film financing process, the insurance by which indie films ensure that a film will be completed on time and on budget. You don’t really hear about them unless you need it. Today, though, two of the largest guarantors of such completion bonds are merging in a move that could have a big impact on the indie film space. ... Film Finances International (FFI), the parent company of completion bond provider Film Finances, is acquiring Media Guarantors Insurance Solutions (MGIS) to create a completion guarantor giant. The combined company is part of STX Entertainment and the Film Services International family of companies, and the merger helps Film Services become not just a studio but also a service provider. It can add an insurance component to complement its indie flywheel — which already includes financing, physical production, and post-production. The combination is being presented as a one-stop shop for the indie film market, something that can give studio-quality support and risk assurance across multiple territories, including the U.S., UK, Australia, Canada, and Europe, while also speeding up the investment in data-driven risk assessment tools, which can make it quicker for indie producers to obtain a bond and give financiers more certainty earlier. ... Fred Milstein, president and CEO of Media Guarantors, will now serve as CEO of the combined bond company. Steve Berman will become president, and Greg Trattner will assume the role of executive chairman, all under group CEO Coleman. Film Finances has been around for decades and has a large history of experience and knowledge, while Media Guarantors has become very hands-on with filmmakers and entrepreneurial, and the idea is that those two strengths will complement each other moving forward. ... The concern is what taking a guarantor out of the space means for indies who might now have to work with just a single company to get their film bonded. We know how consolidation has impacted and threatens to impact the rest of the industry. But in this case, the bond market is still a very niche space. A majority of films don’t bond if they can avoid it. And the broader challenges facing the indie film market mean that some smaller mom-and-pop vendors are struggling, and there isn’t necessarily a single entity with the breadth of knowledge to help indie producers across the board. ... A merger like this creates a healthier vendor that can be a full-service company. Film Services sees this as an opportunity to attract indie projects even if they don’t need a bond, namely because guarantors have the skills necessary to look at scripts and schedules and help identify anything that can go wrong. Through its post-production arms, Pivotal Post and SilverTrak, Film Services can also help at the finishing stage. It’s one of the leading renters of Avid tools, and STX is the studio-facing side of the operation, now building out a new slate from the old STX library. Case in point: the Katie Holmes-directed “Happy Hours,” which premiered at this year’s Tribeca Film Festival, was one film for which Film Services used all its resources to finance, bond, produce, and support post-production. The film is now working through distribution. Film Services believes that would not have been possible without the combined resources of the entire set of brands and services, and other indies will now have an avenue to do the same. ... Deadline first reported the news of the merger."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Kidscreen » Archive » AI prodco Utopai positions itself as an option for producers without buyers,kidscreen.com (Ryan Tuchow),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://kidscreen.com/2026/07/21/ai-prodco-utopai-positions-itself-as-an-option-for-producers-without-buyers/,"Kidscreen » Archive » AI prodco Utopai positions itself as an option for producers without buyers # AI prodco Utopai positions itself as an option for producers without buyers ... ##### The Most Serious Fart film is Utopai’s second kids deal in as many months, but going the AI route may pose its own challenges. By Ryan Tuchow ... July 21, 2026"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Little Island Books has acquired the picture book You Belong to You by Irish author Deirdre Sullivan. 👇 | The Bookseller,www.linkedin.com (The Bookseller),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/the-bookseller-magazine_little-island-to-publish-deirde-sullivan-activity-7483863830943485953-4nXW,# Little Island Books has acquired the picture book You Belong to You by Irish author Deirdre Sullivan. 👇 | The Bookseller · LinkedIn · 2026-07-17 ... [Little Island Books](https://linkedin.com/company/little-island-books) has acquired the picture book You Belong to You by Irish author Deirdre Sullivan. 👇
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"New Business Bulletin: Little Dot Studios, beehiiv, VIOOH and more - New Digital Age",newdigitalage.co (Michael Feeley),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://newdigitalage.co/brands/new-business-bulletin-little-dot-studios-beehiiv-viooh-and-more/,"#### Little Dot Studios launches YouTube optimisation tool ... Little Dot Studios has introduced HyperLaunch, a new addition to its proprietary technology suite designed to automate the ingestion, analysis and distribution of video content to YouTube. ... The tool is intended to help broadcasters, rights holders, brands and other content owners publish larger volumes of archive content more efficiently while managing rights workflows and maintaining human oversight. It has already been deployed across the company’s owned YouTube channel network. ... HyperLaunch forms part of the company’s wider Little Dot OS platform, alongside existing optimisation and analytics tools. Little Dot Studios is part of Banijay Entertainment."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Spain's SETT Invests $7.3 Million in Amuse Labs,variety.com (Emiliano de Pablos),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/global/markets-festivals/sett-invests-amuse-labs-canary-islands-animation-1236812550/,"Spain's SETT Invests $7.3 Million in Amuse Labs Spain’s SETT Invests $7.3 Million in Amuse Labs ... Spain’s government is investing €6.4 million ($7.3 million) in newly established Canary Islands animation company Amuse Labs, accelerating the archipelago’s push to become a global base for children’s IP. ... The deal, structured through state-backed technology investment vehicle SETT, brings together $15.1 million in public and private capital. SETT will hold a 48% stake, while Amuse Studios will become Amuse Labs’ second-largest shareholder. ... The operation is expected to underpin animation projects valued at up to $22.9 million, giving Amuse Labs the financial muscle to expand internationally and operate across the full production and commercial chain. ... Based in Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, Amuse Labs is a digital animation studio and production company focused on creating, producing and internationally exploiting children’s content for broadcasters and digital platforms. ... Central to its business model is ownership of the intellectual property behind its productions, rather than operating solely as a service provider. Amuse Labs will oversee projects from writing, production and technological development through distribution, licensing and merchandising. ... Its expansion plan targets North America, Asia, the European Union and the U.K. Potential clients and partners extend beyond broadcasters and streamers to toy manufacturers and publishing groups, reflecting its ambition to build franchises across multiple revenue streams. ... The company also plans to deploy new technology across its 2D animation and CGI pipelines, localization and production management, including AI tools designed to streamline specific processes. ... The operation is expected to create 40 direct jobs and around 150 indirect positions across animation, post-production, sound, translation, distribution, licensing, merchandising and legal services. ... “Spain is strengthening its leadership in audiovisual production, with the Canary Islands as a strategic engine,” Ángel Víctor Torres, Spain’s minister for territorial policy and democratic memory, said in a statement. ... SETT, which sits under Spain’s Ministry for Digital Transformation and Public Administration, invests public capital alongside private partners in strategic, technology-driven industries. The deal forms part of the second phase of the Spain Audiovisual Hub plan, a government initiative aimed at strengthening the country’s film, TV and digital-content sectors while attracting international production and investment. ... The Amuse Labs deal brings Spanish government commitments to the Canary Islands’ audiovisual sector to nearly $46 million over the past two months. ... It follows SETT’s $28.8 million backing of Las Palmas-based animation studio Anima Kitchent alongside global animation and VFX group DNEG, as well as its participation with South Africa’s Known Associates Group in an audiovisual venture encompassing post-production and digital arts operations in the islands. ... Amuse Labs joins a growing cluster of audiovisual companies operating under the Canary Islands Special Zone (ZEC), the archipelago’s investment-oriented low-tax regime."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Realscreen » Archive » Pixie teams with Silverlining Rights on luxury hotel series for ITV,realscreen.com (Nicholas Sokic),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://realscreen.com/2026/07/16/pixie-teams-with-silverlining-rights-on-luxury-hotel-series-for-itv/,"Realscreen » Archive » Pixie teams with Silverlining Rights on luxury hotel series for ITV ... ##### Cardiff-based indie Pixie Productions has teamed with Bristol-based independent production finance broker and distributor Silverlining Rights on the 6 x 30-minute ITV series Inside the Langham: Britain’s First Grand Hotel. Silverlining ... ... July 16, 2026 ... Cardiff-based indie Pixie Productions has teamed with Bristol-based independent production finance broker and distributor Silverlining Rights on the 6 x 30-minute ITV series Inside the Langham: Britain’s First Grand Hotel. Silverlining ..."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"INFLUENCER REALITY SERIES 'BIKINI ISLAND' SETS SAIL ACROSS YOUTUBE, FANVUE, SOCIALS, AND SWIMWEAR",www.prnewswire.com (Bikini Island LLC),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/influencer-reality-series-bikini-island-sets-sail-across-youtube-fanvue-socials-and-swimwear-302826753.html,"LOS ANGELES, July 16, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Bikini Island, the new fun and flirty creator-reality series and apparel brand will premiere on YouTube July 24th, as a weekly series, bringing together eleven of social media's most recognizable personalities for a six-month adventure that combines a traveling content house, competition, flirty-fashion, and entrepreneurship. Alongside the premiere of Bikini Island, each cast member will launch their own exclusive content page on Fanvue, taking fans beyond the weekly episodes with sneak peeks and behind-the-scenes access. ... Created by Cali10 Management in partnership with Fanvue, the series follows the cast with a collective reach exceeding 100 million followers as they travel across six iconic destinations. Filming kicked off at Miami Swim Week and the cast will continue to travel through Los Angeles, Las Vegas, Hawaii, Mexico and more over the next six months while creating their original swimwear brands from concept to launch. ... Unlike traditional reality television, the swim brands developed during the series won't remain on-screen. Each creator will launch her own collection during the release of Season One, ... fans to purchase the very designs they watched develop throughout the series. ... ""Bikini Island represents everything we believe the future of the creator economy can be,"" said Gabriel Gornell, Co-Founder of Cali10. ""At its core, Bikini Island is a fun, flirty, and completely unpredictable ride. But beneath the escapism, these creators aren't just entertainers—they're entrepreneurs building real businesses in real time. Fans won't just watch from their sofas—they'll step directly into the experience through weekly episodes, the creators' social channels, exclusive content on Fanvue, live appearances at events like Miami Swim Week, and ultimately through the swimwear brands themselves. It's a fully integrated ecosystem that blurs the line between content, community, commerce, and culture. That's something traditional television simply can't do."" ... The series introduces a first-of-its-kind distribution model that combines premium long-form entertainment with socials, direct-to-fan engagement, exclusive content, creator-owned digital storefronts, and IRL experiences. ... Bikini Island is a creator-driven reality series following eleven social media influencers as they travel to six iconic destinations over six months while creating content, building businesses, and launching their own swimwear brands. Combining documentary storytelling, competition, travel, fashion, and entrepreneurship, the series offers a first-of-its-kind look at the future of creator-led entertainment and commerce. ... CALI 10 Management is a talent management, brand development, and media company founded by entertainment executive Gabriel Gornell and attorney Kenneth Ingber. Focused on the rapidly evolving creator economy, Cali10 represents influencers, digital talent, and emerging personalities while developing innovative opportunities across content production, brand partnerships, merchandising, licensing, live events, and direct-to-consumer commerce. The company is built on the belief that today's creators are not only entertainers but entrepreneurs capable of building enduring brands and businesses. Through projects such as Bikini Island, Cali10 is pioneering new models that combine entertainment, commerce, and fan engagement, helping creators transform their influence into scalable enterprises."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Little Bird Signs Production Company Sorry, Ain’t Sorry | LBBOnline",lbbonline.com,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://lbbonline.com/news/Little-Bird-Production-Company-Sorry-Aint-Sorry,"Little Bird Signs Production Company Sorry, Ain’t Sorry | LBBOnline ... # Little Bird Signs Production Company Sorry, Ain’t Sorry ... 14/07/2026 ... Led by founders Thomas Arnell, Joey Szela, James 'JMP' Pereira, and Andrew Percival, Sorry, Ain't Sorry offers end-to-end production services spanning creative development through post-production ... ​ Little Bird has expanded its live-action production roster with the addition of Sorry, Ain't Sorry, a full-service production, creative studio collective, and production services company formed through the merger of award-winning studios 4Bi9 Media and Paperwork Studio. ... Led by founders Thomas Arnell, Joey Szela, James 'JMP' Pereira, and Andrew Percival, Sorry, Ain't Sorry offers end-to-end production services spanning creative development through post-production, along with a fully operational cinema equipment rental house. ... With teams in New York, Miami, Los Angeles, Salt Lake City, and Wyoming, the collective produces commercials, documentaries, music videos, feature films, television, live events, streaming, and social campaigns. ... ""We've always believed the best work comes from bringing the right people together and removing the barriers between creative and execution.” says founding partner Thomas Arnell. “Sorry, Ain't Sorry was built to be a true creative partner - from development through delivery - and joining Little Bird gives us the opportunity to do that on an even larger scale. Their approach is collaborative, forward-thinking, and aligned with how we want to build the future of production."" ... The team has collaborated with globally recognised brands. Select works include Apple, Nike, Lexus, Land Rover, Toyota, Vans, Reebok, Beats by Dre, the NBA, Coach, The North Face, PepsiCo, The Coca-Cola Company, Bose, and New Era, while creating work for artists such as Kanye West, Alicia Keys, Playboi Carti, XXXTENTACION, Lil Wayne, Becky G, Teddy Swims, and Shaboozey. Collectively, they work with some of the largest film, television and streaming services and studios alike on various projects and formats such as The Walt Disney Company, Netflix and Paramount Skydance Corporation, just to name a few. ... “We’ve never really had the full gambit of production, plus production services, plus equipment rental resources on our roster before that spans from short form, long form, music videos and beyond - it’s really exciting to work with such a nimble team who brings all of that together for us to offer our clients! I’m a firm believer in trying to do things out of the box, never really having been into all the ‘traditional’ norms of repping. We’re in a time of hyper-growth-and-change, so Little Bird is embracing that.” reflects Becca on her decision to bring the team onto the roster. ... The signing further strengthens Little Bird's live-action and production capabilities, adding a versatile and experienced team overflowing with cinematic storytelling, ambitious productions, and a seamless creative-to-delivery workflow. ... Production Company, ARIS Signs with Little Bird for East Coast Representation ... Little Bird Signs VFX and Post Production Company BRASH ... 07/04/2026"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Little Dot Studios Launches Tool To Boost YouTube Partner Revenue,www.netinfluencer.com (Dragomir Stojkov),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.netinfluencer.com/little-dot-studios-launches-tool-to-boost-youtube-partner-revenue/,"# Little Dot Studios Launches Tool to Boost YouTube Partner Revenue ... Published on July 14, 2026 ... [Little Dot Studios](https://www.netinfluencer.com/social-media-agency-little-dot-studios-launches-chip-intelligence-platform-for-youtube-channel-management/) has unveiled **HyperLaunch**, a new addition to its Little Dot OS suite of proprietary technologies, designed to help broadcasters, distributors, sports rights holders, brands and content owners scale YouTube output and monetize video archives more efficiently. ... According to a [blog post](https://blog.littledotstudios.com/en-gb/news-views/little-dot-studios-unveils-hyperlaunch-to-supercharge-youtube-revenue-and-scale-channel-growth), the tool allows partners to average tripling their historical returns by turning large content archives that were previously too complex or costly to exploit into monetizable YouTube inventory. HyperLaunch increases upload speeds by 90% and has already distributed more than 21,500 hours of content to YouTube in 2026 across Little Dot Studios’ owned-and-operated network of 135-plus channels. ... uses operational AI and automated workflows to ingest, analyze and distribute video content at volume, integrating rights management while maintaining human oversight throughout the process. ... “For many partners, the challenge isn’t a lack of content, it’s the complexity and speed required to effectively monetize archives across YouTube,” said Dan Jones, CEO of Little Dot Studios. “HyperLaunch dramatically reduces time to market, allowing partners to average tripling what they used to make by unlocking long-term value from their IP that simply wasn’t commercially viable before. By automating the heavy operational lifting, we increase inventory and returns faster, while freeing up our teams to focus on the human side of audience growth – building communities and driving fandoms.” ... HyperLaunch is built on more than 13 years of experience managing over 1,000 YouTube channels for more than 600 global partners, work that the company says has generated over half a billion dollars in partner revenue to date. ... The launch formalizes Little Dot OS (Optimisation Sidekicks) as a named suite of tools rather than a single system. Alongside HyperLaunch, the toolkit includes **EchoScope** for audience intelligence, **ReLaunch** for extracting value from existing content libraries, and **Seismo**, an analytics tool for ongoing performance optimization that was previously known as ChIP. ... Little Dot Studios introduced ChIP in November 2025 as an internal analytics platform built to support more than 800 client channels generating 6.5 billion organic views monthly. The system consolidated data across seven core tools, including channel diagnostics, content benchmarking, and automated demonetization alerts, and the company positioned it at the time as proprietary technology kept internal rather than sold commercially. Wayne Davison, Little Dot Studios’ Chief Revenue Officer, said at the platform’s debut that it was “built by YouTube experts for YouTube experts.” HyperLaunch’s unveiling brings that tool under the newly formalized Little Dot OS name as Seismo. ... Little Dot Studios, part of Banijay Entertainment, frames the expanded suite as addressing a shift in the market as content owners prioritize direct audience relationships and long-term IP monetization on YouTube, which the company describes as the fastest-growing platform in the media and marketing mix."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Former Pineapple Street Studios Pair Launch New Podcast Company,deadline.com (Peter White),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://deadline.com/2026/07/please-and-thanks-productions-podcast-amy-poehler-1236976438/,"Former Pineapple Street Studios Pair Launch New Podcast Company ... EXCLUSIVE: Pineapple Street Studios was one of the premier podcast production companies making narrative series such as Wind of Change, Missing Richard Simmons and The Clearing. ... A year after the company’s owner Audacy filed for bankruptcy, it shut down the studio. ... Two of the company’s top executives have now started their own podcast studio and have started working with some of the figures that helped drive the narrative podcast boom from a few years ago. ... Joel Lovell, who was Executive Editor at Pineapple Street, and Henry Molofsky, an Executive Producer, who were both at the company from its launch in 2016 through to its end, have launched Please and Thanks Productions. ... Please and Thanks is now launching its debut project, a series with Amazon’s Audible Originals from Dan Taberski, who was also responsible for series including Running From Cops, Surviving Y2K, The Line, 9/12 and Hysterical. ... It has also partnered with Amy Poehler‘s Paper Kite Productions, which is behind the Parks and Recreation star’s Good Hang, and Patrick Radden Keefe, the man behind Scorpions-infused CIA story Wind of Change, on new projects. ... Its project with Poehler’s Paper Kite is the company’s foray into documentary audio and has also just been sold to Universal Studio Group Audio. The investigative audio series is expected to launch in 2027 and is produced in association with Long Run. ... Paper Kite’s audio division is now headed up by Jenna Weiss-Berman, who co-founded Pineapple Street, and worked closely with Lovell and Molofsky. ... The project with Radden Keefe, author of recent hit book London Falling, is an audio-documentary podcast in the music space using his investigative reporting. ... “At a time when fewer companies are making narrative documentary podcasts, Please & Thanks is built on the belief that the appetite for great audio storytelling never went away, even as business models have changed. If you tell good stories and produce them at the highest level, audiences will give you their time and attention, and that’s worthwhile culturally and as a business,” Lovell and Molofsky said."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"PROTON 4K 3D WinsNAB 2026 Best of Show – VILLAGE island Co.,Ltd",village-island.com,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://village-island.com/en/proton-4k3d-win-nab-2026-best-of-show/,"PROTON 4K 3D WinsNAB 2026 Best of Show – VILLAGE island Co.,Ltd ... 3D ... 2026 ... PROTON 4K 3D Wins NAB 2026 Best of Show — Village Island ... NAB 2026 Best of Show Award WinnerSelected among the many products exhibited at NAB for its innovative stereoscopic 3D camera system. ... The PROTON 4K 3D, the latest model from PROTON Camera Innovations distributed by Village Island in Japan, has won Best of Show at NAB Show 2026, one of the largest trade events in the broadcast and ProAV industry. The award recognizes it as an innovative stereoscopic 4K camera system among a large field of exhibited products. ... is designed for immersive content production requiring precise ... oscopic capture. Built on the proven ... FLEX architecture, it combines two perfectly synchronized cameras into a ... 3D imagery. ... With frame-accurate synchronization, unified control through a shared CCU, and a compact design that allows optimal interocular positioning, the PROTON 4 ... 3D delivers natural depth perception alongside seamless integration into professional 3D workflows — opening up new creative possibilities for cinematic production, immersive content, and advanced storytelling where size, weight, and precision are critical. ... Village Island Co., Ltd. | village-island.com © 2026 Village Island Co., Ltd. All rights reserved. ... ### July Monthly News: PROTON 4K 3D Award, Cyanview Update, New Podcast Episode ... Village Island Monthly News — July 2026 Monthly Newsletter July 2026 Village Island Co., Ltd. ｜ village-island.com Welcome to our July 2026 newsletter. This month we bring"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"July Monthly News: PROTON 4K 3D Award, Cyanview Update, New Podcast Episode – VILLAGE island Co.,Ltd",village-island.com,2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://village-island.com/en/202607_monthlynews/,"July Monthly News: PROTON 4K 3D Award, Cyanview Update, New Podcast Episode – VILLAGE island Co.,Ltd ... Monthly News: PROTON ... K 3D Award, Cyanview Update, New Podcast Episode ... Village Island Co., Ltd. ｜ ... Welcome to our July 2026 newsletter. This month we bring you three updates: the new PROTON 4K 3D stereoscopic camera system, a Cyanview feature article on cable-free camera control, and the latest episode of our podcast covering Bluetooth® Auracast™. ... , Perfectly Synchronized ... Village Island is pleased to introduce the PROTON 4K 3D, the latest addition to the PROTON Camera Innovations lineup. Built on the proven PROTON 4K FLEX architecture, it combines two perfectly synchronized cameras into a single, streamlined system for true stereoscopic capture. ... With frame-accurate synchronization, shared control, and a compact design that allows optimal interocular positioning, the PROTON 4 ... 3D delivers natural depth perception and seamless integration into professional 3D workflows — ideal for cinematic production, immersive content, and advanced storytelling where size, weight, and precision are critical. ... ## Forget the Cables —Cyanview ... Local zoom and focus control in ... operator’s hands were never compromised. Even during brief wireless dropouts, ... camera kept working, because ... critical camera functions stayed local while only the remote color-grading (shading) data traveled through Cyanview Cloud — a ... example of technology expanding creative freedom rather than limiting ... The same architecture ... skater can just as easily control 12 Sony FX9 cinema cameras simultaneously at a live fashion event, connect remote production (REMI) over ... internet without complex VPN setup, or remotely shade Blackmagic cameras over Haivision DataBridge. Decoupling camera control from the transmission medium dramatically simplifies lightweight cinema gimbal setups, and even allows fixed “beauty shot” cameras hundreds of kilometers away to be operated without anyone on site. ... What all these use cases share isn’t the type of camera — it’s the same engineering challenge, solved the same way: giving directors complete creative freedom without ever sacrificing the operational precision professional broadcast demands. Instead of building a new control system from scratch for every venue, Cyanview provides one common architecture: the RCP keeps a familiar feel, while the RIO interface sits right next to each camera. Camera control data travels over whatever network is available — 4G, fiber, internet, or wireless bridge — while video takes the transmission path best suited to the production. ... This modular approach frees engineers from worrying about infrastructure, so they can focus on storytelling itself. Whether shooting Olympic athletes, producing a live fashion show, building a REMI workflow, or operating a fixed panoramic camera, the goal is always the same: placing the camera where the story needs it — not where the cable happens to end. That, perhaps, is the real innovation. No new camera controller, no new IP protocol — just an architecture that quietly removes technical barriers and lets creativity fly further than ever. That is Cyanview. ... ## Breaking Through the RF Jungle —Bluetooth® Auracast™ ... Episode 6 of our podcast “Talking Eye” is now live. This episode’s theme is Bluetooth® Auracast™, a next-generation wireless audio standard that overturns the conventional rules of pairing. Auracast turns any device into a “pocket radio transmitter,” broadcasting audio to an unlimited number of receivers at once. ... We dig into how this technology has evolved beyond everyday consumer use into a rugged audio return solution built for professional broadcast production, where failure is never an option — including how it holds up in harsh, congested RF environments. Tune in to hear the full story behind this next-generation architecture. ... Village Island Co., Ltd. 〒104-0061 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, Japan ... ### PROTON 4K 3D WinsNAB 2026 Best of Show ... PROTON 4K 3D Wins NAB 2026 Best of Show — Village Island NEWS RELEASE 🏆 Award PROTON 4K 3D WinsNAB 2026 Best of Show The ... y-hasegawa July 9, 2026"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Billionaire developer Neil Bender markets Uptown Kingston holdings as film production campus - Hudson Valley One,hudsonvalleyone.com (Maura Rosner and Zac Shaw),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hudsonvalleyone.com/2026/07/09/billionaire-developer-neil-bender-markets-uptown-kingston-holdings-as-film-production-campus/,"Billionaire developer Neil Bender markets Uptown Kingston holdings as film production campus - Hudson Valley One ... # Billionaire developer Neil Bender markets Uptown Kingston holdings as film production campus ... -pandemic nightlife. Years after the Backstage Studio Productions ( ... ) concert venue shuttered its ... Street Music Hall ... Farm in Tiv ... William Gottlieb Real ... In a statement to Hudson Valley One, the representative said the site has quietly transitioned into “Kingston Studios.” William Gottlieb Real Estate, the firm owned by billionaire developer Neil Bender, says the former BSP building has become a hub for high-profile entertainment industry productions, despite its low-profile street presence. ... Originally built around 1919 as a movie house and vaudeville theater, 323 Wall St. later became BSP Kingston, a high-capacity performance space that helped anchor the city’s culture and nightlife. BSP closed in 2020 amid the pandemic shutdown and later disputes involving the venue. ... According to the William Gottlieb Real Estate statement, 323 Wall St. has served as the backdrop for television and film projects including HBO’s “Pretty Little Liars” series and Nathan Silver’s critically acclaimed feature “Between the Temples.” The firm also said the building served as the set for SZA’s “Drive” music video, which featured an appearance by actor Ben Stiller. ... The firm said Nile Rodgers & CHIC used the space over the weekend of May 30, 2026, for a multiday rehearsal and production session that culminated in a live performance on June 1. In the statement, William Gottlieb Real Estate said the session further underscored “Kingston Studios’ growing reputation as a destination for world-class artists seeking advanced, flexible production capabilities.” ... While the former BSP building is Kingston Studios’ main production facility, the studio’s website displays a “campus map” showing several other Uptown Kingston properties owned by Bender’s firm. A former office building at 317 Wall St. is listed as a production and post-production space, while the 17,000-square-foot former Woolworth’s building at 311 Wall St. is listed as “flex space.” ... Also included on the campus map are the Cioni building, where the Kingston Library is temporarily housed; 63 North Front St., where the restaurant Kingston Nord recently opened; and the former Stella’s space at 44 North Front St. A representative for William Gottlieb Real Estate declined to comment on buildings other than the main facility at 323 Wall St. The firm did not clarify whether those other properties are available for use in film production through Kingston Studios. ... Some of the properties depicted as part of the campus are also being marketed through commercial real estate listings involving Berardi Realty and Coldwell Banker Prime Properties. The former BSP building at 323 Wall St. is listed for commercial lease at $10,000 a month, though the listing describes it as a short-term occupancy opportunity rather than a long-term lease. A unit in the former Woolworth’s building at 311 Wall St. is listed as a retail space available Aug. 1, 2026, at $3,800 a month. The listings add to the uncertainty about how the publicly marketed Kingston Studios campus overlaps with Bender’s broader real estate portfolio. ... Kingston Studios’ website cites “surrounding locations” like historic exteriors, restaurants, shops, galleries, parks, churches and a lumberyard as additional draws for film and TV production. ... Kingston Studios has maintained a relatively low public profile, in part because film and TV productions typically do not court publicity. In its statement, William Gottlieb Real Estate said the facility is active and getting busier. ... “William Gottlieb Real Estate is deeply committed to both Kingston and the continued success of Kingston Studios as a hub where innovation meets artistry,” the statement said. “The space is actively programmed, marketed and operated to meet the needs of a broad creative community, from major productions to emerging talent. Looking ahead, the ownership is excited to build on this momentum by welcoming additional artists and creators, and further positioning Kingston as a vibrant center for cultural production on a regional, national and international stage.” ... Hudson Valley One was unable to independently verify the full extent of production activity at Kingston Studios. A listed phone number for the Hudson Valley Film Commission was not in service, and a message sent through the commission’s social media account was not returned. Multiple inquiries to the Woodstock Film Festival went unanswered. ... Wall Street Music Hall’s event page reads “nothing planned right now,” and its Instagram page has not been updated in years. The initiative was launched after BSP was shuttered. ... Assessment records list Heermance Farm LLC as the owner of the historic Heermance Farm property in the Red Hook/Tivoli area; published reports identify Neil and Marika Bender as the farm’s owners."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Boutique Distributor Motel Fast-Tracks French Slate with Kim Higelin Mental Health Drama Blue Hour,www.dispatchmedia.co (Le Dispatch),2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.dispatchmedia.co/p/boutique-distributor-motel-fast-tracks,"Boutique Distributor Motel Fast-Tracks French Slate with Kim Higelin Mental Health Drama ... # Boutique Distributor Motel Fast-Tracks French Slate with Kim Higelin Mental Health Drama Blue Hour ... ### Launched in April 2026, Simon Robert and Guillaume De Castro’s startup overhauls its maiden lineup, shifting political thrillers to align with the US Midterm elections. ... Jul 09, 2026 ... The independent theatrical distribution market requires extreme tactical agility, particularly for boutique newcomers trying to carve out a permanent lane. Officially incorporated in April 2026 by in…"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Lim Young-woong Proves Popularity Beyond the Sea and in the Mountains... 'Little Island, Big Hero' Extended by One Episode - MK",www.mk.co.kr (김소연),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mk.co.kr/en/broadcasting-service/12093298,"## Lim Young-woong Proves Popularity Beyond the Sea and in the Mountains... 'Little Island, Big Hero' Extended by One Episode 사진 확대 'Little Island, Big Hero.' Photo | SBS 'Little Island, Big Hero' will be extended by one episode and air as a seven-part series. ... The team behind SBS's variety show 'Little Island, Big Hero' announced the extension on the 8th. The production crew said, ""We were able to extend the show by one episode thanks to the passionate support from viewers,"" and added, ""We plan to pack the remaining episodes with a wide range of stories from the mountain village, so please stay tuned until the end."" ... Premiering on the 23rd of last month, 'Little Island, Big Hero' follows Lim Young-woong as he becomes a mountain man deep in the hills, crossing mountains and streams to enjoy an unplanned, eco-friendly life guided by instinct. After last year's four-episode pilot, 'Island Bachelor Hero,' won over viewers, he has returned this time as a 'mountain bachelor.' ... Even after becoming a regular program, the show has continued to perform strongly. In the key 20-49 ratings, one of the broadcaster's main indicators, it held the No. 1 spot among Tuesday variety shows for three consecutive weeks. Its peak minute-by-minute rating also climbed to 6.5%, underscoring solid viewership. ... It is also drawing positive attention on OTT platforms and online. Right after its first broadcast, it entered Netflix's Top 10 and reached as high as No. 4. Lim Young-woong also ranked No. 2 in non-drama cast member buzz in a Fundex report, proving the show's popularity both online and offline. ... More encounters with a variety of friends are expected in 'Little Island, Big Hero.' The episode airing on the 14th will feature the wild mountain-house life of the 'NEW Mountain Bachelors' Kwak Bum, Nucksal, and Roy Kim. Later episodes are also expected to draw attention, with Cha Seung-won and actor Kim Do-hoon, who were connected through the 'Three Meals a Day' series, set to appear."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Harbor Island Studios stays afloat thanks to local nonprofit | The Seattle Times,www.seattletimes.com (Savannah Butcher),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/harbor-island-studios-stays-afloat-thanks-to-local-nonprofit/,"Harbor Island Studios stays afloat thanks to local nonprofit | The Seattle Times ... Harbor Island Studios was thrown a life raft Tuesday from a local nonprofit after the Metropolitan King County Council nearly voted to remove funding to the facility in November of 2025. ... CREATE48 Media Network, a Seattle-based nonprofit, and the Council forged a one-year lease agreement Tuesday, affording the film studio some breathing room, King County Executive Girmay Zahilay said in a news release. ... The region’s only publicly owned sound stage, Harbor Island Studios is an 89,000-square-foot facility equipped with two sound stages, a green screen room, makeup and art rooms, a wardrobe and sewing shop and a construction mill and offices, according to its website. ... Before Harbor Island Studios’ launch in 2021, the building was an unused flour mill. ... The facility has hosted 160 productions from Amazon, HBO, Netflix and Paramount, including independent shorts, features, commercials and music videos. It hosted a season of the reality TV show “Love is Blind” in 2023. ... “Harbor Island Studios has been a unique public asset that supports King County’s film industry and creative economy,” Zahilay said in a news release. “I’m glad we were able to find a nonprofit partner to continue momentum for the community while we work with stakeholders to develop a long-term strategy that supports access to affordable film and production space in our region.” ... In November, 67 members of the film community attended a King County Council public comment session to vouch for the studio after its county funding was cut. ... “This is about keeping a valuable public asset active, accessible, and aligned with the needs of the regional creative economy,” Kirk Nordenstrom, executive director of CREATE48 Media Network, said in a news release. “Harbor Island Studios has the potential to serve both professional productions and the local creative community. Our goal is to provide practical, mission-driven stewardship during this next phase.” ... CREATE48 is kicking off its tenure at Harbor Island Studios with its first public event since taking over — the Seattle 48 Hour Film Project. ... The project will start 5 p.m. Friday at Harbor Island Studios, where filmmakers will see through the entire writing, production, and delivery process within 48 hours."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Little Lorraine screening launches the first Unama’ki/Cape Breton Film Festival - Your Quad Counties,yourquadcounties.ca (Kelly MacMillan),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://yourquadcounties.ca/little-lorraine-screening-launches-the-first-unamaki-cape-breton-film-festival/,"Little Lorraine screening launches the first Unama’ki/Cape Breton Film Festival - Your Quad Counties ... # Little Lorraine screening launches the first Unama’ki/Cape Breton Film Festival ... Update July 11: the 7pm screening is sold out. A 3pm show has been added for Little Lorraine at Strathspey Performing Arts Centre on July 30th! ... Tickets are on sale now for a special fundraising screening of Little Lorraine, the acclaimed Atlantic Canadian movie filmed in Cape Breton. ... The screening will take place on Thursday, July 30th at 7pm at Strathspey Performing Arts Centre in Mabou with all proceeds supporting the inaugural Unama’ki/Cape Breton Film Festival, taking place September 25–27, 2026 at the Inverness County Centre for the Arts. ... If you go, you will get a chance to meet some of the filmmakers from Little Lorraine who will participate in a post-screening talk about the making of the film, filmmaking in Atlantic Canada and the importance of supporting regional stories. ... “Film has the power to connect people through stories, places, and shared experiences. Creating opportunities for audiences to engage with filmmakers and celebrating local talent is essential to building a vibrant cultural community. The Unama’ki / Cape Breton Film Festival is an exciting step forward for our region, and I encourage everyone to support this fundraiser and help establish what I believe will become an important annual event for Cape Breton,” said Tamara Deverell, Academy Award-winning Production Designer for Frankenstein, and Co-Chair of the Inverness County Centre for the Arts. ... Tickets are $15 + service fees and are available on Eventbrite through Strathspey Place until sold out. Click here to purchase."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Executive Zahilay Announces One-Year Lease for Harbor Island Studios with CREATE48 Media Network – King County | Office of the Executive,executive.kingcounty.gov,2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://executive.kingcounty.gov/2026/07/07/executive-zahilay-announces-one-year-lease-for-harbor-island-studios-with-create48-media-network/,"Executive Zahilay Announces One-Year Lease for Harbor Island Studios with CREATE48 Media Network – King County | Office of the Executive ... One-Year Lease for Harbor Island Studios with CREATE48 Media Network ... King County – Today, King County Executive Girmay Zahilay announced a one-year lease agreement with CREATE48 Media Network for the use of Harbor Island Studios, supporting the region’s growing film industry, strengthening the creative economy, and expanding job opportunities for local filmmakers, creatives, and production professionals. ... “Harbor Island Studios has been a unique public asset that supports King County’s film industry and creative economy. I’m glad we were able to find a nonprofit partner to continue momentum for the community while we work with stakeholders to develop a long-term strategy that supports access to affordable film and production space in our region,” said Executive Zahilay. “We’re excited that CREATE48 Media Network will activate and operate this valuable studio space over the next year, bringing more stories to life while also while also empowering creatives and creating pathways into film and media careers.” ... “CREATE48 Media Network is deeply grateful to County Executive Zahilay and his staff for their leadership, responsiveness, and partnership in reaching an agreement that keeps Harbor Island Studios moving forward,” said Kirk Nordenstrom, Executive Director of CREATE48 Media Network. “Their work helps preserve critical production infrastructure while allowing us to continue building pathways to family-wage careers in King County’s creative economy. We also want to thank Councilmembers Balducci and Mosqueda for their encouragement and support throughout this effort. Together with County leadership, KCFAB, industry partners, and community stakeholders, we look forward to helping shape a long-term strategy that maintains a strong, sustainable production studio presence in King County.” ... With programs in Seattle, Montana, Oregon, and the Bay Area, CREATE48 Media Network produces inclusive, career-building opportunities for filmmakers at all stages. Local programs include the Seattle 48 Hour Film Project, which will take place July 10-12, with the kick-off event taking place at Harbor Island Studios, and screenings of all participating films to then be held at SIFF Cinema Uptown July 27-30, 2026. Additional programs include the Seattle 48 Hour Horror Film Project, the Burien Film Festival, Diversity in Representation Fund, as well as co-hosted free networking events with a variety of industry partners, and educational podcasts to break down barriers to entry in film and media. ... Harbor Island Studios is an 89,000 square-foot facility with two sound stages and is the only publicly owned soundstage regionally. Since its official launch in June 2023, Harbor Island Studios has hosted over 160 productions from Paramount Studios, HBO, Amazon, and Netflix, as well as number of independent short films and features, commercials, and music videos. ... King County recently completed a surplussing analysis on the property, which is owned by the Solid Waste Division in the Department of Natural Resources and Parks (DNRP). Due to the cost of ongoing maintenance needs, the Solid Waste Division plans to move forward with the surplussing process over the next year to determine if there is another government or private entity who would like to purchase the space. ... Executive Zahilay’s administration will continue to work closely with County Councilmembers, local film industry advocates, arts organizations, and creatives to identify a long-term, sustainable studio model to support film production in the region. ... “District 8 is home to some of our most cherished cultural institutions and a thriving homegrown arts scene, and I’m thrilled that we have been able to keep a driver of our arts economy alive at Harbor Island Studios,” said King County Councilmember Teresa Mosqueda. “In partnership with Executive Zahilay, this agreement with Create48 allows for continued film and commercial production, providing a space for our next generation of creators to bring their visions to life, while spurring business at our local shops and employing community members in good union wage jobs.” ... “Film is such a rich medium, building community through sharing our stories and our common humanity, both of which we need now as much as ever. Today marks a critical step to preserve Harbor Island Studios as a vital part of our local film industry,” said King County Councilmember Claudia Balducci. “I am grateful to the Executive team and Create48 for stepping up to keep this unique asset alive. There remains hard work ahead, and we will need all hands on deck. I remain committed to working with Executive Zahilay, the County Council, the film community and advocates as we chart a future of long term sustainability and success for Harbor Island Studios and for local film production right here in the heart of King County.”"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Fresh Films production brings economic boost, trains next generation of filmmakers",www.kwqc.com (Wafaa Ezzat),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.kwqc.com/2026/07/07/fresh-films-production-brings-economic-boost-trains-next-generation-filmmakers/,"Fresh Films production brings economic boost, trains next generation of filmmakers ... # Fresh Films production brings economic boost, trains next generation of filmmakers ... ##### Leaders say they’re about $1M from breaking ground on a studio campus designed to attract $5M–$30M projects ... Fresh Films says its latest streaming series, Dearly Departed, is creating business for local companies while giving aspiring filmmakers hands-on experience. ... ROCK ISLAND, Ill. (KWQC) - A local film production is bringing more than cameras to the Quad Cities. ... Fresh Films said its latest streaming series, “Dearly Departed”, is creating business for local companies while giving aspiring filmmakers hands-on experience on a professional set. ... The organization is filming the six-episode streaming series during a 14-day shoot at First Lutheran Church in Rock Island. The production includes local and out-of-town actors and crew members, with about 40 cast and crew members working on set each day. ... She said the production is also generating business for local restaurants, hotels and retailers. ... “There’s all these local restaurants that we’re purchasing breakfast and lunch from, retailers for costumes, wardrobe, and supplies for the set,” Feigley said. ... Fresh Films has spent the past 24 years introducing young people to careers in film and media. The organization started in Chicago before moving its headquarters to the Quad Cities about 10 years ago. ... Fresh Films hopes productions like “Dearly Departed” are only the beginning. ... The nonprofit is leading the effort to build Rockline Studios, a planned $12 million studio campus designed to attract larger film and television productions to the Quad Cities. Leaders said they are about $1 million away from breaking ground and hope to open the facility by summer 2027. ... Feigley said the current production has a budget of about $500,000, but the goal is to attract projects with budgets ranging from $5 million to $30 million. ... She said a major television production could employ more than 100 crew members for several months, creating even greater demand for local hotels, restaurants, retailers and service providers. ... “It’s not just about us making films and television shows or streaming shows,” Feigley said. “It’s about bringing bigger NBC or Netflix shows here to the Quad Cities to employ our local talent.” ... Leaders said that vision would not only expand the region’s film industry but also create more long-term opportunities for both local businesses and the next generation of filmmakers."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Kidscreen » Archive » FEATURE: Cantilever Media perfects the all-in-one model,kidscreen.com (Sadhana Bharanidharan),2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://kidscreen.com/2026/07/06/feature-cantilever-media-perfects-the-all-in-one-model/,"Kidscreen » Archive » FEATURE: Cantilever Media perfects the all-in-one model ... ##### Integrating sales has given the prodco a competitive advantage—and market intelligence—as it champions indie animation. ... #### Cantilever brings in Architect to distribute two family movies per year ... #### Cantilever Media launches Kazoo Films ... #### Cantilever Media secures a US$673,000 investment"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI,www.brazilbusinessinsights.com,2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.brazilbusinessinsights.com/news/moomoo-engine-launch-futu-xp-nubank-brazil,"Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI ... # Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil ... Moomoo is launching 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified trading toolkit designed to capture active retail and professional traders in Brazil, challenging incumbents. ... - ▸ Global user base: Over 22 million users - ▸ Launch date: July 2, 2026 - ▸ Target market: Active retail & pro traders - ▸ Primary region: Brazil expansion ... The Bottom Line: - Moomoo, the digital brokerage subsidiary of Futu Holdings ($FUTU), is set to launch 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified suite of advanced trading tools designed to consolidate market analysis, charting, and execution. - The rollout represents a strategic push to capture high-value retail and professional traders in emerging markets, particularly Brazil, where digital brokerage competition is intensifying. - While the launch enhances $FUTU's technological moat, it poses direct competitive pressure on local incumbents such as XP Inc. ($XP) and Nubank ($NU). Strategic Expansion in Latin America: Futu Holdings ($FUTU), through its international trading platform Moomoo, is accelerating its expansion into Latin America with the exclusive announcement of 'Moomoo Engine.' This unified toolkit is designed to streamline the trading lifecycle for retail and professional investors. By integrating advanced charting, real-time data analytics, and algorithmic execution into a single, cohesive interface, Moomoo aims to address the fragmentation that has historically plagued active traders in emerging markets. The Brazilian market, characterized by a highly sophisticated retail investor base and a rapidly growing interest in global equities, serves as the primary launchpad for this technological deployment. Technological Disruption and the 'Moomoo Engine': The 'Moomoo Engine' represents a significant upgrade to the platform's existing infrastructure. Historically, active traders in Brazil have had to rely on multiple third-party platforms for technical analysis, order routing, and portfolio tracking. This fragmentation often leads to latency issues, higher subscription costs, and execution inefficiencies. Moomoo's unified toolkit addresses these pain points by offering proprietary, low-latency charting algorithms and institutional-grade data feeds directly within the trading application. This integration is expected to lower the barrier to entry for advanced trading strategies, enabling retail investors to execute complex multi-leg options strategies and automated technical trades with greater precision. Competitive Dynamics in the Brazilian Brokerage Sector: The introduction of the 'Moomoo Engine' comes at a time of intense competition within the Brazilian financial services sector. Incumbents like XP Inc. ($XP) and BTG Pactual have traditionally dominated the affluent and active trader segments through extensive advisory networks and proprietary platforms. Concurrently, digital-first platforms like Nubank ($NU) and Inter have successfully democratized access to basic investment products for the mass market. Moomoo's strategy bypasses the traditional advisory model, focusing instead on self-directed, tech-savvy traders who prioritize execution speed, analytical depth, and low transaction costs. By offering institutional-grade tools without the premium price tag, Moomoo is positioning itself to capture market share from both high-end incumbents and mass-market digital banks looking to upsell their user bases. Regulatory and Operational Considerations: Operating a foreign-backed digital brokerage in Brazil requires navigating a complex regulatory framework overseen by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Brazil (CVM) and the Central Bank of Brazil (BCB). Moomoo's expansion strategy relies heavily on seamless integration with local clearing systems and compliance with strict foreign exchange (FX) regulations. For Brazilian investors trading international assets, tax compliance—specifically the calculation of capital gains and the monthly 'Carnê-Leão' tax filing—has historically been a major friction point. To gain widespread adoption, the 'Moomoo Engine' must integrate localized tax reporting tools that simplify these compliance obligations for domestic users. Furthermore, fluctuations in the USD/BRL exchange rate remain a critical variable, as currency volatility can significantly impact the net returns of Brazilian investors trading on US exchanges through the platform. Implications for Futu Holdings ($FUTU): For Futu Holdings ($FUTU), the successful rollout of the 'Moomoo Engine' in Brazil is vital for its broader international diversification strategy. Facing mature markets and regulatory headwinds in mainland China and Hong Kong, Futu has increasingly looked to Southeast Asia and Latin America to drive its next phase of growth. Brazil represents one of the largest retail investment markets in the developing world, making it a high-stakes testing ground for Moomoo's global scalability. If the 'Moomoo Engine' succeeds in capturing a meaningful share of Brazil's active trading volume, it could serve as a blueprint for further expansion into other Latin American markets, such as Mexico and Colombia, thereby bolstering Futu's long-term revenue growth and reducing its geographic concentration risk. ... Market Impact: The launch of the 'Moomoo Engine' has distinct implications for the key players in the digital brokerage space: - Futu Holdings ($FUTU): Bullish. The successful deployment of advanced trading tools in Brazil accelerates Futu's international diversification, reducing its reliance on Asian markets and opening a high-margin revenue stream from active Latin American traders. - XP Inc. ($XP): Bearish. XP faces direct technological competition in its high-value active trader segment. While its advisory network remains a strong moat, Moomoo's low-cost, high-tech offering could pressure XP's commission margins and active client retention. - Nu Holdings ($NU): Neutral. Nubank's primary investment audience consists of mass-market retail investors rather than sophisticated active traders. However, as Nubank seeks to upsell its client base into more complex financial products, Moomoo's advanced platform represents a long-term competitive hurdle. ... > analyst consensus: Bullish on Futu Holdings ($FUTU) international expansion; bearish on XP Inc. ($XP) active trader retention; neutral on Nu Holdings ($NU). > asset_class: Equities"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"Production Company, ARIS Signs with Little Bird for East Coast Representation | LBBOnline",lbbonline.com,2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://lbbonline.com/news/Production-Company-ARIS-Signs-with-Little-Bird-for-East-Coast-Representation,"Production Company, ARIS Signs with Little Bird for East Coast Representation | LBBOnline ... # Production Company, ARIS Signs with Little Bird for East Coast Representation ... Los Angeles-based production company ARIS has signed with Becca Falborn’s Little Bird for East Coast Representation. ARIS, founded in 2016 has been creating iconic commercial work with brands such as Delta, Chevy, Coca-Cola, Pfizer, Lily, Johnson and Johnson, to name a few. Its director roster is made up of notable names like Zoe Malhotra and Michael Miller and its services span across all elements of live action production as well as their full service internal post-production studio partners at FastFollow Post. ... Greg Bassenian started ARIS after nearly a decade of working as a producer and creative in network television on shows like 'The King of Queens' and the 'CSI' franchise, but he found himself wanting more out of the opportunities coming his way. “There are more opportunities than ever in the creative content industry, and we felt the best way to amplify the success of our directors was to partner with Becca’s team at Little Bird.” ... ""Greg and I first connected over a year ago and have been exploring the possibility of working together ever since. The timing couldn't have been better—he reached out just as I was planning my next trip to LA, and once we met in person, it was clear the partnership was the right fit. Greg's experience, welcoming nature, and exceptional roster made bringing him into the Little Bird roster—or, as we call it, 'the nest'—an easy decision,"" says Falborn, who founded the company in 2024 and has rapidly expanded its roster and network of production and post-production partners. ... ARIS specialises in healthcare, pharma and comedy but is constantly expanding their roster of talent and directors."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"'Dear You' Expands , ReelShort and RJOY Add Carriage Deals",patrickfrater.substack.com (Patrick Frater),2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://patrickfrater.substack.com/p/dear-you-distribution-reelshort-rjoy,"Sahamongkol Film Co has acquired distribution rights in Thailand for Chinese hit family drama film “Dear You.” The company plans to give the Teochow (or Chaoshan)-dialect film a local theatrical release from 6 August. ... Rights sales in much of the world outside Southeast Asia were initially handled by Hugoeast. But when the film became a social phenomenon minority investor Damai Entertainment (formerly Alibaba Pictures) took control of sales to other territories. ... film was released on ... on release and looks ... Singapore public broadcaster MediaCorp has issued an open casting call for the third chapter of its period drama TV franchise “The Little Nyonya”. ... “Emerald Hill” drew over 2.1 million viewers locally and made history on Netflix Singapore as the first local drama to debut at #1. Its international footprint now spans Southeast Asia via Netflix; Malaysia via Astro and Netflix; China via Dragon TV and Tencent Video; Taiwan via friDAY, TVBS and CTS; and global travel audiences via Singapore Airlines’ KrisWorld and British Airways ... The new series will be directed and executive produced by Canter Chia from a screenplay by Ang Eng Tee, who also wrote the first two Little Nyonya titles. The new season is expected to air in 20 ... short Secures ... Micro drama platform ReelShort has struck a carriage partnership with Globe, the Philippines’ leading telecommunications company. ... It is the second telco partnership announced by ReelShort in a couple of months. It previously announced one in Thailand with AIS. ... Separately, ReelShort this week held its first ReelShort Accelerate industry education and talent development initiative in Hong Kong. Held on 22 June, the event was organised by the Academy of Film at Hong Kong Baptist University and was initiated with the support of AR Global Media Network. ... #### RJOY Strikes Deals With Astro and IDN ... RJOY, the direct-to-consumer arm of Singapore-based micro drama producer and wholesaler Risingjoy, has expanded into new territories in Southeast Asia. It struck new partnerships with Astro’s Sooka homegrown streaming service in Malaysia and IDN App in Indonesia. Both deals were signed at APOS in Bali last week. ... The launches bring RJOY’s footprint to four markets globally, following its recent debut on TikTok Minis in Japan and the US. ... RisingJoy is advancing its ambitions as a full-service micro-entertainment studio, with original IP and co-production at the centre of its next phase of growth. As a key part of this, RisingJoy has unveiled a microdrama bible for 10 of its titles, that it has developed with strategic partner and investor Double Vision. Each goes beyond a hit script, mapping out story arcs, hooks and settings, with English-language guidance on creation and production tailored to what performs in each region. ... “Southeast Asia is one of the fastest-growing micro drama markets outside China, and the way to win here is local. Astro and IDN App bring the audience and the market expertise; we bring proven content and format know-how – and that combination is how we scale,” said Cassandra Yang, CEO and Co-founder. ... The launches bring R ... to four markets globally, following its recent debut on TikTok Minis in Japan and the US."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,The LAB positions for growth in booming short-drama market - Jamaica Observer,www.jamaicaobserver.com (Kellaray Miles | Reporter),2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.jamaicaobserver.com/2026/06/19/lab-positions-growth-booming-short-drama-market/,"The LAB positions for growth in booming short-drama market - Jamaica Observer ... generated more than 3 ... within two months of ... release and is now set to reach a wider international audience following distribution agreements with major streaming platforms. ... # The LAB positions for growth in booming short-drama market ## …inks streaming partnerships, expands content monetisation strategy ... Media and advertising company Limners and Bards Limited (The LAB) is seeking to capitalise on the rapidly expanding global market for short-form entertainment as new streaming and licensing deals begin to unlock fresh revenue opportunities for its growing portfolio of owned content. ... Encouraged by the early success of Happily Ever Awkward, a short drama produced under its fast-content model, the company said its content strategy is beginning to generate tangible returns, opening new revenue opportunities beyond its traditional advertising and production businesses. ... The film, after generating more than 380,000 views within two months of its release, is now set to reach a wider international audience following recent distribution agreements with major streaming platforms. ... “The film will reach wider audiences through releases on Amazon Prime Video and Apple TV on June 30, 2026 and on Tubi on July 26, 2026. We have also secured our first licensing agreement in the vertical micro-drama space through a partnership with Mansa, a revenue-sharing project expected to launch this summer. Together these milestones signal that the assets we have spent years building are beginning to generate opportunities well beyond their original production,” a recent report to shareholders signed by Chairman Steven Gooden and CEO Kimala Bennett stated. ... The LAB’s venture into content creation, which began to take form over the last five years, has steadily expanded its in-house film production efforts, laying the foundation for a business model centred on content ownership and monetisation. Following the release of its first major short drama, management is seeking to establish a foothold in the rapidly expanding vertical micro-drama market, a segment widely regarded as a multi-billion-dollar industry ... The LAB’s push into the space aligns with its broader ambition to diversify revenues beyond its traditional advertising and production businesses while creating content assets that can be monetised across multiple platforms and markets. ... The company’s broader content pipeline also continues to advance as discussions are progress on the distribution of two additional productions — Love Offside and Spices of Christmas — which management expects will begin to generate revenue in upcoming quarters. ... Additionally, interest generated through SLATE – Jamaica on Screen, coupled with growing demand from international distributors seeking authentic Caribbean stories, have further strengthened confidence in the long-term prospects of the company’s content business. ... At the end of the six-month period ended April 30, 2026, The LAB, despite progress on strategic initiatives, reported weaker financial results which management attributed largely to the lingering effects of Hurricane Melissa which struck Jamaica last October and disrupted commercial activity during one of the company’s strongest seasonal periods. ... During the period, revenue declined 26.6 per cent to total $337.7 million, down from $460.2 million. The media division remaining the strongest contributor to revenue, generated $166.9 million as production delivered $108.3 million, while agency services accounted for $62.4 million. The company, however, posted a net loss of $13.4 million for the period, reversing profit of $20.6 million recorded a year earlier. ... As it works to recover from the downturn, management said it has implemented a series of cost-containment measures, including organisational restructuring and tighter resource allocations — all of which it believes will over the next few quarters help to enhance operational efficiency and support profitability as business activity normalises. ... With audience engagement growing, international distribution expanding and new licensing opportunities emerging, management also expressed confidence that the company is laying the foundation for a more diversified, resilient and sustainable business model. ... While acknowledging that the company remains in an investment phase, the directors likewise said they remain optimistic about the long-term potential of the intellectual property strategy. ... “The opportunity that lies ahead of us is substantial,” they noted. “An intellectual property business rewards those willing to invest patiently and think in years rather than quarters and that is precisely how we are building it. ... “That groundwork is already paying off, with our audience growing, our distribution widening, and new revenue channels opening across the business, each a building block in a portfolio of assets designed to generate value for years to come.”"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,"'Shooom's Odyssey' Follow-Up 'The Little Run' to Charades, Diaphana",variety.com (John Hopewell),2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/film/markets-festivals/charades-diaphana-little-run-julien-bisaro-claire-paoletti-1236779497/,"“The Little Run” (“La Petite Cavale”), Julien Bisaro and Claire Paoletti’s follow-up to “Shooom’s Odyssey” and one of France’s most-awaited of upcoming animated features, has been boarded by Charades and Diaphana Distribution. ... A renowned director-driven sales banner intent on bringing new voices to the world such as Gints Zilbalodis’ Oscar winner “Flow,” Charades is handling international distribution. ... Diaphana Distribution, whose release slate includes Lukas Dhont’s “Coward” and Netflix Cannes big buy “In Waves,” will open “The Little Run” in cinemas in France. ... Directed by Bisaro, co-written by Paoletti and now entering pre-production, “The Little Run” has also clinched pre-sales with Canal+, Ciné+, and France 3 Cinéma in France as well as ZDF in Germany. ... also shared in exclusivity with Variety an unreleased image of “The ... ,” which was a buzzy three-time winner at Annecy’s MIFA Feature Film Pitches in 2023, ... Ciclic Centr-Val-de-Loire Region Award, a SACD award and the Cristal Publishing Award. ... Targeting family audiences from age 5 and up, “The Little Run” is set up at Bisaro and Paoletti’s boutique studio Picolo Pictures. It currently establishing the animation pipeline with partner studios, alongside the development of a Luxembourg co-production with Doghouse Films. ... It follows up “Shooom’s Odyssey,” where plucky hatchling Shoom sets out to find her mother or a replacement. It won Annecy’s 2020 Cristal Award for best TV project and an Annie for outstanding achievement for production design in an animated TV/media production. The exquisite 2D animated preschool film also sold worldwide and was chosen for Variety’s 2020 Annecy selection of 10 Shorts Not to Miss. ... ### Paramount Agrees to Postpone Warner Bros. ... Until After Antitrust Trial ... ### Box Office: ‘The Odyssey’ Holds Strong With $25 Million on Friday"
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,'The Indies' from 'The Currents' Producers Inks Swiss Distribution,variety.com (Annika Pham),2026-06-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/film/global/ecam-forum-the-indies-aline-film-lastor-media-mumenthaler-1236767073/,"'The Indies' from 'The Currents' Producers Inks Swiss Distribution ... Jun 5, 2026 1:56am PT # Switzerland’s Sister Distribution Boards ‘The Indies’ From ‘They Will Be Dust’ Producers: ’It’s Not Character-Driven but Image-Driven’ (EXCLUSIVE) The Swiss-Spanish co-production by debut feature helmers Pauline Julier and Nicolas Chapoulier will bow at Madrid's ECAM Forum as a work in progress ... By Annika Pham After serving as a minority partner to Spain’s Lastor Media on the Toronto-winning Spanish pic “They Will Be Dust,” established Swiss banner Alina Film is majority-producing with Lastor the period road movie “The Indies,” (“Les Indes”) which will be sneak-peeked as a work in progress at ECAM Forum co-production market in Madrid, running June 9-11. Switzerland’s Sister Distribution has just snapped up the rights to the pic, co-written and directed by first-time feature filmmakers Pauline Julier and Nicolas Chapoulier. ### Chloe Fineman Says 'SNL' Boss Lorne Michaels Was at World Cup Match When She Called to Say She Was Leaving the Show A Swiss-French ... -hyphenate artist ... “Sister Distribution is a regular backer of ... ier’s works,” said David Epiney, “The Indies” producer and ... Film co-founder alongside Eugenia Mumenthaler ... Themselves passionate about film as an art and singular filmmakers voices, such as the acclaimed Milagros Mument ... er (“The Currents,” “The Idea of a Lake”) and Elena Lopez Riera (“The Water”), the production duo immediately ... in love with ... Julier and Chapoulier first reached out to them ... -to-seven years ... vision for this ... Commenting on the film’s acquisition for Switzerland, Sister Distribution’s Abel Davoine said: “A historical study with such a contemporary and relevant perspective, where intelligence and grace are not opposed but rather complementary: this is precisely the core of our vibrant lineup.” ... The €2.6 million ($3.0 million) Swiss-Spanish film co-produced with Swiss public broadcaster RTS, received support from Eurimages and ICEC, the Catalan Institute for Cultural Enterprises. ... “Today, thanks to the numerous filming incentives and national and regional support to minority co-productions, Spain has become more competitive and attractive than France for instance, a natural co-production partner to Switzerland. And if Spain is booming these days as a shoot and production hub, it’s not a coincidence; it comes from a political will,” Epiney underscored. ... Besides the pitching of “The Indies “at ECAM Forum, a co-production market Epiney and Mumenthaler have attended since day one – “the organisers have a clear editorial line and generosity, it’s an excellent spot!”– the Swiss producers will take part in Milagros Mumenthaler’s retrospective, jointly organised by ECAM Forum and Filmadrid. ... The duo is also preparing the Argentinian-Swiss filmmaker’s next project after her award-winning “The Currents,” currently screening in U.S. arthouse venues via Kino Lorber Distribution. “We can’t say much, it’s very early days, but it will be a romantic comedy,” said Epiney."
Little Island Productions,,,,Exa,'The Indies' from 'The Currents' Producers Inks Swiss Distribution,variety.com (Annika Pham),2026-06-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/film/markets-festivals/ecam-forum-the-indies-aline-film-lastor-media-mumenthaler-1236767073/,"'The Indies' from 'The Currents' Producers Inks Swiss Distribution ... Jun 5, 2026 1:56am PT # Switzerland’s Sister Distribution Boards ‘The Indies’ From ‘They Will Be Dust’ Producers: ’It’s Not Character-Driven but Image-Driven’ (EXCLUSIVE) The Swiss-Spanish co-production by debut feature helmers Pauline Julier and Nicolas Chapoulier will bow at Madrid's ECAM Forum as a work in progress ... By Annika Pham After serving as a minority partner to Spain’s Lastor Media on the Toronto-winning Spanish pic “They Will Be Dust,” established Swiss banner Alina Film is majority-producing with Lastor the period road movie “The Indies,” (“Les Indes”) which will be sneak-peeked as a work in progress at ECAM Forum co-production market in Madrid, running June 9-11. Switzerland’s Sister Distribution has just snapped up the rights to the pic, co-written and directed by first-time feature filmmakers Pauline Julier and Nicolas Chapoulier. A Swiss-French multi-hyphenate artist and filmmaker, Julier has gained international recognition with her art installations and documentaries such as “Way Beyond” and “Follow the Water,” showcased at festivals and art centres including Visions du Réel, Thessaloniki and The Centre George Pompidou in Paris. Director, visual artist and author Chapoulier for his part has a background in theatre and currently serves as artistic director to the company Les 3 points de suspension. ... Commenting on the film’s acquisition for Switzerland, Sister Distribution’s Abel Davoine said: “A historical study with such a contemporary and relevant perspective, where intelligence and grace are not opposed but rather complementary: this is precisely the core of our vibrant lineup.” ... The €2.6 million ($3.0 million) Swiss-Spanish film co-produced with Swiss public broadcaster RTS, received support from Eurimages and ICEC, the Catalan Institute for Cultural Enterprises. ... “Today, thanks to the numerous filming incentives and national and regional support to minority co-productions, Spain has become more competitive and attractive than France for instance, a natural co-production partner to Switzerland. And if Spain is booming these days as a shoot and production hub, it’s not a coincidence; it comes from a political will,” Epiney underscored. ... Besides the pitching of “The Indies “at ECAM Forum, a co-production market Epiney and Mumenthaler have attended since day one – “the organisers have a clear editorial line and generosity, it’s an excellent spot!”– the Swiss producers will take part in Milagros Mumenthaler’s retrospective, jointly organised by ECAM Forum and Filmadrid. ... The duo is also preparing the Argentinian-Swiss filmmaker’s next project after her award-winning “The Currents,” currently screening in U.S. arthouse venues via Kino Lorber Distribution. “We can’t say much, it’s very early days, but it will be a romantic comedy,” said Epiney."
Little Island Productions,,,,Linkup,Julio Torres and Martine Gutierrez to Debut New Performance,TheaterMania.com,2026-08-27T00:00:00Z,2026-08-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.theatermania.com/news/julio-torres-and-martine-gutierrez-to-debut-new-performance_1842660/,"A new performance directed and written by Julio Torres, starring Martine Gutierrez, will debut at Little Island from August 27-29. The production is an under-the-sea story about romance and self-discovery, featuring a creative team with scenic, costume, lighting, and sound design. This highlights Little Island's ongoing commitment to innovative and original performances."
Little Island Productions,,,,Linkup,Anthony Roth Costanzo and More to Perform at Little Island This Week,BroadwayWorld,2026-08-05T00:00:00Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.broadwayworld.com/article/Anthony-Roth-Costanzo-and-More-to-Perform-at-Little-Island-This-Week-20260805,"Little Island's 2026 summer series continues with performances by Anthony Roth Costanzo and others, featuring a mix of concerts, world premieres, and live radio shows. The season includes 56 performances by over 200 artists, highlighting New York's cultural life with a focused and dynamic programming model. Events take place in open-air spaces throughout the park."
Little Island Productions,,,,Linkup,Little Island Significantly Scales Back Its Summer Schedule,The New York Times,2026-06-29T00:00:00Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/29/arts/music/little-island-schedule-performances-concerts.html,"Little Island announced a reduced six-week summer performance schedule starting July 29, shifting from theatrical spectacles to more concert-style shows and culinary events. This change reflects a strategic rethink of programming, with a focus on affordability and live entertainment. The venue had a resurgence in 2024 with funding for an annual performing arts festival."
Little Island Productions,,,,Linkup,"Little Island's 2026 Summer Season to Feature Shows by Laurie Anderson, Rufus Wainwright, Lillias White, Qween Jean, More",Playbill,2026-06-24T00:00:00Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://playbill.com/article/little-islands-2026-summer-season-to-feature-free-shows-by-laurie-anderson-rufus-wainwright-lillias-white-qween-jean-more,"The 2026 summer season at Little Island will run from July 29 to September 6, featuring 56 events including concerts, world premieres, live radio shows, and culinary events. The venue continues to position itself as a dynamic cultural hub with a diverse lineup and has welcomed over 7.5 million visitors since opening in 2021. The season includes notable artists and a focus on innovative programming."
