Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"Commerzbank Aktie: Rekordergebnis von 1,8 Milliarden Euro",www.boerse-express.com,2026-08-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.boerse-express.com/news/articles/commerzbank-aktie-rekordergebnis-von-18-milliarden-euro-936810,"Commerzbank Aktie: Rekordergebnis von 1,8 Milliarden Euro ... # Commerzbank Aktie: Rekordergebnis von 1,8 Milliarden Euro ... Commerzbank meldet historisch beste Halbjahreszahlen, kündigt Aktienrückkauf über 1,2 Mrd. Euro an und treibt Fusionsverhandlungen mit UniCredit voran. ... - Operatives Ergebnis steigt auf 2,7 Mrd. Euro - Aktienrückkauf über 1,2 Mrd. Euro angekündigt - Fusionsgespräche mit UniCredit konkretisieren sich - Analysten erhöhen Kursziele nach Rekordzahlen ... Die Commerzbank hat am Donnerstag die besten Halbjahreszahlen ihrer Geschichte vorgelegt und zugleich einen milliardenschweren Aktienrückkauf angekündigt. Parallel nehmen die Gespräche mit der italienischen UniCredit über eine mögliche Fusion konkrete Formen an. Am Aktienmarkt kam das gut an: Der Kurs schloss am Freitag bei 39,17 Euro, ein Plus von 1,61 Prozent binnen eines Tages, und liegt damit nur noch 1,71 Prozent unter dem 52-Wochen-Hoch von 39,85 Euro, das ebenfalls am Donnerstag markiert wurde. ... Im ersten Halbjahr 2026 steigerte die Commerzbank ihr operatives Ergebnis um 14 Prozent auf 2,7 Milliarden Euro, wie das Institut in einer Pflichtmitteilung bekanntgab. Unter dem Strich stand ein Nettoergebnis von 1,8 Milliarden Euro – ebenfalls ein Rekordwert. Allein im zweiten Quartal verdiente die Bank 898 Millionen Euro. Die Erträge legten im Halbjahr um 7 Prozent auf 6,5 Milliarden Euro zu, im zweiten Quartal sogar um 9 Prozent auf 3,3 Milliarden Euro. ... Getragen wurde das Wachstum auch vom Provisionsgeschäft: Der Provisionsüberschuss kletterte im Halbjahr um 8 Prozent auf 2,2 Milliarden Euro. Gleichzeitig drückte die Bank ihre Kosten-Ertrags-Relation inklusive Pflichtbeiträgen auf 53 Prozent, ohne diese Beiträge lag sie bei 50 Prozent. Damit bestätigte das Institut, wie es selbst mitteilte, seinen Ausblick für das Gesamtjahr: Man sei voll auf Kurs, das Gewinnziel von mindestens 3,4 Milliarden Euro zu erreichen. ... Zusätzlich zu den operativen Fortschritten kündigte die Commerzbank einen weiteren Aktienrückkauf von bis zu 1,2 Milliarden Euro an, den die Europäische Zentralbank bereits genehmigt hat. Für Anleger ist das ein Signal, dass die Bank trotz der schwebenden Übernahmefrage weiter Kapital an die Eigentümer zurückgeben will, statt es zu horten. Die Kombination aus Rekordgewinn, bestätigter Guidance und Rückkaufprogramm dürfte die zuletzt schon deutlich gestiegene Bewertung – die Aktie liegt seit Jahresbeginn 8,50 Prozent im Plus und binnen zwölf Monaten 17,95 Prozent höher – zusätzlich untermauert haben. ... Die Zahlenvorlage am Donnerstag fiel zeitlich mit einem weiteren Schritt in der Übernahmeschlacht um die Commerzbank zusammen: An genau diesem Tag waren laut Medienberichten Gespräche zwischen Commerzbank und UniCredit angesetzt. Das Institut hatte bereits am 27. Juli seinen Widerstand gegen eine Fusion mit den Italienern aufgegeben, wie berichtet wurde – ein Kurswechsel nach monatelanger Abwehrhaltung. UniCredit-Chef Andrea Orcel hatte sich zuvor, am 23. Juli, zuversichtlich gezeigt, Spielraum für eine Einigung mit der Bundesregierung und weiteren Stakeholdern zu finden. ... Auch aus Berlin kamen zuletzt versöhnlichere Signale. Statt die Übernahme weiter zu blockieren, arbeitete die Bundesregierung Mitte Juli an möglichen Bedingungen für Verhandlungen. Bundeskanzler Merz hatte bereits auf seiner Sommerpressekonferenz erklärt: „Wir verhindern nicht diese Fusion.“ Zur Erinnerung: UniCredit hatte bis zum Ablauf einer Annahmefrist Anfang Juli bereits 17,6 Prozent der Commerzbank-Aktien angedient bekommen. Die Ratingagentur S&P hatte Mitte Juli ihren Ratingausblick für die Commerzbank gesenkt und dabei ausdrücklich auf die drohende Integration in den UniCredit-Konzern verwiesen – ein Hinweis darauf, dass Ratingagenturen die Fusion inzwischen als wahrscheinliches Szenario einpreisen. ... Die Rekordzahlen sorgten am Donnerstag für eine Reihe von Analystenreaktionen. Die DZ Bank hob ihr Kursziel von 42 auf 46 Euro an und bekräftigte ihre Kaufempfehlung. RBC Capital Markets bestätigte die Einstufung „Outperform“ mit einem Kursziel von 43 Euro und lobte, das zweite Quartal habe die Erwartungen übertroffen, wertete den Geschäftsmix aber als durchwachsen. Auch JPMorgan und die Deutsche Bank Research reagierten: JPMorgan erhöhte sein Kursziel leicht von 37 auf 38 Euro, blieb aber bei „Neutral“, während die Deutsche Bank Research ihre Kaufempfehlung mit einem Kursziel von 42 Euro bestätigte. Die Bandbreite der Kursziele reicht damit von 38 bis 46 Euro – durchweg über dem aktuellen Kursniveau, was die grundsätzlich positive Einschätzung der Rekordzahlen unterstreicht, auch wenn einzelne Häuser beim Fusionsthema vorsichtig bleiben. ... #### Commerzbank Aktie: 3,4 Milliarden Euro Gewinnziel ... #### Commerzbank Aktie: UniCredit-Strategie wird positiver bewertet ... #### Commerzbank Aktie: Orcel hält Übernahme im Q4 für möglich ... #### Commerzbank Aktie: Orlopp öffnet sich für UniCredit-Dialog"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Q2: Nettogewinn springt 94% auf 898 Millionen Euro,www.ad-hoc-news.de (Redaktion ad-hoc-news.de),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/wissenschaft/commerzbank-q2-nettogewinn-springt-94-percent-auf-898-millionen-euro/69925456,"Commerzbank Q2: Nettogewinn springt 94% auf 898 Millionen Euro ... Die Vorstandsvorsitzende der Commerzbank, Bettina Orlopp, hat den offiziellen Beginn von Gesprächen mit der italienischen Großbank UniCredit über eine potenzielle Übernahme bestätigt. Eine erste Verhandlungsrunde zwischen den beiden Instituten ist für diesen Freitag angesetzt. Damit tritt der seit Wochen diskutierte Konsolidierungsprozess in eine neue, formelle Phase ein. ... Die UniCredit hat ihre Position gegenüber dem deutschen Mitbewerber massiv ausgebaut. Aktuell hält das italienische Geldhaus 47,59 Prozent des Kapitals sowie 49,65 Prozent der Stimmrechte an der Commerzbank. Weitere 11,48 Prozent sind über Derivate abgesichert. Das Übernahmeangebot der UniCredit beläuft sich auf ein Volumen von rund 45 Milliarden Euro, was einem Preis von etwa 31 Euro pro Aktie entspricht. ... Trotz der Aufnahme von Gesprächen formulierte Orlopp klare Bedingungen für eine mögliche Integration. Sie forderte die Beibehaltung der Börsennotierung der Commerzbank und lehnte einseitige strukturelle Änderungen durch die UniCredit ab. Dennoch räumte die Vorstandsvorsitzende ein, dass ein Zusammenschluss grundsätzlich Potenzial für eine gemeinsame Wertschöpfung biete. ... Die Commerzbank untermauert ihre Eigenständigkeit und Verhandlungsposition durch eine positive Geschäftsentwicklung im ersten Halbjahr 2026. Im zweiten Quartal stieg der Nettogewinn im Vergleich zum Vorjahreszeitraum um 94 Prozent auf 898 Millionen Euro und übertraf damit die Erwartungen der Analysten, die im Konsens von 845 Millionen Euro ausgegangen waren. Der operative Gewinn kletterte um 17 Prozent auf 1,37 Milliarden Euro, während der Umsatz um 9 Prozent auf 3,30 Milliarden Euro zulegte. ... Für das gesamte erste Halbjahr verzeichnete die Bank einen Rekord-Nettogewinn von 1,8 Milliarden Euro, was einem Zuwachs von 40 Prozent entspricht. Der operative Gewinn im Halbjahr lag bei 2,7 Milliarden Euro. Angesichts dieser Zahlen strebt das Institut ein Jahresgewinnziel von mindestens 3,4 Milliarden Euro an. Zudem wurde ein Aktienrückkaufprogramm in Höhe von 1,2 Milliarden Euro angekündigt. Die harte Kernkapitalquote (CET1) lag zuletzt bei soliden 14,4 Prozent. ... Der geplante Zusammenschluss steht vor komplexen regulatorischen Prüfungen. Die Bundesanstalt für Finanzdienstleistungsaufsicht (BaFin) hatte der UniCredit bereits Ende Juli 2026 genehmigt, die Schwelle von 30 Prozent am Kapital der Commerzbank zu überschreiten. Die endgültige Entscheidung der Europäischen Zentralbank (EZB) über den formellen Antrag der UniCredit wird für die zweite Oktoberhälfte erwartet; die Behörde verfügt über einen Prüfungszeitraum von 60 Arbeitstagen, der um weitere 20 Tage verlängert werden kann. ... Zusätzlich müssen Genehmigungen der EU-Wettbewerbsbehörden, der US-Notenbank Fed sowie polnischer Aufsichtsbehörden eingeholt werden. Auch die Europäische Bankenaufsichtsbehörde (EBA) wird die Fusion prüfen. Die deutsche Bundesregierung, die weiterhin einen Anteil von 12,7 Prozent an der Commerzbank hält, äußerte sich kritisch zum aggressiven Vorgehen der UniCredit. ... Im Falle einer erfolgreichen Integration ist mit signifikanten Auswirkungen auf die Belegschaft zu rechnen. Schätzungen zufolge könnten etwa 18 Prozent der kombinierten Belegschaft in den ersten 24 Monaten von einem Stellenabbau betroffen sein. Aufgrund der erforderlichen Genehmigungsverfahren wird eine tatsächliche Integration der beiden Institute frühestens für das Jahr 2027 erwartet. UniCredit proletarier prognostiziert, dass die Übernahme die eigene CET1-Quote um etwa 280 Basispunkte belasten würde, diese jedoch weiterhin über 13 Prozent verbleiben werde."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank seeks accommodation with UniCredit in takeover fight | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-seeks-accommodation-with-unicredit-in-takeover-fight-ce7f50dddb8af220,"Commerzbank seeks accommodation with UniCredit in takeover fight | MarketScreener ... | COMMERZBANK AG ... # Commerzbank seeks accommodation with UniCredit in takeover fight ... In its takeover fight with UniCredit, Commerzbank is moving toward an accommodation with its largest shareholder. ""We have started talks on this,"" Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp said on Thursday as she presented the half-year results. ""I am optimistic that, step by step, we can find common ground on corporate governance and also the business model."" Talks were in the interests of both banks in order to create value for shareholders, customers and employees. The federal government, as the second-largest shareholder, was included in the discussions. ""We are in close coordination."" ... Italy's major bank UniCredit wants to take over Commerzbank and has secured nearly half of the shares. But UniCredit still cannot run the show outright, Orlopp stressed. ""Even if UniCredit has a majority at the next annual general meeting, it cannot decide on major structural measures on its own,"" the Commerzbank CEO said. ""That is a clear mandate for both sides to shape the outcome."" That would require a shared understanding of the business model and the involvement of all stakeholders. ... On Wednesday, the German government had called for talks between the two banks. Asked in Berlin about Commerzbank's upcoming quarterly figures, a government spokesperson said Commerzbank and UniCredit now had to discuss what happens next. Employees needed a secure perspective. At the same time, the German government continued to reject the Italian bank's ""aggressive approach"". ... UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel had announced he would speak with the German government and the works council about a shared future for his group with Commerzbank. The Italian did not mention Commerzbank's management board led by Bettina Orlopp as a counterpart for talks. Commerzbank supervisory board chairman Jens Weidmann, by contrast, had urged UniCredit to hold direct talks with the management board, effectively acknowledging that there is no longer any way around a power grab by the Milan-based major bank. ... Orlopp had long fought for Commerzbank's independence, but after the outcome of the takeover offer repeatedly stressed her willingness to negotiate. Before that, several attempts at talks with Orcel had produced no results. Orcel wants to impose his business model on Commerzbank, while Orlopp is insisting, among other things, on preserving the extensive international network with which the bank supports its mid-sized corporate clients as they export around the world. ... Commerzbank also benefited from its international footprint in the second quarter. Corporate banking loan volumes rose 16 percent to 123bn. ""Key drivers were investments by German and international corporate clients abroad,"" the institution said. ... Overall, Commerzbank posted record profits in the first half, according to its own figures: Operating profit rose 14 percent to 2.7bn. Net profit jumped 40 percent to 1.81bn, beating analysts' expectations. Quarterly profit nearly doubled, rising to 898m. Commerzbank said it remains on track to reach its full-year profit target of at least 3.4bn. Commerzbank shares were little changed. ... ### Latest news about Commerzbank AG ... | Aug. 06 | COMMERZBANK AG : JP Morgan remains Neutral | ZD | | --- | --- | --- | | Aug. 06 | JPMorgan raises Commerzbank target to 38, 'Neutral' | DP | | Aug. 06 | Europe in buy-side mode, new record for the MIB | AN | | Aug. 06 | Powered by Hermès, Paris reaches uncharted highs | | | Aug. 06 | COMMERZBANK AG : DZ Bank reiterates its Buy rating | ZD | | Aug. 06 | Frankfurt stocks close: Dax little changed at earnings season peak | DP | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank wants to reach an understanding with UniCredit | RE | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank AG Reports Earnings Results for the Half Year Ended June 30, 2026 | CI | | Aug. 06 | UniCredit, Commerzbank CEOs briefly spoke but did not start merger talks, source says | RE | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank CEO Calls For Dialogue With UniCredit -- Update | DJ | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank seeks accommodation with UniCredit in takeover fight | RE | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank opens the door to UniCredit to 'create value' together | AN | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank, talks launched with UniCredit - CEO | RE | | Aug. 06 | COMMERZBANK AG : JP Morgan gives a Neutral rating | ZD | | Aug. 06 | Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration | | ... Commerzbank AG is one of the leading German banking groups. Net banking product (NBP) breaks down by activity as follows: - retail banking and private banking (57.3%): sales of classical and specialized banking products and services (consumer loans, leasing, etc.), private banking, etc.; - market and investment banking (30,4%): financial engineering, merger-acquisition consulting, stock operations, specialized and structured financing, capital market operations, etc.; - other (12.3%): public works financing, specialized and structured financing, mortgage loans, etc. ... Aug. 05 Earnings release - Q2 2026 ... Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration August 06, 2026 at 05:43 am EDT"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Reports 94% Profit Gain Amid Potential UniCredit Takeover,www.globalbankingandfinance.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globalbankingandfinance.com/commerzbank-facing-possible-unicredit-takeover-posts-94/,"Commerzbank Reports 94% Profit Gain Amid Potential UniCredit Takeover ... # Commerzbank, facing possible UniCredit takeover, posts 94% profit gain ... ## Commerzbank CEO says takeover by UniCredit can create value ... FRANKFURT, Aug 6 (Reuters) - Commerzbank's Chief Executive Bettina Orlopp said on Thursday a tie-up with UniCredit could create value for both sides, in a significant shift of tone as she looks to direct talks with her counterpart Andrea Orcel. ... Germany's second-biggest bank has been a fierce opponent of UniCredit's overtures, but after a nearly two-year battle to fend off the Milan-based lender it has given up the fight in recent weeks as UniCredit last month secured a 48% stake in Commerzbank, giving it effective control. ... Orlopp said on Thursday Commerzbank had begun talks with UniCredit and that she was ""optimistic"" both sides could find common ground. ... However, Orcel, the architect of one of the most contentious European banking battles in decades, has said he wants to negotiate directly with the German government, which has criticised UniCredit's aggressive attitude and owns around 12% of the bank, and with Commerzbank employees, bypassing management. ... The format of the talks is not clear, but Orlopp's conciliatory tone precedes months of likely negotiations as UniCredit waits for regulatory approvals to be declared in control of Commerzbank , and when and how it will try to buy the rest of the bank it does not own. ... Orlopp and Orcel met on the sidelines of a private event in July, a source close to UniCredit said. The two discussed accounting measures and other steps related to UniCredit's taking control, the person said, adding it ""was not the start of any negotiation."" ... After seeing through a €45 billion ($52 billion) hostile takeover bid for Commerzbank helped by a skilful use of derivatives, UniCredit has outlined pre-merger plans it wants the Frankfurt-based lender to follow to boost profits. ... ""We have started talks on this, which is in the genuine interest of both UniCredit and Commerzbank, as we are both determined to create value for our shareholders, clients and employees,"" Orlopp told analysts. ... ""I'm optimistic that, step by step, we can find common ground on governance and also on the business model."" ... Orcel said UniCredit has laid out a roadmap it wants in place from January and is ready to call an extraordinary shareholder vote to appoint a new supervisory board at Commerzbank if necessary. ... UniCredit and Commerzbank have been holding post-earnings investor meetings since the Milanese lender became a shareholder. Thursday also offered an opportunity for both management teams to exchange views in an investor call. ... Orlopp said on Thursday it was in the best interest of both banks to move as quickly as possible and that they would try to identify possible cost savings and whether the banks could join forces on large investment programmes. ... A Commerzbank presentation also showed the company's increasing willingness to work with UniCredit on a deal since the Italian bank built its 48% stake in the German lender. ... Orlopp said UniCredit, even with that large stake, needs to work with her management team on a path forward rather than act unilaterally on any structural changes. ... ""It requires a shared understanding of the business model and the involvement of all stakeholders,"" she said after Commerzbank reported a 94% jump in second-quarter net profit to €898 million, helped by stronger commission income. ... The earnings beat analyst expectations of €845 million in a consensus forecast published by the bank. ... A person familiar with UniCredit's thinking said before the results announcement that the Italian suitor was watching to see if Commerzbank shifts focus to Germany and away from international lending and trading, exposing a difference in opinion on strategy. ... Commerzbank has said its international network is key to its strategy. ... The German Finance Ministry, which oversees a 12% stake that the government has held since Commerzbank's bailout during the global financial crisis, said through a spokesperson that it was up to the two banks to discuss how to proceed and criticised UniCredit's ""aggressive approach"". ... German opposition to Orcel's overtures has been widespread, underscoring ⁠the difficulty of merging large banks across euro zone countries to help them compete with bigger U.S. rivals. ... - Q2 net profit soared to €898 million from €462 million YoY, outperforming the €845 million analyst consensus - UniCredit’s unsolicited takeover bid—an exchange offer valuing Commerzbank at around €31 per share—has barely attracted independent shareholders, with under 2 % participation - Commerzbank rejects the bid as low‑ball and risky, asserting its standalone “Momentum 2030” strategy delivers stronger value for shareholders ... Commerzbank's net profit rose by 94% in the second quarter to €898 million. ... The article credits improved performance and strong quarterly results for the 94% profit gain. ... Commerzbank is nearing a possible takeover by Italy's UniCredit, potentially impacting market dynamics. ... Yes, the net profit of €898 million topped analysts' average expectation of €845 million."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank sets out UniCredit talks plan | IFR,www.ifre.com (Christopher Spink),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ifre.com/people-and-markets/2466720/commerzbank-sets-out-unicredit-talks-plan,Commerzbank sets out UniCredit talks plan | IFR ... # Commerzbank sets out UniCredit talks plan
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank posts 94% quarterly profit gain as UniCredit talks begin; Wall Street bonuses set to rise - The Banker,www.thebanker.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thebanker.com/content/411d0c4d-07d6-4cb9-ab66-3c51318e21ed,"Commerzbank posts 94% quarterly profit gain as UniCredit talks begin; Wall Street bonuses set to rise - The Banker ... # Commerzbank posts 94% quarterly profit gain as UniCredit talks begin; Wall Street bonuses set to rise ... Commerzbank, which is edging closer to a takeover by Italy’s UniCredit, has reported a second-quarter net profit of €898mn, up 94 per cent from a year earlier and ahead of analyst forecasts. ... The record performance was helped by strong commission income and the absence of €534mn in restructuring expenses booked in the first half of 2025."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank: Record profit strengthens hand in talks with Unicredit | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (dpa-AFX),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-record-profit-strengthens-hand-in-talks-with-unicredit-ce7f50dcd08cf321,"Commerzbank: Record profit strengthens hand in talks with Unicredit | MarketScreener ... # Commerzbank: Record profit strengthens hand in talks with Unicredit ... FRANKFURT (dpa-AFX) - After a surprisingly strong jump in second-quarter profit, Commerzbank says it feels strengthened for further talks with its Milan-based major shareholder. ""We are ready for constructive talks with Unicredit,"" the Frankfurt-based DAX group said on Thursday. A joint approach has the potential to create added value. In the market, Commerzbank shares eased somewhat after their recent surge. ... From April to June 2026, Germany's second-largest listed bank nearly doubled its bottom-line profit from a year earlier. Net income rose from 462m to 898m, beating analysts' average expectations. A year earlier, however, costs tied to cutting thousands of jobs had weighed on the bank's profit. ... After a record result of 1.8bn in the first half, the management board sees Commerzbank ""fully on track to meet its profit target of at least 3.4bn for the full year"". ... The bank now plans to spend up to another 1.2bn on buybacks of its own shares. With share buybacks and higher profits, the management team led by Bettina Orlopp aimed to keep shareholders on board and thereby safeguard the independence of the institution, founded in 1870. ... But Italy's Unicredit, nearly two years after taking a stake in Commerzbank, now has access to almost half of the shares. Unicredit CEO Andrea Orcel said recently that he expects a near-term takeover of control at the Frankfurt-based institution. ... ""Even if Unicredit has a majority at the next annual general meeting, it cannot decide on major structural measures on its own,"" Commerzbank CEO Orlopp said. ""That is a clear mandate to shape outcomes for both sides. That requires a shared understanding of the business model and the involvement of all stakeholders."" ... The federal government, whose share sale in September 2024 became Unicredit's point of entry, still has a say with its remaining stake of just over 12%. The holding is a legacy of the 2008/2009 financial crisis, when the state saved the institution from collapse with taxpayer billions. ... With a takeover of Commerzbank, Orcel wants to forge a European banking heavyweight, also as a counterweight to the far more profitable lenders in the US. Unicredit is already active in Germany through Hypovereinsbank (HVB) and sees potential for billions in savings, including the elimination of thousands of positions. From Commerzbank's perspective, the Italians' ""hostile approach"" is meeting significant resistance from management, the works council, and staff at the DAX group. The federal government has also repeatedly voiced criticism. ... Unicredit, however, did not let up and by early July, through a voluntary takeover offer, had secured another 17.6% of Commerzbank shares, according to its own figures. Together with the 26.77% Unicredit already held, its stake thus rises arithmetically to 44.37%. In addition, the Italians have access via call options to another 3.22% of Commerzbank shares and could, according to recent figures, increase their stake to 47.59%. ... In doing so, investment banker Orcel played every trick in the book. Based on Commerzbank findings, professional investors and retail shareholders tendered just 2.7% of the shares to Unicredit as part of the takeover offer. The rest, it said, came largely from banks with which Unicredit conducts transactions via financial instruments. At one point, Commerzbank accused Unicredit of ""artificially inflating"" its equity position. To clarify the matter, the DAX group has brought in financial regulator BaFin. The outcome of that review is still pending. ... Meanwhile, a criminal complaint by Commerzbank's group works council over suspected market manipulation went nowhere: the Frankfurt public prosecutor's office declined to open an investigation, ""as sufficient factual indications of a criminal offense could not be established,"" the authority said in early July./ben/stw/DP/stw/mis ... ### Latest news about Commerzbank AG ... | 02:31am | German trade deficit with China grows as Beijing relies less on European industry | RE | | --- | --- | --- | | Aug. 07 | The Week in Oil : Diplomatic Efforts to Manage Hormuz Traffic Take Center Stage | DJ | | Aug. 07 | Currencies: Euro Gains After Weak US Jobs Report | DP | | Aug. 07 | After record run, monetary policy returns to center stage | DP | | Aug. 07 | US stocks set for higher open as surprise payrolls fall cools rate-hike bets | RE | | Aug. 07 | RBC: Ownership Structure Uncertainty Clouds Commerzbank's Long-Term Strategy; Forecasts Adjusted | MT | | Aug. 07 | COMMERZBANK AG : Buy rating from Deutsche Bank | ZD | | Aug. 07 | Euro zone bond yields slip after US economy sheds jobs in July | RE | | Aug. 07 | Commerzbank Says Oil Prices Rise on Hormuz Uncertainties, Asia Equities Mixed | MT | | Aug. 07 | European Midday Briefing : Shares Up, Oil Edges Higher as Iran-Oman Talks Remain in Focus | DJ | | Aug. 07 | Futures point to directionless markets | AN | | Aug. 07 | Cicor Technologies Secures CHF425 Million Financing | MT | | Aug. 07 | UniCredit-Commerz, first step toward EU banking consolidation | AN | | Aug. 07 | Italy - Factors to watch on August 7 | RE | | Aug. 06 | COMMERZBANK AG : JP Morgan remains Neutral | ZD | ... Commerzbank AG is one of the leading German banking groups. Net banking product (NBP) breaks down by activity as follows: - retail banking and private banking (57.3%): sales of classical and specialized banking products and services (consumer loans, leasing, etc.), private banking, etc.; - market and investment banking (30,4%): financial engineering, merger-acquisition consulting, stock operations, specialized and structured financing, capital market operations, etc.; - other (12.3%): public works financing, specialized and structured financing, mortgage loans, etc. ... Nov. 04 Earnings release - Q3 2026 ... Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration August 06, 2026 at 05:43 am EDT"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank CEO: We have started talks with Unicredit | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-ceo-we-have-started-talks-with-unicredit-ce7f50dcd08cf02c,"Commerzbank CEO: We have started talks with Unicredit | MarketScreener ... # Commerzbank CEO: We have started talks with Unicredit ... Published on ... 026 at 03:48 am EDT ... Commerzbank said it has opened talks with its major shareholder Unicredit on next steps. ""We have started talks on this,"" Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp said on Thursday on an analyst call on the quarterly results. The talks were in the interest of both banks to create value for shareholders, customers and employees. ""I am optimistic that, step by step, we can find common ground on corporate governance and also the business model,"" Orlopp said. ... ### Latest news about Commerzbank AG ... | 11:58am | Europe in buy-side mode, new record for the MIB | AN | | --- | --- | --- | | 11:54am | Powered by Hermès, Paris reaches uncharted highs | | | 11:54am | COMMERZBANK AG : DZ Bank reiterates its Buy rating | ZD | | 11:50am | Frankfurt stocks close: Dax little changed at earnings season peak | DP | | 09:00am | Commerzbank wants to reach an understanding with UniCredit | RE | | 08:11am | Commerzbank AG Reports Earnings Results for the Half Year Ended June 30, 2026 | CI | | 07:59am | UniCredit, Commerzbank CEOs briefly spoke but did not start merger talks, source says | RE | | 07:49am | Commerzbank CEO Calls For Dialogue With UniCredit -- Update | DJ | | 07:34am | Commerzbank seeks accommodation with UniCredit in takeover fight | RE | | 07:09am | Commerzbank opens the door to UniCredit to 'create value' together | AN | | 06:40am | Commerzbank, talks launched with UniCredit - CEO | RE | | 06:32am | COMMERZBANK AG : JP Morgan gives a Neutral rating | ZD | | 05:43am | Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration | | | 05:28am | Commerzbank CEO Signals Talks With UniCredit for Potential Combination | MT | | 04:37am | Commerzbank Seeks 'Constructive Discussions' with UniCredit as First-half Profit Rises; EUR1.2 Billion Buyback Planned | MT | ... Commerzbank AG is one of the leading German banking groups. Net banking product (NBP) breaks down by activity as follows: - retail banking and private banking (57.3%): sales of classical and specialized banking products and services (consumer loans, leasing, etc.), private banking, etc.; - market and investment banking (30,4%): financial engineering, merger-acquisition consulting, stock operations, specialized and structured financing, capital market operations, etc.; - other (12.3%): public works financing, specialized and structured financing, mortgage loans, etc. ... Aug. 05 Earnings release - Q2 2026 ... Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration August 06, 2026 at 05:43 am EDT"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Q2 Net Result Rises; Confirms Full-year Outlook,www.rttnews.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.rttnews.com/3676478/commerzbank-q2-net-result-rises-confirms-full-year-outlook.aspx,"Commerzbank Q2 Net Result Rises; Confirms Full-year Outlook # Commerzbank Q2 Net Result Rises; Confirms Full-year Outlook By RTTNews Staff Writer ✉ | Published: 8/6/2026 2:15 AM ET | Follow Us | Join Us Commerzbank AG (1CBK.MI, CBK.DE) reported that its second quarter net result attributable to shareholders increased to 898 million euros from 462 million euros, prior year. Operating result increased by around 17% to 1.37 billion euros in the second quarter. ... Second quarter revenues increased by 9% to 3.30 billion euros from 3.02 billion euros, prior year. Revenues excluding exceptional items was 3.31 billion euros, an increase of 7.2%. The Bank maintained net interest income at the prior-year level, reaching 2.06 billion euros. Net commission income rose by 7% to 1.08 billion euros. ... Commerzbank said it remains firmly on track to achieve full-year net result target of at least 3.4 billion euros. The Bank continues to expect net interest income of around 8.6 billion euros and remains committed to achieving growth in net commission income of around 7%. Commerzbank expects revenues of around 13.2 billion euros for the full year. The Bank also confirmed the targets of its Momentum 2030 strategy. At last close on the XETRA exchange, Commerzbank shares were trading at 39.35 euros, down 0.76%."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Halbjahresbilanz: Commerzbank macht Gewinnsprung | tagesschau.de,www.tagesschau.de,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tagesschau.de/wirtschaft/unternehmen/commerzbank-gewinnsprung-unicredit-uebernahme-100.html,"Halbjahresbilanz: Commerzbank macht Gewinnsprung | tagesschau.de ... # Halbjahresbilanz Commerzbank macht Gewinnsprung ... Die Commerzbank hat im ersten Halbjahr ein Rekordergebnis erzielt. Bestärkt durch die guten Zahlen blickt der Vorstand selbstbewusst auf den Übernahmeversuch der UniCredit. Zu dem Thema stehen neue Gespräche an. ... Die Commerzbank hat im zweiten Quartal fast doppelt so viel verdient wie ein Jahr zuvor. Das operative Ergebnis stieg um rund 17 Prozent auf 1,37 Milliarden Euro. Der Überschuss im Zeitraum April bis Juni legte auf 898 Millionen Euro zu, wie der DAX-Konzern mitteilte. Das war noch mehr als von Analysten erwartet. ... Das bescherte der Commerzbank im ersten Halbjahr ein Rekordergebnis: Das operative Ergebnis legte in den ersten sechs Monaten im Vergleich zum Vorjahreszeitraum um 14 Prozent auf 2,7 Milliarden Euro zu. Das Nettoergebnis kletterte um rund 40 Prozent auf 1,81 Milliarden Euro. Das Rekordergebnis aus dem ersten Halbjahr zeige, ""welche Kraft in unserem Geschäftsmodell steckt"", betonte Commerzbank-Chefin Bettina Orlopp. ... Nach einem Rekordergebnis im ersten Halbjahr sieht sich die Commerzbank nun ""voll auf Kurs, ihr Gewinnziel von mindestens 3,4 Milliarden Euro im Gesamtjahr zu erreichen"". Die Bank will weitere bis zu 1,2 Milliarden Euro in den Rückkauf eigener Aktien stecken. Es ist nicht die erste Rückkaufaktion: Bereits zuvor hatte die Bank mit Aktienrückkäufen und höheren Gewinnen Aktionäre bei der Stange halten wollen. ... Doch die Unabhängigkeit der zweitgrößten börsennotierten Bank Deutschlands konnte es nicht sichern: Die italienische Großbank UniCredit hat knapp zwei Jahre nach ihrem Einstieg bei der Commerzbank inzwischen Zugriff auf fast die Hälfte der Anteile. UniCredit-Chef Andrea Orcel erwartet nach jüngsten Aussagen eine baldige Kontrollübernahme bei dem Frankfurter Institut. Bald stehen neue Gespräche an. ... Mit den dafür nötigen Genehmigungen der Aufseher sei vielleicht noch in diesem Jahr zu rechnen, sagte Orcel vor wenigen Tagen. Kurz danach werde man die Kontrolle über die Commerzbank übernehmen und die Strategie implementieren. Wenn nötig, werde UniCredit eine außerordentliche Hauptversammlung einberufen, heißt es in der Präsentation weiter. ... Orlopp gibt sich trotzdem kämpferisch: ""Auch wenn die UniCredit über eine Mehrheit auf der nächsten Hauptversammlung verfügt, kann sie über wesentliche Strukturmaßnahmen nicht allein entscheiden"", bekräftigte Orlopp. ""Das ist ein klarer Gestaltungsauftrag für beide Seiten. Dafür braucht es ein gemeinsames Verständnis des Geschäftsmodells und die Einbindung aller Stakeholder."" ... Die Übernahme durch die UniCredit ist weder dem Commerzbank-Vorstand unter Orlopp, noch den Arbeitnehmern, noch der Bundesregierung willkommen. Es wird vielmehr von einer ""feindlichen Übernahme gesprochen"". ... Der Bund, dessen Aktienverkauf im September 2024 zum Einfallstor für die UniCredit wurde, hält noch gut zwölf Prozent der Anteile. Die Beteiligung ist eine Folge der Finanzkrise 2008/2009, als der Staat das Institut mit Steuermilliarden vor dem Kollaps bewahrte."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Seeks 'Constructive Discussions' with UniCredit as First-half Profit Rises; EUR1.2 Billion Buyback Planned | MarketScreener UK,uk.marketscreener.com (MT Newswires),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uk.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-seeks-constructive-discussions-with-unicredit-as-first-half-profit-rises-eur1-2-billi-ce7f50ddd989f723,"Commerzbank Seeks 'Constructive Discussions' with UniCredit as First-half Profit Rises; EUR1.2 Billion Buyback Planned | MarketScreener UK # Commerzbank AG ## Stocks ## CBK ## DE000CBK1001 ## Banks 1st Jan Change 39.48 EUR +0.34% +5.65% +9.28% | 12:09pm | Commerzbank opens the door to UniCredit to 'create value' together | AN | | --- | --- | --- | | 11:40am | Commerzbank, talks launched with UniCredit - CEO | RE | ... # Commerzbank Seeks 'Constructive Discussions' with UniCredit as First-half Profit Rises; EUR1.2 Billion Buyback Planned Published on 08/06/2026 at 09:37 am BST"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank sucht nach Rekordgewinn Zukunft mit Unicredit | FAZ,www.faz.net (Hanno Mußler),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.faz.net/aktuell/finanzen/finanzmarkt/commerzbank-sucht-nach-rekordgewinn-zukunft-mit-unicredit-accg-201098935.html,"„Unicredit kann auch mit Mehrheit nicht allein entscheiden“: Zukunft der Commerzbank | FAZ ... Die Vorstandsvorsitzende der Commerzbank will mit ihrem ungeliebten Großaktionär Unicredit in den nächsten Tagen und Wochen „einen konstruktiven Dialog“ führen, um künftig gemeinsam „Wert für alle“ zu schaffen. Das kündigte Bettina Orlopp am Donnerstag an, nachdem die Commerzbank einen Rekordgewinn für das Jahr 2026 vorgelegt hatte. In einer Telefonkonferenz mit Journalisten erkannte Orlopp die Realität insofern an, als sie davon ausging, dass Unicredit im vierten Quartal 2026 alle erforderlichen aufsichtsrechtlichen Genehmigungen erhalten haben wird, um über ihren Anteil von derzeit gut 47 Prozent mit Stimmrechten an der Commerzbank zu verfügen. Ob und wann es eine außerordentliche Hauptversammlung geben werde, könne sie nicht sagen. „Das müssen Sie Unicredit fragen“, antwortete Orlopp auf eine Frage der F.A.Z. Es werde aber im Frühjahr 2027, voraussichtlich im Mai, ein reguläres Aktionärstreffen geben, daran anschließend werde die Commerzbank abermals eine höhere Dividende zahlen, rund die Hälfte des Jahresgewinns. Die andere Hälfte des Jahresgewinns will sie für Aktienrückkäufe verwenden."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Opens UniCredit Merger Talks After 94% Profit Surge Sets Asking Price,"www.techtimes.com (Ryan Cook Published: Aug 06 2026, 1:39 PM EDT)",2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.techtimes.com/articles/323375/20260806/commerzbank-opens-unicredit-merger-talks-after-94-profit-surge-sets-asking-price.htm,"Germany's Commerzbank formally opened merger negotiations with Italy's UniCredit on Thursday, August 6 — the same morning it reported a 94% surge in second-quarter net profit, a strategic double-play that transformed Germany's second-largest private bank from a cornered acquisition target into a willing negotiator with an unusually strong hand. ... Commerzbank's Q2 2026 net profit surged 94% year-on-year to €898 million (approximately $1.04 billion), beating the analyst consensus of €845 million (approximately $976 million) and marking a record operating profit for any single quarter in the bank's history. Operating profit for the quarter reached €1.37 billion (approximately $1.58 billion), up 17% year-on-year, as total revenues expanded 9% to €3.30 billion (approximately $3.81 billion). ... Net commission income climbed 7.2% to €1.08 billion (approximately $1.25 billion), while net interest income held broadly stable at €2.06 billion (approximately $2.38 billion) for the quarter. For the first half of 2026, Commerzbank posted record net profit of €1.8 billion(approximately $2.08 billion), up 40% from the prior-year period. ... The bank also announced a €1.2 billion (approximately $1.39 billion) share buyback — pending approval from Germany's Finance Agency — and reaffirmed its full-year capital return target of approximately €3.2 billion (approximately $3.69 billion) through buybacks and dividends. Its Common Equity Tier 1 capital buffer remained robust at 14.4%, and its net return on tangible equity of 12.6% was described by the company as a record result. ... The Thursday announcement closed the curtain on a corporate brinkmanship campaign that began in September 2024, when UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel quietly outbid rivals in a German government sale of Commerzbank shares, acquiring a 4.5% stake that, combined with a prior open-market purchase, gave the Milan-based lender a sudden 9% foothold. German officials labeled the move a""hostile attack"" on national financial sovereignty. ... By March 2025, the European Central Bank had granted UniCredit approval to lift its stake to 29.9%. In March 2026, Orcel escalated further, launching a formal voluntary exchange offer under German takeover law (WpÜG) valued at approximately €35 billion (approximately $40.4 billion) at launch — a figure analysts have estimated could reach €45 billion (approximately $52 billion) accounting for UniCredit's full position. ... 's board rejected the offer in April 2026 as ""financially inadequate"" with a ""vague plan"" carrying ""considerable execution risks."" When the acceptance period closed on July 3, 2026, only about 17.6% of Commerzbank shares had been tendered — and Commerzbank's ... For readers with accounts at Commerzbank or business relationships with the bank, the negotiated merger path is better news than the hostile alternative — but it is not cost-free. Commerzbank has already announced 6,900 cumulative defensive job cuts across two restructuring rounds in 2025 and 2026, against a workforce that stood at approximately 40,000 at the start of the year. Germany's banking union ver.di has estimated that a UniCredit-driven integration could put 10,000 Commerzbank positions at risk, particularly in IT, administration, and back-office functions. ... A merger between Commerzbank and HypoVereinsbank — UniCredit's existing German subsidiary, with approximately €263.5 billion ($304.4 billion) in total assets — is not expected to proceed until after Commerzbank has been ""strengthened and transformed,"" per UniCredit's own public statements. When it does, the combined entity would become Germany's second-largest private lender after Deutsche Bank and, measured by total assets, potentially the eurozone's largest bank. ... Commerzbank's standalone argument has an increasingly concrete technological dimension. Its ""Momentum 2030"" strategy commits approximately €600 million (approximately $693 million) in cumulative AI investments between 2026 and 2030, targeting a 70% reduction in some operating costs, a 20% revenue uplift, and improved risk controls. Its virtual retail banking assistant ""Ava"" now handles approximately 30,000 customer inquiries per month, with more than 70% resolved autonomously, and the bank has deployed AI in partnership with fraud-detection firm Hawk to tackle money laundering. ... The path to a completed merger remains lined with regulatory and political hurdles. The ECB has yet to grant formal approval for UniCredit's acquisition of controlling interest — a decision expected in the fourth quarter of 2026. UniCredit CEO Orcel has publicly targeted Q4 2026 as his completion window, with the qualifier ""maybe later"" acknowledging the persistent uncertainty that has defined the saga throughout. ... S&P Global Ratings affirmed Commerzbank's long-term issuer credit rating at ""A"" but cut its outlook from ""positive"" to ""stable"" in July 2026, citing a specific risk: a full operational absorption into UniCredit could strip Commerzbank of the independent capital buffers that had previously positioned it for a potential upgrade. The agency's caution stands in deliberate contrast to the equity market's enthusiasm: Commerzbank shares have risen approximately 8% since the start of 2026, touching a 52-week high of €39.72 (approximately $45.86) in mid-July. ... Germany's federal government, which still holds a 12% stake in Commerzbank, has softened its position under Chancellor Friedrich Merz, who stated publicly that Berlin would not block a merger in principle — but the government has not tendered its shares, and Hesse's state premier Boris Rhein has separately called for guarantees on headquarters and employment. ... For Orlopp, Thursday's dual-header — a record profit quarter and a formal seat at the negotiating table — represents the strongest possible position from which to shape that outcome in Commerzbank's interest. Whether the final terms protect a separate Frankfurt listing, shield Mittelstand lending relationships, and preserve enough of the AI-led ""Momentum 2030"" strategy to justify the deal will be the test of whether two years of fierce resistance produced a better outcome than capitulation would have. ... The European Central Bank has not yet issued its formal approval for UniCredit's acquisition of controlling interest in Commerzbank. A decision is expected in the fourth quarter of 2026. The ECB has historically and publicly supported European cross-border bank consolidation as a way to build institutions that can compete with American and Asian rivals. However, the ECB's approval may come with capital requirements attached — potentially raising the cost of the acquisition to UniCredit and complicating the deal's economics. S&P Global Ratings flagged this specific risk when it cut Commerzbank's credit outlook to ""stable"" in July 2026, warning that a full operational absorption could erode Commerzbank's independent capital buffers. ... The employment picture is the most concrete consumer concern. Commerzbank has already cut approximately 6,900 positions in two defensive restructuring rounds since early 2025. Ver.di, Germany's banking union, estimates that a UniCredit-driven integration could put 10,000 Commerzbank jobs at risk — particularly in IT, administration, and back-office roles. For small and medium-sized business customers, the risk is more structural than immediate: Commerzbank has long positioned itself as the primary lender to Germany's Mittelstand — the family-owned small and medium enterprise ecosystem that employs roughly 60% of the German private-sector workforce and generates 68% of the country's exports. Critics of the deal, including former Supervisory Board Chairman Jens Weidmann, have pointed to the evolution of HypoVereinsbank and Bank Austria after their 2005 absorption into UniCredit as evidence that German and Austrian banking footprints tend to shrink under Milan's ownership."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"JPMorgan raises Commerzbank target to &#128;38, 'Neutral' | MarketScreener UK",uk.marketscreener.com (dpa-AFX),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uk.marketscreener.com/news/jpmorgan-raises-commerzbank-target-to-128-38-neutral-ce7f50ddd08ff125,"JPMorgan raises Commerzbank target to 38, 'Neutral' | MarketScreener UK ... # JPMorgan raises Commerzbank target to 38, 'Neutral' Published on 08/06/2026 at 10:24 pm BST - Modified on 08/06/2026 at 10:51 pm BST dpa-AFX - Translated by Marketscreener NEW YORK (dpa-AFX) - US bank JPMorgan has raised its price target for Commerzbank to €38 from €37 following the recently published quarterly results, and maintained its 'Neutral' rating. He slightly increased his estimate for the lender's adjusted earnings per share this year, Kian Abouhossein wrote in a study released on Thursday. He now expects somewhat higher revenue and lower costs./rob/la/he ... Commerzbank AG is one of the leading German banking groups. Net banking product (NBP) breaks down by activity as follows: - retail banking and private banking (57.3%): sales of classical and specialized banking products and services (consumer loans, leasing, etc.), private banking, etc.; - market and investment banking (30,4%): financial engineering, merger-acquisition consulting, stock operations, specialized and structured financing, capital market operations, etc.; - other (12.3%): public works financing, specialized and structured financing, mortgage loans, etc. ### Ratings Trader"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,„Unicredit kann auch mit Mehrheit nicht allein entscheiden“: Zukunft der Commerzbank | FAZ,www.faz.net (Hanno Mußler),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.faz.net/aktuell/finanzen/finanzmarkt/unicredit-kann-auch-mit-mehrheit-nicht-allein-entscheiden-zukunft-der-commerzbank-accg-201098935.html,"„Unicredit kann auch mit Mehrheit nicht allein entscheiden“: Zukunft der Commerzbank | FAZ ... Die Vorstandsvorsitzende der Commerzbank will mit ihrem ungeliebten Großaktionär Unicredit in den nächsten Tagen und Wochen „einen konstruktiven Dialog“ führen, um künftig gemeinsam „Wert für alle“ zu schaffen. Das kündigte Bettina Orlopp am Donnerstag an, nachdem die Commerzbank einen Rekordgewinn für das Jahr 2026 vorgelegt hatte. In einer Telefonkonferenz mit Journalisten erkannte Orlopp die Realität insofern an, als sie davon ausging, dass Unicredit im vierten Quartal 2026 alle erforderlichen aufsichtsrechtlichen Genehmigungen erhalten haben wird, um über ihren Anteil von derzeit gut 47 Prozent mit Stimmrechten an der Commerzbank zu verfügen. Ob und wann es eine außerordentliche Hauptversammlung geben werde, könne sie nicht sagen. „Das müssen Sie Unicredit fragen“, antwortete Orlopp auf eine Frage der F.A.Z. Es werde aber im Frühjahr 2027, voraussichtlich im Mai, ein reguläres Aktionärstreffen geben, daran anschließend werde die Commerzbank abermals eine höhere Dividende zahlen, rund die Hälfte des Jahresgewinns. Die andere Hälfte des Jahresgewinns will sie für Aktienrückkäufe verwenden."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Dax-Konzern vor Übernahme?: Commerzbank: Mit Rekordgewinn in Gespräche mit der Unicredit,www.tagesspiegel.de,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tagesspiegel.de/wirtschaft/dax-konzern-vor-ubernahme-commerzbank-mit-rekordgewinn-in-gesprache-mit-der-unicredit-15918400.html,"Dax-Konzern vor Übernahme?: Commerzbank: Mit Rekordgewinn in Gespräche mit der Unicredit ... Die Commerzbank sieht sich nach einem überraschend kräftigen Gewinnsprung im zweiten Quartal gestärkt für weitere Gespräche mit ihrer Großaktionärin aus Mailand. „Wir sind bereit für konstruktive Gespräche mit der Unicredit“, sagte Commerzbank-Chefin Bettina Orlopp. Nur ein gemeinsamer Ansatz habe das Potenzial, Mehrwert zu schaffen. ... De facto habe die Commerzbank nun „einen Kontrollaktionär“, sagte Orlopp in einer Telefonkonferenz mit Journalistinnen und Journalisten. „Vom Zeitplan gehen wir davon aus, dass es im vierten Quartal die Genehmigungen alle geben wird“, sagte sie mit Blick auf Prüfungen der Unicredit-Pläne durch die Aufseher. ... Von April bis Juni 2026 verdiente Deutschlands zweitgrößte börsennotierte Bank unter dem Strich fast doppelt so viel wie ein Jahr zuvor. Der Überschuss kletterte von 462 Millionen Euro auf 898 Millionen Euro. Ein Jahr zuvor hatten allerdings Kosten für den Abbau von Tausenden Jobs den Gewinn geschmälert. ... Nach einem Rekordergebnis von 1,8 Milliarden Euro im ersten Halbjahr sieht der Vorstand die Commerzbank „voll auf Kurs, ihr Gewinnziel von mindestens 3,4 Milliarden Euro im Gesamtjahr zu erreichen“. ... Der Frankfurter Dax-Konzern will nun weitere bis zu 1,2 Milliarden Euro in den Rückkauf eigener Aktien stecken. Mit Aktienrückkäufen und höheren Gewinnen wollte der Vorstand um Konzernchefin Orlopp die Aktionäre bei der Stange halten und so die Unabhängigkeit des 1870 gegründeten Instituts sichern. ... Doch die italienische Großbank Unicredit hat knapp zwei Jahre nach ihrem Einstieg bei der Commerzbank inzwischen Zugriff auf fast die Hälfte der Anteile. Unicredit-Chef Andrea Orcel erwartet nach jüngsten Aussagen eine baldige Kontrollübernahme bei dem Frankfurter Institut. ... „Auch wenn die Unicredit über eine Mehrheit auf der nächsten Hauptversammlung verfügt, kann sie über wesentliche Strukturmaßnahmen nicht allein entscheiden“, bekräftigte Commerzbank-Chefin Orlopp. „Das ist ein klarer Gestaltungsauftrag für beide Seiten. Dafür braucht es ein gemeinsames Verständnis des Geschäftsmodells und die Einbindung aller Stakeholder.“ ... Auf die Frage, ob es in den Gesprächen mit der Unicredit nun auch um die Standortfrage für eine künftige Zentrale gehe - Frankfurt oder München, wo die Unicredit-Tochter Hypovereinsbank (HVB) sitzt und die Unicredit einen neuen Büroturm errichten will - antwortete Orlopp: „Wir werden alle potenziellen Gestaltungskriterien im Hinblick auf die Zielbilder prüfen.“ ... Orcel will mit einer Übernahme der Commerzbank eine europäische Großbank schmieden, auch als Gegengewicht zu den deutlich profitableren Geldhäusern aus den USA. Die Unicredit sieht Potenzial für Milliardeneinsparungen inklusive des Abbaus Tausender Stellen. Das aus Commerzbank-Sicht „feindliche Vorgehen“ der Italiener sorgt für reichlich Widerstand bei Management, Betriebsrat und Belegschaft des Dax-Konzerns. Auch der Bund äußerte sich wiederholt kritisch. ... Die Unicredit jedoch ließ nicht locker und zog bis Anfang Juli per freiwilligem Übernahmeangebot nach eigenen Angaben weitere 17,6 Prozent der Commerzbank-Papiere an Land. Zusammen mit den 26,77 Prozent, die die Unicredit schon zuvor hielt, steigt ihr Anteil damit rechnerisch auf 44,37 Prozent. Zudem haben die Italiener über Kaufoptionen Zugriff auf weitere 3,22 Prozent der Commerzbank-Aktien und könnten so nach jüngsten Angaben auf 47,59 Prozent aufstocken. ... Dabei zog der Investmentbanker Orcel trickreich alle Register. Nach Erkenntnissen der Commerzbank dienten Profi-Investoren und Privatanleger der Unicredit im Zuge des Übernahmeangebots zusammen gerade einmal 2,7 Prozent der Anteile an. Der Rest stammt demnach überwiegend von Banken, mit denen die Unicredit über Finanzinstrumente Geschäfte macht. Zwischenzeitlich hatte die Commerzbank der Unicredit vorgeworfen, ihre Aktienposition „künstlich aufzublähen“. Zwecks Klärung hat der Dax-Konzern die Finanzaufsicht Bafin eingeschaltet. Ein Ergebnis dieser Prüfung steht aus. ... Unterdessen lief eine Strafanzeige des Commerzbank-Gesamtbetriebsrats wegen des Verdachts der Marktmanipulation ins Leere: Die Staatsanwaltschaft Frankfurt lehnte es ab, in der Sache ein Ermittlungsverfahren aufzunehmen, „da zureichende tatsächliche Anhaltspunkte für das Vorliegen einer Straftat nicht festgestellt werden konnten“, wie die Behörde Anfang Juli mitteilte."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank verdient mehr als erwartet und bestätigt Ausblick | MarketScreener Deutschland,de.marketscreener.com (Dow Jones),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://de.marketscreener.com/boerse-nachrichten/commerzbank-verdient-mehr-als-erwartet-und-bestaetigt-ausblick-ce7f50ddd989f12c,"# Commerzbank verdient mehr als erwartet und bestätigt Ausblick ... --Starkes Ertragswachstum, Kostenquote deutlich verbessert ... --Commerzbank-CEO: Müssen Lösung im konstruktiven Austausch mit Unicredit finden ... --Aktienrückkauf von 1,2 Mrd EUR durch EZB genehmigt ... DOW JONES--Die Commerzbank hat im zweiten Quartal von einem deutlichen Ertragswachstum profitiert und den Gewinn stärker gesteigert als erwartet. Den Ausblick für das Gesamtjahr bestätigte die im DAX notierte Bank. Zudem steht ein neues Aktienrückkaufprogramm bevor. ... Der Nettogewinn stieg im Quartal um 94 Prozent auf 898 Millionen Euro. Analysten hatten in einem von der Bank selbst veröffentlichten Konsens mit 845 Millionen Euro gerechnet. Dass die Bank ihren Gewinn nahezu verdoppelte, lag auch an Restrukturierungsaufwendungen von 493 Millionen Euro, die das Ergebnis im Vorjahreszeitraum gedrückt hatten. ... Aber auch operativ legte der Gewinn deutlich um 17 Prozent auf 1,27 Milliarden Euro zu und fiel damit ebenfalls besser aus als erwartet. Dazu trug auch eine stark verbesserte Kostenquote bei. ... Die Aufwand-Ertrags-Relation verbesserte sich auf 52,4 Prozent von 55,4 Prozent im Vorjahr und lag damit auf Zielkurs für das Gesamtjahr. Die Quote bedeutet, dass die Bank für einen Euro Ertrag gut 52 Cent aufwenden musste. Die Risikovorsorge stieg gleichzeitig auf 202 von 176 Millionen Euro. ... Starkes Wertpapiergeschäft sorgt für höhere Provisionserträge ... Die Erträge legten um 9,3 Prozent auf 3,3 Milliarden Euro zu. Hier hatte die Prognose auf 3,25 Milliarden gelautet. Während der Zinsüberschuss stabil blieb, kletterten die Provisionserträge um 7 Prozent, was die Bank mit einem starken Wertpapiergeschäft begründete. Positiv habe sich auch die niedrigere Vorsorge für Rechtsrisiken aus Fremdwährungskrediten bei der polnischen Tochter M-Bank ausgewirkt. ... Für das laufende Jahr strebt die Bank weiterhin einen Gewinn von mindestens 3,4 Milliarden Euro an nach 2,6 Milliarden im Vorjahr. Im ersten Halbjahr hat sie 1,8 Milliarden verdient. Die Eigenkapitalrendite soll 12 Prozent erreichen nach 8,7 Prozent im Vorjahr. Die Gesamterträge werden bei rund 13,2 Milliarden Euro gesehen nach 12,2 Milliarden. Die Risikovorsorge sieht die Bank weiterhin bei rund 850 Millionen Euro, die Aufwand-Ertrags-Relation bei 53 Prozent. ... Die im Mai dargelegten Ziele für 2030 und die zum gleichen Zeitpunkt verschärften Ambitionen für 2028 bestätigte die Bank ebenfalls. So soll die Eigenkapitalrendite bis 2030 auf 21 Prozent steigen. 2028 soll sie 17 Prozent erreichen. Der Nettogewinn soll auf 5,9 Milliarden Euro zulegen, 2028 sollen es 4,6 Milliarden Euro sein. ... Konzernchefin Bettina Orlopp nannte die Strategie für 2030 in einer Analystenkonferenz verlässlich und hochattraktiv mit begrenzten Umsetzungsrisiken. Im Gegensatz dazu seien die Restrukturierungsvorschläge des Großaktionärs Unicredit mit Risiken behaftet. ... Sie sagte weiter, dass Gespräche mit der italienischen Bank aufgenommen worden seien, die sich kürzlich im Rahmen eines Übernahmeangebots fast die Hälfte der Anteile an der Commerzbank gesichert hat. Jetzt komme es darauf an, gemeinsam Schritt für Schritt eine gemeinsame Basis bei der Governance und auch beim Geschäftsmodell zu finden. ... Die Commerzbank teilte weiter mit, dass der nächste Aktienrückkauf von 1,2 Milliarden Euro von der Europäischen Zentralbank (EZB) genehmigt worden sei und noch auf die Zustimmung der Finanzagentur warte. Die Commerzbank will dieses Jahr nach aktuellem Stand etwa 3,2 Milliarden Euro ausschütten, davon mindestens die Hälfte über Dividenden. ... ### Aktuelle Nachrichten zu Commerzbank AG ... | 08:29 | Futures erwarten uneinheitliche Börsen | AN | | --- | --- | --- | | 08:03 | Cicor schliesst neuen Kreditvertrag über 425 Millionen Franken ab | AW | | 07:52 | Devisen: Wenig Bewegung vor US-Jobdaten | AW | | 07:49 | Cicor Technologies sichert sich Finanzierung über CHF 425 Mio. | MT | | 06:43 | UniCredit-Commerz: Erster Schritt in Richtung EU-Bankenkonsolidierung | AN | | 06:02 | Italien - Faktoren, die am 7. August zu beachten sind | RE | | 06.08. | JPMorgan hebt Ziel für Commerzbank auf 38 Euro - 'Neutral' | DP | | 06.08. | Gut behauptet - Unternehmen liefern | DJ | | 06.08. | Europäische Börsen im Kaufmodus; neuer Rekord für den MIB | AN | | 06.08. | Angeführt von Hermès erreicht Paris neue, bislang unerreichte Höhen | | | 06.08. | DZ Bank hebt fairen Wert für Commerzbank auf 46 Euro - 'Kaufen' | DP | | 06.08. | Aktien Frankfurt Schluss: Dax an Berichtssaison-Höhepunkt kaum verändert | DP | | 06.08. | Devisen: Euro gibt etwas nach - aber weiter über 1,15 US-Dollar | DP | | 06.08. | Commerzbank will sich mit Unicredit arrangieren | RE | | 06.08. | Aktien Frankfurt: Dax mit leichtem Auftrieb - Gewinnmitnahmen bei Siemens-Aktien | AW | ... Die Commerzbank AG gehört zu den größten Bankenkonzernen in Deutschland. Das Nettobankergebnis ist wie folgt auf die verschiedenen Geschäftsbereiche verteilt: - Detailbank und Privatbank (57,3%): Verkauf von klassischen und spezialisierten Bankprodukten und -dienstleistungen (Verbraucherkredite, Leasing, usw.), Privatbank usw.; - Markt- und Investmentbank (30,4%): Finanz-Engineering, Beratung bei Fusionen und Übernahmen, Aktiengeschäfte, Kapitalmarktgeschäfte, usw.; - sonstige (12,3%): Finanzierung von öffentlichen Vorhaben, spezielle und strukturierte Finanzierungen, Hypothekenkredite, usw. ... 05.11. Ergebnisveröffentlichung ... 202 ... Commerzbank: Nicht nachhaltige Überraschung, offen für konstruktive Zusammenarbeit Am 06. August 2026 um 11:43 Uhr ... Durch US-Inflation beruhigt: Commerzbank erwartet keine Zinserhöhung Am 14. Juli 2026 um 17:09 Uhr ... Merkwürdiges Dreiecksmanöver bei der Commerzbank Am 28. April 2026 um 09:22 Uhr"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank profit nearly doubles as UniCredit circles — Daily Digest Invest,dailydigestinvest.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://dailydigestinvest.com/commerzbank-profit-nearly-doubles-as-unicredit-circles,"Commerzbank profit nearly doubles as UniCredit circles — Daily Digest Invest # Commerzbank profit nearly doubles as UniCredit circles ... - Commerzbank's second-quarter net profit surged 94% to €898 million, topping expectations. - The strong result comes as Italy's UniCredit moves closer to gaining influence over Germany's second-largest lender. ... Commerzbank reported a sharp jump in second-quarter profit, nearly doubling from a year earlier, and the timing could hardly be more significant. The German lender is at the center of a cross-border banking drama, with Italy's UniCredit circling and building its stake. ... On Tuesday, Commerzbank said net profit rose 94% to €898 million, beating analysts' consensus of €845 million. The bank credited stronger commission income for the beat, a sign that its core businesses are generating more revenue even as the broader economic environment remains uncertain. ... The profit surge lands as UniCredit, Italy's largest bank, edges closer to gaining control of Commerzbank. Reuters reports that UniCredit is ""inching toward control"" after launching a €45 billion hostile takeover approach and steadily increasing its stake in the German lender. ... But Commerzbank's CEO, Bettina Orlopp, pushed back on what that control would actually mean in practice. She stressed that UniCredit cannot ""unilaterally decide on fundamental structural measures"" at the bank. In other words, even if UniCredit builds a large ownership position, it would still face significant hurdles in forcing through major changes without the support of Commerzbank's management and other shareholders. ... . Cross-border ... have long been touted as ... , but they ... For everyday investors, this story matters on a couple of levels. First, Commerzbank's earnings beat is a positive signal for anyone holding the stock or considering it. A 94% profit jump is a strong result, and beating analyst expectations by a meaningful margin often gives shares a short-term boost. ... Second, the UniCredit situation adds a layer of uncertainty. Takeover battles can push stock prices up as acquirers pay a premium, but they can also create volatility if the deal faces obstacles. Investors should be prepared for the possibility of sharp moves in Commerzbank's share price as news about UniCredit's intentions and regulatory responses emerges. ... It's also worth noting that Commerzbank's performance is part of a broader trend in European banking. Many lenders have been reporting solid profits recently, helped by higher interest rates and resilient economies. But the sector also faces headwinds, including the potential for slower growth and the ongoing need to invest in technology and digital services. ... For those watching the banking sector, the key question is whether UniCredit's approach will succeed and what that would mean for Commerzbank's strategy, its employees, and its shareholders. Until then, investors will be watching both the earnings reports and the takeover drama closely. ... As always, it's important to remember that past performance is not a guarantee of future results. While Commerzbank's latest numbers are encouraging, the outcome of the UniCredit situation remains uncertain, and that uncertainty is part of the risk any investor takes on."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,ROUNDUP/Commerzbank: Mit Rekordgewinn in Gespräche mit Unicredit,www.boersennews.de (BörsenNEWS.de),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.boersennews.de/nachrichten/artikel/dpa-afx/roundup-commerzbank-mit-rekordgewinn-in-gespraeche-mit-unicredit/5234562/,"ROUNDUP/Commerzbank: Mit Rekordgewinn in Gespräche mit Unicredit ... # Mit Rekordgewinn in Gespräche mit Unicredit 06.08.2026, 09:42 Uhr von dpa-AFX Jetzt kommentieren: 0 ##### Werte zum Artikel ... Die Commerzbank `DE000CBK1001` sieht sich nach einem überraschend starken Gewinnsprung im zweiten Quartal gestärkt für weitere Gespräche mit ihrer Großaktionärin aus Mailand. ""Wir sind bereit für konstruktive Gespräche mit der Unicredit"", teilte der Frankfurter Dax-Konzern `DE0008469008` am Donnerstag mit. Ein gemeinsamer Ansatz habe das Potenzial, Mehrwert zu schaffen. An der Börse fiel der Commerzbank-Aktienkurs nach ihrem jüngsten Höhenflug etwas. ... Von April bis Juni 2026 verdiente Deutschlands zweitgrößte börsennotierte Bank unter dem Strich fast doppelt so viel wie ein Jahr zuvor. Der Überschuss kletterte von 462 Millionen Euro auf 898 Millionen Euro und übertraf damit die durchschnittlichen Erwartungen von Analysten. Ein Jahr zuvor hatten allerdings Kosten für den Abbau von Tausenden Jobs den Gewinn des Instituts geschmälert. ... Nach einem Rekordergebnis von 1,8 Milliarden Euro im ersten Halbjahr sieht der Vorstand die Commerzbank ""voll auf Kurs, ihr Gewinnziel von mindestens 3,4 Milliarden Euro im Gesamtjahr zu erreichen"". ... Die Bank will nun weitere bis zu 1,2 Milliarden Euro in den Rückkauf eigener Aktien stecken. Mit Aktienrückkäufen und höheren Gewinnen wollte der Vorstand um Bettina Orlopp die Aktionäre bei der Stange halten und so die Unabhängigkeit des 1870 gegründeten Instituts sichern. ... Doch die italienische Großbank Unicredit hat knapp zwei Jahre nach ihrem Einstieg bei der Commerzbank inzwischen Zugriff auf fast die Hälfte der Anteile. Unicredit-Chef Andrea Orcel erwartet nach jüngsten Aussagen eine baldige Kontrollübernahme bei dem Frankfurter Institut. ... ""Auch wenn die Unicredit über eine Mehrheit auf der nächsten Hauptversammlung verfügt, kann sie über wesentliche Strukturmaßnahmen nicht allein entscheiden"", bekräftigte Commerzbank-Chefin Orlopp. ""Das ist ein klarer Gestaltungsauftrag für beide Seiten. Dafür braucht es ein gemeinsames Verständnis des Geschäftsmodells und die Einbindung aller Stakeholder."" ... Orcel will mit einer Übernahme der Commerzbank eine europäische Großbank schmieden, auch als Gegengewicht zu den deutlich profitableren Geldhäusern aus den USA. Die Unicredit ist in Deutschland bereits mit der Hypovereinsbank (HVB) aktiv und sieht Potenzial für Milliardeneinsparungen inklusive des Abbaus Tausender Stellen. Das aus Commerzbank-Sicht ""feindliche Vorgehen"" der Italiener sorgt für reichlich Widerstand bei Management, Betriebsrat und Belegschaft des Dax-Konzerns. Auch der Bund äußerte sich wiederholt kritisch. ... Die Unicredit jedoch ließ nicht locker und zog bis Anfang Juli per freiwilligem Übernahmeangebot nach eigenen Angaben weitere 17,6 Prozent der Commerzbank-Papiere an Land. Zusammen mit den 26,77 Prozent, die die Unicredit schon zuvor hielt, steigt ihr Anteil damit rechnerisch auf 44,37 Prozent. Zudem haben die Italiener über Kaufoptionen Zugriff auf weitere 3,22 Prozent der Commerzbank-Aktien und könnten so nach jüngsten Angaben auf 47,59 Prozent aufstocken. ... Dabei zog der Investmentbanker Orcel trickreich alle Register. Nach Erkenntnissen der Commerzbank dienten Profi-Investoren und Privatanleger der Unicredit im Zuge des Übernahmeangebots zusammen gerade einmal 2,7 Prozent der Anteile an. Der Rest stammt demnach überwiegend von Banken, mit denen die Unicredit über Finanzinstrumente Geschäfte macht. Zwischenzeitlich hatte die Commerzbank der Unicredit vorgeworfen, ihre Aktienposition ""künstlich aufzublähen"". Zwecks Klärung hat der Dax-Konzern die Finanzaufsicht Bafin eingeschaltet. Ein Ergebnis dieser Prüfung steht aus. ... Unterdessen lief eine Strafanzeige des Commerzbank-Gesamtbetriebsrats wegen des Verdachts der Marktmanipulation ins Leere: Die Staatsanwaltschaft Frankfurt lehnte es ab, in der Sache ein Ermittlungsverfahren aufzunehmen, ""da zureichende tatsächliche Anhaltspunkte für das Vorliegen einer Straftat nicht festgestellt werden konnten"", wie die Behörde Anfang Juli mitteilte."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank und Unicredit: Tradition ist kein Geschäftsmodell | FAZ,www.faz.net (Inken Schönauer),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.faz.net/aktuell/finanzen/commerzbank-und-unicredit-tradition-ist-kein-geschaeftsmodell-201101115.html,"Commerzbank und Unicredit: Tradition ist kein Geschäftsmodell | FAZ ... Wenn eines aus der Übernahmeschlacht um die Commerzbank hängen bleibt, dann dieser eine Satz der Commerzbank-Vorstandsvorsitzenden Bettina Orlopp: „Wir wollen Wert schaffen.“ Vielleicht wirkt es merkwürdig, dies auch an diesem Donnerstag von einer Frau zu hören, die sich – zusammen mit rund 40.000 Mitarbeitern – seit fast zwei Jahren gegen die Übernahme durch den italienischen Unicredit stemmt und diesen Kampf sehr wahrscheinlich verlieren wird. ... Doch es ist das Credo ihres Führungsstils. Sie wollte schon während ihrer Zeit als Finanzchefin einer im Mittelstand verankerten Bank nicht akzeptieren, dass dieses zum Sanierungsfall verkommene Institut in der Bedeutungslosigkeit verschwindet. Die Bank liefert inzwischen wieder Rekordergebnisse ab, hat Kosten gesenkt, stellt Kunden zufriedener und ist wieder ein anerkannter Arbeitgeber. Geholfen hat Bettina Orlopp dabei ein nüchterner Blick auf die Dinge. Sie ist stark in der Analyse des Machbaren. ... Genauso hat sie auch die Übernahmeschlacht geführt. Sie verrennt sich nicht in emotional geführten Debatten um die Tradition einer Bank, die doch irgendwie zu diesem Land oder dem Finanzplatz Frankfurt gehört. Tradition ist kein Geschäftsmodell. ... Das musste Orlopp nicht lernen, das brachte sie in ihr Amt mit. Die Commerzbank musste zunächst zeigen, dass sie aus eigener Kraft wachsen, Gewinne steigern und ihren Aktionären ein attraktives Investment sein kann. Das ist gelungen. Der Vorstand hat Zeit gewonnen, den Wert der Bank sichtbar gemacht und die Grundlage für Verhandlungen aus einer Position der Stärke gelegt. ... Dankbarkeit für diesen kräftezehrenden Übernahmekampf sollte niemand erwarten. Aber vermutlich hat er durchaus dazu geführt, Restrukturierungsprozesse in der Commerzbank anzustoßen oder zu beschleunigen. ... Die Commerzbank hat inzwischen eine Kosten-Ertrags-Quote von 53 Prozent. Das schien noch vor wenigen Jahren völlig undenkbar, ist aber eine relevante Größe, wenn man in Zeiten von Künstlicher Intelligenz und sich global wandelnden Geschäftsmodellen bestehen will. ... Orlopp will Wert schaffen. Auch jetzt wieder, wo der Unicredit-Vorstandsvorsitzende Andrea Orcel seinem Ziel der Übernahme immer näher kommt. Die Commerzbank sei bereit zu konstruktiven Gesprächen, sagt Orlopp. ... Es ist ein wohltuender Hinweis auf die Anerkennung der neuen Machtverhältnisse. Sie ist die Vorstandsvorsitzende der Commerzbank. Sie wird diese Gespräche im Sinne ihrer Aktionäre wertschaffend führen müssen – auch wenn es die Aufgabe der Eigenständigkeit bedeutet. ... Die Commerzbank verzichtet nach einem Rekordergebnis nach den ersten sechs Monaten auf eine höhere Jahresprognose. Vorstandschefin Orlopp pocht gegenüber Unicredit auf Mitsprache."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,German Regulator Reportedly Allows UniCredit to Proceed with Commerzbank Bid | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (MT Newswires),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/german-regulator-reportedly-allows-unicredit-to-proceed-with-commerzbank-bid-ce7f50dedf8ff725,"German Regulator Reportedly Allows UniCredit to Proceed with Commerzbank Bid | MarketScreener ... | 05:43am | Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration | | | --- | --- | --- | | 05:28am | Commerzbank CEO Signals Talks With UniCredit for Potential Combination | MT | ... # German Regulator Reportedly Allows UniCredit to Proceed with Commerzbank Bid ... Published on 08/04/2026 at 12:16 pm EDT ... ### Latest news about Commerzbank AG ... | 05:43am | Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration | | | --- | --- | --- | | 05:28am | Commerzbank CEO Signals Talks With UniCredit for Potential Combination | MT | | 04:37am | Commerzbank Seeks 'Constructive Discussions' with UniCredit as First-half Profit Rises; EUR1.2 Billion Buyback Planned | MT | | 04:35am | Commerzbank AG, Q2 2026 Earnings Call, Aug 06, 2026 | | | 03:48am | Commerzbank CEO: We have started talks with Unicredit | RE | | 03:44am | Commerzbank: Record profit strengthens hand in talks with Unicredit | DP | | 03:43am | COMMERZBANK AG : RBC remains its Buy rating | ZD | | 03:40am | Commerzbank Plans EUR1.2 Billion Share Buyback | MT | | 03:21am | Commerzbank CEO says talks have begun with Unicredit | RE | | 03:18am | Frankfurt Stocks at the Open: DAX Takes Another Breather | DP | | 03:02am | Euro zone bond yields steady; hefty French supply due | RE | | 02:14am | Markets Drift Gently Towards the Mid-August Lull | | | 02:07am | Commerzbank boosts profit and strikes a confident tone toward Unicredit | RE | | 01:57am | DAX expected to open higher, earnings and economic data in focus | RE | | 01:47am | Commerzbank CEO Calls For Dialogue With UniCredit | DJ | ... Commerzbank AG is one of the leading German banking groups. Net banking product (NBP) breaks down by activity as follows: - retail banking and private banking (57.3%): sales of classical and specialized banking products and services (consumer loans, leasing, etc.), private banking, etc.; - market and investment banking (30,4%): financial engineering, merger-acquisition consulting, stock operations, specialized and structured financing, capital market operations, etc.; - other (12.3%): public works financing, specialized and structured financing, mortgage loans, etc. ... Aug. 05 Earnings release - Q2 2026 ... Commerzbank: Unsustainable beat, open to constructive collaboration August 06, 2026 at 05:43 am EDT ... ### Quarterly revenue ... German Regulator Reportedly Allows UniCredit to Proceed with Commerzbank Bid"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Banken: Unicredit kommt Übernahme der Commerzbank einen Schritt näher,www.handelsblatt.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.handelsblatt.com/finanzen/banken-versicherungen/banken/banken-unicredit-kommt-uebernahme-der-commerzbank-einen-schritt-naeher/100245032.html,"Banken: Unicredit kommt Übernahme der Commerzbank einen Schritt näher ... # Banken: Unicredit kommt Übernahme der Commerzbank einen Schritt näher ... Unicredit-Chef Andrea Orcel: Er treibt die Übernahme der Commerzbank voran. Foto: Bloomberg ... Frankfurt. Die schrittweise Übernahme der Commerzbank durch Unicredit hat eine wichtige behördliche Hürde genommen. Die deutsche Finanzaufsichtsbehörde Bafin teilte der italienischen Bank mit, dass ihr Antrag auf eine Mehrheitsbeteiligung weiterbearbeitet werden kann. ... Die Bafin habe Unicredit Ende Juli mitgeteilt, dass der Antrag der italienischen Bank zur Aufstockung seines Anteils an der Commerzbank vollständig sei, teilten mit der Angelegenheit vertraute Personen mit. ... Für die Aufsicht über Unicredit und Commerzbank ist federführend die EZB zuständig. Um das Inhaberkontrollverfahren kümmert sich zunächst aber die Bafin, die der EZB dann eine vorläufige Einschätzung inklusive Entscheidungsvorschlag unterbreitet. Die finale Entscheidung liegt dann bei der EZB. Da Unicredit genauso wie die Commerzbank seit Jahren von der EZB kontrolliert wird, sind alle Beteiligten von Anfang an fest davon ausgegangen, dass die Aufsichtsbehörde den Italienern eine Aufstockung ihres Anteils genehmigen werde. ... Vertreter von Unicredit, der EZB, der Bafin und der Commerzbank lehnten eine Stellungnahme ab. Mit der Freigabe durch die Bafin läuft nun die Frist für die EZB, ihre Prüfung innerhalb von 60 Arbeitstagen abzuschließen. Die Aufsichtsbehörde kann theoretisch weitere Informationen anfordern, was die Prüfung um maximal 20 Arbeitstage verlängern würde. ... Banken Unicredit kommt Übernahme der Commerzbank einen Schritt näher"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"Commerzbank to resume talks with UniCredit for pan-European deal, says CEO - International Finance",internationalfinance.com (International Finance Business Desk),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://internationalfinance.com/banking/commerzbank-to-resume-talks-with-unicredit-for-pan-european-deal-says-ceo/,"Commerzbank to resume talks with UniCredit for pan-European deal, says CEO - International Finance ... Commerzbank to resume talks with UniCredit for pan-European deal, says CEO ... While Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp had been opposing the tie-up, she conducted several – yet unsuccessful – talks with UniCredit recently ... In what seems to be the further climbdown from the opposition against the UniCredit’s “hostile” takeover attempts, Commerzbank’s CEO Bettina Orlopp has told employees that there will be further talks with the Italian lender about a potential tie-up as the Andrea Orcel-led venture nears control in its 45 billion euro (USD 51.80 billion) bid for the German counterpart. ... The announcement, made to staff on the bank’s intranet and seen by the media outlet Reuters, marks a significant turn in the months-long battle ⁠over control of Germany’s second-largest lender. ... While Orlopp and her management team have been opposed to a tie-up, they have conducted several – yet unsuccessful – talks with UniCredit in the past months. ... “In the weeks and months ahead, Commerzbank and UniCredit will engage in discussions to determine, step by step, how to move forward,” Orlopp told employees in the internal post, while stating the goal of the talks will be to strengthen the bank’s systemic relevance to Germany. ... “The German federal government, employee representatives, and our supervisory board have ⁠all made clear that they now expect UniCredit to engage with Commerzbank constructively. And I think UniCredit is ready for that, too. Because without dialogue, there can be no value creation,” she said further. ... Orcel also expressed the willingness to negotiate with the German government and Commerzbank employees. However, the approach, as per the analysts, would be a problematic one, as it looks to sidestep the German lender’s management. ... It is worth mentioning that the German Finance Ministry oversees a 12% stake in the Commerzbank, which has been held by the government since the venture’s bailout during the global financial crisis. ... UniCredit invested in Commerzbank in ⁠September 2024, launching a nearly two-year tug-of-war that pitted Italy’s and Germany’s number two banks against each other. UniCredit has since built a 48% stake in its rival. ... Orlopp’s statement comes after the message of the bank’s chairman, Jens Weidmann, who said that the Italian bank’s dominance of its shareholder base ⁠meant “constructive talks” were needed to establish a framework in the interests of shareholders and staff. ... While stating that Commerzbank would have preferred a different outcome from the whole saga, Weidmann implied that he had no other choice but to enter the talks ‌with ⁠the Orcel-led venture. ... “We have to have constructive talks to establish the key parameters for staff, shareholders and the customers of the bank. Everyone needs to act like adults now, because one thing is certain: ⁠These discussions are in UniCredit’s interest as well, and there will be no ⁠shortcut via Berlin,” Weidmann ⁠said. ... Weidmann’s response came within the 24 hours of UniCredit’s remark, in which it asked its German counterpart to start adopting the strategy the Italian bank ‌has mapped out in January 2026. ... Orcel, from his part, raised the pitch further by stating that his business had the option of using its 48% stake to install a new board. ... The whole takeover saga, which has also seen severe opposition from the German government, has been the grim reminder about ⁠the difficulty of merging large banks across Eurozone countries, despite policymakers wanting more tie-ups to compete with bigger American rivals."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank agrees to talks with UniCredit after two-year standoff,"finance.yahoo.com (AFP Fri, July 31, 2026 at 5:36 AM PDT 2 min read)",2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/commerzbank-agrees-talks-unicredit-two-123623806.html,"Commerzbank agrees to talks with UniCredit after two-year standoff ... # Commerzbank agrees to talks with UniCredit after two-year standoff ... UniCredit acquired a stake in Commerzbank in September 2024 and has since raised its holding to nearly 50 percent, despite repeated opposition from the German bank's management and the government in Berlin (GIUSEPPE CACACE) ... Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp has called for the opening of talks with UniCredit regarding the German bank's future, deeming a ""constructive dialogue"" necessary after the Italian group secured nearly half of the voting rights. ... ""In the weeks and months ahead, Commerzbank and UniCredit will engage in discussions to determine, step by step, how to move forward,"" Orlopp said in an interview on Commerzbank's intranet that AFP obtained from a source close to the bank. ... The shift in tone marks a turning point following nearly two years of fierce confrontation over UniCredit's attempt to take control of the German bank. ... ""Our two institutions must now engage in a constructive dialogue to identify a path forward that creates value for everyone involved,"" said the CEO, who set as a prerequisite for the talks ""a shared understanding of the business model and the involvement of all stakeholders"". ... The discussions will be conducted ""in close cooperation with the Supervisory Board and employee representatives, and in close consultation with the German Federal Government"". ... UniCredit acquired a stake in Commerzbank in September 2024 and has since raised its holding to nearly 50 percent, despite repeated opposition from the German bank's management and the government in Berlin. ... The German state, which still holds a 12 percent stake, has in recent weeks significantly shifted its stance, with Chancellor Friedrich Merz saying his government did not want to ""prevent this merger"". ... According to Orlopp, talks with UniCredit will begin ""with the strongest Commerzbank in our 156-year history"". ... In response to UniCredit's takeover bid, Commerzbank raised its financial targets for 2030 in May and announced 3,000 additional job cuts, asserting at the time that remaining independent would create more value than a merger with the Italian bank."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank ready for further talks with UniCredit | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-ready-for-further-talks-with-unicredit-ce7f50dbdd8ff227,"Commerzbank ready for further talks with UniCredit | MarketScreener ... # Commerzbank ready for further talks with UniCredit ... Published on 07/31/2026 at 03:24 am EDT ... Commerzbank is ready for new talks with its largest shareholder UniCredit. 'Over the coming weeks and months, Commerzbank and UniCredit will hold talks to define step by step how we proceed,' Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp said in an interview on Commerzbank's intranet, quoted by Handelsblatt on Friday. The lender wants to do this 'in close coordination with the supervisory board as well as employee representatives and in close dialogue with the German federal government.' She assumes the Italians, who have already secured almost half of Commerzbank's shares, are ready for a constructive dialogue. ... Earlier, Commerzbank supervisory board chairman Jens Weidmann had called on UniCredit to hold direct talks with the management board. The former Bundesbank chief is thereby acknowledging that there is no longer any way around a takeover of power by the Milan-based major bank. UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel had announced he would speak with the German federal government and the works council about a shared future for his group with Commerzbank. The Italian did not mention Commerzbank's management board led by Bettina Orlopp as a counterpart for talks. ... ### Latest news about Commerzbank AG ... | 12:55pm | EU wheat drops as traders take month-end profit after rally | RE | | --- | --- | --- | | 12:23pm | The Week in Oil : Crude on Track for 20% Monthly Gain After Iran War Disrupts Key Shipping Routes | DJ | | 11:26am | Fed dissenters call for a tighter rate path | RE | | 11:14am | Currencies: Euro slips slightly, inflation figures barely move markets | DP | | 10:54am | DAX records in sight, markets remain prone to volatility | RE | | 09:38am | Global markets live: Microsoft, Apple, Tesla, Intel, Coinbase… | | | 09:28am | Eurozone Inflation Rebounds as High Energy Prices Persist -- 3rd Update | DJ | | 07:36am | US wheat falls, on track for over 11% monthly gain | RE | | 07:06am | Eurozone Inflation Rebounds as High Energy Prices Persist -- 2nd Update | DJ | | 06:40am | Commerzbank Says US S&P 500 futures Extend Gains, US Dollar Rises, Oil Lower | MT | | 06:28am | Inflation Picks Up Again, 'ECB Rate Hike Overdue After Summer Break' | RE | | 06:22am | Commerzbank, CEO Orlopp opens to talks with UniCredit | AN | | 06:05am | European stocks trade briskly; MIB up with Amplifon | AN | | 05:23am | Commerzbank CEO: Further Talks with UniCredit | DP | | 03:24am | Commerzbank ready for further talks with UniCredit | RE | ... Commerzbank AG is one of the leading German banking groups. Net banking product (NBP) breaks down by activity as follows: - retail banking and private banking (57.3%): sales of classical and specialized banking products and services (consumer loans, leasing, etc.), private banking, etc.; - market and investment banking (30,4%): financial engineering, merger-acquisition consulting, stock operations, specialized and structured financing, capital market operations, etc.; - other (12.3%): public works financing, specialized and structured financing, mortgage loans, etc. ... Aug. 05 Earnings release - Q2 2026 ... Commerzbank: Aligning our forecasts with upgraded net interest income May 28, 2026 at 07:37 am EDT"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Banken: Commerzbank-Aufsichtsratschef fordert Gespräche mit Unicredit,www.handelsblatt.com,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.handelsblatt.com/finanzen/banken-versicherungen/banken/banken-commerzbank-aufsichtsratschef-fordert-gespraeche-mit-unicredit/100242642.html,"Banken: Commerzbank-Aufsichtsratschef fordert Gespräche mit Unicredit ... # Banken: Commerzbank-Aufsichtsratschef fordert Gespräche mit Unicredit ... ens Weidmann bei der Com ... „Alle sollten sich jetzt wie Erwachsene verhalten.“ Foto: ... Frankfurt. Der Aufsichtsratschef der Commerzbank, Jens Weidmann, hat die italienische Großbank Unicredit zu Gesprächen mit dem Management der Commerzbank aufgefordert. „Der Vorstand und der Aufsichtsrat der Commerzbank haben mehrfach betont, dass sie dazu bereit sind“, sagte Weidmann dem Handelsblatt."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,UniCredit says full Commerzbank acquisition could happen in fourth quarter,www.cnbc.com (Hugh Leask),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/23/unicredit-commerzbank-takeover-acquisition-2q-earnings.html,"UniCredit says full Commerzbank acquisition could happen in fourth quarter ... - UniCredit now has de facto control of Commerzbank, having increased its stake to 48%. - CEO Andrea Orcel said an acquisition could happen ""potentially"" in the fourth quarter - The Italian lender on Thursday posted record second-quarter and first-half earnings. ... UniCredit is aiming to exercise control of Commerzbank in the fourth quarter, the CEO of the Italian bank told CNBC in an exclusive interview. ... Speaking with CNBC's ""Europe Early Edition,"" UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel said the bank is happy with its position in Commerzbank, with the bank now closing in on full control of the German lender, having upped its stake to 48%. ... Orcel said the Italian bank is firing on all cylinders, having raised its full-year guidance after posting its best-ever second-quarter and first-half results Thursday. ... Asked when a full acquisition could take place, Orcel told CNBC's Carolin Roth that certain steps still need to happen. ... ""With respect to the normal regulatory environment and antitrust, and what would allow us to take ownership of tendered shares and therefore exercise control, we think now potentially in Q4, maybe later, and that would mark the moment when we go in."" ... ""That would mark the moment when we go in,"" the CEO said, adding that they would not wait for the AGM in May. ... He said that the two banks remain ""very different,"" adding that a number of alignments need to occur before any full merger takes place. ... In a statement, Commerzbank said its position remains unchanged. ""Only a constructive approach can create value for all stakeholders,"" the bank said. ... UniCredit's swoop for Commerzbank has been one of Europe's most closely-watched takeover tussles in recent years. ... The Italian bank took an initial 9% stake in 2024, before ramping it up to about 30% in March, fueling expectations of a full takeover, a prospect fiercely resisted by Commerzbank management. ... The German Finance Ministry weighed in on the increasingly bitter wrangle Thursday, saying that it was ""now up to the two banks to talk to each other."" ... The comments, which followed CNBC's interview, signal a reversal of the German government's opposition to the deal, though the ministry said it was opposed to UniCredit's ""aggressive approach."" ... The German government holds a 12% stake in Commerzbank. ... Also responding to CNBC's interview, Com ... bank's deputy chair and works council head Sascha Uebel called on each party to ""act like adults."" ... In its second-quarter results statement, UniCredit said the Commerzbank deal has evolved from ""an attractive financial investment"" to a ""strategic transaction of substantial industrial value creation."" ... The Italian bank's net profit fell 13% to 2.9 billion euros ($3.3 billion) in the second quarter, or 3.1 billion euros when excluding one-off hedging and certain other funding costs relating to the increased stake in Commerzbank. ... Its full-year net profit target has been upgraded to more than 11 billion euros."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank works council gives management the lead in UniCredit talks | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-works-council-gives-management-the-lead-in-unicredit-talks-ce7f51ded88df42c,"Commerzbank works council gives management the lead in UniCredit talks | MarketScreener # Commerzbank works council gives management the lead in UniCredit talks Published on 07/23/2026 at 04:06 am EDT UN ... IT S. ... Commerzbank works council chief Sascha Uebel wants to let management take the lead in talks with Italy's UniCredit. ""If we works council members are being named here as negotiating partners, UniCredit is unfortunately mistaken,"" Uebel told Reuters on Thursday. ""Under corporate law, management decides what happens in a company. Talks with the group works council are always conducted via the responsible management. I politely ask that this be respected."" ... UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel had announced talks with the German government and employee representatives as the next steps toward a takeover of Commerzbank. He did not mention management. Several attempts to hold talks with Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp had come to nothing. A Commerzbank spokesman said it had taken note of Orcel's remarks. ""We stand by this: Only a constructive approach can create value for all stakeholders."" ... The German government also sees Commerzbank management as next in line, for now. Sources close to the Federal Finance Ministry said nothing had changed in its critical stance toward UniCredit. First, it must be observed how talks between the two banks develop. The federal government still holds twelve percent of Commerzbank and does not want to sell it. The stake is also seen as leverage for talks about the terms of a takeover. ... | | Add to a list Add to a list 0 selected To use this feature you must be a member Log in Sign up | Off-Hours Price | Change | 5-day change | Capi. | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | COMMERZBANK AG | 37.67 EUR | +0.88% | +3.63% | 46.42B | | | UNICREDIT S.P.A. | 81.61 EUR | -0.11% | +3.02% | 141B | | |"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Brussels Piles Pressure on Berlin as Jefferies Takes 10% Stake and Fitch Sees Rating Reward for UniCredit | NewsCase,www.newscase.com (kashif hafeez),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newscase.com/brussels-piles-pressure-on-berlin-as-jefferies-takes-10-stake-and-fitch-sees-rating-reward-for-unicredit/,"The power struggle over Commerzbank is entering a new phase, with the European Commission openly challenging Berlin’s resistance to cross-border bank mergers while the U.S. investment bank Jefferies has pushed its stake past the 10% threshold. Meanwhile, Fitch has flagged potential rating upside for UniCredit if the Italian lender succeeds in its takeover quest. ... Jefferies Financial Group now holds 10.02% of Commerzbank’s voting rights, crossing the mandatory notification level on 15 July 2026, according to a regulatory filing. The position consists of 2.52% in directly held shares and 7.50% via financial instruments. The move marks a further buildup from the previous 9.91% and underscores how closely institutional investors are tracking the shifting shareholder dynamics. Commerzbank stock closed Monday at €36.70, edging up 0.11%, yet remains roughly 6.3% below its 52-week high of €39.18 reached on 14 July. Over the past week, the shares have shed 5.03%, indicating that takeover enthusiasm has cooled somewhat. ... The European Commission has positioned itself firmly against state intervention in cross-border banking consolidation — a clear rebuke to the German government, which had so far resisted UniCredit’s acquisition plans. Chancellor Friedrich Merz has since signaled a willingness to negotiate. Berlin is now preparing a list of demands for talks with UniCredit, according to reports from Bloomberg and Reuters. The government wants to secure the bank’s continued stock exchange listing, protect financing for small and medium-sized enterprises, and preserve the Frankfurt headquarters. The federal government itself retains roughly 12% of Commerzbank’s shares, giving it a heavyweight seat at the table. ... The EU’s push comes as the outcome of UniCredit’s initial offer period becomes clearer. By the extended acceptance deadline of 3 July 2026, the Italian bank had gathered 17.60% of Commerzbank shares. However, less than 2% of that total came from independent institutional or retail investors, a detail that strengthens Berlin’s hand in negotiations, since the free float’s endorsement was minimal. ... Fitch sees potential for Un ... redit to rise ... Rating agency Fitch has weighed in on the takeover bid, affirming UniCredit’s rating and noting that the Italian bank could eventually be rated two notches above its home country’s sovereign grade if the Commerzbank transaction goes through. Such an assessment would be unusually strong and suggests Fitch views the integration of Commerzbank as strategically valuable for UniCredit’s credit profile. The agency’s comment was picked up by several international financial media outlets during the day. ... Away from the takeover drama, Commerzbank is pushing ahead with its digital strategy. In early July, the bank announced expanded partnerships with Google and Microsoft, integrating the Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise App and the Microsoft 365 Copilot into its day-to-day operations. The efficiency drive has garnered little attention amid the acquisition saga but reflects the bank’s broader cost-cutting efforts. ... Investors now have their sights set on 6 August 2026, when Commerzbank releases its second-quarter results. The date coincides with what could be a critical moment in the Berlin-UniCredit talks, adding extra weight to the numbers. Technically, the stock is trading in neutral territory with a relative strength index of 44.1, after having gained 29.35% over the past twelve months — a premium that underscores how much of the current valuation hinges on the takeover narrative rather than underlying business performance. The 50-day moving average of €37.12, less than 1.1% above Monday’s close, reflects the market’s uncertainty about the final outcome of the poker game. ... Commerzbank Stock: Buy or Sell?! New Commerzbank Analysis from July 28 delivers the answer: ... The latest Commerzbank figures speak for themselves: Urgent action needed for Commerzbank investors. Is it worth buying or should you sell? Find out what to do now in the current free analysis from July 28. ... bank: Buy or sell? Read more here..."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Migrates Card Portfolio to Visa While Defending Against UniCredit’s Advance | NewsCase,www.newscase.com (Brett Shapiro),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newscase.com/commerzbank-migrates-card-portfolio-to-visa-while-defending-against-unicredits-advance/,"Commerzbank Migrates Card Portfolio to Visa While Defending Against UniCredit’s Advance | NewsCase ... # Commerzbank Migrates Card Portfolio to Visa While Defending Against UniCredit’s Advance ... Millions of Commerzbank customers are receiving letters that have nothing to do with the unfolding takeover drama involving UniCredit. The bank is gradually replacing its Mastercard credit cards with Visa, a move that signals business-as-usual even as the Italian lender tightens its grip. Customers who fail to consent to the switch risk having their card cancelled on its expiry date, and those who want to keep their Mastercard must upgrade to a premium current account costing €12.90 a month — nearly three times the €4.90 fee for the digital account that comes with the new Visa offering. ... The migration, first announced as a strategic partnership with Visa in February 2025, is being rolled out in tranches. A Commerzbank spokesperson confirmed that the entire Mastercard portfolio will eventually shift to Visa. For everyday spending, little changes — both networks are accepted in over 200 countries. But the move underscores how the bank is executing operational changes even as it fights a hostile advance from its Italian rival. ... UniCredit now controls a voting stake approaching 50%, including derivatives and tendered shares. A formal takeover still requires approval from the European Central Bank and EU competition authorities, but the pressure on Commerzbank’s management has intensified. CEO Bettina Orlopp is preparing a defence plan designed to convince shareholders that remaining independent offers better value than any offer from Milan. ... According to reports over the weekend, Orlopp’s strategy involves moderate job cuts and sharply higher financial targets. The aim is to lift Commerzbank’s market value sustainably above any takeover premium that UniCredit might offer, thereby cementing confidence in the standalone “Momentum 2030” strategy. ... However, Orlopp’s calculations face an unwelcome complication. The ECB recently urged banks to exercise caution with their capital reserves, citing geopolitical tensions in the Middle East and new market risks from AI-driven trading algorithms. More specifically, a systemic risk buffer that took effect in July 2026 now requires an additional 2% capital cover for loans secured against commercial real estate. Commerzbank’s traditional strength in financing Mittelstand companies and property projects makes it particularly exposed to this rule. ... Analysts are watching closely to see how much room the new buffer leaves for dividends and share buybacks — precisely the tools Orlopp needs to keep shareholders on side. The defence plan’s credibility hinges on delivering returns that outshine a potential UniCredit bid, and any constraint on capital distributions weakens that argument. ... Despite the competing pressures, Commerzbank’s stock has held near its best levels in years. After closing at €38.67 on Friday, shares eased 0.44% to €38.50 on Monday, leaving them just 0.9% below the 52-week high of €38.85 set on June 19. The weekly gain still stands at 1.66%, while the year-to-date advance reaches 34.27%. All major moving averages are trending higher: the stock sits 4.84% above its 50-day average of €36.89 and 11.79% above the 200-day line of €34.44. The Relative Strength Index of 61.7 points to constructive momentum without overheating. ... The next major catalyst arrives on August 6, when Commerzbank publishes its second-quarter results. Until then, the tug-of-war between Frankfurt and Milan — and the actual acceptance rate of UniCredit’s tender — will dominate the narrative. The card migration, while operationally significant, is unlikely to shift the stock; its impact on fee income and customer loyalty will only become apparent in future quarterly reports. For now, the overarching drama remains the battle for control, with Orlopp’s defence plan and the new capital rules adding fresh layers of complexity. ... Commerzbank figures speak for themselves: Urgent action needed for Com ... investors. Is it worth buying or should you sell? Find out what to do now in the current free analysis from July 20."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"Legal Win and Tender Close Push Commerzbank Stock to Doorstep of Highs, but Control Hangs in Balance - Stocks Today",stockstoday.com (Jackson Burston),2026-07-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://stockstoday.com/legal-win-and-tender-close-push-commerzbank-stock-to-doorstep-of-highs-but-control-hangs-in-balance/,"Legal Win and Tender Close Push Commerzbank Stock to Doorstep of Highs, but Control Hangs in Balance - Stocks Today ... # Legal Win and Tender Close Push Commerzbank Stock to Doorstep of Highs, but Control Hangs in Balance ... Commerzbank shares ended the week at €38.67, up 2.41% on the day and within a whisker — just 0.46% — of the 52-week peak of €38.85 touched on June 19. The catalyst was a double dose of news: UniCredit’s takeover bid formally closed, and a market-manipulation probe into the Italian lender was abruptly killed before it could begin. ... The Frankfurt public prosecutor’s office rejected the complaint filed by Commerzbank’s works council, which had alleged that UniCredit misled the market by claiming it was regularly being tendered shares when the offer price sat persistently below the market price. “No sufficient factual indications of a criminal offence,” a spokesman said, declining to elaborate further given the ongoing process. The decision removes one legal sword of Damocles from above UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel’s European banking ambitions. ... On the tender front, UniCredit confirmed on July 8 that shareholders had tendered 17.6% of Commerzbank stock by the July 3 deadline. Combined with its existing holdings, the Italian bank now controls roughly 44% of shares directly, with derivative instruments lifting its economic exposure to 47.59%. That is tantalisingly close to a majority, but the voting rights remain frozen until the European Central Bank and the European Commission sign off on the transaction — a decision that could take weeks or months. ... Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp, who has spent months fighting the unsolicited approach, struck a notably different tone this week. In an interview with the Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung, she stood by the bank’s standalone strategy, noting that the stock had doubled since February 2025 and that 2025 was a record year. Yet in a video message to staff, she acknowledged the novelty of the situation and said the bank “remains open for constructive dialogue with UniCredit.” That marks a meaningful shift in posture from the earlier wall of resistance. ... Still, the tender figures reveal a lukewarm reception from the broader investor base. Only a small portion of the free float was tendered, and institutional and retail investors together contributed less than 2% of the total. The bulk came from banks and parties already linked to UniCredit, suggesting that independent shareholders are not yet convinced the offer — which for much of the period was below the prevailing market price — represents fair value. ... The Bund, which retains a stake in Commerzbank and has labelled UniCredit’s tactics “unacceptable,” remains a powerful obstacle. As long as the German government blocks a full takeover, Orcel’s path to operational control runs through regulatory channels. The next milestone could be the annual general meeting in early 2027, where UniCredit has signalled it would seek to oust the current management if it can muster sufficient shareholder support. ... On the chart, technical indicators still favour the bulls. The 30-day volatility sits at a moderate 22.81%, while the relative strength index of 61.7 points to buying pressure without entering overbought territory. The stock trades 12.40% above its 200-day moving average of €34.40, and 4.84% above the 50-day average of €36.89 — evidence of a sustained uptrend. ... The bull case rests on Commerzbank’s operational independence. Management has reaffirmed its 2026 outlook and medium-term targets through 2030. The second-quarter earnings report, due on August 6, will be a critical test; solid numbers could strengthen the argument that the bank is better off alone. The bear case warns that UniCredit already has a stranglehold in place, regardless of the regulatory paperwork, and that Orcel’s plan to cut 7,000 jobs and extract billions in synergies would inevitably crush the current independence premium in the share price. ... A separate and unresolved issue is the surge in securities lending activity in Commerzbank stock. The bank itself has flagged the rise as “unusual” in both scale and timing. If that activity is linked to hidden control structures, it could inject fresh uncertainty into the ownership picture and prompt deeper regulatory scrutiny. ... For now, two clocks tick simultaneously. One is regulatory: the ECB and EU Commission must decide whether green light the bid. The other is operational: Commerzbank must keep delivering results to justify its share price without the takeover premium. The stock’s next move will likely be determined by which clock strikes first. ... ### Commerzbank’s Stalemate with UniCredit Deepens as Jefferies Takes 10.43% Stake and Payout Promise Bolsters Stock ... deepens-as-jefferies-takes-10- ... 3-stake-and-payout-promise-bolsters-stock"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Kreditkarten: Commerzbank tauscht Mastercard gegen Visa aus,www.handelsblatt.com,2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.handelsblatt.com/finanzen/banken-versicherungen/banken/kreditkarten-commerzbank-tauscht-mastercard-gegen-visa-aus/100239158.html,"Kreditkarten: Commerzbank tauscht Mastercard gegen Visa aus Kreditkarten: Commerzbank tauscht Mastercard gegen Visa aus Das Frankfurter Geldhaus fordert seine Kunden auf, ihre Mastercard-Kreditkarte vorzeitig einzutauschen. Damit stärkt Visa seine Position im deutschen Bankenmarkt. , 10.07.2026 - 10:11 Uhr Commerzbank in Frankfurt am Main: Post für Privatkunden. Foto: Michael Brandt/dpa ... Frankfurt. Viele Privatkunden haben in diesen Tagen Post von der bekommen. Dabei geht es nicht um den Übernahmekampf mit dem italienischen Konkurrenten Unicredit, sondern um ihre Kreditkarten. Das Institut sortiert"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"UniCredit-Commerzbank deal not ‘fully over the line’, analysts warn - The Banker",www.thebanker.com,2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thebanker.com/content/8eeded8e-a643-4edc-be26-d2bd54a9b7c2,"UniCredit-Commerzbank deal not ‘fully over the line’, analysts warn - The Banker ... UniCredit chief Andrea Orcel moved one step closer this week to achieving his longstanding ambition to gain control of Germany’s second-largest lender, but analysts warn that the deal is still not “fully over the line”. ... On Tuesday, the Italian lender announced that it had secured a 47.6 per cent stake in Commerzbank, after investors holding 17.6 per cent of Commerzbank shares accepted its €44bn all-share offer before the deadline. UniCredit already held a near-30 per cent position in Commerzbank before it made the all-share offer. ... give it effective control and the ability to ... meetings based on past attendance at Commerzbank annual meetings. ... But analysts caution that UniCredit’s increased holding remains subject to regulatory approval, and is still below the 50 per cent threshold needed for decisive influence over board appointments, strategy and governance. ... “UniCredit is now serving for the match,” ... Alloatti, head of financials at Federated Hermes, stated in his weekly markets wrap published on Thursday. Yet while ... than 46 per cent stake puts it in a “command ... position”, there are still several important points ... fully over the line ... Any move to consolidate Commerzbank requires approval from German and European antitrust and banking authorities, including the European Central Bank. ... Alloatti said this could potentially take up to six months, with the operational and accounting work associated with consolidation, including purchase price adjustments, likely to extend the timeline further. That points to a “potential completion window” of around spring 2027. ... Johann Scholtz, senior equity analyst at Morningstar DBRS, said a “simple majority” (50 per cent + 1) is still far from the 75 per cent “supermajority” UniCredit needs to implement a merger and push for closer integration between its German operations, HypoVereinsbank and Commerzbank. The German government’s 12 per cent stake therefore remains important, he added. ... According to Scope Ratings analysts, Commerzbank still has some options open to it, such as its ability not to cancel its current treasury stock (shares it owns) and to increase its share capital by up to 10 per cent, which could introduce “some uncertainty” over whether UniCredit will reach the voting rights threshold needed to declare intent of control. ... Yet Alloatti noted Commerzbank’s management has thus far been clear on not wanting to use “poison pills” such as the takeover of a smaller bank or dilutive rights issues to derail UniCredit’s approach. ... Commerzbank has, however, disputed acceptance levels for UniCredit’s all-share offer, saying it does not reflect genuine shareholder support. ... In a statement issued earlier this week following UniCredit’s announcement of its increased stake, it said that fewer than 2 per cent of shares had been tendered by institutional and private investors, which demonstrated its “lack of appeal” among independent shareholders. ... The German lender remains defiant, stating that it will continue to pursue its go-it-alone “Momentum 2030” strategy despite UniCredit’s substantially increased stake, while confirming its 2026 outlook and 2030 targets. ... Commerzbank’s works council, which represents the lender’s staff in workplace matters, on Thursday reiterated its opposition to UniCredit’s approach. ... Scholtz said employee representatives could make a full integration between HVB and Commerzbank slower and more difficult than the shareholding alone would suggest."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank gibt mit Microsoft und Google bei KI-Rollout Gas | Computerwoche,www.computerwoche.de (von Jürgen Hill Chefreporter Future Technologies),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.computerwoche.de/article/4194423/commerzbank-gibt-mit-microsoft-und-google-bei-ki-rollout-gas.html,"Commerzbank gibt mit Microsoft und Google bei KI-Rollout Gas | Computerwoche ... # Commerzbank gibt mit Microsoft und Google bei KI-Rollout Gas ... Beim KI-Rollout an die Breite der Belegschaft setzt die Commerzbank auf Microsoft 365 Copilot sowie Gemini Enterprise. ... Commerzbank AG ... Ein Unternehmen, das jetzt den Schritt angeht, KI direkt und in der Breite in den Arbeitsalltag ihrer Mitarbeiter zu integrieren ist die Commerzbank. Im Gegensatz zum Autobauer Mercedes-Benz, der dabei auf eine Partnerschaft mit dem Berliner Unicorn n8n setzt, verlässt man sich bei der Bank auf die US-amerikanischen Hyperscaler Microsoft und Google. ... So weitet das Geldhaus seine Partnerschaften mit den beiden Konzernen aus, um KI-Assistenten Microsoft 365 Copilot sowie Gemini Enterprise einzuführen. Zielgruppe sind nicht hochspezialisierte Daten-Teams, sondern klassische Sachbearbeiter und Manager. ... Die Bank will so die Grundlage für effizientere Abläufe und ein modernes Arbeitsumfeld schaffen. So sollen Nutzungshürden gesenkt und der produktive Einsatz künstlicher Intelligenz im gesamten Konzern erleichtert werden. ... ## 600 Millionen Invest für KI ... Der Rollout erfolgt im Rahmen der Strategie „ Momentum 2030“ mit der die Bank die Potenziale von KI noch stärker ausschöpfen will. Im Zeitraum von 2026 bis 2030 plant sie kumuliert rund 600 Millionen Euro in diesem Bereich investieren. Ab 2030 erwartet die Commerzbank aus ihren KI-Initiativen einen Wertbeitrag von rund 500 Millionen Euro pro Jahr. ... Dabei ist das Thema KI für die Bank kein Neuland. So hat die Bank bereits 2017 – lange vor dem aktuellen KI-Hype – einen eigenen Bereich für Big Data und Advanced Analytics ins Leben gerufen. Im Zuge der KI-Strategie des Instituts wurden dann Projekte wie der virtuelle Avatar Ava, das Assistenzsystem Sherlock oder Fraud AI realisiert. Ebenso wurde eine eigene AI Academy gegründet, um Mitarbeiter zu schulen."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,UniCredit rises to 47.6% of Commerzbank after final close of offer | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/unicredit-rises-to-47-6-of-commerzbank-after-final-close-of-offer-ce7f5ed8d18ff622,"UniCredit rises to 47.6% of Commerzbank after final close of offer | MarketScreener ... # UniCredit rises to 47.6% of Commerzbank after final close of offer Published on 07/08/2026 at 04:10 am EDT - Modified on 07/08/2026 at 04:29 am EDT ... UniCredit has secured a 47.6% stake in Commerzbank after collecting tenders equal to 17.6% of the share capital in its share exchange offer, whose final results were released today. The stake tendered adds to the 26.77% accumulated in the German bank since September 2024, plus 3.22% held via share-settled derivatives. UniCredit launched the public exchange offer in May at a price Germans judged too low, aiming to surpass the 30% threshold so it could subsequently buy additional shares on the market without triggering a mandatory takeover bid. The first phase of the offer ended in mid-June with tenders equal to 12.5% of the share capital, and on July 3 two additional weeks made available to investors for any new tenders, as required under German rules, also came to a close. ... During the main phase of the offer, the two banks traded accusations and criticism over the figures on tenders. Commerzbank argued that the shares contributed to the offer largely came from investment banks that were counterparties to the swap contracts UniCredit had entered into on Commerzbank shares. ... In a statement, UniCredit said it will continue to pursue constructive dialogue with all interested parties. The German government, which has rebuffed UniCredit's approach as hostile, holds about 12% of Commerzbank. ... (Italian version by Claudia Cristoferi, editing by Stefano Bernabei) ... | | Add to a list Add to a list 0 selected To use this feature you must be a member Log in Sign up | Off-Hours Price | Change | 5-day change | Capi. | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | UNICREDIT S.P.A. | 81.61 EUR | -0.11% | +1.47% | 141B | | | COMMERZBANK AG | 37.67 EUR | +0.88% | +2.42% | 46.8B | | |"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Analysis-UniCredit closes in on Commerzbank as battle enters endgame | KELO-AM,kelo.com (Thomson Reuters),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://kelo.com/2026/07/08/analysis-unicredit-closes-in-on-commerzbank-as-battle-enters-endgame/,"Analysis-UniCredit closes in on Commerzbank as battle enters endgame | ... Analysis-UniCredit closes in on Commerzbank as battle enters endgame ... FRANKFURT/MILAN, July 8 (Reuters) – One of Europe’s most cantankerous banking battles in decades is becoming more a question of how and when, not if, UniCredit secures its prize, after it disclosed it was nearing control of Germany’s Commerzbank in its €45 billion ($51 billion) hostile deal. ... The Milan-based bank led since 2021 by CEO Andrea Orcel on Wednesday revealed it now owns 48% of the German lender’s shares after it launched a low-ball takeover offer for Commerzbank in May. ... It has not ‌been easy. UniCredit first invested in Commerzbank in September 2024, launching a nearly two-year tug-of-war that pitted Italy’s and Germany’s No. 2 banks against each other. ... German opposition to Orcel’s overtures has been widespread, and the deal encapsulates the difficulty of merging large banks across euro zone countries despite central bankers wanting more tie-ups to compete with bigger American rivals. ... Commerzbank responded to Wednesday’s news by saying less than 2% of retail and institutional investors had tendered their shares, with most coming from “banks and parties connected to UniCredit” ‌which underscored the deal’s “low attractiveness”. ... But UniCredit and its CEO are gaining a momentum even critics admit appears unstoppable. ... Boris ⁠Rhein, the premier of Commerzbank’s home state ⁠of Hesse, on Wednesday called on the banks to talk. ... “The priority now is to find common ground and engage in constructive dialogue at the highest levels of management,” he said in an emailed statement. ... All eyes are on Orcel’s next move. His options include amending some swap contracts UniCredit holds to get to 59% of Commerzbank, buying shares on the open market once the approval process is complete next year, or engaging in talks with Commerzbank about a deal. ... Both parties say they are willing to sit down, though they have been unable to find common ground so far. ... Orcel could force through a merger with 75%, but with Berlin still owning 12% it would ⁠be left to contend with the government and other minority shareholders. ... Commerzbank executives who have ⁠fought for months to keep their lender independent now stress the need to get a better premium for shareholders, some of whom say they would tender their shares if the price were right. ... Orcel expects the European Central Bank will soon determine that UniCredit has de facto control of Commerzbank. Doing so at a time when UniCredit has less than 50% of shares will cost it more in capital than if it had majority control. ... Crossing the 50% threshold is also ⁠necessary if UniCredit is to name half of Commerzbank’s supervisory board members, as Orcel has suggested it could do. ... “It is increasingly likely that UniCredit will now have to consolidate it post the tender offer and ECB approvals (and reverse the buyback deduction booked for 2025)”, Citi said this week. ... Yet ⁠reaching the finishing line for Orcel is not guaranteed. ... One ‌complication is the wave of banking M&A in UniCredit’s home market, where rivals are consolidating. ... Going all-in on ⁠Commerzbank would limit its financial ability to participate, pushing UniCredit further down the national ranking. ... Then there is German opposition, which ‌former UniCredit employees involved in its purchase of Germany’s HVB two decades ago said could get the bank mired ⁠in bureaucratic hurdles. ... If Orcel cannot convince Commerzbank or Berlin to talk, he could end up owning most shares but not yet able to push through the full merger he desires. ... “Yes, there is indeed a big risk that this will not work out well for UniCredit. Then again, in finance, money often wins the day, and I can imagine senior management at Commerzbank falling in line once everything is done,” he said."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank calls UniCredit offer unattractive | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-calls-unicredit-offer-unattractive-ce7f5ed8d180fe2c,"Commerzbank calls UniCredit offer unattractive | MarketScreener ... # Commerzbank calls UniCredit offer unattractive Published on 07/08/2026 at 05:04 am EDT - Modified on 07/08/2026 at 05:06 am EDT UNICREDIT S.P.A. -0.11% ... FRANKFURT, July 8 (Reuters) - Commerzbank said on Wednesday that less than 2% of institutional and retail investors had tendered their shares as part of UniCredit's offer. ""The low acceptance rate among independent shareholders is clear evidence of the low attractiveness of the offer,"" Commerzbank said. (Reporting by Tom Sims, editing by Kirsti Knolle) ... | | Add to a list Add to a list 0 selected To use this feature you must be a member Log in Sign up | Off-Hours Price | Change | 5-day change | Capi. | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | COMMERZBANK AG | 37.67 EUR | +0.88% | +2.42% | 46.8B | | | UNICREDIT S.P.A. | 81.61 EUR | -0.11% | +1.47% | 141B | | |"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,UniCredit falls just short of a Commerzbank majority | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/unicredit-falls-just-short-of-a-commerzbank-majority-ce7f5ed9d98ef426,"UniCredit falls just short of a Commerzbank majority | MarketScreener ... # UniCredit falls just short of a Commerzbank majority Published on 07/08/2026 at 07:53 am EDT ... The Italian banking group UniCredit has fallen just short of a majority stake in Commerzbank after its takeover offer for the Frankfurt lender expired. That puts pressure on both sides to finally sit down together after several failed attempts and reach an amicable settlement. After the second acceptance period, UniCredit has access to 47.6 percent of Commerzbank shares. At a shareholders' meeting, the Milan-based bank could even bring 49.65 percent to bear, because treasury shares held by Commerzbank carry no voting rights. The Italians spoke of ""another step toward implementing the strategic investment in Commerzbank"", but struck a more conciliatory tone than before: it said it wanted to engage in talks with all stakeholders around Commerzbank, in a statement on Wednesday. ... Commerzbank management, which is fighting what it views as a hostile takeover, urged a settlement with UniCredit: ""Only with a consensual solution involving the company leadership, employees and their representatives, as well as the federal government as the second-largest shareholder, is it realistic from Commerzbank's perspective to achieve synergies from a merger to an appropriate extent and within an appropriate timeframe."" Management board and supervisory board were ""open to a constructive dialogue with UniCredit"". ... Several attempts to hold talks at leadership level had, however, fizzled out or failed. The strategic plans of Commerzbank management led by CEO Bettina Orlopp are far removed from what UniCredit CEO Andrea Orcel has in mind for the Frankfurt bank. In a takeover, Commerzbank is primarily worried about its extensive international network, which it uses to support Germany's mid-sized companies in exporting. Orcel, by contrast, wants to impose UniCredit's business model on Commerzbank, a model largely limited to its European core markets. Italians have made Munich-based HypoVereinsbank (HVB), which has been part of UniCredit for more than 20 years, significantly more profitable, but at the cost of its relevance and thousands of jobs. ... The federal government, Commerzbank's second-largest shareholder, again backed the bank's leadership. ""The federal government will continue to act in the interests of Commerzbank employees, Germany's mid-sized businesses, and the Frankfurt financial center,"" a spokesperson for the SPD-led finance ministry in Berlin said. ""UniCredit's aggressive and hostile approach remains unacceptable from the federal government's perspective."" He reaffirmed that the government would not sell its 12 percent stake to UniCredit. That does not, however, prevent the takeover. The ministry pointed out that Germany's financial regulator BaFin and the European Central Bank (ECB) banking supervisors would have to review all further steps by UniCredit. ... As a result, Commerzbank shareholders who have tendered their shares to UniCredit will also have to wait for the share exchange to be completed. Numerous approvals are still outstanding. The key question is whether the ECB will now determine that UniCredit already controls Commerzbank de facto. If so, the Italians would also have to absorb the risks on Commerzbank's balance sheet. UniCredit has acknowledged that its core capital ratio would fall by 2.8 percentage points as a result. The Italians had threatened that, with a controlling majority, they could fill all shareholder-side seats on the supervisory board. The federal government, however, has a contractual right to nominate two candidates itself. BaFin President Mark Branson was due to appear before the Bundestag finance committee on Wednesday. ... UniCredit said the offer had been accepted for 17.6 percent of Commerzbank shares. The exchange is hardly worth it for Commerzbank shareholders: the stock was at €38.14 on Wednesday. The 0.485 UniCredit shares Orcel offered in return are worth €38.70. UniCredit had already held 26.8 percent, meaning the Italians have now reached 44.4 percent of the shares. That is significantly more than had been expected at the start of the takeover battle. With call options for additional Commerzbank shares, it can even increase to 47.6 percent. Above 50 percent, UniCredit would have to submit a mandatory offer for Commerzbank's Polish unit mBank, which is valued at the equivalent of €14bn. ... Commerzbank management, however, continues to question how the acceptance rate could have come about. According to its data, fewer than two percent of institutional and retail shareholders accepted the offer. The bulk of the acceptance rate is said to come from banks and parties connected to the Italian bank. ""It remains non-transparent to what extent borrowed shares were tendered and what hedging agreements were concluded in this context,"" the statement said. ... | | Add to a list Add to a list 0 selected To use this feature you must be a member Log in Sign up | Off-Hours Price | Change | 5-day change | Capi. | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | COMMERZBANK AG | 39.00 EUR | +1.33% | +3.53% | 47.9B | | | UNICREDIT S.P.A. | 84.40 EUR | -0.39% | +3.42% | 146B | | | MBANK S.A. | 1,415.00 PLN | -1.50% | +4.70% | 16.38B | | |"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Deadline day for Commerzbank,www.economist.com,2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.economist.com/the-world-in-brief/2026/07/08/87a6ceb9-cdb0-4908-978d-f7b9d58dd921,"Deadline day for Commerzbank ... # Deadline day for Commerzbank ... The battle for Commerzbank, a leading German lender, reached a critical point on Wednesday morning when UniCredit, a big Italian bank, announced the outcome of its takeover bid. It offered Commerzbank’s shareholders the chance to swap one share for 0.485 of UniCredit’s, implicitly valuing the German bank at a discount. When the tender process opened in May, UniCredit owned 26.8% of Commerzbank directly (plus more via derivatives). It says it now has close to 50% in its hands."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank presses for 'amicable solution' with UniCredit | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/commerzbank-presses-for-amicable-solution-with-unicredit-ce7f5ed8d08aff2c,"Commerzbank presses for 'amicable solution' with UniCredit | MarketScreener # Commerzbank presses for 'amicable solution' with UniCredit Published on 07/08/2026 at 05:45 am EDT ... Commerzbank is urging its Italian cornerstone shareholder UniCredit to reach an amicable agreement. 'Only with a mutually agreed solution that involves company management, employees and their representatives, as well as the German federal government as the second-largest shareholder, is it realistic from Commerzbank's perspective to achieve synergies from a merger on an appropriate scale and within an appropriate timeframe,' the bank said in a statement published on Wednesday. The management board and supervisory board were 'open to a constructive dialogue with UniCredit'. Still, the strategy UniCredit has in mind for Commerzbank runs counter to the plans of Commerzbank's management. ... UniCredit had announced that, through a share-exchange offer, it had secured up to 47.6% of Commerzbank shares and 49.65% of the voting rights. Commerzbank's leadership, however, continues to question how the acceptance rate came about for an offer it views as economically barely attractive. According to its data, fewer than 2% of institutional and retail shareholders accepted the offer. The bulk of the 17.6% acceptance rate reported by UniCredit is said to come from banks and parties connected to the Italian bank. 'It remains unclear to what extent borrowed shares were tendered and what hedging arrangements were made in this context,' the statement said. ... 'Going forward, the focus of our actions will remain on the interests of our customers, our employees, and our shareholders,' said Commerzbank CEO Bettina Orlopp. 'As the leading financing partner for Germany's Mittelstand and as a bank serving more than ten million retail customers, we bear a great responsibility, including toward the German economy.' ... | | Add to a list Add to a list 0 selected To use this feature you must be a member Log in Sign up | Off-Hours Price | Change | 5-day change | Capi. | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | | COMMERZBANK AG | 37.67 EUR | +0.88% | +2.42% | 46.8B | | | UNICREDIT S.P.A. | 81.61 EUR | -0.11% | +1.47% | 141B | | |"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,German government says Unicredit's Commerzbank approach remains unacceptable | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/german-government-says-unicredit-s-commerzbank-approach-remains-unacceptable-ce7f5ed8d08df721,German government says Unicredit's Commerzbank approach remains unacceptable | MarketScreener ... AG ... # German government says Unicredit's Commerzbank approach remains unacceptable Published on 07/08/2026 at 05:47 am EDT
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,UniCredit raises Commerzbank holding to 47.6%; Santander overhauls its Apac business - The Banker,www.thebanker.com,2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thebanker.com/content/9ff2aba5-e9e6-4eac-b7e6-260ad58a72b7,"UniCredit raises Commerzbank holding to 47.6%; Santander overhauls its Apac business - The Banker ... # UniCredit raises Commerzbank holding to 47.6%; Santander overhauls its Apac business ... UniCredit has secured a 47.6 per cent stake in Commerzbank, putting chief executive Andrea Orcel close to effective control of Germany’s second-largest lender. ... The Italian bank said investors holding 17.6 per cent of Commerzbank shares accepted its €44bn all-share offer before the deadline, adding to the near-30 per cent position it had built before the bid."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,UniCredit says secures 17.6% of Commerzbank in hostile takeover - Politics - Ansa.it,www.ansa.it (Redazione ANSA),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ansa.it/nuova_europa/en/news/sections/politics/2026/07/08/unicredit-says-secures-17.6-of-commerzbank-in-hostile-takeover_5450b9c5-49d1-4932-b3b0-4d512248ffc6.html,"UniCredit says secures 17.6% of Commerzbank in hostile takeover - Politics - Ansa.it ... UniCredit says secures 17.6% of Commerzbank in hostile takeover ... UniCredit says secures 17.6% of Commerzbank in hostile takeover ... # UniCredit says secures 17.6% of Commerzbank in hostile takeover ... Highly political takeover bid to create a European giant ... 08 luglio 2026, 10:48 ... (ANSA-AFP) - ROME, JUL 8 - Italy's UniCredit said Wednesday it had secured an additional 17.6 percent stake in Germany's Commerzbank as part of its hostile and highly political takeover bid to create a European giant. UniCredit said in a statement that ""shares representing 17.60 percent of Commerzbank's outstanding share capital have been tendered, well ahead of original expectations"". UniCredit said that this added up to 49.65 percent of Commerzbank voting rights, taking into account its directly held 26.77 percent stake and different financial instruments. ""The completion of the tender offer periods represents a further step in the execution of UniCredit's strategic investment in Commerzbank,"" UniCredit, Italy's second biggest lender, said. The Milan-based bank launched its bid, valued at 35 billion euros ($40.6 billion), in early May to gain control of its German rival and cement its status as a European heavyweight. The offer price has been widely seen as too low and marks the latest move in UniCredit's relentless pursuit of Commerzbank that has sparked fury from the lender and top German politicians. (ANSA-AFP)."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"Commerzbank: Unicredit hält jetzt 49,65 Prozent der Stimmrechte | FAZ","www.faz.net (Christian Schubert, Rom)",2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.faz.net/aktuell/wirtschaft/unternehmen/commerzbank-unicredit-haelt-jetzt-49-65-prozent-der-stimmrechte-accg-201008770.html,"Ursprünglich wollte sich Unicredit mit dem Übernahmeangebot für die Commerzbank nur mehr Freiheiten verschaffen. Besonders beim Agieren im Kapital der Bank aus Frankfurt störten Schwellenwerte und behördliche Verpflichtungen. Daher fiel die Offerte bei der Ankündigung im März mit einer Prämie von nur vier Prozent gegenüber dem vorherigen Handelstag ziemlich bescheiden aus. Doch nun hat das Ergebnis des Angebots alle Erwartungen übertroffen: Der Unicredit-Anteil an der Commerzbank steigt auf mehr als 47 Prozent, was der Bank aus Mailand einen Stimmrechtsanteil von fast 50 Prozent sichert. Bei der Hauptversammlung, die nie eine vollständige Präsenz der Anteilseigner aufweist, sichert dies Unicredit künftig eine Mehrheit für die wichtigsten Entscheidungen bis hin zur Besetzung des Aufsichtsrats, der wiederum den Vorstand ernennt. ... Damit steigt der Druck auf alle Verteidiger einer eigenständigen Commerzbank, vor allem die Führung der Bank, die Bundesregierung und die Belegschaftsvertreter. Gleichzeitig kommt der Unicredit-Vorstandsvorsitzende Andrea Orcel in einem entscheidenden Schritt seinem seit fast zwei Jahren verfolgten Ziel näher, die Commerzbank faktisch zu kontrollieren. Eine Fusion mit der Unicredit-Tochtergesellschaft Hypovereinsbank steht zwar nicht unmittelbar an, doch sie ist nicht mehr ausgeschlossen. Sie setzt 75 Prozent der Stimmrechte auf einer Hauptversammlung voraus. Mit dem nun in Aussicht stehenden Gewicht könnte Unicredit gleichwohl bei der Commerzbank wesentliche Restrukturierungsmaßnahmen durchsetzen. ... In der Bankenzentrale in Mailand betonte man am Mittwoch, dass in keiner Weise ein Kahlschlag vorgesehen sei, sondern man sozialverträglich etwa mit Vorruhestandsregelungen vorgehen wolle; und man wolle sich dafür vergleichsweise viel Zeit lassen. Unicredit sucht daher nun das Gespräch mit der Bundesregierung. Diese ist heute mit zwölf Prozent zweitgrößter Aktionär und verfügt über zwei Vertreter im Commerzbank-Aufsichtsrat, die zumindest theoretisch Unicredit bremsen könnten. ... Die Bundesregierung reagierte am Mittwoch kühl und teilte mit, dass sie weiter im Sinne der Commerzbank-Beschäftigten, des deutschen Mittelstands und des Finanzstandorts Frankfurt handeln werde. „Das aggressive und feindliche Vorgehen der Unicredit bleibt aus Sicht der Bundesregierung inakzeptabel“, hieß es in einer Stellungnahme des Bundesfinanzministeriums. Der interministerielle Lenkungsausschuss der Bundesregierung habe das Angebot der Unicredit abgelehnt und die Anteile des Bundes an der Commerzbank nicht verkauft. Die Bundesregierung sieht nach eigenen Angaben derzeit keinen Anlass, diese Position zu verändern. Nun müssten Bafin und EZB ‌weitere Schritte prüfen. ... Aus Kreisen der Bundesregierung verlautete zudem, dass mögliche Pläne der Unicredit, die Commerzbank von der Börse zu nehmen, heute praktisch nur sehr schwer realisierbar wären, solange der Bund seine Anteile an der Commerzbank halte. Die aktuellen Pläne des Unicredit-Vorstands etwa für das Mittelstandsgeschäft seien daher nicht tragfähig, hieß es. ... Die Commerzbank verwies in einer Stellungnahme darauf, dass nach ihren Erkenntnissen nur weniger als zwei Prozent der „unabhängigen“ Aktionäre das Übernahmeangebot angenommen hätten. Dies zeige, wie unattraktiv die Offerte gewesen sei. Die getauschten Aktien stammten „überwiegend von mit der Unicredit verbundenen Banken und Parteien“, die aufgrund von Geschäftsbeziehungen der italienischen Bank einen Gefallen getan hätten. Die von Unicredit direkt gehaltenen Aktien, gemeldete Derivate und angediente Aktien dürften nicht einfach addiert werden, meint die Commerzbank. „Es ist weiterhin nicht transparent, in welchem Umfang geliehene Aktien angedient und welche Absicherungsvereinbarungen in diesem Kontext getroffen wurden“, heißt es in ihrer Stellungnahme. ... Doch der Aufsichtsrat und der Vorstand der Commerzbank stünden „einem konstruktiven Dialog mit Unicredit offen gegenüber“, betont die Bank. Nur einvernehmlich unter Einbindung der Unternehmensführung, der Arbeitnehmervertreter und der Bundesregierung sei es „aus Sicht der Commerzbank realistisch, Synergien aus einem Zusammenschluss in einem angemessenen Umfang und Zeitrahmen zu erreichen“, teilt die Commerzbank mit. Schon in der Vergangenheit forderten beide Seiten Gespräche, warfen sich dann aber gegenseitig vor, diese nicht ernsthaft führen zu wollen. ... Wie Unicredit am Mittwochvormittag bekannt gab, kommt die Bank aus Mailand bei der Commerzbank nun auf einen Stimmrechtsanteil von 49,65 Prozent. Denn 17,6 Prozent der Commerzbank-Aktionäre haben das Umtauschangebot angenommen. Zuvor besaß Unicredit bereits 26,77 Prozent der Commerzbank-Aktien. Zusammen mit 3,22 Prozent an Derivaten entstehe so ein Anteil von 47,59 Prozent. Nach Angaben von Unicredit führt dies zu Stimmrechten von 49,65 Prozent, denn eigene Aktien der Commerzbank sind nicht stimmberechtigt und sollen von der Bank in Frankfurt ohnehin eingezogen werden. Unicredit besitzt darüber hinaus nach eigenen Angaben zusätzlich Derivate für Commerzbank-Aktien von 13 Prozent, die aber keine Stimmrechte mit sich bringen. ... Nun bleibt abzuwarten, wie schnell der Unicredit-Chef Orcel bei der Commerzbank zu seinem Ziel kommen kann: der Verschmelzung von Deutschlands zweitgrößter Geschäftsbank mit der Hypovereinsbank. Die Bank aus München ist schon seit zwei Jahrzehnten eine Tochtergesellschaft der italienischen Großbank, die selbst durch zahlreiche Zusammenschlüsse entstanden ist, nicht zuletzt die verschiedener italienischer Sparkassen. ... Heute besteht der Commerzbank-Aufsichtsrat aus Mitgliedern der Kapitalseite und den Arbeitnehmervertretern, die eine Übernahme vehement ablehnen. Auf der nächsten Hauptversammlung im Frühjahr kommenden Jahres aber stehen acht der zehn Vertreter der Kapitalseite zur Wiederwahl an. Diese könnte Unicredit mit seiner Hauptversammlungsmehrheit bestimmen. Zudem haben im Kontrollgremium zwei Vertreter des Bundes Sitz und Stimme: Harald Christ und Sabine Lautenschläger-Peiter. Letztere ist noch bis zur Hauptversammlung 2028 gewählt. Grund dafür ist eine Selbstverpflichtung der Commerzbank aus dem Jahr 2009. Damals, nach der Finanzkrise, hatte der Bund die Commerzbank durch seine Beteiligung gerettet. Freilich könnte sich Orcel über diese Vereinbarung hinwegsetzen. Ob er damit gut beraten wäre, ist eine andere Frage. ... Letztlich gilt die Vereinbarung auch nur, solange der Bund mehr als zehn Prozent an der Bank hält. Sinkt der Anteil unter diese Marke, steht gemäß der Vereinbarung dem Bund noch ein Vertreter im Kontrollgremium der Bank zu. ... Die Umtauschofferte von Unicredit dürfte auch deshalb erfolgreich gewesen sein, weil sich die Kurse in den vergangenen Wochen günstig entwickelten. Nach Angaben von Bloomberg entfielen mehr als fünf Prozent der getauschten Aktien auf die letzten zwei Wochen der verlängerten Annahmefrist. Am Ende der Frist hatte die Offerte wieder eine Prämie für die Commerzbank-Aktionäre enthalten, nachdem sie zuvor wegen der Kursschwankungen verschwunden war. Der Aufschlag bewegte sich zuletzt indes nur im niedrigen einstelligen Prozentbereich, was bei Übernahmeangeboten häufig nicht reicht, um die Anteilseigner vom Umtausch zu überzeugen. Daher der Verweis der Commerzbank auf die „befreundeten“ Finanzinstitutionen von Unicredit. ... Die italienische Bank argumentierte dagegen, dass die Kurssteigerungen der Commerzbank-Aktie nur durch das Interesse der Unicredit zustande gekommen seien, nicht durch fundamentale Verbesserungen. Diese Wertsteigerungen wollten sich die Commerzbank-Aktionäre sichern, zumal von nun an Kursverluste der Commerzbank-Aktie nicht auszuschließen seien. ... exemplarisch für den Finanzplatz Frankfurt. In den vergangenen zehn Jahren gab es mehrfach die Idee einer Fusion. Ihr Scheitern ist heute eine entscheidende Wegmarke."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Personal letter of 26.6.2026 to all shareholder of Commerzbank - Group Website,www.commerzbank.de,2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.commerzbank.de/group/what-drives-us/commerzbank-as-a-company/20260626-unicredit-letter-to-shareholders.html,"Personal letter of 26.6.2026 to all shareholder of Commerzbank - Group Website ... # New letter to all shareholders of Commerzbank ... Bettina Orlopp once again underlined Commerzbank’s position in another letter to the shareholders on 26 June 2026 (convenience translation) ... The regular acceptance period for the public takeover offer by UniCredit S.p.A. ended on 16 June 2026. The additional acceptance period runs from 20 June to 3 July 2026. Our recommendation remains unchanged: do not accept UniCredit's offer and stay invested in Commerzbank. ... The acceptance rate among our shareholders so far speaks for itself: By the end of the regular acceptance period, Commerzbank's free-float investors – more than 500,000 retail shareholders and several hundred institutional investors – had tendered only just over 1% of the shares. In addition, the German government – our second-largest shareholder – has publicly confirmed that it will not transfer its stake to UniCredit, on the grounds that neither the price offered nor UniCredit's conduct is adequate. The large majority of the remaining shares tendered comes from banks and parties connected to UniCredit as derivative counterparties. ... UniCredit's offer continues to provide no adequate premium for your Commerzbank shares. The average target price set by independent analysts is significantly above both the implied offer price and our current share price – speaking for the value potential of your share. To this day, UniCredit has not put forward a credible plan that builds on the strengths of Commerzbank's business model. ... #### Your Commerzbank is strong – and 2026 will prove it ... You are a shareholder in the largest financing partner to Germany's Mittelstand. In that role, we bear responsibility for our clients and the German economy as a whole – and we take it seriously. We have had a very successful start to 2026: with our ""Momentum 2030"" strategy, we continue to grow profitably and create value reliably. On 6 August 2026, we will present our results for the second quarter – and we are confident they will give you further proof of our company's operational strength. Those who stay invested participate in this value-creation potential. ... ina Orlo ... Chief Executive Officer"
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"Commerz, Berlin’s response: we will not sell our 12.7% stake to UniCredit - Il Sole 24 ORE",en.ilsole24ore.com,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.ilsole24ore.com/art/commerzbank-defence-berlin-we-will-not-sell-our-127-per-cent-stake-in-unicredit-AI5qEwoD,"Commerz, Berlin’s response: we will not sell our 12.7% stake to UniCredit - Il Sole 24 ORE ... Commerz, Berlin’s response: we will not sell our 12.7% stake to UniCredit ... # Commerz, Berlin’s response: we will not sell our 12.7% stake to UniCredit ... ## In this way, it would aim to block Italy’s plans for a hypothetical delisting. Orlopp’s conditions: an appropriate premium and adherence to the current business model ... The German government has stepped up its opposition to the plans of UniCredit regarding Commerzbank, telling the Handelsblatt newspaper that it has no intention of selling its stake of around 12.7 per cent, which makes it the second-largest shareholder after Gae Aulenti. With this decision, Berlin aims to block the Italian bank’s “plans” for Germany’s second-largest bank, which could hypothetically – though this has never been stated – include a delisting, as happened at the time of the friendly takeover of 100 per cent of HVB’s shares. The so-called “plans for Commerz” are deemed by the government to be “unsustainable”, particularly in the interests of German small and medium-sized enterprises. But according to Berlin, they are not even “in the interests of UniCredit’s stakeholders”. The German Ministry of Finance, contacted by *Il Sole 24 Ore*, did not respond to the questions. ... The German government also made it clear to *Handelsblatt* that it intends to “firmly reject aggressive approaches”, including that of UniCredit: using the term “aggressive” already employed by the Finanzagentur last Friday when it rejected, via the Stabilisation Fund, the Voluntary Public Exchange Offer on the grounds that the premium was “inappropriate”. Berlin has reiterated that it “will continue to act in the interests of Commerzbank’s employees, German Mittelstand businesses and Frankfurt as a financial centre”. The defence of shareholders’ interests clearly rests solely with the bank’s board of directors, which, through its CEO Bettina Orlopp, continues to raise two conditions for returning to the negotiating table: a premium commensurate with the bank’s value and adherence to the current business model, which focuses on providing financial services to Mittelstand corporate clients in Germany and, above all, worldwide. ... The transformation of HVB following its acquisition by Unicredit(which took place in 2005, with Andrea Orcel acting as Merrill Lynch’s adviser on the deal) – particularly since 2020 under Orcel’s leadership – is the model being proposed for Commerz. However, this is not in terms of delisting, but rather in terms of greater efficiency, better use of capital and risk reduction. The cost-to-income ratio (a weak point for German banks), for example, fell at HVB over five years from 60.5 per cent in 2000 to 30.2 per cent in 2025.Net operating profit has tripled from 1.1 to 3.1 billion. It is true that HVB’s full-time staff fell in just over five years from just over 12,000 to around 8,400, but staff reductions are a widespread trend across the European banking sector, driven by digitalisation, online banking and branch closures, as well as M&A activity. It is precisely Commerz’s workforce – just over 40,100 and still declining even under the current management – that is at the heart of the federal government’s concerns; the government, which has very low approval ratings, fears the petty populism of the far-right AfD party. Another concern is the Mittelstand: it remains to be seen, however, whether UniCredit’s business model – which in Germany is described as focused on large corporations and retail banking, and thus at odds with Commerz’s model centred on SMEs – will be replicated in Germany’s second-largest bank, or whether the Commerz-HVB merger will give rise to a German banking giant that will focus on the typically German corporate banking model – a strength of both Commerz and HVB – but one that is better managed. ... The Handesblatt article considers all of UniCredit’s “plans” that would fail because of the government, given its unyielding stance with its stake of close to 13 per cent. Following the expiry of the acceptance period for the voluntary exchange offer made to Commerzbank shareholders, UniCredit has secured over 39 per cent of the shares: 12.51 per cent from the exchange offer and 26.77 per cent already held. Furthermore, it can easily increase its stake to 42.5% through total return swaps equivalent to a 3.225% voting stake in Commerzbank shares. ... Apart from delisting, which is impossible whilst Berlin holds a 13 per cent stake, a ‘squeeze-out’ would also be difficult to achieve, as under German law the new owner of a company must hold 90 per cent of the shares in order to force out minority shareholders with mandatory compensation. However, none of this is likely to feature in UniCredit’s actual plans, as, from the very outset of the merger proposal, CEO Orcel has maintained that he favours a friendly deal – certainly with regard to the German government, but also with regard to management and staff. The outcome remains wide open, and further twists and turns cannot be ruled out. Orcel is due to speak at a conference today."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Who owns Commerzbank? A takeover thriller with rules | RÖDL,www.roedl.com,2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.roedl.com/en/insights/who-owns-commerzbank-a-takeover-thriller-with-rules/,"Spectacular takeovers have repeatedly reshaped Germany’s corporate landscape - and German takeover law along with it. Vodafone/Mannesmann, Bayer/Schering, AMS/OSRAM: each of these cases has left its mark. With UniCredit’s attempt to gain control of Germany’s second-largest private bank, another chapter is now unfolding. This article examines the current situation and addresses the legal framework that significantly structures what is happening behind the scenes. ... On May 5, 2026, UniCredit published a voluntary takeover offer to acquire all shares in Commerzbank. Before submitting this takeover offer, UniCredit already held 26.8% of the shares. According to its own statements, by June 12, 2026 UniCredit had received tenders for around 11% of the shares from shareholders under the takeover offer, thereby exceeding the control threshold. ... On March 16, 2026, UniCredit published its decision to submit a takeover bid. The formal takeover bid followed on May 5, 2026: for each Commerzbank share, the Milan-based bank offered 0.485 new UniCredit shares – equivalent to around EUR 34.35 per share at the time of publication. UniCredit complied exactly with the statutory minimum thresholds mentioned and did not offer any premium. ... Commerzbank therefore criticizes the takeover bid as an opportunistic attempt to acquire control without reflecting the bank’s fundamental value and without offering an appropriate premium. Through its systematic share purchases over recent years and the deliberate choice of a voluntary takeover offer, UniCredit is acting with tactical calculation: unlike a mandatory takeover offer, the Milan-based bank determines the timing of the offer itself and can thus exploit price phases that are favorable to it to further expand its influence. ... This is also where Commerzbank’s accusation of market manipulation and misleading conduct by UniCredit comes into play: since the current Commerzbank share price of around EUR 37 (as of June 15, 2026) is significantly above the offer price of EUR 34.35, the offer is unlikely to persuade most shareholders on a rational basis. The fact that UniCredit nevertheless claims to have already received tenders for around 11% of the shares by June 12, 2026 raises questions and fuels Commerzbank’s suspicion that these acceptances did not come from independent investors. ... In addition to its direct shareholding, UniCredit had built up economic exposure to a further roughly 16.4% of Commerzbank shares via so-called cash-settled equity swaps, without formally holding them. Commerzbank accuses UniCredit of the tendered shares largely coming from those banks which, as counterparties to these derivatives, had previously held the shares formally in their own names – and not from independent investors who would have considered the offer attractive of their own accord. ... Commerzbank then involved the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin) to review the matter. In addition, Commerzbank’s group works council instructed its chair to file a criminal complaint on suspicion of market manipulation and misleading conduct under Sections 119 and 120 of the German Securities Trading Act (Wertpapierhandelsgesetz; WpHG). The allegation: the reported acceptance rate of around 11% created the impression of broad market acceptance, while in fact the acceptances largely came from banks contractually connected to UniCredit, thereby distorting the picture of genuine investor demand. ... The Frankfurt public prosecutor’s office is now examining the suspicion of market manipulation, while UniCredit firmly rejects these allegations. In parallel with fending off these accusations, UniCredit, in a statement on June 15, 2026, for the first time indirectly threatened to replace Commerzbank’s top management. ... Due to the strict requirements of the WpÜG, Commerzbank’s management has limited defensive actions available: once a takeover bid has been announced, the management board may no longer take any actions that could prevent the success of the offer (Section 33(1) WpÜG). A frequently used and generally permissible tool in practice is the share buyback of the company’s own shares: it takes shares off the market, makes it harder for the bidder to reach a majority, and can push the stock exchange price above the offer price. ... Based on a resolution of the general meeting on May 15, 2025, Commerzbank is authorized to repurchase its own shares of up to 10% of the share capital until 2030. The bank has already made use of this authorization and acquired around 46.6 million shares (around 4% of the share capital). ... For the 30% threshold, the program no longer plays a significant role. Its real significance lies elsewhere: the share buybacks reduce share capital, increase earnings per share, and send a clear signal to the market. Combined with a stock exchange price above the offer price, the share buybacks are therefore less a legal defense tool than a communicative message: Commerzbank does not need UniCredit. ... Given the target company’s narrow legal room for maneuver, in practice one thing above all makes the difference: targeted communication. The management board must remain factual, because unsubstantiated claims can be deemed market manipulation and, in the worst case, can turn the defense strategy into its opposite. ... those who argue with facts are convincing. ... On May 18, 2026, management board and supervisory board recommended in their reasoned statement not to accept UniCredit’s offer. It offered no appropriate premium, did not reflect the bank’s fundamental value, and was based on overstated synergies and unrealistic implementation assumptions. The bank’s own “Momentum 2030” strategy would create more value at significantly lower risk. ... Alongside this, Commerzbank is pursuing an offensive communications strategy: on a dedicated topic page, it bundles statements, interviews with CEO Bettina Orlopp, and expressions of support from corporate clients and the federal government — making it unmistakably clear that independence is the more value-creating path for shareholders. ... So far, according to Commerzbank, the acceptance rate among independent investors has been low. How it develops by the end of the extended acceptance period on July 3, 2026 remains open. The case highlights the structural limits of the WpÜG: the target company’s tightly constrained defense toolkit shifts the decision to where it belongs — to the shareholders. Whether or not UniCredit improves its offer, who wins the takeover battle for Germany’s second-largest private bank is one of the capital markets law questions of 2026."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Unicredit Raises Commerzbank Stake by More Than 10 Percentage Points,www.finews.com (Written by: Stefan Waldvogel | Redaktor),2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.finews.com/news/english-news/72494-unicredit-beteiligung-commerzbank-uebernahme-europa-banken-konzentrationsprozess-2,"Unicredit Raises Commerzbank Stake by More Than 10 Percentage Points ... # Unicredit Raises Commerzbank Stake by More Than 10 Percentage Points ... Italian banking group Unicredit has increased its prospective stake in Commerzbank despite its takeover offer remaining significantly below the German lender's current market valuation. It remains unclear who has tendered the shares. ... ## Unicredit Raises Commerzbank Stake by More Than 10 Percentage Points ... According to a statement released by Unicredit, shareholders representing 10,91 percent of Commerzbank's share capital have tendered their shares under the takeover offer that has been running since early May. If completed, Unicredit's stake would increase from 26,77 percent to 37,68 percent. ... Under the terms of the offer, Unicredit is offering 0,485 of its own shares for each Commerzbank share. Based on current market prices, the implied offer value remains more than €2 below Commerzbank's share price of €36,80. ... Despite the apparent discount, shareholders representing 7,58 percent of Commerzbank's shares had already accepted the offer by 2 June. ... Commerzbank has accused Unicredit of misleading the market and has requested that Germany's financial regulator, Bafin, investigate the matter. ... The German lender argued last week that the tendered shares should not be viewed as evidence of independent shareholder support for the offer. ... «These shares cannot be regarded as proof of independent support from shareholders for the offer,» the bank said. ... A Commerzbank spokesperson added: «Based on the information available to us, not a single acceptance of the offer by an institutional investor has so far been identified. Furthermore, the combined acceptances by retail investors correspond to a shareholding of only around 0,05 percent.» ... «The seriousness of Commerzbank's allegations, the continued briefings of the press by parties close to Commerzbank, and the ongoing dissemination of increasingly severe and unfounded misinformation require a clear response,» the Italian bank said. ... Unicredit added that while Commerzbank's management is entitled to recommend that shareholders reject the offer, it is not entitled to undermine the integrity of the takeover process. ... «The management of Commerzbank may recommend that its shareholders reject Unicredit's offer. However, it is not entitled to undermine the integrity of the offer process by making unfounded allegations that Unicredit's legally required disclosures are misleading or artificially inflated,» the statement said. ... Derivatives Increase Strategic Flexibility ... In addition to its direct shareholding, Unicredit continues to hold financial instruments equivalent to 3,22 percent of Commerzbank's share capital, which can be converted into shares. ... The Italian bank also maintains cash-settled derivative positions representing 13,19 percent of Commerzbank's stock. ... According to Unicredit, these derivative positions provide flexibility and will help «adjust the final level of ownership in line with the interests of its shareholders.» ... Unicredit first acquired a stake in Commerzbank two years ago and has steadily increased its exposure since then. ... However, resistance to a takeover remains strong. Commerzbank Chief Executive Bettina Orlopp continues to oppose a sale, as does the German government, which remains the bank's second-largest shareholder with a stake of around 13 percent."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,"Commerzbank CEO Touts AI-Driven 2030 Plan, Calls UniCredit Offer Unattractive - Watch List News",www.watchlistnews.com (Micah Haroldson),2026-06-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.watchlistnews.com/commerzbank-ceo-touts-ai-driven-2030-plan-calls-unicredit-offer-unattractive/11104832.html,"Commerzbank CEO Touts AI-Driven 2030 Plan, Calls UniCredit Offer Unattractive - Watch List News ... # Commerzbank CEO Touts AI-Driven 2030 Plan, Calls UniCredit Offer Unattractive ... Commerzbank (ETR:CBK) Chief Executive Bettina Orlopp said the German lender’s updated “Momentum 2030” strategy is built on continued revenue growth, lower costs and efficiency gains from artificial intelligence, while reiterating that the bank sees UniCredit’s current takeover offer as unattractive. ... Speaking at a Goldman Sachs financial institutions event alongside Christoph Wortig, Commerzbank’s head of investor relations, Orlopp said the bank’s May strategy update followed what she described as a “very successful year” and a continued improvement in profitability. She said the plan is based on a robust business model, growth in net interest income and net commission income, and ongoing transformation of the cost base. ... Orlopp said Commerzbank is targeting a return on tangible equity of 17% in 2028 and 21% in 2030, with interim targets of 12% this year, 14% next year and 19% before reaching the 2030 goal. She said the targets reflect “continuous improvement” rather than a “hockey stick” plan and carry “very limited execution risk” from management’s perspective. ... The bank also expects its cost-income ratio to fall from 56% to 53% this year, then to 48% by 2028 and 43% by 2030. Orlopp said artificial intelligence is one of the most important drivers of that efficiency improvement, both by improving customer experience and by accelerating internal processes. ... Commerzbank currently estimates AI will contribute about 500 million euros in value from 2030 onward, with most of that linked to cost reductions. Orlopp also cited cost avoidance, revenue gains and fraud prevention as potential benefits. She described an example from the bank’s legal team, where a first draft of a new policy that would normally take a week was generated in seconds using a legal technology tool. ... On net interest income, Orlopp said growth is expected to come from loan growth and stable deposit development. She said the bank is not assuming significant deposit growth, but rather a modest 2% to 3% increase driven by inflation. ... Orlopp said Commerzbank is assuming its deposit beta will rise from an already high 41% in Germany to 45%, reflecting competitive pressures. Asked about Chase entering the German deposit market, she said the offer has so far attracted the same “interest rate hoppers” that have been moving among direct banks and other competitors. ... She said Chase’s offer is currently a call money account rather than a current account, and that Commerzbank does not see it as a direct threat at the moment. However, she said the bank is monitoring the situation and investing in its mobile app and onboarding processes to improve its own value proposition. ... Orlopp also said Commerzbank’s replicating portfolio is expected to add value each year, assuming no significant change in forward rates and stable deposits. She said the portfolio’s average yield is currently 1.3% for this year and described the related revenue stream as “a very safe bet.” ... On lending, Orlopp said Commerzbank had assumed continued loan growth in its plan and that recent growth had exceeded expectations. She said the bank previously expected annual loan growth of about 8%, but last year achieved 10%. ... She said double-digit growth may not continue, but the figure should remain high. While the bank had expected more growth in Germany due to fiscal stimulus and stronger GDP assumptions, Orlopp said German corporate clients are increasingly investing outside Germany, partly because of geopolitical uncertainty. She said Commerzbank’s international network is supporting that growth. ... She also cited strength in the public sector, institutions business and renewable energy as contributors. ... Turning to UniCredit’s takeover offer, Orlopp said Commerzbank remains open to discussions about a friendly transaction, but only if two conditions are met. First, she said shareholders would need to receive a “decent” or “significant” premium, because they would be giving up control and future value creation potential. Second, she said any combination would need to reflect the value of Commerzbank’s business model and include appropriate governance. ... Orlopp said the current offer contains no premium and instead represents a discount. She argued that, under those circumstances, investors who want UniCredit shares would be better off selling Commerzbank shares and buying UniCredit directly, though she also emphasized Commerzbank’s standalone strategy and capital return plan. ... She said Commerzbank’s current plan would return approximately 50% of its market capitalization to shareholders over the next four years. ... Orlopp also said a hostile approach would be “value destructive” for stakeholders on both sides, including Commerzbank, UniCredit and HVB. She warned that competitors could seek to take clients and employees during a disorderly process. ... Orlopp said Commerzbank issued a press release questioning the progress of the offer because management saw tendering activity it did not view as economically rational, given that the offer was below the prevailing share price. She said the bank’s analysis indicated that some tendering parties were banks connected to UniCredit through tier structures, and that retail investor participation was negligible at 0.05%. ... She also raised concerns about the inclusion of derivative structures in assessing UniCredit’s position, saying Commerzbank wanted the process to be more transparent. Orlopp said the bank had asked German regulator BaFin to review the matter. ... Asked about a potential scenario in which UniCredit holds between 40% and 50%, Orlopp said that is not Commerzbank’s base case. She described such an outcome as a “limbo” or “messy” scenario in which UniCredit could have a large stake but still lack the 75% majority required for structural measures. ... Orlopp closed by saying management would pursue a friendly agreed deal if it believed that was best for the company, but said shareholders should compare the alternatives carefully. “The worst of all options is a hostile takeover because it will destroy a lot of value,” she said. ... Commerzbank AG provides banking and capital market products and services to private and small business customers, corporate, financial service providers, and institutional clients in Germany, rest of Europe, the Americas, Asia, and internationally. It operates through two segments, Private and Small-Business Customers, and Corporate Clients. The company offers saving, checking, business, and current accounts; term deposits; pension; credit and debit cards; payment solutions; overdraft services; various loans; and insurance products."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Exa,Commerzbank Consults BaFin on UniCredit Stake Buildup Disclosure,www.globalbankingandfinance.com,2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globalbankingandfinance.com/commerzbank-contact-german-regulator-unicredit-stake-buildup/,"Commerzbank Consults BaFin on UniCredit Stake Buildup Disclosure ... # Commerzbank in contact with German regulator on UniCredit stake buildup, staff message shows ... ## Commerzbank raises concerns with German regulator over UniCredit stake buildup ... ## Commerzbank and UniCredit: Regulatory Scrutiny and Market Reactions ... FRANKFURT, June 3 (Reuters) - Commerzbank is in contact with German regulator BaFin about recent disclosures by Italy's UniCredit about the take-up of its tender offer for the German lender, it said late on Wednesday. ... Confirming the contents of a notice to staff seen by Reuters, the German bank said that based on ""data available to Commerzbank the reported 7.58% in tendered shares are largely directly or indirectly linked to UniCredit's derivative counterparties - not independent investors."" ... UniCredit holds a 27% equity stake in Commerzbank and around 16% through derivatives, most of which can only be settled in cash. The Italian bank has said it needs those to have flexibility about the final size of its stake. ... Germany's second-biggest bank, which is fighting off UniCredit's bid, urged investors not to draw ""definitive conclusions"" on market support for the offer until ""the facts are fully assessed."" ... ""We are ... analysing and monitoring this process very closely and are also in contact with BaFin regarding this matter,"" the staff message sent on Tuesday read. ... ""Based on the provided information, no tendering of a single institutional investors could be identified yet and the sum of all retail tendering totals ...0.05%"", it later said in the statement. ... The staff message said UniCredit's communication appeared to be misleading, asserting that it was not ""economically rational"" for investors to have tendered a cumulative stake of 7.58%, as reported by UniCredit, given that the Italian bank's offer price is below the market price. ... UniCredit said in response it would not comment on ""insinuations that lack a factual basis,"" adding that the facts about its Commerzbank holdings were as it had reported. ... The development highlights the degree of tensions between the two lenders and may signal challenges ahead for UniCredit in the integration process were it to reach control. ... The years-long battle for control of Commerzbank reached a critical juncture last month after UniCredit launched a bid that was then formally rejected by Germany's second-largest bank. ... UniCredit said on Tuesday it had reached its goal in the bid, which is not intended to gain control of Commerzbank but only to lift UniCredit's 27% direct stake above 30%. Once above the mandatory takeover threshold, UniCredit will be free to buy more Commerzbank shares on the market next year. ... - UniCredit’s stake in Commerzbank—comprising shares and derivatives—now exceeds 40%, prompting regulatory scrutiny (marketscreener.com). - BaFin has earlier acted to curb UniCredit’s tactics, including banning anti-Commerzbank advertising in April 2026 (sueddeutsche.de). - Despite UniCredit’s aggressive buildup via an offer launched in May 2026, Commerzbank continues to assert its independent strategy and scrutiny of UniCredit’s proposal (commerzbank.de). ... Why is Commerzbank in contact with the German regulator BaFin? ... Commerzbank is consulting BaFin due to concerns over UniCredit's recent disclosure about shares it has acquired. ... Commerzbank believes UniCredit's communication about its stake buildup appears to be misleading. ... Commerzbank is closely analyzing and monitoring the process and is in contact with BaFin regarding the matter. ... A spokesperson for Commerzbank confirmed the content of the staff message."
Commerzbank AG,,,,Linkup,Commerzbank Q2 Earnings Call Highlights,MarketBeat,2026-08-06T00:00:00Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/commerzbank-q2-earnings-call-highlights-090409637.html,"Commerzbank reported record first-half 2026 results with broad-based revenue growth and cost discipline, reaffirming its full-year outlook and plans for capital returns totaling €3.2 billion. The bank also confirmed ongoing discussions with UniCredit on governance and potential cooperation, with any structural changes requiring shareholder approval."
