h create value,"" says Nicolai Andersen, Deloitte Global Strategy, Risk & Transactions leader. ... Deloitte provides leading professional services to nearly 90% of the Fortune Global 500® and thousands of private companies. Our people deliver measurable and lasting results that help reinforce public trust in capital markets and enable clients to transform and thrive. Building on its 180+-year history, Deloitte spans more than 150 countries and territories. Learn how Deloitte's over 470,000 people worldwide work together every day to make an impact that matters at www.deloitte.com. ... ### Deloitte is recognized as a Leader in the inaugural 2026 IDC MarketScape for Worldwide Operational Technology Security Services ... Deloitte has been named a Leader in the inaugural 2026 IDC MarketScape for Operational Technology (OT) Security Services Vendor Assessment... ... ### Deloitte named a Leader in the Inaugural 2026 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Supply Chain Strategy, Planning and Operations Consulting ... Deloitte has been named a Leader in the inaugural 2026 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Supply Chain Strategy, Planning and Operations Consulting. In the ..."
Deloitte,,,,Exa,Deloitte adds unified ‘agentic’ AI layer to Omnia audit platform,www.internationalaccountingbulletin.com (Ellichipuram Umesh),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.internationalaccountingbulletin.com/news/deloitte-adds-unified-agentic-ai/,"Deloitte adds unified ‘agentic’ AI layer to Omnia audit platform ... Deloitte has introduced a new agentic intelligence network within Deloitte Omnia, its global audit and assurance platform. ... The network is structured to pull together a range of AI agents, both existing and newly developed, under one framework. ... Deloitte said the approach will provide its nearly 85,000 Audit & Assurance professionals worldwide with “enhanced insights and deep risk analysis”. ... The ‘Big Four’ company added that the agentic intelligence network has been built by its in‑house engineering teams and is designed to expand as new technologies and capabilities become available. ... Deloitte & Touche chair and CEO Dipti Gulati said: “Our continued investments in AI and innovation are central to how we deliver quality and build trust in the capital markets. ... the combination of ... enables us to deliver confidence at ... According to the company, Omnia’s connected agentic intelligence can address data‑heavy client operations by integrating and extending AI already present on the platform. ... Within this environment, AI agents can review information to identify potential risk indicators and generate real-time, context-aware responses to support professional decisions. ... They are also able to handle initial tasks such as extracting data, analysing evidence, drafting core documentation and forming early stage conclusions for auditors to assess. ... In addition, the agents can support reviews of compliance with regulatory rules and disclosure obligations. ... All AI tools on Omnia are developed in line with Deloitte’s Trustworthy AI framework, which the company said embeds governance, controls and compliance throughout the life cycle of the technology. ... Deloitte US Audit and Assurance chief strategy and transformation officer Eric Johnson said: “With Omnia we are enabling our professionals to meet an ever-changing environment, enhance information gathering and validation, and deliver a more connected, insight-driven experience across engagements.” ... Deloitte recently launched the Adopt 100 initiative in partnership with Nvidia to expedite AI adoption in large organisations."
