sses | RE | | 02/07 | Australian shares extend losses; Northern Star soars after naming new CEO | RE | | 01/07 | July Opens With a Very Fed-Shaped Cloud | | | 01/07 | Deals of the day-Mergers and acquisitions | RE | ... Coles Group Limited is an Australia-based company that is engaged in the retail industry. The Company operates through two Supermarkets and Liquor. The Supermarkets segment includes fresh food, groceries, and general merchandise retailing, which includes Coles Online and Coles Financial Services. The Liquor segment includes liquor retailing, including online service. The Companyâ€™s businesses include Coles Supermarkets, Coles Online, Coles Liquor, flybuys, and Coles Financial Services. Coles Supermarkets is a national full-service supermarket retailer operating more than 851 supermarkets. Coles Liquor business includes three trading banners: Liquorland, First Choice Liquor Market and Vintage Cellars. Coles Online provides its customers with a choice of home delivery, including same-day and overnight drop and go services, or pick up from click and collect locations. Coles Liquor offers a range of wines, spirits, beers, and Ready-to-Drink products. ... Food Retail & Distribution ... Earnings release - Annual 2026 ... +3.55% ... Coles Group Appeals ACCC's Rejection of Kalgo"
COLES,,,,Exa,Coles ends talks for Greencross acquisition,www.fool.com.au (Laura Stewart),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.fool.com.au/2026/07/17/coles-ends-talks-for-greencross-acquisition/,"Coles ends talks for Greencross acquisition ... The Coles Group Ltd (ASX: COL) share price is in focus today after the company confirmed it has ended talks concerning a possible acquisition of Greencross Pet Wellness Company. Coles says it regularly assesses strategic opportunities, but has chosen not to progress with this particular deal. ... - Coles Group has ceased discussions with TPG Capital about acquiring Greencross Pet Wellness Company. - No terms or financial details were finalised or disclosed as talks have concluded. - Coles reconfirms its ongoing disciplined approach to potential acquisitions and strategic growth opportunities. - The company remains one of Australia's leading supermarket and retail groups. ... Coles originally announced the talks with Greencross on 1 July 2026. With the discussions now closed, no further negotiations or due diligence will take place regarding this acquisition. Investors will now be looking to see what other strategic moves, if any, Coles may pursue in the future. ... Coles has emphasised its careful and methodical approach to mergers and acquisitions. This signals to shareholders that while the company remains open to growth opportunities, it will not proceed with deals unless they align with its broader strategic priorities. ... Looking ahead, Coles is expected to continue reviewing potential partnerships or acquisitions that could complement its core supermarket and retail operations. Management's decision to step back demonstrates discipline and a focus on protecting shareholder value. ... The company has not signalled any immediate alternative acquisitions. Investors should watch for future company updates regarding growth initiatives or developments in its existing business portfolio. ... Over the past 12 months, Coles shares have risen 10%, outperforming the S&P/ASX 200 Index (ASX: XJO), which has risen 2% over the same period."
COLES,,,,Exa,Coles Flybuys ‘pay with points’ change lets you save up to $100 | news.com.au — Australia’s leading news site for latest headlines,www.news.com.au,2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.news.com.au/finance/business/retail/coles-major-shot-at-supermarket-rival-as-reward-point-schemes-heat-up/news-story/72111acf5f9aaa0012156defebb7b6b3,"Coles Flybuys ‘pay with points’ change lets you save up to $100 | news.com.au — Australia’s leading news site for latest headlines ... # Coles’ major shot at supermarket rival as reward point schemes heat up ... Coles has announced a major shot at supermarket rival Woolworths, unveiling a new Flybuys scheme and a potential $100 saving. ... Coles shoppers can save up to $100 on their groceries in a major change to how Flybuys points can be spent. ... In a national rollout starting on Wednesday, the supermarket giant’s new “pay with points” scheme will allow customers faster and more flexible ways to use their points to save on their grocery shop at Coles. ... Under the new system, Flybuys members with 2000 points can choose to redeem $10, $20, $30, $5 ... $70 ... This will be capped at 20,000 points and potentially save a shopper $100 on their weekly essentials. Wednesday’s announcement is a shot at major supermarket rival Woolworths’ own Everyday Rewards scheme, which allows members with at least 2000 points to save $10 off per shop or use a bank-until-Christmas option and redeem their points at the end of the year. Under Woolworths point scheme there is no limit to how much customers can save on single shop, but it will again depend on how many points the customer has. ... Previously, Flybuys members could save a maximum of $10 per shop at Coles. Coles’ rewards will also be expanded to select Liquorland stores from August 19. ... Coles chief customer experience officer, Michael Courtney said the pay-with-points would give customers more choice and more value when they shop in-store. ... “Our customers are looking for practical ways to save and pay with points that make it easier to use the ... they have already earned for money off their in-store shop instantly at the checkout,” he said. ... “For customers with points sitting in their Flybuys account, this is a simple way to unlock more value and those points can now help pay for more of the weekly shop.”"
COLES,,,,Exa,"Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland - Earnings Decline Risk",gulfsqas.com (News | 2026-07-14 | Quality Score: 90/100),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://gulfsqas.com/first-dry/Chipotle-to-Open-First-Restaurant-in-Mexico-Entering-the-Burritos-Homeland-44-1464,"Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland - Earnings Decline Risk ... News Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland ... Chipotle Mexico Expansion - growth catalysts, expectations, and future outlook. US fast-casual chain Chipotle Mexican Grill is preparing to open its first outlet in Mexico, the country where the burrito originated. The move comes as other American fast food brands have historically struggled to gain traction in the markets that inspired their menus. ... Chipotle Mexico Expansion - growth catalysts, expectations, and future outlook. Some traders rely on alerts to track key thresholds, allowing them to react promptly without monitoring every minute of the trading day. This approach balances convenience with responsiveness in fast-moving markets. Chipotle Mexican Grill, the US-based burrito chain, is set to launch its first restaurant in Mexico, according to recent reports. The expansion marks a significant step for the company as it enters the homeland of the dish that forms the core of its menu. However, this venture is not without historical precedent—many US fast food brands have faced notable challenges when expanding into countries where their cuisine originated. For instance, some American chains that built their identity on Mexican-inspired foods have encountered limited success in Mexico, where consumers prioritize authentic street food and local taquerías. The specific location and opening timeline for Chipotle's first Mexican outlet have not been disclosed, but the move signals the company's ambition to test its ""fast-casual"" model outside the United States. Chipotle's menu features customizable burritos, bowls, and tacos, emphasizing fresh, often locally sourced ingredients—a formula that has driven its domestic growth. The company's entry into Mexico will likely require careful adaptation to local tastes and price expectations, given the abundance of traditional Mexican cuisine. Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland Some traders combine trend-following strategies with real-time alerts. This hybrid approach allows them to respond quickly while maintaining a disciplined strategy.Some investors rely heavily on automated tools and alerts to capture market opportunities. While technology can help speed up responses, human judgment remains necessary. Reviewing signals critically and considering broader market conditions helps prevent overreactions to minor fluctuations.Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland Sector rotation analysis is a valuable tool for capturing market cycles. By observing which sectors outperform during specific macro conditions, professionals can strategically allocate capital to capitalize on emerging trends while mitigating potential losses in underperforming areas.Some investors track currency movements alongside equities. Exchange rate fluctuations can influence international investments. ... Chipotle Mexico Expansion - growth catalysts, expectations, and future outlook. Some investors track currency movements alongside equities. Exchange rate fluctuations can influence international investments. Chipotle's expansion into Mexico could offer valuable insights into the company's ability to replicate its US success in an international market. The fast-casual segment is highly competitive globally, and Chipotle's brand recognition may provide a differentiation advantage. However, the historical struggles of similar US chains in their dishes' countries of origin suggest that success is not guaranteed. Mexican consumers are accustomed to affordable, high-quality food from street vendors and small eateries, which could pose a challenge to Chipotle's pricing model. Additionally, the move might be viewed as a strategic diversification step, potentially reducing reliance on the mature US market where growth has slowed. Market observers will likely pay close attention to early customer traffic and sales data to gauge consumer reception. If positive, this first outlet could pave the way for further international expansion, not only in Mexico but also in other Latin American markets. Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland Observing correlations between markets can reveal hidden opportunities. For example, energy price shifts may precede changes in industrial equities, providing actionable insight.Investors increasingly view data as a supplement to intuition rather than a replacement. While analytics offer insights, experience and judgment often determine how that information is applied in real-world trading.Chipotle to Open First Restaurant in Mexico, Entering the Burrito's Homeland Predictive tools often serve as guidance rather than instruction. Investors interpret recommendations in the context of their own strategy and risk appetite.Sentiment shifts can precede observable price changes. Tracking investor optimism, market chatter, and sentiment indices allows professionals to anticipate moves and position portfolios advantageously ahead of the broader market. ... Chipotle Mexico Expansion - growth catalysts, expectations, and future outlook. Monitoring market liquidity is critical for understanding price stability and transaction costs. Thinly traded assets can exhibit exaggerated volatility, making timing and order placement particularly important. Professional investors assess liquidity alongside volume trends to optimize execution strategies. For investors, Chipotle's entry into Mexico represents a calculated risk with both upside