CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,Constellium Sells Automotive Structures Joint Venture in,www.globenewswire.com (Constellium Paris),2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/06/29/3318754/0/en/Constellium-Sells-Automotive-Structures-Joint-Venture-in-Changchun-China.html,"Constellium Sells Automotive Structures Joint Venture in ... # Constellium Sells Automotive Structures Joint Venture in Changchun, China ... PARIS, June 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Constellium SE (NYSE: CSTM) announced today that it sold its ownership stake in its automotive structures joint venture in Changchun, China, together with its partner, to a Chinese automotive holding company. ... The Changchun facility produces aluminum crash management systems and other structural components for the Chinese automotive market and employs around 200 people. ... “This transaction supports Constellium’s Vision 2028 strategy and our efforts to optimize our footprint and enhance overall competitiveness,” said Stephane Corre, President of Constellium’s Automotive Structures and Industry business unit. “This decision allows us to focus our resources where we can best serve our automotive structures customers and create long-term value.” ... Constellium (NYSE: CSTM) is a global sector leader that develops innovative, value-added aluminum products for a broad scope of markets and applications, including aerospace, packaging and automotive. Constellium generated $8.4 billion of revenue in 2025. ... 026 ... 00 ET ... Constellium Reports Strong Second Quarter and First Half 2026 Results, including Record Segment Adjusted EBITDA; Raises Full Year 2026 Guidance ... PARIS, July 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Constellium SE (NYSE: CSTM) (""Constellium"" or the ""Company"") today reported results for the second quarter and the first half ended June 30, 2026. Second... ... July 15, 2026 08:30 ET | Source: Constellium Paris Constellium to Source Local Renewable Energy for its German Facilities ... PARIS, July 15, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Constellium SE (NYSE: CSTM) today announced that its extrusion and automotive structures plants in Gottmadingen and Singen, Germany, will source locally..."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,"Constellium Sells Automotive Structures Joint Venture in Changchun, China | Markets Insider",markets.businessinsider.com,2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/stocks/constellium-sells-automotive-structures-joint-venture-in-changchun-china-1036282177,"Constellium Sells Automotive Structures Joint Venture in Changchun, China | Markets Insider ... # Constellium Sells Automotive Structures Joint Venture in Changchun, China ... PARIS, June 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Constellium SE (NYSE: CSTM) announced today that it sold its ownership stake in its automotive structures joint venture in Changchun, China, together with its partner, to a Chinese automotive holding company. ... The Changchun facility produces aluminum crash management systems and other structural components for the Chinese automotive market and employs around 200 people. ... “This transaction supports Constellium’s Vision 2028 strategy and our efforts to optimize our footprint and enhance overall competitiveness,” said Stephane Corre, President of Constellium’s Automotive Structures and Industry business unit. “This decision allows us to focus our resources where we can best serve our automotive structures customers and create long-term value.” ... Constellium (NYSE: CSTM) is a global sector leader that develops innovative, value-added aluminum products for a broad scope of markets and applications, including aerospace, packaging and automotive. Constellium generated $8.4 billion of revenue in 2025."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,Constellium sells stake in Chinese automotive structures JV | Grafa,grafa.com,2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://grafa.com/en/news/united-states/constellium-sells-chinese-automotive-structures-joint-venture,"Constellium sells stake in Chinese automotive structures JV | Grafa ... - Constellium (NYSE:CSTM) sold its ownership stake in an automotive structures joint venture in Changchun, China. - The facility produces aluminum crash management systems and structural components for the Chinese market and employs about 200 people. - The divestiture supports Constellium’s Vision 2028 strategy to optimize its footprint and focus resources on core strengths. ... Constellium (NYSE:CSTM) announced the sale of its ownership stake in an automotive structures joint venture in Changchun, China, to a Chinese automotive holding company. ... The facility produces aluminum crash management systems and structural components for the Chinese market and employs about 200 people. ... Constellium stated the divestiture aligns with its Vision 2028 strategy to optimize its global footprint, enhance competitiveness, and focus resources where it can best serve automotive structures customers and create long-term value. ... Constellium is a global leader in the development and manufacturing of high-value added aluminum products and solutions for a broad range of markets, including automotive, aerospace, and packaging. ... The company continues to execute on its strategic priorities, including portfolio optimization and targeted investments in high-growth areas."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,Constellium Sells Stake in Changchun Automotive Structures Joint Venture to FAW-Volkswagen - GeneOnline News,www.geneonline.com (GOAI),2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.geneonline.com/constellium-sells-stake-in-changchun-automotive-structures-joint-venture-to-faw-volkswagen/,"Constellium Sells Stake in Changchun Automotive Structures Joint Venture to FAW-Volkswagen - GeneOnline News ... ### Constellium Sells Stake in Changchun Automotive Structures Joint Venture to FAW-Volkswagen ... Constellium SE finalized the sale of its automotive structures joint venture located in Changchun, China, to its local partner, FAW-Volkswagen, on Monday. The transaction marks the company’s exit from the specific manufacturing partnership, transferring full ownership of the facility to the automotive manufacturer. ... The joint venture previously focused on the production of aluminum structural components for the automotive industry. By divesting its interest, Constellium relinquishes its operational role in the Changchun plant, while FAW-Volkswagen assumes complete control of the site’s assets and ongoing production activities. The companies did not disclose the financial terms of the agreement or the specific strategic reasons behind the divestiture."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,Constellium sells its automotive structures joi... | Pluang,pluang.com,2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pluang.com/en/news-feed/constellium-jual-porsi-joint-venture-struktur-otomotif-di-changchun,"Constellium sells its automotive structures joi... | Pluang ... # Constellium sells its automotive structures joint venture in China to focus on core markets. ... 29 Jun 2026 ... Constellium has sold its stake in the automotive structures joint venture located in Changchun, China, to a Chinese automotive holding company. The facility, which employs about 200 people, produces aluminum crash management systems and structural components for the Chinese automotive market. This sale aligns with Constellium's Vision 2028 strategy to optimize its operations and improve competitiveness by concentrating resources on key automotive structure markets. The financial terms of the deal were not disclosed."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,"Constellium Airbus Aluminum Extrusions Deal Supports Aircraft Production Ramp-Up | The Metalnomist - Raw Material, Metal, Alloy, Scrap News",www.metalnomist.com (The Metalnomist),2026-06-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.metalnomist.com/2026/06/constellium-airbus-aluminum-extrusions.html,"Constellium Airbus Aluminum Extrusions Deal Supports Aircraft Production Ramp-Up | The Metalnomist - Raw Material, Metal, Alloy, Scrap News ... Constellium Airbus aluminum extrusions supply will support new aircraft production under a multiyear agreement between the aluminum products producer and Airbus. The deal covers aerospace-grade aluminum bars and small and large extrusions for use across aircraft manufacturing programmes. ... Constellium Airbus aluminum extrusions will include products made from aerospace-grade aluminum alloys, including the company’s proprietary aluminum-lithium Airware line. Aluminum-lithium alloys are important in aerospace because they can reduce weight while maintaining strength and performance. ... extrusions also underline the importance of ... The companies did not disclose volumes or financial terms. However, the agreement gives Airbus longer-term supply visibility for a material category that remains essential to aircraft structures, components and lightweight design. ... Constellium will supply Airbus from its Issoire and Montreuil-Juigné facilities in France. These sites give the company an established European production base close to Airbus’ manufacturing network. ... house and five ... The agreement therefore supports more than simple metal availability. It gives Airbus access to approved extrusion routes, known production assets and a supplier with established aerospace materials capability. ... The inclusion of Constellium’s Airware aluminum-lithium alloy line is strategically important. Aluminum-lithium materials help reduce aircraft weight, supporting lower fuel consumption and better operating efficiency. ... For Constellium, the agreement reinforces its role as a strategic supplier to major aircraft programmes. Multiyear supply deals provide demand visibility and strengthen the company’s position in high-value aerospace aluminum markets. ... The deal also reflects a broader industry theme. Aerospace manufacturers are securing qualified material flows earlier and for longer periods as supply-chain bottlenecks continue to affect aircraft delivery schedules. ... The Constellium-Airbus agreement shows that aerospace ramp-up depends on more than final assembly capacity. Qualified aluminum extrusions, aluminum-lithium alloys and reliable European processing assets remain critical to keeping aircraft production moving."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,constellr Joins Airbus Sovereign ISR Consortium | Generation Space,generation.space,2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://generation.space/news/constellr-joins-airbus-sovereign-isr-consortium/,"constellr Joins Airbus Sovereign ISR Consortium | Generation Space ... # constellr Joins Airbus Sovereign ISR Consortium ... - Contact - Seraphim portfolio company constellr has signed an MoU with Airbus Defence and Space, Rohde and Schwarz, Orbint and HPS to develop a sovereign Earth observation and ISR solution. - The consortium combines RF, radar, electro-optical and infrared data, with Airbus leading system integration. - constellr contributes thermal infrared satellites to address intelligence gaps not covered by optical or radar sensors. - The initiative supports European demand for independent space intelligence and reduced reliance on non-European systems. ... Airbus Defence and Space has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Rohde & Schwarz, constellr, Orbint and High Performance Space Structure Systems (HPS) to collaborate on a satellite-based Earth observation and Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance (ISR) solution. Led by Airbus as prime contractor and system integrator, the consortium brings together five complementary German specialists to address growing governmental demand for sovereign, end-to-end space-based surveillance capabilities, independent of non-European dependencies. ... “This is a mission before it is a contract. We are joining this consortium because thermal infrared reconnaissance – the ability to detect operational activity, equipment state, and early-warning indicators that remain invisible to optical and radar sensors – is precisely where the ISR capability gap is greatest. We are proud to contribute that alongside Airbus, and to bring an already operational, sovereign German thermal ISR capability into a programme of this strategic importance”, said Max Gulde, CEO and Co-Founder, constellr. ... “It is a very positive sign that German prime contractors like Airbus Defence and Space are already incorporating German supplier SMEs like HPS into their system concepts right from the start. We are technically capable of delivering, extremely agile when it comes to scaling, and, above all, oriented toward the long term. A sovereign space architecture offers sufficient opportunities for the entire German space ecosystem, and the political will can be implemented very effectively. Many thanks to Airbus for his motivation to bring SMEs on board for defense missions”, said Ernst K. Pfeiffer, CEO of HPS GmbH. ... proven expertise along every stage of modern Earth observation and ISR. Airbus is responsible for overall mission and system architecture, end-to-end integration, programme management, and the customer interface. ... Rohde & Schwarz provides high-performance RF components, signal processing technologies, and radar antenna systems, core competencies developed over decades for the most demanding security applications. Orbint brings geolocation methods, data processing algorithms, and system concept contributions. HPS delivers space-qualified deployable mesh reflector antennas optimised for high-frequency Earth observation and communication payloads. constellr contributes thermal infrared satellite systems based on both its current and next-generation platforms, supporting initial and full operational capability. ... The joint solution addresses the full Earth observation chain, covering multi-sensor tasking, collection, processing, exploitation and dissemination. It integrates RF-sensors, electro-optical and infrared (EO/IR), synthetic aperture radar (SAR)-derived products, and signal-related geospatial intelligence outputs into coherent, customer-ready services. ... The consortium’s formation reflects a growing recognition across European governments and defence institutions that strategic autonomy requires indigenous space intelligence capabilities. With all five companies headquartered in Germany, the partnership represents a concentrated national industrial response to that demand and a concrete step towards a European sovereign ISR architecture. ... The parties have started their collaboration on a non-exclusive basis."
CONSTELLIUM,,,,Exa,Constellium Secures U.S. Stocking Distributor for Aheadd® CP1 Powder via Liberty Additive - CSTM News - EveryTicker,everyticker.com,2026-06-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://everyticker.com/quote/CSTM/news/constellium-secures-us-stocking-distributor-for-aheadd-cp1-powder-via-liberty-additive,"Constellium Secures U.S. Stocking Distributor for Aheadd® CP1 Powder via Liberty Additive - CSTM News - EveryTicker ... # Constellium Secures U.S. Stocking Distributor for Aheadd® CP1 Powder via Liberty Additive ... Constellium announced that Liberty Additive, LLC will serve as the first U.S. stocking distributor for its Aheadd® CP1 aluminum powder, effective July 1 2026. The partnership expands Constellium’s domestic distribution network and supports its additive‑manufacturing strategy by providing U.S. aerospace, defense, and industrial customers with local inventory and faster lead times for the high‑performance powder used in heat exchangers and other mission‑critical components. ... Constellium’s U.S. presence includes Muscle Shoals, Alabama, and Bowling Green, Kentucky, where it produces aluminum can sheet, automotive coils, and auto‑body sheet products. The new stocking arrangement aligns with Constellium’s strategy to deepen penetration in the U.S. market and capture a larger share of the additive‑manufacturing demand projected to grow as aircraft and defense programs adopt lighter, more efficient components. ... ""We are pleased to partner with Liberty Additive to expand access to our Aheadd® CP1 aluminum powder in the United States, particularly for the aerospace and defense markets. This collaboration will enable more responsive supply and help unlock the full potential of advanced aluminum solutions for additive manufacturing,"" said Sylvain Henry, Vice President of Research and Development for Constellium. ""This milestone reflects Liberty Additive's commitment to bringing world‑class additive manufacturing materials directly to the U.S. market. By becoming the first stocking distributor in the United States for Constellium Aheadd® CP1 aluminum powder, we are helping customers reduce lead times, improve supply chain reliability, and accelerate adoption of advanced aluminum additive manufacturing technologies,"" added Nick Oyer, President of Liberty Additive. ... The agreement supports Constellium’s broader focus on high‑margin specialty aluminum products. By securing a stocking partner, Constellium can reduce shipping lead times and improve supply‑chain reliability for its key customers, strengthening its competitive position in the high‑performance aluminum powder sector. ... The deal is expected to accelerate adoption of advanced aluminum materials in U.S. aerospace and defense programs, positioning Constellium to benefit from the projected growth in additive manufacturing as aircraft and defense programs adopt lighter, more efficient components."
