CONSTELLIUM,,,,Syracuse,"Constellium sees revenue, net income increase Q2",Recycling News,2026-07-29T22:26:00Z,2026-07-29 22:26:00+00:00,FinancialsActivity,https://www.recyclingtoday.com/news/constellium-reports-q2-first-half-2026-earnings/,"Paris - based Constellium has posted strong second-quarter and half-year results that include record profitability, significantly increased earnings and solid cash flow, causing the aluminum products and recycling company to raise its full-year outlook. In the second quarter, Constellium reported $ 2.7 billion in revenue, a 31 percent increase from the second quarter of 2025, while its net income was $ 148 million compared with net income of $ 36 million a year earlier. Adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization (EBITDA) totaled $ 439 million, which the company credits to stronger results in each of its operating segments-Aerospace & Transportation (A & T) , Packaging & Automotive Rolled Products (P & ARP) and Automotive Structures & Industry (AS & I) - a favorable change in the noncash metal price lag impact and favorable foreign exchange translation, partially offset by higher corporate costs. At 381,000 metric tons, however, Constellium's shipments for the quarter were 1 percent lower than in the second quarter of 2025. For the first half of this year, Constellium reported shipments of 751,000 metric tons, down 1 percent from the first half of last year, while revenue was $ 5.2 billion (a 28 percent increase year over year) and net income was $ 344 million compared with $ 74 million the first half of 2025."
