HAIER,,,,Exa,"Haier Launches Largest AI-Powered Air Conditioner Factory in ASEAN, Embracing the Data Center Trend - Money & Banking Magazine",en.moneyandbanking.co.th (การเงินธนาคาร),2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.moneyandbanking.co.th/2026/243653/,"Haier Launches Largest AI-Powered Air Conditioner Factory in ASEAN, Embracing the Data Center Trend - Money & Banking Magazine ... # Haier launches largest AI-powered air conditioner factory in ASEAN, embracing the Data Center trend. ... Thailand's strategic focus is on connecting global supply chains, exporting to Europe and North America, and targeting the ASEAN real estate and industrial sectors. Demand is projected to reach 2.2 units by 73. The focus is on upgrading to Smart Factories with 65% automation and pursuing green energy solutions. ... May 13, 2569 – In an era where the global economy is transitioning to an “AI Economy,” the growth of digital infrastructure such as data centers is a major catalyst for the exponential increase in demand for high-efficiency cooling systems. Coupled with the sustainability trend that forces industries to switch to energy-efficient and environmentally friendly air conditioning systems, the commercial HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning) industry has become a new battleground where global technology companies must rapidly expand their production base. ... Haier Smart Home A global residential technology giant saw an opportunity in this economic crisis and expansion, choosing WHA Eastern Seaboard Industrial Estate in Rayong Province, under the Eastern Economic Corridor (EEC), as the site for the groundbreaking of its new ""AI Intelligent Manufacturing Base"" for commercial air conditioning production. ... This project is not just a typical assembly plant, but the largest commercial air conditioner manufacturing base in Southeast Asia, spanning over 76 rai (approximately 22 acres). Leveraging its geographical advantage near Laem Chabang Port, it will serve as a spearhead for exporting products to high-purchasing power markets such as Europe and North America. Full-scale production is scheduled to begin in June 2027. ... The highlight of this factory is its full adoption of AI and automation technologies to enhance its competitiveness in terms of cost and quality: ... - Automation 65%: More than 65% of the production line uses automation. - Vertical Integration: Manufacturing all core components in-house to reduce supply chain risks. - AI Quality Control: Using artificial intelligence to control quality and production processes throughout the entire supply chain. - R&D Center: Establishing a research center in Thailand to develop products specifically suited to tropical climates. ... The products leaving this factory will range from VRF systems and large-scale air conditioning systems for buildings, and most importantly, data center cooling systems. This is a crucial piece of the puzzle in supporting investment from major technology companies that are increasingly entering the Thai market. ... Currently, Haier holds the number one market share in air conditioners in Thailand for five consecutive years and has installed large-scale cooling systems in key locations across the country, such as Suvarnabhumi Airport and Chulalongkorn University. This major investment in Rayong clearly underscores Haier's intention to use Thailand as a ""springboard"" to the global market. ... Haier's senior executives. The overall success and goals are reflected in the key sentence: “This Rayong factory will be the world's first AI Intelligent Factory for the production of commercial air conditioners. This will help reduce delivery times and enhance competitiveness through high-efficiency, energy-saving technologies and green energy solutions, creating long-term growth opportunities in the global market.” ... From a business perspective, ... is not just a newcomer to the commercial market, but has a strong global foundation, as follows: ... 1. Magnetic Bearing Centrifugal Chiller: Ranked #1 in the world for the 8th consecutive year. 2. Europe: HVAC business grows by more than 20% annually. 3. Global Network: We have 173 manufacturing facilities and a distribution network of over 230,000 locations worldwide. ... This expansion into Thailand further completes the supply chain, aiming for the Rayong factory to serve as a model of a smart factory delivering sustainable cooling solutions for the future. This will ultimately propel Thailand to become a true global hub for the air conditioning industry."
HAIER,,,,Exa,Bangkok Post - Haier sets up region's largest AC base in Rayong,www.bangkokpost.com (Bangkok Post Public Company Limited),2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bangkokpost.com/business/general/3254109/haier-sets-up-regions-largest-ac-base-in-rayong,"Bangkok Post - Haier sets up region's largest AC base in Rayong ... # Haier sets up region's largest AC base in Rayong PUBLISHED : 13 May 2026 at 01:01 WRITER: Kuakul Mornkum Haier, a Chinese household appliance manufacturer, is investing 5 billion baht to build a commercial air conditioner manufacturing plant in Rayong, with operations scheduled to begin in June 2027. ... The plant, covering approximately 76 rai, is located in the WHA Eastern Seaboard Industrial Estate 5 in Rayong. ... According to a press release, the facility will be the largest central air conditioning manufacturing base in Southeast Asia. ... Dong Jianping, president of Haier Electrical Appliances (Thailand) Co Ltd, said the company expects production capacity to reach 800,000 units per year by 2028. ... Haier aims to sell 30% of the products from this facility domestically, with the remainder exported to Southeast Asia, North America and South Asia. ... Products manufactured at the facility include packaged terminal air conditioners, light commercial air conditioners, chillers, variable refrigerant flow systems, fan coil units, and data centre cooling equipment, according to Haier. ... The company expects the plant to create roughly 1,000 jobs for locals. ... Furthermore, the site is to house a dedicated R&D centre for local research, manufacturing and marketing operations. ... The centre is expected to focus on developing customised heating, ventilation and air conditioning solutions tailored to Southeast Asia's tropical climate and diverse commercial applications, including water chillers, multi-split systems, light commercial air conditioners, central air conditioning systems, and commercial heat pumps, according to the company. ... The company operates commercial air conditioner plants in China, Pakistan, India and Egypt. ... Last year, Haier opened a 10-billion-baht air conditioner manufacturing plant in Chon Buri, focusing on household air conditioners."
