AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,"XRG chemicals portfolio delivers resilient second-quarter earnings, value for UAE | Emirates News Agency",www.wam.ae (Emirates News Agency),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.wam.ae/en/article/c1m4m6a-xrg-chemicals-portfolio-delivers-resilient,"XRG chemicals portfolio delivers resilient second-quarter earnings, value for UAE | Emirates News Agency ... ABU DHABI, 7th August, 2026 (WAM) -- XRG, ADNOC's international investment arm, has built its chemicals portfolio on a clear strategic rationale. ... The second quarter of 2026 provided an early indication of how that strategy can translate into value creation. Across the portfolio, Borouge International, Covestro and Fertiglobe delivered resilient earnings, demonstrating the benefits of geographic diversification, operational resilience and disciplined execution. ... Borouge International, formed in March 2026 through the combination of Borouge plc, Borealis and NOVA Chemicals, reported adjusted EBITDA of US$1.8 billion in its first full quarter as a combined business. ... The company is also progressing initiatives expected to deliver more than $500 million in EBITDA synergies over time. ... Covestro, which joined XRG's portfolio in late 2025, delivered first-half EBITDA of €669 million, supported by disciplined commercial execution, cost management and continued strength in its speciality materials business. ... In the second quarter, Fertiglobe more than doubled adjusted EBITDA to $371 million, supported by stronger nitrogen fertiliser markets and solid operational performance across its international asset base. ... iglobe's ability to capture opportunities across multiple geographies and trade routes while maintaining its position as ... 's leading producers of nitrogen fertilisers, a critical input for ... That breadth is one way XRG's international growth creates value for the UAE. Earnings generated across global markets return to XRG and its shareholders, while Borouge plc and Fertiglobe's listings on the Abu Dhabi Securities Exchange allow UAE investors to participate directly in their performance. A more diversified international portfolio also strengthens ADNOC's resilience by reducing exposure to any single market or economic cycle. ... XRG's growth also brings industrial capability and technology into the UAE. Borouge International, jointly owned by XRG and OMV, combines more than 16,500 patents and seven global innovation centres. ... That expertise is helping support the development of Borouge 4 in Ruwais, which will increase the site's production capacity to approximately 6.4 million tonnes per year and make it the world's largest single-site polyolefins complex. ... Collaboration across the portfolio is also beginning to emerge. During the first half of 2026, Covestro, Fertiglobe and TA’ZIZ (a joint venture between ADNOC and ADQ) announced initiatives to explore opportunities across the ammonia, nitric acid and advanced materials value chains in the UAE. ... As XRG continues to expand its international chemicals platform, the performance of Borouge International, Covestro and Fertiglobe demonstrates how scale, diversification and portfolio integration can support sustainable growth, strong cash generation and long-term value creation for both shareholders and the UAE."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aurubis predicts H2 2026 profits - Recycling Today,"www.recyclingtoday.com (By Brian Taylor, Senior Editor Published August 06, 2026)",2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.recyclingtoday.com/news/aurubis-metals-production-recycling-germany-usa-earnings-2026-copper/,"Aurubis predicts H2 2026 profits - Recycling Today ... # Aurubis predicts H2 2026 profits ... The recycled-content metals producer cites the ramp-up of its Georgia facility as one reason for anticipated profitability in the second half of 2026. ... Aurubis says increased revenue from the sale of copper—its largest volume metal—has positively influenced its recent results. Photo courtesy of Aurubis AG ... Hamburg, Germany-based Aurubis AG, with global metals production operations that include facilities in the United States, says its most recent quarterly earnings before taxes (EBT) figure has caused it to move its full fiscal year guidance to the upper end of its previous forecast range. ... The company, for which the 2025/2026 fiscal year runs from Oct. 1, 2025, to Sept. 30, credits its “heightened operating performance year over year with increased metal result and higher revenues from [our] recycling and product business” as reasons for its optimistic guidance. ... Aurubis estimates about 90 percent of its recent investment agenda has been completed, including the start of its recycling plant in Hamburg and the ramp-up of the Aurubis Richmond recycling facility in Georgia. ... The company says it has increased its EBT figure by 31 percent—to 374 million euros ($431 million) in the first nine months of its current fiscal year ... “Central positive factors impacting the first nine months included high capacity utilization in production with an improved metal result due to higher metal prices, especially for precious metals, higher revenues from sulfuric acid sales and a slight increase in earnings from the processing of recycling material,” Aurubis says. ... According to the company, increased revenue from the sale of copper—its largest volume metal—has positively influenced its recent results as well. The company’s CEO says its presence in a wider range of metals, including tin and precious metals, also has been beneficial. ... “Our focus on the multimetal business is paying off,” says Aurubis AG CEO Toralf Haag. “We are delivering reliability, even in a highly demanding market environment. This is reflected in our smelters’ heightened operating performance.” ... Aurubis says in operations comprising its Multimetal Recycling segment, it achieved operating EBT of 87 million euros ($100 million) so far in its fiscal year, representing a 142 percent increase compared with the 36 million euros ($41.5 million) of EBT one year earlier. ... Regarding its footprint in the U.S., Aurubis states, “The gradual ramp-up of Aurubis Richmond, the first secondary smelter for multimetal recycling in the U.S., continues to move forward with focus. The advanced technology and processing capabilities of its recycling system make Aurubis a pioneer in sustainable multimetal recycling in the U.S. The new site also opens up prospects for additional profitable growth along the metallurgical value chain in the U.S.” ... Aurubis states its forecast for fiscal year 2025/26 includes operating EBT between 425-525 million euros ($431-$605 million), which it says is at the upper end of its previously stated forecast range."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Brazil’s Unipar posts stronger Q2 on higher caustic soda and PVC prices | ChemOrbis,www.chemorbis.com (ChemOrbis),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.chemorbis.com/en/plastics-news/Brazil-s-Unipar-posts-stronger-Q2-on-higher-caustic-soda-and-PVC-prices/2026/08/07/982157,"Brazil’s Unipar posts stronger Q2 on higher caustic soda and PVC prices | ChemOrbis Just two weeks ago, the question was whether the renewed war premium in crude oil could finally put a floor under polymer markets after months of relentless declines. Brent crude extended its rally far beyond expectations, climbing from the mid-$80s/bbl in H1 July to briefly settle above $100/bbl on July 23 as geopolitical tensions in the Middle East intensified. This visibly shifted the sentiment upwards in Asia including China, Southeast Asia and India as well in Türkiye and Egypt while the slump slowed down in Europe... Dow’s €1.1 billion claim puts Europe’s ethylene cartel dispute back in focus Europe’s long-running ethylene cartel dispute has returned to the spotlight after Dow Europe filed a €1.1 billion damages claim against four companies accused of manipulating Europe’s ethylene benchmark price. The lawsuit is the latest in a series of civil actions stemming from the European Commission’s 2020 decision that found Clariant, Celanese, Orbia and Westlake had coordinated their ethylene purchasing strategies between 2011 and 2017 to influence the Monthly Contract Price (MCP)... Crude oil surges on renewed war premium; will it reverse the polymer slump? The renewed geopolitical tensions have pushed Brent crude back into the mid-$80s/bbl, rapidly rebuilding some of the war-risk premium that had evaporated after June's ceasefire hopes. This has also helped buoy the sentiment recently in polymer markets, where prices have been on a downturn for the past couple of months. After months of sluggish demand, ample supplies, and relentless price erosion, sellers are seizing on higher feedstock costs to argue that the market has reached its bottom... India's proposed anti-dumping duties on LLDPE imports could significantly reshape the country's sourcing patterns, with suppliers from the UAE, Saudi Arabia and Malaysia at risk of losing a combined 36% share of India's import market. The US appears best positioned to capture much of this displaced demand, reinforcing an export shift already underway as Chinese buying continues to weaken…"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aestura named No. 1 dermocosmetic skincare brand in South Korea by Euromonitor - The Herald Business,biz.heraldcorp.com (Kang Seung-yeon),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://biz.heraldcorp.com/article/10832665,"Amorepacific announced Thursday that its derma brand Aestura has been named the No. 1 dermocosmetic skincare brand by sales in South Korea by Euromonitor International. ... Aestura traces its roots to Pacific Pharma, where its derma heritage began in 1982, and was built on Amorepacific's research expertise. The brand entered the dermocosmetics market through hospital and dermatology channels in 2008, then helped bring derma cosmetics to a mainstream audience when it introduced the Atobarrier365 Cream at CJ Olive Young in 2018. ... The Atobarrier365 Cream remains the brand's bestseller. Designed as a barrier-moisturizing care solution for sensitive skin, it sells at a rate of one unit every five seconds. The product has also won the top spot in the cream category at the CJ Olive Young Awards for two consecutive years. ... Aestura is also accelerating its global push. After entering major Asian markets including Japan, Vietnam and Thailand, the brand launched at Sephora in the United States last year. This year it expanded its sales channels into key European markets, with products now available at Sephora across approximately 860 stores in 19 countries. ... ""We will grow into a globally recognized derma brand by bringing our domestically proven sensitive-skin solutions to markets around the world,"" an Aestura official said."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Hexpol Buys Specialty Compounder Vipa Group - Canadian Plastics,www.canplastics.com,2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.canplastics.com/materials/hexpol-buys-specialty-compounder-vipa-group/1003469760/,"Hexpol Buys Specialty Compounder Vipa Group - Canadian Plastics ... # Hexpol buys specialty compounder Vipa Group August 5, 2026 By Canadian Plastics The deal expands Hexpol's presence in the wire and cable market. ... In a move designed to expand its presence in the wire and cable market, material supplier Hexpol AB has acquired Italy-based specialty compounder Vipa Group for 143.5 million euros. ... The acquisition includes ... Group, consisting of the companies Vi. ... Founded in 1969, Vipa is being acquired from the Paolini family, which will support the transition for 18 months. CEO Nicola Vigolo will continue to lead the business as a subsidiary of Hexpol. Vipa develops and manufactures thermoplastic compounds for wire and cable applications. ... “[The acquisition] demonstrates our ambition to build a leading thermoplastics platform through both organic growth and acquisitions,” said Hexpol’s acting CEO and CFO Peter Rosén. Last year, Hexpol company announced an increased focus on thermoplastics as a key growth platform, he added. ... The acquisition is expected to close during the third quarter of 2026."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Petkim swings to profit in Q2 on stronger margins | ChemOrbis,www.chemorbis.com (ChemOrbis),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.chemorbis.com/en/plastics-news/Petkim-swings-to-profit-in-Q2-on-stronger-margins/2026/08/06/981900,"Petkim swings to profit in Q2 on stronger margins | ChemOrbis Just two weeks ago, the question was whether the renewed war premium in crude oil could finally put a floor under polymer markets after months of relentless declines. Brent crude extended its rally far beyond expectations, climbing from the mid-$80s/bbl in H1 July to briefly settle above $100/bbl on July 23 as geopolitical tensions in the Middle East intensified. This visibly shifted the sentiment upwards in Asia including China, Southeast Asia and India as well in Türkiye and Egypt while the slump slowed down in Europe... Dow’s €1.1 billion claim puts Europe’s ethylene cartel dispute back in focus Europe’s long-running ethylene cartel dispute has returned to the spotlight after Dow Europe filed a €1.1 billion damages claim against four companies accused of manipulating Europe’s ethylene benchmark price. The lawsuit is the latest in a series of civil actions stemming from the European Commission’s 2020 decision that found Clariant, Celanese, Orbia and Westlake had coordinated their ethylene purchasing strategies between 2011 and 2017 to influence the Monthly Contract Price (MCP)... Crude oil surges on renewed war premium; will it reverse the polymer slump? The renewed geopolitical tensions have pushed Brent crude back into the mid-$80s/bbl, rapidly rebuilding some of the war-risk premium that had evaporated after June's ceasefire hopes. This has also helped buoy the sentiment recently in polymer markets, where prices have been on a downturn for the past couple of months. After months of sluggish demand, ample supplies, and relentless price erosion, sellers are seizing on higher feedstock costs to argue that the market has reached its bottom... The EU-US tariff agreement has largely been viewed through the lens of polymers, particularly PE, and as a boost for US polymer exports. Yet the implications reach well beyond resin markets. By eliminating customs duties across the entire Chapter 39, the regulation also covers a broad range of semi-finished and finished plastic products, potentially reshaping competition across Europe's downstream plastics value chain..."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,UFlex opens WPP bag manufacturing facility in Mexico,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/uflex-mexico-wpp-bag-facility/,"UFlex opens WPP bag manufacturing facility in Mexico ... # UFlex opens WPP bag manufacturing facility in Mexico ... The facility includes a recycling unit and a zero solid waste discharge system for improving material recovery and cutting waste. ... Vidhya Edwards Munnangi August 5, 2026 The company invested $52m in the plant, which covers ten acres in Altamira. Credit: UFlex. ... UFlex has started operations at its first woven polypropylene (WPP) bag manufacturing site outside India, with a new facility in Mexico. ... The company invested $52m in the plant, which covers ten acres in Altamira. ... The site forms part of its wider international expansion and adds to its manufacturing footprint in the Americas. ... The facility includes a recycling unit and a zero solid waste discharge system aimed at improving material recovery, reducing waste and supporting disposal processes. ... UFlex said the plant can produce 80 million WPP bags a year, supplying demand for industrial packaging products across the Americas. ... UFlex flexible packaging and new product development president Jeevaraj Gopal Pillai said: “The commissioning of our WPP packaging plant in Mexico represents a strategic step in expanding our global manufacturing network and strengthening our presence in the Americas. ... “The new facility will enable us to deliver innovative, high-quality packaging solutions closer to our customers, ensure shorter turnaround times, and support the evolving sustainability and performance needs of the region’s fast-growing pet food industry.” ... Last month, UFlex received an Indian patent for a reclosable packaging format for large bags. The packaging is intended for products such as chemicals, coffee, flour, pet food, protein powders, raw materials and other industrial goods."
