nd relentless price erosion, sellers are seizing on higher feedstock costs to argue that the market has reached its bottom... Europe’s ABS correction gathers pace, steeper July falls loom The European ABS market turned softer in June after producers' initial rollover attempts proved unsustainable amid weakening market fundamentals. Transactions were concluded with reductions of up to €200/ton, while even steeper discounts were reported by some sources, particularly in the distribution channel..."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,"Financial News | myMotherLode.com - Aura Announces Q2 2026 and H1 2026 Financial and Operational Results, a Record First Half Result",money.mymotherlode.com (By: Aura Minerals Inc via GlobeNewswire),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,http://money.mymotherlode.com/clarkebroadcasting.mymotherlode/article/gnwcq-2026-8-5-aura-announces-q2-2026-and-h1-2026-financial-and-operational-results-a-record-first-half-result,"# Aura Announces Q2 2026 and H1 2026 Financial and Operational Results, a Record First Half Result By: Aura Minerals Inc via GlobeNewswire August 05, 2026 at 17:20 PM EDT ... ROAD TOWN, British Virgin Islands, Aug. 05, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Aura Minerals Inc. (NASDAQ: AUGO) (B3: AURA33) (“Aura” or the “Company”) announces that it has filed its audited consolidated financial statements and earnings release (together, “Financial and Operational Results”) for the period ended June 30, 2026. The full version of the Financial and Operational Results can be viewed on the Company’s website at www.auraminerals.com, on SEDAR+ at www.sedarplus.ca. or on SEC www.sec.com. ... Rodrigo Barbosa, Aura’s President, and CEO commented: “ Aura delivered a record first half, producing 158k GEO in H1 2026. With second-half guidance of 182k to 232k GEO, we remain firmly on track with our full-year target of 340k to 390k GEO. Our LTM Adjusted EBITDA reached US$802 million — the 12th consecutive quarterly increase — supported by an average gold price of US$4,260 per ounce and LTM production of 313k GEO. Beyond the numbers, we are rapidly advancing our next phase of growth: construction at Era Dorada is on schedule with earthmoving 60% complete; the turnaround at MSG is laying the infrastructure and underground development for a significant production step-up in 2027; Almas is advancing its expansion toward 3 Mtpa; we are finalizing engineering studies at Borborema to increase capacity; and we are now incorporating Serrinhas and Pé Quente into the Matupá studies. We are delivering both strong production growth and a clear path toward 600k GEO annually, while rewarding our shareholders with robust returns — generating a approximately 4.3% yield over the last twelve months through dividends and share buybacks.” ... - Record First-Half Production: Q2 2026 total production reached 75,437 GEO, an 8% decrease compared to Q1 2026 and 18% higher than Q2 2025 at current metal prices (at constant prices, -9% QoQ and +16% YoY). In H1 2026, Aura produced 157,574 GEO (158,448 GEO at constant prices), a 27% increase over H1 2025 and the highest first-half production in the Company's history and is on track to deliver its consolidated guidance of 340k – 390k GEO in 2026. Q2 2026 and H1 2026 highlights: ... - Almas: 16,130 GEO (+25% YoY; +2% QoQ), driven by higher ore processed volumes from the ongoing plant expansion. In H1 2026, production totaled 31,968 GEO (+23% YoY), driven mainly by 20% higher ore moved volumes and 30% higher ore plant feed, reflecting the results of the plant expansion. ... - MSG, 7,186 GEO (-16% QoQ), as Aura continues to invest in underground infrastructure and primary development to invert the mining method to bottom-up. In H1 2026, production reached 15,766 GEO. ... - Sales Volumes: Q2 2026 sales were 78,414 GEO, a 4% decrease QoQ but a 26% increase YoY at current prices, mainly due to better sales at Almas, Borborema now under commercial production, and the addition of MSG. In H1 2026, Aura sold 159,782 GEO, up 30% YoY. ... - AISC Performance: Q2 2026 AISC was US$1,985/GEO, up 9% QoQ and 37% YoY, largely driven by MSG (US$5,277/GEO, +41%) as Aura focused the quarter on preparing the mine and advancing on primary development as part of the Company’s plan to shift the mining method to bottom-up. Excluding this impact, Aura’s AISC would have been US$1,653/GEO, up 5% QoQ and 14% YoY, reflecting the mine sequencing at Almas and Apoena, and lower production at Minosa. These results were partially offset by a decrease at Borborema. In H1 2026, AISC was US$1,906/GEO (+31% YoY) and US$1,615/GEO ex-MSG and the Company remains on track to deliver its AISC Guidance of US$1,720-US$1,865 in 2026, including MSG. ... Repurchase Program: In June 2026, Aura's Board approved share repurchase programs for the Company's common shares and Brazilian Depositary Receipts. Aura may repurchase up to an aggregate US$200 million in the open market or through privately negotiated transactions, from June 18, 2026 through June 18, 2027, or until completed, whichever comes first. The Board will review the programs periodically and may adjust their terms and size, or suspend or discontinue them. ... Advancing Construction, Environment, and Community at Era Dorada: the project continues to advance on all fronts toward becoming a new standard for sustainable mining. Following full Board approval in April 2026, construction is progressing on schedule, with earthmoving at 60% completion, Long Lead Items in manufacture, the EPCM company on board, and civil works mobilization underway. Environmentally, the project features a closed water circuit reusing 100% of processed water, approved capex for potable water — a first in Guatemala — and a fully licensed, Aura-owned geothermal energy source. On the social side, the Era Dorada House in Asunción Mita has driven over 1,300 hours of community engagement and official recognition from local communities, while employment has grown to over 366 people (53% local; 93% Guatemalan), positively impacting around 25,000 people nearby. Cumulative investment reached US$15.3 million as of June. ... Sale Agreement to São Francisco Mine: In May 2026, Aura completed the previously announced sale of the São Francisco Mine (part of the Apoena Mine complex) for a total purchase price of $9.0 million, following satisfaction of the final closing condition. The mine had been under care and maintenance, with fully depreciated property, plant and equipment. As of June 30, 2026, Aura had received US$ 3 million in cash proceeds — a US$1 million advance payment at signing and a US $2 million payment at closing — with the remaining balance recorded in Other Receivables and Assets. ... production at Borborema during Q3 2025; (ii) the addition of MSG; and (iii) Almas, up 34% on higher ore plant feed and improved operational performance from its ongoing plant expansion. These gains were partially offset by lower production at Apoena, down 31% on lower grades and recovery rates which are expected to improve during H2 2026; Minosa, down 21% on higher stacking levels within the leach pad and lower ore plant feed; and Aranzazu, down 20% in line with the mine plan. At constant metal prices, production increased 16% above Q2 2025. ... In H1 2026, production reached a record 157,574 GEO, the highest first-half production in Aura's history, a 27% increase at current metal prices and also 27% at constant prices (158,448 GEO) compared to the 124,120 GEO produced in H1 2025. This growth was primarily driven by Borborema commercial production, the addition of MSG and Almas' performance, as described above. ... In H1 2026, Cash Cost was US$1,499/GEO (US$1,287/GEO excluding MSG) and AISC was US$1,906/GEO (US$1,615/GEO excluding MSG), reflecting the impacts described above. The Company continues to expect consolidated 2026 Cash Cost and AISC to be within the Company's Guidance range, as results at MSG are expected to improve as the Company advances its turnaround strategy, Apoena's costs should benefit from the higher grades to be accessed later in the year once the Nosde development is completed, as well as the positive impacts of mine sequencing in H2 2026 from other operations. ... General and Administrative expenses increased 43% compared to Q1 2026, primarily due to a non-recurring provision for judicial contingencies at Apoena of approximately US$4.7 million as well as expenses related to personnel turnover at MSG and professional fees for Era Dorada construction. Versus Q2 2025, G&A increased 99%, reflecting the consolidation of Borborema and MSG (which were not included in the prior-year results) together with these non-recurring legal impacts and higher professional fees related to the Era Dorada Project. In H1 2026, G&A totaled US$38.2 million, an 83% increase from US$20.9 million in H1 2025, mainly driven by the reasons above."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Victaulic Expands European Modular Construction Capabilities with Acquisition of Arumani,www.prnewswire.com (Victaulic),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/victaulic-expands-european-modular-construction-capabilities-with-acquisition-of-arumani-302843437.html,"Expands European Modular Construction Capabilities ... umani Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... The acquisition of Arumani strengthens Victaulic's modular capabilities, accelerating project timelines and improving construction efficiency. ... CASTELLON, Spain, Aug. 5, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Victaulic, the world's leading manufacturer of mechanical pipe joining, fire protection, and flow control solutions, announced the acquisition of modular construction and mechanical assemblies specialist Arumani, expanding its modular construction capabilities in Europe. ... This move enhances Victaulic's ability to deliver fully engineered modular skids across Europe, helping to speed up project timelines, boost construction efficiency, and minimize on-site labor through advanced off-site fabrication. ... Victaulic has completed the acquisition of Arumani in Castellón , Spain. The acquisition brings new modular capabilities to projects across Europe, highlighting our continued commitment to delivering industry-leading technology and cutting-edge build strategies to the European construction sector. ... ""The future of construction belongs to those willing to rethink how things are built,"" said Rick Bucher, President and CEO at Victaulic. ""By integrating Arumani's advanced modular construction expertise with Victaulic's proven engineering excellence and innovative products, we are now uniquely positioned to enhance project efficiency, accelerate timelines, and set new benchmarks for construction certainty for our European customers. Together, we are even better equipped to deliver innovative solutions for the world's most complex projects and push the boundaries of what's possible for our customers and the industry."" ... ""Modularization is transforming the construction industry. Arumani allows us to bring a different approach to the market by combining the innovative build strategies that Arumani is known for with the engineering excellence and reliability that define Victaulic,"" added Branden Kotyk, Vice-President and General Manager for EMEA at Victaulic. ""This acquisition represents a natural extension of Victaulic's capabilities and a strategic step forward in how we serve customers across Europe."" ... Arumani, a family-founded and Spain-based mechanical assemblies company, will now serve as Victaulic's European center of excellence for modular construction, supporting key industry sectors with Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DfMA) strategies, improving project certainty, reducing risk, and enhancing overall efficiency. ... ""This acquisition marks an exciting new chapter for Arumani,"" said Arumani CEO Jesús Policarpio. ""We are excited to combine our strengths with Victaulic, a company with whom we share a profound alignment in our vision for innovation and delivering exceptional customer value. Just as importantly, we are bringing together two teams that share a commitment to engineering excellence, collaboration, and customer success. This collaboration not only validates our expertise in Design for Manufacturing and Assembly but also provides a powerful platform to expand our reach and collectively deliver even greater solutions across Europe. Together, we are poised to set new standards in the industry."" ... This acquisition marks Victaulic's third investment in Europe over the past three years, highlighting the organization's continued commitment to delivering industry-leading technology and cutting-edge build strategies to the European construction sector. ... Since 1919, Victaulic's innovative solutions and design services continue to increase construction productivity and reduce risk, ensuring projects are completed safely, on time and within budget. With more than 6,000 employees and 50 facilities worldwide, Victaulic helps customers in 140+ countries succeed in the global construction industry. Learn more about how our solutions engineer confidence into every build at www.victaulic.com. ... ### Victaulic Expands European Modular Construction Capabilities with Acquisition of Arumani ... Victaulic, the world's leading manufacturer of mechanical pipe joining, fire protection, and flow control solutions, announced the acquisition"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,"Aurobindo Pharma Q1 net rises 25% to ₹1,032 cr; approves merger of three arms - The Hindu",www.thehindu.com (The Hindu Bureau),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thehindu.com/business/aurobindo-pharma-q1-net-rises-25-to-1032-cr-approves-merger-of-three-arms/article71310442.ece,"Aurobindo Pharma Q1 net rises 25% to ₹1,032 cr; approves merger of three arms - The Hindu # Aurobindo Pharma Q1 net rises 25% to ₹1,032 cr; approves merger of three arms ## The U.S. formulations revenue increase was primarily driven by volume gains and new launches, partially offset by no transient product sales; Europe formulations revenue driven by robust performance across all key market. Published - August 05, 2026 09:24 pm IST - HYDERABAD The Hindu Bureau ... Aurobindo Pharma | Photo Credit: The Hindu Generic drugmaker Aurobindo Pharma reported a 25.2% year-on-year (YoY) increase in consolidated net profit to ₹1,032 crore in the June quarter FY27. ... The higher net profitability came on a 16.3% YoY increase in revenue from operations to ₹9,150 crore on the back of growth across businesses. ... Formulations revenue surged 16.5% YoY to ₹8,101 crore, including a 8.1% YoY increase in the U.S. revenue to ₹3,770 crore ($399 million) and 25.6% in Europe revenue to ₹2,937 crore (€267 million). Total API revenue rose 14.6% YoY to ₹1,049 crore in the review quarter. ... On the U.S. formulations revenue, the company, in a release, said the increase was primarily driven by volume gains and new launches, partially offset by no transient product sales; while in Europe, the formulations revenue was driven by robust performance across all key markets. Merger of three arms ... In a filing, Aurobindo Pharma said its Board on Wednesday approved a proposal for merger of wholly owned step-down subsidiaries Eugia Steriles and Eugia SEZ with subsidiary Eugia Pharma Specialities. The three companies are engaged in the business of manufacturing injectable pharmaceutical products. ... The proposed amalgamation will simplify the existing group structure by consolidating three companies carrying on substantially similar businesses into a single legal entity. ... It will lead to elimination of corporate and administrative functions and overheads, cost reduction, better treasury management and synergy benefits, the parent company said."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,"Aurona lifts ABF and CCL shipments, eyes capacity expansion in 3Q26",www.digitimes.com (Flora Wang),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260804PD238/aurona-shipments-materials-demand-2026.html,"Aurona lifts ABF and CCL shipments, eyes capacity expansion in 3Q26 ... # Aurona lifts ABF and CCL shipments, eyes capacity expansion in 3Q26 ... Flora Wang , Taipei Aug 5, 2026, 06:19 0 Credit: DIGITIMES Aurona said shipments of ABF substrate pads and CCL-related packaging materials both rose, extending its growth momentum in the second quarter of 2026..."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Mutares launches former Sabic engineering thermoplastics business as NexPoint - Plastics News,www.plasticsnews.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.plasticsnews.com/suppliers/materials/sp-mutares-sabic-engineering-thermoplastics-business-acquisition-launch-nexpoint/,"Mutares launches former Sabic engineering thermoplastics business as NexPoint - Plastics News ... # Mutares launches former Sabic engineering thermoplastics business as NexPoint ... Sabic's manufacturing site in Cartagena, Spain is one of the acquired business units. (Sabic) ... August 04, 2026 04:12 AM EDT"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Swedish Hexpol acquires Italian compounder Vipa | ChemOrbis,www.chemorbis.com (ChemOrbis),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.chemorbis.com/en/plastics-news/Swedish-Hexpol-acquires-Italian-compounder-Vipa/2026/08/04/981587,"Swedish Hexpol acquires Italian compounder Vipa | ChemOrbis Just two weeks ago, the question was whether the renewed war premium in crude oil could finally put a floor under polymer markets after months of relentless declines. Brent crude extended its rally far beyond expectations, climbing from the mid-$80s/bbl in H1 July to briefly settle above $100/bbl on July 23 as geopolitical tensions in the Middle East intensified. This visibly shifted the sentiment upwards in Asia including China, Southeast Asia and India as well in Türkiye and Egypt while the slump slowed down in Europe... Dow’s €1.1 billion claim puts Europe’s ethylene cartel dispute back in focus Europe’s long-running ethylene cartel dispute has returned to the spotlight after Dow Europe filed a €1.1 billion damages claim against four companies accused of manipulating Europe’s ethylene benchmark price. The lawsuit is the latest in a series of civil actions stemming from the European Commission’s 2020 decision that found Clariant, Celanese, Orbia and Westlake had coordinated their ethylene purchasing strategies between 2011 and 2017 to influence the Monthly Contract Price (MCP)... Crude oil surges on renewed war premium; will it reverse the polymer slump? The renewed geopolitical tensions have pushed Brent crude back into the mid-$80s/bbl, rapidly rebuilding some of the war-risk premium that had evaporated after June's ceasefire hopes. This has also helped buoy the sentiment recently in polymer markets, where prices have been on a downturn for the past couple of months. After months of sluggish demand, ample supplies, and relentless price erosion, sellers are seizing on higher feedstock costs to argue that the market has reached its bottom... India's domestic polymer market underwent a major pricing reset on July 2 after leading local producers, spearheaded by a major private-sector refiner, rolled out unprecedented one-day cuts for PP and PE while extending the ongoing correction in PVC..."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,UFlex Commissions First Overseas WPP Bags Plant in Mexico | Packaging Strategies,www.packagingstrategies.com (Packaging Strategies Editorial Team),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingstrategies.com/articles/106598-uflex-commissions-first-overseas-wpp-bags-plant-in-mexico,"UFlex Limited, India’s largest multinational packaging and solutions company, has commissioned its first overseas WPP (woven polypropylene) bags manufacturing plant in Mexico. Established with an investment of approximately US$52 million, the state-of-the-art facility — spread across 10 acres — marks a major milestone in the company’s global expansion strategy and significantly strengthens its presence in the Americas. ... With an annual production capacity of 80 million WPP bags, UFlex says the facility is well positioned to serve the growing demand for high-performance packaging solutions across the Americas. The WPP bags produced at the site are engineered for greater strength, incorporate mite-preventive laser venting technology that allows air to escape while preventing the ingress of mites, and feature precision hot-air sealing technology adaptable to a variety of ... sizes and specifications, ensuring ... durability and product safety. ... Commenting on the announcement, Jeevaraj Gopal Pillai, President - Flexible Packaging and New Product Development, UFlex Limited, said, “The commissioning of our WPP packaging plant in Mexico represents a strategic step in expanding our global manufacturing network and strengthening our presence in the Americas. Pet ownership is steadily rising across North and South America, driving increased demand for premium pet food and high-performance packaging solutions. ... “The North American pet food packaging market, valued at over US$12 billion in 2026, is projected to witness sustained growth, while Latin America continues to emerge as a high-potential market driven by urbanization, rising disposable incomes, and growing awareness of pet nutrition. “This growth trajectory is driving demand for durable, hygienic, and sustainable WPP bag formats that can withstand the challenges of transportation and storage while preserving product freshness. The new facility will enable us to deliver innovative, high-quality packaging solutions closer to our customers, ensure shorter turnaround times, and support the evolving sustainability and performance needs of the region’s fast-growing pet food industry.” The plant houses an integrated converting facility incorporating sustainable water-based inks and operating at speeds of up to 300 meters per minute. It also includes an integrated quality and environmental control laboratory to ensure consistent ... quality and environmental compliance. ... UFlex is India’s largest multinational flexible packaging and solutions company. Since its inception in 1985, UFlex has built a strong presence across all verticals of the packaging value chain — from PET resin, packaging films, chemicals, holography, printing cylinders and engineering solutions to flexible packaging, aseptic packaging and recycling. For more details, visit www.uflexltd.com"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Mutares completes landmark acquisition of the Engineering Thermoplastics Business in the Americas and Europe from SABIC - Mutares SE & Co. KGaA,mutares.com (WordPress Service),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mutares.com/en/mutares-completes-landmark-acquisition-of-the-engineering-thermoplastics-business-in-the-americas-and-europe-from-sabic/,"Mutares completes landmark acquisition of the Engineering Thermoplastics Business in the Americas and Europe from SABIC - Mutares SE & Co. KGaA ... Munich/Chicago, August 4, 2026 – Mutares SE & Co. KGaA (ISIN: DE000A2NB650) has completed the acquisition of the regional Engineering Thermoplastics business in the Americas and Europe (“the ETP Business”) of SABIC for an Enterprise Value of USD 450 million. The acquisition represents the largest transaction in Mutares’ history and has marked the establishment of a new strategic segment, “Chemicals & Materials”. The company will operate under the new name NexPoint Materials in the future. ... With resin production capacity of approx. 1,085 KT and compounding capacity of approx. 780 KT, the ETP Business operates a broad international platform with approximately 2,800 full-time employees and eight producing facilities across the Americas and Europe. The product range includes Polycarbonates (PC), Polybutylene Terephthalate (PBT), and Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene (ABS) resin and compounding lines, supported by globally recognized brands such as LEXAN™, CYCOLOY™, VALOX™ and CYCLOLAC™. The business is generating approx. USD 2.5 billion in revenues. ... The ETP Business is the world’s second-largest producer of PC, the leading ABS producer in the United States and the sole producer of PBT in the United States – underlining its strong competitive position across key engineering thermoplastics categories. Moreover, it serves a diversified customer base across Automotive (39%), Building & Construction (20%), Consumer Products (17%), Electrical & Electronics (10%) and Healthcare (3%), with additional exposure to water containers and other industrial applications. Geographically, the business is well balanced with 66% of revenues in the Americas and 34% in Europe. ... This transformational acquisition enables Mutares to leverage the ETP Business’ upstream-integrated platform, broad technical capabilities and strong innovation pipeline to accelerate growth, operational excellence and value creation across the Chemicals & Materials segment. ... Johannes Laumann, CIO of Mutares, comments: “The closing of the ETP Business from SABIC marks a major milestone and achievement for Mutares as the largest transaction in our history and further expansion into the US. We are delighted to welcome the company to our portfolio and look forward to working closely with the management team to support the company’s continued development and future growth.”"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Epoch scales polymer biorecycling with Domo factory,www.just-style.com (Jangoulun Singsit),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.just-style.com/news/epoch-domo-nylon-plant/,"Epoch scales polymer biorecycling with Domo factory ... Epoch purchased the factory, formerly operated by Domo Chemicals before its Spanish business entered insolvency, for €4m, making it the first enzymatic recycler to own commercial-scale production. ... The facility offers production capacity of 52,000t per year, providing the scale to expand Epoch’s offering of both traditional and recycled nylon 6,6. ... Epoch says it can offer brands a route to closed-loop recycled nylon, ahead of EU rules on recycled-content tightening in 2030. ... The acquisition brings 60 jobs under Epoch’s stewardship and builds on the site’s more than 50-year history supplying materials for customers in the apparel, automotive, and industrial sectors. ... Earlier this year Epoch secured $12m in new investment from lululemon, KOMPAS VC, Extantia and others, to accelerate the commercialisation of its recycled nylon 6,6 technology. ... “This acquisition is a key step on our journey to deliver something that the market simply hasn’t been able to offer: a secure supply of genuinely circular material, at scale,” says Jacob Nathan, founder and CEO at Epoch. ... to deliver a new ... and safeguard 6 ... However, the company noted that less than 1% is currently recycled at the end of its life, leaving industry and regulators facing a substantial supply shortfall. ... Epoch said that major brands and manufacturers are setting 2030 targets for recycled material integration, driving demand for reliable sources of recycled nylon 6,6. ... Epoch Biodesign chief commercial officer Luciano Caruso added: “Owning commercial-scale polymerisation means we can now offer customers something the market has been waiting for: a genuine timeline to secure closed-loop supply of recycled nylon 6,6. This acquisition enables us to partner with brands and manufacturers at a deeper level. ... “Starting today, we will work together to validate Epoch polymer in their supply chains and products so that we can seamlessly integrate recycled content over the coming years. In an industry facing tightening regulation and real material shortages, Epoch Biodesign is proud of this deal and what it represents.”"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,ExxonMobil and partners redefine performance of thermoforming films | Packaging Strategies,www.packagingstrategies.com (Packaging Strategies Editorial Team),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingstrategies.com/articles/106596-exxonmobil-and-partners-redefine-performance-of-thermoforming-films,"ExxonMobil and partners redefine performance of thermoforming films By Packaging Strategies ... ExxonMobil, one of the largest publicly traded international energy companies, uses technology and innovation to help meet the world's growing energy needs. ExxonMobil Signature Polymers brings together ExxonMobil’s polyolefin products under a single portfolio brand, simplifying portfolio navigation and promoting enhanced collaboration across the value chain. Grupo Plastilene faced the challenge of elevating locally produced thermoforming film performance. By implementing Tube Water Quench (TWQ) blown film technology, the company developed a high-performance local solution in Colombia that matches and replaces imported structures while delivering premium optics, mechanical strength, barrier performance, and strong shelf impact. ... A longtime regional leader in thermoforming films, Grupo Plastilene strengthened its technology platform by integrating TWQ extrusion from Windmöller & Hölscher (W&H), in close collaboration with ExxonMobil Signature Polymers. Prior to this investment, conventional blown barrier technology limited performance in deep-draw applications. The adoption of TWQ in 2021 marked a transformative leap in optical, mechanical, and thermoforming capability. ... To fully leverage TWQ, Groupo Plastilene incorporated ExxonMobil’s high-performance polyethylene resins: Exceed™ Flow m 0520, providing toughness and deep-draw durability, and Exxtra™ Seal POP 2008, ensuring robust hermetic sealing and contributing to exceptional optical performance. ... This combination enabled the development of medium- and high-barrier structures with superior strength, clarity, and sealability. “Importantly, there are no changes in oxygen or water vapor barrier values between the two technologies, with both delivering satisfactory results of OTR < 1.0 cc/m²·day and WVTR < 3.0 g/m²·day, levels fully suitable for the products intended to be packaged using these solutions,” ExxonMobil notes. ... Real-world validation with Colombian meat purveyor Carnes Casablanca confirmed strong forming behavior, excellent sealing, and premium shelf appearance. “Combining TWQ technology, ExxonMobil’s advanced resin portfolio, and Plastilene’s conversion expertise sets a benchmark for thermoforming films,” ExxonMobil says. To check out the full case study, visit here."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,"UFlex Expands Global Footprint with New $52 Million Woven Polypropylene Bags Facility in Mexico, Stock Rises 4%",www.fortuneindia.com (Chitranjan Kumar),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.fortuneindia.com/markets/uflex-sets-up-first-overseas-wpp-bags-plant-in-mexico-with-52-mn-investment-share-jumps-4/151608,"UFlex Expands Global Footprint with New $52 Million Woven Polypropylene Bags Facility in Mexico, Stock Rises 4% ... UFlex sets up first overseas WPP bags plant in Mexico with $52 mn investment; share jumps 4%August 3, 2026, 15:31 IST ... The 10-acre facility has an annual production capacity of 80 million woven polypropylene bags and is expected to strengthen the company's packaging solutions portfolio in the U.S., UFlex said in a release. ... Packaging solutions company UFlex on Monday announced the commissioning of its first overseas woven polypropylene (WPP) bags manufacturing plant in Mexico with an investment of around $52 million. The facility marks a key milestone in the company's global expansion strategy and is expected to strengthen its presence across the Americas. ... Located in Altamira, Mexico, the 10-acre facility has an annual production capacity of 80 million woven polypropylene bags and has been built to cater to the growing demand for high-performance packaging solutions across North and South America, particularly for the fast-growing pet food industry. WPP bags are commonly used in agriculture for packaging essential products like grains, seeds, fertilizers, and animal feed. ... ""With an annual production capacity of 80 million WPP bags, the facility is well positioned to serve the growing demand for high-performance packaging solutions across the Americas,"" the Noida-based company said in a release. ... Shares of UFlex reacted positively to the announcement, rising as much as 3.96% to an intraday high of ₹490.20 on the BSE. At the time of writing, the small-cap stock was trading 2.1% higher at ₹481.40, taking the company's market capitalisation to around ₹3,476 crore. ... Jeevaraj Gopal Pillai, President – Flexible Packaging and New Product Development at UFlex, said the commissioning of the Mexico facility is a strategic step towards expanding the company's global manufacturing network and strengthening its footprint in the Americas. ... He said rising pet ownership across North and South America is driving demand for premium pet food and high-performance packaging solutions. The North American pet food packaging market, valued at more than $12 billion in 2026, is expected to witness sustained growth, while Latin America continues to emerge as a high-potential market, supported by urbanisation, rising disposable incomes and increasing awareness of pet nutrition. ... ""The new facility will enable us to deliver innovative, high-quality packaging solutions closer to our customers, ensure shorter turnaround times, and support the evolving sustainability and performance needs of the region's fast-growing pet food industry,"" Pillai said. ... The company said the new plant is equipped with advanced European machinery and operates through clean, low-noise and emission-free processes in line with its environmental, social and governance (ESG) commitments. It also houses an in-house recycling unit and a zero solid waste discharge facility designed to maximise material recovery, minimise waste generation and promote responsible waste disposal. ... The WPP bags manufactured at the facility are engineered for enhanced strength and durability. They feature laser venting technology that allows air to escape while preventing mite ingress, along with precision hot-air sealing technology that can be adapted to different bag sizes and specifications, improving both product safety and shelf life. ... The plant also houses an integrated converting facility that uses sustainable water-based inks and operates at speeds of up to 300 metres per minute. Additionally, it includes a quality and environmental control laboratory to ensure consistent product quality and regulatory compliance, besides producing high-quality woven polypropylene fabric used in the manufacture of WPP bags."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Hydrofarm Completes Sale of Aurora Peat Products and,"www.globenewswire.com (Hydrofarm Holdings Group, Inc.)",2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/08/03/3337406/0/en/Hydrofarm-Completes-Sale-of-Aurora-Peat-Products-and-Launches-Project-Agility-to-Scale-Its-Logistics-Services-Platform.html,"Hydrofarm Completes ... # Hydrofarm Completes Sale of Aurora Peat Products and Launches Project Agility to Scale Its Logistics Services Platform ... ## $16 million transaction reduces debt and simplifies the Company’s operating footprint ... SHOEMAKERSVILLE, Pa., Aug. 03, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Hydrofarm Holdings Group, Inc. (Nasdaq: HYFM) (“Hydrofarm” or the “Company”), today announced that it has completed the sale of Aurora Peat Products ULC (“Aurora Peat”) to Raven Holdings LLC, a private company, for total consideration of $16 million, a portion of which is represented by a promissory note in the amount of $5 million. The Aurora Peat sale proceeds will be applied to reduce outstanding Term Loan debt, and the sale also removes the capital spend of owning and operating peat harvesting assets. Aurora Peat will continue producing and marketing high-quality peat products for the global horticultural market under private ownership led by longtime operators in the peat industry. The two companies will continue an ongoing commercial relationship whereby Aurora Peat remains a supplier to Hydrofarm’s grow media business, and Hydrofarm will continue to distribute Aurora Peat’s consumer gardening products pursuant to the terms of a supply agreement. ... “The Aurora Peat sale is a key strategic step toward optimizing our portfolio and focus, and strengthening the Company’s capital structure,” said Bill Toler, Chief Executive Officer. “Aurora Peat is a sound business, and it is going to owners who know the peat industry well. For Hydrofarm, the divestiture continues to simplify our operating model and reduce debt. We are committed to our strategic priorities to drive high-quality revenue streams, and improve profit margins and profitability. We are excited about our core CEA business including our proprietary brand offerings, and heightened focus on our logistics services business, which has been a key driver in reducing our facility costs the past few years.” ... “As part of Aurora Peat Products' previous management team, several key members and I are grateful to return with the opportunity to carry the business forward to a new level of success,” said Bowe McGinnis, Manager of Raven Holdings LLC. “For our customers, the important things remain unchanged as they have for Aurora Peat Products' decades of history - our product quality, reliability, and supply commitments remain paramount. We are also enthusiastic about expansion opportunities, as Aurora Peat has secured one of the largest premium-quality Sphagnum peat moss reserves in North America. We deeply value our continuing relationship with Hydrofarm, a key partner on the supply side. By combining their top-notch distribution network with our focus on bulk peat and mix sales, we create the perfect partnership. We are excited for this strategy to support our customers and grow revenue across all categories.” ... “The actions in our announcement today support a change in Hydrofarm’s trajectory - we are now a leaner and more focused organization,” said Eric Ceresnie, Senior Vice President of Strategy, Corporate Development and International Markets. “We are also excited to announce Project Agility, which will drive resources to scale our logistics services platform as we pursue opportunities in adjacent high-growth sectors. While the logistics services business currently represents only a small portion of our operating results, our global distribution center footprint and operational excellence position us well going forward.” ... Hydrofarm is a leading independent manufacturer and distributor of branded hydroponics equipment and supplies for controlled environment agriculture (“CEA”), including grow lights, climate control solutions, grow media and nutrients, as well as a broad portfolio of innovative proprietary branded products. For nearly 50 years, Hydrofarm has helped growers make growing easier and more productive. The Company’s mission is to empower growers, farmers and cultivators with products that enable greater quality, efficiency, consistency and speed in their grow projects. ... This press release contains “forward-looking statements” within the meaning of the safe harbor provisions of the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995. Forward-looking statements may be identified by words such as “believe,” “expect,” “intend,” “anticipate,” “plan,” “will,” “project,” “potential” and similar expressions, and include, among others, statements regarding the anticipated benefits of the sale of Aurora Peat; the application of transaction proceeds and expected reduction of indebtedness; the continuing supply and distribution relationship between Hydrofarm and Aurora Peat; the objectives, scope and anticipated results of the logistics services business and Project Agility, including expansion of the Company’s logistics services business and ability to execute on opportunities in adjacent high-growth sectors; and the Company’s future financial performance, liquidity and capital allocation plans. ... These statements are based on management’s current expectations and assumptions and are subject to risks and uncertainties that could cause actual results to differ materially, including risks relating to the collectability of the promissory note; the Company’s level of indebtedness and ability to comply with the terms of its credit facilities; demand conditions in the CEA and hydroponics markets; the Company’s ability to attract and retain logistics services customers and to execute on new initiatives; the Company’s ability to maintain compliance with Nasdaq continued listing requirements; and the other factors described under “Risk Factors” in the Company’s Annual Report on Form 10-K and subsequent periodic reports filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission. Forward-looking statements speak only as of the date of this release, and the Company undertakes no obligation to update them except as required by law."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Ingenia Polymers Opens Innovation Centre In Ontario - Canadian Plastics,www.canplastics.com,2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.canplastics.com/canplastics/ingenia-polymers-opens-innovation-centre-in-ontario/1003469736/,"Ingenia Polymers Opens Innovation Centre In Ontario - Canadian Plastics ... # Ingenia Polymers opens Innovation Centre in Ontario ... July 31, 2026 By Canadian Plastics ... The centre in Brantford will allow Ingenia to collaborate with customers, with improvements in material and process technology. ... Ingenia Polymers Corp. officially opened its new Innovation Centre in Brantford, Ont., on July 22, significantly expanding its operational capabilities. The enhanced facility features advanced plastics processing and testing equipment, including a seven-layer blown film line from Macro Engineering, which will aid in developing multilayer film structures. ... - The expansion doubles the original building's footprint. - Guests at the grand opening included Brant County MP Larry Brock and Brantford Mayor Kevin Davis. - Ingenia, founded in 1986, operates eight manufacturing sites globally, serving markets such as rotational molding and film. ... This development highlights Ingenia's commitment to innovation in the plastics industry and strengthens its position in the competitive market. ... Houston-based materials maker Ingenia Polymers Corp. opened its new Innovation Centre in Brantford, Ont., on July 22. ... The newly expanded centre doubles the footprint of the original building; has additional plastics processing and testing equipment, including twin-screw and continuous mixer lines, and a seven-layer blown film line from Ontario firm Macro Engineering; and has upgraded and additional office areas for employees. In a statement, Ingenia officials noted that the system from Macro Engineering expands its capabilities to develop, evaluate, and optimize advanced multilayer film structures while accelerating material innovation and product development. ... The grand opening event was attended by guests that included Brant County Member of Parliament Larry Brock, who represented the Canadian government and Brantford Mayor Kevin Davis. Professors of Chemical Engineering from the University of Western Ontario, McMaster University, and the University of Waterloo, along with Ingenia’s customers, suppliers and banking partners, were additional delegates in attendance. ... Ingenia was founded in 1986 by John and Maria Lefas as a joint venture between Wedco Technologies and Polyvector Corp. The Lefas family were Greek immigrants who moved to Canada in 1979. John Lefas had worked for ExxonMobil, formerly Imperial Oil, in Sarnia, Ont. ... The firm has eight manufacturing sites worldwide, making compounds as well as white, black, color and additive concentrates at plants in Canada, the U.S., and Saudi Arabia. Ingenia also offers services including blending and size reduction. Markets served by the firm include rotational molding, pipe, and film."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,VIG Partners Wins Yulgok Aerospace Acquisition Bid | Gate News,www.gate.com,2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gate.com/news/detail/vig-partners-wins-yulgok-aerospace-acquisition-bid-23096246,"- VIG Partners was selected as preferred bidder to acquire Yulgok aerospace manufacturer on May 31. - Yulgok's enterprise value is discussed in 400 billion won range on 100% equity basis. - Founder Wi Ho-cheol will retain residual stake and continue participating in management decisions. ... VIG Partners was selected as the preferred bidder to acquire Yulgok, an aerospace parts manufacturer, according to investment banking industry sources on May 31. The JKL Partners and WJ Private Equity consortium chose VIG Partners over competing bidders including Stick Investment, Anchor Equity Partners, and KCGI. The selection was driven by defense security considerations and business continuity requirements, with the sellers preferring domestic capital over foreign investors due to Yulgok's role as a key supplier to Korea Aerospace Industries and its involvement in defense-related operations. The transaction involves the consortium's entire 47.09% stake plus a portion of founder and current largest shareholder Wi Ho-cheol's 47.23% stake, with Yulgok's enterprise value discussed in the 400 billion won range on a 100% equity basis. ... The JKL Partners and WJ Private Equity consortium recently selected VIG Partners as the preferred bidder for Yulgok. The transaction targets the consortium's full 47.09% stake and a portion of founder Wi Ho-cheol's 47.23% holding. The exact residual ownership percentage Wi will retain is currently under detailed discussion and will be finalized through a shareholders' agreement with VIG Partners. Industry sources indicated Yulgok's enterprise value is discussed in the 400 billion won range on a 100% equity basis. ... The outcome of this acquisition process was determined by qualitative deal factors rather than purely quantitative price conditions, according to industry assessments. Defense security linked to national security and supply chains, along with business continuity requirements from the founder and global clients, shaped the selection decision. Yulgok serves as a core partner to Korea Aerospace Industries, supplies components to Boeing and Airbus supply chains, and operates certain defense business segments. The sellers preferred domestic funds over foreign capital due to the special nature of the defense sector. ... An investment banking industry source stated that verification procedures for foreign capital are necessarily strict given the characteristics of defense and aerospace parts businesses, noting that the sellers likely considered strategies to prevent technology leakage concerns and maintain long-term partnerships with clients. VIG Partners' trust and deal experience built as pure domestic capital is interpreted as a decisive strength in the preferred bidder selection. ... VIG Partners gained an advantage in terms of post-acquisition corporate value enhancement possibilities. The sellers also preferred a partner capable of driving substantive growth for the acquired company. VIG Partners reportedly drew positive evaluation from the sellers by presenting aggressive capital injection and growth strategies including additional paid-in capital increases and bolt-on acquisitions. The firm's high industry understanding accumulated through operating existing aerospace industry portfolios such as Estar Aviation also served as a key competitive advantage, according to analysis. ... The ownership structure was designed with multifaceted consideration of business continuity. This transaction involves the sale of the consortium's holdings along with a portion of founder Wi's stake. Wi is expected to continue participating in management and key decision-making while retaining his residual stake. This outcome comprehensively considered requests from global clients concerned about Wi's absence, given his core role in project orders, as well as the founder's management intentions. ... This acquisition proceeds through VIG Partners' Fund V blind fund. Once the Yulgok acquisition is finalized, the fund's utilization rate is expected to reach approximately 80%. Industry observers anticipate VIG Partners will begin work in earnest on forming a sixth blind fund soon, using Fund V's depletion as a starting point. ... A: VIG Partners was selected over Stick Investment, Anchor Equity Partners, and KCGI based on defense security considerations, business continuity requirements, and domestic capital preference. The sellers favored a pure domestic fund due to Yulgok's role as a key supplier to Korea Aerospace Industries and its defense-related operations, aiming to prevent technology leakage concerns and maintain long-term partnerships with clients. ... A: The transaction involves the JKL Partners and WJ Private Equity consortium's entire 47.09% stake plus a portion of founder Wi Ho-cheol's 47.23% stake. Wi will retain a residual stake and continue participating in management and key decision-making. The exact residual ownership percentage is under discussion and will be finalized through a shareholders' agreement. Yulgok's enterprise value is discussed in the 400 billion won range on a 100% equity basis."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Univar Solutions Expands EMEA CASE Portfolio Through Acquisition | PCI Magazine,www.pcimag.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.pcimag.com/articles/115000-univar-solutions-expands-emea-case-portfolio-through-acquisition,"Univar Solutions Expands EMEA CASE Portfolio Through Acquisition | PCI Magazine ... Univar Solutions has acquired Interpur Chemicals, a European distributor of polyurethanes and powder coatings. Financial terms were not disclosed. ... The acquisition expands the technical capabilities and regional coverage of the Performance Materials business within Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions across Europe, the Middle East and Africa. ... Interpur Chemicals has more than 20 years of experience supplying raw materials and technical consulting services to the polyurethane, resin and powder coatings industries. Eighteen employees will join Univar Solutions through the transaction. ... “This acquisition marks an important milestone for our performance materials business as we respond to growing customer demand for the essential products that enable modern, high-performance applications,” said Matthew Oliver, senior vice president of Performance Materials for Univar Solutions. ... The acquisition expands Univar Solutions’ access to polyurethane and powder coatings materials while adding technical expertise and distribution coverage across EMEA. ... # Univar Solutions Expands Global Offerings with Acquisition of Spanish Specialty Distributor Vicom"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,"ExxonMobil Signature Polymers, Bandera develop PE pet food pouch | Packaging Strategies",www.packagingstrategies.com (Packaging Strategies Editorial Team),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingstrategies.com/articles/106587-exxonmobil-signature-polymers-bandera-develop-pe-pet-food-pouch,"ExxonMobil Signature Polymers, a newly launched brand focused on delivering best-in-class service and partnerships within the polymers industry, is collaborating with Bandera to develop PE substrate films using conventional blown film extrusion. ... Bandera is a worldwide leader in designing and manufacturing extrusion lines for packaging and converting industries. Together, the companies developed a PE mono-material pet food pouch designed for recyclability. The pouch was made using a substrate film to provide stiffness and optics while also meeting converting requirements for printing and lamination. Made on a conventional Bandera blown film extrusion line, the resulting substrate film features good optical properties, high stiffness and dimensional stability at elevated temperatures — which are important requirements for printing and lamination, the companies share. ... For a sealant film for the pouch, an EVOH-containing film was made on Bandera’s Barrier FLEX extrusion line using an ExxonMobil Signature Polymers Exxtra Seal enhanced polymer to ensure a broad sealing window. Bandera Barrier FLEX blown film lines and ExxonMobil Signature Polymers developed a solution using conventional blown film extrusion technology for a still, high-clarity substrate film that can be used for PE mono-material pouch applications designed for recyclability, it says. The solution uses a non-oriented blow, yet stiff PE film that serves as a replacement for PET — without MDO for a mono-material solution. ... # ExxonMobil Leads Effort to Develop Mono-Material PE Pet Food Packaging Solution ... # ExxonMobil Launches Signature Polymers Brand for Polyolefin Products ... # New Pet Food Pouch Boasts Food-Contact Compliance, Advanced Recycled Content"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Country Life Acquires Aura Cacia - Vitamin Retailer Magazine,vitaminretailer.com (Eric Munson),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://vitaminretailer.com/country-life-acquires-aura-cacia/,"Country Life Acquires Aura Cacia - Vitamin Retailer Magazine ... # Country Life Acquires Aura Cacia ... Country Life (Hauppauge, NY) announced its acquisition of Aura Cacia from Frontier Co-op (Norway, IA). The acquisition expands Country’s Life portfolio to four wellness brands alongside Country Life, Desert Essence and BioChem. ... Aura Cacia was founded in 1982 and specializes in essential oils, skin care and aromatherapy products. Since joining the Frontier Co-op family of brands in the 1990s, it has become one of the top selling aromatherapy and natural hair care brands. ... “Aura Cacia is a strong fit within the Country Life family,” said Rob Robillard, CEO of Country Life. “Together, we bring more than a century of combined experience helping consumers live healthier, more balanced lives. Aura Cacia’s leadership in essential oils and aromatherapy complements our portfolio of supplements, sports nutrition and personal care products, all developed with integrity, transparency and care.” ... Effective immediately, Aura Cacia will operate as a brand within Country Life, ensuring continuity for existing consumers and partners. The company will maintain manufacturing operations in Urbana, IA and headquarters in Hauppauge, NY. ... “After stewarding Aura Cacia’s growth for more than 30 years, we believe this decision allows both organizations to focus, scale and thrive,” said Tony Bedard, CEO of Frontier Co-op. “Country Life has the expertise and resources to help Aura Cacia fully capitalize on the growing consumer demand for high-quality essential oils and aromatherapy products. We are proud to entrust this mission-driven brand to a partner that will build on the values that have made it successful, while we remain focused on our herbs and spices business with Frontier Co-op and Simply Organic brands.”"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,VIG Partners wins preferred bidder status for aerospace parts maker Yulgok in W400b deal - The Herald Business,biz.heraldcorp.com (An Hyo-jung),2026-07-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://biz.heraldcorp.com/article/10819846,"VIG Partners wins preferred bidder status for aerospace parts maker Yulgok in W400b deal - The Herald Business ... preferred bidder status for ... ulgok in ... 0b deal ... VIG Partners has been selected as the preferred bidder to acquire Yulgok, an aerospace components manufacturer. The domestic private equity firm edged out formidable rivals — including Stic Investments, Anchor Equity Partners and KCGI — by emphasizing defense security credentials, business continuity and a post-acquisition growth strategy. ... According to investment banking industry sources, the JKL Partners–WJ Private Equity consortium designated VIG Partners as the preferred bidder for Yulgok on Tuesday. The transaction covers the consortium's entire 47.09 percent stake as well as a portion of the shares held by founder and current largest shareholder Wi Ho-cheol, who owns 47.23 percent. ... The exact size of the residual stake Wi will retain is still under discussion and will be finalized through a shareholders' agreement with VIG Partners. Yulgok's enterprise value on a 100 percent equity basis is cited at around 400 billion won ($272 million). ... Industry observers say the outcome was decided less by who offered the highest price than by the qualitative strength of each bid. Defense security — directly tied to national security and supply chain integrity — and business continuity, as demanded by the founder and global clients, are seen as the factors that shifted the deal's dynamics. ... Yulgok is a key partner of Korea Aerospace Industries (KAI) and supplies components to the Boeing and Airbus supply chains, while also operating in some defense business segments. The sellers are understood to have preferred a domestic fund over foreign capital, given the sensitive nature of the defense operations. ... ""Given the nature of the defense and aviation parts business, the vetting process for overseas capital is inevitably stringent,"" an investment banking industry official said. ""The sellers would have been thinking carefully about how to block risks such as technology leakage and maintain long-term partnerships with their clients."" VIG Partners' accumulated trust and deal experience as a purely domestic fund are seen as decisive advantages in securing preferred bidder status. ... VIG Partners also held an edge in terms of post-acquisition value enhancement potential. The sellers favored a partner capable of driving genuine growth at the acquired company. ... VIG Partners won positive marks from the sellers by presenting an aggressive capital deployment and growth strategy, including additional paid-in capital increases and bolt-on acquisitions. Its deep understanding of the aviation industry, built through managing existing portfolio companies such as Eastar Jet, is also cited as a key competitive strength. ... The ownership structure was designed with business continuity in mind from multiple angles. The deal involves the acquisition of both the consortium's stake and a portion of founder Wi's shares, with Wi retaining a residual interest and continuing to participate in management and key decision-making. The arrangement reflects requests from global clients concerned about his absence and Wi's own desire to remain involved in running the company — a recognition of the central role he has played in winning project contracts. ... The acquisition will be carried out through VIG Partners' fifth blind fund. Once the Yulgok deal closes, the fund's deployment rate is expected to reach approximately 80 percent. Industry watchers expect VIG Partners to move soon after that milestone to begin raising its sixth blind fund in earnest. ... - Keystone to close acquisition of ... equipment maker SSP ... VIG Partners wins preferred bidder status for aerospace parts maker Yulgok in W400b deal - TaylorMade set for sale as US sports mogul joins bidding race"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aurobindo Pharma Subsidiary Acquires 80% Stake in A1 Biochem CRO Business for $17 Million,tradebrains.in (Agrima Agarwal),2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://tradebrains.in/aurobindo-pharma-subsidiary-acquires-80-stake-in-a1-biochem-cro-business-for-17-million/,"Aurobindo Pharma Subsidiary Acquires 80% Stake in A1 Biochem CRO Business for $17 Million ... # Aurobindo Pharma Subsidiary Acquires 80% Stake in A1 Biochem CRO Business for $17 Million ... Synopsis: Aurobindo Pharma’s wholly owned subsidiary, Apitoria Pharma, will acquire an 80 percent stake in A1 Biochem Group’s Contract Research Services business for an enterprise value of USD 17 million. The acquisition expands Aurobindo’s presence beyond API manufacturing into integrated Contract Research, Development and Manufacturing (CRDMO) services while strengthening its global pharmaceutical innovation platform. ... Shares of Aurobindo Pharma Limited are likely to remain in focus after the company announced that its wholly owned subsidiary, Apitoria Pharma Private Limited, has approved the acquisition of 80 percent ownership in the Contract Research Services (CRO) business of A1 Biochem Group at an enterprise value of USD 17 million on a debt-free and cash-free basis. ... According to the company’s exchange filing, Apitoria Pharma will acquire an 80 percent stake in A1 Biochem Labs (India) Private Limited, while A1 Biochem Labs (India) will subsequently acquire 100 percent ownership of A1 Biochem Labs LLC, USA, along with the CRO business of A1 Biochem Research (India) Private Limited. The transaction values the business at USD 17 million, with Aurobindo investing USD 13.6 million for its 80 percent ownership. The acquisition is expected to be completed within 90 to 120 days, subject to customary approvals. ... The acquisition marks an important strategic step in Aurobindo Pharma’s evolution from being primarily an Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (API) manufacturer to becoming an integrated Contract Research, Development and Manufacturing Organisation (CRDMO). While Apitoria already operates large-scale regulatory-compliant API manufacturing facilities, acquiring front-end research and development capabilities enables the company to offer customers end-to-end pharmaceutical development services—from early-stage research through commercial manufacturing. ... The acquired A1 Biochem Group brings established capabilities in custom synthesis, medicinal chemistry, route scouting, analytical development and rapid process scale-up services, serving pharmaceutical companies, biotechnology firms and academic institutions, primarily in the United States. The business generated a turnover of Rs. 102.44 crore (INR 1,024.42 million) with an EBITDA of Rs. 46.55 crore (INR 465.46 million) during FY26 and operates scientific laboratories in North Carolina, USA, and Hyderabad, India, supported by over 90 scientists, 50+ fume hoods, a client base of more than 50 customers and a track record of completing over 800 projects. ... The acquisition is expected to strengthen Aurobindo’s competitive position in the rapidly growing global CRDMO market, where pharmaceutical companies increasingly outsource drug discovery, process development and manufacturing to specialised partners. By combining A1 Biochem’s research expertise with Apitoria’s large-scale manufacturing infrastructure, Aurobindo can participate across a larger portion of the pharmaceutical value chain, improve customer retention through longer-term engagements and diversify revenue streams beyond conventional API manufacturing. ... For investors, the transaction represents a strategic growth initiative rather than a short-term earnings trigger. The acquisition expands Aurobindo’s presence in high-value pharmaceutical research services, enhances its global capabilities and strengthens its exposure to innovation-driven outsourcing opportunities. As global pharmaceutical companies continue to increase spending on outsourced research and development, the integrated CRDMO platform could support higher-margin business opportunities and contribute to sustainable long-term growth. ... Aurobindo Pharma Limited is principally engaged in the manufacturing and marketing of active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs), generic pharmaceuticals and related services. The company has a diversified global presence across formulations, injectables, biosimilars and APIs, supplying products to more than 150 countries while serving regulated markets including the United States, Europe and emerging economies."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,LI drugmaker Country Life acquires competitor Aura Cachia,www.longislandpress.com (James Bernstein),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.longislandpress.com/2026/07/22/country-lifie-drugmaker-aura/,"LI drugmaker Country Life acquires competitor Aura Cachia ... Hauppauge-based Country Life LLC bought Aura Cachia. ... Long Island’s rapidly expanding pharmaceutical-nutraceutical industry has grown larger with Hauppauge-based Country Life LLC, one of the oldest of the companies, recently acquiring a Midwestern competitor. ... So, a number of local economy-watchers took note in early July when Country Life, a company founded in 1971, announced that it had acquired Aura Cachia from Frontier Distribution LLC, described as a member-owned cooperative, based in Norway, Iowa, and established in 1976. ... Country Life is privately held, and no terms of the deal were announced. The company has about 150 employees. Once the acquisition is completed, Country Life’s sales will be over $100 million. The company declined to state what sales are currently. ... neutral industry has been rapid. ... industry employs about ... more people than any other ... . Salaries in key executive or technical positions ... Stacey Sikes, acting president and CEO of the Long Island Association, the Island’s largest business and civic organization, told the Press the acquisition was a positive for the region. ... State economic development officials say Country Life is “a significant regional manufacturer in the industry.” ... Country Life describes itself as a “holistic wellness company” that makes health supplements and personal care products. The company said that the acquisition will expand its portfolio. Frontier Co-Op’s products include culinary herbs, spices, oils and aroma therapies. ... “Aura Cacia is a strong fit within the Country Life family,” Rob Robillard, CEO of Country Life, said in a statement. “Together, we bring more than a century of combined experience helping consumers live healthier, more balanced lives.” ... Tony Bedard, CEO of Frontier Co ... Op, said, “We believe this decision allows both organizations to focus, scale and thrive.” ... Country Life said that effective immediately, Aura Cacia will operate as a brand within Country Life’s portfolio. Country Life said that the organization will “maintain manufacturing operations” in Urbana, Iowa, and corporate headquarters in Hauppauge. ... A company spokesman said no jobs will be eliminated as a result of the acquisition. ... Tom Mariner, executive director of LIBO, an organization that supports the biotechnology industry on Long Island, said the pharmaceutical and nutraceutical business has been expanding here because of available space for warehouses and the available pool of talent from the State University at Stony Brook and support from other institutions, such as Cold Spring Harbor Lab and the Feinstein Institute, the research arm of Northwell Health. ... “New York City is trying to invest” in pharma and neutral, “but the costs of property there are prohibitive,” Mariner said. ... do,” Mariner said ... on how much ... want to invest, and it depends on what we want Long Island to look"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Bandera and ExxonMobil develop mono-material PE pet food pouch using conventional blown film technology - Packaging MEA,www.packagingmea.com (PackagingMEA),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingmea.com/bandera-and-exxonmobil-develop-mono-material-pe-pet-food-pouch-using-conventional-blown-film-technology/,"Bandera and ExxonMobil develop mono-material PE pet food pouch using conventional blown film technology - Packaging MEA ... Bandera and ExxonMobil Signature Polymers have jointly developed a mono-material polyethylene (PE) pet food pouch designed for recyclability by replacing conventional PET-based substrate films with a PE alternative produced on standard blown film extrusion equipment. The development demonstrates an approach to creating recyclable flexible packaging without requiring machine direction-oriented (MDO) film technology. ... The case study combines Bandera’s blown film extrusion technology with ExxonMobil Signature Polymers’ PE materials to produce a full PE pouch intended for pet food packaging. While MDO PE films can improve mechanical, barrier and optical properties, their adoption typically requires investment in specialised processing equipment. The new solution instead utilises conventional blown film extrusion lines to achieve comparable performance characteristics for printing and lamination. ... According to the companies, the substrate film was manufactured on a conventional Bandera blown film extrusion line, producing a non-oriented PE film with high stiffness, optical clarity and dimensional stability at elevated temperatures. These properties are important during downstream converting processes, including printing and lamination, while enabling the replacement of PET in mono-material pouch structures designed for recyclability. ... For the sealant layer, the partners produced an EVOH-containing film on a Bandera Barrier FLEX® extrusion line using ExxonMobil Signature Polymers’ Exxtra™ Seal enhanced polymer. The sealant film provides a broad sealing window while maintaining the functional requirements of flexible packaging for pet food applications. ... The innovation focuses on enabling converters to manufacture PE mono-material pouches using conventional blown film extrusion technology rather than investing in dedicated MDO production lines. This approach could reduce barriers to producing flexible packaging structures intended to support recycling where appropriate collection, sorting and recycling infrastructure exists. ... The companies noted that the pouch was designed with features intended to support recyclability. Actual recyclability, however, depends on local collection, sorting and recycling infrastructure, as well as the condition and configuration of the packaging after use."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aliplast acquires majority stake in LDPE recycler Kronos Polymer Polska,"www.euwid-recycling.com (Eva Riebeling, EUWID)",2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.euwid-recycling.com/news/business/aliplast-acquires-majority-stake-in-kronos-polymer-polska-170726/,"Aliplast acquires majority stake in LDPE recycler Kronos Polymer Polska ... Kronos Polymer is headquartered in Gniew, about 70 kilometers south of Gdańsk. The newly built recycling facility began operations in early 2023. ... Italian plastics recycler Aliplast is expanding its presence in Poland by acquiring a 70 per cent stake in polyethylene specialist Kronos Polymer Polska. Completion of the transaction is expected by the end of the year, Aliplast announced on Wednesday. Financial details were not disclosed. ... The transaction has been structured as a spin-off from recycling company Kronos Polymer, which will retain a 30 per cent stake in the new company. According to its own information, the Polish plastics recycler produces high-quality LDPE regranulates from 100 per cent post-consumer material originating from commercial, packaging and agricultural applications, and also provides toll regranulation services...."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,ACR Acquires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business - Distribution Strategy Group,distributionstrategy.com (Mark Brohan),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://distributionstrategy.com/2026/07/acr-acquires-redibagusa-to-expand-sustainable-packaging-business/,"ACR Acquires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business - Distribution Strategy Group ACR Acquires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business - Distribution Strategy Group ... ires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business ... Why This Matters to Distributors: The acquisition expands ACR’s packaging portfolio and strengthens its presence in grocery, food service, healthcare, and industrial markets. It also highlights continued private equity-backed consolidation as distributors broaden product offerings and build scale through targeted acquisitions. ... ACR has acquired the assets of RediBagUSA, expanding its sustainable packaging portfolio and extending its reach across grocery, foodservice, healthcare, and industrial markets. ... Financial terms of the transaction, announced July 14, were not disclosed. ... The acquisition is the 11th add-on completed by ACR since the company was acquired by private equity firm Oridian Capital Partners, underscoring the firm’s strategy of building a larger packaging and foodservice supplies distribution platform through acquisitions. ... ACR said the acquisition expands its environmentally focused product portfolio while enhancing its ability to serve a broader range of end markets, including grocery stores, restaurants, delis, healthcare providers, and industrial customers. ... “This acquisition represents another important milestone in ACR’s growth journey,” Chief Executive Officer Scott Milberg said in a statement. “By bringing RediBagUSA into our organization, we are expanding our product breadth and strengthening our ability to meet evolving customer needs.” ... The deal also strengthens ACR’s sourcing capabilities and adds RediBagUSA’s portfolio of reusable, recyclable, and compostable packaging products as businesses continue shifting toward more sustainable packaging options. ... Oridian Capital Partners, formerly HCI Equity Partners, has pursued an active acquisition strategy since acquiring ACR, targeting distributors and manufacturers that expand the company’s product offerings and market reach. ... “RediBagUSA is the 11th acquisition under Oridian’s ownership and continues to underscore ACR’s disciplined approach to building scale through businesses that align strategically and culturally,” Managing Partner Doug McCormick said. ... Based in Exton, Pennsylvania, ACR distributes packaging, foodservice, janitorial and sanitation products, as well as operational supplies, through a network of distribution facilities across North America. Its customers include foodservice operators, healthcare providers, hospitality companies, schools, industrial businesses, and national retailers. ... The acquisition broadens ACR’s presence in the growing market for sustainable packaging while adding complementary products that can be sold through its existing distribution network. ... The acquisition reflects continued consolidation in the packaging and food service distribution sector, where distributors are using acquisitions to expand product categories, strengthen sourcing capabilities and offer customers a broader range of consumable products through a single supplier. ... - Avnet ... Electronics Demand Rebounds ... Through Specialty Products ... Supplier Partnerships and Digital Transformation ... Deepens Customer Integration Strategy to Fuel Growth ... Strategy Shifts Toward Data Centers, Customer Productivity and Distribution Network Expansion"
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aliplast (Hera Group) strengthens its leadership in plastics regeneration by acquiring 70% of Kronos Polymer Polska,www.prnewswire.com (Aliplast (Hera Group)),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/aliplast-hera-group-strengthens-its-leadership-in-plastics-regeneration-by-acquiring-70-of-kronos-polymer-polska-302825671.html,"Polska Accessibility Statement Skip ... BOLOGNA, Italy, July 15, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Aliplast (Hera Group) is further strengthening its leadership in high-quality plastics recycling, thanks to the binding agreement signed by its Polish subsidiary Aliplast Polska to acquire 70% of Kronos Polymer Polska, a new company that will be formed by spin-off from Kronos Polymer, a Polish operator active in the recycling and processing of polyethylene (PE). ... With plants in Italy, France, Spain and Poland, Aliplast has developed an integrated industrial model: from the collection of plastic waste to its transformation into secondary raw material, to the production of 100,000 tonnes/year of recycled products (including PET and LDPE flakes and granules, PET sheet, LDPE film, PP and HDPE flakes). Its communication campaign invite people to overcome their prejudices and view recycled plastics as a strategic resource, when managed within a secure, certified and compliant European supply chain ... Kronos Polymer operates at a newly built industrial site located in Gniew (Pomerania, Poland), about 300 kilometres from Aliplast Polska's branch in Tuszyn. The newco involved in the transaction will receive a plant equipped with a complete polyethylene sorting, grinding and washing line, with an installed production capacity of 12,000 tonnes per year. This will allow Aliplast to progressively expand also in the local market, carrying out recycling and regeneration directly on site, thereby optimising flows and logistics. ... Thanks to this transaction and other Italian projects currently underway – such as the rigid plastics recycling plant in Modena and the new PE-LD recycling plant in Borgolavezzaro (Novara) – the industrial synergies already existing within the Group will be further strengthened, and Aliplast will be able to increase its recycling flexibility, doubling its capacity to over 210,000 tonnes per year. ... Aliplast is continuing the path that has characterised it in recent years: expansion of production capacity, including in foreign markets; an increasing focus on the quality and traceability of recycled material; and targeted expertise to provide a concrete response to the needs of the European market, also leveraging its already consolidated presence in countries such as France and Spain. These activities are even more strategic, especially at a time like the present, when the PPWR Regulation has introduced new European rules for the design, production and management of packaging waste, with the aim of reducing environmental impact and fostering the circular economy, making it essential to review the entire packaging supply chain, including from a structural point of view. ... a company with deep roots in Poland such as ... os Polymer, the partnership with ... plast represents a major opportunity to further develop its industrial experience and advanced know-how. ... The acquisition of 70% of Kronos Polymer Polska by Aliplast Polska is subject to certain standard conditions precedent (including the completion of the demerger and the transfer of environmental permits), the fulfilment of which for the purposes of finalising the transaction is expected by the end of 2026. ... ""This transaction will enable us to further expand Aliplast's production capacity, in line with the Hera Group's strategy, which sees resource regeneration as a fundamental pillar,"" commented Michele Petrone, Aliplast CEO. ""The launch of the process that will lead to the acquisition of the majority stake in the newco Kronos Polymer Polska is also in line with the parent company's Business Plan, which provides for continued growth in the waste services value chain by expanding the reference markets. Strengthening our presence in Poland, where Aliplast's branch has been operating for some time, will in fact allow us to intercept the promising growth in demand for recycled plastic in this country."""
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aguia banks $2.3M in phosphate sales as Brazilian demand builds | The West Australian,thewest.com.au,2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thewest.com.au/business/bulls-n-bears/aguia-banks-23m-in-phosphate-sales-as-brazilian-demand-builds--c-22580601,"Aguia banks $2.3M in phosphate sales as Brazilian demand builds | The West Australian ... # Aguia banks $2.3M in phosphate sales as Brazilian demand builds ... Aguia Resources has locked in a whopping $2.3 million in sales of its Pampafos organic phosphate product within just six weeks of commissioning its Três Estradas plant in Brazil. ... The company says its sales haul includes a fresh $1.6 million secured just this week from three established agricultural distributors in Brazil’s Rio Grande do Sul state, as its premium Pampafos product starts to gain momentum. ... The sales figures mark a significant milestone for the multi-commodity South American company, which is now successfully generating revenue from its dual operations in gold and fertiliser. ... Aguia says it has completed the first delivery of Pampafos to the Markus family farm, a major local soybean producer and cattle operator. The adoption of the product by a major local producer highlights the substantial support for Aguia’s locally sourced product and its promise as a Brazilian specialty fertiliser. ... The company’s wholly owned Três Estradas phosphate project sits 320 kilometres northwest of Porto Alegre, in the state of Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil. The development was only given the nod of approval to begin mining its phosphate material in May and has wasted no time in presenting the in-demand product to a suite of potential buyers. ... Mr Hosking continued in his praise for Pampafos’ credentials, indicating the company expected sales to continue accelerating as the local agricultural sector kicks off soil preparation ahead of the summer planting season. ... With the processing facility at the project now up and running, Aguia says its plant is performing ahead of management’s expectations. Following an unexpected 30 per cent increase in plant capacity during commissioning to more than 200,000 tonnes per annum, the facility is now well positioned to support regular customer deliveries. ... While the Brazilian phosphate operation is firing on all cylinders, Aguia is also advancing its Santa Barbara gold operations in Colombia. ... Recent updates from the mine showed a threefold increase in monthly production in June to 851.9 grams of gold, along with significant cost reductions and the start of phase three mining a month ahead of schedule. ... Although the improvement in gold output is promising, for now, all eyes are on Brazil. After navigating the long road from explorer to producer, Aguia has put its first points on the board with impressive early sales. With a product tailored for the local market, a plant ready to scale and its first revenue locked in, the company looks to have moved into a new, commercially focused chapter in South America."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Hera grows in Poland: binding agreement to acquire Kronos Polymer Polska - FIRSTonline,www.firstonline.info (Redazione FIRSTonline),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.firstonline.info/en/Hera-grows-in-Poland--binding-agreement-for-the-purchase-of-Kronos-Polymer-Polska/,"Hera grows in Poland: binding agreement to acquire Kronos Polymer Polska - FIRSTonline ... # Hera grows in Poland: binding agreement for the purchase of Kronos Polymer Polska ... 14 July 2026, 17:26 | di FIRSTonline editorial team | 0 Hera strengthens its position in the environmental sector, particularly in the recycling of high-quality plastics, thanks to the binding agreement signed by its Polish subsidiary Aliplast Polska for the purchase of 70% of Kronos Polymer Polska. ... Hera further strengthens its position in the environmental sector, particularly in the recycling of high-quality plastics, thanks to the binding agreement signed today by its Polish subsidiary Aliplast Polska for the purchase of 70% di Kronos Polymer Polska, a new company that will be established through a split from Kronos Polymer, a Polish operator active in the recycling and in polyethylene processing. ... Kronos Polymer operates a recently built industrial site – completed at the end of 2022 and operational from the first quarter of 2023 – located in Gniew (Pomerania, Poland), approximately 300 kilometers from Aliplast Polska's branch in Tuszyn. The new company involved in the transaction will incorporate a plant equipped with a complete line for selecting, grinding and washing polyethylene with an installed production capacity of 12.000 tons per year, which will allow Aliplast to progressively expand the local market as well, carrying out recycling and regeneration on site, thus optimizing flows and logistics. ... Thanks to this operation and other projects currently underway – such as the rigid plastic recycling plant in Modena and the new PE-LD recycling plant in Borgolavezzaro (Novara) – the industrial synergies already existing in Hera and the subsidiary Aliplast will be able to increase recycling flexibility, doubling its capacity and exceeding 210.000 tons annually. Aliplast is thus continuing the path of recent years: expanding production capacity abroad, increasing focus on the quality and traceability of recycled material, and developing targeted expertise to provide a concrete response to the needs of the European market, leveraging its already consolidated presence in countries such as France and Spain. ... The acquisition of 70% of Kronos Polymer Polska by the Hera Group, through Aliplast Polska, is subject to certain standard conditions precedent (including the completion of the aforementioned demerger and the transfer of environmental authorisations), the fulfilment of which is expected for the purposes of finalising the transaction. by the end of 2026. ... “This operation will allow us to further expand Aliplast's production capacity, in line with the Hera group's strategy which sees the regeneration of resources as a fundamental pillar,” says Michele Petrone, CEO of Aliplast. ""Furthermore, the launch of the process leading to the acquisition of a majority stake in the new company Kronos Polymer Polska is in line with the parent company's business plan, which envisions continued growth in the environmental sector by expanding its target markets. Strengthening our presence in Poland, where the Aliplast subsidiary has been operating for some time, will allow us to tap into the promising growth in demand for recycled plastic in this country,"" adds the manager."
AURIGA POLYMERS,,,,Exa,Aurona sees strong PCB demand as AI and high-end chip trends lift sales,www.digitimes.com (Flora Wang),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260708PD244/demand-aurona-pcb-high-end-materials.html,"Aurona sees strong PCB demand as AI and high-end chip trends lift sales ... # Aurona sees strong PCB demand as AI and high-end chip trends lift sales ... Aurona Industries said demand for its PCB process materials remains strong, with order intake rising year over year, and high-end products in particular are seeing robust traction. The company's update reflects continued momentum for global electronics supply..."
