203,373 and $324,845 compared to $148,302 and $286,183 for the same periods in 2025, representing an increase of 37.1% and 13.5%. The increase in revenue was primarily due to the timing of construction and maintenance work as compared to the same period in 2025, as the second quarter of 2026 reflected a strong quarter for the Company, underpinned by a compacted turnaround season and ramp up of activity on key strategic contract wins. ... three and six ... were 4. ... % compared to ... and 6. ... % for the ... periods in 20 ... The decrease in SG&A expenses for the three months ended June ... SG&A expenses for the six months ended June 30, 20 ... 6 were primarily driven by lower professional fees resulting from the absence of one-time legal, consulting and advisory costs incurred in connection with the Company's recapitalization transaction in 2025. These savings were largely offset by higher personnel, occupancy and software costs. As a percentage of revenue, SG&A expenses decreased for both the three- and six-month periods primarily due to higher revenue in the current period. ... Net income for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 was income of $2,390 and $433 compared to income of $1,100 and a loss of $2,241 for the same periods in 2025. The increase in net income for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 was primarily attributable to lower interest expense resulting from reduced debt levels following the Company's recapitalization transaction in 2025. This improvement was partially offset by lower gross profit, higher long-term incentive plan expense, higher restructuring expenses and other non-operating items. ... The Company anticipates that its liquidity (cash at banks, cash equivalents and available credit facilities) and cash flows from operations will be sufficient ... meet its short-term contractual obligations and maintain compliance with its financial covenants through June ... , 2027. As ... CORPORATE UPDATES The annual meeting of holders of common shares of the Corporation was held on June 23, 2026. At the meeting, shareholders approved the election of Sean McMaster, Barry Card, H. Fraser Clarke, Katrisha Gibson, Karl Johannson and Dean MacDonald as directors and the appointment of Ernst & Young LLP as auditors. The Board also approved the Omnibus Incentive Plan to support long-term employee retention and align compensation with shareholder value creation. ... On May 19, 2026, Neil Wotton retired as Chief Operating Officer and effective June 1, 2026 Mark Nelson was appointed Chief Operating Officer. ... About FLINT Corp. With a legacy of excellence and experience stretching back more than 100 years, FLINT provides solutions for the energy and industrial markets including: oil & gas (upstream, midstream and downstream), petrochemical, mining, power, agriculture, forestry, infrastructure and water treatment. With offices strategically located across Canada and a dedicated workforce, we provide maintenance, construction, wear technology and environmental services that help our customers bring their resources to our world. For more information about FLINT, please visit www.flintcorp.com or contact: ... Advisory regarding Forward-Looking Information ... Certain information included in this press release may constitute “forward-looking information” within the meaning of Canadian securities laws. In some cases, forward-looking information can be identified by terminology such as “may”, “will”, “should”, “expect”, “plan”, “anticipate”, “believe”, “estimate”, “predict”, “potential”, “continue” or the negative of these terms or other similar expressions concerning matters that are not historical facts. This press release contains forward-looking information relating to: our business plans, strategies and objectives; the Company's expectation to see contract awards and backlog momentum continue for the second half of 2026; that as the Company's business mix diversifies, it is well positioned for the second half of 2026; the Company's commitment to safe, high-quality execution, operational excellence and continuous improvement remains paramount to delivering sustainable long-term value; the Company's approach to dividends; and the sufficiency of our liquidity and cash flow from operations to meet our short-term contractual obligations and maintain compliance with our financial covenants through June 30, 2027. ... Forward-looking information involves significant risks and uncertainties. A number of factors could cause actual events or results to differ materially from the events and results discussed in the forward-looking information including, but not limited to, compliance with debt covenants, access to credit facilities and other sources of capital for working capital requirements and capital expenditure needs, availability of labour, dependence on key personnel, economic conditions, commodity prices, interest rates, regulatory change, weather and risks related to the integration of acquired businesses. These factors should not be considered exhaustive. Risks and uncertainties about FLINT’s business are more fully discussed in FLINT’s disclosure materials, including its annual information form and management’s discussion and analysis of the operating and financial results, filed with the securities regulatory authorities in Canada and available on SEDAR+ at www.sedarplus.ca. In formulating the forward-looking information, management has assumed that business and economic conditions affecting FLINT will continue substantially in the ordinary course, including, without limitation, with respect to general levels of economic activity, regulations, taxes and interest rates. Although the forward-looking information is based on what management of FLINT considers to be reasonable assumptions based on information currently available to it, there can be no assurance that actual events or results will be consistent with this forward-looking information, and management’s assumptions may prove to be incorrect."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Greif Expands Manufacturing Presence in Spain with Acquisition of Envaplast - Greif,www.greif.com,2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.greif.com/greif-expands-manufacturing-presence-in-spain-with-acquisition-of-envaplast/,"## Blog # Greif Expands Manufacturing Presence in Spain with Acquisition of Envaplast * July 29, 2026 ... **DELAWARE, Ohio** — Greif, Inc. (NYSE: GEF), a global leader in industrial packaging products and services, today announced it has completed the acquisition of Envaplast, a leading manufacturer of premium small polymer containers based near Valencia, Spain. ... The acquisition strengthens Greif’s Customized Polymer Solutions business and expands the company’s manufacturing presence in Spain, where it previously had a limited position in the small polymer packaging market. Envaplast primarily serves the agrochemical industry and has built a strong reputation for quality, innovation, and customer service. ... The acquisition supports Greif’s disciplined strategy of pursuing growth-enabling bolt-on acquisitions that expand its presence in attractive markets while strengthening its leadership in advanced polymer technologies. Envaplast provides Greif with a strong foothold to accelerate its organic growth strategy across Europe, the Middle East and Africa while expanding its position in the agrochemical market, which represents the majority of Envaplast’s business. The company also aligns with Greif’s disciplined acquisition criteria, including strong profitability, cash generation, and exposure to resilient end markets. ... “We are excited to welcome Envaplast to Greif,” said Ole Rosgaard, President and Chief Executive Officer of Greif. “Spain is an important market with strong long-term growth opportunities, particularly in agriculture. Envaplast gives us an outstanding platform to expand our small polymer packaging business across the region while bringing together two organizations that share a deep commitment to quality, innovation, and customer service. We are especially pleased to welcome the talented Envaplast team and look forward to building on the strong relationships they have established throughout Spain.” ... Envaplast is a respected family-founded business whose proprietary technologies complement Greif’s existing portfolio of advanced polymer packaging solutions. The acquisition also strengthens Greif’s position in the agrochemical market while expanding manufacturing capacity and technical expertise in one of Europe’s most important agricultural regions. Together with the acquisition of Ipackchem, Envaplast further enhances Greif’s ability to serve customers across Europe with innovative, high-performance packaging solutions. ... The Valencia-area operation will continue to be led by Joan Oriola Lledó, providing continuity for customers and employees while supporting the integration into Greif’s Customized Polymer Solutions business."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,P&G Announces Fourth Quarter and Fiscal Year 2026 Results | Procter & Gamble Investor Relations,www.pginvestor.com,2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.pginvestor.com/news/news-details/2026/PG-Announces-Fourth-Quarter-and-Fiscal-Year-2026-Results/default.aspx,"“Fiscal 2026 was a year of foundation building while continuing to grow sales and profit and return high levels of cash to shareowners despite a very challenging geopolitical and economic environment,” said Shailesh Jejurikar, President and Chief Executive Officer. “In fiscal 2027, we expect to deliver progress on each of these key measures despite continued volatility. We believe the best path to sustainable, balanced growth is to double down on our strategy and put the consumer first in everything we do. Stronger, integrated execution to delight consumers with superior products at a superior value. We are confident in our plans to accelerate growth from semester-to-semester, and our investments will be funded with a strong productivity program. We are building momentum with consumers, and we are excited about the long-term opportunities ahead.” ... The Company reported fiscal year 2026 net sales of $87.0 billion, an increase of three percent versus the prior year, comprised of a two percent increase due to favorable foreign exchange impacts and a one percent increase from higher pricing. Volume and mix were unchanged versus prior year. Organic sales, which excludes the impacts of foreign exchange and acquisitions and divestitures, increased one percent from higher pricing. ... In June 2025, the Company announced a portfolio and productivity plan to streamline its portfolio and organization to improve its cost structure and invest in growth. The Company expects to incur non-core restructuring costs of approximately $1 to $1.6 billion before-tax over a two-year period. The Company incurred over half of the costs under this plan in fiscal 2026, with the remainder expected in fiscal 2027. ... P&G expects fiscal year 2027 all-in sales growth in the range of one to three percent versus the prior year. The Company also expects organic sales growth in the range of one to three percent versus prior year. Included in this organic sales growth guidance is a headwind of 30 to 50 basis points from brand, product form and go-to-market discontinuations. ... P&G expects fiscal year 2027 diluted net earnings per share growth in the range of one to five percent versus fiscal 2026 GAAP EPS of $6.62. GAAP EPS includes expected non-core restructuring charges of $0.13 to $0.17 per share. P&G expects its fiscal 2027 core earnings per share growth in the range of in-line to three percent versus fiscal 2026 core EPS of $6.89. This outlook equates to a range of $6.89 to $7.11 per share, with a mid-point estimate of $7.00, or an increase of one and a half percent. ... Risks and uncertainties to which our forward-looking statements are subject include, without limitation: (1) the ability to successfully manage global financial risks, including foreign currency fluctuations, changes in global interest rates and rate differentials, currency exchange, pricing controls or tariffs; (2) the ability to successfully manage local, regional or global economic volatility, including reduced market growth rates, and to generate sufficient income and cash flow to allow the Company to effect the expected share repurchases and dividend payments; (3) the ability to successfully manage uncertainties related to changing political and geopolitical conditions and potential implications such as exchange rate fluctuations, market contraction, boycotts, variability and unpredictability in trade relations, sanctions, tariffs or other trade controls; (4) the ability to manage disruptions in credit markets or to our banking partners or changes to our credit rating; (5) the ability to maintain key manufacturing and supply arrangements (including execution of supply chain optimizations and sole supplier and sole manufacturing plant arrangements) and to manage disruption of business due to various factors, including ones outside of our control, such as natural disasters, acts of war or terrorism or disease outbreaks; (6) the ability to successfully manage cost fluctuations and pressures, including prices of commodities and raw materials and costs of labor, transportation, energy, pension and healthcare; (7) the ability to compete with our local and global competitors in new and existing sales channels, including by successfully responding to competitive factors such as prices, promotional incentives and trade terms for products; (8) the ability to manage and maintain key customer relationships; (9) the ability to protect our reputation and brand equity by successfully managing real or perceived issues, including concerns about safety, quality, ingredients, efficacy, packaging content, supply chain practices, social or environmental practices or similar matters that may arise; (10) the ability to successfully manage the financial, legal, reputational and operational risk associated with third-party relationships, such as our suppliers, contract manufacturers, distributors, contractors and external business partners; (11) the ability to rely on and maintain key company and third-party information and operational technology systems, networks and services and maintain the security and functionality of such systems, networks and services and the data contained therein; (12) the ability to successfully manage the demand, supply and operational challenges, as well as governmental responses or mandates, associated with a disease outbreak, including epidemics, pandemics or similar widespread public health concerns; (13) the ability to stay on the leading edge of innovation, obtain necessary intellectual property protections and successfully respond to changing consumer habits, evolving digital marketing and selling platform requirements and technological advances attained by, and patents granted to, competitors; (14) the ability to successfully manage our ongoing acquisition, divestiture and joint venture activities, in each case to achieve the Company’s overall business strategy and financial objectives, without impacting the delivery of base business objectives; (15) the ability to successfully achieve productivity improvements and cost savings and manage ongoing organizational changes while successfully identifying, developing and retaining key employees, including in key growth markets where the availability of skilled or experienced employees may be limited; (16) the ability to successfully manage current and expanding regulatory and legal requirements and matters (including, without limitation, those laws, regulations, policies and related interpretations involving product liability, product and packaging composition, manufacturing processes, intellectual property, labor and employment, antitrust, privacy, cybersecurity, data protection and data transfers, artificial intelligence, tax, the environment, due diligence, risk oversight, accounting and financial reporting) and to resolve new and pending matters within current estimates; (17) the ability to manage changes in applicable tax laws and regulations; and (18) the ability to continue delivering progress towards our environmental sustainability ambitions. ... $250 - $500 million before tax. During the period ended September 30, 2024, the Company completed its limited market portfolio restructuring with the substantial liquidation of its operations in Argentina. In June 2025, the Company announced a portfolio and productivity plan to streamline its portfolio and organization to improve its cost structure and competitiveness. The Company incurred over half of the costs under this plan in fiscal 2026, with the remainder expected to be ... - Glad joint venture agreement: In January 2026, the Glad joint venture agreement between the Company and Clorox expired. Under the terms of the agreement, Clorox purchased the Company’s minority interest in the venture at fair market value for $476 million. This transaction was accounted for as a dissolution of the Glad joint venture business and the Company recorded an after-tax gain of $261 million."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Packaging Solutions prepares for LOUPE Americas - Label and Narrow Web,www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/library/flint-group-packaging-solutions-prepares-for-loupe-americas-2/,"Flint Group Packaging Solutions prepares for LOUPE Americas - Label and Narrow Web ... # Flint Group Packaging Solutions prepares for LOUPE Americas ... L&NW speaks to Anna Niewiadomska and Paulo Vieira about the company's plans for LOUPE Americas and how its meeting market demand. ... Released By Flint ... July 27, 2026 ... Flint Group Packaging Solutions will bring a new identity to the similarly refreshed LOUPE Americas. To learn more about the company’s latest products, L&NW sat down with Anna Niewiadomska, Marketing Manager, Narrow Web, and Paulo Vieira, Global Key Accounts Technical Director & Packaging Coatings Director. ... L&NW: What are your expectations for LOUPE and the new format?AN: The new LOUPE format is exciting and represents a natural progression for the event, building on its proven past success while delivering additional value for visitors. We see it as a great fit for Flint Group Packaging Solutions as a business, as we already operate across labels, flexible packaging, and paper & board. The broader scope simply reflects the reality of many of our customers’ businesses today. Converters and brand owners are seeking new ways to optimize performance and sustainability across their entire portfolio. The expanded LOUPE creates a more relevant environment for holding those conversations and demonstrating how integrated solutions can support them moving forward. For us, LOUPE remains a key platform to engage with customers and partners across North America. It provides an opportunity to show how Flint Group Packaging Solutions supports the industry as a solutions partner rather than solely a supplier – delivering inks, coatings, and digital print technologies alongside value-added programs that improve efficiency, reduce waste, and support regulatory and sustainability goals. The event fosters meaningful discussions on collaboration and innovation. ... L&NW: What products will the company highlight at its LOUPE booth?AN: Our primary focus will always be on inks. Our focus is to present Flint Group Packaging Solutions as an integrated supplier of inks, coatings and digital print solutions. ... As it pertains to inks, the solutions we deliver are integral to achieving high-quality, safe, and more sustainable printing. At LOUPE, we plan to showcase our UV LED technologies across the EkoCure range, alongside our water-based ink systems. Both ranges are designed to help printers improve energy efficiency and reduce their environmental impact while maintaining consistent print quality. We will also highlight our Flexocure LEAP ink series – a food contact material solution for the US market – which helps to simplify regulatory compliance and testing. ... Alongside these inks, we will highlight a selection of our coatings for converters seeking to enhance print with added functionality, protection, or visual impact. Our teams will be ready to discuss technologies that support recyclability and circular packaging goals, such as our Evolution coatings and primers. Our intention is to show how our inks and coatings work together as a complete system for achieving quality, efficiency, and sustainability – rather than as standalone products. ... Rounding out our integrated approach, we will also highlight our Flint Group Digital Xeikon business and digital consumables. Visitors can see demonstrations of three engines running live digital print jobs. ... L&NW: What trends are you seeing with coatings?PV: One of the main shifts we have seen in relation to coatings is the move away from viewing them as a purely decorative finishing step. Increasingly, coatings are recognized as a core strategic component within the overall packaging design and performance architecture, and are considered earlier in the overall development process as converters recognize the influence they can have across everything from recyclability to durability and brand perception. ... Sustainability remains a major driver of this shift. Coatings can play an important role in enabling recyclability by facilitating de-inking and supporting mono-material structures that are simpler to reprocess into new material. They also support the growing demand for functional performance by providing barrier properties, surface protection, and the overall preservation of graphic integrity throughout the value chain. ... L&NW: What are the benefits of your newest coating products?PV: Our coating technologies help converters combine strong visual impact with lasting functional performance. For example, our DecaCode portfolio elevates packaging designs without making them more complex than necessary, avoiding the need for additional laminates or secondary materials. Products can be selected to deliver a range of desired finishes while providing the durability needed to maintain a premium look and feel throughout distribution and handling. ... Consistency is another key benefit as our coatings help preserve color integrity and surface quality from production through to the point of sale or delivery, which is increasingly important in e-commerce-driven supply chains. They also give designers greater creative freedom, enabling distinctive textures and finishes that help products stand out. Importantly, this is delivered with reliable performance across different substrates and print technologies, alongside shorter, more flexible production runs. ... We will also highlight our Evolution range, which includes a caustic-resistant overprint varnish for floatable materials and a de-inking primer for crystallizable PET shrink sleeves. These products simplify recycling and enable greater quantities of material to be reclaimed, thus aligning packaging performance with circular economy requirements."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Nestlé launches €4.9bn Peranel water and beverages business,www.foodnavigator.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.foodnavigator.com/Article/2026/07/23/nestle-launches-49bn-peranel-water-and-beverages-business/,"Nestlé launches €4.9bn Peranel water and beverages businessdefault-output-block.skip-main ... # Nestlé unveils €4.9bn drinks giant Peranel in portfolio shake-up ... ## Nestlé announces new €4.9bn standalone water and premium beverages company, in partnership with Platinum Equity ... - Nestlé and Platinum Equity will create Peranel in 2027 - Peranel combines over 30 beverage brands across 120 countries - The standalone business focuses on water and premium beverages - Nestlé expects €3bn cash proceeds from the €4.9bn transaction - The move supports portfolio simplification and future growth ambitions ... Nestlé has announced the launch of a brand new €4.9bn beverage company named Peranel. ... Created in partnership with global investment firm Platinum Equity, the 50:50 venture will focus on water and premium beverages, with the goal of accelerating growth in the category. ... Spanning more than 30 brands, sold across 120 countries, the newly-created Peranel will be home to major names including S.Pellegrino, Source Perrier, Acqua Panna, and Nestlé Pure Life, alongside premium and functional hydration beverages. ... The move forms part of Nestlé’s wider strategy to simplify its portfolio and focus resources on higher-growth, higher-margin categories. It also marks the latest step in the company’s efforts to reshape its business around a smaller number of core growth platforms. ... As a standalone business, Peranel will focus exclusively on water and premium beverages, giving it the flexibility to invest in its brands and pursue new growth opportunities. The company will also benefit from a dedicated in-house R&D team to support continued product innovation. ... Expected to close in the first half of 2027, the deal values Peranel at €4.9bn and will provide Nestlé with an estimated €3bn in cash, subject to the necessary regulatory and employee approvals. ... The proceeds will provide Nestlé with additional financial flexibility as it continues its programme of portfolio reshaping and investment in priority business areas. ... “By partnering with Platinum Equity, Peranel will be better positioned to execute its strategy with enhanced agility,” says CEO Philipp Navratil. “Through additional focus, it will be well equipped to drive its long-term growth ambitions by strengthening this unique portfolio of international and local brands, with continued investments in innovation, premiumisation, operational excellence and sustainability.” ... Platinum Equity is a US-based firm with approximately $48bn in assets under management, as well as significant experience in corporate carve-outs, business transformations and standalone company creation. ... “We are excited to partner with Nestlé and take this next step together,” says Platinum Equity co-president, Louis Samson. “Our joint venture creates a powerful partnership and a very strong team. We have great respect for Peranel’s brands, the people that bring them to life and the customers and communities they serve. We will leverage our extensive experience in establishing and supporting stand-alone companies to create long-term value.” ... The news comes as Nestlé continues to navigate heavy scrutiny surrounding parts of its water business, including alleged dumping of plastic waste and the use of the term ‘natural mineral water’. ... Headquartered in Paris, Peranel will be led by Muriel Lienau, the current CEO of Nestlé Waters. ... “This announcement marks an important milestone for our teams and an exciting new chapter in the evolution of our business,” says Muriel Lienau. “I am grateful both for the continued support of Nestlé and pleased to be joined by Platinum Equity in our ambitious journey.” ... The creation of Peranel marks a significant milestone in Nestlé’s ongoing portfolio transformation, giving the Swiss food and beverage giant a dedicated vehicle for its waters and premium beverages business, while freeing up capital for future investment. ... As the company refocuses on higher-growth categories, the spotlight will be on whether Peranel can fulfil its potential as a standalone player."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Fluoride Varnish Market to Reach USD 248.1 Million by 2032 at 5.1% CAGR — PW Consulting – News24 Philippines,www.news24.ph (News24 Pinoy),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.news24.ph/biz/82561/,"Fluoride Varnish Market to Reach USD 248.1 Million by 2032 at 5.1% CAGR — PW Consulting – News24 Philippines ... As public- and private-sector actors recalibrate their oral health portfolios, the fluoride varnish market presents a steady, actionable growth story — one that rewards timely strategic moves. PW Consulting’s latest market study, based on a 2025 base year and a detailed historical review from 2020–2025, quantifies that the global market has expanded meaningfully over the past half-decade and is forecast to continue expanding through 2032 at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 5.1% (forecast period 2026–2032). Our bottom-up model anticipates clear upside from product innovation, reimbursement alignment, and broadened points-of-care adoption. This brief preview synthesizes the report’s high-value insights for executives preparing 2026 plans while deliberately withholding the granular segment tables to drive deeper engagement with the full study. Fluoride Varnish Market ... M&A and partnership targeting: We map capability gaps and strategic adjacencies that incumbents and private equity buyers should prioritize to capture share in a moderately concentrated market landscape. ... Regulatory & reimbursement timing: With evolving FDA guidance and existing CPT pathways, timing market entry and labeling claims is a material determinant of 2026 launch success. Our regulatory timelines and reimbursement playbook de-risk product launches. ... The fluoride varnish market is characterized by steady growth driven by preventive-dentistry adoption, greater integration of oral health into primary care, and product innovation. From a baseline reflecting the market’s state as of 2025, the sector is poised to grow at ~5.1% CAGR across the 2026–2032 forecast window. While growth is broad-based, the competitive structure shows a moderate level of concentration: the top three players control approximately half of the market and the top five capture roughly three-fifths, signaling both scale advantages for incumbents and clear room for focused challengers. ... Key demand drivers identified in our research include expanded preventive programs in pediatric and community health settings, clearer reimbursement pathways for topical fluoride application in medical settings, and clinician preference shifts toward multi-functional products (e.g., combined remineralization plus desensitization). On the supply side, manufacturers are competing on formulation science, single-patient packaging innovations and channel reach into non-dental clinical settings. ... A & partnership scanner: A ranked list of strategic targets (by capability and geography), valuation sensitives and integration risk checklists. ... Across incumbents and innovators, recent product approvals and launches during 2025–2026 materially shift the competitive terrain. Key developments we profile in depth include: ... Centrix, Inc. (Shelton, CT) — commercial positioning strengthened by regulatory clearance for its FluoroDose varnish and a differentiated single-patient packaging design. This combination enhances patient safety narratives and supports scalable distribution into pediatric and school-based programs. ... Theodent (New Orleans) — achieved clearance for a fluoride-free professional varnish, representing a category-expanding clinical claim set that could appeal to specific clinician segments and consumer preferences for fluoride alternatives. ... VOCO GmbH (Cuxhaven) — launched a dual-action formulation that pairs conventional fluoride with bioactive crystalline materials, directly targeting longer-term enamel protection and remineralization narratives. ... Kettenbach LP (Germany) — introduced an upgraded varnish formulation with enhanced clinical appeal, reinforcing the importance of iterative product improvements even in mature product classes. ... Strategic implications: These moves highlight three converging competitive themes — formulation differentiation, regulatory claims as a growth lever, and packaging/dispensing formats as distribution accelerants. For incumbents, defending share will require rapid evidence generation and channel expansion. For new entrants, targeted clinical claims and nimble reimbursement strategies can yield disproportionate traction in specialty and non-dental settings. ... A shifting regulatory and reimbursement environment is central to 2026 playbooks. FDA device classification and clearance remain foundational: cavity varnish devices are generally regulated as Class II under the relevant product code, and conformity with updated standards has become a gating factor for market entry. Additionally, recent international standards updates and the transition timelines for declarations of conformity have compressed time-to-market considerations for product teams. ... On the reimbursement front, topical fluoride application in medical settings is increasingly codified: procedural coding now allows qualified non-dental clinicians to be reimbursed for varnish application under defined circumstances. This creates a near-term commercial opportunity to expand into pediatric primary care, community clinics and school-based health programs — provided manufacturers align labeling, training, and payer documentation with coding requirements. ... Engage payers proactively: Build value dossiers and pilot reimbursement agreements tied to performance metrics (reduced referrals, avoided restorative procedures) to secure coverage in new care settings. ... Plan regulatory timelines conservatively: Anticipate standard harmonization windows and plan submissions to avoid last-minute compliance risks. ... Leverage partnership and M&A options: Use partnerships to bridge distribution gaps and consider bolt-on acquisitions to secure key formulation or packaging IP. ... Our full Fluoride Varnish Market study provides the operational models, competitive playbooks, and regulatory roadmaps needed to move from strategy to execution. For executive teams preparing capital allocations, commercial launches, or M&A mandates in 2026, we offer tailored workshops that map your organization’s capabilities against the market opportunities identified in the report and build a prioritized 18-month action plan."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Graphic Packaging introduces inaugural URB product | Packaging Dive,www.packagingdive.com (Katie Pyzyk),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingdive.com/news/graphic-packaging-international-urb-uncoated-recycled-paperboard-waco-texas-production/825042/,"# Graphic Packaging introduces inaugural URB product ... GPI’s mill in Waco, Texas, will produce the new product, with the ability to switch between producing the new URB and the existing CRB. ... Graphic Packaging International's recycled paperboard mill in Waco, Texas, began commercial operations in October 2025 and will begin producing the company's new URB product. Permission granted by Graphic Packaging International ... - Graphic Packaging International announced Monday it is entering the uncoated recycled paperboard market with the introduction of an offering called PaceSetter Ridgeline. - The URB product contains at least 45% postconsumer recycled content and will be manufactured at GPI’s mill in Waco, Texas, which has been commercially operational since October 2025. That mill will be able to switch between existing production of coated recycled paperboard and the new URB based on customer demand, according to a news release. - This offering will help GPI’s recycled paperboard reach new markets, namely industrial applications, according to a statement from President and CEO Robbert Rietbroek. ... Throughout years of planning and construction, GPI had previewed the Waco site as a CRB mill that would meet growing demand for that grade. It introduced PaceSetter Rainier three years ago as a flagship CRB product suitable for packaging applications in healthcare, beauty, confectionery, dry goods and dairy. ... The new PaceSetter Ridgeline product is suitable for folding cartons, laminations, edge protectors, tubes and cores and other specialty purposes, according to the news release. Entering the URB space will allow Graphic Packaging to serve a broader spectrum of paperboard and consumer packaging customers, the company says. ... “We believe the decision to produce URB is due to softer CRB demand and pricing, and potential difficulty filling Waco’s 550k ton CRB capacity,” said Michael Roxland, senior paper and packaging analyst at Truist Securities, in a Monday note to investors. ... “We also believe that there could be some major contract renewals occurring this year which [GPI] was hoping to procure for Waco and this announcement could be an indication that some of them may not come to fruition,” he said. ... Executives at GPI have discussed in recent months the ongoing changes to demand dynamics among fiber grades. “The two grades that really matter most to us, as you know, are recycled and unbleached, because that's what we primarily use. And both of those markets are in good balance,” CEO Robbert Rietbroek said during a May earnings call. ... At that time, he touted PaceSetter Rainier as being cheaper to make than bleached board, adding that “we continue to believe that PaceSetter Rainier will take volume from bleached over time.” While further discussing the balance of supply and demand, Rietbroek noted the company’s numerous CRB closures in recent years, including plants in Tama, Iowa; Middletown, Ohio; East Angus, Quebec; as well as the K3 line in Kalamazoo, Michigan. He also mentioned the sale of a bleached paperboard mill in Augusta, Georgia, to Clearwater Paper. ... “We have been very proactive in our approach to supply, while others have added capacity,” Rietbroek said during the May call. ... GPI began production on its K2 CRB machine at Kalamazoo in 2022. Company executives have repeatedly described Waco as being built to mirror Kalamazoo’s operations. “Waco and Kalamazoo are world-class assets, the highest quality and most efficient recycled paperboard manufacturing facilities in North America,” Rietbroek said during a February earnings call. Still, he noted at the time that “the market has been weak” and GPI hoped for a return to more normalized consumer spending to boost volumes at Waco and Kalamazoo. ... GPI’s foray into the URB space marks a portfolio adjustment at a time when other fiber companies’ executives also have rebalanced their boxboard grades and volumes. Companies continue to raise the issue of a solid bleached sulfate oversupply, with Clearwater Paper announcing in April that it would halve production and cut 20% of employees at its SBS mill in Cypress Bend, Arkansas. ... That followed Smurfit Westrock’s February announcement that it would permanently close an SBS machine at its mill in La Tuque, Quebec. SW disclosed another boxboard shift during an October earnings call, when executives announced a plan to transition more customers away from CRB and toward SBS and coated unbleached kraft. ... Roxland mentioned that GPI entering the URB space could put pressure on Sonoco and Greif, the two largest North American producers of that grade which he said account for approximately 75% of the market. It could also put pressure on pricing. In June, major URB producers announced their second round of price hikes this year — $60 per ton — following an initial wave of announcements in March for $60 to $70 per ton, depending on producer. ... - Graphic Packaging International begins operating Waco mill By Katie Pyzyk• Nov. 4, 2025"
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,The Griff Network awarded US patent for 'Grip N Strip' split-release liner technology - Label and Narrow Web,www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/breaking-news/the-griff-network-awarded-us-patent-for-grip-n-strip-split-release-liner-technology/,"The Griff Network awarded US patent for 'Grip N Strip' split-release liner technology - Label and Narrow Web ... # The Griff Network awarded US patent for ‘Grip N Strip’ split-release liner technology ... The patented design has potential applications in labels, graphics, tapes, and other pressure-sensitive products. ... The Griff Network has been awarded US Patent No. 12,662,819 for its Grip N Strip technology, an integrated split-release liner designed to simplify the application of pressure sensitive materials. ... Originally developed for self-adhered roofing membranes, the patented design incorporates a folded pull tab directly into the split-release liner, allowing users to quickly locate and remove the second liner section without the need for separate pull strips or additional components. According to the company, the design improves installation efficiency while also simplifying liner manufacturing. ... While initially targeting the building products market, Griff Network said the technology has broader potential for pressure sensitive adhesive applications, including labels, graphics, tapes, waterproofing products, vehicle wraps, and other adhesive-backed materials. The patented release liner folding process is also available for licensing. ... “Grip N Strip was developed with one goal in mind—to make installation easier for contractors,” says Alex Phinn, president of The Griff Network. “By integrating the pull tab directly into the release liner, we’ve created a solution that helps installers work faster, reduces frustration on the jobsite, and improves the overall application process.”"
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Packaging Solutions prepares for LOUPE Americas - Label and Narrow Web,www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/library/flint-group-packaging-solutions-prepares-for-loupe-americas/,"Flint Group Packaging Solutions prepares for LOUPE Americas - Label and Narrow Web ... # Flint Group Packaging Solutions prepares for LOUPE Americas Anna Niewiadomska and Paulo Vieira discuss how the rebranded show ideally fits Flint Group Packaging Solutions' diverse portfolio. Released By Flint Group Packaging Solutions ... July 8, 2026 ... Flint Group Packaging Solutions will bring a new identity to the similarly refreshed LOUPE Americas. To learn more about the newest trends and how the company’s latest engineering will stand out to attendees, L&NW sat down with Anna Niewiadomska, Marketing Manager, Narrow Web, and Paulo Vieira, Global Key Accounts Technical Director & Packaging Coatings Director. ... AN: The new LOUPE format is exciting and represents a natural progression for the event, building on its proven past success while delivering additional value for visitors. We see it as a great fit for Flint Group Packaging Solutions as a business, as we already operate across labels, flexible packaging, and paper & board. The broader scope simply reflects the reality of many of our customers’ businesses today. ... The reality is that, for the most part, converters and brand owners are seeking new ways to optimize performance and sustainability across their entire portfolio. The expanded portfolio of LOUPE creates a more relevant environment for holding those conversations and demonstrating how integrated solutions can support them moving forward. ... For us, LOUPE remains a key platform to engage with customers and partners across North America. It provides an important opportunity to demonstrate how Flint Group supports the industry as a solutions partner rather than solely a supplier – delivering inks, coatings, and digital print technologies alongside value-added programs that improve efficiency, reduce waste, and support regulatory and sustainability goals. It is an event that fosters meaningful discussions on collaboration and innovation, and we are very much looking forward to attending again. ... AN: Our primary focus will always be on inks. Our focus is to present Flint Group Packaging Solutions as an integrated supplier of inks, coatings and digital print solutions. ... As it pertains to inks, the solutions we deliver are integral to achieving high-quality, safe, and more sustainable printing. At LOUPE, we plan to showcase our UV LED technologies across the EkoCure range, alongside our water-based ink systems. Both ranges are designed to help printers improve energy efficiency and reduce their environmental impact while maintaining consistent print quality. We will also highlight our Flexocure LEAP ink series – a food contact material solution for the US market – which helps to simplify regulatory compliance and testing. ... Alongside these inks, we will highlight a selection of our coating solutions for converters seeking to enhance their prints with added functionality, protection, or visual impact. Moreover, our teams will be ready to discuss technologies that support recyclability and circular packaging goals, such as our Evolution coatings and primers. Our intention is to show how our ink and coating products work together as a complete system for achieving quality, efficiency, and sustainability, rather than as standalone products. ... And, to round out our unique integrated approach, we will highlight our Flint Group Digital Xeikon business and our digital consumables and engine technology. Visitors to our stand at LOUPE see demonstrations of three state-of-the-art engines running live digital print jobs. ... PV: One of the main shifts we have seen in relation to coatings is the move away from viewing them as a purely decorative finishing step. Increasingly, coatings are recognised as a core strategic component within the overall packaging design and performance architecture, and are considered earlier in the overall development process as converters recognize the influence they can have across everything from recyclability to durability and brand perception. ... Sustainability, as ever, remains a major driver of this move. Coatings can play an important role in enabling recyclability by facilitating de-inking and supporting mono-material structures that are simpler to reprocess into new material. They also support the growing demand for functional performance in packaging by providing barrier properties, surface protection, and the overall preservation of graphic integrity throughout the value chain. ... Furthermore, the impact of the growing complexity of the packaging landscape on the coatings market cannot be ignored. Converters are frequently handling shorter runs and an expanding SKU count. Consistent adhesion and performance across different substrates are becoming core requirements, and this shift has only reinforced the need for a system-based approach in which inks and coatings are developed to work together seamlessly. With digital printing being an important part of the growth in packaging printing technologies when addressing the increase in short runs, customized and with more variable printing, Coatings play an instrumental part in both decoration and protection. Flint Group Packaging Solutions’ Digital Coatings portfolio has been a key area of development and expansion. ... PV: Our coating technologies help converters combine strong visual impact with lasting functional performance. Ranges such as our DecaCode portfolio elevate packaging designs without making them more complex than necessary, avoiding the need for additional laminates or secondary materials. Products can be selected to deliver a range of desired finishes while providing the durability needed to maintain a premium look and feel throughout distribution and handling. ... Consistency is another key benefit of these solutions, as they help preserve color integrity and surface quality from production through to the point of sale or delivery, which is increasingly important in e-commerce-driven supply chains. They also give designers greater creative freedom, enabling distinctive textures and finishes that help products stand out in crowded markets. Importantly, this is delivered with reliable performance across different substrates and print technologies, alongside shorter, more flexible production runs. ... In addition, we intend to highlight the benefits of our Evolution range, which includes a caustic-resistant Overprint Varnish for floatable materials and a De-inking Primer for Crystallisable PET Shrink Sleeves. These products simplify recycling in both PET and HDPE streams, enabling greater quantities of usable material to be reclaimed and aligning packaging performance with circular economy requirements. ... PV: At Flint Group Packaging Solutions, we work closely with customers to understand their specific applications and end-use requirements, ensuring we match them with the right solution. Our expert team considers all aspects, from colour management and performance to sustainability and regulatory compliance, and places a strong emphasis on reducing customer complexity. This approach supports supply security and the ease of job transfers. Our unified organization enables us to combine expertise in inks and coatings and offer a comprehensive portfolio backed by strong technical support. As a result, we can act as a partner to support customers across multiple packaging segments and ensure they achieve consistent, reliable results."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,"Flint to Showcase Inks, Coatings, and Digital Printing Technologies at LOUPE Americas 2026 in the USA - Wedoany",en.wedoany.com,2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.wedoany.com/shortnews/363589.html,"Flint to Showcase Inks, Coatings, and Digital Printing Technologies at LOUPE Americas 2026 in the USA - Wedoany ... Flint to Showcase Inks, Coatings, and Digital Printing Technologies at LOUPE Americas 2026 in the USA ... en.Wedoany.com Reported - Flint Group Packaging Solutions, a UK-based ink and printing materials supplier, has confirmed its participation in the LOUPE Americas exhibition, taking place from September 15 to 17, 2026, in Chicago, USA. The company will showcase inks, coatings, and digital printing technologies from its Narrow Web business unit and its digital printing division, Flint Group Digital Xeikon, at booth 5821. The company states this will be its largest presence at the event to date. ... The company will also showcase Flexocure LEAP traditional UV inks, developed on a new resin platform designed to reduce the risk of photoinitiator migration while ensuring packaging integrity and meeting future regulatory compliance requirements. ... The Narrow Web business unit will highlight the Hydrokett and Hydrofilm water-based ink systems for narrow-web paper and film applications, alongside a range of traditional and digital coatings that enhance functional performance and visual appeal. ... Flint Group Digital Xeikon will conduct live demonstrations of three machines at the booth. The TX500, featuring TITON dry toner technology, is designed for food-safe and durable label production without the need for additional varnishing or lamination steps. The PX3300 HD utilizes a 1200 dpi UV inkjet platform with PantherCure UV inks, reportedly achieving the widest color gamut in CMYK+W mode at a speed of 70 meters per minute. The Ecolyne is a subscription-based digital label press offering a low-risk entry into the label market for commercial printers and converters through a fully managed model. ... Additionally, technical experts from Flint Group Digital Xeikon will be on-site to introduce the IDERA solution for post-print corrugated packaging. IDERA is a single-pass UV inkjet platform specifically designed for high-speed digital printing on corrugated board. Visitors can request printed samples to understand how this platform serves the fastest-growing segment of the digital packaging market. ... Ser van de Graaf, Director of Sales and Marketing for North America at Flint Group Digital Xeikon, noted that converters need technology tailored to their production requirements. The company will conduct live demonstrations of digital innovation technologies throughout the exhibition. He added that the product portfolio covers both dry toner and UV inkjet solutions, supporting a range of applications, capacities, and substrate needs from entry-level production to high-volume label printing, while TITON technology simultaneously achieves the print quality of dry toner and the durability of UV inkjet. ... At the exhibition, Flint Group Packaging Solutions will also demonstrate the FlintLink customer portal, which provides 24/7 access to SDS and other business documents, order management, troubleshooting, and remote technical support. Visitors can also learn about the latest advancements in the VIVO Colour Solutions digital color management platform, which helps printers achieve fast and accurate color matching through end-to-end management. It integrates press return color functionality to simplify ink reuse, aiming to optimize workflows, improve operational efficiency, and reduce ink inventory costs. ... Kenneth Keathley, Director of Narrow Web for North America, stated that the company plans to present the full capabilities of Flint Group Packaging Solutions to attendees of LOUPE Americas 2026. He emphasized that UV, UV LED, water-based, and coating technologies can be seamlessly integrated into existing operations, delivering stable performance, predictable curing results, and support for evolving regulatory compliance requirements. He invited attendees to visit booth 5821 to learn how the company can support their current and future business needs."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,LANXESS Launches Disflamoll Advance,lanxess.com,2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://lanxess.com/en/media/press-releases/2026/08/lanxess-launches-disflamoll-advance,"LANXESS Launches Disflamoll Advance ... # LANXESS Launches Disflamoll Advance Platform for extremely Low TPP Plasticizing Flame Retardants ... - New platform combines regulatory preparedness and proven performance for evolving formulation requirements - First product of the platform designed for polar polymer systems ... CologneAugust 03, 2026 ... Specialty chemicals company LANXESS has launched Disflamoll® Advance, its next-generation platform for plasticizing flame retardants featuring extremely low triphenyl phosphate (TPP) content of less than 0.1 percent. Tailored to diverse applications, it is designed to help manufacturers navigate an increasingly complex regulatory landscape and emerging compliance requirements while maintaining the performance standards customers expect. ... Beyond its extremely low TPP content, Disflamoll® Advance maintains high flame retardancy and strong smoke suppression. Due to its properties, it helps reduce or eliminate antimony trioxide (ATO) in formulations and improves processing efficiency. ... “Disflamoll® Advance helps customers stay ahead of regulatory developments while continuing to achieve outstanding product performance,” said Heiko Tebbe, Head of Application Development for Polymer Additives at LANXESS. “The platform brings together regulatory preparedness, technical performance and sustainability in a flexible portfolio designed to help customers address both current and future market requirements.” ... The first product introduced under the new platform is Disflamoll® Advance OT. It is specifically designed for use in polar polymer systems. Key applications include flexible polyvinyl chloride (PVC) used in flooring, tarpaulins and synthetic leather, insulation foams, thermoplastic polyurethanes (TPU), synthetic rubbers, and cellulose esters. ... Developed to address evolving market, regulatory and sustainability needs, Disflamoll® Advance OT combines extremely low TPP content with the flame-retardant, plasticizing and smoke-suppressing properties customers expect from the Disflamoll brand. ... Disflamoll® Advance OT is available now, with additional solutions planned as the platform expands to address evolving customer, market and regulatory requirements. ... - LANXESS Launches Disflamoll Advance Platform for extremely Low TPP Plasticizing Flame Retardants(PDF, ... 3 KB) ... ### LANXESS Increases Prices for Poly alpha olefin base stocks (PAO) ... ### LANXESS successfully issues €500 million benchmark bond ... Rainier van Roessel re-elected Chairman ... ### LANXESS confirms guidance despite subdued start to the year"
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Wintipak expands aseptic packaging capacity in Halle - IN Food,in-food.co.uk (IN Food Team),2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://in-food.co.uk/wintipak-expands-aseptic-packaging-capacity-in-halle/,"Wintipak expands aseptic packaging capacity in Halle - IN Food ... # Wintipak expands aseptic packaging capacity in Halle ... July 6, 2026 ... Wintipak is expanding aseptic packaging print capacity in Germany’s Halle. The Heidelberg Boardmaster investment supports faster job changes, lower start-up waste, and higher-volume liquid food packaging. #### IN Brief: ... - Wintipak is investing in a Heidelberg Boardmaster inline flexo press at its Halle/Saale operation in Germany. - The press is designed for speeds of up to 600 metres per minute and rapid job changes across aseptic packaging production. - The project supports rising demand for carton-based liquid food packaging with tighter cost, waste, and sustainability requirements. ... Wintipak is expanding its printing capacity for aseptic liquid food packaging with an investment in a Heidelberg Boardmaster inline flexo press at its Halle/Saale site in Germany. ... The investment will increase productivity, add operational flexibility, and support higher production volumes for carton-based aseptic packaging used in liquid food applications. Wintipak supplies aseptic packaging materials for categories including milk, juice, and plant-based drinks, with both blank-fed and roll-fed systems in its wider portfolio. ... Heidelberg’s Boardmaster platform is designed for high-volume folding carton and cartonboard production, with production speeds of up to 600 metres per minute. The system also supports rapid job changes and reduced start-up waste, allowing converters to handle multiple orders per day while limiting material losses at the beginning of each production run. ... The Halle investment also reflects the changing economics of waste. Start-up losses, misregistration, colour adjustment, and changeover inefficiency become material issues when cartonboard volumes are high and input costs remain exposed. Reducing start-up waste can improve production cost while supporting sustainability reporting at a point when packaging material use is under closer scrutiny. ... Packaging regulation is adding pressure to that operating environment. Retailer concern over the PPWR transition has already shown how stock, conformity declarations, PFAS restrictions, and packaging already in circulation can create production and compliance risk. Wintipak’s capacity investment sits on the manufacturing side of the same transition: more sustainable packaging formats still have to be printed, converted, supplied, and filled at industrial speed. ... The project also fits Wintipak’s broader expansion in Halle, where additional capacity is being developed for next-generation aseptic carton packaging. Adding high-speed print capability is a logical part of that build-out, particularly as liquid food manufacturers seek suppliers able to handle volume without losing flexibility. ... Wintipak’s Halle investment shows how packaging sustainability is becoming a factory issue as much as a material issue. The strongest carton concept still needs converting capacity, print reliability, line compatibility, and predictable supply. In aseptic liquid foods, that operational layer will decide how quickly lower-waste packaging ambitions can be translated into filled packs."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Digital Xeikon focusing on North American growth - Label and Narrow Web,www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/exclusives/flint-group-digital-xeikon-focusing-on-north-american-growth/,"Flint Group Digital Xeikon focusing on North American growth - Label and Narrow Web ... # Flint Group Digital Xeikon focusing on North American growth ... The new rebrand is intended to focus on the company’s diverse portfolios that serve a wide range of label and packaging needs. ... on the first North American install of ... As part of its global rebrand, Flint Group Digital Xeikon will continue to promote growth across the globe. Formerly Xeikon, the rebranded digital printing specialist will work closely with Flint Group Packaging Solutions to bring new and innovative solutions to the market. In addition to global growth, the company has its sights set on expansion in North America. ... Currently, Flint Group Digital Xeikon boasts one of the most prominent digital portfolios in the world. Plus, the portfolio is backed by global success. That growth has historically been absent in North America, though. Now, with new hires and a greater synergy with its parent company, Flint Group Digital Xeikon will focus on driving growth in the North American market. ... Flint Group’s recent rebrand to Flint Group Packaging Solutions is intended to focus on the global packaging sector. Within this renewed structure, Flint Group Digital Xeikon will more closely align with its parent company. ... Flint Group Digital Xeikon has made numerous changes to position itself in the North American market. In addition to focusing on its established dry toner and inkjet solutions, the company recently unveiled the Ecolyne – a digital press featuring a subscription-based model to help label converters avoid a significant upfront capital investment. On the personnel side, Robert Welford has taken on the role of president in North America. ... “We want to be more focused on the North American market and bring the culture we have in Europe back here,” says van de Graaf. “We’re going to be more customer friendly and customer oriented, and focus on added value. Customers shouldn’t be saying they’re looking for an inkjet press or a toner press. They should say they’re looking for a label press, let’s talk to Xeikon because they offer UV inkjet, they offer dry toner, and they offer LED cured toner. So, we want to start from a different position.” ... In addition to Welford, Flint Group Digital Xeikon is investing in its entire team in North America. New hires will help the company position itself in the region, especially as Ecolyne targets a different segment of the print space. ... “We have a very competitive press in there that can really bring a lot of growth,” comments van de Graaf. “So, we’re really investing in our employees. We’re putting a lot of effort into training and new marketing campaigns, focusing on different types of customers. We are not just looking for traditional label converters. We’re also seeking commercial printers who want to go into labels, or startups that want to start printing labels because it’s a growth market. We are one of the best hidden gems in this market, and we need to spread the word.” ... Flint Group Digital Xeikon has targeted different employees that can tout the benefits of various technologies – from inkjet and dry toner to software. The company has also installed a new head of global service in order to ensure synergy between the North American and European markets. ... Flint Group Packaging Solutions and Flint Group Digital Xeikon will work in tandem at LOUPE Americas, where a robust product portfolio will be on display. LOUPE Americas takes place September 15-17, 2026, in Rosemont, IL, USA. ... LOUPE, ... to make an impact to show all ... techniques,” remarks van de Graaf ... We’re going to ... “We’re going to show people that Flint Group Packaging Solutions and Flint Group Digital Xeikon are investing in developments – developments in people, in organization, and in products,” he adds.” And I think that’s unique at the moment. Where most people are just standing still or letting people go, we are actively changing and spending money to improve our machines, our people, our portfolio, and our organization.”"
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,"Fluent, Inc. Files Form 8-K with SEC: Company Details, Stock Info, and Key Regulatory Disclosures for 2026 – Minichart",www.minichart.com.sg,2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-18 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.minichart.com.sg/2026/06/18/fluent-inc-files-form-8-k-with-sec-company-details-stock-info-and-key-regulatory-disclosures-for-2026/,"Fluent, Inc. Files Form 8-K with SEC: Company Details, Stock Info, and Key Regulatory Disclosures for 2026 – Minichart ... # Fluent, Inc. Files Form 8-K with SEC: Company Details, Stock Info, and Key Regulatory Disclosures for 2026 ... ## Fluent, Inc. Announces Results of 2026 Annual Meeting of Stockholders ... NEW YORK, June 17, 2026 — Fluent, Inc. (NASDAQ: FLNT), a leading provider in the advertising services sector, has announced the detailed results of its 2026 Annual Meeting of Stockholders. The meeting was held virtually, with an impressive turnout: 24,933,091 shares were represented in person or by proxy out of a total 29,815,712 shares outstanding and eligible to vote as of the record date (April 23, 2026). ... Key Points from the 2026 Annual Meeting ... - Directors Elected: All seven nominees for director were elected to serve until the 2027 Annual Meeting or until their successors are duly elected and qualified. This signals stability in leadership and ongoing confidence in the Company’s strategic direction. ... - Say-on-Pay Approved: The advisory vote to approve executive compensation (“Say-on-Pay” for 2025) passed with a substantial majority, reflecting broad shareholder support for the Company’s executive pay practices. ... - Auditor Ratified: Grant Thornton LLP was ratified as the independent registered public accounting firm for the fiscal year ending December 31, 2026. ... - Approval of Warrants: Stockholders approved, for purposes of complying with Nasdaq Listing Rules 5635(b) and 5635(c), the issuance of pre-funded warrants to certain directors and/or officers under securities purchase agreements dated May 15, 2025 and August 19, 2025. This also includes the shares issuable upon exercise of those warrants. ... - Equity Incentive Plan Amended: The 2022 Omnibus Equity Incentive Plan was amended to increase the number of reserved shares from 3,666,666 to 5,566,666. This provides greater flexibility for future equity compensation, which could be used to attract, retain, and incentivize key personnel. ... - Adjournment Proposal: A proposal to adjourn the meeting, if necessary, to solicit additional proxies in favor of the above proposals was also approved, though it was not required for this meeting. ... Approval of Pre-Funded Warrants (May 15, 20 ... 5 Agreements): ... Pre-Fund ... 2025 Agreements): ... Equity Incentive Plan Amendment (Increase to 5,566,666 Shares): ... ,728,486 ... 1,365,509 ... Abstain: 8,983 ... Broker Non-Vote: 3,830,113 ... ### Key Shareholder Considerations and Potential Price Sensitivity ... - Approval of Pre-Funded Warrants to Insiders: The approval of pre-funded warrants issued to directors and/or officers could be price-sensitive. This action increases potential dilution but also aligns management incentives with shareholder interests. Investors should monitor any subsequent insider transactions or warrant exercises for impact on share count and market sentiment. ... - Equity Plan Expansion: The increase in the equity incentive plan pool signals an intention to grant more stock-based compensation, which may dilute existing shareholders but also supports attracting and retaining key talent in a competitive sector. ... - Strong Shareholder Support: The high level of support for all proposals, particularly the Say-on-Pay and board elections, reflects confidence in the Company’s leadership and strategy. This may be interpreted positively by the market. ... - No Indication of Emerging Growth Company Status: Fluent, Inc. indicated it does not qualify as an Emerging Growth Company, signaling maturity in its public company compliance obligations. ... The 2026 Annual Meeting of Fluent, Inc. resulted in the approval of all key management proposals, including director elections, executive compensation, auditor ratification, and important equity-related authorizations. The potential for future share dilution due to new warrants and an expanded equity plan is noteworthy for investors and could impact share value, particularly as awards are granted or warrants exercised. The strong shareholder support overall underscores confidence in management and the Company’s strategic direction."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Digital Xeikon unveils Ecolyne ahead of Innovation Days - Label and Narrow Web,www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/exclusives/flint-group-digital-xeikon-unveils-ecolyne-ahead-of-innovation-days/,"Flint Group Digital Xeikon unveils Ecolyne ahead of Innovation Days - Label and Narrow Web ... # Flint Group Digital Xeikon unveils Ecolyne ahead of Innovation Days ... The digital printing specialist debuted the press at the company’s North American headquarters in Elgin, IL, on June 16. ... On June 16, 2026, Flint Group Digital Xeikon unveiled a new concept for digital printing adoption with the launch of Ecolyne. This digital printing platform has been engineered to meet demand for shorter runs, faster turnaround times, and greater production flexibility – at an affordable cost. ... Now available to the North American market, Flint Group Digital Xeikon originally launched the press in the Asia-Pacific market in 2025. The press features a subscription-based model to help label converters avoid a significant upfront capital investment. Converters have the option of purchasing or leasing the entry-level digital press. ... As part of the event, Flint Group Digital Xeikon welcomed in Thunderbird Molding’s Mike Vicino, who touted the benefits of the new press. Thunderbird Molding marks the first North American installation of Ecolyne. ... “When commercial printers tell us ... are interested in the label market, we ... don’t want ... add complexity to an operation that’s running well or get locked into a technology decision they might regret in two years,” explained Walter Benz, president, ... Group Digital Solutions ... yne is an entry-level industrial press. The customer does not have to buy it, although they can. ... With this model, customers do not have to purchase or own the press. Instead, they can access digital label printing capacity through a fixed monthly fee, giving them a predictable cost structure. Flint Group Digital Xeikon manages the installation, service, and uptime of the Ecolyne system. According to the company, this strategy enables customers to focus on production and business growth rather than equipment ownership and maintenance. ... “We have very high expectations for the coming months,” said Ser van de Graaf, sales and marketing director, Flint Group Digital Xeikon. “The Ecolyne features an easy setup and easy learning curve. It’s proven technology at a very affordable price for a model where you don’t have to make a capital investment.” ... Since digital printing continues as one of the most prominent trends in label printing, Flint Group Digital Xeikon sought to increase adoption – with affordability in mind. Ecolyne features a 330mm web width and runs at 25 m/m printing speeds, all while providing 1200 dpi resolution. Flint Group Digital Xeikon touts the press’ ability to run substrates from coated or uncoated paper to PP (white or clear), PET and metallized films. Ecolyne also boasts a food-safe dry toner system. The Ecolyne press is available in both a 4-color (CMYK) and 5-color (CMYK+white) configuration. ... Under the theme, “Print. Smarter. Together.”, Flint Group Digital Xeikon hosted Innovation Days in 2026. Following the launch of Ecolyne on June 16, the company welcomed attendees for two more days of knowledge sharing, live demonstrations, and networking on June 17-18. ... Innovation Days also allows the company to highlight its rebrand. Flint Group and Xeikon have evolved to Flint Group Packaging Solutions and Flint Group Digital Xeikon, respectively. ... “This is a big step for us,” stated Benz. “And there will be no change for our customers. Our products, competencies, and commitment remains. We now consider ourselves a global company, and we can combine our strengths within this one company.” ... Flint Group Digital Xeikon is providing live demonstrations of the PX3300HD press, as well as its patented Titon technology. Company experts are on-hand to deliver key insights into UV inkjet technology, market variations, and value-added applications. ... The North American edition of Innovation Days comes one week after the European version took place in Lier, Belgium, at the company’s headquarters. “It was an exciting week for us in Belgium, meeting a lot of customers, stakeholders, and partners,” noted Benz. “ These events allow us to have a lot of valuable conversations, and there is always an opportunity to learn, especially about what the demands are of our customers. This is why these kinds of events are so invaluable.” ... Flint Group Digital Xeikon also brought in two keynote speakers to the Chicago Innovation Center. Marco Boer, vice president at I.T. Strategies, is speaking on label printing market trends and the importance of evolving business models for industry growth. Meanwhile, Flint Group Digital Xeikon’s Jeroen Van Bauwel is providing a deep dive into security print elements, variable data, and food safety in the printing industry, as well as how digital printing will meet these demands."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Polyart Group acquires Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd - Polyart,www.polyart.com (Polyart),2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.polyart.com/polyart-group-acquires-glatfelter-caerphilly-ltd/,"Polyart Group acquires Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd - Polyart ... # Polyart Group acquires Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd ... ## Polyart Group acquires Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd, strengthening its leadership in premium and sustainable label solutions ... The new UK-based entity will be named Polyart Metallised UK Ltd ... June 12, 2026 — Polyart Group, part of Prudentia Capital, is pleased to announce the successful acquisition of Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd from Magnera Corporation. This strategic move further establishes Polyart Group as a major player in the high-value, premium label market. ... About Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd Based in Caerphilly, Wales (UK), near Cardiff, Glatfelter Caerphilly Ltd employs 44 people and is recognized as a leading manufacturer of metallised facestock papers for pressure-sensitive label applications."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group wins FIA UK gold award for TerraCode Bio ink range - Label and Narrow Web,www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/breaking-news/flint-group-wins-fia-uk-gold-award-for-terracode-bio-ink-range/,"Flint Group wins FIA UK gold award for TerraCode Bio ink range - Label and Narrow Web ... # Flint Group wins FIA UK gold award for TerraCode Bio ink range ... The bio-renewable water-based inks are recognized for combining sustainability gains with high-performance flexo printing. ... June 15, ... Flint Group Packaging Solutions has received a gold award in the Technical Innovation (Supplier) category at the 2026 Flexographic Industry Association (FIA UK) Awards for its TerraCode Bio range of bio-renewable inks. ... Presented at the June 11 ceremony, the award recognizes TerraCode Bio for delivering both environmental and performance benefits. The water-based ink system is formulated with up to 90% bio-renewable and recycled materials and is reported to achieve CO₂ reductions of up to 25% compared to conventional alternatives. ... Designed for applications including corrugated packaging, industrial bags and sacks, food service packaging, and film, the ink range is engineered to match the performance of traditional water-based systems. Flint Group notes that the formulation supports high press speeds and consistent print quality, enabling converters to adopt more sustainable materials without disrupting production. ... The technology has already gained traction across Europe, particularly in the post-print corrugated segment, where it has outperformed traditional extender systems. According to Flint Group, customers have reported a smooth transition with no measurable impact on throughput, alongside improved environmental performance. ... “TerraCode Bio was developed to address a clear challenge facing printers today: how to reduce environmental impact without adding risk or complexity into the pressroom,” says Paul Winstanley, vice president of technology and product management at Flint Group Packaging Solutions. “This recognition reflects the strength of the technology in both performance and carbon reduction.” ... The award highlights ongoing innovation in ink formulation, as suppliers work to align sustainability goals with the operational demands of high-speed flexographic printing."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Web Offset Expands European Capabilities - Ink World magazine,www.inkworldmagazine.com,2026-06-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.inkworldmagazine.com/breaking-news/flint-group-web-offset-expands-european-capabilities/,"Flint Group Web Offset Expands European Capabilities - Ink World magazine ... # Flint Group Web Offset Expands European Capabilities ... A €2 million investment in its Frankfurt facility will help support multiple product streams. ... Flint Group Web Offset has strengthened its European manufacturing network with a €2 million investment in its Frankfurt [Frankfurt/Main] facility in Germany. ... Operational since January 2026, the upgraded site has been transformed into a state-of-the-art hybrid manufacturing platform designed to support multiple product streams and meet the evolving needs of the web offset market. ... David Fotheringham, Vice President Sales & Service, Global Web Offset, said: “Our additional investment in Frankfurt represents another important step in our long-term strategy to strengthen Flint Group Web Offset’s position across our key markets.” ... This investment includes a newly installed energy-efficient varnish plant, designed to enable more flexible production. The site is supported by a highly experienced, knowledgeable team with deep expertise in both heatset and coldset applications. ... Fotheringham added, “By creating a future-ready, hybrid manufacturing platform, we are ensuring we can respond quickly to changing customer requirements while supporting the industry’s shift toward more sustainable solutions, including the growing demand for mineral oil-free inks. Combined with our experienced team and strong customer focus, this additional investment ensures we are well equipped to support our customers with reliable products, technical expertise, and a consistently high level of service.” ... The Frankfurt facility complements Flint Group Web Offset’s manufacturing site in the Netherlands, providing an agile and resilient supply network across Central and Eastern Europe. The dual-site approach strengthens logistics efficiency and ensures reliable, responsive service for customers throughout the region."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Victory for the Modern Workplace: Flint Avenue Wins Federal Legal Challenge Against DOL Rule - Flint Avenue Marketing,flintavenue.com,2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://flintavenue.com/2026/06/01/victory-for-the-modern-workplace-flint-avenue-wins-federal-legal-challenge-against-dol-rule/,"LUBBOCK, TX : May 29, 2026 : In a landmark conclusion to a multi-year legal battle, Flint Avenue has secured a final victory for workplace flexibility. The U.S. Department of Labor (DOL) has officially withdrawn its appeal of a 2024 summary judgment, cementing a federal court ruling that vacated the controversial 2024 overtime salary-threshold rule. ... This finality brings much-needed clarity to business owners across the nation who have been navigating the shifting sands of federal employment regulations. For Flint Avenue, a marketing clarity and performance consulting firm based in Lubbock, Texas, the win is more than a legal milestone: it is a validation of the modern, flexible work models that define the future of the professional world. ... The legal challenge, Flint Avenue, LLC v. U.S. Department of Labor, centered on a 2024 rule that sought to significantly raise the minimum salary thresholds for ""white-collar"" exemptions under the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). The rule would have moved the goalposts for executive, administrative, and professional employees, forcing businesses to prioritize arbitrary salary levels over actual job duties and performance. ... Flint Avenue argued that the DOL exceeded its statutory authority by effectively making salary the sole determining factor for exemption status. In a modern economy where performance and results matter more than ""hours in a seat,"" such rigid mandates threatened the very flexibility that allows small and mid-sized agencies to thrive. ... ""We believe in a workplace where talent and contribution are the primary metrics of success,"" says Amy Wood, CEO of Flint Avenue. ""The DOL rule attempted to force a one-size-fits-all model onto a diverse business landscape that increasingly relies on remote work, flexible hours, and performance-based compensation. This victory ensures that businesses can continue to innovate how they structure their teams without unnecessary federal overreach."" ... The federal court’s decision to vacate the rule in its entirety: invalidating the July 2024 increase, the planned 2025 hike, and the automatic update mechanism: restores a sense of order. By withdrawing their appeal, the DOL has finally provided the business community with ""clarity and closure."" ... The win is particularly poignant for Flint Avenue, as it aligns with our recent recognition as a ""Culture Champion."" We have long advocated for a workplace that prioritizes the human element of business. Whether we are conducting a Marketing Clarity Audit or managing a complex CRM migration, our focus is always on the people and the performance. ... At Flint Avenue, we help businesses navigate these shifts: not just in the legal realm, but in the marketing landscape as well. Just as we fought for the freedom to manage our team effectively, we help our clients find the freedom to market effectively. ... Flint Avenue is a marketing clarity and performance consulting firm that helps businesses evaluate marketing effectiveness, optimize investments, and make more confident strategic decisions. Through audit-driven insights, consulting, and targeted support services, we bridge the gap between marketing activity and measurable business impact. ... We bring over 11 years of real-world agency and performance evaluation experience to every engagement, combining AI-powered analysis with practical business expertise. From Strategic Marketing Direction to Brand and Customer Experience Consulting, we provide the independent, strategic insight needed to navigate a complex digital world. ... LUBBOCK, TX : May 29, 2026 : In a landmark conclusion to a multi-year legal battle, Flint Avenue has secured a final victory for workplace flexibility. The U.S. Department of Labor (DOL) has officially withdrawn its appeal of a 2024 summary judgment, cementing a federal court ruling that vacated the controversial 2024 overtime salary-threshold rule. ... This finality brings much-needed clarity to business owners across the nation who have been navigating the shifting sands of federal employment regulations. For Flint Avenue, a marketing clarity and performance consulting firm based in Lubbock, Texas, the win is more than a legal milestone: it is a validation of the modern, flexible work models that define the future of the professional world. ... The legal challenge, Flint Avenue, LLC v. U.S. Department of Labor, centered on a 2024 rule that sought to significantly raise the minimum salary thresholds for ""white-collar"" exemptions under the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). The rule would have moved the goalposts for executive, administrative, and professional employees, forcing businesses to prioritize arbitrary salary levels over actual job duties and performance. ... Flint Avenue argued that the DOL exceeded its statutory authority by effectively making salary the sole determining factor for exemption status. In a modern economy where performance and results matter more than ""hours in a seat,"" such rigid mandates threatened the very flexibility that allows small and mid-sized agencies to thrive. ... ""We believe in a workplace where talent and contribution are the primary metrics of success,"" says Amy Wood, CEO of Flint Avenue. ""The DOL rule attempted to force a one-size-fits-all model onto a diverse business landscape that increasingly relies on remote work, flexible hours, and performance-based compensation. This victory ensures that businesses can continue to innovate how they structure their teams without unnecessary federal overreach."" ... At Flint Avenue, our guiding philosophy is Marketing Clarity Before More Marketing Spend. We apply this same rigor to how we run our business. When the DOL rule was first proposed, we saw it as a source of ""regulatory noise"": a complication that added cost without adding value to the employer-employee ... The federal court’s decision to vacate the rule in its entirety: invalidating the July 2024 increase, the planned 2025 hike, and the automatic update mechanism: restores a sense of order. By withdrawing their appeal, the DOL has finally provided the business community with ""clarity and closure."" ... - Freedom to Structure: You can continue to define roles based on job duties and strategic impact rather than being forced into reclassifications based on a federal salary floor. - Budgetary Confidence: The threat of automatic, triennial salary increases has been removed, allowing for more stable long-term financial planning. - Performance Over Presence: The victory protects the ""flexibility"" that modern professionals crave, allowing for work arrangements that suit both the business’s needs and the employee’s lifestyle. ... The win is particularly poignant for Flint Avenue, as it aligns with our recent recognition as a ""Culture Champion."" We have long advocated for a workplace that prioritizes the human element of business. Whether we are conducting a Marketing Clarity Audit or managing a complex CRM migration, our focus is always on the people and the performance. ... At Flint Avenue, we help businesses navigate these shifts: not just in the legal realm, but in the marketing landscape as well. Just as we fought for the freedom to manage our team effectively, we help our clients find the freedom to market effectively. ... Flint Avenue is a marketing clarity and performance consulting firm that helps businesses evaluate marketing effectiveness, optimize investments, and make more confident strategic decisions. Through audit-driven insights, consulting, and targeted support services, we bridge the gap between marketing activity and measurable business impact. ... We bring over 11 years of real-world agency and performance evaluation experience to every engagement, combining AI-powered analysis with practical business expertise. From Strategic Marketing Direction to Brand and Customer Experience Consulting, we provide the independent, strategic insight needed to navigate a complex digital world."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Web Offset Invests in the Americas - Ink World Magazine,www.inkworldmagazine.com,2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.inkworldmagazine.com/breaking-news/flint-group-web-offset-invests-in-the-americas/,"Flint Group Web Offset Invests in the Americas - Ink World magazine ... # Flint Group Web Offset Invests in the Americas ... This new manufacturing investment supports the company’s facility in Elizabethtown, Kentucky. ... Flint Group Web Offset has reaffirmed its commitment to the Americas with a significant investment in its manufacturing facility in Elizabethtown, Kentucky. ... The Elizabethtown plant has been established as the operational hub of Flint Group Web Offset’s operations across North America, Latin America, and the Caribbean. ... A $750,000 investment in varnish manufacturing capabilities has enabled the site to advance its technology offering, supporting the redevelopment of ink systems in line with Flint Group Web Offset’s European heatset portfolio. ... David Fotheringham, Vice President Sales & Service, Global Web Offset, said: “The transformation of our Elizabethtown facility is a key milestone in our long-term strategy for Web Offset. What was once primarily a pigment manufacturing site is now the heartbeat of our operations across the Americas, enabling us to deliver high-performance ink solutions to our customers with speed and consistency.” ... Formerly focused on pigment and colorant production, the facility is now fully aligned with Flint Group’s Web Offset business, supporting a more agile, customer-focused ink manufacturing operation. ... Alongside these technical advancements, Flint Group Web Offset has strengthened its route-to-market strategy, expanding and restructuring its commercial team to deliver a more technically led approach for customers across the region. ... Fotheringham added, “As well as investing in equipment, we’ve been sure to invest in our people, structure, and culture. We have built a stronger, more agile organization with a clear customer focus and a ‘can-do’ mindset. With our enhanced manufacturing capabilities, expanded technical sales team, and strategic location in Kentucky, we are ideally positioned to serve customers across the Americas quickly and cost-effectively. As Flint Group Web Offset, we are building a strong, recognizable brand in the market, and we are here to support our customers’ success today and into the future.” ... The evolution of the Elizabethtown site reflects a broader strategic repositioning of Flint Group Web Offset as a dedicated business unit within Flint Group. ... ### Flint Group Packaging Solutions Will Present at LOUPE Americas ... The company will showcase its largest-ever presence at the event with a combined portfolio of ink, coating, and digital print technologies."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,Flint Group Digital Xeikon Launches Ecolyne Worldwide - Packaging Impressions,www.packagingimpressions.com,2026-05-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingimpressions.com/article/flint-group-digital-xeikon-launches-ecolyne-worldwide/,"Flint Group Digital Xeikon Launches Ecolyne Worldwide - Packaging Impressions ... # Flint Group Digital Xeikon Launches Ecolyne Worldwide ... Flint Group Digital Xeikon announced the worldwide launch of Ecolyne, extending the availability of its subscription-based digital label production model beyond the Asia-Pacific market, where it was first introduced in late 2025. As production capacity expands, the company is now bringing Ecolyne to a broader global audience of converters and commercial printers looking for a more accessible route into digital label production. ... At the heart of Ecolyne is a simple commercial proposition: customers do not purchase or own the press. Instead, they access digital label printing capacity through a fixed monthly fee, giving them a predictable cost structure and avoiding the large upfront capital expenditure often associated with digital label production. Flint Group Digital Xeikon manages the installation, service and uptime of the system, allowing customers to focus on production and business growth rather than equipment ownership and maintenance. ... This model is particularly relevant in a market increasingly shaped by shorter runs, faster turnaround expectations and the need for greater production flexibility. It is also aimed specifically at smaller converters and printers looking to enter digital label production or expand their digital offering without taking on the financial and operational burden of a conventional capital purchase. ... “Ecolyne was developed to answer a very practical market need,” said Frank Jacobs, Senior Product Manager, Flint Group Digital Xeikon. “Many printers want to enter or expand digital label production, but they do not want to tie up capital in ownership from day one. With Ecolyne, they gain access to industrial digital label capacity through a fixed monthly fee, with Xeikon taking responsibility for installation, service and uptime.” ... FG Larsson chose Ecolyne because it combined the toner technology the company preferred with a commercial model that offered cost clarity and reduced financial exposure. Within the first weeks of operation, the company reported improved flexibility, faster responses to customer requests, and a stronger foundation for local short-run food-label production. ... The FG Larsson case reflects the broader role Ecolyne is intended to play in the market: lowering the threshold for digital adoption while maintaining the reliability, compliance and print performance expected from industrial production. Rather than treating digital label printing as an all-or-nothing capital decision, Flint Group Digital Xeikon is positioning Ecolyne as a more flexible commercial path into digital growth. ... Ecolyne is a fully managed dry-toner ... label press designed for food-safe label production and a broad range of mainstream applications. The platform offers 1200 dpi resolution, a 330 mm web width, 25 m/min print speed, and support for a broad range of label substrates with different face stocks. The Ecolyne comes standard with five printing stations, CMYK+White. ... To support the worldwide rollout, Flint Group Digital Xeikon will host two exclusive Ecolyne launch events this June: ... - On 11 June 2026 at Xeikon HQ in Lier, Belgium - On 16 June 2026 in Elgin, Illinois, USA ... Both events will allow customers and prospects to experience the Ecolyne model first-hand and explore how subscription-based digital label capacity can support their growth plans."
FLINT GROUP,,,,Exa,"Fluent, Inc. (FLNT) 10-Q Quarterly Report May 2026",last10k.com,2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://last10k.com/sec-filings/flnt/0001437749-26-016747.htm,"Fluent Announces First Quarter 2026 Financial Results; Commerce Media Solutions Annual Revenue Run Rate Exceeds $110 Million ... | • | Q1 2026 revenue of $44.9 million | | --- | --- | | • | Q1 2026 Commerce Media Solutions revenue grew 104% to $25.9 million, representing 58% of consolidated revenue from $12.7 million or 23% of consolidated revenue in Q1 2025 | | • | Commerce Media Solutions annual revenue run rate now exceeds $110 million, with gross margin of 19% | | • | Expects full year double-digit revenue growth on aggregate continuing business and adjusted EBITDA improvement for 2026 | ... New York, NY – May 13, 2026 – Fluent, Inc. (NASDAQ: FLNT), a commerce media solutions provider, today reported unaudited financial results for the first quarter ended March 31, 2026. ... Don Patrick, Chief Executive Officer of Fluent, commented, “Commerce Media Solutions continued its strong momentum in the first quarter, reaching $25.9 million in revenue — a 104% increase year over year — and representing 58% of total consolidated revenue, compared to 23% in the first quarter of 2025. This marks the second consecutive quarter in which Commerce Media Solutions has exceeded half of our consolidated revenue, underscoring the rapid evolution of our business mix. Total revenue declined 19% year over year, primarily reflecting the loss of revenue from the Call Solutions conveyance in January 2026. Revenue from our aggregate continuing business declined approximately 3% year over year, as Commerce Media Solutions growth largely offset the expected contraction of our owned and operated business. ... ""The sale of Call Solutions earlier this year allows us to focus resources on the Commerce Media Solutions opportunity,"" Mr. Patrick continued. ""In January, we launched with Wyndham Hotels & Resorts, extending our platform into travel and hospitality. In March, we added Squire, an appointment-based platform — reflecting the applicability of our model across transaction-rich environments beyond traditional retail. Our pipeline reflects growing demand across these verticals. ... ""With the visibility we have today, we believe we are well positioned to deliver full-year double-digit consolidated growth on revenue from aggregate continuing businesses and full-year adjusted EBITDA improvement,"" Mr. Patrick concluded. ... | • | Revenue of $44.9 million, a decrease of 19%, compared to $55.2 million in Q1 2025 • Owned and Operated revenue decreased 50% to $15.7 million compared to $31.1 million in Q1 2025, as the Company continued its shift in focus and revenue mix to Commerce Media Solutions • Commerce Media Solutions revenue increased 104% to $25.9 million, compared to $12.7 million in Q1 2025 | ... | --- | --- | | • | Net loss of $5.4 million, or $0.17 per share, compared to a net loss of $8.3 million, or $0.39 per share, for Q1 2025 | ... | • | Gross profit (exclusive of depreciation and amortization) of $10.0 million, a decrease of 12% compared to Q1 2025 and representing 22% of revenue. Commerce Media Solutions reported gross profit (exclusive of depreciation and amortization) of $5.0 million, an increase of 78% over Q1 2025 and representing 19% of revenue for Q1 2026 | ... | • | Media margin of $14.0 million, an increase of 2% compared to Q1 2025 and representing 31% of revenue. Commerce Media Solutions reported media margin of $7.7 million, an increase of 149% over Q1 2025 and representing 30% of revenue for Q1 2026 | ... | • | Adjusted EBITDA loss of $3.6 million, compared to $3.1 million for Q1 2025, and representing 8% of revenue | | • | Adjusted net loss of $5.9 million, or $0.19 per share, compared to $6.7 million, or $0.31 per share, for Q1 2025 | ... Business Outlook & Goals ... | • | Continue to scale and grow Commerce Media Solutions as a percentage of total consolidated revenue; return Commerce Media Solutions gross margins to the mid-twenties. | | --- | --- | | • | Enhance Fluent’s Commerce Media Solutions partnership network by adding top-tier media partners and expanding beyond traditional retail channels and into new verticals including appointment-based platforms, travel, lifestyle, and home services. | | • | Drive consolidated revenue growth and improved profitability. Given current visibility, the Company expects full-year double-digit consolidated growth in revenue on aggregate continuing businesses and improved full-year adjusted EBITDA improvement in 2026. | ... > Ticker: FLNT CIK: 1460329 Form Type: 10-Q Quarterly Report Accession Number: 0001437749-26-016747 Submitted to the SEC: Wed May 13 2026 4:31:24 PM EST Accepted by the SEC: Wed May 13 2026 Period: Tuesday, March 31, 2026 Industry: Advertising"
