ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Taiyang to acquire control of Cold Spray AM company Chaozhuo Hangke,www.metal-am.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.metal-am.com/taiyang-to-acquire-control-of-cold-spray-am-company-chaozhuo-hangke/,"Taiyang to acquire control of Cold Spray AM company Chaozhuo Hangke ... Taiyang Technology will acquire the controlling shares of Cold Spray Additive Manufacturing company Chaozhuo Hangke for approximately $151 million (Courtesy Chaozhuo Hangke) ... Chaozhuo Hangke, a Shanghai STAR Market-listed Cold Spray Additive Manufacturing company based in Xiangyang, China, announced on July 22 that its controlling shareholders have agreed to transfer a 26.58% equity stake, representing 23.8372 million shares, to Taiyang Technology, Shanghai, at RMB 42.80 per share. The transaction is valued at approximately RMB 1.02 billion (approx $151 million). ... Upon completion of the transaction, control of Chaozhuo Hangke will pass from the company’s founding shareholders to Jiang Jiafu and Jiang Shicheng, who control Taiyang Technology. Trading in Chaozhuo Hangke shares resumed following the announcement. ... The change in ownership is said to represent a corporate governance development rather than any indication of changes to the company’s technology, products or commercial activities. Chaozhuo Hangke has not announced any changes to its technology roadmap, customer programmes or qualification activities. The company specialises in Cold Spray Additive Manufacturing and is one of the few public companies focused on the technology. ... It was not confirmed if Taiyang Technology intends to retain Chaozhuo Hangke’s existing management and technical teams, or alter the company’s strategic direction following completion of the acquisition."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,What Did China’s Porcelain Capital Bring to Kuala Lumpur This... - United Daily News,uniteddaily.my (联合日报newsroom),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uniteddaily.my/en/bad22388-8966-4920-b007-b043b2144390,"From July 29th to August 1st, the 25th Malaysia International Architecture, Interior Design and Building Materials Exhibition (ARCHIDEX 2026) was held at the Malaysia International Trade and Exhibition Centre (MITEC) in Kuala Lumpur. This year’s exhibition attracted nearly 900 exhibitors from around the world and about 40,000 professional buyers. Ten key enterprises from Chaozhou, Guangdong made a collective appearance in the form of the “Chaozhou Smart Sanitary Ware Pavilion”, with an exhibition area of more than 200 square meters, becoming one of the most popular zones at the event. The Chaozhou Pavilion showcased a full range of products, including integrated smart toilets, smart bathroom cabinets, water-saving sanitary ware, and shower sets. Among them, several smart toilets are equipped with independently developed high-efficiency water-saving flushing technology, antibacterial seat materials, and a water-electricity separation safety protection system, achieving a high industry standard in both water conservation and safety. ... Particularly notable was the contactless smart toilet brought by Hangpai Sanitary Ware from Chaozhou. Responding to the common issue of low water pressure in old residential buildings and high-rise buildings in Southeast Asia, this product uses “zero water pressure limitation” technology to ensure strong flushing even when water pressure is insufficient. At the same time, its “no power required + dual-mode flushing” design does not require existing circuit modifications and allows flushing simply by hand press or foot kick, greatly lowering installation requirements. The product also features dual separate nozzles for feminine and posterior cleaning, structurally avoiding cross-contamination and supporting a constant temperature hot water connection. According to buyers on site, this local-adapted design precisely addresses the practical needs of Southeast Asian households. ... According to statistics, the Chaozhou Pavilion has received more than 600 buyers from Malaysia, Singapore, Indonesia, Thailand and other countries since its opening. Several companies have reached preliminary cooperation intentions with local distributors. Many buyers commented that Chaozhou’s sanitary ware products offer exceptional cost-effectiveness and are well positioned for the local mid- to high-end home renovation and engineering project market. ... A relevant person in charge of the Chaozhou Ceramics Industry Association said that Malaysia serves as the springboard for Chaozhou sanitary enterprises’ entry into the ASEAN market. As RCEP dividends continue to be realized, demand for smart sanitary ware and green building materials in Southeast Asia is growing rapidly. Leveraging the China Pavilion platform for collective exhibition not only reduces the cost of companies participating independently, but also helps to establish overall brand recognition. ... During the exhibition, the Chaozhou delegation also plans to participate in a number of industry activities, including the ASEAN Real Estate Conference, the China-funded Enterprises Roundtable, and the Construction Technology Industry Exchange Meeting. They will also visit the Federation of Teochew Associations of Malaysia, the Chaozhou Business Federation, and other local Teochew business associations to further connect with ASEAN market resources. ... The Chaozhou Industry and Information Technology Bureau stated that participating companies generally hope to deepen their ties with Malaysia and neighboring markets through this regional professional platform at ARCHIDEX and to establish a broader distribution network. ... Chaozhou is China’s largest production base for sanitary ceramics and is known as the “Porcelain Capital of China.” The city has formed a complete industrial chain covering everything from porcelain clay mining, mold development, ceramic firing to smart electronic control modules, hardware accessories, and final product testing. Data show that Chaozhou’s annual output of smart toilets reaches 6.38 million sets, accounting for one-third of the national total, with output of basic smart toilets making up about half of the country’s production. Currently, there are over 400 smart toilet enterprises in the city with 3C certification—the highest number in the country. Products are exported to more than 160 countries and regions worldwide."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,What Did China’s Porcelain Capital Bring to Kuala Lumpur This... - United Daily News,uniteddaily.my (联合日报newsroom),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uniteddaily.my/index.php/en/bad22388-8966-4920-b007-b043b2144390,"From July 29th to August 1st, the 25th Malaysia International Architecture, Interior Design and Building Materials Exhibition (ARCHIDEX 2026) was held at the Malaysia International Trade and Exhibition Centre (MITEC) in Kuala Lumpur. This year’s exhibition attracted nearly 900 exhibitors from around the world and about 40,000 professional buyers. Ten key enterprises from Chaozhou, Guangdong made a collective appearance in the form of the “Chaozhou Smart Sanitary Ware Pavilion”, with an exhibition area of more than 200 square meters, becoming one of the most popular zones at the event. The Chaozhou Pavilion showcased a full range of products, including integrated smart toilets, smart bathroom cabinets, water-saving sanitary ware, and shower sets. Among them, several smart toilets are equipped with independently developed high-efficiency water-saving flushing technology, antibacterial seat materials, and a water-electricity separation safety protection system, achieving a high industry standard in both water conservation and safety. ... Particularly notable was the contactless smart toilet brought by Hangpai Sanitary Ware from Chaozhou. Responding to the common issue of low water pressure in old residential buildings and high-rise buildings in Southeast Asia, this product uses “zero water pressure limitation” technology to ensure strong flushing even when water pressure is insufficient. At the same time, its “no power required + dual-mode flushing” design does not require existing circuit modifications and allows flushing simply by hand press or foot kick, greatly lowering installation requirements. The product also features dual separate nozzles for feminine and posterior cleaning, structurally avoiding cross-contamination and supporting a constant temperature hot water connection. According to buyers on site, this local-adapted design precisely addresses the practical needs of Southeast Asian households. ... According to statistics, the Chaozhou Pavilion has received more than 600 buyers from Malaysia, Singapore, Indonesia, Thailand and other countries since its opening. Several companies have reached preliminary cooperation intentions with local distributors. Many buyers commented that Chaozhou’s sanitary ware products offer exceptional cost-effectiveness and are well positioned for the local mid- to high-end home renovation and engineering project market. ... A relevant person in charge of the Chaozhou Ceramics Industry Association said that Malaysia serves as the springboard for Chaozhou sanitary enterprises’ entry into the ASEAN market. As RCEP dividends continue to be realized, demand for smart sanitary ware and green building materials in Southeast Asia is growing rapidly. Leveraging the China Pavilion platform for collective exhibition not only reduces the cost of companies participating independently, but also helps to establish overall brand recognition. ... During the exhibition, the Chaozhou delegation also plans to participate in a number of industry activities, including the ASEAN Real Estate Conference, the China-funded Enterprises Roundtable, and the Construction Technology Industry Exchange Meeting. They will also visit the Federation of Teochew Associations of Malaysia, the Chaozhou Business Federation, and other local Teochew business associations to further connect with ASEAN market resources. ... The Chaozhou Industry and Information Technology Bureau stated that participating companies generally hope to deepen their ties with Malaysia and neighboring markets through this regional professional platform at ARCHIDEX and to establish a broader distribution network. ... Chaozhou is China’s largest production base for sanitary ceramics and is known as the “Porcelain Capital of China.” The city has formed a complete industrial chain covering everything from porcelain clay mining, mold development, ceramic firing to smart electronic control modules, hardware accessories, and final product testing. Data show that Chaozhou’s annual output of smart toilets reaches 6.38 million sets, accounting for one-third of the national total, with output of basic smart toilets making up about half of the country’s production. Currently, there are over 400 smart toilet enterprises in the city with 3C certification—the highest number in the country. Products are exported to more than 160 countries and regions worldwide."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Xiaomi Backs Battery-Swap Startup But Won't Make EVs - Smarti News,smarti.news,2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://smarti.news/11735/xiaomi-backs-battery-swap-startup,"## Xiaomi-backed Hanxing Venture Capital bought about 23% of Zhejiang Xinglixing, boosting its capital to RMB 130M. The move signals strategic interest in battery swapping, but Xiaomi is unlikely to produce swappable EVs soon. ... Chinese corporate filings show Zhejiang Xinglixing New Energy Technology Co., Ltd has just completed a capital increase and shareholder reshuffle. The new investor is Hanxing Venture Capital, a Xiaomi-backed fund, which lifted the firm's registered capital from RMB 100 million to RMB 130 million (about $14.8M to $19.3M). After the deal, Hanxing holds roughly 23% of the company — Xiaomi's first disclosed move into the battery-swapping space. ... Zhejiang Xinglixing is a very new regional startup, established earlier this year. Its stated business scope includes battery swap equipment, power batteries, station operations, and battery asset management. In short, it aims to operate and service battery swap stations rather than invent next-generation cell chemistry or pack designs. ... - Capital raised: RMB 100M -> RMB 130M - Hanxing (Xiaomi-backed) stake: ~23% - Company focus: swap equipment, station ops, battery asset management ... This investment should not be read as Xiaomi preparing to launch a swappable-battery car tomorrow. Xiaomi only recently revealed its SkyNomad EREV duo and is still building manufacturing and supply-chain capabilities for its current models. Zhejiang Xinglixing operates regionally and appears to be aimed at delivering services and deploying existing swap technologies rather than producing a proprietary, large-scale battery-swap solution. ... Strategically, the move looks like option-keeping: Xiaomi gains visibility into battery-swap operations and infrastructure without committing to heavy capital investment in manufacturing or building a national swap network. ... Battery swapping is dominated by incumbents such as NIO, SAIC and CATL. NIO in particular has aggressively expanded its swap network and aims to keep growing. For a newcomer like Xiaomi, catching up would require massive investment in stations, standardization and logistics — not just a minority stake in a regional operator. ... In the near term, expect Xiaomi to treat this as a strategic foothold: monitor technology, understand station operations and keep future product options open. Whether Xiaomi evolves from investor to full competitor in battery-swap infrastructure will depend on market economics, standardization across EV manufacturers and the pace of consumer adoption of swapping versus fast charging. ... For car and EV enthusiasts, the takeaway is clear: Xiaomi is exploring the ecosystem, but it is not yet a player in large-scale battery-swapping or a threat to established swap networks."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Philips expands Malaysia’s presence as connected security gains ground in smart home sector,focusmalaysia.my (FocusM),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://focusmalaysia.my/philips-expands-malaysias-presence-as-connected-security-gains-ground-in-smart-home-sector/,"Philips expands Malaysia’s presence as connected security gains ground in smart home sector ... # Philips expands Malaysia’s presence as connected security gains ground in smart home sector ... PHILIPS smart lock is making a deeper push into Malaysia as demand for connected security technologies accelerates, driven by changing expectations around how homes are designed, managed and secured. ... The roll-out of Philips smart lock 902MFVP and 720FVP at ARCHIDEX 2026 – an architecture and interior design showcase happening at MITEC Kuala Lumpur from tomorrow (July 29) to Aug 1 – marks a strategic move to strengthen the brand’s presence in Malaysia’s growing smart home sector. ... The expansion is supported by CONEX, Philips brand licensee for smart locks which combines Philips’ global brand equity with its own capabilities in smart access technology, product development and local market execution. ... Beyond introducing two new models, Philips smart lock is responding to changing expectations in residential security where traditional locks are increasingly being replaced by intelligent access systems that offer greater control, identity verification and real-time visibility. ... Malaysia’s adoption of connected home technologies is gaining momentum, supported by digitalisation, urban development and changing expectations among home-owners. ... For Philips smart lock, Malaysia is becoming an increasingly important market within Southeast Asia’s expanding connected living sector. ... The partnership between Philips and CONEX brings together two complementary strengths – Philips’ global brand recognition and CONEX’s expertise in smart access technology, product development and local market requirements. ... Rather than focusing solely on retail distribution, the Dutch multinational technology group is building relationships across the wider property and construction value chain, including developers, architects, interior designers, distributors and system integrators. ... As connected home adoption matures, companies are increasingly investing beyond product development by strengthening user experience, after-sales support and customer engagement to build long-term market confidence. ... “Malaysia is one of the important markets for Philips smart lock in Southeast Asia,” enthused CONEX’s general manager Aaron Ma. ... “Through product innovation, professional installation services and stronger industry partnerships, we hope to enable more Malaysian households to experience the benefits of intelligent home security.” ... With Philips smart lock solutions adopted by more than 2.5 million households worldwide, the brand enters Malaysia with an established international user base and strong consumer familiarity. ... The milestone provides Philips smart lock with additional credibility as it expands into new markets where consumers are transitioning from conventional locking systems towards digitally connected alternatives. ... For Malaysian households, this means access to internationally recognised technology supported by installation expertise, technical assistance and service capabilities tailored to local needs. – July 28, 2026"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,K-SURE Supports Expansion in European Smartphone Market with $100 Million Trade Insurance - The Asia Business Daily,www.asiae.co.kr (Kang Nahum),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2026072810330805872,"K-SURE Supports Expansion in European Smartphone Market with $100 Million Trade Insurance - The Asia Business Daily ... ## Financial Support for Spanish Telecom’s Purchase of Samsung Devices First Application of Reverse Factoring... Reducing Local Buyers’ Burden to Expand Market Share ... Korea Trade Insurance Corporation (K-SURE) will provide trade insurance support worth 100 million dollars (80 million euros) to strengthen the competitiveness of Korean companies in the European smartphone market. ... On July 28, K-SURE announced that it would offer trade insurance worth 100 million dollars to enable a Spanish telecommunications company to secure financing necessary for purchasing Samsung Electronics' mobile devices. ... This support will be provided via a trade insurance-backed method, in which financial institutions extend the payment period for the importer. This approach allows local buyers to reduce liquidity burdens, while ensuring that Korean exporters can stably secure export payments. ... Notably, this is K-SURE’s first case of supporting trade through the “Reverse Factoring” method, which involves securitizing the importer's accounts payable. While previous financial support generally focused on exporters, this initiative aims to strengthen the export competitiveness of Korean companies by supporting the financing needs of overseas buyers. ... K-SURE expects that this financial support will help enhance the local competitiveness of Korean companies in the Spanish smartphone market, where competition with Chinese firms is particularly fierce. ... Youngjin Jang, President of Korea Trade Insurance Corporation, stated, ""This is a case where we have helped boost the overseas competitiveness of our companies through trade insurance,"" adding, ""We will continue to actively support the overseas expansion of Korean companies by providing customized trade insurance for individual export transactions."""
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,AM Best says MAPFRE's Safety Insurance acquisition is strategically compelling - Reinsurance News,www.reinsurancene.ws (Taylor Mixides),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.reinsurancene.ws/am-best-says-mapfres-safety-insurance-acquisition-is-strategically-compelling/,"AM Best says MAPFRE's Safety Insurance acquisition is strategically compelling - Reinsurance News ... # AM Best says MAPFRE’s Safety Insurance acquisition is strategically compelling ... Credit rating agency AM Best has described Spain-based multinational insurance group MAPFRE S.A.’s planned acquisition of Safety Insurance Group, Inc. as strategically compelling, saying the transaction brings together two insurers with similar regional footprints and product offerings while strengthening MAPFRE’s position in Massachusetts and supporting its expansion across the New England region. ... The group’s US subsidiary, MAPFRE U.S.A. Corporation (MAPFRE USA), has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Safety, a property and casualty insurer with a leading market position in Massachusetts and operations in several north-eastern US states. ... Following the announcement, AM Best said the Credit Ratings of MAPFRE’s rated operating subsidiaries remain unchanged. The subsidiaries continue to hold a Financial Strength Rating of A (Excellent) and a Long-Term Issuer Credit Rating of “a+” (Excellent), with stable outlooks. ... The agency stated that the ratings continue to reflect its assessment of MAPFRE’s balance sheet strength as very strong, together with the group’s strong operating performance, favourable business profile and appropriate enterprise risk management. ... AM Best also highlighted MAPFRE’s international scale and diversification, noting its broad product offering, geographical reach, strong franchise and long-standing customer relationships."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,MAPFRE to acquire Safety Insurance for $1.54 billion amid shareholder probe | Insurance Business,www.insurancebusinessmag.com (Jonalyn Cueto),2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.insurancebusinessmag.com/uk/news/mergers-acquisitions/mapfre-to-acquire-safety-insurance-for-1-54-billion-amid-shareholder-probe-583604.aspx,"MAPFRE to acquire Safety Insurance for $1.54 billion amid shareholder probe | Insurance Business ... # MAPFRE to acquire Safety Insurance for $1.54 billion amid shareholder probe ... ### As company reveals financials, deal creates an auto and homeowners leader, but a law firm is already investigating whether board got shareholders a fair price ... MAPFRE has agreed to acquire Massachusetts-based Safety Insurance Group in an all-cash transaction valued at $1.54 billion, one of the Spanish insurer's largest strategic moves in North America - a deal announced alongside stronger first-half earnings but one that has already drawn scrutiny from a shareholder rights law firm questioning whether the price is fair. ... The acquisition is expected to close during the first quarter of 2027, subject to regulatory and shareholder approvals. Once completed, MAPFRE said the combination will create the second-largest private passenger auto insurer in New England and the region's largest homeowners and commercial auto insurer, significantly strengthening its position across the US Northeast. The insurer estimates annual pre-tax synergies of more than $30 million, with full benefits expected within three years, and forecasts the deal will increase group net income by more than 5% after full integration. ... The proposed acquisition has drawn legal scrutiny within days of being announced. Shareholder rights law firm Ademi LLP said it was investigating whether Safety's board of directors fulfilled its fiduciary duties in agreeing to the transaction. The firm said it is examining whether the $105-per-share cash offer provides a fair price to public shareholders and whether provisions in the merger agreement could discourage competing bids by imposing a significant termination penalty. ... Ademi said the investigation concerns potential breaches of fiduciary duty and other possible legal violations but has not alleged wrongdoing by MAPFRE or Safety, ... no court has made any findings regarding the transaction. ... To finance the acquisition, MAPFRE has secured bridge financing that it expects to replace with approximately €700 million of Tier 2 capital instruments, €500 million of senior debt and additional bank financing. The company said the transaction would reduce its Solvency II ratio by about 10 percentage points while remaining comfortably within its target range. ... MAPFRE said the acquisition would reinforce its long-term US growth strategy by combining Safety's underwriting expertise, agency relationships and regional franchise with MAPFRE USA's existing operations, while allowing Safety to continue operating within the group. ... The acquisition was announced alongside MAPFRE's first-half 2026 results, which the insurer said gave it the confidence to pursue the deal. MAPFRE reported net profit of €624 million for the six months ended June 30, up 9.4% from a year earlier, while premiums exceeded €16.1 billion. The group's non-life combined ratio improved to 92.8% from 93.1%, supported by disciplined underwriting, lower catastrophe losses and stronger investment returns. Return on equity reached 12.5%, while shareholders' equity rose to nearly €9.6 billion. ... Group executive chairman Antonio Huertas (pictured) said the first-half results demonstrated the resilience of MAPFRE's diversified business model. ""The diversified business model allows us, with the necessary prudence, to be optimistic for the second half of the year. The operation in the United States will strengthen our leadership position in several states in the Northeast, generating greater value for our clients and shareholders,"" he said. ... North America contributed to that momentum, with profit rising 14.1% to €69 million as the regional combined ratio improved to 94.6% following technical underwriting measures and tariff adjustments implemented in recent years. US operations generated more than €1.1 billion in premiums and €63 million in profit during the first half. ... Elsewhere, Iberia remained the group's largest earnings contributor with profit increasing 16.6% to €279 million, while MAPFRE Re posted a 24.6% increase in profit to €186 million as lower catastrophe losses and stronger investment income supported results. Latin America contributed €218 million despite varying market conditions across the region."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,捷科工具：手握2800万元订单全力冲刺-婺城新闻网,jhwcw.zjol.com.cn,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://jhwcw.zjol.com.cn/wcnews/system/2026/07/24/035257921.shtml,捷科工具：手握2800万元订单全力 ... 刺-婺 ... # 捷科工具：手握2800万元订单全力冲刺 ... 2026-07-24 17:30:39 来源：婺城新闻网作者： 洪珊 ... 眼下，位于婺城智能制造产业园的金华捷科工具有限公司(以下简称“捷科”)生产车间内，各条生产线全速运转，上百名工人正开足马力赶制订单，一派热火朝天的生产景象。 ... “从4月中旬开始，我们就进入了‘连轴转’状态，目前未生产在手订单已超2800万元，在线订单创历史新高。”捷科董事长冯铭望着车间内满负荷运转的产线，语气中既有压力，更透出底气。 ... 这份忙碌，来自市场真切的认可。作为一家专业生产高空安全带、缓冲带、速差器、救生绳、攀岩用品等系列个人安全防护用品的企业，捷科具备完整的产业链，产品主要出口至德国、美国、澳大利亚、巴西等国家和地区，广泛应用于建筑、矿业、电信、消防、交通和应急救援等领域。今年上半年，捷科交出了一份亮眼的成绩单：产值同比增长21%，订单量同比大增超30%，发展势头强劲。 ... 在全球贸易波动的背景下，海运费暴涨、原材料价格上涨等因素给企业带来严峻考验。面对重重挑战，捷科是如何突出重围？答案便是捷科选择了一条更“笨”但也更扎实的路——靠技术和品质说话。 ... “低价竞争的时代结束了，标准才是未来的话语权。”捷科董事长冯铭告诉记者，捷科早在多年前就开始布局全球标准赛道，在国内同行中最早成立CNAS资质的产品检测中心，潜心培养标准专业人才跟踪研究国内外最新行业标准，并深度参与国家标准的修改制定。去年，捷科主导起草的《速差自控器》顺利通过“浙江制造”团体标准技术审查，并于同年发布。其参与制定的《个体防护装备标准化应用指南(2025版)》等5个国标的修制定工作已全部发布执行，公司的速差器、安全绳等多个品类产品被收录其中，为整个行业提供标准化的技术指南。 ... 如今，随着行业的标准越来越严格，这道“先手棋”反而成了企业的“护城河”。“我们的产品性能对标国际顶级品牌，在性价比上更有优势。”冯铭表示，客户不是只看价格，更看重产品的稳定性和企业的持续交付能力。 ... 技术上的长期积淀，最终转化为产品端的硬核竞争力。目前，捷科最受欢迎的产品是其自主研发的防坠速差器——可实现0.17米内极速锁止，4米高度坠落平均作用力从2700公斤降至250公斤，锐减90%，产品寿命提升4.5倍，且仍在不断升级迭代。技术上的持续突破，让捷科在激烈的国际竞争中站稳了脚跟。 ... 此外，精耕细作的展会策略，也是捷科订单量明显增长的主要原因。“今年上半年我们团队几乎没有停过。”冯铭告诉记者，从广交会，到土耳其、墨西哥等国际展会，团队马不停蹄。很多今年落单的新客户，都源于去年展会上的初次接触。“展会的转化周期比较长，但一旦建立起联系，后续的信任成本和沟通成本都会大大降低。”冯铭表示。 ... 深耕海外市场的同时，捷科也在加速拓展国内版图。目前，企业已先后在武汉、青岛、北京等地达成合作。“国内市场的需求正在从‘有’向‘好’转变，这对于我们这样注重品质和技术的企业来说，是一个重要机遇。”冯铭表示。 ... 订单充足，产能也要跟上。今年，捷科租下一处7000平方米的新厂区，规划引入6条全自动化生产线，专门用于速差器生产扩产，首条线预计今年10月安装调试，届时整体产能有望提升5至6倍。 ... 进入7月以来，受欧美暑期长假的影响，新订单有所减少。面对暂时的“淡季”，冯铭反而觉得这是难得的“充电期”，“我们的产品线越来越丰富，接下来我们将加大创新投入，要用更硬的产品和更优的质量，为下一轮爆发做好准备。”
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Landi Renzo's Subsidiary SAFE Sells Canadian IMW Industries for €3.5 Million – ItalWire,italwire.com (ItalWire Editorial),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://italwire.com/2026/07/landi-renzos-subsidiary-safe-sells-canadian-imw-industries-for-e3-5-million/,"Landi Renzo's Subsidiary SAFE Sells Canadian IMW Industries for €3.5 Million – ItalWire ... # Landi Renzo’s Subsidiary SAFE Sells Canadian IMW Industries for €3.5 Million ... Landi Renzo S.p.A., with its headquartered operations in Italy, announced that its subsidiary SAFE S.p.A., known for designing and manufacturing gas compression equipment, has successfully sold 100% of the shares in the Canadian company IMW Industries Ltd. to EcoFusion Energy Holdings Inc.. EcoFusion is based in Vancouver, British Columbia. ... The transaction, valued at €3.5 million, is subject to potential price adjustments upon closing. This sale is part of SAFE’s strategic plan to streamline and optimize its industrial portfolio. For EcoFusion, the acquisition aims to integrate IMW Industries’ manufacturing expertise to enhance its presence in the compressed natural gas (CNG) infrastructure sector. EcoFusion is already active in this field through its subsidiary AltaStream Energy Systems. IMW Industries will continue its current operations and provide manufacturing support to AltaStream’s power generation business. ... - SAFE S.p.A. has sold its entire stake in IMW Industries to Vancouver-based EcoFusion. - The transaction, part of SAFE’s strategic portfolio optimization, is valued at €3.5 million. - EcoFusion plans to leverage IMW’s manufacturing capabilities to bolster its CNG infrastructure operations."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Zhejiang Meida Family Sells Control for 1.29 Billion Yuan,www.newsglobenow.com,2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newsglobenow.com/new402885.html,"Zhejiang Meida Family Sells Control for 1.29 Billion Yuan ... # Zhejiang Meida Family Sells Control for 1.29 Billion Yuan ... NewsGlobeNow Editorial Team 2026-07-21 11:32:36 EDT ## Executive Narrative ... Zhejiang Meida's founding family agreed to sell a 29.99% stake for nearly 1.29 billion yuan as the appliance maker forecast an interim loss. ... Zhejiang Meida founder Xia Zhisheng and his son Xia Ding have agreed to sell a combined 29.99% stake in the integrated-stove maker to Shenzhen Xinglantu for nearly 1.29 billion yuan, transferring control as the listed company faces falling sales and its first projected interim loss. The shares will be transferred at 6.656 yuan each, according to a company announcement. After the transaction, Shenzhen Xinglantu will become Zhejiang Meida's controlling shareholder. Corporate records cited in the source show the buyer was established on July 7, 2026, 10 days before the agreement was signed. Zhejiang Meida shares hit their daily downside limit on July 21, closing at 6.44 yuan, down 10.06% and below the agreed transfer price. Zhang Haizheng committed not to sell the acquired shares for 60 months, not to pledge them for 36 months and not to inject assets into the listed company for 36 months. Zhejiang Meida reported 2025 revenue of 454 million yuan, down 48.24%, while net profit attributable to shareholders fell nearly 90% to 11.54 million yuan. First-quarter 2026 revenue declined another 25.59%, and net profit dropped 62.66%. The company expects a first-half loss of 10 million yuan to 14 million yuan, its first interim loss since listing in 2012. The Xia family received an estimated 794 million yuan in dividends from 2021 through 2025, based on its 52.41% holding, as the company distributed more than 1.5 billion yuan in cash. Industry data from AVC showed China's integrated-stove retail sales fell 43.1% to 9.8 billion yuan in 2025, while unit sales dropped 40.4% to 1.2 million. The source identified Xingshang Innovation, a cross-border e-commerce company associated with the buyer, as having 2025 revenue of 14.17 billion yuan and net profit of 713 million yuan, with operations in more than 100 countries and regions. Zhang plans to use its overseas sales channels to expand Zhejiang Meida's international business, although the source noted that integrated stoves require installation and after-sales service."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,A First in Zhejiang! SINOSURE Provides an “Insurance Safety Net” for Advance Payments on Agricultural Imports,market.tdd-global.com,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://market.tdd-global.com/article-platform-information/a-first-in-zhejiang-sinosure-provides-an-insurance-safety-net-for-advance-payments-on-agricultural-imports.html,"# A First in Zhejiang! SINOSURE Provides an “Insurance Safety Net” for Advance Payments on Agricultural Imports July 13, 2026 Lydodo Highlights at a glance ... Ningbo Lydodo E-Commerce Co., Ltd. has achieved a significant milestone by securing Zhejiang Province’s first advance payment insurance policy for agricultural imports from China Export & Credit Insurance Corporation (SINOSURE). The policy safeguards USD 10 million in import advance payments, expanding policy-based insurance to support imports and bolstering Lydodo's cross-border agricultural procurement efforts. As a subsidiary of leading industrial internet platform operator IBI, Lydodo has long imported bulk commodities like palm oil and peanuts from various regions globally. The insurance addresses key risks such as political instability, payment-before-delivery setups, and limited supplier insights, protecting Lydodo against potential losses due to supplier bankruptcy, civil unrest, or government restrictions in source countries. By leveraging SINOSURE's expertise in credit risk management and global networks, Lydodo enhances its supply chain resilience, strengthens its bargaining power, and is positioned to expand operations with greater confidence. Looking forward, both entities aim to collaborate on innovative solutions to further global agricultural trade expansion. Recently, Ningbo Lydodo E-Commerce Co., Ltd. (“Lydodo”) successfully obtained Zhejiang Province’s first advance payment insurance policy for agricultural imports issued by China Export & Credit Insurance Corporation (“SINOSURE”). The policy provides credit risk protection for USD 10 million in import advance payments. This marks an expansion of policy-based insurance from its traditional role of supporting exports to empowering imports, providing a strong boost to Lydodo’s cross-border procurement operations. As a core subsidiary of IBI, one of China’s leading industrial internet platform operators, Lydodo focuses on the cross-border procurement of bulk agricultural commodities. It has long imported products such as palm oil, peanuts and sesame from Southeast Asia, South America, Central Asia and Africa, with average annual imports exceeding USD 10 million. However, as its import volume continues to grow, associated risks have also increased. Bulk agricultural commodities are generally settled on a “payment before delivery” basis, tying up substantial working capital. Political instability in source countries and frequent adjustments to export policies may also cause supply chain disruptions. In addition, companies often have limited visibility into the operating conditions of overseas suppliers. The risk of advance payments being made without the corresponding goods being delivered has therefore remained a significant concern, placing considerable pressure on the stability of import operations. “After gaining an in-depth understanding of Lydodo’s business model and key risk-control challenges, SINOSURE Ningbo Branch developed a customized insurance solution for us. On the one hand, it assisted us in optimizing contractual terms, improving our receivables management system and screening reliable business partners through its global credit information network, thereby controlling risks at the source. On the other hand, the policy explicitly covers advance payment losses caused by the bankruptcy or payment default of overseas suppliers, as well as war, civil unrest, government expropriation and foreign exchange restrictions in the countries of origin. This has established a robust safeguard for the security of our funds.” The successful issuance of the policy demonstrates how policy-based insurance can significantly enhance enterprises’ bargaining power and supply chain resilience in the international agricultural commodities market. It also provides solid support for Lydodo to further expand its import scale and optimize its global procurement network. Looking ahead, Lydodo will continue working with SINOSURE to explore innovative solutions across broader areas of agricultural imports and exports, advancing into global markets with greater stability and confidence."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,A First in Zhejiang! SINOSURE Provides an “Insurance Safety Net” for Advance Payments on Agricultural Imports,m-alisg.tdd-global.com,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://m-alisg.tdd-global.com/article-platform-information/a-first-in-zhejiang-sinosure-provides-an-insurance-safety-net-for-advance-payments-on-agricultural-imports.html,"# A First in Zhejiang! SINOSURE Provides an “Insurance Safety Net” for Advance Payments on Agricultural Imports ... Ningbo Lydodo E-Commerce Co., Ltd. has achieved a significant milestone by securing Zhejiang Province’s first advance payment insurance policy for agricultural imports from China Export & Credit Insurance Corporation (SINOSURE). The policy safeguards USD 10 million in import advance payments, expanding policy-based insurance to support imports and bolstering Lydodo's cross-border agricultural procurement efforts. As a subsidiary of leading industrial internet platform operator IBI, Lydodo has long imported bulk commodities like palm oil and peanuts from various regions globally. The insurance addresses key risks such as political instability, payment-before-delivery setups, and limited supplier insights, protecting Lydodo against potential losses due to supplier bankruptcy, civil unrest, or government restrictions in source countries. By leveraging SINOSURE's expertise in credit risk management and global networks, Lydodo enhances its supply chain resilience, strengthens its bargaining power, and is positioned to expand operations with greater confidence. Looking forward, both entities aim to collaborate on innovative solutions to further global agricultural trade expansion. ... - A First in Zhejiang! SINOSURE Provides an “Insurance Safety Net” for Advance Payments on Agricultural Imports 375 ... the Vietnam Institute for Green and ... Transformation Development Visits IBI 382"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Tigerking Safe Launches Specialized Multi-Functional Jewelry Safes for B2B Markets,"www.einpresswire.com (NINGBO TIGER KING SAFE CO., LTD.)",2026-07-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.einpresswire.com/article/925388299/tigerking-safe-launches-specialized-multi-functional-jewelry-safes-for-b2b-markets,"announced the global launch of its latest product line: specialized multi-functional jewelry pistol safes. This strategically engineered product category targets the rapidly growing B2B commercial markets, premium hospitality sectors, and international safe distributors. Developed to bridge the gap between heavy-duty secure storage and organized internal layout, these advanced security boxes feature high-density velvet-lined jewelry drawers, adjustable shelving, and dedicated lockable compartments. By seamlessly integrating robust mechanical anti-burglary protection with advanced biometric fingerprint entry, Tigerking’s new line answers a vital market demand for versatile, multi-layered commercial storage solutions that safeguard both delicate luxury valuables and tactical defensive assets in a single footprint. Global Security Industry Outlook and Market Trends The global commercial and residential safe box industry is undergoing a profound structural transformation driven by shifting macroeconomic factors, rising high-net-worth demographics, and rapid technological acceleration. According to recent global security market intelligence, the definition of secure asset management has expanded dramatically beyond traditional bank vaults and basic office cash boxes. Today, commercial enterprises, high-end hospitality chains, boutique luxury retailers, and modern residential estates are demanding active intelligent security solutions that blend seamlessly into connected smart environments. The market is shifting from passive steel storage to proactive, interconnected security nodes. Furthermore, international safe distributors face unprecedented supply chain pressures and a tightening regulatory framework across major Western economies. In regions like North America and Western Europe, there is a heightened commercial emphasis on verified product performance metrics. Buyers are no longer satisfied with uncertified economy safes; instead, they prioritize certified fireproof safe box manufacturers who can guarantee specific performance windows—such as surviving extreme house or building fires—while maintaining structural resistance against sophisticated physical tampering and forced entry. This trend has driven the accelerated obsolescence of low-tier generic suppliers, forcing progressive manufacturers to invest heavily in lean production methodologies, state-of-the-art laboratory testing, and compliance with rigid international testing bodies to secure certifications like CE, SGS, ETL, and ISO9001. Simultaneously, the global surge in the luxury jewelry and timepiece market, coupled with evolving regional laws regarding secure personal asset storage, has created a unique cross-category demand. Premium commercial buyers and affluent property owners refuse to manage cluttered, separate units for different types of valuables. The modern market preference heavily favors consolidated, high-security multi-functional designs that offer tailored interior environments. This macroeconomic shift highlights the strategic importance of Tigerking Safe’s latest product launch, positioning the brand to capture high-margin segments across international wholesale and procurement networks. Tigerking Safe’s Core Competitive Advantages and Manufacturing Power Established in 2000, Tigerking Safe has maintained its global competitive edge by anticipating market demands and anchoring its operations in its massive 38,000 square meter advanced manufacturing facility in Ningbo, China. Strategically situated near major global shipping hubs like the Ningbo and Shanghai ports, the company offers unmatched logistics efficiency and seamless supply chain integration for large-scale international export. Utilizing precision automated laser cutting systems, robotic welding cells, and strict 6S lean production management, Tigerking guarantees unwavering quality and structural integrity across every production run. The foundational strength of Tigerking Safe lies in its comprehensive OEM and ODM customization capability. Supported by over 30 proprietary patents and a seasoned in-house R&D team, Tigerking helps global brands transform conceptual security requirements into market-ready assets. Whether a distributor requires a customized digital safe lock configuration, dual keylock heavy mechanisms, or highly specific biometric sensor integrations, Tigerking delivers flexible manufacturing scale. Backed by elite global credentials including ISO9001, CE, SGS, BSCI, and ETL certifications, the brand stands out as a low-risk, high-value manufacturing partner for major commercial clients worldwide. Versatile Product Application Scenarios The newly introduced specialized multi-functional jewelry safes are specifically engineered to deliver optimal security across diverse commercial and premium environments: ·Luxury Hospitality and Executive Hotels: Modern premium hotels utilize these safes as elite guestroom upgrades, allowing VIP international travelers to securely organize high-value jewelry, luxury watches, and sensitive travel documents with maximum privacy and elegance. ·Commercial Jewelry Boutiques and Retailers: High-end retailers leverage these units for secure back-office or under-counter storage, enabling rapid employee access to premium inventory during business hours while maintaining an impenetrable barrier against smash-and-grab theft. ·Elite Residential Estates and Smart Closets: For the residential market, these safes act as an elegant, high-security centerpieces hidden within master dressing rooms, perfectly matching smart biometric accessibility with premium velvet-lined interior care. Proven Client Track Record and International Case Success Over more than two decades, Tigerking Safe has established a legendary track record as a reliable B2B wholesale partner. A primary example includes a long-term partnership with a premier North American security distributor. Facing intense local competition, the distributor partnered with Tigerking to develop an exclusive line of ETL-certified fireproof gun safes and intelligent digital security boxes. By utilizing Tigerking's lean production scheduling and agile R&D, the client compressed their time-to-market by 35%, achieving record-breaking sales and an expanded market share in their regional territory. Similarly, Tigerking has collaborated with leading hotel supply corporations across Europe and the Asia-Pacific, deploying thousands of electronic digital hotel safes equipped with advanced audit trail systems. These specialized systems allow hotel security management to track opening logs accurately, mitigating liability and enhancing guest trust. These successful international case histories reinforce Tigerking’s market position not merely as a high-capacity factory, but as a strategic business accelerator for global distributors. About Tigerking Safe Founded in 2000, Tigerking Safe is an industry-leading manufacturer and exporter of premium intelligent security solutions, specializing in anti-burglary safes, fireproof safe boxes, commercial hotel safes, and specialized biometric storage. Operating out of an advanced 38,000 m² facility with world-class certifications (ISO9001, ETL, CE, SGS, BSCI), Tigerking Safe delivers unmatched OEM/ODM manufacturing expertise to distributors, wholesalers, and commercial brands worldwide. For more product information, catalog requests, or to view the latest digital sample album, please visit the official corporate portal: https://www.tigerkingsafe.com/ Media Contact: Tigerking Safe Email: sales@tigerkingsafe.com Website: https://www.tigerkingsafe.com/ Corporate Address: NO.96 & 98, Huandao West Road, Daxie Development Zone, Ningbo, Zhejiang, China. # Tigerking Safe Launches Specialized Multi-Functional Jewelry Safes for B2B Markets July 09, 2026, 05:52 GMT"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Kingstone to Launch Proactive Electrical Fire Prevention,www.globenewswire.com (Kingstone Companies),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/07/3323175/0/en/Kingstone-to-Launch-Proactive-Electrical-Fire-Prevention-Program-for-New-York-Policyholders.html,"KINGSTON, N.Y., July 07, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Kingstone Companies, Inc. (Nasdaq: KINS) (“Kingstone” or the “Company”), a regional property and casualty insurance holding company, today announced a new loss-prevention initiative under which its principal operating subsidiary, Kingstone Insurance Company (“KICO”), will provide Ting smart sensors and three years of electrical fire prevention service at no cost to eligible New York homeowners insurance policyholders. The program, enabled through Kingstone’s new partnership with vipHomeLink, a homeowner engagement and prevention platform serving the insurance industry, reflects the Company’s continued focus on proactive risk management and policyholder engagement. ... “Our policyholders trust us to help protect their homes and families, and we take that responsibility very seriously,” said Meryl Golden, President and Chief Executive Officer of Kingstone. “The best claim is the one that never happens, both for the family involved and for the quality of our book of business. By offering Ting at no cost through our partnership with vipHomeLink, we are helping homeowners identify hidden electrical fire hazards before they become devastating losses.” ... The Ting program extends the disciplined approach to risk management that underpins Kingstone’s operating model. Alongside the Company’s focus on risk selection, rate adequacy, and claims execution, proactive loss prevention is intended to help reduce the frequency and severity of avoidable losses over time. Electrical fires and water-related damage are among the most common and costly homeowner perils, and Ting’s electrical fire hazard detection and frozen pipe alerts are designed to help address both. ... Whisker Labs designed ... detect electrical fire hazards ... detect hidden electrical fire hazards that ... originate from incoming ... , plugged-in devices, wiring behind ... , and appliances ... Safety Team works directly with the ... to help resolve the ... power outage and ... pipe risk alerts ... “We’re pleased to welcome Kingstone as a new prevention partner and to support its policyholders,” said Geoff Martin, CEO & Co-Founder of vipHomeLink. “By including Ting in Kingstone’s loss prevention strategy, alongside the vipHome.app experience, we’re able ... provide homeowners with proactive tools, timely reminders, and insights that help them reduce risk and make their homes safer.” ... Kingstone’s Ting program is expected to launch in July 2026. ... Kingstone is a regional property and casualty insurance holding company whose principal operating subsidiaries write business through retail and wholesale agents and brokers. Kingstone delivers tailored homeowners insurance solutions through its sophisticated product suite, Select, supported by a scalable and efficient operating platform that enables the Company to pursue significant market opportunities and strategic expansion. Kingstone was the 11th largest writer of homeowners insurance in New York in 2025 and also writes homeowners coverage in California on a non-admitted basis. ... July 01, 2026 08:30 ET | Source: Kingstone Companies ... Kingstone Announces its 2026/2027 Catastrophe Reinsurance Placement ... KINGSTON, N.Y., July 01, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Kingstone Companies, Inc. (Nasdaq: KINS) (“Kingstone” or the “Company”), a regional property and casualty insurance holding company, today announced... ... June 22, 2026 08:30 ET | Source: Kingstone Companies ... Kingstone Appoints Sylvie Widjaja to Lead California Business ... KINGSTON, N.Y., June 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Kingstone Companies, Inc. (Nasdaq: KINS) (“Kingstone” or the “Company”), a regional property and casualty insurance holding company, today announced..."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,How this second-generation Noida SME is building a global edge in home improvement exports - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Shariq Khan),2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/small-biz/sme-sector/how-this-second-generation-noida-sme-is-building-a-global-edge-in-home-improvement-exports/articleshow/132152207.cms,"As supply chain disruptions, triggered by geopolitical tensions, impact exporters, especially MSMEs in the country, home improvement product manufacturer KSP Inc. is leveraging automation, AI, and an export-first strategy to compete with China and Vietnam. ... Noida-based KSP Inc., a home improvement exporter, has transformed into a system-driven manufacturer by embracing automation and digital upgrades. The company now leverages robotic welding, AI-driven planning, and integrated systems to enhance efficiency and consistency, catering to major global retailers. ... As India's manufacturing sector pushes towards higher-value exports, Noida-based KSP Inc. offers a glimpse of how traditional family-run businesses are reinventing themselves through automation, integrated manufacturing and technology. Built over two generations, this SME(small and medium enterprise), which operates in the home improvement market, has reinvented itself for the digital era by embracing automation and other technical upgrades while staying true to its legacy. Founded in 1987 by Puneet Bery as a traditional export unit, KSP Inc. has now evolved into a more system-driven manufacturing enterprise.A visit to the company’s Noida manufacturing facility offers a glimpse of that strategic shift. Inside its 350,000 sq. ft vertically integrated complex, automated lines produce a wide range of export-bound home improvement goods, from fire pits and fireplace tools to garden décor and storage solutions. It reflects how India’s MSMEs are leveraging automation and integrated operations to cater to some of the largest retailers across North America and Europe. ... Scale, automation, and systemsThat shift is closely tied to the company’s recent growth trajectory. In FY25, KSP reported an annual turnover of Rs 128.9 crore compared to Rs 106.2 crore in FY24, Rs 153.87 crore in FY22, and Rs 104.43 in FY21, as per the company data. “We have delivered an estimated revenue CAGR of 22-25%, with export revenue growing at around a 25-28% CAGR,” says Siddhant Bery, CFA, Head of Strategy at KSP Inc. ... The company, which describes itself as a diversified manufacturer, marketer, and exporter of home improvement goods, claims that its container volumes have grown nearly threefold in the past five years, supported by repeat orders and deeper integration with large global buyers. Today, the company ships roughly 1,200 containers annually; the US accounts for nearly 70% of its exports, while Europe contributes 20-22%, as per data from CRISIL. ... Currently, KSP exports to 12-13 countries, including the US, Canada, the UK, Germany, France, and Australia, and supplies products across all categories to retailers, such as Walmart, Home Depot, Lowe’s, Tesco, and Sainsbury’s. ... The company attributes this scale-up to its early investment in automation. “As part of our long-term strategy to improve efficiency, consistency, and scalability, we have consistently invested in automation, amounting to Rs 30 lakh so far, across critical manufacturing processes,” says Bery. “As a result, our output per worker has improved by 40-50% compared to the pre-automation phase. Defect rates have come down by 25-30%, and turnaround times have improved by 20-25%, allowing us to handle higher volumes without proportional increases in manpower,” he adds. ... , braziers, and torches for outdoor living spaces, as well as bird baths and bird feeders for garden enthusiasts.KSP claims around 75% of its manufacturing and finishing processes are now automated, while assembly lines remain partially automated. This hybrid approach allows for both scale and flexibility, particularly when handling customised orders for global clients, the company says.Beyond physical automation, KSP has also built an internal digital layer that is increasingly driving operational decisions. “We have built in-house systems to digitise and optimise decision-making across production, procurement and inventory,” Bery says, adding that AI-driven scheduling aligns machine loading with order priorities, while procurement systems track raw material trends to optimise buying cycles.”These systems are now beginning to show measurable results in terms of efficiency and working capital for the firm. “Inventory holding has reduced by 10-15%, and on-time delivery has improved by 8-10% through better planning cycles,” he adds, noting that tighter integration between planning and execution has improved predictability across operations.As operations scale, digital systems are becoming central to how the business runs. “ERP layers combined with AI-driven decision systems become critical once you cross a certain scale,” Bery says, pointing to a shift where execution is increasingly system-led rather ... The focus, however, is not on full automation but on intelligent automation, says Bery. “At KSP, AI is being used to enhance efficiency, planning, and quality control, while skilled human expertise continues to play a critical role in manufacturing,” he says.So, despite automation, the company has increased its employee count. “Our workforce has grown from around 350 to 1,100 over the last five years, aligned with strong revenue expansion.Navigating markets, costs, and constraintsThe company’s broader strategy reflects a deliberate shift towards becoming a more reliable and predictable supplier in the global supply chain.“Global customers in the home improvement segment today are looking for consistency, scale, and reliability as much as price competitiveness,” says Khalid Masood, MD, Shalimar Group. He believes manufacturers that combine automation with strong operational systems are better positioned to benefit from supply-chain diversification away from China. India’s advantage no longer lies in low-cost labour alone but increasingly in its ability to deliver quality, compliance, and large-scale production for global markets, he says.In agreement with Masood, Bery says, “We are seeing clear supplier diversification away from China, with India benefiting structurally. Automation is helping us move closer to cost parity, while stronger ESG and traceability standards are improving our positioning with Western buyers.”However, competing globally also exposes structural constraints within India’s manufacturing ecosystem. Masood points out that logistics bottlenecks, infrastructure gaps, and regulatory delays continue to affect competitiveness and must be addressed for more Indian MSMEs to achieve similar export-led growth.“Transit delays have increased by 15-20 days in recent periods, and freight costs have gone up by 20-30% during peak disruptions,” KSP’s Bery says, adding that this has extended the company’s working capital cycle by 10-15 days due to higher in-transit inventory. ... Despite these challenges, the KSP is gradually working towards diversifying its geographic exposure. While the US and Europe remain its core markets, KSP is exploring expansion into Australia and the Middle East, with a medium-term goal of reducing dependence on any single geography, especially after the recent supply chain disruptions due to the geopolitical and trade tensions.Globally, the home improvement market is projected to reach $1,354.48 billion by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 4.07% during 2026-2034, as per Fortune Business Insights, driven by an increasing focus on home organisation, outdoor living, and renovation trends. India’s home improvement market, estimated at Rs 3 lakh crore in 2025, is also growing at about 9-10% annually, according to data from global consulting firm Alvarez & Marsal. This shows the tremendous potential of this market.As global supply chains continue to realign, companies like KSP show how traditional family-run exporters are adapting to a more complex and competitive environment. In many ways, the shift is not just about scale but about building systems that can sustain that scale over time."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Zkseasy Micro Servo Motors Successfully Exported To South Korea, Marking Domestic High-End Micro Servo's Entry Into Global Market - News - Zkseasy Intelligent Technology",www.micro-servo.com,2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.micro-servo.com/news/zkseasy-micro-servo-motors-successfully-export-85575498.html,"Zkseasy Micro Servo Motors Successfully Exported To South Korea, Marking Domestic High-End Micro Servo's Entry Into Global Market - News - Zkseasy Intelligent Technology ... Recently, Shandong Zhongke Siyi Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as ""Zkseasy"") achieved a significant breakthrough in expanding its international market, with its self-developed micro servo motor series successfully entering the South Korean market. This milestone marks a solid step forward in the globalization journey of this national high-tech enterprise based in Jining, Shandong. ... Founded in 2019, Z ... is the National Robot Innovation Center (Jining Base) and a national high-tech enterprise specializing in the R&D, production, and sales of micro servo motors. The company's R&D team is based in Shanghai, its production base is located in Jining, Shandong, and it boasts strong technical expertise-its technical director comes from the Institute of Computing Technology of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, its process team hails from Japan, and its automation team from Taiwan. ... In product development ... seasy has ... critical ""bottleneck"" technologies, achieving ... substitution for micro servo motors ... The company's self-developed 15-flange micro servo motor stands just 15 mm tall and weighs less than 40 grams, yet with a push rod, it can carry a 3 kg load-its price per gram even exceeds that of some rare metals. Currently, Zkse ... 's product portfolio covers over 60 standard and custom micro servo motor models across 15, 25, and 40 flange series, making it the most comprehensive domestic alternative to foreign products ... this field. The company has an automated annual production capacity of 200, ... 0 high-performance servo motors, with its self-developed 25-flange micro servo motor being the ... of its kind in ... . These products are widely applicable in ... Zkseasy's collaboration with the Korean market has a long history. On April 9, 2024, a delegation of eight agents and client representatives from Japan and South Korea visited Zkseasy. The company's general manager accompanied them throughout the visit, providing detailed introductions to product design, production processes, and application scenarios. The delegation highly praised the performance and quality of Zkseasy's products and expressed great anticipation for the company's upcoming new releases. ... On May 31, 2024, a delegation of 11 key executives from renowned Korean companies Mikipulley and LS visited Zkseasy specially to conduct in-depth discussions on cooperation and development in the micro servo motor field. The Korean guests toured the company's production workshops, R&D departments, and quality inspection centers, giving high recognition to Zkseasy's technical capabilities. Both sides expressed a strong willingness to strengthen collaboration, aiming to establish Zkseasy's micro servo motors as a leading brand in Korea's micro servo sector. ... From September 24 to 28, 2024, at the 24th China International Industry Fair, Zkseasy made a striking appearance with its core micro servo products. During the exhibition, Zkseasy successfully attracted a major Korean client, and both parties reached an on-site consensus on agency cooperation and signed an agreement, marking the official international launch of Zkseasy's micro servo products. ... On October 14, 2024, Mr. Sun, founder and chief technical director of Zkseasy, was invited to fly to South Korea to attend a product presentation meeting hosted by Mikipulley. This meeting further implemented the product agency agreement signed at the Shanghai Industry Fair. At the meeting, Mr. Sun analyzed in depth the application prospects of micro servo motors in the medical aesthetics industry, 3C automation, and other fields, tailored to the actual conditions of the Korean market. Both parties also reached multiple consensus items on adjusting product strategies and optimizing product performance according to Korean market demands. ... On April 1, 2025, representatives from Korean companies once again visited the Jining Industrial Technology Research Institute and reached multiple consensus items with Zkseasy's chairman, Sun Hanming, on deepening business cooperation and jointly building the Asia-Pacific market. The clients noted that as a benchmark project nurtured by the municipal research institute, Zkseasy possesses strong technical capabilities and promising product prospects. ... This successful export of micro servo motor products to South Korea is the fruit of Zkseasy's years of technological accumulation and market development. Zkseasy stated that it will continue to uphold the development philosophy of ""innovation-driven, quality-first,"" follow the spirit of ""doing business with the perseverance of the Long March and making products with the dedication of craftsmen,"" and persistently increase R&D investment while enhancing product intelligence and customized service capabilities. In the future, leveraging the Korean market as a springboard, Zkseasy aims to further expand into the Asia-Pacific and global markets, providing superior micro-space servo power solutions to customers worldwide and contributing to the global advancement of China's high-end intelligent manufacturing."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,High-Security Anti-Theft Safes Dominate Southeast Asian Market - TIGERKING,www.tigerkingsafe.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tigerkingsafe.com/news/tiger-king-safe-high-security-anti-theft-safes-dominate-southeast-asian-market-with-premium-quality-and-reliable-service/,"es Dominate Southeast ... # High-Security Anti-Theft Safes Dominate Southeast Asian Market with Premium Quality and Reliable Service ... 2026-07-01 ... Founded in 2000, Ningbo Tiger King Safe Factory is a professional and experienced manufacturer specializing in the research, development, production and sales of high-grade Anti-theft safe s. With more than 26 years of deep cultivation in the security storage equipment industry, the factory has evolved from a traditional production workshop into a modern standardized manufacturing base integrating intelligent production, precise quality inspection and global sales services. Adhering to the core development concept of “Quality First, Technology Empowerment, Service Supreme”, the enterprise has always taken product safety and customer satisfaction as the core development goals, constantly optimizing production processes and upgrading product performance to adapt to the increasingly stringent security needs of the global market, especially the diverse consumption demands of the Southeast Asian market. ... Quality certification is the core foundation of product market competitiveness, and Tiger King Safe has obtained a full set of authoritative international and domestic certifications, laying a solid quality foundation for its popularity in Southeast Asia. The factory has passed the strict ISO9001 international quality management system certification, which standardizes every link from raw material procurement, production processing to finished product inspection, ensuring stable and consistent product quality. In addition, all core products are equipped with CE, UKCA and ETL international safety certifications, fully complying with European, British and American safety standards as well as Southeast Asian regional import and sales specifications. These authoritative qualifications not only verify the excellent quality of Tiger King safes but also eliminate market access barriers, enabling products to smoothly enter mainstream sales channels in various Southeast Asian countries and gain the trust of local regulatory authorities and consumers. ... Behind the excellent product quality is the factory’s advanced production equipment and professional talent team. Ningbo Tiger King Safe Factory has introduced a full set of modern intelligent production equipment, including precision laser cutting machines, automatic welding robots, intelligent spraying production lines and high-precision quality testing instruments. The advanced automated production system effectively improves production efficiency, reduces manual errors, and ensures the accuracy and durability of every safe’s structural components. Meanwhile, the factory has built a first-class professional team covering technology research and development, quality inspection, market sales and after-sales service. The technical team focuses on anti-theft structure optimization and functional innovation, continuously upgrading core anti-theft technologies; the quality inspection team implements full-process tracking and testing to eliminate unqualified products from entering the market; the professional sales team has in-depth insight into the consumption characteristics and market rules of Southeast Asian countries, providing targeted product matching and market solutions for local customers. The perfect combination of advanced equipment and professional talents provides a strong guarantee for product quality and market service. ... Superior anti-theft performance is the key reason why Tiger King safes are widely popular in Southeast Asia. Aiming at the complex security risks in daily use and commercial scenarios, the factory’s products adopt high-strength thickened steel plates, integrated die-casting molding technology and multi-layer anti-prying structural design. Equipped with high-precision anti-theft password locks, intelligent fingerprint recognition systems and anti-violent damage devices, the safes have excellent anti-prying, anti-drilling, anti-smashing and anti-technical unlocking capabilities, reaching industry-leading high anti-theft grades. Whether for storing family valuables such as jewelry, cash and documents, or protecting commercial confidential materials, cash reserves and important office supplies for enterprises and stores, Tiger King safes can provide all-round, reliable safety protection. Compared with ordinary safe products on the Southeast Asian market, its superior anti-theft performance and stable quality make it more competitive in high-end and mid-end markets, winning a large number of repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. ... In addition to superior product quality and performance, comprehensive after-sales service is another core advantage of Tiger King Safe to capture the Southeast Asian market. The factory always adheres to the service tenet of “customer-oriented, full-cycle protection” and provides a one-year free warranty service for all sold products. During the warranty period, any non-human damage and quality problems of the product will be solved with free maintenance, part replacement and technical support by the professional after-sales team. To adapt to the localized development of the Southeast Asian market, the factory has set up localized service outlets and logistics support systems in many Southeast Asian countries, realizing rapid response to customer demands, quick after-sales processing and efficient technical guidance. The perfect after-sales guarantee system eliminates customers’ worries about product use and maintenance, greatly improving customer loyalty and product market reputation. ... Up to now, Ningbo Tiger King Safe Factory’s anti-theft safe products have covered most regions of Southeast Asia, with market share growing year by year, and have become a well-known Chinese security brand in the local market. In the future, the factory will continue to focus on technological innovation and quality upgrading, further optimize product functions for the climatic characteristics, usage scenarios and consumption habits of Southeast Asian countries, improve localized sales and service systems, and bring safer, more intelligent and more cost-effective anti-theft storage solutions for global users."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Kidde Expands Commercial Reach With New Sales Partners -- Security Today,"securitytoday.com (Jesse Jacobs Jun 29, 2026)",2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://securitytoday.com/articles/2026/06/29/kidde-expands-commercial-reach-with-new-sales-partners.aspx,"Kidde Expands Commercial Reach With New Sales Partners -- Security Today ... ### Kidde Expands Commercial Reach With New Sales Partners ... The fire safety brand names regional manufacturer representatives to drive commercial growth in the South and Midwest. ... Fire safety manufacturer Kidde has expanded its commercial market footprint through new partnership agreements with two regional manufacturer representatives. ... Under the new agreements, Hossley Lighting and Power Solutions will represent Kidde and its sister brand, Edwards Signaling, across Texas, Oklahoma, Arkansas, Louisiana and Mississippi. Concurrently, Illinois-based firm The Agency Sales will represent both brands across the Chicagoland and Northwest Indiana markets. ... The dual appointments aim to accelerate the regional growth of both commercial fire safety lines and Edwards Signaling's audible and visual notification systems. Both partnerships took effect earlier this month. ... According to company officials, the choices were driven by the firms' existing market relationships. Hossley brings more than 40 years of electrical industry experience in the South and Southeast, while The Agency Sales, founded in 2019, has quickly established specialized divisions handling electrical and lighting distribution in the Midwest. ... Matt Piotrowski, senior director of U.S. commercial sales for Kidde, said the partnerships align with strategies to expand the company's presence in key regional electrical channels. He noted that the regional expertise and customer networks of both firms make them ideal fits for supporting the commercial product lines. ... Both distributor agencies provide localized access and product support to networks of electrical contractors, engineers, distributors and end users within their respective geographical territories."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,CPHI China 2026: Kingvolt Expands Portfolio & Global Partners,www.kingvolt.com,2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.kingvolt.com/cphi-china-2026-kingvolt-expands-portfolio-global-partners.html,"# CPHI China 2026: Kingvolt Showcases Expanded Product Portfolio and Strengthens Global Partnerships ... At CPHI China 2026, Kingvolt strengthened global partnerships and showcased pharmaceutical intermediates, APIs, and fine chemicals, delivering reliable solutions worldwide. ... 2026-06-26 10:05:11Zhejiang Kingvolt New Material ... CPHI China 2026 was successfully held at the Shanghai New International Expo Centre (SNIEC) from June 16th–18th, 2026. As one of the most influential pharmaceutical industry events in Asia, the exhibition brought together pharmaceutical manufacturers, chemical suppliers, distributors, and industry professionals from around the world. ... As a professional supplier of pharmaceutical intermediates, Zhejiang Kingvolt New Materials participated in the exhibition and welcomed customers and partners from various countries and regions. The event provided an excellent opportunity for face-to-face communication, business development, and strengthening international cooperation. ... During the exhibition, Kingvolt showcased its five major product categories: Pharmaceutical Intermediates, Fine Chemicals, Specialty Chemicals, Basic Chemicals, and Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (APIs). Our flagship product, P-Hydroxybenzaldehyde (PHBA), remained one of the highlights of the exhibition, attracting considerable interest from customers across different markets. ... Meanwhile, newly promoted products such as P-Toluenesulfonic Acid (PTSA), 6-Methyl-5-Hepten-2-One, and 4-Chlorostyrene also drew strong attention from visitors. The expanded product portfolio reflects Kingvolt's continuous efforts to broaden its offerings and provide more comprehensive solutions for customers in the pharmaceutical, agrochemical, and specialty chemical sectors. ... ### 2. Expanding Global Business Opportunities ... The exhibition attracted customers from Asia, the Middle East, Europe, and other international markets. Kingvolt conducted in-depth discussions with both existing partners and new prospects regarding product sourcing, market cooperation, and future development opportunities. ... The positive feedback received during the event further strengthened our confidence in expanding our global presence and building long-term partnerships with customers worldwide. ... These valuable exchanges will help us continuously optimize our products, improve service quality, and better support the evolving needs of the global pharmaceutical and chemical industries. ... Although CPHI China 2026 has come to a successful conclusion, the relationships established and strengthened during the event will continue to grow. Kingvolt sincerely appreciates every customer, partner, and visitor who stopped by our booth and shared valuable insights with us. ... Looking ahead, Zhejiang Kingvolt New Materials Co., Ltd. will continue to uphold its commitment to innovation, quality, and customer satisfaction. We remain dedicated to providing reliable products, professional services, and sustainable value to our global partners. ... Zhejiang Kingvolt New Materials Co., Ltd. is a leading enterprise specializing in the research, development, and production of high-quality chemical products, with a core focus on Sulfonated Intermediates, Pharmaceutical Intermediates and Blowing Agent & Activator and Disinfectants."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"China Fireproof Safe Export Specialist: 38,000m² Factory, CE/ETL/SGS C - TIGERKING",www.tigerkingsafe.com,2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tigerkingsafe.com/news/china-fireproof-safe-export-specialist-38-000m-factory-ce-etl-sgs-certified/,"# China Fireproof Safe Export Specialist: 38,000m² Factory, CE/ETL/SGS Certified 2026-06-25 If You Only Have 30 Seconds ... , and export track record ... - TIGERKING Safe operates a 38,000m² dedicated safe manufacturing facility in Ningbo, Zhejiang — not a shared metal shop — with 23+ years of fireproof safe-specific manufacturing since 2000. - Six international certifications: CE, ETL (Intertek), SGS fire & burglary tested, UL72 fire endurance, ISO 9001, and BSCI — the complete stack that international buyers require. - Strategically located near Shanghai and Ningbo ports — the two largest container ports in the world — for faster logistics and lower inland transportation costs. - Products exported to 50+ countries across North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia Pacific, and South America. ... I have visited safe factories across Zhejiang, Guangdong, and Hebei provinces — ... the correlation between factory size and export ... is unmistakable. Facilities under 5,000m² typically outsource fireproof material pouring, powder coating, ... lock integration — introducing quality variance that becomes visible only when the product reaches the end consumer, thousands of kilometers and 4–8 weeks after it left ... TIGERKING ... m² facility keeps ... in-house: ... fireproof material mixing and pouring, robotic welding, electrostatic powder coating, lock integration and cycling testing, assembly, ... International certification is the currency of trust in the fireproof safe export business. Each certification mark represents months of testing, factory auditing, and ongoing compliance surveillance — and each one opens a specific set of retail and distribution channels in its respective market. ETL Listed Intertek SEMKO SGS Tested Fire & Burglary UL72 Class 350 Fire CE EU Compliance ISO 9001 Quality Mgmt BSCI Social Compliance | Certification | Issuing Body | Covers | Market Benefit | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | ETL Listed | Intertek SEMKO | Electrical safety of locking systems | Required by major US retailers | | SGS Tested | SGS SA, Geneva | Fire & burglary resistance | Recognized in EU, ME, APAC | | UL72 Class 350 | UL Solutions | Fire endurance <177°C internal | Insurance company recognition | | CE Mark | Self-declared + NB | EU health, safety, environment | Mandatory for EU market access | | ISO 9001 | Accredited CB | Quality management system | Prerequisite for tenders | | BSCI | amfori BSCI | Social compliance: labor, safety | Required by European retailers | ... TIGERKING's Ningbo location — Daxie Development Zone, Ningbo, Zhejiang — provides a logistics advantage that directly affects landed cost for international buyers. The factory is approximately 2 hours from Shanghai port (the world's largest container port) and under 1 hour from Ningbo-Zhoushan port (the world's third-largest). This dual-port access means: ... - Container availability: Both Shanghai and Ningbo ports have extensive container availability, reducing the risk of shortages that delay shipments from factories served by smaller ports. - Carrier options: Access to Maersk, MSC, CMA CGM, COSCO, Hapag-Lloyd, ONE — with competitive freight rates through carrier competition. - Lower inland transportation: 2-hour trucking to port versus 8–12 hours for inland factories saves $200–$400 per container — meaningful on 5–10 container orders. - Transit times: 14–18 days to US West Coast, 28–32 days to US East Coast, 25–30 days to Northern Europe, 18–22 days to Middle East. ... ## Global Export Reach: 50 ... Countries Across Six ... Since 2000, TIGERKING Safe has established distribution across North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia Pacific, and South America. This geographic diversity demonstrates that our products meet the different regulatory, electrical, and consumer requirements of multiple markets simultaneously. A factory that exports only to one region has optimized for one set of standards; a factory that exports globally has built the engineering infrastructure to adapt to multiple standards. ... Our company's 23-year history of safe-specific manufacturing means deep institutional knowledge about regional requirements: North American UL/ETL electrical standards, European EN fire and burglary resistance classifications, Middle Eastern SASO conformity requirements, and Asia-Pacific market-specific locking preferences. ... Three factors: (1) 38,000m² vertically integrated facility with all critical processes in-house. (2) Six international certifications — ETL, CE, SGS, UL72, ISO 9001, BSCI — not just a generic claim. (3) 23+ years of safe-specific manufacturing since 2000. Visit our About Us page for complete details. ... Yes — we actively encourage factory visits. Tour our 38,000m² facility, observe production, review QC documentation, and inspect finished products. Located Daxie Development Zone, Ningbo — 2 hours from Shanghai Pudong Airport, 1 hour from Ningbo Lishe Airport."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,ESPOINT Secures Strategic Investment From Fire Safety Specialist Safe Korea,www.kspost.biz,2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.kspost.biz/en-us/articles/2652,"ESPOINT Secures Strategic Investment From Fire Safety Specialist Safe Korea ... ESPOINT Secures Strategic Investment From Fire Safety Specialist Safe Korea ... ## Plans joint efforts to further develop and commercialize a lithium-battery fire prevention solution, “Safe:L” ... Lithium-battery fire prevention solution company ESPOINT (S POINT, CEO Moon Jong-hyuk) said on June 23 that it secured strategic investment from Safe Korea Co., Ltd. (CEO Noh Sang-eun) and signed a business cooperation agreement. ... The investment carries significance in that it went beyond a simple financial stake and reflected that a fire-safety company specializing in the field evaluated ESPOINT’s technology direction and commercialization prospects highly and chose to participate. Through this collaboration, the two sides plan to jointly pursue further development and commercialization of a lithium-battery fire prevention solution. ... As lithium-battery use expands into aviation, logistics, electric vehicles, personal mobility, energy storage systems (ESS), and industrial sites, the need to address abnormal heating and thermal runaway risks in the realm of preemptive management—not post-incident suppression—has also grown. ... The flagship solution Safe:L is a preventive fire safety system that confirms such risk signals early, supports cooling and wetting responses in the stage before a fire, and accumulates response histories as data. It can expand into a range of industry areas where lithium-battery use is increasing, including aircraft cabin environments, logistics, industrial safety, mobility, and ESS. ... Safe Korea said it believes ESPOINT’s preventive approach and the business potential of Safe:L are aligned with these market changes, and therefore participated in the strategic investment. ... Safe Korea Co., Ltd. will take part as a strategic collaboration partner in the process of further developing and commercializing Safe:L based on field experience accumulated in the fire-safety sector and industrial infrastructure. The two sides focus on strengthening product reliability and real-world applicability and securing a practical test-and-validation foundation in the lithium-battery fire prevention market. ... Key areas of cooperation are ▲technical advisory in the fire-safety field ▲test-and-validation collaboration using Safe Korea’s infrastructure ▲collaboration through the industry network and with customer companies of both sides ▲new materials and new technology R&D cooperation ▲joint review of potential new business items in the future, among others. ... Moon Jong-hyuk, CEO of ESPOINT, said, “We sincerely thank you for recognizing ESPOINT’s technology direction and commercialization potential at an early stage as a specialized company in the fire-safety field.” He added, “With this strategic investment as an opportunity, we will work to create practical synergies so that not only ESPOINT can grow, but also Safe Korea can grow together.” ... ESPOINT plans to further strengthen Safe:L’s test-and-validation framework based on strategic cooperation with Safe Korea and to push ahead with product upgrades and expanded application at industrial worksites."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,[Best Brand] Sun Safes eyes global expansion with smart tech - The Korea Herald,www.koreaherald.com (Lee Han-gyoul),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.koreaherald.com/article/10786050,"[Best Brand] Sun Safes eyes global expansion with smart tech - The Korea Herald ... # [Best Brand] Sun Safes eyes global expansion with smart tech ... Sun Safes has secured more than 80 percent of South Korea's safe market, solidifying its position as the industry leader. ... Founded in 1972, Sun Safes has grown into a global safe manufacturer exporting to 100 territories since making its first overseas shipment to Australia in 1976. ... The company was selected as a prestigious, long-standing company by the Ministry of SMEs and Startups in 2020, and it became the first Korean company to obtain key global certifications, such as the Underwriters Laboratories, Japanese Industrial Standards, and the Swedish Fire & Safety Certification. ... Its LuCell was the world’s first safe design to feature a touch lock and tempered glass, and the company was the first in the industry to debut in major department stores such as Lotte, Shinsegae, Hyundai and Galleria. ... Recently, Sun Safe has strengthened its ESG business by introducing a new manufacturing process using pre-coated metal sheets. ... Furthermore, the company is positioning its safes as smart security appliances rather than regular storage cabinets. It launched a global partnership with Samsung’s smart-home platform SmartThings, incorporating IoT into its products. ... In addition, the company partnered with Korea’s three major telecommunications companies SKT, LG U+ and KT, as well as its three major security companies S-1, SK Shieldus, and KT Telecop to release the world’s first camera-equipped safe with Internet of Things functions. ... Sun Safe is also expanding its reach in the global market through top brand suppliers across Asia, Europe, the Americas, Oceania and Africa. In recognition of this achievement, the brand won the first Korea’s 100-year Company award, certified by the Ministry of SMEs and Startups, in 2024. ... “We will continue our growth in the global market as a leading safe company by expanding our safes to include smartphone connectivity and monitoring environments,” said Sun Safes CEO Kim Yung-sook."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Brembo, Ningbo SAFE Brakes Sign India ABS JV For India - Production In Pune - DriveSpark News",www.drivespark.com (Dennis Abraham James),2026-06-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.drivespark.com/two-wheelers/2026/brembo-ningbo-safe-brakes-sign-abs-joint-venture-for-india-086611.html,"Brembo, Ningbo SAFE Brakes Sign India ABS JV For India - Production In Pune - DriveSpark News ... Brembo and Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems have signed a joint venture agreement to produce motorcycle ABS systems in India. The new entity, BRSF Active Safety Solutions, will handle local assembly and supply of ABS units for the Indian two-wheeler market. ... Brembo holds a 60 percent majority stake in the venture, while Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems, the market leader in China's motorcycle ABS segment, brings its manufacturing experience to the partnership. Operations will run out of Chakan, Pune, right beside Brembo India's existing plant. ... The new facility will house automated assembly lines and is expected to employ around 50 people initially. Brembo and Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems plan a progressive ramp-up tied to production volumes and supply chain localisation over time. ... The plant sits in Chakan, one of India's key automotive and motorcycle manufacturing hubs. Closing of the joint venture remains subject to customary regulatory approvals before operations can begin at the site. ... BRSF Active Safety Solutions will offer both single-channel and dual-channel ABS solutions for motorcycles. The single-channel ABS setup will suit lower-cost, mass-market motorcycles, while the dual-channel systems will target larger and premium machines with higher performance demands. ... Andrea Paganessi, Motorcycle GBU Chief Operating Officer of Brembo, said the joint venture reflects the company's commitment to supporting evolving motorcycle safety standards in India. Hill Shan, Founder of Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems, added that the partnership aims to build a manufacturing platform focused on quality and reliability for Indian market needs. ... India remains the world's largest two-wheeler market, with up to 25 million registered vehicles. The country has seen solid expansion rates alongside growing attention to safety technology across price segments. ... Commuter motorcycles typically use simpler braking hardware, while premium and performance models have shifted toward better calipers, discs and dual-channel ABS. The joint venture also strengthens foundation brake solutions under Brembo's BYBRE brand, expanding supply to Original Equipment customers in India. More advanced braking technologies could be added to the venture in future as market requirements evolve. ... Article Published On: Saturday, June 20, 2026, 21:27 [IST]"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Brembo and Ningbo SAFE Establish Joint Venture to Manufacture Advanced Motorcycle ABS Systems in India! - MTDCNC - The home of CNC milling. turning, 5 axis and precision machining",mtdcnc.com,2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mtdcnc.com/news/mtdcnc/brembo-and-ningbo-safe-establish-joint-venture-to-manufacture-advanced-motorcycle-abs-systems-in-india/,"Brembo, the globally renowned leader in braking technology and mobility solutions, has entered into a strategic partnership with Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems, one of China’s leading providers of motorcycle anti-lock braking systems (ABS), to establish a new joint venture dedicated to manufacturing and supplying advanced motorcycle ABS solutions for the Indian market. The initiative represents a significant investment in India’s rapidly evolving two-wheeler industry and underscores the growing importance of vehicle safety technologies in one of the world’s largest motorcycle markets. ... The new company, named BRSF Active Safety Solutions, will combine Brembo’s global expertise in braking systems and vehicle safety technologies with Ningbo SAFE’s extensive experience in ABS development and production. Together, the partners aim to strengthen the availability of advanced braking technologies for Indian motorcycle manufacturers while supporting the broader adoption of safety systems across the country’s expanding two-wheeler sector. ... Under the terms of the agreement, Brembo will hold a 60 percent majority stake in the venture, reinforcing its long-term commitment to India’s automotive industry. The new company will operate from a dedicated manufacturing facility located in Chakan, Pune, one of India’s most important automotive and engineering hubs. Positioned adjacent to Brembo’s existing operations, the facility will support local production, assembly, and supply of motorcycle ABS systems specifically tailored to the requirements of Indian original equipment manufacturers (OEMs). ... The manufacturing plant will incorporate highly automated assembly lines designed to ensure consistent quality, production efficiency, and operational reliability. Initial operations are expected to create approximately 50 direct jobs, with further workforce expansion anticipated as production volumes increase and supply chain localization efforts advance. The project is also expected to contribute to the development of local manufacturing capabilities, technology transfer, and supplier ecosystem growth within India’s automotive sector. ... Ningbo SAFE Founder Hill Shan emphasized the strategic importance of creating a localized manufacturing platform capable of delivering reliable and cost-effective ABS solutions tailored to the specific needs of Indian customers. He stated that the collaboration combines the strengths of both organizations and provides a foundation for building an efficient operation that can support the continued growth of India’s two-wheeler market. ... Initially, BRS ... Solutions will manufacture both single-channel and dual-channel ABS systems ... covering a broad range of motorcycle categories and engine capacities. The production platform has also been designed with future scalability in mind, allowing ... introduction of more sophisticated braking and vehicle safety technologies as customer requirements and market expectations evolve. This flexibility positions the venture to support future developments in connected mobility, intelligent safety systems, and advanced rider-assistance technologies. ... India remains the world’s largest two-wheeler market, with annual sales reaching up to 25 million vehicles. The increasing focus on rider safety, coupled with stricter regulatory requirements and growing consumer demand for premium features, is creating substantial opportunities for manufacturers of advanced braking systems. The new venture is expected to strengthen local availability of these technologies while helping motorcycle manufacturers integrate globally recognized safety solutions into their product portfolios. ... For Brembo, the partnership builds upon nearly two decades of operations in India. Since establishing its presence in the country in 2008, the company has become a key supplier of braking solutions through its ByBre brand, which focuses on braking systems for small- and medium-displacement motorcycles. Brembo India currently operates manufacturing facilities in Pune and Chennai and employs approximately 1,250 people, supplying components such as brake discs, calipers, master cylinders, and complete ABS systems to both domestic and international customers. ... Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems, founded in 2014, has emerged as a major force in the development and production of motorcycle ABS technologies. Between 2019 and 2025, the company consistently maintained a leading position in China’s two-wheeler ABS market. Its operations are supported by six ABS assembly lines, four ECU assembly lines, and advanced testing laboratories that comply with international quality standards. The company operates under the IATF 16949 quality management system and is recognized for its strong engineering capabilities, product reliability, and commitment to continuous innovation. ... Subject to customary regulatory approvals, the formation of BRSF Active Safety Solutions marks a significant milestone in the development of India’s automotive safety ecosystem. By combining global expertise, advanced manufacturing capabilities, and local production infrastructure, Brembo and Ningbo SAFE are creating a platform that will support technology transfer, strengthen domestic manufacturing, and help motorcycle manufacturers meet the growing demand for safer and more technologically advanced vehicles. ... As India’s two-wheeler market continues to evolve, the joint venture is expected to play an important role in expanding access to advanced braking technologies while contributing to the broader goals of improving road safety, enhancing local manufacturing capabilities, and supporting the long-term growth of the country’s automotive industry."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"세이프라이프, 독일 ‘인터슐츠 2026’ 성료… 사용 편의성 고려한 Z노즐 적용 제품 선봬",www.gosiweek.com (피앤피뉴스),2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-18 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gosiweek.com/article/1065599901909420,"세이프라이프, 독일 ‘인터슐츠 2026’ 성료… 사용 편의성 고려한 Z노즐 적용 제품 선봬 ... ### 세이프라이프, 독일 ‘인터슐츠 2026’ 성료… 사용 편의성 고려한 Z노즐 적용 제품 선봬 ... 차량용소화기 디자인과 Z노즐 적용 제품에 높은 관심 탈출용망치·수납형 가방 결합한 차량안전키트 주목 유럽 바이어 및 참관객 대상 다양한 수출 상담 진행 ... 소화기 전문 브랜드 세이프라이프(대표 김진영)는 지난 독일 하노버에서 개최된 국제 소방ㆍ안전 전시회 '인터슐츠(INTERSCHUTZ) 2026' 참가를 성공적으로 마무리했다고 밝혔다.이번 전시는 한국소방산업기술원의 해외수출 판로개척 지원사업을 통해 참가했으며, 세이프라이프는 유럽 시장을 겨냥한 차량안전키트를 선보이며 현지 바이어와 참관객들의 관심을 끌었다.특히 세이프라이프가 전시한 차량용소화기는 기존 소화기와 차별화된 디자인과 사용 편의성을 고려한 Z노즐 적용 제품으로 많은 주목을 받았다. 현장을 찾은 바이어들은 기능뿐 아니라 차량 내부와 조화를 이루는 제품 디자인에 높은 관심을 보였으며, 차량 내 비치를 고려한 실용성에 긍정적인 평가를 내렸다.차량안전키트에 포함된 탈출용망치 역시 현지 참관객들의 관심을 받았다. 차량 화재 및 교통사고 발생 시 신속한 탈출을 지원하는 안전장비로서 차량용소화기와 함께 구성된 점을 주목 받았다. 또한 차량용소화기와 탈출용망치를 하나의 가방에 담은 원스텝 차량안전키트는 전시 기간 동안 가장 많은 문의를 받은 제품 중 하나였다. 해당 가방은 차량 트렁크 및 다양한 공간에 걸어둘 수 있으며, 내부에 비상용품을 추가 수납할 수 있도록 설계되어 차량 안전을 위한 통합 솔루션이라는 평가를 받았다.김진영 세이프라이프 대표는 ""사용 편의성과 차량 안전 전반을 고려한 제품 구성에 대한 관심이 높다는 것을 확인할 수 있었다. 이번 인터슐츠 참가를 통해 세이프라이프 차량안전키트의 글로벌 시장 경쟁력을 확인하는 계기가 됐다""고 말했다."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Nongfu Spring founder-backed lab deepens bet on battery safety startup - The Yangtzeer,yangtzeer.com (Yangtzeer observers),2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://yangtzeer.com/news/deals/nongfu-spring-founder-battery-safety-startup/,"Nongfu Spring founder-backed lab deepens bet on battery safety startup - The Yangtzeer ... - Qiantang Materials Lab raises stake in Qifang New Materials to 12% - Move adds to founder’s growing push into advanced materials and energy storage supply chains ... Nongfu Spring founder and multibillionaire Zhong Shanshan (钟睒睒) has increased his exposure to battery safety materials, backing Qifang (齐方新材料), a new materials startup, for a second time through his Qiantang Materials Lab (钱塘材料实验室) platform. ... The latest transaction marks the second time Qiantang Materials Lab has invested in Qifang, lifting its stake to 12%. The financial terms were not disclosed. ... The lab first entered the company in December 2025, when Qifang was still registered in Beijing. In February 2026, the company relocated its registration to Hangzhou’s Xihu District and moved into the headquarters of Qiantang Materials Lab. ... Qiantang Materials Lab is a Hangzhou-based advanced materials research and commercialization platform wholly owned by Yangshengtang ( ... The sequence of investment, relocation and follow-on funding points to a deeper consolidation of Qifang within Zhong’s expanding advanced materials portfolio. ... In May, a private equity vehicle backed by Yangshengtang led a Series A round in Zhejiang Zhibang Lithium Battery New Material Co. (智邦锂电), a solid-state electrolyte company, marking Zhong’s entry into the new-energy materials sector. ... That deal was valued at about 500 million yuan ($74 million), with Yangshengtang indirectly taking roughly a 10% stake in Zhibang Lithium. ... The material is designed as a safety barrier for electric vehicle battery packs. ... Qifang was founded by post-90s entrepreneur Lang Jialiang, a materials science postdoctoral researcher from Tsinghua University. ... The company was established in Beijing in February 2023. By April 2024, its production base had been moved to the Wuzhen microelectronics industrial park in Zhejiang’s Tongxiang, home an extensive network of manufacturers. ... Its first mass production line was built in under a year, and batch shipments began in the second half of 2025."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Brembo and Ningbo SAFE Brakes form Indian ABS joint venture | MCNews,www.mcnews.com.au (Trev),2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mcnews.com.au/brembo-safe-brakes-india-motorcycle-abs-joint-venture/,"# Brembo and Ningbo SAFE Brakes form Indian motorcycle ABS joint venture ... ## Brembo has taken a 60 per cent stake in a new Indian joint venture with Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems, targeting motorcycle ABS production in the world’s largest two-wheeler market. ... ### Brembo takes majority stake in new Indian motorcycle ABS operation ... Brembo has taken another step in its push to become a broader motorcycle systems supplier, signing a joint venture with Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems to produce motorcycle ABS units for the Indian market. ... The new company, BRSF Active Safety Solutions, will focus on local assembly and supply of anti-lock braking systems for motorcycles in India, with Brembo taking a 60 per cent majority stake in the venture. ... The agreement is the latest in a series of motorcycle-focussed moves from Brembo. The Italian braking giant has expanded well beyond calipers and discs in recent years, adding Danish brake pad specialist SBS Friction and Spanish motorcycle braking systems manufacturer J.Juan to its portfolio before completing its acquisition of Swedish suspension specialist Öhlins at the start of 2025. Brembo has also been investing in additional Asian production capacity, including a dedicated motorcycle braking systems plant in Thailand. ... That broader strategy is now being applied to India, the world’s largest two-wheeler market, where Brembo sees a long-term opportunity tied to rising safety standards and greater ABS fitment across both commuter and higher-capacity motorcycles. ... BRSF Active Safety Solutions will operate from a dedicated manufacturing facility at Chakan, near Pune, one of India’s major automotive and motorcycle manufacturing hubs. The site will sit alongside Brembo India’s existing plant. ... The facility will use automated assembly lines, with Brembo stating that the project has been designed around quality, efficiency and progressive localisation of the supply chain. Around 50 people are expected to be employed initially, with staffing and production to ramp up in line with demand. ... The joint venture remains subject to customary regulatory approvals. ... The new operation will supply both single-channel and dual-channel ABS solutions for Indian motorcycle manufacturers. Single-channel ABS remains common on lower-cost motorcycles, while dual-channel ABS is increasingly expected on larger and more premium machines. ... Brembo says more advanced technologies could also be introduced through the joint venture in future, depending on market requirements and changes to Indian safety standards. ... The move also strengthens Brembo’s BYBRE business. BYBRE, short for “By Brembo”, is the group’s brand aimed at small- and medium-displacement motorcycles, and is already well established in India. Brembo India produces brake discs, fixed and floating calipers, front and rear master cylinders and ABS braking systems, with plants in Pune and Chennai. ... Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems brings specialist ABS knowledge to the partnership. Established in 2014, the Chinese company develops and manufactures anti-lock braking systems for two-wheelers and has been a major player in China’s motorcycle ABS sector. ... Brembo said the partnership would help it support the “progressive evolution of motorcycle safety standards in India”. ... “The joint venture with Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems reflects our commitment to supporting the progressive evolution of motorcycle safety standards in India,” said Andrea Paganessi, Motorcycle GBU Chief Operating Officer of Brembo. Leveraging our long-standing experience in the Indian market and by investing in local production and industrial capabilities, we aim to accompany the market’s transition toward more advanced braking solutions.” ... Brembo and Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems have signed a joint venture to produce motorcycle ABS systems for the Indian market. ... Hill Shan, Founder of Ningbo SAFE Brakes Systems, said the joint venture would create a localised manufacturing base tailored to Indian requirements. ... “Within this joint venture, our role is to translate this shared vision into an efficient and localized industrial operation,” Shan said. “Together with Brembo, we are establishing a manufacturing platform focused on quality, reliability and the specific requirements of the Indian motorcycle market.” ... For Brembo, the Indian ABS venture is another step in a clear motorcycle-sector consolidation strategy. ... SBS Friction added brake pad expertise, J.Juan broadened Brembo’s motorcycle braking systems capability, and Öhlins moved the group further into suspension and chassis-control territory. When added to existing brands such as Marchesini and AP Racing, Brembo’s portfolio now stretches well beyond the traditional image of red calipers on premium motorcycles. ... Brembo agreed to acquire Öhlins in October 2024, with the acquisition completed in January 2025 ... India’s sheer scale makes that especially important. Brembo describes the country as the world’s largest two-wheeler market, with up to 25 million motorcycles and scooters, and says the market continues to show strong prospects for technological development and increased attention to safety. For motorcycle manufacturers in India, the appeal is likely to be a localised supplier. ... For Brembo, it gives the group a stronger foothold in one of the world’s most important motorcycle markets at a time when safety regulations and consumer expectations are both moving in the same direction."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"SU Group Announces Distribution Agreement with Germany's GEZE, Expanding Smart Building and Safety Technology Portfolio",www.prnewswire.com (SU Group Holdings Limited),2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/su-group-announces-distribution-agreement-with-germanys-geze-expanding-smart-building-and-safety-technology-portfolio-302801167.html,"SU Group Announces Distribution Agreement with Germany's GEZE, Expanding Smart Building and Safety Technology Portfolio Accessibility Statement Skip ... HONG KONG, June 16, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- SU Group Holdings Limited (Nasdaq: SUGP) (""SU Group"" or the ""Company""), an integrated security-related engineering services company in Hong Kong, today announced a distributorship agreement with Germany's GEZE, a multi-national manufacturer in innovative door, window and safety technology for Smart Buildings. ... The agreement broadens SU Group's product and solutions portfolio with GEZE's extensive range of advanced building technologies, including automatic door systems, window technology, safety systems, smoke and heat extraction solutions, access control-related applications and building automation capabilities. ... GEZE has been in the industry for over a century and has one of the industry's most extensive product portfolios of smart building and safety technologies. This includes many award-winning products, popular for their innovative functions, high efficiency and clear focus on design, convenience and safety. GEZE's portfolio is particularly relevant to the next generation of Smart Buildings, where doors, windows, safety systems and building management platforms are increasingly expected to work together. Its technologies help support controlled access, barrier-free movement, preventive fire protection, natural ventilation, smoke and heat extraction, energy efficiency and centralized monitoring. ... SU Group's Chairman and CEO, Dave Chan, said, ""This is a big win for our customers, which put security at the forefront of planning and development decisions. The addition of GEZE to our product array will enable us to compete with top tier players, and participate in projects we could not have before, including those with the most advanced technological requirements. These technologies are increasingly important as developers, property owners and public-sector operators seek buildings that are not only secure, but also more accessible, efficient, connected and easier to manage."" ... - New distributorship agreement with GEZE, a German-headquartered global specialist in door, window and safety technology for Smart Buildings - Expands SU Group's product offering into advanced automatic door systems, window technology, building automation, access control, fire protection and safety-related applications - Positions SU Group to pursue larger, more technically demanding projects across commercial properties, public facilities, infrastructure and residential developments - Strengthens SU Group's ability to provide customers with integrated, end-to-end solutions that combine security engineering, safety, accessibility, convenience and smart building functionality - Adds a globally established brand founded in 1863, with deep expertise, international scale and a broad product portfolio focused on quality, design and innovation ... GEZE is a German-headquartered, family-run technology company founded in 1863. The company develops and produces innovative door, window and safety technology for Smart Buildings and is recognized for its broad portfolio of products, systems and services. GEZE's solutions support automatic door systems, window technology, smoke and heat extraction, safety technology, access control-related applications and building automation. With a global presence, more than 3,000 employees and subsidiaries across numerous international markets, GEZE combines engineering expertise, quality, design and digital connectivity to help create safer, more comfortable and more efficient buildings. ... SU Group (Nasdaq: SUGP) is an integrated security-related services company that primarily provides security-related engineering services, security guarding and screening services, and related vocational training services in Hong Kong. Through its subsidiaries, SU Group has been providing turnkey services to the existing infrastructure or planned development of its customers through the design, supply, installation, and maintenance of security systems for over two decades. The security systems that SU Group provides services include threat detection systems, traffic and pedestrian control systems, and extra-low voltage systems in private and public sectors, including commercial properties, public facilities, and residential properties in Hong Kong. For more information visit www.sugroup.com.hk. ... ### SU Group Holdings Limited Announces Board Approval of Warrant Exercise Price Adjustment ... ### SU Group Awarded Next-Generation Cross-Border Security and High-Speed Vehicle Clearance System Installation ... Group"" or the ""Company""), an integrated security-related engineering services company in Hong Kong"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,GSHE 2026 Adds Matter/Zigbee Sourcing Zone in Shenzhen,www.atfxcent.com,2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.atfxcent.com/news/connectivity-protocols/Zigbee_Tech/GSHE_2026_Adds_Matter_Zigbee_Sourcing_Zone.html,"On June 8, 2026, organizers of the Global Smart Home Expo 2026 (GSHE) announced a new Matter & Zigbee Dual-Certified Procurement Zone for the show in Shenzhen, scheduled for August 20–23. With pre-registration set to open on June 24, the move is especially relevant for overseas importers, distributors, system integrators, and upstream hardware suppliers because it places dual-certified smart home sourcing at the center of a formal trade setting rather than leaving it as a fragmented supplier-by-supplier search. ... According to the information provided, GSHE 2026 will take place in Shenzhen from August 20 to 23. On June 8, the organizing committee said it will establish a dedicated “Matter & Zigbee Dual-Certified Procurement Zone.” ... The zone is intended to provide a direct procurement channel for hardware that carries dual certification from CSA and the Zigbee Alliance, with overseas importers, distributors, and system integrators identified as the primary target audience. ... The first group of participating companies includes Tuya, Espressif, Telink, and 12 PCBA solution providers that have passed NHI benchmark testing. Pre-registration for this new procurement area is scheduled to open on June 24. ... From an industry perspective, overseas importers and distributors may be affected first because the new zone is framed as a direct procurement channel tied to dual-certified hardware. The practical impact is likely to center on supplier screening, product comparison, and early-stage commercial discussions. What deserves closer attention is whether buyers begin to treat dual-certification status as a baseline filter when evaluating suppliers at trade events. ... Analysis shows the announcement could raise the visibility of supplier credentials within the exhibition environment. For participating hardware and PCBA vendors, the most immediate business effect is likely in how they present certification status, testing results, and product readiness to international customers. Companies in these segments should pay attention to how qualification proof and technical documentation are expected to support procurement conversations. ... System integrators are directly named in the announcement, which suggests the zone is not only about component sourcing but also about solution assembly and deployment planning. Observably, the main areas to watch are interoperability positioning, component selection, and delivery coordination between certified hardware suppliers and integration projects. The business question is less about exhibition visibility alone and more about whether procurement decisions can be accelerated with clearer certification-backed options. ... Because the procurement zone is explicitly tied to CSA and Zigbee Alliance dual certification, and the first PCBA participants are identified through NHI benchmark testing, suppliers should be ready to present qualification-related documents clearly and consistently. For commercial teams, the issue is not abstract branding but whether procurement, technical, and compliance information can be communicated without gaps. ... Analysis shows this is better understood as a market-organization signal than as proof of a finished procurement shift. The confirmed fact is the creation of a dedicated dual-certified sourcing area inside GSHE 2026; the broader commercial outcome still depends on participation quality, buyer turnout, and how effectively certification-backed products are matched with procurement needs. ... It is more appropriate to understand this as an indicator that dual-certification is becoming a more visible commercial filter in smart home trade discussions, especially where overseas channel partners and integration buyers are concerned. At the same time, the announcement alone does not establish transaction volume, category dominance, or long-term sourcing preferences. ... In practical terms, this update deserves attention because it moves certification-related positioning into a dedicated procurement context at a major 2026 smart home event in Shenzhen. For the industry, the immediate significance lies in how buyers and suppliers prepare for August, while the longer-term relevance depends on whether this format becomes a repeatable mechanism for cross-border hardware sourcing rather than a one-off exhibition feature. ... At this stage, the most balanced reading is that the announcement marks a concrete short-term change at GSHE 2026 and a longer-term signal worth tracking, not a completed market outcome. ... No specific official source link was provided in the input, so the exact primary reference still requires ongoing verification. Follow-up attention should focus on any additional organizer notices before June 24, participation details for the procurement zone, and any clarified rules related to certification, exhibitor eligibility, or procurement procedures. ... Previous: GSHE 2026 Opens With New Matter/Zigbee Sourcing Access ... - Dr. Aris ThorneTelink Joins CSA Board as Multi-Protocol SoC Output Scales - Dr. Aris ThorneEU Enforces EN 303 647 v2.1.1 for Zigbee Exports - Dr. Aris ThorneEN 303 647 v2.1.1 Now Mandatory for Zigbee Devices - Dr. Aris ThorneGSHE 2026 Adds Matter/Zigbee Sourcing Zone ... - Dr. Aris ThorneGSHE 2026 Opens With New Matter/Zigbee Sourcing Access ... - Dr. Aris ThorneBrazil Exempts Import Duties on Cross-Border Parcels Under USD 50 - Dr. Aris ThorneFruit Attraction 2026 Booth Bookings Top 90% - Dr. Aris ThorneVietnam Tightens Zigbee Import Checks: Full-Temp RF Attenuation Report Now Mandatory - Dr. Aris ThorneVietnam Tightens Zigbee Import Checks: Full-Temperature RF Attenuation Report Required - Dr. Aris ThorneVietnam Tightens Zigbee Import Checks with Full-Temp RF Attenuation Requirement"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Chinese firefighting equipment makers target untapped EU market - Nikkei Asia,asia.nikkei.com,2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://asia.nikkei.com/economy/trade/chinese-firefighting-equipment-makers-target-untapped-eu-market,"Chinese firefighting equipment makers target untapped EU market - Nikkei Asia ... # Chinese firefighting equipment makers target untapped EU market ... Big China presence at Hanover fair but lack of certification hampers expansion ... Shaoxing-based Xingli Safe Way Fire wants to market its extinguishers, including one specifically for fires caused by lithium batteries, in Germany and the EU. (Photo by Jens Kastner) ... HANOVER, Germany -- Nearly 300 Chinese manufacturers of firefighting and civil protection equipment exhibited their products last week at a trade show in Germany, by far the biggest contingent from outside of the European Union aiming for a foothold on the continent."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Chinese fire‑safety firms set their sights on Europe’s biggest market | Finexus,api.finexus.net,2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://api.finexus.net/api/news/events/ca9d4a44-9995-4a37-8787-16e140853bae/html,"For many of the exhibitors, the fair represented a first foray into direct engagement with European buyers. A sales representative from Guangzhou‑based Wanzen Energy Safety explained that the company has long supplied parts to German fire‑truck manufacturers, but has never sold a finished product under its own name to a fire department or municipal authority. “We have been present in the market indirectly, through parts that end up on German‑branded equipment,” the spokesperson said. “Our goal at this exhibition was to open a direct channel to end‑users, especially in a country where standards are rigorous and the demand for new‑energy fire protection is soaring.” The firm hopes to promote its Fire Fly brand, which it says is tailored to the needs of data‑centres, electric‑vehicle charging stations and power‑grid installations – sectors that are expanding rapidly across the continent. ... Rebecca Zhi, a sales executive for Zhejiang Wanlida Firefighting Equipment, underscored the importance of the process. Her company, which produces specialised nozzles for fire‑hoses, has historically sold its products to fire‑truck manufacturers rather than directly to fire brigades because it lacked the required certifications. “The cost of obtaining VdS or CE approval can exceed twenty thousand euros for a single product line,” Zhi explained, “but the opportunity to access the German market – and by extension the whole European Union – makes the investment worthwhile.” ... Other firms are tackling the certification hurdle by seeking local representation that can navigate the regulatory maze. Wen Xingrong, who works for Hebei‑based Yunsentai Machinery Manufacturing, told reporters that the company is looking for a German agent who can help it understand the nuances of European standards and set up a service network capable of providing after‑sales support. Yunsentai’s flagship offering is a high‑capacity water pump capable of drawing water from lakes or rivers and delivering it over distances of up to five kilometres, with a lift capacity of six hundred metres – a capability that is especially valuable for fighting forest fires in remote terrain. ... by thirty to ... recognised certifications and market insight ... Despite such reservations, the momentum behind the Chinese presence at Interschutz suggests that the continent’s fire‑safety landscape will become increasingly diverse in the coming years. Companies like Wanzen Energy Safety, Zhejiang Wanlida, Yunsentai and Xingli Safe Way Fire are investing heavily in certification, local partnerships and price strategies designed to win over European fire services. Their collective ambition reflects a broader trend: Chinese industrial firms are moving from the role of low‑cost parts suppliers to that of full‑scale technology providers capable of competing on quality, innovation and service. ... The German fire‑protection sector now faces a dual challenge. On one hand, it must safeguard the high standards that have long defined European safety equipment; on the other, it must accelerate its own research and development to stay ahead of a new class of competitors that are rapidly closing the technological gap. As the next edition of Interschutz approaches, the dialogue between German manufacturers, Chinese entrants and European regulators will likely shape the future of fire‑safety solutions across the continent, determining whether collaboration or competition will dominate the market. ... only influence procurement ... The story unfolding in Hanover is a microcosm of a larger shift in global trade: as Chinese firms continue to invest in research, certification and direct market access, they are reshaping the competitive dynamics of sectors that were once thought to be insulated from rapid change. Whether European fire‑protection companies can adapt quickly enough to maintain their historic edge remains to be seen, but the pressure to innovate has never been more acute. ... The next few years will reveal how the interplay of technology, regulation and market strategy will redefine the standards of safety that protect lives and property across Europe."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Chinese Firefighting Equipment Makers Bet on Europe, but Certification Walls Slow the Push | LavX News",news.lavx.hu,2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.lavx.hu/article/chinese-firefighting-equipment-makers-bet-on-europe-but-certification-walls-slow-the-push,"Chinese Firefighting Equipment Makers Bet on Europe, but Certification Walls Slow the Push | LavX News ... Chinese Firefighting Equipment Makers Bet on Europe, but ... Nearly 300 Chinese manufacturers showed up at Hanover's civil protection fair, the largest non-EU contingent on the floor. The ambition is clear, but European safety certification stands between them and a market worth billions. ... Nearly 300 Chinese manufacturers of firefighting and civil protection equipment exhibited at a trade show in Hanover, Germany last week, the largest single contingent from outside the European Union. The scale of the presence signals a coordinated attempt to convert China's dominance in low-cost safety hardware into share of one of the world's most regulated and lucrative end markets. ... Shaoxing-based Xingli Safe Way Fire was among the firms working the floor, pitching a line of extinguishers that includes a unit designed specifically for fires triggered by lithium-ion batteries. That product choice is not incidental. Battery fires are one of the fastest-growing categories of fire risk in Europe, driven by the spread of electric vehicles, home energy storage, and e-bikes, and they require suppression chemistry that standard ABC powder extinguishers do not reliably deliver. By leading with a niche where demand is rising and incumbent supply is thin, Chinese vendors are trying to enter through a gap rather than fight established European brands head-on. ... Europe's fire protection equipment market is large and steady, estimated in the range of several billion dollars annually and growing in the low-to-mid single digits as building codes tighten and retrofit cycles continue. Unlike consumer electronics, demand here is anchored by regulation: commercial buildings, vehicles, and public infrastructure are legally required to carry certified suppression equipment, and that equipment must be inspected and replaced on schedule. That creates a recurring revenue base rather than one-off sales, which is precisely what makes the segment attractive to manufacturers that already produce at volume. ... China's advantage is the same one it has carried into solar panels, batteries, and EVs: scale and cost. Domestic producers can manufacture extinguisher bodies, valves, and suppression agents at prices European factories struggle to match. In commoditized hardware, that cost gap is usually decisive. ... The obstacle is not price or distribution. It is conformity. To sell firefighting equipment in the EU, products must carry CE marking and meet harmonized standards such as EN 3 for portable extinguishers, frequently backed by third-party approvals like those issued under Germany's certification regime. The testing is expensive, slow, and unforgiving, and it has to be repeated for each product variant. For a Chinese manufacturer with a broad catalog optimized for the domestic market, re-engineering and re-certifying each SKU for European norms can erase much of the cost advantage that made the expansion attractive in the first place. ... This is why a packed exhibition hall does not automatically translate into market share. A vendor can demonstrate a product in Hanover without yet holding the paperwork to sell it commercially across the bloc. The pattern echoes what other Chinese consumer-goods categories have run into in Germany, where vape makers built strong sales before colliding with regulatory enforcement. The lesson for fire equipment is that distribution follows certification, not the trade-show handshake. ... For European incumbents, the strategic risk is medium-term rather than immediate. The certification moat buys time, but it is not permanent. Chinese firms have repeatedly shown the willingness to absorb compliance costs and the patience to grind through approval processes when the prize is a recurring, regulation-protected market. The lithium-battery extinguisher angle is the tell: it is a category where European supply is still forming, certification standards are still maturing, and an early entrant with certified product could establish itself before the market consolidates. ... The broader read is that China's export playbook is moving up the regulatory difficulty curve. Solar and batteries were about cost. Safety equipment is about cost plus the ability to clear compliance gates that were designed, in part, to keep low-cost entrants out. The firms that crack certification at scale will not just win extinguisher sales, they will validate a template for pushing into Europe's other regulated industrial niches. For now, the gap between presence and permission keeps the threat contained, and how quickly Chinese manufacturers close that gap is the number worth watching."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Chinese Language Firefighting Tools Makers Goal Untapped EU Market | DNews World,dnews.co.in,2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://dnews.co.in/chinese-language-firefighting-tools-makers-goal-untapped-eu-market/,"Chinese Language Firefighting Tools Makers Goal Untapped EU Market | DNews World ... Huge China presence at Hanover honest however lack of certification hampers enlargement ... Shaoxing-based Xingli Protected Method Hearth needs to market its extinguishers, together with one particularly for fires attributable to lithium batteries, in Germany and the EU. (Photograph by Jens Kastner) ... HANOVER, Germany — Almost 300 Chinese language producers of firefighting and civil safety tools exhibited their merchandise final week at a commerce present in Germany, by far the most important contingent from outdoors of the European Union aiming for a foothold on the continent."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Jialekang at Canton Fair: Defining Excellence as a China Top 10 Electric Massage Machine Exporter - EMWNews.com,emwnews.com (Jordan Taylor),2026-06-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://emwnews.com/jialekang-at-canton-fair-defining-excellence-as-a-china-top-10-electric-massage-machine-exporter/,"Xiamen, Fujian Jun 9, 2026 (EMWNews.com) – How do international commercial buyers identify manufacturing partners that consistently balance structural regulatory compliance with cost-efficient product innovation? In the highly competitive global health and wellness apparatus market, sourcing managers frequently encounter the challenge of finding factories that offer both advanced technical customization and long-term production stability. At the China Import and Export Fair, commonly known as the Canton Fair, global procurement professionals systematically filter suppliers to identify verified leaders in the personal care sector. During this premier trade event, Jialekang (Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co., Ltd,) recognized broadly by its brand name Jialekang, presents its comprehensive portfolio as a premier China Top 10 Electric Massage Machine Exporter, demonstrating how localized specialized manufacturing addresses the shifting requirements of the international wellness industry. ... The Canton Fair serves as China’s largest comprehensive trade exhibition, positioning its dedicated health, medicine, and recreation pavilion as a primary sourcing hub for international electronics and wellness appliance buyers. For systemic sourcing operations, this platform functions as an essential venue to evaluate structural technical advancements, verify operational compliance, and establish direct relationships with original equipment manufacturers (OEM) and original design manufacturers (ODM). ... As a regular participant within this specialized pavilion, Jialekang utilizes the exhibition to validate its established export infrastructure, advanced research and development capabilities, and comprehensive international certification portfolio. For professional buyers from Europe, South America, and Southeast Asia, a sustained presence at the Canton Fair provides crucial institutional validation. It signals that a manufacturer possesses the scale, technical compliance, and administrative capacity required to fulfill large-scale international supply contracts while adhering to strict regional market entry criteria. ... Operating a dedicated production facility in Xiamen, China, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co., Ltd has focused exclusively on the design, engineering, and manufacturing of personal health and massage equipment. The company structures its specialized manufacturing operations around specific high-demand consumer categories, including an advanced handheld electric massage machine, ergonomic massage pillows, multi-functional massage cushions, specialized massage mattresses, localized foot massagers, and automated massage chairs. ... The contemporary international wellness market requires a clear shift away from standardized, generic commodities toward highly differentiated, market-specific product lines. To address this commercial reality, Jialekang structures its corporate capabilities to function as an adaptive ODM and OEM solution partner rather than a rigid product vendor. The company provides international brand owners, healthcare distributors, and e-commerce enterprises with flexible customization options across multiple operational layers. ... By supplying detailed technical compliance files, rigorous quality assurance data, and structured after-sales support, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co., Ltd mitigates operational risks for international importers. This comprehensive methodology establishes a reliable framework for long-term commercial relationships, allowing global partners to introduce innovative products with reduced time-to-market overhead. ... At the Canton Fair, the Jialekang exhibition space serves as an active hub for technical demonstration and commercial negotiation, explicitly illustrating the company’s operational role as a major electric massage machine exporter. The booth layout features dedicated functional demonstration zones where international procurement managers can directly evaluate the mechanical integrity, material quality, and electronic responsiveness of the equipment. ... Throughout the exhibition, technical staff provide transparent, data-driven explanations of internal product components, circuit safety features, and structural materials. Commercial visitors regularly emphasize that product reliability and comprehensive regulatory compliance form the basis of their supplier selections. The factory satisfies these critical prerequisites by maintaining full compliance with essential international standards, including CE, RoHS, and specialized electronic safety marks. This systematic adherence to international safety and environmental regulations ensures that the machinery meets the stringent entry requirements of competitive consumer markets in western Europe and the Americas, providing buyers with verifiable quality assurance during face-to-face evaluations. ... Looking forward, the global demand for personal health appliances continues to expand, driven by an increasing consumer focus on daily physical recovery, ergonomics, and preventative wellness. In response to these market dynamics, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co., Ltd intends to leverage its performance at the Canton Fair to deepen its penetration across established and emerging international markets. ... While maintaining its robust market share in Europe and South America, the enterprise is systematically expanding its distribution networks within North America and across rapid-growth markets along the Belt and Road initiative. This long-term corporate strategy focuses on upgrading operations from traditional contract manufacturing to high-value, collaborative brand partnerships. By consistently reinvesting in structural product innovation, optimizing manufacturing efficiency in Xiamen, and participating in major international trade platforms, the company reinforces its position as a reliable, compliant, and innovative electric massage machine exporter, delivering sustainable value to the global health and wellness supply chain."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Professional Durable Foot and Leg Massager Exporter: Jialekang's Strategic Presence at Hong Kong Electronics Fair - EMWNews.com,emwnews.com (Jordan Taylor),2026-06-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://emwnews.com/professional-durable-foot-and-leg-massager-exporter-jialekangs-strategic-presence-at-hong-kong-electronics-fair/,"Presence at Hong Kong Electronics Fair ... EMWNews ... # Professional Durable Foot and Leg Massager Exporter: Jialekang’s Strategic Presence at Hong Kong Electronics Fair Jordan Taylor June 9, 2026 ... Xiamen, ... Kong Electronics Fair: A ... Whether it is the exhaustion following a long shift on a retail floor or the stagnant circulation resulting from prolonged desk work, the demand for specialized recovery tools is no longer confined to clinical environments. As global wellness trends shift toward accessible, high-performance home recovery, the role of a professional durable foot and leg massager exporter becomes vital in bridging the gap between professional therapy and domestic convenience. Jialekang (Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co.,Ltd.,) utilized the Hong Kong Electronics Fair to demonstrate how structural integrity and biomechanical precision are reshaping the global health equipment landscape. ... The Hong Kong Electronics Fair, organized by the Hong Kong Trade Development Council (HKTDC), remains one of the most influential sourcing platforms globally. It serves as a critical nexus where technological innovation meets commercial viability, particularly within the dedicated healthcare and smart home sectors. For international distributors, the fair is not merely a display of gadgets but a rigorous vetting ground for manufacturing excellence. Jialekang recognized the strategic importance of this venue, positioning itself as a professional durable foot and leg massager exporter capable of meeting the stringent quality expectations of the European and South American markets. In an area where consumer electronics are often criticized for short lifespans, the emphasis on durability at this fair provided a refreshing perspective for procurement specialists looking for sustainable partnerships. ... To substantiate the claim of being a professional durable foot and leg massager exporter, the company featured a “Technical Integrity” display. This area allowed buyers to see the internal components that are usually hidden behind fabric and plastic. By showcasing high-performance copper motors, high-density industrial-grade airbags, and reinforced internal frames, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co.,Ltd. provided tangible proof of its commitment to product longevity. This level of transparency addressed a common concern among international buyers regarding the internal build quality of mass-market health devices. ... In the competitive world of health equipment, technical specifications are only as valuable as the certifications that back them. Jialekang has built its reputation over 15 years by ensuring that its design and manufacturing processes meet global benchmarks. Every product in the lineup adheres to CE, RoHS, and FDA standards, which are essential for entry into the highly regulated markets of North America and Europe. These certifications act as a universal language of trust between the exporter and the global buyer. ... Beyond individual use, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co.,Ltd. is increasingly targeting the professional health management and B2B sectors. Sports rehabilitation centers and physiotherapy clinics are beginning to adopt these durable massagers as auxiliary tools to assist in patient recovery. Furthermore, there is a burgeoning market for high-quality massagers within corporate wellness initiatives. Many organizations now view providing professional-grade recovery tools as a key component of employee benefit packages, aimed at reducing workplace fatigue and improving productivity. As a professional durable foot and leg massager exporter, Jialekang provides the customization options necessary to serve these varied institutional requirements. ... One of the most compelling arguments for partnering with Jialekang is its robust manufacturing foundation in Xiamen, China. Unlike many trading companies, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co.,Ltd. maintains full control over the production cycle, from initial industrial design to final quality control. This vertical integration allows for a level of agility that is rare in the industry. During the Hong Kong Electronics Fair, the company highlighted its ability to offer a standard 35-day delivery cycle, a significant advantage for retailers managing seasonal inventory. ... Moreover, Jialekang addresses the needs of small-to-medium-sized enterprises by offering flexible cooperation models. With a Minimum Order Quantity (MOQ) starting at 300 units for certain models, the company lowers the barrier to entry for emerging brands or regional distributors. This flexibility, combined with 15 years of export experience, ensures that the logistical complexities of international trade are handled with professional precision. The company’s history of maintaining long-term relationships with hundreds of clients across Europe and South America is a testament to its reliability as a foot and leg massager exporter. ... The strategic presence of Jialekang at the Hong Kong Electronics Fair marks a significant milestone in its journey as a global health advocate. By moving beyond the role of a traditional factory and embracing the identity of a professional durable foot and leg massager exporter, Xiamen Happiness Manufacture Technology Co.,Ltd. has demonstrated that it understands the nuances of the international market. The fair provided an ideal platform to showcase how 15 years of manufacturing expertise can be distilled into products that improve the daily lives of users across the globe. ... As the boundary between medical-grade therapy and home wellness continues to blur, the demand for reliable, effective, and durable massage solutions will only grow. Jialekang remains at the forefront of this movement, committed to delivering products that combine excellent quality with professional service. For global buyers looking to capitalize on the wellness boom, the company offers a partnership built on transparency and a proven track record of export success."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,GSHE 2026 Opens Matter/Zigbee Sourcing Access,www.atfxcent.com,2026-06-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.atfxcent.com/news/connectivity-protocols/Zigbee_Tech/GSHE_2026_Opens_With_New_Matter_Zigbee_Sourcing_Access.html,"On June 24, 2026, the Global Smart Home Expo and Shenzhen International Smart Home Exhibition (GSHE) opens in Shenzhen for a three-day run through June 26, drawing industry attention not only for the event itself but for the launch of a new sourcing channel built around cross-certified smart home products. For manufacturers, overseas buyers, sourcing teams, and supply-chain service providers, the key point is that interoperability verification, buyer matching, factory review, and prototyping support are being presented together in one exhibition setting, which makes this development relevant beyond a standard trade show update. ... According to the provided event information, GSHE 2026 will be held at the Shenzhen Convention and Exhibition Center from June 24 to 26. The exhibition is introducing, for the first time, a “Matter & Zigbee Cross-Certified Sourcing Zone.” ... The zone brings together 127 Chinese manufacturers whose products have passed dual-protocol interoperability verification under joint certification by CSA Group and the Zigbee Alliance. The product categories named in the event summary are smart locks, HVAC automation controllers, and power monitoring modules. ... The same zone is open for overseas buyer pre-registration and will offer live factory-inspection video connections on site, together with PCBA Solutions customized sampling services. ... From an industry perspective, this arrangement may matter because product verification and supplier access are being linked more directly at the point of sourcing. The practical impact is likely to be strongest in supplier screening, early technical review, and sample evaluation, especially for buyers looking at products where interoperability claims affect purchasing decisions. What deserves closer attention is how buyers use pre-registration, remote factory review, and sampling support to shorten their initial qualification process. ... Analysis shows that the immediate relevance for participating manufacturers is not only ... but also how certification status is presented ... a commercial setting. The business impact may appear in customer communication, quotation discussions, technical clarification, and response speed for custom sampling. Companies in the ... attention to how ... Observably, the inclusion of customized PCBA sampling adds a practical layer for service providers involved in prototyping and product adaptation. The effect is likely to be felt in ... handoff between product selection and engineering follow-up, where speed, documentation, and manufacturability discussions become part of the sourcing conversation rather than a later step. ... Companies should watch the exact wording used around cross-certification and interoperability verification. In this case, the confirmed fact is that the zone features manufacturers whose products have passed dual-protocol interoperability verification under the stated joint certification arrangement. Any broader commercial interpretation should be checked carefully against official event or certification wording. ... . For companies ... concentrates on finished products, technical ... The combination of overseas buyer pre-registration, live factory-inspection video links, and customized sampling support suggests that procurement conversations may move beyond display-only interactions. Companies should therefore prepare certification materials, production communication records, and sampling coordination workflows that can support faster follow-up if buyer interest turns immediate. ... Analysis shows that this is better understood as a market-facing signal about how smart home sourcing is being organized, rather than as proof of a completed shift in the industry. The notable feature is not only the presence of dual-protocol verified products, but the effort to combine certification visibility with buyer access, remote factory review, and sampling support in one dedicated zone. ... Observably, the event points to a more operational conversation around interoperability: not just whether a product meets a protocol requirement, but how that status is translated into sourcing confidence and procurement action. Even so, it is still appropriate to treat this as a development that requires continued observation rather than a settled market outcome. ... At this point, the GSHE update is most appropriately read as a concrete but still developing industry signal. It highlights that cross-certified smart home products are being framed more directly for procurement use, especially for overseas buyers and supplier-matching scenarios. The longer-term significance will depend on how consistently this model influences sourcing behavior, supplier selection, and follow-up transactions after the exhibition. ... This article is based on the user-provided news title, event date, and event summary related to GSHE 2026. For this type of industry update, relevant source categories would typically include official event announcements, company statements, industry association releases, authoritative media coverage, and standards-organization documents. No specific official source link was provided in the input, so the exact source chain still requires ongoing verification. Areas that merit continued attention include any later official wording on the sourcing zone, certification-related descriptions, and post-event developments in buyer engagement and supplier follow-up. ... Next: GSHE 2026 Adds Matter/Zigbee Sourcing Zone ... Dr. Ar ... 5.4 ... Zigbee UWB ... - Dr. Aris Thorne ... 802.15.4z-2026 Sets New UWB Benchmark for Zigbee Tech ... - Dr. Aris ThorneIEEE 802.15.4-2026 Lifts Zigbee Mesh to 256 Nodes ... - Dr. Aris ThorneZigbee Mesh