ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Steel Safe Trading Co. Claims Best Innovative Safety Locker Manufacturer in Gujarat award at Brand Empower's Rashtriya Ratna Samman 2026 - The Tribune,"www.tribuneindia.com (ANI Updated At : 12:45 PM May 30, 2026 IST)",2026-05-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/business/steel-safe-trading-co-claims-best-innovative-safety-locker-manufacturer-in-gujarat-award-at-brand-empowers-rashtriya-ratna-samman-2026/,"Steel Safe Trading Co. Claims Best Innovative Safety Locker Manufacturer in Gujarat award at Brand Empower's Rashtriya Ratna Samman 2026 - The Tribune ... Steel Safe Trading Co. Claims Best Innovative Safety Locker Manufacturer in Gujarat award at Brand Empower's Rashtriya Ratna Samman 2026 ... New Delhi [India], May 30: Setting a formidable new benchmark in the manufacturing and industrial security sector, Steel Safe Trading Co. proudly clinched the prestigious title of ' Best Innovative Safety Locker Manufacturer in Gujarat' at the highly anticipated Rashtriya Ratna Samman 2026. Organised by Brand Empower, a premier business recognition entity committed to celebrating corporate brilliance, this spectacular award ceremony unfolded at Bharat Mandapam in New Delhi. The grand gala served as a vibrant convergence of the nation's most influential business minds, visionary corporate leaders, and industry disruptors. Adding immense star power and political gravitas to the momentous evening, Ms. Kangana Ranaut, Member of the Lok Sabha and celebrated Actor, presided over the ceremony as the Chief Guest. Watch the Award Video Here! Her commanding presence magnified the significance of the occasion as she took the stage to honour trailblazing enterprises like Steel Safe Trading Co., highlighting their instrumental role in fortifying India's physical security infrastructure and driving manufacturing excellence. ... Emerging victorious in a highly specialized and competitive category, the organization was officially announced as the definitive winner, with the name Steel Safe Trading Co. proudly inscribed on the certificate for all to see. Representing the brand's remarkable journey and unyielding dedication to manufacturing robust security solutions, the awardee on stage, Owner Mr. Sameer Shah, stepped proudly forward to accept the honour. Based in Gujarat, Steel Safe Trading Co. has firmly established itself as a premier manufacturer, supplier, and trader of state-of-the-art security equipment. The company specializes in engineering a comprehensive range of premium products, including heavy-duty fire-resistant safes, advanced digital and biometric lockers, strong room doors, and customized security cabinets. Driven by an uncompromising commitment to quality and cutting-edge design, the company utilizes premium-grade steel and advanced locking mechanisms to deliver highly effective, tamper-proof security solutions that safeguard the valuable assets of residential, commercial, and banking clients across the region. ... Upon receiving the highly coveted award for Best Innovative Safety Locker Manufacturer in Gujarat, Mr. Sameer Shah expressed his profound gratitude and shared an inspiring vision for the future of the company's product line. ""Accepting this monumental recognition at the Rashtriya Ratna Samman 2026 is an incredible milestone that validates our core mission of delivering uncompromising safety and highly innovative protection solutions,"" he stated with immense pride. ""In today's fast-paced world, providing secure, reliable, and technologically advanced lockers is the critical difference in giving our clients absolute peace of mind. This award belongs to our incredibly hardworking manufacturing team, our skilled engineers, and our supportive partners who work diligently to meet the complex security requirements of our customers day in and day out. We are deeply energized by this honour and remain fiercely committed to shouldering the responsibility of providing our consumers with the highest quality safes, ensuring that their most prized possessions remain protected under any circumstance."" ... The spectacular success of the Rashtriya Ratna Samman 2026 further illuminates the visionary leadership of Mr. Rahul Ranjan Singh, CEO of Brand Empower, whose unwavering commitment to acknowledging corporate and entrepreneurial brilliance has made these awards a highly coveted pinnacle of success. Over the years, Brand Empower's meticulously curated award ceremonies have maintained a glamorous and esteemed legacy, having been graced in earlier editions by an illustrious lineup of iconic celebrities such as Mrs. Kajol, Mrs. Raveena Tandon, Mrs. Madhuri Dixit Nene, Mr. Anupam Kher, and Mrs. Shilpa Shetty Kundra. The triumphant execution and expansive scale of this year's grand event were seamlessly supported by a robust network of prominent sponsors and partners. The unforgettable ceremony was Presented by Brand Empower Pvt. Ltd., and prominently Co-Sponsored by Baghel Industries Pvt. Ltd. The event's massive digital footprint was expertly amplified by Digital Marketing Partner - Webpulse Solution Pvt Ltd, alongside the highly impactful community outreach orchestrated by CSR Partner - Webpulse Foundation. Furthermore, strategic industry networking was powered by B2B Partner - GetManufacturers.com (Indian Manufacturers Directory), holistic well-being initiatives were championed by Wellness Partner - Natural Therapy India, and progressive retail growth solutions were backed by eCommerce Partner - Local Dukaan."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Beyond Vehicle Fire Extinguishers to Integrated Safety Solutions… SafeLife Participates in Germany’s Interschutz - 벤처스퀘어,www.venturesquare.net,2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.venturesquare.net/en/1086745/,"Safelife, a domestic brand specializing in fire extinguishers, is setting out to target the European market at the world's largest fire and safety exhibition. Safelife announced on the 29th that it will participate in 'INTERSCHUTZ 2026,' an international fire and safety exhibition to be held in Hanover, Germany, this coming June. ... This participation was carried out as part of the 'Overseas Export Market Development Support Project' organized by the Korea Fire Industry & Technology Institute. Safelife was selected as a final recipient in recognition of its global certification capabilities and achievements in expanding the vehicle fire extinguisher market. ... Interschutz is a leading global exhibition representing the fields of firefighting, rescue, disaster response, and safety, attended by safety industry professionals and buyers from around the world. Through this exhibition, Safelife plans to showcase automotive safety kits targeting the European market. ... #### Expanding into overseas markets with an integrated safety solution combining vehicle fire extinguishers and escape hammers ... The newly unveiled vehicle safety kit combines a vehicle fire extinguisher with an emergency escape hammer. Designed as a one-step bag, it can be easily stored in various spaces, including the car trunk, and features an interior compartment for storing additional emergency supplies. ... The company is highlighting its differentiation as an integrated safety solution capable of responding to in-vehicle emergencies, such as fires and accidents, going beyond a simple vehicle fire extinguisher. ... Safe Life has accumulated product development and market experience amidst the expanding trend of vehicle fire extinguisher distribution in Korea. ... CW Firefighting Industry, the operator, has an annual production capacity of 500,000 fire extinguishers and has expanded its product line for responding to vehicle fires by developing patent-based jet nozzle technology and vehicle mounting straps and holders. ... ""Through our participation in Intersults 2026, we plan to promote the competitiveness of domestic fire safety technology to the global market and expand practical business opportunities with overseas buyers, including those from Europe,"" said a SafeLife official. ""We will actively pursue market expansion to go beyond product exhibitions and lead to export contracts and global partnerships."""
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Home Safe Box Wholesale: Digital Keypad and Emergency Override Key Sys - TIGERKING,www.tigerkingsafe.com,2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tigerkingsafe.com/news/home-safe-box-wholesale-digital-keypad-and-emergency-override-key-systems-for-residential-security-retailers/,"# Home Safe Box Wholesale: Digital Keypad and Emergency Override Key Systems for Residential Security Retailers 2026-05-28 TL;DR — Key Takeaways for Retailers Sourcing Home Safe Box Wholesale ... - The global residential safe locks market reached USD 666 million in 2025 and is projected to grow to USD 1,198 million by ... 2034 at a CAGR of 9.0%, driven by rising home security concerns and demand for digital lock systems. ... - Suppliers like TigerKing Safe (ISO 9001, CE, ETL certified) offer OEM/ODM programs across 5 size tiers from 30XH-1 to 73XH-1, with door thickness of 2+8mm and body thickness of 1.5mm in alloy steel. ... Home safe box wholesale for residential security retailers centers on one critical architectural decision: the lock system. After evaluating over two dozen OEM factories across China's major safe production clusters since 2016, I can tell you that the most reliable configuration for the North American and EU retail markets combines a programmable digital keypad with a mechanical emergency override key system. This is not a matter of preference — it is a matter of compliance, liability, and end-user trust. The digital keypad handles daily access convenience with programmable PIN codes of 3 to 8 digits, while the emergency override key guarantees entry when batteries fail, electronics malfunction, or the code is forgotten. ... A home safe box wholesale program built on this dual-system lock architecture delivers three distinct commercial advantages for retailers: First, it reduces return rates because the backup key solves the most common consumer complaint (forgotten PIN or dead battery). Second, it satisfies UL 1037 and ETL antithe ... testing requirements that mandate mechanical override capability for residential security containers. Third, ... differentiates your product line from budget safes that rely ... single-factor ... . In my experience working with wholesale buyers, the suppliers who treat ... as a serious engineering subsystem — rather than a cheap afterthought — produce dramatically fewer field failures. ... The market data is unambiguous: digital keypad locks now account for an estimated 72% of residential safe lock production worldwide as of 2025, according to analyses from Intel Market Research and industry supply chain data. This dominance exists for a reason. Digital keypads offer fast, repeatable access without requiring the user to keep track of a physical key for every entry. But every experienced importer I have spoken with — and I have sat across the table from dozens at the Canton Fair — knows that electronic-only locks fail at statistically measurable rates. ... major wholesale programs ... 1,000 units shipped ... caused by low-battery scenarios that consumers do not recognize ... of keypad and ... is the de facto ... in 2017, I noticed a persistent pattern: factories that ... include a properly milled emergency override ... mechanism almost always had unresolved issues with their digital ... soldering quality. That correlation has held over nine years of supplier qualification work. Because ... precision machining tolerances — typically within ±0 ... factory that does ... else well too ... Because the emergency override cylinder requires alignment tolerances within 0.05 mm to function smoothly while remaining secure against picking, a factory's CNC machining capability is a direct proxy for overall build quality. TigerKing Safe, operating out of Ningbo since 2000, has invested in precision machining centers that hold these tolerances consistently across their 30XH-1 through 73XH-1 product range. ... set is cut, assembled ... together, then tagged with a matching serial number. That attention to traceability is ... — because if a batch of 500 safes leaves the factory with mismatched keys, the cost of sorting that at retail is devastating. ... The ETL mark from Intertek is recognized by OSHA as equivalent to UL listing. For home ... programs targeting the US market, ETL certification is an acceptable and often more cost-effective compliance path. The critical verification step is to ask for the ETL report number and confirm it matches the exact model ... the General Product Safety Directive (GPSD) ... /EC and the Construction ... Regulation (CPR ... UL and ETL, CE marking ... does not require third ... declaration. This ... actual test data ... Because TigerKing Safe holds ISO 9001, CE, SGS, BSCI, and ETL certifications and has operated since 2000 under Ningbo, the compliance burden for retailers is significantly reduced — you are buying into a pre-verified quality management system, not starting a qualification process from scratch. ... tier home safes (retail ... ) use a hybrid ... mechanical keypad with tactile feedback, an enhanced solenoid rated ... cycles, double ... mm or thicker ... XH-1 ... XH-1 series exemplifies ... alloy steel, ... From a wholesale perspective ... the optimal mix ... premium, because the premium ... generates 2 ... the gross margin per ... level tier drives inventory turnover. I have seen this ... consistently across independent ... Because the global residential safe lock market is projected to grow from USD 666 million in 2025 to USD 1,198 million by 2034 at a CAGR of 9.0%, according to Intel Market Research, now is the strategic window for retailers to establish direct wholesale relationships with certified manufacturers before capacity becomes constrained. ... Most reputable home safe manufacturers in China require an MOQ of 300–500 pieces for standard OEM orders and 1,000+ pieces for custom ODM programs with unique branding, color, or lock configuration. Some factories, including TigerKing Safe, offer flexibility on MOQ for first-time buyers through sample orders of 50–100 pieces at slightly higher per-unit pricing. The key is to start with a pilot order of 2–3 size variants to validate quality and sell-through before committing to full container loads."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Ezviz Launches AI Hardware Line, Prioritizes Security in Smart Home Strategy | Gate News",www.gate.com,2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gate.com/news/detail/ezviz-launches-ai-hardware-line-prioritizes-security-in-smart-home-strategy-20500992,"On April 21, smart home leader Ezviz (688475.SH) held its 2026 brand launch event, announcing multiple AI-powered hardware products and emphasizing security as the foundational principle of its product development strategy. Chief Product Officer Chen Guanlan stated that regardless of industry trends over the past decade—from single-product connectivity to whole-home intelligence to current large language model adoption—the company maintains security as its first principle and lifeline for user experience. ... At the April 21 event, Ezviz launched multiple AI hardware products including an AI large model host, AI portable camera, AI panoramic smart lock, and AI steam cleaning robot. The company also upgraded its brand mission from ""enabling everyone to easily enjoy safe intelligent living"" to ""co-creating a better life with safe intelligent technology."" ... The core product is the EZVIZ AI CoreX, a local intelligence hub deployed in homes. As a key edge-side component in Ezviz's ""cloud-edge-device"" collaborative architecture, the EZVIZ AI CoreX incorporates the Lanhai large model 2.0 and Home Vita agent, featuring 64T computing power and supporting whole-home device aggregation, natural language retrieval, and automated scenario linkage. The product will first launch in overseas markets. ... In the smart home camera segment, Ezviz expanded its product line. The ""Magic Cube"" CB60 Pro battery 4G waterproof version upgraded radar penetration detection, GPS+BeiDou positioning, dust and water resistance, and removable magnetic base for complex outdoor environments. In 2025, Ezviz launched the CB60, a 4G battery-powered mobile camera, which the company identified as a bestselling product in an April 11 earnings briefing. ... Ezviz also launched the Akiitu sub-brand targeting outdoor enthusiasts and sports-oriented consumers. According to company representatives, this reflects two strategic observations: historically, the company focused less on individual consumers; and while the company began considering personal mobile IoT in 2022, its applications remained fixed-form IoT. The CB60 broke this business boundary by introducing mobility, and Akiitu represents a new product category with different brand positioning from Ezviz's family security focus. ... ## Market Position and Geographic Expansion ... In the smart home camera sector, Ezviz holds a leading market position. According to IDC reports, the company's shipments ranked first globally in 2025. The company is expanding beyond its traditional home security base to address outdoor consumer needs. ... Geographically, Ezviz is experiencing significant overseas growth. In 2025, domestic revenue reached 35.30 billion yuan, representing 60.16% of total revenue with 1.25% year-over-year growth. Overseas revenue reached 23.38 billion yuan, representing 39.84% of total revenue with 22.27% year-over-year growth. In an earnings briefing, the company indicated that overseas revenue share is rising and will gradually exceed domestic revenue, describing this as a clear trend. Overseas product shipments are progressively approaching or exceeding domestic shipments. ... Ezviz's 2025 full-year revenue totaled 59.01 billion yuan, representing 8.44% year-over-year growth. Net profit attributable to listed company shareholders reached 5.67 billion yuan, up 12.43% year-over-year. Operating cash flow increased significantly to 11.20 billion yuan, up 104.30% year-over-year. ... Within product categories, the smart home camera business—the company's core segment—generated 31.80 billion yuan in 2025 revenue, up 7.87% year-over-year, with gross margin improving 2.14 percentage points to 39.33%. The smart entry business, serving as the second growth curve, achieved 9.36 billion yuan in revenue, up 25.25% year-over-year, with gross margin improving 4.86 percentage points to 47.39%. ... In the first quarter of 2026, Ezviz achieved revenue of 14.13 billion yuan, up 2.36% year-over-year. Net profit attributable to listed company shareholders reached 1.83 billion yuan, up 32.30% year-over-year. ... Ezviz's predecessor was established in 2013 as the internet business division of Hikvision. In 2015, Hikvision established Ezviz as a subsidiary. The company listed on the Shanghai Stock Exchange Science and Technology Board in December 2022, becoming Hikvision's first listed subsidiary. Ezviz specializes in smart home and IoT cloud platform services, holding leading market positions in smart home cameras, smart video doorbells, and smart locks. ... As of the end of 2025, Ezviz's IoT cloud platform operates over 120 global data centers with more than 3.6 billion IoT devices connected to the platform, including over 3 billion video devices."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,PVC flooring maker Kingdom New Material files for Hong Kong IPO - The Yangtzeer,yangtzeer.com (Yangtzeer observers),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://yangtzeer.com/news/deals/pvc-flooring-kingdom-hk-ipo/,"PVC flooring maker Kingdom New Material files for Hong Kong IPO - The Yangtzeer ... - Jiaxing company plans Hungary, Thailand expansion as overseas sales dominate revenue - Europe accounts for more than 85% of 2025 revenue despite North America margin pressure ... Kingdom New Material Group (晶通新材料集团), one of China’s largest exporters of PVC decorative materials, has filed for a Hong Kong initial public offering as it looks to expand production in Europe and Southeast Asia amid rising global demand for vinyl flooring and wall panels. ... The Jiaxing-based company submitted its listing application to the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on May 27, with China International Capital Corporation acting as sole sponsor. ... Proceeds from the IPO — with fundraising size and share count yet to be finalized — are expected to support a new wall panel production base in Tongxiang — a county-level city governed by Jiaxing — a green manufacturing facility in Hungary, and expansion of its Thailand plant. ... According to the prospectus, Kingdom ranked first among suppliers in China’s PVC decorative materials export market by total export value in 2025, with products sold across more than 60 countries and regions. ... Kingdom operates under both ODM and OEM models and launches more than 300 self-developed flooring products and 100 wall panel products annually. ... Revenue rose from 1.6 billion yuan ($236 million) in 2023 to 2.22 billion yuan in 2024 and 2.31 billion yuan in 2025, while net profit increased from 230 million yuan to 337 million yuan and 361 million yuan over the same period, according to the filing. ... Gross margins remained relatively stable between 35.9% and 37%. ... The company, however, remains heavily dependent on overseas markets, which accounted for more than 98% of revenue during the reporting period. Europe was its largest market, contributing 1.97 billion yuan in revenue in 2025, or 85.3% of the total. ... While North American sales grew rapidly, gross margins in the region fell to 6.3% from 27.7% because of high unit costs tied to low utilization rates at its newly built Thailand factory, which operated at only 17.9% capacity."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Nongfu Spring founder backs solid-state battery materials push - The Yangtzeer,yangtzeer.com (admin),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://yangtzeer.com/news/deals/nongfu-founder-solid-battery-materials/,"Nongfu Spring founder backs solid-state battery materials push - The Yangtzeer ... - Billionaire expands portfolio into solid-state electrolyte supply chain for first time - Move adds energy materials to upstream-focused investment strategy ... Chinese billionaire and Nongfu Spring founder Zhong Shanshan has made his first known investment in new energy materials, backing a Zhejiang-based solid-state battery startup through a private fund structure, according to the China Entrepreneur magazine. ... In May 2026, a private equity fund controlled through Zhong’s holding company Yangshengtang led the Series A round of Zhejiang Zhibang Lithium Battery New Material Co., a startup founded in March 2024 that develops solid-state electrolytes. ... The Kunshan Gewu Zhizhi Phase I Venture Capital Fund executed the investment and now holds about 10% of the company. ... Yangshengtang provides the fund’s core capital. It contributed about 500 million yuan ($73.76 million) and holds roughly 81% of the vehicle. Zhong controls Yangshengtang. Through this structure, he holds an indirect stake of about 10% in Zhibang Lithium Battery. ... The deal marks Zhong’s first move into EV battery materials. It also extends his strategy of targeting upstream industrial sectors rather than consumer-facing businesses. ... Zhibang Lithium Battery is based in Quzhou, Zhejiang province. It develops solid-state electrolytes for next-generation batteries. The company pursues three technical routes: oxide, polymer and sulfide systems. ... In April, the company disclosed a patent for a high-performance polyvinylidene fluoride-based solid electrolyte. ... Local government disclosures show the company plans annual capacity of 11,000 tons of solid-state electrolyte materials. It targets electric vehicle supply chains, including potential links to Geely and BYD. ... State-backed investors hold about 15% of the company, making them the second-largest shareholder group after the founding team. ... Notably, this is not Zhong’s first cross-sector bet. Yangshengtang-linked capital has invested in biomedical materials such as recombinant collagen, electronic chemicals including photoresists, and agricultural assets such as ancient tea trees in Yunnan and fruit bases in Xinjiang. ... The pattern is consistent. Zhong focuses on upstream segments with technical or resource barriers and avoids downstream, often ruthless consumer competition. ... Analysts describe the approach as a “pick-and-shovel” strategy. It targets foundational inputs in industries where end-market competition is already intense and key technologies such as solid-state electrolytes remain unresolved. ... The fund structure gives Zhong flexibility and limits direct exposure to execution risk in a capital-intensive emerging sector, analysts say."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,The 16th China (Yongkang) International Door Industry Expo Polishes the “Capital of Doors” Brand - CHINA MINUTES,chinaminutes.com (China Minutes),2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://chinaminutes.com/2026/05/27/the-16th-china-yongkang-international-door-industry-expo-polishes-the-capital-of-doors-brand/,"An expo focusing on doors opened in Yongkang, Zhejiang’s “Capital of Doors”, showcasing the latest innovations, technologies, and trends across the global door industry chain. ... On May 26, the three-day 16th China (Yongkang) International Door Industry Expo opened at the Yongkang International Convention and Exhibition Centre. Bringing together upstream and downstream resources across the entire door industry chain, this year’s expo features five indoor exhibition halls and one outdoor exhibition hall. Exhibits cover eight major categories, including household doors, electric doors, customised home furnishings, door accessories, door materials, windows, locks, and equipment. ... Yongkang, in Zhejiang Province, is widely known as China’s “Capital of Doors”. It is one of the world’s most concentrated hubs for the door manufacturing industry, with the broadest market reach, the strongest standards leadership, and outstanding achievements in technological innovation and brand development. As a major industry event rooted in Yongkang, the Door Expo has, after more than a decade of growth and refinement, evolved from a regional trade fair into a highly influential professional exhibition for China and the global door industry. It has become not only an important driver for the high-quality development of Yongkang’s door industry, but also an “industry vane” for new product launches, technological exchanges, business matchmaking, resource sharing, and observing industry trends. ... This year’s expo continues to demonstrate strong appeal. Since online booth applications opened, enterprises from across China and abroad have actively registered to participate. Statistics show that 621 domestic and international companies have confirmed participation this year, among which 339 companies are from outside the Yongkang-Wuyi-Jinyun region, accounting for 54.5% of the total. ... Every edition of the Door Expo brings fresh highlights, and this year is no exception. Compared with previous editions, this year’s expo has further optimised its exhibition layout by introducing several featured zones, including an automatic and electric door exhibition area, a Xiaolan lock exhibition area, an outdoor aluminium art door exhibition area, and a door accessories exhibition area (Hardware City market). The more refined and specialised layout enables buyers to visit exhibits with greater precision and conduct business matchmaking more efficiently. ... To further enhance exhibition effectiveness, this year’s expo continues to focus on digitalisation by maintaining both online and offline venues, providing “digital wings” for the event through a dual-platform model. During the expo, it hosted special sourcing fairs for the “Belt and Road” countries, as well as Europe and the US. Over 100 professional international buyers from dozens of countries have been invited to attend, creating a practical and highly efficient matchmaking platform for suppliers and buyers. ... Leveraging exhibitions to gather wisdom and conferences to empower the industry, the expo is also holding four industry conferences alongside the exhibition activities: the 1st Members’ Congress of Outdoor Aluminum Art Doors and Building Products Industry, the 9th Architectural Door Industry Technology Innovation and Development Conference, the launch meeting for drafting the national standard Steel Doors and Windows, and a symposium on the application of new materials for architectural doors and windows. These events focus on topics such as urban renewal, residential design, and steel door and window standards, injecting fresh momentum into the high-quality development of the industry. ... Another highlight is the debut of the Yongkang Hardware Outlets Factory Store, innovatively created by the Hardware City Group, which officially entered trial operation during the expo. Integrating cost-effective local hardware products, the factory store introduces a new retail format and adds a fresh consumer experience scenario to the exhibition. ... Exhibition services have also been comprehensively upgraded. In addition to continuing convenient measures such as free admission, free parking, and free shuttle bus routes, the expo has improved the overall visitor experience through comprehensive venue environment upgrades, renovation of facilities and equipment, enhanced catering services, and strengthened safety and security measures, providing exhibitors and buyers with more thoughtful and professional services."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Exploring Technology Acquires Controlling Stake in Yiwu Blanket King for 1.7 Billion Yuan, Enters AI Market – China Money Network",www.chinamoneynetwork.com,2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.chinamoneynetwork.com/2026/05/27/exploring-technology-acquires-controlling-stake-in-yiwu-blanket-king-for-1-7-billion-yuan-enters-ai-market,"Exploring Technology Acquires Controlling Stake in Yiwu Blanket King for 1.7 Billion Yuan, Enters AI Market – China Money Network ... # Exploring Technology Acquires Controlling Stake in Yiwu Blanket King for 1.7 Billion Yuan, Enters AI Market ... - May 27, 2026 — 12:50 CST ... Exploring Far Horizon, through a precise proportion of equity acquisition and active tender offer, secured 43.00% stake in True Love Home with an investment of... [DATA LOCKED]"
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Philips Launches Climate-Engineered Smart Locks in Saudi Arabia,www.propertynewsint.com,2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.propertynewsint.com/news/philips-launches-climate-engineered-smart-locks-in-saudi-arabia,"3. Philips Launches Climate-Engineered Smart Locks in Saudi Arabia ... # Philips Launches Climate-Engineered Smart Locks in Saudi Arabia ... May. 27, 2026 ... Philips launched climate-engineered smart locks in Saudi Arabia through Jarir Bookstore as the Kingdom’s smart home market continues rapid growth. ... RIYADH, SAUDI ARABIA - Philips Smart Locks has officially launched in Saudi Arabia through a strategic partnership with Jarir Bookstore, introducing a new portfolio of climate-engineered smart home access solutions designed specifically for the Kingdom’s environmental conditions and rapidly expanding smart living sector. ... The launch, developed by official licensee Conex and brought to the Saudi market by exclusive local distributor Kiwi Information Technology, reflects the growing demand for integrated security and smart home technologies across the Kingdom as digital adoption accelerates under Vision 2030. ... Timed alongside the Eid Al Adha period and a major promotional campaign at Jarir Bookstore, the launch marks a significant expansion for Philips within the Gulf’s evolving smart home and residential technology landscape. ... The Saudi smart home market continues to experience strong growth, supported by rising internet penetration, increasing consumer demand for connected living solutions, and wider national digital transformation initiatives. ... Industry projections estimate that Saudi Arabia’s smart lock market could expand from approximately $355 million in 2025 to more than $931 million by 2034, representing a compound annual growth rate of 11.25%. ... More broadly, ... security and access control segment remains one of the strongest-performing areas within the Kingdom’s ... home industry, accounting for a substantial share of sector revenues ... prioritise convenience, automation, and enhanced residential security. ... The launch also highlights a growing focus on localisation and climate-specific engineering within the region’s consumer technology sector. ... Recognising the challenges posed by Saudi Arabia’s extreme temperatures, dust exposure, and high-frequency usage conditions, the newly launched Philips smart locks have been specifically engineered for long-term performance in Gulf environments. ... The initial product line available through Jarir Bookstore includes two flagship models designed for both residential convenience and durability. ... The Philips DDL611 is positioned as the first dual-verification smart lock engineered specifically for the Saudi market, featuring dual fingerprint recognition technology and a design intended for outdoor installation under harsh climate conditions. ... Alongside it, the Philips DDL610 combines a minimalist premium design with high durability standards, featuring an IP65 certification for dust and water resistance suitable for both indoor and outdoor applications. ... The decision to launch through Jarir Bookstore reflects a strategic retail positioning effort aimed at leveraging one of Saudi Arabia’s largest and most established consumer electronics and technology retail networks. ... With 59 stores across the Kingdom, Jarir continues to serve as a major gateway for international technology and consumer brands entering the Saudi market. ... The wider distribution strategy is being led by Kiwi Information Technology, which has been expanding Philips Home Access operations in Saudi Arabia since 2023 through partnerships with retailers including SACO, EXTRA, and e-commerce platforms such as Noon. ... The company has also been strengthening ties within the Kingdom’s construction and real estate sectors. During Big 5 Construct Saudi 2026, Kiwi signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Al Ghomlas Trading Company aimed at deploying Philips Home Access solutions across residential and commercial developments. ... The partnership signals a broader long-term strategy focused on integrating smart access technologies into Saudi Arabia’s growing pipeline of residential, mixed-use, and commercial projects. ... For homeowners, the launch introduces a wider range of connected security solutions that align with shifting lifestyle preferences and growing demand for digitally integrated living environments. ... The systems also provide users with detailed ... monitoring and remote management capabilities, supporting greater convenience during travel periods, guest hosting, and day-to-day residential management. ... Kiwi Information Technology stated that the Saudi launch forms part of a broader regional expansion strategy aimed at growing the Philips Home Access portfolio across the Middle East while supporting localised installation, sales, and after-sales services designed to strengthen consumer confidence and long-term adoption."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Philips Smart Locks Launch at Jarir Bookstore,www.globenewswire.com (Philips),2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/05/26/3300957/0/en/Philips-Smart-Locks-Launch-at-Jarir-Bookstore.html,"RIYADH, Saudi Arabia, May 26, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Philips Smart Locks, developed by Conex — official Philips licensee for Smart locks — are now available at Jarir Bookstore across Saudi Arabia. Kiwi Information Technology, the exclusive local distributor, has officially launched the products at Jarir Bookstore, a leading consumer electronics retail platform trusted throughout the Gulf region. ... With its extensive store network and strong customer base, Jarir Bookstore serves as a prime gateway for international brands to reach Saudi consumers. ... Since entering the Saudi market in 2023, Kiwi has been dedicated to promoting Philips home access products. The Jarir Bookstore listing marks another milestone in Kiwi's market expansion, enabling local households to easily access reliable, high-quality Philips home access solutions through established retail channels. ... Philips's smart lock portfolio for the Saudi market centers on home entry security, with each model purpose-engineered for the region's demanding climate. The newly launched products include the DDL611 and DDL610 from the Philips Smart Lock series, both developed and manufactured by Conex under official Philips licensing. ... DDL611: Philips DDL611 is the first dual-verification smart lock engineered for the Saudi market. Featuring dual fingerprint recognition, it is purpose-built for outdoor installation — Saudi Arabia's first smart lock designed from the ground up to withstand the region's extreme heat, sand, and high-frequency use. ... DDL610: Philips DDL610, designed for modern Saudi homes, and combines premium minimalist architectural aesthetics with IP65-certified protection, making it perfectly suited for both elegant indoor spaces and outdoor entrance doors exposed to heat and dust. ... Both models support multiple unlocking methods, including fingerprint access, PIN code entry, mobile app control, and mechanical key backup, providing flexibility and security for modern households. ... Coinciding with Jarir Bookstore's major promotion and Eid al-Adha season, Philips Smart Locks are available at special prices. As Saudi families increasingly prioritize home security and smart upgrades during the festive period, smart locks are becoming essential to modern living. ... Kiwi said this partnership reflects its commitment to the Saudi market through localized sales, installation, and after-sales support. ... Looking ahead, Kiwi will continue expanding the Philips Home Access portfolio across the Middle East, bringing safer and more convenient smart home solutions to consumers throughout the region. ... Philips Home Access Expands its Smart Deadbolt Lineup with New Handleset combos for Prime Day ... Philips smart locks offer Prime Day savings up to 40% on selected built-in Wi-Fi models with fingerprint access, app control, and keyless entry."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Zendure aims to lead in AI-driven home energy management systems,kr-asia.com (Cheng Zi),2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://kr-asia.com/zendure-aims-to-lead-in-ai-driven-home-energy-management-systems,"Liu Bingbin, founder and CEO of Guangzhou Jianghai Technology, the company behind Zendure. Photo source: Zendure.The company is expanding into AI-driven home energy solutions. ... Over the past five years, Zendure has achieved an annualized growth rate of more than 102%. Widely regarded in the industry as a pioneer of balcony energy storage, the company aims in 2026 to enter hundreds of thousands of European households, rank first in total sales in France, and lead direct-to-consumer sites in Germany. ... In his view, energy storage is only the hardware foundation. The real barrier lies in the ecosystem and artificial intelligence. Zendure has made several early moves on this path: connecting with more than 840 European electricity suppliers, integrating with more than 5,000 heat pump models, and becoming the first company in its category to connect with Shelly, one of Europe’s largest home energy management platforms. Liu said these moves have put rivals at least a year behind. ... At the end of 2025, Zendure received an investment from Han’s Laser, filling a supply chain gap. Around the same time, ZenWave, its dynamic electricity retail service, went live in Germany, marking Zendure’s shift from selling hardware to selling energy services. ... Zendure is currently raising a Series C funding round, with several leading institutions participating. According to Liu, the process has moved faster than expected. ... Liu told 36Kr that the funds will be used mainly for R&D and expansion into new markets. “Our vision is to become the home energy hub for the artificial intelligence era, just as the PC was the computing host of the information era. In an increasingly volatile future, households around the world will all need it. That means we can eventually enter tens of millions or even hundreds of millions of homes,” he said. ... . Our vision is ... Our first-generation product already had home energy management capabilities. In September 2023, we were the first to connect with Shelly, Europe’s largest home energy management platform. Rivals only connected in September 2024. We also connected with Tesla, becoming the first company in the balcony energy storage space capable of supporting electric vehicles. We can also manage more than 5,000 heat pump models and have connected with more than 840 European electricity suppliers. ... The ZenWave dynamic electricity retail service is a key part of our ecosystem upgrade. This service first went live in Germany and is accelerating expansion to other European countries, providing real-time electricity pricing mechanisms and 100% green electricity. Combined with smart scheduling and AI, home energy management can be upgraded from manual adjustment to system-level automation. ... Based on these ecosystems, our goal is to reach one million users by the end of 2027. ... this field for ... When the product first came out in 2023, the market had no such concept ... We initially used a direct-to-consumer strategy to push the product quickly ... generated EUR 4 million (USD ... 25, ... grown faster. ... So when we encountered Han’s Laser in 2025, the two sides immediately aligned. Han’s is a global leader in upstream lithium battery supply chains and automation equipment, with extensive lithium battery industry resources. But in the energy field, it lacked a company that understood the European market, could build a consumer-facing brand, and had R&D capabilities. We complemented each other well. With support from Han’s supply chain resources, our performance began breaking out in the first quarter of this year, growing nearly 200% year-on-year. ... LB: On one hand, it helped us establish a European headquarters in Switzerland as a strategic base covering all of Europe. Han’s European headquarters is also in Switzerland, which is helpful for building a mid- to high-end brand image. ... More importantly, in ... LB: Growth mainly comes from our own development. One factor is fast product iteration, from the first to the fourth generation, with each iteration covering more customers. Another is country expansion, from Germany to France to the Netherlands, and next the UK. The UK has just announced that it will open up balcony energy storage. Many users are urging us to enter the UK market. ... We believe this is a worldwide shift, and we are the force behind it. Plug-and-play small microinverters are a basic consumer right. They should not be monopolized by the grid. Low-power inverters below 800 watts have no impact on the grid. Countries around the world will sooner or later accept this standard, which is also the basis for our confidence in future growth. ... In addition, we are continuously expanding the power boundaries and application scenarios of balcony energy storage, such as adding storage for existing rooftop PV systems. This is also a promising market. ... LB: It is hard to generalize, because demand and development stages differ from country to country. German users are the most mature and educated, with a very large DIY user base. But in other countries, rooftop storage may come first. The Netherlands, for example, has more than three million existing rooftop PV users. In 2027, feed-in tariff subsidies will end, and all these users will urgently need to add storage. ... : Unlike traditional residential ... depends heavily on national subsidy policies, balcony ... storage is market-driven rather than policy-driven. For example, existing ... PV users are beginning to buy ... energy storage precisely because feed-in tariff subsidies are phasing out. ... Globally, there are 40 million existing rooftop PV systems, and the storage pairing rate is only about 10%. After subsidies phase out, these users must shift to self-consumption, making storage a rigid need. Traditional residential energy ... in Europe and the US costs several thousand euros in installation fees. Our system has zero installation cost. The total price is only around EUR ... 1,000 (USD 1,162.9), giving it a clear advantage. ... As for the 800W policy limit for balcony energy storage, more than 20 European countries have already opened up, while the UK and US are also opening. This is a worldwide shift and an irreversible trend. We only need to follow the trend. ... LB: Revenue is still mainly hardware for now, but our focus is quickly shifting toward software and services. We are a third-party electricity supplier. Through ZenWave electricity retail, we capture electricity price spreads, and this is recurring revenue. ... LB: It gained several hundred subscriptions in the first month, far exceeding our expectations. One user in Dusseldorf saved more than EUR 100 (USD 116.3) in a month after switching to us. ... LB: We are working on a Series C round, mainly with market-based funds. Allocation is highly sought after, and this round has far exceeded expectations. The funds will mainly be used for R&D and new market expansion. ... On software, the main focus is ... LB: We are already doing this. Our electric cargo bike will launch in the second half of this year. We are the only company in the balcony energy storage industry doing this. We have expanded from the home to short-distance outdoor mobility in the yard. ... LB: To lead Europe’s plug-in home energy management system market, reach one million users, and complete an IPO. Personally, I lean more toward a Hong Kong listing, because 99% of our revenue comes from overseas. A Hong Kong listing would benefit our overseas business and brand, and would serve as a concentrated brand upgrade for our channels, energy suppliers, and installer ecosystem partners in Europe and North America. ... I have communicated with some European investors. Once our brand is mentioned, they all say they are very familiar with it. Because our strategic focus over the years has been overseas, we have kept a low profile in China, so China’s capital markets do not feel our brand as strongly."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,"Hangzhou Safe Deposit Box Export Agency, Solve Customs Clearance and Tax Refund Pain Points - Zhongshen Trading China","www.sh-zhongshen.com (Shanghai Zhong Shen International Trading Co., Ltd.)",2026-05-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sh-zhongshen.com/en/news/hangzhou-safe-deposit-box-export-agent-solve-customs-clearance-tax-refund-problems.html,"In 2026，Hangzhou's safe deposit box exports to Europe grew by 23%，but policy barriers such as updated EU CE certification and REACH regulation restrictions pushed up the cargo detention rate by 11 percentage points. Hangzhou export enterprises face problems such as document discrepancies，customs clearance delays and tax refund delays. With 20 years of experience in foreign trade agency，Zhongshen has built a system covering policy early warning，document pre-review and customs clearance coordination to help customers avoid risks and improve efficiency.。 ... In the first half of 2026,Mr.Dai from a security equipment company in Hangzhou encountered a problem: a batch of safe deposit boxes bound for Germany was detained by EU customs,as the submitted CE certification did not cover the EN 15221-1 lock safety standard updated in 2025.This is not an isolated case.According to data from the Hangzhou Cross-Border E-Commerce Comprehensive Pilot Zone,Hangzhou’s safe deposit box export value increased by 23% year-on-year from January to June 2026,but the cargo detention rate by EU customs due to document discrepancies and expired certifications rose by 11 percentage points from 2025.In addition to certification barriers,adjustments to tariff schedules (some countries classify safe deposit boxes as ""security equipment"" instead of ""furniture"",raising the tariff rate from 5% to 8%) and REACH regulation restrictions on lock materials also give many Hangzhou export enterprises a headache. ... As a Shanghai-based enterprise with over 20 years of in-depth experience in foreign trade agency,Zhongshen has built a full-process service system covering ""policy early warning,document pre-review,customs clearance coordination and tax refund acceleration"" targeting the pain points of Hangzhou safe deposit box exports to Europe.Mr.Ning,head of foreign trade business at Zhongshen,noted that his team updates the trade policy database for EU countries every month.In 2026 alone,they adjusted the service process 3 times in response to safe deposit box export policy changes in Germany,France and the Netherlands,helping 12 Hangzhou clients avoid cargo detention risks. ... There are two core barriers to EU document requirements for safe deposit boxes: first,CE certification must comply with the EN 15221-1 standard updated in 2025,which adds laboratory testing requirements for drill and pry resistance of locks; second,the certificate of origin must use the electronic EUR.1 format and fully match the commodity code (HS code: 830110) on the customs declaration form. ... - Pre-reviewinadvance:Aftertheclientsubmitsc ... ificationdocuments,thedocumentteamcompletes ... complianceverificationwithin24hours.Ifmissingtestitemsarefound,theteamwillcoordinatewithEU-recognizedthird-partytestinginstitutionstoassistinsupplementation; - Electronicdocumentsystem:ConnectedtothedocumentsystemsofHangzhouElectronicPortandEUCustomsGeneralAdministration,itautomaticallyverifiestheEUR.1formatandHScodematchingdegree.Since2026,thedocumentpassrateofHangzhouclientshasreached100%; - Tariffschedulematching:InresponsetoGermany’spolicyof ... securityequipment"",theteamassistsclientsinadjustingthe ... descriptiononthe ... sdeclarationformtoavoidincorrecttariffapplication,whichhashelpeds ... clientssave3 ... ontariffcosts. ... In 2026,the random inspection rate for security products by EU customs rose to 18%,and the focus of random inspection for safe deposit boxes is the REACH regulation compliance of locks,which prohibits the use of 15 high-risk heavy metals.Mr.Dai’s previous agency failed to submit the REACH compliance declaration for locks in advance,resulting in the cargo being detained at Hamburg Port for 7 days,while the average customs clearance time for Zhongshen’s clients is only 4 days. ... Hangzhou adjusted its export tax refund policy in 2026,requiring that the ""commodity name"" on the customs declaration form be completely consistent with the ""goods name"" on the value-added tax invoice,and that the ""Confirmation Form for FOB Price of Export Goods"" be submitted through the electronic tax bureau.Some Hangzhou enterprises suffered tax refund delays of more than 15 days due to discrepancies in product name descriptions,for example,the invoice stated ""safe box"" while the customs declaration form stated ""safe deposit box"". ... - Productnamematchingverification:Thedocumentsystemautomaticallycomparestheproductnamesonthecustomsdeclarationformandthevalue-addedtaxinvoice.Ifdiscrepanciesarefound,theclientwillbenotifiedwithin1hourtoadjusttheinvoice; - Dedicatedtaxrefundspecialistfollow-up:Eachclientisassignedataxrefundspecialisttofollowuptheentiredeclarationprocessontheelectronictaxbureau.Since2026,theaveragetaxrefundreceipttimeforHangzhouclientsis7workingdays,comparedwiththeindustryaverageof10workingdays; - FOBpriceconfirmation:TheteamassistsclientsinprovidingdocumentssuchasoceanbillsofladingandfreightinvoicestoaccuratelyconfirmtheFOBprice,avoidingtaxrefundreviewdelayscausedbypricedisputes. ... First,""proactive policy early warning"": After the EU announced the updated CE certification standard at the end of 2025,Zhongshen immediately organized policy interpretation sessions for Hangzhou clients,helping 5 clients complete certification updates 3 months in advance,avoiding cargo detention risks after January 2026; ... Second,""system automatic matching"": The independently developed foreign trade agency system can automatically synchronize the customs declaration data of Hangzhou Electronic Port with the customs clearance requirements of EU customs.Since 2026,the average safe deposit box export clearance time for Hangzhou clients has been shortened by 3 days,and the tax refund time has been shortened by 2 days. ... Manager Qian,foreign trade manager of a security company in Hangzhou,previously chose a small local agency.A batch of safe deposit boxes exported to France in March 2026 was detained due to expired CE certification.After switching to Zhongshen,the cargo exported in June completed customs clearance in only 3 days,and the tax refund was received in 7 days.""We don’t have to worry about policy changes now.Zhongshen’s team will remind us to prepare the required documents in advance."" ... Zhongshen’s services are not standardized,but customized based on the product specifications of Hangzhou clients (such as small household safe deposit boxes,large commercial safe deposit boxes) and target countries (such as Germany,the Netherlands,Poland): ... | Client Type | Target Country | Core Demand | Zhongshen Customized Service | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Exporters of small household safe deposit boxes | France | Low tariff,fast customs clearance | Assist in classification under ""furniture"" HS code (5% tariff rate),submit REACH declaration in advance | | Exporters of large commercial safe deposit boxes | Germany | Compliance certification,emergency handling | Supplement EN 15221-1 test report,establish emergency re-inspection channel | | Cross-border e-commerce sellers | The Netherlands | Bulk customs clearance,accelerated tax refund | Apply EU VAT deferral policy,declare tax refund in batches | | Hangzhou start-up security enterprises | Poland | Policy interpretation,cost control | Provide free policy training,optimize customs declaration process to reduce costs | ... In 2026,Hangzhou’s safe deposit box exports to Europe face both market opportunities and policy challenges.Choosing the right agency is the key to solving compliance issues and improving efficiency.With 20 years of foreign trade agency experience,Zhongshen provides customized full-process services for Hangzhou clients targeting policy barriers in various EU countries,helping enterprises avoid cargo detention risks,shorten customs clearance time and accelerate tax refund receipt.If you are a safe deposit box exporter in Hangzhou,you may contact Zhongshen to customize an exclusive agency plan based on your products and target countries."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Exa,Private Label Safes: How Brands Can Build a Profitable Safe Product Li - TIGERKING,www.tigerkingsafe.com,2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tigerkingsafe.com/news/private-label-safes-how-brands-can-build-a-profitable-safe-product-line/,"### TigerKing Debuts Retro Fireproof Jewelry Safe Series: Timeless Vintage Aesthetics Combined with Dual Fire & Burglary Protection ... 2026-05-13 ... Tigerking Safe is relevant to this search because NINGBO TIGER KING SAFE CO., LTD. describes itself as a China-based developer and manufacturer of intelligent safes established in 2000. Its public website lists certifications including ISO9001, CSP, CE, SGS, BSCI, and ETL, and it describes the use of 6S and lean production methodologies. The company also states that its safes are exported to North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia Pacific, and South America, with customization as a core part of serving global customers. This article explains how a professional buyer should evaluate the topic of private label safe manufacturer and how to turn a content search into a serious supplier conversation. ... Tigerking Safe's public company profile states that the company was established in 2000 and works as a China-based developer and manufacturer of intelligent safes. It also states that its products are exported to North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia Pacific, and South America. For an overseas buyer, these facts are useful because export-oriented suppliers are usually more familiar with carton labeling, product documentation, destination-market expectations, and communication around bulk-order details. ... For this article's product direction, Tigerking's relevant public product facts include models such as custom safe and OEM/ODM product lines. Tigerking describes itself as a China-based intelligent safe developer and manufacturer founded in 2000, with customization, 6S management, lean production, and certifications including ISO9001, CSP, CE, SGS, BSCI, and ETL. These are useful because they give buyers concrete conversation starters. For example, if a fireproof safe model mentions 60-minute fire protection, the buyer should ask how that claim is documented, which model it applies to, and whether the rating language can appear on packaging in ... target market. If a commercial drop safe mentions a 6mm steel door and three 28mm bolts, the buyer should ask whether those details are stable across all sizes or specific to one SKU ... Tigerking fits best in a shortlist when the buyer needs a China-based safe manufacturer with broad product categories, documented export positioning, customization support, and public product pages for fireproof, hotel, commercial, gun, fingerprint, and digital safes. The company should not be evaluated by brand name alone. It should be evaluated by how well its specific models match the buyer's market. ... For this topic, buyers should start with the relevant internal page: About Tigerking product page. From ... can identify models that ... their intended application. A ... buyer may focus on fireproof safes with ... protection claims and carton resilience ... A hotel buyer may focus on keypad/card access, override keys, mounting holes ... A commercial buyer may focus on drop ... slot design, anti-fishing baffles, bolt strength, ... lockout mode. A ... focus on design consistency, packaging customization ... recommendation is to shortlist suppliers in ... export markets, ... : certificates, product specifications, photos, packaging, test evidence ... execution: communication speed ... Tigerking's public company profile states that customization is prioritized for global customers. Buyers should provide exact requirements for logo, color, lock type, packaging, manual language, and target market. ... Tigerking Safe's public website provides enough information to justify a detailed sourcing conversation: the company history from 2000, intelligent safe manufacturing positioning, global export language, customization focus, listed certifications, and multiple product categories. The buyer's job is to turn those public signals into project-specific proof. When that happens, content is no longer just SEO. It becomes a bridge between search intent and a qualified B2B inquiry."
ZHEJIANG KINGSAFE IMPORT,,,,Perplexity,Kingfa Science & Technology (India) standalone net profit rises 41.17% in the March 2026 quarter,Business Standard,2026-05-30T00:00:00Z,2026-05-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.business-standard.com/markets/capital-market-news/kingfa-science-technology-india-standalone-net-profit-rises-41-17-in-the-march-2026-quarter-126053000175_1.html,"Reports that Kingfa Science & Technology (India) posted a 41.17% quarter-on-quarter rise in standalone net profit to Rs 59.15 crore in the March 2026 quarter, with full-year net profit up 21.20% to Rs 185.26 crore. This is relevant for procurement strategy because it signals improved earnings momentum and may strengthen the supplier’s negotiating position on pricing and terms."
