BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,From briefing to finished product: industry leading companies bring sustainable label production to life at LOUPE Americas 2026 (formerly Labelexpo Americas),www.packagingworldinsights.com (API PWI),2026-08-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingworldinsights.com/press-releases/from-briefing-to-finished-product-industry-leading-companies-bring-sustainable-label-production-to-life-at-loupe-americas-2026-formerly-labelexpo-americas/,"Avery Dennison, CarbonQuota, CERM, Esko, Grafisk Maskinfabrik (GM), KURZ, SCRIBOS and Flint Group Digital Xeikon join forces to showcase innovative and carbon-reducing live label production this September. Attendees to LOUPE Americas 2026 (formerly Labelexpo Americas) will be able to experience a live production of sustainable labels from inception to finish, thanks to a collaboration engaging some of the labels and package printing industry’s leading companies: Avery Dennison, CarbonQuota, CERM, Esko, Grafisk Maskinfabrik (GM), KURZ, SCRIBOS and Flint Group Digital Xeikon. ... With over 400 exhibitors, a revitalized focus on education and expanded technology showcase, LOUPE Americas 2026 is the ideal platform to stage the initiative, which is guided by a brief featuring fictional brand “Dancing Fish” which is expanding into the nutritional supplements market. Requirements include producing new food-safe labels while also measuring and reducing its carbon footprint. To ensure product authenticity and consumer safety, brand protection features need to be integrated into the labels of its new nutritional supplements line. ... Participants will gain insights into how low-impact materials, carbon measurement and sustainable processes contribute to reducing environmental impact, aligning with the industry’s commitment to sustainability. The Label Trail also delves into the integration of smart packaging technologies, illustrating how digital content and traceability features enhance consumer engagement and meet compliance requirements. Furthermore, industry experts will share valuable knowledge on topics such as carbon data management, regulatory compliance, and supply chain transparency."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"Berkshire accelerates buybacks, lowers cash stake as profit tops forecasts",bluewaterhealthyliving.com (Reuters),2026-08-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bluewaterhealthyliving.com/news/business-and-economy/berkshire-lowers-cash-stake-as-buybacks-accelerate-reports-higher-profit/,"Berkshire accelerates buybacks, lowers cash stake as profit tops forecasts ... Home» News» Business & Economy» Berkshire accelerates buybacks, lowers cash stake as profit tops forecasts ... Aug 8 (Reuters) – Berkshire Hathaway said it began reducing its enormous stockpile of cash in the second quarter, investing billions of dollars in stocks such as Alphabet and repurchasing billions of its own, as it reported higher-than-expected profit. ... The conglomerate said on Saturday it repurchased $4.5 billion of its own stock between April and June and over $3.3 billion more in July, accelerating repurchases it began in March following a nearly two-year hiatus. ... Berkshire also bought nearly $20 billion more stocks than it sold, ending 14 straight quarters as a net seller of shares. ... Purchases included a $10 billion addition to an already-large investment in Alphabet, the parent of Google and YouTube, which is now one of its largest stock holdings. ... Quarterly operating profit rose 16% to $12.98 billion, topping analyst forecasts, as improvement at the BNSF railroad and service businesses including the NetJets luxury plane unit and TTI electronic components distributor helped offset weakness at the Geico auto insurer. ... Net income more than doubled to $25.67 billion, including unrealized gains and losses on stocks that Omaha, Nebraska-based Berkshire still owns. Berkshire urges investors to ignore the resulting volatility. ... Revenue, which had been stagnating, rose 10% to $101.81 billion. ... Berkshire said “considerable uncertainty” remains about macroeconomic and geopolitical events, including tariffs and wars. ... It also said falling demand at consumer businesses including its 103 car and truck dealerships, Fruit of the Loom underwear and Forest River RVs reflects changes in consumer confidence. ... The quarter was the second since Greg Abel became Berkshire’s chief executive, succeeding Warren Buffett, who remains chairman. ... Investors and analysts have been eager ... Berkshire’s capital differs from that of ... , who had difficulty deploying cash toward the ... of his 60 years at the helm of the $1.12 trillion conglomerate. ... Berkshire ended June with $364.7 billion of cash, down from a record $380.2 billion three months earlier. ... Its policy allows buybacks when the stock price is below intrinsic value, as “conservatively determined” by Abel following consultation with Buffett. ... Berkshire’s market capitalization is close to 1.5 times book value, or assets minus liabilities. ... The pace of stock repurchases is comparable to Buffett’s peak ... early this decade. ... Berkshire’s biggest year for buybacks was 2021, when it repurchased $27 billion of stock. ... The reported cash stake includes $6.8 billion that Berkshire spent in late July to buy home builder Taylor Morrison. ... Berkshire’s $12.98 billion of operating profit equaled about $9,068 per Class A share, and rose from $11.16 billion a year earlier. ... The $25.67 billion of net income was about $17,928 per Class A share, and rose from $12.37 billion. ... Berkshire’s Class A shares are up 3% this year, trailing the Standard & Poor’s 500’s 13% gain. The shares have lagged the index by 40 percentage points since Buffett announced in May 2025 he was stepping down as chief executive. ... Geico saw pre-tax underwriting profit fall 45%, as accident claims rose while marketing expenses increased. ... The car insurer has spent more on advertising to regain customers it lost during a multi-year effort to improve underwriting quality and reduce overheads. ... Seifert said Geico’s results were “absolutely abysmal” and raised “red flags,” at a time rivals, which include Allstate and Progressive, are performing better. ... Overall profit from insurance and reinsurance fell 11%, with lower-than-expected property losses and some insurance business offsetting Geico. ... Profit at BNSF rose 6% to $1.56 billion, as the railroad shipped more consumer, agricultural and energy products and charged more for fuel. ... Berkshire Hathaway Energy said profit rose 27% to $891 million, benefiting from higher utility margins and tax credits. ... #### Berkshire says operating profit rises, conducts stock buybacks"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"Securikett expands label functionality with sealing, security and digital integration",www.packaginginsights.com (07 Aug 2026 | By Milana Nikolova),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaginginsights.com/news/securikett-multifunctional-security-label-dpp.html,"Securikett expands label functionality with sealing, security and digital integration ... # Securikett expands label functionality with sealing, security and digital integration ... - Securikett’s multifunctional label combines sealing, tamper evidence, authentication, and digital capabilities, replacing conventional heat sealing. - Its Codikett platform connects serialized labels with production, logistics, and enterprise data, providing a bridge between physical packaging and DPPs. - Securikett says DPP adoption challenges increasingly center on data governance, interoperability, and durable code implementation. ... Packaging labels are increasingly becoming the interface between physical products and digital information, extending their role to include sealing, authentication, traceability, and secure data management. Packaging Insights meets with Securikett to explore the digital transformation of labels amid tightening regulations. ... Securikett is responding to this trend with a multifunctional label that replaces heat sealing while integrating security technologies and digital capabilities into a single solution. ... The multifunctional label is said to integrate structured adhesive coatings, Void technology, silicone coatings, and custom die-cutting to provide tamper evidence, functionality, and regulatory compliance. ... The sealing mechanism uses a label to secure the tray without the need for a welded lid, outlines the Austrian provider of tamper-evident security labels and digital product verification. The Void effect makes unauthorized openings “immediately” visible, the company adds, while also allowing the integration of features such as ventilation holes or viewing windows directly on the label. ... Securikett shares that the application is fully compatible with automated labeling or dispensing systems to enable faster processing and reduce machinery and operational costs compared to heat-sealing equipment. ... “We have combined ... This creates a ... Securikett label for secure tray closure without heat sealing (Image credit: Securikett).The launch reflects a broader shift toward labels performing multiple roles, including sealing and tamper evidence, but also authentication and digital connectivity. ... Speaking to Packaging Insights, a company spokesperson highlights Securikett’s Codikett platform, which is said to act as a code hub that connects different systems and data sources without requiring companies to replace or fully standardize their existing IT landscape. ... “Codikett can generate and route unique codes, manage role-based access and scan contexts, and connect production and logistics processes. Master data can remain in the existing source systems while being presented consistently through interfaces.” ... “Where required, these can be combined with tamper-evident and authentication features. We therefore see our role as building a reliable bridge between the physical product, its packaging, and the associated digital information.” ... The spokesperson further highlights how Securikett is supporting its clients affected by the EU’s Digital Product Passport (DPP). The European Commission recently introduced a DPP Registry and testing environment to support data-sharing and transparency for packaging companies. ... “We provide the physical connection to the DPP through serialized labels and secure data carriers. We also encourage clients to begin with a clearly defined pilot involving a real product, real data, and actual packaging. This allows technical, organizational, and user-experience questions to be addressed before regulatory deadlines create unnecessary time pressure,” Securikett’s spokesperson elaborates. ... Securikett highlights that the launch of the DPP Registry is a “significant” milestone moving DPP from a regulatory concept toward an operational system. The spokesperson says that the Registry provides the common EU-level infrastructure for registering unique product identifiers and associated metadata. ... “It does not centrally store all detailed product data; this information remains with the economic operator or an authorized DPP service provider.” ... “For the packaging industry, this is particularly important because packaging and labels often provide the physical access point to the passport. Data carriers such as QR codes must therefore be integrated into packaging design, printing, quality control, and production processes. They must remain readable, reliable, and securely connected to the correct digital product information.” ... According to the spokesperson, there are some challenges to DPP compliance, although these are organizational rather than technological. “Many of the necessary technologies already exist, including unique identification, digital platforms, and interfaces to enterprise systems.” ... “However, many companies still lack clean, consistent, and well-governed master data across their historically developed IT environments. Scaling also requires clear responsibilities, interoperable systems, role-based access rights, and reliable processes for keeping information accurate throughout the product lifecycle.” ... A further challenge is the physical implementation of DPP, according to Securikett, as codes need to remain readable despite abrasion, ultraviolet exposure, moisture, and mechanical stress. ... “Variable printing and serialization require stable print quality and defined verification processes. Where authenticity matters, a standard copyable QR code is not sufficient; secure identities, verification mechanisms, and tamper-evident features may be necessary.” ... Meanwhile, standards and product-specific requirements are still evolving. The company spokesperson argues that companies should therefore design flexible systems based on interoperability and open standards rather than waiting for final details. ... The strongest near-term demand for DPP-ready packaging solutions is coming from industries that are closest to concrete regulatory deadlines or already have advanced traceability requirements, explains Securikett’s spokesperson. ... “Batteries are currently leading because DPPs will become mandatory for certain battery categories in February 2027. Other priority areas include iron and steel, textiles and apparel, and construction products.” ... “We are also seeing strong interest from luxury goods and other branded consumer products. In these sectors, companies are not only preparing for compliance. They are also interested in authentication, provenance, grey-market detection, consumer engagement, and the ability to provide verified sustainability information.” ... The key factors influencing demand, according to the company, include regulatory timelines, as well as the commercial value of trusted product identities and traceability. ... “Implementation will take place progressively by product group. Nevertheless, the Registry makes it clear that companies should now move from observation to practical preparation.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"Applied Adhesives Expands in Netherlands, U.S. with Pair of Deals - Modern Distribution Management",www.mdm.com (MDM Staff),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mdm.com/news/top-distributor-sectors/industrial-supplies/applied-adhesives-expands-in-netherlands-u-s-with-pair-of-deals/,"# Applied Adhesives Expands in Netherlands, U.S. with Pair of Deals The industrial adhesives distributor continues an acquisition run under private equity owner Bertram Capital. - MDM Staff - August 7, 2026 Applied Adhesives has completed acquisitions in the Netherlands and Rhode Island, extending the industrial adhesives distributor’s international reach while expanding its U.S. silicone capabilities and East Coast presence. ... The Minnetonka, MN-based company announced Aug. 6 that it acquired Van Asperen Kleefstoffen — a Lelystad, Netherlands-based adhesive solutions provider serving packaging, labeling and paper converting markets. Terms were not disclosed. ... Founded in 1982, Van Asperen is a premium partner of Henkel and a distribution partner for 3M. The deal establishes Applied’s first presence in the Netherlands and represents its second European acquisition. ... acquisition represents another important milestone in ... ’s international growth strategy,” ... Applied entered Europe in January when it acquired Interlock Adhesives, a Scunthorpe, England-based adhesive technology company serving the packaging, labeling and bookbinding industries. Interlock is also a Henkel Premium Partner. Its senior leadership team remained in place following the acquisition. The Netherlands deal followed Applied’s July acquisition of Industrial Sales and Distribution Inc. (ISD) — a Westerly, RI-based distributor of adhesives and silicones that has served manufacturing customers for more than 35 years. ... ISD, formerly R.P. Morrison Company, specializes in solutions for aerospace, product assembly and pad printing markets. Applied said the acquisition expands its adhesives and silicones portfolio, customer base and East Coast presence. ... Applied has announced four acquisitions so far in 2026. Along with Van Asperen, ISD and Interlock, the company acquired Malvern, PA-based LJD Packaging in March. LJD distributes adhesives and equipment for packaging, printing, labeling and product assembly applications. ... The deals come after private equity firm Bertram Capital acquired Applied from Arsenal Capital Partners in April 2025. Arsenal had invested in Applied in 2021 and said the company completed 17 acquisitions during its ownership, expanding its geographic reach, product offerings and technical capabilities. Terms of the sale to Bertram were not disclosed. ... Bertram’s investment made Applied its fourth industrial distribution platform investment and third platform investment through Fund V."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Logo Brands Acquires Brass Reminders,www.accessnewswire.com (Logo Brands),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.accessnewswire.com/newsroom/en/sports-leisure-and-entertainment/logo-brands-expands-u.s.-manufacturing-capabilities-with-acquisiti-1204102,"Logo Brands Acquires Brass Reminders # Logo Brands Expands U.S. Manufacturing Capabilities with Acquisition of Brass Reminders Thursday, 06 August 2026 05:10 PM #### Mergers and Acquisitions Strategic acquisition expands manufacturing in Spring Hill, Tennessee, while continuing production at Brass Reminders' existing Mexico facility, broadens specialty retail distribution, and creates new opportunities for customers across North America. ... FRANKLIN, TN / ACCESS Newswire / August 6, 2026 / Logo Brands, a leading designer, manufacturer, and distributor of licensed sports and lifestyle products, announced the acquisition of Brass Reminders, a respected manufacturer of premium decals and magnets serving the specialty retail and destination markets. ... The acquisition represents another strategic step in Logo Brands' long-term commitment to expanding its domestic manufacturing capabilities while strengthening its position in the specialty name-drop industry. By combining the strengths of both organizations, Logo Brands will further enhance its North American manufacturing network, enabling the company to offer retailers a broader assortment of high-quality products while increasing U.S. production capacity. ... ""At Logo Brands, we are focused on expanding our vertical domestic manufacturing capabilities and increasing our capacity to build more of our products here in the United States,"" said Matt McCauley, CEO of Logo Brands. ""Brass Reminders allows us to do exactly that while also introducing Logo Brands to new retail customers. Together, we can offer a more complete collection of products with the same marks and designs, creating greater value for our customers, and increasing opportunities for growth."" ... Brass Reminders previously operated production facilities in Kentucky and Mexico. As part of the integration, Logo Brands will move the Kentucky manufacturing operation to its manufacturing and distribution facility in Spring Hill, Tennessee, further expanding the company's U.S. production capabilities and creating greater operational efficiencies. The Mexico production facility will remain in operation for strategic manufacturing purposes, providing additional production capacity, supply chain flexibility, and uninterrupted service for customers across North America. ... The acquisition strengthens Logo Brands' manufacturing footprint and reinforces the company's commitment to investing in domestic production, operational excellence, and long-term partnerships with retailers across North America. ... Together, Logo Brands and Brass Reminders are well positioned to deliver expanded product offerings, enhanced manufacturing capabilities, and continued innovation while maintaining the quality and customer service both companies are known for."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Crown Labels boosts digital press capacity with Domino,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/crown-labels-domino-press-capacity/,"Crown Labels boosts digital press capacity with Domino ... UK-based self-adhesive labels manufacturer Crown Labels has added a Domino N730i digital label press to expand output. ... The machine has taken the place of one of the company’s two Domino N610i presses. ... The change is intended to help the business handle rising order volumes, lift throughput and undertake more high-end label work. ... With the N730i, production speeds have reached 90m/min in high-speed productivity mode while print resolution goes up to 1,200dpi. ... Its seven-colour configuration, including orange and violet inks, has also enabled Crown Labels to move a larger share of work from flexographic processes to digital production. ... Crown Labels director Tom Hardy said: “When we saw the quality of the N730i, the higher resolution, and the faster speeds, it was a complete no-brainer for us. ... “The gradations are beautifully printed, the text reversals are finer, and everything we have seen from the new machine has been superb. It takes us to the next level and boosts our production capacity.” ... The company installed its first Domino press in 2019 after customers sought shorter lead times, a wider number of stock keeping units (SKUs) and more regular artwork revisions. ... A second N610i followed in 2022. ... More recently, the company decided to replace one of those presses with the N730i in order to further increase capacity and broaden its production capabilities. ... Digital printing now represents more than 65% of Crown Labels’ turnover, compared with 20% in 2019. Domino supported the company during that period of expansion. ... Domino Printing Sciences UK sales manager Craig Clawson said: “Crown Labels are more than just our customers—they are our long-term partners. ... “It’s been very rewarding to support them on their digital journey – first with the N610i and now, to see how the N730i is helping them to take quality and capacity to the next level. We look forward to supporting Crown Labels for many years to come.” ... Meanwhile, US-based Paez Packaging installed a Domino N610i digital UV inkjet label press earlier this year."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,A4 Labels launches labels range made from ocean-bound plastic,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/a4-labels-ocean-bound-plastic-range/,"A4 Labels launches labels range made from ocean-bound plastic ... UK-based label manufacturer A4 Labels has introduced a product line called Ocean Action Labels that uses ocean-bound plastic as a feedstock. ... The aim is to offer packaging labels that reduce use of virgin fossil-based plastics and address plastic leakage into marine environments. ... The material is made from plastic waste collected in coastal areas. ... The Ocean Action Labels range includes white and clear top-coated polypropylene (PP) film produced from chemically recycled ocean-bound plastic. ... The products carry ISCC PLUS certification under a mass balance approach and are intended to match the performance of standard PP film. ... According to A4 Labels’ website, the white version is a waterproof film intended to be used where moisture and wear are factors while the clear version is a transparent film developed for packaging designs that use a “no-label look”. ... Across both materials, the company said the films are synthetic and waterproof, suitable for indoor and outdoor use, and designed for dimensional stability and tear resistance. ... The launch sits alongside its Eco-Pledge partnership with Seven Clean Seas."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Carby Label invests in fourth Lombardi press,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/carby-label-fourth-lombardi-press/,"Carby Label invests in fourth Lombardi press ... Italian label and packaging producer Carby Label has ordered a fourth printing press from Lombardi Converting Machinery. ... The Invicta i1 670 will be deployed at the company’s site in Casamassima, near Bari. ... The purchase aims to support Carby Label’s move into flexible packaging and lifting capacity for customers in the fruit and vegetable packaging segment. ... Carby Label marketing manager Anna Carbonara said: “We decided to invest in the Invicta i1 670 to double our production capacity and better meet the needs of our customers in the fruit and vegetable packaging sector. ... “What we value most about Lombardi is the reliability of its presses and their outstanding printing performance in terms of both quality and speed. These are essential characteristics that allow us to continue delivering high production standards while remaining competitive in a rapidly evolving market.” ... With a web width of 670mm, the inline flexo press is intended for both conventional label work and broader web flexible packaging jobs. ... According to Lombardi, the equipment includes automation, shorter changeover times, consistent print quality and flexibility in production. ... The installation is also part of Lombardi’s focus on the flexible packaging market, where it is broadening its range of inline flexo printing systems for converters looking to widen their production mix. ... Lombardi Italy sales director Enrico Gandolfi said: “Every new press sold to a long-standing customer is the greatest recognition we can receive. ... “Carby Label’s decision to invest in Lombardi once again confirms the strength of a partnership built over many years and founded on tangible results. This new Invicta i1 670 will support the company’s expansion into the flexible packaging market, a segment in which Lombardi continues to strengthen its presence and reputation both in Italy and internationally.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Basic Capital Management buys Malugo Label Group stake | Bitget News,www.bitget.com,2026-07-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bitget.com/news/detail/12560605546616,"Basic Capital Management buys Malugo Label Group stake | Bitget News ... Basic Capital Management buys Malugo Label Group stake ... # Basic Capital Management buys Malugo Label Group stake ... Reuters2026/07/27 01:45 ... - Basic Capital Management acquired Malugo Label Group via an SPC backed by its BCM-VI fund, effective June 30, 2026. - The deal covers Japan-based Malugo Label and its operating units in Singapore, Indonesia, and the Philippines. - Malugo Label makes and sells labels mainly for office automation and industrial equipment, with production and sales across Southeast Asia. - The acquisition supports a phased succession from the founder-owner, with BCM targeting governance upgrades and expansion."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Peak Rock Tests Sale of Berner Food & Beverage | PE Hub,headlinesbriefing.com (PE Hub),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://headlinesbriefing.com/private-markets/pe-hub/peak-rock-tests-sale-of-berner-food-beverage-79474639,"Peak Rock Tests Sale of Berner Food & Beverage | PE Hub ... ### Peak Rock Tests Sale of Berner Food & Beverage ... Peak Rock Capital is in the pre-stages of launching a sale process for 2015 portfolio company Berner Food & Beverage, a private-label manufacturer of dips, spreads and beverages, three sources briefed on the matter told PE Hub. ... Peak Rock, an Austin, Texas-based private equity firm, recently retained Lazard as Berner's sellside adviser, two of the sources said. Since Peak Rock acquired Berner in 2015, the business has increased 3x in revenue and 6x in EBITDA, one source told PE Hub. ... The potential sale marks a significant exit opportunity for Peak Rock Capital, which has overseen substantial growth at the private-label food manufacturer. Lazard will manage the auction process, which is expected to attract strategic buyers and other private equity firms interested in the food and beverage sector. ... Sources indicate the process is in early stages, with no final decision made on valuation or timing. Berner's portfolio of private-label dips, spreads and beverages positions it well in the current market for food manufacturing assets. ... - Peak Rock to test market for Berner Food & Beverage, sources say; IVEST and Cloverlay grew Care Bears through licensing before exit to Authentic Brands - Peak Rock sells geospatial services SAM to New Mountain - Peak Rock scoops up health tech firm Asembia - Directors’ Deals: Rosebank executives add to stakes - Peak Rock Capital acquires ingredients biz JR Dalziel"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Asteria Group expands UK packaging presence with Mercian Labels acquisition - The Deal Wire,thedealwire.com (ybalkind),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thedealwire.com/asteria-group-expands-uk-packaging-presence/,"Asteria Group expands UK packaging presence with Mercian Labels acquisition - The Deal Wire ... # Asteria Group expands UK packaging presence with Mercian Labels acquisition ... Hill Dickinson has advised Asteria Group, a leading European provider of label and packaging solutions, on its acquisition of Mercian Labels. This transaction marks the 41st production site for the Belgian-headquartered group. ... Founded in 1969 and based in Burntwood, Staffordshire, Mercian Labels is a manufacturer of self-adhesive labels, serving clients across the food, beverage, and pharmaceutical sectors. The acquisition provides Asteria with access to Mercian’s technical expertise in specialised tamper-evident and security label products. ... The deal is part of Asteria’s broader strategy to scale its operations and achieve its goal of becoming a sustainable leader in the packaging industry by 2030. Asteria Group is backed by the private equity firm Waterland Private Equity. ... Commenting on the transaction, Olivia Jones said: “We are delighted to have supported Asteria and Waterland on this latest strategic acquisition, which further strengthens its presence in the UK market and its broader European platform.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,P.E. Labellers at interpack: all the AI-based technological innovation on board the labeling machines - Packaging International,www.packaging-mag.com (Walter Zannoni),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-mag.com/p-e-labellers-at-interpack-all-the-ai-based-technological-innovation-on-board-the-labeling-machines/,"P.E. Labellers at interpack: all the AI-based technological innovation on board the labeling machines - Packaging International ... P.E. Labellers at interpack: all the AI-based technological innovation on board the labeling machines ... The most flexible labeling machines in the world showcase in Düsseldorf all the technological innovation that the Mantuan company has been able to conceive, to make them even easier to manage and maintain. ... This year there are three very valid reasons to stop by the P.E. Labellers stand at Interpack 2026. In Hall 13 – A75, visitors arriving from all over the world will be able to experience three live experiences: ... Modular SL: is the new generation modular labeling machine, designed to offer maximum flexibility in terms of applications and a very high level of technological innovation on board, from vision and control systems to AI-based ones for incredibly easy management. ... stations that can ... interchanged with just a ... gestures, with all the application technologies on board, available in both fixed and trolley versions. ... Safety is a priority: rolling shutter guards stop the machine immediately, even on cold glue stations. It will be possible to see Modular SL live and explore the machine through the on-board AI systems. ... SkyLine: linear labeling solution with pressure sensitive technology, completely ergonomic with automatic adjustments and easy maintenance. This innovative solution, with an ergonomic and attractive design, contains a combination of advantages and functionality that distinguish it from any other linear labeller on the market. The new layout with an elegant design and the high technology on board the machine makes SkyLine a unique solution for multiple markets and different application needs. ... SkyLine allows multiple applications: front and back labels, wraparounds, collars, I-L-U seals. It will be possible to see SkyLine live and see it in operation. ... Aurora 5.0: heat shrink sleeve applicator, high speed and with rapid format changes without the use of equipment. This solution offers intuitive interfaces, optional shrink tunnels, for simple and efficient use and integration, and handles five application types: full-body, full-body over cap, partial-body, tamper-evident and multi-pack. It will be possible to see Aurora 5.0 live and see it in operation. ... The highly awaited Düsseldorf fair represents the ideal showcase to exhibit innovative labeling solutions for multiple applications and sectors. The new P.E. systems Labellers open a window onto the future. ... P.E. Labellers participates in Interpack 2026 within the large ProMach exhibition area, together with ten other Product Brands part of the American multinational. In the ProMach area there will be present: P.E. Labellers • Zacmi • Zalkin • Reepack • Shuttleworth • Bartelet • Pace • Pharma • FLTècnics • PMIS • L&C, with a total of 12 machines on display."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"Stahls’ Acquires Siser, Adds Heat-Transfer Vinyl Brand to Its Family of Companies",members.asicentral.com (ASI Central),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://members.asicentral.com/news/industry-news/july-2026/stahls-acquires-siser-adds-heat-transfer-vinyl-brand-to-its-family-of-companies/,"Stahls’ Acquires Siser, Adds Heat-Transfer Vinyl Brand to Its Family of Companies ... • Stahls’ (asi/88984) has acquired heat-transfer vinyl company Siser, expanding its portfolio of apparel-decoration products and technologies. ... • Siser will continue to operate under its own name while collaborating with Stahls’ on innovation, customer support and global growth. ... St. Clair Shores, MI-based Stahls’ (asi/88984) has acquired Siser, a heat-transfer vinyl (HTV) and accessories company, bringing the brand into its family of companies. Financial terms of the deal weren’t disclosed. ... Stahls’ and Siser already have a history of working together to support apparel decorators through product innovation, industry education and a commitment to customer success, the companies said. Last November, Stahls’ became an official distributor of Siser HTV products. ... “This next phase of our relationship with Siser allows us to focus on innovation and helping decorators succeed,” said Carleen Gray, CEO of Stahls’, a member of the Counselor Power 50 and the 2025 Counselor International Person of the Year. “Together, we’re focused on delivering outstanding products, education and support while continuing to create new opportunities for our customers and the industry as a whole.” ... The acquisition brings together complementary expertise in materials, decoration technologies, equipment and application solutions, Stahls’ noted. As part of the Stahls’ family of companies, Siser will continue to operate under its own name while collaborating with Stahls’ to advance innovation and drive growth across global markets."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"STAHLS’ Welcomes Siser to Family of Companies, Expanding Global Heat Printing Innovation | Impressions",impressionsmagazine.com (Dustin Shrader),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://impressionsmagazine.com/news/stahls-siser-family-of-companies-heat-printing-innovation/170046/,"STAHLS’ Welcomes Siser to Family of Companies, Expanding Global Heat Printing Innovation | Impressions - ... # STAHLS’ Welcomes Siser to Family of Companies, Expanding Global Heat Printing Innovation ... Longtime industry partners unite under one family of companies, combining expertise in heat transfer materials, equipment and apparel decoration technologies to better serve decorators worldwide ... : Dustin Shrader ... STAHLS' has announced that Siser has joined its family of companies, expanding collaboration in heat transfer vinyl, decorating technology and customer support for apparel decorators worldwide. Image courtesy of STAHLS' ... STAHLS’ has announced that Siser, a global leader in heat transfer vinyl (HTV) and material innovation, has officially joined the STAHLS’ family of companies, strengthening a longtime relationship focused on advancing apparel decoration technology and supporting decorators worldwide. ... The announcement marks the next chapter in a partnership that has spanned years, with both organizations working together to provide innovative products, educational resources and business solutions for apparel decorators. By bringing together complementary expertise in heat transfer materials, decorating equipment, application technologies and customer education, the companies aim to create additional value for businesses across the decorated apparel industry. ... - Siser officially joins the STAHLS’ family of companies. - Combines expertise in heat transfer vinyl, decorating equipment and application technologies. - Strengthens customer education, technical support and product innovation. - Siser will continue operating under its established global brand. - Expands opportunities for apparel decorators through integrated decoration solutions. ... Carleen Gray, CEO of STAHLS’, said the expanded relationship is centered on helping decorators succeed through continued innovation and customer support. ... “This next phase of our relationship with Siser allows us to focus on innovation and helping decorators succeed,” Gray said. “Together, we are focused on delivering outstanding products, education, and support while continuing to create new opportunities for our customers and the industry as a whole.” ... Under the new structure, Siser will continue operating under its trusted global brand while collaborating closely with STAHLS’ to accelerate innovation, strengthen customer support and expand growth opportunities across international markets. Both companies said they remain committed to providing apparel decorators with the products, knowledge and resources needed to grow successful businesses."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,STAHLS' Announces Siser as Part of Its Family of Companies - Apparelist,www.apparelist.com (Apparelist),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.apparelist.com/2026/07/15/stahls-announces-siser-as-part-of-its-family-of-companies/,"STAHLS' Announces Siser as Part of Its Family of Companies - Apparelist ... # STAHLS' Announces Siser as Part of Its Family of Companies ... STAHLS’ announces that Siser is now part of the STAHLS’ family of companies. ... The two organizations share a long history of working together to support apparel decorators through innovative products, industry education, and a commitment to customer success, according to the press release announcement from STAHLS’. The expanded relationship brings together complementary expertise in materials, decoration technologies, equipment, and application solutions, allowing both companies to continue delivering value to customers across the apparel decoration industry. ... “This next phase of our relationship with Siser allows us to focus on innovation and helping decorators succeed,” said Carleen Gray, CEO of STAHLS’, in a press statement. “Together, we are focused on delivering outstanding products, education, and support while continuing to create new opportunities for our customers and the industry as a whole.” ... As part of the STAHLS’ family of companies, Siser will continue to operate under its brand while collaborating with STAHLS’ to advance innovation, strengthen customer support, and drive growth across global markets, the press release shares. ... Together, STAHLS’ and Siser state they remain committed to empowering apparel decorators with the products, knowledge, and resources they need to thrive."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Lappí boosts Iberian footprint with Alempack purchase,www.packaging-gateway.com (Satarupa Bhowmik),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/lappi-iberian-footprint-alempack-purchase/,"Lappí boosts Iberian footprint with Alempack purchase ... Lappí Labels and Flexible Packaging has purchased Portuguese flexible packaging provider Alempack. ... The deal broadens the buyer’s manufacturing reach and product portfolio across the Iberian market. ... Through the acquisition, Lappí adds industrial capacity in doypack and flowpack, formats regarded to be ideal for fast-moving consumer goods. ... The move also extends the company’s industrial base in Iberia and is said to deliver a 15% growth. ... Alempack will be integrated into Lappí while continuing under its existing management team, and retaining its technical, commercial and industrial expertise. ... The Portuguese company contributes specialist knowledge in doypack, flowpack, high-barrier packaging, reel-fed films, shrink bags, vacuum bags and other flexible packaging formats. ... Those capabilities add to Lappí’s existing range in labels, sleeves, wraparound labels and flexible packaging while reinforcing its presence in sectors, including beverages, cosmetics, food, home care, hygiene, personal care, and pet food. ... Supported by private equity company Diana Capital, Lappí is targeting estimated organic sales of €65m ($74m) in 2026. ... With the addition of Alempack, estimated combined sales are expected to exceed €70m ($79.7m). ... Upon the acquisition, Lappí now operates as a group of six companies with seven production sites across the Iberian Peninsula. ... Alempack employs over 40 people and its addition lifts the group’s workforce from 350 employees to more than 390. ... The deal also expands Lappí’s industrial space, increasing total production facilities in Spain and Portugal from 51,000m² to around 60,000m²."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"Reelables, Hubble Network partner to expand smart label tracking - Label and Narrow Web",www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/breaking-news/reelables-hubble-network-partner-to-expand-smart-label-tracking/,"Reelables, Hubble Network partner to expand smart label tracking - Label and Narrow Web ... # Reelables, Hubble Network partner to expand smart label tracking ... The collaboration extends visibility for Bluetooth-enabled smart labels across global supply chains. ... Reelables, a UK-based smart label manufacturer, has partnered with Hubble Network to extend the tracking capabilities of its printable smart labels, enabling continuous visibility of cargo and inventory as it moves through global supply chains. ... The partnership combines Reelables’ Bluetooth-enabled smart labels with Hubble’s network of more than 100 million gateways spanning 170 countries. Together, the technologies provide location and condition monitoring beyond warehouses and distribution centers, allowing companies to track shipments throughout transit without requiring GPS, cellular connectivity, or dedicated RFID infrastructure. ... Designed to run through standard barcode printers, Reelables’ ultra-thin, disposable smart labels can be applied directly to pallets, parcels, and other cargo. Through the expanded network, users receive real-time notifications when shipments arrive, are delayed, change condition, or deviate from planned routes. ... According to the companies, the integrated platform is intended for logistics providers, manufacturers, retailers, warehouses, and cold chain operators seeking greater supply chain visibility while reducing the cost and complexity associated with traditional tracking technologies. ... “We’re at a turning point for supply chain visibility,” comments Alex Haro, co-founder and CEO of Hubble Network. “Bluetooth networks have reached the scale and coverage needed to track shipments continuously, without adding cost or complexity to Reelables’ labels.” ... David Stanton, co-founder and CEO of Reelables, says the partnership creates a new category of shipment tracking by combining low-cost printable smart labels with a global Bluetooth network, making continuous tracking practical for a wider range of supply chain applications."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Amberley Labels partners with Henderson’s Relish - Food and Drink Technology,www.foodanddrinktechnology.com,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.foodanddrinktechnology.com/news/68574/68574/,"Amberley Labels, part of Paranova Print and Packaging, has partnered with Sheffield-based Henderson’s Relish to produce a limited-edition run of bottles supporting the Pride of Yorkshire fundraising campaign. ... Launched on 8th June, the bottles will be sold via the Henderson’s website, with all profits donated to Sheffield Children’s Hospital Charity as part of its 150th anniversary appeal. The Pride of Yorkshire campaign will see 150 life-sized lion and lioness sculptures installed across the region, celebrating art, community and Yorkshire pride while raising funds to transform the hospital’s Emergency Department. ... As a Sheffield-made brand with a long-standing connection to the region, Henderson’s Relish has built a loyal following since its beginnings in 1885, with its closely guarded recipe known to just three family members. Its limited edition releases, from football club collaborations to artist-led designs, continue to play a role in connecting the brand with its audience while supporting local causes. ... Produced at Amberley Labels, over 3,000 labels were printed using flexographic technology and finished with a dual varnish to make the artwork standout even further. The project marks the second time Amberley has worked with Henderson’s on a charity-focused limited edition range, building on a partnership that began in 2021."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Olimpias Group Unveils New O-Label Brand at 43rd Milano Unica,bjournal.net,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bjournal.net/olimpias-unveils-o-label-brand-at-43rd-milano-unica/,"Olimpias Group Unveils New O-Label Brand at 43rd Milano Unica ... Italy’s Olimpias Group has launched a new brand, O-label, dedicated to labels, ribbons, swing tags and broader product identity solutions, marking a strategic shift as the company deepens its focus on brand identity within the textile value chain. ... The unveiling took place at the 43rd edition of Milano Unica, one of Europe’s leading textile trade fairs, where the group introduced O-label alongside a creative campaign titled “O-fake,” aimed at provoking discussion around authenticity and value in modern fashion. ... The new brand represents what Olimpias describes as the first visible step in a broader restructuring initiative, positioning O-label as a specialized division centered on elevating labeling from a functional component to a strategic brand asset. The company has anchored the brand around the concept of “Identity Substance,” emphasizing that product identity is integral to a garment’s value and not merely decorative. ... Chief executive Guido Molese said the initiative reflects a shift in how the company approaches product development and market positioning. He noted that identity is not an accessory but a defining element that shapes how brands are perceived, recognized and remembered. Labels, ribbons and swing tags, he added, play a critical role in communicating authenticity and brand storytelling to consumers. ... The O-label portfolio includes woven labels, ribbons, piping, printed labels, patches, elastic tapes and hangtags. These products are organized into thematic categories such as classic, luxury, urban, denim, active and sustainable lines, allowing brands to align identity elements with their market positioning. ... Olimpias has also introduced seasonal collections under the O-label umbrella, including Spring Summer 2025 and Fall Winter 2026-2027 ranges. These collections feature a variety of design concepts and named lines, including Aerials, Ottone, Milanors, Augusta, Palu, Root, Essentia, Aureum, Syntax and Pulse, reflecting a blend of aesthetic innovation and technical functionality. ... The launch comes as fashion brands face increasing pressure to demonstrate authenticity, traceability and transparency across supply chains. Industry analysts note a growing trend among European textile manufacturers to reposition trims and labeling components as critical tools for brand differentiation, particularly in response to concerns over counterfeiting and sustainability claims. ... Olimpias is leveraging this shift by positioning O-label as a partner for fashion companies seeking to strengthen their identity and communication with consumers. By consolidating its offerings under a single brand, the group aims to move beyond component manufacturing toward a more integrated role in shaping brand narratives. The company’s strategy is also underpinned by its ongoing sustainability commitments. ... Olimpias said it has been reporting on its environmental performance for three consecutive years, adopting an industrial model focused on efficiency and reduced environmental impact while maintaining strict oversight of production processes. In 2025, the group reported that all purchased electricity came from renewable sources, marking a significant milestone in its energy transition. Its sustainability reporting framework has expanded to include Scope 3 emissions, aligning with the United Nations 2030 Agenda and its Sustainable Development Goals. ... Olimpias has also achieved Global Organic Textile Standard certification for organic cotton and operates in accordance with OEKO-TEX Standard 100, reinforcing its focus on safety and environmental responsibility. The company has implemented an integrated management system covering quality, environmental sustainability, occupational safety and social responsibility, supported by certifications and participation in international programs to ensure transparency and traceability. ... The introduction of O-label follows a period of organizational change within the group, with Molese’s appointment in March marking a turning point in its strategic direction. The company has indicated that the brand is part of a longer-term transformation aimed at strengthening specialization and expanding its presence in high-value segments of the textile market. ... As global fashion supply chains evolve, the Olimpias Group’s move highlights the increasing importance of identity-driven solutions in textiles. By combining design, innovation and sustainability under the O-label platform, the company is seeking to position itself at the intersection of branding and manufacturing, offering fashion brands new ways to communicate authenticity and value in a competitive marketplace.@"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Amberley Labels relishes limited-edition charity bottle challenge | Packaging Scotland,packagingscotland.com (Gary Moug),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://packagingscotland.com/2026/07/amberley-labels-relishes-limited-edition-charity-bottle-challenge/,"Amberley Labels relishes limited-edition charity bottle challenge | Packaging Scotland ... Home Food & Drink Amberley Labels relishes limited-edition charity bottle challenge ... AMBERLEY Labels has teamed up with Henderson’s Relish to produce a limited-edition run of bottles supporting the Pride of Yorkshire fundraising campaign. ... The bottles will be sold via the Henderson’s website, with all profits donated to Sheffield Children’s Hospital Charity as part of its 150th anniversary appeal. The Pride of Yorkshire campaign will see 150 life-sized lion and lioness sculptures installed across the region, celebrating art, community and Yorkshire pride while raising funds to transform the hospital’s emergency department. ... As a Sheffield-made brand, Henderson’s Relish has built a loyal following since its beginnings in 1885, with its closely guarded recipe known to just three family members. Its limited edition releases, from football club collaborations to artist-led designs, are designed to help connect the brand with its audience while supporting local causes. ... For this latest release, the labels feature artwork by Sheffield illustrator Abi Landridge, known as Paperface. The design centres on a ‘bold’ celebratory composition, with a heart-shaped crest surrounded by hand-drawn food illustrations and flowing forms inspired by the relish itself. Set against Henderson’s signature orange, the illustration is intended to bring together the campaign’s community focus and the brand’s local roots. ... Produced at Amberley Labels, part of Paranova Print and Packaging, over 3,000 labels were printed using flexographic technology and finished with a dual varnish. ... From traditional booming industries like whisky and food to the burgeoning craft spirits sector, Scotland has always been a strong and diverse market in its own right. As such, it cannot be treated simply as a region. A growing number of businesses are attempting to expand their presence north of the border and increase market share and visibility. As the only packaging magazine published in Scotland, Packaging Scotland is uniquely placed to cover the Scottish market and the many people and businesses operating within it."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Ravenwood selects Wedderburn to expand linerless labelling in Australia,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/ravenwood-wedderburn-linerless-labelling-australia/,"Ravenwood selects Wedderburn to expand linerless labelling in Australia ... The agreement expands access in Australia to Ravenwood’s linerless labelling technology. Credit: photobyphotoboy / Shutterstock.com. ... Ravenwood Packaging said Wedderburn Australia has been added to its international network as an authorised distributor of machinery and a print partner. ... The agreement expands access in Australia to Ravenwood’s linerless labelling technology. ... Under the agreement, Wedderburn will distribute Ravenwood’s Nobac linerless labelling machines. ... It is also set to install a Ravenwood Com500 linerless coating system, allowing linerless labels to be manufactured within Australia. ... Ravenwood said the arrangement means Wedderburn will be able to supply a full linerless labelling offering with local expertise. ... Ravenwood Packaging managing director Paul Beamish said: “Australia represents an important growth market for linerless technology, and we’re excited to be partnering with Wedderburn to expand the availability of our solutions across the region. ... “By combining Ravenwood’s linerless machinery and coating technology with Wedderburn’s established market presence and technical expertise, we’re creating a strong platform to support customers looking to improve efficiency, reduce waste and adopt more sustainable labelling practices.” ... Established in 1896, Wedderburn is a family-owned business that operates in Australia and New Zealand across labels, labelling systems, weighing equipment, packaging machinery and food technology. ... The company has also taken part in initiatives aimed at cutting packaging waste and improving recyclability, including the use of FSC-certified materials, involvement in circular economy schemes such as RafCycle, and collaboration with industry bodies focused on packaging sustainability and compostable materials. ... Wedderburn executive chairman Philip Wedderburn said: “This partnership represents an exciting step forward in our commitment to delivering innovative and sustainable labelling solutions to the Australian market. ... “Ravenwood has established itself as a global leader in linerless technology and we are proud to become both an approved distributor of its machinery and printer partner for linerless labels. Together, we look forward to helping Australian businesses access proven linerless solutions that support greater efficiency, reduced waste and improved sustainability outcomes.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Woodberry Packaging acquires two UK packaging businesses,www.packaging-gateway.com (Satarupa Bhowmik),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/woodberry-packaging-acquires-two-uk-packaging-businesses/,"Woodberry Packaging acquires two UK packaging businesses ... The move strengthens Woodberry’s foothold in Europe, expanding its capabilities in pharmaceutical, healthcare and personal care packaging. Credit: SNeG17 / Shutterstock.com. ... Woodberry Packaging has acquired UK packaging manufacturers Medica Packaging and FG Curtis, which trades as Curtis Packaging. ... Financial terms of the deal were not revealed. ... The move strengthens Woodberry’s foothold in Europe, expanding its capabilities in pharmaceutical, healthcare and personal care packaging. ... existing brands and management, preserving continuity ... and suppliers. ... The expanded group employs 650 people across the UK and Ireland and generates combined turnover of more than €120m ($137m). ... Backed by Dublin-based Woodberry Capital, Woodberry Packaging has grown through acquisitions across Ireland and the UK. ... Medica specialises in pharmaceutical and healthcare cartons while Curtis adds expertise in cosmetics and personal care packaging. ... Medica Packaging’s owner Medication Packaging acquired FG Curtis in 2022. ... Woodberry Packaging Group CEO Peter Santo called the deal part of a “clear, long-term strategy of bringing high-quality businesses together and integrating them well to create a stronger whole”. ... Alongside Woodberry Packaging’s existing Reelvision site, the deal gives the group three PS 9000-accredited carton sites in the UK, meeting the pharmaceutical industry’s quality standard. Its Irish business, Colorman, is working toward the same accreditation. ... Woodberry Packaging said the enlarged group can act as a single accredited partner for customers while providing the security of supply increasingly required in regulated markets. ... Curtis managing director James Williams said: “Joining the wider Woodberry group gives us the scale and investment to build on that while keeping the service and standards our customers value.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,"Bedford acquires Tach-It, expands packaging automation | Baking Business",www.bakingbusiness.com (Lucas Cuni-Mertz),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bakingbusiness.com/articles/66528-bedford-acquires-tach-it-expands-packaging-automation,"Bedford acquires Tach-It, expands packaging automation | Baking Business ... # Bedford acquires Tach-It, expands packaging automation ... WORTHINGTON, MINN. — Twist tie and automation manufacturer Bedford Industries acquired Tach-It, a producer of entry-level automated packaging equipment. ... The acquisition of Tach-It, which offers labeling, closing and sealing technology, expands Bedford’s automated packaging portfolio. ... “Like Bedford, Tach-It is a family-owned business with a respected industry reputation built on innovation, reliability and long-standing customer relationships,” said Jay Milbrandt, president of Bedford. “Tach-It’s products complement Bedford’s existing automation capabilities and accelerate our ability to serve customers seeking practical, scalable automation solutions.” ... Current Tach-It customers will continue to receive full support of their machines with no service interruptions, Bedford said. ... “As an industry leader in tabletop and hand-held twist tie machines, labeling solutions and other unique and exclusive product lines, Tach-It is excited about the acquisition with Bedford,” said Steven Clements, president of Tach-It. “The synergies between Bedford and Tach-It are extensive and will open the door to new opportunities, applications and enhanced service and support for our combined customer base.” ... Bedford said it plans to build out the Tach-It brand and integrate its products into broader automation solutions. Bedford, which celebrates its 60th anniversary this year, manufactures twist ties, bag closures, hangtags and identification solutions for a variety of industries, including bakery."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Woodberry Packaging acquires Medica and Curtis | Packaging Scotland,packagingscotland.com (Craig Quirie),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://packagingscotland.com/2026/07/woodberry-packaging-acquires-medica-and-curtis/,"Woodberry Packaging acquires Medica and Curtis | Packaging ... WOODBERRY Packaging has announced that it has acquired Medica Packaging and F.G. Curtis. ... The deal for the two long-established British packaging manufacturers will see the group almost double the size. ... Both businesses will continue to operate under their existing brands and management, with their teams remaining and customer and supplier relationships maintained, Woodberry Packaging said. ... The acquisition strengthens Woodberry’s position across Europe and broadens its capability across pharmaceutical, healthcare and personal care packaging. The enlarged group employs around 650 people across the UK and Ireland and has a combined turnover in excess of €120 million. Financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed. ... Woodberry Packaging is backed by Dublin-based Woodberry Capital and has built its group by acquisition across Ireland and the UK. The acquisition of Medica and Curtis is a significant step in that growth, the company said. ... Medica adds a specialist position in pharmaceutical and healthcare cartons, while Curtis adds expertise in cosmetics and personal care. Combined with the group’s existing Reelvision site, the acquisition gives Woodberry three PS 9000-accredited carton sites in the UK, the pharmaceutical industry’s quality standard, with its Irish business Colorman working toward the same accreditation. ... For customers, the enlarged group is said to offer a single accredited partner with the security of supply that regulated markets increasingly require. ... Curtis, based in Redhill, Surrey, was founded in 1937 and manufactures cartons for the cosmetics and personal care markets, with additional capability in healthcare. It was the first UK carton manufacturer to become a certified B Corporation and the first UK company to achieve World Land Trust carbon-balanced packaging. ... Peter Santo, chief executive of Woodberry Packaging Group, said, “The acquisition of Medica and Curtis is a major step in building our group across Europe. This is part of a clear, long-term strategy of bringing high-quality businesses together and integrating them well to create a stronger whole.” ... Gerard Harford, Medica MD, added, “Joining Woodberry Packaging is an exciting step for Medica. We have built our business on the quality, compliance and security of supply that pharmaceutical customers depend on, and becoming part of a larger group gives us greater scale and investment to do more for them. Our customers will work with the same team, to the same standards, now with a wider group behind them.” ... James Williams, Curtis MD, commented, “Becoming part of Woodberry Packaging is a natural step for Curtis. We have built a strong reputation in cosmetics and personal care packaging, and we are one of the most sustainable carton manufacturers in the country. Joining the wider Woodberry group gives us the scale and investment to build on that, while keeping the service and standards our customers value.” ... From traditional booming industries like whisky and food to the burgeoning craft spirits sector, Scotland has always been a strong and diverse market in its own right. As such, it cannot be treated simply as a region. A growing number of businesses are attempting to expand their presence north of the border and increase market share and visibility. As the only packaging magazine published in Scotland, Packaging Scotland is uniquely placed to cover the Scottish market and the many people and businesses operating within it."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Asteria Group boosts UK labelling infrastructure with Mercian Labels acquisition,www.packagingnews.co.uk (Tony Corbin),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingnews.co.uk/news/asteria-group-boosts-uk-labelling-infrastructure-with-mercian-labels-acquisition-24-06-2026,"Asteria Group boosts UK labelling infrastructure with Mercian Labels acquisition ... # Asteria Group boosts UK labelling infrastructure with Mercian Labels acquisition ... Mercian Labels has joined the Asteria Group, having been acquired for an undisclosed fee. It becomes the 41st production site in the group. ... The expansion of Asteria’s UK label offering signifies another step in its progress as one of Europe’s leading label and packaging solution providers. ... Based in Burntwood, Staffordshire, Mercian Labels is a well-established and highly respected manufacturer of self-adhesive labels serving customers across the food, beverage and pharmaceutical sectors. With extensive capabilities in both flexographic and digital printing technologies, including inkjet and varied embellishments, the company also provides blank labels, and variable data solutions. ... In addition to its broad portfolio of self- ... , Mercian adds technical expertise in specialised tamper-evident and security label initiatives that help customers protect high-value products and strengthen product integrity. The LabelLock tamper evident security labels and tape ranges have been engineered for maximum security. ... Asteria said Mercian’s commitment to quality and sustainability aligns closely with its values and long-term ambitions. The company holds an AA+ BRCGS Packaging Materials certification and is certified to ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 standards, reflecting a focus on quality management and environmental responsibility. These standards demonstrate a shared vision, supporting Asteria’s ambition to become a sustainable frontrunner in the label and packaging industry by 2030. ... “We are delighted to welcome the Mercian team to Asteria,” said Ives Declerck, CEO of Asteria Group. ... “Mercian has earned an excellent reputation for quality, expertise and customer focus. Their capabilities complement our existing UK operations perfectly, while their strong position in food, beverage and pharmaceutical markets strengthens opportunities for future growth.” ... acquisition Mercian Labels 2026-06-24 ... : acquisition Mercian Labels"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Asteria expands in UK with Mercian Labels acquisition - Narrative News,narrative-news.com (NarrativeNews),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://narrative-news.com/asteria-expands-in-uk-with-mercian-labels-acquisition/,"Asteria expands in UK with Mercian Labels acquisition - Narrative News ... Home Finance Asteria expands in UK with Mercian Labels acquisition ... Asteria Group has taken over Mercian Labels, including the UK-based company as its forty first manufacturing location. ... Financial phrases of the deal stay undisclosed. ... Mercian Labels operates from Burntwood, Staffordshire, and develops self-adhesive labels for food, drinks and pharmaceutical clients. ... Its manufacturing work contains flexographic and digital printing, including inkjet, as effectively as ending choices. ... The business also provides clean labels and variable knowledge merchandise. ... According to a company assertion by Asteria, the acquisition broadens its presence in the UK labels market. ... Mercian presents expertise in tamper-evident and security labels used to support product safety and traceability for higher-value items. ... Its LabelLock vary contains security labels and tapes with options such as micro textual content on a clear adhesive edge and an ‘in-register’ void message. ... Mercian holds an AA+ BRCGS Packaging Materials accreditation and is licensed to ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 requirements. ... Asteria Group CEO Ives Declerck said: “We are delighted to welcome the Mercian team to Asteria. Mercian has earned an excellent reputation for quality, expertise and customer focus. Their capabilities complement our existing UK operations perfectly while their strong position in food, beverage and pharmaceutical markets strengthens opportunities for future growth.” ... “Asteria expands in UK with Mercian Labels acquisition” was initially created and revealed by Packaging Gateway, a GlobalData owned model."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Asteria brings Mercian Labels into the group – Print Business – for Forward Thinking Printing,printbusiness.co.uk,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://printbusiness.co.uk/asteria-brings-mercian-labels-into-the-group/,"## Mercian Labels has agreed to acquisition by one of Europe’s fastest growing label businesses. ... Mercian Labels has been acquired by Asteria, one of the fastest growing label conglomerates in Europe. Mercian joins the likes of CS Labels, Berkshire Labels and Proprint Group in the Belgian headquartered business. ... attracted interest from the expanding Belgian ... Ives Declerck in a LinkedIn ... This is endorsed by Declerck who says “the Mercian ethos means the cultural fit is a natural one” adding: “Mercian has earned an excellent reputation for quality, expertise and customer focus. Their capabilities complement our existing UK operations perfectly, while their strong position in food, beverage and pharmaceutical markets strengthens opportunities for future growth.“ ... As part of Asteria Mercian gains the support of a supportive owner and a greater number of cross selling opportunities as Asteria has 40 other plants across Europe. “The expansion of our UK label offering signifies another exciting step in our progress as one of Europe’s leading label and packaging solution providers,” says Asteria. ... The acquisition means that Mercian has had to drop out of the Concordia Group of independent European label printers where Dr Steele has been president. ... The site at Burtwood will be renamed following the takeover, but little else is expected to change in the day to day operation of the business under general manager Ricard Joines. ... - Mercian picks Screen for latest press - Mercian wins Computype barcode business - Asteria adds ProPrint to growing network"
