eutical, household, food, beverage, and other end markets. Complementing its vast portfolio of packaging solutions, O.Berk also operates an e-commerce platform, BottleStore.com, that supports small businesses, entrepreneurs, and emerging brands as the one-stop-shop for their packaging needs. O.Berk's additional value-added services include design and innovation, custom tooling, decoration, warehousing and logistics management, quality assurance, and regulatory compliance support. ... ""We are excited to welcome O.Berk to Berlin Packaging. Like Berlin, O.Berk has a long history of supporting customers with packaging products and value-added services,"" said Rick Brandt, CEO of Berlin Packaging Americas. ""This combination expands our industry-leading capabilities and strengthens our expertise in growing beauty, personal care, pharmaceutical, and nutraceutical markets."" ... ""We are proud to join forces with Berlin Packaging and excited for the opportunities this partnership creates,"" said Marc Gaelen, President and CEO of O.Berk Company. ""Berlin's global supply chain, digital capabilities, sustainability expertise, logistics platform, and Studio One Eleven® design services will enhance the solutions available to our customers and create new opportunities for our employees and suppliers."" ... ""Family-owned businesses like O.Berk bring deep industry expertise, entrepreneurial spirit, and deep relationships with stakeholders,"" said Bill Hayes, Global CEO and President of Berlin Packaging. ""We are excited to bring our organizations together and build on that momentum for years to come."" ... Berlin Packaging is the world's largest Hybrid Packaging Supplier® of glass, plastic, and metal containers and closures. The company supplies billions of items annually along with package design, financing, consulting, warehousing, and logistics services for customers across all industries. Berlin Packaging brings together the best of manufacturing, distribution, and income-adding service providers. Its mission is to increase the net income of its customers through packaging products and services. ... ### Berlin Packaging expands its presence in EMEA with the acquisition of BlueSky in the United Kingdom ... Berlin Packaging, the world's largest Hybrid Packaging Supplier®, specializing in the supply of glass, plastic and metal packaging and closures,..."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Berlin Packaging Acquires O.Berk Company To Expand North American Presence,pulse2.com (Amit Chowdhry),2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pulse2.com/berlin-packaging-acquires-o-berk-company-to-expand-north-american-presence/,"Berlin Packaging Acquires O.Berk Company To Expand North American Presence ... # Berlin Packaging Acquires O.Berk Company To Expand North American Presence ... Berlin Packaging Acquires O.Berk Company To Expand North American Presence ... Berlin Packaging, the world’s largest hybrid packaging supplier, announced the acquisition of O.Berk Company, a family-owned provider of plastic, glass, and metal containers, closures, and value-added packaging solutions. The transaction expands Berlin Packaging’s presence in key pharmaceutical, nutraceutical, beauty, and personal care markets across North America. ... Founded in 1910 in Newark, New Jersey, O.Berk began as a supplier of bottles and jars to local chemical plants and food companies. The company later transitioned to family ownership and played a role in the commercialization of plastic bottles and closures. Today, under fourth-generation owners Marc Gaelen and Meryl Japha, O.Berk operates facilities in New Jersey, Connecticut, Maryland, and Southern California and serves customers in beauty, personal care, pharmaceutical, nutraceutical, household, food, and beverage markets. ... In addition to its packaging portfolio, O.Berk operates BottleStore.com, an e-commerce platform that supports small businesses and emerging brands. The company also provides design and innovation services, custom tooling, decoration, warehousing, logistics management, quality assurance, and regulatory compliance support. ... Berlin Packaging said the acquisition enhances its capabilities in fast-growing end markets, adds to its value-added services, and expands its North American footprint. The combination also provides O.Berk customers with access to Berlin Packaging’s global supply chain, sustainability expertise, logistics capabilities, digital tools, and Studio One Eleven design services. ... Berlin Packaging supplies billions of glass, plastic, and metal containers and closures annually, combining manufacturing, distribution, and value-added services to support customers across multiple industries. ... “We are excited to welcome O.Berk to Berlin Packaging. Like Berlin, O.Berk has a long history of supporting customers with packaging products and value-added services. This combination expands our industry-leading capabilities and strengthens our expertise in growing beauty, personal care, pharmaceutical, and nutraceutical markets.” ... “We are proud to join forces with Berlin Packaging and excited for the opportunities this partnership creates. Berlin’s global supply chain, digital capabilities, sustainability expertise, logistics platform, and Studio One Eleven design services will enhance the solutions available to our customers and create new opportunities for our employees and suppliers.” ... “Family-owned businesses like O.Berk bring deep industry expertise, entrepreneurial spirit, and deep relationships with stakeholders. We are excited to bring our organizations together and build on that momentum for years to come.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Paranova sets out major investment plans following sale to Kingswood Capital,www.packagingnews.co.uk (Waqas Qureshi),2026-06-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingnews.co.uk/features/news-analysis/amberley-labels-purchase-central-to-kingswood-s-luxury-packaging-plans-08-06-2026,"Paranova sets out major investment plans following sale to Kingswood Capital ... # Paranova sets out major investment plans following sale to Kingswood Capital ... Coveris recently sold its paper business, now Paranova, to Kingswood Capital Management, including labelling division Amberley and graphics business Rivendell. Waqas Qureshi spoke to Paranova CEO Jo Ormrod. ... Kingswood Capital Management recently acquired Coveris’ BU Paper Unit, which specialises in premium labels and folding carton box boards. ... The unit, which was renamed Paranova, manufactures self-adhesive, linerless labels, lined board, cartons and trays for leading manufacturers and brands and also supplies luxury labelling from its Amberley Labels Blandford and Boston plants, and most recently acquired label site in Brno, Czech Republic. ... Are there new markets Paranova is considering entering? We’re always looking ahead. Paranova continually explores opportunities to complement our existing capabilities and expand into markets where our expertise in innovation, sustainability and high-quality manufacturing can add value. In 2024, we made our first acquisition in mainland Europe, establishing a presence in the Czech Republic. Looking forward, our strategy is to continue expanding in mainland Europe, supplying fibre-based packaging solutions and serving end markets that demand a high-service, partnership-led model. ... What investment plans do you have? Paranova is committed to ongoing investment in our people, technology and manufacturing infrastructure. Remaining at the forefront of innovation, sustainability and operational excellence requires continual development across our operations. With demand for fibre-based packaging continuing to grow, we will continue to invest in additional capacity, capability and process improvement across our label and board businesses to ensure we can support our customers as their needs evolve. ... What plans do you have for Amberley Labels – a key luxury labels specialist? Amberley Labels is a key part of the Paranova group and will remain central to our premium packaging strategy. Its award-winning output and technical expertise set a benchmark within the luxury packaging market. Building on that strong foundation, Amberley has recently expanded its offer to include luxury cartons, enabling the business to deliver a more complete, premium packaging solution for brands seeking consistency, quality and impact across their packaging portfolios. ... How has Q1 been for Paranova? Q1 has been a strong and encouraging start, particularly given the growth targets tied to our new business offering. We’ve seen solid momentum with strong performance in non-food markets, which reflects the growing customer demand in those segments. ... How has Paranova handled EPR, NI contributions, and supply chain issues from the Middle East war? We’ve taken a proactive and transparent approach in managing these challenges. Open communication with both customers and supply partners has been central, particularly when navigating EPR. This has allowed us not only to remain compliant, but also to support customers in making informed packaging choices aligned to both cost and environmental considerations. From a supply chain perspective, the inflationary pressures and raw material disruption linked to the situation in the Middle East have required close coordination. Our teams have worked collaboratively with customers to provide clear guidance on lead times and availability, ensuring expectations are well managed and supply continuity is maintained. A key differentiator for us has been our industry-leading SIOP processes. These enable more accurate forecasting and closer alignment with customers, allowing us to anticipate disruption and plan more effectively together. At the same time, we continue to invest in the right technology and operational capabilities to improve efficiency and offset rising cost pressures, ensuring we remain both competitive and reliable as a partner. ... What does a good 2026 look like for Paranova in December 2026? A good 2026 for Paranova would see us deliver a smooth and well-recognised transition to our new brand, while reinforcing our position as a truly customer-first partner. From a commercial standpoint, success means deepening our key partnerships and driving growth in targeted areas, consistently delivering value and reliability to our customers. At the same time, continuing to build our reputation as an employer of choice remains critical, as attracting and retaining the right talent underpins our long-term success. Operationally, we will have successfully executed several transformational investment projects that enhance our scale, speed, and technical capability, making us more agile and responsive."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Harkwell signs for an HP Indigo 200K - Digital Labels & Packaging,www.dlpmag.com,2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.dlpmag.com/news/102995/harkwell-signs-for-an-hp-indigo-200k/,"Harkwell signs for an HP Indigo 200K - Digital Labels & Packaging ... # Harkwell signs for an HP Indigo 200K ... Dorset-based labels and packaging manufacturer, Harkwell, has signed an agreement to purchase an HP Indigo 200K to provide the company with additional capacity and improve lead times. ... The Digital Labels & Packaging Group Member, signed for the new press on 2 June, 2026. The new press is 35% faster than the company’s current machine, giving it additional capacity and helping us continue to provide the service and lead times for its customers. ... Harkwell managing director, Andrew Mansfield, said: “We look forward to welcoming a new addition to the HP fleet. It’s a great step forward for Harkwell and its future prospects. Thank you to Edwin Dalby and Darren Pickford for their time spent bringing this new addition to reality.” ... According to a post on the company’s LinkedIn in page, the investment is another important step in Harkwell’s continued growth."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,CCL completes acquisition of Sleever - Digital Labels & Packaging,www.dlpmag.com,2026-06-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.dlpmag.com/news/102980/ccl-completes-acquisition-of-sleever/,"CCL completes acquisition of Sleever - Digital Labels & Packaging ... # CCL completes acquisition of Sleever ... CCL Industries has completed its acquisition of Sleever International, its subsidiaries and related companies. Digital Labels & Packaging first reported on the acquisition in March 2026. ... Sleever is a privately owned manufacturer of shrink sleeve labels, extruded films and application equipment serving consumer packaged goods and healthcare customers worldwide. Following the transaction, the acquired label and film businesses will be renamed CCL Label and Innovia Films, respectively. The application equipment business will continue operating under the Sleever name. ... Geoffrey Martin, president and chief executive officer of CCL Industries, said: “I am pleased that Sleever’s former principal shareholder, Eric Fresnel, has been retained in an advisory capacity while Guenther Birkner, president of CCL Label’s Food & Beverage sector and Innovia Films, will now have overall responsibility for this acquisition with immediate effect.”"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Printweek - BGM launches new Compact range - Printweek,www.printweek.com (Richard Stuart-Turner),2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.printweek.com/content/product-news/bgm-launches-new-compact-range,"Printweek - BGM launches new Compact range - Printweek ... # BGM launches new Compact range ... Bar Graphic Machinery (BGM) has launched a new range of finishing lines targeted at producers of digitally printed labels. ... Devised and developed by BGM’s engineering team in collaboration with managing director Adam James, Compact and Compact Pro are built on a heavy-duty, small footprint frame. Compact is 2.5m-long and Compact Pro is 3.5m-long. ... The Compact range is a new addition to Bradford, West Yorkshire-based BGM’s portfolio and hasn’t replaced anything from the company’s existing lineup. ... James said: “The digital label printing market continues to grow strongly. To support this growth and allow label printers to take advantage of the opportunities, finishing must grow with the market. ... “Through conversations with customers, internal research, and my own experience, we know that as much as 80% of the volume of labels printed digitally can be finished using a standard gloss varnish or lamination coupled with semi-rotary die-cutting. ... “In reality, many label printers continue to run work down finishing lines that are overspecified for the needs of the digital label printing market. These finishing lines can offer high-value foiling, embossing, or laser die-cutting. ... “This causes bottlenecks and costs printers time and money as equipment utilisation is not optimised to match their job basket. With the Compact range, we address this imbalance.” ... Compact was formally introduced to the market during an open house event at BGM’s headquarters and manufacturing centre in Bradford earlier this month that hosted around 50 guests. ... With Compact and Compact Pro currently going through final development and testing, commercial availability is expected to follow later this year, in the Q3/Q4 timeframe. ... Orders can be placed now and BGM said there is already strong interest off the back of the open house. ... Duplo acquired BGM last summer."
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Self-adhesive labels: La Prensa absorbs 100% Scriba,www.efanews.eu,2026-05-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.efanews.eu/item/60390-self-adhesive-labels-la-prensa-absorbs-100-scriba.html,"Self-adhesive labels: La Prensa absorbs 100% Scriba ... # Self-adhesive labels: La Prensa absorbs 100% Scriba ... ## Integration to support the growth of the acquiring company ... lml - 60390 Milan, MI, Italy, 05/25/2026 12:44 EFA News - European Food Agency"
BERKSHIRE LABELS,,,,Exa,Printweek - Printed.com supports labels division with Titanium install - Printweek,www.printweek.com (Richard Stuart-Turner),2026-05-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.printweek.com/content/news/printedcom-supports-labels-division-with-titanium-install,"Printweek - Printed.com supports labels division with Titanium install - Printweek ... # Printed.com supports labels division with Titanium install ... Web-to-print firm Printed.com has upgraded its labels and stickers division with the installation of a Titanium 330 R digital label cutter. ... Installed last week at the company’s Cramlington site, the Titanium 330 R is equipped with nine cutting blades that work in tandem and provides end-to-end finishing including cold lamination, digital die-cutting, waste weeding (stripping), and slitting in a single pass. ... The machine was supplied by International Graphic Supplies (IGS), which in the past also supplied two Titanium 2516 large-format flatbed cutters already operated by Printed.com. ... It joined a Konica Minolta AccurioLabel 230 press that has also recently been installed to support the labels division, with the two new machines together enabling the company to produce complex kiss-cut labels on demand. ... David Duncan, production director at Printed.com, said: “We are continuously investing in technology so our customers can achieve more with their branding. ... “The short-run label market is incredibly vibrant right now, and the addition of the AccurioLabel 230 and the Titanium 330 R ensures we can deliver the precision, quality, and flexibility that today’s market demands. ... “We have successfully transitioned these systems into full-scale production, and the results speak for themselves. The output is consistently excellent, maintaining high-fidelity quality while stripping away the operational friction that typically hinders traditional label production.” ... Peter Flynn, managing director of IGS, added: “We are delighted to support Printed.com once again as they expand their production capabilities. ... “We have a longstanding relationship with the team and having seen the success they’ve achieved with their two existing Titanium 2516 flatbed cutters it was a natural progression to integrate the Titanium 330 R into their new label department. ... “It’s a testament to the reliability and ROI that the Titanium range delivers.” ... Printed.com is The Printed Group’s main trading brand. Nick Green originally founded Printed.com in 2011 but left the business last year, with Rob Haycock appointed CEO of The Printed Group. Simon Dunn was subsequently appointed to the role of CEO at Printed.com in March this year.Late last year Printed.com took the wraps off its plans for international expansion when a new US version of its site went live. ... In its most recent accounts, to 31 March 2025, the overall group had sales of £23.2m and it employed around 185 staff on average during the year."
