TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Japan's Eneos to buy Texas chemical maker TPC in US push - Nikkei Asia,asia.nikkei.com,2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://asia.nikkei.com/business/business-deals/japan-s-eneos-to-buy-texas-chemical-maker-tpc-in-us-push,"Japan's Eneos to buy Texas chemical maker TPC in US push - Nikkei Asia ... # Japan's Eneos to buy Texas chemical maker TPC in US push ... Oil company to be 3rd-largest global producer of feedstock used in auto tires ... Japanese oil company Eneos Holdings is looking for opportunities in the U.S. chemical market, which is eight times as large as Japan's. (Photo by Takashi Miyazaki) ... TOKYO -- Japanese oil company Eneos Holdings will purchase all of Texas-based chemical manufacturer TPC Holdings for an undisclosed sum under plans announced Friday."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Petro Chems Maker TPC Group Sells to Eneos - The Deal,www.thedeal.com (David Elman),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thedeal.com/scoops-exclusives/petro-chems-maker-tpc-group-sells-to-eneos/,"Petro Chems Maker TPC Group Sells to Eneos - The Deal ... Tokyo-based energy company Eneos will acquire TPC for an undisclosed sum two years after The Deal reported that TPC was working with advisers on a sale. ... Petrochemicals maker TPC Group Inc. on Friday, Aug. 7, said it’s agreed to sell to Eneos Holdings Inc. ... Neither TPC nor Eneos in its own statement disclosed the financial terms of the transaction, which will see Eneos acquire TPC’s petrochemical operations in Houston, along with terminal operations in Port Neches, Texas, and Lake Charles, La. ... Tokyo-based Eneos said it will make the acquisition through a merger with a special purpose vehicle established under a U.S. subsidiary. The company added that TPC will enhance its supply capabilities and responsiveness to market fluctuations, as well as strengthen its supply chain. By combining its expertise in safe and stable operations with TPC’s business platform, Eneos said it plans to enhance corporate value and strengthen the reach of its materials business, including in North America. ... The Deal reported in 2024 that TPC and its financial backers, including Redwood Capital Management LLC, had engaged Moelis & Co. LLC to solicit interest in the company, with TPC marketed on Ebitda approaching $250 million. ... The Deal said at the time that the process was expected to attract large financial sponsors capable of writing equity checks north of $500 million, with TPC expected to fetch 5 to 7 times Ebitda, representing a price tag of somewhere between $1.25 billion and $1.75 billion. ... Eneo’s statement shows TPC has $25 million in operating profit on $1.51 billion in net sales last year. Redwood Capital is its largest shareholder, with a 40.5% stake, followed by Monarch Alternative Capital LP (21.4%) and PGIM Inc. (19.8%). ... Group, a processor of crude C4 hydrocarbons including butadiene, butene-1 and isobutene, was previously owned by private equity firms SK Capital Partners LP and First Reserve Corp. before years of diminishing performance and a plant explosion ultimately led the business to seek bankruptcy protection in 2022. ... with operations spanning oil, natural gas, metals and renewable energy. ... was established in 2 ... 10 as JXTG Holdings Inc. through the merger of Nippon Oil Corp. and Nippon Mining Holdings Inc. ... Eneos in May agreed to acquire the downstream fuels and lubricants marketing businesses of Chevron Corp. (CVX) in Singapore, Malaysia, the Philippines, Australia, Vietnam and Indonesia, expanding its footprint across Southeast Asia and Oceania. ... TPC and Eneos expect the transaction to close in October, subject to customary closing conditions, including applicable regulatory approvals. ... TPC Group tapped Moelis for financial advice and Paul Hastings LLP for counsel. CEO Ed Dineen worked on the deal internally along with Redwood Capital co-chief investment officers Ruben Kliksberg and Sean Sauler"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Tronox posts Q2 miss, forecasts continued TiO2 price gains",chemweek.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://chemweek.com/document/show/phoenix/6265851/Tronox-posts-Q2-miss-forecasts-continued-TiO2-price-gains,"Tronox posts Q2 miss, forecasts continued TiO2 price gains ... # Tronox posts Q2 miss, forecasts continued TiO2 price gains ... 11:50 AM August 06, 2026 Clay Boswell ... Adjusted EPS came to a 51-cent loss, down from a 28-cent loss in the year-ago quarter, short of analysts’ consensus estimate of a 37-cent loss."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"US Trinseo reports wider Q2 loss, eyes year-end bankruptcy exit | ChemOrbis",www.chemorbis.com (ChemOrbis),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.chemorbis.com/en/plastics-news/US-Trinseo-reports-wider-Q2-loss-eyes-year-end-bankruptcy-exit/2026/08/07/982067,"US Trinseo reports wider Q2 loss, eyes year-end bankruptcy exit | ChemOrbis Just two weeks ago, the question was whether the renewed war premium in crude oil could finally put a floor under polymer markets after months of relentless declines. Brent crude extended its rally far beyond expectations, climbing from the mid-$80s/bbl in H1 July to briefly settle above $100/bbl on July 23 as geopolitical tensions in the Middle East intensified. This visibly shifted the sentiment upwards in Asia including China, Southeast Asia and India as well in Türkiye and Egypt while the slump slowed down in Europe... Dow’s €1.1 billion claim puts Europe’s ethylene cartel dispute back in focus Europe’s long-running ethylene cartel dispute has returned to the spotlight after Dow Europe filed a €1.1 billion damages claim against four companies accused of manipulating Europe’s ethylene benchmark price. The lawsuit is the latest in a series of civil actions stemming from the European Commission’s 2020 decision that found Clariant, Celanese, Orbia and Westlake had coordinated their ethylene purchasing strategies between 2011 and 2017 to influence the Monthly Contract Price (MCP)... Crude oil surges on renewed war premium; will it reverse the polymer slump? The renewed geopolitical tensions have pushed Brent crude back into the mid-$80s/bbl, rapidly rebuilding some of the war-risk premium that had evaporated after June's ceasefire hopes. This has also helped buoy the sentiment recently in polymer markets, where prices have been on a downturn for the past couple of months. After months of sluggish demand, ample supplies, and relentless price erosion, sellers are seizing on higher feedstock costs to argue that the market has reached its bottom... The EU-US tariff agreement has largely been viewed through the lens of polymers, particularly PE, and as a boost for US polymer exports. Yet the implications reach well beyond resin markets. By eliminating customs duties across the entire Chapter 39, the regulation also covers a broad range of semi-finished and finished plastic products, potentially reshaping competition across Europe's downstream plastics value chain..."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Traxion Materials to Expand Tire Shredding, Recycling Operations in Campbell County - TNECD",tnecd.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://tnecd.com/news/traxion-materials-to-expand-tire-shredding-recycling-operations-in-campbell-county/,"Traxion Materials to Expand Tire Shredding, Recycling Operations in Campbell County - TNECD ... # Traxion Materials to Expand Tire Shredding, Recycling Operations in Campbell County ... NASHVILLE, Tenn. – Tennessee Gov. Bill Lee, Deputy Gov. and Department of Economic and Community Development (TNECD) Commissioner Stuart C. McWhorter and Traxion Materials officials announced today the company will expand operations in Campbell County. ... Traxion Materials has invested more than $5 million in Jacksboro, Tennessee, through an ongoing project that will expand the company’s recycling and upcycling processes and create 49 new jobs across the region. With existing infrastructure that includes structured tire collection, wholesale tire distribution, tire shredding and processing and Tire Derived Fuel (TDF) supply, the company is well-positioned for continued growth and increased production across its network. ... Anchored by its primary facility in LaFollette, Traxion Materials operates the Traxion Tire LifeCycle Network across Tennessee, Kentucky, Florida, Georgia, North Carolina and South Carolina, partnering with tire retailers, automotive dealerships, manufacturers, fleet operators and logistics companies to sustainably manage the flow of used tires across the country. Expanding its regional footprint supports Traxion’s mission to keep second-life tire materials in productive use rather than in landfills or stockpiles. ... “We’ve built our operation here in both LaFollette and Jacksboro because this region has the workforce, the location and the partnerships to support our steadfast mission. We’ve intentionally planted our roots at home in Campbell County, Tennessee, and this investment reflects our commitment to our employees and our community for the long haul.” – Greg Coleman, founding investor and president/CEO, Traxion Materials ... “TVA and the LaFollette Utilities Board congratulate Traxion on its plans to expand operations in Campbell County. We are proud to partner with the Tennessee Department of Economic and Community Development, East Tennessee Economic Development Agency, Campbell County Industrial Development Board and Campbell County in our shared commitment to fostering economic growth in the region and to support companies like Traxion Materials in its continued business success.” – Heidi Smith, vice president of economic development, TVA ... “Traxion’s continued investment in Campbell County is another example of the innovation and economic momentum we are seeing across East Tennessee. These 49 new jobs will create new opportunities for local families, and I appreciate the company’s confidence in our community and workforce as it continues to grow.” – Sen. Ken Yager (R-Kingston) ... “Traxion’s decision to expand in Campbell County is another strong vote of confidence in Tennessee’s business climate. This investment will create quality jobs, strengthen our local economy and provide new opportunities for families across our community. I’m grateful to everyone who helped make this project possible and look forward to seeing its positive impact for years to come.” – Rep. Dennis Powers (R-Jacksboro) ... Traxion Materials, LLC is a used tire wholesale and processing company headquartered in LaFollette, Tennessee, empowering businesses across the region to recycle tires responsibly and sustainably. Through its Traxion Tire LifeCycle Network, the company manages structured collection, wholesale distribution, and Tire Derived Fuel (TDF) supply, serving hundreds of customers across Tennessee, Kentucky, Florida, Georgia, North Carolina and South Carolina. Traxion is working toward a zero-landfill standard, ensuring used tires entrusted to the company are responsibly processed, repurposed or converted into cleaner energy alternatives. For more information, visit Traxion at traxionmaterials.com. ... - Local tire recycler to create 49 new jobs, invests $5M in Jacksboro - New project will enhance primary facility in LaFollette"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Trucordia acquires Shipley & Pease in specialty liability push | Insurance Business,www.insurancebusinessmag.com (Josh Recamara),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.insurancebusinessmag.com/us/news/mergers-acquisitions/trucordia-acquires-shipley-and-pease-in-specialty-liability-push-584942.aspx,"Trucordia acquires Shipley & Pease in specialty liability push | Insurance Business ... # Trucordia acquires Shipley & Pease in specialty liability push ... ### The deal follows a similar move into lawyers' professional liability, suggesting a deliberate strategy beyond volume-driven consolidation ... Trucordia has acquired the assets of Shipley & Pease Insurance, a specialized architects and engineers (A&E) professional liability brokerage, in a deal that points to a broader shift in what well-capitalized acquirers are prioritizing. ... The deal follows Trucordia's acquisition of Dominion Insurance Services, a California-based boutique brokerage specializing in lawyers' professional liability, completed in late July 2026, according to Coverager. ... Together, the two deals suggest a deliberate strategy: building out specialty professional liability capabilities through targeted acquisitions of established niche brokerages, rather than pursuing the volume-driven consolidation typically associated with private equity-backed platforms. ... Founded in 1996 by Dave Shipley and later expanded under Stan Pease, the Woodinville, Washington-based firm grew to become one of the largest independently owned brokerages in the country specializing in A&E professional liability. ... The firm recently marked its 30th year in business and achieved 500% growth over the past decade, driven largely by client referrals. It serves clients primarily across Washington, Oregon, and California, with expansion already underway into Idaho and Arizona, and is a founding member of AE ProNet, a nationally recognized group of brokers, insurers, and attorneys focused on improving insurance products and risk management services for architects and engineers. ... Shipley & Pease did not sell from a position of distress. It sold from strength, after three decades in business and a decade of strong growth, using the acquisition to extend its regional footprint through a national platform's resources rather than building that expansion alone. ... As part of Trucordia, the team will continue delivering the personalized service it is known for while gaining broader reach and added resources to serve clients on a larger national scale. ... Founded in 1987 and headquartered in Lindon, Utah, Trucordia has grown to more than 5,000 employees nationwide. The company is backed by private equity investors including The Carlyle Group and Blue Owl Capital, according to PitchBook's company profile. ... Brokers competing against Trucordia for A&E or professional liability clients, particularly in the Pacific Northwest, should expect a more resourced rival than before. ... What was previously a boutique operation now carries the backing of a national, well-capitalized platform, a shift worth factoring into competitive strategy for anyone pitching against Shipley & Pease's former client base or similar prospects in the region. ... - Trucordia acquires Connecticut agency Paradiso Financial - Trucordia acquires CADA Insurance, expands in Louisiana"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Atlas Copco acquires compressed air business of 3C Industrial | M&A & Corporate Strategy | gasworld,www.gasworld.com (gasworld),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gasworld.com/story/atlas-copco-acquires-compressed-air-business-of-3c-industrial/2256367.article/,"Atlas Copco acquires compressed air business of 3C Industrial | M&A & Corporate Strategy | gasworld ... # Atlas Copco acquires compressed air business of 3C Industrial By Sophie Gregory 3 hours ago 1 min read Compressed air and vacuum solutions company Atlas Copco Group has expanded its Texas footprint through the acquisition of the compressed air business of 3C Industrial (3C). ... Part of the service division within Atlas Copco’s compressor technique business area, 3C provides industrial air compressor equipment, air compressor services, and air treatment products in Texas. ... The company is headquartered in Corpus Christi and has a network spanning Houston, Fort Worth, San Antonio, and Austin. ... In 2025, it generated revenues of approximately $11m. ... Philippe Ernens, Business Area President, Compressor Technique, said the acquisition further expands the company’s presence and customer outreach in Texas. ... The purchase price was not disclosed. ... Atlas Copco’s compressor technique business area provides compressed air and gas solutions through a global network."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Francisco Partners Buys Majority Stake in Building Materials Provider Command Alkon | Engineering News-Record,www.enr.com (Jeff Yoders),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.enr.com/articles/63426-francisco-partners-buys-majority-stake-in-building-materials-provider-command-alkon,"Francisco Partners Buys Majority Stake in Building Materials Provider Command Alkon | Engineering News-Record ... ## Terms were not disclosed but Command Alkon will continue to operate under current leadership ... Command Alkon announced Aug. 4 that global investment firm Francisco Partners has agreed to acquire a majority stake in the concrete materials company. Thoma Bravo Heidelberg Materials, an integrated manufacturer of concrete and other heavy building materials, will retain its minority stake in Command Alkon. ... ""Over the past several years, together with Thoma Bravo and Heidelberg Materials, we have executed a clear long-term strategy focused on helping our customers modernize and connect their operations through Command Cloud,"" said Command Alkon CEO Martin Willoughy, who will stay on as leader of the Dublin, Ohio-based materials provider. ""Together, we have expanded our cloud platform, strengthened our services and laid the foundation for the next generation of AI-powered capabilities."" ... In addition to its homegrown Command Cloud platform that allows contractors and other customers to manage concrete batch creation and delivery, Command Alkon last summer acquired Digital Fleet, a cloud platform for ready mix truck dispatch and delivery. Tim Oakes, former CEO of Digital Fleet, will continue as senior vice president and global head of fleet solutions at Command Alkon. ... not replacing it,"" ... Command Alkon will continue to operate under its own name and serve all of the concrete and cementitious materials markets in the U.S. it serves. ... ""Command Alkon has built a technology platform that powers mission-critical operations across one of the world’s most essential industries,"" said Petri Oksanen and Quentin Lathuille, Partners at Francisco Partners. ""Infrastructure investment is accelerating across major markets, and artificial intelligence is significantly enhancing the value Command Alkon can bring to its customers."" ... Willoughby said Francisco Partners shares Command Alkon's long-term vision because ""they believe, as we do, that the heavy building materials industry deserves technology purpose-built for its unique needs. They are investing in the strategy we've been executing—not replacing it."""
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"MMS Group Acquires TMI-Orion and TMI-USA, Anchoring JRI's Commitment to the North American Market",www.prnewswire.com (JRI USA),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/mms-group-acquires-tmi-orion-and-tmi-usa-anchoring-jris-commitment-to-the-north-american-market-302841423.html,"MMS Group Acquires TMI-Orion and TMI-USA, Anchoring JRI's Commitment to the North American Market Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... CHICAGO, Aug. 4, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- JRI, a global leader in environmental monitoring and metrology, today announced that parent company MMS Group has completed the acquisition of TMI-Orion and TMI-USA, now operating as JRI TMI and JRI TMI USA. ... The acquisition brings JRI TMI's 30+ years of expertise in precision validation and monitoring into the MMS Group ecosystem, creating organic synergy with JRI. ... JRI TMI USA, based in Reston, Virginia, provides North and Latin American customers local production, aftermarket service, and an in-house metrology lab accredited to ISO/IEC 17025 (ANAB-certified) for temperature, humidity, and pressure. ... JRI and J ... full value chain for environmental monitoring, validation, and compliance. ... ""We are thrilled to welcome the JRI TMI, JRI TMI USA, and TMI-Dynamics teams to MMS Group,"" said Pascal Vermeersch, President of MMS Group. ""This acquisition gives our customers a comprehensive range of complementary premium solutions: reliable, user-friendly monitors and software for virtually any controlled environment."" ... A key part of JRI's expansion is its new cleanroom monitoring module, allowing organizations to modernize infrastructure without disruptive replacements by integrating with existing particle counters, airflow monitors, and pressure sensors. ... JRI's mobile asset-tracking capabilities also deliver full traceability from manufacturing to point of sale, meeting requirements including GDP, DSCSA, and WHO Annex 5. ... ""Organizations in regulated environments face increasing pressure to prove compliance and maintain visibility into their environments,"" said Jim Lehr, Business Development Director, North America at JRI. ... ""With JRI's metrology expertise and JRI TMI's extreme-environment validation capabilities, customers can modernize their monitoring systems while preserving investments and meeting the most demanding regulatory standards."" ... JRI has also launched a new North American website, giving organizations easier access to its monitoring, mapping, and metrology technologies. ... About JRI JRI is a global provider of environmental monitoring, mapping, and metrology solutions designed to ensure compliance, product safety, and operational visibility in highly regulated industries. The company serves pharmaceutical, life sciences, healthcare, food and beverage, and industrial organizations worldwide through scalable monitoring platforms and precision measurement technologies. JRI is a member of the MMS Group, which also includes https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0&l=en&o=4744454-1&h=1831004845&u=https%3A%2F%2Fciet-mms.com%2F&a=%C2%A0 CIET Pharma and JRI TMI, forming a complete ecosystem for environmental monitoring, validation, and compliance across regulated industries."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,TS Trillion Sees Operating Profit Soar 15-Fold in H1... Distribution Restructuring Delivers Strong Results - The Asia Business Daily,www.asiae.co.kr (Jang Hyowon),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2026080416471990621,"TS Trillion Sees Operating Profit Soar 15-Fold in H1... Distribution Restructuring Delivers Strong Results - The Asia Business Daily ... TS Trillion (317240) announced on August 4 that, thanks to the restructuring of its distribution channels, its operating profit for the first half of this year surged more than 15 times compared to the same period last year, achieving a turnaround in performance. ... According to the company’s provisional standalone results for the first half, revenue reached 15.14156 billion won, up 18% compared to the same period last year. Operating profit skyrocketed by 1,511% to 1.183 billion won, while net profit surged by approximately 1.6 billion won year-on-year to 636 million won, successfully returning to profitability. ... The company attributed this improvement primarily to the restructuring of its distribution channels with a focus on profitability. By reducing the proportion of home shopping and military supply channels, which incurred high commissions and fixed costs, and instead focusing on expanding general retail partners and online sales channels, the company significantly enhanced its profitability. ... In fact, home shopping sales decreased by 31.4% compared to the same period last year, and military supply sales also declined by 27.5%. On the other hand, sales through general retail partners, such as Olive Young (joined in November last year) and Daiso (joined in January this year), increased by 71.7%, and Smart Store sales rose by 67%, driving the company’s performance growth. ... The company assessed that by shifting its sales structure to focus on high-margin distribution channels, it achieved both top-line growth and improved profitability at the same time. ... Industry insiders analyzed that, even amid a downturn in domestic consumption that has led to sluggish results for consumer goods companies, TS Trillion has achieved meaningful results through business restructuring focused on profitability. They evaluated that the company succeeded in strengthening its profit-generating capacity, rather than merely expanding its scale. ... An industry official said, ""The fact that operating profit increased more than 15-fold and net profit turned positive means the company’s profit structure has normalized,"" adding, ""If global market expansion and new business momentum are added in the second half, annual performance improvement as well as a revaluation of corporate value may be possible."" ... This performance is significant in that it demonstrates the company’s profitability-focused transformation, as its strategy to reduce low-profit distribution channels and shift sales toward online and general retail partners delivered tangible results."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Doosan's SK Siltron acquisition reshapes semiconductor supply chain, accelerates AI-focused portfolio shift",www.digitimes.com (Jingyue Hsiao),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260803VL201/doosan-sk-siltron-acquisition-wafer-materials.html,"Doosan's SK Siltron acquisition reshapes semiconductor supply chain, accelerates AI-focused portfolio shift ... # Doosan's SK Siltron acquisition reshapes semiconductor supply chain, accelerates AI-focused portfolio shift ... Jingyue Hsiao ... , DIGITIMES, Taipei Aug 3, 2026, 09:11 0 Doosan Group's agreement to acquire a controlling stake in SK Siltron for KRW2.3 trillion (US$1.6 billion) will expand its semiconductor footprint from materials and testing into wafer manufacturing, while giving SK Group additional resources for its AI..."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"The Bottom Line: Itaconix, Albany and Unitil - NH Business Review",www.nhbr.com (Amanda Andrews),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.nhbr.com/the-bottom-line-itaconix-albany-and-unitil/,"ITACONIX REPORTS RECORD FIRST-HALF REVENUE ... Itaconix plc (AIM: ITX) (OTCQB: ITXXF) reported record first-half revenue of $8.3 million for the six months ended June 30, a 72% increase from the same period in 2025 and a 46% gain over the second half of last year. ... The specialty polymer company said growth was driven across all major product segments, with gross profit margin expected to remain in line with full-year 2025 at 36%. ... Performance Ingredients, which primarily serves the dish detergent market, posted strong growth in Europe, the Middle East and Africa, and North America. The company attributed the increase to higher reorder volumes from existing customers and new unit-dose detergent customers in both regions. ... Revenue also increased for SPARX Formulated Solutions as demand grew for its formulations used in solid unit-dose dish and laundry detergents in North America. ... Itaconix said it continues to develop longer-term growth opportunities through its BIO*Asterix specialty monomers and binders for paints and its BioVail plant nutrition ingredient for crop production. ... Based on its first-half performance, the company raised its full-year outlook and now expects 2026 revenue to be at least $14.8 million, ahead of current market expectations. The board also reaffirmed its expectation of delivering a small positive EBITDA for the year while continuing to invest in staffing and product development. ... The company plans to release its full interim results around September 8. ... 4.9-megawatt solar array in Kingston ... than 9 ... kilowatt-hours of ... during its first year of operation, surpassing expectations and producing ... energy to power more than 1,00 ... The facility, which was fully commissioned on May 21, 2025, is the first solar array owned and operated by a regulated electric distribution utility in New Hampshire. Built on 36 acres off Towle Road, the project includes 11,232 solar panels and is among the largest solar installations in ... 0,00 ... the winter months of December through February, according ... The project is expected to generate an average of 8.6 million kilowatt ... -year life ... , with estimated customer savings of about $2 million."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Truelink Picks Up JT Thorpe From HIG Capital - The Deal,www.thedeal.com (David Elman),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thedeal.com/scoops-exclusives/truelink-picks-up-jt-thorpe-from-hig-capital/,"Truelink Picks Up JT Thorpe From HIG Capital - The Deal ... Truelink acquires the provider of specialty industrial maintenance and thermal management services after The Deal reported its parent was on the block. ... Truelink Capital on Thursday, July 30, said it will acquire JT Thorpe Group Inc., a provider of specialty industrial maintenance and thermal management services for infrastructure and industrial end markets. ... Los Angeles-based Truelink didn’t disclose financial terms of the transaction, which will also mark an exit for HIG Capital LLC, which invested in JT Thorpe in 2022. ... JT Thorpe’s management team, led by CEO Kevin Howard, will continue to lead the business and will retain a significant ownership stake in the company. ... The Deal in March reported HIG was holding conversations with advisers as it looked to explore a sale process for industrial services platform Terra Millennium Corp., the parent of JT Thorpe. Salt Lake City-based Terra Millennium generates around $150 million to $160 million in Ebitda, The Deal reported, adding the business generated about $80 million in Ebitda when HIG acquired it in 2022. ... Founded in 1906, JT Thorpe provides thermal management services including refractory, fireproofing and insulation, as well as asset integrity services such as access and mechanical services. The company supports maintenance and operations at complex industrial facilities across power generation, semiconductor, liquefied natural gas, mining, steel, cement and broader infrastructure and industrial end markets. ... HIG in a separate statement said JT Thorpe expanded its service offering and geographic footprint across North America during the firm’s ownership, strengthened its position in key industrial markets, enhanced its go-to-market strategy and completed four accretive acquisitions. ... Truelink plans to support JT Thorpe’s growth organically and through strategic M&A. The transaction marks the third platform investment for Truelink Capital’s Fund II and reflects the firm’s continued focus on industrials and business services companies. ... Luke Myers, co-founder and managing partner at Truelink, in the statement said the investment comes as the company benefits from growth tailwinds across infrastructure end markets, including liquefied natural gas, semiconductors, data centers and power generation. ... Founded by Platinum Equity LLC veterans Todd Golditch and Myers, Truelink targets middle market companies in the technology-enabled services and industrial sectors with $20 million to $75 million in Ebitda. ... Last July, the company announced the closing of its inaugural fund, Truelink Capital I LP, with $875 million in commitments, exceeding its $600 million initial target and $750 million hard cap. ... The firms expect to close the deal by the end of the third quarter, subject to customary closing conditions."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Univar Solutions Expands EMEA CASE Portfolio Through Acquisition | PCI Magazine,www.pcimag.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.pcimag.com/articles/115000-univar-solutions-expands-emea-case-portfolio-through-acquisition,"Univar Solutions Expands EMEA CASE Portfolio Through Acquisition | PCI Magazine ... Univar Solutions has acquired Interpur Chemicals, a European distributor of polyurethanes and powder coatings. Financial terms were not disclosed. ... The acquisition expands the technical capabilities and regional coverage of the Performance Materials business within Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions across Europe, the Middle East and Africa. ... Interpur Chemicals has more than 20 years of experience supplying raw materials and technical consulting services to the polyurethane, resin and powder coatings industries. Eighteen employees will join Univar Solutions through the transaction. ... “This acquisition marks an important milestone for our performance materials business as we respond to growing customer demand for the essential products that enable modern, high-performance applications,” said Matthew Oliver, senior vice president of Performance Materials for Univar Solutions. ... The acquisition expands Univar Solutions’ access to polyurethane and powder coatings materials while adding technical expertise and distribution coverage across EMEA. ... # PSG Grows European Reach With Acquisition ... # Fenix Expands Coatings Reach With Latest Acquisition ... # Univar Solutions Expands Global Offerings with Acquisition of Spanish Specialty Distributor Vicom"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,TriMas - TriMas Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results | 2026 | News,trimas.com (Super User),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://trimas.com/news/2026/trimas-reports-second-quarter-2026-results/,"BLOOMFIELD HILLS, Michigan, July 30, 2026 - TriMas (NASDAQ: TRS) today announced financial results for the second quarter ended June 30, 2026. ... TriMas reported second quarter 2026 net sales of $174.6 million, a 1.6% increase compared to $171.8 million in second quarter 2025, driven by organic growth within Specialty Products and the benefit of favorable foreign currency exchange. Operating profit increased to $10.9 million in second quarter 2026, compared to $7.4 million in second quarter 2025. Adjusting for Special Items(1), second quarter 2026 adjusted operating profit was $14.9 million, a 29.1% increase compared to $11.5 million in the prior year period, reflecting the successful execution of cost-reduction and streamlining initiatives. ... ""As we move through the second half of the year, we expect the run-rate benefits of our cost reduction and operational excellence initiatives to continue building, supporting further performance improvement. At the same time, we remain focused on disciplined capital deployment, having repurchased more than five million shares since announcing the Aerospace divestiture, while preserving the flexibility to invest in organic growth initiatives and strategically aligned, high-quality acquisition opportunities that elevate our Packaging and Life Sciences platforms. We believe the actions we have taken to simplify and strengthen TriMas have positioned us well to continue delivering improved results and long-term shareholder value.” ... During the second quarter of 2026, the Company returned capital to shareholders through the repurchase of 509,264 shares of its outstanding common stock for $18.9 million. Year to date through June 30, 2026, the Company repurchased 1,996,321 shares for $73.5 million, contributing to a 4.7% net reduction in outstanding shares compared to December 31, 2025. Since announcing the decision to divest TriMas Aerospace in November 2025, the Company has repurchased more than five million shares. As of June 30, 2026, approximately 35.9 million shares were outstanding and $76.5 million remained available under the Company's share repurchase authorization. TriMas also declared and paid a quarterly cash dividend of $0.04 per share. ... of $142.9 million, essentially flat compared to the second quarter of 2025. Sales growth in the industrial and life sciences end markets, along with the benefit of favorable foreign currency translation, was ... The divestiture of TriMas Aerospace was completed on March 16, 2026, for approximately $1.5 billion in cash, generating net after-tax proceeds of approximately $1.2 billion. To date, proceeds have been used to repay borrowings under the Company's revolving credit facility, fund additional share repurchases and satisfy a portion of transaction-related tax obligations, while the remaining balance has been invested in liquid, interest-bearing accounts. The Company intends to deploy the remaining proceeds in support of capital allocation priorities, which may include organic growth investments, strategic acquisitions and additional share repurchases. ... TriMas has completed the closure and consolidation of its Atkins, Arkansas, packaging facility. The Company remains on track to deliver approximately $10.5 million of savings in 2026 and $16.0 million of annualized savings related to the previously communicated cost-out actions. ... The Company has raised the low end and midpoint of its previously issued full-year 2026 adjusted diluted earnings per share(2) (EPS) outlook and now expects adjusted diluted EPS in the range of $1.60 to $1.70, compared to the prior outlook of $1.50 to $1.70, provided on February 26, 2026. This outlook assumes between $9 million and $10 million of interest income per each remaining quarter of 2026, and assumes no significant change in interest rates or the redeployment of the cash proceeds for the remainder of the year. The Company continues to expect sales growth of 3% to 6% year-over-year across its combined Packaging and Specialty Products businesses, along with more than 300 basis points of adjusted operating profit margin improvement, driven by cost reductions and organizational realignment initiatives. ... Any ""forward-looking"" statements, within the meaning of Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933 and Section 21E of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, contained herein, including those relating to TriMas’ business, financial condition or future results, involve risks and uncertainties with respect to, including, but not limited to: general economic and currency conditions; competitive factors; market demand; our ability to realize our business strategies; government and regulatory actions, including, without limitation, the impact of current and future tariffs and reciprocal tariffs, quotas and surcharges, as well as climate change legislation and other environmental regulations; our ability to identify attractive acquisition candidates, successfully integrate acquired operations or realize the intended benefits of such acquisitions; our ability to recognize the benefits of and effectively deploy the net proceeds from the sale of TriMas Aerospace; pressures on our supply chain, including availability of raw materials and inflationary pressures on raw material and energy costs, and customers; the performance of our subcontractors and suppliers; risks and uncertainties associated with intangible assets, including goodwill or other intangible asset impairment charges; risks associated with a concentrated customer base; information technology and other cyber-related risks; risks related to our international operations; changes to fiscal and tax policies; intellectual property factors; uncertainties associated with our ability to meet customers’ and suppliers’ sustainability and environmental, social and governance (""ESG"") goals and achieve our sustainability and ESG goals in alignment with our own announced targets; litigation; contingent liabilities relating to acquisition and disposition activities; interest rate volatility; our leverage; liabilities imposed by our debt instruments; labor disputes and shortages; the disruption of operations from catastrophic or extraordinary events, including, but not limited to, natural disasters, geopolitical conflicts and public health crises; the amount and timing of future dividends and/or share repurchases, which remain subject to Board approval and depend on market and other conditions; our future prospects; and other risks that are detailed in the Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2025. The risks described are not the only risks facing our Company. Additional risks and uncertainties not currently known to us or that we currently deemed to be immaterial also may materially adversely affect our business, financial position and results of operations or cash flows. These risks and uncertainties may cause actual results to differ materially from those indicated by the forward-looking statements. All forward-looking statements made herein are based on information currently available, and the Company assumes no obligation to update any forward-looking statements, except as required by law. ... TriMas designs, manufactures and supplies a broad range of innovative and high‑quality products for the consumer packaging, life sciences and industrial markets through its TriMas Packaging and Specialty Products groups. With approximately 2,500 employees in 12 countries, TriMas is committed to empowering customer success through deep partnerships, strong technical expertise, focused innovation, and exceptional quality and service. Guided by a culture of continuous improvement and operational excellence, TriMas invests in its people and capabilities to deliver long‑term value for all stakeholders. Headquartered in Bloomfield Hills, Michigan, TriMas is publicly traded on NASDAQ under the ticker symbol “TRS.” For more information, please visit www.trimas.com."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,TRIXIE outlines growth strategy after Central Garden & Pet’s €400M acquisition - GlobalPETS,globalpetindustry.com (David Palacios Rubio),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://globalpetindustry.com/news/trixie-outlines-growth-strategy-after-central-garden-pets-e400m-acquisition/,"TRIXIE outlines growth strategy after Central Garden & Pet’s €400M acquisition - GlobalPETS ... # TRIXIE outlines growth strategy after Central Garden & Pet’s €400M acquisition ... The German pet supplier tells GlobalPETS it sees an opportunity to strengthen its sourcing, product development and logistics capabilities and expand its presence in the US market. ... Earlier this week, Central Garden & Pet Company announced a definitive agreement to acquire an 80% majority stake in the German pet supply manufacturer TRIXIE. ... The transaction, valued at up to €400 million ($458M), marks a major consolidation in the global pet industry, combining Central’s North American distribution capabilities with TRIXIE’s established European market presence. ... The financial structure of the acquisition includes an upfront cash payment of approximately €340 million ($389M) at closing, with an additional earn-out potential of up to €60 million ($68.7M) contingent upon TRIXIE’s fiscal 2026 performance metrics. ... TRIXIE currently generates approximately 90% of its sales from its proprietary brands and supplies more than 30,000 retailers worldwide. ... Central CFO Brad Smith identified M&A opportunities as one of the company’s objectives for 2026 during a conference in August 2025, citing weak consumer demand. ... In a conversation with GlobalPETS, TRIXIE emphasized that the acquisition will not result in immediate changes to its operating model. ... The transaction is expected to close in early 2027, subject to customary regulatory approvals and other closing conditions. Until then, TRIXIE and Central Garden & Pet will continue to operate independently. ... ## Integration and US expansion ... One of the main objectives is to provide TRIXIE with access to Central’s infrastructure. ... While it develops roughly 500 new products annually and maintains a dominant footprint in Europe, scaling in North America requires significant local presence. ... “The partnership provides access to additional resources, international expertise and expanded capabilities in areas such as sourcing, product development, logistics and market expansion, especially in the USA,” it says. ... TRIXIE also sees “significant opportunities” in this agreement. “Central Garden & Pet brings extensive market knowledge, established distribution capabilities and a strong presence within the North American pet industry. This creates the potential to accelerate TRIXIE’s growth and brand awareness in the US.” ... While the integration of operations is still months away, TRIXIE maintains that its core retail strategies will not shift. “While it is too early to discuss specific initiatives, we believe the partnership positions us well to expand our presence and better serve customers in this important market.” ... Central Garden & Pet CEO Niko Lahanas described the acquisition as a “once-in-a-lifetime” opportunity that “overnight turns Central and Trixie into the largest pet supplies company globally.” ... Central’s management expects the transaction to be accretive to both margins and earnings, citing cross-selling opportunities and sourcing synergies that are projected to begin materializing in the second year post-closing. ... Net sales in Central Garden & Pet’s pet portfolio grew 5% year-over-year(YoY) to $477 million (€421.3M) for the second quarter of fiscal year (FY) 2026, ended 28 March."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Univar Solutions Acquires Interpur Chemicals, Expanding",www.globenewswire.com (Univar Solutions LLC),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/28/3334028/0/en/Univar-Solutions-Acquires-Interpur-Chemicals-Expanding-Access-to-Polyurethanes-and-Powder-Coatings-in-EMEA.html,"Univar Solutions Acquires Interpur Chemicals, Expanding ... # Univar Solutions Acquires Interpur Chemicals, Expanding Access to Polyurethanes and Powder Coatings in EMEA ... DOWNERS GROVE, Ill., July 28, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Univar Solutions LLC (“Univar Solutions” or “the Company”), today announced it has acquired Interpur Chemicals, a leading distributor of polyurethanes and powder coatings in Europe. The addition strengthens the Performance Materials business within Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions, expanding technical capabilities and regional coverage across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA). By combining Interpur Chemicals local market expertise with Univar Solutions’ supplier relationships and distribution network, customers will benefit from improved access to materials, stronger supply continuity, and greater support in addressing formulation and performance requirements. ... “We’re excited to welcome Interpur Chemicals to Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions, bringing together complementary portfolios, technical expertise, and strong customer relationships,” said Nick Powell, CEO of Ingredients + Specialties from Univar Solutions. “Interpur Chemicals’ position in one of Europe’s fastest-growing CASE markets aligns with where we’re focused. This step allows us to broaden what we offer customers while continuing to invest in capabilities that support long-term growth in key applications and end markets.” ... “This acquisition marks an important milestone for our performance materials business as we respond to growing customer demand for the essential products that enable modern, high-performance applications,” said Matthew Oliver, senior vice president of Performance Materials for Univar Solutions. “By expanding our solutions and reach into high-demand markets and applications, we’re enhancing our ability to support customers where it matters most - at the formulation and application level.” ... “We’re excited for this new chapter of our business with Univar Solutions, a company that shares similar values and a long-term, relationship-driven approach to the market,” said Óscar García, CEO of Interpur Chemicals. “This acquisition represents a meaningful next step for the CASE industry, combining technical credibility, strong supplier relationships, and trusted customer engagement to create an ideal platform for accelerating specialty product capabilities.” ... Univar Solutions brings more than a century of experience in chemical and ingredient distribution. Interpur Chemicals offers over 20 years of experience supplying chemical raw materials and technical consultancy for the polyurethane, resins, and powder coating industries. The companies have a shared commitment to transparency, service excellence, and social responsibility. 18 employees will join Univar Solutions through the transaction, supporting continuity for customers, suppliers, and other business partners. ... About Univar SolutionsUnivar Solutions is a leading global specialty chemical and ingredient distributor representing a premier portfolio from the world’s leading producers. With one of the industry’s largest private transportation fleets and technical sales force, unparalleled logistics know-how, deep market and regulatory knowledge, formulation and recipe development, and leading digital tools, the Company is well-positioned to offer tailored solutions and value-added services to a wide range of markets, industries, and applications. While fulfilling its purpose to help keep communities healthy, fed, clean, and safe, Univar Solutions is committed to helping customers and suppliers innovate and focus on Growing Together. Learn more at univarsolutions.com. ... August 04, ... Source: Univar Solutions LLC ... Univar Solutions 收购 H.M. Royal，扩大在美国橡胶、塑料及胶粘剂助剂领域的布局 ... 融合百年技术积淀与值得信赖的客户关系，强化在美国关键市场的服务与供应能力 伊利诺伊州唐纳斯格罗夫, Aug. 05, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- 全球领先的特种原料和化学品解决方案提供商 Univar Solutions LLC（简称“Univar Solutions”或“公司”）今日宣布已收购 H.M. Royal——一家拥有 101... ... August 03 ... 026 ... Source: Univar Solutions LLC ... Univar Solutions Acquires H.M. Royal, Expanding Reach in Rubber, Plastics, and Adhesive Additives in the United States ... Univar Solutions Acquires H.M. Royal, Expanding Reach in Rubber, Plastics, and Adhesive Additives in the United States"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Trican Reports Second Quarter Results for 2026 and Declares Quarterly Dividend - Cantech Letter,www.cantechletter.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cantechletter.com/newswires/trican-reports-second-quarter-results-for-2026-and-declares-quarterly-dividend/,"28, 2026) – Trican Well Service Ltd. (TSX: TCW) (“Trican” or the “Company”) is pleased to announce its second quarter results for 2026. ... While revenues remained largely consistent with the prior year, ongoing pricing pressure and inflationary cost increases continued to impact operating expenses, resulting in margin compression. In addition, although the acquisition of Iron Horse expanded the Company’s service offering and increased its operating scale, Iron Horse’s contribution reflected its seasonally weaker second quarter operating profile, which further impacted consolidated profitability during the period. ... On August 27, 2025, the Company closed on its agreement to acquire all the issued and outstanding shares of Iron Horse Coiled Tubing Inc. or Iron Horse Energy Services (“Iron Horse”) in exchange for $77.25 million in cash consideration, and 33.76 million common shares of Trican. Iron Horse was a privately owned fracturing and coiled tubing services provider operating primarily in the Cardium, Charlie Lake, Mannville Stack, Viking, Montney and Shaunavon plays in the Western Canadian Sedimentary Basin (“WCSB”). ... On July 28, 2026, the Company’s board of directors approved a quarterly dividend of $0.055 per share, reflecting a 10% increase from the $0.050 per share dividend declared in the comparable quarter of the prior year. The dividend is scheduled to be paid on September 30, 2026 to shareholders of record as of the close of business on September 15, 2026. ... Capital expenditures1 for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 totaled $20.8 million and $39.3 million, respectively ($16.2 million and $28.7 million for the three and six months ended June 30, 2025). Capital expenditures¹ during the period primarily related to maintenance capital to support the reliability and efficiency of the Company’s equipment fleet, as well as growth capital associated with the construction of Canada’s first 100% natural gas fueled, continuous, heavy-duty hydraulic fracturing fleet and the purchase of electric ancillary fracturing equipment. ... The Company has approved a capital budget for 2026 of $122 million, underscoring Trican’s commitment to disciplined investment and long-term growth. The approved capital budget reflects the Company’s continued focus on maintenance capital to ensure reliability and efficiency across its operations, while allocating targeted growth capital to advance modernization initiatives and position the Company for future opportunities. Growth capital includes Canada’s first 100% natural gas fueled, continuous, heavy-duty hydraulic fracturing fleet, which is expected to be field ready in the fourth quarter of 2026. ... The Company is undertaking a significant technology modernization initiative starting with our base financial system and implementing an integrated enterprise resource planning (“ERP”) platform. Trican anticipates ongoing technology enhancements including advanced data analytics to enhance operational efficiency, reliability and competitiveness over the years. The investment for 2026 is anticipated to be $13 million which will be presented as general and administrative (“G&A”) expense in accordance with IFRS. ... We continue to advance the modernization of our fracturing fleet through targeted investments in lower-emission and next-generation technologies, including the addition of a 100% natural gas fueled, continuous, heavy-duty hydraulic fracturing fleet. This approach builds on our modernization strategy over recent years, including prior investments in upgrading existing equipment with Tier 4 Dynamic Gas Blending (“Tier 4 DGB”) engine technology alongside the construction of new fully electric ancillary equipment. The combination of Tier 4 DGB engines and fully electric ancillary equipment can displace up to 90% of the diesel used in a conventional fracturing operation with natural gas resulting in lower overall fuel costs and reduced emissions. Our ongoing fleet modernization also includes the deployment of industry leading continuous heavy duty pumps and idle reduction technology packages which enable longer pumping times and improved operating efficiencies. ... Tier 4 upgrades, electric ancillary equipment, the development of a 100% natural gas fueled, continuous, heavy-duty hydraulic fracturing fleet, and the expansion of coiled tubing-integrated fracturing operations through the acquisition of Iron Horse are key components of Trican’s operating strategy. Our ongoing initiatives, including fleet upgrades, are intended to improve operating performance, cost efficiency, and reduce our emissions profile, thereby improving the sustainability of our operations while supporting our customers in achieving their goals. ... Trican’s outlook for the next several years remains constructive, supported by expanding LNG export capacity, improved market access for Canadian energy production, and continued development of the Montney and Duvernay resource plays. These factors are expected to support drilling and completion activity across the Western Canadian Sedimentary Basin (“WCSB”) through 2026 and beyond. ... Increasing completion intensity within these resource plays, including longer lateral lengths and higher proppant loading per well, continues to support demand for pressure pumping, coiled tubing, and cementing services. While commodity prices remain volatile and pricing pressure persisted through the first half of 2026, customer activity levels continue to be supported by the attractive economics of Canada’s leading resource plays. ... The commencement and continued ramp-up of LNG Canada represents a structural shift for the Canadian natural gas market by providing producers with improved access to global LNG markets and reducing reliance on US natural gas pricing. Additional LNG export projects currently under construction or in development are expected to further strengthen long-term demand fundamentals for Canadian natural gas and support future drilling and completions activity. ... The Montney and Duvernay continue to attract a significant portion of industry capital given their large resource bases, attractive well economics and high liquids content. Both plays require increasingly complex completion designs and elevated service intensity, supporting demand for Trican’s integrated service offering. ... Trican continues to focus on operational execution, technology leadership and disciplined investment in its equipment fleet. The Company is investing in Canada’s first 100% natural gas fueled, continuous, heavy-duty hydraulic fracturing fleet, which is expected to be field ready in the fourth quarter of 2026. This investment complements Trican’s existing Tier 4 DGB fleet, electrified ancillary equipment and broader emissions reduction initiatives. ... The acquisition of Iron Horse has strengthened Trican’s coil-integrated fracturing capabilities, increased operating scale and expanded the Company’s ability to provide integrated solutions across customer operations. Trican also continues to invest in logistics capabilities to support increasingly complex completion programs and evolving customer procurement strategies. ... Beyond field operations, Trican is implementing an integrated ERP platform as part of a broader technology modernization initiative designed to improve operational efficiency, scalability and decision-making capabilities across the organization. ... Headquartered in Calgary, Alberta, Trican supplies oil and natural gas well servicing equipment and solutions to our customers through the drilling, completion and production cycles. Our team of technical experts provide state-of-the-art equipment, engineering support, reservoir expertise and laboratory services through the delivery of hydraulic fracturing, cementing, coiled tubing, nitrogen services and chemical sales for the oil and gas industry in Western Canada."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Matrix Adhesives Group Acquires IPS Adhesives | TruArc Partners,truarcpartners.com (Written By Sara White),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://truarcpartners.com/news/matrix-acquires-ips-adhesives,"Matrix Adhesives Group Acquires IPS Adhesives | TruArc Partners ... # Matrix Adhesives Group Acquires IPS Adhesives to Expand its Technology, Branded Portfolio, and Market Reach ... Westerville, OH – July 27, 2026 - Matrix Adhesives Group (“Matrix” or the “Company”), a TruArc Partners (“TruArc”) portfolio company and provider of advanced adhesive and sealant solutions for renovation and construction, industrial, commercial, and specialty applications, today announced that it has acquired IPS Adhesives (“IPSA”), a provider of high-performance adhesives serving building and construction, transportation, industrial, and marine industries, from the parent company of IPS Corporation (“IPS”). Terms of the transaction were not disclosed. ... In partnering with IPSA, Matrix reinforces its position as a scaled specialty adhesives platform by expanding its branded product offering, technologies portfolio, and global reach. As part of the acquisition, IPSA will add six established brands and broaden Matrix’s exposure to specification-driven applications across industrial durables, marine, building and construction, and sign and display markets. The transaction also expands Matrix's international presence through IPSA's established European footprint, distributor network, and customer relationships. ... Previously owned by IPS, an innovator in specialty chemical solutions for plumbing and construction applications, IPSA is a provider of high-performance adhesives with expertise in Methyl Methacrylate (MMA) technology and other advanced technologies. MMA adhesives are increasingly specified in demanding applications due to their fast cure times, minimal surface preparation requirements, and ability to bond dissimilar materials. The addition of IPSA further expands Matrix's technical capabilities and positions the Company to pursue growth opportunities driven by demand for advanced adhesive solutions. Scott McDowell, President of IPSA, will remain on board as a key member of the Matrix leadership team. ... “Joining Matrix represents an exciting milestone for the IPS Adhesives team,” said Scott McDowell, President of IPS Adhesives. “Our associates have worked tirelessly to create a company that is widely recognized for its broad suite of products, trusted brands, and passion for solving our customers’ toughest bonding challenges. Becoming part of the Matrix family will allow us to preserve our strong market position in MMA solutions, while gaining the scale, resources, and global platform to support our growth plans. I couldn't be more excited about what this partnership means for our customers, our team, and our future.” ... IPSA represents Matrix’s first acquisition following TruArc’s strategic investment in March 2026. ... TruArc Operating Partner Rich Rowe commented; “We are very pleased to welcome the IPSA team into the Matrix family as we believe this acquisition strengthens the Company’s capability to deliver differentiated solutions to customers in its core markets in North America and abroad.” ... “This acquisition represents an important milestone in Matrix’s growth strategy and provides Matrix with the ability to further expand its portfolio of branded products, advanced adhesive technologies, and global market reach,” said John Pless, Co-Managing Partner at TruArc. “We look forward to supporting the Matrix team as they integrate IPS Adhesives’ highly complementary capabilities and continue building a high-quality specialty adhesives platform.” ... Matrix Adhesives Group is an adhesive and sealant solutions development partner. The company specializes in formulating, filling, blending, and contract packaging for consumer and industrial markets. For more information, please visit www.matrixadhesives.com. ... IPS Adhesives is a provider of adhesives serving the surfacing, structural, and assembly industries. With a combined 65 years of expertise in research and development, its products are recognized by OEMs and fabricators globally for their quality, strength, and reliability. IPS Adhesives has three state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities on two continents and a broad network of distributors serving countries worldwide. For more information, please visit: www.ipsadhesives.com. ... TruArc Partners is a private equity firm focused on middle-market investments. TruArc focuses on companies in attractive sub-sectors across specialty manufacturing and business services. The TruArc investment team collaborates with its operating partners and portfolio management teams to create value through a transformational growth strategy led by organic or acquisition-driven growth. To learn more about TruArc visit www.truarcpartners.com."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Belgium’s Prayon to acquire Colombia’s HRA Uniquímica – HCNTimes.com,hcntimes.com,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hcntimes.com/belgiums-prayon-to-acquire-colombias-hra-uniquimica/,"Belgium’s Prayon to acquire Colombia’s HRA Uniquímica – HCNTimes.com ... # Belgium’s Prayon to acquire Colombia’s HRA Uniquímica ... Colombian company HRA Uniquímica has signed a binding agreement for the potential acquisition of HRA Uniquímica and HRA Ingredients by Prayon, a global leader in phosphorus chemistry headquartered in Belgium. ... This deal holds significant strategic value for HRA Uniquímica and HRA Ingredients, as it aligns with their joint growth and international expansion plans., according to law firm Cuatrecasas, which advised HRA Uniquímica on the agreement. “The objective is to create greater value for customers and strengthen both companies’ ability to offer innovative, competitive solutions with a global reach,” the firm said. ... Prayon has a market history spanning over 130 years, operates in more than 100 countries, and maintains production facilities in Belgium, France, Switzerland, Morocco, and the United States. The announced transaction is subject to the necessary regulatory approvals. ... “In providing this advice, we successfully facilitated an understanding between our client and a world-class strategic partner capable of enhancing their capabilities while maintaining their close ties to the local market,” Jaime Moya, the Cuatrecasas corporate/M&A partner who led the advisory team, said. ... “This combination of expertise will enable HRA to offer a broader portfolio, expand its geographic reach, strengthen its research capabilities, and become more competitive in the international market,” he added."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Charlotte firm buys Montreal HVAC maker for US$430 million | Charlotte Observer,www.charlotteobserver.com (Catherine Muccigrosso),2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.charlotteobserver.com/news/business/article316648482.html,"Charlotte firm buys Montreal HVAC maker for US$430 million | Charlotte Observer ... SPX Technologies acquired Neptronic for US$ 430 million, the company announced on Thursday. ... SPX Technologies purchased a Montreal-based HVAC manufacturer for CA $605 million, equivalent to about US$ 430 million. ... Neptronic will become a part of the Charlotte-based company’s HVAC segment, according to a Thursday, July 23, statement from SPX Technologies. ... The Canadian company designs and produces products including HVAC controls, humidifiers and heaters. Neptronic has about 300 employees and an annual estimated revenue of US$ 75 million, according to the statement. ... “SPX’s scale, operational resources and strong channel relationships in the HVAC market will help accelerate our growth while preserving the engineering expertise, innovation and customer focus that have defined our business for nearly 50 years,” said Biagio Di Lorenzo, Neptronic CFO and president, in the statement. ... SPX Technologies supplies infrastructure equipment in the HVAC and detection and measurement fields. More information about the impact of the acquisition will be released on July 30 in SPX Technologies’ quarterly report. ... This year, the company also bought Thermolec, an electric duct heating manufacturer, and Crawford United, an industrial holding company. ... Among other acquisitions, SPX Technologies announced an agreement to buy ASPEQ Heating Group for $418 million in 2023. ... ### Charlotte-based SPX Technologies expanding HVAC business with $418M acquisition"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,CM Equity Sells GracoRoberts to Tinicum,www.thedeal.com (David Elman),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thedeal.com/scoops-exclusives/cm-equity-sells-chemicals-distribution-platform-gracoroberts-to-tinicum/,"CM Equity Sells GracoRoberts to Tinicum ... Tinicum invests an undisclosed amount in GracoRoberts, which The Deal in April reported had retained Harris Williams on an auction process. ... CM Equity Partners LP has sold chemicals distribution platform GracoRoberts to Tinicum LP. ... Arlington, Texas-based GracoRoberts didn’t disclose terms of Tinicum’s investment in a Thursday, July 23, statement but noted company management will retain a significant interest and continue to lead the business. ... The Deal in April reported Harris Williams LLC was running a broad auction process for GracoRoberts, which could result in a deal valued at north of $550 million. Sources expected GracoRoberts to be marketed on Ebitda around $55 million, with CM Equity likely looking for up to a low double-digit multiple of Ebitda. ... repair and overhaul ... New York-based middle market investor CM Equity started GracoRoberts in September 2015 with the acquisition of Fort Worth-based Graco Supply & Integrated Services Inc. for an undisclosed sum. In April 2019, the firm merged Graco with E.V. Roberts to create what it said then was the largest aerospace-focused specialty chemicals distributor in North America. ... GracoRoberts has completed six add-on deals during CM Equity’s hold of the platform, the company wrote in a January statement, including E.V. Roberts, Able Aerospace Adhesives, Silmid, SkyGeek, Pacific Coast Composites and Sky Mart. ... Most recently, the company purchased Miami-based Sky Mart in January to expand its footprint in Latin America, where it said the addressable MRO market is $6.5 billion. ... New York-based Tinicum owns manufacturing, infrastructure, distribution and industrial technology businesses and typically targets equity investments of $50 million to $500 million. It pursues buy-and-build strategies focused on operational improvement and complementary acquisitions. ... Tinicum’s latest significant fund is the 2022 vintage Tinicum Fund, with roughly $2.3 billion in commitments. ... ., a producer of ... and electromagnetic interference filtering ... , to TE Connectivity ... acoRoberts and CM Equity used Harris Williams for financial advice and David S. Cole, Andy C. Erickson and Cooper Littlejohn of Holland & Knight LLP for counsel. CM Equity managing partner Jeffrey Mark was on"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Wipro Consumer Care acquires Good Home, Eva brands from TTK Healthcare for ₹256 cr - The HinduBusinessLine",www.thehindubusinessline.com (Anya Sapru),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/wipro-consumer-care-acquires-good-home-eva-brands-from-ttk-healthcare-for-256-cr/article71258149.ece,"Wipro Consumer Care acquires Good Home, Eva brands from TTK Healthcare for ₹256 cr - The HinduBusinessLine ... # Wipro Consumer Care acquires Good Home, Eva brands from TTK Healthcare for ₹256 cr ... ## The two brands together generated revenue of ₹148 crore in FY26 ... Updated - July 23, 2026 at 09:22 PM. ... Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting has signed definitive agreements to acquire the Good Home and Eva brands from TTK Healthcare for ₹256 crore, strengthening its presence in the home care and personal care segments as it sharpens its focus on high-growth consumer categories through acquisitions. ... The two brands together generated revenue of ₹148 crore in FY26, valuing the transaction at about 1.7 times revenue. The acquisition is Wipro Consumer Care’s 17th and adds established brands in air care, household cleaning and deodorants to its fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG) portfolio. The company, part of Wipro Enterprises, reported a revenue of ₹10,800 crore in FY26. ... The deal comes as demand for premium home hygiene and personal care products continues to rise, driven by higher consumer spending, greater hygiene awareness and increasing adoption of branded products. Wipro Consumer Care said the acquisition would deepen its presence in categories where it sees long-term growth opportunities while strengthening its portfolio of trusted consumer brands. ... Good Home has built a presence in home care products such as air fresheners, odour removers, scrubbers and drain cleaners. Eva, one of India’s early deodorant brands, has a portfolio spanning body sprays, no-gas perfumes, underarm roll-ons and talcum powders. ... The acquisition also reflects Wipro’s increasing focus on the home care segment, where it sees significant headroom for growth. ... “We became very focused on growing the home care categories. Good Home strengthens our footprint across household cleaning while giving us a strong play in the mass-market air care segment,” said Neeraj Khatri, Chief Executive of Wipro Consumer Care, adding that India’s ₹2,000-crore air care market is expanding at 12-15 per cent annually. ... The company also sees Eva as a strategic addition to its existing personal care portfolio. Wipro already owns Yardley, a consumer goods brand, in India, and Eva will help it widen its consumer base by targeting a younger demographic. ... “Yardley is largely focused on consumers aged 25 years and above. Eva gives us a complementary opportunity to address teenagers and younger women while operating in the same fragrance and deodorant categories,” said Khatri. ... According to him, India’s fragrances and deodorants market, estimated at around ₹5,000 crore, remains significantly underpenetrated. Per capita consumption is only about one-tenth of markets such as Indonesia despite comparable demographics, indicating ample room for long-term growth. ... ## Expansion plans ... Beyond expanding the portfolio, Wipro plans to leverage its distribution network to scale both brands across traditional retail as well as modern trade and digital channels. ... “We think both these brands are underleveraged in modern trade, quick commerce and e-commerce. Wipro brings a very strong distribution network, and that’s where we see significant upside,” said Khatri. ... The company is also evaluating opportunities to take the products to international markets using its global manufacturing and distribution capabilities. ... “Air care is becoming an exciting category not just in India but across Southeast Asia, South Africa and China. We may take the products to these markets, even if not under the same brand name. The brands may remain local, but the backend can be common. That gives us procurement scale and allows us to invest more behind the brands,” added Kumar Chander, Chief Executive Officer of Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting and Managing Director of Wipro Enterprises. ... Chander said the acquisition aligns with the company’s long-term strategy of building leadership positions across high-potential consumer categories through a mix of organic growth and acquisitions. ... “Good Home and Eva are well-established brands with a strong legacy and enduring consumer trust. We look forward to building on the equity these brands have created over the years through innovation, wider market reach and sustained investment in brand development,” he said. ... For TTK Healthcare, the transaction marks an exit from two legacy consumer brands. Executive Chairman T T Raghunathan said Good Home and Eva had built strong consumer trust over the years and expressed confidence that Wipro Consumer Care’s manufacturing, distribution and brand-building capabilities would help accelerate their next phase of growth. ... Wipro Consumer Care said it would retain the identities of both brands while investing in product innovation, wider distribution and market expansion."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Wipro buys TTK’s Good Home, Eva Brands for Rs 256 crore - The Economic Times",economictimes.indiatimes.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/cons-products/fmcg/wipro-buys-ttks-good-home-eva-brands-for-rs-256-crore/articleshow/132577144.cms,"Wipro buys TTK’s Good Home, Eva Brands for Rs 256 crore - The Economic Times ... Wipro buys TTK ... s Good Home, Eva Brands for Rs 256 crore ... Wipro buys TTK’s Good Home, Eva Brands for Rs 256 crore ... Wipro buys TTK’s Good Home, Eva Brands for Rs ... 256 crore ... ET BureauLast Updated: Jul 23, 2026, 03:3 ... :00 ... Wipro Consumer Care is acquiring TTK Healthcare's Good Home and Eva brands for Rs 256 crore. This strategic move expands Wipro's home and personal care product portfolios significantly. The acquired brands reported combined revenues of Rs 148 crore in the last fiscal year. Wipro plans to invest in distribution, innovation, and marketing for these established brands. This acquisition marks Wipro Consumer Care's seventeenth successful brand acquisition to date. ... Wipro is set to acquire TTK Healthcare Ltd.’s Good Home and Eva brands to expand its home care and personal care portfolio ... Mumbai: Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting will acquire TTK Healthcare Ltd.’s Good Home and Eva brands for Rs 256 crore, expanding its home care and personal care portfolio as consumer companies increasingly use acquisitions to drive growth.The two brands, which reported combined revenue of Rs 148 crore in FY26, sell products including air fresheners, drain cleaners, deodorants, perfumes and talcum powder. The deal is Wipro Consumer Care’s 17th acquisition. ... “Good Home and Eva are well-established brands with a strong legacy and enduring consumer trust,” Kumar Chander, chief executive officer of Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting and managing director of Wipro Enterprises, said. “This acquisition… strengthens our home care and personal care portfolio while expanding our presence in categories that continue to see strong consumer relevance and long-term growth.” ... The deal adds products across home cleaning, air care and fragrances, categories benefiting from rising hygiene awareness and premiumisation. Wipro said it will retain the brands while investing in wider distribution, innovation and marketing.TTK Healthcare Executive Chairman TT Raghunathan said Wipro’s FMCG capabilities and track record of nurturing acquired brands would help take Good Home and Eva to the next stage of growth."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Fluoride Varnish Market to Reach USD 248.1 Million by 2032 at 5.1% CAGR — PW Consulting – News24 Philippines,www.news24.ph (News24 Pinoy),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.news24.ph/biz/82561/,"As public- and private-sector actors recalibrate their oral health portfolios, the fluoride varnish market presents a steady, actionable growth story — one that rewards timely strategic moves. PW Consulting’s latest market study, based on a 2025 base year and a detailed historical review from 2020–2025, quantifies that the global market has expanded meaningfully over the past half-decade and is forecast to continue expanding through 2032 at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 5.1% (forecast period 2026–2032). Our bottom-up model anticipates clear upside from product innovation, reimbursement alignment, and broadened points-of-care adoption. This brief preview synthesizes the report’s high-value insights for executives preparing 2026 plans while deliberately withholding the granular segment tables to drive deeper engagement with the full study. ... ide Varnish Market ... M&A and partnership targeting: We map capability gaps and strategic adjacencies that incumbents and private equity buyers should prioritize to capture share in a moderately concentrated market landscape. ... Regulatory & reimbursement timing: With evolving FDA guidance and existing CPT pathways, timing market entry and labeling claims is a material determinant of 2026 launch success. Our regulatory timelines and reimbursement playbook de-risk product launches. ... The fluoride varnish market is characterized by steady growth driven by preventive-dentistry adoption, greater integration of oral health into primary care, and product innovation. From a baseline reflecting the market’s state as of 2025, the sector is poised to grow at ~5.1% CAGR across the 2026–2032 forecast window. While growth is broad-based, the competitive structure shows a moderate level of concentration: the top three players control approximately half of the market and the top five capture roughly three-fifths, signaling both scale advantages for incumbents and clear room for focused challengers. ... drivers identified in our research include expanded ... and community health settings, ... in medical settings, and ... products (e. ... ). On the supply side, manufacturers are competing on formulation science, single ... packaging innovations and ... & partnership scanner: A ranked list of strategic targets (by capability and geography), valuation sensitives and integration risk checklists. ... Across incumbents and innovators, recent product approvals and launches during 2025–2026 materially shift the competitive terrain. Key developments we profile in depth include: ... Centrix, Inc. (Shelton, CT) — commercial positioning strengthened by regulatory clearance for its FluoroDose varnish and a differentiated single-patient packaging design. This combination enhances patient safety narratives and supports scalable distribution into pediatric and school-based programs. ... Theodent (New Orleans) — achieved clearance for a fluoride-free professional varnish, representing a category-expanding clinical claim set that could appeal to specific clinician segments and consumer preferences for fluoride alternatives. ... VOCO GmbH (Cuxhaven) — launched a dual-action formulation that pairs conventional fluoride with bioactive crystalline materials, directly targeting longer-term enamel protection and remineralization narratives. ... Kettenbach LP (Germany) — introduced an upgraded varnish formulation with enhanced clinical appeal, reinforcing the importance of iterative product improvements even in mature product classes. ... Strategic implications: These moves highlight three converging competitive themes — formulation differentiation, regulatory claims as a growth lever, and packaging/dispensing formats as distribution accelerants. For incumbents, defending share will require rapid evidence generation and channel expansion. For new entrants, targeted clinical claims and nimble reimbursement strategies can yield disproportionate traction in specialty and non-dental settings. ... A shifting regulatory and reimbursement environment is central to 2026 playbooks. FDA device classification and clearance remain foundational: cavity varnish devices are generally regulated as Class II under the relevant product code, and conformity with updated standards has become a gating factor for market entry. Additionally, recent international standards updates and the transition timelines for declarations of conformity have compressed time-to-market considerations for product teams. ... On the reimbursement front, topical fluoride application in medical settings is increasingly codified: procedural coding now allows qualified non-dental clinicians to be reimbursed for varnish application under defined circumstances. This creates a near-term commercial opportunity to expand into pediatric primary care, community clinics and school-based health programs — provided manufacturers align labeling, training, and payer documentation with coding requirements. ... Engage payers proactively: Build value dossiers and pilot reimbursement agreements tied to performance metrics (reduced referrals, avoided restorative procedures) to secure coverage in new care settings. ... Plan regulatory timelines conservatively: Anticipate standard harmonization windows and plan submissions to avoid last-minute compliance risks. ... Leverage partnership and M&A options: Use partnerships to bridge distribution gaps and consider bolt-on acquisitions to secure key formulation or packaging IP. ... Our full Fluoride Varnish Market study provides the operational models, competitive playbooks, and regulatory roadmaps needed to move from strategy to execution. For executive teams preparing capital allocations, commercial launches, or M&A mandates in 2026, we offer tailored workshops that map your organization’s capabilities against the market opportunities identified in the report and build a prioritized 18-month action plan."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Tinicum Acquires Aerospace Chemicals Distributor GracoRoberts,peprofessional.com,2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://peprofessional.com/2026/07/tinicum-acquires-aerospace-chemicals-distributor-gracoroberts/,"Tinicum Acquires Aerospace Chemicals Distributor GracoRoberts ... # Tinicum Acquires Aerospace Chemicals Distributor GracoRoberts ... ## The GracoRoberts management team retains a significant stake and continues to lead the business, ending an 11-year ownership by CM Equity Partners ... GracoRoberts supplies the adhesives, sealants, coatings, composites, and other specialty chemicals that aircraft and defense manufacturers use to build and maintain their products. ... Tinicum has acquired GracoRoberts, a distributor of specialty chemicals and composites used in the aerospace and defense industry, from CM Equity Partners. ... GracoRoberts supplies the adhesives, sealants, coatings, composites, and other specialty chemicals that aircraft and defense manufacturers use to build and maintain their products. The company sells through an omnichannel model, combining an eCommerce operation with a technical sales team that helps customers select and apply the right materials. ... GracoRoberts is certified to the aerospace industry’s AS and ISO quality standards and to the Department of Defense’s CMMC Level II cybersecurity standard, and it is authorized to distribute more than 50 specialty chemical brands, including 3M, AkzoNobel, Eastman, ExxonMobil, Henkel, Hexcel, Huntsman, Momentive, and Resin Formulators. ... Beyond distribution, GracoRoberts runs a defense logistics and compliance program that manages the supply chain for military operations end to end, and it offers services such as custom kitting, labeling, repackaging, cold storage, and vendor-managed inventory. ... The business is made up of parent GracoRoberts together with Silmid, SkyGeek, Pacific Coast Composites, and Sky Mart, and it operates an on-site, staffed chemical laboratory and testing facility. Arlington, Texas-headquartered GracoRoberts is led by chief executive officer Jason Caldwell.CM Equity acquired Graco Supply in September 2015 and has spent the past 11 years growing the business through a series of acquisitions that added California-based E.V. Roberts (May 2019) — the merger that produced the GracoRoberts name — UK-based Silmid (March 2021); New York-based SkyGeek (July 2022); Washington-based Pacific Coast Composites (May 2023); and Florida-based Sky Mart (January 2026). ... “Tinicum shares our commitment to our people, our partners, and the long-term success of this business,” said Mr. Caldwell. “This partnership provides additional resources to invest in our team, strengthen our capabilities, and continue delivering exceptional value to the customer and supplier partners we serve. We are incredibly proud of what our employees have built over the past decade alongside financial partner CM Equity, and we are excited to build on that foundation in this next chapter of growth.” ... “It has been a privilege to partner with the GracoRoberts management team over the past 11 years,” said Jeffrey Mark, a managing partner at CM Equity. “Working together, we executed a value creation strategy centered on strategic acquisitions, operational excellence, and sustained organic growth, transforming GracoRoberts into the market-leading company it is today. We are proud of what the team has accomplished and believe the company is exceptionally well positioned for continued success with Tinicum.” ... “We greatly admire the business that the GracoRoberts team has built. It is distinguished by the team’s technical depth, unwavering commitment to customer service, and longstanding partnerships with the world’s leading material manufacturers,” said Erik Blumenkranz, a partner at Tinicum. “We intend to invest behind that foundation with a long-term mindset — in the people, the capabilities, and the platform,” added Roddy Cruz, a partner at Tinicum. “It is exactly the kind of durable, market-leading business we seek to partner with.” ... The buy of GracoRoberts lands in a corner of the aerospace supply chain buoyed by rising defense budgets and a busy aftermarket. The US aerospace adhesives and sealants market was worth roughly $360 million in 2025 and is expected to grow at about 5.7% a year through 2035, according to Precedence Research, while global estimates for 2026 range between $1.2 billion and $1.5 billion across research firms. North America accounts for more than 40% of volume, a lead that traces to sustained US military spending and the contractors and distributors that supply it. Demand is driven by the move to lightweight composite airframes, which rely on bonded rather than fastened joints, and by a maintenance, repair, and overhaul cycle that keeps specialty chemicals moving long after an aircraft is delivered. Distributors that pair technical support with compliance and logistics, as GracoRoberts does, sit at the center of that flow.For Tinicum, the appeal is a distributor with defensible characteristics: certifications and compliance standards that are difficult for new entrants to clear, deep technical relationships with both suppliers and aerospace customers, and a recurring aftermarket revenue base. The firm has signaled a long-hold approach rather than a quick flip, planning to invest behind the platform’s people and capabilities and to keep the management team in place with a meaningful equity stake. That continuity, paired with additional capital for acquisitions and internal investment, positions GracoRoberts to extend the buy-and-build strategy CM Equity began — consolidating a fragmented supply chain for specialty aerospace chemicals while deepening its position with blue-chip material manufacturers."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Betco® and Minuteman® Announce Strategic Asset Exchange,www.issa.com (Courtney Perry),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.issa.com/industry-news/betco-and-minuteman-announce-strategic-asset-exchange/,"Betco® Corporation (“Betco”), a leading manufacturer of specialty chemicals, today announced it has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Multi-Clean®, the Minnesota-based commercial cleaning chemical manufacturer, from Minuteman® International, a member of the Hako Group. As part of the same transaction, Betco is divesting its powered equipment business to Minuteman. The transaction is expected to close on July 31. ... This strategic transaction allows each company to better serve its customers by building on its category leadership and specialized expertise: ... - Multi-Clean’s chemical customers will be supported by a company dedicated exclusively to professional cleaning chemistry, with Betco’s broader product portfolio, research and development capabilities, and operating scale behind the Multi-Clean brands they rely on. - Betco’s powered equipment customers will be supported by a company dedicated exclusively to powered cleaning equipment, with Minuteman’s global manufacturing platform and service infrastructure behind the brands they rely on. ... “Multi-Clean has built an exceptional chemical business with strong customer relationships and distinctive products in the Multi-Task family,” Brad Betz, President and CEO of Betco, said. “We’re excited to build on that legacy and expand the reach of the Multi-Clean products customers rely on. We are equally confident that Minuteman is the right partner for our powered equipment customers going forward.” ... “In a consolidating marketplace, customers of both businesses benefit when companies focus on their core categories,” Jack Hill, President and CEO of Minuteman International, said. “Betco is the ideal home for Multi-Clean’s chemical customers, and we look forward to supporting Betco’s powered equipment customers with the quality and service they expect.” ... “This transaction creates long-term value by allowing each company to focus on what it does best,” said Toby Jercovich, Chief Financial Officer of Betco. “I want to thank the leadership teams at Minuteman International and Multi-Clean for their professionalism and collaborative approach throughout this process. Transactions of this complexity are built on trust, transparency and a shared focus on achieving the best outcome for our customers, team members and business partners. We also extend our sincere appreciation to our advisors who helped bring this transaction to a successful conclusion.” ... Both companies have developed detailed transition plans designed to support continuity of supply and service throughout the transition. For Multi-Clean’s chemical customers, bridge inventory will help ensure a seamless transition as production moves to Betco facilities. For Betco’s powered equipment customers, warranty coverage, service, parts availability, and dealer relationships will continue seamlessly under Minuteman. ... Betco is a privately held specialty chemical and equipment manufacturer known for high-performing products and programs that help our customers WIN in the commercial cleaning industry. For more information about Betco’s products and services, please call customer service at (888) GO-BETCO or visit betco.com. Follow us on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, and X! ... Since 1946, Multi-Clean has been a trusted manufacturer of high-performance commercial cleaning chemicals and floor maintenance solutions for the professional cleaning industry. With nearly eight decades of innovation and manufacturing excellence, the company develops products that deliver exceptional cleaning performance while prioritizing safety, sustainability, and ease of use. ... Multi-Clean partners with a nationwide network of authorized professional distributors to provide customers with expert guidance, technical support, training, and comprehensive cleaning solutions across a wide range of commercial, institutional, healthcare, education, and industrial facilities. ... Driven by its commitment to being Safe. Effective. Sustainable., Multi-Clean continues to invest in innovative technologies and industry-leading solutions that help organizations maintain cleaner, healthier, and more sustainable environments. The company remains dedicated to being the trusted resource for solving the cleaning industry’s toughest challenges through quality products, technical expertise, and outstanding customer support."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. Secures License for “Hatchi” Character Toothpaste and Toothbrushes, Following in the Footsteps of Pororo - EDAILY",en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202607205457/,"KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. Secures License for “Hatchi” Character Toothpaste and Toothbrushes, Following in the Footsteps of Pororo - EDAILY ... ## KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. Secures License for “Hatchi” Character Toothpaste and Toothbrushes, Following in the Footsteps of Pororo ... [Edaily Reporter YU JIN-HEE ] KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd.(225430), the company behind the “Pororo” phenomenon that dominated the infant and toddler oral care market, is now launching a global K-culture marketing campaign featuring “Haech’i,” the official mascot of Seoul. Following the recent announcement of a Seohan aimed at a head-on breakthrough after being designated as a “monitored stock”—which demonstrated the company’s commitment to structural reform—this move is a strategic step to drive a turnaround in performance by securing a character intellectual property (IP) that is sure to attract foreign tourists.KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd., a life care specialist, announced on the 20th that it has signed a licensing agreement with Iconix, one of Korea’s leading animation companies, for toothpaste and toothbrush products featuring the new character “Hatchi.”(Photo: KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd.) This agreement has drawn anticipation from the capital markets as it represents a joint effort between KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. and Iconix, which have maintained a strong partnership for over 20 years. KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. first entered the infant and toddler oral care market in 2005 by signing a licensing agreement with Iconix for “Pororo.” In 2017, the company made a surprise move to acquire a 4% stake in Iconix’s common stock to enhance synergies.The resulting Pororo toothpaste and toothbrushes have been mega-hits for nearly 20 years, riding the wave of the explosive popularity of Korean animation in not only the domestic market but also in China and Southeast Asia, becoming the company’s core growth engine.The Hatch toothpaste and toothbrushes, set for a surprise launch in the domestic market in the second half of this year, are also expected to follow this same formula for success. “Hatch,” the brand applied to these new products, is the official mascot of Seoul and the protagonist of the 3D animated series *My Secret Friend Hatch*, produced by Iconix. By reinterpreting Hatch—a mythical creature from legend—with a modern and approachable sensibility, the brand has secured high name recognition.KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. has set the main target audience for this Hatch lineup as foreign tourists visiting Seoul with their families. The strategy is to elevate the product’s value beyond mere hygiene items to “K-culture merchandise” that visitors can collect to commemorate their trip to Korea, thereby contributing to foreign exchange earnings.The actual market environment is extremely positive. According to the Korea Tourism Organization, driven by the global K-culture craze, the number of foreign tourists visiting Korea this year has already surpassed 10 million. As of May of this year, their domestic card spending exceeded the 2 trillion won mark for the first time since relevant statistics were first compiled in 2018. Notably, unlike in the past, spending is no longer limited to duty-free shops; tourists are increasingly spending freely across various retail channels, including street shops, drugstores, and novelty shops in major commercial districts such as Myeongdong.KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. plans to maximize exposure for its Haechi brand by focusing on high-traffic retail stores and large gift shops located in major tourist areas, including Myeongdong in Seoul—a location with the highest accessibility for foreign buyers and tourists.An official from KMPHARMACEUTICAL Co.,Ltd. stated, “Seoul is the heart of global K-culture and the ideal market for foreign tourists seeking unique shopping experiences,” adding, “We will significantly ramp up our online and offline campaigns, including large-scale pop-up stores that combine the Haechi character’s signature humor with relatable stories.”"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,ACR Acquires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business - Distribution Strategy Group,distributionstrategy.com (Mark Brohan),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://distributionstrategy.com/2026/07/acr-acquires-redibagusa-to-expand-sustainable-packaging-business/,"ACR Acquires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business - Distribution Strategy Group ACR Acquires RediBagUSA to Expand Sustainable Packaging Business - Distribution Strategy Group ... Why This Matters to Distributors: The acquisition expands ACR’s packaging portfolio and strengthens its presence in grocery, food service, healthcare, and industrial markets. It also highlights continued private equity-backed consolidation as distributors broaden product offerings and build scale through targeted acquisitions. ... ACR has acquired the assets of RediBagUSA, expanding its sustainable packaging portfolio and extending its reach across grocery, foodservice, healthcare, and industrial markets. ... Financial terms of the transaction, announced July 14, were not disclosed. ... The acquisition is the 11th add-on completed by ACR since the company was acquired by private equity firm Oridian Capital Partners, underscoring the firm’s strategy of building a larger packaging and foodservice supplies distribution platform through acquisitions. ... RediBagUSA, founded in 1957, supplies reusable retail bags, paper packaging, food safety bags, gloves, trash can liners and other disposable products to customers nationwide. The company also offers custom packaging solutions and sources products through a global supplier network. ... ACR said the acquisition expands its environmentally focused product portfolio while enhancing its ability to serve a broader range of end markets, including grocery stores, restaurants, delis, healthcare providers, and industrial customers. ... “This acquisition represents another important milestone in ACR’s growth journey,” Chief Executive Officer Scott Milberg said in a statement. “By bringing RediBagUSA into our organization, we are expanding our product breadth and strengthening our ability to meet evolving customer needs.” ... The deal also strengthens ACR’s sourcing capabilities and adds RediBagUSA’s portfolio of reusable, recyclable, and compostable packaging products as businesses continue shifting toward more sustainable packaging options. ... Oridian Capital Partners, formerly HCI Equity Partners, has pursued an active acquisition strategy since acquiring ACR, targeting distributors and manufacturers that expand the company’s product offerings and market reach. ... “RediBagUSA is the 11th acquisition under Oridian’s ownership and continues to underscore ACR’s disciplined approach to building scale through businesses that align strategically and culturally,” Managing Partner Doug McCormick said. ... Based in Exton, Pennsylvania, ACR distributes packaging, foodservice, janitorial and sanitation products, as well as operational supplies, through a network of distribution facilities across North America. Its customers include foodservice operators, healthcare providers, hospitality companies, schools, industrial businesses, and national retailers. ... The acquisition broadens ACR’s presence in the growing market for sustainable packaging while adding complementary products that can be sold through its existing distribution network. ... The acquisition reflects continued consolidation in the packaging and food service distribution sector, where distributors are using acquisitions to expand product categories, strengthen sourcing capabilities and offer customers a broader range of consumable products through a single supplier. ... - Avnet ... Supplier Partnerships and Digital Transformation - Global ... Deepens Customer Integration Strategy to Fuel Growth - ... Toward Data Centers, Customer Productivity and Distribution Network Expansion"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Sentinel Sells Autronica: Focuses Spectrum Safety on the US – HCNTimes.com,hcntimes.com,2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hcntimes.com/sentinel-sells-autronica-focuses-spectrum-safety-on-the-us/,"Sentinel Sells Autronica: Focuses ... Safety on the US – HCNTimes.com ... # Sentinel Sells Autronica: Focuses Spectrum Safety on the US On Jul 17, 2026 Sentinel Capital Partners has sold Autronica Fire and Security, the Norway-based fire and gas detection unit of its Spectrum Safety Solutions platform, to MSA Safety for $555 million, the second European business it has divested from Spectrum this year as it concentrates the platform on its U.S. detection and monitoring operations. ... Sentinel built Spectrum Safety Solutions in 2024 through a carveout of fire and gas detection and suppression assets from Carrier Global, assembling four businesses under one platform: Autronica and Marioff in Europe, and Det-Tronics and Fireye in the United States. Over the past year, Sentinel has moved to narrow that portfolio around the two U.S. brands. ... The Autronica transaction is the second step in that repositioning. In March 2026, Sentinel agreed to sell Spectrum’s Marioff unit, a Finland-based provider of high-pressure water mist fire suppression systems, to private equity firm Inflexion. The sale of Autronica to MSA Safety completes the exit from Spectrum’s European operations and leaves the platform centered on Det-Tronics and Fireye, its U.S.-headquartered detection and monitoring businesses. ... According to MSA Safety, Autronica generated revenue of approximately $160 million in 2025 at an adjusted EBITDA margin of about 20%, implying adjusted EBITDA of roughly $32 million. At a purchase price of $555 million, the sale values Autronica at approximately 17.3 times adjusted EBITDA. ... “It’s been a privilege to work alongside Sindre and the talented Autronica team,” said Eric Bommer, co-managing partner at Sentinel. “Over the past two years, the team has strengthened the business, expanded its global footprint, and built a strong foundation for the future. We thank them for a productive partnership and wish them continued success as part of MSA Safety.” ... The buyer, MSA Safety, is a publicly traded developer of industrial safety products and technology that has operated since 1914. The company reported 2025 revenue of $1.9 billion and employs approximately 5,300 people across more than 40 international locations from its headquarters near Pittsburgh in Cranberry Township, Pennsylvania. ... Fire and gas detection sits within a market shaped by tightening industrial safety regulation and the adoption of connected monitoring. The U.S. fire and gas detection market was estimated at about $3.7 billion in 2024 and is projected to expand at a compound annual rate of roughly 7.1%, according to Global Growth Insights. Demand is driven by stricter fire codes, rising investment in public and worker safety, and the migration toward IoT-enabled, multi-sensor systems in hazardous settings, trends that favor established providers with certifications for severe environments."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,SRM Concrete adds Troy Ready Mix to US operations - Aggregates Business,www.aggbusiness.com (Adam Daunt),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.aggbusiness.com/srm-concrete-adds-troy-ready-mix-to-us-operations/,"SRM Concrete adds Troy Ready Mix to US operations - Aggregates Business ... # SRM Concrete adds Troy Ready Mix to US operations ... by Adam Daunt July 17, 2026 ... SRM Concrete has acquired Troy Ready Mix, Inc. Image: SRM Concrete ... SRM Concrete has expanded its presence in North Carolina after acquiring Troy Ready Mix, Inc., adding one ready-mix concrete plant and one precast facility to its operations. ... The acquisition increases SRM Concrete’s network in the state to 20 locations and establishes the company’s first operation in central North Carolina. ... SRM Concrete chief executive officer Jeff Hollingshead said the acquisition supports the company’s ongoing investment strategy across the state. ... “The acquisition of Troy Ready Mix is another meaningful step in our continued investment across North Carolina,” Hollingshead said. ... Founded in 1999, SRM Concrete has grown to become one of the largest ready-mix concrete producers in the United States. The family-owned company operates an integrated network of ready-mix concrete plants, quarries, cement terminals and related building materials businesses across 24 states. ... company, SRM Concrete employs more than 8500 people and supplies construction materials to commercial and residential projects across its operating footprint."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Mexico Chemical Distribution Market: Growth Trends and Industry...,www.pikumil.com,2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.pikumil.com/blogs/104641/Mexico-Chemical-Distribution-Market-Growth-Trends-and-Industry-Opportunities,"Mexico chemical distribution market is expected to gain market growth in the forecast period of 2022 to 2029. Data Bridge Market Research analyses that the market is growing at a CAGR of 5.0% in the forecast period of 2022 to 2029 and expected to reach USD 3,145,549.96 thousand by 2029. The major factor driving the market is rising consumption of chemicals across numerous industries. ... - Brenntag: One of the leading players in the Mexico chemical distribution market, Brenntag offers a wide range of chemicals to various industries. With a strong distribution network and expertise in handling different chemicals, Brenntag holds a significant market share. ... - Univar Solutions: Another key player in the market, Univar Solutions provides customized chemical solutions to meet the unique needs of its customers. With a focus on sustainability and innovation, Univar Solutions is a trusted partner for many industries. ... - Quimica Alemana: A prominent player in the specialty chemicals segment, Quimica Alemana specializes in providing high-value chemicals for specific applications. With a strong reputation for quality and reliability, Quimica Alemana has established itself as a key player in the market. ... - Grupo Carso: Known for its diversified business operations, Grupo Carso is also involved in the chemical distribution market in Mexico. With a wide portfolio of chemicals and a strong distribution network, Grupo Carso caters to a diverse range of industries. ... - Norka: With a focus on sustainability and responsible chemical distribution, Norka is an emerging player in the market. The company offers eco-friendly alternatives and innovative solutions to meet the changing needs of the industry. ... The Mexico chemical distribution market is poised for steady growth due to several factors such as increasing industrialization, rising demand for specialty chemicals, and the expansion of key end-use industries like automotive, construction, agriculture, and healthcare. The market players mentioned earlier have established strong footholds in the industry by offering diverse chemical solutions tailored to meet the specific needs of their customers. As the market continues to evolve, players are focusing on innovation, sustainability, and quality to stay competitive and capture a larger market share. ... -friendly alternatives is gaining momentum ... environmentally conscious and demand ... that have minimal impact on the planet ... offer innovative, ... Another key aspect shaping the Mexico chemical distribution market is the regulatory landscape. Compliance with local and international regulations governing the handling, distribution, and use of chemicals is non-negotiable for market players. Companies that prioritize regulatory adherence and invest in robust compliance frameworks will not only ensure the safety of their operations but also build trust with customers who prioritize ethical business practices. ... Collaborations and partnerships within the industry also play a significant role in driving growth and innovation in the Mexico chemical distribution market. By forming strategic alliances with suppliers, manufacturers, and customers, market players can access new markets, expand their product portfolios, and leverage each other's strengths to deliver comprehensive chemical solutions. These collaborations can lead to synergies that benefit all parties involved and contribute to the overall growth of the market. ... Overall, the Mexico chemical distribution market presents ample opportunities for existing players to expand their market presence and for new entrants to establish themselves in a rapidly growing industry. By focusing on innovation, quality, sustainability, and regulatory compliance, companies can navigate the complexities of the market landscape and drive future success. As the demand for diverse chemical solutions continues to rise across various industries, market players that can adapt to changing customer needs and market dynamics will be well-positioned for long-term growth and prosperity in the Mexico chemical distribution market.The Mexico chemical distribution market is undergoing significant transformation driven by factors such as increasing industrialization, rising demand for specialty chemicals, and the growth of key end-use industries including automotive, construction, agriculture, and healthcare. Market players are focusing on differentiation strategies to stand out in a crowded marketplace by investing in research and development to create unique chemical formulations tailored to meet the evolving needs of diverse industries. Sustainability and eco-friendly alternatives are gaining traction as customers increasingly prioritize environmentally conscious products with minimal impact on the planet. Companies that can adapt to these changing trends and offer innovative, sustainable solutions are poised to gain a competitive edge and capture a larger market share. ... Regulatory compliance is a critical aspect shaping the Mexico chemical distribution market, with companies emphasizing adherence to local and international regulations governing the handling, distribution, and use of chemicals. Prioritizing robust compliance frameworks not only ensures operational safety but also builds trust with customers who value ethical business practices. Collaborations and partnerships within the industry are key drivers of growth and innovation, enabling market players to access new markets, expand product portfolios, and leverage each other's strengths to deliver comprehensive chemical solutions. Strategic alliances with suppliers, manufacturers, and customers can foster synergies that benefit all