TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Tradewater Acquires Carbon Shield, Accelerating Development of Projects Preventing Methane Emissions from Orphaned Oil and Gas Wells",www.prnewswire.com (Tradewater),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/tradewater-acquires-carbon-shield-accelerating-development-of-projects-preventing-methane-emissions-from-orphaned-oil-and-gas-wells-302826524.html,"CHICAGO, July 15, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Tradewater, LLC, a global leader in developing projects to permanently eliminate superpollutants, announced that they have acquired Carbon Shield, a Colorado-based company that plugs actively leaking orphaned oil and gas wells. ... Tradewater's strategic acquisition of Carbon Shield ensures and accelerates Tradewater's development of methane abatement projects in Colorado and Wyoming, where Carbon Shield has built relationships and a pipeline of orphaned oil and gas wells to be plugged. Tradewater began developing projects in the orphaned oil and gas space in 2023 and has completed projects across Illinois, Indiana, and Kansas with an impact of over 1.6 million tons of CO₂ e. The Carbon Shield acquisition facilitates Tradewater's expansion into new geographies in the US, and their overall impact in the orphaned oil and gas space. ... ""Methane is the make-or-break gas for climate action, and ... are an uncontrolled source of methane that can be mitigated through known technologies ... ,"" says Kirsten Dueck, CEO of ... ""Tradewater is committed to rapidly scaling ... important work. The acquisition ... enables us to do just that."" ... Tradewater's mission is to permanently eliminate superpollutants and bend the curve on global warming as quickly as possible. To do this, Tradewater focuses on collecting, controlling, and permanently preventing the release of non-CO₂ superpollutants thousands of times more potent than carbon dioxide–and methane is a critical part of this mission. This includes projects that destroy legacy ozone-depleting refrigerants at their end of life, as well as projects that plug orphaned oil and gas wells. ... year timeframe accelerating ... Environmental Protection Agency ... 0 documented orphaned wells – ... thousands more undocumented ... Yet, no ... requires their cleanup ... Left unchecked, these wells will continue to leak methane ... fuel climate change ... Tradewater's goal is to prevent over 30 million tons of CO₂e emissions by 2030, and the development of projects to address methane from orphaned oil and gas wells is critical in achieving this milestone. ... Scaling the work to plug orphaned wells goes hand in hand with scaling the demand for high-quality climate solutions. Tradewater has worked to turn overlooked emissions into immediate, scalable impact, offering a fast, results-driven path to slow global warming today while complementing long-term carbon mitigation strategies for companies. Workday, Duke University, and Airbnb are among Tradewater's growing list of cross-sector partners looking to prioritize the inclusion of superpollutants in their climate portfolios. ... About Tradewater A certified B Corp, Tradewater directly combats climate change by identifying, collecting, and eliminating the release of non-CO₂ superpollutants—including halocarbons from old refrigerants, excess halon gasses from canisters, and methane from actively leaking oil and gas wells. These critical environmental actions generate high-quality carbon offset credits. The Tradewater team has eliminated over 11.3 million tons of CO2 equivalent since inception and is on a path to prevent at least 30 million tons by 2030 — similar to removing nearly 7 million gas-powered cars from U.S. roads. Every Tradewater credit is backed by rigorous third-party verification and issued by leading registries to ensure maximum integrity, additionality, and accuracy. Learn more at www.tradewater.co. ... ### Tradewater Announces New CEO - and New Ownership Structure - as it Accelerates Mission to Eliminate Super Pollutants ... Tradewater, a global leader in permanently eliminating super pollutants, announced a CEO transition this month with cofounder and CEO Tim Brown..."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Customer Agreement for Compact Plastic-Free Dish Detergent Tablet,itaconix.com,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://itaconix.com/blog/customer-agreement-for-compact-plastic-free-dish-detergent-tablet,"Itaconix plc (AIM: ITX) (OTCQB: ITXXF), a leading innovator in high-performance plant-based specialty polymers used in everyday consumer products such as homecare detergents, announces its first customer supply agreement for its 8-gram plastic-free dish detergent tablets. ... Under its SPARX Formulated Solutions business, Itaconix will supply dish detergent tablets to a North American purpose-driven brand using the pilot-scale tableting capacity at its North American Innovation Center. The tablet was developed around the unique performance advantages of Itaconix® TSI® polymers and the Bonals tablet press. The new tablet was introduced at the American Cleaning Institute’s Innovation Showcase in February 2026 and is available to brand managers and retail customers on the Company’s deeperclean.com ecommerce site. ... This supply agreement is an important milestone in the commercial introduction of the Company’s patented plastic-free detergent tablets in North America. The new tablets are expected to be available on retail shelves by the end of 2026. ... “Our plant-based ingredients are leading a new generation of plastic-free solid unit-dose detergents in Europe and North America because they are safe for the environment and offer unique value with their multi-functional performance. We are already gaining volumes in dish and laundry detergent tablets in North America. Supply agreements to a select number of purpose-driven brands will allow us to push further innovation onto the market and progress efforts with North American contract detergent manufacturers to produce our proprietary tablets on high-speed tablet presses.” ... Itaconix uses its proprietary plant-based polymer technology platform to produce and sell specialty ingredients that improve the safety, performance, and sustainability of consumer products. The Company's current ingredients are enabling and leading new generations of products in detergents, hygiene, and hair care. Itaconix's products contribute to the global low carbon economy. ... Bonals Technologies is a tableting technology provider serving customers worldwide. With 1000+ machines currently producing, the company developed strong partnerships with leading detergent tablet brands and contract manufacturers in Europe and Asia thanks to innovative and ecological solutions dedicated to homecare, laundry care and chemicals. ... Investor News Itaconix signs agreement with Nouryon for Itaconix’s bio-based polymers for the detergents industry Jan 15, 2019 2 min read ... Investor News Itaconix and AkzoNobel move from the technical evaluation phase to defining a joint marketing effort for Itaconix bio-based chelates May 18, 2018 1 min read ... Investor News Itaconix plc (“Itaconix”) Q1 2018 Trading Update Apr 16, 2018 2 min read"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,White Cap to Acquire Iowa-Based Gierke Robinson - Modern Distribution Management,www.mdm.com (MDM Staff),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mdm.com/news/top-distributor-sectors/building-materials-construction/white-cap-to-acquire-iowa-based-gierke-robinson/,"White Cap to Acquire Iowa-Based Gierke Robinson - Modern Distribution Management ... White Cap to Acquire Iowa-Based Gierke Robinson ... The century-old contractor equipment and concrete supplies distributor will add four Iowa locations and expand White Cap’s product and service capabilities across portions of the Midwest. ... Construction supplies distributor White Cap has signed a definitive agreement to acquire the business of Gierke Robinson Company, an Iowa-based distributor of concrete accessories and tools that also provides equipment rentals and repair services. ... Financial terms of the pending transaction were not disclosed. ... Founded in 1919, Gierke Robinson serves concrete, paving and general contractors across eastern Iowa, western Illinois and southwestern Wisconsin. The company operates four Iowa locations in Davenport, Bettendorf, Dubuque and Waterloo. ... Gierke Robinson’s offerings include construction equipment and supplies, decorative concrete products, safety gear and equipment rentals. The company also services and repairs equipment from a range of manufacturers. ... White Cap said the acquisition will expand its presence and product offering in the Midwest. ... “Gierke Robinson has had an incredible reputation as an expert in construction equipment for more than a century,” White Cap CEO Alan Sollenberger said in the July 13 announcement. “We are excited to welcome their talented associates to the White Cap family, enabling our combined teams to offer our customers expanded presence and greater service capabilities in a growing Midwestern market.” ... Gierke Robinson owner Terry Kilburg said joining White Cap will provide the company with expanded solutions and resources while maintaining its focus on customer service. ... The agreement marks White Cap’s fourth announced acquisition of 2026. The Atlanta-based distributor acquired specialty concrete products manufacturer VoidForm Products in January, followed by its combination with Colony Hardware in February. The Colony deal added more than 60 locations across the eastern and central U.S. White Cap acquired Albuquerque, NM-based Concrete Systems Inc. and its El Paso, TX, location in May. ... White Cap distributes concrete accessories and chemicals, tools and equipment, building materials, fasteners, erosion and waterproofing products and safety supplies. The Clayton, Dubilier & Rice portfolio company operates approximately 575 branches across North America, with more than 12,000 employees serving about 200,000 customers. ... White Cap Acquires Concrete Systems Inc. in Albuquerque ... White Cap gains a nearly 60-year-old distributor with two locations serving the U.S. Southwest."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Battery Power Online | Stryten Energy Acquires C&D Technologies, Trojan Battery",www.batterypoweronline.com (Irene Yeh),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.batterypoweronline.com/news/stryten-energy-acquires-cd-technologies-trojan-battery/,"Stryten Energy Acquires C& ... Technologies, Trojan Battery ... ## Stryten Energy Acquires C&D Technologies, Trojan Battery ... July 14, 2026 | Stryten Energy has acquired C&D Technologies, Inc. and Trojan Battery Company, creating a scaled platform to advance global battery manufacturing and deliver comprehensive energy storage solutions across critical markets. Upon completion of the transaction, the company will continue to be led by Stryten’s Chief Executive Officer and President, Mike Judd. The transaction is anticipated to close in the third quarter of 2026 and is subject to customary closing conditions and regulatory approvals. Terms of the transaction were not disclosed. ... “This combination brings together two highly complementary organizations with a shared commitment to delivering reliable, high-performance energy storage solutions,” said Mike Judd, Chief Executive Officer and President of Stryten Energy, in a press release. “By combining our capabilities, we will accelerate innovation, expand our manufacturing footprint, and better serve customers across transportation, industrial, essential power and military and government sectors.” ... “C&D Trojan and Stryten Energy share a strong commitment to innovation, manufacturing excellence, and serving customers in critical markets,” said Rick Heller, President and CEO of C&D Trojan in the same press release. “By bringing our organizations together, we are expanding our capabilities, broadening our solutions portfolio, and creating a stronger foundation to support customers’ evolving energy storage needs.” ... The combined organization will offer a broad set of lead and lithium-based energy storage technologies, markets, and applications. ... - Transportation: automotive, truck, heavy-duty, lawn & garden, marine, LSEV, RV and other applications - Essential Power: AI/data centers, uninterruptible power supply (UPS), telecommunications, utilities, nuclear and grid infrastructure - Industrial: material handling, mining, railway, floor care, aerial work platforms and industrial equipment - Military and government: wheeled tactical vehicles, missile defense systems, submarines, logistics and mission-critical infrastructure ... “The addition of C&D Trojan will strengthen our ability to deliver a full portfolio of energy storage solutions to our customers,” Judd added. “Together, we will build a stronger and more agile company that is ideally positioned to meet evolving energy demands.” ... Expanding U.S. Manufacturing ... Following the close of the transaction, Stryten will operate 15 battery manufacturing and component facilities across the U.S., supported by 3,700 employees. This expanded domestic footprint will strengthen Stryten’s vertically integrated manufacturing supply chain and its ability to produce energy storage solutions at scale to meet growing demand. Additionally, Stryten plans to expand Absorbent Glass Mat (AGM) battery manufacturing capacity to meet increased demand for advanced lead batteries required for hybrid and start-stop vehicle technologies, as well as data center and telecom resiliency applications. ... The enhanced scale, expanded product breadth and strengthened domestic manufacturing capabilities will also enable Stryten to expand its support of U.S. Department of War programs and mission-critical infrastructure, delivering reliable, domestically produced solutions designed to meet stringent performance and security requirements."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Energy storage brand merger: Stryten to acquire C&D Trojan,www.solarpowerworldonline.com (Kelly Pickerel),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/07/energy-storage-brand-merger-stryten-to-acquire-cd-trojan/,"Energy storage brand merger: Stryten to acquire C&D Trojan ... Energy storage solutions provider Stryten Energy announced it would acquire C&D Trojan, another American battery brand with a storied history. The transaction is anticipated to close in Q3 2026, and the combined company will continue to be led by Stryten’s CEO and president Mike Judd. ... “This combination brings together two highly complementary organizations with a shared commitment to delivering reliable, high-performance energy storage solutions,” Judd said. “By combining our capabilities, we will accelerate innovation, expand our manufacturing footprint, and better serve customers across transportation, industrial, essential power and military and government sectors.” ... Trojan Battery formed in 1925 and has been a leading deep-cycle battery manufacturer in the global market. In 2018, C&D Technologies acquired the Trojan brand to form C&D Trojan. ... “C&D Trojan and Stryten Energy share a strong commitment to innovation, manufacturing excellence, and serving customers in critical markets,” said Rick Heller, President and CEO of C&D Trojan. “By bringing our organizations together, we are expanding our capabilities, broadening our solutions portfolio, and creating a stronger foundation to support customers’ evolving energy storage needs.” ... The combined Stryten-Tojan organization will offer one of the industry’s most comprehensive portfolios of lead and lithium-based energy storage technologies, spanning a broad set of markets and applications. ... Following the close of the transaction, Stryten will operate 15 battery manufacturing and component facilities across the United States, supported by 3,700 employees. This expanded domestic footprint will strengthen Stryten’s vertically integrated manufacturing supply chain and its ability to produce energy storage solutions at scale to meet growing demand. Additionally, Stryten plans to expand absorbent glass mat (AGM) battery manufacturing capacity to meet increased demand for advanced lead batteries required for hybrid and start-stop vehicle technologies, as well as data center and telecom resiliency applications."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Diamond Chemical Acquires Nyco Products - Textile Rental Services Association,www.trsa.org,2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.trsa.org/news/diamond-chemical-acquires-nyco-products/,"Diamond Chemical Acquires Nyco Products - Textile Rental Services Association ... # Diamond Chemical Acquires Nyco Products ... Diamond Chemical Co. Inc., East Rutherford, NJ, announced that it acquired Nyco Products Co., a Countryside, IL-based manufacturer of cleaning products and solutions for a range of industries and markets including building and facilities maintenance, janitorial cleaning, industrial cleaning, food processing, healthcare and education. ... The acquisition brings together Diamond Chemical’s coastal operations with Nyco’s Midwest manufacturing footprint, creating a national provider of commercial, institutional, industrial cleaning solutions and specialty chemical products. ... “Nyco brings deep formulation expertise, a strong brand portfolio and a Midwest manufacturing footprint that perfectly complements our coastal operations,” said Diamond Chemical CEO Wesley Alves. “Together, we can offer our customers broader product availability and stronger national service. But beyond the logistics, what makes me most excited about this next chapter is the people. We are uniting two incredibly talented teams that share a relentless dedication to doing things right for the customer. I am honored to lead this combined organization and build on the phenomenal foundation that Bob (Stahurski, CEO of Nyco) and his team have established.” ... Stahurski will retire as CEO of Nyco. However, he will remain involved as an investor and adviser, ensuring a seamless transition and continuing to lend his expertise to the newly combined team. ... “The sale of our business preserves our history and culture while ensuring that our customers continue to receive the same high level of quality, reliability and service,” Stahurski said. “I am confident that our customers, partners and legacy will continue to thrive under Diamond’s leadership.” ... Publish Date May 29, 202"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Nippon Sanso rebrands US dry ice division to Nippon Sanso Carbonic Products | M&A & Corporate Strategy | gasworld,www.gasworld.com (gasworld),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gasworld.com/story/nippon-rebrands-us-dry-ice-division-to-nippon-sanso-carbonic-products/2253967.article/,"Nippon Sanso rebrands US dry ice division to Nippon Sanso Carbonic Products | M&A & Corporate Strategy | gasworld ... # Nippon Sanso rebrands US dry ice division to Nippon Sanso Carbonic Products ... Industrial gas specialist Nippon Sanso Matheson has rebranded its US dry ice business from Continental Carbonic Products to Nippon Sanso Carbonic Products. ... Nippon Sanso Matheson, operating as Matheson Tri-Gas, acquired Continental Carbonic Products in February 2014. ... Over the past twelve years, the company has scaled its distribution network to become the largest US dry ice supplier, with over 40 domestic facilities. ... Andrew Gregory, President of Nippon Sanso Carbonic Products, said, “The launch of Nippon Sanso Carbonic Products reflects both our heritage and our position as part of a global leader.” ... The company provides food-grade dry ice, blasting pellets, dry ice equipment, and liquid carbon dioxide solutions to support reliable operations across industries. ... Its dry ice distribution has a range of processing and transportation applications, including, food processing, pharmaceutical manufacturing, biotechnology, airline catering, industrial cleaning and maintenance operations. ... According to market research, the global dry ice market is projected to be worth around $2.79bn by 2032, up from roughly $1.67bn in 2025. ... Nippon Sanso opens automated dry ice plant in Sweden ... Reliant Dry Ice expands across the Midwest ... Nippon Gases and HOYER lead with Germany’s first hydrogen-powered dry ice truck"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Beauty dealmaking heats up with Trilogy and Thriving Brands portfolio expansions,www.personalcareinsights.com (03 Jul 2026 | By Ela Jade Ünal),2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.personalcareinsights.com/news/trilogy-thriving-brands-beauty-acquisitions.html,"# Beauty dealmaking heats up with Trilogy and Thriving Brands portfolio expansions ... - Trilogy Laboratories acquired YNS Cosmeceuticals to strengthen its skin care portfolio with pharmaceutical formulation expertise and FDA-compliant manufacturing. - Thriving Brands acquired Colab Dry Shampoo and Johnny’s Chop Shop from SLG Brands to expand its everyday personal care portfolio. - Beauty and personal care mergers and acquisitions activity is rising, with recent deals spanning skin care, hair care, ingredients, and silicones across the US, UK, and Europe. ... Beauty and personal care dealmaking is ripe across skin care, hair care, and ingredients, as companies acquire brands to scale science-backed portfolios, manufacturing capabilities, and global market reach. ... Trilogy Laboratories has acquired YNS Cosmeceuticals, incorporating its pharmaceutical heritage and FDA-compliant manufacturing capabilities into the skin care brand. YNS has a background in clean beauty aligned with “skinimalism” trends. ... Meanwhile, UK-based beauty incubator SLG Brands has finalized the offload of two of its flagship hair care brands to Thriving Brands. Colab Dry Shampoo and Johnny’s Chop Shop will enter the US-based acquisition platform’s repertoire of everyday personal care brands. ... Trilogy states that part of the motivation for its acquisition of YNS was to avoid introducing a new skin care line in an already saturated market, but to leverage YNS’s existing consumer base. ... The acquisition is said to embolden YNS’s manufacturing capabilities with the support of Trilogy’s existing manufacturing infrastructure. ... Trilogy boasts an FDA-registered cosmetic manufacturing facility and offers formulation development, manufacturing, quality assurance, regulatory oversight, and product innovation to skin care brands. ... “We acquired YNS because it already represented many of the qualities we value most — thoughtful formulations, a clear philosophy, and the trust of its customers,” says Dr. Kristen Flaharty, CEO at Trilogy Laboratories. “Our responsibility is to preserve that foundation while supporting the brand’s future with pharmaceutical formulation expertise, physician leadership, and continued innovation.” ... Trilogy says that the acquisition is meant to provide “continuity rather than change” for existing YNS customers. ... ## Scaling hair with Thriving BrandsTrilogy Laboratories has acquired YNS Cosmeceuticals to strengthen its science-backed skin care portfolio. ... Of Thriving Brands’ acquisitions, Colab is a science-backed dry shampoo brand, and Johnny’s Chop Shop operates in the men’s grooming and hair care space. ... “We conceived and founded Colab and Johnny’s Chop Shop and grew them into internationally recognized brands. This transaction frees SLG to focus on what comes next,” says Lucy Beresford, CEO at SLG Brands. ... Craig Cappozzo, CEO of Thriving Brands, adds: “Colab and Johnny’s Chop Shop are the kind of brands that win on shelf because they were built with genuine consumer insight and cultural relevance.” ... “Our job is to protect what makes them work and scale what makes them grow. SLG established an exceptional foundation — we’re here to build the next chapter.” ... Thriving Brands’ existing portfolio includes men’s body care brand Right Guard and deodorant label Dry Idea Brands. The company maintains a dedicated growth platform across various industries and markets."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Resorcinol-Derivative Skincare Market Poised to Grow at 7.8% CAGR During 2026–2032 – News24 Philippines,www.news24.ph (News24 Pinoy),2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.news24.ph/biz/70202/,"PW Consulting’s latest market study on Resorcinol Derivatives for Skincare (base year 2025; forecast period 2026–2032) delivers a distilled, decision-ready view for senior executives and strategic teams preparing to act in 2026. The market has expanded from approximately USD 162.45 Million in 2020 to USD 229.33 Million in 2025 and is modelled to grow at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 7.8% through the forecast window, reaching an estimated USD 387.97 Million by 2032. This bulletin highlights the report’s strategic value — showcasing the analytical depth you can expect while preserving the proprietary subsegment detail that remains available in the full report. Resorcinol Derivative For Skincare Market ... Resorcinol derivatives occupy an outsized strategic niche in skincare formulation: they span high-value brightening actives, antioxidant/anti-aging adjuncts and targeted blemish treatments. Growth drivers are a mix of demand-side dynamics (persistent consumer appetite for efficacious brightening solutions and evidence-based adjuncts for aging skin) and supply-side forces (advances in synthetic routes and specialty suppliers refining cosmetic-grade chemistries). Our modeling shows steady, above-market expansion for the category as formulators continue to balance performance claims with regulatory and safety considerations. Resorcinol Derivative For Skincare Market ... Input-cost volatility: Upstream benzene and phenol dynamics remain a core margin lever. Regional pricing snapshots and supply tightness — including notable premium environments in parts of Europe versus lower-cost pockets elsewhere — materially alter pricing sensitivity for manufacturers and formulators: procurement strategies and hedging are therefore tactical priorities for 2026. ... Regulatory boundary conditions: Authorities in major markets continue to calibrate use-limits and labelling obligations tied to sensitization risk. Existing EU and SCCS positions constrain certain resorcinol uses and require careful dossier work for newer derivatives; expect regulatory scrutiny to be a gating item for commercial launches. ... Product innovation: Suppliers are introducing derivative chemistries designed to retain efficacy while reducing irritancy and improving stability in diverse formulation matrices. Recent industry activity — including new offerings from established chemical majors — underscores a market pivot toward differentiated chemistries that can be credibly substantiated in claims and safety dossiers. ... M&A and partnership screen: prioritised target archetypes, valuation multiples observed in adjacent actives markets, and integration checklists for upstream or formulation-led acquisitions. ... The competitive set blends large specialty chemicals groups with regional and niche producers. Key players identified in our primary research include global formulators and chemical producers that integrate resorcinol derivatives into broader personal care portfolios, alongside regional manufacturers focusing on cost-competitive, cosmetic-grade resorcinol and derivatives. ... Leveraging scale and R&D, ... for multinational brands ... reliable supply and regulatory completeness. ... Notable recent development: Mitsubishi Chemical Corporation introduced a new line of 4-Chlororesorcinol derivatives targeted at high-performance personal care formulations — a sign that majors continue to invest in differentiated chemistries to unlock new claims and circumvent existing limits tied to traditional resorcinol use. ... Prioritise derivative R&D with a safety-first lens: Invest in chemistries that reduce sensitization potential and generate the clinical and in-vitro data needed for trustworthy claims. Winning products in 2026 will tie efficacy to safety through robust human and analytical evidence. ... Secure upstream: Negotiate feedstock-linked contracts and consider strategic offtakes or minority investments in phenol/benzene conversion pathways to stabilise costs and assure supply continuity. ... Adopt a tiered go-to-market approach: For ingredient suppliers, pair premium, fully-supported actives with a lower-cost commodity offering aimed at private label — this preserves margin while expanding addressable demand. ... Execute targeted M&A or partnerships: Look for bolt-on specialists that bring unique derivatives, regulatory dossiers or formulation IP to accelerate market entry without internal R&D timelines. ... Hedge regulatory risk with diligence: Build a regulatory heatmap per market and per derivative that informs launch sequence, label strategy and required clinical packages; this is non-negotiable for premium claims. ... Clients who have used our market products cite three immediate wins: speed to a credible investment thesis (weeks, not months), reduction in commercial execution uncertainty through supplier and formulation playbooks, and greater confidence in M&A pricing via our target archetype analysis. The full report combines primary interviews, proprietary scenario modeling and supplier benchmarking into a practical toolkit — not just a market narrative. ... As a “trailer,” this release purposefully sets out strategic conclusions, contextual drivers and recommended actions while reserving granular subsegment breakouts and transaction-level data for report subscribers. If your team is evaluating entry, expansion, or acquisition in resorcinol derivatives for skincare in 2026, our report is designed to reduce your time-to-decision and articulate the practical trade-offs executives will face."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,"Alexium levels up cooling for bedding, foam and fabrics | Home Textiles Today",www.hometextilestoday.com (Home Textiles Today Staff),2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.hometextilestoday.com/textiles/alexium-expands-cooling-materials-with-micronal-acquisition/,"# Alexium levels up cooling for bedding, foam and fabrics ... Home Textiles Today Staff// News & Commentary//June 30, 2026 ... - Alexium has integrated the Micronal brand into its portfolio - Micronal technology uses phase-change materials for heat regulation - The brand came as part of Alexium’s recent acquisition of Microtek Laboratories. - Alexium offers diverse cooling solutions including NexTek and VivTek ... Greer, S.C. – Alexium International Group, a materials science company known for heat-regulating and flame-resistant technologies, has expanded its cooling materials business by adding the Micronal brand to its product lineup. ... The brand came as part of Alexium’s recent acquisition of Microtek Laboratories. ... By bringing Micronal in-house, Alexium says it can now offer customers more options for tailoring cooling solutions to specific products, backed by in-house manufacturing and product development support. ... “Micronal carries strong recognition within the marketplace as one of the foundational PCM technologies in thermal management,” said Billy Blackburn, CEO of Alexium. He said the acquisition positions the company to build on that reputation with broader manufacturing capacity and new innovations in the space. ... Alexium now offers a full range of cooling technologies under one roof, each suited to different needs: ... - Micronal for general-purpose cooling across textiles, mattresses and construction materials - NexTek for applications needing fast heat transfer - VivTek for maximum cooling power with a sustainability angle - AlexiCool and BioCool, a two coatings designed specifically for mattress and foam systems. ... says further next-generation technologies are also in development. ... Rather than relying on simple “cool-to-the-touch” claims, Alexium is positioning itself to help brands test and engineer cooling performance across an entire product, not just a single material. The company recently introduced a tool called the Predictive Thermal Profile platform, which models how heat moves through multi-layer products such as a mattress combining foam, fabric and cooling treatments together. ... “With increasing demand for meaningful cooling performance, brands are looking beyond simple cool-to-the-touch claims toward more holistic thermal management strategies,” Blackburn said, adding that the broader platform allows Alexium to work with customers on cooling duration, comfort and manufacturability. ... The company says the move also strengthens its domestic supply chain for cooling materials as it continues investing in thermal management innovation. ... - Cool it: Alexium unveils triple action tech for bedding, mattresses - Next-gen BioCool bedding tech ups the ante on sleep solutions - Bedding technology leaders unite through acquisition"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,TCC Materials® Acquisition of Concrete Products Company - TCC Materials,www.tccmaterials.com (Gabby Robinson),2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tccmaterials.com/2026/06/29/tcc-materials-acquisition-of-concrete-products-company/,"TCC Materials® Acquisition of Concrete Products Company - TCC Materials ... ## TCC Materials® Acquisition of Concrete Products Company ... Mendota Heights, MN – TCC Materials today announced the acquisition of Concrete Products Co., a well-established provider of construction materials located in Sioux City, Iowa which will be operating as TCC Materials • Sioux City. Product offerings include concrete masonry units, hardscape units and construction supply products. ... Established in 1946, Concrete Products Co. has built a strong and enduring presence in its local market. “After 80 years in business, the time has come to transition the company for the future. Finding a partner that both honors our history and shares our vision forward is an extraordinary opportunity,” said Bob Batcheller, CEO of Concrete Products Co. “Becoming part of the TCC family represents a natural alignment of companies, cultures, and purpose.” ... “I am pleased to welcome Concrete Products Co. to TCC Materials and extend my personal thanks to Bob Batcheller for his exceptional stewardship of the business,” said Brian DiGrado, Senior Vice President & General Manager of TCC Materials. “The culture of Concrete Products Co. strongly complements our own commitment to service excellence, deep customer understanding, technical support, and uncompromising quality assurance. We are excited about the opportunities to integrate our product portfolios with Concrete Products Co.’s established offerings as we look toward continued growth and long-term success.” ... Established in 1927, TCC Materials is a leading manufacturer of packaged construction products and hardscape solutions. Headquartered in Mendota Heights, Minnesota, thecompany operates more than 33 facilities across ten states and is organized into four core divisions: Standard Products Packaging, Specialty & Chemicals Packaging, Masonry, andHardscapes & Precast. TCC Materials offers a comprehensive portfolio that includes prepackaged concrete, mortars, grouts, concrete repair and restoration solutions, spec-blended construction materials, masonry systems, hardscapes, and precast products—serving both professional contractors, dealers, distributors, retail and commercial markets. The company is committed to delivering consistent quality, technical expertise, and superior customer service. The organization brings a comprehensive and highly complementary portfolio across packaging, hardscapes, and masonry: ... Packaging Brands: Tenon®, Tenon Conproco®, Tech Mix®, Tech Mix ... Masonry®, Tech Mix Akona®, Rapid Patch ... ikrete®, ... rete®, Spec ... Stone®.Hardscaping Brands: ... Creek®, LedgeRock®, and NorthRock®.Masonry Brands: ... ®, Spec-Brik®, Spec-Thermal®, and ... ## TCC Materials’ Traction Grit Featured by Gertens ... ## TCC Materials® Acquisition of Conproco, Inc. ... 025"
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,LION Expands TotalCare Services Into California Through Acquisition,www.uniformmarketnews.com (Nina Evans),2026-06-09T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.uniformmarketnews.com/lion-expands-totalcare-services-into-california,"LION Expands TotalCare Services Into California Through Acquisition ... Home News Companies LION Expands TotalCare Services Into California Through Acquisition ... LION Safety Solutions has acquired Turnout Maintenance Company, a Los Angeles area provider specializing in the cleaning, inspection, and repair of firefighter protective gear. ... The acquisition expands LION’s TotalCare service network into Southern California and strengthens its presence on the West Coast. ... Care Facility in California ... The newly acquired location becomes LION’s first TotalCare facility in California and its second on the West Coast. ... LION says the facility will help meet growing demand for firefighter PPE maintenance services throughout California and neighboring states. ... The site will offer inspection, repair, and CO2 decontamination services for turnout gear, a cleaning method widely used to remove contaminants while helping preserve garment performance. ... With the addition of the California location, LION now operates nine TotalCare facilities across the United States. ... The company serves fire departments nationwide through gear maintenance programs designed to help departments maintain compliance with NFPA requirements and extend the life of protective equipment. ... “We’re excited to expand TotalCare services into California,” said Mark Smith, CEO of LION Safety Solutions. “This acquisition will help us widen our reach and support even more fire departments across the country.” ... Care and Training Services ... In addition to gear cleaning and repair, LION TotalCare provides PPE rental programs for fire departments and training academies. ... The company also offers firefighter training solutions, including digital and live fire training programs, designed to help departments improve preparedness and safety. ... LION says the acquisition reinforces its commitment to supporting fire departments with comprehensive PPE care, maintenance, and training services across North America."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Diamond Chemical Acquires Nyco Products Co. | American Laundry News,americanlaundrynews.com (https://americanlaundrynews.com/authors/staff-writer),2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://americanlaundrynews.com/articles/diamond-chemical-acquires-nyco-products-co,"Diamond Chemical Acquires Nyco Products Co. | American Laundry News ... RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Diamond Chemical Co., based here, reports it has acquired Nyco Products Co., a cleaning chemicals manufacturer headquartered in Countryside, Illinois. ... “Nyco brings deep formulation expertise, a strong brand portfolio and a Midwest manufacturing footprint that perfectly complements our coastal operations,” says Diamond Chemical CEO Wesley Alves. “Together, we can offer our customers broader product availability and stronger national service.” ... Beyond the operational expansion, Diamond says the acquisition represents a “true union of two deeply aligned cultures.” ... “The sale of our business preserves our history and culture while ensuring that our customers continue to receive the same high level of quality, reliability, and service,” says Bob Stahurski, Nyco’s CEO. “I am confident that our customers, partners and legacy will continue to thrive under Diamond’s leadership.” ... Stahurski ... 40 years with his company. ... “For the past 40 years, Bob has been an exceptional leader and a dedicated steward of Nyco’s century-long legacy,” states Diamond. “He cultivated a culture defined by quality, reliability and deep loyalty to his customers. It is a massive responsibility to take over a business with that kind of history, and it is an honor that Bob has trusted Diamond to carry the torch forward.” ... The company adds that Stahurski will remain involved as an investor and adviser, ensuring a seamless transition and continuing to lend his expertise to the combined team."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,TR Capital Portfolio Company Pharmacity Raises Growth Capital from LeapFrog Investments - BusinessNewsAsia.com,www.businessnewsasia.com (Marie Jones),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.businessnewsasia.com/2026052852396381-tr-capital-portfolio-company-pharmacity-raises-growth-capital-from-leapfrog-investments/,"TR Capital Portfolio Company Pharmacity Raises Growth Capital from LeapFrog Investments ... # TR Capital Portfolio Company Pharmacity Raises Growth Capital from LeapFrog Investments ... Following a successful turnaround under the control of TR Capital, Vietnam’s leading modern retail pharmacy chain has reached full profitability and is entering its next phase of institutional growth. ... TR Capital, a leading secondary private equity investor, today announced that its portfolio company, Pharmacity, is raising growth capital from LeapFrog Investments, a global private equity firm focused on healthcare and financial services in emerging markets. The transaction marks an important milestone in Pharmacity’s development and reflects continued investor interest in Vietnam’s consumer healthcare sector. Under the leadership of Deepanshu Madan, Partner at TR Capital, who stepped in as CEO to lead the turnaround of the company, Pharmacity has delivered strong operating performance over the past two years, positioning the business for its next stage of growth. ... Founded in 2011, Pharmacity was among the first companies to scale the modern pharmacy retail model in Vietnam. Today, it is one of the country’s largest pharmacy chains, with a nationwide network of more than 1,100 stores across major urban centres as well as Tier II and Tier III cities. The company serves nearly 19 million loyal customers and offers a portfolio of more than 7,000 active products, supported by technology-enabled operations and a disciplined supply chain platform. ... The transaction follows a multi-year value creation journey under the stewardship of TR Capital and a sustained improvement in operating performance. Pharmacity achieved EBITDA profitability in the fourth quarter of 2025, and that momentum continued into the first quarter of 2026. The business has also improved unit economics and store selection discipline, with more recent store cohorts progressing toward EBITDA breakeven. ... In the first quarter of 2026, Pharmacity recorded more than 35% year-on-year revenue growth and more than 20% same-store sales growth. The company added 140 new stores in 2025 and plans to continue expanding its footprint over the coming years. ... In addition to its retail pharmacy operations, Pharmacity is expanding its healthcare offering through preventive health consultations, diagnostics, and pharmacy benefits management, with the objective of building a broader consumer healthcare platform. ... Paul Robine, Founder and CEO of TR Capital, said: “When TR Capital made its investment in Pharmacity, we saw a compelling opportunity to support the development of a modern, scaled pharmacy platform in Vietnam. Since then, we have undertaken a meaningful operational transformation, supported by stronger governance, sharper execution, and a clear focus on profitability. LeapFrog’s investment is an important endorsement of Pharmacity’s progress and positions the company well for its next phase of growth.” ... Deepanshu Madan, CEO of Pharmacity and Partner at TR Capital, said: “Our ambition is to be the most trusted pharmacy brand in Vietnam. Over the past two years, we have invested substantially in our people, systems, store standards, and customer proposition. Achieving profitability in the fourth quarter of 2025 was an important milestone for the business. With LeapFrog’s support, we look forward to expanding our reach, strengthening our service offering, and continuing to improve access to high-quality healthcare across Vietnam.” ... LeapFrog Investments brings relevant sector experience to Pharmacity’s next phase of development, drawing on its track record of investing in healthcare and essential services businesses across emerging markets. ... The transaction also underscores the increasing relevance of Vietnam’s consumer healthcare market within the broader Southeast Asian private equity landscape. ... TR Capital has ... Pharmacity is a pharmacy retail chain in Vietnam focused on improving access to quality healthcare products and pharmaceutical services nationwide. With more than 1,100 pharmacies and nearly 19 million loyalty customers, the company combines scale with standardized pharmacy practices, technology-enabled supply chain management, and medicine storage protocols."
