6. The business has also improved unit economics and store selection discipline, with more recent store cohorts progressing toward EBITDA breakeven. ... In the first quarter of 2026, Pharmacity recorded more than 35% year-on-year revenue growth and more than 20% same-store sales growth. The company added 140 new stores in 2025 and plans to continue expanding its footprint over the coming years. ... In addition to its retail pharmacy operations, Pharmacity is expanding its healthcare offering through preventive health consultations, diagnostics, and pharmacy benefits management, with the objective of building a broader consumer healthcare platform. ... Paul Robine, Founder and CEO of TR Capital, said: “When TR Capital made its investment in Pharmacity, we saw a compelling opportunity to support the development of a modern, scaled pharmacy platform in Vietnam. Since then, we have undertaken a meaningful operational transformation, supported by stronger governance, sharper execution, and a clear focus on profitability. LeapFrog’s investment is an important endorsement of Pharmacity’s progress and positions the company well for its next phase of growth.” ... Deepanshu Madan, CEO of Pharmacity and Partner at TR Capital, said: “Our ambition is to be the most trusted pharmacy brand in Vietnam. Over the past two years, we have invested substantially in our people, systems, store standards, and customer proposition. Achieving profitability in the fourth quarter of 2025 was an important milestone for the business. With LeapFrog’s support, we look forward to expanding our reach, strengthening our service offering, and continuing to improve access to high-quality healthcare across Vietnam.” ... LeapFrog Investments brings relevant sector experience to Pharmacity’s next phase of development, drawing on its track record of investing in healthcare and essential services businesses across emerging markets. ... The transaction also underscores the increasing relevance of Vietnam’s consumer healthcare market within the broader Southeast Asian private equity landscape. ... Capital is a secondary private equity ... , providing bespoke liquidity solutions through single-asset and portfolio transactions. The firm invests in businesses across the technology, next-generation consumer, and healthcare sectors in Asia and the US. ... in 20 ... TR Capital has ... , and has ... 0 secondary investments. The firm’s investor base includes sovereign wealth funds, pension funds, asset managers, entrepreneurs, and family offices ... integrates environmental, social, ... governance considerations throughout ... Responsible Investment Policy ... Pharmacity is a pharmacy retail chain in Vietnam focused on improving access to quality healthcare products and pharmaceutical services nationwide. With more than 1,100 pharmacies and nearly 19 million loyalty customers, the company combines scale with standardized pharmacy practices, technology-enabled supply chain management, and medicine storage protocols."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Oxidium Technologies acquires Aseptrol line from BASF,delawarebusinesstimes.com (Katie Tabeling),2026-05-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://delawarebusinesstimes.com/news/oxidium-acquires-aseptrol-basf/,"Oxidium Technologies acquires Aseptrol line from BASF ... # Oxidium Technologies acquires Aseptrol line from BASF ... WILMINGTON — A biosafety product manufacturer that has been run by one family for 40 years has started a new business now that it bought a key disinfection product line. ... Quip Laboratories of North Wilmington established Oxidium Technologies as a new brand earlier this year after it completed a deal to buy the Aseptrol line from BASF Corp., the largest chemical producer in the world. ... Terms of the deal were not disclosed. WSFS was the banking partner of record for the transaction. ... The Aseptrol product line was developed by Engelhard Corporation, which was later acquired by German chemical manufacturer BASF for U.S. $5 billion. Quip Laboratories has been selling Aseptrol tablets for about 20 years, or half as long as the company’s lifespan, and was its largest customer. ... The family was in negotiations with BASF for a year before closing the deal – and with it created Oxidium Technologies to sell the Aseptrol product line to other distributors. ... Included in the deal are the patents for Aseptrol, the 15 U.S. Environmental Protection Agency registrations, as well as established manufacturing processes in Europe. All other distributor relationships transferred to BASF. With the acquisition, the family business aims to broaden the product line. ... While the family declined to provide exact figures on how Oxidium Technologies’ business stands two months after the deal, Anthony Hidell said the company was “in a really healthy spot.” ... “But we’re viewing it as the floor. We felt this acquisition made a tremendous amount of sense for us and the family of businesses, because of the true upside growth potential,” he said. ... The family believes that Oxidium Technologies can build a book of business in the Mid-Atlantic region, as Aseptrol can be flown into the Philadelphia International Airport and then shipped by freight from anywhere on the East Coast – or potentially through the ports overseas. Nick Hidell also spent about 16 years in California developing the business on the West Coast. ... Oxidium Technologies’ target markets are water purification, animal driving water and medical device sterilization, which is a rapidly growing market for the family business."
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Graycliff Announces Diamond Chemical's Acquisition of Nyco Products — Graycliff Partners,graycliffpartners.com,2026-05-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://graycliffpartners.com/news/diamond-acquires-nyco,"Graycliff Announces Diamond Chemical's Acquisition of Nyco Products — Graycliff Partners ... Graycliff Partners LP announced today that its portfolio company, Diamond Chemical Company, LLC (""Diamond""), a manufacturer of commercial and institutional soaps, detergents and warewash products, has acquired Nyco Products Company (""Nyco""), creating one of the leading independent providers of sanitization chemicals in the U.S. ... Nyco, based in Countryside, IL, manufactures specialty cleaning chemicals, including cleaners, disinfectants, sanitizers, and floor care products, for distributors serving facility maintenance, janitorial, food processing, healthcare, and education end markets. Founded in 1920, Nyco offers more than 450 stock and custom formulations, nationally -recognized brands, and its Building Better Brands® private chemical branding program. ... ""This combination is a transformative step for Diamond,"" said Wesley Alves, CEO of Diamond. ""Nyco brings deep formulation expertise, a strong brand portfolio, and a Midwest manufacturing footprint that complements our coastal operations. Together, we can offer customers and distributors broader product availability and stronger national service.” ... With over 200 years of combined industry experience, Diamond and Nyco look forward to leveraging their complementary product lines and coast-to-coast manufacturing footprint to drive continued growth. ""Diamond and Nyco are exceptional businesses with deeply loyal customer bases built over generations,"" said Matt Smith, Principal at Graycliff. ""We're excited that the Nyco team is joining Diamond and look forward to supporting the team and the combined organization in this next phase of growth."""
TRICON DRY CHEMICALS,,,,Exa,Tricon Strengthens Presence in Africa with Full Acquisition of West African International Group - West African Group,westafricangroup.co.za (Natalie Conde),2026-05-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://westafricangroup.co.za/2026/05/14/tricon-strengthens-presence-in-africa-with-full-acquisition-of-west-african-international-group/,"Tricon Strengthens Presence in Africa with Full Acquisition of West African International Group - West African Group ... West African International Group ... Houston, Texas – Tricon, a global leader in the distribution of plastics and chemicals, has, through its wholly owned South African subsidiary, completed the full acquisition of West African International Proprietary Limited (WAG) from enX Group, building on its initial strategic investment in March 2025. ... “This acquisition reflects our confidence in both the African market and in WAG’s strong position within it,” said Ignacio Torras, Tricon President & CEO. “Over the past year, our partnership has shown the value of combining WAG’s regional expertise with Tricon’s global capabilities. Bringing WAG fully into Tricon allows us to move faster, invest further, and deliver even greater value to our business partners in the region.” ... Headquartered in Durban with a strong presence in Johannesburg and Cape Town, WAG is a leading distributor of plastics, rubber, fillers, and rubber chemicals across Southern Africa. Since Tricon’s initial investment, the companies have worked closely to strengthen supply chain operations, expand product access, and enhance service capabilities in key markets. ... WAG will continue to operate under its established name and leadership team, maintaining the same high level of service. With full integration, Tricon and WAG will further scale their combined distribution network, deepen customer and supplier relationships, and expand technical and logistics support across the continent. ... Grant Rosettenstein, WAG CEO, added: “Our partnership with Tricon has delivered meaningful progress for WAG and our customers. This next step strengthens our ability to grow and, with the support of our dedicated local team, continues to deliver value to our customers and suppliers as part of Tricon’s global platform.” ... About Tricon With 30 years in business, ... on is an industry leader in ... distribution and trade of basic chemicals, polymers, and raw materials. Our purpose is to efficiently and sustainably connect the world with essential goods. We do that by providing logistics, financing, risk management, sustainability, market intelligence, distribution, and technical support to thousands of business partners in over 120 countries. ... We originate and market products globally, meeting specific location, quality, timing, and volume requirements, and moved more than 23.2 million metric tons of product in 2025. Our diverse, global workforce is committed to providing our clients and suppliers with streamlined services, so they can focus on their core business."
