GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Gains 8.19%: 4 Key Technical and Fin...,www.marketsmojo.com,2026-08-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketsmojo.com/news/stocks-in-action/gandhar-oil-refinery-gains-819-4-key-technical-and-financial-factors-driving-the-rally-4142987,"# Gandhar Oil Refinery Gains ... .19%: 4 Key Technical and Financial Factors Driving the Rally Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd delivered a strong weekly performance, rising 8.19% from ₹224.15 to ₹242.50 between 3 and 7 August 2026, significantly outpacing the Sensex’s 1.13% gain over the same period. The stock’s price action was marked by notable volatility and shifting technical momentum, reflecting a complex interplay of robust financial results, rating adjustments, and evolving market sentiment. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery began the week on a positive note, closing at ₹231.25, a 3.17% increase from the previous Friday’s close of ₹224.15. This outpaced the Sensex’s 0.82% gain to 36,985.17. The stock’s volume of 165,798 shares indicated healthy investor interest. The positive start was supported by the company’s strong fundamentals and anticipation of upcoming financial disclosures. ... On 4 August, Gandhar Oil Refinery’s mojo grade was downgraded from Strong Buy to Buy by MarketsMOJO, reflecting a more cautious stance despite the company’s robust financials. The stock closed at ₹236.30, up 2.18%, even as the Sensex declined slightly by 0.14%. The downgrade was driven by a shift in technical momentum from bullish to mildly bullish, with mixed signals from MACD, RSI, and other indicators. The company’s exceptional net profit growth of 455.71% in Q1 2026 and a 51.52% increase in net sales over six months underpinned the positive sentiment, but technical caution tempered enthusiasm. ... The stock experienced a pullback on 5 August, closing at ₹231.75, down 1.93% from the previous day’s close. This contrasted with the Sensex’s 0.38% gain to 37,074.66. The decline reflected the mixed technical signals highlighted by MarketsMOJO’s analysis: weekly MACD remained bullish but monthly MACD and RSI turned mildly bearish, indicating weakening longer-term momentum. The Know Sure Thing (KST) indicator was bearish weekly, and On-Balance Volume (OBV) showed no clear trend, suggesting a lack of volume confirmation for price moves. Despite the dip, the stock maintained a strong relative performance year-to-date and over the past year. ... On 6 August, Gandhar Oil Refinery rebounded sharply, closing at ₹243.40, a 5.03% increase. This surge outperformed the Sensex’s 0.28% gain to 37,177.57. The technical trend upgraded from mildly bullish to bullish, supported by bullish daily moving averages and expanding Bollinger Bands on weekly and monthly charts. The stock traded within a relatively tight intraday range, signalling consolidation ahead of potential further gains. While the monthly MACD remained mildly bearish, the weekly MACD and daily indicators suggested strengthening upward momentum. The micro-cap stock’s strong relative returns continued to attract attention despite inherent volatility. ... The week concluded with a slight decline to ₹242.50, down 0.37% from the previous close. The Sensex also fell 0.21% to 37,099.57. Despite the minor pullback, Gandhar Oil Refinery’s technical momentum shifted from bullish to mildly bullish. Weekly MACD remained positive, but monthly MACD and RSI continued to signal caution. Bollinger Bands stayed bullish, and daily moving averages supported the short-term uptrend. The Know Sure Thing (KST) indicator was bearish weekly, and Dow Theory showed no clear trend, reflecting some indecision. The stock’s strong year-to-date return of 57.69% versus the Sensex’s 7.35% decline underscored its resilience amid mixed technical signals. ... Robust Financial Performance: Gandhar Oil Refinery’s exceptional net profit growth of 455.71% in Q1 2026 and 51.52% increase in net sales over six months underpin the stock’s strong fundamentals. The company’s conservative debt-to-equity ratio of 0.09 and healthy ROCE of 13.3% further reinforce financial strength. ... Mixed Technical Signals: The week saw a transition from bullish to mildly bullish technical momentum. While daily moving averages and weekly MACD supported short-term gains, monthly MACD and RSI indicated caution, suggesting potential consolidation or correction risks ahead. ... Strong Relative Performance: The stock outperformed the Sensex significantly, gaining 8.19% versus the index’s 1.13% rise. Year-to-date returns of 57.69% and one-year gains of 49.69% highlight sustained outperformance in a volatile market. ... Rating Adjustment Reflects Balanced View: The downgrade from Strong Buy to Buy by MarketsMOJO reflects a nuanced reassessment balancing strong fundamentals against emerging technical caution, advising measured optimism. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd demonstrated impressive price appreciation and financial resilience during the week of 3 to 7 August 2026, significantly outperforming the Sensex. The company’s strong earnings growth and conservative capital structure provide a solid foundation amid a micro-cap environment characterised by volatility. However, the mixed technical momentum—shifting from bullish to mildly bullish—signals the need for vigilance. Investors should monitor key technical indicators and volume trends closely to navigate potential near-term fluctuations. The MarketsMOJO rating downgrade to Buy encapsulates this balanced outlook, recognising both the stock’s growth potential and the caution warranted by evolving technical signals."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Resumes Silvassa Plant Operations After Flood Disruption,scanx.trade (Dhan),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://scanx.trade/stock-market-news/companies/gandhar-oil-refinery-resumes-operations-at-silvassa-plant-following-flood-disruption/47378919,"Plant Operations After ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd has resumed operations at its Silvassa facility following disruption caused by unprecedented heavy rainfall and flood-like conditions, as disclosed on August 04, 2026. The company completed necessary cleaning, inspection, repair, and remedial measures, and is closely monitoring the situation for full normalisation. Damage assessment is ongoing, with the incident covered under an existing insurance policy. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery(India) Ltd has resumed operations at its manufacturing facility located in Silvassa, Dadra and Nagar Haveli, U.T. – 396230, following a period of disruption caused by unprecedented heavy rainfall and flood-like conditions. The company made this disclosure to the stock exchanges on August 04, 2026, in continuation of its earlier intimation dated July 24, 2026, filed pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. ... The company has undertaken a series of measures to restore normal functioning at the Silvassa facility. According to the regulatory filing, necessary cleaning, inspection, repair, and remedial measures have been completed to ensure safe and smooth functioning of the plant. The company stated it is closely monitoring the situation to achieve full normalisation of operations. ... | Parameter: | Details | | --- | --- | | Facility Location: | Silvassa, Dadra and Nagar Haveli, U.T. – 396230 | | Nature of Disruption: | Unprecedented heavy rainfall and flood-like conditions | | Operational Status: | Operations resumed | | Loss/Damage Assessment: | Currently being assessed | | Insurance Coverage: | Available; incident intimated to insurance company | | Restoration Steps: | Cleaning, inspection, repair, and remedial measures completed | ... Gandhar Oil Refinery has confirmed that the incident is covered under its existing insurance policy and has been duly intimated to the insurance company. The quantum of loss or damage, if any, arising from the flood-like conditions is currently under evaluation. The company has not disclosed any specific financial impact at this stage, as the assessment remains ongoing. ... The filing was submitted in compliance with the SEBI circular bearing reference number HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFD-POD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026, which mandates listed entities to disclose disruptions to operations caused by natural calamities, force majeure events, or similar occurrences. The disclosure was signed by Binal Khosla, Company Secretary and Compliance Officer (Mem. No.: A29802), on August 04, 2026. ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery posts record ₹206 crore Q1FY27 profit on margin surge ... Gandhar Oil Refinery achieved record Q1 FY27 profits of ₹206 crore, driven by exceptional margin expansions and strong export growth amid geopolitical supply disruptions. The company declared an interim dividend and maintains a debt-free stand-alone balance sheet. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery delivered its strongest financial performance in company history during the quarter ended June 30, 2026 (Q1 FY27), reporting a record profit after tax (PAT) of ₹206 crore. This represents a 688% year-on-year increase from ₹26 crore in Q1 FY26 and exceeds the total profit generated in the entire previous fiscal year. The exceptional results were driven by a sharp expansion in gross margin spreads to ₹28,145 per kilolitre and a 92% year-on-year rise in consolidated revenue to ₹1,732 crore. Management attributed the outperformance to agile sourcing strategies amid geopolitical disruptions in the Middle East, disciplined inventory management, and robust demand across personal care and industrial segments. The Board has declared an interim dividend of 100% of the face value of shares. ... The earnings call transcript, released on July 28, 2026, pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI Listing Regulations, provided detailed insights into the operational drivers. Joint Managing Director Aslesh Parekh and Chief Financial Officer Indrajit Bhattacharyya highlighted that while the operating environment was challenging due to Strait of Hormuz tensions and supply chain volatility, the company’s diversified sourcing network allowed it to capitalize on elevated realizations. The disclosure ensures transparency regarding the firm’s initial performance in the new fiscal year, allowing investors to review strategic updates directly from leadership. ... | Metric | Q1 FY27 | Q1 FY26 | YoY Change | Q4 FY26 | QoQ Change | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Revenue | ₹1,732 crore | ₹903 crore | +92% | ₹1,093 crore | +58% | | EBITDA | ₹281 crore | ₹46 crore | +512% | ₹64 crore | +342% | | PAT | ₹206 crore | ₹26 crore | +688% | ₹37 crore | +456% | | EBITDA Margin | 16.20% | 5.1% | N/A | N/A | N/A | | Sales Volume | ~131,000 KL | ~121,000 KL | +8% | N/A | N/A | ... Management noted that gross margin spreads expanded significantly from approximately ₹8,274 per kilolitre in Q1 FY26 to ₹28,145 per kilolitre in Q1 FY27. This improvement was supported by favorable market conditions, disciplined sourcing, and effective inventory management. CFO Indrajit Bhattacharyya emphasized that these spreads should be viewed in the context of exceptional market conditions but expressed confidence that margins would remain at stellar levels for the next one to two quarters. ... The Personal Care, Healthcare, and Performance Oil (PHPO) segment remained the primary growth engine, registering an 18% year-on-year increase. This segment accounted for over 50% of total sales. The Process and Insulating Oil (PIO) business also performed robustly, growing 28% year-on-year, driven by healthy demand from transformer, power, and rubber manufacturers. Exports contributed approximately 51% of consolidated revenue, up from 37% in the previous year, with export volumes increasing by 54% year-on-year. The company operates a fungible production capacity across its three plants, which were utilized at 97% on a two-shift basis during the quarter. ... Geopolitical tensions in the Middle East led to supply constraints and delayed shipments from key suppliers like Saudi Aramco. However, Gandhar Oil mitigated these risks by diversifying sourcing to South Korea and domestic producers. The subsidiary, Texol, located in the Hamriyah Free Zone, Sharjah, faced temporary operational impacts due to regional supply disruptions but maintained business continuity through regional sourcing agility. ... The divergence between volume growth (8% YoY) and revenue growth (92% YoY) underscores that the primary driver of this quarter’s performance was price realization rather than volume expansion. With EBITDA margins expanding from 5.1% to 16.2%, the company successfully passed on higher input costs to customers while benefiting from supply-side constraints in the global base oil market. The debt-free stand-alone balance sheet, combined with strong cash generation, provides significant financial flexibility. Management indicated that internal accruals would support future capital expenditure, including potential capacity expansions, without relying heavily on external term lending. The declaration of an interim dividend signals confidence in sustained cash flows despite the volatile operating environment. ... ## More News on Gandhar Oil Refinery ... Gandhar Oil sets July 31 record date for ₹2 interim dividend payout 9 days ago ... Gandhar Oil Refinery assesses flood damage at Silvassa plant 9 days ago ... Gandhar Oil Refinery seeks postal ballot nod for director appointments Jul 17, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery JMD to appear on NDTV Profit on July 14 Jul 14, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery hosts analyst plant visit on June 30 Jun 24, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery promoter raises stake to 28.74% Jun 18, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil promoter confirms no encumbrances in FY26 Jun 16, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery to attend investor meet on June 11 Jun 09, 2026"
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Pakistan’s Ghandhara Tyre approved for exports to six Gulf countries - Business & Finance - Business Recorder,www.brecorder.com (BR Web Desk),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.brecorder.com/news/40433054,"Pakistan’s Ghandhara Tyre approved for exports to six Gulf countries - Business & Finance - Business Recorder ... # Pakistan’s Ghandhara Tyre approved for exports to six Gulf countries ... - Certification enables the company to export to countries, namely Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia and UAE Published August 3, 2026 Updated August 3, 2026 10:35am By BR Web Desk ... Ghandhara Tyre & Rubber Company Limited (GTYR) has received Gulf Standardisation Organisation (GSO) certification, enabling the company to export its tyre products to six Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) countries. ... The listed company disclosed the development in a notice to the Pakistan Stock Exchange (PSX) on Monday. ... “We are pleased to inform our valued shareholders that GTR Tyres has been officially approved and certified by the Gulf Standardization Organization (GSO),” the notice read. ... The tyre maker said that the achievement enables the company to export its tyre products to GSO member countries, namely Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates. ... Pakistan’s Ghandhara Tyre clears key ... regulatory requirement for exports ... “This development marks an important milestone for the company and reflects its ongoing commitment to expanding its export portfolio, exploring new international markets, and strengthening its position in the global tyre industry,” it added. ... The company said it remains focused on enhancing its international presence and delivering high-quality products in compliance with global standards. ... The company’s main business is the manufacturing and trading of tyres and tubes for automobiles and motorcycles. ... GTYR is currently diversifying its product portfolio by introducing new tyre sizes for SUV/crossover segments and aiming to increase export sales."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Societe Generale pares 0.53% stake in Gandhar Oil Refinery,www.moneycontrol.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/markets/societe-generale-pares-0-53-stake-in-gandhar-oil-refinery-13986189.html,"Societe Generale pares 0.53% stake in Gandhar Oil Refinery ... # Societe Generale pares 0.53% stake in Gandhar Oil Refinery ... This was out of total 1.59 percent stake bought by Societe Generale in Gandhar Oil Refinery in later part of last week. ... Bulk deals on July 28, 2026 ... - Societe Generale pares 0.53% stake in Gandhar Oil Refinery - Pine Oak Global Fund buys additional 0.98% stake in Aqylon Nexus - Nova Global Opportunities Fund picks up 0.67% stake in Asian Granito India ... European lender Societe Generale pared a 0.53 percent stake in white oils maker Gandhar Oil Refinery India through open market transactions on July 28. ... According to bulk deals data, the bank sold 5.22 lakh shares, representing 0.53 percent of the company's equity, for Rs 12.62 crore at an average price of Rs 241.88 per share. ... The sale comes days after Societe Generale accumulated a 1.59 percent stake in the company. It had bought 6.84 lakh shares (0.7 percent stake) at Rs 280.93 per share on July 23 and another 8.53 lakh shares (0.89 percent stake) at Rs 288.97 per share on July 24, following the company's strong June quarter earnings. ... Based on the transaction prices, Societe Generale sold the latest tranche at a lower price than its acquisition cost. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery India shares have corrected sharply after hitting a record high of Rs 303.15 last Friday. The stock has declined 21.5 percent from that peak. It fell 3.07 percent on Tuesday to close at Rs 237.93, after tumbling 13.1 percent in the previous session. The sharp rally-triggered gap created on July 23 has now been filled. ... Meanwhile, Axis Bank sold 34.33 lakh units of Raajmarg Infra Investment Trust at Rs 116.5 per unit in a transaction worth Rs 40 crore.In another bulk deal, Mauritius-based arbitrage fund Pine Oak Global Fund acquired an additional 25 lakh shares, or 0.98 percent stake, in technology company Aqylon Nexus,(formerly Sri Adhikari Brothers Television Network) for Rs 6.29 crore at Rs 25.19 per share. ... Asian Granito India also remained in focus, with its shares rising 7.86 percent to Rs 57.62 amid heavy volumes on the NSE. Nova Global Opportunities Fund PCC – Touchstone bought 20 lakh shares, representing 0.67 percent equity, at Rs 60 per share in a deal worth Rs 12 crore."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Silvassa Plant Disrupted by Floods After Record 698% Net Profit Increase in Q1 FY27,tradebrains.in (Pranab Mohanty),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://tradebrains.in/gandhar-oil-silvassa-plant-disrupted-by-floods-after-record-698-net-profit-increase-in-q1-fy27/,"Gandhar Oil Silvassa Plant Disrupted by Floods After Record 698% Net Profit Increase in Q1 FY27 ... # Gandhar Oil Silvassa Plant Disrupted by Floods After Record 698% Net Profit Increase in Q1 FY27 ... Synopsis: Gandhar Oil Refinery informed exchanges that unprecedented heavy rainfall has caused flood-like conditions at its Silvassa manufacturing plant, just a day after the Company reported a record 689% jump in Q1 FY27 consolidated net profit. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited informed the BSE and NSE on July 24, 2026, that its manufacturing plant at Silvassa, Dadra & Nagar Haveli, has been affected by flood-like conditions following unprecedented heavy rainfall in the region over the preceding 48 hours. ... The Company said the extremely heavy rainfall caused severe waterlogging and flooding across several parts of Silvassa, impacting the facility identified as Unit No. 2, located at Survey No. 678/1/3, Village Naroli, within the Union Territory. ... Management stated it is currently assessing the impact of this natural calamity on the Company’s assets, operations and production, with the extent of damage still being evaluated and appropriate measures being taken to restore normal operations at the earliest opportunity. ... The Company confirmed it carries adequate insurance coverage and has already intimated the incident to its insurer, while committing to keep stock exchanges informed of any material developments in accordance with SEBI Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements Regulations. ... The flooding at Gandhar Oil’s Silvassa manufacturing facility comes immediately after the company reported its strongest-ever quarterly performance, making the duration of the disruption an important factor. Although the company has adequate insurance coverage, any prolonged shutdown could temporarily affect production, deliveries and working capital. ... Silvassa is one of Gandhar Oil’s three integrated manufacturing facilities and houses its DSIR-recognised R&D centre. While the company also operates plants in Taloja and the UAE with a combined installed capacity of 5.97 lakh kilolitres, certain specialised products and manufacturing processes may remain plant-specific. ... The disruption follows a record Q1 FY27, where consolidated revenue surged 91.8% YoY to Rs. 1,731.9 crore, EBITDA jumped 512.1% to Rs. 281.3 crore, and net profit rose 689.2% to Rs. 205.9 crore. EBITDA margins also expanded significantly to 16.2% from 5.1% a year earlier. ... The timing is particularly significant because exports have become a major growth driver. Export revenue nearly tripled to Rs. 882 crore in Q1 FY27 from Rs. 337 crore a year earlier, contributing 51% of consolidated revenue. Any disruption in fulfilling export commitments could temporarily weigh on future sales growth. ... Despite the operational risk, Gandhar Oil’s financial position provides some resilience. The company reported a debt-to-equity ratio of 0.23, Rs. 128 crore in operating cash flow during FY26 and a current ratio of 2.61, supporting restoration efforts. Investors will now watch the production impact, insurance recovery and timeline for resuming normal operations. ... Manufacturers with concentrated production in flood-prone industrial zones such as Dadra & Nagar Haveli face recurring monsoon-related operational risk, making diversified manufacturing footprints and comprehensive insurance coverage important structural safeguards, both of which the Company has signalled it possesses in this disclosure. ... Given the strength of the preceding quarter’s export-led growth and margin expansion, the Company’s ability to manage this disruption without material earnings impact would reinforce confidence in its operational resilience, while any prolonged shutdown at the Silvassa unit would need to be weighed against the growth trajectory the stock has just re-rated on. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is a Mumbai-headquartered manufacturer of white oils, specialty petroleum products, automotive and industrial oils, transformer oils, and rubber processing oils, serving pharmaceutical, healthcare, automotive and industrial end markets domestically and globally. Its products carry FDA, ISO, Kosher, BIS and Halal certifications, with international operations supported through subsidiary Texol Lubritech FZC."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd (NSE:GANDHAR) Q1 2027 Earnings Call Highlights: Record Profit ...,"ca.finance.yahoo.com (GuruFocus News Sat, July 25, 2026 at 4:00 a.m. GMT+3 4 min read)",2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/gandhar-oil-refinery-india-ltd-010052974.html,"Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd (NSE:GANDHAR) Q1 2027 Earnings Call Highlights: Record Profit ... ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd (NSE:GANDHAR) Q1 2027 Earnings Call Highlights: Record Profit ... ... Revenue: INR1,732 crores, up 92% year-on-year. ... Sales Volume: Approximately 131,000 kiloliters, reflecting an 8% year-on-year growth. ... EBITDA: INR281 crores, up 512% year-on-year. ... EBITDA Margin: Expanded to 16.20% from 5.1% in Q1 FY26. ... Profit After Tax: INR206 crores, representing a 6.88% year-on-year growth. ... Gross Margin Spread: INR28,145 per kiloliter, significantly above historical levels. ... Export Growth: Export volumes increased by 54% year-on-year, contributing 51% of consolidated revenue. ... Interim Dividend: Declared at 100% of the face value of shares. ... Release Date: July 23 ... 20 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd (NSE:GANDHAR) reported the highest quarterly profit in the company's history, demonstrating strong financial performance. ... The company achieved a 92% year-on-year increase in consolidated revenue, reaching INR1,731.9 crores. ... Export business recorded a robust 54% year-on-year growth, contributing significantly to the company's revenue. ... The PHPO segment, a primary growth engine, registered an 18% year-on-year growth, driven by sustained demand from personal care, healthcare, and pharmaceutical sectors. ... The company declared an interim dividend of 100% of the face value of its shares, reflecting strong cash generation and financial flexibility. ... The operating environment was challenging due to geopolitical tensions in the Middle East, affecting raw material availability and pricing. ... There were intermittent disruptions across global supply chains, leading to elevated freight and insurance costs. ... Operations at the subsidiary, Textol, were temporarily impacted by regional supply constraints and vessel movement disruptions. ... The company faces uncertainties in maintaining the exceptional margin levels achieved this quarter due to volatile market conditions. ... There is a risk of potential degrowth in subsequent quarters if the exceptional market conditions do not persist. ... Q: Congratulations on the strong results. Could you break down the margin expansion between product mix and inventory gains? How do you see EBITDA margins for the year? A: We don't carry significant inventory to attribute gains to it. The margin expansion is mainly due to higher selling prices. We are hopeful that margins will remain at current levels throughout the year. The exceptional market conditions and efficient sourcing contributed to this quarter's performance. ... Q: How do you foresee revenue growth for the year? What volume growth are you targeting? A: Historically, we've achieved volume growth of 8% to 11%. We expect similar growth this year. Revenue growth will be driven by both volume and price increases. ... Q: Export performance has been strong. What is the outlook for exports this year? A: We export to over 100 countries and maintain strong relationships with overseas customers. We expect export revenue to remain at similar levels in the coming quarters. ... Q: Can you elaborate on the impact of geopolitical tensions on your sourcing strategy? A: The geopolitical situation, particularly in the Middle East, led to some supply disruptions. We adjusted our sourcing strategy by buying more from domestic producers and South Korea, which helped us maintain supply and expand margins. ... Q: What is the outlook for the PHPO segment, and are there any changes expected in the segmental mix? A: The PHPO segment remains a key growth driver, supported by demand from personal care and healthcare sectors. We expect the current segmental mix to continue, with PHPO and PIO being the primary contributors. ... Q: How do you plan to manage capital allocation between dividends and future capacity expansion? A: The strong performance allows us to allocate capital for dividends and potential CapEx. We have declared an interim dividend and have sufficient internal accruals to fund future expansions without additional borrowing. ... Q: What are your plans for entering new geographies like South Africa? A: The strategy for South Africa is being developed, and more clarity will emerge in the next few quarters. It is premature to provide specific details at this time. ... Q: Can you provide insights into the competitive landscape in the specialty oils market? A: The industry is expected to grow at a 5% CAGR globally. With our strong balance sheet, sourcing capabilities, and customer relationships, we are well-positioned to capitalize on this growth and maintain a competitive advantage."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Evaluates Silvassa Plant Flood Damage Caused By Heavy Rain,www.sahi.com,2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sahi.com/news/gandhar-oil-refinery-evaluates-silvassa-plant-flood-damage-caused-by-heavy-rain-3929-PE1_COR,"har Oil Refinery ... Plant Flood Damage Caused By Heavy Rain ... Gandhar Oil Refinery Evaluates Silvassa Plant Flood Damage Caused By Heavy Rain ... - **Rain Disruption:** Extremely heavy rain over 48 hours has flooded Gandhar Oil's Silvassa manufacturing plant. - **Evaluation Underway:** Operations and asset impacts are being assessed; recovery measures have commenced to restore normalcy. - **Risk Mitigation:** The plant's operations and assets are protected by adequate insurance coverage. - **Strong Financial Base:** This operational hurdle comes immediately after the company reported its highest-ever quarterly net profit of ₹206 crore in Q1 FY27. ... Market snapshot: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited has reported flood-like conditions at its manufacturing facility in Silvassa, Dadra & Nagar Haveli, due to unprecedented heavy rainfall over a 48-hour period. The company is actively assessing the impact of this natural calamity on its assets, operations, and production. To mitigate financial exposure, Gandhar Oil has confirmed that the facility maintains adequate insurance coverage. ... - The company recorded a consolidated revenue of ₹1,732 crore for the first quarter of FY27, registering a growth of 92% year-on-year. - Consolidated net profit (PAT) surged 633% year-on-year to reach a record high of ₹206 crore in Q1 FY27, up from ₹26 crore in Q1 FY26. - In May 2026, the company finalized the acquisition of a 18,353 square meter land parcel adjoining its Silvassa factory for ₹22.78 crore. ... - The Silvassa facility, which is a key contributor to the company's manufacturing capability, is temporarily dealing with waterlogging and flood-like conditions instead of operating at normal capacity. - The management is now evaluating potential losses to assets and production schedules, shifting focus to recovery and insurance claims process. ... - Unprecedented heavy rainfall over 48 hours has created flood-like conditions at Gandhar Oil's Silvassa manufacturing plant. - Operational and production schedules at the Silvassa plant are temporarily disrupted while damage assessment is carried out. - The financial impact is expected to be substantially mitigated as the company maintains adequate insurance coverage for its assets. - Strong Q1 FY27 earnings, with a net profit of ₹206 crore, provide a strong buffer to absorb near-term operational challenges. ... The temporary disruption at the Silvassa plant represents a short-term operational bottleneck for Gandhar Oil Refinery. However, the business is backed by a highly robust balance sheet and stellar Q1 FY27 financial results, where net profits expanded over six-fold. Since the company operates two other major facilities in Taloja and Sharjah, the geographic diversification of its manufacturing base should help cushion the overall production volume impact. Furthermore, the presence of comprehensive insurance coverage ensures that the capital value of assets remains protected. ... While the news of flood disruption may cause minor near-term volatility or pressure on the stock price, the overall impact is expected to be contained. Investors are likely to focus on the speed of operational recovery and the efficiency of the insurance settlement process. The company's strong structural growth story, highlighted by its leadership in the white-oil segment and recent record quarterly results, remains intact. ... The flood at the Silvassa plant presents a near-term operational risk, but is balanced by adequate insurance cover and a stellar Q1 FY27 performance featuring a ₹206 crore PAT. ... and insurance claims filed by the ... Movement in base ... prices which influences overall margins ... Gandhar Oil Refinery is the largest manufacturer of white oils in India and ranks among the top five global players. It operates three facilities in Taloja, Silvassa, and Sharjah, with a combined annual capacity of 5,97,403 KL. The specialty oil and chemicals industry is highly dependent on continuous manufacturing operations and efficient raw material sourcing. While local monsoonal disruptions are common in western India during July, companies with diversified plant locations and strong working capital are better positioned to handle these logistics and manufacturing shocks. ... - Extended Production Shutdown: If waterlogging persists, it could delay the resumption of operations, leading to temporary supply chain disruptions for white oil and specialty lubricants. - Logistics and Supply Bottlenecks: Localized flooding in the Dadra & Nagar Haveli region could impede the movement of raw materials (like base oil) and finished products. - Uncompensated Losses: While the company has adequate insurance, some indirect costs or business interruption losses might not be fully covered. ... On July 22, 2026, Gandhar Oil Refinery announced its Q1 FY27 results, reporting its highest-ever quarterly net profit of ₹206 crore, up 633% year-on-year, on a revenue of ₹1,732 crore. In May 2026, the company completed the acquisition of a 18,353 square meter land parcel adjoining its Silvassa plant for ₹22.78 crore to support future expansion. Additionally, senior management changes occurred in May 2026 with the resignation of the Senior Vice President of Manufacturing at the Silvassa Plant. ... The localized flooding at Silvassa is an operational test for Gandhar Oil, but its strong financial health, strategic insurance backstops, and multi-location operational footprint are robust structural defenses. Long-term investors are likely to view this as a transitory event rather than a threat to the company's secular growth trajectory."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Assesses Impact on Operations Following Severe Flooding at Silvassa Plant,investoomarket.com,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://investoomarket.com/news/gandhar-oil-refinery-assesses-impact-on-operations-following-severe-flooding-at-silvassa-plant.45483/,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Assesses Impact on Operations Following Severe Flooding at Silvassa Plant ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery Assesses Impact on Operations Following Severe Flooding at Silvassa Plant ... ## Gandhar Oil Refinery Assesses Impact on Operations Following Severe Flooding at Silvassa Plant​ ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd is currently assessing the operational and asset impact of a natural calamity affecting its manufacturing plant located in Silvassa, Dadra & Nagar Haveli, U.T. The company confirmed that unprecedented heavy rainfall over the past 48 hours led to severe waterlogging and flooding across various parts of the Silvassa area. The company has initiated comprehensive steps to evaluate the extent of the damage caused by the flood-like conditions on its assets, operations, and production capabilities. Appropriate measures are being taken to restore normal functioning at the earliest opportunity. Regarding mitigation and exposure, Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd stated that it holds adequate insurance coverage for the incident, and this matter has been intimated to the relevant insurance company. The specific unit affected is Unit No. 2, located at Plot No. 2, Survey No. 678/1/3, Village Naroli, Silvassa (D & N H)- 396230, U.T. The details regarding the impact assessment are as follows: ... | Particulars | Details | | --- | --- | | Expected quantum of loss/damage caused | The Company is assessing the impact of this natural calamity, if any, on the Company's assets, operations, and production. | | Whether loss/damage covered by insurance or not including amount | The Company has adequate insurance coverage and the incident has been intimated to the insurance company. | ... | Estimated impact on the production/operations in case of strikes/lock outs | The Company is currently assessing the impact on production/operations. | ... | Factory/Unit where the strike/lock out takes place including reasons for such strike | Unit No. 2, Plot No. 2, Survey No. 678/1/3, Village Naroli, Silvassa (D & N H)- 396230, U.T. | ... ### GANDHAR Stock Price Movement​ ... Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited slipped on Friday, shedding 0.46% to settle at ₹282.46 after trading activity that included a volume of 35.87 million shares. The stock's performance was notable as it had previously tested its 52-week high mark at ₹303.17 earlier in the year. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery Announces Resignation of Senior Vice President at Silvassa Plant ... - May 11, 2026"
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Shares Jump To 20% Upper Circuit After Robust Q1 Results,www.ndtvprofit.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ndtvprofit.com/markets/gandhar-oil-shares-jump-to-20-upper-circuit-after-robust-q1-results-11809579,"![Download App ... ](https://www.ndtvprofit.com/estatic/images/profit/download- ... -scanner.png ... Scan to Download Advertisement # Gandhar Oil Shares Jump To 20% Upper Circuit After Robust Q1 Results ## Management said the company has historically delivered 8-11% volume growth and expects to sustain that trajectory going forward. Read Time: 2 mins [ ... Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) hit the 20% upper circuit on July 23 after the manufacturer of specialty oils, lubricants and petroleum derivatives reported a strong sequential performance for the June quarter. ... **Gandhar Oil Refinery Q1 Result Highlights (Cons, YoY)** ... * Net Profit at Rs 192 crore versus Rs 26.2 crore. * Revenue up 91.8% at Rs 1,732 crore versus Rs 903 crore. * Ebitda at Rs 281 crore versus Rs 46 crore. * Ebitda Margin at 16.2% versus 5.1%. ... On a standalone basis, the company posted a net profit of Rs 179 crore for Q1FY27, sharply higher than Rs 44.13 crore in the March quarter. Revenue rose to Rs 1,591 crore from Rs 929 crore, while EBITDA nearly quadrupled to Rs 249.2 crore from Rs 65.5 crore over the same period. ... The company's operating performance also improved significantly, with EBITDA margin expanding to 15.7% from 7% in the previous quarter, reflecting stronger profitability. ... Management said the company has historically delivered 8-11% volume growth and expects to sustain that trajectory going forward. Gandhar Oil currently exports to more than 100 countries, while its personal care business emerged as the best-performing segment in the June quarter, management added."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Domino effect: Gandhar Oil’s 20% upper circuit spurs rally in Savita Oil and Panama Petro. Here’s why - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Veer Sharma),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/domino-effect-gandhar-oils-20-upper-circuit-spurs-rally-in-savita-oil-and-panama-petro-heres-why/articleshow/132574516.cms,"Domino effect: Gandhar Oil’s 20% upper circuit spurs rally in Savita Oil and Panama Petro. Here’s why - The Economic Times ... Gandhar Oil’s ... in Savita Oil and ... Petro. Here ... # Domino effect: Gandhar Oil’s 20% upper circuit spurs rally in Savita Oil and Panama Petro. Here’s why ... ino effect: Gandhar Oil’s ... % upper circuit spurs rally in Savita Oil and Panama Petro. Here’s why ... Gandhar Oil Refinery hit the 20% upper circuit after reporting a 689% year-on-year jump in Q1 net profit, triggering a rally in peers Savita Oil and Panama Petrochem. Strong demand across PHPO, PIO and lubricants, along with expanding exports and higher-margin products, boosted investor sentiment. ... Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery hit the 20% upper circuit at Rs 284 on the BSE on Thursday after the company reported a 689% year-on-year surge in net profit to Rs 206 crore for the June quarter, compared with Rs 26 crore a year ago. The strong earnings also lifted peers, with Panama Petrochem gaining 10% and Savita Oil rising 12%.Gandhar Oil Refinery's revenue from operations for the quarter under review nearly doubled YoY to 1,732 crore, up 92% from the Rs 903 crore reported in the corresponding quarter of the previous financial year. ... EBITDA zoomed over 500% to Rs 281 crore from Rs 46 crore in the same quarter of the previous financial year. Its EPS gained 633% to Rs 19.65 from Rs 2.68 for the quarter under review. Gandhar Oil management said the PHPO segment continued to drive growth, supported by sustained demand from the personal care, healthcare and pharmaceutical sectors. The PIO business also saw encouraging traction, backed by healthy demand from transformer, power and rubber manufacturers. ... Growth in the lubricants segment remained largely stable, while the business continued to make a meaningful contribution to the company's diversified product mix. The company also sustained positive business momentum during the quarter, supported by an expanding export presence and stronger engagement with marquee customers. ... Gandhar Oil management said the operating environment during the quarter remained dynamic amid geopolitical developments in West Asia, crude oil price volatility and periodic supply chain disruptions. The company responded through agile sourcing, prudent inventory management and a favourable product mix, supporting strong financial performance. ... The performance was supported by healthy demand across key end user industries and sustained momentum across product categories. Management said its focus on value added offerings, efficient procurement and cost optimisation helped deliver superior margins while also supporting volume growth. ... Despite global macroeconomic developments and geopolitical uncertainties, management said the underlying demand environment remained encouraging and expressed confidence in sustaining profitable growth and creating long term value for stakeholders.(Disclaimer: Recommendations, suggestions, views and opinions given by the experts are their own. These do not represent the views of The Economic Times)"
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,20% Upper Circuit: Oil Refinery Stock Jumps 20% After 692% YoY Growth in Net Profits,tradebrains.in (Nikhil Naik),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://tradebrains.in/20-upper-circuit-oil-refinery-stock-jumps-20-after-692-yoy-growth-in-net-profits/,"> Synopsis: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited reported 92% Q1 FY27 revenue growth and 692% profit growth, driven by higher exports, strong manufacturing volumes, and expanding global operations across diversified end markets. ... This Small-Cap Stock, engaged in manufacturing specialty oils, white oils, lubricants, process oils, transformer oils, and healthcare products, serving automotive, personal care, pharmaceutical, industrial, and global export markets, hit a 20 percent upper circuit after the company reported June quarterly results with a 692.31 percent YoY increase in net profit. ... With a market capitalization of Rs. 2,778.31 crores, the shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited hit a 20 percent upper circuit of Rs. 283.85 per share on Thursday, up from its previous closing price of Rs. 236.55 per share. ... Coming into the quarterly results of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited, the company’s consolidated revenue from operations increased by 91.81 percent YOY, from Rs. 903 crore in Q1 FY26 to Rs. 1,732 crore in Q1 FY27, and grew by 58.46 percent QoQ from Rs. 1,093 crore in Q4 FY26. ... In Q1 FY27, Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited’s consolidated net profit increased by 692.31 percent YOY, reaching Rs. 206 crore compared to Rs. 26 crore during the same period last year. As compared to Q4 FY26, the net profit has increased by 456.76 percent, from Rs. 37 crore. The basic earnings per share increased by 633.21 percent and stood at Rs. 19.65 as against Rs. 2.68 recorded in the same quarter in the previous year, FY2026. ... Gandhar Oil has built a strong global presence, with exports contributing a significant share of its revenue over the years. In Q1 FY27, export revenue increased to Rs. 882 crore from Rs. 337 crore in Q1 FY26, with exports contributing 51 percent of consolidated revenue. The company currently serves customers in more than 100 countries across six continents, reflecting its diversified international business. ... India remains Gandhar Oil’s core market, supported by manufacturing facilities at Taloja and Silvassa and its leading position in the white oil segment. The company is also expanding its presence across the Middle East, Africa, Asia-Pacific, the Americas, and Europe. It plans to enter South Africa while identifying Indonesia, Europe, and the US as key future growth markets, strengthening its global expansion strategy. ... In Q1 FY27, Gandhar Oil reported total sales manufacturing volume of 1,31,247 kilolitres. The company sold 68,815 kilolitres of PHPO products, 17,998 kilolitres of process oils (PIO), and 30,073 kilolitres of lubricants during the quarter. Sales through channel partners stood at 14,360 kilolitres, reflecting steady demand across its key product segments and distribution network. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited serves customers across more than 100 countries and caters to over 10 diversified end markets, helping it maintain a broad and balanced business. Gandhar Oil has built long-standing relationships with more than 4,000 customers, reflecting its strong market presence and customer trust. Gandhar Oil operates three integrated manufacturing facilities with a total installed production capacity of 597,403 kilolitres. Its global reach, diversified customer base, and strong manufacturing capabilities position the company well to benefit from rising demand for specialty oils in both domestic and international markets. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is one of India’s leading manufacturers of specialty oils, serving industries such as healthcare, personal care, automotive, and industrial applications. The company offers a diversified range of value-added products through globally certified manufacturing facilities. With more than 30 years of experience, Gandhar Oil has built a strong reputation for quality, innovation, and long-term customer relationships. It is also the largest white oil player in India and among the top five global white oil manufacturers. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited’s revenue has increased from Rs. 3,897 crore in FY25 to Rs. 4,241 crore in FY26, which has grown by 8.83 percent. The net profit has also grown by 65.06 percent from Rs. 83 crore in FY25 to Rs. 137 crore in FY26. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited’s revenue and net profit have grown at a CAGR of 14 percent and 6 percent, respectively, over the last five years. In terms of return ratios, the company’s ROCE and ROE stand at 13.2 percent and 10.5 percent, respectively. Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited’s debt-to-equity ratio is 0.23x."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Q1 FY27: Stellar 633% Profit Surge P...,www.marketsmojo.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketsmojo.com/news/result-analysis/gandhar-oil-refinery-q1-fy27-stellar-633-profit-surge-powers-micro-cap-to-52-week-high-4117920,"Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd. delivered an extraordinary first-quarter performance for FY2027, posting consolidated net profit of ₹192.29 crores—a staggering 633.09% surge year-on-year and 372.69% quarter-on-quarter growth. The micro-cap oil refiner's shares surged 20.00% to ₹283.85 on July 23, touching a fresh 52-week high as investors responded enthusiastically to the company's best-ever quarterly performance. ... With a market capitalisation of ₹2,778.31 crores, the Parekh family-controlled company has delivered remarkable returns of 69.36% over the past year, significantly outperforming the oil sector's negative 7.15% return by a massive 76.51 percentage points. The quarter's standout feature was an operating margin expansion to 16.24%—the highest in recent history—driven by robust revenue growth and improved operational efficiency. ... The June 2026 quarter marked a watershed moment for Gandhar Oil Refinery, with net sales reaching an all-time high of ₹1,731.93 crores—a remarkable 91.81% increase compared to ₹902.96 crores in the corresponding quarter last year. The sequential growth of 58.40% from March 2026's ₹1,093.37 crores underscores the company's accelerating momentum. This revenue surge translated into operating profit (PBDIT excluding other income) of ₹281.32 crores, representing a dramatic improvement from ₹45.96 crores a year earlier. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery's Q1 FY27 results showcase exceptional operational leverage, with the company achieving its highest-ever operating margin of 16.24%—a substantial expansion from 5.09% in Q1 FY26 and 5.81% in the preceding quarter. The profit after tax (PAT) margin similarly surged to 11.89%, compared to just 2.89% a year ago, reflecting improved cost management and favourable market dynamics in the oil refining sector. ... The company's gross profit margin expanded to 15.68% in Q1 FY27 from 4.32% in the year-ago quarter, whilst the PAT margin of 11.89% represents a significant improvement from 2.89% previously. Interest costs remained well-controlled at ₹12.74 crores despite higher working capital requirements, whilst depreciation stood at ₹7.84 crores. The tax rate of 21.94% in the quarter was notably lower than the 29.40% recorded in the preceding quarter, contributing to the bottom-line surge. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery's Q1 FY27 performance has been classified as ""Outstanding"" based on multiple record-breaking metrics: highest-ever quarterly net sales (₹1,731.93 crores), highest operating profit (₹281.32 crores), highest operating margin (16.24%), and highest earnings per share (₹19.64). This marks a dramatic turnaround from the ""Flat"" trend observed in Q1 FY26. ... , Gandhar Oil Refinery's return on equity (ROE) stands at 9.49% on average over recent years, with the latest ROE at 10.01%—below the peer group average of approximately 14%. However, the company demonstrates stronger capital efficiency through its return on capital employed (ROCE) of 13.32% (latest) and 17.13% on average, indicating effective utilisation of invested capital in generating operating profits. ... The shareholding structure reveals steady promoter consolidation, with the Parekh family's stake increasing to 66.60% in June 2026 from 65.01% in March 2025. This gradual accumulation—adding 1.59 percentage points over five quarters—signals strong promoter confidence in the company's prospects. Notably, there is zero promoter pledging, eliminating concerns about financial stress or forced selling. ... Foreign institutional investor (FII) participation surged dramatically to 1.28% in June 2026 from just 0.14% in the previous quarter—an addition of 1.14 percentage points that suggests growing international recognition of the company's turnaround story. Other domestic institutional investors (DIIs) similarly increased their stake to 1.02% from 0.09%, adding 0.93 percentage points in a single quarter. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery's stock has delivered exceptional returns across virtually all timeframes, dramatically outperforming both the broader market and its sectoral peers. The one-year return of 69.36% compares to the Sensex's negative 7.28% return, generating positive alpha of 76.64 percentage points. Even more impressive, the stock has delivered 83.90% returns year-to-date against the Sensex's negative 9.99%, creating alpha of 93.89 percentage points. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery's investment case rests on three pillars: exceptional recent financial performance, attractive valuation metrics, and strong technical momentum. The proprietary Mojo Score of 85 out of 100 places the stock firmly in ""Strong Buy"" territory, reflecting the confluence of ""Very Attractive"" valuation, ""Bullish"" technical trend, and ""Outstanding"" quarterly financial performance. ... However, the company's ""Average"" quality grade—downgraded from ""Good"" in November 2024—introduces a note of caution. The five-year sales growth of just 1.33% and negative five-year EBIT growth of 11.05% suggest the recent surge may represent a cyclical upturn rather than sustainable structural improvement. The average ROE of 9.49% remains below peer averages, whilst the EBIT to interest coverage of 4.33 times, though adequate, falls into the ""weak"" category by stringent quality standards. ... - Record quarterly net sales of ₹1,731.93 crores—highest ever achieved - Operating margin expansion to 16.24%, up from 5.09% year-ago - Consolidated net profit surge of 633.09% YoY to ₹192.29 crores - Conservative balance sheet with debt-to-equity of just 0.14 - Zero promoter pledging eliminates governance concerns - Attractive valuation with PEG ratio of 0.25 and P/BV of 1.71x - Strong technical momentum with stock above all moving averages ... The critical question for investors is whether Gandhar Oil Refinery's Q1 FY27 performance represents a sustainable new operating level or a temporary margin spike driven by favourable market conditions. The company's ability to maintain operating margins above 12-15% in subsequent quarters will be crucial in validating the current valuation premium. ... - Sustained operating margins above 12% in coming quarters - Continued sequential revenue growth demonstrating market share gains - ROE improvement towards 12-15% range through operational leverage - Increased institutional participation, particularly mutual funds - Capacity expansion announcements supporting long-term growth ... Management commentary on the sustainability of margin improvements, order book visibility, and capacity utilisation levels will be critical datapoints in the coming quarters. The oil refining sector's inherent cyclicality means investors should monitor crude oil price trends, refining spreads, and inventory levels closely. Any signs of margin normalisation towards historical averages of 4-6% would likely trigger significant valuation compression. ... For Fresh Investors: Gandhar Oil Refinery presents a compelling opportunity at current levels, with the combination of record financial performance, attractive valuation metrics (PEG ratio of 0.25, P/BV of 1.71x), and strong technical momentum justifying fresh accumulation. However, position sizing should reflect the stock's high volatility (44.07%) and micro-cap liquidity constraints. Consider building positions gradually over 2-3 months rather than a single large allocation. Suitable only for investors with high risk tolerance and 2-3 year investment horizon. ... For Existing Holders: Continue holding with trailing stop-loss at ₹240-245 levels (approximately 15% below current price). The 633% YoY profit growth and margin expansion to 16.24% validate the turnaround thesis, but monitor quarterly results closely for signs of margin normalisation. Consider booking partial profits (25-30% of holdings) above ₹300 to lock in gains whilst retaining exposure to potential further upside. Reassess if operating margins fall below 10% or institutional investors begin exiting."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Highest-Ever Quarterly Net Profit, Sees Revenue Surge 92% in Q1 FY27",investoomarket.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://investoomarket.com/news/gandhar-oil-refinery-reports-highest-ever-quarterly-net-profit-sees-revenue-surge-92-in-q1-fy27.44168/,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Highest-Ever Quarterly Net Profit, Sees Revenue Surge 92% in Q1 FY27 ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Highest-Ever Quarterly Net Profit, Sees Revenue Surge 92% in Q1 FY27 ... ## Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Highest-Ever Quarterly Net Profit, Sees Revenue Surge 92% in Q1 FY27​ ... Mumbai: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd announced its unaudited financial results for the quarter ending June 30, 2026, reporting a record quarterly net profit exceeding ₹ 200 crore. The company noted that this strong performance was achieved despite operating within a dynamic and challenging external environment. The consolidated revenue increased by 92% year-on-year, reaching ₹ 1,732 crore. Furthermore, the Gross Margin Spread expanded 3.4 times compared to Q1 FY26, standing at ₹ 28,145 per kiloliter (kl). In terms of operational performance, overall volumes improved by 8% year-on-year. The company also declared an Interim Dividend equivalent to 100% of Face Value. ... | Particulars (kl) | Q1 FY27 | Q1 FY26 | | --- | --- | --- | | PHPO | 68,815 | 58,379 | | Lubricants | 30,073 | 30,482 | | PIO | 17,998 | 14,085 | | Channel Partners | 14,360 | 18,787 | | Total Manufacturing Volumes | 1,31,247 | 1,21,733 | ... Commenting on the results, Mr. Aslesh Parekh, Joint Managing Director of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd, stated that the company was pleased with its strongest quarter in history, driven by robust gross margin spreads and healthy revenue growth. Mr. Parekh noted that the operating environment included volatility in crude oil prices and geopolitical developments in West Asia. The company attributed its strong financial performance to agile sourcing, prudent inventory management, and a favorable product mix. The PHPO segment was highlighted as an anchor for growth, benefiting from sustained demand across the healthcare, personal care, and pharmaceutical sectors. Additionally, the PIO business showed encouraging traction, reflecting good demand from transformer, power, and rubber manufacturers. While the Lubricants segment remained stable, it continues to contribute significantly to the diversified business mix. Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd maintains a focus on operational excellence, efficient procurement practices, and cost optimization initiatives. The company remains confident in its ability to sustain profitable growth by maintaining a customer-centric approach and focusing on value-added offerings. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is a specialty oil manufacturer and a leading producer of white oils by revenue, with a growing focus on consumer and healthcare end-industries. The company possesses a diversified customer base and produces a wide range of specialty oils and lubricants, including white oils, waxes, jellies, automotive oils, industrial oils, transformer oils, and rubber processing oils. These products are sold under the flagship brand 'Divyol'. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd. experienced a strong finish on Wednesday, with its stock surging 4.02% to settle at ₹236.19. This performance saw the company achieve its 52-week high as it closed amidst significant activity, trading 6.97 million shares that day."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,"Business News | Gandhar Oil Delivers Highest PAT Driven by Strong Demand from the Personal Care, Healthcare, and Pharmaceutical (PHPO) Sectors | LatestLY",www.latestly.com (ANI),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.latestly.com/agency-news/business-news-gandhar-oil-delivers-highest-pat-driven-by-strong-demand-from-the-personal-care-healthcare-and-pharmaceutical-phpo-sectors-7528562.html,"Business News | Gandhar Oil Delivers Highest PAT Driven by Strong Demand from the Personal Care, Healthcare, and Pharmaceutical (PHPO) Sectors | LatestLY ... ## Get latest articles and stories on Business at LatestLY. Mumbai (Maharashtra) [India], July 23: Gandhar Oil reported its highest-ever quarterly net profit, crossing Rs 200 crs. This record performance was driven by healthy revenue growth and robust gross margin spreads despite operating in a dynamic and challenging external environment. ... Gandhar Oil delivers Highest PAT driven by strong demand from the Personal Care, Healthcare, and Pharmaceutical (PHPO) ... Mumbai (Maharashtra) [India], July 23: Gandhar Oil reported its highest-ever quarterly net profit, crossing Rs 200 crs. This record performance was driven by healthy revenue growth and robust gross margin spreads despite operating in a dynamic and challenging external environment. ... Revenue from operations increased to Rs 1,732 crs in Q1 FY 2026-27, up 92% YoY. ... Profit After Tax (PAT) reached Rs 206 crs, marking a 689% increase YoY. ... EBITDA grew by 633% YoY, reflecting strong operational performance. ... Total manufacturing volumes improved to 1,31,449 kl, an 8% increase YoY. ... Gross margin spread expanded to Rs 28,145 per kl, a 3.4x increase YoY. ... Declared an interim dividend of 100% of face value. ... A blockbuster quarter with exceptional growth across all key financial metrics. The company delivered a remarkable jump in revenue, margins, and profitability, indicating a significant improvement in business performance during the quarter. ... The operating environment during the quarter remained dynamic, shaped by geopolitical developments in West Asia, crude oil price volatility, and periodic supply chain disruptions. Company's ability to respond swiftly through agile sourcing, prudent inventory management, and a favourable product mix translated into strong financial performance. ... Strong performance was supported by healthy demand across key end-user industries and sustained momentum across product categories. Continued focus on value-added offerings, efficient procurement practices, and cost optimisation initiatives enabled us to achieve superior margins while also supporting volume growth. ... The PHPO segment continued to anchor company's growth, driven by sustained demand from the personal care, healthcare, and pharmaceutical sectors. The quarter also witnessed encouraging traction in the PIO business, reflecting healthy demand across transformer, power & rubber manufacturers. ... While Gandhar Oil remains watchful of global macroeconomic developments and geopolitical uncertainties, the underlying demand environment continues to remain encouraging. With a strong business foundation, a customer-centric approach, and an unwavering focus on operational excellence, company remains confident in their ability to sustain profitable growth and create long-term value for all stakeholders. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is a known name in the world of specialty oils. Our Company is a leading manufacturer of white oils by revenue with a growing focus on the consumer and healthcare end-industries. We have a diversified customer base. We produce a broad variety of specialty oils and lubricants such as White oils, waxes, jellies, automotive oils, industrial oils, transformer oils and rubber processing oils. Our products are sold under our flagship brand ""Divyol""."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Q1 Consolidated Net Profit Of ₹1.92 Billion, Up QoQ",www.sahi.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sahi.com/news/gandhar-oil-refinery-reports-q1-consolidated-net-profit-of-1-92-billion-up-qoq-3929-PE1_COR,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Q1 Consolidated Net Profit Of ₹1.92 Billion, Up QoQ ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery Reports Q1 Consolidated Net Profit Of ₹1.92 Billion, Up QoQ ... Gandhar Oil's Q1 FY27 consolidated net profit soared sequentially, driven by robust performance in its core petroleum products and specialty oils segment. Revenue jumped to ₹1,731.93 crore, while the EBITDA margin expanded significantly to 16.27% from 5.83% in the preceding quarter. ... Market snapshot: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited declared its consolidated financial results for the first quarter ended June 30, 2026, delivering an exceptional quarter-on-quarter expansion. The company registered sharp increases in net profit, operational revenue, and EBITDA margins compared to the previous quarter. ... - Consolidated Net Profit rose to ₹192 crore from ₹40.7 crore in the previous quarter. - Consolidated Revenue from Operations reached ₹1,731.93 crore, compared to ₹1,093.37 crore QoQ. - Consolidated EBITDA stood at ₹281 crore with the EBITDA margin expanding to 16.27% from 5.83% QoQ. ... - Consolidated Net Profit increased to ₹192 crore, up significantly from ₹40.7 crore QoQ. - Consolidated Revenue increased by ≈58.4% QoQ (derived: ₹1,731.93 cr vs ₹1,093.37 cr). - EBITDA Margin improved by 1,044 basis points QoQ to 16.27% from 5.83%. ... - Massive quarter-on-quarter growth in profitability highlights strong operating leverage. - Texol Lubritech FZC, a key subsidiary, contributed revenue of ₹144.54 crore and profit after tax of ₹27.3 crore, bolstering the consolidated numbers. - The board declared an interim dividend of ₹2 per equity share for the financial year 2026-27. ... The remarkable surge in Gandhar Oil's Q1 performance demonstrates strong sequential recovery and improved realizations. High-margin specialty chemical segments, combined with solid contributions from overseas operations like Texol Lubritech, are acting as strong growth engines. The dramatic margin expansion indicates that the company successfully managed raw material price volatility during the quarter. ... The strong sequential turnaround is expected to enhance investor confidence in Gandhar Oil's earnings consistency. The declaration of a ₹2 per share interim dividend (100% of face value) further underscores management's commitment to returning capital to shareholders amid robust profitability. This operational momentum could lead to positive earnings revisions for the full year. ... Strong quarter-on-quarter surge across all operational parameters, with EBITDA growing to ₹281 crore and margin expanding by over 10 percentage points, backed by strong subsidiary performance. ... - Sustained sequential volume growth in the white oils and healthcare segments. - Stability in base oil raw material prices supporting high margins. - Overseas subsidiary Texol Lubritech FZC maintaining its high profitability levels. ... The specialty chemicals and white oils industry is experiencing steady demand from consumer, personal care, and healthcare sectors. Companies like Gandhar Oil, which hold significant domestic market share and maintain stringent quality approvals, benefit from sticky customer relationships. Lower input cost pressures sequentially have acted as a tailwind for the broader petroleum products manufacturing sector. ... - Volatility in global crude and base oil prices which are key raw materials. - Foreign exchange fluctuations affecting overseas operations and export margins. - Slowdown in key end-user segments like automotive lubricants or industrial processing oils. ... The company's board approved an interim dividend of ₹2 per share on July 22, 2026, with the record date set for July 24, 2026. The statutory auditor, M/s. K J K & Associates, issued a limited review report on the unaudited standalone and consolidated results. Additionally, the company is hosting an earnings call with analysts and investors on July 23, 2026, to discuss the performance. ... Gandhar Oil's robust sequential performance positions it well within the specialty chemicals sector. Investors should monitor the upcoming earnings call for management commentary on margin sustainability and demand trends in key export markets."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,"Gandhar Oil delivers Highest PAT driven by strong demand from the Personal Care, Healthcare, and Pharmaceutical (PHPO) sectors - english.punjabkesari.com",english.punjabkesari.com,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://english.punjabkesari.com/business/gandhar-oil-delivers-highest-pat-driven-by-strong-demand-from-the-personal-care-healthcare-and-pharmaceutical-phpo-sectors/,"Gandhar Oil delivers Highest PAT driven by strong demand from the Personal Care, Healthcare, and Pharmaceutical (PHPO) sectors - english.punjabkesari.com # Gandhar Oil delivers Highest PAT driven by strong demand from the Personal Care, Healthcare, and Pharmaceutical (PHPO) sectors ... VMPL Mumbai (Maharashtra) [India], July 23: Gandhar Oil reported its highest-ever quarterly net profit, crossing Rs 200 crs. This record performance was driven by healthy revenue growth and robust gross margin spreads despite operating in a dynamic and challenging external environment. Revenue from operations increased to Rs 1,732 crs in Q1 FY 2026-27, up 92% YoY. Profit After Tax (PAT) reached Rs 206 crs, marking a 689% increase YoY. EBITDA grew by 633% YoY, reflecting strong operational performance. Total manufacturing volumes improved to 1,31,449 kl, an 8% increase YoY. Gross margin spread expanded to Rs 28,145 per kl, a 3.4x increase YoY. Declared an interim dividend of 100% of face value. A blockbuster quarter with exceptional growth across all key financial metrics. The company delivered a remarkable jump in revenue, margins, and profitability, indicating a significant improvement in business performance during the quarter. The operating environment during the quarter remained dynamic, shaped by geopolitical developments in West Asia, crude oil price volatility, and periodic supply chain disruptions. Company’s ability to respond swiftly through agile sourcing, prudent inventory management, and a favourable product mix translated into strong financial performance. Strong performance was supported by healthy demand across key end-user industries and sustained momentum across product categories. Continued focus on value-added offerings, efficient procurement practices, and cost optimisation initiatives enabled us to achieve superior margins while also supporting volume growth. The PHPO segment continued to anchor company’s growth, driven by sustained demand from the personal care, healthcare, and pharmaceutical sectors. The quarter also witnessed encouraging traction in the PIO business, reflecting healthy demand across transformer, power & rubber manufacturers. While Gandhar Oil remains watchful of global macroeconomic developments and geopolitical uncertainties, the underlying demand environment continues to remain encouraging. With a strong business foundation, a customer-centric approach, and an unwavering focus on operational excellence, company remains confident in their ability to sustain profitable growth and create long-term value for all stakeholders. About Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is a known name in the world of specialty oils. Our Company is a leading manufacturer of white oils by revenue with a growing focus on the consumer and healthcare end-industries. We have a diversified customer base. We produce a broad variety of specialty oils and lubricants such as White oils, waxes, jellies, automotive oils, industrial oils, transformer oils and rubber processing oils. Our products are sold under our flagship brand “Divyol”. For more information, visit https://gandharoil.com/ (ADVERTORIAL DISCLAIMER: The above press release has been provided by VMPL. ANI will not be responsible in any way for the content of the same.)"
