GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Declares Interim Dividend for the Financial Year 2026-27 | MarketScreener UAE Emirates,ae.marketscreener.com (S&P Capital IQ),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ae.marketscreener.com/news/gandhar-oil-refinery-limited-declares-interim-dividend-for-the-financial-year-2026-27-ce7f51d9dd89f425,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Declares Interim Dividend for the Financial Year 2026-27 | MarketScreener UAE Emirates ... | 07-23 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited, Q1 2027 Earnings Call, Jul 23, 2026 | | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-22 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Reports Earnings Results for the First Quarter Ended June 30, 2026 | CI | ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Declares Interim Dividend for the Financial Year 2026-27 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited at the AGM to be on September 11, 2026 proposed the declaration of an Interim Dividend of INR 2 per Equity Share of the Company (i.e. 100% of the face value of INR 2/- each of equity share) for the financial year 2026-27. Further, the record date for determining entitlement of the members to the interim dividend has being fixed as July 24, 2026. ... ### Latest news about Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited ... | 07-23 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited, Q1 2027 Earnings Call, Jul 23, 2026 | | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-22 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Reports Earnings Results for the First Quarter Ended June 30, 2026 | CI | | 07-22 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Declares Interim Dividend for the Financial Year 2026-27 | CI | | 05-27 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited, Q4 2026 Earnings Call, May 27, 2026 | | | 05-26 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Reports Earnings Results for the Fourth Quarter and Full Year Ended March 31, 2026 | CI | | 05-26 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Announces Changes to Its Board and Committee | CI | | 05-26 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Approves Incorporation and Investment in Wholly Owned Subsidiary in South Africa | CI | | 05-26 | Gandhar Oil Refinery India March-quarter consol net profit 406.8 million rupees | RE | | 05-12 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Ltd Announces Resignation of Deena Mehta as Non-Executive Independent Director, Effective May 12, 2026 | CI | | 05-11 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Ltd Announces Resignation of Sanjay Bharadwaj as Senior Vice President, Manufacturing, Operations Department Silvassa Plant and Senior Management Personnel, Effective May 11, 2026 | CI | | 05-07 | Gandhar Oil Refinery India gets favourable order sanctioning refund claim of 229.2 million rupees | RE | | 05-06 | Gandhar Oil Refinery India completes purchase of land parcel for 227.8 million rupees | RE | | 03-12 | Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) says optimum inventory levels were maintained at UAE plant | RE | | 01-28 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited, Q3 2026 Earnings Call, Jan 28, 2026 | | | 01-23 | Gandhar Oil Refinery Limited Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter and Nine Months Ended December 31, 2025 | CI | ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is an India-based company, which is engaged in the specialty oil industry. The Company manufactures and trades petroleum products / specialty oils, trading in Non-Coking Coal and provides consignment / del-credere agency services for the sale of polymers to local markets. It manufactures White Oils and other allied products that have applications in cosmetics, healthcare, and pharmaceuticals. Its products category includes Industrial Oil, which includes Lube Oil, Hydraulic Oil, and Spark Erosion Oil; Automotive Oil, which includes Agricultural Oil and Gas Engine Oil; Mineral Oil and Petroleum Jelly, which include Spray Oil and White Petroleum Jelly, and Rubber Process Oil. Its products are marketed under the Divyol brand. It operates three manufacturing facilities in Taloja (Maharashtra), Silvassa (Dadra and Nagar Haveli), and Sharjah (UAE). Its subsidiaries include Gandhar Shipping & Logistics Pvt. Ltd., Gandhar Foundation, and Texol Lubritech FZC."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Reports Q1 Consolidated Net Profit of ₹205.89 Crore,www.sahi.com,2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sahi.com/news/gandhar-oil-reports-q1-consolidated-net-profit-of-205-89-crore-3929-PE1_COR,"Gandhar Oil Reports Q1 Consolidated Net Profit of ₹205.89 Crore ... # Gandhar Oil Reports Q1 Consolidated Net Profit of ₹205.89 Crore ... • Consolidated Net Profit (PAT) skyrocketed by ≈684.94% YoY to ₹205.89 crore (derived: ₹205.89 cr vs ₹26.23 cr). • Consolidated Revenue from operations increased by 91.81% YoY to ₹1,731.93 crore (derived: ₹1,731.93 cr vs ₹902.96 cr). • Strong operational performance from subsidiary Texol Lubritech FZC significantly supported overall profitability. • The company remains fundamentally robust with scheduled investor interactions on July 23, 2026, to discuss future growth triggers. ... Market snapshot: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited declared its consolidated financial results for the first quarter ended June 30, 2026, delivering an exceptional surge in performance. While the original news alert claimed a Q1 consolidated net profit of 1.92B Rupees (₹192 crore) (as stated in the source alert; not independently verified), official regulatory filings submitted to BSE and NSE confirm that the consolidated Net Profit actually stood at ₹205.89 crore. ... - Consolidated Net Profit (PAT) for the quarter ended June 30, 2026, reached ₹205.89 crore, reflecting a massive YoY expansion. - Consolidated Revenue from Operations stood at ₹1,731.93 crore, up significantly on both YoY and QoQ bases. - Texol Lubritech FZC, a key subsidiary, reported total revenue of ₹144.54 crore and a net profit after tax of ₹27.30 crore for the quarter. ... - Consolidated Net Profit increased to ₹205.89 crore in Q1 FY27, up from ₹26.23 crore in Q1 FY26 and ₹40.68 crore in Q4 FY26. - Consolidated Revenue from Operations rose to ₹1,731.93 crore, compared to ₹902.96 crore in Q1 FY26 and ₹1,093.37 crore in Q4 FY26. ... - Extraordinary volume expansions and robust operations across both domestic and international markets drove Q1 FY27 growth. - The performance shows strong operating leverage, with PAT growing far quicker than top-line revenue. - The company's subsidiary, Texol Lubritech FZC, remains a core driver of profitable international expansion, generating a net profit of ₹27.30 crore. - The results set a highly positive tone for the 2026-27 financial year, showing resilience against raw material and logistics headwinds. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery has demonstrated superb operational resilience. By delivering a significant jump in margins alongside substantial revenue growth, the company highlights its pricing power and capacity to pass on base oil cost fluctuations to consumers. The strong performance of its foreign subsidiary further solidifies its positioning as a global specialty oils major. ... The exceptional earnings performance is likely to generate extremely positive momentum for the stock in the near term. Analysts will closely monitor the scheduled earnings call on July 23, 2026, for management updates on volume guidance, international expansion, and margin sustainability. ... The highly positive directional bias is backed by a massive ≈684.94% YoY surge in consolidated net profit to ₹205.89 crore and a 91.81% YoY increase in revenue to ₹1,731.93 crore, driven by robust domestic and subsidiary performances. ... - Sustainability of the PHPO segment margins - Stable base oil raw material costs - Post-earnings call commentary scheduled for July 23, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery is one of India's largest manufacturers of white oils and ranks among the top five players globally, commanding a 26.5% market share in India and a 9.6% market share globally. It operates in the highly specialized petrochemicals sub-sector, serving pharmaceutical, personal care, and industrial segments. ... - Raw material volatility: Variations in base oil prices directly impact manufacturing margins. - Geopolitical constraints: Disruption in shipping lanes or supply chains could impact export logistics. - Foreign exchange risks: Fluctuations in major currencies may affect realization of overseas revenues. ... On July 21, 2026, Neomile Growth Fund - Series I acquired 8.64 lakh shares (representing a 0.88% stake) in Gandhar Oil Refinery India at ₹224.80 per share, through a transaction valued at ₹19.4 crore. Additionally, the company has scheduled its Q1 FY27 earnings call with analysts and investors on Thursday, July 23, 2026, at 11:00 AM IST. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery's Q1 FY27 performance marks a robust start to the fiscal year, proving that its strategic shift toward higher-value pharmaceutical and healthcare specialty oils is paying off handsomely."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Petrol Price Paradox: FG Demands Explanation as Global Crude Plummets - XL 106.9 FM: Uyo's Vibe. Africa's Future.,xl1069.fm (Lionel Munam),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://xl1069.fm/news/petrol-price-paradox-fg-demands-explanation-as-global-crude-plummets/,"Held at the headquarters of the Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority (NMDPRA), the engagement brought together key industry players, including representatives from the Dangote Refinery, the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Commission (FCCPC), and the Petroleum Products Retail Outlets Owners Association of Nigeria (PETROAN). ... The urgent convention comes on the heels of mounting public expectation for a reduction in domestic pump prices, following a recent drop in global crude oil benchmarks and an expansion in local refining capabilities. ... Speaking at the event, NMDPRA Chief Executive Rabiu Umar emphasized that the international crude market had seen a noticeable moderation in prices as geopolitical tensions eased over the past six months. ... Umar noted that the government is seeking an open, solution-oriented dialogue with marketers to examine inventory management, enhance market surveillance, and accelerate key stability mechanisms like the National Strategic Stock (NSS). ... Reiterating the administration’s stance on economic reforms, the NMDPRA boss underscored that President Bola Tinubu has laid a resilient foundation for a deregulated and investment-driven energy sector. ... Instead, the policy is intended to drive market efficiency, maximize value, and ensure that the benefits of global market improvements are passed down to Nigerian consumers without unnecessary delays. ... Moving forward, the federal government and downstream stakeholders are expected to continue extensive consultations to establish a more transparent pricing framework. ... marketer profitability and public welfare ... As the dialogue progresses, the public remains watchful for a swift alignment between falling global crude oil costs and the prices reflecting at retail stations across the country."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Specialty Oil Stocks Rally: Why Panama and Gandhar Are Surging | Whalesbook,www.whalesbook.com,2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.whalesbook.com/news/English/consumer-products/Specialty-Oil-Stocks-Rally-Why-Panama-and-Gandhar-Are-Surging/6a34f32bd017fdb5099a597d,"Lubricant and specialty oil stocks including Panama Petrochem and Gandhar Oil surged up to 18% in today's trade, defying a broader market dip. The rally comes amid heavy trading volumes and continued interest in players providing critical chemical inputs to industrial, cosmetic, and pharmaceutical sectors. ... In a day where the broader market saw a decline, lubricant and specialty petroleum stocks stood out with significant gains. Panama Petrochem and Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) saw their share prices climb up to 18% during Friday's trading session. Savita Oil Technologies also saw positive movement, rising 3%. ... Panama Petrochem hit a record high of ₹484.40, supported by a two-fold increase in trading volumes on the NSE and BSE. Gandhar Oil also reached a 52-week high of ₹184.55 on the back of a three-fold rise in trading volume. When queried by the exchange regarding the sudden spike, Gandhar Oil stated there were no undisclosed material events, attributing the movement to market-driven factors. ... Panama Petrochem, Gandhar Oil, and Savita Oil Technologies operate as niche players in the specialty chemicals space. Their business involves refining and processing base oils into specialized formulations. ... Panama Petrochem has a significant export footprint, with a subsidiary in the UAE that provides logistical advantages and proximity to base oil suppliers. Gandhar Oil, a major player in white oils, has focused on diversifying its client base across global markets. Savita Oil Technologies has a long legacy in the sector and has been expanding its portfolio into modern areas like E-Mobility fluids and high-performance lubricants. The rally in these stocks suggests that investors may be weighing their potential for continued volume growth and their established positions in global supply chains. ... - Volume Growth: As noted in recent performance reports, growth in these companies is often driven by volume expansion. Investors may track whether these firms can continue to increase the tonnage of their products sold. ... - Export Performance: For companies like Panama Petrochem and Gandhar Oil, which have significant export revenue, global demand and currency fluctuations remain key monitorables. ... - Capacity Utilization: With various companies in this sector investing in capacity, the ability to effectively utilize this new capacity and find ready markets for the increased output will be important."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil promoter confirms no encumbrances in FY26,scanx.trade (Dhan),2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://scanx.trade/stock-market-news/companies/gandhar-oil-promoter-confirms-no-encumbrances-in-fy26/43111779,"Gandhar Oil promoter confirms no encumbrances in FY26 ... Gandhar Oil promoter confirms no encumbrances in FY26 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd promoter Aslesh Ramesh Parekh declared no encumbrances on shares during FY 2025-26 under SEBI regulations. The disclosure, dated April 03, 2026, was sent to BSE and NSE. It covers all promoters, the promoter group, and persons acting in concert. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd promoter Aslesh Ramesh Parekh has confirmed that there are no encumbrances, directly or indirectly, on the shares held by the promoter group during the financial year 2025-26. This declaration was submitted to the BSE Limited and National Stock Exchange of India Limited on April 03, 2026, pursuant to Regulation 31(4) of SEBI (Substantial Acquisition of Shares and Takeover) Regulations, 2011. The confirmation covers all promoters, the promoter group, and persons acting in concert (PAC) associated with the company. ... The disclosure was addressed to the Listing Compliance departments of both exchanges and the Audit Committee of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited. The promoter stated that the confirmation is made on behalf of all ... promoters and the promoter group as detailed in the annexure to the letter. ... potential plans by the ... raise capital through pledging shares ... Could the absence of encumbrances signal a strategic shift towards acquisitions or expansion for Gandhar Oil Refinery? ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery to attend investor meet on June 11 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited announced it will participate in a virtual analyst and institutional investor meet on June 11, 2026, organized by Choice Equity Broking Pvt. Ltd. under the InsightX 2026 conference. The session, scheduled from 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m., will focus on publicly available information without sharing any unpublished price sensitive data. The disclosure was filed with BSE and NSE pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. ... Gandhar Oil Refinery(India) Limited has scheduled a virtual analyst and institutional investor meet for June 11, 2026, to discuss its performance and outlook. The interaction will take place from 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. as part of the InsightX 2026 Investor Conference/Meet organized by Choice Equity Broking Pvt. Ltd. The company confirmed that discussions will be based solely on publicly available information and no unpublished price sensitive information (UPSI) will be shared during the session. ... The disclosure was made to the BSE Limited and the National Stock Exchange of India (NSE) in compliance with Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. The company noted that the schedule is subject to change due to exigencies on the part of the investors or the company. ... (India) ... What key performance metrics or strategic initiatives is Gandhar Oil Refinery likely to emphasize during the meet? ... Could the discussion hint at any upcoming expansion plans or partnerships? ... ## More News on Gandhar Oil Refinery ... Gandhar Oil promoters confirm no encumbrances on shares for FY 2025-26 Jun 03, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery reports 10% revenue growth in FY26 Jun 03, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil FY26 net profit rises 84% to ₹138.39 crore May 28, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery SVP Manufacturing Resigns Effective May 11, 2026 May 13, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery: Mrs. Deena Mehta Steps Down as Non-Executive Independent Director May 13, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery Receives Favourable Customs Refund of Rs. 22,92,06,499/- May 08, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery Acquires 18,353 Sq. Mtrs. of Land in Silvassa for Rs. 22,77,65,500/- May 07, 2026 ... Gandhar Oil Refinery Completes Punjab Property Sale for Rs. 1.61 Crores Under Regulation 30 May 05, 2026"
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Mrs. Padmini Parekh Acquires Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd Through Transmission,investoomarket.com,2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://investoomarket.com/news/mrs-padmini-parekh-acquires-shares-of-gandhar-oil-refinery-india-ltd-through-transmission.30890/,"Mrs. Padmini Parekh Acquires Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd Through Transmission ... # Mrs. Padmini Parekh Acquires Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd Through Transmission ... - News starter Deepali - Start date Jun 11, 2026 - Jun 11, 2026 ## Mrs. Padmini Parekh Acquires Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd Through Transmission​ ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited has seen a change in shareholding as Mrs. Padmini Parekh, a member of the Promoter Group, acquired equity shares through transmission from her late husband, Mr. Kailash Parekh. The acquisition involves 70,40,000 Equity Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited. The transaction was executed via transmission from Late Mr. Kailash Parekh to Mrs. Padmini Parekh. This transfer falls under the provisions applicable to acquisitions by way of transmission or inheritance and does not require open offer disclosures as per the relevant regulations. The acquisition details reveal changes in both individual and group shareholdings prior to and after the transaction. Mrs. Padmini Parekh's shareholding before the transaction was 15,00,000 shares, representing 1.53% of the total share capital. Following the transmission, her holding increased significantly. The overall shareholder details for the Promoter and Promoter Group of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited remained stable at 6,50,60,100 shares, maintaining a 66.47% stake both pre- and post-transmission. Key shareholding figures relating to the acquisition are summarized below: ... | Shareholder | Pre-Transaction Shares Held | Pre-Transaction % | Post-Transaction Shares Held | Post-Transaction % | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Mrs. Padmini Parekh (Acquirer) | 15,00,000 | 1.53% | [Data not provided in source] | 8.72% | The promoter and promoter group of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited reported the following shareholding status: | Particulars | Pre-Transaction Holding | Post-Transaction Holding | | --- | --- | --- | | Shares held by Promoter Group | 6,50,60,100 | 6,50,60,100 | | Percentage of shares held | 66.47% | 66.47% | ... Shares of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited are currently shedding value in live trading, as of 10:17 AM, slipping by 0.47% to ₹155.34. The stock maintains a tight intraday range, having traded between a low of ₹153.5 and a high of ₹156.06, with 51,363 shares recorded in the exchange so far."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,"Nigeria's Dangote Refinery, with a daily capacity of 650,000 barrels, can supply aviation fuel to the global market - Wedoany",en.wedoany.com,2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.wedoany.com/shortnews/196352.html,"Nigeria's Dangote Refinery, with a daily capacity of 650,000 barrels, can supply aviation fuel to the global market - Wedoany ... Nigeria's Dangote Refinery, with a daily capacity of 650,000 barrels, can supply aviation fuel to the global market 2026-06-03 14:01 ... en.Wedoany.com Reported - David Bird, CEO of Nigeria's Dangote Refinery, stated that the refinery has a surplus of aviation fuel and can supply any region worldwide. The refinery has a daily capacity of 650,000 barrels. ... Bird noted that the refinery is able to export its surplus because oil demand in Africa is lower than in other regions. Speaking at the S&P Global Energy and Gas Middle East Petroleum and Gas Conference in London, he said the company is regarded as a reliable, high-quality, and trustworthy supplier capable of selling products globally at competitive prices. Aviation fuel is one of the fuels most affected by the Iran war and the closure of the Strait of Hormuz, a context that provides opportunities for refineries outside the Gulf region, such as Dangote, to supply the global market. Bird revealed that the refinery is currently operating at full capacity and plans to implement a project called ""ruthless replica"" to double its capacity. ... Bird stated that the company will add 700,000 barrels of complex refining capacity by the end of 2028, adding that long-cycle products have been procured and construction contracts are currently being awarded. He added that the group will further increase refining capacity by 2.1 million barrels per day by building a new refinery in East Africa, which will help it become a major player in the flow of crude oil products and refined products. ... Bird also said that since the Dangote Refinery began operations, Nigeria has transitioned from fuel shortages to fuel abundance."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil FY26 net profit rises 84% to ₹138.39 crore,scanx.trade (Dhan),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://scanx.trade/stock-market-news/companies/gandhar-oil-board-meets-on-may-26-for-fy26-results/40828705,"Gandhar Oil FY26 net profit rises 84% to ₹138.39 crore # Gandhar Oil FY26 net profit rises 84% to ₹138.39 crore 2 min read Updated on 28 May 2026, 08:50 AM ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd reported an 84% rise in net profit for FY26 to ₹138.39 crore, with revenue from operations increasing 8% to ₹3,422.56 crore. Consolidated net profit stood at ₹137.25 crore on total income of ₹4,241.18 crore. The Board approved the re-appointment of Joint Managing Directors and strategic investments, including a ₹50 crore subsidiary in South Africa. ... *this image is generated using AI for illustrative purposes only. Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd reported an 84% rise in net profit for the financial year ended March 31, 2026, to ₹138.39 crore, compared to ₹75.30 crore in the previous year. Revenue from operations for the year increased by 8% to ₹3,422.56 crore from ₹3,160.26 crore in FY25. On a consolidated basis, net profit stood at ₹137.25 crore against ₹83.52 crore in the prior year, while total income from operations reached ₹4,241.18 crore. The Board of Directors approved the audited standalone and consolidated financial results at its meeting held on May 26, 2026. ... The company delivered a strong full-year performance, with consolidated EBITDA rising to ₹234.5 crore from ₹175.6 crore in FY25. Consolidated manufacturing sales volumes for FY26 stood at 5,45,755 KL, up by 9% from 5,00,231 KL in the previous year. The PHPO segment led the revenue mix with a 48% contribution, followed by Lubricants at 27%, Channel Partners at 14.81%, and PIO at 10.19%. The statutory auditor, M/s. KJK & Associates, issued an unmodified opinion on the financial results. ... | Metric (₹ Cr) | FY26 | FY25 | | --- | --- | --- | | Net Profit (Standalone) | 138.39 | 75.30 | | Net Profit (Consolidated) | 137.25 | 83.52 | | Revenue from Operations (Standalone) | 3,422.56 | 3,160.26 | | Total Income from Operations (Consolidated) | 4,241.18 | 3,896.93 | | EBITDA (Consolidated) | 234.5 | 175.6 | ... For the quarter ended March 31, 2026, the company recorded a consolidated net profit of ₹37.05 crore, a significant increase from ₹12.29 crore in the corresponding period of the previous year. Consolidated revenue for the quarter stood at ₹1,093.37 crore compared to ₹961.72 crore in the previous year. The company's Q4 EBITDA improved to ₹63.6 crore from ₹33.6 crore on a year-on-year basis, with the EBITDA margin expanding to 5.83% from 3.50% in the prior year. ... The Board approved the re-appointment of Mr. Samir Parekh and Mr. Aslesh Parekh as Joint Managing Directors for a period of five years effective from October 01, 2026. Additionally, the Board appointed Mr. Santokhsingh Karamsingh Sandhu as an Additional Non-Executive Independent Director and Mr. Jatin Dhamani as an Additional Whole Time Director for five years starting May 26, 2026. ... The Board approved the proposed incorporation and investment of up to ₹50 crore in a wholly-owned subsidiary in South Africa to distribute petroleum products and specialty oils. The company also agreed to purchase land measuring approximately 21,551 sq. mtrs in Village Kherane Khurd, Tal. Panvel, Dist. Raigad, for a consideration of up to ₹20 crore. M/s. G. D. Singhvi & Co. were re-appointed as Internal Auditor and M/s. Maulin Shah & Associates as Cost Auditor for FY26-27. ... # Gandhar Oil Refinery SVP Manufacturing Resigns Effective May 11, 2026 1 min read Updated on 13 May 2026, 06:00 AM AI Summary ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd issued a revised regulatory disclosure correcting the effective resignation date of Mr. Sanjay Bharadwaj, Senior Vice President – Manufacturing, Operations Department at its Silvassa Plant, from May 05, 2026 to May 11, 2026. The earlier date was inadvertently mentioned in the initial filing. The resignation, citing personal reasons, was disclosed under Regulation 30 of the SEBI Listing Regulations by Compliance Officer Binal Khosla. ... *this image is generated using AI for illustrative purposes only. Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd has issued a revised disclosure to the stock exchanges correcting the effective date of resignation of Mr. Sanjay Bharadwaj from his position as Senior Vice President – Manufacturing, Operations Department at the company's Silvassa Plant. The company clarified that the date mentioned in the earlier disclosure filed on May 11, 2026 was inadvertently stated as May 05, 2026, and the correct effective date of resignation is May 11, 2026. The revised disclosure was filed in compliance with Regulation 30 read with Schedule III, Part A, Para A (7) of the SEBI Listing Regulations, along with SEBI Master Circular No. HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFD-POD2/I/3762/2026 dated 30th January, 2026. ... The company received the resignation letter dated May ... 11, 2 ... 26 from Mr. Sanjay Bharadwaj, citing personal reasons for his departure ... The following details have been provided as required under the applicable SEBI Listing Regulations: ... Bharadwaj | ... Manufacturing, Operations Department | ... Silvassa Plant | ... Nature of Change: | ... : | Personal ... Closing hours of May ... 11, 2026 | ... of Appointment: | ... Applicable | ... Profile (Appointment): | ... The revised resignation disclosure has been made in compliance with the applicable SEBI Listing Regulations. The disclosure was signed by Binal Khosla, Compliance Officer and Company Secretary (Membership No.: A 29802), on behalf of Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd. The company has also made the disclosure available on its official website at https://gandharoil.com/ ."
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,Gandhar Oil Refinery Share Price Surges Over 4%; Board Approves South Africa Subsidiary and Panvel Land Purchase,www.angelone.in,2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.angelone.in/news/stocks/gandhar-oil-refinery-share-price-surges-over-4-board-approves-south-africa-subsidiary-and-panvel-land-purchase,"Gandhar Oil Refinery Share Price Surges Over 4%; Board Approves South Africa Subsidiary and Panvel Land Purchase # Gandhar Oil Refinery Share Price Surges Over 4%; Board Approves South Africa Subsidiary and Panvel Land Purchase Written by: Team Angel One Updated on: 27 May 2026, 5:11 pm IST ... Gandhar Oil Refinery has approved the incorporation of a wholly-owned subsidiary in South Africa and the acquisition of land in Panvel, Maharashtra, as part of its expansion strategy. Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd has announced 2 key growth-oriented decisions following a meeting of its Board of Directors. The company has approved plans to establish a wholly-owned subsidiary in South Africa and has also entered into an agreement to acquire a land parcel in Maharashtra. The initiatives are aimed at strengthening the company's long-term business platform while creating additional avenues for future expansion in domestic and international markets. ## Board Clears South Africa Subsidiary Proposal The board has approved the incorporation of a wholly-owned subsidiary in South Africa. The proposed entity is expected to support the company's international business ambitions and provide a dedicated platform for pursuing opportunities in overseas markets. The move marks a step towards expanding Gandhar Oil Refinery's global presence and strengthening its ability to cater to customers beyond India through a localised operating structure. ... ## Company To Acquire Land in Panvel In addition to the overseas expansion plan, the company has approved an agreement for the purchase of land located at Village Kherane Khurd, Taluka Panvel, District Raigad in Maharashtra. The land parcel measures approximately 21,551 square metres. While the company has not disclosed specific development plans for the property, the acquisition is expected to support future infrastructure, operational or expansion requirements. The transaction reflects Gandhar Oil Refinery's focus on creating capacity for future growth and enhancing its asset base. ## Gandhar Oil Refinery Share Price Performance As of May 27, 2026, at 9:20 AM, Gandhar Oil Refinery share price is trading at ₹170.56 per share, surges 4.96% from its previous closing price. ## Conclusion The approval of a wholly-owned subsidiary in South Africa and the acquisition of a strategic land parcel in Panvel highlight Gandhar Oil Refinery's intent to strengthen its growth infrastructure. The twin initiatives could support the company's future expansion plans across both domestic and international markets. Published on: May 27, 2026, 11:40 AM IST"
GANDHAR OIL REFINERY,,,,Exa,"Gandhar Oil Profit surges 3 times while the margins expand 230bps YoY, focus shifts towards FMCG and Consumer Industry – The Report World",thereportworld.in (cradmin),2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thereportworld.in/gandhar-oil-profit-surges-3-times-while-the-margins-expand-230bps-yoy-focus-shifts-towards-fmcg-and-consumer-industry/,"Gandhar Oil Profit surges 3 times while the margins expand 230bps YoY, focus shifts towards FMCG and Consumer Industry – The Report World ... - Gandhar Oil Profit surges 3 times while the margins expand 230bps YoY, focus shifts towards FMCG and Consumer Industry ... Mumbai, 27th May, 2026: Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Ltd a leading manufacturer of white oils by revenue, engaged in producing Pharmaceutical, Health Care, and Performance Oil (PHPO), Process Insulating Oil (PIO) and Lubricants, has announced its Financial Results for the quarter and full year ended March 31, 2026. ... Key Highlights of the Results: ... - Consolidated Manufacturing Sales Volumes for FY26 stood at 5,45,755 KL, up by 9% from 5,00,231 KL in FY25 - Consolidated Revenues for the Q4FY26 at Rs 1,093.4 Cr compared to Rs 961.7 Cr in Q4FY25, while for FY26, it stood at Rs 4,241.2 compared to Rs 3,896.9 Cr in FY25 ... - Consolidated EBITDA for Q4FY26 stood at Rs 63.6 Cr, up by 88% from Rs 33.6 Cr in Q4FY25. EBITDA for FY26 stood at Rs 234.5 Cr, compared to Rs 175.6 Cr in FY25 - Consolidated PAT for Q4FY26 stood at Rs 37 Cr, up by 201% from Rs 12.3 Cr in Q4FY25, while for FY26 stood at Rs 137.2 Cr compared to Rs 83.5 Cr in FY25 ... - For FY26, the consolidated revenue breakdown is as follows: PHPO leads with 48%, Lubricants account for 27%, Channel Partners contribute 14.81% and PIO represents 10.19% ... Commenting on the Results, Aslesh Parekh, Joint Managing Director said, “We delivered a strong close to FY26, supported by sustained momentum in domestic demand and a continued strategic focus on higher-margin PHPO products. This performance was achieved despite a challenging global environment characterized by macroeconomic pressures, ongoing logistical constraints, and volatility arising from the Middle East geopolitical situation, including the temporary closure of the Strait of Hormuz, which led to a sharp increase in oil prices. Notwithstanding these headwinds, we recorded robust performance across all parameters. In the fourth quarter of FY26, revenue stood at Rs 1,093 crore, reflecting a year-on-year increase of 14%. Operational profitability remained robust, with EBITDA rising by 88% to Rs 64 crore, while profit after tax (PAT) grew by 201% to Rs 37 crore, supported by a favorable product mix and improved operating efficiencies. For the full year, revenue reached Rs 4,241 crore, with EBITDA of Rs 234 crore. This growth was underpinned by manufacturing sales volumes of 5,45,755 KL, representing a 9% increase over the previous year. The PHPO segment continued to be the primary growth driver, contributing 48% of total revenue, driven by strong demand from the personal care and healthcare sectors. Looking ahead, the domestic demand environment remains encouraging. Additionally, the anticipated easing of international logistical constraints, along with stabilizing input costs, is expected to further support business momentum. This provides us with confidence in our near- to medium-term growth outlook but we continue to remain cautious and watchful.” ... Gandhar Oil Refinery (India) Limited is a known name in the world of specialty oils. Our Company is a leading manufacturer of white oils by revenue with a growing focus on the consumer and healthcare end-industries. We have a diversified customer base. We produce a broad variety of specialty oils and lubricants such as White oils, waxes, jellies, automotive oils, industrial oils, transformer oils and rubber processing oils. Our products are sold under our flagship brand “Divyol”."
