REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Canopius grows profit while cutting Bermuda contracts on price | Insurance Business,www.insurancebusinessmag.com (Jonalyn Cueto),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.insurancebusinessmag.com/uk/news/breaking-news/canopius-grows-profit-while-cutting-bermuda-contracts-on-price-585304.aspx,"Canopius grows profit while cutting Bermuda contracts on price | Insurance Business ... # Canopius grows profit while cutting Bermuda contracts on price ... ### Casualty, cyber and financial lines are where this carrier is still chasing business - property and reinsurance are a different ... Canopius Group reported a 10% rise in insurance contract written premium to US$2.66 billion (1H25: US$2.41 billion) and an improved undiscounted combined ratio of 87.3% (1H25: 89.7%) for the six months to 30 June 2026, even as rates fell 7% across its overall portfolio amid continued softening in several commercial insurance lines. ... Net insurance revenue rose 15% to US$1.59 billion (1H25: US$1.39 billion), and profit after tax increased 76% to US$391 million (1H25: US$222 million), largely reflecting the sale of Vave Holdings to a subsidiary of Acrisure; excluding that sale, profit after tax rose 18% to US$261 million. Annualised return on opening tangible equity was 23.2%, against 24.5% a year earlier. Tangible net asset value rose 12% to US$2.50 billion. ... Property faced strong competition on rate, particularly in direct and facultative business, though delegated authorities still delivered underlying growth. Casualty saw better rate alongside organic growth. Cyber ""continues to perform well"" despite rate pressure, and reinsurance performed satisfactorily ""despite considerable pressure on rate,"" aided by active portfolio management. Natural resources continued to suffer from over-capacity and pressure on signings. ... Specialty performed satisfactorily in a relatively stable rate environment, Portfolio Solutions saw substantial development from new broker facilities including in the US, and financial lines recorded good growth on rising submission volume, giving Canopius broader-based growth than the headline property and casualty lines alone suggest. ... By region, the UK delivered positive performance overall even as much of the portfolio faced rate pressure in a competitive environment, with Canopius saying its propositions continue to be well received by the market while it remains disciplined where it cannot achieve required rate. In the US, Portfolio Solutions continues to attract significant wholesale market interest; property saw pressure on rate ""although rate adequacy remains robust,"" while casualty, cyber, specialty and financial lines all continued to develop positively. In Bermuda, Canopius non-renewed several significant contracts based on price, though the operation continues to benefit from new underwriting capabilities and a broadening client and product base. APAC recorded solid growth across property and casualty, reinsurance and specialty, with strong retention. ... The result comes as Lloyd's warns the market is ""softening"" rather than ""soft,"" and could ""turn on a knife edge,"" according to chief of market performance Rachel Turk, speaking in January 2026. A separate Oxbow Partners report found net underwriting results across the Lloyd's market fell 14% to £4.8 billion in 2024, down from £5.5 billion in 2023. ... Hiscox, which reported a day earlier, posted insurance contract written premiums of US$3.24 billion, up 10.1%, and an improved undiscounted combined ratio of 90.4% from 92.6%. The insurer also provided more detailed underwriting disclosures, reporting London Market rates down 5% overall, major property rates down 14%, and the non-renewal of 17% of major property risks and 23% of its power and renewables portfolio. Chief underwriting officer Jo Musselle said the results reflected ""lots of different microcycles"" across the business. ... ""Despite a more challenging trading environment, the breadth and diversity of our business and the momentum we have generated in recent periods continues to be reflected in premium growth and ongoing rate adequacy. Once again, we delivered growth across all business regions - the UK, US, Bermuda and APAC - achieving year-on-year growth of 10%, a result of which we are collectively proud,"" said group chief executive Neil Robertson. He added the group's investment portfolio ""continues to deliver strong levels of income with low volatility as our asset base grows."" ... Robertson said the group will ""continue to apply a disciplined and selective approach to capital allocation with a strongly held commitment to pricing integrity"" as competition intensifies. ... Canopius’s 7% portfolio-wide rate decline sits alongside Bermuda contract non-renewals and property rate pressure most acute in D&F and, to a lesser extent, US markets. By contrast, casualty is an area of improving rate alongside organic growth, and cyber is an area of continued appetite despite rate pressure, suggesting brokers may find more favourable conditions placing those two classes with this carrier through the second half. The additional strength in Portfolio Solutions, particularly its US broker-facility growth, and in financial lines on rising submission volume, gives brokers two further, less-obvious areas of active appetite worth testing alongside the headline casualty and cyber picture. ... - Canopius appoints group COO ahead of international expansion - Canopius backs Manchester as new global operations hub"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"Regus opens HQ office, coworking space near downtown Allen | Allen | Community Impact",communityimpact.com (Mary Katherine Shapiro),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://communityimpact.com/allen/business/regus-opens-hq-office-coworking-space-near-downtown-allen/,"Regus opens HQ office, coworking space near downtown Allen | Allen | Community Impact ... # Regus opens HQ office, coworking space near downtown Allen ... Published August 6, 2026 at 3:00 p.m. CT ... HQ is now open in Allen, Gillett Commercial owner Bucky Gillett said. ... Developed by Regus, HQ offers office space rentals for individuals and teams, as well as coworking spaces, per its website. HQ is part of the International Workplace Group network. ... HQ takes up about 17,000 square feet inside The Asher, a business center developed by Gillett Commercial. ... - Opened August 3 - 400 N. Allen Drive, Ste. 104-107, Allen - www.hq.com/en"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,CapitaLand Ascott Trust Buying Coliwoo Singapore Co-Living Asset - Mingtiandi,www.mingtiandi.com (Christopher Caillavet),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mingtiandi.com/real-estate/finance/capitaland-ascott-trust-buying-coliwoo-singapore-co-living-asset/,"CapitaLand Ascott Trust Buying Coliwoo Singapore Co-Living Asset - Mingtiandi ... CapitaLand Ascott Trust has agreed to buy a 212-room co-living property on the fringe of Singapore’s downtown for S$134 million ($104.5 million), as the SGX-listed lodging REIT recycles proceeds from a recent hotel disposal into a higher-yielding living sector asset. ... CLAS is buying Coliwoo Midtown in the Bugis-Bras Basah precinct at a 4.1 percent EBITDA yield, using capital from its S$360 million divestment of The Robertson House by The Crest Collection, the trust’s managers said Thursday in a release. The entry yield is 180 basis points above the Robertson Quay hotel’s 2.3 percent exit yield. ... The agreed price works out to S$632,075 ($493,100) per key. CLAS expects the acquisition to lift pro forma distribution per stapled security by 2.4 percent, with completion targeted for the fourth quarter of 2026 and the property contributing to income immediately thereafter. ... “This yield-accretive acquisition demonstrates strong execution of CLAS’s portfolio reconstitution strategy and commitment to deliver stable DPS,” said Serena Teo, CEO of the managers, which are owned by Temasek-controlled CapitaLand Investment. The deal raises living assets to 19.5 percent of CLAS’s portfolio value, moving the trust closer to its medium-term target of 25 to 30 percent. ... Coliwoo Midtown reopened in March after a major refurbishment and recorded average occupancy of nearly 90 percent in July, four months after launching. The property serves corporate professionals, expatriates, international students and local residents, with average stays expected to reach six to nine months once operations stabilise. ... Coliwoo Midtown occupies a 99-year leasehold site with a tenure commencing in May 1978 and has 62,856 square feet (5,839 square metres) of gross floor area. Savills valued the property at S$130 million as of 1 August, putting the transaction price 3.1 percent above the independent appraisal. ... CLAS sees an opportunity to extend the remaining 51-year lease to a fresh 99-year tenure, subject to regulatory approval. The acquisition will give the trust five Singapore properties and increase the country’s share of portfolio value to 17 percent from 15.4 percent. ... On the sell side, Coliwoo’s 80 percent-owned project company said the disposal constitutes a major transaction requiring shareholder approval and is expected to generate a gross gain of S$9.2 million. ... “The sale and leaseback of a sizeable asset such as Coliwoo Midtown not only underscores our commitment to an asset-light and capital-efficient growth strategy, but also demonstrates our ability to transform underutilised properties into institutional-grade investment assets,” Coliwoo chairman and CEO Kelvin Lim said in a release. Coliwoo will lease the property for 10 years and retain all 212 rooms in its managed portfolio. ... The sale will generate S$41 million in available cash after transaction expenses and debt repayment, with the funds earmarked for working capital and project development. LHN listed Coliwoo on the Singapore Exchange last November after raising S$101 million in gross proceeds from the co-living unit’s initial public offering. ... For the six months through March, Coliwoo posted revenue of S$26.9 million, up 16.6 percent from a year earlier, with average occupancy of 97 percent across 3,568 rooms. The operator is also marketing seven Singapore properties for a combined S$218.5 million, with several parties having submitted expressions of interest. ... Coliwoo last month opened Coliwoo Resort Changi, a 380-room resort-style co-living property created from a former state-owned holiday chalet in Pasir Ris. First announced in June 2025 as a 350-key project, the completed resort includes pools, a gym, co-working and social spaces across a 380,866 square foot site, extending the operator’s expansion into eastern Singapore."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Primus Partners opens Gurugram hub as GCCs shift beyond Bengaluru - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Sharmistha Mukherjee),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/company/corporate-trends/primus-partners-opens-gurugram-hub-as-gccs-shift-beyond-bengaluru/articleshow/132995890.cms,"Primus Partners opens Gurugram hub as GCCs shift beyond Bengaluru - The Economic Times # Primus Partners opens Gurugram hub as GCCs shift beyond Bengaluru Primus Partners opens Gurugram hub as GCCs shift beyond Bengaluru ... Primus Partners launched its Global Capability Hub in Gurugram. The firm now offers ""Build & Operate"" services for multinational companies. Linde-Wiemann, a German automotive supplier, is the hub's first client. Gurugram is becoming a prime destination for Global Capability Centres. Haryana's policy and talent pool attract firms to the region. ... Primus Partners launched its Global Capability Hub in Gurugram (Representative image) New Delhi: Primus Partners has launched its Global Capability Hub in Gurugram, repositioning itself from a GCC advisory firm into an end-to-end “Build & Operate” partner covering strategy, talent, technology and operations. The hub’s first client is Linde-Wiemann, a Germany-based Tier-1 automotive supplier, which will run a technology-focused centre from Gurugram supporting ERP, business intelligence, finance, and sales and supply chain functions, with plans to expand into engineering and digital design. Also Read: India's GCCs create world-class research, but rarely own the IP that generates future wealth ... Nilaya Varma, Global CEO of Primus Partners, said the firm’s role is evolving. “We are taking the next step by helping them build, operate and scale these centres from India,” he said. Speaking on the company’s decision to invest in Haryana, Varma said Gurugram is fast becoming an attractive destination for multinational Global Capability Centres (GCCs), as Haryana’s newly announced GCC Policy 2026 and the city’s deep talent pool have started drawing firms that were traditionally anchored in Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Pune. ##"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Bain Capital to buy Gong cha as MBK grapples with regulatory pressure,www.cnbc.com (Jenny Lee),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/06/bain-capital-to-buy-gong-cha-as-mbk-grapples-with-regulatory-pressure.html,"Bain Capital to buy Gong cha as MBK grapples with regulatory pressure ... - Bain Capital announced Thursday it will acquire global bubble tea chain Gong cha. - The regulatory pressure in South Korea made it difficult for MBK to pursue the acquisition on its own, according to a source familiar with the matter. - Gong cha operates around 2,200 stores globally with leading positions in the Asia-Pacific region. ... Bain Capital won a battle to buy a global bubble tea chain as one of its top rivals remains under scrutiny from South Korean regulators. ... Bain on Thursday announced it has agreed to acquire Gong cha from U.S.-based private equity firm TA Associates. MBK Partners, one of the largest private equity firms in Asia, was among the bidders for the chain and had been seeking a Korean private equity partner for a joint bid, according to communications seen by CNBC. ... Under the proposed structure, MBK was to acquire Gong cha's Japan business, while its partner was to take over the company's South Korean operations, according to two people familiar with the matter said. ... But MBK's bid came as the private equity firm faced mounting regulatory scrutiny in South Korea following the collapse of its portfolio company Homeplus, once the country's second-largest supermarket chain by market share, according to a person familiar with the matter. The heightened regulatory pressure made it difficult for MBK to secure the deal on its own, given Gong cha's significant operations in South Korea, the person added. ... Gong cha, which offers a wide range of tea and fruit-based beverages, operates more than 2,200 stores worldwide, including in the U.S. and Central America. Bain said it will continue expanding Gong cha in Japan and South Korea, where the brand has a strong footprint, while accelerating growth in the U.S., according to a press release."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Mindspace REIT’s Q1 net operating income rises 28% to Rs 788 crore - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Kailash Babar),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/services/property-/-cstruction/mindspace-business-parks-reit-q1-net-operating-income-rs-788-cr-up-27-8/articleshow/132937811.cms,"Mindspace REIT’s Q1 net operating income rises 28% to Rs 788 crore - The Economic Times ... 1 net operating income rises 2 ... % to Rs ... 88 crore ... Mindspace REIT’s Q1 net operating income rises 28% to Rs 788 crore ... Mindspace REIT achieved a remarkable 27.8% growth in net operating income this quarter. The firm broadened its development pipeline by adding new office spaces and hotels, declaring a record quarterly distribution per unit of Rs 6.67. The period also saw gross leasing of nearly 0.9 million square feet, leading to a total portfolio size of about 46.2 million square feet. ... MUMBAI: Mindspace Business Parks REIT has reported a 27.8% year-on-year rise in net operating income(NOI) at Rs 788 crore for the quarter ended June, driven by healthy leasing activity, higher rentals and the addition of new assets.The office REIT expanded its development pipeline with two new office buildings and two hotels totalling 1.7 million sq ft across Pune, Mumbai and Hyderabad.The company has also announced its highest-ever quarterly distribution per unit(DPU) of Rs 6.67, up 15.2% from a year earlier. Revenue from operations rose 26.4% on-year to Rs 951 crore during the quarter from Rs 752 crore a year ago. ... “The performance reflects the strength of our portfolio, the quality of assets, and disciplined execution. With most of our under-construction office assets due for delivery over the next twelve months already pre-committed, demand for our campuses remains strong. Building on this momentum, we have started work on two new office projects and hotels to further enhance our integrated campus ecosystems and elevate the occupier experience,"" said Ramesh Nair, MD and CEO, Mindspace REIT.During the quarter, the REIT recorded gross leasing of about 0.9 million sq ft In-place rents across the portfolio stood at about Rs 81 per sq. ft. per month, with a mark-to-market rental potential of about 19.6%. ... The REIT is actively developing an under-construction pipeline of 6.6 million sq ft and has launched two new office buildings and two hotels spanning about 1.7 million sq ft across Pune, Mumbai and Hyderabad. With these additions, its total portfolio has expanded to about 46.2 million sq ft. ... As part of its diversification strategy, Mindspace REIT has announced two hotels in Pune and Hyderabad that have been pre-let to Chalet Hotels, taking the total number of hotels across its campuses to five. Its data centre portfolio now stands at 1.7 million sq. ft. ... The REIT's gross asset value increased to Rs 51,890 crore following the addition of newly acquired assets. Its loan-to-value ratio stood at about 29.7%, while the cost of debt remained flat sequentially at 7.42% per annum.Mindspace REIT completed the acquisition of a 100% stake in Commerzone Pallikaranai and a 51% stake in International Tech Park Chennai - Radial Road, now re-branded as One Radial. Following these acquisitions, the portfolio's committed occupancy stands at 92.1%.The board declared a distribution of Rs 442 crore for the quarter. The record date for the distribution is August 8. Since listing, the REIT has distributed about Rs 7,201 crore, or about Rs 119 per unit, to unitholders."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG Acquires French Coworking Operator Wojo To Expand European Footprint,allwork.space (Allwork.Space News Team),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://allwork.space/2026/08/iwg-acquires-french-coworking-operator-wojo-to-expand-european-footprint/,"Coworking Operator Wojo To Expand ... Coworking Operator ... ## The acquisition expands IWG's French portfolio to about 157 flexible workspace centers. by Allwork.Space News Team August 4, 2026 The acquisition follows IWG's purchase of Germany's Design Offices, continuing the company's expansion through major European coworking operators. ... International Workplace Group (IWG) has completed its acquisition of French flexible workspace operator Wojo, expanding its presence in France and strengthening its European network. The deal, approved by the French Competition Authority, sees IWG acquire Wojo from Bouygues Immobilier and Accor, according to Coworking Europe. ## IWG ... Founded in 2015 and rebranded as Wojo in 2019, the company operates 17 coworking and flexible office locations across France, including sites in Paris, Lyon, Lille, Bordeaux, Brest, La Défense, and Issy-les-Moulineaux. Its portfolio spans nearly 100,000 square meters and serves more than 900 companies. ... With the acquisition, IWG’s operated network in France grows to approximately 157 flexible workspace centers, adding to its existing brands, including Regus, Spaces, HQ, Signature, Stop & Work, and Factories. ... The acquisition broadens IWG’s hospitality-focused workspace offering and expands its reach across Europe, giving customers access to both companies’ networks. ... The transaction follows IWG’s acquisition of German flexible workspace operator Design Offices earlier this year, reflecting the company’s strategy of expanding through acquisitions alongside organic growth. ... IWG now operates more than 4,000 flexible workspace locations across more than 120 countries, continuing to build its presence in key European markets."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"International Workplace Group: IWG opens four new Regus centres in Noida, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, ETRealty",realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com (www.ETRealty.com),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/iwg-opens-four-new-regus-centres-in-noida-bengaluru-hyderabad/132887590,"International Workplace Group: IWG opens four new Regus centres in Noida, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, ETRealty ... # IWG opens four new Regus centres in Noida, Bengaluru, Hyderabad International Workplace Group has opened four new Regus centres across Noida, Bengaluru and Hyderabad, adding over 3,180 sq metres of flexible workspace. The company plans to expand its India network to over 325 centres over the next three to five years. - Online Bureau ... - Published On Aug 4, 2026 at 03:30 PM IST ... NEW DELHI: International Workplace Group (IWG) has opened four new Regus centres across Noida, Bengaluru and Hyderabad. Together, the centres add more than 3,180 sq metres of flexible workspace to the company's India network. The new centres include Regus Starling Edge and Regus Knowledge Centre in Noida, Regus Trinity Pothraj in Bengaluru, and Regus Fairmount Downtown in Hyderabad. It currently operates 125 centres in India under the Regus, Spaces, HQ and Open Office brands. It has 200 additional centres in the pipeline, which will take its India network to over 325 centres over the next three to five years. - Published"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"Japan's SoftBank telecom unit, Singapore's SC ZEUS , Malaysia's Robust HPC sign AI data center pact for Southeast Asia - TNGlobal",technode.global (Duc Dao),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://technode.global/2026/08/04/japans-softbank-telecom-unit-singapores-sc-zeus-malaysias-robust-hpc-sign-ai-data-center-pact-for-southeast-asia/,"SB Telecom Singapore, a subsidiary of Japan’s SoftBank, Singapore’s SC ZEUS Data Centers, and Malaysia’s Robust HPC Group will collaborate to develop AI data center infrastructure across Southeast Asia, with initial deployments focused on Malaysia, Thailand, Indonesia, and Vietnam. ... The three sides signed a memorandum of understanding for the move, effective August 1, 2026, SB Telecom Singapore said in a statement on Monday. ... Under the three-way agreement, SC ZEUS Data Centers will source land, design, build, and operate core data center infrastructure. Robust HPC Group will handle the procurement, setup, and management of high-performance GPU clusters. SB Telecom Singapore will manage data hall fit-out, ICT infrastructure integration, localised deployment support, and connectivity solutions. ... Together, the parties will develop AI Factory solutions and explore GPU-as-a-Service platforms and AI Token Factory commercial models. ... The planned facilities will feature liquid cooling infrastructure, 800 VDC architecture, and low-latency networking. The partnership covers two primary areas: GPU infrastructure supply, build, and operation; and dedicated AI data center construction and development across the region. ... Hisao Inoue, Managing Director of SB Telecom Singapore, said the alliance combines ICT connectivity, SC ZEUS’s infrastructure capabilities, and Robust HPC’s supercomputing expertise to deliver scalable, real-time computing environments for AI workloads across Southeast Asia. ... Singapore tightens data center growth as Johor, Bangkok, Jakarta race ahead"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Segro Accepts Prologis' £14B Takeover Offer,"www.bisnow.com (Mike Phillips, UK Editor)",2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bisnow.com/news/national/industrial/segro-accepts-prologis-offer,"Segro Accepts Prologis' £14B Takeover Offer ... The dance is over. Segro has accepted a £14.3B takeover offer from U.S. giant Prologis. ... The deal will be the largest-ever European real estate deal and one of the largest deals for any European company in any sector to be struck this year. ... And in one swoop, it removes 20% of the market capitalisation of the UK listed real estate sector — Segro, with a 100-year history, was the largest listed UK property company by far. ... The acquisition tips Prologis’ assets under management to just over $200B (£149B) and creates a European portfolio spanning 368M SF. Its market capitalisation was $138B before the deal was announced, making it the world’s second-largest REIT. ... The courtship goes back to March 2024, when Prologis first bid for Segro, an offer that was never made public. Prologis made four bids from June to July of this year before sealing the deal. ... The value and deliverability of data centres has been a key question during takeover talks between the two companies, and the combined company will have a short- to medium-term data centre development pipeline of 6.2 gigawatts, with another potential 12.5 GW in longer-term opportunities identified. ... Prologis initially offered £12.6B for Segro in June, the same level as the European firm’s net asset value. Segro’s board dismissed that offer as an attempt to buy the company “on the cheap.” ... The offer that was eventually accepted was a 14% premium to Segro’s 30 June net asset value and a 39% premium to its share price before Prologis’ bid was revealed. ... Brookfield Accelerates Launch Of Giant Real Estate Fund As Market Improves ... Brookfield Accelerates Launch Of Giant Real Estate Fund As Market Improves"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG bets on hybrid work with PHL expansion - eBizToday,ebiztoday.news (ebiztoday.news),2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ebiztoday.news/index.php/2026/08/01/iwg-bets-on-hybrid-work-with-phl-expansion/,"INTERNATIONAL Workplace Group (IWG) plans to expand its Philippine network to 76 locations by the top of 2026, betting on continued demand for hybrid work as flexible workspaces are expected to account for 30% of the industrial real estate market by 2030. ... The worldwide flexible workspace provider is adding five centers in Taguig, Bohol, and Cebu while introducing Humanly, its workspace brand for healthcare and wellness professionals, to the Philippine market with its first facility in Aurora. ... “Our move to supply purpose-designed facilities for the healthcare and wellness sector reflects how the role of flexible workspace platforms is evolving. We’re past the purpose where these spaces are simply offices,” IWG Philippines Country Head Rowena Natividad said in a press release on Thursday. ... The five recent locations are HQ Plaza Helena and Regus Island Central Mactan in Cebu; Regus Savya Financial Center and Regus Alveo Park Triangle Tower in Taguig; and Humanly APECO Super Health Center in Aurora. ... Humanly’s first Philippine site will offer treatment rooms, therapy suites, and consultation spaces for medical and wellness professionals. ... IWG said the expansion reflects growing demand for hybrid work arrangements as businesses proceed moving away from traditional office setups. ... The corporate cited market data showing that 82% of organizations within the Philippines have adopted hybrid work models, while about one-third plan to take a position further in workplace upgrades this 12 months. ... “Flexible and decentralized working is a megatrend, and it’s everlasting. Leading academic research points to somewhere between 30% and 40% of white-collar staff settling into this model for good,” IWG Executive Chairman Mark Dixon said. ... In 2025, IWG signed 1,132 recent locations and opened 782 centers worldwide. ... Its global network now spans greater than 5,000 locations across greater than 120 countries, including the Philippines. — Juliana Chloe A. Gonzales"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG bets on hybrid work with PHL expansion - BusinessWorld Online,bworldonline.com (CEDTyClea),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bworldonline.com/corporate/2026/07/31/767097/iwg-bets-on-hybrid-work-with-phl-expansion/,"IWG bets on hybrid work with PHL expansion - BusinessWorld Online ... INTERNATIONAL Workplace Group (IWG) plans to expand its Philippine network to 76 locations by the end of 2026, betting on continued demand for hybrid work as flexible workspaces are expected to account for 30% of the commercial real estate market by 2030. ... The global flexible workspace provider is adding five centers in Taguig, Bohol, and Cebu while introducing Humanly, its workspace brand for healthcare and wellness professionals, to the Philippine market with its first facility in Aurora. ... “Our move to provide purpose-designed facilities for the healthcare and wellness sector reflects how the role of flexible workspace platforms is evolving. We’re past the point where these spaces are simply offices,” IWG Philippines Country Head Rowena Natividad said in a statement on Thursday. ... The five new locations are HQ Plaza Helena and Regus Island Central Mactan in Cebu; Regus Savya Financial Center and Regus Alveo Park Triangle Tower in Taguig; and Humanly APECO Super Health Center in Aurora. ... site will offer treatment rooms, therapy suites, and consultation spaces for medical and wellness professionals. ... IWG said the expansion reflects growing demand for hybrid work arrangements as businesses continue moving away from traditional office setups. ... The company cited market data showing that 82% of organizations in the Philippines have adopted hybrid work models, while about one-third plan to invest further in workplace upgrades this year. ... “Flexible and decentralized working is a megatrend, and it’s permanent. Leading academic research points to somewhere between 30% and ... 0% of white-collar workers settling into this model for good,” IWG Executive ... Mark Dixon said. ... In 2025, IWG signed 1,132 new locations and opened 782 centers worldwide. ... Its global network now spans more than 5,000 locations across more than 120 countries, including the Philippines. — Juliana Chloe A. Gonzales"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"International Workplace Group launches new healthcare and wellness brand, Humanly, in Aurora as part of five-center expansion in the Philippines – onetechavenue",onetechavenue.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://onetechavenue.com/international-workplace-group-launches-new-healthcare-and-wellness-brand-humanly-in-aurora-as-part-of-five-center-expansion-in-the-philippines/,"International Workplace Group launches new healthcare and wellness brand, Humanly, in Aurora as part of five-center expansion in the Philippines – onetechavenue ... # International Workplace Group launches new healthcare and wellness brand, Humanly, in Aurora as part of five-center expansion in the Philippines ... - IWG’s expansion spans both established business districts and emerging provincial markets, reflecting growing demand for flexible workspaces beyond Metro Manila. - Each new center is designed to support organizations of all sizes, offering a full suite of flexible workspace solutions including co-working areas, private offices, and fully equipped meeting rooms. - Humanly APECO Super Health Center in Casiguran, Aurora, marks the first Humanly location in the Philippines. The facility provides purpose-designed space for medical, therapy, wellness, and allied healthcare practitioners. ... Manila, Philippines – International Workplace Group(IWG), the world’s largest platform for work with brands including https://protect.checkpoint.com/v2/___https:/www.spacesworks.com/___.bXQtcHJvZC1jcC1ldXcyLTE6bmV4dDE1OmM6bzozZWQ5Y2JiNDJhZWVlZDYyZDZiZmI5MWRlNmNlMTZiNTo2OjI4NTY6OGFmMzkxYzhjMzkyMjNlNmNiNTMxYWE5ZjNiYTQyNDhkMjhmZDAyMjU1MGJkNGJkNWE5Y2ViMjJiZmUwYjkwMTpwOkY Spaces and https://protect.checkpoint.com/v2/___https:/www.regus.com___.bXQtcHJvZC1jcC1ldXcyLTE6bmV4dDE1OmM6bzozZWQ5Y2JiNDJhZWVlZDYyZDZiZmI5MWRlNmNlMTZiNTo2OmIzOWE6ZGI4NDhmYmRhYTVhNmU2NTRjM2ZjZDUwNDJkM2VkMmEyMDVkNWU1YmMyZTE2MzIyMDQ0N2I2NjAwMTAzOGRkODpwOkY Regus, announces the opening of five new workspaces in the Philippines in 2026 including the launch of its first Humanly location in the country at the APECO Super Health Center in Casiguran, Aurora, alongside four new HQ and Regus centers in Bohol, Lapu-Lapu City, and Taguig City. ... Each new center is designed to support organizations of all sizes, offering a full suite of flexible workspace solutions including co-working areas, private offices, and fully equipped meeting rooms. The new locations in the Philippines are: ... - HQ Plaza Helena in Panglao Island, Bohol - Regus Island Central Mactan in Lapu Lapu City - Regus Savya Financial Center in Arca South, Taguig - Regus Alveo Park Triangle Tower in Alveo Park Triangle Tower, Taguig - Humanly APECO Super Health Center in Casiguran, Aurora ... IWG’s new Humanly format provides flexible, purpose-designed space for medical, therapy, wellness, beauty and fitness practitioners, enabling professionals to access fully equipped facilities without the upfront investment and long-term commitments associated with traditional premises. ... The Humanly APECO Super Health Center in Casiguran is designed specifically for healthcare and wellness practioners and their clients. Humanly offers a range of specialist treatment and consultation spaces including private consultation rooms, therapy suites, treatment rooms, and reception facilities. It enables professionals to provide high-quality care in a professional environment without the overheads of a traditional clinic. ... IWG Philippines continues to advance its ambition of adding 29 locations nationwide and growing its local network to 76 centers by the end of 2026, in line with increasing demand for hybrid and flexible working solutions. ... According to the latest IWG research, more than 83% of CEOs have put policies in place enabling their employees and teams to embrace flexible working from more than one location. And its 2026 Asia Pacific Workplace Insights Report, Colliers reports that 82% of organizations in the Philippines are already operating under hybrid work models, with 32% planning to invest further in workplace upgrades over the coming year. As companies of all sizes continue to shift toward more flexible and decentralized operating models, the report highlights accelerating structural change in the commercial real estate landscape. By 2030, flexible workspaces are expected to account for around 30% of total commercial real estates. ... Our move to provide purpose-designed facilities for the healthcare and wellness sector reflects how the role of flexible workspace platforms is evolving. We’re past the point where these spaces are simply offices. They’re becoming essential infrastructure that enables growth across healthcare, enterprise services, and regional development alike.” ... “We’re already operating in more than 120 countries, and we intend to keep expanding, going deeper into markets around the world. Much of that growth is happening closer to where people actually live, so that millions of people can finally say goodbye to the long daily commute. ... Flexible and decentralized ... atrend, and it’s permanent. Leading academic research points to somewhere between 30% and ... 40% ... white-collar ... settling into this model for good. ... ’s why our industry is ... , and why I ... is growing faster than at any ... in our more than 35-year history ... benefits for people, for ... In 2025, International Workplace Group signed 1,132 locations and opened 782 new centers, counting 85% of Fortune 500 companies among its customer base. The Group reached a significant milestone, signing and opening more new locations in a single year than in the first two decades of its operations combined. ... Today, the Group’s global network comprises more than one million rooms across over 120 countries, supported by a substantial development pipeline that is expected to further accelerate growth in the years ahead."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Regency Centers Reports Second Quarter 2026 Results,www.globenewswire.com (Regency Centers Corporation),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/29/3335597/37116/en/Regency-Centers-Reports-Second-Quarter-2026-Results.html,"JACKSONVILLE, Fla., July 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Regency Centers Corporation (“Regency Centers,” “Regency” or the “Company”) (Nasdaq: REG) today reported financial and operating results for the period ended June 30, 2026, and provided updated 2026 earnings guidance. For the three months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, Net Income Attributable to Common Shareholders was $0.61 and $0.56, respectively, per diluted share. ... - Reported Nareit Funds From Operations (""FFO"") of $1.21 per diluted share and Core Operating Earnings of $1.16 per diluted share - Increased quarterly Same Property Net Operating Income (""NOI"") year-over-year by 3.8% - Raised full year 2026 Nareit FFO guidance to a range of $4.84 to $4.88 per diluted share and 2026 Core Operating Earnings guidance to a range of $4.62 to $4.66 per diluted share - The midpoint of 2026 Core Operating Earnings guidance now represents year-over-year growth exceeding 5% - Raised full year 2026 guidance for Same Property NOI growth to a range of 3.7% to 4.1% year-over-year ... - Same Property percent leased ended the quarter at 96.9%, up 40 basis points year-over-year, and Same Property percent commenced ended the quarter at 94.5%, up 50 basis points year-over-year ... - Executed 2.1 million square feet of comparable new and renewal leases during the quarter at blended rent spreads of 10.4% on a cash basis and 19.5% on a straight-lined basis ... - Started $68 million of ground-up development and redevelopment projects - As of June 30, 2026, Regency's in-process development and redevelopment projects had estimated net project costs of $680 million at a blended estimated yield of approximately 9% - Acquired one shopping center and two outparcels for a total of approximately $48 million, or $19 million at Regency's share ... - Issued the Company's annual Corporate Responsibility report, highlighting achievements and progress within our corporate responsibility program - Subsequent to quarter end, acquired two shopping centers for $101 million, or $42 million at Regency's share ... “Our team delivered another excellent quarter, highlighted by strong earnings and NOI growth, robust tenant demand, and continued momentum across our investments platform,” said Lisa Palmer, President and Chief Executive Officer. “These results reflect the strength of our strategy, anchored by our high-quality portfolio, leading national development program, fortress balance sheet and exceptional team. Together, these position us to drive attractive, sustainable growth and long-term value for our shareholders.” ... - During the three months ended June 30, 2026, Regency executed approximately 2.1 million square feet of comparable new and renewal leases at a blended cash rent spread of +10.4% and a blended straight-lined rent spread of +19.5%. - During the twelve months ended June 30, 2026, Regency executed approximately 7.1 million square feet of comparable new and renewal leases at a blended cash rent spread of +11.8% and a blended straight-lined rent spread of +22.7%. ... - On May 28, 2026, Regency issued its annual Corporate Responsibility Report, demonstrating the Company’s continued leadership in and commitment to ... - For the three months ended June 30, 2026, the Company started ground-up development and redevelopment projects with estimated net project costs of approximately $68 million, at the Company's share. - - Second quarter starts included The Berkeley at Durbin Park, a $55 million Whole Foods and TJ Maxx-anchored ground-up development project in Jacksonville, FL. ... - For the three months ended June 30, 2026, the Company completed approximately $20 million of redevelopment projects. - As of June 30, 2026, Regency’s in-process development and redevelopment projects had estimated net project costs of $680 million at the Company’s share, 49% of which had been incurred. ... - On June 11, 2026, the Company acquired Shops at Highland Walk in Denver, CO, a 95,000 square foot shopping center anchored by King Soopers. - - The property was acquired through the Company's State of Oregon joint venture for approximately $37 million, or $7 million at Regency's share. ... - Subsequent to quarter end, on July 8, 2026, the Company acquired Franklin Crossing in Franklin Lakes, NJ, an 88,000 square foot shopping center anchored by Stop & Shop, for $27 million. - Subsequent to quarter end, on July 14, 2026, the Company acquired Cornerstone at Westford in Westford, MA, a 236,000 square foot shopping center anchored by Market Basket. - - The property was acquired through the Company's State of Oregon joint venture for $74 million, or $15 million at Regency's share. ... Regency Centers is providing updated 2026 Guidance, as summarized in the table below. Please refer to the Company’s second quarter 2026 ""Earnings Presentation"" and ""Quarterly Supplemental Disclosure"" for additional detail. All materials are posted on the Company’s website at investors.regencycenters.com. ... | Same property NOI growth | | 4.1% | +3.7% to +4.1% | +3.25% to +3.75% | ... Regency Centers is a preeminent national owner, operator, and developer of shopping centers located in suburban trade areas with compelling demographics. Our portfolio includes thriving properties merchandised with highly productive grocers, restaurants, service providers, and best-in-class retailers that connect to their neighborhoods, communities, and customers. Operating as a fully integrated real estate company, Regency Centers is a qualified real estate investment trust (REIT) that is self-administered, self-managed, and an S&P 500 Index member. For more information, please visit RegencyCenters.com. ... The Company has published additional financial information in its second quarter 2026 supplemental package that may help investors estimate earnings. A copy of the Company’s second quarter 2026 supplemental package will be available on the Company's website at investors.regencycenters.com or by written request to: Investor Relations, Regency Centers Corporation, One Independent Drive, Suite 114, Jacksonville, Florida, 32202. The supplemental package contains more detailed financial and property results including financial statements, an outstanding debt summary, acquisition and development activity, investments in partnerships, information pertaining to securities issued other than common stock, property details, a significant tenant rent report and a lease expiration table in addition to earnings and valuation guidance assumptions. The information provided in the supplemental package is unaudited and includes non-GAAP measures, and there can be no assurance that the information will not vary from the final information in the Company’s Form 10-Q for the period ended June 30, 2026. Regency may, but assumes no obligation to, update information in the supplemental package from time to time. ... Our real estate assets may decline in value and be subject to impairment losses which may reduce our net income. We face risks associated with development, redevelopment, and expansion of properties. We face risks associated with the development of mixed-use commercial properties. We face risks associated with the acquisition of properties. We may be unable to sell properties when desired because of market conditions. Changes in tax laws could impact our acquisition or disposition of real estate. ... Regency Centers Invites You to Join Its Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Conference Call ... JACKSONVILLE, Fla., June 25, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Regency Centers Corporation (“Regency Centers” or the “Company”) (NASDAQ: REG) will announce its second quarter 2026 earnings results on... ... Regency Centers Releases 2025 Corporate Responsibility Report ... JACKSONVILLE, Fla., May 28, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Regency Centers Corporation (“Regency”, “Regency Centers” or the “Company”) (Nasdaq:REG) today released its 2025 Corporate Responsibility Report...."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Swiss Coworking Company Adds 5 New Locations to Washington Roster | News | southsoundbiz.com,www.southsoundbiz.com (J.A. Aleman),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.southsoundbiz.com/news/swiss-coworking-company-adds-5-new-locations-to-washington-roster/article_4d6143ca-785c-520a-93fc-ec2ae91eff1e.html,"Swiss Coworking Company Adds 5 New Locations to Washington Roster | News | southsoundbiz.com ... Switzerland-based International Workplace Group is expanding its presence in Washington with five new flexible workspaces under its Regus brand, bringing the company’s total to more than 45 locations across the state. ... The new branches include private offices, meeting rooms, and coworking and creative spaces for businesses ranging from startups to more established companies. ... “As an important business hub, the state of Washington is a fantastic place for us to boost our expansion plans as the need for cutting-edge flexible workspaces continues to soar and hybrid working becomes the new normal,” said Jeff Doughman, CEO for IWG in the Americas, in a press release. ... The new locations are expected to open between the third quarter of 2026 and the first quarter of 2027 in the following areas: ... - 9208 20th Ave. SW, Seattle — Q3 2026 - 6840 Fort Dent Way, Tukwila — Q3 2026 - 6720 Fort Dent Way, Tukwila — Q3 2026 - 16201 E Indiana Ave., Spokane Valley — Q4 2026 - 14419 Redmond-Woodinville Road, Woodinville — Q1 2027 ... These centers are being developed through partnerships with the building owners, who are investing in IWG’s flexible workspace platform to bring Regus locations into their properties, the release noted. It added that the company signed 1,132 new locations globally in 2025 and another 382 during the first quarter of 2026. ... “Our workplace model is proven to increase productivity and allows for a business to scale up or down at significantly reduced costs while providing access to thousands of locations,” added Doughman in the release."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Prologis To Buy Segro In One Of Industrial's Largest Mergers Ever,"www.bisnow.com (Jarred Schenke, Atlanta)",2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bisnow.com/national/news/industrial/uk-industrial-giant-signals-acceptance-of-fourth-prologis-offer-135540,"Prologis To Buy Segro In One Of Industrial's Largest Mergers Ever ... The San Francisco-based industrial giant made what it described as a firm final preliminary offer to buy U.K.-based industrial developer Segro for more than $18.7B (£14B) on Wednesday, a $500M increase from its third rejected offer on Monday. ... And this time, Segro recommended its board of directors take the offer if officially made, The Wall Street Journal reported. ... The deal is one of the largest mergers ever of industrial REITs and comes in 14% above Segro’s estimated net asset value at the end of June. ... News of the pending deal initially sent Prologis’ shares tumbling Thursday before rebounding midday, while Segro’s stock rose more than 7% on the London Stock Exchange. Already among the largest industrial development firms in the world, with some $240B in assets under management, Prologis’ acquisition of Segro would add 117M SF of European industrial and data center space valued at $29.3B (£22B). ... Segro extended the deadline for Prologis’ formal offer, which also includes a partial cash alternative of up to $4.6B, until Aug. 12. ... is said in a statement that a final deal isn’t guaranteed. ... “Prologis' goal has always been a constructive process. The proposed combination represents a compelling opportunity for shareholders of both companies,” Prologis said in a press release. “Prologis welcomes the additional time afforded by the extension and is ready to work with the Segro Board in reaching an outcome that delivers value for all stakeholders.” ... Segro’s board unanimously rejected three previous offers for acquisition by Prologis, beginning on June 24 with a $16.6B bid. Earlier this week, Prologis offered $18.2B, 9.7% higher than Segro’s estimated NAV. ... Prologis argued that its ownership of Segro could accelerate the firm’s growth strategy, especially in the data center sector. But Segro countered that Prologis’ bids were opportunistic and that shareholders could benefit more with Segro as an independent company. ... According to the WSJ, Prologis decided to raise its bid again after shareholder feedback. On July 21, Norges Bank Investment Management — which holds 1.3% of Prologis and 8.3% of Segro — encouraged the firms to come to “mutually beneficial terms” on a merger. ... Prologis’ latest potential bid comes as the company raised its earnings guidance for 2026 after signing a record of more than 67M SF of leases, pushing occupancy up 20 basis points to 95.5%, the company reported in its earnings ending June 30. Prologis also broke ground on $1.6B in new logistics and data center projects as it rapidly ramps up its spec development pipeline."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"A new wave of flexible workspace expansion is underway in central New Jersey, strengthening IWG’s footprint across one of the US Northeast’s most established and strategically located commercial corridors. | Bonnie Fisher",www.linkedin.com (Bonnie Fisher),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/bonnie-fisher-65885b3_a-new-wave-of-flexible-workspace-expansion-activity-7485026457224687616-jRx_,"# A new wave of flexible workspace expansion is underway in central New Jersey, strengthening IWG’s footprint across one of the US Northeast’s most established and strategically located commercial corridors. | Bonnie Fisher · LinkedIn · 2026-07-20 ... A new wave of flexible workspace expansion is underway in central New Jersey, strengthening IWG’s footprint across one of the US Northeast’s most established and strategically located commercial corridors. ... The two new Regus centers, spanning Plainsboro and Cranbury, add more than 29,000 sq ft of workspace across high-demand suburban markets. Plainsboro is recognised for its thriving business community, proximity to major research and technology hubs, and convenient access to the wider Princeton region. Cranbury combines a rich history dating back to the 18th century with a strong logistics sector and direct connections to key transport routes linking New York City and Philadelphia. Together, these locations strengthen coverage across a well-connected and dynamic regional business ecosystem. ... IWG continues to sign record-breaking numbers of partnership agreements with building owners in the U.S. and around the world to turn building space into profitable income-generating flexible workspaces. Reach out to me directly or visit our website to find out how you can partner with us: https://lnkd.in/ey8pCPWa"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Un nouvel espace de coworking ouvre ses portes dans le quartier de la gare - Actualité Angers Villactu,www.angers.villactu.fr (Rédaction),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.angers.villactu.fr/un-nouvel-espace-de-coworking-ouvre-ses-portes-dans-le-quartier-de-la-gare/,"# Un nouvel espace de coworking ouvre ses portes dans le quartier de la gare ... 20 juillet ... 026 #### L’entreprise International Workplace Group a ouvert son espace Regus Angers le 29 juin dernier, un espace de travail mêlant coworking, bureaux privatifs et salles de réunion dans le quartier de la gare. ... Dans le quartier d’affaires Cours Saint-Laud, au sud de la gare, International Workplace Group (IWG), entreprise spécialisée dans les bureaux équipés et les espaces de coworking, vient d’ouvrir un nouveau site de 1 275 m² sur deux niveaux. ... Au 10, rue Fulton, cet espace nommé Regus propose deux salles de réunion et 160 postes de travail, répartis entre des bureaux individuels et un espace de coworking. ... Les usagers bénéficient d’un accueil de 9 h à 17 h, d’une cuisine, de douches et d’espaces communs. Ce nouveau centre Regus, le premier dans le Maine-et-Loire, offre la possibilité aux entreprises d’aménager leurs espaces selon leurs besoins. « Nous pouvons commander du mobilier spécifique et modifier les espaces pour répondre aux attentes », explique Mégane Gasnier, responsable des lieux. ... Depuis son ouverture, il y a trois semaines, les premiers usagers sont notamment des salariés de grandes entreprises travaillant à distance. « Les demandes sont déjà nombreuses pour le mois de septembre », se réjouit Mégane Gasnier, qui voit la proximité de la gare comme un atout non négligeable. ... Les bureaux peuvent être réservés à la journée, à partir de 19 € HT pour l’espace coworking et 49 € HT pour les bureaux individuels. « Les salles de réunion peuvent également être réservées de manière ponctuelle », ajoute la responsable du site. ... Pour les entreprises qui souhaitent s’implanter à plus long terme, un devis personnalisé leur est proposé."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Saba in talks with IWG and JLL over Workspace management,citywire.com,2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://citywire.com/wealth-manager/news/exclusive-saba-in-talks-with-iwg-and-jll-over-workspace-management/a2494347,"Exclusive: Saba in talks with IWG and JLL over Workspace management ... Saba Capital has been negotiating with International Workplace Group and Jones Lang LaSalle over the potential management of Workspace (WKP), Citywire understands. ... The US activist has been steadily upping its position in the £682m office real estate trust since January and aims to replace the board with its own nominees at next Thursday’s annual general meeting (AGM). It currently holds 29.1% of its shares. ... Saba revealed last week that it was in ‘advanced discussions’ with two external managers to oversee the operational side of the business should its nominees be elected. ... Citywire understands that the two parties are Mark Dixon’s International Workplace Group (formerly Regus) and Jones Lang LaSalle, which manages 275m sq ft of commercial property across the UK, including major office spaces. ... Saba hopes that outsourcing the day-to-day property management to one of these two firms whilst assets are sold will help narrow the trust’s over 50% discount, which is the widest among the 19 other comparable UK Reits. ... Workspace released a trading update on Wednesday that included a 1.9% rise in quarterly rent roll and third consecutive increase in stabilised occupancy. But whilst markets responded positively to the news (with shares up 3.4% since), one of Saba’s director nominees Andrew Sim responded with caution. ‘The quality of Workspace’s London portfolio remains attractive; however, the market is increasingly sceptical that the current speed of incremental changes is sufficient to turn the business around,’ he told Citywire. ... ‘To properly enhance shareholder returns, a far more dynamic strategy is now required for portfolio optimisation, capital recycling and allocation, and a reduction in the excessive cost base.’ Sim added that such measures would ‘accelerate value realisation and help narrow the divergence between the company’s public market evaluation and the underlying value of its real estate portfolio’. ... ‘After years of disappointing returns, it feels appropriate now for a refreshed board that can work constructively with management to unlock the value that is clearly there,’ he said. ... Saba says it has identified 50-75 potential buyers for the Workspace portfolio, raising some questions from analysts and the Workspace board who branded the proposals ‘high risk’ and ‘short-sighted’. ... Others argue the plans are consistent with high demand for flexible property in London. Real estate giant Cushman & Wakefield sees ‘abundant demand’ from buyers in Central London and its sub-markets that offer an opportunity to convert desirable buildings from office to hotel and residential space. ‘We believe the London market can support significantly in excess of the £8bn to £10bn of annual transaction activity seen over the past couple of years,’ a representative from the firm said. ‘There is no shortage of active capital which would like to deploy from debt through to equity and we are aware of many institutional and high-net-worth investors, both domestic and international, who understand that many of these buildings do not become available very often and when offered to market and priced correctly these buyers are willing to pay at, or near to, the asking price.’"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG 2026 Midyear Update: Record Results Meet A Historic Leadership Transition,allwork.space (Jonathan Price),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://allwork.space/2026/07/iwg-2026-midyear-update-record-results-meet-a-historic-leadership-transition/,"IWG is entering a new era with record operating results and a historic leadership transition, as founder Mark Dixon steps aside after nearly four decades. ... IWG plc, the Jersey-incorporated, Switzerland-domiciled owner of Regus, Spaces, HQ and Signature, enters mid-2026 in an unusual position: delivering its strongest-ever operating results just as it ends the nearly four-decade era of founder Mark Dixon as chief executive. ... IWG’s preliminary results for the year ended December 31, 2025, published on March 3, 2026, showed system-wide revenue of $4.5 billion and adjusted EBITDA of $531 million, its strongest operational year to date. Growth was modest at the group level — system-wide revenue rose 4% year-over-year, while adjusted EBITDA increased 6% from 2024 — but the composition of that growth is the real story. Adjusted gross profit increased 9% to over $1 billion, and the Company-owned segment margin rose to 26% from 25%. ... The standout was the Managed & Franchised division, IWG’s capital-light growth engine. System-wide revenue in that division increased 28%, with recurring management fees surging 140% to $45 million from $19 million in 2024. Recurring management fees are expected to reach $80 million in 2026 and $125 million in 2027, and the company has repeatedly compared its trajectory to established hotel franchisors such as Marriott and Hilton, noting it is still well below their typical proportion of fee-based revenue. ... Network expansion also hit records: 1,132 centers were signed (up 26%) and 782 centers opened (up 25%), giving IWG over 1 million rooms across 4,609 centers in more than 120 countries, with an additional 230,000 rooms in the pipeline. ... On the balance sheet, IWG continued a multi-year deleveraging effort. Net debt declined to $715 million from $729 million in 2024, improving the leverage ratio to 1.35x EBITDA from 1.45x. This came despite returning $144 million to shareholders through $130 million in buybacks and $14 million in dividends. ... Guidance for 2026 points to further progress, with adjusted EBITDA guidance set at $585 million to $625 million and a new $100 million buyback program announced for 2026, though the company has flagged that net debt is expected to rise slightly in 2026 even as capital returns continue. ... Despite the record headline figures, the market reaction was muted to negative: IWG’s stock declined 8.4% to £2.13 on the day of the results presentation. Analysts have pointed to structural concerns rather than execution — one summary noted the stock’s score is primarily constrained by high balance-sheet leverage, including negative equity, and a sharp 2025 deterioration in revenue, margins and cash flow versus 2024 on certain measures, even as the underlying franchise transition progresses. ... There is also a broader sector overhang: reports note the share price was negatively impacted by market concerns over AI, which affected perceptions of the commercial property sector, given fears that AI-driven productivity gains could eventually reduce corporate demand for physical office space — an irony given IWG’s own flexible-space model is often pitched as a hedge against exactly that uncertainty. ... On June 16, 2026, IWG announced a significant reshaping of its top leadership. Christian Schmitz was appointed Chief Executive Officer, with founder Mark Dixon transitioning to Executive Chair and Douglas Sutherland becoming Deputy Chair, moving up from his prior role as Non-Executive Chair. ... Dixon’s departure from the CEO role is historically significant. The transition sees Dixon hand over the reins to insider Christian Schmitz after nearly 40 years in the role, having founded IWG in 1989 and built a network spanning more than 120 countries through brands such as Regus, Spaces, HQ and Signature. In the company’s own words, Dixon reflected that it had been a privilege to lead the company as it grew to 6,000 locations open and in the pipeline worldwide since founding it with a single Brussels center. ... Schmitz is very much an internal appointment rather than an outside hire, which the company has framed as ensuring continuity. He joined IWG last year as chief transformation officer before being promoted to Global Head of Regions, and brings a background as a partner at McKinsey, a director at KKR Capstone, and previously CEO of Selecta for six years. Dixon has publicly endorsed the choice, saying Schmitz has made a significant impact, bringing deep insight into our business and a clear focus on execution, and is well placed to lead the company’s next growth phase. ... Dixon’s new role is not a clean exit. As Executive Chair, he will continue to provide strategic guidance to the Board and act as an adviser to the CEO — a structure IWG has explicitly linked to preserving his industry knowledge through what it calls an orderly CEO transition process, reflecting the desire of the board and shareholders to retain Dixon’s unrivalled industry knowledge, experience and long-term strategic perspective. ... It is also notable that Dixon remains IWG’s largest shareholder by a wide margin, and reporting around the FY2025 results indicated his personal stake had increased because he did not participate in the 2025 buyback program — a detail investors may read as a signal of continued confidence even as he steps back operationally. ... Reuters framed the reshuffle in blunter commercial terms, reporting the changes come as the company seeks to cut debt and costs amid geopolitical and AI-driven pressures, and that IWG has been tackling rising debt and costs, pressured by the fallout of the Middle East conflict and AI-driven shifts in workplace strategy. That framing sits somewhat in tension with the company’s own “record results” narrative, and underscores that the succession, while presented as proactive and orderly, is also occurring against a backdrop of real financial and macro pressure. ... Taken together, the results and the succession tell a coherent story about an inflection point rather than a crisis. IWG’s underlying operating metrics — network growth, fee income, EBITDA, deleveraging — are moving in the right direction, and the shift toward a franchise-heavy, capital-light model mirrors a well-trodden playbook from the hotel industry. ... At the same time, elevated leverage, a still-large net debt position, and investor anxiety about AI’s long-term effect on office demand mean the market has not fully rewarded that operational progress. ... Handing day-to-day execution to an internal transformation specialist, while keeping the founder engaged as an adviser and the company’s largest shareholder, is a low-disruption way to test whether professional management can accelerate the deleveraging and franchise-fee growth story without losing strategic continuity. ... Whether investors come to see this as effective succession planning or as evidence of deeper pressure on the business will likely depend on how quickly Schmitz can translate record operating metrics into a re-rating of the stock, and on whether net debt reduction resumes in 2026 despite the guided uptick."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"IWG Adds 5,100 sqm of Flexible Workspaces in Iasi, Bucharest and Timisoara — Four New Centres by Early 2027",www.officerentinfo.ro,2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.officerentinfo.ro/article/officemarket-news/iwg-adds-5-100-sqm-of-flexible-workspaces-in-iasi-bucharest-and-timisoara-four-new-centres-by-early-2027,"International Workplace Group (IWG) is expanding its Romanian network with four new hybrid working centres in Bucharest, Iasi and Timisoara, totalling over 5,100 sqm of modern coworking spaces, private offices and meeting rooms — at a time when demand for flexible workspace solutions continues to grow. ... The new centres will open in stages during the second half of 2026 and in early 2027. The first to open will be Spaces Business Garden in Bucharest, followed by HQ Egros Office in Iasi and HQ City Gate North Tower in Bucharest — both in the final quarter of the year. At the start of 2027, IWG will open a new Regus centre within the ISHO project in Timisoara. ... Each of the four new locations is positioned within a high-profile office development. In Bucharest, Spaces Business Garden will operate within the Business Garden complex, while HQ City Gate North Tower will open in Piața Presei Libere. In Iasi, HQ Egros Office will offer access to a commercial area connected to the city's technology and university ecosystem. The Timisoara centre will be integrated into the ISHO project, one of the largest urban regeneration developments in western Romania. ... Alina Gomotirceanu-Dumitrașcu, Country Manager of IWG Romania, stated: ""Romania is a strong market in our region. Our expansion, including the new Spaces Business Garden centre, is a direct response to this demand. The flexible office is no longer just an alternative — for many companies it is already the first choice. Our goal is that wherever business is developing in Romania, there should be an IWG workspace nearby to support their activity."" ... The Romanian expansion is part of IWG's accelerating global growth trajectory. The company signed 382 new locations in Q1 2026, compared to 224 in the same period of the previous year, and opened 222 centres. The global network now exceeds one million workspaces across 121 countries, serving 83% of Fortune 500 companies. ... Mark Dixon, Executive Chairman and Founder of International Workplace Group, commented: ""More and more companies are adopting flexible and cost-efficient operational models, and we are seeing growing demand for high-quality workspaces that offer employees greater flexibility and allow companies to adapt their operations quickly. By expanding our network, we provide organisations with more options and access to modern spaces, closer to where people live and work."" ... The expansion is supported by structural shifts in the labour market. Hybrid and decentralised working models are gaining ground, and flexible spaces are becoming an increasingly important component of corporate infrastructure. Estimates suggest that by 2030 approximately 30% of total global office space will be represented by flexible workspaces. Demand growth is driven by cost optimisation, operational flexibility and employees' preferences for workspaces closer to residential areas. ... Office Leasing Market Expanded in Both Bucharest and Cluj-Napoca in H1 2026, While Demand Declined in Iasi and Timisoara ... #### Regus (International Workplace Group)"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"International Workplace Group opens four new hybrid work centres in Bucharest, Iași and Timișoara - Business Review",business-review.eu (Newsroom),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://business-review.eu/property/offices/international-workplace-group-opens-four-new-hybrid-work-centres-in-bucharest-iasi-and-timisoara-298279,"International Workplace Group opens four new hybrid work centres in Bucharest, Iași and Timișoara - Business Review ... International Workplace Group opens four new hybrid work centres in Bucharest, Iași and Timișoara ... International Workplace Group (IWG), which owns brands including Regus, Spaces, and HQ, has announced the opening of four new centres in three Romanian cities, as part of its efforts to meet growing demand from organisations seeking modern, accessible and adaptable workspace solutions. ... The new centres will open in phases during the second half of this year and early next year. The expansion begins with the opening of Spaces Business Garden in Bucharest, followed by HQ Egros Office in Iași and HQ City Gate North Tower in Bucharest during the final quarter of the year. Early next year, IWG will further expand its presence in Timișoara with a new Regus centre at ISHO, one of western Romania’s landmark urban regeneration developments. ... is strong market ... flexibility on terms ... scale up or down as ... capital costs. Our expansion, including the new Spaces Business Garden ... is a direct answer to that ... is no longer an alternative – for ... is the default,” added ... Dumitrascu. ... Our ambition is ... Romania, there is ... Together, the four locations will add more than 5,100 sqm of flexible workspace to IWG’s network in Romania, offering private offices, coworking areas, meeting rooms and collaborative spaces, alongside the Design Your Own Office service, which enables businesses to tailor their workspace to their specific requirements. ... The new centres will be located within some of Romania’s most prominent office developments. In Bucharest, Spaces Business Garden will operate from the award-winning Business Garden development, strategically positioned at the intersection of the city’s business, academic and transport networks, while HQ City Gate North Tower will be located in Piața Presei Libere (Free Press Square), within one of the capital’s leading Grade A office buildings, offering excellent access to the city centre and Henri Coandă International Airport. ... In Iași, the new HQ centre at Egros Office will provide businesses with access to a well-connected commercial district renowned for its strong technology ecosystem and academic heritage. Meanwhile, the Regus centre at ISHO will be located within a landmark mixed-use development on the banks of the Bega River, close to Timișoara’s historic city centre and one of the region’s most dynamic business and innovation ecosystems. ... Following a record-breaking 2025, the company maintained its momentum in 2026, signing 382 new locations worldwide during the first quarter of the year. International Workplace Group’s global network now comprises more than one million workspaces across 121 countries. ... “Romania is an important market for International Workplace Group’s continued expansion, and these four new centres reflect our commitment to meeting the growing demand for modern flexible workspace solutions,” said Mark Dixon, Executive Chairman and Founder of International Workplace Group PLC. “As more companies adopt flexible and cost-efficient operating models, we are seeing increasing demand for high-quality workspaces that provide employees with greater flexibility while enabling businesses to adapt quickly to changing needs. By expanding our network, we are giving organisations greater choice and access to high-quality workspaces closer to where people live and work.” ... As the market continues to evolve towards hybrid and decentralised working models, demand for flexible workspaces continues to grow. Research shows that workplace flexibility contributes to higher productivity, improved employee satisfaction and lower operating costs for businesses. It is estimated that by 2030, around 30% of all commercial real estate will consist of flexible workspace, according to IWG."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,International Workplace Group to open four new hybrid work centres in Romania | Romania Insider,www.romania-insider.com,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.romania-insider.com/international-workplace-group-center-romania-july-2026,"International Workplace Group (IWG) will open four new hybrid work centers in Bucharest, Iași, and Timișoara, expanding its flexible office network in Romania by more than 5,100 sqm. The new locations are scheduled to open in phases during the second half of 2026 and early 2027. ... The company said the expansion reflects growing demand for hybrid working solutions, as more businesses adopt flexible office models instead of traditional long-term leases. ... The rollout will begin with the opening of a Spaces center at Business Garden in Bucharest, followed by HQ Egros Office in Iași and HQ City Gate North Tower in Bucharest later this year. A fourth location, a Regus center at the ISHO mixed-use development in Timișoara, is scheduled to open in early 2027. ... Together, the four sites will offer more than 5,100 sqm of workspace, including private offices, coworking areas, meeting rooms, and collaborative spaces. The centers will also offer IWG's ""Design Your Own Office"" service, allowing businesses to customize office layouts to their needs. ... The Romanian expansion comes as IWG continues to grow its global network. The company said it signed 382 new locations worldwide during the first quarter of 2026, following a record expansion in 2025. Its global network now spans more than one million workspaces across 121 countries. ... “Romania is an important market for International Workplace Group’s continued expansion, and these four new centres reflect our commitment to meeting the growing demand for modern flexible workspace solutions,” said Mark Dixon, Executive Chairman and Founder of International Workplace Group PLC. ... IWG operates several flexible workspace brands, including Regus, Spaces, HQ, and Signature. ... International Workplace Group (IWG) will open four new hybrid work centers in Bucharest, Iași, and Timișoara, expanding its flexible office network in Romania by more than 5,100 sqm. The new locations are scheduled to open in phases during the second half of 2026 and early 2027. ... The company said the expansion reflects growing demand for hybrid working solutions, as more businesses adopt flexible office models instead of traditional long-term leases. ... The rollout will begin with the opening of a Spaces center at Business Garden in Bucharest, followed by HQ Egros Office in Iași and HQ City Gate North Tower in Bucharest later this year. A fourth location, a Regus center at the ISHO mixed-use development in Timișoara, is scheduled to open in early 2027. ... Together, the four sites will offer more than 5,100 sqm of workspace, including private offices, coworking areas, meeting rooms, and collaborative spaces. The centers will also offer IWG's ""Design Your Own Office"" service, allowing businesses to customize office layouts to their needs. ... The Romanian expansion comes as IWG continues to grow its global network. The company said it signed 382 new locations worldwide during the first quarter of 2026, following a record expansion in 2025. Its global network now spans more than one million workspaces across 121 countries. ... “Romania is an important market for International Workplace Group’s continued expansion, and these four new centres reflect our commitment to meeting the growing demand for modern flexible workspace solutions,” said Mark Dixon, Executive Chairman and Founder of International Workplace Group PLC. ... IWG operates several flexible workspace brands, including Regus, Spaces, HQ, and Signature. ... International Workplace Group (IWG) will open four new hybrid work centers in Bucharest, Iași, and Timișoara, expanding its flexible office network in Romania by more than 5,100 sqm. The new locations are scheduled to open in phases during the second half of 2026 and early 2027. ... The company said the expansion reflects growing demand for hybrid working solutions, as more businesses adopt flexible office models instead of traditional long-term leases. ... The rollout will begin with the opening of a Spaces center at Business Garden in Bucharest, followed by HQ Egros Office in Iași and HQ City Gate North Tower in Bucharest later this year. A fourth location, a Regus center at the ISHO mixed-use development in Timișoara, is scheduled to open in early 2027. ... Together, the four sites will offer more than 5,100 sqm of workspace, including private offices, coworking areas, meeting rooms, and collaborative spaces. The centers will also offer IWG's ""Design Your Own Office"" service, allowing businesses to customize office layouts to their needs. ... The Romanian expansion comes as IWG continues to grow its global network. The company said it signed 382 new locations worldwide during the first quarter of 2026, following a record expansion in 2025. Its global network now spans more than one million workspaces across 121 countries. ... “Romania is an important market for International Workplace Group’s continued expansion, and these four new centres reflect our commitment to meeting the growing demand for modern flexible workspace solutions,” said Mark Dixon, Executive Chairman and Founder of International Workplace Group PLC. ... IWG operates several flexible workspace brands, including Regus, Spaces, HQ, and Signature."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"IWG deschide patru noi centre coworking la București, Iași și Timișoara",moneybuzz.ro (Cristian Hățiș),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://moneybuzz.ro/iwg-patru-noi-centre-coworking-bucuresti-iasi-timisoara/,"IWG deschide patru noi centre coworking la București, Iași și Timișoara ... # IWG deschide patru noi centre coworking la București, Iași și Timișoara Cristian Hățiș 13 iulie 2026 Spații de coworking Regus ... International Workplace Group, cea mai mare platformă globală pentru munca hibridă, care operează branduri precum Regus, Spaces și HQ, deschide patru noi centre în București, Iași și Timișoara. ... Noile centre vor fi inaugurate etapizat, în a doua jumătate a acestui an și la începutul anului viitor. Prima inaugurare va fi Spaces Business Garden din București, urmată de noile locații HQ Egros Office din Iași și HQ City Gate North Tower din București, în ultimul trimestru al anului. ... La începutul anului viitor, IWG se va extinde pe piața din Timișoara prin deschiderea unui nou centru Regus în cadrul proiectului ISHO, unul dintre cele mai reprezentative proiecte de regenerare urbană din vestul României. ... Cele patru locații totalizează peste 5.100 mp de spații flexibile și vor pune la dispoziția companiilor birouri private, spații de coworking, săli de întâlnire și zone de muncă în colaborare, alături de serviciul Design Your Own Office, care permite configurarea spațiilor în funcție de nevoile fiecărei organizații. Extinderea din România are loc în contextul unei dezvoltări accelerate a rețelei IWG la nivel mondial. Numai în primul trimestru al anului 2026, compania a deschis 382 de noi locații la nivel globa. Rețeaua IWG depășește în prezent un milion de spații de lucru în 121 de țări."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG Expands In Illinois With 12 More Flexible Workspaces,allwork.space (Allwork.Space News Team),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://allwork.space/2026/07/iwg-expands-in-illinois-with-12-more-flexible-workspaces/,"# IWG Expands In Illinois With 12 More Flexible Workspaces ... ## After opening 22 Illinois centers last year, IWG is targeting major metros and regional cities where businesses are seeking flexible workspace closer to employees. ... The Regus and Spaces parent is expanding beyond Chicago with planned locations in central Illinois. ... IWG is expanding its Illinois presence with plans to open 12 new flexible workspace locations, extending beyond the Chicago metro into central Illinois as demand for hybrid work continues to support the sector. ... The expansion includes a planned Regus location at Peoria’s Twin Towers and several additional sites across the Chicago area, according to industry reporting. While most opening dates have not yet been announced, the rollout marks another step in IWG’s aggressive U.S. growth strategy, according to CoStar. ... The Illinois announcement comes after a strong period of global expansion for IWG, the parent company of Regus and Spaces. ... In its first-quarter 2026 trading update, the company reported continued momentum in new center signings and openings while maintaining a substantial pipeline of additional locations. IWG has also described 2025 as a record year for new center openings, with growth continuing into 2026. ... ## Illinois Network Continues to Grow ... The latest expansion builds on IWG’s rapid growth across the state. ... Last year, the company added 22 centers throughout Illinois, significantly increasing its footprint through franchise and managed partnership agreements. Earlier expansions also focused heavily on the Chicago metropolitan area before extending into additional markets across the state. ... The newest locations suggest IWG is continuing to target both major business districts and smaller regional cities where companies are seeking flexible office options closer to where employees live. ... While the broad expansion plan is now public, detailed opening schedules and final lease announcements are still expected as the projects move through development."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,LCECOM Boosts Cross-Border Digitalization,www.martechcube.com (GlobeNewswire),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.martechcube.com/lcecom-boosts-cross-border-digitalization-to-drive-regional-expansion/,"# LCECOM Boosts Cross-Border Digitalization to Drive Regional Expansion ... LUCKCAT E-COMMERCE PTE. LTD. (hereinafter referred to as “LCECOM”), an international company registered in New York, USA, today announced its continued commitment to advancing its global operational strategy. The company’s forward-looking initiatives will focus heavily on regulatory compliance, systemic transparency, and the long-term enhancement of cross-border digital operational capabilities. ... LCECOM stated that its strategic direction will center on strengthening structured digital operational capabilities across multiple regions while ensuring strict alignment with relevant regulatory requirements in each local jurisdiction. ... Operating lawfully within the U.S. legal framework, LCECOM engages in cross-border digital commerce coordination, operational process management, and brand-related support services under the U.S. federal tax system via its Employer Identification Number (EIN). ... The Company notes that because different countries employ distinct business identification systems, minor localized discrepancies naturally arise between corporate registration networks. LCECOM emphasizes that any inability to query its corporate information on local regional tax systems does not indicate that the Company is unregistered, but rather reflects a normal divergence between disparate jurisdictional data systems. The Company reaffirms that it strictly complies with all applicable local laws and regulatory requirements in every region where it maintains operations. ... LCECOM is continuously expanding its international operational structure through several key ongoing initiatives: ... - Establishing localized operational workspaces in select global regions. - Strengthening cross-regional collaborative operational systems. - Promoting the broad standardization of operational processes across multiple markets. - Gradually exploring alignment with local regulatory frameworks in future phases, subject to localized approvals and operational conditions. ... To support this infrastructure, LCECOM continues to invest heavily in the development of internal digital systems designed to improve consistency, traceability, and scalability. These core components include digital workflow coordination systems, cross-regional task management frameworks, data tracking systems, and standardized communication mechanisms. ... LCECOM’s 2026–2028 strategic plan prioritizes structural growth opportunities within international expansion zones to further refine its global business footprint. The Company identifies these target regions as high-priority sectors due to several critical growth drivers, including a youthful demographic profile, rising digital connectivity, rapid mobile payment adoption, and sustained demand for cross-border e-commerce. ... Within this strategic framework, key regional hubs have been identified as essential strategic nodes for regional positioning, offering significant trade connectivity, a stable business environment, and a growing receptiveness to international digital business models. LCECOM emphasizes that this international strategy will be implemented in phases, with gradual execution based carefully on market conditions and regulatory environments. ... “Global commerce is progressively shifting from traditional geographic structures toward operational models centered on digital collaboration,” the Company noted in a statement. LCECOM’s long-term objective is to lead this transition by advancing cross-border digital operating models that reduce geographical constraints and enhance systemic interconnectivity for teams worldwide."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI,www.brazilbusinessinsights.com,2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.brazilbusinessinsights.com/news/moomoo-engine-launch-futu-xp-nubank-brazil,"Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI ... # Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil ... Moomoo is launching 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified trading toolkit designed to capture active retail and professional traders in Brazil, challenging incumbents. ... - ▸ Global user base: Over 22 million users - ▸ Launch date: July 2, 2026 - ▸ Target market: Active retail & pro traders - ▸ Primary region: Brazil expansion ... The Bottom Line: - Moomoo, the digital brokerage subsidiary of Futu Holdings ($FUTU), is set to launch 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified suite of advanced trading tools designed to consolidate market analysis, charting, and execution. - The rollout represents a strategic push to capture high-value retail and professional traders in emerging markets, particularly Brazil, where digital brokerage competition is intensifying. - While the launch enhances $FUTU's technological moat, it poses direct competitive pressure on local incumbents such as XP Inc. ($XP) and Nubank ($NU). Strategic Expansion in Latin America: Futu Holdings ($FUTU), through its international trading platform Moomoo, is accelerating its expansion into Latin America with the exclusive announcement of 'Moomoo Engine.' This unified toolkit is designed to streamline the trading lifecycle for retail and professional investors. By integrating advanced charting, real-time data analytics, and algorithmic execution into a single, cohesive interface, Moomoo aims to address the fragmentation that has historically plagued active traders in emerging markets. The Brazilian market, characterized by a highly sophisticated retail investor base and a rapidly growing interest in global equities, serves as the primary launchpad for this technological deployment. Technological Disruption and the 'Moomoo Engine': The 'Moomoo Engine' represents a significant upgrade to the platform's existing infrastructure. Historically, active traders in Brazil have had to rely on multiple third-party platforms for technical analysis, order routing, and portfolio tracking. This fragmentation often leads to latency issues, higher subscription costs, and execution inefficiencies. Moomoo's unified toolkit addresses these pain points by offering proprietary, low-latency charting algorithms and institutional-grade data feeds directly within the trading application. This integration is expected to lower the barrier to entry for advanced trading strategies, enabling retail investors to execute complex multi-leg options strategies and automated technical trades with greater precision. Competitive Dynamics in the Brazilian Brokerage Sector: The introduction of the 'Moomoo Engine' comes at a time of intense competition within the Brazilian financial services sector. Incumbents like XP Inc. ($XP) and BTG Pactual have traditionally dominated the affluent and active trader segments through extensive advisory networks and proprietary platforms. Concurrently, digital-first platforms like Nubank ($NU) and Inter have successfully democratized access to basic investment products for the mass market. Moomoo's strategy bypasses the traditional advisory model, focusing instead on self-directed, tech-savvy traders who prioritize execution speed, analytical depth, and low transaction costs. By offering institutional-grade tools without the premium price tag, Moomoo is positioning itself to capture market share from both high-end incumbents and mass-market digital banks looking to upsell their user bases. Regulatory and Operational Considerations: Operating a foreign-backed digital brokerage in Brazil requires navigating a complex regulatory framework overseen by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Brazil (CVM) and the Central Bank of Brazil (BCB). Moomoo's expansion strategy relies heavily on seamless integration with local clearing systems and compliance with strict foreign exchange (FX) regulations. For Brazilian investors trading international assets, tax compliance—specifically the calculation of capital gains and the monthly 'Carnê-Leão' tax filing—has historically been a major friction point. To gain widespread adoption, the 'Moomoo Engine' must integrate localized tax reporting tools that simplify these compliance obligations for domestic users. Furthermore, fluctuations in the USD/BRL exchange rate remain a critical variable, as currency volatility can significantly impact the net returns of Brazilian investors trading on US exchanges through the platform. Implications for Futu Holdings ($FUTU): For Futu Holdings ($FUTU), the successful rollout of the 'Moomoo Engine' in Brazil is vital for its broader international diversification strategy. Facing mature markets and regulatory headwinds in mainland China and Hong Kong, Futu has increasingly looked to Southeast Asia and Latin America to drive its next phase of growth. Brazil represents one of the largest retail investment markets in the developing world, making it a high-stakes testing ground for Moomoo's global scalability. If the 'Moomoo Engine' succeeds in capturing a meaningful share of Brazil's active trading volume, it could serve as a blueprint for further expansion into other Latin American markets, such as Mexico and Colombia, thereby bolstering Futu's long-term revenue growth and reducing its geographic concentration risk. ... Market Impact: The launch of the 'Moomoo Engine' has distinct implications for the key players in the digital brokerage space: - Futu Holdings ($FUTU): Bullish. The successful deployment of advanced trading tools in Brazil accelerates Futu's international diversification, reducing its reliance on Asian markets and opening a high-margin revenue stream from active Latin American traders. - XP Inc. ($XP): Bearish. XP faces direct technological competition in its high-value active trader segment. While its advisory network remains a strong moat, Moomoo's low-cost, high-tech offering could pressure XP's commission margins and active client retention. - Nu Holdings ($NU): Neutral. Nubank's primary investment audience consists of mass-market retail investors rather than sophisticated active traders. However, as Nubank seeks to upsell its client base into more complex financial products, Moomoo's advanced platform represents a long-term competitive hurdle. ... > analyst consensus: Bullish on Futu Holdings ($FUTU) international expansion; bearish on XP Inc. ($XP) active trader retention; neutral on Nu Holdings ($NU). > asset_class: Equities"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,International Workplace Group (IWG) Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express workspace in Partnership with Crowne Plaza KLCC – kopiandproperty.com,kopiandproperty.com,2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://kopiandproperty.com/international-workplace-group-iwg-launches-malaysias-first-regus-express-workspace-in-partnership-with-crowne-plaza-klcc/,"International Workplace Group (IWG) Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express workspace in Partnership with Crowne Plaza KLCC – kopiandproperty.com ... # International Workplace Group (IWG) Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express workspace in Partnership with Crowne Plaza KLCC ... on June ... , 2 ... Press Release: International Workplace Group (IWG) Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express workspace in Partnership with Crowne Plaza KLCC ... International Workplace Group (IWG), the world’s largest platform for hybrid work with brands including Regus and Spaces, has launched Malaysia’s first Regus Express at Crowne Plaza Kuala Lumpur City Centre (KLCC). Located in Kuala Lumpur’s central business district along Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, the 148 square meter workspace is designed as a compact, hotel-based working environment focused on mobility and convenience. It is within a 10-minute walk of MRT and LRT stations, offering citywide connectivity, and is located near embassies, dining and retail districts, as well as key landmarks including the Petronas Twin Towers and Kuala Lumpur Convention Centre. The launch comes amid continued global expansion by International Workplace Group, which delivered its highest ever revenue, cash flow, and earnings growth in Q1 2026. The company now operates 48 centres nationwide under its Signature, HQ, Regus and Spaces brands, with 36 located Kuala Lumpur and Selangor, reflecting its growing footprint in Malaysia’s flexible workspace market. ... Building on this expansion, the introduction of the Regus Express hotel-integrated workspace combines IWG’s global platform with the hotel’s premium hospitality network to serve business travelers and corporate professionals, as demand for flexible working continues to rise both globally and locally. This trend is further supported by industry forecasts suggesting flexible workspaces could account for up to 30% of commercial real estate by 2030, as businesses increasingly adopt hybrid and agile workplace strategies. ... Mark Dixon, CEO & Founder of International Workplace Group PLC, commented, “Kuala Lumpur is an excellent fit for our continued expansion in Malaysia, strengthening our presence in an established market and introducing the Regus Express brand. As demand continues to grow for more flexible, capital-light workspace solutions, we are well positioned to support businesses with greater choice, efficiency and access to high-quality workspaces through this latest opening.” ... Vijayakumar Tangarasan, IWG Country Head for Malaysia, Singapore and Brunei, added, “The KLCC area remains one of Kuala Lumpur’s most sought-after business districts, and this landmark launch allows us to meet the rapidly growing demand for flexible workspace solutions in an exceptionally connected and strategic location. As corporate Malaysia shifts away from traditional fixed office leases toward capital-light, agile strategies, businesses require premium spaces that match their pace. This collaboration with Crowne Plaza KLCC establishes a new benchmark for prime real estate utilization, delivering a highly connected, productive environment that seamlessly blends core business functionality with luxury lifestyle amenities.” ... As part of the partnership, IWG members will have access to preferential rates on food and beverage offerings, room bookings, and banquet packages at Crowne Plaza KLCC, subject to registration through the IHG application. ... This collaboration reflects International Workplace Group’s ongoing expansion of hotel-integrated workspaces globally, as it continues to scale its network of more than 5,000 flexible workspaces across 120 countries. For more information, visit International Workplace Group."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Coworking boomt: Regus eröffnet weitere Büroflächen in Augsburg - b4bschwaben.de,www.b4bschwaben.de (Stefanie Birkle),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,"https://www.b4bschwaben.de/b4b-nachrichten/augsburg_artikel,-coworking-boomt-regus-eroeffnet-weitere-bueroflaechen-in-augsburg-_arid,275273.html","Coworking boomt: Regus eröffnet weitere Büroflächen in Augsburg - b4bschwaben.de ... Coworking boomt: Regus eröffnet weitere Büroflächen in Augsburg ... # Coworking boomt: Regus eröffnet weitere Büroflächen in Augsburg ... Im Bürokomplex ""The Arc"" in Lechhausen eröffnet ein Regus-Standort. Foto: Chrisca B6 Augsburg GmbH & Co. KG ... Der neue Coworking-Space soll im Bürokomplex „The Arc“ in Lechhausen entstehen und sich über zwei Stockwerke erstrecken. Für die IWG, dem Unternehmen hinter der Marke Regus, ist es eine von 80 Neueröffnungen in Deutschland diesem Jahr. ... Die International Workspace Group, kurz IWG und Unternehmensgruppe hinter der Marke Regus, eröffnet einen weiteren Standort in Augsburg, genauer gesagt im Bürokomplex „The Arc“ im Stadtteil Lechhausen. ... Laut der Website des Betreibers wurden in Augsburg bereits 16 Coworking-Büros eröffnet: ... - Innovationspark / Weitblick 1.7 - Hauptbahnhof (Helio-Quartier) - Maximilianstraße - Prinzregentenstraße - Rathausplatz - Königsplatz - Jakoberstraße - Göggingerstraße - Hermanstraße - Fuggerstraße - Am Schäfflerbach - Am Alten Schlachthof - Am Messezentrum - Provinostraße - Stettenstraße - Alter Postweg ... ## Coworking-Space soll bereits im Juli eröffnen ... Regus plant, zwei vollständige Stockwerke in dem Komplex zu beziehen. Auf den insgesamt 1.300 Quadratmetern sollen neben 29 buchbaren Büros auch ein Besprechungsraum sowie flexible Räumlichkeiten für Coworking und/oder Kreativarbeiten entstehen. Die Eröffnung ist für Juli geplant. Laut der Chrisca B6 Augsburg GmbH & Co. KG, Inhaberin von „The Arc“, trage man mit dem neuen Regus-Standort zum weiteren Wachstum Augsburgs als „bedeutender Wirtschaftsknotenpunkt“ bei. ... ## Bedarf nach flexiblen Büroflächen wächst rasant ... Für die IWG ist der neue Regus-Standort in Augsburg eine von mehr als 80 Neueröffnungen in Deutschland in diesem Jahr, weltweit waren es bisher 382. Diese zahlreichen Vertragsabschlüsse sowie das Unternehmenswachstum des vergangenen Geschäftsjahrs – die Gruppe eröffnete 2025 1.132 Coworking-Spaces und damit mehr als in den ersten beiden Jahrzehnten seit der Gründung zusammen – seien ein deutliches Zeichen für einen immens steigenden Bedarf nach Flexibilität im Arbeitsalltag. Immer mehr Arbeitnehmer als auch Arbeitgeber würden auf hybride Modelle, wie es die Regus-Standorte etwa ermöglichen, setzen. Aufgrund dieser Entwicklung erwartet die IWG auch für die kommenden Jahre ein exponentielles Wachstum. ... ### Regus eröffnet zweiten Standort im Innovatiospark Augsburg ... ### Strategische Expansion: Regus eröffnet Bürofläche im Weitblick ... Arbeitsplatzlösungen von Leona Strohmayer| ... 04.07.25 ... Regus Business Center in Augsburg 16.07.21"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG bringt Regus nach Augsburg,www.iz.de,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.iz.de/transaktionen/news/-iwg-bringt-regus-nach-augsburg-2000045313,"IWG bringt Regus nach Augsburg ... IWG bringt Regus nach Augsburg ... # IWG bringt Regus nach Augsburg ... Mittwoch, 24. Juni 2026 ... Die International Workplace Group (IWG) eröffnet im Juli einen Standort des Flexbüroanbieters Regus in Augsburg./AB#Die International Workpl ... IWG schluckt den nächsten Premiumanbieter Übernahme. Der Marktführer International Workplace Group (IWG) verleibt sich nach dem deutschen Premiumanbieter Design Offices (DO) auch die deutschen Flächen des Londoner … Mehr dazu ... IWG eröffnet Standort von Regus im Memminger Maxx-Forum Die International Workplace Group (IWG) wandelt ehemalige Ladenflächen im Memminger Maxx-Forum in Flexbüros um … Mehr dazu"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Innov8 acquires Vatika Business Centres to expand co-working biz - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com,2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/services/property-/-cstruction/innov8-acquires-vatika-business-centres-to-expand-co-working-biz/articleshow/131927344.cms,"Innov8 acquires Vatika Business Centres to expand co-working biz - The Economic Times ... › Industry› Services› Property / C'struction›Innov8 acquires Vatika Business Centres to expand co-working biz ... # Innov8 acquires Vatika Business Centres to expand co-working biz ... Innov8 acquires Vatika Business Centres to expand co-working biz ... ILast Updated: ... , 2026 ... Coworking firm Innov8 has acquired Vatika Business Centres, significantly expanding its footprint across India. This strategic move integrates 11 prime business centres in major cities, bolstering Innov8's presence in key commercial hubs. The acquisition aims to enhance client value through expanded offerings and improved technology, aligning with Innov8's vision for a leading premium workspace platform. ... New Delhi: Coworking firm Innov8 on Tuesday said it has acquired Vatika Business Centres to expand business amid rising demand for flexible managed workspaces.The company did not disclose the deal value.Read more: Incuspaze acquires coworking firm iKeva to scale operations ... ""The deal brings 11 prime business centres across New Delhi, Gurugram, Chennai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Noida and Pune under Innov8's direct management, immediately strengthening its presence in key commercial hubs,"" the company said in a statement.Varun Jain, Chief Operating Officer-Asia, PRISM and Innov8 said, ""This acquisition aligns with our vision of building a leading premium coworking and managed workspace platform in India. Vatika Business Centres has built a strong reputation for quality and enterprise-grade offerings, and we see significant synergies in integrating their portfolio with Innov8's design-led, community-driven approach."" ... Gaurav Bhalla, Managing Director, Vatika Hospitality said this would open up new avenues for growth and innovation. ... ""Together, we aim to deliver enhanced value to our clients through expanded offerings, improved technology integration, and a broader network of premium workspaces,"" Bhalla added.Established in 2015, Innov8 is one of the leading coworking space operators in the country."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Solaria Mall attracts Regus through partnership with IWG,realty-eg.net (Mahmoud khalil),2026-06-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://realty-eg.net/solaria-mall-regus-iwg/,"Solaria Mall attracts Regus through partnership with IWG ... ### Solaria Mall attracts Regus through strategic partnership… ... - Solaria Mall attracts Regus through strategic partnership with IWG to expand flexible workspaces in Shorouk City ... ## Aswaq Developments has signed a partnership with IWG to bring the Regus brand to Solaria Mall in Shorouk City. ... ##### The agreement supports the company’s strategy to enhance the investment value of its projects. Moreover, it aims to provide flexible workspaces that meet international standards. As a result, Solaria Mall strengthens its position as a leading mixed-use destination in Shorouk City. ... ##### Aswaq Developments announced the signing of a cooperation agreement with IWG. IWG is the world’s largest provider of flexible work solutions. ... ##### Under the agreement, the company will add a Regus center to Solaria Mall in Shorouk City. This step reflects Aswaq Developments’ commitment to attracting leading international companies and renowned brands. ... ##### The agreement was signed by Moamen Rehan, CEO of Aswaq Developments, and Youssef Naguib, General Manager of IWG in Egypt. ... ##### Moamen Rehan, CEO of Aswaq Developments, said the strategic partnership aligns with the company’s plan. Moreover, the company seeks to enhance the investment value of its projects. ... ##### In addition, it aims to create an integrated business environment that meets international standards. Therefore, the project fulfills the aspirations of investors, entrepreneurs, and companies seeking modern workspaces. ... ##### He noted that Regus was selected to establish its new headquarters within Solaria Mall in Shorouk City. Furthermore, he described the project as a leading destination for companies and entrepreneurs. ... ##### These companies seek flexible workspaces equipped with advanced technologies and world-class services. As a result, the agreement enhances the project’s position in the market. Moreover, Solaria Mall becomes one of the most prominent integrated commercial and service centers in the region. ... ##### He emphasized that Solaria Mall is the fourth commercial project by Aswaq Developments. In addition, it is one of the most important mixed-use projects in Shorouk City. ... ##### He expressed pride in hosting one of the world’s leading workspace brands at Solaria Mall. Furthermore, Regus represents a qualitative addition to the project. ... ##### Consequently, the brand enhances the project’s standing and raises service levels. Moreover, the presence of a global brand reflects international confidence in the company’s projects. ... ##### In addition, the agreement helps attract more companies and entrepreneurs. Therefore, clients benefit from an integrated business environment that supports growth and innovation. As a result, it creates added value for investors and users. ... ##### He pointed out that Solaria Mall enjoys a prime strategic location in the heart of Shorouk City. Moreover, it is located directly next to the French University in Egypt. ... ##### It is also situated on two main roads with a pedestrian walkway between them. Therefore, the project serves as a vital link between residential and service areas. ... ##### Consequently, this location gives Solaria Mall a strong competitive advantage. As a result, it represents an integrated destination for commercial, administrative, and medical activities. ... adheres to the highest ... operational standards. Therefore, the ... aims to ensure maximum investment ... Moreover, it meets the evolving needs of the real estate market, especially in new cities experiencing rapid population growth. ... ## IWG Expansion in Egypt ... ##### Youssef Naguib, General Manager of IWG in Egypt, said the company continues to strengthen its presence. Moreover, IWG is expanding its operations across Egypt. ... ##### This expansion coincides with the increasing adoption of flexible work solutions. According to him, more companies are discovering the benefits of flexible working. ... Most notably, employees benefit from improved work-life balance. In addition, flexible working offers advantages for companies, including higher productivity and lower operating costs. ... ##### Furthermore, companies can scale operations up or down more efficiently. Clients also gain access to thousands of global locations. ... ##### Naguib added that Egypt’s business landscape is evolving rapidly. As a result, companies are changing how they use office spaces. ... ##### They now prioritize flexibility and low-capital models. Therefore, IWG continues expanding its network across more Egyptian cities. ... ##### Moreover, the company aims to provide highly productive environments for startups and large corporations. Consequently, businesses can scale efficiently and better serve employees. ... ##### IWG is the world’s largest provider of flexible workspaces. In addition, clients can use the IWG app to access its global network. ... ##### This network includes thousands of locations across more than 120 countries worldwide. Moreover, it provides seamless access to flexible workspace solutions globally."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Aswaq Signs IWG Agreement for Regus at Solaria Mall,invest-gate.me (Heba Gamal),2026-06-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://invest-gate.me/news/aswaq-developments-signs-an-agreement-with-iwg-global-to-establish-regus-headquarters-at-solaria-mall-in-shorouk-city/,"Aswaq Signs IWG Agreement for Regus at Solaria Mall ... Aswaq Developments company announced the signing of a cooperation agreement with IWG, the world’s largest provider of flexible work solutions, to add Regus brand center to Solaria Mall project in Shorouk City, driven by its commitment to attracting leading international companies and renowned brands, Invest-Gate reports. ... The agreement was signed by Moamen Rehan, Aswaq Developments CEO, and Youssef Naguib, IWG general manager in Egypt. ... Moamen Rehan, Aswaq Developments CEO, said that this strategic partnership aligns with the company’s plan to enhance the investment value of its projects and create an integrated business environment that meets the highest international standards, fulfilling the aspirations of investors, entrepreneurs, and companies seeking modern and advanced workspaces. ... He noted that due to this agreement, REGUS was chosen to establish its new headquarters within Solaria Mall in Shorouk City, regarding it a leading destination for companies and entrepreneurs seeking flexible workspaces equipped with the latest technologies and world-class services, which will enhance the project’s position as one of the most prominent integrated commercial and service centers in the region. ... He expressed his pride in having one of the world’s leading brands specializing in workspaces joining Solaria Mall project, pointing out that Regus represents a qualitative addition that enhances the project’s standing and raises the level of services offered within it. ... The presence of a global brand of this magnitude reflects the confidence of global institutions in the quality of the company’s projects, and also contributes to attracting more companies and entrepreneurs, while providing clients with an integrated business environment that supports growth and innovation and delivers real added value for both investors and users. ... He pointed out that Solaria Mall enjoys a prime strategic location in the heart of Shorouk City, directly next to the French University in Egypt and on two main roads with a pedestrian walkway in between, making it a vital link between residential and service areas and giving it a strong competitive advantage as an integrated destination for commercial, administrative, and medical activities. ... He confirmed that the project was designed according to a comprehensive vision for mixed-use developments, encompassing commercial, administrative, and medical units of varying sizes, while adhering to the highest planning and operational standards to ensure maximum investment returns for clients and meet the evolving needs of the real estate market in new cities, especially in areas experiencing rapid population growth. ... #### IWG expands its footprint in Egypt amid rising demand for flexible workspaces ... Youssef Naguib, IWG General Manager in Egypt, said that “with this latest opening, we continue to establish a stronger and larger presence in Egypt. ... Our ongoing expansion coincides with more companies discovering the advantages of flexible working, most notably its immense popularity among employees as it improves work-life balance. Flexible working has also proven numerous benefits for companies, including increased productivity, the ability to expand or contract at reduced costs, and access to thousands of locations.” ... He added: “The business landscape in Egypt is evolving rapidly, and we are witnessing a clear shift in how Egyptian companies of all sizes and industries utilize office space, prioritizing flexibility and low-capital models. We will continue to expand our network to include more cities across Egypt, providing a highly productive environment for both startups and large corporations, enabling them to scale their operations efficiently and best serve their employees.” ... IWG is the world’s largest provider of flexible workspaces, enabling its clients to use the IWG app to access its international network of thousands of locations across more than 120 countries."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Aswaq Developments Partners with IWG to Launch Regus Workspace at Solaria Mall in El Shorouk City,economickey.com (يسرا),2026-06-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economickey.com/2026/06/21/aswaq-developments-partners-with-iwg-to-launch-regus-workspace-at-solaria-mall-in-el-shorouk-city/,"Aswaq Developments Partners with IWG to Launch Regus Workspace at Solaria Mall in El Shorouk City ... Aswaq Developments company announced the signing of a cooperation agreement with IWG, the world’s largest provider of flexible work solutions, to add Regus brand center to Solaria Mall project in Shorouk City, driven by its commitment to attracting leading international companies and renowned brands. ... The agreement was signed by Moamen Rehan, Aswaq Developments CEO, and Youssef Naguib, IWG general manager in Egypt. ... Moamen Rehan, Aswaq Developments CEO, said that this strategic partnership aligns with the company’s plan to enhance the investment value of its projects and create an integrated business environment that meets the highest international standards, fulfilling the aspirations of investors, entrepreneurs, and companies seeking modern and advanced workspaces. ... He noted tgat due to this agreement, REGUS was chosen to establish its new headquarters within Solaria Mall in Shorouk City, regarding it a leading destination for companies and entrepreneurs seeking flexible workspaces equipped with the latest technologies and world-class services, which will enhance the project’s position as one of the most prominent integrated commercial and service centers in the region. ... Aswaq Developments Begins Construction of ... aria Mall in El Shorouk City and Plans New Project Launches ... He emphasized that Solaria Mall is the fourth commercial project by Aswaq Developments and one of the most important mixed-use projects in Shorouk City, as it includes commercial, administrative, and medical activities, along with restaurants, services, and modern workspaces, creating a comprehensive experience for both visitors and investors. ... He expressed his pride have one of the world’s leading brands specializing in workspaces joining Solaria Mall project, pointing that Regus represents a qualitative addition that enhances the project’s standing and raises the level of services offered within it, as the presence of a global brand of this magnitude reflects the confidence of global institutions in the quality of the company’s projects, besides contributing to attract more companies and entrepreneurs and provide clients with an integrated business environment that supports growth and innovation, achieving real added value for both investors and users. ... He pointed that Solaria Mall enjoys a prime strategic location in the heart of Shorouk City, located directly next to the French University in Egypt and on two main roads with a pedestrian walkway in between, which makes it a vital link between residential and service areas, giving it a strong competitive advantage as an integrated destination for commercial, administrative, and medical activities. ... He assured that the project was designed according to a comprehensive vision for mixed-use developments, encompassing commercial, administrative, and medical units of varying sizes, while adhering to the highest planning and operation to ensure maximum investment returns for clients and meets the evolving needs of the real estate market in new cities, especially in areas experiencing rapid population growth. ... Youssef Naguib, IWG General Manager in Egypt, said that “with this latest opening, we continue to establish a stronger and larger presence in Egypt, our ongoing expansion coincides with more companies discovering the advantages of flexible working, most notably its immense popularity among employees as it improves work-life balance, besides flexible working has also proven numerous benefits for companies, including increased productivity, the ability to expand or contract at reduced costs, and access to thousands of locations. ... He added “business landscape in Egypt is evolving rapidly, and we are witnessing a clear shift in how Egyptian companies of all sizes and industries utilize office space, prioritizing flexibility and low-capitalization models, thus we will continue to expand our network to include more cities across Egypt, providing a highly productive environment for both startups and large corporations, enabling them to scale their operations efficiently and best serve their employees. ... IWG is the world’s largest provider of flexible workspaces, as it enables its clients to use the IWG app to access its international network of thousands of locations all over 120 countries. ... ### أسواق للتطوير توقع شراكة مع IWG العالمية لافتتاح مقر Regus في مول سولاريا"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG launches Openoffice in Oslo and expands across Norway | Spacefinder,spacefinder.no,2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://spacefinder.no/en/insights/iwg-openoffice-expansion-oslo,"IWG launches Openoffice in Oslo and expands across Norway | Spacefinder ... We are a little late with this one, but the news is too good to pass over in silence. In May, Næringseiendom reported that IWG, the world's largest provider of flexible office solutions, is launching an entirely new concept in Norway. It is called Openoffice, and it is only the latest piece of an expansion that has moved surprisingly fast over the past year. ... Openoffice is a new brand from IWG, which already operates Regus and Spaces in Norway. The concept is built around smaller spaces, from 300 to around 600 m², placed in the four largest cities. The centres are unstaffed and located close to centres IWG already runs, which lets the company extend its network without building up new staffing at every site. ... IWG is open about its ambitions. The company says Openoffice will offer smaller spaces of 300 to around 600 m² in the four largest cities, according to partnership manager Moeez Asif speaking to Næringseiendom. The plan is five Openoffice locations during 2026, spread across Oslo, Trondheim, Bergen and Stavanger. ... Openoffice does not arrive alone. Over the past year IWG has signed one partnership after another with Norwegian landlords. ... At Høvik they opened a 734 m² Regus centre at Fjordveien 1, and in Oslo, IWG took over the former 657 premises at Fredensborgveien 22 under the Spaces brand, alongside landlord Heimstaden. The latter is a story worth noting. For more than a decade, 657 was one of Oslo's best-known gathering points for creative and startup communities, before the operation was sold on, went bankrupt, and finally ended up with a global operator. It says something about how demanding it is to run coworking on your own, and why many landlords now prefer to bring in an established operator instead. ... The numbers speak clearly. IWG went from 24 centres in Norway in January 2025 to 27 centres by June of the same year, and the figure has only continued to grow. The company says it wants to cover the whole country by 2030, aiming to open around ten new centres a year, including in smaller towns such as Tønsberg, Lillestrøm and Tromsø. IWG reports an average occupancy of 78 percent across its Norwegian centres. ... What makes this interesting is that IWG is growing into a market that is actually struggling. UNION's coworking survey for the winter of 2025 showed that occupancy in Oslo centres fell to 69 percent, while operators themselves say occupancy needs to exceed 82 percent for operations to be profitable. Only around 40 percent of the centres were at a level that implies profitable operation."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express At Crowne Plaza KLCC,www.businesstoday.com.my,2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-18 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.businesstoday.com.my/2026/06/18/iwg-launches-malaysias-first-regus-express-at-crowne-plaza-klcc/,"IWG Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express At Crowne Plaza KLCC ... # IWG Launches Malaysia’s First Regus Express At Crowne Plaza KLCC ... International Workplace Group (IWG) has launched Malaysia’s first Regus Express workspace at Crowne Plaza Kuala Lumpur City Centre (KLCC), marking a new step in the expansion of hotel-integrated flexible workspaces in the country. The new facility spans 148 square metres and is designed as a compact, hotel-based workspace for business travellers and professionals seeking mobility and convenience in Kuala Lumpur’s central business district. Located along Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, the workspace sits within walking distance of MRT and LRT connections and is close to major commercial hubs, embassies, retail and dining areas as well as key landmarks including the Petronas Twin Towers and Kuala Lumpur Convention Centre. The launch comes as demand for flexible working solutions continues to grow, with businesses increasingly shifting towards hybrid and capital-light office models. Industry forecasts suggest flexible workspaces could account for up to 30% of commercial real estate by 2030. ... IWG said the opening follows a strong start to 2026, with the group recording its highest ever revenue, cash flow and earnings growth in the first quarter. The company added more than 382 new locations globally during the period and now operates more than 5,000 flexible workspaces across 120 countries. ... In Malaysia, IWG currently runs 48 centres under its Regus, Spaces, HQ and Signature brands, with 36 located in Kuala Lumpur and Selangor. ... IWG founder and chief executive Mark Dixon said Kuala Lumpur remains an important growth market for the group as demand for flexible workspace continues to rise. ... “Kuala Lumpur is an excellent fit for our continued expansion in Malaysia, strengthening our presence in an established market and introducing the Regus Express brand. As demand continues to grow for more flexible, capital-light workspace solutions, we are well positioned to support businesses with greater choice, efficiency and access to high-quality workspaces through this latest opening,” he said. ... IWG Country Head for Malaysia, Singapore and Brunei Vijayakumar Tangarasan said the KLCC launch reflects a shift in corporate workspace needs. ... “The KLCC area remains one of Kuala Lumpur’s most sought-after business districts, and this landmark launch allows us to meet the rapidly growing demand for flexible workspace solutions in an exceptionally connected and strategic location. As corporate Malaysia shifts away from traditional fixed office leases toward capital-light, agile strategies, businesses require premium spaces that match their pace. This collaboration with Crowne Plaza KLCC establishes a new benchmark for prime real estate utilisation, delivering a highly connected, productive environment that seamlessly blends core business functionality with luxury lifestyle amenities,” he said. As part of the partnership, IWG members will also be able to access preferential rates on food and beverage, room bookings and banquet packages at Crowne Plaza KLCC through registration via the IHG application."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,International Workplace Group opens its biggest Regus centre in Egypt,www.zawya.com,2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.zawya.com/en/press-release/companies-news/international-workplace-group-opens-its-biggest-regus-centre-in-egypt-c7f9s0lj,"International Workplace Group opens its biggest Regus centre in Egypt | ZAWYA ... # International Workplace Group opens its biggest Regus centre in Egypt ... - Regus District 5 is an impressive workspace complete with co-working spaces, private offices, meeting rooms and creative areas - The signing coincides with the rising demand in Egypt for platform working as companies of all sizes increasingly provide employees with access to a network of locations to maintain productivity and employee satisfaction - This opening follows a partnership agreement with ElTarek Group for 2 centres in Cairo & Alexandria - The location comes on the heels of International Workplace Group’s rapid global network expansion in Q1 2026, with record signings and openings - In Q1 2026, IWG signed 382 new locations globally ... International Workplace Group, the world's largest platform for work with brands including Spaces and Regus, is opening a state-of-the-art flexible workspace in District 5 Mall in Cairo. With the long-term shift to more flexible ways of working, IWG is expanding its network to keep pace with rising demand across Egypt and the Middle East. ... The addition of International Workplace Group’s latest location comes on the heels of the business posting its highest-ever revenue, cashflow and earnings growth in its history and achieving rapid network growth, with more new locations signed and opened in 2025 than in the entire first two decades of its operations. In Q1 2026, IWG’s network expanded even faster, with record signings and openings representing significant year-on-year growth. IWG’s network now comprises more than one million rooms in 121 countries. ... Situated in the bustling Cairo destination, this new location is part of a drive by International Workplace Group to meet the sharply rising demand for top-class flexible working space in the country. This opening comes as part of IWG partnership with ElTarek Group, with plans to open an additional centre in Alexandria. ... The 1,560 square-metre building is considered IWG’s biggest centre in Egypt, and will provide space for established firms and start-ups across a range of industries, while International Workplace Group’s Design Your Own Office service allows companies to tailor their space entirely to their requirements. The new Regus location will include facilities including private offices, meeting rooms, co-working and creative spaces. ... On this occasion, Mark Dixon, CEO & Founder of International Workplace Group PLC, commented:“We are establishing a stronger and much-needed footprint in Egypt with this latest opening. As an important business hub, District 5 is a fantastic place for us to boost our expansion plans. We are very pleased to work in partnership with ElTarek Group to develop the Regus brand under a management agreement that will add a cutting-edge workspace to their building.” ... Kory Thompson, Senior Vice President of IWG for the Middle East and Africa stated: “The opening of our largest Centre in Egypt represents a pivotal milestone in our ongoing mission to broaden our network. Recognizing Egypt's profound economic significance and its role as a vital nexus for businesses in the Middle East & North Africa region, we are accelerating our expansion to meet the surging demands for flexible working solutions, ensuring we provide the essential infrastructure that empowers businesses to thrive in a dynamic, modern economy."" ... Youssef Najeeb, IWG Country Manager for Egypt added: “Egypt’s dynamic business landscape is evolving rapidly. We are seeing a distinct shift in how Egyptian companies of all sizes are consuming real estate with firms prioritizing flexibility and capital light models. We will continue to expand our network to more cities across Egypt, providing companies, start-ups, and freelancers a highly productive environment that allows them to scale their operations for the best interest of their business needs and their people.” ... As the ongoing shift towards more flexible, decentralised and hybrid models of working accelerates, the potential for further growth is exponential with an estimated 1.2 billion white-collar workers globally and a total addressable market of more than $2 trillion. In 2025, International Workplace Group signed 1,132 new locations, 99% of which are partnership agreements, and counts 83 per cent of Fortune 500 companies among its customer base. ... With explosive market growth as companies of all sizes adopt more flexible and decentralised models for the long-term, it is predicted that 30% of all commercial real estate will be flexible workspace by 2030. With International Workplace Group, partners are able to capitalise on this fast-growing sector, while being supported by International Workplace Group’s unparalleled experience. Hybrid working offers companies a significantly lower cost base with an average saving of $11,000 per employee[ii]. ... International Workplace Group (IWG) is the world’s leading platform for work enabling companies of all sizes to work more productively and profitably. We create personal, financial, and strategic value for the most exciting companies and well-known organizations on the planet as well as individuals and the next generation of industry leaders. All of them harness the power of IWG’s platform to increase their productivity, efficiency, agility, and market proximity. ... International Workplace Group’s unrivalled network coverage includes more than 5,000 locations across 120 countries and 83% of Fortune 500 companies are amongst our growing customer base. In Q1 2026, IWG’s network expanded even faster with 382 signings and 222 openings in 2026 vs 224 signings and 165 openings in 2025. ... Our brands including Regus, Spaces, HQ and Signature serve millions of people, providing professional, inspiring and collaborative workspaces and all our digital services are available via the IWG app."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,INTERNATIONAL WORKPLACE GROUP (IWG) EXPANDS ITS PRESENCE IN SERBIA WITH NEW BUSINESS CENTRES IN NIŠ AND BELGRADE,www.officerentinfo.rs,2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.officerentinfo.rs/article/officemarket-news/international-workplace-group-iwg-expands-its-presence-in-serbia-with-new-business-centres-in-nis-and-belgrade,"HQ IRIN Business Center in Niš and Regus Hyde Park City in Belgrade are impressive IWG workspace locations, offering coworking areas, private offices, meeting rooms, and creative workspaces. These new openings follow IWG’s strong global expansion in the first quarter of 2026, during which the company recorded a record number of new signings and openings, with 382 new locations contracted worldwide. ... International Workplace Group, the world’s leading provider of hybrid work solutions, with brands including Spaces and Regus, is opening a state-of-the-art flexible workspace in Belgrade. This expansion follows the recent launch of the HQ IRIN Business Center location in Niš, further strengthening IWG’s presence in Serbia. The adoption of hybrid working continues to grow across the country, and IWG is expanding its network to meet the increasing demand for flexible workspaces. ... The opening of new IWG locations in Belgrade and Niš is part of the company’s continued growth following its strongest business performance in history and the accelerated expansion of its network. During 2025 alone, IWG signed and opened more new locations than it had during its first two decades of operation combined. In the first quarter of 2026, the IWG network continued to expand at an even faster pace, achieving a record number of signed agreements and new openings, representing significant growth compared to the same period the previous year. As the global leader in hybrid work, IWG now operates a network of more than one million workspaces across 121 countries, enabling companies to operate through a global workplace platform supported by flexible infrastructure and digital connectivity. ... Located in Belgrade and Ni ... , the new sites are part of International Workplace Group’s efforts to meet the growing demand for premium flexible workspaces in these parts of Serbia. This trend is driven by the continued shift toward hybrid work models, alongside the increasing adoption of technological solutions and platforms that help companies improve agility, productivity, and employee satisfaction. ... Regus Hyde Park City, a premium business facility spanning 739 square meters within The Hyde Park City business park, which covers 65,000 square meters, combines contemporary architecture with sophisticated functionality. Situated near Belgrade’s newly built railway station, the location offers significant potential due to its position within one of the region’s key transportation hubs, connecting local, regional, and international high-speed rail services. The complex features energy-efficient systems, flexible layouts, and advanced infrastructure designed to meet the needs of modern businesses. ... Opened in May, the building provides space for established companies and startups from a wide range of industries, including technology and software development, financial services, consulting, and other professional services. IWG’s Design Your Own Office solution enables businesses to fully customize their workspace according to their needs, responding to the growing demand for flexible and scalable workplace solutions. The new Regus location includes private offices, meeting rooms, coworking areas, and creative spaces. ... The building owners chose to invest in the IWG platform to maximize the potential of their property and generate higher returns on investment while responding to the growing demand for hybrid working. ... HQ IRIN Business Center in Niš, with a total area of 1,187 square meters, is located in a strategically important industrial and business zone on the site of the former Electronics Industry Niš complex. The location has long been recognized as one of the city’s key industrial and commercial centers, giving it strong business credibility. Its proximity to universities and technical schools also provides access to highly qualified talent in engineering, IT, and manufacturing, supporting the needs of modern knowledge-based industries. ... As the shift toward more flexible, decentralized, and hybrid working models continues to accelerate, the potential for further growth remains substantial, with an estimated 1.2 billion office workers worldwide and a total market opportunity valued at more than $2 trillion. During 2025, IWG signed agreements for 1,132 new locations, 99% of which were partnership agreements, while 83% of Fortune 500 companies are part of its customer base. ... “We are seeing growing demand for our solutions as companies of all sizes transition to operating models that require lower capital investment. As a result, businesses are experiencing firsthand the benefits of hybrid and more flexible working models, which directly contribute to higher employee satisfaction, increased productivity, and greater operational efficiency. Our latest openings in Belgrade and Niš further mark IWG’s expansion into a strategically important market, enabling us to provide businesses with greater flexibility and access to high-quality workspaces closer to where people live and work.” ... IWG’s network spans more than 5,000 locations across 120 countries, while 83% of Fortune 500 companies form part of its growing customer base. In the first quarter of 2026, the IWG network continued to expand at an accelerated pace, with 382 agreements signed and 222 locations opened, compared to 224 agreements signed and 165 locations opened during the same period in 2025. ... The company’s brands, including Regus, Spaces, HQ, and Signature, serve millions of people worldwide by providing professional, inspiring, and collaborative workspaces, while all digital services are available through the IWG app."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"IWG Focuses on Expansion Across Hungary to Meet Demand for Flexible, Hybrid Working - Budapest Business Journal",bbj.hu,2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bbj.hu/business/people/hr/iwg-focuses-on-expansion-across-hungary-to-meet-demand-for-flexible-hybrid-working/,"IWG Focuses on Expansion Across Hungary to Meet Demand for Flexible, Hybrid Working - Budapest Business Journal ... As companies of all sizes increasingly shift toward capital-light operating models, prioritizing flexibility and opting to rent rather than own office space, global workspace platform IWG is expanding its footprint across Hungary to meet the growing demand. ... With a network spanning more than 120 countries, IWG operates not only as a workspace provider but as a platform, offering access to a global ecosystem of offices alongside additional business support services. László Márkus, the company’s country manager, speaks to the Budapest Business Journal about regional opportunities, partner-driven growth, and how flexibility is becoming a core business expectation rather than a perk. ... László Márkus: We are focused on growth right across Hungary to meet the growing demand for hybrid and flexible workspace solutions. Budapest remains our core market, as it is the country’s primary business hub, and demand is naturally very strong. At the same time, there is a clear and growing need beyond the capital, particularly in larger regional cities and in suburban areas around Budapest. ... We operate 23 locations across Hungary, including 19 Regus centers, two Spaces locations, one HQ and one Signature site. The majority of these are located in Budapest, with two locations in Debrecen, and one each in Szeged and Miskolc. Each workspace provides state-of-the-art private offices, meeting rooms, co-working and creative environments for companies of all sizes, accessible through the IWG app, which also connects members to the company’s global network and a range of additional business support services. ... We are looking at new locations with thriving business communities. This includes not only major regional cities but also fast-growing suburban zones, enabling professionals to work wherever is most convenient and productive. I see strong potential around Lake Balaton. The “staycation” concept has gained traction, and flexible workspaces could fit very well into that lifestyle, allowing people to combine work and leisure more seamlessly. I would also like to see further expansion in western Hungary, closer to the Austrian border, where there is strong cross-border economic activity. ... LM: Our brand portfolio is similar to that of major hotel chains like Marriott or Hilton; we have a solution for every type of building and customer. Regus, our largest and best-known brand, caters to a broad business audience, including corporates and SMEs that require professional, efficient workspace solutions in well-connected locations. Spaces targets businesses seeking a more creative, collaborative experience, combining design-led environments with a strong sense of community. In Hungary, we look at factors such as the local business ecosystem, workforce demographics, and the maturity of the flexible workspace market when deciding which brand to introduce in a given location. At the same time, we are looking to further expand our portfolio by introducing more HQ-branded locations, as well as smaller centers under our OpenOffice brand. These concepts allow us to stay ahead of local market needs across Hungary, providing greater flexibility and long-term value for partners and customers, particularly in secondary cities or suburban areas. A new HQ center will be opening in Budapest’s District XIV in the near future. This expansion brings coverage to a previously underserved residential area, opening up new access to workspace closer to where people live. ... LM: Our expansion model is based on a partnership model with property owners and investors. We work closely with local landlords and property owners to transform traditional or underutilized office spaces into profitable, flexible work environments that better match today’s market needs. For partners, this approach offers several advantages. It significantly improves occupancy rates, diversifies income streams, and helps future-proof their assets in a rapidly changing office landscape. At the same time, it allows us to expand our network quickly and efficiently, with terrific mutual incentives. A strong partner in Hungary is typically one who understands the local market well, wants to capitalize on the long-term shift towards flexibility, and is open to innovation. This model has proven highly effective across markets globally where the office sector is transforming, as it enables both sides to adapt more quickly to changing demand. ... : The competition for talent in Hungary has intensified in recent years, and flexibility has become a key differentiator for employers. Companies are increasingly using flexible workspaces to offer employees greater choice in where and how they work. This can mean working closer to home, avoiding long commutes, or having access to a professional workspace on demand. These factors directly impact employee satisfaction and retention, while also enabling companies to tap into a wider talent pool beyond their immediate headquarters. One of our recent studies reveals that 81% of CHROs state that eliminating long daily commutes would positively impact performance, and 67% believe it would improve employee wellbeing. ... also seeing a shift in ... clients we serve. ... flexible workspaces were traditionally associated with SMEs and startups, large corporations and companies of all sizes are now showing growing interest in immediate, scalable solutions. They value the ability to adjust their office footprint without long-term commitments quickly. Flexibility is ... seen as an added benefit. It is becoming a baseline expectation among employees, and companies that fail ... provide it risk falling behind in ... talent competition. ... with cost efficiency and risk management ... long-term ... . This shifts ... cost structure from capital expenditure ... efficient in terms ... resource use, as they reduce underutilized office ... and optimize energy consumption. Access to ... significantly reduces carbon emissions by removing ... long daily commutes ... a»CBD five days"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"Hybrid Work, Local Hubs and the Future of Offices - CanadianSME Small Business Magazine",canadiansme.ca (SK Uddin),2026-06-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://canadiansme.ca/hybrid-work-local-hubs-and-the-future-of-offices/,"In an exclusive interview with The CanadianSME Small Business Magazine, Mark Dixon, Founder and CEO of International Workplace Group, shares a forward-looking perspective on how work is being reshaped across cities, suburbs, and communities. Drawing on decades of experience building one of the world’s largest workspace networks, Mark explains why ... future of work is no longer tied to ... how flexibility, technology, and access are redefining ... Mark Dixon is one of Europe’s best-known entrepreneurs and, since founding the Regus Group in Brussels, Belgium in 1989, he has achieved a formidable reputation for leadership and innovation. By understanding the way that globalization, personal mobility and digital technology have enabled new ways of working, Mark has overseen the growth of IWG into the world’s largest workspace provider. Prior to Regus and IWG he established businesses in the retail and wholesale food industry. Mark has received many awards for enterprise and is widely acknowledged as one of the pioneers of the workspace industry who revolutionized the way business approaches its property needs with his vision of the future of work. ... In 2025, more new locations were signed and opened in a single year than in the entire first two decades of our operations. Our network now comprises more than one million rooms in 122 countries and with a substantial pipeline in place, our growth will continue to accelerate rapidly in the years ahead. ... We are focused on rapidly expanding our coverage to create a truly global network of buildings from the largest cities to smaller towns and the provinces. Our capital-light expansion strategy, delivered through partnerships with property owners and investors, enables companies of all sizes to work productively in locations that are convenient to their people. ... Increasingly, our solutions are helping companies move away from the expense and inflexibility of long-term leases, replacing them with flexible, cost-effective agreements for smaller fully equipped spaces in one of our centres. At the same time, they retain the ability to access more than 5,000 locations worldwide. ... IWG operates a portfolio of 15 workplace brands – the largest workspace platform in the world – including Regus, Spaces, and HQ. In 2025, IWG signed 1,132 new centres globally and opened 782 new workspaces. ... IWG is adding a record number of locations globally and expanding rapidly across Canadian cities and suburbs—from Burnaby and Surrey to Mississauga and Moncton—what’s driving this demand for more localized working, and what are the main benefits for both employees and employers? ... Today, the remarkable advances in cloud technology and video conferencing software – both vital to enabling effective hybrid working – mean workers no longer need to travel long distances daily. As a result, we are seeing a redistribution of the geography of work with teams able to spend a meaningful amount of time in their local communities alongside the city centre. Innovations in technology will continue to advance in years to come and will radically underline and fuel the flexibility of location. ... The rising demand for more localized working has led to a large number of our new IWG centres opening in the heart of local communities, suburbs and rural areas, enabling many people around the world to say farewell to long daily commutes. ... Smaller cities and towns right across the globe including in Canada have seen a dramatic increase in signings including Moncton, NB, Bracebridge, ON and Mission BC. ... Burnaby, British Columbia, ranked as Canada’s best commuter town due to its exceptional transport connectivity to the city centre, its many lifestyle amenities, and access to flexible workspaces. The town is an example of a central location with multi-line rapid transit access via the SkyTrain, a pedestrian-friendly core, strong digital infrastructure and a thriving local economy – making it well-suited to hybrid workers seeking balance without sacrificing career opportunities. IWG currently has four flexible workspace locations in Burnaby and opened a new Regus just last year at 4185 Still Creek Drive. ... Hamilton, Ontario, was the runner-up, scoring highly for housing affordability, access to green spaces, creative and social venues, and lifestyle amenities. Even though it isn’t the closest commuter town in the GTA, its direct access to Toronto via the GO Train, a revitalized downtown core, a growing cultural hub, affordability, and ease of access to nature, balances local living with access to Canada’s major city centre. In Hamilton, IWG has a bustling and vibrant Regus location at 21 King Street West. ... In much the same way that hotel groups like Marriott and IHG offer a brand for every market segment, we do the same with our workplace brands. By offering a range of brands in Canada, we’re able to meet the needs of corporates, SMEs and solo professionals alike. ... There is a different brand for every type of customer. Spaces, for example, offers professional, collaborative workspaces in beautiful and creative environments. Our largest network of workspaces Regus supports any individual or business looking for a professional workspace environment that gives them the scale they need to succeed, and HQ appeals to businesses of all shapes and sizes by providing efficient, functional space, with all the essentials needed to set up and be ready to go at a lower price point. ... base that includes the ... Fortune 5 ... the next major shift in how and where work gets done ... small and medium‑ ... to stay ahead of"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"ZAWYA: IWG Global Q1 system-wide revenue grows 9%, fueled by unprecedented demand and expansion in Egypt | Longbridge",longbridge.com,2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://longbridge.com/news/288570093,"YA: IWG Global Q1 system-wide revenue grows 9%, fueled by unprecedented demand and expansion in Egypt | Longbridge ... IWG reported a 9% year-on-year increase in Q1 2026 system-wide revenue, driven by strong global demand and rapid expansion in Egypt. The company signed 382 new centers globally, with Managed and Franchise fee income surging 70%. Maintaining full-year guidance, IWG anticipates adjusted EBITDA between $585 million and $625 million. CEO Mark Dixon highlighted the success of their capital-light growth strategy, noting over 1 million rooms across 120 countries. ... - Egypt among IWG’s fastest-growing markets for second consecutive year, with plans for 150 centers in the country by 2030 ... CAIRO, EGYPT - International Workplace Group (IWG), the world's largest provider of hybrid work solutions with brands like Regus and Spaces, announced strong first-quarter 2026 results, including a 9% year-on-year growth in system-wide revenue. This steady global performance is mirrored by explosive growth in Egypt, where surging demand is making it one of IWG's fastest-growing markets and a hub for major investment. ... A significant driver of this success was the rapid expansion of its capital-light partnership model, which saw Managed and Franchise fee income grow by an impressive 70% to $39 million. This growth is set to continue, with 382 new centers signed globally in the first quarter alone. Based on this strong performance, the company has maintained its full-year 2026 guidance, with an anticipated adjusted EBITDA in the range of $585 million to $625 million. ... The company's strong first-quarter performance was reflected across its key metrics. Globally, IWG achieved a group revenue of $958 million, a 4% increase from the previous year, and a system-wide revenue of $1,166 million, up 9% year-on-year. ... The global trend towards flexible work, driven by economic uncertainty and the need for business agility, is particularly pronounced in Egypt. Companies across the country are rapidly adopting hybrid models to reduce costs, which can average up to $11,000 per employee, while employees are seeking a better work-life balance and an escape from the 2-3 hour daily commutes common in Cairo. This demand has prompted IWG to embark on an aggressive expansion plan, with a goal of reaching 150 centers across Egypt by 2030. ... This expansion includes several high-profile new centers in Cairo, including the upcoming ""Spaces at The Arc"" in New Cairo is set to be IWG's largest flexible workspace in the world, signaling Egypt's critical importance to the company's global strategy. ... Mark Dixon, Chief Executive of IWG plc, commented on the global performance, stating, ""We set out a clear strategy at our first Investor Day in New York in December 2023 for capital light growth to deliver cashflow and business simplification. As we outlined in our Investor Day in December 2025 – this is what we have been delivering on, and we will continue to do so. We continue to have structural tailwinds and a business which is both prepared for and delivering network growth. In the last twelve months, more locations were opened than we had open after fifteen years of operating. We now have over 1 million rooms in over 120 countries with a significant pipeline. This is expected to drive our future growth in revenue, EBITDA and cash flow”. ... IWG's investment is not only changing the commercial real estate landscape but is also attracting multinational corporations to Egypt, boosting the economy, and supporting the decentralization of work away from congested city centers and into suburban hubs, coastal cities, and the New Administrative Capital. ... International Workplace Group’s unrivalled network coverage includes more than 4,600 locations across 120 countries and 83% of Fortune 500 companies are amongst our growing customer base. ... Our brands including Regus, Spaces, HQ and Signature serve millions of people, providing professional, inspiring and collaborative workspaces and all our digital services are available via the IWG app."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,Flexible Workspace Provider Regus Expands in Abuja,punchng.com (Our Reporters),2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://punchng.com/flexible-workspace-provider-eyes-abuja-business-growth/,"Flexible Workspace Provider Regus Expands in Abuja ... # Flexible workspace provider eyes Abuja business growth May 28, 2026 1:25 am Caption: Sales Director, IWG, Joshua Durunguma; IWG Growth and Property Director, Oyebimpe Oyedeji; Logitech Integrated Services, represented by Arc. Sylvester Egweni; IWG Country Manager, Ayo Akinmade, during the opening of a new Regus facility in Abuja... recently Photo: IWD ... A global workspace provider, Regus, has expanded its presence in Abuja with the opening of a new facility aimed at providing flexible office solutions for entrepreneurs, startups and corporate organisations. Speaking during the opening ceremony recently, the Country Manager of International Workplace Group, Ayo Akinmade, said the project was inspired by growing demand for ready-to-use office spaces in major business districts across the Federal Capital Territory. According to him, the company’s vision is to strategically position workspace hubs in key commercial areas to ease the burden of setting up conventional offices for businesses. He explained that the firm had already established centres in the Central Business District and other commercial corridors, adding that Jabi was the next natural expansion point as part of plans to cover between eight and 10 locations in Abuja. ... “We are in 132 countries with more than 7,000 locations. If you sign up here and travel to Lagos, Port Harcourt, London, or any other city where we operate, you can use our spaces freely once your subscription is active,” he added. ... “Our business is ... to facilitate fraud. Our business is to facilitate legitimate ... operating. But where suspicious patterns emerge, we immediately alert law enforcement authorities,” ... . Akinmade added that the company continues to work closely with security agencies to strengthen preventive measures against fraudulent activities within its facilities. Also, a representative of Logitech Integrated Services, Sylvester Egweni said the collaboration was a natural decision for the indigenous company, given Regus’ global reputation in the co-working and serviced office industry. He described the partnership with the global workspace provider Regus as a strategic move aimed at aligning with an internationally recognised brand while expanding its footprint in Nigeria’s property development sector. ... According to him, Logitech, which was incorporated in December 2019, is positioning itself for international relevance through partnerships with established global brands. “I think that’s a no-brainer because Regus is a renowned international brand, and for us at Logitech, an indigenous Nigerian company looking to go global too, it’s not rocket science that you partner with a renowned global brand like Regus,” he said. Egweni explained that Logitech’s role in the partnership focused on the development and delivery of the physical infrastructure that supports Regus’ operations. He noted that the company handled facility development, including infrastructure and interior finishing required to make the workspace fully operational. “Part of our core mandate is property development and projects similar to the kind of services delivered for Regus. What they do is co-working, and all that, but the facilities people come to use have to be provided by someone, and that’s where we come in,” he added. The opening of the facility is expected to strengthen the growing demand for flexible workspaces and modern business environments in Nigeria’s commercial landscape."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG Revenue Rises as Network Expansion Accelerates in Q1 - Budapest Business Journal,bbj.hu,2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bbj.hu/business/real-estate/office-market/iwg-revenue-rises-as-network-expansion-accelerates-in-q1/,"IWG Revenue Rises as Network Expansion Accelerates in Q1 - Budapest Business Journal ... International Workplace Group started 2026 with continued revenue growth, supported by rising enterprise customer demand and strong momentum in its Managed & Franchised business. ... IWG, the world’s largest hybrid workspace platform, operates in more than 120 countries through workspace, professional services and digital brands including Regus, Spaces, HQ, Signature and Instant Offices. The group released its trading statement for the three months ended March 31, 2026. ... System-wide revenue reached USD 1.166 billion in the first quarter, representing 9% year-on-year growth. Group revenue increased by 4% to USD 958 million. The company-owned business returned to revenue growth, with revenue up 2% year-on-year and revenue per available room, or RevPAR, rising by 6%. ... The company also continued to expand its global network at a faster pace than a year earlier. IWG signed 382 new locations in the first quarter of 2026, compared with 224 in Q1 2025. It opened 222 locations during the period, up from 165 in the same quarter last year. ... The Managed & Franchised division remained a key growth driver. Fee income in the business reached USD 39 million, up 70% year-on-year. Recurring managed fee income also continued to rise strongly, reflecting the increasing maturity of locations signed and opened in earlier periods. ... IWG said capital returns to shareholders are progressing in line with its strategy, with USD 75 million returned so far in 2026. ... “I am delighted with our strong start to 2026 as we continue the rapid growth of our network supported by increasing sales despite the challenging economic backdrop. Potential customers are requiring more flexibility in their Real Estate strategy to address the uncertainty arising from the impact of conflicts and the growing influence of AI. This is resulting in record levels of Enterprise customer enquiries as our coverage and network enable us to provide unique, flexible, global solutions. ... “Signings and openings continue to grow, allowing the flywheel of our business model to deliver greater cashflow while requiring less capital to grow than historically. This combination has enabled a return of over USD 230 mln to shareholders since our Investor Day in New York in December 2023 as we continue our journey of capital returns,” said Mark Dixon, CEO of IWG plc. ... Hungary remains an established market within IWG’s international network, with all of the company’s main brands represented locally. IWG currently operates 23 active office locations in Hungary, including 19 in Budapest and four in regional cities: two in Debrecen, one in Szeged and one in Miskolc. ... The local portfolio includes 19 Regus locations, two Spaces locations, one HQ location and one Signature location. ... IWG Revenue Rises as Network Expansion Accelerates in Q1"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG starts 2026 with revenue growth and accelerated network expansion,www.officerentinfo.hu,2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.officerentinfo.hu/article/officemarket-news/iwg-starts-2026-with-revenue-growth-and-accelerated-network-expansion,"International Workplace Group plc (IWG), the world’s largest hybrid workspace platform with a network in over 120 countries through workspace, professional services and digital brands such as Regus, Spaces, HQ, Signature and Instant Offices, today announces its trading statement for the three months ended 31 March 2026. ... The Group delivered continued year-on-year revenue growth in the first quarter, supported by rapid network expansion, increasing enterprise customer enquiries and strong growth in its Managed & Franchised business. ... Group performance – revenue growth supported by network expansion IWG delivered system-wide revenue of $1,166m, representing 9% year-on-year growth, while Group revenue increased by 4% year-on-year to $958m. The Company-owned business returned to revenue growth, with year-on-year revenue up 2% and RevPAR increasing by 6%. ... Network growth – higher signings and openings year-on-year The Group continued to expand its network and coverage rapidly in the first quarter, with both signings and openings ahead of the same period last year. IWG signed 382 new locations in Q1 2026, compared with 224 in Q1 2025, and opened 222 locations, compared with 165 in the same period last year. ... Divisional performance – Managed & Franchised continues to drive scalable growth The Managed & Franchised division continued to be a key growth driver, with fee income of $39m, up 70% year-on-year. Recurring managed fee income also continued to grow strongly, reflecting the increasing maturity of previously signed and opened locations. ... Shareholder returns – continued progress in line with strategy Capital returns to shareholders are progressing in line with IWG’s strategy, with $75m returned to shareholders so far in 2026. ... “I am delighted with our strong start to 2026 as we continue the rapid growth of our network supported by increasing sales despite the challenging economic backdrop. Potential customers are requiring more flexibility in their Real Estate strategy to address the uncertainty arising from the impact of conflicts and the growing influence of AI. This is resulting in record levels of Enterprise customer enquiries as our coverage and network enable us to provide unique, flexible, global solutions. ... Signings and openings continue to grow, allowing the flywheel of our business model to deliver greater cashflow while requiring less capital to grow than historically. This combination has enabled a return of over $230m to shareholders since our Investor Day in New York in December 2023 as we continue our journey of capital returns.” ... Hungary remains an established market within IWG’s international network, with all of the company’s main brands represented locally. IWG currently operates 23 active office locations in Hungary, including 19 in Budapest and four in regional cities: two in Debrecen, one in Szeged and one in Miskolc. The local portfolio includes 19 Regus locations, two Spaces locations, one HQ and one Signature location. ... Outlook Despite the wider macroeconomic backdrop, centre signings and openings continued to accelerate globally in the first quarter, while enterprise customer enquiries increased, sales rose and pricing remained positive. Accordingly, IWG’s expectations for 2026 remain unchanged. ... #### Regus Business Centres Hungary Kft. ... #### Flexible workspace ... #### Accelerate success in style — discover Regus Budapest Infopark ... #### Flexible workspace in Regus Köki Terminal Offices ... #### Flexible workspace in Regus Cedrus Offices ... #### Discover many ways"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG Q1 Earnings Call Highlights - Stock Observer,www.thestockobserver.com (George Bondi),2026-05-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thestockobserver.com/2026/05/15/iwg-q1-earnings-call-highlights.html,"IWG (LON:IWG) reported a stronger start to 2026, with executives saying demand for flexible workspace remained resilient despite macroeconomic uncertainty, geopolitical volatility and rising inflationary pressures. ... In a first-quarter trading update, Mark Dixon said the company delivered 4% group revenue growth and 9% system-wide revenue growth, describing the system revenue performance as “the best we’ve seen so far.” He said the results reflected both demand resilience and the strength of IWG’s global platform. ... Chief Financial Officer Charlie Steel said system-wide revenue rose 9% year-over-year to $1.17 billion, while group revenue increased 4% to $958 million. He said growth was increasingly being driven by IWG’s managed and franchised platform, which the company views as higher-margin, more scalable and more cash-generative. ... In the managed and franchised business, system revenue increased 41% year-over-year in the first quarter to $260 million, while fee income rose 70%. Recurring managed fee income grew 80% year-over-year to GBP 16 million for the quarter, which Steel said reflected both new openings and the maturity curve of existing centers. ... The company also reported continued expansion of its network. Dixon said IWG signed a record 380 deals in the quarter and opened more than 200 centers. Steel said the managed and franchised segment now has 336,000 rooms open, with a further 231,000 signed but not yet opened. Once those rooms are open and mature, Steel said the segment has potential annual system revenue of more than $1.9 billion. ... Dixon said the company-owned segment returned to headline revenue growth, giving ... WG growth from both its capital-light platform and its company-owned units. Steel said company-owned revenue increased 2% year-over-year, while revenue per available room, or RevPAR, rose 6 ... first-quarter ... was in line ... -year guidance ... - Adjusted EBITDA of $585 million to $625 million; - Revenue growth of at least ... 4%; - Recurring ... income of $80 million; - Maintenance of an investment- ... credit rating. ... Steel said IWG’s direct exposure to the Middle East is limited, though the company is monitoring the broader macroeconomic impact of the conflict, including global inflationary pressures. In response to an analyst question, Dixon said the Middle East represents “a couple of percent of revenue,” with roughly 70% to 80% of that in managed and franchised operations. He said current sales and performance in the region are down because of lower traffic, but managed and franchised signings have not been interrupted. ... broader uncertainty, including around artificial intelligence and future headcount needs, is encouraging companies to avoid long-term fixed commitments and seek more flexible workspace options. He said companies are focused on avoiding capital expenditures, securing shorter-term commitments, reducing space requirements and accessing globally scalable solutions. ... Steel said net debt increased during the quarter, primarily due to share buybacks, annual bonus payments and working capital timing effects. He said the company expects net debt to reduce from current levels by the end of the year, and later said it should return to year-end 2025 levels by the end of 2026. Steel added that IWG’s debt is fixed-rate, the company has no near-term financing requirements and management remains committed to maintaining an investment-grade rating. ... Executives said inflationary pressures have increased, particularly in areas such as energy and other costs that may ultimately affect salaries in some markets. Dixon said IWG is focused on keeping costs down and that improvements to its accounting and data systems are giving management better real-time visibility. He also said artificial intelligence could become a significant driver of cost efficiency over the coming years, although he cautioned that savings will take time to implement. ... On mergers and acquisitions, Steel said IWG is not pursuing transformational deals. Dixon described activity as small, low-cost bolt-ons, with some companies joining the platform through managed and franchised arrangements to gain access to IWG’s network and operating model. ... IWG plc, together with its subsidiaries, provides workspace solutions in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company offers office, coworking and collaboration, flexible and scalable, meeting, and lounges spaces; workplace recovery; memberships workspaces; and reception services and conference products. It provides its services franchise partners, landlords, and property owners under the Regus, Spaces, HQ, Signature, Basepoint, Stop & Work, The Office Operators, BizDojo, Open Office, No18, The Clubhouse, Central Working, and Copernico brands."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG grows revenue as global network expansion continues | Property Week,www.propertyweek.com (Jamie Bennett-Ness),2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.propertyweek.com/finance/iwg-grows-revenue-as-global-network-expansion-continues,"IWG grows revenue as global network expansion continues | Property Week ... International Workplace Group (IWG) has posted system-wide revenue of $1,166m (£861m) in Q1, up 9% year on year, led by the continued expansion of its global network of workspaces. ... Its global network continued to expand rapidly as it completed 382 signings, up from 224 on Q1 last year, and 222 openings, up from 165. Earlier this week, the group opened Humanly, a health and wellbeing centre, in South Kensington, London. ... The group – which is behind brands such as Regus, Spaces, HQ, Signature and Instant Offices – said it was maintaining full-year 2026 guidance with an adjusted EBITDA range of $585m to $625m (£585m to £462m) and company-owned revenue growth of at least 4% (currently at 2%). ... “strong start to 2026”, ... to its growing ... “Signings and openings continue to grow, allowing the flywheel of our business model to deliver greater cashflow while requiring less capital to grow than historically. This combination has enabled a return of over $230m [£170m] to shareholders since our Investor Day in New York in December 2023 as we continue our journey of capital returns.” ... The company said it was taking proactive steps to reduce costs during Q2 and beyond in response to global inflationary pressures, but pointed to rising numbers of enterprise customer enquiries and sales and the growing number of centre openings, despite the challenging backdrop."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,IWG reports 4% revenue growth in the first quarter | Estates Gazette,www.estatesgazette.co.uk,2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.estatesgazette.co.uk/news/iwg-reports-4-revenue-growth-in-the-first-quarter/,"IWG reports 4% revenue growth in the first quarter | ... International Workplace Group has posted a 4% increase in group revenue for the first quarter, driven by rapid expansion of its managed and franchised platform. ... The hybrid workspace operator, which owns brands including Regus, Spaces and HQ, reported group revenue of $958m (£708m) for the three months to 31 March 2026, up from $924m (£682.4) a year earlier, a 4% increase. System-wide revenue rose 9% year on year to $1.17bn (£947m). ... The company said network expansion continued to accelerate during the quarter, with 382 new signings compared with 224 in the same period last year, while openings increased from 165 to 222. ... The strongest growth came from IWG’s managed and franchised division, where fee income increased 70% year on year to $39m (£28.7m). Recurring management fee income rose 80% to $16m, as more previously signed locations opened and matured. ... IWG said the model was increasingly becoming the “go-to” option for landlords and partners despite a more uncertain macroeconomic backdrop. The group ended the quarter with 336,000 managed and franchised rooms open and a further 231,000 rooms in the pipeline. ... The company said the managed and franchised division had the potential to generate more than $1.9bn (£1.5bn) of annual system revenue, once all pipeline rooms were open and mature. ... In the company-owned portfolio, revenue rose 2% to $906m (£670m), while revenue per available room increased 6% year on year to $389. Across the wider network, system-wide RevPAR fell 2% year on year to $348, which the company attributed to the impact of newly opened centres that had not yet reached maturity. ... Net financial debt increased to $858m at the end of March from $715m at the end of 2025. ... Despite heightened geopolitical and economic uncertainty, IWG said enterprise customer enquiries were increasing, sales had risen and pricing remained positive. The company added that it was taking proactive steps to reduce costs through the second quarter and beyond. ... Mark Dixon, chief executive of International Workplace Group, said: ” Potential customers are requiring more flexibility in their real estate strategy to address the uncertainty arising from the impact of conflicts and the growing influence of AI. This is resulting in record levels of enterprise customer enquiries, as our coverage and network enable us to provide unique, flexible, global solutions. ... “Signings and openings continue to grow, allowing the flywheel of our business model to deliver greater cashflow while requiring less capital to grow than historically. This combination has enabled a return of over $230m to shareholders since our Investor Day, in New York in December 2023, as we continue our journey of capital returns.”"
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"International Workplace backs outlook after ""strong"" first quarter | MarketScreener UK",uk.marketscreener.com (Alliance News),2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uk.marketscreener.com/news/international-workplace-backs-outlook-after-strong-first-quarter-ce7f5bded880fe2c,"International Workplace backs outlook after ""strong"" first quarter ... (Alliance News) - International Workplace Group PLC on Tuesday reiterated its full-year guidance as it posted top-line gains in the first quarter of 2026. ... The Zug, Switzerland-based provider of hybrid workspace under Regus and other brands said system-wide revenue grew 8.8% to USD1.17 billion in the first quarter, from USD1.07 billion a year prior. ... Group revenue improved 3.7% to USD958 million from USD924 million. ... Looking to the full-year, the company maintained its guidance, with adjusted earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation expected between USD585 million and USD625 million. For 2025, adjusted Ebitda was USD531 million. ... IWG also guides company-owned revenue growth of at least 4% and recurring managed fee income of USD80 million. ... ""I am delighted with our strong start to 2026 as we continue the rapid growth of our network supported by increasing sales despite the challenging economic backdrop,"" said Chief Executive Mark Dixon. ... ""Potential customers are requiring more flexibility in their Real Estate strategy to address the uncertainty arising from the impact of conflicts and the growing influence of AI. This is resulting in record levels of Enterprise customer enquiries as our coverage and network enable us to provide unique, flexible, global solutions."" ... | 05-19 | Iwg all AGM resolutions passed by poll vote | RE | | --- | --- | --- | | 05-13 | International Workplace Group Poised for Growth as Berenberg Notes Strong Q1 Results | MT | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group plc, Q1 2026 Sales/ Trading Statement Call, May 12, 2026 | | 05-12 | International Workplace backs outlook after ""strong"" first quarter | AN | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group says group's direct exposure from ongoing conflicts is limited | RE | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group's Q1 Revenue Grows | MT | | 05-12 | Earnings Flash (IWG.L) International Workplace Group Reports Q1 Revenue $958.0M | MT | | 05-12 | UK stocks-factors to watch on May 12 | RE | | 04-28 | BNP Paribas Starts International Workplace Group at Outperform | MT | | 04-28 | Exane BNP initiates coverage; UBS cuts SSP | AN | | 04-16 | UzNIF confirms IPO plans in London, Tashkent; pricing expected in May | AN | | 03-19 | International Workplace Group plc, 2025 Earnings Call, Mar 13, 2026 | | 03-09 | International Workplace Group plc, 2025 Earnings Call, Mar 03, 2026 | | 03-03 | International Workplace Group plc Reports Earnings Results for the Full Year Ended December 31, 2025 | CI | | 03-03 | Stocks down as Middle East ""drama"" continues | AN | ... Mark Leslie James Dixon founded IWG Plc, Regus Plc SA and Regus Group (Belgium). Mr. Dixon is Chief Executive Officer & Director at IWG Plc and Chief Executive Officer & Executive Director at Regus Plc SA (a subsidiary of IWG Plc). He is also on the board of TKP Corp. In his past career Mr. Dixon occupied the position of Chief Executive Officer for Regus Group Ltd. ... INTERNATIONAL WORKPLACE GROUP PLC is a Switzerland based Company operating in the real estate industry. The Company operates under the Regus, Signature, Spaces, HQ, Basepoint, Stop&Work, Too, The Clubhouse, Bizdojo, OpenOffice, No18, Central Working and Copernic brands. These brands provide a global network of places to work for various kinds of businesses ranging from home-based workers to corporations. The Company focuses not only on single location but also integrated national networks, also providing sales, management services, subscription services, virtual offices, meeting rooms, coworking spaces and workplace recovery services. The Company, with the brands it owns, is present around the globe."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,International Workplace Group Reports Strong… | Joshua Thompson,joshthompson.co.uk,2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://joshthompson.co.uk/investing/international-workplace-group-q1-2026-results/,"# International Workplace Group Reports Strong Q1 2026 Results with Revenue Growth and Maintains Guidance ... IWG Q1 2026: managed & franchised fee income jumps 70%, driving growth. Revenue up 4% but net debt rises. Full-year guidance maintained. ... This article covers ... ## International Workplace Group Q1 2026 trading update: a good start driven by capital-light growth ... International Workplace Group has opened 2026 with a decent first quarter. The headline numbers are positive enough: group revenue rose 4% year-on-year to $958 million, system-wide revenue climbed 9% to $1,166 million, and management kept full-year guidance unchanged. ... The bit I think matters most for investors is where the growth is coming from. The managed and franchised side – the more capital-light part of the model – is growing much faster than the traditional company-owned estate. That is usually a healthier mix because it can support cash generation without needing as much capital to expand. ... There are still a couple of watchpoints, especially higher net debt and the fact that company-owned revenue growth at 2% is still below the full-year target of at least 4%. But taken together, this looks like a reassuring Q1 rather than a game-changing one. ... | Metric | Q1 2026 | Q1 2025 | Change | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | System-wide revenue | $1,166 million | $1,072 million | 9% | | Group revenue | $958 million | $924 million | 4% | | Company-owned revenue | $906 million | $888 million | 2% | | Managed & franchised fee income | $39 million | $23 million | 70% | | Recurring managed fee income | $16 million | $9 million | 80% | | Net financial debt | $858 million | $721 million | Higher year-on-year | ... ## Managed and franchised growth is ... real engine in these IWG results ... This is where the update gets interesting. Managed and franchised system revenue jumped 41% to $260 million, while fee revenue rose 70% to $39 million. Recurring managed fee income – the stickier, repeatable part of the income stream – increased 80% to $16 million. ... That matters because IWG has been pushing harder into a model where partners and landlords provide more of the capital. In plain English, IWG can expand its network with less balance sheet strain than if it had to fund every location itself. If that works at scale, it should improve returns over time. ... Operationally, growth was strong too. Rooms open in managed and franchised rose 48% to 336,000, centres open increased 53% to 2,082, and rooms in pipeline reached 231,000. The company says that when these rooms are open and mature, the potential annual system revenue of the managed and franchised division is over $1.9 billion. ... IWG said Q1 2026 signings were 382 versus 224 a year earlier, while openings were 222 versus 165. In the segment detail, managed and franchised new centre deals signed were 377, and company-owned signings were 5, which adds up to the 382 headline figure. ... The company-owned estate returned to revenue growth, which is a positive. Revenue rose 2% to $906 million and RevPAR – revenue per available room, a common property metric – increased 6% to $389. ... That suggests pricing is improving and mature locations are performing better. Management also said company-owned RevPAR increased 6% before any methodology changes, which helps reassure investors that this is not just an accounting quirk. ... Still, there is a slight catch. Full-year guidance still calls for company-owned revenue growth of at least 4%, so Q1 at 2% means the pace needs to improve as the year goes on. ... At network level, RevPAR was down 2% to $348. Managed RevPAR fell 5% to $164, while franchised and joint venture RevPAR rose 1% to $492 and company-owned rose 6%. ... ## Net debt has risen, and that is the main negative in the Q1 statement ... Net financial debt increased to $858 million at 31 March 2026, up from $715 million at 31 December 2025 and $721 million a year earlier. That is the number I would keep an eye on. ... Management gave several reasons. It bought back 19,484,055 shares for $53 million, paid annual cash bonuses, and said a rollout of automated invoice software reduced payment days in Q1, which temporarily lifted debt. ... The company expects that timing effect to normalise through 2026, although it also said net debt is expected to end 2026 at slightly elevated levels compared with 31 December 2025. So yes, there is an explanation, but no, this is not something investors should ignore. ... On the more reassuring ... until 2 ... IWG has returned $75 million to shareholders so far in 2026 and said it has announced $100 million of share buybacks so far for the year. Since its Investor Day in December 2023, it says more than $230 million has been returned to shareholders. ... ## 2026 guidance maintained: the market will probably like that most ... The company maintained its 2026 guidance despite ongoing macroeconomic uncertainty and the wider effects of global conflicts. It still expects adjusted EBITDA of $585 million to $625 million, company-owned revenue growth of at least 4%, recurring management fee income of $80 million, and maintenance of an investment grade credit rating. ... In this market, holding guidance can be nearly as useful as upgrading it. It tells investors that Q1 trading has been solid enough not to knock management off course. ... It also helps that management said enterprise customer enquiries are increasing, sales have risen and pricing has been positive. None of that guarantees a stronger second half, but it does support the idea that demand for flexible workspace remains intact. ... My read is fairly simple. This was a positive update because growth is being driven by the part of the business that should be more scalable and less capital-hungry over time. ... The biggest positives were the 70% rise in fee income, the 80% increase in recurring managed fee income, and the sharp rise in signings and openings. Those are the numbers that best fit the long-term investment case. ... The main negatives were higher net debt and the still-modest 2% growth in company-owned revenue. Neither is fatal, but both need watching. ... Not explosive, not perfect, but good ... to keep the 2 ... 26 story intact."
REGUS BUSINESS CENTERS,,,,Exa,"Transcript : International Workplace Group plc, Q1 2026 Sales/ Trading Statement Call, May 12, 2026 | MarketScreener UK",uk.marketscreener.com (S&P Capital IQ),2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://uk.marketscreener.com/news/transcript-international-workplace-group-plc-q1-2026-sales-trading-statement-call-may-12-2026-ce7f5bdede8bf127,"Transcript : International Workplace Group plc, Q1 2026 Sales/ Trading Statement Call, May 12, 2026 | MarketScreener UK ... | 05-13 | International Workplace Group Poised for Growth as Berenberg Notes Strong Q1 Results | MT | | --- | --- | --- | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group plc, Q1 2026 Sales/ Trading Statement Call, May 12, 2026 | ... # Transcript : International Workplace Group plc, Q1 2026 Sales/ Trading Statement Call, May 12, 2026 ... Presenter SpeechMark Dixon (Executives) ... Good morning, everyone, and thank you for joining our trading update for the first quarter of 2026. We made a strong start to the year with continued momentum ... ### Latest news about International Workplace Group plc ... | 05-13 | International Workplace Group Poised for Growth as Berenberg Notes Strong Q1 Results | MT | | --- | --- | --- | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group plc, Q1 2026 Sales/ Trading Statement Call, May 12, 2026 | | 05-12 | International Workplace backs outlook after ""strong"" first quarter | AN | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group says group's direct exposure from ongoing conflicts is limited | RE | | 05-12 | International Workplace Group's Q1 Revenue Grows | MT | | 05-12 | Earnings Flash (IWG.L) International Workplace Group Reports Q1 Revenue $958.0M | MT | | 05-12 | UK stocks-factors to watch on May 12 | RE | | 04-28 | BNP Paribas Starts International Workplace Group at Outperform | MT | | 04-28 | Exane BNP initiates coverage; UBS cuts SSP | AN | | 04-16 | UzNIF confirms IPO plans in London, Tashkent; pricing expected in May | AN | | 03-19 | International Workplace Group plc, 2025 Earnings Call, Mar 13, 2026 | | 03-09 | International Workplace Group plc, 2025 Earnings Call, Mar 03, 2026 | | 03-03 | International Workplace Group plc Reports Earnings Results for the Full Year Ended December 31, 2025 | CI | | 03-03 | Stocks down as Middle East ""drama"" continues | AN | | 03-03 | International Workplace shares fall as annual profit down; ups buyback | AN |"
