SODEXO,,,,Exa,Bain Capital to buy Gong cha as MBK grapples with regulatory pressure,www.cnbc.com (Jenny Lee),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/06/bain-capital-to-buy-gong-cha-as-mbk-grapples-with-regulatory-pressure.html,"Bain Capital to buy Gong cha as MBK grapples with regulatory pressure ... - Bain Capital announced Thursday it will acquire global bubble tea chain Gong cha. - The regulatory pressure in South Korea made it difficult for MBK to pursue the acquisition on its own, according to a source familiar with the matter. - Gong cha operates around 2,200 stores globally with leading positions in the Asia-Pacific region. ... Bain Capital won a battle to buy a global bubble tea chain as one of its top rivals remains under scrutiny from South Korean regulators. ... Bain on Thursday announced it has agreed to acquire Gong cha from U.S.-based private equity firm TA Associates. MBK Partners, one of the largest private equity firms in Asia, was among the bidders for the chain and had been seeking a Korean private equity partner for a joint bid, according to communications seen by CNBC. ... Under the proposed structure, MBK was to acquire Gong cha's Japan business, while its partner was to take over the company's South Korean operations, according to two people familiar with the matter said. ... But MBK's bid came as the private equity firm faced mounting regulatory scrutiny in South Korea following the collapse of its portfolio company Homeplus, once the country's second-largest supermarket chain by market share, according to a person familiar with the matter. The heightened regulatory pressure made it difficult for MBK to secure the deal on its own, given Gong cha's significant operations in South Korea, the person added. ... Gong cha, which offers a wide range of tea and fruit-based beverages, operates more than 2,200 stores worldwide, including in the U.S. and Central America. Bain said it will continue expanding Gong cha in Japan and South Korea, where the brand has a strong footprint, while accelerating growth in the U.S., according to a press release."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo Appointed as Soft FM Partner to Homerton Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust | FM Business Daily News,news.fmbusinessdaily.com (Claire Middleton),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.fmbusinessdaily.com/2026/08/sodexo-appointed-as-soft-fm-partner-to-homerton-healthcare-nhs-foundation-trust/,"Sodexo Appointed as Soft FM Partner to Homerton Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust | FM Business Daily News # Sodexo Appointed as Soft FM Partner to Homerton Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust - Claire Middleton - / 20 hours ago Homerton Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust has appointed Sodexo Health & Care to deliver soft FM services at its acute hospital and Mary Seacole Nursing Home. The contract also includes East London NHS Foundation Trust’s mental health services at City & Hackney Centre for Mental Health, which sits alongside the acute hospital. ... Sodexo will provide a range of soft FM services to the east London sites, including cleaning, catering for patients, staff and visitors, portering, helpdesk, security, laundry, and waste management. ... The new five-year contract, with option to extend for two years, is scheduled to begin on 1 October 2026. ... Rob Jepson, CEO Health & Care, Sodexo UK & Ireland, said: “We are incredibly proud to be partnering with Homerton Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust to support the delivery of exceptional patient care. By bringing together our expertise in food and facilities management, we will deliver a smarter way of working that supports frontline teams to focus on what matters most and helps create resilient, high-performing services. We look forward to building a partnership that delivers benefits for the Trust, staff and the wider community.”"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo Deutschland übernimmt Menü2000,www.facility-manager.de (Robert Altmannshofer),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.facility-manager.de/aktuelles/sodexo-deutschland-uebernimmt-menue2000/,"Sodexo Deutschland übernimmt Menü2000 ... # Sodexo Deutschland übernimmt Menü2000 ... 4. August 2026 ... Übernahme in der Betriebsgastronomie: Sodexo Deutschland kauft Menü2000. (Bild: Engel Drohnenpilot/stock.adobe.com) ... Übernahme in der Betriebsgastronomie: Sodexo Deutschland hat am 3. August 2026 bekanntgegeben, dass sie im Rahmen eines Sales and Purchase Agreements das Unternehmen Menü2000, einen Anbieter von Betriebsgastronomie in Deutschland, gekauft hat. Der Zukauf soll eine gezielte Ergänzung des Food-Services-Geschäfts von Sodexo in Deutschland darstellen, die Präsenz im Markt für Betriebsgastronomie stärken sowie die Produktionskapazitäten ausbauen. ... Menü2000 wurde 1969 gegründet und erwirtschaftete einen Umsatz von 77 Mio. Euro in 2025/2026. Das familiengeführte Unternehmen betreibt rund 250 Betriebsrestaurants für etwa 200 Kunden aus verschiedenen Branchen. Das Geschäftsmodell kombiniert ein Frischküchensystem und eigene Kulinarik-Teams vor Ort mit hausgemachten Produkten aus einer eigenen Manufaktur (Central Production Unit – CPU) sowie einer Logistikflotte. ... „Diese Übernahme ist ein wichtiger Schritt in unserer Ambition, unser Food-Services-Geschäft in Deutschland weiter auszubauen. Menü2000 verfügt über ein bewährtes Betriebsmodell, starke Kundenbeziehungen und umfassende Expertise in der Betriebsgastronomie“, sagt Renato Salvatore, CEO von Sodexo Deutschland. Oliver Beckmann, CEO von Menü2000, will im Rahmen der Übernahme „die Stärken von Menü2000 bewahren und gemeinsam mit Sodexo neue Wachstumsperspektiven für die Zukunft zu schaffen“. Die Transaktion steht noch unter dem Vorbehalt der Genehmigung durch die zuständigen Wettbewerbsbehörden. Angaben zum Kaufpreis machten die Unternehmen nicht. ... Sodexo Deutschland übernimmt Menü2000 ... ### Sodexo Deutschland übernimmt Menü2000 ... Sodexo Deutschland übernimmt Menü2000"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo expande su negocio y abre un nuevo frente en salud | ECONOMIA | GESTIÓN,gestion.pe (Redacción Gestión),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://gestion.pe/economia/empresas/sodexo-expande-su-negocio-y-abre-un-nuevo-frente-en-salud-noticia/,"Sodexo expande su negocio y abre un nuevo frente en salud | ECONOMIA | GESTIÓN ... # Sodexo abre nueva etapa de crecimiento y se enfoca en nuevos sectores ... ## La compañía francesa de servicios de alimentación busca ampliar su presencia en un segmento donde hasta ahora tenía una participación limitada. ... La meta de superar los S/1,000 millones de facturación en el 2026 sigue tomando forma para Sodexo. Mientras la compañía francesa avanza hacia ese objetivo, enfoca sus siguientes pasos en abrir nuevos frentes de crecimiento más allá de la minería. ¿Qué sectores están en la mira? ... El primero de ellos será salud. Juan Montoya Bamberger, country managing director de Sodexo Perú, adelantó a Gestión que la empresa reforzará su presencia en este sector tras integrar a la española Mediterránea Catering a finales de 2025, una operación que le abre la puerta a un negocio donde antes no tenía participación. ... Y es que de consolidar esta estrategia, la compañía estima que el negocio de salud podría duplicar su peso dentro de su portafolio local. Actualmente, este segmento representa entre el 5% y el 7% de su facturación. ... “ Las Asociaciones Público-Privadas (APP) nos permitirán duplicar nuestra participación en el sector salud”, afirmó Montoya. ... Sodexo también apunta a crecer en segmentos como los centros logísticos y a reforzar su oferta con soluciones de inteligencia artificial (IA), automatización y sostenibilidad, en línea con los cambios que observa en la demanda de sus clientes. ... ## Hospitales concesionados abren un nuevo mercado para Sodexo ... Ahora bien, sucede que al integrar a la española Mediterránea Catering, la compañía asumió la continuidad del servicio de alimentación del Instituto Nacional de Salud del Niño de San Borja, un contrato que, según Montoya, “ representa una parte muy importante de la cartera” que mantiene en el país. ... El contrato vigente culmina en diciembre de este año. Frente a ese escenario, Sodexo participa en el proceso para mantener la prestación del servicio con el nuevo concesionario del hospital. ... Asimismo, de lograrlo, la empresa espera utilizar esa experiencia para ingresar a un segmento donde hasta ahora no participaba: el de los hospitales públicos operados bajo asociaciones público-privadas. ... “ Vamos a continuar brindando el servicio en el Hospital del Niño y con esa experiencia esperamos empezar a evaluar la posibilidad de entrar en el sector de las asociaciones público-privadas de salud”, sostuvo Montoya. ... El ejecutivo comentó que se trata de “ un sector interesante, con un modelo de negocio comprobado”, por lo que la empresa evaluará extender este modelo conforme avancen nuevos proyectos hospitalarios que forman parte de la cartera del Ministerio de Salud. Además, de mantenerse en esta operación, Sodexo prevé trabajar mediante contratos de entre tres y cinco años, similares a los que mantiene con otros clientes. Para Montoya, estas iniciativas deberían comenzar a ejecutarse a partir del próximo año. ... Más allá del sector salud, Sodexo también viene identificando nuevas oportunidades de crecimiento en otros mercados. Uno de ellos es el de los centros logísticos, un segmento que ha ganado dinamismo por el desarrollo de nuevos complejos de almacenamiento en Lima. ... La compañía dio su primer paso en este negocio con un contrato para brindar servicios al centro logístico de Farmacias Peruanas y evalúa seguir ampliando su presencia conforme se desarrollen nuevos proyectos. ... El ejecutivo señaló que otro cambio importante es la recuperación de la presencialidad en las oficinas. Luego de la caída registrada tras la pandemia, la ocupación de los espacios corporativos volvió a incrementarse, impulsando nuevamente la demanda por servicios de alimentación, limpieza y facility management. ... “ En los últimos dos años, con mayor énfasis tal vez en el último año, se ha visto un incremento nuevo en la ocupación de las oficinas. Sobre todo de la Generación Z, quienes son más exigentes”, comentó. ... En respuesta, Sodexo reforzó sus inversiones en digitalización y sostenibilidad. Por ejemplo, incorporó robots autónomos de limpieza en operaciones de los sectores financiero y minero, además de desarrollar herramientas de trazabilidad e inteligencia artificial para anticipar necesidades y mejorar la gestión de las instalaciones. ... En paralelo, Sodexo mantiene su interés por seguir creciendo en minería. La compañía participa en diversos procesos de licitación y observa con expectativa el avance de proyectos como Tía María, además de futuras expansiones de clientes con los que ya trabaja. “ Nosotros esperamos que siga avanzando el desarrollo del proyecto y, llegado el momento, podamos participar de las licitaciones que se abran para dar el servicio cuando sea necesario”, señaló Montoya. ... A estas oportunidades se suman el retorno a Antamina y Cerro Lindo, así como los nuevos contratos obtenidos este año en sectores como logística y transporte."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo uses AI to accelerate R&D and optimize recipes.,www.foodservicedirector.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.foodservicedirector.com/food-beverage-trends/in-sodexo-s-kitchens-ai-is-evolving-into-a-valued-sous-chef,"Sodexo uses AI to accelerate R&D and optimize recipes. ... # In Sodexo’s kitchens, AI is evolving into a valued sous chef ... The foodservice company is using AI to help with menu planning, recipe development, nutrition requirements, ingredient swaps, and more. But the right prompts are the key to success. ... Sodexo ... to generate images and optimize ... .Photo courtesy of Sod ... Sodexo runs foodservice operations at about 27,000 locations around the world, ranging from health care to college dining, schools, and workplaces. ... “We have over 70,000 recipes in North America alone that support our diverse menu needs,” said Richard Arakelian, VP of culinary and service development for Sodexo North America. “We have team members that are moving from different business segments, and quality, consistency, continuity, and execution are critical. We’re utilizing AI agents now to help with that consistency and continuity and support all our brands from ideation to the central development process.” ... Arakelian noted that it’s critical these days to get to market quicker and AI helps accelerate systems, menus, photography and a host of other tasks. “We are utilizing AI almost like a sous chef or chef’s companion,” he said. “It helps us develop the culinary brief document we use going into R&D, bringing us on a journey much more rapidly than we had before. AI condenses the development timelines by 50% to 60%.” ... Sodexo has found it expedient to use one of the mainstream AI platforms, like Chat GBT or Claude. “We looked into developing our own platform but we found that the investment that goes into the mainstream ones is more advanced,” said Lloyd Mann, VP of culinary for Sodexo. “We did some investigating and testing, but the tools out there were better than what we could build.” ... That said, the better the prompts and information fed to the AI agents, the better the responses and solutions you’ll get in return. “The agents need to understand the prompts and how we’re making those prompts relevant to our brands and our consumer sets. The more information you put in, the quicker it learns,” Mann added. ... The two Sodexo vice presidents detailed several specific wins they’ve had with AI. ... Optimizing recipes was tops on the list. “Having one source of truth and one style is really important,” said Mann. “For example, we did a trial across 25 to 30 recipes to see how we could minimize food waste, and we got suggestions, whether it was ingredient swapping or another solution.” They also used AI to see how they could reduce the carbon footprint of a recipe. ... Improving nutrition was another win. “In healthcare, we have many different diet types and patient needs that we have to manage in the course of the day. That can be very time consuming and challenging, but the agent could swap things out and have the nutrient analysis done very quickly,” said Arakelian. The same with allergens, food sensitivities, and sodium. ... He and his team also used AI to find alternative ingredients that could perform a particular task in a recipe. Here again, the prompts made all the difference. “If we want to remove white rice and substitute something that is more drought tolerant or supported regenerative agriculture, it would give us a list of suggestions,” Arakelian said. AI could even drill down to a specific country or region where the crop was grown if given specific prompts. ... AI’s image generating capabilities have been particularly useful to the Sodexo teams. In the early stages of R&D, the chefs will develop a bench recipe. “We’ll ask AI to create a photo of the dish before we go into development in the kitchen to really test the recipe. A picture speaks 1,000 words and helps us get the idea to market much faster when we have that bench photo,” said Alakerian. After the development is done, the Sodexo crew takes a more professional photo, but the AI generated image puts everyone on the same page from the start. ... Mann’s team gets an AI assist around the visualization of the plating. Once the prompts are provided and the image generated, “if we want to make any tweaks, it’s much easier to turn around, especially when you’re working with teams dotted around different countries or regions,” said Mann. “So if you want to make the portion size smaller or turn the pork chop 50 degrees on the plate, you can make an adaptation really quickly, within about 30 seconds … without buying new ingredients and prepping the dish again. It’s costing you nothing in time or money.” ... The Sodexo teams have reaped the benefits of using AI as a sounding board, “but you still need the human touch,” said Mann. “You can’t take away intuition; you still need the culinary knowledge to build on.” ... And chatbots can’t yet taste a dish or critique it. In the end, Sodexo sees AI is a tool that can increase efficiencies and allow chefs more time to do what they’re good at—cooking, tasting, and flavor exploration."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Electric Bidet Seats Market to Reach USD 394.2 Million by 2032 (9.2% CAGR) – Big News,www.bignews.uk,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bignews.uk/business/electric-bidet-seats-market-to-reach-usd-394-2-million-by-2032-9-2-cagr,"to Reach USD 39 ... 2 Million by ... .2% CAGR) – ... Seats Market to ... 2032 (9. ... As PW Consulting’s Senior Strategic Advisor and Lead Industry Analyst, I present a focused preview of our latest market study on electric bidet seats. The market is entering a decisive growth phase: our base year is 2025, the forecast window runs from 2026–2032, and the industry is projected to expand at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 9.2% through the forecast period. By the end of the horizon the market is expected to approach the high hundreds of millions (USD), demonstrating clear runway for product innovation, channel expansion, and institutional adoption. This briefing highlights the strategic implications for corporations planning investments, partnerships, or go-to-market moves in 2026—while intentionally withholding granular segment tables to preserve the “preview” purpose and to encourage access to the full report for transaction‑level detail. Electric Bidet Seats Market ... Regulatory and reimbursement tailwinds: Recent policy moves—most notably Medicaid waiver programs increasingly recognizing electric bidet seats as durable medical equipment—create a runway into healthcare procurement channels (notably long‑term care and assisted living). Early institutional adopters report reductions in infection rates, driving evidence-based procurement decisions. Electric Bidet Seats Market ... Growth profile: The market posted steady expansion through the 2020–2025 period and is forecast to continue expanding at ~9.2% annually over 2026–2032. That pace implies meaningful scale opportunities for players that can execute on product differentiation, cost control, and distribution reach by 2026. ... Regulatory compliance and product positioning: GFCI outlet requirements and hygiene performance standards (e.g., UV/nozzle sterilization) are now market norms. Compliance is table stakes; differentiation will depend on user experience, integrated services (warranty, subscription maintenance), and demonstrable clinical outcomes for institutional buyers. ... TOTO Ltd. — With its flagship Washlet platform, TOTO continues to set feature benchmarks (instant heating, self‑cleaning nozzles, app control). For strategic planners, TOTO’s playbook emphasizes premium product engineering, global brand leverage, and deep channel partnerships—particularly in regions where its name carries strong consumer trust. ... Kohler Co. — The January 2026 launch of the PureWash E930 with dual-wand, app connectivity, and voice control underscores Kohler’s strategy to blend design-led premium positioning with smart-home integration. Expect Kohler to push through both retail and specification channels (high-end residential and boutique commercial projects). ... features and institutional-ready ... g., UV sterilization, robust sterilizable nozzles ... Bio Bidet appeals to buyers who prioritize ... -control outcomes ... footprint in institutional ... residential segments makes ... credible partner for ... in healthcare settings ... Brondell Inc. — Recent distribution expansions indicate a channel-driven growth strategy. By broadening retailer availability and offering a range of Swash models, Brondell is pursuing volume growth through mainstream shelf presence and competitive product breadth. ... . Alpha Bidet’s ... New product introductions and refreshed model lineups (early 2026) indicate that incumbents are accelerating product roadmaps to capture share among smart-home consumers and commercial specifiers alike. ... Distribution expansions suggest retailers and online marketplaces see sufficient demand elasticity to justify broader assortments—this will intensify pricing competition but also help normalize install costs through bundled promotions with plumbing and renovation services. ... Policy/coverage updates that explicitly recognize bidet seats as necessary medical equipment for certain populations can catalyze institutional procurement contracts and third-party reimbursement pathways—an attractive growth lever for vendors that can demonstrate clinical evidence and compliance. ... reimbursement impact assessments, with a prioritized checklist for product compliance and clinical evidence generation. ... Actionable M&A and partnership screening criteria for bolt-on acquisitions, OEM relationships, and white‑label opportunities. ... Prioritize platform modularity: Design product platforms that allow configuration for residential, commercial, and clinical settings without wholesale re-engineering—leveraging common back‑end electronics while varying user-facing features and service packages. ... Invest in compliance and clinical evidence: Vendors that can demonstrate reduced infection rates, validated safety compliance (GFCI and sterilization standards), and cost-savings in care settings will unlock institutional contracts and reimbursement channels. ... Manage cost-to-serve aggressively: Material sourcing strategies, installation partnerships, and bundled service offers (installation + extended warranty) will be decisive in protecting margins as competition intensifies. ... Choose channel strategy by cohort: Premium brands should double down on specification channels and design partnerships; value brands should expand big-box and e-commerce presence; D2C players should prioritize subscription and recurring-revenue services for aftermarket filters/wash cycles. ... Explore partnerships with healthcare integrators and O&P providers: Integration into durable medical equipment catalogs and hospital procurement frameworks requires both product certification and care pathway alignment. ... Fragmented standards: Divergent regional safety and hygiene regulations could raise compliance costs for global players. ... and distribution expansion by challengers ... The electric bidet seat market in 2026 represents a compelling blend of growth and strategic complexity. With a clear CAGR trajectory and visible institutional adoption pathways, firms that act now to align product architectures, compliance programs, and go-to-market channels will secure advantaged positions for the rest of the decade. Our study provides the operational playbooks, financial models, and competitive maps to inform M&A diligence, product roadmaps, and channel investments."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo selected by Clariant to deliver global integrated,www.globenewswire.com (Sodexo SA),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/22/3331082/0/en/Sodexo-selected-by-Clariant-to-deliver-global-integrated-workplace-services.html,"Sodexo selected by Clariant to deliver global integrated ... # Sodexo selected by Clariant to deliver global integrated workplace services ... July 2 ... , 2026 02:00 ET | Source: Sodexo SA Sodexo SA ... Sodexo announces today a new five-year global partnership with Clariant, one of the world’s leading speciality chemical companies. The agreement includes a wide range of soft and hard FM services from cleaning, to building, grounds maintenance and technical support. The scope covers more than 50 sites in 13 countries across key markets in Europe, Americas and Asia Pacific. ... Clariant’s diverse global portfolio includes industrial, laboratory, office and production environments, such as its multi-building campus in Louisville, USA, its Innovation Center in Frankfurt, Germany, and its flagship office and R&D centre in Shanghai, China. Through this partnership, Sodexo will help Clariant enhance operational performance, strengthen service consistency across its global estate and elevate quality of workplace experience across their diverse range of environments worldwide. Leveraging its global expertise, local delivery model and digital capabilities, Sodexo will provide streamlined governance to manage services at scale and data-driven insights to support continuous improvement and long-term value creation. The mobilization will start in October 2026. ... | Martin Boden, CEO Enterprise Partnerships & Solutions, Sodexo, said: | | | --- | --- | | | ""Our relationship with Clariant reflects a shared ambition to transform workplace experience into a driver of business performance. By combining global expertise, digital innovation and a people-focused approach, we look forward to providing high-quality services that upgrade operational efficiency and deliver a consistent employee experience across Clariant’s global portfolio.” | ... | Nicola Comiotto, Chief Procurement Officer, Clariant, said: | | | | ""Moving to a single global IFM partner is a powerful enabler of consistency, transparency and innovation. By partnering with Sodexo, Clariant will unlock greater value from its facilities management operations while creating a more seamless and engaging workplace experience for our employees worldwide.” | ... About SodexoFounded in Marseille in 1966 by Pierre Bellon, Sodexo is the leader in Food and Services, shaping better everyday experiences at every moment in life: work, heal, learn and play. The Group stands out for its independence, its founding family shareholding and its responsible business model. With its services, Sodexo meets all the challenges of everyday life with a dual goal: to improve the quality of life of our employees and those we serve, and contribute to the economic, social and environmental progress in the communities where we operate. Our purpose is to create a better everyday for everyone to build a better life for all. Sodexo is included in the CAC Next 20, CAC SBT 1.5, FTSE 4 Good et DJSI indices. ... | 24.1 billion euros Fiscal 2025 consolidated revenues 426,000 employees as at August 31, 2025 #2 France-based private employer worldwide | 43 countries 80 million consumers served daily 7.8 billion euro in market capitalization (as July 15, 2026) | | --- | --- | ... selected by Clariant to deliver global integrated ... July 21, 2026 12:00 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Sodexo - Interim report on liquidity contract as at June 30, 2026 ... Regulated Information Issy-les-Moulineaux, July 21, 2026 Interim report on liquidity contract as at June 30, 2026 Pursuant to the liquidity contract entrusted by Sodexo to BNP Paribas Arbitrage, the... ... July 16, 2026 01:01 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Sodexo secures a major food services contract with Meta ... Issy-les-Moulineaux, July 16, 2026 Sodexo today announced that it has been selected by Meta to deliver food services across its global portfolio. The enterprise partnership covers more than 130..."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo Secures a 5-Year Global Contract with Clariant Across 50 Sites,www.ideal-investisseur.fr,2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ideal-investisseur.fr/en/stock-news/sodexo-secures-a-5-year-global-contract-with-clariant-across-50-sites/22885.html,"Sodexo Secures a 5-Year Global Contract with Clariant Across 50 Sites ... ## Cleaning, Maintenance, and Technical Support Services Across 50 Sites ... Sodexo has signed a five-year partnership agreement with Clariant to manage all of its real estate services (both soft and hard FM) globally. The contract includes cleaning, building and outdoor space maintenance, as well as technical support. It spans more than 50 sites located in 13 countries across Europe, the Americas, and Asia-Pacific.Clariant's portfolio includes a variety of environments: industrial facilities, laboratories, offices, and production environments, including its multi-site campus in Louisville, USA, its innovation center in Frankfurt, Germany, and its headquarters and research and development center in Shanghai, China. ... ## Services to Commence in October 2026 with Standardization of Operational Standards ... Service mobilization will begin in October 2026. Through this partnership, Sodexo will assist Clariant in enhancing its operational performance and standardizing service standards across its global real estate portfolio. The group will leverage its global expertise, local presence, and digital capabilities to offer simplified governance and will rely on data to support a continuous improvement process and long-term value creation. ... Period: ... 202 ... - Revenue: 6.2MD€ ... - Third-quarter organic growth was above expectations, reflecting resilient demand across the business. - La performance du troisième trimestre a été supérieure aux attentes. ... - Maintien d'une vue prudente de l'environnement extérieur. - Impact négatif sur la croissance organique à cause de pertes de contrats dans l'éducation. ... - Mise à profit des nouvelles gagnées dans les soins de santé et seniors. - Progression commerciale encourageante dans les centres de conférences et les stades. ... Sodexo Secures Catering for Meta Across 130 Sites in 30 Countries Published on Jul 16, 2026 ... Sodexo Unveils Shift & Grow 2030: Targeting Growth and Margins Beyond 5% Published on Jul 16, 2026"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Global caterers ride first-time outsourcing wave as food prices r,www.globalbankingandfinance.com,2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globalbankingandfinance.com/global-caterers-ride-first-time-outsourcing-wave-food-prices/,"July 21 (Reuters) - Global catering groups are increasingly finding growth from hospitals, schools and businesses outsourcing food and facilities services for the first time, opening up a large pool of potential customers beyond the industry's traditional contract battles. ... Outsourcing specialists such as Compass Group, Sodexo and Aramark have benefited as organisations seek outside help managing food purchasing, labour shortages and increasingly complex operations. ... Market leader Compass said on Tuesday that around half of its new contract wins come from organisations outsourcing catering and facilities management for the first time. ... First-time-outsourcing customers accounted for 51% of new business signed in the six months to March, up from 45% three years ago. ... Sodexo Chief Executive Thierry Delaporte told Reuters last week that roughly half of the French group's contract wins come from first-time outsourcing customers. ... ""There is a global trend towards first-time outsourcing,"" Delaporte said. ... A Sodexo spokesperson said healthcare and education are expected to be the company's fastest-growing segments, while Compass highlighted both sectors as major first-time-outsourcing opportunities in investor materials published in May. ... ""Just the education segment in America is a massive opportunity for us,"" Delaporte told investors this month. ... The shift provides a medium-term growth opportunity for the industry's largest players because it expands the market rather than forcing them to compete solely for one another's customers. ... The world's four largest caterers -- Compass, Sodexo, Aramark and Elior -- still account for less than 30% of the global contract catering market, according to analyst estimates. ... ""I do not think this is an endless gravy train,"" Slupecki said, warning that competition between major providers is likely to intensify in the next five to ten years as the pool of first-time outsourcing customers gradually shrinks. ... - Compass reports that 50% of its new business—$4.1 billion in six months to March—comes from first-time outsourcing clients, up from 45% three years ago, as inflation and complex operations drive demand (compass-group.com). - Sodexo similarly notes that roughly half of its contract wins stem from first-time outsourcing, with strong momentum in healthcare and education segments (uk.sodexo.com). - The global outsourced catering market, valued at $341 billion in 2025, is expanding at a 5.8 % CAGR; healthcare represents nearly 29 % of the market (~$97.9 billion), underscoring the scale of growth potential (dataintelo.com). ... - Compass Group Half Year 2026 Press Release.pdf - Jean Renton on Sodexo's first half fiscal 2025 results - Outsourced Catering Services Market Research Report 2034 ... Major companies such as Compass Group, Sodexo, Aramark, and Elior are leading the trend and benefiting from increased outsourcing demand. ... that 51% of its new business in the recent period came from organizations outsourcing catering for the first time, up from 45% three years ago."
