ith Clariant, one of the world’s leading speciality chemical companies. The agreement includes a wide range of soft and hard FM... ... July 16, 2026 01:01 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Sodexo secures a major food services contract with Meta ... Issy-les-Moulineaux, July 16, 2026 Sodexo today announced that it has been selected by Meta to deliver food services across its global portfolio. The enterprise partnership covers more than 130..."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Weekly Recap: Shift & Grow 2030 turnaround plan and Meta contract — TradingView News,www.tradingview.com,2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tradingview.com/news/tradingview:9be279133a97c:0-weekly-recap-shift-grow-2030-turnaround-plan-and-meta-contract/,"Weekly Recap: Shift & Grow 2030 turnaround plan and Meta contract — TradingView News ... Weekly Recap: Shift & Grow 2030 turnaround plan and Meta contract ... Sodexo SA (EURONEXT:SW) launched Shift & Grow 2030 to regain competitiveness then accelerate growth, prioritizing heavy investment and North America under CEO Thierry Delaporte’s direct leadership, while securing a major phased global food-services roll‑out with Meta. ... - Sodexo Unveils Shift & Grow 2030: Sodexo SA (SW) unveiled Shift & Grow 2030: a two‑phase plan to restore competitiveness (2026–27) then accelerate growth (from 2028), with major investments and North America as primary market. 1 ... - Sodexo Wins Meta Contract: Sodexo SA won a major global workplace food-services contract with Meta to serve 130+ sites across 30+ countries. Rollout will be phased and services start in coming months; financials undisclosed. 2 3 4 ... - Delaporte to Lead North America: Sodexo SA: CEO Thierry Delaporte will directly run North America to boost U.S. growth. Priorities: stronger client acquisition and retention, with a mid‑term retention target of 95–96%. 5"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo secures Meta food services contract,www.verdictfoodservice.com (Umesh Ellichipuram),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.verdictfoodservice.com/news/sodexo-secures-meta-food-services-contract/,"Sodexo secures Meta food services contract ... Sodexo marked the ... as one of biggest for its standalone global corporate dining business. Credit: Jean ... Ichard / Shutterstock.com. ... Sodexo has won a contract from Meta to provide food services across the technology company’s global estate. ... The agreement covers more than 130 locations in over 30 countries, spanning all regions. ... In a statement, the French catering group said the contract includes catering operations in a wide variety of settings, including conference centres, corporate offices, data centres, large campuses and smaller office sites. ... The company said services will be introduced gradually over the coming months. ... Sodexo described the deal as one of the largest standalone global workplace food services contracts it has secured so far. ... It added the contract followed a “highly competitive” global tender process. ... Under the arrangement, Sodexo will supply integrated workplace food services through a global operating model, supported by digital and data tools. ... Sustainability was a key part of the selection process and will be built into the programme, Sodexo added. ... Sodexo CEO Thierry Delaporte said: “This success was driven by our people, anchored in strong leadership commitment and a 60-year heritage of hospitality services. Meta’s ambition for exceptional culinary experiences everywhere they operate aligns perfectly with our proven expertise to deliver at scale. ... “This contract win is a reflection of the level of commercial intensity Sodexo can unlock when our global team come together to build the right offer and showcase our global capabilities. It shows our ability to convert wide-scale competitive tenders into material growth opportunities.” ... In April, Sodexo reduced its guidance for fiscal 2026 (FY26), warning of weaker sales growth after highlighting internal execution problems and the impact of a review of its contracts and assets. ... The company now anticipates organic revenue growth of between 0.5% and 1%, a reduction from its previous projection of 1.5% to 2.5%."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo unveils its 2030 growth acceleration plan - FMJ,www.fmj.co.uk (Sarah OBeirne),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.fmj.co.uk/sodexo-unveils-its-2030-growth-acceleration-plan/,"Sodexo unveils its 2030 growth acceleration plan - FMJ https://plus.google.com/101473517976210992589 ... Home/ Business/ Sodexo unveils its 2030 growth acceleration plan ... # Sodexo unveils its 2030 growth acceleration plan ... Sodexo has unveiled ‘Shift & Grow 2030’ the Company’s roadmap focused on accelerating growth and restoring competitiveness. ... Launched by Sodexo’s CEO, Thierry Delaporte at an Investor Update in Paris yesterday, the plan is designed to address the execution gaps that have held back the Group’s performance through three pillars: ... - Rebuilding the growth engine by reinforcing client proximity, proactive account management and business development, disciplined price-to-win competitiveness and a dedicated large-client approach, leveraging Sodexo’s distinctive position across both food and facilities management. ... - Simplifying and standardising the operating model by making execution faster, more consistent and more scalable through operational excellence, organisational simplification and procurement at scale. ... - Reigniting a high-performance culture ... strengthening leadership, performance management, incentives, talent and succession to drive ... To enable its plan, Sodexo says it is investing decisively in tech, data and scaling digital and AI to support growth, productivity and decision-making. ... Shift & Grow 2030 is a two-phased roadmap with Fiscal 2026 and Fiscal 2027 focused on rebuilding competitiveness, and Fiscal 2028 onwards focused on accelerating growth, expanding margin and improving ROCE. ... Sodexo states early progress is already visible, including the recent award of a large global food services contract with Meta. ... For Fiscal 2027, Sodexo expects: ... - Organic revenue growth of +2% to +3%; - Underlying operating margin broadly in line with Fiscal 2026 guidance: between 3.2% and 3.4%, reflecting continued investment to strengthen capabilities and restore competitiveness. ... For Fiscal 2030, Sodexo expects to deliver: ... - Above +5% organic revenue growth, including net new business above +3%; - Underlying operating margin above 5%. ... Sharing her thoughts on the growth acceleration plan for the UK and Ireland, Jean Renton, CEO Sodexo UK&I said: ... “Across the UK and Ireland, we’re already bringing that strategy to life through commercial growth, contract retentions, investment in innovation and technology, developing our people and delivering long-term value for our clients and communities. ... “That momentum is reflected in our commercial performance. With 30,000 colleagues delivering food and support services across multiple industries, we’ve recently secured significant new multi-service partnership and contract extensions. These include the Scottish Parliament, George Watson’s College, HM Naval Base Portsmouth, Leyland Trucks, the Wallace Collection, Kent County Cricket, plus EY and ESB in Ireland, with further wins to announce in the coming weeks. ... “Technology is transforming how we support our clients, consumers and colleagues. It helps us create better experiences, deliver greater value for our clients and improve the way we operate, while remaining true to one simple principle: technology should enhance human experiences, not replace them. ... “We’re investing in digital solutions and AI that help clients better understand their organisations and the people they serve. By analysing millions of interactions, we generate insight that enables smarter decisions, more personalised experiences and stronger commercial outcomes. ... “Alongside technology, our commitment to sustainability, our people and the communities we serve is central to how we create long-term value. We have a focus on attracting, developing and retaining talented people and creating opportunities for those who face barriers to employment. Together with our progress towards net zero and recognition as Employer of the Year at the British Business Awards, this demonstrates the values and long-term thinking clients increasingly expect from a strategic partner. ... “I’m proud to lead our UK & Ireland business into this next chapter and, above all, proud of our front-line teams who bring our purpose to life every day. Since 1966, we’ve been committed to improving quality of life, and Shift & Grow 2030 gives us an exciting platform to build on that legacy for many years to come.”"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,"How Sodexo’s “Shift & Grow 2030” Blueprint Targets North America, Tech Upgrades & Meta Deal to Boost Growth and Margins :: AktienSensor",aktiensensor.com,2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://aktiensensor.com/articles/how-sodexos-shift--grow-2030-blueprint-targets-north-america-tech-upgrades--meta-deal-to/,"Tech Upgrades ... ## Corporate Update: Sodexo Unveils “Shift & Grow 2030&rdquo; Growth Blueprint ... At an investor briefing held in Paris, Sodexo S.A. presented its “Shift & Grow 2030&rdquo; strategy, a four‑year roadmap designed to restore competitiveness and drive sustainable expansion. The plan foregrounds North America as the principal growth engine, while allocating substantial capital toward operational efficiency and technology-enabled transformation. ... Sodexo will channel approximately €100 million per annum into operating costs from 2026 to 2030, complemented by €1 billion earmarked for technology, procurement, and organizational overhaul. These outlays aim to underpin the company’s medium‑term objectives: an organic revenue increase of >5 % and an underlying operating margin exceeding 5 % by fiscal 2030. In line with shareholder expectations, the firm maintains a dividend policy of roughly 50 % of earnings, signaling a balance between reinvestment and return. ... The phased approach prioritizes North American operations, reflecting the region’s robust demand for workplace‑meal services and higher profit margins. The company’s emphasis on client proximity, operational discipline, accountability, and an entrepreneurial mindset suggests a shift from traditional, cost‑centered models to a more customer‑centric, data‑driven framework. This aligns with broader industry trends where service firms increasingly deploy analytics to optimize supply chains and personalize offerings. ... A highlight of the presentation was the announcement of a sizeable global food‑services contract with Meta Platforms. Covering over 130 sites across more than 30 countries, the agreement is described by Sodexo as one of its largest workplace‑meal contracts to date. The deal’s initiation in the coming months will provide early evidence of the strategy’s effectiveness, reinforcing the narrative that the company’s renewed focus on client proximity and operational excellence is already delivering tangible results. ... Following the disclosure, Sodexo’s share price experienced a modest uptick, indicating a favorable market reaction to the clarified growth plan and the Meta partnership. Analysts note that while the price movement is incremental, it reflects confidence in the company’s ability to execute a differentiated strategy amid a competitive landscape that includes other global food‑service providers and emerging technology‑driven players. ... Sodexo’s “Shift & Grow 2030&rdquo; resonates beyond the food‑service sector. The emphasis on technology integration, procurement optimization, and organizational transformation mirrors initiatives across manufacturing, logistics, and even healthcare, where firms grapple with rising labor costs and the need for digital agility. The company’s focus on “underlying operating margin” echoes the financial discipline seen in high‑growth tech firms, underscoring a convergence of strategic priorities across seemingly disparate industries. ... The broader economic environment—characterized by inflationary pressures, labor market tightening, and geopolitical uncertainties—has prompted service providers to reassess cost structures and value propositions. By investing in technology and operational discipline, Sodexo positions itself to mitigate volatility and capture market share in regions where cost efficiencies translate directly into competitive advantage. ... The “Shift & Grow 2030&rdquo; blueprint presents a cohesive framework that balances aggressive growth targets with disciplined capital allocation. The Meta contract offers a concrete benchmark to assess the strategy’s impact, while the emphasis on North America signals a targeted, geography‑specific approach. As the company embarks on this transformation, stakeholders will likely monitor key performance indicators such as revenue growth, margin expansion, and the pace of technology adoption to gauge the effectiveness of its renewed corporate strategy."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan,www.globenewswire.com (Sodexo SA),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/16/3328211/0/en/Sodexo-launches-its-2030-growth-acceleration-plan.html,"Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan ... # Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan ... Sodexo is hosting today its Investor Update in Paris, where Thierry Delaporte, Chief Executive Officer of Sodexo, and members of the management team will present Shift & Grow 2030, the Company’s roadmap focused on accelerating growth and restoring competitiveness, alongside the Group’s mid-term financial ambition. ... - Shift & Grow 2030, a clear execution framework to accelerate growth and restore competitiveness - Ambition to reach above +5% organic growth and above 5% operating margin by Fiscal 2030. - Client-first approach, supported by clearer focus across geographies, client segments and services, with North America as the primary growth priority. - Significant investment program to strengthen commercial capabilities, simplify the operating model and leverage technology to support growth and margin ambitions. ... - A two-phased roadmap, with Fiscal 2026 and Fiscal 2027 focused on rebuilding competitiveness, and Fiscal 2028 onwards focused on accelerating growth, expanding margin and improving ROCE. ... - Early progress already visible, including the recent award of a large global food services contract. Further details in the separate press release issued today and available on sodexo.com ... ""Sodexo is a business with tremendous strengths: leading positions in food and facilities management, a global footprint, an outstanding service culture and a deeply embedded purpose to positively impact its clients, people and society.Shift & Grow 2030 is about reconnecting with the values and operating principles that have always defined Sodexo: client proximity, operational discipline, accountability and an entrepreneurial mindset. By executing them consistently, we will restore our competitiveness and unlock the full potential of the company. Our ambition is clear. By 2030, we want Sodexo to be fully back in the game: competing with the best in our industry, delivering consistent growth, improving profitability in a disciplined way and becoming the partner of choice for our clients. The work is already underway and we are confident in our ability to deliver."" ... The plan is designed to address the execution gaps that have held back the Group's performance through three pillars: ... - Rebuilding the growth engine by reinforcing client proximity, proactive account management and business development, disciplined price-to-win competitiveness and a dedicated large-client approach, leveraging Sodexo's distinctive position across both food and facilities management. ... - Simplifying and standardizing the operating model by making execution faster, more consistent and more scalable through operational excellence, organizational simplification and procurement at scale. ... - Reigniting a high-performance culture by strengthening leadership, performance management, incentives, talent and succession to drive greater accountability and better execution. ... To enable its plan, Sodexo is investing decisively in tech, data and scaling digital and AI to support growth, productivity and decision-making. ... - Fiscal 2026 and Fiscal 2027 focused on strengthening commercial capabilities, simplifying operations and accelerating investment.For Fiscal 2027, Sodexo expects: ... - - Organic revenue growth of +2% to +3%; ... - Underlying operating margin broadly in line with Fiscal 2026 guidance: between 3.2% and 3.4%, reflecting continued investment to strengthen capabilities and restore competitiveness. ... - From Fiscal 2028 onwards: acceleration phase with progressive benefits from these actions, supporting improved growth, profitability and returns.For Fiscal 2030, Sodexo expects to deliver: ... - - Above +5% organic revenue growth, including net new business above +3%; - Underlying operating margin above 5%. ... - Increased investment, including around 100 million euros of incremental annualized operating costs to sustainably strengthen commercial capabilities, together with approximately 1 billion euros of non-recurring investments across tech, procurement and organizational transformation over Fiscal 2026 to Fiscal 2030. ... - Capital expenditure of around 2.5% to 3.0% of revenue, to support the Group's commercial ambitions and productivity improvements while maintaining the Group's capital-light model. ... - A balanced shareholder return policy with a dividend payout ratio maintained at 50%, providing attractive shareholder returns while preserving the capacity to invest in the business. ... - Targeted bolt-on acquisitions, focused on strengthening capabilities, building scale in priority markets and enhancing long-term returns, while maintaining strict financial discipline. ... - A solid investment-grade financial policy, preserving financial flexibility throughout the transformation, supporting future investment opportunities and maintaining access to attractive financing conditions. ... | Fiscal 2026 Annual Results | October 23, 2026 | | --- | --- | | Fiscal 2026 Annual Shareholders Meeting | December 16, 2026 | | Fiscal 2027 First quarter Revenues | January 7, 2027 | ... About SodexoFounded in Marseille in 1966 by Pierre Bellon, Sodexo is the leader in Food and Services, shaping better everyday experiences at every moment in life: work, heal, learn and play. The Group stands out for its independence, its founding family shareholding and its responsible business model. With its services, Sodexo meets all the challenges of everyday life with a dual goal: to improve the quality of life of our employees and those we serve, and contribute to the economic, social and environmental progress in the communities where we operate. Our purpose is to create a better everyday for everyone to build a better life for all. Sodexo is included in the CAC Next 20, CAC SBT 1.5, FTSE 4 Good et DJSI indices.Key figures ... | 24.1 billion euros Fiscal 2025 consolidated revenues 426,000 employees as at August 31, 2025 #2 France-based private employer worldwide | 43 countries 80 million consumers served daily 7.8 billion euros in market capitalization (as July 15, 2026) | | --- | --- | ... July 22, 2026 02:00 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Sodexo selected by Clariant to deliver global integrated workplace services ... Sodexo announces today a new five-year global partnership with Clariant, one of the world’s leading speciality chemical companies. The agreement includes a wide range of soft and hard FM... ... Sodexo - Interim report on liquidity contract as at June 30, 2026 ... Regulated Information Issy-les-Moulineaux, July 21, 2026 Interim report on liquidity contract as at June 30, 2026 Pursuant to the liquidity contract entrusted by Sodexo to BNP Paribas Arbitrage, the..."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo secures a major food services contract with Meta,www.globenewswire.com (Sodexo SA),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/16/3328218/0/en/Sodexo-secures-a-major-food-services-contract-with-Meta.html,"Sodexo secures a major food services contract with Meta ... # Sodexo secures a major food services contract with Meta ... Sodexo today announced that it has been selected by Meta to deliver food services across its global portfolio. ... The enterprise partnership covers more than 130 locations in over 30 countries across all regions, including a highly diverse range of environments, such as corporate offices, large campuses, data centres, conference hubs and smaller office locations. Service delivery will start progressively in the coming months. ... This represents one of the largest single global workplace food services contracts secured by Sodexo to date. It was awarded following a highly competitive global tender process, during which Sodexo demonstrated strong team capabilities and a true partnership approach. The Group also proved its ability to drive value, meet client needs at every stage, and deliver at an international scale with solid mobilization expertise. ... A food program that goes far beyond serving mealsSodexo will deliver integrated workplace food services through a structured global operating model, combining consistent global standards with local execution and innovation, whilst leveraging advanced digital and data capabilities. ... By combining Meta’s workplace vision brand standards with Sodexo’s global expertise in food services and hospitality, the partnership delivers an integrated food program - designed to support human connection, productivity and employee experience, at scale. ... Focus on sustainability and innovationSustainability formed an integral part of the selection process and will be fully embedded in the program, supporting both partners’ shared ambitions. ... | Thierry Delaporte, Sodexo Chief Executive Officer said: | | | --- | --- | | | This success was driven by our people, anchored in strong leadership commitment and a 60-year heritage of hospitality services. Meta’s ambition for exceptional culinary experiences everywhere they operate aligns perfectly with our proven expertise to deliver at scale.This contract win is a reflection of the level of commercial intensity Sodexo can unlock when our global team come together to build the right offer and showcase our global capabilities. It shows our ability to convert wide-scale competitive tenders into material growth opportunities.” | ... About SodexoFounded in Marseille in 1966 by Pierre Bellon, Sodexo is the leader in Food and Services, shaping better everyday experiences at every moment in life: work, heal, learn and play. The Group stands out for its independence, its founding family shareholding and its responsible business model. With its services, Sodexo meets all the challenges of everyday life with a dual goal: to improve the quality of life of our employees and those we serve, and contribute to the economic, social and environmental progress in the communities where we operate. Our purpose is to create a better everyday for everyone to build a better life for all. Sodexo is included in the CAC Next 20, CAC SBT 1.5, FTSE 4 Good et DJSI indices.Key figures ... | 24.1 billion euros Fiscal 2025 consolidated revenues 426,000 employees as at August 31, 2025 #2 France-based private employer worldwide | 43 countries 80 million consumers served daily 7.8 billion euros in market capitalization (as July 15, 2026) | | --- | --- | ... July 22, 2026 02:00 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Sodexo selected by Clariant to deliver global integrated workplace services ... Sodexo announces today a new five-year global partnership with Clariant, one of the world’s leading speciality chemical companies. The agreement includes a wide range of soft and hard FM... ... July 21, 2026 12:00 ET | Source: Sod ... Sodexo - Interim report on liquidity contract as at June 30, 2026 ... Regulated Information Issy-les-Moulineaux, July 21, 2026 Interim report on liquidity contract as at June 30, 2026 Pursuant to the liquidity contract entrusted by Sodexo to BNP Paribas Arbitrage, the..."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo to deliver Meta’s global catering in one of its largest ever wins - News,www.thecaterer.com,2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thecaterer.com/news/sodexo-to-deliver-metas-global-catering-in-one-of-its-largest-ever-wins,"Sodexo to deliver Meta’s global catering in one of its largest ever wins - News ... # Sodexo to deliver Meta’s global catering in one of its largest ever wins ... Foodservice 16 Jul 202611:13 by Emma Lake ... Sodexo has secured a contract to deliver food services across technology company Meta’s global portfolio ... Sodexo has secured a contract to deliver food services across technology company Meta’s global portfolio, in one of its largest single wins to date. ... The caterer will deliver services across more than 130 locations in over 30 countries including offices, data centres, conference hubs and campuses. ... Thierry Delaporte, Sodexo’s chief executive officer, said: “This success was driven by our people, anchored in strong leadership commitment and a 60-year heritage of hospitality services. Meta’s ambition for exceptional culinary experiences everywhere they operate aligns perfectly with our proven expertise to deliver at scale. ... “This contract win is a reflection of the level of commercial intensity Sodexo can unlock when our global team come together to build the right offer and showcase our global capabilities. It shows our ability to convert wide-scale competitive tenders into material growth opportunities.” ... Sodexo said the win followed a “highly competitive global tender process”, during which it demonstrated “its ability to drive value, meet client needs at every stage, and deliver at an international scale with solid mobilization expertise.” ... The contract will be mobilised across the coming months. ... Recent wins for Sodexo have included George Watson’s College in Edinburgh as well as extensions to its contracts with the Wallace Collection in London and Kent Cricket. ... Sodexo was founded in Marseille in 1966 by Pierre Bellon."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo Targets North America to Accelerate Growth from 2027,www.globalbankingandfinance.com,2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globalbankingandfinance.com/sodexo-bets-north-america-drive-growth-recovery/,"Sodexo Targets North America to Accelerate Growth from 2027 ... # Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery ... ## Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery ... July 16 (Reuters) - French food caterer Sodexo said on Thursday it expects faster revenue growth from 2027 as it seeks to revive performance through stronger execution and expansion in North America, its largest market. ... The company, which generates roughly half of its revenue in North America, warned in October 2025 that weak performance in education and healthcare in its single largest market would weigh on this year's results, aiming to restore growth from 2027. ... Sodexo now expects organic revenue growth of 2% to 3% in 2027, compared with expected growth of 1.2% to 1.5% in 2026. ... Sodexo's new CEO announced in April a review of the company's execution and contracts, citing underinvestment, inconsistent performance and slow decision-making. ... ""In terms of countries, obviously, the absolute priority is the United States,"" CEO Thierry Delaporte said on a wire call. ... ""It's the largest market in the world, and it's also a rapidly growing market,"" Delaporte added. ... The company also announced a global contract with tech giant Meta, one of its largest to date. ... Sodexo also said it would increase investments to €1 billion ($1.15 billion) and maintain a 50% dividend payout ratio through 2030. ... - Sodexo raised its full‑year 2026 organic growth guidance to 1.2–1.5% following stronger Q3 performance, up from the prior 0.5–1% forecast (live.euronext.com). - First‑half fiscal 2026 results showed organic growth of 1.7%, though North America lagged at –1.8%, weighed down by contract losses in Education and Business & Administration (sodexo.com). - CEO Thierry Delaporte assumed direct leadership of North America from January 1, 2026 to accelerate turnaround efforts in the region (sodexo.com). - Sodexo’s shares lost about 40% in the past two years versus peers Compass and Aramark, driven by execution challenges that Delaporte is addressing (investing.com). - The company targets organic revenue growth of 2–3% in 2027 and over 5% by 2030, with net new business above 3% (investing.com). ... - Q3 Fiscal 2026 revenues above expectations; focus on execution - Sodexo First half Fiscal 2026 results - Sodexo Announces Change to North America Leadership - Sodexo cuts 2026 targets as new CEO gears to tackle long-standing issues ... Sodexo expects organic revenue growth of 2% to 3% in 2027. ... Why is North America a priority for Sodexo's expansion? ... North America is Sodexo's largest and fastest-growing market, contributing roughly half of the company's revenue. ... The new CEO initiated a review of company execution and contracts, targeting better performance and faster decision-making. ... By 2030, Sodexo aims for organic revenue growth above 5% and net new business above 3%. ... Weak results in education and healthcare in North America negatively impacted Sodexo's performance, prompting efforts to restore growth."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery | MarketScreener Saudi Arabia,sa.marketscreener.com (Reuters),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://sa.marketscreener.com/news/sodexo-expects-higher-2027-sales-growth-ce7f5ed2df8ef023,"Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery | MarketScreener Saudi Arabia ... | 07-22 | Clariant AG Selects Sodexo SA To Deliver Global Integrated Workplace Services | CI | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-22 | Sodexo Bags Global Facilities Management Contract with Clariant | MT | ... # Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery ... July 16 (Reuters) - French food caterer Sodexo said on Thursday it expects faster revenue growth from 2027 as it seeks to revive performance through stronger execution and expansion in North America, its largest market. ... The company, which generates roughly half of its revenue in North America, warned in October 2025 that weak performance in education and healthcare in its single largest market would weigh on this year's results, aiming to restore growth from 2027. ... Sodexo now expects organic revenue growth of 2% to 3% in 2027, compared with expected growth of 1.2% to 1.5% in 2026. ... Sodexo's new CEO announced in April a review of the company's execution and contracts, citing underinvestment, inconsistent performance and slow decision-making. ... ""In terms of countries, obviously, the absolute priority is the United States,"" CEO Thierry Delaporte said on a wire call. ... ""It's the largest market in the world, and it's also a rapidly growing market,"" Delaporte added. ... ""The [2030] objectives appear reachable, but are also relatively far away and require a re-acceleration phase before reaching them,"" analysts at Deutsche Bank said in a note. ... The company also announced a global contract with tech giant Meta, one of its largest to date. ... Sodexo also said it would increase investments to EUR1 billion ($1.15 billion) and maintain a 50% dividend payout ratio through 2030. ... | 07-22 | Clariant AG Selects Sodexo SA To Deliver Global Integrated Workplace Services | CI | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-22 | Sodexo Bags Global Facilities Management Contract with Clariant | MT | | 07-21 | Global caterers ride first-time outsourcing wave as food prices rise | RE | | 07-21 | RBC Updates Model for Sodexo After Capital Markets Day; Sector Perform Rating Maintained | MT | | 07-21 | Caterer Compass logs sales boost from AI data centres but unchanged outlook disappoints | RE | | 07-17 | AlphaValue/Baader Europe Upgrades Sodexo to Reduce, Boosts PT | MT | | 07-16 | Sodexo S.A. - Special Call | | | 07-16 | Sodexo: Opinion change, from Sell to Reduce | | | 07-16 | Sodexo: A convincing Investor Day that raises questions about past execution | | | 07-16 | European Equities Mostly Lower in Thursday Trading; Sodexo Picked by Meta for Global Food Services | MT | | 07-16 | France's Sodexo Wins Food Services Contract With Meta | DJ | | 07-16 | The CAC 40 slips back into the red | | | 07-16 | Sodexo Outlines EUR1 Billion Investment Under Five-year Growth Strategy | MT | | 07-16 | Sodexo Secures Global Workplace Food Services Contract from Meta | MT | | 07-16 | Sodexo Secures Major Food Services Contract with Meta Platforms, Inc | CI | ... Sodexo is a world leader in food and facilities management services. The group offers onsite services: meal preparation, management of restaurants, reception and conference centers, reception services, mail processing, transport, cleaning, gardening, technical maintenance, security, facility management, sanitation, etc. Net sales break down by market between companies and government departments (47.4%), healthcare facilities and senior-citizen residences (24.3%), schools and universities (19.7%) and entertainment (9.6%; Sodexo Live!). Net sales are distributed geographically as follows: Europe (35.7%), North America (46.4%), Asia/Pacific/Middle East/Africa/Latin America (17.9%). ... 10-23 Earnings release - Annual 2026 ... Sodexo: Opinion change, from Sell to Reduce July 16, 2026 at 09:20 pm ... Sodexo benefits from sequential improvement in North America and raises its outlook, the stock jumps +8% July 02, 2026 at 11:18 am ... Sodexo severely punished by market since beginning of the year April ... 07, 2025 at 11:42 am"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery | MWC Sandbox/Syndication,d2233.cms.socastsrm.com (Thomson Reuters),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://d2233.cms.socastsrm.com/2026/07/16/sodexo-bets-on-north-america-to-drive-growth-recovery/,"Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery | MWC Sandbox/Syndication ... Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery ... July 16 (Reuters) – French food caterer Sodexo said on Thursday it expects faster revenue growth from 2027 as it seeks to revive performance through stronger execution and expansion in North America, ‌its largest market. ... The company, which generates roughly half of its revenue in North America, warned in October 2025 that weak performance in education and healthcare in its single largest market would weigh on this year’s ‌results, aiming to restore growth from 2027. ... Sodexo ⁠now expects organic revenue growth ⁠of 2% to 3% in 2027, compared with expected growth of 1.2% to 1.5% in 2026. ... Sodexo’s new CEO announced in April a review of the company’s execution and contracts, citing underinvestment, inconsistent performance and slow decision-making. ... “In terms of countries, obviously, the absolute priority is the United States,” ⁠CEO Thierry Delaporte said on a ⁠wire call. ... “It’s the largest market in the world, and it’s also a rapidly growing market,” Delaporte added. ... require a re- ... The company also announced a global contract ⁠with tech giant Meta, one of its largest to date. ... Sodexo also said it would increase investments to €1 billion ($1.15 billion) and maintain a 50% dividend payout ratio through 2030."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery,bluewaterhealthyliving.com (Reuters),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bluewaterhealthyliving.com/news/business-and-economy/sodexo-bets-on-north-america-to-drive-growth-recovery/,"Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery ... # Sodexo bets on North America to drive growth recovery by Reuters July 16, 2026 July 16, 2026 (This story has been refiled to change the picture with no changes to the text) By Lucie Barbier and Dimitri Rhodes July 16 (Reuters) – French food caterer Sodexo said on Thursday it expects faster revenue growth from 2027 as it seeks to revive performance through stronger execution and expansion in North America, its largest market. ... The company now expects organic revenue growth of 2% to 3% in 2027, compared with expected growth of 1.2% to 1.5% in 2026. ... Sodexo’s new CEO announced in April a review of the company’s execution and contracts, citing underinvestment, inconsistent performance and slow decision-making. “In terms of countries, obviously, the absolute priority is the United States,” CEO Thierry Delaporte said on a wire call. ... The company, which generates roughly half of its revenue in North America, warned in October 2025 that weak performance in education and healthcare in its single largest market would weigh on this year’s results, aiming to restore growth from 2027. ... “It’s the largest market in ... world, and it’s also a rapidly growing market,” Delaporte added. ... The group also aims for organic revenue growth above 5% in full-year 2030, with net new business above 3%."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,"Sodexo Unveils Shift & Grow 2030 Strategy, Targets Revenue Growth Above 5% By FY30",www.finanznachrichten.de,2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.finanznachrichten.de/nachrichten-2026-07/69042485-sodexo-unveils-shift-grow-2030-strategy-targets-revenue-growth-above-5-by-fy30-020.htm,"Sodexo Unveils Shift & Grow 2030 Strategy, Targets Revenue Growth Above 5% By FY30 ... PARIS (dpa-AFX) - French food services and facilities management company Sodexo S.A. (SDXAY) on Thursday unveiled its Shift & Grow 2030 strategy at an investor update in Paris, outlining plans to accelerate growth, restore competitiveness and improve profitability, while setting new medium-term financial targets through the end of the decade. 'Shift & Grow 2030 is about reconnecting with the values and operating principles that have always defined Sodexo: client proximity, operational discipline, accountability and an entrepreneurial mindset. By executing them consistently, we will restore our competitiveness and unlock the full potential of the company,' said hierry Delaporte, Sodexo Chief Executive Officer. The company said the strategy is designed to address execution gaps that have weighed on recent performance and position Sodexo for sustainable long-term growth. The plan will be rolled out in two phases, with fiscal 2026-2027 focused on restoring competitiveness and fiscal 2028 onward focused on accelerating growth and expanding margins. For fiscal 2027, Sodexo expects organic revenue growth of 2% to 3% and an underlying operating margin of between 3.2% and 3.4%. Looking further ahead, the company targets organic revenue growth of more than 5% and an underlying operating margin above 5% by fiscal 2030. The revenue target includes net new business growth of more than 3%. Under the plan, North America will be Sodexo's primary growth market, supported by a client-focused approach and increased investment in commercial capabilities, technology, data and artificial intelligence. To support the transformation, Sodexo plans around €100 million in incremental annualized operating costs and approximately €1 billion of non-recurring investments in technology, procurement and organizational transformation between fiscal 2026 and fiscal 2030. The company said it will maintain a disciplined capital allocation framework, including capital expenditures of around 2.5% to 3.0% of revenue, a dividend payout ratio of 50%, targeted bolt-on acquisitions and an investment-grade financial policy. Sodexo cited its recent selection by Meta as an early sign of progress under the plan. The contract covers food services at more than 130 locations across over 30 countries and is expected to be rolled out in the coming months. Sodexo shares closed up 2.47% at $12.04 on Wednesday on the OTC market. Copyright(c) 2026 RTTNews.com. All Rights Reserved Copyright RTT News/dpa-AFX"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan,www.advfn.com,2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.advfn.com/stock-market/EURONEXT/SW/stock-news/98928324/sodexo-launches-its-2030-growth-acceleration-plan,"Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan ... # SW Sodexo ... Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan ... July 16 2026 - 1:00AM ... Sodexo is hosting today its Investor Update in Paris, where Thierry Delaporte, Chief Executive Officer of Sodexo, and members of the management team will present Shift & Grow 2030, the Company’s roadmap focused on accelerating growth and restoring competitiveness, alongside the Group’s mid-term financial ambition. ... - Shift & Grow 2030, a clear execution framework to accelerate growth and restore competitiveness - Ambition to reach above +5% organic growth and above 5% operating margin by Fiscal 2030. ... - Client-first approach, supported by clearer focus across geographies, client segments and services, with North America as the primary growth priority. ... - Significant investment program to strengthen commercial capabilities, simplify the operating model and leverage technology to support growth and margin ambitions. ... - A two-phased roadmap, with Fiscal 2026 and Fiscal 2027 focused on rebuilding competitiveness, and Fiscal 2028 onwards focused on accelerating growth, expanding margin and improving ROCE. ... - Early progress already visible, including the recent award of a large global food services contract. Further details in the separate press release issued today and available on sodexo.com ... ""Sodexo is a business with tremendous strengths: leading positions in food and facilities management, a global footprint, an outstanding service culture and a deeply embedded purpose to positively impact its clients, people and society.Shift & Grow 2030 is about reconnecting with the values and operating principles that have always defined Sodexo: client proximity, operational discipline, accountability and an entrepreneurial mindset. By executing them consistently, we will restore our competitiveness and unlock the full potential of the company. Our ambition is clear. By 2030, we want Sodexo to be fully back in the game: competing with the best in our industry, delivering consistent growth, improving profitability in a disciplined way and becoming the partner of choice for our clients. The work is already underway and we are confident in our ability to deliver."" ... A growth acceleration plan driven by three pillars ... The plan is designed to address the execution gaps that have held back the Group's performance through three pillars: ... - Rebuilding the growth engine by reinforcing client proximity, proactive account management and business development, disciplined price-to-win competitiveness and a dedicated large-client approach, leveraging Sodexo's distinctive position across both food and facilities management. ... - Simplifying and standardizing the operating model by making execution faster, more consistent and more scalable through operational excellence, organizational simplification and procurement at scale. ... - Reigniting a high-performance culture by strengthening leadership, performance management, incentives, talent and succession to drive greater accountability and better execution. ... To enable its plan, Sodexo is investing decisively in tech, data and scaling digital and AI to support growth, productivity and decision-making. ... Embedded in Shift & Grow 2030, sustainability and positive impact are core drivers of Sodexo’s client differentiation, supporting employee attractiveness and engagement and long-term value creation. ... A financial trajectory aligned with ... - Fiscal 2026 and Fiscal 2027 focused on strengthening commercial capabilities, simplifying operations and accelerating investment.For Fiscal 2027, Sodexo expects: ... - - Organic revenue growth of +2% to +3%; ... - Underlying operating margin broadly in line with Fiscal 2026 guidance: between 3.2% and 3.4%, reflecting continued investment to strengthen capabilities and restore competitiveness. ... - From Fiscal 2028 onwards: acceleration phase with progressive benefits from these actions, supporting improved growth, profitability and returns.For Fiscal 2030, Sodexo expects to deliver: ... - - Above +5% organic revenue growth, including net new business above +3%; - Underlying operating margin above 5%. ... A disciplined capital allocation framework ... - Increased investment, including around 100 million euros of incremental annualized operating costs to sustainably strengthen commercial capabilities, together with approximately 1 billion euros of non-recurring investments across tech, procurement and organizational transformation over Fiscal 2026 to Fiscal 2030. ... - Capital expenditure of around 2.5% to 3.0% of revenue, to support the Group's commercial ambitions and productivity improvements while maintaining the Group's capital-light model. ... - A balanced shareholder return policy with a dividend payout ratio maintained at 50%, providing attractive shareholder returns while preserving the capacity to invest in the business. ... - Targeted bolt-on acquisitions, focused on strengthening capabilities, building scale in priority markets and enhancing long-term returns, while maintaining strict financial discipline. ... - A solid investment-grade financial policy, preserving financial flexibility throughout the transformation, supporting future investment opportunities and maintaining access to attractive financing conditions. ... , presentation and replay will ... | Fiscal 2026 Annual Results | October 23, 2026 | | --- | --- | | Fiscal 2026 Annual Shareholders Meeting | December 16, 2026 | | Fiscal 2027 First quarter Revenues | January 7, 2027 | ... About SodexoFounded in Marseille in 1966 by Pierre Bellon, Sodexo is the leader in Food and Services, shaping better everyday experiences at every moment in life: work, heal, learn and play. The Group stands out for its independence, its founding family shareholding and its responsible business model. With its services, Sodexo meets all the challenges of everyday life with a dual goal: to improve the quality of life of our employees and those we serve, and contribute to the economic, social and environmental progress in the communities where we operate. Our purpose is to create a better everyday for everyone to build a better life for all. Sodexo is included in the CAC Next 20, CAC SBT 1.5, FTSE 4 Good et DJSI indices.Key figures ... | 24.1 billion euros Fiscal 2025 consolidated revenues 426,000 employees as at August 31, 2025 #2 France-based private employer worldwide | 43 countries 80 million consumers served daily 7.8 billion euros in market capitalization (as July 15, 2026) | | --- | --- |"
