e total de droits de vote et d'actions ERRATUM 31 mai 2026Quarta, 10 de Junho de 2026 (4 semanas atrás) • UK Regulatory |"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo supera projeções e eleva previsão para 2026 - FoodBiz,foodbizbrasil.com (portal),2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://foodbizbrasil.com/negocios/sodexo-supera-projecoes-eleva-previsao-crescimento-2026/,"Sodexo supera projeções e eleva previsão para 2026 - FoodBiz ... # Sodexo supera projeções e eleva previsão para 2026 ... - portal - julho 2, 2026 - 2:00 pm A Sodexo registrou resultados acima das expectativas do mercado no terceiro trimestre fiscal de 2026, impulsionada pela resiliência da demanda e pelo desempenho de áreas estratégicas do negócio. A companhia francesa de serviços de alimentação e gestão de facilities reportou crescimento orgânico de receita de 2%, revertendo a expectativa de retração de 0,1% projetada por analistas. ... A receita do período alcançou € 6,17 bilhões, acima dos € 6,04 bilhões esperados pelo consenso de mercado e superior aos € 6,12 bilhões registrados no mesmo trimestre do ano anterior. ... Com o desempenho, a empresa revisou para cima sua perspectiva para o ano fiscal. A Sodexo agora projeta crescimento orgânico da receita entre 1,2% e 1,5%, ante a estimativa anterior de 0,5% a 1%. A previsão para a margem operacional subjacente foi mantida entre 3,2% e 3,4%. ... Segundo o CEO Thierry Delaporte, a companhia conseguiu compensar um cenário operacional mais cauteloso ao capturar novas oportunidades de crescimento. ... > “Embora tenhamos iniciado o trimestre com uma visão prudente do ambiente de negócios, conseguimos mitigar diversos riscos e aproveitar oportunidades em todo o portfólio, especialmente na operação da Sodexo Live! na América do Norte”, afirmou o executivo. ... Um dos destaques do trimestre foi a operação da Sodexo Live! na América do Norte, divisão responsável pela gestão de alimentação e hospitalidade em arenas, estádios, centros de convenções e grandes eventos. O segmento apresentou crescimento superior a 15%, ajudando a compensar perdas anteriores de contratos na área de educação. ... Na América do Norte, o crescimento orgânico consolidado ficou praticamente estável, com leve queda de 0,1%. Já os segmentos de Saúde & Idosos e Sodexo Live! mantiveram trajetória positiva. ... Na Europa, a receita orgânica avançou 0,6%, impactada pelo encerramento de um grande contrato global de gestão de instalações e pela menor atividade no setor de educação. ... O melhor desempenho regional veio do grupo “Resto do Mundo”, que registrou crescimento orgânico de 10,6%, impulsionado pela entrada de novos contratos, especialmente no segmento de Energia & Recursos. ... O crescimento total da receita foi de 0,9%, refletindo diferentes fatores. A valorização do euro frente ao dólar gerou impacto cambial negativo de 2,5%, enquanto as aquisições contribuíram positivamente em 1,4%. ... Entre elas está a incorporação do Grupo Mediterránea, concluída em fevereiro de 2026, que reforçou a presença da Sodexo em mercados estratégicos. ... Além dos resultados operacionais, a companhia informou que liquidou antecipadamente um título de US$ 328 milhões com recursos próprios e conquistou a Medalha de Ouro EcoVadis, reconhecimento que posiciona a empresa entre as 2% mais bem avaliadas em práticas de sustentabilidade dentro do seu setor. ... Os resultados agradaram investidores e analistas. As ações da Sodexo chegaram a subir mais de 6% após a divulgação do balanço. ... O Morgan Stanley destacou que a receita ficou entre 2% e 3% acima das estimativas do banco e do consenso do mercado. Para a instituição, a revisão das projeções para o restante do ano ainda pode ser conservadora, considerando o desempenho apresentado no terceiro trimestre. ... A expectativa agora se volta para a reunião com investidores marcada para 16 de julho, quando a companhia deverá detalhar sua estratégia para acelerar o crescimento e fortalecer sua competitividade."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen | Fortune,fortune.com (John Kell),2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fortune.com/2026/07/01/foodservice-giant-sodexo-ai-robotics/,"How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen | Fortune ... # How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen ... July 1, 2026, 12:42 PM ET ... Alice Guehennec is the chief tech, data, and digital officer at Sodexo.Courtesy of Sodexo ... technology career got ... As a child raised in"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen – DNYUZ,dnyuz.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://dnyuz.com/2026/07/01/how-foodservice-giant-sodexo-is-embracing-ai-and-robotics-to-reshape-the-kitchen/,"How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen – DNYUZ ... # How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen ... After more than a decade in consulting, Guéhennec’s career quickly accelerated and she has held C-suite technology titles four times during her career, including as deputy chief information officer at the government agency Préfecture de Police in Paris, CIO in France at foodservice giant Sodexo, and then group chief digital and information officer at water management services company Saur, before returning to Sodexo in September 2023 to serve as chief tech, data, and digital officer. ... It is in this role that Guéhennec oversees an annual tech budget of around 500 million euros ($571 million USD) for the Fortune 500 Europe company, which ranked No. 156 on the latest list. Those technology investments include an artificial intelligence tool that’s intended to get chefs away from their laptops and allow them to spend more time in the kitchen conceptualizing new dishes. AI is also being used to manage staffing levels and automate purchasing and pricing decisions. ... Sodexo, which generates around $28 billion in annual revenue, operates a vast business tht generates 60% of sales from food services provided to schools, corporate offices, stadiums, hospitals, and airport lounges. This part of the business is subject to choppy swings in demand, from when schools are in or out of session to when stadiums host a game, and even the uneven return-to-office policies that can make it difficult for Sodexo and the companies and government agencies it serves to plan for demand. ... On top of that, Sodexo has to confront ingredient variabilities due to the seasonality of fresh produce and volatile food prices; the latter linked to external stressors such as the war in Iran and global tariffs. ... Guéhennec developed an internal AI tool called “Menu AI,” which she says helps automate all the decisions chefs need to make to conceptualize a new menu item, while also taking into account raw material price fluctuations, seasonality, and on-site demand. Sodexo says this AI tool has been able to generate and manage menus from a pool of 400 seasonal recipes in a single day, rather than the two to four weeks of manual work that would have been necessary before AI. ... Sodexo is also exploring the application of AI to help incorporate food trends that emerge on social media and other external channels, which could help speed up the creation of trendier menu creations. “We are working to have AI that builds new recipes based on the trends on the market,” adds Guéhennec. “But it’s still under construction.” ... The other 40% of Sodexo’s revenue comes from facilities management. It is there that Guéhennec has invested in AI tools that help on-site managers plan their staffing levels and track when a room has been used enough to require a cleaning, rather than just sprucing up every room on a regular basis even if it isn’t needed. AI is also being used to make data-driven recommendations, such as telling to tell one site it should restock coffee at 4 PM to meet demand, but that another location can skip afternoon refills. ... Guéhennec says that every major AI use case is initially piloted at around five to ten sites in a couple of the 43 countries that Sodexo serves. She believes that on-the-ground, localized feedback at this stage “helps us to encourage and facilitate adoption.” Every employee is encouraged to request licenses for AI services like Microsoft Copilot or Google Gemini Enterprise if they think it can help make them more productive at work. ... Sodexo is in the very early stages of experimenting with frictionless stores, which use AI and computer vision to eliminate a dedicated cashier station. The technology, which hasn’t had the smoothest rollout when big retailers like Amazon tried to create their own version of it, has been deployed at two different universities in St. Louis. At one school, Sodexo says the checkout-free retail experience has increased revenue by 56%. The other, unnamed university is seeing a 28% lift in sales and an 11% boost to the average check size. ... The company has also deployed about 200 robots globally, including 100 floor-cleaning robots across all regions and 85 delivery robots, most of them in the U.S. What could be next: robots in the kitchen that can take on highly repetitive and, at times, potentially risky tasks. ... “We are looking for some robots like this,” says Guéhennec. “To reduce the danger and level of accidents in our kitchens and to replace the less safe tasks with robots.” ... The post How foodservice giant Sodexo is embracing AI and robotics to reshape the kitchen appeared first on Fortune."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo appoints Agnès Park as Group Chief Human Resources,www.globenewswire.com (Sodexo SA),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/06/22/3315056/0/en/Sodexo-appoints-Agn%C3%A8s-Park-as-Group-Chief-Human-Resources-Officer.html,"Sodexo appoints Agnès Park as Group Chief Human Resources ... # Sodexo appoints Agnès Park as Group Chief Human Resources Officer ... Sodexo announces that Agnès Park is named Group Chief Human Resources Officer as of July 1st, 2026. She will report to Sodexo CEO Thierry Delaporte and will join the Global Executive Team. ... Agnès Park joins Sodexo with extensive international experience across multiple industries, including Automotive, Pharmaceuticals, and Technology Life Sciences.Throughout her career, she has consistently focused on designing and implementing human resources strategies that support both short- and long-term business objectives. Agnès Park has led major organizational transformations to support ambitious growth agendas, built robust talent and leadership development programs, and implemented effective workforce planning strategies grounded in constructive labor relations and social dialogue. ... | Thierry Delaporte, Sodexo Chief Executive Officer said: | | --- | | ""I am delighted to welcome Agnès Park to Sodexo. Her expertise aligns strongly with Sodexo’s current priorities. She will play a key role in shaping the Group’s “Shift & Grow” program, with a particular focus on advancing talent development and reinforcing a high-performance culture. She will be instrumental in supporting our ambition to accelerate growth while continuing to elevate service quality as a key differentiator.” | ... Agnès Park brings over 27 years of experience in human resources across a wide range of industries and international environments. She most recently served as Chief Human Resources Officer at Valeo, a global automotive company operating in 32 countries with over 100,000 employees. In this role, she was responsible for the Group’s human resources strategy, driving cultural and organizational transformation, and strengthening talent and leadership development. Prior to joining Valeo, Agnès Park held senior human resources leadership roles in the pharmaceutical and technology life sciences sectors, where she partnered with executive teams in complex, global organizations. Agnès Park is French and speaks English and Korean. She is based in France. ... About SodexoFounded in Marseille in 1966 by Pierre Bellon, Sodexo is the leader in Food and Services, shaping better everyday experiences at every moment in life: work, heal, learn and play. The Group stands out for its independence, its founding family shareholding and its responsible business model. With its services, Sodexo meets all the challenges of everyday life with a dual goal: to improve the quality of life of our employees and those we serve, and contribute to the economic, social and environmental progress in the communities where we operate. Our purpose is to create a better everyday for everyone to build a better life for all. Sodexo is included in the CAC Next 20, CAC SBT 1.5, FTSE 4 Good et DJSI indices.Key figures ... - 24.1 billion euros Fiscal 2025 consolidated revenues - 426,000 employees as at August 31, 2025 - #2 France-based private employer worldwide - 43 countries - 80 million consumers served daily - 6.5 billion euro in market capitalization (as April 9, 2026) ... Company ProfileSodexo SAIndustry: Restaurants & BarsWebsite: ... July 02, 2026 01:00 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Q3 Fiscal 2026 revenues above expectations; focus on execution ... Issy-les-Moulineaux, July 2, 2026 (7:00 a.m. CEST)Sodexo (Euronext Paris FR 0000121220-OTC: SDXAY) Q3 organic revenue growth of +2.0%Revised Fiscal 2026 organic revenue growth guidance, reflecting... ... June 10, 2026 04:34 ET | Source: Sodexo SA ... Monthly disclosure on share capital and voting rights ERRATUM May 31, 2026 ... Regulated Information Issy-les-Moulineaux, June 10, 2026 Sodexo: Monthly disclosure on share capital and voting rights ERRATUM Pursuant to Article L.233-8-II of the French Commercial Code and..."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,How a $36B Global Procurement Network Drives Innovation in GPO Solutions - News Usa Today,news-usa.today (Chief Editor: Rhea Montrose),2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news-usa.today/how-a-36b-global-procurement-network-drives-innovation-in-gpo-solutions/,"How a $36B Global Procurement Network Drives Innovation in GPO Solutions - News Usa Today ... ## Sodexo Expands Midwest Presence with New Sales Executive Role in North and South Dakota ... Sodexo, the global facility services provider managing $36 billion in annual procurement spend, has announced a regional sales executive position for North and South Dakota, according to a job posting reviewed by News-USA.today. The role, part of the company’s Entegra procurement network, aims to strengthen relationships with clients serving 120,000+ sites worldwide, the posting states. This move comes as the company continues to prioritize growth in the U.S. Midwest, a region that has seen a 12% increase in contract value since 2020, according to a 2023 report by the National Association of Purchasing Managers. ... The job posting emphasizes the need for a “strategic thinker” with expertise in “enterprise-level procurement solutions,” highlighting Sodexo’s focus on expanding its GPO (group purchasing organization) model. This approach, which aggregates buying power to secure better pricing, has been a cornerstone of the company’s strategy since the early 2000s. However, the role’s emphasis on “regional customization” suggests a shift toward localized solutions, a trend that could reshape how businesses in the Dakotas approach supply chain management. ... While Sodexo touts its ability to reduce costs for clients, critics argue that the expansion of GPOs like Entegra may have unintended consequences for smaller, independent vendors. “There’s a risk that local businesses could be outcompeted by larger suppliers leveraging GPO discounts,” said Dr. Emily Carter, an economics professor at the University of North Dakota. “This isn’t just about savings—it’s about how power is consolidated in the supply chain.” ... Historical data supports this concern. A 2018 study by the Federal Reserve Bank of Minneapolis found that regions with high GPO penetration saw a 7% decline in small business startups over a decade. North and South Dakota, which have historically relied on local suppliers for foodservice and janitorial services, may face similar challenges as Sodexo’s influence grows. The company’s 2023 annual report notes that 68% of its U.S. clients are now part of its GPO network, up from 52% in 2015. ... The new sales executive role is likely to attract professionals with experience in both procurement and regional business development. Sodexo’s job posting specifies a preference for candidates with “10+ years in B2B sales within the Midwest,” a requirement that reflects the company’s focus on building relationships with local stakeholders. This could create a pipeline for career advancement in the region, particularly for those with expertise in healthcare, education, or government contracts—sectors that are major clients of Sodexo. ... However, the role’s emphasis on “innovative GPO solutions” also raises questions about the skills required for future jobs. As Sodexo continues to integrate AI-driven analytics into its procurement processes, the demand for data literacy among sales teams may increase. A 2025 survey by the Society for Human Resource Management found that 62% of U.S. employers now prioritize digital skills in sales roles, a trend that could reshape hiring criteria in the Dakotas. ... Sodexo’s official website states that the company has invested $2.1 billion in technology upgrades since 2021, including tools to optimize supply chain efficiency. While this could lead to cost savings for clients, it also underscores the growing importance of tech-savvy professionals in the sector. ... Proponents of Sodexo’s expansion argue that the company’s scale allows it to offer services that smaller providers cannot. “For schools and hospitals in rural areas, GPOs like Entegra are a lifeline,” said Sarah Lin, a spokesperson for the National Association of State Procurement Officers. “They provide access to national pricing and reduce administrative burdens.” This perspective is echoed in a 2024 report by the U.S. Department of Agriculture, which found that GPOs helped rural healthcare providers save an average of 18% on medical supplies. ... The tension between efficiency and local autonomy is a recurring theme in the debate over GPOs. While Sodexo’s model has proven effective in urban centers, its impact on rural areas remains less studied. A 2022 report by the Rural Policy Research Institute noted that only 15% of GPO-related studies focused on non-metropolitan regions, highlighting a gap in the data. ... As Sodexo moves forward with its hiring, the success of the new sales executive will likely depend on their ability to balance national strategies with local needs. The role"
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo Live wins Mizzou athletics F&B business,www.sportsbusinessjournal.com,2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sportsbusinessjournal.com/Articles/2026/06/11/sodexo-live-wins-mizzou-athletics-fb-business/,"Sodexo Live wins Mizzou athletics F&B business ... # Sodexo Live wins Mizzou athletics F&B business ... The Univ. of Missouri has picked Sodexo Live as its new athletics venues concessionaire. ... Sodexo Live partnered with Columbia, Mo.-based Upper Crust Food Service on its bid. Upper Crust is led by CEO and Mizzou grad Adam Guy. ... Sodexo Live takes over from Levy, and inherits a Memorial Stadium that will look markedly different this coming fall when its$250M North End Zone project opens. ... Tiger athletics generated $8.2M in food and beverage revenue in 2024, according to sales data obtained by SBJ through a public records request. The seven premium seating products and two clubs added in the north end zone -- 4,000 additional seats take the 100-year-old stadium’s capacity over 65,000 -- should boost F&B gross sales and per-cap numbers. Mizzou has sold alcohol at Tiger athletic events since the fall of 2019. ... Sodexo Live’s other college athletics clients include the Texas, Ole Miss, Louisville, Florida, Cincinnati, and Miami (at Hard Rock Stadium). Mizzou was a welcome win for Sodexo after it was ousted at Michigan(by Levy)."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Sodexo launches hospitality services for the oil sector and wants to quadruple revenue in Brazil,www.tridge.com,2026-05-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tridge.com/news/sodexo-launches-hospitality-services-for-the-lbgkylxu,"Sodexo launches hospitality services for the oil sector and wants to quadruple revenue in Brazil ... # Sodexo launches hospitality services for the oil sector and wants to quadruple revenue in Brazil ... Published May 14, 2026 ... Sodexo has initiated a new cycle of expansion in Brazil with the ambition to quadruple its revenue in the country over the next decade, supported by a segmented portfolio of brands and services. The move repositions the Brazilian operation - which has doubled in size over the last ten years - and showcases the creation of offerings designed for different environments, from corporate to hospital, education to remote operations of high complexity, such as the oil and natural gas sector. The company, founded in Marseille, France, in 1966, belongs to the Sodexo Group. The former Sodexo Benefícios (meal voucher company) is now called Pluxee and is no longer related to the Sodexo Group, following the spin-off in 2024, the company reported. The highlight of the move is focused on the oil and gas sector - Offshore Living - a ""maritime hospitality"" solution aimed at onboard workers who spend 15 to 20 days at sea. Sodexo states that the model was structured based on the company's global ..."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,The Sodexo India growth story has reached a new milestone! | Sodexo,www.linkedin.com (Sodexo),2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sodexo_sodexoindia-masterkitchen-gurugram-activity-7460261696503259136-cPIu,"# The Sodexo India growth story has reached a new milestone! | Sodexo · LinkedIn · 2026-05-13 ... **Sodexo**: Sodexo Group is a company that integrates catering, facilities management, and employee benefits services to create an improved quality of life for the people they serve, their clients, employees, customers, and the community. Sodexo has 40,000-50,000 employees (+10% YoY) and has annual revenue in the EUR20B-EUR30B range. Headquartered in France, operates in 8 countries (including United States, United Kingdom, Philippines, Singapore, and Brazil). Its workforce is distributed across 125 countries (including United States, Brazil, India, United Kingdom, and France). Has a market cap in the EUR10B-EUR20B range. IPO 2002. ... The Sodexo India growth story has reached a new milestone! ... We officially inaugurated our newest MasterKitchen in Gurugram, in the presence of [Nicolas LANNUZEL](https://linkedin.com/in/nicolas-lannuzel-158987), CEO - APMEA, Sodexo, and [Sambit Sahu](https://linkedin.com/in/sambit-sahu-81b1ba49), MD, Sodexo India. ... Compliant with FSSAI guidelines and HACCP principles of food safety, this state-of-the-art facility is a critical step in our growth strategy for India. ... Centrally located in the NCR with easy access to major industrial and commercial hubs, the MasterKitchen is designed as a comprehensive solution offering scale, agility and consistency to our clients. Currently delivering 22,000 meals daily from an 11,000 sq ft built-up space, it features an 80% scalability margin as we grow. ... The kitchen is equipped with PNG-based systems and high-tech kitchen gadgets that reduce cooking times while retaining nutritional integrity. Our commitment to operational resilience and sustainability is reflected in our 200% equipment backup, 70% pot-free water efficiency, and the use of ETP for wastewater recycling. ... Following the success of our central kitchens in Bengaluru and Hyderabad, this third launch acts as a strategic hub to address the growing demand for high-volume, premium food services across the region. ... This is an exciting chapter as we continue to innovate and keep our clients at the centre of everything we do. ... > Proud moment for all of us. This new MasterKitchen reflects our commitment to food safety, innovation, and scalable operations — a great step forward in strengthening service delivery across the region. ... > What stands out is that this is far more than just the launch of another facility. It reflects how food services in India are evolving through scale, technology, sustainability, and operational precision, while keeping the end-consumer experience at the core. > ... > The Gurugram MasterKitchen is a strong example of future-ready infrastructure meeting real business demand. From HACCP-driven food safety standards to smart utility optimization and scalable production capability, every detail seems thoughtfully designed for long-term impact. > ... > Congratulations & the entire Sodexo team on this remarkable milestone."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,"Sodexo India Launches State-of-the-Art MasterKitchen in Gurugram to Enhance Food Services, ETHospitalityWorld",hospitality.economictimes.indiatimes.com (www.ETHospitalityWorld.com),2026-05-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hospitality.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/operations/food-and-beverages/sodexo-india-strengthens-north-india-presence-with-launch-of-new-masterkitchen-in-gurugram/131015471,"Sodexo India Launches State-of-the-Art MasterKitchen in Gurugram to Enhance Food Services, ETHospitalityWorld ... # Sodexo India strengthens north India presence with launch of new MasterKitchen in Gurugram ... Spread across 11,000 square feet, the facility is engineered for high-volume productivity without compromising on nutritional integrity or food safety. It is equipped to deliver up to 22,000 meals per day across breakfast, lunch, and dinner, with 80 percent scalability margin, allowing production to expand to 40,000 meals daily, supporting services for a growing client base across the region, said a release. ... - Published On May 11, 20 ... 6 at ... 8:00 PM IST ... Read by 100 Professionals ... Food services and integrated facilities management company Sodexo India, announced the commencement of operations at its new high-capacity MasterKitchen in Sector 37, Gurugram. The state-of-the-art central kitchen significantly strengthens Sodexo’s service capabilities across North India, complementing an established network of central kitchens in Hyderabad and Bengaluru. The facility also reflects Sodexo’s focus on scaling operational efficiency, and enhancing service proximity to key markets.Speaking on the launch, Sambit Sahu, managing director, Sodexo India, said, “The launch of our MasterKitchen in Gurugram marks a pivotal milestone and a key differentiator for Sodexo in the Indian market. By combining high-quality nutrition with our signature food concepts and diverse portfolio of brands, this facility serves as a strategic hub to address the growing demand for high-volume, premium food services across the region. It is designed to be a comprehensive solution that offers our clients the distinct advantages of scale, agility and service consistency.” ... “Following the successful establishment of our MasterKitchens in South India, this third launch is a critical step in our growth strategy for India. It further strengthens our service capabilities in North India, allowing us to meet the evolving needs of our clients while driving innovation and setting new benchmarks in food services,” he added.Spread across 11,000 square feet, the facility is engineered for high-volume productivity without compromising on nutritional integrity or food safety. It is equipped to deliver up to 22,000 meals per day across breakfast, lunch, and dinner, with 80 percent scalability margin, allowing production to expand to 40,000 meals daily, supporting services for a growing client base across the region, said a release. ... Key features of the facility include:—Advanced cooking systems: High-efficiency PNG-based systems and advanced appliances and kitchen gadgets reduce cooking times, curb heat loss, and retain nutritional value.—Operational resilience: The kitchen is 70% pot-free for water efficiency, and designed with 200 percent equipment backup to ensure uninterrupted operations.—Freshness & logistics: Meals are transported via a dedicated fleet of temperature-controlled, EV vehicles to ensure optimal freshness while supporting lower-carbon delivery operations.&mdash;Certified safety standards: The facility adheres to world-class health, safety, and hygiene protocols, mirroring Sodexo's commitment to industry-leading food safety management. ... With its combination of scale, strategic location, and advanced infrastructure, the Gurugram MasterKitchen reinforces Sodexo’s leadership in delivering efficient, sustainable and client focused food service solutions across the region by enhancing everyday experiences, supporting healthier choices and enabling more sustainable operations, the release added."
SODEXO,,,,Exa,Plano de crescimento da Sodexo tem fusões e aquisições - 11/05/2026 - Painel S.A. - Folha,www1.folha.uol.com.br,2026-05-11T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-11 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/colunas/painelsa/2026/05/plano-de-crescimento-da-sodexo-tem-fusoes-e-aquisicoes-de-outras-empresas.shtml,"Plano de crescimento da Sodexo tem fusões e aquisições - 11/05/2026 - Painel S.A. - Folha ... A Sodexo tem fusões e aquisições de outras empresas como um dos vetores para o crescimento que planeja para a próxima década. A visão é a compra de companhias que não apenas tenham fatia relevante do mercado de fornecimento de refeições corporativas e gestão operacional de estruturas físicas, mas também outras que possam incorporar outras funções. ... Para Danielle Totti, vice-presidente de estratégia, marketing, comercial e performance, isso é um movimento inorgânico. ... Como ela disse à coluna na edição deste domingo (10), a Sodexo Brasil vê espaço para crescer 400% na próxima década. Pesquisas da empresa mostram um mercado altamente fragmentado, em que os três maiores nomes do setor têm, juntos, 25% do market share. ... Outros três vetores que fazem parte do plano de expansão passam por ter serviço diferenciado da concorrência em serviços já prestados; alcançar segmentos ainda não atendidos; e novos modelos de negócio. ... Nestes dois últimos casos, estão no radar edifícios comerciais com muitos inquilinos e sem cozinha própria, assim a Sodexo poderia montar serviços operacionais de alimentação. Também fornecimento de refeições a eventos de grande porte."
SODEXO,,,,Linkup,Sodexo exceeds expectations for Q3 2026,FinanzWire,2026-07-16T00:00:00Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.finanzwire.com/press-release/sodexo-epa-sw-chiffre-daffaires-du-3e-trimestre-de-lexercice-2026-superieur-aux-attentes-focus-sur-lexecution-g1GMm12fdAa,"Sodexo reported third-quarter 2026 revenue exceeding expectations with 2.0% organic growth and a positive revision of its annual growth forecast to 1.2%-1.5%. The company benefited from resilient demand, especially in North America, and strengthened its market position through acquisitions like Grupo Mediterránea and Prestige Purchasing."
SODEXO,,,,Linkup,Sodexo secures a major food services contract with Meta,Sodexo Newsroom,2026-07-16T00:00:00Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sodexo.com/news/newsroom/2026/sodexo-secures-major-food-services-contract-meta,"Sodexo was selected by Meta to deliver food services across its global portfolio, marking one of Sodexo's largest global workplace food services contracts. The partnership combines Meta’s workplace standards with Sodexo’s expertise, leveraging digital and data capabilities to enhance employee experience at scale."
SODEXO,,,,Linkup,Sodexo launches its 2030 growth acceleration plan,Sodexo Newsroom,2026-07-16T00:00:00Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sodexo.com/news/newsroom/2026/sodexo-launches-2030-growth-acceleration-plan,"At its Investor Update in Paris, Sodexo presented Shift & Grow 2030, a roadmap focused on accelerating growth and restoring competitiveness. The plan aims for consistent growth, improved profitability, and becoming the partner of choice by 2030, with early progress including the award of a large global food services contract."
SODEXO,,,,Linkup,Sodexo unveils ambitious growth plan with increased spending to boost margins by 2030,StockInvest.us,2026-07-16T00:00:00Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://stockinvest.us/digest/sodexo-unveils-ambitious-growth-plan-with-increased-spending-to-boost-margins-by-2030,"Sodexo aims for over 5% organic growth and a 5% operating margin by 2030, supported by €1 billion in investments and higher operating costs to enhance competitiveness and adopt AI technology. The company forecasts 2%-3% organic revenue growth in fiscal 2027 and plans to maintain a 50% dividend payout ratio despite increased spending."
