NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,GoNexus Group adds Assist Card services to NexusCube,www.traveldailynews.com (Theodore Koumelis),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.traveldailynews.com/mice-industry/business-travel/gonexus-group-adds-assist-card-services-to-nexuscube/,"Group adds Assist Card services to NexusCube ... # GoNexus Group adds Assist Card services to NexusCube ... GoNexus Group has integrated Assist Card travel assistance services into NexusCube, expanding its global B2B marketplace alongside experiences, transfers and mobility products for travel distributors. ... CANCUN, MEXICO – GoNexus Group has partnered with Assist Card to integrate travel assistance services into NexusCube, its global B2B marketplace for travel distribution. ... GoNexus Group serves 7.4 million customers annually across its experiences and mobility activities. The agreement expands the NexusCube portfolio by adding travel assistance alongside experiences, transfers and mobility products through a single technology platform. ... NexusCube connects thousands of travel partners with travel products across hundreds of destinations. Through a single integration, the platform provides access to experiences, transfers and mobility solutions for distributors operating in different travel segments. ... Following the integration of Assist Card, travel agencies, tour operators, online travel agencies, hoteliers and other travel businesses working with GoNexus Group will be able to offer travel assistance alongside the platform’s existing products. ... Rubén Gutiérrez, President of GoNexus Group, said: “Our ambition is for our GoNexus Group’s B2B platform, NexusCube, to become the travel industry’s preferred B2B marketplace for complementary travel services. By partnering with leading providers such as Assist Card, we continue expanding an ecosystem that enables our customers to access best-in-class solutions through a single connection. This collaboration enhances the value we deliver to our partners while making it easier for them to build richer travel experiences for their customers”. ... For Assist Card, the agreement provides an additional international B2B distribution channel for its travel assistance services through the NexusCube ecosystem. ... Carlos Bricka, Country Manager of Assist Card Mexico, said: “At Assist Card, we believe that great partnerships are built between companies that share the same vision: putting the customer at the centre of every decision. The integration of our services into NexusCube represents a strategic step in expanding our global reach alongside a leader in travel innovation and distribution. By combining NexusCube’s technology and international ecosystem with Assist Card’s leadership in travel assistance, we will deliver an even stronger value proposition, giving thousands of business partners and travellers access to reliable, agile and high-quality travel assistance solutions wherever they are in the world,” ... The companies said the collaboration forms part of their wider focus on digital travel distribution, with the integration designed to make complementary services available through a single B2B connection. ... For Assist Card, participation in NexusCube also expands the distribution of its services through a global network of travel businesses using the platform. ... The agreement comes as travel distribution platforms increasingly combine multiple product categories within unified technology ecosystems. NexusCube will now offer experiences, mobility products and travel assistance through the same B2B marketplace. ... expands into sports ... GoNexus Group and Peregrino report major efficiency gains from omnichannel service platform ... ###### GoNexus Group reports record year of growth ... ###### GoNexus Group’s Global DMC Network unveils bold global expansion strategy ... ###### GoNexus Group adds Assist Card services to NexusCube"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nectar Introduces Nectar Cue: A Week of Amazon Marketing Cloud Analysis Becomes a Same-Day Answer, Measured in Dollars",www.einpresswire.com (B2B Marketing),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.einpresswire.com/article/932024416/nectar-introduces-nectar-cue-a-week-of-amazon-marketing-cloud-analysis-becomes-a-same-day-answer-measured-in-dollars,"Nectar Introduces Nectar Cue: A Week of Amazon Marketing Cloud Analysis Becomes a Same-Day Answer, Measured in Dollars ... # Nectar Introduces Nectar Cue: A Week of Amazon Marketing Cloud Analysis Becomes a Same-Day Answer, Measured in Dollars ... August 06, 2026, 12:00 GMT ... Nectar Cue, built on iDerive, lets brands query Amazon Marketing Cloud audiences, sales, and margin in plain language and measure what ads returned in margin. ... MOORESTOWN, NJ, UNITED STATES, August 6, 2026 / EINPresswire.com/ -- Nectar, an independent retail media and commerce agency and Amazon Ads Advanced Partner, today introduced Nectar Cue, an AI workflow platform for Amazon and marketplace brands. Cue is built on two systems Nectar already operates: iDerive, its proprietary commerce analytics platform, and the iDerive MCP server, which connects that data securely to AI assistants including Claude. Together they let a brand ask a question about its entire Amazon business in plain language and get an answer the same day. The same analysis has historically taken an analyst most of a week. Most brands can build a custom audience in Amazon Marketing Cloud. Most never act on it. Audiences built in AMC, Amazon’s clean-room analytics environment — lapsed Subscribe & Save customers, competitor-cart shoppers, high-LTV lookalikes, true new-to-brand segments with five-year suppression logic — only matter if their impact can be measured. iDerive unifies AMC audience and measurement data with sales, advertising, and profitability down to the SKU and search-term level, so every question about growth is answered against profit. That measurement layer is what Cue runs on. Access runs through the iDerive MCP server, built on Model Context Protocol, the open standard introduced by Anthropic for connecting AI assistants to live data. Brands query their own marketplace data from their own Claude account, with no analyst in the loop. A brand manager can ask which new-to-brand segments are growing, how they overlap with current spend, and where the next dollar earns the most margin, and see the answer in seconds instead of waiting for a report to be assembled. The insight does not stop at analysis. Nectar’s advertising teams take the same audience logic into Amazon DSP, Amazon’s programmatic ad platform, and into audience-based bid modifiers on Sponsored Products and Sponsored Brands, reaching the shoppers search alone cannot: competitor buyers, lapsed customers, and category newcomers. iDerive then measures whether that activation was incremental, in new-to-brand rate and contribution margin rather than ROAS alone. Cue extends the same foundation from answering questions to running the work. Reaching Amazon Marketing Cloud, Vendor and Seller Central, Amazon Ads, and additional marketplaces through one connection, Cue turns recurring analysis into monitored workflows. It surfaces exceptions, such as a suppressed listing or an emerging revenue opportunity, and routes them to the person who can act. For brands running thousands of SKUs, the binding constraint is rarely analysis; it is the hours available to catch and act on what the analysis finds. Cue is in use across Nectar’s own analyst teams today and is rolling out to brand partners in phases. “AMC changed the question from where should we bid to who are we bidding on,” said Harriet Carson, VP of Advertising at Nectar. “Nectar Cue lets us answer that question in plain language and act on it the same day. We take the audiences we build straight into the DSP and Sponsored Ads campaigns our team runs, and we can prove in dollars whether they were incremental.” The approach is already producing results for Nectar’s partners. Petmate grew new-to-brand orders by about 85 percent and Core ASIN revenue by 12 percent through audience-led advertising measured in iDerive. Boxie increased ordered revenue on Amazon Canada by 55.4 percent on roughly half a percent more ad spend. Epson lifted ad-attributed sales 153 percent while keeping ad spend steady. “A custom audience is only as valuable as your ability to prove it moved the business,” said Youval Peltier, Chief Strategy Officer at Nectar. “Nectar Cue gives our team and our clients the same answer, in dollars, the same day. Connecting iDerive to Claude means a brand can ask its own data a question and see where the profitable growth is, without waiting for a report.” The iDerive MCP server is available to iDerive clients today, and brands can connect iDerive to Claude as part of their engagement. Nectar Cue is rolling out in phases, beginning with Nectar’s team and select brand partners. About Nectar Nectar (thinknectar.com) is a full-service e-commerce performance-marketing agency for mid-market and enterprise brands, managing more than $3 billion in Amazon sales across 120+ brands. An Amazon Ads Advanced Partner and Walmart Connect Partner Network member, Nectar combines an in-house creative studio, marketplace advertising across Sponsored Ads, DSP, and AMC, 1P and 3P operations, and its proprietary iDerive analytics platform. Built by Amazon operators, for Amazon operators. Media Contact Alex Ferrari and Camila Gallate b2bmarketing@thinknectar.com"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai Expands Enterprise Customer Base, Generating $874,000 in New Contract Value, 160 New Customer Contracts and 92% Software Gross Margins in 2026",www.accessnewswire.com (NexTech3D.AI Corp),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.accessnewswire.com/newsroom/en/computers-technology-and-internet/nextech3d.ai-expands-enterprise-customer-base-generating-874-000-1203168,"Nextech3D.ai Expands Enterprise Customer Base, Generating $874,000 in New Contract Value, 160 New Customer Contracts and 92% Software Gross Margins in 2026 ... # Nextech3D.ai Expands Enterprise Customer Base, Generating $874,000 in New Contract Value, 160 New Customer Contracts and 92% Software Gross Margins in 2026 ... TORONTO, ON / ACCESS Newswire/ August 6, 2026 / Nextech3D.ai Corp. (CSE:NTAR)(OTCQB:NEXCF)(FSE:1SS) (""Nextech3D.ai"" or the ""Company""), a leader in AI-powered event technology and immersive digital solutions, today announced strong year-to-date growth across its Eventdex, Map D, and KraftyLab platforms. ... From January 1, 2026 through August 5, 2026, the Company secured 160 new customer contracts with a combined contracted value of approximately $874,000, compared to 18 new customer contracts representing approximately $55,470 during the same period in 2025. ... The Company generated approximately $874,000 in new customer contract value, compared to approximately $55,470 during the same period in 2025, representing growth of approximately 1,476% year-over-year. ... Management believes this increase reflects a combination of larger enterprise engagements, growing software adoption, and the successful launch of KraftyLab. ... Average contract value across Eventdex, Map D, and KraftyLab increased to approximately $5,464, compared to approximately $3,082 during the same period in 2025, representing an increase of approximately 77% year-over-year. ... Nextech3D.ai secured 160 new customer contracts, compared to 18 new customer contracts during the same period in 2025, representing growth of approximately 789% year-over-year. ... Launched in January 2026, KraftyLab has secured 112 new customer contracts valued at approximately $311,100 in less than eight months of operation. ... Management believes KraftyLab is becoming an increasingly meaningful contributor to customer acquisition and revenue growth while expanding Nextech3D.ai's software platform ecosystem. ... The Company's software platforms continue to generate gross margins of approximately 92%, highlighting the scalability of Nextech3D.ai's business model and the potential operating leverage associated with continued customer growth and increased platform adoption. ... the combination of larger average contract values, increasing customer acquisition, and strong software margins reflects growing enterprise demand for AI-powered event technology solutions. ... Nextech3D.ai continues to expand relationships with organizations across enterprise, consulting, government contracting, education, financial services, healthcare, technology, and professional association markets. ... The Company is seeing increasing demand for integrated solutions that combine event registration, attendee engagement, interactive mapping, surveys, analytics, lead generation, and AI-powered workflow automation within a unified platform environment. ... ""Our results through the first seven months of 2026 demonstrate that our strategy is working on multiple levels,"" said Evan Gappelberg, CEO of Nextech3D.ai. ... ""During the period, new customer contract value increased to approximately $874,000 from approximately $55,470, while average contract value increased to approximately $5,464 from approximately $3,082. These results indicate that we are not only attracting more customers, but increasingly winning larger enterprise-level opportunities and broader platform deployments."" ... ""At the same time, KraftyLab has quickly emerged as an important growth driver, generating 112 new customer contracts in just a few months since launch. Combined with our approximately 92% software gross margins, we believe this demonstrates the strength and scalability of our AI-first software platform strategy."" ... ""What excites me most is that we are seeing growth across multiple dimensions of the business simultaneously. Customer acquisition is accelerating, contract values are increasing, enterprise adoption continues to expand, and KraftyLab has emerged as a powerful new growth engine. We believe these results validate our strategy and position Nextech3D.ai to capitalize on the growing demand for AI-powered software solutions across the global events industry."" ... Management believes the Company's growth in customer acquisition, rising average contract values, and successful launch of KraftyLab demonstrate increasing demand for integrated AI-powered event technology solutions. ... With a growing roster of enterprise customers, expanding platform capabilities, recurring software revenue opportunities, and approximately 92% software gross margins, Nextech3D.ai remains focused on creating long-term shareholder value through innovation, enterprise adoption, and scalable software growth. ... Nextech3D.ai Unveils Strategic AI Growth Roadmap Focused on Workforce Intelligence and Event Technology Innovation ... July 3, 2026Roadmap outlines multiple AI-driven growth initiatives designed to expand the Company's technology platform and create new revenue opportunities. ... Nextech3D.ai Reports Strong Q4 and Audited Full-Year Results: +207% YoY Revenue Growth, 91% Gross Margins ... June 25, 2026Company reported significant revenue growth, improving margins, and continued progress toward a scalable AI-powered software business model. ... Nextech3D.ai to Host Livestream Shareholder Update on Financial Results and AI Platform Growth Outlook ... June 12, 2026Management provided investors with updates on audited financial results, platform growth initiatives, and future business strategy. ... tech3D.aiNextech3D.ai ... an AI-first technology company focused on transforming how businesses create, manage and experience digital content, events and immersive environments. Through its portfolio of event technology, AI-powered solutions and spatial computing products, Nextech helps organizations modernize customer engagement and accelerate digital transformation."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai: 160 new contracts, 92% margins, biggest deal ever due August | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF",www.proactiveinvestors.co.uk (Stephen Gunnion),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.co.uk/companies/news/1096673/nextech3d-ai-160-new-contracts-92-margins-biggest-deal-ever-due-august-1096673.html,"Nextech3D.ai: 160 new contracts, 92% margins, biggest deal ever due August | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF ... # Nextech3D.ai: 160 new contracts, 92% margins, biggest deal ever due August ... Published: 16:05 06 Aug 2026 BST ... Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) Evan Gappelberg tells Proactive's Stephen Gunnion the company has reported $874,000 in new customer contract value and 160 new customer contracts, with software gross margins of 92%. He describes these as proof points of a new phase of growth for the AI-powered event technology business. ... Gappelberg says average contract value is up 77% and that the company is increasingly signing three-year deals rather than one-year deals, providing greater revenue visibility. Enterprise customers including Microsoft, Meta, Google, Deloitte, and BNP Paribas are among those buying from the company's three platforms: Eventdex, MapD, and KraftyLabs. ... On KraftyLabs, Gappelberg says it is the most underappreciated platform Nextech currently owns, and that the company is building it into an AI-first corporate culture platform with an AI avatar layer set to launch in the coming weeks. ... Gappelberg also reveals that Nextech is imminently close to signing what he calls the biggest deal in the company's history, describing it as a multimillion-dollar contract he expects to close in August. He says this deal, combined with 92% gross margins, will significantly accelerate the path to profitability and cash flow. ... ### Nextech3D.AI launches global AI matchmaking and event assistant platforms... ... Nextech3D.AI CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to announce the worldwide rollout of the company’s new AI Matchmaking and AI Event Assistant technologies, ushering in a new era of intelligent networking and real-time event support for conferences, expos, and trade shows... ... NexTech AR Solutions breaks ground with ""Try it on"" AR technology"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai Signs Strategic Partnership with F2B Services to Drive AI Software Adoption, Expand LED Display Opportunities and Accelerate Event Technology Growth",www.accessnewswire.com (NexTech3D.AI Corp),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.accessnewswire.com/newsroom/en/computers-technology-and-internet/nextech3d.ai-signs-strategic-partnership-with-f2b-services-to-dri-1201411,"Nextech3D.ai Signs Strategic Partnership with F2B Services to Drive AI Software Adoption, Expand LED Display Opportunities and Accelerate Event Technology Growth ... # Nextech3D.ai Signs Strategic Partnership with F2B Services to Drive AI Software Adoption, Expand LED Display Opportunities and Accelerate Event Technology Growth ... Partnership Opens New Enterprise Sales Channels While Expanding Nextech's Presence at the Intersection of Physical Infrastructure and AI-Powered Software Solutions ... TORONTO, ON AND NEW YORK, NY / ACCESS Newswire/ August 5, 2026 / Nextech3D.ai (CSE:NTAR)(OTCQB:NEXCF)(FSE:1SS), an AI-first event technology company, signed on August 4th, a strategic partnership with F2B Services, LLC, creating new opportunities to expand revenue through LED display solutions, event technology services, and AI-powered software offerings. The partnership is designed to leverage the strengths of both organizations to capture opportunities across the rapidly growing event, exhibition, corporate communications, and experiential marketing sectors. ... Under the partnership, Nextech3D.ai and F2B will collaborate on opportunities involving LED display systems, LED screen rentals, LED installations, event technology services, and the introduction of Nextech's software solutions to F2B's customer network. The agreement also establishes a framework for identifying and pursuing additional commercial opportunities that may further expand the relationship in the future. ... Management believes this partnership represents more than a new revenue opportunity. It reflects Nextech3D.ai's broader strategy of combining high-value physical infrastructure with AI-powered software to create scalable, recurring revenue streams across multiple industries. As LED displays become increasingly central to events, enterprise communications, retail environments, hospitality venues, and public spaces, Nextech is positioning itself at the convergence of hardware, software, artificial intelligence, and customer engagement. By expanding its distribution channels, strengthening enterprise relationships, and creating new pathways for software adoption, Nextech believes it is building a foundation for long-term growth while increasing its ability to participate in the rapidly expanding global experience economy. ... The partnership also establishes a framework for additional commercial initiatives that may be explored over the next 30 to 60 days as both organizations identify further opportunities for collaboration. Any expansion of the relationship would be documented through future written agreements. ... Nextech3D.ai Unveils Strategic AI Growth Roadmap Focused on Workforce Intelligence and Event Technology Innovation ... July 3, 2026Roadmap outlines multiple AI-driven growth initiatives designed to expand the Company's technology platform and create new revenue opportunities. ... Nextech3D.ai Reports Strong Q4 and Audited Full-Year Results: +207% YoY Revenue Growth, 91% Gross Margins ... June 25, 2026Company reported significant revenue growth, improving margins, and continued progress toward a scalable AI-powered software business model. ... Nextech3D.ai to Host Livestream Shareholder Update on Financial Results and AI Platform Growth Outlook ... June 12, 2026Management provided investors with updates on audited financial results, platform growth initiatives, and future business strategy. ... Nextech3D.ai is an AI-first technology company focused on transforming how businesses create, manage and experience digital content, events and immersive environments. Through its portfolio of event technology, AI-powered solutions and spatial computing products, Nextech helps organizations modernize customer engagement and accelerate digital transformation."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai signs LED display partnership with F2B Services | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF","www.proactiveinvestors.com (Angela Harmantas, Emily Jarvie)",2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1096594/nextech3d-ai-signs-led-display-partnership-with-f2b-services-1096594.html,"Nextech3D.ai signs LED display partnership with F2B Services | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF ... Nextech3D.ai signs LED display partnership with F2B Services ... Published: 09:31 05 Aug 2026 EDT Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) has signed a strategic partnership with F2B Services, LLC aimed at expanding revenue through LED display solutions, event technology services and AI-powered software offerings. ... The deal brings together Nextech's software and AI capabilities with F2B's presence in the event, exhibition, corporate communications and experiential marketing sectors. ... Under the agreement, the two companies will collaborate on LED display systems, LED screen rentals, LED installations and event technology services, while also introducing Nextech's software solutions to F2B's customer network. ... The partnership sets up a framework for identifying further commercial opportunities that could expand the relationship going forward, according to a statement from Nextech. ... Evan Gappelberg, CEO of Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF), said the company continues to execute on its strategy of expanding both its market reach and revenue-generating capabilities, noting that LED displays have become fundamental to how organizations communicate, engage and deliver experiences. ... Thomas Pappalardo, president of F2B Services, said the company has built its reputation as a trusted partner for major clients including Hewlett-Packard Enterprises, Boston Scientific, Astrolab, FujiFilm and CrowdStrike. He said the partnership with Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF) fits with F2B's approach of combining reliable delivery with innovative software solutions to offer a more complete experience for its clients and events. ... The companies said additional commercial initiatives may be explored over the next 30 to 60 days as they identify further opportunities for collaboration, with any expansion of the relationship to be documented through future written agreements."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"360training Acquires Multiple Brands, Expanding Its Compliance Training Portfolio Across Healthcare, EHS, Food Safety, and Transportation","www.prnewswire.com (360training.com, Inc.)",2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/360training-acquires-multiple-brands-expanding-its-compliance-training-portfolio-across-healthcare-ehs-food-safety-and-transportation-302844271.html,"360training Acquires Multiple Brands, Expanding Its Compliance Training Portfolio Across Healthcare, EHS, Food Safety, and Transportation Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... AUSTIN, Texas, Aug. 5, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- 360training.com, Inc., recognized by Newsweek's America's Top Online Learning Providers list, today announced the acquisition of select assets from the San Antonio-based operators of seven specialized compliance training brands. The acquired portfolio spans mandatory training and certificate programs across healthcare, OSHA and workplace safety, food handling, forklift operations, hazardous materials, defensive driving, and transportation safety. This acquisition meaningfully broadens 360training's multi-industry compliance footprint, adding established brands and a diverse learner base to its growing family of training providers supporting the United States and Canada. ... ""The depth and diversity of this portfolio is what makes this acquisition so strategically compelling,"" said Tom Anderson, CEO of 360training. ""From healthcare training to HAZWOPER compliance to food handler training, the experts behind these brands have built trusted, regulation-aligned brands that serve learners across the full spectrum of the workforce. Adding these platforms to our ecosystem strengthens our ability to serve both individual professionals and enterprise employers who need comprehensive, multi-disciplinary compliance solutions in one place."" ... Expanding Across Regulated Industries with Complementary DepthWith over 4,000 courses already in its catalog, 360training adds 57 unique courses through this acquisition, deepening its breadth across compliance training verticals. ... - National Health Training addresses expanded healthcare training needs across international markets, complementing 360training's growing global compliance strategy. ... Enhancing the Customer ExperienceWith the addition of these seven brands, employers and individual learners gain access to a broader range of accredited training programs, all supported by 360training's scalable learning platform, centralized compliance reporting tools, and enterprise-grade administrative infrastructure. ... whether they're a solo food handler ... director managing thousands of employees ... deserve a training experience that is simple, credible, and built around their ... requirements,"" said Ryan Linders, CMO of ... . ""These brands have already earned the trust of learners in highly ... 36 ... platform, we're delivering enhanced digital experiences, improved learner tracking, and a broader catalog of ... solutions that serve learners wherever their ... take them."" ... About 360trainingEstablished in 1997, 360training.com, Inc. is a trusted leader specializing in comprehensive online training solutions for individuals and businesses across various industries, including food and beverage, environmental health and safety, real estate, healthcare, financial services, and power and utilities. Having issued over 21 million training certificates to 12.5+ million learners across 17+ brands, 360training embraces innovative technology and a commitment to quality education to offer accredited courses, fostering safe and healthy communities. As part of this commitment, the company continues to seek acquisition opportunities that build synergies and enhance value for its customers. ... 360training's family of brands include Learn2Serve, OSHAcampus, AgentCampus, OSHA.com, VanEd, AdvanceOnline, ACLS Medical Training, American Resuscitation Council, Canadian Food Safety/ SafeCheck®, Compliance Training Online, Hard Hat Training, HIPAA Exams, Mortgage Educators and Compliance (MEC), My Mortgage Trainer, Ready Training Online (RTO®), TABC On The Fly, BASSET On The Fly, Certified On The Fly, TIPS, and UST Training. 360training is a portfolio company of GreyLion and Vestar Capital Partners. ... About American Health Training, National OSHA Foundation, and the Acquired BrandsBased in San Antonio, Texas, the portfolio includes industry-recognized brands such as American Health Training, National OSHA Foundation, and National Food Handlers Foundation, along with four additional specialized compliance training brands serving learners and employers across the United States. Together, the brands deliver regulatory-aligned certification programs in healthcare, workplace safety, food handling, hazardous materials, forklift operations, defensive driving, and international health training. ... ### 360training Acquires Canadian Food Safety Group, Including Brands SafeCheck® Learning and SafeCheck Safety®, Expanding Canadian Food Safety Leadership ... 360training.com, Inc., a global leader in regulated online training and workforce compliance solutions, today announced the acquisition of select... ... ### 360training Acquires UST Training to Expand Regulated Training Solutions, Accelerate Growth for Tank Safety Markets ... 360training.com, Inc., a global provider of compliance and professional education, announced today the acquisition of UST Training. Founded in 2003,..."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nexus Select bets on premium brands as consumption stays resilient - The HinduBusinessLine,www.thehindubusinessline.com (Aishwarya Kumar),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/nexus-select-bets-on-premium-brands-as-consumption-stays-resilient/article71305952.ece,"# Nexus Select bets on premium brands as consumption stays resilient ... ## This comes after the trust posted a strong quarter, with consumption growing 17%, footfalls rising 5%, net operating income (NOI) increasing 11% and occupancy reaching 96% ... Blackstone-backed Nexus Select Trust is doubling down on premiumisation across malls with plans to replace underperforming large-format retailers with high-value brands, even as it pursues acquisitions to expand its portfolio. ... This comes after the trust posted a strong quarter, with consumption growing 17 per cent, footfalls rising 5 per cent, net operating income (NOI) increasing 11 per cent and occupancy reaching 96 per cent. Distribution per unit also rose 10 per cent. “We’re seeing premiumisation play out over the next two to three years,” Pratik Dantara, Chief Investor Relations Officer and Head of Strategy, told businessline. “We’ll be doubling down on categories such as watches, beauty, jewellery, eyewear and accessories, which offer higher trading densities and stronger long-term economics. ... Hypermarkets, which contributed around 7 per cent of portfolio sales two to three years ago, now account for about 4 per cent and recorded just 1 per cent growth during the quarter. Nexus plans to continue optimising these large spaces in favour of faster-growing premium categories. ... ## acquisition trail ... The REIT also remains on the acquisition trail. Dantara said the previously announced Diamond Plaza acquisition is expected to close over the next month, while two more transactions currently under due diligence are likely to be announced within the next 60 days. The company expects another potential acquisition later in the financial year as it continues to evaluate a healthy pipeline of assets. ... Despite concerns over macroeconomic conditions, the company said it has not seen any meaningful slowdown in discretionary spending among its target consumers. July consumption has continued to register double-digit growth, albeit lower than the 17 per cent recorded in the June quarter, providing confidence ahead of the festive season. ... Looking ahead, Nexus expects premiumisation to vary across markets. While metro malls will see a greater concentration of premium and luxury brands, value-led centres in tier-II and tier-III cities will continue to cater to aspirational consumers, with the premium mix increasing gradually over time."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Tandem PV acquires nexTC Corp. for perovskite solar tech - Portland Business Journal,www.bizjournals.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bizjournals.com/portland/news/2026/08/04/tandem-pv-next-tc-acquisition.html,Tandem PV acquires nexTC Corp. for perovskite solar tech - Portland Business Journal ... The acquisition brings intellectual property and expertise in transparent oxide coatings to Tandem PV. Financial terms were not disclosed. ... ##### Tandem PV names Saritha Peruri its Vice President of Commercialization ... Tandem PV names Saritha Peruri its Vice President of Commercialization ... ##### Solar panel startup raises funds to start pilot production ... ##### Solar tracker firm buys inverter business ... Solar tracker firm buys inverter business
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nexus Select Trust Q1 NOI rises 11% on strong retail demand - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Kailash Babar),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/services/property-/-cstruction/nexus-select-trust-q1-noi-rises-11-on-strong-retail-demand/articleshow/132834149.cms,"Nexus Select Trust Q1 NOI rises 11% on strong retail demand - The Economic Times ... Nexus Select Trust reported an eleven percent increase in net operating income. Retail consumption rose seventeen percent, supporting strong leasing activity across its portfolio. The trust declared a distribution of Rs 370 crore, a ten percent rise. It also plans portfolio expansion with new acquisitions and existing asset renewals. Nexus Select Trust aims to double its portfolio by the year 2030. ... Mumbai: Nexus Select Trust, India’s maiden listed retail real estate investment trust(REIT), has reported an 11% year-on-year increase in net operating income(NOI) to Rs 510 crore for the quarter ended June, supported by strong retail consumption and leasing activity across its portfolio.The REIT recorded retail consumption of Rs 3,850 crore during the quarter, up 17% from a year ago, with growth seen across categories. It has declared a distribution of Rs 370 crore, or Rs 2.442 per unit, marking a 10% increase in distribution per unit (DPU) from a year ago and a 7% sequential rise.Also Read: Nexus Trust may buy Galaxy's Guwahati project for ₹1,300 crore ... The trust also reported double-digit re-leasing spreads on 0.4 million sq ft of space re-leased during the quarter, while maintaining a balance sheet with an average debt cost of 7.2%, 30 basis points lower than a year earlier, and a loan-to-value ratio of 18%.During the quarter, Nexus renewed and re-leased 0.2 million sq ft of space ahead of lease expiries at spreads exceeding 20%, while adding brands such as Lego, Kurt Geiger and Harajuku Bakehouse to its portfolio. ... “We have delivered robust double-digit consumption growth during the quarter despite heightened global uncertainties. This performance reflects the resilience of our portfolio and the strength of our operational execution in a challenging environment,” said Dalip Sehgal, ED & CEO, Nexus Select Trust. ... According to him, the REIT remains focused on expanding its portfolio and has announced the acquisition of Diamond Plaza mall in Kolkata, with the transaction expected to close in the first half of 2026-27.It has also built an acquisition pipeline comprising eight retail assets across India, with two currently under due diligence. Backed by low leverage and nearly $1 billion of available debt headroom, the REIT plans to pursue inorganic growth opportunities as it works towards doubling its portfolio by 2030, he added.Nexus Select Trust’s portfolio comprises 19 Grade-A consumption centres with a gross leasable area of 10.7 million sq ft across 15 cities, along with three hotel assets and three office assets. The retail portfolio houses around 1,100 domestic and international brands across more than 3,200 stores."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai CEO discusses ARway acquisition strategy - ICYMI | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF",www.proactiveinvestors.com (Emily Jarvie),2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1096389/nextech3d-ai-ceo-discusses-arway-acquisition-strategy-icymi-1096389.html,"ai CEO discusses ARway acquisition strategy - ... :NTAR ... NEXCF ... # Nextech3D.ai CEO discusses ARway acquisition strategy - ICYMI ... Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) earlier this week announced progress toward acquiring the remaining ownership interest in ARway, a move that Chief Executive Officer Evan Gappelberg said would simplify the company's structure while strengthening its software-focused growth strategy. ... Speaking with Proactive, Gappelberg said the transaction should not be viewed as a conventional acquisition because Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF) already owns approximately 40% of ARway and has spent several years integrating its technology, customer relationships and product strategy. ... He said completing the acquisition would allow the businesses to operate under a single platform, engineering team and go-to-market strategy while eliminating operational duplication. ... We are moving forward with the acquisition of the remaining ownership of ARway. This isn't a traditional acquisition because we already own about 40% of ARway. We've spent years integrating the technologies, customers and product strategy. What changes now is the ownership structure. We move from operating two companies to one company, one platform, one engineering team and one go-to-market strategy. ... The transaction brings about $1.5 million in annual ARway revenue and approximately $1.5 million in profit. It's a very profitable business, so it's immediately accretive from a revenue perspective. It also moves us further toward a software-driven revenue business while simplifying things for shareholders. We've heard questions about ARway, Nextech and even Toggle, so simplifying the corporate structure, eliminating duplication, streamlining operations and creating a more scalable organization is important. ... It is. Our goal is to become the operating system for live events. Every acquisition supports that vision. ARway has been showing strong growth with gross margins above 90%, so we don't believe it should continue as a standalone company. ... Across Nextech, sales momentum is accelerating. ARway is part of that. We're seeing larger enterprise deals and multi-year contracts. Where we previously signed one-year agreements almost exclusively for Map D, nearly every new agreement is now for two, three or four years. That gives shareholders greater confidence because the business becomes less dependent on annual renewals. ... From where I'm sitting, I see enormous growth, especially through the AI capabilities we're building. We've communicated this strategy to shareholders across Map D, ARway, Eventdex and CraftyLabs Intelligence. AI is becoming a major growth driver, and customers are responding very positively as these platforms become increasingly AI-enabled. ... That's the plan. Of course, there are lawyers, auditors and all the regulatory requirements that public companies must work through. ... To close, this acquisition is about much more than adding $1.5 million in annual revenue. It's about creating a simpler company, a stronger platform, a more efficient organization and a significantly larger growth opportunity, combined with accelerating sales momentum across the business. I believe Nextech is entering the most exciting growth phase in the company's history, and ARway is an important part of that story. ... ### Nextech3D.ai provides update in acquisition of remaining ARway shares,... ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to provide an update on the company's proposed acquisition of all outstanding shares of ARway Corporation that it does not already own, following the recent signing of a definitive agreement between the two companies.On a... ... 1 week, 1 ... Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce... ... 2 weeks, 6 days ago ... Nextech3D.ai Livestream event highlights Q4 revenue surge and... ... on 06/25/2026 Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI... ... on 06/25/2026 ... Nextech3D.ai appoints industry veteran Jesse Carrillo as VP of Sales ... on 05/28/2026"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nextech3D.ai CEO discusses ARway acquisition strategy - ICYMI,"finance.yahoo.com (Proactive Sat, August 1, 2026 at 11:00 AM EDT 3 min read)",2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/nextech3d-ai-ceo-discusses-arway-150000075.html,"discusses ARway ... Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) earlier this week announced progress toward acquiring the remaining ownership interest in ARway, a move that Chief Executive Officer Evan Gappelberg said would simplify the company's structure while strengthening its software-focused growth strategy. ... Speaking with Proactive, Gappelberg said the transaction should not be viewed as a conventional acquisition because Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF) already owns approximately 40% of ARway and has spent several years integrating its technology, customer relationships and product strategy. He said completing the acquisition would allow the businesses to operate under a single platform, engineering team and go-to-market strategy while eliminating operational duplication. ... We are moving forward with the acquisition of the remaining ownership of ARway. This isn't a traditional acquisition because we already own about 40% of ARway. We've spent years integrating the technologies, customers and product strategy. What changes now is the ownership structure. We move from operating two companies to one company, one platform, one engineering team and one go-to-market strategy. ... The transaction brings about $1.5 million in annual ARway revenue and approximately $1.5 million in profit. It's a very profitable business, so it's immediately accretive from a revenue perspective. It also moves us further toward a software-driven revenue business while simplifying things for shareholders. We've heard questions about ARway, Nextech and even Toggle, so simplifying the corporate structure, eliminating duplication, streamlining operations and creating a more scalable organization is important. ... It is. Our goal is to become the operating system for live events. Every acquisition supports that vision. ARway has been showing strong growth with gross margins above 90%, so we don't believe it should continue as a standalone company. ... Across Nextech, sales momentum is accelerating. ARway is part of that. We're seeing larger enterprise deals and multi-year contracts. Where we previously signed one-year agreements almost exclusively for Map D, nearly every new agreement is now for two, three or four years. That gives shareholders greater confidence because the business becomes less dependent on annual renewals. ... From where I'm sitting, I see enormous growth, especially through the AI capabilities we're building. We've communicated this strategy to shareholders across Map D, ARway, Eventdex and CraftyLabs Intelligence. AI is becoming a major growth driver, and customers are responding very positively as these platforms become increasingly AI-enabled. You're hoping to complete the transaction by October? That's the plan. Of course, there are lawyers, auditors and all the regulatory requirements that public companies must work through. To close, this acquisition is about much more than adding $1.5 million in annual revenue. It's about creating a simpler company, a stronger platform, a more efficient organization and a significantly larger growth opportunity, combined with accelerating sales momentum across the business. I believe Nextech is entering the most exciting growth phase in the company's history, and ARway is an important part of that story. Great to see you again. Thanks for joining us."
