eamlining operations and creating a more scalable organization is important. ... It is. Our goal is to become the operating system for live events. Every acquisition supports that vision. ARway has been showing strong growth with gross margins above 90%, so we don't believe it should continue as a standalone company. ... Across Nextech, sales momentum is accelerating. ARway is part of that. We're seeing larger enterprise deals and multi-year contracts. Where we previously signed one-year agreements almost exclusively for Map D, nearly every new agreement is now for two, three or four years. That gives shareholders greater confidence because the business becomes less dependent on annual renewals. ... From where I'm sitting, I see enormous growth, especially through the AI capabilities we're building. We've communicated this strategy to shareholders across Map D, ARway, Eventdex and CraftyLabs Intelligence. AI is becoming a major growth driver, and customers are responding very positively as these platforms become increasingly AI-enabled. You're hoping to complete the transaction by October? That's the plan. Of course, there are lawyers, auditors and all the regulatory requirements that public companies must work through. To close, this acquisition is about much more than adding $1.5 million in annual revenue. It's about creating a simpler company, a stronger platform, a more efficient organization and a significantly larger growth opportunity, combined with accelerating sales momentum across the business. I believe Nextech is entering the most exciting growth phase in the company's history, and ARway is an important part of that story. Great to see you again. Thanks for joining us."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,AI for bosses first: 360 launches 'Nano Work' enterprise agent platform - Chinadaily.com.cn,global.chinadaily.com.cn (闫星周),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://global.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202607/30/WS6a6b0de4a310986e2b4682eb.html,"AI for bosses first: 360 launches 'Nano Work' enterprise agent platform - Chinadaily.com.cn ... # AI for bosses first: 360 launches 'Nano Work' enterprise agent platform ... By Ma Si | chinadaily.com.cn | Updated: 2026-07-30 16:39 Zhou Hongyi, founder and chairman of 360 Security Group, officially unveils the company's next-generation enterprise intelligent agent work platform, ""Nano Work"". [Photo provided to chinadaily.com.cn] Zhou Hongyi, founder and chairman of 360 Security Group, has officially unveiled the company's next-generation enterprise intelligent agent work platform, ""Nano Work"", positioning it as a productivity engine for the AI-driven organization. ... ""When enterprises embrace AI, the boss must be the first to use it,"" Zhou said at the launch event in Beijing. Nano Work is tailored for business owners, startups, sole proprietorships, and rank-and-file employees alike, aiming to create a ""super organization"" where human and machine intelligence coalesce. ... To catalyze adoption, Zhou announced a trial giveaway of 100 million tokens per early user, coupled with dedicated training and hands-on accompaniment services, with the goal of helping 1,000 small businesses achieve tangible AI deployment and operational efficiency gains in the first wave. ... Notably, Zhou revealed that 360 subjected itself to a five-month internal stress test before releasing the product. The team deployed various agents – including the OpenClaw framework – across more than 1,000 real business scenarios, collected over 56,000 pieces of user feedback, and rolled out 166 iterative updates. ... To tackle these challenges, Nano Work integrates a five-pillar architecture – a multi-agent engine, a multi-model foundation, a cloud-based office, multiple work modes, and a roster of specialized ""expert"" agents. Users simply state their objectives; the platform orchestrates the right combination of AI experts, models, and execution pathways without requiring any manual tuning. ... For business owners, Nano Work assists in operational analysis, growth tracking, and progress management. For solo entrepreneurs, it accelerates opportunity discovery, product validation, content creation, and marketing. For employees, it boosts research, planning, production, and delivery – effectively turning every user into an AI-empowered professional."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Onco360® Has Been Selected as a National Pharmacy Partner,www.globenewswire.com (Onco360 Oncology Pharmacy),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/29/3335617/0/en/Onco360-Has-Been-Selected-as-a-National-Pharmacy-Partner-for-VEPPANU-vepdegestrant.html,"Onco360® Has Been Selected as a National Pharmacy Partner ... # Onco360® Has Been Selected as a National Pharmacy Partner for VEPPANU™ (vepdegestrant) ... LOUISVILLE, Ky., July 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Onco360®, the nation’s leading independent Specialty Pharmacy, has been selected as a pharmacy partner by Rigel Pharmaceuticals for VEPPANU™ (vepdegestrant), which is indicated for the treatment of adults with estrogen receptor (ER)-positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-negative, estrogen receptor-1 (ESR1)-mutated advanced or metastatic breast cancer, as detected by an FDA-authorized test, with disease progression following at least one line of endocrine therapy.1 ... “We are thrilled to continue our partnership with Rigel Pharmaceuticals to expand treatment options for patients living with breast cancer,” said Benito Fernandez, Chief Commercial Officer. “Our partnerships allow us to accelerate patient access to new therapies while delivering personalized clinical support and compassionate care throughout every stage of the patient journey.” ... About Onco360 Oncology PharmacyOnco360 is the nation’s largest independent Oncology Pharmacy and clinical support services company. Onco360 was founded in 2003 to bring together the stakeholders involved in the cancer treatment process and serve the specialized needs of oncologists, patients, hospitals, cancer centers of excellence, manufacturers, health plans, and payers. It dispenses nationally through its network of URAC-, and ACHC-accredited Oncology Pharmacies. Onco360 is headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky, and is a flagship specialty pharmacy brand of PharMerica Corporation, a leading institutional pharmacy, specialty infusion, and hospital services company servicing healthcare facilities in the United States. For more information about Onco360, please visit Onco360.com. ... June 04, 2026 07:30 ET | Source: Onco360 Oncology Pharmacy Onco360® Has Been Selected as a National Specialty Pharmacy Provider for JYLAMVO® (methotrexate) Oral Solution ... LOUISVILLE, Ky, June 04, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Onco360®, the nation’s leading independent Specialty Pharmacy, has been selected as a pharmacy partner by Shorla Oncology for... ... June 02, 2026 16:30 ET | Source: Onco360 Oncology Pharmacy ... Onco360® Has Been Selected as a National Specialty Pharmacy Provider for IMKELDI® (imatinib) Oral Solution LOUISVILLE, KY, June 02, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Onco360®, the nation’s leading independent Specialty Pharmacy, has been selected as a pharmacy partner by Shorla Oncology for IMKELDI® (imatinib)..."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai provides update in acquisition of remaining ARway shares, strengthening AI platform | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF",www.proactiveinvestors.com (Steve Darling),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1096087/nextech3dai-provides-update-in-acquisition-of-remaining-arway-shares-strengthening-ai-platform.html,"Nextech3D.ai provides update in acquisition of remaining ARway shares, strengthening AI platform | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF ... # Nextech3D.ai provides update in acquisition of remaining ARway shares, strengthening AI platform ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to provide an update on the company's proposed acquisition of all outstanding shares of ARway Corporation that it does not already own, following the recent signing of a definitive agreement between the two companies. ... On a standalone basis, ARway generated approximately $1.58 million in revenue and $1.52 million in gross profit for the fiscal year ended March 31, 2026, highlighting the strength of its augmented reality navigation business. ... Nextech currently owns approximately 40% of ARway's outstanding shares, while management and insiders hold an additional 20%. Upon completion of the transaction, expected in October 2026, ARway will become a wholly owned subsidiary, bringing its technology, intellectual property, and event technology assets fully under the Nextech umbrella. ... Gappelberg said combining ARway with Map Dynamics will create a more unified AI-powered platform for the global events industry. Management expects the integration to accelerate product innovation, eliminate duplicate overhead, improve operational efficiency, and expand recurring SaaS revenue opportunities. ... The company believes consolidating its event technology portfolio will further strengthen Nextech's position as an AI-first technology company focused on event technology, augmented reality, spatial computing, and digital engagement while creating long-term value through a more streamlined business. ... ### Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce intelligence platform ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to discuss the launch of the enterprise pilot program for KraftyLab Intelligence™, an AI-powered workforce intelligence and employee engagement platform designed to help organizations better understand and support their... ... Nextech3D.ai Livestream event highlights Q4 revenue surge and... ... on 06/25/2026 Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI... ... on 06/25/2026 Nextech3D.ai appoints industry veteran Jesse Carrillo as VP of Sales ... on 05/28/2026 ... Nextech3D.ai launches Krafty Labs AI event marketplace ... on 05/12/2026"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Beyond Traditional Project Management: Why Heavy Civil Contractors Choose Nektar.io’s Field-first Data Collection Over Procore | PressReleaseCC,www.pressreleasecc.com (PressReleaseCC),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.pressreleasecc.com/2026/07/23/beyond-traditional-project-management-why-heavy-civil-contractors-choose-nektar-ios-field-first-data-collection-over-procore/,"Nektar announces its field-first data collection platform is gaining traction among heavy civil contractors seeking alternatives to traditional project management software like Procore. ... Edmonton, Canada, July 23, 2026 — EDMONTON, AB — July 22, 2025 — Nektar.io, a field data collection platform built specifically for heavy civil construction, has published an industry report outlining why a growing number of heavy civil contractors are supplementing or replacing traditional project management software with field-first data collection systems designed around how civil construction work actually gets done. The report, available now at Nektar.io, addresses the structural limitations of office-centric platforms like Procore when applied to heavy civil, earthworks, pipeline, and infrastructure projects — and explains why the data collection model matters as much as the feature set. ... Was built to solve this problem at the source — capturing production data, equipment utilization, and field observations at the point of work, in formats that field personnel can complete without administrative support, and in conditions where connectivity cannot be guaranteed. ... Connectivity is a baseline assumption in most commercial construction environments — job site trailers have internet access, and most field personnel work within cellular range. Heavy civil projects routinely operate in locations where neither is true. The report documents how N ... -first architecture ensures that data captured in the field is stored locally and synced when the device reconnects, without requiring field personnel to hold incomplete records until they return to a connected environment. Pro ... ’s mobile functionality degrades significantly without connectivity, making it poorly suited as a primary field data tool on remote civil projects. ... Daily reporting in heavy civil construction requires a different structure than the daily logs used in commercial building. A civil daily production report captures equipment hours by machine, operator assignments, production quantities by activity code, material haul volumes, weather and site conditions, and subcontractor activity — all tied to ... cost codes for real-time job cost tracking. Nektar.io’s daily reporting module was built specifically for ... ’s daily log tool captures the same categories in broad strokes but lacks the production quantity and equipment utilization depth that civil ... to track job cost performance ... The report addresses how data flows from field capture into cost control and project performance reporting. Nektar.io integrates production data directly with civil-specific cost code structures, allowing project managers to compare actual unit costs against bid rates in real time. This integration gives contractors visibility into whether a production activity is trending profitable or over-budget before the overrun becomes unrecoverable. General-purpose platforms can approximate this functionality but require significant configuration and manual data mapping that most civil project teams do not have the administrative capacity to maintain. ... The report is directed at heavy civil contractors who are currently using a general-purpose project management platform as their primary field data tool and are experiencing the gap between what the software tracks and what their operations actually require. This includes earthworks and grading contractors, pipeline and utility installers, road and highway contractors, site development companies, and civil general contractors managing large-scale infrastructure projects. ... also relevant to ... technology decision-makers evaluating platforms for ... first time — ... those coming from commercial or institutional construction backgrounds who are being ... select or recommend software for a heavy ... The full industry report is available at no cost through Nektar.io. Contractors who want to see how Nektar.io’s field data collection works within their specific project type can request a demo or speak with a Nektar.io implementation specialist directly through the website. ... Nektar.io is a field data collection and production reporting platform purpose-built for heavy civil construction. The platform captures daily production quantities, equipment utilization, operator hours, and field conditions at the point of work, with offline functionality designed for remote project environments. Nektar.io serves earthworks, grading, pipeline, road construction, and infrastructure contractors across North America, giving project teams real-time visibility into production performance and job cost tracking without requiring office-based administrative support to close the data loop."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Beyond traditional project management: Why heavy civil contractors choose Nektar.io's field-first data collection over Procore | Herald-Whig,"whig.marketminute.com (Edmonton, Canada, July 23, 2026)",2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://whig.marketminute.com/article/marketersmedia-2026-7-23-beyond-traditional-project-management-why-heavy-civil-contractors-choose-nektarios-field-first-data-collection-over-procore,"Nektar announces its field-first data collection platform is gaining traction among heavy civil contractors seeking alternatives to traditional project management software like Procore. ... -- EDMONTON, AB — July 22, 2025 — Nektar.io, a field data collection platform built specifically for heavy civil construction, has published an industry report outlining why a growing number of heavy civil contractors are supplementing or replacing traditional project management software with field-first data collection systems designed around how civil construction work actually gets done. The report, available now at Nektar.io, addresses the structural limitations of office-centric platforms like Procore when applied to heavy civil, earthworks, pipeline, and infrastructure projects — and explains why the data collection model matters as much as the feature set. ... Heavy civil work does not conform to ... assumptions. A grading crew finishing a ... 0-mile road corridor, a pipeline contractor working across multiple spread locations, or ... earthworks team managing a cut-and- ... operation on a remote mine site cannot reliably route daily production data through a software system designed for ... -based project administrators. The ... is a data lag that distorts cost tracking ... Connectivity is a baseline assumption in most commercial construction environments — job site trailers have internet access, and most field personnel work within cellular range. Heavy civil projects routinely operate in locations where neither is true. The report ... offline-first architecture ensures that data captured in the field is stored locally and synced when the ... reconnects, without requiring field personnel to hold incomplete records until they return to a connected environment. Pro ... 's mobile functionality degrades significantly without connectivity, making it ... suited as a primary field data tool on remote ... Daily reporting in heavy civil construction requires a different structure than the daily logs used in commercial building. A civil ... production report captures equipment hours by machine, operator assignments, production quantities by activity code, material haul volumes, weather and site ... subcontractor activity — ... broad strokes but ... equipment utilization depth ... The report addresses how data flows from field capture into cost control and project performance reporting. Nektar.io integrates production data directly with civil-specific cost code structures, allowing project managers to compare actual unit costs against bid rates in real time. This integration gives contractors visibility into whether a production activity is trending profitable or over-budget before the overrun becomes unrecoverable. General-purpose platforms can approximate this functionality but require significant configuration and manual data mapping that most civil project teams do not have the administrative capacity to maintain. ... The report is directed at heavy civil contractors who are currently using a general-purpose project management platform as their primary field data tool and are experiencing the gap between what the software tracks and what their operations actually require. This includes earthworks and grading contractors, pipeline and utility installers, road and highway contractors, site development companies, and civil general contractors managing large-scale infrastructure projects. ... The full industry report is available at no cost through Nektar.io. Contractors who want to see how Nektar.io's field data collection works within their specific project type can request a demo or speak with a Nektar.io implementation specialist directly through the website. ... Nektar.io is a field data collection and production reporting platform purpose-built for heavy civil construction. The platform captures daily production quantities, equipment utilization, operator hours, and field conditions at the point of work, with offline functionality designed for remote project environments. Nektar.io serves earthworks, grading, pipeline, road construction, and infrastructure contractors across North America, giving project teams real-time visibility into production performance and job cost tracking without requiring office-based administrative support to close the data loop."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Innovaccer’s CEO walked away from Disney and NASA. Now, the startup has crossed $200 million in ARR | Fortune",fortune.com (Lily Mae Lazarus),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fortune.com/2026/07/23/innovaccers-ceo-walked-away-from-disney-and-nasa-to-fix-healthcares-data-mess-now-the-startup-has-crossed-200-million-in-arr/,"Innovaccer’s CEO walked away from Disney and NASA. Now, the startup has crossed $200 million in ARR | Fortune ... # Innovaccer’s CEO walked away from Disney and NASA to fix healthcare’s data mess. Now the startup has crossed $200 million in ARR ... July 23, 2026, 6:00 PM ET ... Innovaccer has raised $675 million total, including a $275 million round last year.Courtesy of Innovaccer ... Innovacer CEO Abhinav Shashank was 26 when he walked away from paying customers like Disney and NASA to bet his general data analytics company on healthcare instead. Then he and his cofounders moved into Mercy Medical Center in Des Moines, Iowa, for four months. They lived inside the hospital’s IT department, seeing firsthand why doctors still start every visit by asking a patient’s name and date of birth. Word spread to hospitals in Nebraska, Texas, and California before Innovaccer had much of a sales team at all."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Hybrid-Ceramic Dental CAD/CAM Market to Reach USD 344.8M by 2032 at 7.92% CAGR | Media Info Today,mediainfotoday.com (PRNEWS),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mediainfotoday.com/biz/hybrid-ceramic-dental-cad-cam-market-to-reach-usd-344-8m-by-2032-at-7-92-cagr/,"2% CAGR ... As hybrid-ceramic CAD/CAM materials move from niche clinical curiosity to mainstream restorative option, 2026 represents a pivotal inflection point for manufacturers, distributors, dental chains, and investors. This preview distills the strategic implications of PW Consulting’s full market study — integrating rigorous market-sizing, regulatory mapping, competitive benchmarking, and executable go-to-market playbooks — and explains why the intelligence contained in the full report is indispensable for high-stakes decisions over the next 12–36 months. Hybrid-Ceramic Dental CAD/CAM Material Market ... Hybrid-ceramic CAD/CAM materials have demonstrated steady expansion since 2020 and are projected to continue growing at a compound annual growth rate of approximately 7.92% across the forecast window. The market has expanded from the low hundreds of millions (USD) in 2020 to a materially higher base in 2025, and PW Consulting’s modeling indicates sustained momentum into the early 2030s. That growth is being driven by a confluence of factors: improved material properties enabling broader indications, faster chairside workflows, favorable reimbursement coding shifts, and a growing installed base of digital impressioning and milling systems. Hybrid-Ceramic Dental CAD/CAM Material Market ... - Timing of investments: With measurable market acceleration underway, manufacturers must decide whether to front-load R&D and scale-up capacity in 2026 to capture share at a lower marginal cost, or to pursue a more conservative, margin-first strategy. The report quantifies payoff scenarios for both approaches and models breakeven thresholds under multiple demand and pricing assumptions. ... - Regulatory pathway optimization: Regulatory dynamics in 2026 are a gating factor. FDA and Health Canada continue to enforce stringent approvals for hybrid-ceramic CAD/CAM materials; adherence to ISO testing standards (notably those governing flexural strength and restorative-specific certification) is non-negotiable. The study maps regulatory timelines by product profile and highlights fast-tracks and pitfalls relevant to different jurisdictions. ... shifts have materially improved the ... - Channel and partnership decisions: Distribution and CAD/CAM platform compatibility are core determinants of adoption. The study evaluates distribution models, from direct OEM relationships to strategic partnerships with dental distributors and digital-platform incumbents, and quantifies relative time-to-adoption and revenue upside for each model. ... - Executive synthesis with prioritized strategic actions and an investment heat map tailored for executives evaluating R&D, manufacturing, distribution, or M&A moves in 2026. ... - Historical market sizing (2020–2025) and a detailed forecast (2026–2032) under three adoption scenarios; sensitivity tests against price, clinical acceptance, and regulatory delays. ... - Regulatory and standards playbook: stepwise checklists to secure market access in major jurisdictions and recommended clinical dossiers aligned to ISO expectations and payer documentation needs. ... - M&A and partnership screening tool with prioritized target profiles and valuation heuristics informed by market concentration dynamics and technology differentiation. ... The market is characterized by a mix of specialty material houses and multinational dental manufacturers. A handful of established players lead with clinically validated hybrid-ceramic block lines designed specifically for CAD/CAM milling, while others are pursuing distribution expansion and portfolio integration to capture chairside workflows. ... - Product portfolio plays: Several incumbents are expanding hybrid-ceramic options to improve workflow integration with leading CAD/CAM systems; expect incremental product introductions focused on polishing response, milling efficiency, and shade systems that match existing restorative lines. ... - Distribution consolidation: Recent distribution agreements and channel expansions have intensified access in key markets. Strategic alliances with major dental distributors or CAD/CAM platform providers can materially shorten path-to-adoption. ... - Clinical evidence and platform certification: Clinical outcomes and system compatibility (chairside milling integration, ... ) are now the ... platform integrations will have out ... Notable recent developments include strategic distribution enhancements and catalog expansions among leading suppliers, underscoring the competitive emphasis on reach and workflow alignment. Those moves are signals to market participants: access and interoperability can be as valuable as incremental material performance gains. ... Regulatory oversight and standards compliance are central to market access. ISO testing regimes for flexural strength and restorative materials establish minimum thresholds manufacturers must meet; failure to align with these standards creates market risk and restricts reimbursement eligibility. Meanwhile, recent payer and coding reforms have broadened the pathway for reimbursement of hybrid-resin restorative categories — a development that materially improves the clinician and patient economic case. The report provides a jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction matrix showing approval timelines, required test batteries, and evidence expectations for payers. ... - Secure platform certifications and distribution deals early: Align product launches with major CAD/CAM system providers and regional distributors to minimize friction for chairside adoption. ... - Scan M&A selectively: Target assets that add clinical evidence, platform compatibility, or distribution in high-growth corridors — the market’s low top-end concentration creates multiple opportunistic entry points. ... - Monitor standards evolution: Anticipate tightening of testing standards and prepare upgrade paths for product portfolios to avoid relabeling or market withdrawal costs. ... Our full study translates market momentum and regulatory shifts into runnable plays: investment sizing for production scale-up, prioritized clinical and regulatory investments, channel strategies tailored to platform ecosystems, and scenario-based valuation models for M&A and capex decisions. For executives making 2026 budget and strategic choices, the difference between a proactive play and a reactive scramble will often be access to the granular segmentation and sensitivity analysis we intentionally omit from this preview. ... This preview outlines the strategic contours every executive should consider as hybrid-ceramic CAD/CAM materials move from promising to mainstream. For access to the full datasets, segmented forecasts, company-level benchmarking, and the interactive financial model that underpins our recommendations, please consult the PW Consulting report page. The full intelligence package contains the granular regional and application splits, price matrices, and downloadable scenario tools necessary to operationalize a winning 2026 strategy. ... PW Consulting’s hybrid-ceramic CAD/CAM market study is structured to convert market insight into operational action — enabling you to prioritize investments, secure regulatory pathways, design channel strategies, and evaluate M&A opportunities with confidence as the market scales through the remainder of the decade."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Unilever and Coke big up Nectar retail media platform - Britain | EUROPESAYS.COM,www.europesays.com,2026-07-18T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-18 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.europesays.com/britain/85433/,"Unilever and Coke big up Nectar retail media platform - Britain | EUROPESAYS.COM ... big up Nectar retail media platform ... Unilever and Coca-Cola are hailing the launch of the Nectar360 Pollen unified retail media platform, reporting faster activation, improved measurement and more effective cross-partner collaboration. ... Built in-house by Sainsbury’s and Nectar360 and co-created with partner brands and agencies, Pollen combines audience insights, media planning and activation, optimisation and measurement into one single platform, enabling brands to run connected campaigns across in store, online and offsite channels. ... Nectar360 managing director Amir Rasekh said: “Pollen brings our audiences, media, creativity and measurement together in a way the industry never experienced before. What we are seeing now is proof that when you remove complexity through technology and focus on outcomes, brands can drive stronger, more measurable growth and deliver better customer experiences.” ... Pollen uses AI to improve performance, from pre-campaign planning to in-flight optimisation, based on what is driving sales and incrementality. This includes AI-powered tools such as advanced multi-touch attribution, designed to give a clearer view of how each channel contributes to results, and a creative checker, which can reduce compliance checks from weeks to seconds. ... Launched late last year, early campaigns highlight a simpler, more joined-up experience and impressive results, including over 2.5x higher incremental sales from omnichannel campaigns, with the strongest results seen when brands connect multiple touchpoints across the customer journey. ... Nectar360 maintains that Pollen enables brands to measure true incremental impact, moving beyond siloed reporting and last-click attribution to understand what is really driving growth. ... Unilever UK and Ireland head of retail media Charlotte Murphy said: “We are evolving our approach to retail media, with Pollen enabling a more connected and efficient way of working. This allows for faster activation and stronger measurement, marking a meaningful step forward in how we plan, activate and optimise investment, with insights directly informing future decisions.” ... Coca Cola Europacific Partners associate director of sales Gemma Nicholas added: “For big consumer and customer moments, multi-channel retail media campaigns like our Devil Wears Prada 2 activation (pictured) are essential to get right. Moving to Pollen means we can move faster as one team, including ourselves, Nectar360, WPP, and the Coca-Cola company to evaluate the campaign’s effectiveness together.” ... Nectar360 is working with PHD UK and its client Lipton Teas and Infusions, to optimise creative messaging and drive improved retail media performance. Using Pollen’s creative optimisation AI tooling, assets will be benchmarked and scored against years of historical insights to suggest improvements to help drive results against campaign objectives. ... This will enable brands to clearly identify what works and optimise their campaigns to drive more impact and deliver better business outcomes. ... PHD UK managing partner Lucy Holmes said: “Pollen brings together creative, targeting, performance and measurement. Our exclusive testing with Pollen will enable us to link creative performance with campaign outcomes and is a real step forward in helping clients to optimise impact and sales.” ... Related stories Nectar360 Pollen buzzes into the retail media market Decision Marketing at 15: The ‘Big Bang’ for retail media Sainsbury’s tech and data chief to steer future of ISBA Decision Marketing at 15: The rise of omnichannel retail"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,$30 Million AI Startup Says Pakistan Is One of Its Biggest Engineering Bets,propakistani.pk (Jehangir Nasir),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://propakistani.pk/2026/07/15/30-million-ai-startup-says-pakistan-is-one-of-its-biggest-engineering-bets/,"One of the latest examples is Nectar Social. In an interview with ProPakistani, its co-founder Misbah Uraizee said the company did not initially set out with a dedicated Pakistan strategy. Instead, it expanded organically after discovering the country’s strong engineering talent and finding it easier to operate than many outsiders assume. ... The company is an AI startup that recently raised $30 million in Series A funding. Its Lahore engineering team is developing core AI technology that powers more than 10 million brand conversations every week. ... Nectar Social is an AI-powered operating system that helps consumer brands turn online social engagement into measurable revenue. It uses autonomous AI agents to automate social listening, community management, and conversational commerce across platforms like TikTok, Instagram, and Reddit. ... Uraizee said the company continues investing where it finds the strongest engineering returns and Pakistan has consistently justified further investment. ... She said Lahore serves as one of Nectar’s core engineering hubs. Engineers based in Pakistan work on the same AI products, codebase and production systems as colleagues in Silicon Valley and New York. However, the company’s structure also reflects a broader reality. ... While Lahore is home to a growing engineering team, senior engineering and product leadership remains concentrated in the Bay Area (San Francisco, US). Uraizee said this is intentional for developing Pakistan’s early-career engineers into future leaders over time. ... ’s most capable ... eventually move abroad or join foreign companies to ... exposure to world-class product development, mentorship and larger ... opportunities. Uraizee said ... opportunity to rapidly upgrade the ... product teams, where ... by building real products rather than ... on isolated outsourced projects. ... Uraizee added that money alone will not build Pakistan’s AI ecosystem. Exposure to high engineering standards, experienced mentors, global customers and production-scale software development creates lasting value that eventually attracts investment, not the other way around. ... She explained that Pakistan’s biggest untapped advantage is the gap between perception and reality. While many international companies still overlook the country, those that have invested (including Careem, Motive and now Nectar) have demonstrated that Pakistan can support world-class engineering organizations at scale. ... Looking ahead, Uraizee sees Pakistan’s most realistic opportunity as becoming a global AI talent hub before aspiring to become a major AI product powerhouse. This will require predictable regulations, stronger protection of intellectual property, easier business conditions and tax policies that encourage skilled engineers and founders to remain in the country instead of seeking opportunities elsewhere. ... For now, ... ’s AI engineers are already helping shape products used by millions worldwide. ... The next challenge is ensuring that the talent nurtured in Pakistan not only powers global AI companies but also drives the country’s own innovation ecosystem in the years ahead, she added."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce platform KraftyLab Intelligence | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF","www.proactiveinvestors.com (Angela Harmantas, Emily Jarvie)",2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1095489/nextech3d-ai-launches-enterprise-pilot-for-ai-workforce-platform-kraftylab-intelligence-1095489.html,"Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce platform KraftyLab Intelligence | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF ... # Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce platform KraftyLab Intelligence ... Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) has launched an enterprise pilot program for KraftyLab Intelligence, an AI-powered platform designed to help organizations collect employee feedback and generate workforce insights. ... Built on the existing KraftyLab platform, KraftyLab Intelligence combines workforce data, employee feedback, onboarding programs, training initiatives, leadership development and workforce analytics into a single environment. ... The platform supports AI-powered surveys, workforce analytics, team-building, onboarding, training, employee recognition and AI-driven recommendations. ... CEO Evan Gappelberg said the company designed KraftyLab Intelligence to function as an AI layer across the workforce experience, helping organizations move beyond data collection toward generating insights, recommendations and support for decision-making. ... ""As organizations continue to invest in employee engagement, onboarding, learning, and workforce development, we believe artificial intelligence can play an increasingly important role in helping organizations better understand workforce feedback and identify potential engagement opportunities,"" Gappelberg told shareholders. ... Gappelberg said the platform builds on existing customer relationships, noting KraftyLab already works with enterprise organizations using its engagement, team-building, onboarding and learning offerings. ... “The Intelligence platform represents the next phase of that evolution by bringing workforce insights, AI-powered recommendations, engagement programs, and measurement capabilities together into a more integrated software solution,” the CEO added. ... Since 2018, KraftyLab has delivered employee engagement experiences, team-building programs, workshops, onboarding and workforce development activities for a base of Fortune 500 enterprise customers. ... The pilot program is intended to evaluate platform adoption, collect customer feedback, refine onboarding workflows and assess AI-driven recommendation capabilities, with the company planning to pursue commercialization opportunities for KraftyLab Intelligence in the third quarter of 2026. ... ### Nextech3D.ai provides update in acquisition of remaining ARway shares,... ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to provide an update on the company's proposed acquisition of all outstanding shares of ARway Corporation that it does not already own, following the recent signing of a definitive agreement between the two companies.On a... ... Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce... ... Nextech3D.ai Livestream event highlights Q4 revenue surge and... ... on 06/25/2026 ... Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI... ... on 06/25/2026 ... Nextech3D.ai appoints industry veteran Jesse Carrillo as VP of Sales ... 28/2026"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR partner to accelerate technology-led governance and inclusive development - The Tribune,"www.tribuneindia.com (ANI Updated At : 11:08 AM Jul 04, 2026 IST)",2026-07-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/business/protean-egov-technologies-and-nectar-partner-to-accelerate-technology-led-governance-and-inclusive-development/,"Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR partner to accelerate technology-led governance and inclusive development - The Tribune ... Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR partner to accelerate technology-led governance and inclusive development ... Mumbai (Maharashtra) [India], July 4: Protean eGov Technologies Limited, a pioneer in building Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI) and citizen-centric digital solutions, has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the North East Centre for Technology Application and Reach (NECTAR), an autonomous institution under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India, to collaborate on advancing technology-led governance, digital innovation, and inclusive development initiatives across India, with a special focus on the North Eastern Region. ... The strategic partnership brings together Protean's nearly three decades of experience in designing and operating population-scale digital platforms with NECTAR's expertise in technology applications, geospatial solutions, and regional development. Together, the two organisations will work towards developing scalable, technology-enabled solutions that strengthen governance, improve public service delivery, and address last-mile development challenges. ... The MoU establishes a framework for identifying and implementing high-impact projects across areas such as digital governance, information and communication technologies (ICT), geospatial technologies, capacity building, and technology-enabled socio-economic development. The collaboration will also explore opportunities to design innovative digital solutions that can be scaled for wider public benefit. ... By combining their complementary capabilities, Protean and NECTAR aim to accelerate the adoption of emerging technologies that improve citizen outcomes, strengthen institutional capacity, and contribute to sustainable and inclusive development. The partnership reflects a shared commitment to leveraging technology for public good while supporting the digital transformation agenda of the country, particularly in the North Eastern Region. ... Commenting on the partnership, Rakesh Dosi, Chief Business & Product Officer, Protean eGov Technologies Limited, said: ""For nearly three decades, Protean has been building population-scale digital infrastructure that enables governments to deliver trusted and inclusive citizen services at scale. We are delighted to partner with NECTAR to support the Northeastern Region's digital transformation journey. By combining our strengths, we aim to create scalable technology solutions that strengthen governance, accelerate socio-economic development, and contribute meaningfully to the region's growth as well as India's broader digital development agenda."" ... Commenting on the collaboration, Dr. Arun Kumar Sarma, Director General, NECTAR, said: ""The Northeastern Region presents immense opportunities for technology-led growth and innovation. Our partnership with Protean brings together strong regional expertise and proven capabilities in building Digital Public Infrastructure at scale. Together, we look forward to developing impactful digital solutions that enhance governance, improve citizen outcomes, and accelerate inclusive development across the region."" ... The partnership underscores the shared vision of Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR to harness technology as a catalyst for inclusive growth, stronger governance, and sustainable development, creating long-term value for citizens and contributing to India's digital transformation journey. ... Over the past 30 years, Protean eGov Technologies Ltd has been at the forefront of building population-scale DPIs across taxation, identity services and social security. Aligned with India's visionary DPI framework built on open standards and protocols, the company continues to contribute towards multisectoral Open Digital Ecosystems across e-commerce, transport/mobility, agriculture, education & skilling, and health. Protean has evolved from being a system integrator into a high tech, agile product organisation, instrumental in powering enterprise digitization by offering consumer and corporate tech, along with infrastructure services in cloud and cybersecurity. With a deep-rooted focus on innovation and open digital ecosystems, the company remains a key enabler in the country's ongoing digital transformation."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR Join Forces to Drive Tech-Powered Governance and Inclusive Growth - PressReleaseCloud.io,pressreleasecloud.io (Press Release),2026-07-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pressreleasecloud.io/technology/protean-egov-technologies-and-nectar-join-forces-to-drive-tech-powered-governance-and-inclusive-growth/,"- Protean eGov Technologies Limited has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the North East Centre for Technology Application and Reach (NECTAR) to advance technology‑led governance and inclusive development in India, with a special emphasis on the North Eastern Region (NER). ... - The partnership leverages Protean’s nearly three‑decade experience in building population‑scale Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI) and NECTAR’s expertise in geospatial solutions, ICT applications, and regional development. ... - Collaboration will focus on high‑impact projects in digital governance, ICT, geospatial technologies, capacity building, and technology‑enabled socio‑economic development, aiming to create scalable solutions for broader public benefit. ... - Both organisations intend to accelerate adoption of emerging technologies, strengthen institutional capacity, improve citizen outcomes, and support sustainable, inclusive growth in the NER and nationwide digital transformation agenda. ... Overview of the MoU Signing On July 4, 2026, Protean eGov Technologies Limited and NECTAR formalised their cooperation through a Memorandum of Understanding announced via PRNewswire. The agreement signals a strategic alliance designed to merge Protean’s proven track record in delivering population‑scale digital platforms with NECTAR’s deep regional knowledge and technological capabilities. By signing the MoU, both parties commit to jointly identifying, designing, and implementing projects that harness technology for better governance and inclusive development, particularly in India’s North Eastern Region. ... Strategic Rationale Behind the Partnership The collaboration is built on complementary strengths: Protean brings almost 30 years of experience in constructing Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI) that supports taxation, identity, and social‑security services at scale, while NECTAR contributes expertise in geospatial mapping, ICT applications, and region‑specific development initiatives. Together, they aim to create solutions that are not only technologically robust but also contextually appropriate for the diverse socio‑economic landscape of the NER. This synergy is expected to accelerate the adoption of emerging technologies such as AI, IoT, and cloud‑based services across government functions. ... Scope of Collaboration: Core Focus Areas Under the MoU, the two organisations will work across several thematic domains. Digital governance initiatives will seek to streamline administrative processes, enhance transparency, and improve service delivery through online portals and mobile applications. Information and Communication Technologies (ICT) will be deployed to strengthen connectivity and data exchange between government departments and citizens. Geospatial technologies will support land‑record management, disaster‑risk reduction, and infrastructure planning. Capacity‑building programmes will train officials and local stakeholders on digital tools and best practices. Finally, technology‑enabled socio‑economic projects will target livelihood enhancement, agricultural productivity, education, and health outcomes. ... Objectives for Scalable, Impact‑Driven Solutions A central goal of the partnership is to develop scalable models that can be replicated beyond the pilot sites in the NER. By designing solutions with open standards and modular architectures, Protean and NECTAR intend to ensure that successful interventions can be expanded nationally. The emphasis on scalability aligns with India’s broader Digital Public Infrastructure framework, which promotes interoperability, open APIs, and reusable building blocks across sectors such as e‑commerce, transport, agriculture, education, and health. ... Leadership Perspectives on the Alliance Rakesh Dosi, Chief Business & Product Officer of Protean eGov Technologies, highlighted the firm’s legacy of building trusted, inclusive citizen‑service platforms and expressed enthusiasm for supporting the NER’s digital transformation. He stressed that combining Protean’s scale‑ready DPI expertise with NECTAR’s regional insight would yield solutions that strengthen governance, accelerate socio‑economic development, and contribute to India’s national digital agenda. ... Dr. Arun Kumar Sarma, Director General of NECTAR, echoed these sentiments, noting the immense potential for technology‑led growth in the North Eastern Region. He affirmed that the partnership unites strong regional expertise with proven capabilities in constructing large‑scale DPI, positioning the collaboration to deliver impactful digital solutions that enhance governance, improve citizen outcomes, and foster inclusive development across the region. ... Alignment with National Digital Transformation Goals The MoU underscores a shared vision of leveraging technology as a catalyst for inclusive growth, stronger governance, and sustainable development. Both organisations see the partnership as a concrete step toward advancing India’s digital transformation agenda, which seeks to universalise access to digital services, improve efficiency of public administration, and bridge urban‑rural divides. By concentrating efforts on the NER—a region historically underserved in digital infrastructure—the alliance aims to create demonstrative models that can inform policy and investment decisions elsewhere in the country. ... Protean eGov Technologies: Three Decades of DPI Leadership For over 30 years, Protean eGov Technologies has been at the forefront of building population‑scale Digital Public Infrastructure in critical domains such as taxation, identity management, and social security. The company’s offerings are aligned with India’s DPI framework, which rests on open standards and protocols to foster interoperable, open ... NECTAR’s Role in Regional Technology Application The North East Centre for Technology Application and Reach (NECTAR) functions as an autonomous institution under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India. Its mandate centres on applying science and technology to regional development, with particular expertise in geospatial solutions, ICT applications, and technology transfer tailored to the North Eastern Region. NECTAR’s deep understanding of local challenges—ranging from difficult terrain to limited connectivity—enables it to design context‑sensitive interventions that maximize the impact of digital tools. ... Expected Outcomes and Future Roadmap Through joint projects, the partnership expects to deliver measurable improvements in service delivery times, citizen satisfaction, and administrative efficiency. Pilot initiatives may include digital land‑record systems, mobile‑based health‑information platforms, e‑learning solutions for remote schools, and smart‑agriculture modules that utilise satellite data and IoT sensors. Success metrics will likely encompass adoption rates, cost savings, and socio‑economic indicators such as income levels and literacy. The MoU also outlines a framework for continuous monitoring, knowledge sharing, and scaling up successful pilots to other states and union territories. ... Conclusion: A Catalyst for Inclusive Development The MoU between Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR represents a purposeful step toward harnessing technology for public good in one of India’s most strategically important yet under‑served regions. By merging Protean’s scale‑ready DPI capabilities with NECTAR’s regional insight and technical expertise, the collaboration is poised to create replicable, technology‑driven models that strengthen governance, improve citizen welfare, and promote sustainable development. As the partnership moves from agreement to implementation, its outcomes will likely serve as a benchmark for future public‑private collaborations aimed at achieving inclusive digital growth across the nation."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Protean Partners with NECTAR for North East Digital Governance | Wow News,www.wownews24x7.com,2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.wownews24x7.com/protean-partners-with-nectar-for-north-east-digital-governance,"Protean Partners with NECTAR for North East Digital Governance | Wow News ... # Protean Partners with NECTAR for North East Digital Governance ... Protean eGov Technologies Limited has entered into a five-year Memorandum of Understanding with NECTAR, an autonomous body under India's Department of Science & Technology. The strategic tie-up will deploy advanced digital governance, ICT, and geospatial technologies to enhance public service delivery across the North Eastern Region. ... MUMBAI — Digital infrastructure major Protean eGov Technologies Limited announced on Friday that it has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the North East Centre for Technology Application and Reach (NECTAR). The domestic technology partnership aims to jointly deploy digital governance frameworks, geospatial solutions, and Information and Communication Technology (ICT) systems across India's North Eastern Region. ... The strategic development, finalized on July 3, 2026, marks a critical step forward in bringing population-scale public infrastructure into remote and mountainous topographies. By combining sovereign technological applications with public service delivery frameworks, the initiative aims to systematically bridge the digital divide and address last-mile socio-economic development challenges in the border states. ... The primary purpose of entering into the agreement is to build a collaborative baseline for identifying and executing transformative digital governance projects. According to corporate statements, the five-year agreement brings together Protean’s extensive operational history in engineering citizen-centric public platforms with NECTAR’s specialized expertise in technology deployment and regional development. ... Geospatial Technologies: Utilizing satellite data and mapping tools to plan ... and track regional assets. ... The corporate disclosure was processed under Regulation 30 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India(Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. Publicly listed corporations are legally mandated to report any material contracts or collaborative agreements that could influence long-term commercial trajectories or open new business channels. ... The compliance filing was authenticated by Maulesh Kantharia, Company Secretary & Compliance Officer of Protean eGov Technologies Limited, and distributed to the National Stock Exchange of India Limited and BSE Limited. The disclosure explicitly stated that the agreement does not involve any equity shareholding transfers, nor do the participating parties share any promoter group relationships, confirming the transaction was handled via an arm's-length arrangement. ... According to official administrative announcements filed by the corporate relations desk of Protean eGov Technologies Limited (Trading Symbol: PROTEAN; Scrip Code: 544021), the execution of the contract is locked for a fixed tenure of 5 years from the date of execution. The collaborating agency, NECTAR, is an autonomous institution operating directly under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India. ... ""According to officials, combining Protean's experience in building population-scale digital public infrastructure with NECTAR's specialized geospatial and application capabilities will create an efficient mechanism to deliver innovative, scalable tech solutions for public good across the North Eastern Region."" ... For citizens and communities living in the North Eastern Region, this technology partnership will translate into smoother access to online government services, welfare disbursements, and localized infrastructure mapping. For small businesses, contractors, and local state departments, the deployment of advanced geospatial and ICT solutions simplifies logistical planning and accelerates regional development projects. Additionally, for public market investors tracking Protean eGov Technologies Limited, this five-year alliance solidifies the firm's position as a preferred technology partner for major government-backed socio-economic projects, expanding its service portfolio within a key demographic region. ... Partnership Mandate: Protean eGov Technologies and NECTAR have signed a five-year MoU to advance digital governance. ... Regional Focus: The primary geographical target of the tech deployment is the North Eastern Region of India. ... Core Technology: Projects will focus heavily on ICT systems, geospatial technologies, and public capacity building. ... Regulatory Status: NECTAR operates as an autonomous body under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India. ... Financial Alignment: The contract does not involve any related-party transactions or special board-level rights. ... The main objective is to jointly identify and implement transformative projects in digital governance, ICT, geospatial technologies, and technology-enabled socio-economic development with a clear focus on the North Eastern Region. ... The North East Centre for Technology Application and Reach (NECTAR) is an autonomous institution under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India, focused on applying technology to regional challenges. ... The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) has been executed for a formal tenure of 5 years from its date of signing. ... No. The official regulatory filing confirms that there is no shareholding or equity swap involved in this commercial collaboration. ... ###### Protean eGov, NECTAR Partner to Accelerate India’s... ... https://www.wownews24x7.com/protean-egov-nectar-partner-to-accelerate-indias-digital-governance 04 Jul 2026, 03:00 PM ... ###### Protean eGov, NECTAR Partner to Accelerate India’s... ... https://www.wownews24x7.com/protean-egov-nectar-partner-to-accelerate-indias-digital-governance 04 Jul 2026, 03:00 PM"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nectar360 becomes first UK retail media network to secure IAB Europe certification - Retail Gazette,www.retailgazette.co.uk (Kieran Howells),2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.retailgazette.co.uk/blog/2026/07/nectar360-becomes-first-uk-retail-media-network-to-secure-iab-europe-certification/,"Nectar360 becomes first UK retail media network to secure IAB Europe certification - Retail Gazette ... ## Nectar360 becomes first UK retail media network to secure IAB Europe certification ... Nectar360 has become the first UK retail media network to achieve IAB Europe’s Retail Media Certification, as the industry pushes for more consistent measurement standards across the fast-growing channel. ... The Sainsbury’s Group retail media, loyalty and insights business completed the certification following an independent audit by ABC. ... The milestone follows the certification of Dutch retailer Albert Heijn in 2025 and marks the first time a UK retailer has completed the programme. ... IAB Europe said the certification showed growing industry momentum behind standardised retail media measurement across Europe. ... Nectar360’s certification covers display and video ad products for off-site properties, including Meta’s Instagram and Facebook, Google DV360 and YouTube. ... The certification validates how key performance metrics are defined, calculated and reported across those channels in line with IAB Europe’s programme requirements. ... IAB Europe senior director of industry development and marketing Marie-Clare Puffett said Nectar360’s certification was “an important milestone” for both the business and the wider retail media market. ... Nectar360 managing director Amir Rasekh said: “We’re incredibly proud to be the first UK business to achieve IAB Europe’s Retail Media Measurement Certification, an important milestone not just for Nectar360, but for the evolution of retail media as a whole. ... “As the industry continues to scale, standardisation in measurement is critical. It underpins trust, enables better investment decisions, and ultimately drives stronger outcomes for our clients. ... “We’re excited to be working alongside IAB Europe to help shape a more consistent and credible future for retail media.” ... ABC audit director Clare Langstaff said the independent auditor had reviewed evidence supporting Nectar360’s measurement approach, tested campaign reporting and validated how key retail media metrics are defined, calculated and reported. ... is an important milestone for the ... and a positive ... Independent audit helps provide ... and agencies with greater assurance that reported metrics are aligned to ... IAB Europe said the next phase of the programme would extend certification across the wider ecosystem, with ad tech companies now progressing through the audit process. ... The organisation said the expansion would support better alignment between retailers and technology partners, improve interoperability and help create more consistent reporting across retail media. ... The programme is also beginning to move beyond Europe, with IAB Australia adapting retail media certification for the APAC region. ... For Nectar360, the certification strengthens its position in the UK retail media market at a time when grocers are competing to prove the value of their customer data, loyalty platforms and advertising networks to brand partners. ... It also underlines a broader shift in grocery retail media, as advertisers demand clearer evidence of performance and more comparable reporting across different retailers’ media networks. ... ## Nectar360 becomes first UK retail media network to secure IAB Europe certification ... Nectar360 has become the first UK retail media network to achieve IAB Europe’s Retail Media Certification, as the industry pushes for more consistent measurement standards across the fast-growing channel. ... The Sainsbury’s Group retail media, loyalty and insights business completed the certification following an independent audit by ABC. ... The milestone follows the certification of Dutch retailer Albert Heijn in 2025 and marks the first time a UK retailer has completed the programme. ... IAB Europe said the certification showed growing industry momentum behind standardised retail media measurement across Europe. ... The Retail Media Certification Programme is designed to bring greater clarity and consistency to how retail media is measured and reported, giving advertisers and agencies more confidence when assessing campaign performance. ... Nectar360’s certification covers display and video ad products for off-site properties, including Meta’s Instagram and Facebook, Google DV360 and YouTube. ... The certification validates how key performance metrics are defined, calculated and reported across those channels in line with IAB Europe’s programme requirements. ... IAB Europe senior director of industry development and marketing Marie-Clare Puffett said Nectar360’s certification was “an important milestone” for both the business and the wider retail media market. ... “Following Albert Heijn, it’s encouraging to see another leading retailer complete the process, signalling growing momentum,” she said. ... “Each certification helps strengthen transparency and comparability in retail media, building greater trust across the ecosystem.” ... Nectar360 managing director Amir Rasekh said: “We’re incredibly proud to be the first UK business to achieve IAB Europe’s Retail Media Measurement Certification, an important milestone not just for Nectar360, but for the evolution of retail media as a whole. ... “As the industry continues to scale, standardisation in measurement is critical. It underpins trust, enables better investment decisions, and ultimately drives stronger outcomes for our clients. ... “We’re excited to be working alongside IAB Europe to help shape a more consistent and credible future for retail media.” ... ABC audit director Clare Langstaff said the independent auditor had reviewed evidence supporting Nectar360’s measurement approach, tested campaign reporting and validated how key retail media metrics are defined, calculated and reported. ... “This is an important milestone for the UK market and a positive step towards greater confidence in retail media measurement,” she said. ... “Independent audit helps provide advertisers and agencies with greater assurance that reported metrics are aligned to industry standards and can be compared more consistently across the market.” ... IAB Europe said the next phase of the programme would extend certification across the wider ecosystem, with ad tech companies now progressing through the audit process. ... The organisation said the expansion would support better alignment between retailers and technology partners, improve interoperability and help create more consistent reporting across retail media. ... The programme is also beginning to move beyond Europe, with IAB Australia adapting retail media certification for the APAC region. ... For Nectar360, the certification strengthens its position in the UK retail media market at a time when grocers are competing to prove the value of their customer data, loyalty platforms and advertising networks to brand partners. ... It also underlines a broader shift in grocery retail media, as advertisers demand clearer evidence of performance and more comparable reporting across different retailers’ media networks."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Flipkart-backed Ninjacart raises $6 million from Accel, Nilekani, Tiger Global - The Economic Times",economictimes.indiatimes.com (ET),2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/technology/flipkart-backed-ninjacart-raises-6-million-from-accel-nilekani-tiger-global/articleshow/132141146.cms,"Flipkart-backed Ninjacart raises $6 million from Accel, Nilekani, Tiger Global - The Economic Times ... Ninjacart, a Flipkart-backed agritech firm, has secured $6 million from existing investors, signaling its readiness for a public listing within two years. The company has achieved Ebitda profitability, a significant milestone driven by improved category mix, deeper sourcing, and supply-chain efficiencies. This funding marks a crucial step as Ninjacart expands its services beyond traditional fulfillment, aiming for a stronger market presence. ... Bengaluru: Flipkart-backed agritech startup Ninjacart said it has raised $6 million from existing investors Accel, Nandan Nilekani, and Tiger Global, marking the first tranche of a larger funding round as it prepares for a public listing over the next two years.The Bengaluru-based company, which supplies fruits and vegetables to quick-commerce platforms, modern trade, kirana stores, restaurants, and exporters, said it has turned Ebitda (earnings before income, tax, depreciation, and amortisation) positive. It did not disclose the valuation or the total size of the planned multi-tranche round.The funding is modest but comes after a prolonged gap for Ninjacart, which last raised $9 million from STIC and Mainstream Digital in 2022 at a valuation of $812 million, after a $145 million investment from Walmart and Flipkart in December 2021. Its backers include Syngenta Group Ventures and Steadview Capital as well. ... Ninjacart’s focus on profitability follows a shift in its business over the past two years. ET had reported in 2023 that the company was expanding beyond its legacy fulfilment operations —connecting farmers with retailers and wholesalers — to build a marketplace for farmers and traders and offer financial services, while keeping fulfilment as its main revenue contributor.The company said improvement in the category and channel mix, deeper sourcing, lower wastage, and supply-chain efficiencies helped it reach Ebitda profitability. “Profitability has been our biggest focus, while growing steadily,” cofounder and CEO Kartheeswaran KK said in the statement. “We improved our margins through the right category and channel mix and by going backwards on the sourcing side.”Ninjacart said it now operates in more than 40 cities and manages over 150 fresh-produce categories. It moves over 1,500 tonnes of produce a day and works with more than 150,000 farmers, 30,000 retailers, and 5,000 resellers. It said its core business has grown threefold in the last year, helped by demand from quick-commerce companies and modern trade. ... The profitability claim follows a mixed financial performance. Ninjacart had reported a 74% rise in FY24 operating revenues, at Rs 2,003 crore, while reducing losses by 20% to Rs 260 crore. In FY25, however, revenue declined to Rs 1,634 crore, while losses remained largely flat at Rs 256 crore."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Retail media and Google Ads updates point to workflow… | Pivot News,pivotnews.ai,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pivotnews.ai/advertising/retail-media-google-ads-workflow-standardization-advertisers,"practical signals on workflow ... Nectar360, the retail media, loyalty and insights business of the Sainsbury's Group, moved on a different part of the same problem. It became the first UK retail media network to achieve certification under IAB Europe's Retail Media Certification Programme, after an independent audit carried out by ABC. ... The certification follows Albert Heijn's certification in 2025 and points to growing adoption of standardized retail media practices in Europe. For retail media buyers, that gives procurement, measurement and trading teams a more concrete basis for comparing network claims. The caveat is that certification does not say whether every advertiser will change budget allocation, or how quickly retail media networks outside this group will follow. ... Taken together, the Google Ads and N ... 360 updates are about operating consistency rather than a single campaign result. One change sits inside the buying platform. The other sits inside the retail media measurement and assurance process. Both reduce ambiguity in places where advertisers already spend time checking structure, definitions and control points. ... The next signal in Google Ads is how broadly the redesigned All Campaigns selector reaches advertisers and whether the hierarchy and search changes alter daily account workflows. In retail media, watch which UK and European networks pursue IAB Europe certification after Nectar360 and Albert Heijn. ... Nectar360’s certification gives buyers another signal for comparing retail media networks against emerging standards."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nectr Launches Focus+, Its New Flagship Nootropic Pouch with a 320mg+ Stack","news.marketersmedia.com (San Diego, CA, California, United States, July 1, 2026)",2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.marketersmedia.com/nectr-launches-focus-its-new-flagship-nootropic-pouch-with-a-320mg-stack/89196548,"Nectr Launches Focus+, Its New Flagship Nootropic Pouch with a 320mg+ Stack ... # Nectr Launches Focus+, Its New Flagship Nootropic Pouch with a 320mg+ Stack ... Nectr Launches Focus+, Its New Flagship Nootropic Pouch with a 320mg+ Stack. The functional pouch maker introduces a fully dosed, seven-ingredient nootropic pouch across the United States ... -- Nectr, the functional oral pouch company behind “The Functional Pouch Category,” today launched Focus+, its most loaded nootropic pouch and the new flagship of the brand’s lineup. Focus+ is available now to customers across the United States. ... Focus+ is a 320mg+ blend of seven active ingredients in a single pouch: L-Theanine (100mg), Alpha-GPC (85mg), L-Tyrosine (85mg), Caffeine (50mg), Huperzine A (30mcg), and vitamins B6 and B12 in the bioactive methylcobalamin form. Sold as a dietary supplement, the pouch is designed to support focus, memory, attention, and sustained mental energy, with sublingual onset in 10 to 15 minutes and a focus window of one to two hours. ... Focus+ replaces Nectr’s legacy Focus pouch, which is being discontinued. The new flagship roughly doubles the caffeine and adds six additional actives over the product it succeeds, consolidating the brand’s nootropic offering into a single, fully dosed pouch. ... The launch extends a positioning Nectr has held since its founding in 2023. The company frames the everyday slide into autopilot and stimulant dependency as “the Drift,” and its products as a way to stay present and deliberate rather than reliant on the spike-and-crash cycle of conventional energy drinks and dependence on nicotine pouches. ... Focus+ launches in four flavors: Fresh Mint, Mango, Wintergreen, and Watermelon. One pouch is placed under the top lip and is intended to deliver a steady focus block of 60 to 120 minutes, with a stated daily limit of no more than four pouches. The line is sold on its site, Amazon and select retailers across the United States. (18 and up) ... Nectr enters the launch as oral nootropic and caffeine pouches continue to gain traction among consumers in the United States seeking alternatives to energy drinks and nicotine pouches. The Swedish-style pouch format, long established in Northern Europe, has expanded rapidly across the American functional category in recent years. Product specifications, ingredient details, and usage directions are published on each product listing. ... Nectr is a San Diego, CA-based functional pouch company built by three friends who were hooked on energy drinks and tired of the trade-off of the spike, the crash, and the dependency. They bet on themselves with four pallets of a Swedish pouch format that nobody in America had tried, given a Southern California twist. Today the brand makes oral pouches across three lines, Energy, Zero, and Focus+, positioned as “The Stimulation Control System” for people who want clean performance and total discipline."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Unlimitail, Douglas, Nectar360 on Retail Media's Next Chapter | RetailNews.ai",www.retailnews.ai (Retailnews.ai),2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.retailnews.ai/article/retail-media-next-chapter-unlimitail-douglas-nectar360-shoptalk-europe,"Retail media is evolving beyond ad sales to focus on platforms, insights, and measurable outcomes, with Unlimitail, Douglas, and Nectar360 leading structural transformations to enhance collaboration, data, and AI-powered personalization. ... - 1Next-generation retail media prioritizes sophisticated data capabilities and AI-powered personalization, as evidenced by Nectar360's Pollen platform, which automates audience building in seconds and creative resizing in 90 seconds, unifying in-store, onsite, and offsite environments. ... - 2Retail media success hinges on building technology platforms and unlocking customer insights, with Nectar360's analysis revealing that omnichannel campaigns across in-store, onsite, and offsite channels generate a significant multiplier effect compared to single-channel efforts. ... - 3Organizational structures for retail media are diverse yet share a common philosophy: Unlimitail operates as a separate joint venture of Carrefour and Publicis Groupe, Douglas Marketing Solutions is a wholly-owned subsidiary leveraging Douglas Group's 62M loyalty members, and Nectar360 (Sainsbury's) maintains an arm's-length relationship to offer agency-like services. ... That was the central message from executives representing Unlimitail, Douglas Group, and Nectar360 during a panel discussion at Shoptalk Europe titled ""Think Like an Agency, Grow Like a Retailer,"" moderated by Ben Miller, VP of Original Content & Strategy at Shoptalk, where leaders explored how retail media networks are evolving to meet the changing expectations of brands and retailers. ... Amir Rasekh, Managing Director of Nectar360 at Sainsbury''s, has lived through the longest evolution of the three. Nectar360 began life 15 years ago as a joint venture and has been wholly owned by Sainsbury''s for the past decade, operating the Nectar loyalty scheme alongside the retail media networks for both Sainsbury''s and Argos. The deliberate choice, Rasekh explained, was to remain a separate trading entity operating at arm''s length. ""Clients don''t want a retailer-supplier relationship,"" he said. ""They want an agency service in the retail media space."" ... ## Nectar360''s Pollen: AI Built to Unify, Not Just Automate ... Among the most significant technology stories discussed during the session was Pollen, Nectar360''s AI-powered retail media platform, which the company describes as a blend of buy and build that is becoming increasingly proprietary over time. ... Rasekh explained that clients consistently ask for two things: genuine ease of use, and returns that outperform every other media channel available to them, even when those other channels are notoriously difficult to measure against. Pollen was built specifically to answer both demands by unifying in-store, onsite, and offsite environments within a single technology and data stack, enabling self-service alongside managed campaign delivery, and finally addressing what Rasekh called ""the measurement conundrum"" around multi-touch attribution and incrementality. ... The platform automates work that previously consumed enormous amounts of time. Building a customer audience from a campaign brief, which used to take days of manual targeting work, now happens in seconds. Creative resizing across the many different formats required across online and physical store environments, work that used to take a team three weeks, now takes approximately 90 seconds inside the platform. Rasekh was clear that this is only the first version of Pollen, with creative scoring and in-flight optimisation already live and considerably more capability still to come. ... is exactly where the ... advantage lies. ... Early analysis from Nectar360, drawn from multi-touch attribution data across Pollen, confirmed something the team had long suspected but struggled to prove while data sat in three disconnected environments: campaigns spanning in-store, onsite, and offsite generate a genuine multiplier effect compared with any single channel running alone. Last-click attribution, Rasekh noted, has always taken the credit, when the reality is that different channels are playing genuinely different roles throughout the customer journey. ... Bringing that personalisation into the physical store is harder than doing it online, and Rasekh was candid about the practical work involved. Sainsbury''s and Argos both required serious investment in connectivity, Wi-Fi coverage across the store estate, and tools like the Scan and Go handsets, known internally as Smart Shop, that let Sainsbury''s deliver tailored offers directly to a customer''s device mid-shop. Fully personalised digital screens remain harder to achieve than handset-based personalisation, but Nectar360 has worked to make screen placement and content at least contextually relevant, based on time of day and which products a specific store location tends to over-index on. ... Where Douglas believes it has a genuine structural advantage is in its 1,900 stores across 22 countries, each staffed with at least 15 trained beauty advisors capable of delivering real-time, in-person personalisation that no digital screen can fully replicate. The challenge, Lumley acknowledged, is that this kind of personalisation does not scale easily, particularly when new products are launching almost daily across thousands of stores. Her ambition for the in-store retail media layer is to create what she called a cinematic, theatrical experience, language she borrowed directly from a recent conversation with Christian Louboutin''s team about their own approach to physical retail. ""How do we make a standout feeling for the customer and for the brand,"" she said, ""in an environment that is already so dense with choice?"" ... Hennion added a useful caution to that ambition from Unlimitail''s broader market view: dynamic in-store digital content does genuinely work, including in food retail and general merchandise where the customer mission is very different from beauty, but only when it is deployed at the right moments in a customer''s journey rather than blanketing stores with screens. The formats that perform best, in his experience, are those tied closely to a specific shopper mission and supported by clean measurement, rather than added simply because the screens exist. ... final shared theme. Every panellist returned to the idea that retail ... can no longer sit in a silo. Closer alignment with merchandising ... brand teams inside the ... brand partners on ... , is now ... structural necessity rather ... As retail media enters its next stage of maturity, competitive advantage will come less from selling advertising space and more from combining AI, customer intelligence, and genuinely cross-functional collaboration into a unified growth platform. For retailers, that transformation may ultimately redefine retail media from a marketing channel into one of the most strategic capabilities within modern commerce."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai CEO discusses strongest quarterly results yet - ICYMI | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF",www.proactiveinvestors.com (Emily Jarvie),2026-06-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1094605/nextech3d-ai-ceo-discusses-strongest-quarterly-results-yet-icymi-1094605.html,"# Nextech3D.ai CEO discusses strongest quarterly results yet - ICYMI ... Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) earlier this week discussed its Q4 and full-year 2026 financial results with Proactive, outlining record revenue growth, improving margins and a clearer path toward profitability as recent acquisitions begin to contribute to performance. ... Chief executive Evan Gappelberg said the latest results reflected several years of operational restructuring and strategic repositioning. ... He indicated that the company had focused on rebuilding its business model, improving execution and establishing itself as a high-growth, high-margin participant in the AI-powered event technology market. ... A standout metric was fourth-quarter revenue growth of 216% year-over-year. According to management, the company generated nearly $1 million in revenue during the quarter, almost matching the revenue produced during the previous three quarters combined. ... Chief financial officer Anum Waqas attributed the growth to stronger sales execution, contributions from the Eventdex and Kratylabs acquisitions, and increased demand for the company's software offerings. Waqas said the benefits of integrating technologies and customer relationships were beginning to emerge and suggested there remained meaningful upside as those integrations progress. ... Profitability metrics also moved in a positive direction. Waqas reported software margins above 90%, lower costs of sales and substantial operational efficiencies. The company reduced overhead, streamlined teams and increased its use of AI and automation across the organization. ... Operating losses improved by approximately 80% for the full year and by approximately 96% in the fourth quarter, according to management. Waqas said these trends provided a clearer view of the company's future financial trajectory, adding that increasing revenue should allow more earnings to flow to the bottom line. ... Gappelberg further highlighted reduced accounts payable, lower operating losses and what he described as exceptionally strong gross margins. He suggested that, excluding certain one-time charges, the company would be cash-flow positive and that profitability could be achieved in the foreseeable future. ... Looking ahead, management identified continued integration of recent acquisitions, sustained revenue growth and expanding software adoption as key catalysts. Gappelberg also pointed to growing investor interest in the event technology sector, citing recent multibillion-dollar transactions involving BlackRock and Apollo as evidence of increasing industry momentum. ... The executives expressed confidence that the company's operational improvements and market positioning could support continued growth into 2027. ... ### Nextech3D.ai provides update in acquisition of remaining ARway shares,... ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to provide an update on the company's proposed acquisition of all outstanding shares of ARway Corporation that it does not already own, following the recent signing of a definitive agreement between the two companies.On a... ... Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce... ... Nextech3D.ai Livestream event highlights Q4 revenue surge and... ... 25/ ... Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI... ... on 06/25/2026 ... Nextech3D.ai appoints industry veteran Jesse Carrillo as VP of Sales ... 8/2026"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nectar360 harnesses AI to drive campaign performance -,mediashotz.co.uk (Giles Crosse),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mediashotz.co.uk/nectar360-harnesses-ai-to-drive-campaign-performance/,"360 ... AI to drive campaign performance - ... Nectar360 has revealed early results from campaigns on Pollen, its unified retail media platform, with leading global brands including Unilever and Coca-Cola Europacific Partners seeing clear impact. ... Less than a year since launch, Pollen is helping brands run more connected, effective campaigns – combining insight, media and measurement in one place. ... Early feedback highlights a simpler, more joined-up experience and a clearer view of what drives results. ... Built in-house by Nectar360 and in collaboration with brands and agencies, Pollen is designed to solve one of the industry’s biggest challenges: fragmentation. ... Pollen brings together audience insight, media planning, campaign activation, in-flight optimisation and measurement into a single environment, enabling brands to run connected campaigns across in-store, online and offsite channels. ... At its core is a leading multi-touch attribution model. This gives brands a clear view of performance across the full customer journey, helping them understand what is driving growth and where to optimise for better results. ... Amir Rasekh, Managing Director at Nectar360, said: “Pollen brings our audiences, media, creativity and measurement together in a way the industry never experienced before. ... “What we are seeing now is proof that when you remove complexity through technology and focus on outcomes, brands can drive stronger, more measurable growth and deliver better customer experiences.” ... Early campaign performance shows over 2.5 times higher incremental sales from omnichannel campaigns, with the strongest results seen when brands connect multiple touchpoints across the customer journey. ... From those incremental sales, up to 25% are driven by mid and upper-funnel activity, with up to 10 times higher conversion rates from targeted activity, powered by first-party data. ... Charlotte Murphy, Head of Retail Media, Unilever UK and Ireland, said: “We are evolving our approach to retail media, with Pollen enabling a more connected and efficient way of working. ... “This allows for faster activation and stronger measurement, marking a meaningful step forward in how we plan, activate and optimise investment, with insights directly informing future decisions.” ... Gemma Nicholas, Associate Director, Sales, Coca Cola Europacific Partners, added: “For big consumer and customer moments, multi-channel Retail Media campaigns like our Devil Wears Prada activation are essential to get right. ... “Moving to Pollen means we can move faster as one team, including ourselves, Nectar360, WPP, and the Coca-Cola company to evaluate the campaign’s effectiveness together.” ... Pollen uses AI to improve performance, from pre-campaign planning to in-flight optimisation, based on what is driving sales and incrementality. ... This includes AI-powered tools such as advanced multi-touch attribution, giving a clearer view of how each channel contributes to results, and a creative checker, which can reduce compliance checks from weeks to seconds. ... Nectar360 is working with PHD UK and its client, Lipton Teas and Infusions, to optimise creative messaging and drive improved retail media performance. ... Lucy Holmes, Managing Partner at PHD UK, said: “Pollen brings together creative, targeting, performance and measurement. ... “Our exclusive testing with Pollen will enable us to link creative performance with campaign outcomes and is a real step forward in helping clients to optimise impact and sales.”"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai reports higher Q4 revenue, narrows operating loss in fiscal 2026 | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF","www.proactiveinvestors.co.uk (Emily Jarvie, Angela Harmantas)",2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.co.uk/companies/news/1094508/nextech3d-ai-reports-higher-q4-revenue-narrows-operating-loss-in-fiscal-2026-1094508.html,"Nextech3D.ai reports higher Q4 revenue, narrows operating loss in fiscal 2026 | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF ... # Nextech3D.ai reports higher Q4 revenue, narrows operating loss in fiscal 2026 ... Last updated: 15:15 25 Jun 2026 BST, First published: 14:35 25 Jun 2026 BST Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF, FRA:1SS) has reported its audited financial results for the fourth quarter and full fiscal year ended March 31, 2026, showing higher revenue, improved margins and a reduced operating loss as the company continues its transition toward an AI-focused software business. ... For the full fiscal year 2026, Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF) reported revenue of $2.13 million and gross profit of $1.94 million. Gross margin increased to 91.2% from 63.6% in fiscal 2025, while cost of sales declined 85% year over year. ... Nextech3D.AI (CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF) CEO Evan Gappelberg said the results reflected the company's restructuring efforts and increasing emphasis on software-based offerings. ... ""We reported strong year-over-year improvements in revenue and profitability metrics, including revenue growth of 207% and gross margins ... 91%,"" Gappelberg said ... a statement. ... The company said its shift toward a software-first, AI-supported platform has contributed to sustained gross margins above 90%, lower costs of sales and improved operating efficiency. ... ""Our cost structure has changed significantly, with cost of sales reduced by 85% and operating loss improved year-over-year. These results reflect the impact of our restructuring and our increased focus on software-based offerings,” Gappelberg said. ... ""We continue to focus on execution, improving efficiency, and expanding our product capabilities."""
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,"Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI platform gains traction | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF",www.proactiveinvestors.com (Steve Darling),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1094504/nextech3dai-reports-q4-revenue-surge-and-margin-expansion-as-ai-platform-gains-traction.html,"Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI platform gains traction | CSE:NTAR, OTCQX:NEXCF ... # Nextech3D.ai reports Q4 revenue surge and margin expansion as AI platform gains traction ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg and CFO Anum Waqas joined Steve Darling from Proactive to discuss the company’s Q4 and full-year fiscal 2026 financial results, highlighting what management described as clear evidence that the business has entered a new phase of accelerating growth following its 2024 restructuring. ... Gappelberg said Nextech delivered its strongest quarterly performance to date since the restructuring, driven by growing traction across its AI-powered, software-focused platform. ... For the fourth quarter ended March 31, 2026, the company reported revenue of $966,000, representing an increase of approximately 216% compared with $306,000 in Q4 2025. Gross profit rose 275% year over year to $885,000, while gross margin expanded to 91.6%, up from 77.2% in the prior-year quarter. The company also reported a major improvement in profitability metrics. Operating loss improved by 96% compared with Q4 2025, while net loss narrowed to $992,000 from $7.25 million in the same period last year. The quarter’s net loss included a non-cash impairment charge of approximately $930,000. ... On the balance sheet, Nextech reduced accounts payable to $1.69 million from $3.19 million, a 47% decrease, which management attributed to stronger financial discipline and improved vendor management. ... Gappelberg said the results reflect accelerating momentum across the company’s AI-powered product suite and continued progress in transforming Nextech into a higher-margin, software-driven business. Looking ahead to fiscal 2027, management expects continued progress supported by the expansion of AI-powered product offerings, growing enterprise adoption, and an ongoing focus on margin expansion and cost discipline. ... Management believes the latest results demonstrate that Nextech’s restructuring efforts are beginning to translate into stronger operating leverage, improved margins, and a clearer path toward scalable growth. ... ### Nextech3D.ai launches enterprise pilot for AI workforce intelligence platform ... www.proactiveinvest ... .com/companies/news/1 ... tech3dai-launches-enterprise-pilot-for-ai-workforce-intelligence-platform.html ... Nextech3D.ai CEO Evan Gappelberg joined Steve Darling from Proactive to discuss the launch of the enterprise pilot program for KraftyLab Intelligence™, an AI-powered workforce intelligence and employee engagement platform designed to help organizations better understand and support their... ... Nextech3D.ai Livestream event highlights Q4 revenue surge and... ... Nextech3D.ai appoints industry veteran Jesse Carrillo as VP of Sales ... Nextech3D.ai launches Krafty Labs AI event marketplace ... on 05/12/2026 ... Nextech3D.ai partners with HotelPlanner to add lodging to event..."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nectar360 Says Pollen Delivers Strong Early Results,www.grocerytradenews.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.grocerytradenews.com/nectar360-pollen-strong-early-results/,"Nectar360 Says Pollen Delivers Strong Early Results ... # Nectar360 Says Pollen Delivers Strong Early Results for Brands ... - June 24, 2026 ... Nectar360 said early campaigns run through its Pollen retail media platform have delivered strong results for brands including Unilever and Coca-Cola Europacific Partners, with omnichannel campaigns generating more than 2.5 times higher incremental sales. ... The company said up to 25% of incremental sales came from mid- and upper-funnel activity, while targeted campaigns powered by first-party data achieved conversion rates up to ten times higher than broader campaigns. ... Less than a year after launching Pollen, Nectar360 said the platform is helping brands manage audience insights, campaign activation and performance measurement through a single environment. ... The company also highlighted the role of artificial intelligence within the platform, including tools that can reduce creative compliance checks from several weeks to around 90 seconds. ... Pollen’s multi-touch attribution technology is designed to give brands a clearer view of how different channels contribute to sales, moving beyond traditional last-click measurement. ... Nectar360 works with more than 900 brands and has access to more than 24 million loyalty members through partnerships including Sainsbury’s, Argos, British Airways, Esso and American Express. ... The results are significant for supermarkets because retail media has become one of the fastest-growing sources of additional revenue for grocery retailers. By using loyalty data and shopper insights, retailers can sell targeted advertising to consumer brands and better measure its impact on sales. Platforms such as Pollen are increasingly turning supermarket customer data into a high-margin digital business. ... The latest results underline growing investment in retail media technology as retailers and consumer goods companies seek better measurement and more targeted advertising capabilities. ... UK retail technology companies are increasingly investing in retail media platforms and AI-driven analytics to improve advertising performance and create new revenue opportunities from customer data and loyalty programmes. ... Editor’s Note: This article is based on information released by Nectar360 on 23 June 2026 regarding the early performance of its Pollen retail media platform. Performance figures, customer numbers and campaign data cited in the article originate from the company’s announcement and statements from participating brands and partners, including Unilever and Coca-Cola Europacific Partners. Global Supermarket News has not independently verified the reported campaign performance metrics."
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Nectar360 Pollen delivers strong early results for brands - Nectar360,www.nectar360.co.uk,2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.nectar360.co.uk/news/nectar360-pollen-delivers-strong-early-results-for-brands/,"Nectar360 Pollen delivers strong early results for brands - Nectar360 ... Nectar360 Pollen delivers strong early results for brands ... With client onboarding underway, Nectar360 is sharing an early view of Pollen, its unified retail media platform, with brands reporting a more seamless omnichannel experience, stronger measurement capabilities and more relevant experiences for customers. ... London, UK, Tuesday 23 June 2026 ... - Early campaigns are delivering strong results: over 2.5x higher impact when using multiple channels, of which up to 25% of these are through mid and upper-funnel activity - AI-creative compliance checker reduces weeks of work down to 90 seconds - Market leading multi-touch attribution technology provides a true view of performance, moving beyond last click measurement - Leading brands, including Unilever and Coca-Cola Europacific Partners, report faster activation, improved measurement and more effective cross-partner collaboration using Pollen ... Nectar360 has revealed strong early results from campaigns on Pollen, its unified retail media platform, with leading global brands including Unilever and Coca-Cola Europacific Partners already seeing clear impact. ... Less than a year since launch, Pollen is helping brands run more connected, effective campaigns – combining insight, media and measurement in one place. Early feedback highlights a simpler, more joined-up experience and a clearer view of what drives results. ... Retail media has grown quickly, but it can still be complex to plan, run and measure campaigns. Pollen is designed to change that. Built in house by Nectar360 and in collaboration with brands and agencies, it is designed to solve one of the industry’s biggest challenges: fragmentation. ... Pollen brings together audience insight, media planning, campaign activation, in-flight optimisation and measurement into a single environment. Enabling brands to run connected campaigns across in store, online and offsite channels. ... Importantly, at its core is a leading multi-touch attribution model. This gives brands a clear view of performance across the full customer journey, helping them understand what is driving growth and where to optimise for better results. ... Amir Rasekh, Managing Director at Nectar360, said: “Pollen brings our audiences, media, creativity and measurement together in a way the industry never experienced before. What we are seeing now is proof that when you remove complexity through technology and focus on outcomes, brands can drive stronger, more measurable growth and deliver better customer experiences.” ... - Over 2.5x higher incremental sales from omnichannel campaigns, with the strongest results seen when brands connect multiple touchpoints across the customer journey - From those incremental sales, up to 25% are driven by mid and upper-funnel activity - Up to 10x higher conversion rates from targeted activity, powered by first-party data ... full customer journey. ... Crucially, Pollen enables brands to measure true incremental impact, moving beyond siloed reporting and last-click attribution to understand what is really driving growth. ... Charlotte Murphy, Head of Retail Media, Unilever UK and Ireland, said: “We are evolving our approach to retail media, with Pollen enabling a more connected and efficient way of working. This allows for faster activation and stronger measurement, marking a meaningful step forward in how we plan, activate and optimise investment, with insights directly informing future decisions.” ... Gemma Nicholas, Associate Director, Sales, Coca Cola Europacific Partners, added: “For big consumer and customer moments, multi-channel Retail Media campaigns like our Devil Wears Prada activation are essential to get right. Moving to Pollen means we can move faster as one team, including ourselves, Nectar360, WPP, and the Coca-Cola company to evaluate the campaign’s effectiveness together.” ... Pollen uses AI to improve performance, from pre-campaign planning to in-flight optimisation, based on what is driving sales and incrementality. ... This includes AI-powered tools such as advanced multi-touch attribution, giving a clearer view of how each channel contributes to results, and a creative checker, which can reduce compliance checks from weeks to seconds. ... Nectar360 is working with PHD UK and its client, Lipton Teas and Infusions, to optimise creative messaging and drive improved retail media performance. Using Pollen’s creative optimisation AI tooling, assets will be benchmarked and scored against years of historical insights to suggest improvements to help drive results against campaign objectives. This will enable brands to clearly identify what works and optimise their campaigns to drive more impact and deliver better business outcomes. ... Lucy Holmes, Managing Partner at PHD UK, said: “Pollen brings together creative, targeting, performance and measurement. Our exclusive testing with Pollen will enable us to link creative performance with campaign outcomes and is a real step forward in helping clients to optimise impact and sales.”"
NECTAR 360 SERVICES,,,,Exa,Coca-Cola and Unilever see strong results from Nectar360’s Pollen platform one year on - InternetRetailing,internetretailing.net (Paul Skeldon),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://internetretailing.net/coca-cola-and-unilever-see-strong-results-from-nectar360s-pollen-platform-one-year-on/,Coca-Cola and Unilever see strong results from Nectar360’s Pollen platform one year on - InternetRetailing
