DOMINION ENERGY,,,,Tavily,"Dominion Energy Reports Strong Q2 Results, Reaffirms Guidance | Steven Ridge posted on the topic | LinkedIn",,,,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/steven-ridge-34a4235_dominion-energys-strong-second-quarter-results-activity-7490785277909680128--bEu,"US power & utility M&A hit $216B in the six months to May — up 173% year over year. NextEra's $67B merger with Dominion, the largest regulated-utility deal ever announced, entered its six-month Virginia regulatory review this week. What changed isn't ambition, it's added value. I saw this shift coming inside utility client's boardrooms. AI load growth made dispatchable capacity scarce: PJM capacity prices jumped 833% into the 2025/26 delivery year — then hit the FERC price cap in the next two auctions. In Brandenburger & Stuart's (1996) terms: when no deal happens without you, you capture more of the pie. And when regulation caps your price, the negotiation moves to who funds the grid. That's exactly where hyperscalers went. Co-opetition, not confrontation. [...] Dominion Energy’s strong second-quarter results reflect both the strength of our business and the dedication of our employees who provide the reliable, affordable, and increasingly clean energy to power our customers every day"
