LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Kalshi launches 'Blanket' to help small businesses hedge against risk — with help from the guru of 'hypergamblification' | Fortune,fortune.com (Nick Lichtenberg),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fortune.com/2026/08/07/exclusive-kalshi-blanket-small-business-hedge-hypergamblification/,Exclusive: Kalshi partners with Blanket to help small businesses hedge against risk—with help from the guru of ‘hypergamblification’ | Fortune ... # Exclusive: Kalshi partners with Blanket to help small businesses hedge against risk—with help from the guru of ‘hypergamblification’ ... An independent financial economist has partnered with Kalshi on a new AI tool on top of the prediction-market exchange that aims to help small businesses hedge against everything from bad weather to election shocks—without hiring a Wall Street bank.
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,How Can One Card Manage Multiple Currency Wallets?,fintechnews.sg (Izzat Najmi Abdullah),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fintechnews.sg/135272/sponsored/lulu-exchange-multi-currency-card-stitch-wallet/,"LuLu Exchange’s programme shows how Stitch coordinates wallets, real-time FX, processing, settlement and reconciliation through one infrastructure layer. ... LuLu Exchange encountered an operating challenge when it set out to build a multi-currency card programme in the UAE. Although the product launched in one market, the architecture questions apply much more widely. Any institution building a similar product needs a clear operating layer to coordinate the programme across the systems and partners involved. ... At the company’s transaction volumes, ... arrangement placed a ceiling on how far the product could develop. Introducing another currency could require a new integration, while adjusting a transaction limit or fee became a coordination exercise involving ... > Joseph Cleetus > > “We were looking for the right partner to support launching our multi-currency cards, and Stitch clicked right away,” said Joseph Cleetus, Vice President of Business Transformation at LuLu Exchange. ... Cleetus said Stitch worked closely with LuLu Exchange’s teams and helped the company manage the external stakeholders involved in bringing the programme to market. ... Stitch consolidated issuing, processing, FX, ledger management and reconciliation within one operating environment. A common data model gave LuLu Exchange a shared view of balances and transaction activity, while a consistent set of APIs allowed programme rules to be managed without maintaining separate connections for every function. ... The architecture diagram shows processing and FX connected with wallet management on one side, while card-scheme connectivity, settlement and reconciliation operate on the other. A ledger underneath them maintains the programme’s record of balances and transaction movements. ... External institutions remain part of the arrangement. The bank sponsor and payment networks continue performing their respective functions, while Stitch coordinates the card, wallets and transaction logic across those relationships. ... A common operating layer also gives the product team more control over how the card behaves. Currencies, fees, transaction limits and wallet priorities can be configured within the programme rather than distributed across several vendor systems. ... Architecture decisions determine how much control a product team retains after launch. An institution needs to know whether currencies, limits and pricing can be changed through configuration, or whether each update will require engineering work, vendor approval and another release. The answer affects how quickly the programme can respond when a new travel corridor becomes commercially relevant or customer behaviour changes. ... LuLu Exchange’s reloadable prepaid travel card supports AED and 25 other currencies, giving customers access to 26 currency wallets through one product. It is available in digital and physical formats through the LuLu Money app. ... Supporting those currencies creates a continuing operational requirement. Travel patterns change, new corridors emerge, and pricing needs to be reviewed. Product teams may also want to introduce another wallet or alter the order in which balances are used. ... Stitch allows LuLu Exchange to adjust call of those without rebuilding the underlying architecture for every change. The card connects to the LuLu Money app through APIs and PCI-certified card widgets. Customers can manage their PIN, adjust spending limits, freeze or unfreeze the card and review transaction history without leaving the existing app. ... Implementation time will also influence whether an institution builds the stack internally or works through one operating layer. Stitch says its wider platform can reduce implementation time by 80%, with some programmes going live in as little as 90 days, compared with the nine to 12 months it associates with traditional providers."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Italy fines Lusha €2m and claims jurisdiction over data brokers with no EU office | emailexpert,emailexpert.com,2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://emailexpert.com/italy-fines-lusha-e2m-and-claims-jurisdiction-over-data-brokers-with-no-eu-office/,"Italy fines Lusha €2m and claims jurisdiction over data brokers with no EU office | emailexpert ... # Italy fines Lusha €2m and claims jurisdiction over data brokers with no EU office By Emailexpert Editorial Team 06/08/2026 4 min read Italy’s data protection authority has fined US data broker Lusha Systems Inc. €2m and ordered it to stop processing, and delete, the personal data of everyone located in Italy held on its platform. The Garante adopted decision no. 542 on 14 July and announced it on 27 July, finding breaches of GDPR Articles 5(1)(a), 5(1)(c), 6, 12 and 25. Lusha is incorporated in Boston, wholly owned by Israeli-founded Lusha Systems Ltd, and has no establishment in the European Union. That last fact is why this decision matters well beyond one company. ... usha operates a subscription platform selling “enriched” contact records: job titles, email addresses and phone numbers, assembled from social network scraping, purchases from other data brokers, and contributions from its own users, including calendar and email integrations and CRM uploads through its community programme. The records on the platform included contact details for senior institutional figures, public administration staff, law enforcement officers and members of the judiciary. The investigation began in part from reports of those institutional contacts appearing on the platform, and from complaints by people in Italy who had received commercial communications ... The fine of €2m represents 10% of the applicable ceiling. Lusha must prove deletion of Italian-territory data within 60 days, may settle for half the fine within the appeal window, and the decision itself is ordered published. The number of people affected is redacted throughout the decision; the Garante describes it only as a large number, and no reliable estimate exists. ... The second reason is jurisdictional. Lusha argued, in effect, that a US company with no EU establishment sits outside the GDPR. The Garante rejected this under Article 3(2)(b): because the platform continuously checks and refreshes its contact records, on a weekly cycle, it is monitoring the behaviour of people in the Union. The weekly refresh of a contact card, the routine hygiene function of every data enrichment product, is the very feature that establishes jurisdiction. ... No EU establishment also means no one-stop-shop mechanism, so any member state authority can act alone, as Italy just did. The theory reaches every non-EU B2B contact data vendor whose product involves keeping records current, which is to say all of them. It arrives in the same season as Rome’s tracking pixel provision and the wider European enforcement pattern we analysed in the spring, and the direction of travel is consistent: the mechanics of data operations, not just their outputs, are what regulators are examining."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,M&A: Unite Us Acquires Vircho Health to Advance Performance Analytics for Community Care Networks -,hitconsultant.net (Fred Pennic),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hitconsultant.net/2026/08/06/ma-unite-us-acquires-vircho-health-to-advance-performance-analytics-for-community-care-networks/,"M&A: Unite Us Acquires Vircho Health to Advance Performance Analytics for Community Care Networks - ... - Social care coordination leader Unite Us has acquired Vircho Health, a technology platform providing performance, quality, and financial accountability analytics for community care networks. Financial terms of the acquisition were not disclosed. - The acquisition includes the full Vircho Health team, led by co-founders Craig Manson and Evan Jones. - The deal transitions Unite Us from proving that a social service occurred (closed-loop referrals) to providing intelligent infrastructure for network performance, quality analytics, and dollar-level financial tracking. ... - Vircho Health’s tools are already deployed alongside Unite Us technology in North Carolina through Impact Health, supporting the Healthy Opportunities Pilot (HOP) and the state’s Rural Health Transformation Program (NC ROOTS Hub). ... Unite Us Integrates Vircho Health for Outcome-Based Validation ... Unite Us has acquired Vircho Health to integrate financial measurement, performance analytics, and outcome validation tools into its health and community care platform. The acquisition targets a key shift in social determinants of health (SDoH) funding, where government payers, health plans, and foundations are requiring proof of service delivery and quantifiable financial returns rather than basic closed-loop referral tracking. ... Unite Us brings a 13-year dataset of nearly 125 million care connections across clinical, social, and economic services. By embedding Vircho’s clinical informatics and analytics tools, the combined platform allows network administrators to track community care expenditures down to individual services and dollars. The system generates performance reporting for each organization in a network, surfacing high-performing nodes and identifying areas that require operational support. ... The two platforms already operate together in real-world initiatives, supporting Impact Health in Western North Carolina’s Healthy Opportunities Pilot (HOP) and the state’s Rural Health Transformation Program (NC ROOTS Hub). Full terms of the transaction were not disclosed, and the Vircho Health team, including co-founders Craig Manson and Evan Jones, has joined Unite Us. ... “We earned the trust of the communities we serve by taking on the problem everyone else thought was too complicated: going the last mile to close the loop,” said Taylor Justice, CEO and co-founder of Unite Us. “Vircho’s analytics expertise, combined with what we’ve built over 13 years, gives our network a new layer of intelligence and gets the right insight to the right decision maker, so issues get resolved the first time.”"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Longsys Showcases End-to-End AI Storage Solutions at FMS 2026,www.prnewswire.com (Longsys),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/apac/news-releases/longsys-showcases-end-to-end-ai-storage-solutions-at-fms-2026-302843826.html,"Longsys Showcases End-to-End AI Storage Solutions at FMS 2026 ... SAN JOSE, Calif., Aug. 6, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Longsys(301308.SZ) is presenting its ""Edge AI Storage Fusion"" showcase at the Future of Memory and Storage (FMS) 2026, spanning three core scenarios: AI Agent Hosts (AI BOX), AI PCs, and AI Mobile embedded devices. ... To address memory bottlenecks, KV cache expansion, and latency challenges in local LLM deployment, Longsys has partnered with AMD to integrate AIDIMM™ high-bandwidth memory, the iSA™ (Intelligent Storage Agent), and AISSD™. A live demo, jointly developed with SixUnion, showed a system running 70B-, 80B-, and 122B-parameter models smoothly using just 64GB of AIDIMM™ memory, with significantly lower memory usage and higher inference efficiency. Longsys also unveiled an AMD Ryzen™ AI Halo platform integrated with AISSD™ and iSA™, now AMD AVL-certified and ready for mass deployment. ... Longsys' 5nm SPU™ (Storage Processing Unit) powers a DRAM-less PCIe Gen5 SSD achieving 14.8 GB/s sequential read and 13 GB/s write speeds — flagship-class performance at ≤6.3W, roughly 10% lower than comparable controllers. Built-in lossless compression (up to 2:1) expands usable capacity without impacting speed. Longsys' PCIe Gen5 mSSD reaches 11 GB/s read, 10 GB/s write, and 2200K/1800K IOPS. With flexible form factors (M.2 2230/2242/2280 and more) and manufacturing capacity exceeding one million units monthly, Longsys supplies various partners including Lenovo and ASUS. ... Longsys' HLCache™ UFS technology intelligently offloads cold data from DRAM to storage. Tested on a Google Pixel 7a, a 4GB LPDDR5 device saw background app capacity rise 64% (17 to 28 apps) and DRAM usage drop 20% (3.1GB to 2.5GB) — performance approaching a native 6GB configuration, while supporting 13B–20B parameter models. AILPBGA™ complements this with a 256-bit, 307GB/s embedded memory solution in a compact 22×22mm package, purpose-built for space- and power-constrained devices. ... Longsys operates a multi-brand strategy — including the consumer brand Lexar and South America manufacturing and operations center Zilia — supporting localized production, delivery, and technical support worldwide. ... Looking ahead, Longsys will continue advancing its proprietary technologies and collaborating with global ecosystem partners to deliver efficient, scalable, and customized Edge AI storage solutions, accelerating the adoption of intelligent computing. ... Founded in 1999, Longsys (301308.SZ) is a globally leading branded semiconductor memory enterprise, integrating R&D, design, packaging and testing, manufacturing, and sales services. For more information please visit https://www.longsys.com/, and follow Longsys on LinkedIn and Facebook."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Leumas rents out robotic factory lines to brands that do not want to build a factory | YourStory,yourstory.com (YS Content Desk),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://yourstory.com/2026/08/leumas-robotic-factory-rental,"Leumas rents out robotic factory lines to brands that do not want to build a factory | YourStory ... | Company Overview | | | --- | --- | | Founded | 2016 (most sources; some records list 2022) | | Founders | Nitesh Kumar, Subhajit Biswas | | Headquarters | Bengaluru | | Sector | Manufacturing technology, pharmaceuticals and wellness | | Funding Raised | About ₹19 crore ($2.2 million) seed round (June 2025); ₹7 crore pre-seed (2023) | | Key Investors | Capital 2B (seed lead), Capital-A, Anicut Capital | | Product | Modular robotic production lines sold as manufacturing capacity | ... Leumas offers a way to skip that trade-off entirely. The company builds modular robotic production lines and offers them as capacity, so a brand can manufacture small batches on demand without owning a plant. Its founders are Nitesh Kumar, the CEO, and Subhajit Biswas, the CTO, and it operates from Bengaluru. ... This approach has two direct benefits. First, traceability is built in because a software-controlled line records what it did, which matters in pharmaceuticals where regulators require it. Second, the lines can run continuously with little human presence, which the company describes as unmanned operation. ... It serves the nutrition, cosmetics and pharmaceuticals sectors, which share a regulatory burden and which share a heavy regulatory burden and a tendency to launch many products in small batches. Direct-to-consumer brands in particular launch and retire lines faster than a conventional plant can retool. ... The company says it has co-developed the technology with wellness brands over the past year and has helped scale more than 120 products across India, the United States and the Middle East and North Africa. It has also signed agreements with pharmaceutical and food research institutions to build dedicated factory capacity, which would give it access to formulation expertise as well as production volume. ... Leumas raised $2.2 million, about Rs 19 crore, in a seed round announced in June 2025, led by Capital 2B with Capital-A and Anicut Capital participating. It had earlier raised Rs 7 crore in a pre-seed round in 2023 from the same group of investors. ... The money is for research and development, expanding the manufacturing infrastructure, and launching pilot factories built for wellness and pharmaceutical brands. ... Leumas is targeting the outsourced manufacturing market, which the company and its investors say will exceed $400 billion globally by 2030, a projection with no independent source behind it. ... Leumas has not published a customer name, a revenue figure, or the number of lines it operates. Its 120-product figure reflects activity, not scale, and the pilot factories the round was meant to fund are still planned, not running."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Humla announces its digital nurse staffing marketplace is now a qualified solution on leading healthcare platform – Health Technology Net,healthtechnologynet.com,2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://healthtechnologynet.com/2026/08/05/humla-announces-its-digital-nurse-staffing-marketplace-is-now-a-qualified-solution-on-leading-healthcare-platform/,"Humla announces its digital nurse staffing marketplace is now a qualified solution on leading healthcare platform – Health Technology Net ... MINNEAPOLIS, Aug. 5, 2026 /PRNewswire/ — Humla, a digital marketplace that matches qualified nurses directly with health systems to fill open shifts, today announced that its tool is now a qualified solution on the Mayo Clinic Platform. Founded by nurses in 2022 and available nationally, Humla replaces the traditional staffing agency model with a transparent marketplace where facilities build and manage their own pools of vetted nurses and pay only when a shift is worked. ... Humla manages credentialing and continuous compliance inside the solution — including license re-verification against source-of-truth databases and certifications every 24 hours, specialty and regulatory assessments, background checks, and drug screening — while giving facilities full visibility into every nurse’s profile. Based on Humla client data, facilities using the solution have reduced staffing costs while increasing nurse take-home pay and onboarded nurses in days rather than the traditional four to five weeks. Through the Mayo Clinic Platform qualification process, Humla’s claims, performance, and compliance practices were evaluated, supporting transparent, credible adoption by health systems. ... “Nurses built Humla because we know the need for staffing solutions firsthand,” said Jessica Sylvester, founder and CEO of Humla. “Becoming a qualified solution allows us to bring transparent, direct and emergency preparedness staffing to more health systems. Imagine you had a traumatic event and you needed nurses to walk into your health system immediately, through Humla, that is a reality. We are living our mission and vision to create a tool that supports a sustainable nurse staffing alternative.” ... Mayo Clinic Platform supports digital health solutions developers with the infrastructure and ecosystem needed to bring digital solutions into real-world clinical and administrative workflows. The program evaluates each solution for intended use, proposed value, and clinical and algorithmic performance, providing transparency and credibility, and enabling the adoption of transformative health technologies. ... “Mayo Clinic Platform is committed to advancing solutions that transform healthcare,” says Steve Bethke, vice president of Solution Developer Market at Mayo Clinic Platform. “Mayo Clinic Platform’s unique ecosystem and technical infrastructure enables potential deployment of qualified solutions into clinical and administrative systems.” ... About Humla: Founded in 2022 by nurses, for nurses, Humla is a digital marketplace that connects health systems directly with qualified nurses to fill shifts — from ad-hoc per diem needs to long-term placements. Humla employs nurses under a W-2 model, automates credentialing and continuous compliance, and charges a flat, transparent platform fee with no contract minimums, implementation fees, or long-term agreements. Humla is available nationally. Learn more at www.humla.com. ... Humla announces its digital nurse staffing marketplace is now a qualified solution on leading healthcare platform ... ### Humla announces its digital nurse staffing marketplace is now a qualified solution on leading healthcare platform"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Longsys Showcases Edge AI Storage Fusion Solutions At FMS 2026 | MarketScreener,www.marketscreener.com (S&P Capital IQ),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/longsys-showcases-edge-ai-storage-fusion-solutions-at-fms-2026-ce7f50dcd88af121,"Longsys Showcases Edge AI Storage Fusion Solutions At FMS 2026 | MarketScreener ... ## Shenzhen Longsys Electronics Co., Ltd. | 12:05pm | Longsys Showcases Edge AI Storage Fusion Solutions At FMS 2026 | CI | | --- | --- | --- | | 08:21pm | Certain A Shares of Shenzhen Longsys Electronics Co., Ltd. are subject to a Lock-Up Agreement Ending on 5-AUG-2026. | CI | ... # Longsys Showcases Edge AI Storage Fusion Solutions At FMS 2026 Published on 08/05/2026 at 12:05 pm EDT S&P Capital IQ SHENZHEN LONGSYS ELECTRONICS CO., LTD. +8.59% ... Longsys presented its ""Edge AI Storage Fusion"" showcase at the Future of Memory and Storage (FMS) 2026, spanning three core scenarios: AI Agent Hosts (AI BOX), AI PCs, and AI Mobile embedded devices. To address memory bottlenecks, KV cache expansion, and latency challenges in local LLM deployment, Longsys has partnered with AMD to integrate AIDIMM? high-bandwidth memory, the iSA? ... (Intelligent Storage Agent), and AISSD?. A live demo, jointly developed with SixUnion, showed a system running 70B-, 80B-, and 122B-parameter models smoothly using just 64GB of AIDIMM? memory, with significantly lower memory usage and higher inference efficiency. ... Longsys also unveiled an AMD Ryzen? AI Halo platform integrated with AISSD? and iSA?, now AMD AVL-certified and ready for mass deployment. ... AIDIMM? delivers a native 256-bit interface, up to 307.2 GB/s peak bandwidth, and up to 128GB capacity per module, with a plug-and-play design suited for scaled manufacturing. iSA?, Longsys' proprietary scheduling engine, uses MoE offloading, tiered cache management, and predictive prefetching to dynamically balance memory and storage resources in real time. ... Longsys' 5nm SPU? (Storage Processing Unit) powers a DRAM-less PCIe Gen5 SSD achieving 14.8 GB/s sequential read and 13 GB/s write speeds?flagship-class performance at =6.3W, roughly 10% lower than comparable controllers. Built-in lossless compression (up to 2:1) expands usable capacity without impacting speed. ... Longsys' PCIe Gen5 mSSD reaches 11 GB/s read, 10 GB/s write, and 2200K/1800K IOPS. With flexible form factors (M.2 2230/2242/2280 and more) and manufacturing capacity exceeding one million units monthly, Longsys supplies various partners including Lenovo and ASUS. Longsys' HLCache? ... UFS technology intelligently offloads cold data from DRAM to storage. Tested on a Google Pixel 7a, a 4GB LPDDR5 device saw background app capacity rise 64% (17 to 28 apps) and DRAM usage drop 20% (3.1GB to 2.5GB)?performance approaching a native 6GB configuration, while supporting 13B?20B parameter models. AILPBGA? ... complements this with a 256-bit, 307GB/s embedded memory solution in a compact 22×22mm package, purpose-built for space- and power-constrained devices. Product performance data is based on Longsys internal testing; actual results may vary."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Jusfy raises $15M Series A led by Quona Capital - LatamList,latamlist.com (Araceli Dominguez),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://latamlist.com/jusfy-raises-15m-series-a-led-by-quona-capital/,"Jusfy raises $15M Series A led by Quona Capital - LatamList ... # Jusfy raises $15M Series A led by Quona Capital ... Brazilian legaltech Jusfy raised a $15M Series A round led by Quona Capital, with participation from Spectra E Investments, The LegalTech Fund, FJ Labs, MAYA Capital, and Thomson Reuters Ventures. ... Founded in 2021, Jusfy develops an AI-powered platform for Brazil’s legal industry that combines legal workflow tools with embedded financial services. Its flagship financial product, Jusfy Pay, helps lawyers manage payments and other financial operations. ... Jusfy will use the funding to expand Jusfy Pay, develop new AI capabilities, and launch a version of its platform for law students."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Kalshi Extends Solidus Labs Surveillance to Kinetic Markets After $31 Billion June Volume | The Currency analytics,thecurrencyanalytics.com (James Thorp),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thecurrencyanalytics.com/crypto-exchanges/kalshi-extends-solidus-labs-surveillance-to-kinetic-markets-after-31-billion-june-volume-281225,"Kalshi Extends Solidus Labs Surveillance to Kinetic Markets After $31 Billion June Volume | The Currency analytics ... Kalshi Extends Solidus Labs Surveillance to Kinetic Markets After $31 Billion June Volume ... Kalshi is pushing its trade surveillance deeper into its own infrastructure. The prediction-market operator has brought Solidus Labs’ monitoring technology into Kinetic Markets, its futures commission merchant arm — a move that stretches compliance coverage well beyond the exchange floor and into the brokerage layer where institutional clients actually access event-contract markets. ... The Solidus relationship isn’t new. It started in February 2026, when Kalshi first brought the firm on to cover KalshiEx, its designated contract market. Now Kinetic Markets gets the same treatment. The timing isn’t random either — Kalshi’s trading volumes cleared $31 billion in June 2026, a number that probably got the attention of both institutional allocators and regulators. When volumes run that hot, the compliance infrastructure has to keep pace. It didn’t, and now it does. ... The stated goal is straightforward: give institutional investors the regulatory reassurance they need to commit real capital to prediction markets. That’s harder to do than it sounds. ... Kalshi isn’t the first to go down this road. Big exchanges have been layering on surveillance tech for years, usually after a regulatory scare or a volume surge forced their hand. The pattern is pretty consistent — markets grow fast, regulators notice, and suddenly compliance becomes a strategic priority rather than a back-office headache. ... Kinetic Markets is basically making that same bet now. By extending Solidus Labs’ coverage to the FCM layer — not just the exchange — Kalshi is saying that the entire trading workflow, from market access through margin and clearing, sits under one compliance umbrella. That’s a harder thing to build than it looks. And it matters more than most people realize. ... By pulling Kinetic Markets into the Solidus Labs framework, Kalshi closes that gap. Institutional clients get a cleaner picture of the full risk environment. Regulators get a more complete audit trail. And Kalshi gets to tell the market that its compliance infrastructure runs end-to-end, not just at the front door. ... That’s probably the real story here. It’s not just about following rules. It’s about being the platform that institutional money trusts when prediction markets get serious regulatory scrutiny — and that scrutiny is coming, if it isn’t already here. A $31 billion monthly volume number tends to draw eyes. ... Smaller platforms, for their part, won’t find this easy to replicate. Third-party surveillance tools cost money. FCM registration is a long, expensive process. The compliance overhead that Kalshi is building out is, in a real sense, a moat. Not every competitor can afford to dig one. ... Monthly volume on Kalshi’s platforms is the obvious one. If volumes stay above $31 billion — or climb — it’s a decent sign that institutional engagement is holding and that the compliance build-out is doing its job. A sustained drop would raise questions. ... The adoption rate of third-party surveillance tools across other prediction-market venues is worth watching too. Kalshi isn’t the only operator in this space. Rothera and Novig are also out there, and broader acknowledgment of the need for enhanced oversight is already visible across the industry. If more platforms move toward external surveillance providers, it probably means institutional demand is pulling the whole market in that direction. ... And then there’s the institutional feedback loop. Kalshi’s bet is that better compliance infrastructure translates directly into more institutional participation. If that plays out, the model basically validates itself and other platforms will have to follow or fall behind. ... Unclear yet whether the Solidus expansion covers every corner of Kinetic Markets’ operations or just the core trading functions. No details on that from the available reporting. Worth asking. ... What’s not unclear: Kalshi just made its brokerage arm considerably harder to ignore for any institution that’s been sitting on the sidelines waiting for prediction markets to look more like real financial infrastructure. The $31 billion June volume was the headline. The Solidus expansion into Kinetic Markets is the infrastructure behind it."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,"Busha expands its innovation portfolio with the launch of licensed prediction market, Signal by Busha | Business Insider Africa",africa.businessinsider.com (BI Africa),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://africa.businessinsider.com/local/markets/busha-expands-its-innovation-portfolio-with-the-launch-of-licensed-prediction-market/rlqjvfd,"Busha expands its innovation portfolio with the launch of licensed prediction market, Signal by Busha | Business Insider Africa ... # Busha expands its innovation portfolio with the launch of licensed prediction market, Signal by Busha ... As prediction markets gain global recognition as tools for forecasting trends across business, politics, technology, and sports, Busha today announced the launch of Signal by Busha, a prediction market licensed by the Lagos State Lottery and Gaming Authority. ... Available immediately as a web platform, Signal by Busha is accessible to existing Busha users using their current Busha accounts. ... New users can get started by creating a Busha account before connecting it to Signal. Users fund their Signal wallets directly from their Busha wallets using supported balances, including Naira, stablecoins, and other cryptocurrencies available within the Busha app. ... At launch, users can trade in markets across sports, crypto, culture, politics, economics, and trending topics, with additional categories expected over time. Rather than simply placing one-off predictions, users can buy and sell positions throughout the life of a market, allowing them to adjust their exposure as new information becomes available. Markets are settled using official event sources wherever available, while an internal resolution team determines outcomes for markets that do not have a single authoritative source, operating strictly in accordance with Busha’s publicly available, transparent market resolution policies and consumer protection guidelines. Once a market is resolved, eligible payouts are automatically credited to users' Signal wallets, and funds can be withdrawn to their Busha wallets. ... Globally, prediction markets are gaining recognition as a complementary forecasting tool for businesses, researchers, analysts, and policymakers. Unlike opinion polls, which capture sentiment at a single point in time, or sentiment analysis, which reflects how people feel, prediction markets aggregate what participants are willing to back with conviction. As trading activity evolves, market prices continuously update to reflect changing expectations, creating a real-time signal that can sit alongside traditional research and forecasting methods. ... ""Markets have always been powerful information systems,"" said Olaoluwa Samuel-Biyi, co-founder of Busha. ""When people put their conviction behind a prediction, they collectively generate valuable signals about where they believe the future is headed. Signal by Busha is designed to surface those insights in real time, giving individuals, businesses, and researchers a new lens for understanding markets and emerging trends. We believe prediction markets will become an increasingly important complement to traditional research, and we want African users to participate in that evolution through a trusted, regulated platform."" ... For Busha, the launch represents another step in the company's evolution from a digital asset platform to a broader technology company that builds products at the intersection of finance, information, and emerging technology. ... ""From inception, our vision has been to build technology that gives Africans access to the financial tools shaping the future,"" said Michael Adeyeri, co-founder and CEO of Busha. ""We started by making digital assets more accessible. Today, we are building products across savings, payments, global money movement, and now prediction markets. Signal by Busha reflects our belief that technology can do more than help people transact, it can also help them make better-informed decisions by harnessing collective intelligence in real time. By expanding beyond saving, investing, and digital assets into forecasting and market predictions, we are continuing to redefine what a modern African financial technology company can build."" ... The launch builds on a period of rapid product expansion for Busha. Over the past six months, the company introduced Busha 3.0, a redesigned all-in-one money app with high-yield savings products, expanded into enterprise financial infrastructure through Busha Business, enabling stablecoin-powered cross-border payments for businesses, and is soon to launch stablecoin-backed virtual Visa cards that allow users to spend directly from their digital asset and fiat balances. ... With Signal by Busha, the company is extending its innovation portfolio beyond financial services into technology-powered forecasting and market intelligence. The launch reinforces the company's commitment to building innovative technologies that help Africans make smarter decisions, move money more efficiently, and engage with the future through trusted, regulated products. ... Busha is a Pan-African digital asset exchange and one of Nigeria's first SEC-licensed digital asset platforms. Operating across Nigeria and Kenya, Busha provides consumers and businesses with access to traditional savings, crypto trading, crypto-backed loans, and stablecoin-powered business infrastructure. Through Busha Business, companies, fintechs, and developers access licensed payment infrastructure for cross-border payments, stablecoin treasury, merchant payments, and API integration. Trusted for its compliance-first approach, deep liquidity, and exceptional user experience, Busha is at the forefront of driving responsible innovation in Africa's digital financial ecosystem."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Busha Signal Brings Prediction Markets Into Nigerian Fintech,www.techbooky.com (Paul Balo),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.techbooky.com/busha-signal-prediction-market-nigeria-regulated-fintech/,"# Busha Signal Brings Prediction Markets Into Nigeria’s Regulated Fintech Conversation ... Busha is moving beyond its original crypto exchange identity with the launch of Signal by Busha, a licensed prediction-market product that brings one of the internet more controversial financial ideas into Nigerias regulated fintech conversation. ... In a partner announcement carried by Disrupt Africa, Busha said Signal will allow users to take positions on real-world outcomes through a regulated platform. The company is framing prediction markets as a way for African users to participate in a global shift where information, probability and finance are beginning to overlap. ... That is why the word licensed matters in this story. Busha is already known as a Nigerian digital-assets company, and its own website describes it as an SEC-licensed digital assets provider. The company was also among the early firms to receive approval-in-principle under Nigerias Securities and Exchange Commission digital asset rules. That regulatory positioning gives Busha a stronger base than a prediction product launched casually outside the system. ... is real. Millions ... wallets, transfers ... products, betting apps ... an audience quickly ... but that also ... careful about disclosure, ... , dispute resolution and how events ... Busha launch also fits a broader African fintech shift. The sector is moving from simple payment rails into savings, credit, crypto, stablecoins, cross-border money movement and now event-based markets. We have seen that same expansion pressure in stories like LemFi and BVNK moving diaspora payments onto stablecoin rails and Visa building stablecoin rails for banks and fintechs. ... The caution is that innovation in African fintech now has to mature faster than before. Regulators, banks and users are less willing to accept vague promises. If Busha can make Signal transparent, compliant and useful beyond speculation, it could open a new category in Nigerian fintech. If not, prediction markets may quickly run into the same trust and regulatory questions that have followed crypto and online betting. ... For now, Signal by Busha is worth watching because it shows where African fintech is heading next. The market is no longer only about moving money. It is increasingly about turning information, identity, assets and expectations into financial products. That is exciting, but it also raises the bar for responsibility."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,"Busha expands its innovation portfolio with the launch of licensed prediction market, Signal by Busha | TechCabal",techcabal.com (Partner),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://techcabal.com/2026/08/03/busha-expands-its-innovation-portfolio-with-the-launch-of-licensed-prediction-market-signal-by-busha/,"Busha expands its innovation portfolio with the launch of licensed prediction market, Signal by Busha | TechCabal"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Elula's Sweeper wins work as regulators tighten scrutiny,itbrief.com.au (Sean Mitchell),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://itbrief.com.au/story/elula-s-sweeper-wins-work-as-regulators-tighten-scrutiny,"Elula's Sweeper wins work as regulators tighten scrutiny ... # Elula's Sweeper wins work as regulators tighten scrutiny Mon, 3rd Aug 2026 (Today) SEAN MITCHELL Publisher Elula says its AI data monitoring product, Sweeper, is winning new and expanded client work as regulators increase scrutiny of operational breaches. ... The Sydney-based software group says Sweeper scans large data sets for anomalies that can lead to regulatory and operational failures. It is designed to identify problems including overcharging, undercharging, duplicate services and compliance breaches. ... The launch comes as Australian companies face growing scrutiny over data handling, customer treatment and control failures. In a recent review, the Australian Securities & Investments Commission examined 204,000 bank loans across eight banks and found widespread errors in how some lenders calculated interest for borrowers with offset accounts. ... Elula is positioning Sweeper as a tool for earlier detection of these issues. Many internal remediation programs remain manual and begin only after customers complain, while data often sits in separate, poorly integrated systems. ... ""Sweeper prevents regulatory and compliance breaches, reduces operational revenue loss, and safeguards corporate brand and reputation. Like all of Elula's products, it's fast, secure and scalable,"" he said. ... Elula says its products have been in the market since 2017 and are already used by more than 20 banks, non-bank lenders, superannuation funds and insurers. With Sweeper, it is also targeting sectors beyond finance, including mining and energy, telecommunications, and government agencies. ... The broader pitch reflects a problem that extends beyond financial services. Any large organisation with fragmented data, legacy systems and high customer volumes can face losses, remediation costs and regulatory pressure when billing, service records or compliance checks fail. ... Alongside Sweeper, Elula sells three other AI products to financial services customers. Sticky is aimed at predicting which customers are most likely to leave within the next three months, including superannuation members and mortgage borrowers considering refinancing with another provider. ... Nudge is designed to identify people most likely to restart superannuation contributions or apply for new lending within six months, with a focus on member reactivation, account consolidation and win-back campaigns. Elastic is built for lenders and focuses on pricing decisions, helping them weigh portfolio growth against margin in competitive repricing markets. ... Those products suggest the company's main focus remains financial services, even as it pursues opportunities in other regulated industries. The addition of a monitoring tool such as Sweeper also broadens its offering from customer acquisition, retention and pricing into operational controls and remediation. ... The tougher compliance environment has created demand for systems that can identify errors before they become customer scandals or formal enforcement matters. That is particularly relevant in sectors where mistakes can affect large numbers of consumers and generate significant compensation costs. ... For lenders, insurers and superannuation funds, the challenge is not only to identify errors but to do so quickly enough to avoid prolonged customer harm. Recent regulatory actions in Australia have highlighted how small administrative faults can persist for long periods when firms lack clear oversight of data across products and systems. ... ""Sweeper proactively identifies anomalies to enable quicker remediation, helping companies avoid regulatory action and enabling a better customer experience,"" Shipman said."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Kinetic Markets Taps Solidus Labs for Trade Surveillance | FinancialContent,www.financialcontent.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.financialcontent.com/article/bizwire-2026-8-3-kinetic-markets-taps-solidus-labs-for-trade-surveillance,"Kinetic Markets Taps Solidus Labs for Trade Surveillance | FinancialContent ... Markets Taps Solidus Labs for ... Kinetic Markets LLC, the futures commission merchant (FCM) affiliate of Kalshi, today announced it has selected Solidus Labs as its trade surveillance partner. ... This latest addition to the Kalshi ecosystem comes as prediction markets reach an inflection point: Kalshi's monthly trading volume surpassed $31 billion in June 2026, while institutional clients have shown a growing appetite to enter prediction markets, provided they have regulated clearing, institutional liquidity, and margin access to participate at scale. ... Solidus Labs has provided trade surveillance technology to Kalshi since February 2026, monitoring KalshiEX's event contract markets for market abuse and insider trading risk. Kinetic Markets' FCM registration introduces a new dimension to that risk surface, driving the decision to extend Solidus' HALO surveillance capabilities across both layers of this structure. ... ""Kalshi set the gold standard for advancing prediction markets while recognizing that market integrity is a clear competitive edge and a business enabler,"" said Asaf Meir, Founder & CEO of Solidus Labs. ""That's why it was only natural that Kalshi's affiliated futures commission merchant chose a surveillance partner built for the future - providing multidimensional protection across the full structure, not just the exchange's order book. That's the coverage we've built for Kinetic Markets."" ... ""As we bring institutional-grade capabilities to prediction markets, compliance infrastructure has to scale right alongside it,"" said James Hill, Kinetic Markets’ Chief Compliance Officer. ""Solidus Labs emerged as the ideal partner for us because of their expertise in trade surveillance and deep understanding of the prediction markets landscape. Extending their relationship with Kalshi to Kinetic Markets was the fastest, most credible path to surveillance that can stand up to CFTC scrutiny from day one."" ... Founded in 2018, Kalshi is the world’s next-generation financial exchange. Prediction markets provide accurate, real-time information on the likelihood of events, making humanity more informed about the future. As the first regulated exchange for events, Kalshi is credited with legalizing and establishing prediction markets as a financial asset class. It’s the leading safe and regulated platform, trusted by millions of people and a growing number of institutions in America. To learn more about Kalshi, visit www.kalshi.com. ... Born in crypto and built for Wall Street, Solidus Labs is the gold standard for multidimensional market integrity and trade surveillance. Founded in 2018 by Goldman Sachs veterans, the company merges institutional rigor with crypto-native innovation and Agentic AI to reinvent compliance for the modern financial era. At the core is HALO, an AI-powered risk-based platform trusted by financial institutions, crypto firms, and regulators globally to drive proactive, intelligence-led oversight across any product, venue, or asset class. For more information, visit www.soliduslabs.com."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lunit Signs Supply Deals with Major UK and US Healthcare Providers - Seoul Economic Daily,en.sedaily.com (Lee Jeong-Min),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/08/03/lunit-signs-supply-deals-with-major-uk-and-us-healthcare,"Lunit Signs Supply Deals with Major UK and US Healthcare Providers - Seoul Economic Daily ... Lunit (328130), a medical artificial intelligence (AI) company, is expanding its global customer base by signing a series of supply contracts with major healthcare institutions in the United Kingdom and the United States. ... Lunit said on the 3rd that it has secured GenesisCare UK, which operates more than 10 premium cancer centers and diagnostic centers across the UK, as a new client. ... Through this contract, Lunit will supply Analytics and Scorecard, its mammography quality and operations management solutions, as well as Lunit INSIGHT MMG and Lunit INSIGHT DBT, its AI-based breast cancer diagnosis solutions. ... GenesisCare UK will build an integrated screening system spanning from imaging quality control to AI reading support for 2D and 3D mammography. This will enable the provider to offer more accurate and efficient breast cancer screening services. ... In the United States, VA Tulsa, a medical institution under the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), has joined as a new client. VA Tulsa is a large medical institution that provides healthcare services to about 36,000 veterans annually. ... In 2024, Lunit signed a five-year breast cancer screening solution supply contract worth a total of 7.3 million dollars (about 10.6 billion won) with the US Defense Health Agency (DHA) through its subsidiary Lunit International (formerly Volpara). With this latest contract, Lunit has further strengthened its position in the US public healthcare market. ... Lunit will supply VA Tulsa with ""Patient Hub,"" which supports overall patient management including screening appointments, tracking, and result notifications, and ""Risk Pathways,"" which supports the screening of high-risk breast cancer groups and the operation of customized screening programs. ... Lunit also signed a new contract with DeTar Healthcare System, a general hospital in Texas. The company plans to supply Patient Hub and Risk Pathways to this hospital, which has more than 200 specialists and medical staff, to advance its patient management and risk-based customized screening system. ... ""This contract shows that demand from global healthcare institutions for platforms that support the entire cancer screening process, beyond AI image reading, is rapidly expanding,"" Lunit CEO Suh Bum-seok stressed. ""We will continue to expand our push into the global healthcare market with a product portfolio that combines image-reading AI and screening operations solutions."""
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Kalshi's Kinetic Markets Selects Solidus Labs for Trade Surveillance as Monthly Volume Hits $31B | Gate US,www.gate.com,2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gate.com/en-us/news/detail/kalshis-kinetic-markets-selects-solidus-labs-for-trade-surveillance-as-17828888,"Kalshi's Kinetic Markets Selects Solidus Labs for Trade Surveillance as Monthly Volume Hits $31B | Gate US ... Kalshi's Kinetic Markets Selects Solidus Labs for Trade Surveillance as Monthly Volume Hits $31B ... Kalshi's Kinetic Markets Selects Solidus Labs for Trade Surveillance as Monthly Volume Hits $31B ... According to Kalshi, Kinetic Markets, its futures commission merchant subsidiary registered with the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission, has selected Solidus Labs to provide trade surveillance across its brokerage and exchange operations in June. The selection extends an existing relationship with Solidus Labs' HALO surveillance platform, which has monitored Kalshi's exchange since February 2026. ... Kalshi reported monthly trading volume surpassed $31 billion in June. The expanded surveillance deployment enables oversight of both brokerage and exchange infrastructure, addressing compliance requirements as institutional participation accelerates in prediction markets. James Hill, Chief Compliance Officer at Kinetic Markets, stated that surveillance infrastructure must scale alongside institutional-grade capabilities to meet CFTC standards."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,HashMicro rolls out AI OS for Philippine enterprises → Context.ph,context.ph (Context.ph),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://context.ph/2026/07/31/hashmicro-rolls-out-ai-os-for-philippine-enterprises/,"HashMicro rolls out AI OS for Philippine enterprises → Context.ph ... Home Communications & Technology ... # HashMicro rolls out AI OS for Philippine enterprises July 31, 2026 ... Enterprise software provider HashMicro has launched an artificial intelligence (AI) operating system in the Philippines, betting that businesses are ready to move beyond experimenting with AI and begin embedding it into core operations. ... The new platform, Hashy OS, integrates AI directly into the company’s enterprise resource planning (ERP) ecosystem, allowing organizations to access company data, automate workflows and execute business processes from a single digital workspace. ... The launch comes as Philippine companies accelerate digital transformation efforts, but many still face challenges integrating AI into existing enterprise systems rather than deploying it as a standalone productivity tool. ... “Businesses today are not struggling to access AI but to make it work cohesively within their organization,” said Lusiana Lu, HashMicro chief of business development. ... “When AI systems operate in silos, teams still need to interpret outputs and coordinate actions manually. Hashy OS brings together AI coworkers, enterprise knowledge, and workflows into a single platform, enabling AI to collaborate across functions and support processes from start to finish,” she added. ... HashMicro said disconnected AI tools often create operational bottlenecks by requiring employees to manually translate AI-generated insights into business actions. Hashy OS aims to address this by combining enterprise data, AI agents and workflow automation within a unified platform. ... The system is built around four components. Nexus consolidates enterprise knowledge across business modules to generate context-aware insights. Coworkers automate operational tasks such as data analysis, reporting and cross-functional coordination. Hashy Apps allows companies to build customized AI applications with minimal coding, while Hashy Hub connects external software and services through the Model Context Protocol. ... The company said the integrated approach can reduce inefficiencies, shorten deployment times and improve collaboration across departments, an increasingly important advantage as enterprises seek measurable returns from AI investments. ... HashMicro serves more than 3,000 companies across the Asia-Pacific region, providing AI-enabled ERP, finance, manufacturing, supply chain, procurement, human resources and customer relationship management solutions for mid-sized and large enterprises."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Italy fines Lusha €2 million for GDPR breaches and expands definition of monitoring | Noah Intelligence,noah-news.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://noah-news.com/italy-fines-lusha-2-million-for-gdpr-breaches-and-expands-definition-of-monitori/,"Italy fines Lusha €2 million for GDPR breaches and expands definition of monitoring | Noah Intelligence ... # Italy fines Lusha €2 million for GDPR breaches and expands definition of monitoring ... Italy’s data protection authority has imposed a €2 million fine on Lusha Systems Inc. and mandated the erasure of Italian personal data, marking a significant expansion in the interpretation of monitoring under GDPR and... ... Italy’s data protection authority has imposed a €2 million fine on Lusha Systems Inc. and mandated the erasure of Italian personal data, marking a significant expansion in the interpretation of monitoring under GDPR and raising concerns over data enrichment practices in the B2B sector. ... Italy’s data protection authority has hit Lusha Systems Inc. with a €2 million fine and ordered the US sales intelligence company to stop processing and erase the personal data of people in Italy, after finding that it had gathered, refreshed and sold enriched contact profiles without a lawful basis. The Garante said the case concerned job titles, email addresses and phone numbers assembled through sources that included social media scraping and purchases from other data brokers, and that the company’s practices breached the GDPR’s rules on lawfulness, fairness, transparency and data minimisation. ... The regulator’s decision is notable not just for the size of the penalty, but for the reach of its reasoning. According to the Garante, Lusha’s ongoing updating and maintenance of professional profiles amounted to monitoring under the GDPR, bringing the company within the regulation’s jurisdiction even though it has no establishment in the European Union. The authority said this was not a simple static directory: the repeated verification of people’s professional details was treated as a form of tracking, which was enough to trigger Article 3’s monitoring criterion. ... The authority was also sceptical of Lusha’s reliance on legitimate interest. It concluded that the company lacked a valid legal basis for processing the data in the first place, and that its privacy information was neither clear nor easily accessible to the people concerned. That finding matters because data brokers often have no direct relationship with the individuals they list, leaving notice and transparency as the main safeguards available to those whose data is collected, enriched and resold. ... has been following ... as commercially important signals for platform ... , licensing, ... The order goes beyond a financial sanction. Lusha must cease processing the personal data of individuals located in Italy and delete those records, a remedy that strikes at the core of its business model rather than allowing it to continue after paying the fine. Privacy and compliance professionals have already begun debating the wider implications, particularly for companies that buy enrichment data from brokers and then rely on it for sales, marketing or anti-fraud work. ... The case also fits a broader European enforcement pattern. Recent actions in Spain and elsewhere have targeted data firms over the commercial use of personal information, while the wider debate over legitimate interest has sharpened after major rulings and guidance on behavioural advertising and web scraping. For the B2B data industry, the Italian decision is a warning that routine contact enrichment may be treated less as harmless business intelligence and more as regulated surveillance when it is done at scale and without proper safeguards."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Juspay teams with Recurly on subscription payments,ecommercenews.asia (Karen Joy Bacudo),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ecommercenews.asia/story/juspay-teams-with-recurly-on-subscription-payments,"Juspay teams with Recurly on subscription payments ... Juspay has partnered with Recurly to integrate its Hyperswitch payments platform into Recurly's subscription billing system, giving Recurly merchants access to more than 300 payment service providers and acquirers. ... The agreement connects Recurly's recurring billing software with Hyperswitch, Juspay's open-source payment orchestration platform. The integration is designed to help subscription businesses add payment providers and methods without building separate technical connections for each one. ... Under the arrangement, Recurly is also using Hyperswitch's Platform Organisation mode, allowing it to onboard and manage merchants across its customer base through a single setup. As a result, subscription companies using Recurly can connect to new providers through the same integration layer rather than making direct changes to their own payment systems. ... The partnership is intended to improve checkout and recurring payment flows for end users by expanding the range of payment options available in different markets. It is also expected to shorten the time merchants need to launch in new geographies or add local payment methods. ... Juspay provides infrastructure that sits between merchants and payment providers. It says it serves more than 500 enterprises and banks, processing more than 300 million daily transactions and more than USD $1 trillion in annualised total payment volume. ... Founded in Bangalore, Juspay has expanded across Asia-Pacific, the Middle East, Latin America, Europe, the UK and North America. The company says it employs more than 1,500 payment specialists and works with companies including Amazon, Google, HSBC, Agoda and Zurich Insurance. ... Earlier this year, Juspay raised USD $50 million in a Series D funding round led by WestBridge Capital, which valued the company at USD $1.2 billion. The fundraising highlighted investor interest in payment infrastructure groups that help merchants gain more control over how transactions are routed and managed. ... Recurly is known for subscription management and recurring billing software used by brands ranging from streaming services to airlines and software companies. The company says its platform is used by thousands of businesses, including Paramount+, Alaska Airlines, Sling, FabFitFun and Sprout Social. ... The partnership gives Recurly a broader payments network through Hyperswitch's connections to payment service providers and acquirers. That could be especially relevant for subscription businesses in markets where local payment methods or specialist acquirers are important for maintaining conversion and reducing failed renewals. ... Matt Healey, Director of Product Partnerships at Juspay, said subscription businesses need payment infrastructure that is reliable and built to scale. ... ""Subscription businesses need a payment infrastructure that is reliable and built to scale,"" said Matt Healey, Director of Product Partnerships, Juspay. ""Through Hyperswitch, we enable merchants to reduce payment friction, and expand into new markets without rebuilding their payment stack from scratch. Our partnership with Recurly brings these capabilities directly into the subscription management workflow, where payment performance matters most."" ... Recurly said the integration is intended to give merchants more flexibility in how they connect payments to their subscription operations. ... ""Flexibility and performance are non-negotiable for subscription businesses operating at global scale,"" said Jonas Flodh, Head of Strategic Partnerships, Recurly. ""By integrating Juspay Hyperswitch with Recurly's platform, merchants gain access to best-in-class integrations in a vast payments network that will open up access to new payment methods and markets."" ... Juspay has positioned Hyperswitch as an open-source alternative in a payments market often dominated by proprietary systems. The platform is designed to let merchants and platforms connect payment processing, acquiring, fraud tools, tokenisation, vaulting and 3DS authentication through a modular structure. ... For Recurly customers, the practical effect of the deal will likely depend on how quickly they can activate additional payment options and improve transaction acceptance in the markets where they operate. Access to a larger network of providers may also help subscription merchants maintain payment resilience if a single provider experiences disruption. ... Juspay said Hyperswitch has more than 42,000 stars on GitHub. ... Recurly partners Juspay to boost subscription payments"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Hush lands $30m as AI agents outpace enterprise security,fintech.global (dwillis),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fintech.global/2026/07/29/hush-lands-30m-as-ai-agents-outpace-enterprise-security/,"Hush lands $30m as AI agents outpace enterprise security ... Hush Security, a pioneer in securing the non-human workforce, has closed a $30m Series A round as enterprises scramble to govern autonomous AI agents operating inside their most critical systems. ... Akamai Technologies joined the round as a strategic investor, participating alongside existing backers Battery Ventures and YL Ventures. The raise lifts Hush’s total funding to $41m, less than a year after the company emerged from stealth. ... Hush provides a sanctioned route for AI agents to operate across enterprise systems. Each agent is enrolled in a central registry, removed from standing credentials and issued scoped just-in-time (JIT) permissions at runtime, with all activity logged and a centralised kill switch available. ... The platform’s expansion to the agentic workforce enables companies to discover every desktop assistant, enterprise AI agent and custom-built agent, whether managed or shadow, and map the MCPs, tools and resources each can access. ... It also allows firms to govern from a single point, registering agents against existing permissions and enforcing least agency by default, while maintaining a full audit trail to support security investigations, governance and compliance. ... The technology is already being adopted in the field. Kyndryl, the world’s largest IT infrastructure services provider, has rolled out Hush internally and started reselling the platform to its own enterprise customers. ... The new capital will fund growth of Hush’s engineering and sales operations, with a US focus, accelerate support for enterprise IAM and agentic ecosystems through deeper Enterprise AI platform integrations, and broaden corporate partnerships. ... Hush Security CEO and co-founder Micha Rave said, “Every company already knows how to manage identity for its people and its applications. But now software acts autonomously, on its own initiative, inside your most sensitive systems. AI agents need strict identity, not just API keys. We solved that for non-human identities, and now we’re extending governance to AI agents.”"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,"Hush Security Raises $30M to Close the AI Agent Governance Gap, with Akamai Joining as Strategic Investor",www.prnewswire.com (Hush Security),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/il/news-releases/hush-security-raises-30m-to-close-the-ai-agent-governance-gap-with-akamai-joining-as-strategic-investor-302836307.html,"Hush Security Raises $30M to Close the AI Agent Governance Gap, with Akamai Joining as Strategic Investor Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... Less than a year out of stealth, the company extends its proven identity-based approach to securely control enterprise AI agents and the infrastructure they run on – as Battery Ventures and YL Ventures double down and more Fortune 500 customers sign on ... TEL AVIV, Israel, July 28, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Hush Security, a pioneer in securing the non-human workforce, today announced a $30 million Series A funding round, with Akamai Technologies joining as a strategic investor alongside existing investors Battery Ventures and YL Ventures. Less than a year out of stealth, the round brings Hush's total capital raised to $41 million. ... That shift is already playing out on the ground for companies across the globe, including Kyndryl, the world's largest IT infrastructure services provider, which has deployed Hush internally and has begun reselling it to its own enterprise clients. ... Hush's new expansion to the agentic workforce allows companies to: ... ""A year ago, we said Hush had the right technology at the right time for machine identity,"" added Yoav Leitersdorf, Managing Partner at YL Ventures. ""That thesis has only sharpened, with AI agents already a core element in the enterprise workforce, and multiple Fortune 500 companies trusting Hush as they prioritize governance of the AI workforce. Akamai joining this round is a strong signal that the identity gateway for AI agents is quickly becoming core infrastructure, as well."" ... ""When we backed Hush at seed, static secrets were already a liability and agentic AI has turned that liability into something enterprises can't ignore,"" said Barak Schoster, Partner at Battery Ventures. ""Companies are handing autonomous software real authority over real systems, often through the same standing credentials Hush was built to eliminate. Our expanded support of Hush is a bet that proactively securing identities is what will make that authority safe to grant as we head deeper into the agentic age."" ... Hush will use the funding to expand its engineering and sales teams, particularly in the United States; accelerate support for enterprise IAM and agentic ecosystems, including deeper integrations with Enterprise AI platforms; and strengthen and expand corporate partnerships. ... Hush Security secures the entire non-human workforce – from secrets, service accounts, and other non-human identities (NHIs) to the fast-growing workforce of AI agents. The platform eliminates standing access and gives AI agents and non-human identities scoped, just in time access, every action governed, logged and revocable from one place. Founded by the team behind Meta Networks (acquired by Proofpoint in 2019) and backed by YL Ventures, Battery Ventures, and Akamai Technologies, Hush is trusted by leading enterprises worldwide. Learn more at http://www.hush.security/ www.hush.security. ... ### Hush Security Launches Free Plan to Help Teams Stop Secrets-Based Attacks ... ### Hush Security Launches the First Unified Access Management Platform for Agentic AI and Non-Human Identities ... Hush Security, an innovator in non-human identity security, today announced the general availability of its Unified Access Management Platform...."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Former Meta Networks founders raise $30 million Series A to secure the AI workforce | Ctech,www.calcalistech.com (Meir Orbach),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/sjactjlsfl,"Meta Networks founders raise $30 million Series A to secure the AI workforce | ... # Former Meta Networks founders raise $30 million Series A to secure the AI workforce ... ## Hush Security, led by the team behind the Zero Trust startup acquired by Proofpoint, is building identity infrastructure for AI agents and other non-human identities. ... Cybersecurity startup Hush Security has raised $30 million in a Series A round led by Akamai Technologies, as investors place new bets on a growing challenge created by the rise of autonomous artificial intelligence systems: how to control software agents that can act independently inside enterprise networks. ... The round, which includes participation from existing investors Battery Ventures and YL Ventures, brings Hush’s total funding since its founding in 2024 to $41 million. ... The investment comes as companies increasingly deploy AI agents capable of performing tasks without direct human involvement. According to Gartner, the average Fortune 500 company is expected to operate more than 150,000 AI agents by 2028, compared with fewer than 15 just last year. ... But the security infrastructure needed to manage ... has not kept pace. Recent research cited by ... found that ... Hush was founded in 2024 by Raveh, CTO Shmulik Ladkani, VP R&D Alon Horowitz and Chief Customer Officer Chen Nisnkorn. The founders previously worked together at Meta Networks, which developed a Zero Trust platform and was acquired by Proofpoint in 2019 for $120 million. ... Hush employs 31 people across Israel and the U.S. ... The company initially focused on the broader challenge of securing non-human identities, accounts, services and machines that operate without a person directly controlling them. It is now extending that approach to AI agents, which Hush describes as a new category of non-human workers. ... to end vaults ... The company’s platform creates a central registry for AI agents and other machine identities, connects them to existing organizational permissions, and replaces permanent credentials with just-in-time access. ... Instead of allowing an AI agent to hold long-term API keys or passwords, Hush gives it temporary permissions only when needed, while logging every action and allowing organizations to revoke access. ... The platform is designed to help companies discover all AI agents operating across cloud environments, employee devices and AI platforms; control what those agents can access; and maintain audit trails for security and compliance. ... Hush is already working with enterprise customers, including Kyndryl, the world’s largest IT infrastructure services provider. Kyndryl has deployed Hush internally and has begun offering the platform to its own customers."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Hush Security raises $30 million to expand AI agent governance platform,www.ynetnews.com (ynet Global),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ynetnews.com/business/article/s1mqixuhfx,"Hush Security raises $30 million to expand AI agent governance platform ... # Hush Security raises $30 million to expand AI agent governance platform ... ## The company says its platform gives companies a way to identify, control and audit AI agents as they act across sensitive systems, a growing security challenge as autonomous software gains broader access inside enterprises. ... Hush Security has raised $30 million in Series A funding as the company expands its identity-security platform to cover AI agents, an emerging area of enterprise risk as companies increasingly allow autonomous software to act inside sensitive systems. ... Akamai Technologies joined the round as a strategic investor, alongside existing backers Battery Ventures and YL Ventures. The new financing brings Hush’s total funding to $41 million, less than a year after the company emerged from stealth. ... Hush focuses on securing non-human identities, a category that includes secrets, service accounts, machine identities and now AI agents. The company says its platform gives enterprises a way to register AI agents, remove standing credentials and grant scoped just-in-time permissions when agents act across corporate systems. It also logs agent activity and allows organizations to revoke access from a central control point. ... The company is positioning the product as a response to a governance gap created by the rapid adoption of AI agents. Citing Gartner, Hush said the average Fortune 500 company is expected to run more than 150,000 AI agents by 2028, compared with fewer than 15 last year. It also cited Omdia research indicating that 96% of organizations are using governance models for AI agents that were not designed for them. ... AI agents are increasingly being deployed to perform tasks across enterprise applications, cloud environments and internal systems. That autonomy has created concern among security teams because agents may rely on broad or persistent credentials, making it harder to attribute actions, limit permissions or shut down activity when something goes wrong. ... “Every company already knows how to manage identity for its people and its applications,” said Micha Rave, Hush Security’s CEO and co-founder. “But now software acts autonomously, on its own initiative, inside your most sensitive systems. AI agents need strict identity, not just API keys. We solved that for non-human identities, and now we’re extending governance to AI agents.” ... The company said its expanded platform is designed to help organizations discover AI agents across managed and shadow environments, cloud systems, endpoints and AI platforms; control their permissions through a centralized registry; and audit their actions for investigations, governance and compliance. ... Investors said the company is benefiting from two converging trends: the long-standing challenge of securing machine identities and the newer risks created by AI agents acting with real authority inside corporate environments. ... Hush said it will use the funding to grow its engineering and sales teams, particularly in the United States, expand support for enterprise identity and access management systems and AI agent ecosystems, deepen integrations with enterprise AI platforms and build additional corporate partnerships. ... The company was founded by the team behind Meta Networks, which was acquired by Proofpoint in 2019."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Altus-LSA partners with Shield AI to enhance Greek drone capabilities with offensive edge | Noah Intelligence,noah-news.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://noah-news.com/altus-lsa-partners-with-shield-ai-to-enhance-greek-drone-capabilities-with-offen/,"Altus-LSA partners with Shield AI to enhance Greek drone capabilities with offensive edge | Noah Intelligence ... Altus-LSA partners with Shield AI to enhance Greek drone capabilities with offensive edge ... Greek drone manufacturer Altus-LSA has formed a strategic partnership with US defence group Shield AI, integrating their systems to bolster military offerings in Greece and beyond amidst plans for expansion and... ... Greek drone manufacturer Altus-LSA has formed a strategic partnership with US defence group Shield AI, integrating their systems to bolster military offerings in Greece and beyond amidst plans for expansion and increased production. ... ALTUS-LSA, the Greek drone maker, has struck a strategic agreement with US defence technology group Shield AI that is designed to link its KMB Hunter interception drone and M3NTOR command-and-control software with Shield AI's V-BAT unmanned aerial system and Hivemind autonomy stack. The deal signals a closer industrial relationship between the two companies and a push to create a more capable package for military users in Greece and overseas. ... At the signing in Paiania, chief executive Zacharias Saris framed the partnership as a milestone for ALTUS-LSA’s international ambitions, saying it would support the company’s growth in the fast-moving unmanned aircraft market and help meet demand from the Greek armed forces as well as other countries. He said the company’s approach with KMB centres on systems that combine effectiveness with lower cost, pointing to its ability to engage both aerial and ground targets. ... Shield AI’s regional director for eastern and south-eastern Europe, James Lythgoe, said the collaboration would deepen the American company’s presence in Greece. He described the tie-up as transformative because it adds an offensive dimension to a platform that has traditionally been used mainly for observation, while also allowing the two firms to work together on both hardware and software integration. ... The partnership comes as ALTUS-LSA prepares to scale up production. The company is said to be drawing up an expansion plan that includes increasing headcount by at least 30%, with much of the focus on KMB Hunter. ALTUS-LSA, founded in Chania in 2011 and backed 48% by VNK Capital Investments, has already built a client base that includes NATO, the OSCE, EMSA, FRONTEX and the Greek armed forces. It was recently ranked 80th among the world’s top UAV manufacturers. ... The company reported turnover of about €10 million in 2025 and is profitable, according to the material released alongside the agreement. It is aiming to broaden sales in Europe, third countries and the domestic market, while improving margins and adding technology to its product line. Shield AI, meanwhile, is planning to open an Athens office in September 2026 with an initial team of 11, from where it intends to serve customers in Greece, Cyprus and the Western Balkans."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Hush Security Raises $30 Million Series A to Expand AI Agent Security Platform | citybiz,www.citybiz.co (Sobeida Dilone),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.citybiz.co/article/879967/hush-security-raises-30-million-series-a-to-expand-ai-agent-security-platform/,"Hush Security Raises $30 Million Series A to Expand AI Agent Security Platform | citybiz ... Hush Security has raised $30 million in a Series A financing round to expand its platform for securing AI agents and other non-human identities, with Akamai Technologies joining existing investors Battery Ventures and YL Ventures. ... The funding brings the company’s total capital raised to $41 million and will support growth of its engineering and sales teams, expansion of enterprise identity and access management integrations, and broader partnerships. ... The company’s platform enables organizations to register AI agents in a centralized identity system, provide just-in-time access to enterprise resources, monitor agent activity and revoke permissions when needed. It also provides discovery, governance and audit capabilities for AI agents operating across enterprise environments. ... Hush said the new funding will also be used to expand support for enterprise AI platforms and strengthen integrations across identity and access management ecosystems. ... Founded by the team behind Meta Networks, which was acquired by Proofpoint in 2019, Hush Security develops identity security technology for AI agents, service accounts and other non-human identities. The company is backed by YL Ventures, Battery Ventures and Akamai Technologies."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Rothera adopts Eventus Validus to enhance prediction market oversight amid rising volumes | Noah Intelligence,noah-news.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://noah-news.com/rothera-adopts-eventus-validus-to-enhance-prediction-market-oversight-amid-risin/,"Rothera adopts Eventus Validus to enhance prediction market oversight amid rising volumes | Noah Intelligence ... # Rothera adopts Eventus Validus to enhance prediction market oversight amid rising volumes ... Rothera, a joint venture between Robinhood and Susquehanna, implements Eventus' Validus system to strengthen compliance and monitoring as prediction market trading volumes soar, reflecting a broader industry shift... ... Rothera, a joint venture between Robinhood and Susquehanna, implements Eventus' Validus system to strengthen compliance and monitoring as prediction market trading volumes soar, reflecting a broader industry shift towards regulated market infrastructure. ... Rothera has moved to bolster oversight of its event-contract exchange by adopting Eventus' Validus surveillance system, a step that underscores how prediction markets are being brought under the same compliance expectations long associated with futures and other regulated venues. The platform is already used across broker-dealers, futures firms and other trading businesses, and Rothera's decision signals that the sector is treating market integrity controls as core infrastructure rather than an optional extra. ... According to the company, Rothera is a joint venture between Robinhood and Susquehanna and operates as a designated contract market and derivatives clearing organisation under the supervision of the US Commodity Futures Trading Commission. It launched its first products in May, and by mid-July its World Cup markets had generated 3.5 billion traded contracts, a scale that helps explain why the exchange says it needs more sophisticated surveillance as volumes rise. ... Eventus says Validus is designed to scan orders, executions and participant behaviour for signs of manipulation, including spoofing, layering and wash trading, while also producing alerts for compliance teams to review. The company says the platform can be deployed across both fully collateralised and margined products, a useful feature for event contracts, where monitoring must cover not only familiar derivatives risks but also the possibility that traders may possess outcome-sensitive information or be able to affect an event. ... The move also reflects a broader trend among prediction market operators. Novig adopted Validus in June, while Kalshi said earlier this year that it would supplement its internal controls with technology from Solidus Labs. The CFTC has already highlighted conduct in this market that regulators and exchanges are trying to prevent, including cases involving a trader linked to a political candidacy and another person who may have had access to non-public information before publishing videos. Rothera says it needs a system capable of monitoring thousands of event contracts, with alert review and an audit trail for both internal governance and regulatory scrutiny."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Italy's privacy authority fines Lusha Systems €2 million - TopNews - Ansa.it,www.ansa.it (ANSA English Desk),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ansa.it/english/news/2026/07/27/italys-privacy-authority-fines-lusha-systems-2-million_fdc8db9b-1a50-44c0-aaf3-d6741ef17c64.html,"Italy's privacy authority fines Lusha Systems €2 million - TopNews - Ansa.it ... Italy's privacy authority fines Lusha Systems €2 million ... Italy's privacy authority fines Lusha Systems €2 million ... # Italy's privacy authority fines Lusha Systems €2 million ... Company selling data about high-ranking officials, members of judiciary says watchdog ... ROME, 27 July 2026, 16:48 ... Italy 's privacy authority fines Lusha Systems €2 million - ALL RIGHTS RESERVED ... Italy's privacy authority said Monday that has fined Lusha Systems Inc., a US-based data broker, two million euros. It said Lusha Systems sells ""enriched"" data, including job titles, email addresses, and phone numbers, and had processed the personal data of a large number of individuals in Italy ""in violation of the principles of lawfulness, fairness, transparency, and data minimization"". It said information available on the platform included data concerning high-ranking officials, civil servants, law enforcement officers, and members of the judiciary."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lesaka Unites Its Fintech Brands Under One Name - Bizmag.co.za,bizmag.co.za (Heidi Kruger),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://bizmag.co.za/lesaka-fintech-brands-united/,"# Lesaka Unites Its Fintech Brands Under One Name ... July 27, 2026 ... JSE-listed fintech group Lesaka Technologies, Inc. (Nasdaq: LSAK; JSE: LSK) is consolidating its merchant-focused businesses under the name of Lesaka. The new brand signals how Lesaka has brought together leading fintech companies into a single platform that mirrors how merchants run their businesses. ... The move follows Lesaka acquiring the Connect Group in 2021 and Adumo in 2024 to broaden its value proposition and offer a comprehensive set of solutions that address pain points for businesses in South Africa. Lesaka brings the following brands together under a single banner: ... - Cash Connect focuses on automated cash management. This entity provides automated cash vaults built to SABS Category 4 vault standards to leading South African retailers. - Capital Connect provides unsecured, hassle-free working capital of up to R5 million to retail businesses. - Kazang is a fintech that focuses on prepaid value-added services (VAS) and payments solutions for informal merchants. - Adumo is South Africa’s largest independent payments processor and brings integrated card acquiring and loyalty technology. - GAAP is the largest point of sale and software-as-a-service solutions provider to the hospitality sector in Southern Africa. ... The new brand consolidates payments, cash management and point-of-sale software solutions that were previously delivered under different names. The rebranding will deliver continuity for merchants, who will have the same access the products and services they currently use across the group companies. ... Businesses currently using any of the services now provided under Lesaka do not need to take any action. Existing terminals, software and cash management infrastructure will continue operating as before, and current account and support contacts remain unchanged. ... “We want to make it easier for merchants to do business, which means we need to be wherever they are,” says Kagiso Khaole, CEO of Lesaka Merchant Division. “Our goal is to stand alongside businesses with the human-first products and support they need to grow.The One Lesaka brand signals our commitment to this mission.” ... The consolidation underpins plans from Lesaka to offer merchants a simpler customer experience and a wider set of services. Lesaka brings everything a merchant needs to run its business together under one roof, including acquiring, cash management, lending and retail software. ... The move is the next step in a longer-term strategy to integrate the platforms of the merchants businesses Lesaka has acquired over the years. The more integrated the platform becomes, the more accessible and affordable Lesaka services will be for businesses of all sizes, from a single-store operator to a multi-site retail or restaurant group. ... JSE-listed fintech group Lesaka Technologies, Inc. (Nasdaq: LSAK; JSE: LSK) is consolidating its merchant-focused businesses under the name of Lesaka. The new brand signals how Lesaka has brought together leading fintech companies into a single platform that mirrors how merchants run their businesses. ... The move follows Lesaka acquiring the Connect Group in 2021 and Adumo in 2024 to broaden its value proposition and offer a comprehensive set of solutions that address pain points for businesses in South Africa. Lesaka brings the following brands together under a single banner: ... - Cash Connect focuses on automated cash management. This entity provides automated cash vaults built to SABS Category 4 vault standards to leading South African retailers. - Capital Connect provides unsecured, hassle-free working capital of up to R5 million to retail businesses. - Kazang is a fintech that focuses on prepaid value-added services (VAS) and payments solutions for informal merchants. - Adumo is South Africa’s largest independent payments processor and brings integrated card acquiring and loyalty technology. - GAAP is the largest point of sale and software-as-a-service solutions provider to the hospitality sector in Southern Africa. ... The new brand consolidates payments, cash management and point-of-sale software solutions that were previously delivered under different names. The rebranding will deliver continuity for merchants, who will have the same access the products and services they currently use across the group companies. ... Businesses currently using any of the services now provided under Lesaka do not need to take any action. Existing terminals, software and cash management infrastructure will continue operating as before, and current account and support contacts remain unchanged. ... “We want to make it easier for merchants to do business, which means we need to be wherever they are,” says Kagiso Khaole, CEO of Lesaka Merchant Division. “Our goal is to stand alongside businesses with the human-first products and support they need to grow.The One Lesaka brand signals our commitment to this mission.” ... The consolidation underpins plans from Lesaka to offer merchants a simpler customer experience and a wider set of services. Lesaka brings everything a merchant needs to run its business together under one roof, including acquiring, cash management, lending and retail software. ... The move is the next step in a longer-term strategy to integrate the platforms of the merchants businesses Lesaka has acquired over the years. The more integrated the platform becomes, the more accessible and affordable Lesaka services will be for businesses of all sizes, from a single-store operator to a multi-site retail or restaurant group."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,"Shush Signs Modica Group as Demand Partner to Accelerate Network Authentication Across Oceania, Asia and Latin America",www.einpresswire.com (Daryl Carlough),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.einpresswire.com/article/928851577/shush-signs-modica-group-as-demand-partner-to-accelerate-network-authentication-across-oceania-asia-and-latin-america,"Shush Signs Modica Group as Demand Partner to Accelerate Network Authentication Across Oceania, Asia and Latin America ... # Shush Signs Modica Group as Demand Partner to Accelerate Network Authentication Across Oceania, Asia and Latin America ... DALLAS, TX, UNITED STATES, July 27, 2026 / EINPresswire.com/ -- Shush Inc., the U.S.-based leader in carrier-grade network authentication, today announced that Modica Group Limited, an Australian and New Zealand-based global CPaaS platform provider, has signed an agreement to become an official Demand Partner for Mobile Network Operators utilizing the Shush award-winning Sherlock platform. This positions Modica Group as a key distribution partner for Network Authentication APIs across Oceania, Asia and Latin America, expanding Shush’s global footprint in the high-growth Asia-Pacific-Latin America market. ... Under the agreement, Modica Group will access services by utilizing carriers within Shush’s network to access their APIs on behalf of its enterprises, enabling Modica’s enterprise customers, including organizations in finance, government, retail, healthcare, and logistics, to access silent authentication, SIM swap detection, device status, and number lookup capabilities. Modica’s existing relationships with mobile network operators and enterprise accounts across Oceania, Asia and Latin America provide Shush with immediate reach into a region where mobile-first authentication is rapidly becoming a business necessity. ... Expanding the Shush Sherlock Ecosystem in Asia-Pacific-Latin AmericaModica Group operates as a trusted CPaaS platform for enterprises, telcos, and aggregators worldwide, with an established presence serving multiple customers including the Australian and New Zealand Government’s, Banking, Aviation, Logistics, and Utilities. By integrating Shush’s Sherlock platform into its security and identity product suite, Modica Group can offer its enterprise clients a frictionless, SIM-based alternative to SMS OTP, eliminating a primary attack vector for SIM swap and account takeover fraud.Shush Sherlock enables Modica Group to leverage over 47 network APIs, including 10 CAMARA Network Authentication and Identity APIs, through a single platform, enabling silent authentication, SIM swap detection, and real-time device status verification — all without user friction, OTP codes, or new app downloads. ... “Partnering with Shush gives us the ability to deliver a genuinely new category of security capability to our enterprise customers across the region. Network authentication represents the next evolution beyond SMS OTP, and Shush’s Sherlock platform is purpose-built for the carrier ecosystem we operate in. We look forward to bringing this technology to market across Oceania, Asia and Latin America.”“Partnering with Shush gives us the ability to deliver a genuinely new category of security capability to our enterprise customers across the region. Network authentication represents the next evolution beyond SMS OTP, and Shush’s Sherlock platform is purpose-built for the carrier ecosystem we operate in. We look forward to bringing this technology to market across Oceania, Asia and Latin America.”— Richard Babanour, Head of Partnerships & International Development, Modica Group Limited ... “Modica Group’s deep-rooted presence across Oceania, Asia and Latin America, combined with their enterprise messaging relationships, makes them the ideal demand partner to bring network authentication capabilities to the region. The APAC and Latin America market is primed for a shift away from SMS OTP, and Modica has the enterprise customer base and technical infrastructure to drive adoption at scale. This partnership accelerates our mission to make silent, SIM-based authentication the global standard.”— Eddie DeCurtis, Co-Founder & CEO, Shush Inc. ... About Modica GroupModica Group is the global intelligent messaging company for enterprises, telcos, and aggregators worldwide. Modica’s unified CPaaS platform supports SMS, MMS, email, WhatsApp, voice, video, push notifications, Payments, and more — backed by enterprise analytics, security, and world-class support. Trusted by organizations including the Australian and New Zealand Governments, ANZ Bank, Kiwibank, Virgin Australia, Woolworths, and New Zealand Defence Force. Modica provides mission-critical communications infrastructure across Oceania, Asia and Latin America, and beyond. Modica’s Security & ID solutions include 2(M)FA, number lookup, identity and access management, and threat intelligence capabilities.Learn more at www.modicagroup.com. ... About Shush Inc.Shush Inc. is a U.S.-based innovator in carrier-grade identity and fraud prevention. Through its Sherlock platform, Shush enables mobile network operators to expose secure APIs that deliver real-time signals for SIM swap detection, device validation, and other critical fraud indicators, while generating new revenue streams. Shush helps telecom operators globally transform their networks into strategic anti-fraud infrastructure.Learn more at www.shush.pw Follow Modica on LinkedIn at https://www.linkedin.com/company/modica-group-ltd/"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Ushur launches the Ushur Agentic Platform: AI agents that,www.globenewswire.com (Ushur),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/22/3331397/0/en/Ushur-launches-the-Ushur-Agentic-Platform-AI-agents-that-finish-the-job.html,"Ushur launches the Ushur Agentic Platform: AI agents that ... # Ushur launches the Ushur Agentic Platform: AI agents that finish the job ... ## Enterprises describe a customer experience in plain language and deploy AI agents that carry it all the way to done, with built-in governance forged in regulated industries ... , 2 ... :00 ... ur Ushur ... SANTA CLARA, Calif., July 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Ushur today announced the Ushur Agentic Platform (UAP), a platform for building and operating AI agents designed to complete customer journeys from first contact to final resolution. ... intent, gather information, retrieve documents, act across ... member's ... , moving an ... , onboarding a banking customer ... Ushur has served insurance, healthcare, and financial services for more than a decade, and the platform carries that history. Governance, security, compliance, auditability, and human oversight are embedded into every interaction as core elements of Ushur's trust-native architecture. ... Initial UAP use cases include servicing health plan members, Medicaid redetermination, and automating ride requests for member transportation. ... The platform also enables partners to build industry-specific customer experiences. “Build on Ushur” ships with more than 200 integrations to enterprise systems, and more connectors are coming, so partners can deliver agentic customer experiences for their own markets. ... “Everyone has taught AI to talk,” said Simha Sadasiva, CEO and Co-founder of Ushur. “The bar now is whether the claim gets paid, the member gets enrolled, and the customer walks away done. We built the Ushur Agentic Platform so AI agents can complete work end to end, with the governance regulated industries demand.” ... Ushur is the most comprehensive platform for agentic customer experiences. The Ushur Agentic Platform enables organizations to build and operate AI agents that complete customer journeys from first contact to final resolution. By combining AI agents, omnichannel engagement, document intelligence, enterprise integrations, and trust-native governance, Ushur helps organizations deliver customer experiences with the control, security, and compliance enterprises require. ... June 30, 2026 10:00 ET | Source: Ushur ... Gartner® Predicts 70% of Payers Will Address Workflow, Data and Service Automation using No-Code AI Agent Builders (NCABs) by 2028; Ushur Named a Representative Provider ... Gartner® predicts 70% of payers will use no-code agent builders by 2028; Ushur is listed as a Representative Provider."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Recurly partners Juspay to boost subscription payments,ecommercenews.com.au (Karen Joy Bacudo),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ecommercenews.com.au/story/recurly-partners-juspay-to-boost-subscription-payments,"urly partners Juspay to boost subscription payments ... # Recurly partners Juspay to boost subscription payments ... Juspay has partnered with Recurly to integrate its Hyperswitch payments platform into Recurly's subscription management platform, giving Recurly merchants access to more than 300 payment service providers and acquirers through a single integration. ... The integration is aimed at subscription businesses that want to add payment providers and local payment methods without rebuilding existing payment systems. Recurly is also using Hyperswitch's Platform Organisation mode to onboard and manage merchants programmatically across its portfolio. ... Under the arrangement, merchants using Recurly can connect to a broad payments network through Hyperswitch instead of setting up separate integrations with each provider. The approach is intended to shorten the time needed to enter new markets and expand payment options. ... Juspay describes Hyperswitch as an open-source payment orchestration platform that connects with more than 300 payment service providers and acquirers globally. It is designed to give merchants and platforms direct control over how they manage payments. ... Recurly provides subscription management and recurring billing for businesses in sectors including digital media, streaming, eCommerce, software and consumer goods. Adding Hyperswitch brings payment routing and provider access closer to the subscription workflow those merchants already use. ... The partnership reflects a wider push among subscription businesses to reduce involuntary churn, which often occurs when recurring transactions fail because of card issues, routing problems or gaps in local payment support. Improving payment success rates has become a commercial priority for companies that depend on recurring revenue. ... For platforms such as Recurly, offering access to multiple payment providers through one connection can also reduce integration work for merchants. That can be especially relevant for businesses expanding internationally, where local customer preferences and acquiring arrangements vary widely by market. ... ""Subscription businesses need a payment infrastructure that is reliable and built to scale,"" said Matt Healey, Director of Product Partnerships, Juspay. ""Through Hyperswitch, we enable merchants to reduce payment friction and expand into new markets without rebuilding their payment stack from scratch. Our partnership with Recurly brings these capabilities directly into the subscription management workflow, where payment performance matters most."" ... Recurly said the agreement is intended to widen the payment choices available to merchants using its platform. It framed flexibility in payments as a central requirement for subscription companies operating internationally. ... ""Flexibility and performance are non-negotiable for subscription businesses operating at global scale,"" said Jonas Flodh, Head of Strategic Partnerships, Recurly. ""By integrating Juspay Hyperswitch with Recurly's platform, merchants gain access to best-in-class integrations in a vast payments network that will open up access to new payment methods and markets."" ... Juspay says it serves more than 500 enterprises and banks and processes more than 300 million transactions a day. Its annualised total payment volume exceeds USD $1 trillion. ... Founded in 2012, the business is headquartered in Bangalore and operates across Asia-Pacific, the Middle East, Latin America, Europe, the UK and North America. It employs more than 1,500 payments specialists and works with companies including Amazon, Google, HSBC, Agoda and Zurich Insurance. ... Juspay was valued at USD $1.2 billion in a USD $50 million Series D funding round led by WestBridge Capital. Existing backers include SoftBank, VEF, Wellington Management, Accel and Kedaara Capital. ... Juspay positions Hyperswitch as an open-source system for integrating payment processing, acquiring, fraud tools, tokenisation, vaulting and 3DS authentication. The software has attracted more than 42,000 stars on GitHub, according to the company. ... Recurly, based in Austin with offices including London and Medellín, says thousands of brands use it. Its customer base includes Paramount+, Alaska Airlines, Sling, FabFitFun and Sprout Social. ... The partnership links a subscription billing platform with a payments orchestration system at a time when merchants are under pressure to improve recurring transaction success while adapting payment options market by market."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Can Tether and Busha Build the Financial Rails African Businesses Need to Compete Globally? - Africa Digest News,fintechnews.co.ke,2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fintechnews.co.ke/can-tether-and-busha-build-the-financial-rails-african-businesses-need-to-compete-globally/,"Busha Business has partnered with Tether, the issuer of USDt and the largest company in the digital asset industry. ... This Busha Tether stablecoin Africa business collaboration expands access to licensed stablecoin infrastructure for companies operating across the continent. ... Busha Business is the B2B infrastructure arm of Busha, one of Africa’s licensed stablecoin and payments platforms. ... Moyo Sodipo, Busha’s co-founder and COO, said businesses need financial infrastructure that moves at the speed of modern commerce. ... He described the collaboration as giving businesses access to globally connected liquidity on licensed infrastructure. ... That infrastructure is built for faster payments, stronger treasury management, and more efficient international trade. ... He called it another step toward building the financial rails African businesses need to compete globally. ... By tapping into Tether’s global ecosystem, Busha Business gives companies access to stablecoin liquidity that supports international commerce. ... Busha Business tackles this through several connected products. ... Businesses can accept international payments from customers worldwide through Busha Pay, with settlement handled in USD. ... The platform’s business savings products go a step further. Companies can earn daily yields on idle USD and Naira balances. ... These returns come through licensed third-party asset management partners, offering market-driven rates rather than funds simply sitting unused. ... #### Who Busha Business Nigeria Kenya Fintech Serves ... Busha Business Nigeria Kenya fintech operations currently span these two markets. ... The platform serves a wide range of business types. Large corporates, importers and exporters, e-commerce merchants, SMEs, fintech companies, and developers building financial products all use Busha Business infrastructure. ... The full range of services includes cross-border payments, stablecoin treasury management, business savings, merchant payment solutions, and API infrastructure for other fintechs and developers to build on. ... All of this runs on Busha’s SEC-licensed foundation, giving the platform a regulated base for handling business transactions across African markets. ... This partnership builds on views Busha’s leadership has voiced publicly before. ... Speaking earlier this year at the Africa Tech Summit in Nairobi, Sodipo called for greater use of African and locally relevant stablecoin infrastructure. ... His argument centered on improving trade across Sub-Saharan Africa while reducing reliance on legacy payment systems that were never built with African markets in mind. ... That philosophy shapes how Busha Business approaches this Tether partnership. ... Rather than treating stablecoins as a speculative asset class, the company positions them as practical financial plumbing. ... The goal is moving money faster, managing treasury more efficiently, and settling international trade with fewer intermediaries slowing things down. ... #### What This Means for African Businesses Competing Globally ... The core question behind this partnership is whether stablecoin infrastructure can genuinely become the financial rail African businesses use to compete on a global stage. ... Traditional banking channels have long added delays and costs to cross-border transactions involving African companies. ... If Tether’s global liquidity network combined with Busha’s licensed local infrastructure can meaningfully cut those delays, the impact could extend well beyond convenience. ... For SMEs and larger corporates alike, faster settlement and better treasury tools translate directly into more competitive positioning against international counterparts. ... As more African fintechs pursue similar stablecoin partnerships, this collaboration offers an early signal of how digital dollar infrastructure might reshape the practical mechanics of doing business across and beyond the continent."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Busha Business and Tether Partner to Expand Stablecoin Infrastructure for African Businesses - TechAfrica News,techafricanews.com (Jennifer Onyeagoro),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://techafricanews.com/2026/07/20/busha-business-and-tether-partner-to-expand-stablecoin-infrastructure-for-african-businesses/,"Busha Business and Tether Partner to Expand Stablecoin Infrastructure for African Businesses - TechAfrica News ... # Busha Business and Tether Partner to Expand Stablecoin Infrastructure for African Businesses ... July 20, 2026 ... The collaboration enables businesses to access globally connected stablecoin liquidity for faster cross-border payments, more efficient treasury management, and quicker settlement of international transactions, reducing many of the delays and costs associated with traditional banking channels. ... Busha Business, the B2B infrastructure arm of Busha, has collaborated with Tether, the largest company in the digital asset industry and the issuer of USD₮, to expand access to licensed stablecoin infrastructure for African businesses. ... The collaboration enables businesses to access globally connected stablecoin liquidity for faster cross-border payments, more efficient treasury management, and quicker settlement of international transactions, reducing many of the delays and costs associated with traditional banking channels. ... This announcement comes as businesses across Africa increasingly seek faster and more reliable ways to move money internationally. Cross-border payments remain expensive and slow, treasury management has become more complex amid currency volatility, and fragmented banking systems continue to create friction for businesses operating across multiple markets. At the same time, the International Monetary Fund recently noted that Nigeria ranks second globally on Chainalysis’ Crypto Adoption Index and highlighted the importance of regulated infrastructure to support continued adoption. ... Built on Busha’s SEC-licensed digital asset foundation, Busha Business was created to meet that need by providing compliant financial infrastructure that helps businesses move, manage, and grow money across borders. ... Today, Busha Business serves more than 1,500 businesses across Nigeria and Kenya. In Kenya alone, more than 250 businesses process millions of Kenyan shillings in daily transactions through the platform to pay international suppliers, manage treasury operations, and settle cross-border payments. ... By leveraging Tether’s global ecosystem, Busha Business provides businesses with access to stablecoin liquidity that supports international commerce, simplifies treasury operations, and reduces dependence on slower, more expensive payment rails. ... Busha Business serves large corporates, importers and exporters, e-commerce merchants, SMEs, fintech companies, and developers building financial products for African markets. Through Busha Pay, businesses can accept international payments from customers worldwide, with settlement in USD. In contrast, its business savings products enable companies to earn daily yields on idle USD and Naira balances, offering highly competitive, market-driven rates powered by licensed third-party asset management partners. ... The collaboration reflects a broader shift in global commerce as businesses increasingly adopt stablecoins for international payments, liquidity management, and treasury operations. Rather than treating stablecoins solely as investment assets, businesses are using them as practical financial infrastructure and quicker settlement rails for everyday commercial activity. ... The announcement also builds on Busha’s long-term vision of expanding stablecoin-powered financial infrastructure across Africa. Earlier this year, speaking at Africa Tech Summit Nairobi, Busha Co-founder and COO Moyo Sodipo called for greater usage of African and locally relevant stablecoin infrastructure to improve trade across Sub-Saharan Africa and reduce reliance on legacy payment systems built for other markets. ... “Businesses need financial infrastructure that moves at the speed of modern commerce. Through our collaboration with Tether, we are giving businesses access to globally connected liquidity on licensed infrastructure designed for faster payments, stronger treasury management, and more efficient international trade. This is another step toward building the financial rails that African businesses need to compete globally.” ... As African businesses continue to expand beyond their domestic markets, demand for regulated stablecoin infrastructure is expected to grow alongside the increasing adoption of digital assets for commercial use. Collaboration between licensed regional infrastructure providers and global stablecoin networks will play an important role in shaping how businesses access capital, settle international transactions, and participate in the global economy."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,"Shush Inc. Welcomes Infobip as Global Demand Partner, Expanding Network Authentication Reach",www.einpresswire.com (Daryl Carlough),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.einpresswire.com/article/928031206/shush-inc-welcomes-infobip-as-global-demand-partner-expanding-network-authentication-reach,"Shush Inc. Welcomes Infobip as Global Demand Partner, Expanding Network Authentication Reach ... # Shush Inc. Welcomes Infobip as Global Demand Partner, Expanding Network Authentication Reach ... DALLAS, TX, UNITED STATES, July 20, 2026 / EINPresswire.com/ -- Shush Inc., the U.S.-based innovator in carrier-grade network authentication and fraud prevention, today announced a strategic demand partnership with Infobip, the global AI-first cloud communications platform behind billions of customer conversations across 6 continents. Under this agreement, Infobip will integrate into the Shush Sherlock platform into its industry-leading communications stack, enabling Infobip’s enterprise customers worldwide to access silent authentication, SIM swap detection, device status verification, and number lookup capabilities, all delivered through GSMA Open Gateway–compliant APIs. ... Digital fraud is not a regional challenge. It is a global one. Infobip’s global footprint and its direct relationships with enterprise customers in finance, retail, healthcare, telecoms, logistics, and government make it uniquely positioned to accelerate the adoption of network authentication at a scale no other demand partner has yet reached. For Shush, this partnership is a force multiplier: Infobip’s commercial reach, developer ecosystem, and enterprise trust allow Sherlock’s capabilities to be deployed into markets and use cases that would otherwise take years to penetrate independently.Infobip was founded in 2006 in Croatia by Silvio Kutić and Izabel Jelenić with a mission to democratize communication, making it more accessible, intuitive, and meaningful for everyone, everywhere. 20 years later, Infobip grew into one of the most recognized communications platforms in the world, operating from more than 75 offices, employing 3,500+ people, serving global clients and partnering with global organizations. The company has been named a Leader in the Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for CPaaS four consecutive times, most recently in 2026, where it was positioned furthest for Completeness of Vision. ... Through the Shush–Infobip demand partnership, Infobip will leverage mobile network operators within the Shush carrier network to access Sherlock’s suite of GSMA Open Gateway and CAMARA-compliant authentication APIs on behalf of its enterprise customers. The global communications industry is undergoing a structural shift. Enterprises are moving away from knowledge-based and OTP-based authentication toward network-native, invisible, and biometrically anchored identity verification. The GSMA Open Gateway initiative, now being adopted by dozens of operators globally, provides the regulatory and technical framework for this transition. Shush’s Sherlock platform was built from the ground up to be fully compliant with this framework, and Infobip’s participation in the Shush ecosystem signals that the transition is accelerating. Together, Shush and Infobip are positioned to define the next generation of enterprise identity security. ... Executive Perspectives“Shush represents the kind of foundational infrastructure the communications industry has needed for years. Network-native authentication is the inevitable future and Shush has built the right platform at the right moment. Infobip’s global scale and reach give Sherlock the distribution it deserves, and together we will bring a new standard of security to our enterprise customers worldwide.”— Matija Ražem, Chief Commercial Telecom Officer, Infobip ... “Infobip’s early support was instrumental in helping Shush find its footing and its confidence. They understood the opportunity before most of the market did, and that kind of belief from a market leader of this caliber means everything to a young company. Having Infobip — with its extraordinary global reach, its enterprise trust, and its technical depth — as a formal demand partner is a defining moment for Shush. This partnership puts Sherlock’s capabilities in front of some of the world’s largest enterprises, and it puts us one step closer to making carrier-grade silent authentication the global default.”— Eddie DeCurtis, Co-Founder & Chief Executive Officer, Shush Inc. ... About InfobipInfobip is a global cloud communications platform that enables businesses to build connected experiences across all stages of the customer journey, with AI as the driving force of innovation. Through a single, natively built platform, Infobip delivers omnichannel engagement, identity, user authentication, and contact centre solutions that help businesses and partners overcome the complexity of consumer communications while driving growth and increasing customer loyalty. Infobip is focused on enabling and accelerating AI adoption as it continues its transformation into an AI-first company. Infobip’s technology has the capacity to reach over seven billion mobile devices in 6 continents, connected to 10k+ connections, of which 800+ are direct operator connections. The company was established in 2006 and is led by its co-founders, CEO Silvio Kutić and CTO Izabel Jelenić.Learn more at www.infobip.com. ... About Shush Inc.Shush Inc. is a U.S.-based innovator in carrier-grade identity and fraud prevention. Through its award-winning Sherlock platform, Shush enables mobile network operators to expose secure, GSMA Open Gateway–compliant APIs that deliver real-time signals for silent authentication, SIM swap detection, device status verification, and number lookup, all without user friction, OTP codes, or app downloads. Shush helps telecom operators globally transform their networks into strategic anti-fraud infrastructure while generating new revenue streams. Sherlock supports 47+ CAMARA-compliant APIs and is purpose-built for rapid integration by CPaaS providers, enterprise software platforms, and financial institutions worldwide."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,ShelterZoom subsidiary Mithra launches AI 'trust infrastructure' platform - SiliconANGLE,siliconangle.com (Duncan Riley),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://siliconangle.com/2026/07/20/shelterzoom-subsidiary-mithra-launches-ai-trust-infrastructure-platform/,"ShelterZoom subsidiary Mithra launches AI 'trust infrastructure' platform - SiliconANGLE ... ### ShelterZoom subsidiary Mithra launches AI ‘trust infrastructure’ platform ... Mithra Technologies Inc., a subsidiary of blockchain and document-security company ShelterZoom Corp., today launched Mithra AI, a product built to vet the data behind an enterprise artificial intelligence answer before the model ever produces it. ... The platform sits underneath the major commercial models, among them OpenAI Group PBC’s systems, Anthropic PBC’s Claude, Google LLC’s Gemini, Microsoft Corp.’s Copilot and Space Exploration Technologies Corp.’s Grok. Some customers connect through an application programming interface or software development kit. Others go through original equipment manufacturer partners and the largest buy a full enterprise deployment. ... The security layer draws on ShelterZoom’s roots. Mithra logs a chain of custody for each record and wraps it in post-quantum, blockchain-based encryption. The company says that setup cuts hallucinations and catches unauthorized or unlicensed data before it turns into a compliance problem. ... A lighter version targets buyers with less technical muscle. It ships as an AI-native content management system. The company likens it to a security deposit box for corporate files and intellectual property. Mithra is aiming at fields where a wrong or leaked answer gets expensive fast, including healthcare, government, financial services, legal and education. ... “Mithra was built around one simple belief: the future of AI depends on trust,” said Chao Cheng-Shorland, co-founder and chief executive of ShelterZoom and Mithra Technologies. She likened the new category to cybersecurity, which she pegged at more than $200 billion and called a foundational layer of the internet. ... ShelterZoom has used the Mithra name before. In 2019 it belonged to a blockchain smart contract platform. Last October the company carved Mithra out as a separate subsidiary and pointed it at AI data provenance. ... Early users include Conscience IQ. Founder Kirby de Lanerolle said Mithra lets his firm run AI inside tight governance limits on healthcare and defense projects. Dr. Barry Morgan, who founded the healthcare group Sage Matters, said his team plans to bring in the platform to square AI tools with the privacy demands of the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act. ... Mithra AI is available now. Companies can sign up on the Mithra platform directly or license the technology through enterprise and OEM agreements."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Busha Business has collaborated with Tether.io to expand licensed stablecoin infrastructure for African businesses. | Techpoint Africa,www.linkedin.com (Techpoint Africa),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/techpointafrica_busha-business-has-collaborated-with-tetherio-activity-7484911616770064384-WEXm,"# Busha Business Expands Stablecoin Infrastructure with Tether.io ... Busha Business has collaborated with Tether.io to expand licensed stablecoin infrastructure for African businesses. Built on Busha’s SEC-licensed foundation, the collaboration aims to support faster cross-border payments, stablecoin treasury management and international settlements. Busha Business currently serves 1,500+ businesses across Nigeria and Kenya, providing financial infrastructure for cross-border commerce. Read more: https://lnkd.in/gV6X6fwR-Brand Press ... Busha Business has partnered with Tether.io to expand access to stablecoin-powered financial infrastructure for businesses across Africa. Built on Busha's SEC-licensed platform, the collaboration supports faster cross-border payments, treasury management and international settlements. Busha Business serves more than 1,500 businesses in Nigeria and Kenya, including over 250 Kenyan firms processing millions of shillings in daily transactions."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,FIS Adopts AI Tool to Scrutinize Software and other Digital Transactions News briefs from 7/17/26 – Digital Transactions,www.digitaltransactions.net (Digital Transactions News staff),2026-07-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.digitaltransactions.net/fis-adopts-ai-tool-to-scrutinize-software-and-other-digital-transactions-news-briefs-from-7-17-26/,"FIS Adopts AI Tool to Scrutinize Software and other Digital Transactions News briefs from 7/17/26 – Digital Transactions ... # FIS Adopts AI Tool to Scrutinize Software and other Digital Transactions News briefs from 7/17/26 ... - Payments processor FIS Inc. said it has adopted Project Glasswing, a system from Anthropic that relies on AI to detect and fix security weaknesses in software. As part of the initiative, FIS is also testing Anthropic’s Mythos 5 AI model to scan its operating systems. ... - Payments platform Lightspeed Commerce Inc. announced a number of new products and services for both its retail and restaurant divisions, including customer prompts on Lightspeed Scanner to increase basket sizes and a dashboard for multi-location operations to manage multiple venues. ... - Property management platform ID Plans said its ID Tenant launched a payments service through the embedded-payments provider Payabli to offer full and partial rent-payment plans to tenants. ID Plans works primarily with commercial real estate."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,The Data Decay Report: H1 2026 | Lusha,www.lusha.com (Nirit Braun),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lusha.com/blog/data-decay-report-h1-2026/,"The Data Decay Report: H1 2026 | Lusha ... If your CRM snapshotted 25 fast-moving accounts on January 1, how much of it would still be true by June? We ran that test on live Lusha signal data. The answer: at 23 of 25 companies, something material changed — and the most damaging changes are exactly the ones threshold-based alerts are built to miss. ... All data in this report is drawn directly from Lusha’s live signal database — monthly headcount tracking, executive-move events, and funding signals for 25 named AI-native companies, January 1 to June 22, 2026. This is a focused sample of named companies, not a full population census. Source: Lusha live signal database, pulled June 22, 2026. ... one executive move ... three categories at once | ... team monitoring this account with a standard alert ... notify me if headcount moves 10 ... have received nothing ... Five alert checks, five passes, and at ... the account is ... growth assumptions the January plan made are wrong. And this wasn’ ... a story anyone ... the news instead: ... layoff was announced, ... public layoff trackers list ... layoffs for the ... in this period. ... dangerous decay pattern precisely because ... Cursor’s tracked headcount record shows 53 employees in January 2026. One month later: 1,988. That is not hiring — no company staffs up 1,935 people in four weeks. What happened is simpler and more damning: the record was frozen. Public reporting puts the company at roughly 60 employees in March 2025, growing to nearly 2,000 within a year — one of the fastest scale-ups in software. The tracked profile held the early-2025 figure while the real company 30x’d underneath it, then snapped to reality in a single update. The same class of record-identity problem surfaced elsewhere in this sample: the company Writer still returns under its pre-rebrand legal name, Qordoba, and Cursor itself is legally Anysphere, Inc., doing business as Cursor— a naming split that makes profile fragmentation easy ... Here’s why this matters more than a data-trivia footnote. A CRM that synced this account in January carried a record saying 53 employees — an SMB, routed to an SMB rep, priced for an SMB deal. By June, the reality was a roughly 2,400-person company that SpaceX had agreed to acquire for $60 billion. Every downstream decision built on the January record — segmentation, territory, tiering, deal sizing — was wrong, not by degrees but by category. And unlike the slow leak, this failure announces itself loudly in the data and is still routinely missed, because nobody re-checks a field that was “verified” five months ago. ... This is one sample over one half-year, in the fastest-moving category in software — AI-native companies are the stress test, not the average, and decay in a portfolio of regional manufacturers will run slower. But the three patterns aren’t category-specific. Slow leaks, identity events, and ghost signals exist in every account base; the AI-native sample just compresses them into a timeframe where you can watch them happen. As more GTM teams wire signals directly into automated outreach, the cost of each pattern goes up: an automation acting on a ghost signal or a pre-rebrand record doesn’t just log a bad data point, it sends the email. The teams that win with signal automation will be the ones that build these three checks in before scaling the sends, not after the first embarrassing sequence goes out. ... Data source: Lusha live signals API — monthly headcount tracking, executive hire/departure events (with publish and effective dates), and funding/investment events. Pulled June 22, 2026. ... Sample: 25 named AI-native companies across foundation model labs, AI coding tools, AI customer service platforms, and AI-native infrastructure vendors. A sample study, not a census. ... Material change definition: a company counts as materially changed if, between January 1 and June 22, 2026, at least one of the following occurred: detected headcount moved 10% or more in any tracked window; at least one executive hire or departure was detected with a 2026 event or publish date; or at least one funding, strategic investment, or asset investment event was detected. 23 of 25 companies met at least one criterion; 11 met all three. ... 1,437 ... % contraction. ... No. This is a focused sample of 25 named AI-native companies tracked through Lusha’s live signal data — a deliberately fast-moving category chosen because it compresses decay patterns into an observable window. It shows verified patterns across that sample, not population-wide decay rates. ... ### Lusha’s US data by industry: where hit rate holds, and where it dips ... ### How accurate is Lusha’s US contact data? We tested it across metros and company sizes ... ### Lusha vs. ZoomInfo hit rate: native data vs. a 25-vendor waterfall"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Cents Acquires Insight Systems To Expand Laundry Industry Data And Reporting,pulse2.com (Amit Chowdhry),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pulse2.com/cents-acquires-insight-systems-to-expand-laundry-industry-data-and-reporting/,"Cents Acquires Insight Systems To Expand Laundry Industry Data And Reporting ... Cents Acquires Insight Systems To Expand Laundry Industry Data And Reporting ... Cents has acquired Insight Systems, a business intelligence, dashboarding, and reporting platform developed for the garment care industry. The financial terms of the transaction were not disclosed. ... The acquisition will integrate Insight Systems’ data and reporting capabilities into the Cents platform, providing laundromat and dry-cleaning operators with a more centralized view of their businesses. ... Insight Systems’ team will also join Cents and help expand the company’s software and payments products for dry cleaners. Industry veterans Wash Respess and Joe Patalano will play leading roles in that effort. ... The transaction follows Cents’ $140 million Series C financing, which closed in March 2026. Cents described the round as the largest single software investment made in the laundry and garment care industry. ... Cents plans to use the additional resources to develop specialized technology for laundromats, dry cleaners, self-service businesses, route operators, and multifamily laundry providers. ... Insight Systems provides business intelligence tools designed specifically for garment care operators. Its platform offers data visualization, advanced reporting, automated customer tagging, dashboards, and marketing capabilities. ... Following the acquisition, Insight Systems’ reporting tools will be incorporated into Cents’ broader platform, which already provides point-of-sale software, payment technology, marketing automation, pickup and delivery management, and AI-powered customer service tools. ... Cents said the integration will help operators better understand financial performance, customer behavior, transaction activity, and operational trends without relying on multiple disconnected systems. ... The acquisition is also intended to accelerate Cents’ expansion within the dry cleaning market. ... Cents has previously supported dry cleaners, but the company described the transaction as a significant step toward building a more comprehensive platform specifically designed for dry cleaning operations. ... Wash Respess will join Cents as General Manager of Dry Cleaning and lead the company’s strategy for the sector. ... Together, Respess and Patalano will help Cents add functionality for advanced dry cleaning operators while integrating Insight Systems’ reporting and business intelligence technology into the existing platform. ... Cents said its dry cleaning expansion will not reduce its investment in laundromats, self-service locations, route operators, or other existing customer groups. ... The company plans to build separate, specialized product experiences for each segment rather than offering a single, standardized system for every type of laundry operation. ... Cents currently serves more than 5,000 garment care locations that collectively process over $1 billion in annual payments. ... Its platform combines software, hardware, and payment-processing capabilities, enabling operators to manage transactions, machines, marketing, customer communication, delivery services, and business reporting through a single technology provider. ... expected to continue ... integration process. ... The companies will work to integrate their products while continuing to collect feedback from garment care businesses on additional features and operational tools. ... “From the day we started Cents, our mission has been to give independent operators the tools to run every part of their business with confidence. We’ve always believed better decisions start with better data, and Wash, Joe, and the Insight Systems team built the best reporting and intelligence technology our industry has ever seen. Bringing Insight Systems into Cents means our laundromat customers get even more powerful tools to understand and grow their business, and it gives us the foundation to build something the dry cleaning industry has never had. This is an investment in the customers we serve today and the operators we will serve tomorrow.” ... “I’ve seen dry cleaning from every angle: as an operator, as a product builder inside the software serving this industry, and as someone who set out to build what was missing. What we built at Insight Systems is the foundation, and now, as part of Cents, we get to take it further. The industry has been waiting for this.” ... “I’ve spent nearly 30 years building software for this industry. When I met Alex and saw what Cents had built, the decision was clear. They’re not carrying legacy constraints, they have the team and capital to execute, and now we get to add the features advanced dry cleaning operations actually need, right into a platform that’s already proven with laundromats. Pair that with what Wash knows about running these businesses, and dry cleaners finally get a partner built for how they actually work.”"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,"Big day for Lusha, we're launching a new plugin in Codex available to everyone in ChatGPT. | Yoni Tserruya",www.linkedin.com (Yoni Tserruya),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.linkedin.com/posts/yonitserruya_big-day-for-lusha-were-launching-a-new-activity-7482793111304167424-vW8Q,"Lusha Plugin Now Available in Codex for Everyone | Yoni Tserruya posted on the topic | LinkedIn ... Big day for Lusha, we're launching a new plugin in Codex available to everyone in ChatGPT. Here’s what you can do with it now. Start simple: > Build prospect lists > Enrich companies and contacts > Find decision makers using live buying signals Then take it further: → Build your own GTM intelligence systems → Create AI-powered workflows that find, score, and prioritize accounts → Stack signals like funding, hiring, leadership changes, and ICP fit → Turn your lists into actionable recommendations for your team Anyone can ask their AI agent ""Find me leads."" Now you can ask Codex: ""Build my business a GTM system powered by Lusha’s verified B2B data and real-world signals that continuously finds my next best customers, explains why they fit, and tells me why now is the right time to reach out."" Start here: Codex ➡️ Plugins ➡️ Search “Lusha” ➡️ Install ➡️ Authorize Huge thanks to everyone on the team who made this happen 👏 👏 ... GTM teams can ask Codex to find their next customers before their competitors even know they are in market! That's not just a sales plugin, that's competitive advantage as we see it. ... We just added another plugin to a system that can prioritize accounts and stack buying signals. If you still think Lusha is just a data provider, you haven't been paying attention. - we're way past that. ... Finally! every connector and plug we add is another place our users can reach Lusha without breaking their flow. GPT, now Codex, same verified data and signals. Less friction, more reach, more reasons to start a search wherever you already work. love this ... All around the world founders and GTM teams are asking what are the best plugins for Codex in ChatGPT? well, here's a new answer: the Lusha plugin is now LIVE in ChatGPT and Codex (am I doing this right, Ohad Zafrir?) ... ChatGPT just became a lot better at company research. 👀 PredictLeads is now available in ChatGPT’s Plugin Directory, bringing real-time company intelligence directly into your conversations. Instead of switching between databases, dashboards and spreadsheets, you can simply ask ChatGPT to: ☑️ Find companies hiring for specific roles ☑️ Identify businesses using particular technologies ☑️ Track financing rounds and company news ☑️ Explore portfolios and similar companies ☑️ Research and enrich individual businesses ☑️ Build highly targeted company lists ☑️And much, much more. Ask a question. Get structured company data. Continue working without leaving ChatGPT. 🦾 🤖 Turn ChatGPT into a powerful company research tool with PredictLeads and get 100 free API calls when you create an account. https://lnkd.in/e2KmBqAp ... Well, the “next step” did not stay a surprise for very long. 😅 A few days ago, I wrote about PredictLeads becoming available in Claude Code’s Connectors Directory and how every new integration opens another door. Now the next one is already open. 🚪 PredictLeads is officially available in ChatGPT’s Plugin Directory. The goal was never to build one integration, celebrate it and move on. The goal is to make PredictLeads available wherever people already work, research, automate and make decisions. First > data marketplaces. Then > workflow tools. Then > Claude. Now > ChatGPT. And other are allready lined up! Step by step, PredictLeads is moving closer to the user and further away from being “just another API.” You can now ask ChatGPT to research companies, find hiring signals, explore technologies, track financing events and build targeted company lists using real-time PredictLeads data. No extra dashboard. No complicated setup. Just ask. 🦾 ... ChatGPT just became a lot better at company research. 👀 PredictLeads is now available in ChatGPT’s Plugin Directory, bringing real-time company intelligence directly into your conversations. Instead of switching between databases, dashboards and spreadsheets, you can simply ask ChatGPT to: ☑️ Find companies hiring for specific roles ☑️ Identify businesses using particular technologies ☑️ Track financing rounds and company news ☑️ Explore portfolios and similar companies ☑️ Research and enrich individual businesses ☑️ Build highly targeted company lists ☑️And much, much more. Ask a question. Get structured company data. Continue working without leaving ChatGPT. 🦾 🤖 Turn ChatGPT into a powerful company research tool with PredictLeads and get 100 free API calls when you create an account. https://lnkd.in/e2KmBqAp ... mentions, citations on ... , review velocity. Once a competitor stacks enough ... and the cite-rate ... later costs 3 ... we've gotten ... the top 3 ... last 6 months ... what the next 6 ... are more likely to ... from any other channel. ... data (via ... puts a number on it: 📊 ... 49% of the time, about 10 ... likely reason? They already did their research inside the assistant, so they ... further along in ... decision. Which raises one question: is ... can only recommend what ... reads, and ... reads third-party articles, not your ... . That's what ... building earns: you ... cited for, and our ... from."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lotus Microsystems Advances AI Power Delivery with Silicon Power Interposer Technology,www.everythingpe.com,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.everythingpe.com/news/details/10702-lotus-microsystems-advances-ai-power-delivery-with-silicon-power-interposer-technology,"10702- ... -power-delivery- ... # Lotus Microsystems Advances AI Power Delivery with Silicon Power Interposer Technology July 13, 2026 | everything PE https://www.everythingpe.com https://cdn.everythingpe.com/images/logo.png 240 70 Editorial Team As artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, and high-performance computing (HPC) systems continue to demand unprecedented processing power, conventional power delivery architectures are reaching their physical and thermal limits. Lotus Microsystems is addressing these challenges with its integrated power delivery and thermal management platform, combining proprietary silicon Power Interposer Technology, advanced packaging, and novel power converter architectures to deliver higher power density, improved efficiency, and superior thermal performance for next-generation computing platforms. ... At the core of the company's technology is its proprietary silicon Power Interposer Technology, which integrates power conversion, passive components, and advanced packaging into compact, high-performance power modules. This fully integrated design eliminates the need for external passive components, reducing parasitic losses, simplifying system architecture, and minimizing printed circuit board (PCB) area. The platform is optimized for Vertical Power Delivery, utilizing an ultra-slim package profile that enables power converters to be positioned closer to AI processors, thereby reducing electrical losses and improving overall power delivery efficiency. ... A key innovation within the portfolio is the vStrata™ Vertical Power Delivery platform, developed to simultaneously address electrical, thermal, and mechanical constraints in modern AI processors. By shortening the electrical path between the power converter and the processor, the technology minimizes resistive losses and self-heating while delivering industry-leading power efficiency and more than double the solution-level current density of conventional alternatives. The integrated architecture enables higher rack densities and improved thermal performance for increasingly power-hungry AI accelerators and advanced computing devices. ... Lotus Microsystems has also introduced the LSC0580 power converter for Vertical Power Delivery and the LBK0504 miniaturized step-down converter, both designed for compact, high-efficiency power conversion in advanced electronic systems. The company's technologies support applications requiring high-current, low-voltage power delivery, including AI accelerators, xPU modules, GPUs, FPGAs, hyperscale data center compute trays, HPC clusters, supercomputers, optical transceivers, telecom infrastructure, networking equipment, and next-generation consumer electronics. The platform is also engineered to meet the thermal and power density requirements of emerging 5G, 6G, and edge AI applications. ... Beyond individual products, Lotus Microsystems combines expertise in nanofabrication, power electronics, integrated circuit design, and advanced semiconductor packaging to develop highly integrated power modules for next-generation computing. With global semiconductor partners, the company is advancing power delivery architectures that support higher compute performance, lower energy consumption, and better thermal management for increasingly complex electronic systems. ... By integrating proprietary silicon Power Interposer Technology, Vertical Power Delivery, advanced packaging, and highly integrated power converters into a unified platform, Lotus Microsystems is enabling more efficient, compact, and thermally optimised power delivery for AI, HPC, cloud computing, networking, and next-generation semiconductor applications. ... Lotus Microsystems is a Denmark-based fabless semiconductor company specializing in advanced power delivery solutions for AI, high-performance computing, and next-generation electronic systems. The company develops highly integrated power modules that combine proprietary silicon Power Interposer Technology, advanced packaging, and innovative power converter architectures to improve power density, efficiency, and thermal performance. Originating from research conducted at the Technical University of Denmark (DTU), Harvard University, Fraunhofer, and IMEC, Lotus Microsystems collaborates with global semiconductor partners to advance power management technologies for AI, cloud computing, telecommunications, and advanced electronics."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,LCECOM Boosts Cross-Border Digitalization,www.martechcube.com (GlobeNewswire),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.martechcube.com/lcecom-boosts-cross-border-digitalization-to-drive-regional-expansion/,"# LCECOM Boosts Cross-Border Digitalization to Drive Regional Expansion ... LUCKCAT E-COMMERCE PTE. LTD. (hereinafter referred to as “LCECOM”), an international company registered in New York, USA, today announced its continued commitment to advancing its global operational strategy. The company’s forward-looking initiatives will focus heavily on regulatory compliance, systemic transparency, and the long-term enhancement of cross-border digital operational capabilities. ... LCECOM stated that its strategic direction will center on strengthening structured digital operational capabilities across multiple regions while ensuring strict alignment with relevant regulatory requirements in each local jurisdiction. ... Operating lawfully within the U.S. legal framework, LCECOM engages in cross-border digital commerce coordination, operational process management, and brand-related support services under the U.S. federal tax system via its Employer Identification Number (EIN). ... The Company notes that because different countries employ distinct business identification systems, minor localized discrepancies naturally arise between corporate registration networks. LCECOM emphasizes that any inability to query its corporate information on local regional tax systems does not indicate that the Company is unregistered, but rather reflects a normal divergence between disparate jurisdictional data systems. The Company reaffirms that it strictly complies with all applicable local laws and regulatory requirements in every region where it maintains operations. ... LCECOM is continuously expanding its international operational structure through several key ongoing initiatives: ... - Establishing localized operational workspaces in select global regions. - Strengthening cross-regional collaborative operational systems. - Promoting the broad standardization of operational processes across multiple markets. - Gradually exploring alignment with local regulatory frameworks in future phases, subject to localized approvals and operational conditions. ... To support this infrastructure, LCECOM continues to invest heavily in the development of internal digital systems designed to improve consistency, traceability, and scalability. These core components include digital workflow coordination systems, cross-regional task management frameworks, data tracking systems, and standardized communication mechanisms. ... LCECOM’s 2026–2028 strategic plan prioritizes structural growth opportunities within international expansion zones to further refine its global business footprint. The Company identifies these target regions as high-priority sectors due to several critical growth drivers, including a youthful demographic profile, rising digital connectivity, rapid mobile payment adoption, and sustained demand for cross-border e-commerce. ... Within this strategic framework, key regional hubs have been identified as essential strategic nodes for regional positioning, offering significant trade connectivity, a stable business environment, and a growing receptiveness to international digital business models. LCECOM emphasizes that this international strategy will be implemented in phases, with gradual execution based carefully on market conditions and regulatory environments. ... “Global commerce is progressively shifting from traditional geographic structures toward operational models centered on digital collaboration,” the Company noted in a statement. LCECOM’s long-term objective is to lead this transition by advancing cross-border digital operating models that reduce geographical constraints and enhance systemic interconnectivity for teams worldwide."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI,www.brazilbusinessinsights.com,2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.brazilbusinessinsights.com/news/moomoo-engine-launch-futu-xp-nubank-brazil,"Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI ... # Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil ... Moomoo is launching 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified trading toolkit designed to capture active retail and professional traders in Brazil, challenging incumbents. ... - ▸ Global user base: Over 22 million users - ▸ Launch date: July 2, 2026 - ▸ Target market: Active retail & pro traders - ▸ Primary region: Brazil expansion ... The Bottom Line: - Moomoo, the digital brokerage subsidiary of Futu Holdings ($FUTU), is set to launch 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified suite of advanced trading tools designed to consolidate market analysis, charting, and execution. - The rollout represents a strategic push to capture high-value retail and professional traders in emerging markets, particularly Brazil, where digital brokerage competition is intensifying. - While the launch enhances $FUTU's technological moat, it poses direct competitive pressure on local incumbents such as XP Inc. ($XP) and Nubank ($NU). Strategic Expansion in Latin America: Futu Holdings ($FUTU), through its international trading platform Moomoo, is accelerating its expansion into Latin America with the exclusive announcement of 'Moomoo Engine.' This unified toolkit is designed to streamline the trading lifecycle for retail and professional investors. By integrating advanced charting, real-time data analytics, and algorithmic execution into a single, cohesive interface, Moomoo aims to address the fragmentation that has historically plagued active traders in emerging markets. The Brazilian market, characterized by a highly sophisticated retail investor base and a rapidly growing interest in global equities, serves as the primary launchpad for this technological deployment. Technological Disruption and the 'Moomoo Engine': The 'Moomoo Engine' represents a significant upgrade to the platform's existing infrastructure. Historically, active traders in Brazil have had to rely on multiple third-party platforms for technical analysis, order routing, and portfolio tracking. This fragmentation often leads to latency issues, higher subscription costs, and execution inefficiencies. Moomoo's unified toolkit addresses these pain points by offering proprietary, low-latency charting algorithms and institutional-grade data feeds directly within the trading application. This integration is expected to lower the barrier to entry for advanced trading strategies, enabling retail investors to execute complex multi-leg options strategies and automated technical trades with greater precision. Competitive Dynamics in the Brazilian Brokerage Sector: The introduction of the 'Moomoo Engine' comes at a time of intense competition within the Brazilian financial services sector. Incumbents like XP Inc. ($XP) and BTG Pactual have traditionally dominated the affluent and active trader segments through extensive advisory networks and proprietary platforms. Concurrently, digital-first platforms like Nubank ($NU) and Inter have successfully democratized access to basic investment products for the mass market. Moomoo's strategy bypasses the traditional advisory model, focusing instead on self-directed, tech-savvy traders who prioritize execution speed, analytical depth, and low transaction costs. By offering institutional-grade tools without the premium price tag, Moomoo is positioning itself to capture market share from both high-end incumbents and mass-market digital banks looking to upsell their user bases. Regulatory and Operational Considerations: Operating a foreign-backed digital brokerage in Brazil requires navigating a complex regulatory framework overseen by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Brazil (CVM) and the Central Bank of Brazil (BCB). Moomoo's expansion strategy relies heavily on seamless integration with local clearing systems and compliance with strict foreign exchange (FX) regulations. For Brazilian investors trading international assets, tax compliance—specifically the calculation of capital gains and the monthly 'Carnê-Leão' tax filing—has historically been a major friction point. To gain widespread adoption, the 'Moomoo Engine' must integrate localized tax reporting tools that simplify these compliance obligations for domestic users. Furthermore, fluctuations in the USD/BRL exchange rate remain a critical variable, as currency volatility can significantly impact the net returns of Brazilian investors trading on US exchanges through the platform. Implications for Futu Holdings ($FUTU): For Futu Holdings ($FUTU), the successful rollout of the 'Moomoo Engine' in Brazil is vital for its broader international diversification strategy. Facing mature markets and regulatory headwinds in mainland China and Hong Kong, Futu has increasingly looked to Southeast Asia and Latin America to drive its next phase of growth. Brazil represents one of the largest retail investment markets in the developing world, making it a high-stakes testing ground for Moomoo's global scalability. If the 'Moomoo Engine' succeeds in capturing a meaningful share of Brazil's active trading volume, it could serve as a blueprint for further expansion into other Latin American markets, such as Mexico and Colombia, thereby bolstering Futu's long-term revenue growth and reducing its geographic concentration risk. ... Market Impact: The launch of the 'Moomoo Engine' has distinct implications for the key players in the digital brokerage space: - Futu Holdings ($FUTU): Bullish. The successful deployment of advanced trading tools in Brazil accelerates Futu's international diversification, reducing its reliance on Asian markets and opening a high-margin revenue stream from active Latin American traders. - XP Inc. ($XP): Bearish. XP faces direct technological competition in its high-value active trader segment. While its advisory network remains a strong moat, Moomoo's low-cost, high-tech offering could pressure XP's commission margins and active client retention. - Nu Holdings ($NU): Neutral. Nubank's primary investment audience consists of mass-market retail investors rather than sophisticated active traders. However, as Nubank seeks to upsell its client base into more complex financial products, Moomoo's advanced platform represents a long-term competitive hurdle. ... > analyst consensus: Bullish on Futu Holdings ($FUTU) international expansion; bearish on XP Inc. ($XP) active trader retention; neutral on Nu Holdings ($NU). > asset_class: Equities"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Orisha is accelerating its consolidation strategy and reinforcing its technological leadership in AI-powered industry-specific software. - Orisha,www.orisha.com (Nathalie MOREL),2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.orisha.com/en/blog/news-en/orisha-is-accelerating-its-consolidation-strategy-and-reinforcing-its-technological-leadership-in-ai-powered-industry-specific-software/,"Orisha announces a triple acquisition—a transaction marking a new milestone in its growth strategy and reinforcing its ambition to become a leading European player in B2B software. ... Paris, June 30, 2026 — In a rapidly shifting European B2B software market, driven by the rise of AI-native platforms and accelerating investment in artificial intelligence, Orisha, a European publisher of business software for the real estate, retail, healthcare, construction, and agrifood sectors, announces the simultaneous acquisition of three fast-growing software companies to strengthen three of its strategic verticals: ... - Follow joins Orisha Health & Safety, - Soneka joins Orisha Real Estate, - A fully web-based SaaS ERP publisher for SMEs in the construction industry joins Orisha Construction. ... These transactions accelerate Orisha’s proactive strategy of sector-focused consolidation in vertical business software, strengthening its positions in healthcare, real estate, and construction. They also aim to support the Group’s European expansion ambitions through an enhanced offering addressing mission-critical use cases for all of its professional clients. ... The European vertical software market is entering a new phase of consolidation. Specialized software vendors must now accelerate their investments in product, data, AI, cybersecurity, and internationalization to remain competitive and scale up. In this context, Orisha intends to act as a driving force by bringing together high-potential vertical software companies capable of strengthening its strategic verticals and accelerating the construction of a European leader in B2B software. ... - Founded in 2015, Follow develops a SaaS platform dedicated to surgical specialists, currently supporting 1,500 specialists and covering the entire patient journey (scheduling, clinical follow-up, medical documents, prescriptions, billing, and electronic claims submission). Positioned in a premium medical segment, Follow has established itself among demanding specialties such as orthopedics, neurosurgery, urology, and digestive surgery. The acquisition strengthens Orisha’s position in healthcare, a vertical now exceeding €100 million in revenue in 2026. ... - Founded in 2017, Soneka develops a Real Estate Asset Management SaaS solution that enables real estate investors and asset managers to oversee their assets, financial data, forecasts, and reporting from a single unified platform. With operations in Germany and Spain, Soneka adds a modern, profitable PropTech asset, already well established in its market, to Orisha Real Estate’s portfolio. ... - Orisha also confirms the acquisition of a 100% web-based SaaS ERP vendor serving SMEs in the construction sector, maintenance companies, and field service providers. Its platform, which covers site management, interventions, inventory, CRM, time tracking, absences, business intelligence, and a customer portal, strengthens the Group’s offering with a modern, modular solution tailored to the operational needs of construction companies. ... Faced with accelerating technological, regulatory, and commercial demands, these specialized software vendors are now seeking partners capable of scaling their operations and supporting their development without sacrificing their product DNA, their domain expertise, or their proximity to customers. These vendors thus benefit from a unique industrial platform combining: ... - Sector expertise - Product excellence - Substantial investment capacity - Go-to-market acceleration - International expansion ... The integration of these solutions allows Orisha to strengthen its position in three critical-use markets (healthcare, real estate, and construction), accelerate the modernization of its SaaS offerings, and consolidate its positioning in vertical business software. They also illustrate the Group’s ability to attract modern, growing companies positioned around mission-critical use cases for their customers. Through these transactions, the Group confirms its strong drive for expansion. Backed by Francisco Partners and TA Associates, Orisha intends to continue pursuing its strategy of organic growth and targeted acquisitions to become one of Europe’s leading vertical B2B software platforms. ... The Group is targeting €400 million in revenue in 2026 and aims to reach €600 million by 2028. ... > The European vertical software market is entering a new phase. The best software vendors are no longer simply looking for a buyer, but for a platform capable of giving them an industrial future, accelerating their growth, and preserving what makes them strong. That is exactly what we are building with Orisha: an industrial group, backed by the investment power of Francisco Partners and TA Associates, capable of helping the best vertical software companies scale across Europe. The fact that we are announcing three acquisitions at once reflects our deep belief in the future of vertical software and our commitment to a growth-driven strategy.— Alexandre Fretti, CEO of Orisha ... > We were looking for a partner capable of helping us accelerate much faster, without compromising on our product vision. Orisha brings us unique industrial, technological, and commercial strength in the European market.— Steven Kavay, CEO of Follow ... > We wanted to join a group capable of giving us the means to bring our vision of a single platform for commercial real estate to life and to accelerate our European expansion. With Orisha, we found an ambition aligned with our own.— Victor Beth and Benoit André, co-founders of Soneka. ... ## Orisha strengthens its Executive Committee with two strategic appointments. ... Orisha appoints Alexandra Durand-Escribe CEO of Orisha Agrifood and Raphaël Giraud Group Chief Operating Officer."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lusha: Interview With Co-Founder & CEO Yoni Tserruya About The Sales Intelligence Platform,pulse2.com (Amit Chowdhry),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pulse2.com/lusha-profile-yoni-tserruya-interview/,"Lusha is the B2B data and intelligence layer for GTM teams and AI agents. It delivers verified contact and company data, enriched with buying signals and shaped by what works for your business. Pulse 2.0 interviewed Lusha co-founder and CEO Yoni Tserruya to learn more. ... “It started with a simple problem: connecting with the right people was harder than it should be. Assaf and I saw an opportunity to help business professionals find each other. We originally thought it would be useful for recruiters. But very quickly, salespeople came to the product and found a lot of value in it. Within months of launching Lusha as a Chrome extension, it went viral organically with no marketing budget. That validated that people didn’t just need more data, they needed better data. If your data is wrong, every insight, every action, every decision downstream is wrong too. That became the foundation of everything we’ve built since, and it’s even more important now with AI, agents, and automation.” ... “Lusha is accessible across three surfaces. Lusha Workspace is where teams prospect, build lists, and run AI-powered workflows. The browser extension sits on top of LinkedIn and other sites so reps can pull verified contact data without leaving their workflow. And the API and MCP make all of Lusha’s data and deep intelligence available to developers and AI agents.” ... “Our data includes verified contact and company data, real-time signals like job changes and department growth, AI-powered lead recommendations that refresh daily based on your ICP, and CRM integration so everything syncs back to where your team already works. We’ve also built ICP Hub, which lets you define your ideal customer profile in plain language and share it across the whole team—so a rep who joined last week is working from the same targeting strategy as your most experienced AE.” ... comprehensive, verified, and ... B2B dataset. Contacts, companies, real-time signals, ... market triggers. Fast, accurate, ... access this kind of data. ... the most complete and the most ... “The biggest challenge right now is something the whole industry is dealing with. AI is moving so fast that GTM teams are deploying agents before the data infrastructure underneath them is ready. Agents are only as good as the data they run on. We’ve seen this play out internally and with customers. That’s shaped a lot of our product decisions over the past year: making our data accessible via API and MCP, so that whatever stack a team is using, Lusha can serve as the intelligence layer underneath it.” ... “We started as a browser extension that surfaced contact data. That was the right place to begin — simple, valuable, immediate. Over time, we built out the full platform: enrichment, CRM integrations, search, and filtering. The bigger shift came when we decided to build the Deep Intel layer. That meant investing seriously in machine learning—lookalike engines, recommendation engines, scoring models that learn from your business. We’ve improved our lookalike accuracy by 50% recently. And the next layer is what we’ve just started: making all of this accessible to AI agents through MCP and API, so that autonomous workflows can tap into Lusha data the same way a human would. That’s a fundamentally different architecture than where we started.” ... “A few stand out. Getting to profitability while bootstrapped was a big one, it meant we proved the model before we raised. Reaching 1 million users was meaningful because it was organic. And recently, sharing our data with the world – in Claude, ChatGPT, Clay, and the launch of our MCP integration, which means AI agents can now call Lusha data. That one felt like crossing a threshold into a new era of what this company is building toward.” ... “We don’t share specific revenue figures publicly. What I can say is the business is healthy. We’ve been profitable, we’re growing, and we haven’t needed to optimize for fundraising headlines over building a real business. That independence has let us make product decisions based on what customers actually need.” ... “The B2B data and sales intelligence market is large—commonly cited in the multi-billion dollar range, but I think the more interesting framing is what’s happening to the TAM itself. As AI agents become a real part of how companies operate, the need for verified, structured, agent-ready B2B data grows significantly. Every agent doing any kind of outbound or account research is a potential Lusha customer. That expands the addressable market well beyond traditional sales tools.” ... “The AI pilot phase is over. Companies that were experimenting are now deploying agents to do actual work. The teams that will win are the ones that build their agentic G ... on a solid data foundation. An agent with bad data ... worse than a human with bad data; it scales the mistakes.” ... “The most crucial thing for success in the next 1-2 years is getting the data layer right. That means verified data, real-time signals, and a system that understands your specific business context — not just generic market data. Companies that sort that out early will build a structural advantage. Not a quarterly edge. A permanent one.” ... “Second, the Deep Intel layer. Most competitors are in the Search layer business; they give you just data. We give you data plus a system that learns your business and tells you where to focus. That’s a different product category.” ... “Third, how we’ve built for the agentic era. Our MCP integration means AI agents can access Lusha data natively, the same way they access any tool in their stack. Most of our competitors haven’t gotten there yet.” ... “And fourth, compliance. Lusha built GDPR, CCPA, and ISO 27701 in, and we feel good about it. In a world where enterprise buyers are increasingly scrutinizing data practices, that’s a moat that took years to build and can’t be copied quickly.” ... “The north ... is becoming the B2B intelligence layer that ... every CRM, every workflow ... “More specifically: we want to be the default data and intelligence layer for AI agents doing GTM work. That means deeper integrations so Lusha is accessible wherever agents are operating It means continuing to make the Deep Intel layer smarter with each use. We want to reach a point where a seller can ask “Who do I need to talk to today?” and get an answer they can trust and act on immediately.”"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lotus Microsystems launches AI data centre power module,itbrief.asia (Joseph Gabriel Lagonsin),2026-06-10T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-10 00:00:00+00:00,,https://itbrief.asia/story/lotus-microsystems-launches-ai-data-centre-power-module,"Lotus Microsystems launches AI data centre power module ... # Lotus Microsystems launches AI data centre power module ... Lotus Microsystems has launched its first vStrata module for AI data centre infrastructure, marking the company's first commercial product built around a vertical power delivery approach. ... Engineering samples of the first module, known as LSC0580, are due to ship in the third quarter of 2026. The Copenhagen semiconductor startup described it as a combined power delivery and thermal management platform for AI accelerators and other high-current compute systems. ... The first module has already completed tape-out work for what Lotus Microsystems described as leading xPU and AI infrastructure partners. It did not name those partners, but said it is working with Tier-1 hyperscalers and other companies through an early access programme. ... According to the company, the LSC0580 is designed to cut power conversion losses by more than 50% and achieve point-of-load efficiency of up to 96%. It also said the module can reduce operating temperatures by as much as 25C in optimised configurations, while its thin design could allow operators to fit more boards into each rack. ... Lotus Microsystems said the LSC0580 has been engineered for kiloampere-class power demands and can support load transients exceeding 10 A/ns without external capacitors. It added that the module is designed to work with established reference designs and existing power management controllers, which could reduce redesign work for customers considering adoption. ... The company framed the launch as a response to a broader architectural challenge in AI computing, where system design rather than chip design alone is becoming a limiting factor. ... ""We have reached a point where AI compute performance is constrained by physical architecture,"" said Hans Hasselby-Andersen, Chief Executive Officer, Lotus Microsystems. ... ""vStrata was developed to address the reality that power delivery and thermal management have become inseparable system constraints. By integrating both into a single co-engineered platform, we help data centres increase compute density while reducing the power and cooling overhead that drives AI infrastructure cost,"" said Hasselby-Andersen. ... Lotus Microsystems said its approach is based on multi-domain co-design, bringing electrical, thermal and mechanical engineering into one architecture. That reflects a broader trend in advanced semiconductor packaging, where chipmakers and system suppliers are looking beyond the processor die to improve overall system performance. ... AI servers have become a focal point for those efforts because of their unusually high power density. Operators are under pressure to contain both electricity use and cooling costs as they build out larger clusters for model training and inference workloads. ... Lotus Microsystems argued that the bottleneck lies not only in delivering more current, but also in handling sudden and unpredictable swings in processor demand. Reducing the distance between the power source and the processor is intended to improve response time while managing heat at the same location. ... ""The industry has been trying ... scale AI compute using an architecture that was never designed for this level of intensity,"" said Yasser Nour, Co-founder and Chief Technology Officer, Lotus Microsystems. ... ""The real bottleneck isn't just delivering power - it's how the system responds to rapid, unpredictable load changes. By collapsing the distance between the power supply and the processor, vStrata is designed to deliver current where and when it's needed, without compromising thermal behaviour or transient stability,"" said Nour. ... Founded in 2020, Lotus Microsystems is based in Copenhagen and focuses on low-profile vertical power delivery and thermal management products for next-generation compute systems. The company said it holds multiple patents covering the underlying technology."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,From Limited Contact Coverage to Closed Deals: insightsoftware’s Lusha Success - Demand Gen Report,www.demandgenreport.com (James Hickey),2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.demandgenreport.com/case-studies/from-limited-contact-coverage-to-closed-deals-insightsoftwares-lusha-success/53107/,"From Limited Contact Coverage to Closed Deals: insightsoftware’s Lusha Success - Demand Gen Report ... # From Limited Contact Coverage to Closed Deals: insightsoftware’s Lusha Success ... Published: June 4, 2026Author: James Hickey ... - insightsoftware improved EMEA contact data quality with Lusha, helping BDR teams reach the right buyers faster and reduce lead-to-action response time. - The team doubled pipeline ROI within two weeks, onboarded 25+ users in one hour and closed several deals through stronger multithreading. ... When Andrew Knox joined insightsoftware as Director of Business Development for EMEA, the team was already using a global sales intelligence tool rolled out from U.S. headquarters. But the data provided wasn’t strong enough for their regional needs. ... To tackle the issues, Knox contacted a company that he had worked with in a previous role that he knew would help solve these issues: Lusha. ... A B2B data intelligence solution, the company provides two layers of data: one universal, the other unique to each client’s business. Lusha’s Search layer covers contacts, companies and real-time signals. It’s fast, objective and available to everyone. Their Deep Intel layer is tailored specifically to each client’s business—it learns from configuration, usage patterns, integrated systems, and unique data and signals, producing smart, relevant predictions that adapt and improve with every use. ... With more than 25 users on an Enterprise plan, Lusha became a complementary tool alongside the existing global platform. “We found the data from Lusha was better in EMEA,” says Knox. “So whilst the team was using our existing business intelligence tool to some extent, Lusha has been a complementary tool to clarify data and give us another option to phone people.” ... Ease of adoption was immediate. It took just one hour to get users onboarded. “When I think of Lusha’s superpower, simplicity comes to mind. The ease of use is just great,” Andrew says. ... The impact showed up fast. Within the first two weeks, insightsoftware doubled their return on investment in terms of pipeline built with contacts they didn’t previously have details for in their CRM or business information provider. Among the improvements and results seen were: ... - 2x ROI within less than a month of using Lusha - 2 weeks to double pipeline - 1 hour to onboard users - 25+ users on Enterprise plan - Closed several deals via multithreading - Decreased lead-to-action response time ... As a result, insightsoftware was able to close several deals using Lusha to multithread more effectively and decreased its lead-to-action response time thanks to better contact data. ... results were “transformational” and went beyond pipeline ... “We’ve not only been able to forge better relationships with customers because we’ve been able to engage with them earlier on, but we’ve also seen improvements in the net-new space as well,” he said. “Lusha has helped get us to the people that we need to speak to much more quickly than normal.”"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lulapay Brings Cash Flow Flexibility To Cloud On Demand’s Reseller Network,techfinancials.co.za (Staff Writer),2026-05-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://techfinancials.co.za/2026/05/14/lulapay-brings-cash-flow-flexibility-to-cloud-on-demands-reseller-network/,"Lulapay Brings Cash Flow Flexibility To Cloud On Demand’s Reseller Network ... Lulapay has partnered with leading cloud distributer Cloud on Demand to introduce integrated cash flow flexibility for ICT resellers and managed service providers across South Africa. Lulapay is a buy-now-pay-later (BNPL) offering powered by Lula. ... Through the partnership, qualifying Cloud on Demand partners will now have access to structured 30-day payment flexibility, helping them better align supplier payments with customer billing cycles, and easing one of the most persistent pressures facing profitable technology SMEs. ... Cloud on Demand is a major player in South Africa’s ICT ecosystem, enabling resellers to procure and manage subscription-based cloud and software solutions at scale. But as the technology channel shifts toward recurring revenue models, many partners are experiencing a structural cash flow mismatch: supplier accounts are settled monthly, while customers often pay 30 to 60 days later. ... “South Africa’s SME technology sector is growing rapidly, but subscription models have fundamentally changed how cash moves through these businesses,” says Jordan Gosling, Vice President of Lulapay. ... “By embedding flexible funding directly into the Cloud on Demand ecosystem, we’re enabling partners to unlock growth without taking on rigid, traditional debt structures. ... “This partnership reflects Lulapay’s focus on embedding flexible payment options directly into the supplier ecosystems where SMEs already transact. By working with distributors like Cloud on Demand, Lulapay aims to help suppliers support partner growth while maintaining predictable cash flow and stronger trading relationships across the B2B channel.” ... Rather than applying for standalone bank loans, qualifying partners can access funding within the platform where they already transact. This embedded finance approach allows them to extend repayment terms when needed, smooth out cash flow gaps and pursue larger opportunities with greater confidence. ... “This partnership with Lulapay is about more than payments – it’s about empowering our partners to grow by unlocking additional working capital. By strengthening their financial capabilities, we’re enabling them to remove growth constraints, improve cash flow, and scale with confidence – turning their ambitions into reality,” remarks Anthony Roberts, Chief Financial Officer at Cloud On Demand. ... is transforming B2 ... by integrating financial services directly into ... funding as a separate banking ... transaction infrastructure itself ... For ICT resellers and MSPs, this shift could be significant. As demand for cloud and software solutions accelerates, smaller channel players often face liquidity constraints that limit deal sizes or slow expansion, despite strong underlying demand. ... By integrating structured working capital into its marketplace, Cloud on Demand is positioning its partner network to scale more sustainably in an increasingly subscription-driven economy. ... In a constrained economic environment, aligning payment timing with real revenue cycles is no longer simply a competitive advantage — it is becoming essential to sustainable growth. ... South African VC Exits Show Early Signs Of A Maturing Venture Capital Ecosystem"
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Exa,Lulapay brings cash flow flexibility to Cloud on Demand’s reseller network,www.bizcommunity.com,2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bizcommunity.com/article/lulapay-brings-cash-flow-flexibility-to-cloud-on-demands-reseller-network-845103a,"Lulapay brings cash flow flexibility to Cloud on Demand’s reseller network ... # Lulapay brings cash flow flexibility to Cloud on Demand’s reseller network Lulapay has partnered with leading cloud distributor Cloud on Demand to introduce integrated cash flow flexibility for ICT resellers and managed service providers across South Africa. Lulapay is a buy-now-pay-later (BNPL) offering powered by Lula. Issued by Lula ... 12 May 2026 ... Through the partnership, qualifying Cloud on Demand partners will now have access to structured 30-day payment flexibility, helping them better align supplier payments with customer billing cycles, and easing one of the most persistent pressures facing profitable technology SMEs. ... Cloud on Demand is a major player in South Africa’s ICT ecosystem, enabling resellers to procure and manage subscription-based cloud and software solutions at scale. But as the technology channel shifts toward recurring revenue models, many partners are experiencing a structural cash flow mismatch: supplier accounts are settled monthly, while customers often pay 30 to ... 60 days later. ... “South Africa’s SME technology sector is growing rapidly, but subscription models have fundamentally changed how cash moves through these businesses,” says Jordan Gosling, vice president of Lulapay. “By embedding flexible funding directly into the Cloud on Demand ecosystem, we’re enabling partners to unlock growth without taking on rigid, traditional debt structures.” ... “This partnership reflects Lulapay’s focus on embedding flexible payment options directly into the supplier ecosystems where SMEs already transact. By working with distributors like Cloud on Demand, Lulapay aims to help suppliers support partner growth while maintaining predictable cash flow and stronger trading relationships across the B2B channel,” says Gosling ... “This partnership with Lulapay is about more than payments – it’s about empowering our partners to grow by unlocking additional working capital. By strengthening their financial capabilities, we’re enabling them to remove growth constraints, improve cash flow, and scale with confidence – turning their ambitions into reality,” remarks Anthony Roberts, chief financial officer at Cloud On Demand. ... By integrating structured working capital into its marketplace, Cloud on Demand is positioning its partner network to scale more sustainably in an increasingly subscription-driven economy. ... In a constrained economic environment, aligning payment timing with real revenue cycles is no longer simply a competitive advantage – it is becoming essential to sustainable growth."
LUSHA SYSTEMS,,,,Linkup,Italy fines US data broker Lusha €2 million over unlawful data collection,CyberInsider,2026-07-28T00:00:00Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://cyberinsider.com/italy-fines-us-data-broker-lusha-e2-million-over-unlawful-data-collection/,"Italy's data protection authority fined Lusha Systems €2 million for unlawfully collecting and selling personal data, including that of officials and public figures, without a valid legal basis under GDPR. The ruling applies despite Lusha having no EU establishment, due to ongoing data monitoring activities."
