CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"CJ CGV Turns to Profit in Q2, Driven by 4DPLEX Growth - The Asia Business Daily",www.asiae.co.kr (Lee Jonggil),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2026080716300746918,"CJ CGV Turns to Profit in Q2, Driven by 4DPLEX Growth - The Asia Business Daily ... # CJ CGV Turns to Profit in Q2, Driven by 4DPLEX Growth ... Published 07 Aug.2026 16:30(KST) Updated 07 Aug.2026 16:30(KST) ## Record-High 4DX Performance in North America, Sales Up 20.8% Domestic Film Market Rebounds, Further Improvement Possible ... CJ CGV announced on August 7 that it achieved sales of 593.9 billion won and an operating profit of 11.5 billion won in the second quarter of this year, turning a pre-tax profit of 9 billion won into the black. Sales increased by 20.8% compared to the same period last year, driven by the global growth of CJ 4DPLEX and the recovery of the domestic film market. CJ 4DPLEX showed the most notable growth, posting sales of 46.9 billion won and an operating profit of 8.3 billion won. Sales rose by 56%, and operating profit soared by 260%, thanks to the global expansion of premium formats such as ScreenX and 4DX and the strong box office performance of titles like ""Super Mario Galaxy"" and ""Toy Story 5"". In particular, box office results in North America reached record highs for the first half of the year. ... The domestic theater business posted sales of 166 billion won and an operating loss of 6.2 billion won, continuing to operate at a loss but with clear improvement. Sales grew by 17% due to the film market recovery, box office success of movies such as ""Gunché"" and ""Salmoekji"", and the effect of government-issued discount coupons. Operating losses also narrowed by 11.1 billion won compared to last year. ... Results from the overseas theater business varied by country. In Vietnam, the company recorded 64 ... won in sales and 7. ... billion won in operating profit, supported by successful self-distributed content. Despite a shrinking market in Indonesia ... the company maintained profitability with 25.8 billion won in sales and ... 1 billion won in operating profit. In contrast, Turkey and China recorded operating losses of ... .1 billion won and ... 9 billion won, respectively. ... CJ OliveNetworks, the non-film business unit, posted sales of 254.5 billion won and an operating profit of 20 billion won. Sales rose by 29% thanks to the expansion of AX businesses, including next-generation ERP and AI Factory operations. Operating profit also grew by 16% due to cost-efficiency measures. ... In the second half of the year, the company expects recovery momentum to continue with the release of global blockbusters such as ""Spider-Man: Brand New Day"" and ""Odyssey,"" as well as Korean films like ""Hope."" Conditions for screenings will also improve. CGV Yongsan I’Park Mall renewed its ScreenX auditorium last month, and CGV Yeouido will introduce the world's first three-sided LED ScreenX auditorium later this year. ... Jongmin Jung, CEO of CGV, stated, ""We achieved a turnaround to pre-tax profit as the results of global investments by CJ 4DPLEX were combined with the recovery of the domestic film market,"" and added, ""In the second half of the year, we aim to further increase both profitability and growth through expansion of our global premium format business, AX business growth at CJ OliveNetworks, and strengthened competitiveness in the domestic theater business."""
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,CGV reports 593.9 billion won in revenue for the second quarter; pre-tax profit turns positive at 9 billion won | STARNEWS,www.starnewskorea.com (Kim Mihwa),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.starnewskorea.com/en/movie/2026/08/07/2026080716223432965,"CGV reports 593.9 billion won in revenue for the second quarter; pre-tax profit turns positive at 9 billion won | STARNEWS ... # CGV reports 593.9 billion won in revenue for the second quarter; pre-tax profit turns positive at 9 billion won ... CJ CGV recorded consolidated revenue of 593.9 billion won and an operating profit of 11.5 billion won for the second quarter this year, achieving a pre-tax profit of 9 billion won and turning profitable. ... On the 7th, CJ CGV announced these results through its second-quarter 2026 performance report. ... Driven by global growth in CJ 4DPLEX and recovery in the domestic film market, revenue increased by 20.8% compared to the same period last year, significantly improving profitability. A detailed breakdown shows that CJ 4DPLEX generated revenue of 46.9 billion won and an operating profit of 8.3 billion won. Global expansion of technology-specialized theaters such as SCREENX and 4DX, along with the box office success of global hits like ""Super Mario Galaxy"" and ""Toy Story 5,"" led to a 56% year-on-year increase in revenue and a 260% rise in operating profit. In North America, the company recorded its highest-ever first-half box office performance. ... In Korea, revenue reached 166 billion won with an operating loss of 6.2 billion won. Supported by recovery in the domestic film market, strong performances of Korean films such as ""COLONY"" and ""Sal-mok-ji,"" the government's distribution of movie ticket discount coupons, and improvements in the domestic business structure, revenue grew by 17% compared to the same period last year, while the operating loss improved by 11.1 billion won year-on-year, continuing its trend of performance recovery. ... In Vietnam, driven by the success of self-distributed content, revenue reached 64 billion won with an operating profit of 7.4 billion won. In Indonesia, revenue was 25.8 billion won and operating profit stood at 4.1 billion won. In Turkey, supported by the box office success of foreign films such as ""Obsession"" and ""Toy Story 5,"" revenue increased by 36% year-on-year to 39.7 billion won, though an operating loss of 4.1 billion won was recorded. In China, rising audience numbers due to the popularity of local content resulted in revenue of 45.8 billion won and an operating loss of 11.9 billion won. ... CJ OliveNetworks reported revenue of 254.5 billion won and an operating profit of 20 billion won. ... CJ CGV is expected to continue its growth trajectory in the second half of the year, supported by the release of global blockbusters and strengthened competitiveness in technology-specialized theaters. ... CJ CGV Jeong Jong-min (CEO) stated, ""The global investment results of CJ 4DPLEX are now beginning to materialize, combined with the recovery trend in the domestic film market, enabling us to achieve a pre-tax profit for the second quarter."" He added, ""In the second half of the year, we will further enhance both profitability and growth by expanding our global technology-specialized theater business, scaling up CJ OliveNetworks' AX operations, and strengthening the competitiveness of our domestic theater business."""
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"In Brief: Vista, Amcor & Charter Hall Social Infra - FNArena.com",fnarena.com,2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://fnarena.com/index.php/2026/08/07/in-brief-vista-amcor-charter-hall-social-infra/,"In Brief: Vista, Amcor & Charter Hall Social Infra - FNArena.com ... ## Blockbuster films to boost Vista ... GL)) has, thus ... , been one of ... pleasant earnings surprises in ... 26 revenue guidance to NZ$179m-NZ$184m from NZ ... 76m-NZ$182m, signifying annual growth of ... In terms of the ongoing cloud migration, Shaw highlights several major client wins over the first half, including Cinepolis Mexico, Cineworld, Cineplexx and returning customer Cinemax. ... Vista has a cloud backlog of around 1,000 sites and management reconfirmed the FY26 target for 1,300 operational excellence sites. ... The Shaw analyst attributes the upgrade in revenue guidance to the cloud migration, as well as growth in the domestic box office, up 15% y/y in 1H2026, with a strong 2H film slate including The Odyssey and Spider-Man. ... The Canaccord analyst emphasises three growth drivers for Vista, the ongoing shift of the existing customer base onto the cloud platform, boosting ARR, growing market share via a rise in the enterprise site base, and monetising transaction volumes via the Vista Payments platform. ARR is over $2m. ... Shaw confirms the growth in Payments, with eleven live customers. Management reconfirmed FY30 targets. Shaw believes there is scope for this division to be a substantial growth driver. ... Jarden ponders if it's time to revisit industrial stalwart Amcor ((AMC)) ahead of its FY26 result after the close of trade on Wednesday, 12th August. ... Market expectations are currently positioned at the lower end of guidance for EPS, with consensus forecast at US$3.98, compared to the recently downgraded guidance at the 3Q update of US$3.98-US$4.03. ... Jarden views gearing and free cash flow generation as the two key factors, with management pointing to leverage guidance of 3.4x-3.5x and FY26 cash flow of US$1.5bn-US$1.6bn. ... Cost outs and synergies have underpinned earnings (EBIT) to date. Jarden is forecasting flat 4Q26 volumes y/y, which is presumed to be above market expectations. Earnings (EBIT) forecasts for Flexibles are US$1.763bn, which sits 0.7% above consensus. ... Regarding Berry synergy targets, the packaging company is targeting US$260m and Jarden is forecasting US$270m with a particular focus on procurement-related strategies from suppliers. ... The outlook for gearing is also significant, with management committed to retaining its ""investment grade credit rating"" against a backdrop of more elevated financial leverage in FY26 at 3.4x-3.5%, well in excess of the targets. ... UBS also lent support to the Amcor narrative this week, noting the stock is trading at a near-cyclical low PER. UBS is forecasting a resilient EPS growth outlook supported by merger synergies."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"CRG details material trends, Iconex announces acquisition and more - Label and Narrow Web",www.labelandnarrowweb.com,2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.labelandnarrowweb.com/breaking-news/crg-details-material-trends-iconex-announces-acquisition-and-more/,"CRG details material trends, Iconex announces acquisition and more - ... # CRG details material trends, Iconex announces acquisition and more Cindy White sits down with L&NW to talk about current industry challenges, plus the other top stories of the week. August 7, 2026 ... Meanwhile, Iconex, an M2S Group Company, and provider of innovative variable information labels, has announced the acquisition of Heartland Label Printers. This acquisition strengthens the industry-leading position of Iconex, expands manufacturing capabilities and capacity, and creates new growth opportunities for customers and team members. ... Heartland Label Printers, headquartered in Little Chute, WI, USA, is a North American producer of direct thermal, thermal transfer, linerless, and specialty variable-information labels. The business has a strong culture and legacy supported by approximately 170 team members across two locations."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Leap India raises Rs 743.6 crore from 32 anchor investors ahead of IPO launch - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Ritesh Presswala),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/leap-india-raises-rs-743-6-crore-from-32-anchor-investors-ahead-of-ipo-launch/articleshow/133019081.cms,"Leap India raises Rs 743.6 crore from 32 anchor investors ahead of IPO launch - The Economic Times ... s/F ... Leap India raises Rs ... 743.6 crore from 3 ... anchor investors ahead of ... # Leap India raises Rs 743.6 crore from 32 anchor investors ahead of IPO launch ... Leap India raises Rs 743.6 crore from 32 anchor investors ahead of IPO launch ... The anchor allocation witnessed participation from some of the world’s most prominent institutional investors, including the Monetary Authority of Singapore, Morgan Stanley India Investment Fund Inc., Goldman Sachs Investments (Mauritius) I Ltd., Government Pension Fund Global, Citigroup Global Markets Mauritius Private Limited, Société Générale – ODI, and BNP Paribas Financial Markets – ODI. ... Leap India backed by global investment firm KKR, has raised Rs 743.6 crore through its anchor book, with participation from 32 marquee investors. Ahead of the public issue, Leap India allotted 46,768,854 equity shares to anchor investors at an issue price of Rs 159 per share.The anchor allocation witnessed participation from some of the world’s most prominent institutional investors, including the Monetary Authority of Singapore, Morgan Stanley India Investment Fund Inc., Goldman Sachs Investments (Mauritius) I Ltd., Government Pension Fund Global, Citigroup Global Markets Mauritius Private Limited, Société Générale – ODI, and BNP Paribas Financial Markets – ODI. ... Domestic mutual funds also showed significant interest in the issue. Shares were allotted to leading equity-oriented schemes, including Axis Mutual Fund’s Axis Flexi Cap Fund, JM Financial Mutual Fund’s JM Flexicap Fund, and Motilal Oswal Large Cap Fund.Of the total anchor allocation, 18,735,422 equity shares were allotted to six domestic mutual funds through 15 schemes, along with One Life Insurance Company, highlighting strong institutional appetite for the company’s growth story. ... JM Financial Limited, Avendus Capital Private Limited, IIFL Capital Services Limited, and UBS Securities India Private Ltd are acting as the book-running lead managers for the issue, while MUFG Intime India Private Limited is the registrar. The company’s equity shares are proposed to be listed on both the BSE and NSE. ... ## IPO Details: Rs 2,480 Crore Issue Opens on August 7 ... Leap India has fixed a price band of Rs 151 to Rs 159 per equity share for its maiden public offering. The IPO will open for subscription on Friday, August 7, 2026, and close on Tuesday, August 11, 2026. ... The IPO comprises a fresh issue of Rs 480 crore and an offer-for-sale (OFS) of Rs 2,000 crore by promoters Vertical Holdings II Pte Ltd and KIA EBT Scheme 3, acting through its trustee Catalyst Trusteeship Limited.From the fresh issue proceeds, Rs 360 crore will be utilised towards repayment or prepayment of certain borrowings, either fully or partially, with the balance allocated towards general corporate purposes.The offer is being conducted through the book-building route, with up to 50% of the net issue reserved for qualified institutional buyers (QIBs), at least 15% for non-institutional investors, and a minimum of 35% for retail individual investors. ... Founded in 2013, Leap India has built its business around a “share and reuse” model, commonly known as asset pooling. According to the F&S Report, the company is the largest on-demand asset pooling provider in India’s supply chain management industry based on the number of pooled assets.As of March 31, 2026, Leap India managed 14.70 million assets through a nationwide network spanning 10,100 customer touchpoints. Its circular business model enables companies to improve supply chain efficiency while reducing costs, environmental impact, and operational complexities.The company provides technology-enabled supply chain solutions that connect multiple stages of customers’ value chains — from manufacturing and warehousing to distribution and retail.Pallets play a crucial role in modern logistics by enabling safer, faster, and more efficient movement of goods. Leap India’s pallet pooling model allows businesses to access shared pallet networks instead of owning and maintaining their own assets.Under this model, ownership, maintenance, tracking, and availability management of pallets are outsourced to specialised providers. This helps businesses reduce procurement costs, minimise storage requirements, lower manpower dependency, and ensure consistent asset quality across operations.With supply chains becoming increasingly technology-driven, pallet pooling is emerging as a cost-effective and sustainable solution for industries looking to optimise logistics operations.Through its extensive asset base and pan-India presence, Leap India caters to customers across multiple sectors, including fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG), food and beverages, third-party logistics (3PL), e-commerce, quick commerce, automotive, and industrial segments.As of March 31, 2026, the company served more than 1,000 customers. Its integrated solutions and deep operational relationships have helped create strong customer retention, with the company’s top 10 customers by revenue in FY26 having partnered with Leap India for over five years.Technology remains central to Leap India’s operations. Its proprietary MyLEAP platform provides customers with real-time visibility into orders, asset tracking, damaged asset replacement, reports, and support services. The company has also integrated SAP S/4HANA and Salesforce into its systems to enable seamless electronic data exchange with customers. ... ## Strong Financial Growth ... Leap India has demonstrated significant financial momentum in recent years. The company’s revenue from operations increased to Rs 729.5 crore in FY26 from Rs 364.9 crore in FY24, reflecting strong business expansion. Net profit also grew to Rs 62.3 crore in FY26, compared with Rs 37.1 crore in FY24, underscoring improving operational scale and profitability.With backing from global investors, a scalable asset-light model, and growing demand for efficient supply chain solutions, Leap India’s IPO is expected to attract considerable attention from investors seeking exposure to India’s rapidly evolving logistics and infrastructure ecosystem.(Disclaimer: Recommendations, suggestions, views and opinions given by the experts are their own. These do not represent the views of Economic Times)"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"CJ ENM CO., Ltd. Reports 33.4 Billion Won in Second-Quarter Operating Profit… Up 16.9% Year-Over-Year - EDAILY",en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202608065846/,"4 Billion Won in Second-Quarter Operating Profit ... 6.9 ... Year-Over-Year - EDAILY ... ## CJ ENM CO., Ltd. Reports 33.4 Billion Won in Second-Quarter Operating Profit… Up 16.9% Year-Over-Year ... Expansion of Global Brand Zone… KBO and Original Content Prove Popular Fan-Based IP Integrated into E-Commerce… MLC’s Sales Volume Up 161.3% ""Media Platform Division Returns to Profit…Proving Structural Improvements"" ... [Edaily Reporter Choi Hee-jae ] CJ ENM ( CJ ENM CO., Ltd.(035760)) announced on the 6th that it posted consolidated revenue of 1.2033 trillion won and operating profit of 33.4 billion won for the second quarter. This represents an 8.3% decrease in revenue and a 16.9% increase in operating profit compared to the same period last year.(Photo: CJ ENM CO., Ltd.) CJ ENM CO., Ltd. disclosed on the 6th that, under Korean-adopted International Financial Reporting Standards (K-IFRS) on a consolidated basis, it recorded revenue of 1.2033 trillion won and operating profit of 33.4 billion won for the second quarter of 2026. The Entertainment division continued to improve profitability by leveraging the competitiveness of its content intellectual property (IP) and expanding its platform reach, while the Commerce division boosted both revenue and profitability by strengthening its app competitiveness through short-form content and accelerating the growth of mobile live commerce (MLC).By division, the Media Platform division posted revenue of 380 billion won—a 19.0% increase year-over-year—and an operating profit of 11 billion won, returning to profitability, driven by the expansion of brand stores through global partnerships and the success of KBO and original content.(Photo: CJ ENM CO., Ltd.) TVING had previously signed partnerships with HBO Max and Disney+ and expanded into Japan and 17 other Asia-Pacific countries through brand stores. However, TV advertising revenue fell by 20.9% due to a combination of the advertising market’s concentration on mega-events like the World Cup and an overall contraction in demand.The Film and Drama division recorded revenue of 190.2 billion won and an operating loss of 10.5 billion won, respectively. The division focused on securing a stable global distribution base through individual sales to local overseas platforms and demonstrated steady growth as demand for variety content continued to rise.In particular, through “The Legend of the Mess Sergeant,” which aired simultaneously on TVING and tvN, the company reduced production costs through efficient casting and the use of AI-based CG/VFX. At the same time, it demonstrated the potential to transition to a high-efficiency, profit-expanding IP business structure by expanding its IP through initiatives such as VPPL (interactive AI virtual product placement) linked to AI technology, the album release by “Taste Boys,” and the Dosirak F&F business.However, the global studio FIFTH SEASON operates under a structure where content delivery timelines are adjusted according to the scheduling of global OTT platforms, resulting in no major series deliveries this quarter.The music division recorded revenue of 230.2 billion won and operating profit of 10.9 billion won. “Modisei” successfully established itself in the market with first-week sales of 300,000 copies for its debut album, and the company secured new growth drivers, such as the launch of the global boy group “KO1KEYZ” following the success of “Produce 101 Japan: Shinsegae Co.,Ltd.”Album sales by existing artists such as “INI” and “ZEROBASEONE” also performed well, supporting revenue growth, while the diversification of revenue streams through the reboot of past IPs, such as “Wanna One” and “I.O.I,” continued.Although costs increased due to a focus on new IP and investments in ENPLUS, the success of a series of global live events for key IPs—including “Alpha Drive One’s” first global fan concert tour, “JO1’s” dome tour, and “KCON JAPAN 2026”—helped alleviate pressure on profitability.Revenue in the Commerce segment reached 402.8 billion won, up 4.4% year-over-year, while operating profit rose 21.2% to 26.0 billion won. The company actively distributed short-form content—edited from live broadcasts—across external channels such as YouTube, Instagram, and TikTok, and expanded app traffic by integrating fandom IP content—including the KBO, the movie *The Devil Wears Prada 2*, *Wally Run*, and *Minions*—into its commerce platform.As a result, mobile live commerce (MLC) sales volume increased by 161.3% year-over-year, while new app installations rose by 25.6% and monthly active users (MAU) grew by 10.5%.A virtuous cycle—where customers who discover content through external channels are directed to the app and proceed to make purchases—was strengthened, leading to simultaneous growth in both the customer base and purchase conversion rates. On the product front, the expansion of the premium travel and children’s categories drove overall growth, and the enhanced lineup of health supplements and premium beauty products also played a key role.A CJ ENM CO., Ltd. official stated, “The Media Platform division successfully turned a profit, demonstrating the structural improvement of our platform business,” adding, “It was a quarter marked by the expansion of ancillary businesses leveraging content IPs such as *The Legend of the Cook* and the outstanding performance of our music artists.”The spokesperson continued, “In the second half of the year, we plan to continue expanding our platform customer base while maintaining the trend of improved profitability through the diversification of content and music IP businesses and the expansion of global distribution.” ... ###### [Market In] CJ LOGISTICS to Close Multiple Subsidiaries in Southeast Asia… Accelerating the Streamlining of Overseas Operations ... [Market In] CJ LOGISTICS to Close Multiple Subsidiaries in Southeast Asia… Accelerating the Streamlining of Overseas Operations"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"[Market In] Battery Pouches Soared, but It’s ‘Awkward’… YoulchonChemical Sees Both Core and New Businesses Plunge - EDAILY",en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202608075029/,"Soared, but ... ward’… ... Sees Both Core and New Businesses ... YoulchonChemical Specifies “Battery Pouches” in Its First-Quarter Business Report Despite Signs of Business Strengthening, Exports of Electronic Materials Plummeted 11.4% Trusted ‘Nongshim-branded’ captive volume shrinks by 6.3%… Net outflow of 8.7 billion in FCF Debt-to-Equity Ratio at 41.8% and Net Debt Ratio at 92.9%…Exceeding Appropriate Levels ... LEE GEON-EOM 2026-08-07 06:06:05 [Edaily Marketin Reporter LEE GEON-EOM ] YoulchonChemical(008730)has expressed its commitment to expanding its pouch battery business—a new growth engine—but finds itself in an awkward position as its core indicator, export performance, has plummeted. On top of this, observers point out that its profit structure is being severely shaken as even its cash cow—the packaging business—and its reliable source of captive orders from Nongshim are declining. With its shrinking cash generation capacity compounded by the burden of large-scale capital investments, the uncertainty surrounding YoulchonChemical appears to be deepening. Infographic generated by generative AI. According to the Financial Supervisory Service’s electronic disclosure system on the 6th, YoulchonChemical listed “battery pouches” as a revenue item for the first time in the “Business Details” section of its first-quarter report this year. This marks the first time the company has separated this new growth engine—which had previously been mentioned only in the business description—from the revenue category previously lumped together under “Other Electronic Materials.” This move is interpreted as a sign that the company is shifting its focus toward the rechargeable battery materials business. YoulchonChemical has been investing in the development and mass production of materials such as aluminum pouch films for rechargeable batteries since 2021, targeting the rapidly expanding electric vehicle market. This is the result of applying the know-how accumulated in the food packaging business to rechargeable battery aluminum pouches. Although YoulchonChemical is promoting its rechargeable battery pouch business in this way, it has yet to produce tangible results. On the contrary, it is assessed that the company’s persistent losses are exacerbating its financial burden. Looking specifically at exports from the electronic materials division in the first quarter of this year, they totaled 31.7 billion won, an 11.4% decrease from the 35.8 billion won recorded in the same period last year. As the slowdown in electric vehicle demand drags on, the new business—which had been the focus of market expectations—appears to be holding the company back. What is even more critical is that the company’s existing cash cow—which should serve as its mainstay—is also crumbling. As sales from its core business, which the company had relied on, have faltered, YoulchonChemical’s overall profitability metrics have also plummeted. YoulchonChemical’s consolidated operating profit for the first quarter was 561.37 million won, a sharp 94.5% drop from the 10.2 billion won recorded in the same period last year. A breakdown by division reveals an even more complex situation. The packaging division, the company’s cash cow, posted an operating profit of 8.8 billion won, maintaining a profit level similar to that of the same period last year (9.1 billion won). The problem lies with the electronics materials division, a new business venture. The electronics materials division shifted from a profit of 6.8 billion won in the same period last year to a loss of 2.5 billion won in the first quarter of this year. In addition, a loss of 5.7 billion won was recorded under the “Common Division and Others” category, which covers corporate overhead costs and adjustments for interdepartmental transactions. Ultimately, most of the profit generated by the packaging division was eroded by the electronics materials division’s shift to a loss and the loss in the common division, causing total operating profit to shrink to the 500 million won range. The decline in captive volume, which had previously served as a safety net, also dealt a significant blow. Total revenue from transactions with related parties fell from 51.4 billion won in the same period last year to 49.1 billion won. Sales to Nongshim, a key client, decreased by approximately 6.3%, from 38.3 billion won to 35.9 billion won. As a result, cash flow also slowed. With 16.4 billion won in cash tied up in working capital—including inventory buildup—both cash flow from operating activities and free cash flow (FCF) recorded net outflows. YoulchonChemical’s cash flow from operating activities and FCF for the first quarter of this year stood at minus (-) 6.5 billion won and minus (-) 8.7 billion won, respectively. A negative FCF indicates that the company cannot cover even the essential costs of maintaining operations and funding investments with the cash generated from its core business alone. For YoulchonChemical, which must continue making large-scale capital investments to expand into new businesses, the deterioration in free cash flow will inevitably lead to an increase in external borrowing, acting as a trigger that exacerbates its financial burden. In fact, YoulchonChemical’s reliance on external financing to cover its cash shortfall is placing a significant strain on its financial soundness. As of the end of the first quarter of this year, YoulchonChemical’s total debt (including lease liabilities) stood at approximately 284 billion won. The debt-to-asset ratio—the proportion of debt relative to total assets—has soared to 41.8%. Generally, an appropriate debt-to-asset ratio is considered to be 30% or less. Given this, observers point out that the company’s debt burden is currently quite excessive. The actual debt burden, after deducting cash on hand, is even greater. YoulchonChemical’s net debt—calculated by subtracting cash and cash equivalents—stood at 267.4 billion won as of the end of the first quarter of this year. The net debt ratio—which represents the ratio of net debt to total capital (287.7 billion won)—stands at 92.9%. Given that the credit rating industry generally considers a net debt ratio of 50% to be appropriate, YoulchonChemical is exceeding this level by nearly double. Regarding this, a representative of YoulchonChemical explained, “We plan to improve profitability in our new rechargeable battery pouch business through cost-efficiency measures,” adding, “Overall sales are showing a growth trend.” The official added, “The decline in captive sales reflects the impact of the overall slump in domestic consumption,” and noted, “We expect performance to gradually improve starting in the second quarter.”"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,NEXUS Reports 8.08 Billion Won Net Profit in Q2 on One Store Acquisition Gain < IT·Gaming < 기사본문 - The Elec Inc.,www.thelec.net (KimSeonghun),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thelec.net/news/articleView.html?idxno=12824,"NEXUS Reports 8.08 Billion Won Net Profit in Q2 on One Store Acquisition Gain < IT·Gaming < 기사본문 - The Elec Inc. ... NEXUS Reports 8.08 Billion Won Net Profit in Q2 on One Store Acquisition Gain ... NEXUS said it returned to profitability in the first half of the year, supported by gains related to its acquisition of One Store, while accelerating efforts to expand its platform business and build an artificial intelligence (AI) and blockchain gaming ecosystem. ... The company said on Aug. 4 that, under consolidated K-IFRS standards, it recorded second-quarter revenue of 5.8 billion won, an operating loss of 5.3 billion won and net income of 8.08 billion won. Compared with the same period a year earlier, revenue declined 37.8%, operating profit swung to a loss and net income returned to positive territory. ... NEXUS said the quarter reflected a 15.7 billion won gain arising from the acquisition of One Store, as well as higher platform revenue generated through participation in network operations as a validator. Cumulative first-half revenue reached 17.42 billion won, up 9.4% from a year earlier. Net income totaled 5 billion won, compared with a loss in the same period last year. ... On June 29, NEXUS acquired an 89.03% stake in One Store for 62.6 billion won. Following the acquisition, the company reorganized its ecosystem under the ""ONE"" brand, renaming its mainnet from CROSS to ONEchain and changing its native token from $CROSS to $ONE. It also unified its payment infrastructure around $ONEUSD. ... The company plans to expand its AI and blockchain gaming platform centered on One Store. This month, it will launch an AI Games section featuring AI-powered gaming services. In mid-August, it plans to integrate its embedded wallet, ONEpocket, into the One Store application. Later this month, the company will launch a global version of One Store in 124 countries using a single-build deployment model, expanding its international gaming platform business. ... NEXUS is also strengthening its content portfolio. Through cooperation with Chinese technology company Tencent, One Store plans to introduce a series of mini-games on its ONEPlay platform, including Run for Survival, Legend of Divine Artifact and Oh! The Cat Is Here. The company also plans to add AI and blockchain games as it seeks to differentiate its content offerings."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,CHAR Tech Completes Thorold Kiln Installation,www.accessnewswire.com (CHAR Technologies Ltd.),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.accessnewswire.com/newsroom/en/metals-and-mining/char-tech-completes-thorold-kiln-installation-1201597,"# CHAR Tech Completes Thorold Kiln Installation ... Installation of the commercial high-temperature pyrolysis ("" ... is complete, including the ... 's heat tube, a long-lead critical-path component ... Commercial operations targeted by the end of September 2026, with production and revenue increasing through year-end as the facility ramps up ... TORONTO, ON / ACCESS Newswire/ August 5, 2026 / CHAR Technologies Ltd. (""CHAR Tech"" or the ""Company"") (TSXV:YES)(OTC PINK:CTRNF)(FSE:68K), a leader in sustainable biomass energy solutions, is pleased to provide an update on commissioning activities at its Thorold Renewable Energy Facility (the ""Thorold Facility""), the Company's first commercial renewable energy and biocarbon production facility that is jointly owned 50/50 between the Company and The BMI Group (""BMI""), which specializes in the acquisition and conversion of heavy industrial infrastructure into deployment-ready, multi-sector platforms, following BMI's previously announced $8,000,000 project-level equity investment directly into the Thorold Facility. ... Installation of the commercial HTP kiln is now complete, including the kiln's heat tube, a long-lead critical-path component. With mechanical installation of the kiln finished, the remaining construction step is the connection of the pyrogas piping and instrumentation. With the kiln installation complete, kiln commissioning can now commence, and following completion of the pyrogas piping and instrumentation, final commissioning will continue through to commercial operations. ... The Company is targeting commercial operations at the Thorold Facility by the end of September 2026, with production and associated revenue expected to increase through the end of 2026 as the facility ramps toward its Phase 1 run-rate. Phase 1 of the Thorold Facility is designed to produce up to 5,000 tonnes per year of biocarbon, with clients including ArcelorMittal Dofasco under the previously announced offtake agreement to reduce fossil carbon in the steelmaking processes. ... Following completion of Phase 1, the Company intends to proceed with Phase 2 construction, which includes installation of a second HTP kiln, addition of methanation equipment to upgrade synthetic gas into Renewable Natural Gas (""RNG""), and construction of an onsite RNG pipeline injection point. ... ""The team and our partners at BMI have brought the kiln through to completed installation, and we are now down to the final pyrogas piping before commissioning advances to commercial operations,"" said Andrew White, Chief Executive Officer of CHAR Tech. ""This is the last major step on Phase 1, and it moves the Thorold Facility toward its first commercial biocarbon revenues and it sets the stage for Phase 2 to commence."" ... In December 2022, the Government of Ontario announced approved funding of $6,438,168 for the project through the Forest Sector Investment and Innovation Program, a business support program designed to improve productivity and innovation, enhance competitiveness, support new market access and strengthen regional economies. ... In December 2025, the Government of Ontario announced approved funding of $2,259,142 for the project through the Forest Biomass Program, a business support program that is a key element of Ontario's actions to drive forest sector growth. ... The Government of Canada provided $4,938,168 for the project through the Investments in Forest Industry Transformation program and also provided $1,500,000 for the project through the Federal Economic Development Agency for Southern Ontario Jobs and Growth Fund. ... The BMI Group made a $8,000,000 project-level equity investment directly into the CHAR Tech Thorold Renewable Energy Facility, resulting in 50/50 ownership of the facility between CHAR Tech and BMI. ... CHAR Tech (TSXV:YES)(OTC PINK:CTRNF)(FSE:68K) is a Canadian clean-technology company developing first-in-kind high-temperature pyrolysis (""HTP"") systems that process unmerchantable wood and organic waste to generate two renewable energy revenue streams, renewable natural gas or green hydrogen, and a solid biocarbon that serves as a carbon-neutral, drop-in replacement for metallurgical coal. ... CHAR Tech's HTP platform is also advancing a new vertical focused on the permanent destruction of PFAS in wastewater biosolids. Operating at temperatures sufficient to break down long-chain fluorinated compounds, the system enables municipalities and industrial operators to eliminate PFAS while converting biosolids into energy and low-carbon solid products. ... Statements contained in this press release contain ""forward-looking information"" within the meaning of Canadian securities laws (""forward-looking statements"") about CHAR and its business and operations. The words ""may"", ""would"", ""will"", ""intend"", ""anticipate"", ""expect"" and similar expressions as they relate to CHAR Tech, are intended to identify forward-looking information. Forward-looking statements include, but are not limited to, statements relating to the timing for full facility construction, securing project financing, expectations regarding the offtake agreements, future plans, operations and activities, expectations regarding the scale up of production, and other statements that are not historical facts. Such statements reflect CHAR Tech's current views and ‎intentions with respect to future events, and current information available to CHAR Tech, and are subject to ‎certain risks, uncertainties and assumptions, including, among others, those risk factors discussed or referred to in CHAR Tech's disclosure documents filed with the securities regulatory authorities in certain provinces of Canada, including the Management Discussion & Analysis dated January 27th, 2026 for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2025, and available under CHAR Tech's profile on www.sedarplus.ca. Any such forward-looking information is expressly qualified in its ‎entirety by this cautionary statement. Moreover, CHAR Tech does not assume responsibility for the accuracy or ‎completeness of such forward-looking information. The forward-looking information included in this press release ‎is made as of the date of this press release and CHAR Tech undertakes no obligation to publicly update or revise ‎any forward-looking information, other than as required by applicable law."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,CJ ENM and Studio Dragon Report Q2 Earnings Beat Amid Stocks Turnaround | Gate News,www.gate.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gate.com/news/detail/cj-enm-and-studio-dragon-report-q2-earnings-beat-amid-stocks-turnaround-23267781,"CJ ENM and Studio Dragon Report Q2 Earnings Beat Amid Stocks Turnaround | Gate News ... # CJ ENM and Studio Dragon Report Q2 Earnings Beat Amid Stocks Turnaround ... - CJ ENM reported Q2 operating profit of 33.4 billion won on the 6th, representing 17% year-over-year increase. - Tving achieved first-ever quarterly operating profit of 6 billion won through 41% revenue growth from KBO broadcasts. - CJ ENM secured exclusive KBO broadcasting rights from 2027 through 2031, extending partnership five additional years. ... CJ ENM and Studio Dragon reported second-quarter earnings that met market expectations, with analysts at Hana Securities projecting both entertainment companies have passed their performance trough. CJ ENM announced on the 6th that Q2 revenue reached 1.2 trillion won with operating profit of 33.4 billion won, representing an 8% year-over-year decline and 17% increase respectively, exceeding the market consensus of 31 billion won. The turnaround was driven by Tving's subscriber growth fueled by KBO professional baseball season broadcasts and original content including 'Yumi's Cells 3' and 'The Legend of the Military Mess Hall,' enabling the streaming platform to achieve its first-ever operating profit of 6 billion won despite a 21% decline in TV advertising revenue that has persisted for four consecutive years. Studio Dragon, CJ ENM's subsidiary, posted Q2 revenue of 145.3 billion won (up 27% YoY) and operating profit of 15.4 billion won, returning to profitability through increased episode counts and AI-driven production cost reductions. Hana Securities maintained 'buy' ratings on both stocks with target prices of 53,000 won for CJ ENM and 37,000 won for Studio Dragon, stating that the industry downturn has already bottomed out. ... CJ ENM's media platform division returned to profitability with 11 billion won in operating profit during Q2. TV advertising revenue declined 21%, continuing a 16-quarter consecutive decline, but Tving's 41% revenue growth offset the weakness. The streaming service benefited from exclusive KBO professional baseball broadcasts and the success of original series 'Yumi's Cells 3' and 'The Legend of the Military Mess Hall.' ... CJ ENM secured exclusive broadcasting rights for KBO games from 2027 through 2031, extending its partnership for five additional years. The contract covers both wired and wireless broadcast rights as well as video business rights. Hana Securities analyst Lee Ki-hoon stated that the KBO rights extension will prevent subscriber churn and create synergies with digital advertising. ... The film and drama division posted a 10.5 billion won operating loss due to programming gaps at U.S. subsidiary Fifth Season, despite strong performance from Studio Dragon. The music division's operating profit fell 36% to 10.9 billion won as new group production costs offset comebacks from ZB1, INI, and MODITSAE. The commerce division generated 26 billion won in operating profit as luxury live commerce transaction volume surged 161%. ... Tving recorded 6 billion won in operating profit during Q2, marking the streaming platform's first quarterly profit since launch. The milestone resulted from a 41% revenue increase driven by KBO baseball season viewership and original content performance. ... Analyst Lee Ki-hoon noted that July TV advertising showed signs of recovery due to South Korea's early World Cup exit creating viewing alternatives, with further improvement anticipated from August onward. He stated that TV advertising recovery could directly translate into increased production budgets and programming expansion, benefiting both CJ ENM and Studio Dragon. ... Studio Dragon posted Q2 operating profit of 15.4 billion won, returning to the black after previous quarters of losses. The company broadcast 77 episodes during the quarter (50 on TV, 27 on OTT platforms) compared to 36 episodes in the prior-year period. Key titles included 'Secret Audit,' 'Yumi's Cells 3,' and 'The Legend of the Military Mess Hall.' ... The company implemented artificial intelligence tools to reduce production costs while changing its content amortization methodology. Starting in Q2, general drama amortization periods extended from 18 months to 48 months, with 70% of costs recognized within the first 7 months instead of 13 months. OTT pre-sale productions shifted from 6-month straight-line amortization to 4-month accelerated amortization. ... Analyst Lee Ki ... Hana Securities maintained 'buy' investment opinions on both CJ ENM and Studio Dragon on the 7th, setting target prices at 53,000 won and 37,000 won respectively. Analyst Lee Ki-hoon stated that the industry has already passed its bottom. ... Studio Dragon's share price surged following the Q2 earnings announcement, which Lee attributed to strong reflection of parent company CJ ENM's business turnaround. The analyst noted that CJ ENM's market capitalization includes approximately 54% from its Netmarble stake, with potential divestiture remaining a catalyst, though the company could recover annual operating profit to the 200 billion won range next year as Fifth Season's programming normalizes. ... Studio Dragon faces upcoming contract renewal negotiations with Netflix, with expectations for improved recoup rates (content supply revenue versus production costs) and enhanced profit-sharing terms to strengthen global competitiveness and margins."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Tops 90% Seat Occupancy in SCREENX, 4DX on Opening Weekend",www.cineplay.co.kr,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cineplay.co.kr/en-us/articles/29074,"# 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Tops 90% Seat Occupancy in SCREENX, 4DX on Opening Weekend ... ## Strong performance in special formats at home and abroad as CGV’s Golden Egg Index hits 97% and word of mouth spreads ... Since its July 29 opening last month, 〈Spider-Man: Brand New Day〉 has filled more than 90% of seats in major SCREENX and 4DX auditoriums across South Korea during its first weekend, extending strong momentum in premium formats. ... On the 4th, CGV said the title set a record for advance SCREENX bookings ahead of release, and immediate post-opening demand produced sold-out screenings across multiple showtimes. The CGV Golden Egg Index, which reflects real audience praise, is holding at 97%. The film has also posted exceptional results overseas: in major markets including the United Kingdom, India, Australia, Mexico, France, Germany, Taiwan and Thailand, both SCREENX and 4DX formats recorded their highest-ever openings on opening weekend. ... In particular, Spider-Man’s soaring web-swinging action through the heart of New York has resonated strongly in the premium formats. SCREENX’s 270-degree panoramic screen extends the sense of depth onto the side walls, and 4DX’s range of environmental effects—designed to simulate aerial gliding—has drawn enthusiastic reactions from viewers, who say ""it feels like ... ’ve stepped into the movie"" and ""it’s like experiencing ... action firsthand."" ... Jang Ji-yeon, head of CGV’s content operations team, said, ""After setting a pre-release booking record, the film has continued to perform strongly in premium formats after opening. Audience satisfaction among those who experienced Spider-Man’s action in SCREENX and 4DX is very high, and we expect steady demand for special-format screenings to continue."" ... The action blockbuster 〈Spider-Man: Brand New Day〉, which tells the story of Peter Parker—forgotten by all—confronting a mysterious enemy who knows his identity, is now playing nationwide in CGV SCREENX, 4DX and other premium-format auditoriums. ... NEWS7/28/2 ... 6First reactions〈Spider-Man: Brand New Day〉 opens tomorrow ... seeing the film at a press screening, Cineplay reporters shared their first impressions of the latest Spider-Man action blockbuster ... film follows Peter Parker ... events of 〈Spider ... Man: No Way Home〉."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Nexth logs Q2 operating loss of 5.3 billion won; net profit turns positive on OneStore acquisition gain,www.digitaltoday.co.kr (Ho-jung Lee),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.digitaltoday.co.kr/en/view/89165/nexth-logs-q2-operating-loss-5-3-billion-won-net-profit-turns-positive-on-onestore-acquisition-gain,"Nexth logs Q2 operating loss of 5.3 billion won; net profit turns positive on OneStore acquisition gain ... Nexth logs Q2 operating loss of 5.3 billion won; net profit turns positive on OneStore acquisition gain ... Nexth posted a second-quarter operating loss of 5.3 billion won as revenue fell 37.8 percent from a year earlier to 5.8 billion won, preliminary results showed. Net profit returned to the black at 8.1 billion won, reflecting a 15.7 billion won one-off gain from buying an 89.03 percent stake in OneStore for 62.6 billion won. Nexth said it will expand its AI and blockchain-based platform ecosystem in the second half. - Writer ... Nexth swung to a profit in net income in the second quarter this year after reflecting a one-off gain from the acquisition of OneStore. The company plans to expand its artificial intelligence (AI) and blockchain-based platform ecosystem in the second half. ... According to Nexth's preliminary consolidated results under Korean International Financial Reporting Standards (K-IFRS) disclosed on Monday, second-quarter revenue fell 37.8 percent from a year earlier to 5.8 billion won. The company posted an operating loss of 5.3 billion won, turning to a loss. ... Net profit, however, came to 8.1 billion won, returning to the black. The result reflected a one-off gain of 15.7 billion won generated when it acquired 89.03 percent of OneStore for 62.6 billion won on June 29. Revenue for the first half rose 9.4 percent from a year earlier to 17.4 billion won, and net profit was 5.0 billion won. ... During the second quarter, Nexth reorganised the entire ecosystem under the 'ONE' brand, including the mainnet ONEchain, the native token ONE ($ONE) and the common means of transaction ONEUSD ($ONEUSD). Through the ONEchain 2.0 upgrade, in which the company directly participates in network operations as a validator, it secured a rising trend in platform revenue. ... It also plans to create an 'AI Games' tab within OneStore in August and to embed the 'ONEpocket' wallet in the OneStore application in mid-August. By the end of this month, it plans to simultaneously launch a global OneStore in 124 countries through OneBuild to roll out its platform business in earnest. ... It will also pursue content and community integration in parallel. In cooperation with Tencent, it will sequentially introduce 'Dallyeoyasanda', 'Singijeonseol' and 'Oh! Yangiwasseo' on the mini-game platform 'ONEplay'. ... It also plans to integrate and operate Telegram, wallet and web-based participatory promotion 'ONEquest' and streamer platform 'ONEwave' within OneStore. As of July, the number of streamers affiliated with the ONE ecosystem was tallied at 33,419. ... Chief executive Hyun-kuk Jang (장현국) said, ""In the second quarter, we achieved a large increase in net profit due to the OneStore acquisition."" He added, ""From the third quarter, we will be able to confirm the effects of revenue growth and improved operating profit."""
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Nexus announced on the 4th that it recorded 5.8 billion won in sales and 5.3 billion won in operatin.. - MK,www.mk.co.kr (정호준),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mk.co.kr/en/it/12116465,"Nexus announced on the 4th that it recorded 5.8 billion won in sales and 5.3 billion won in operatin.. - MK ... Q2 Sales of KRW 5.8 Billion...Down 37.8% year-on-year Representative Jang Hyun-guk ""Improves sales and operating profit from Q3"" ... Nexus announced on the 4th that it recorded 5.8 billion won in sales and 5.3 billion won in operating losses in the second quarter of this year. Sales fell 37.8% year-on-year, and operating profit turned to a deficit. However, the net profit recorded 8.1 billion won. This is the result of reflecting 15.7 billion won in profits generated by the acquisition of One Store in June. ... Since the second quarter, Nexus explained that platform sales have increased significantly as it directly participated in network operation after upgrading its blockchain network, ""One Body."" 2.0. ... Since the second half of the year, Nexus has been focusing its efforts on the game platform business through synergy with One Store. Nexus is transforming One Store into a mobile game platform when it acquired an 89.03% stake in One Store for 62.6 billion won on June 29. ... Nexus plans to distribute AI-generated global games through the One Store ecosystem by establishing an ""AI Game"" tab in One Store this month. In addition, it plans to install the embedded wallet ""One Pocket"" in the One Store app in the middle of this month. ... At the end of this month, it will launch its global one-store platform simultaneously in 124 countries around the world, challenging its global game platform business in earnest. ... To secure content on the platform, One Store will join hands with Tencent to introduce mini-games popular in the Chinese market on the mini-game platform ""One Play."" ... ""In the second quarter, we saw a significant increase in net profit due to the acquisition of One Store,"" said Jang Hyun-guk, CEO of Nexus. ""From the third quarter, we will be able to see the effect of growing sales and improving operating profit."""
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Tandem PV acquires nexTC to bring perovskite coating in-house - PV Tech,www.pv-tech.org (JP Casey),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.pv-tech.org/tandem-pv-acquires-nextc-perovskite-metal-oxide-coating-process-in-house/,"Tandem PV acquires nexTC to bring perovskite coating in-house - PV Tech ... # Tandem PV acquires nexTC to bring perovskite metal oxide coating process in-house ... Tandem PV said that its acquisition of nexTC ‘prepares for commercial-scale production’. Image: Tandem PV. ... US perovskite manufacturer Tandem PV has acquired fellow US company nexTC, which develops thin-film metal oxide coating processes for tandem solar modules. ... Tandem PV said the move would bring the development of “critical” coating technology “in-house”, and give the company more control over the coating process, which is a key component of perovskite cell manufacturing. PV Tech has asked Tandem PV for further details on the metal oxide coating process and whether it uses tin, as other companies in the space, such as Sofab Inks, have. ... develops for use in ... As part of the nexTC-Tandem PV deal, the former’s founder and CEO Dr Cory Perkins will join the latter, and he expressed optimism about the potential to deploy the company’s coating processes on a larger scale. ... “After collaborating with Tandem PV on several projects, I saw a team that combines strong science with the ability to move technology onto a manufacturing line,” said Perkins. “Joining Tandem gives us the opportunity to integrate nexTC’s coating technology directly into a manufacturing platform advancing toward commercial-scale production.” ... The news follows Tandem PV’s start of operations at its Fremont, California facility that the company described as a “commercial demonstration factory” with an annual silicon-perovskite tandem module production capacity of 40MW. This week, the company said that the nexTC acquisition “prepares for commercial-scale production”, although did not provide an update on its expansion timeline, published in April, that it aims to begin “high-volume” manufacturing in 2028. ... The deal follows a number of agreements signed between leaders in the perovskite space, many of which have involved UK-based Oxford PV. The company signed a patent licensing agreement with US cadmium telluride (CdTe) module manufacturer First Solar in February and unveiled a new module prototype, developed in tandem with German research institute Fraunhofer ISE, in June."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' pioneers 'Shot for SCREENX' in Hollywood - The Korea Times,www.koreatimes.co.kr,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/companies/20260803/spider-man-brand-new-day-pioneers-shot-for-screenx-in-hollywood,"“Spider-Man: Brand New Day” is the first Hollywood film to use CJ 4DPLEX’s “Shot for SCREENX” production model, which was developed to incorporate the SCREENX viewing experience from the filming stage. ... Released Wednesday, the film was designed with the SCREENX viewing experience in mind from the outset. SCREENX extends images from the main screen onto both side walls, creating a 270-degree panoramic viewing experience. ... Unlike the conventional approach of converting a completed movie into SCREENX, Shot for SCREENX involves filmmakers and CJ 4DPLEX capturing footage specifically for the format during production. ... For “Spider-Man: Brand New Day,” director Destin Daniel Cretton, the production team and CJ 4DPLEX worked together on set to capture footage specifically for SCREEN ... The film is also available in 4DX, another cinema format developed by CJ 4DPLEX. The format uses motion seats, wind and other environmental effects to enhance action sequences, including Spider-Man’s movements and rapid changes in direction. ... “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” is notable not only as a major Hollywood release but also for showing how premium cinema formats are beginning to influence filmmaking, with the theatrical experience considered during production rather than added after completion. ... The premium cinema market has continued to grow in Korea. According to the Korean Film Council’s first-half 2026 report, revenue from special screenings, including SCREENX, 4DX and IMAX, reached 45.7 billion won ($31.9 million), up 56.3 percent from a year earlier. Attendance rose 49 percent to 2.85 million. ... SCREENX revenue increased 31.3 percent to 5.6 billion won, while attendance rose 32.3 percent to 410,000. The format accounted for 12.3 percent of special-screening revenue and 14.4 percent of attendance. ... Industry observers say such formats are increasingly moving beyond enhancing visual spectacle to influence the production process itself, as filmmakers and cinema technology companies work more closely to create immersive theatrical experiences."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,CJ 4DPLEX's SCREENX and 4DX Deliver Record-Breaking $31 Million Global Opening for Sony Pictures' Spider-Man: Brand New Day,www.prnewswire.com (CJ 4DPLEX),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cj-4dplexs-screenx-and-4dx-deliver-record-breaking-31-million-global-opening-for-sony-pictures-spider-man-brand-new-day-302841412.html,"BURBANK, Calif., Aug. 3, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- CJ 4DPLEX, the world's leading entertainment technology and content company specializing in premium film formats, cinematic production, visual effects and immersive experiences, today announced that Sony Pictures' Spider-Man: Brand New Day achieved a record-breaking global opening of more than $31 million across SCREENX and 4DX combined, marking the biggest opening weekend in CJ 4DPLEX history. ... Domestically, both SCREENX and 4DX set new opening weekend records. SCREENX shattered its previous all-time high, grossing $7 million, 2.6 times its previous opening weekend record. 4DX also delivered its biggest opening weekend ever, generating $5.2 million from 77 locations while achieving an industry-leading per-screen average of $68,000, the highest among all premium formats. Cineplex Laval was the top-performing domestic SCREENX location, grossing $315,000 while reaching 91% occupancy. Regal Times Square 4DX, the world's largest 4DX auditorium, led all domestic 4DX locations with an impressive $200,000 gross and 94% occupancy. ... ""Spider-Man: Brand New Day delivered an unprecedented domestic debut and demonstrated that audiences continue to seek out premium theatrical experiences that simply can't be replicated at home,"" said Don Savant, CEO & President, CJ 4DPLEX Americas. ""We are deeply grateful to Sony Pictures, Marvel Studios, Director Destin Daniel Cretton, and our exhibition partners for allowing SCREENX and 4DX to play a small role in this extraordinary success. Congratulations to the entire Sony Pictures team on a remarkable achievement."" ... Internationally, Spider-Man: Brand New Day generated $19 million across SCREENX and 4DX, with standout performances in the United Kingdom, India, Australia, Mexico, France, Germany, Taiwan, Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, and Thailand, reflecting the growing global demand for CJ 4DPLEX's premium theatrical experiences. ... ""The global launch of Spider-Man: Brand New Day represents a defining moment for CJ 4DPLEX,"" said Jun Bang, CEO, CJ 4DPLEX. ""In addition to delivering the biggest opening weekend in our company's history, we're proud that SCREENX set new records in 34 countries and 4DX established new records in 19 countries, underscoring the extraordinary global momentum behind our premium formats. These historic results reflect the strength of our partnerships with Sony Pictures and exhibitors worldwide, as well as audiences' growing appetite for immersive theatrical experiences that continue to elevate the cinema experience."" ... Sony Pictures' Spider-Man: Brand New Day was""Shot for SCREENX"" and marks the first time CJ 4DPLEX collaborated with the filmmakers from on-set production through theatrical exhibition, providing them with a new creative canvas. Designed specifically for SCREENX, the experience is an authentic extension of the filmmakers' vision that further brings fans into ... world of Spider-Man™, surrounding audiences in ways uniquely possible in SCREENX auditoriums. ... Spider-Man: Brand New Day is now playing in SCREENX and 4DX theaters worldwide. ... About CJ 4DPLEXCJ 4DPLEX is a proud subsidiary of CJ Group, Korea's leading lifestyle and culture company. Headquartered in Sangam, Seoul, CJ 4DPLEX develops and operates the world's leading premium cinema technologies, partnering with major exhibitors across the Americas, Europe, Asia and the Middle East to deliver SCREENX, 4DX and ULTRA 4DX experiences. Through continuous innovation, the company is committed to expanding immersive storytelling and creating new ways for audiences around the world to experience cinema. ... ### CJ 4DPLEX PREMIUM FORMATS ACHIEVE RECORD-BREAKING FIRST HALF OF 2026 AS SCREENX SOARS 55% IN DOMESTIC BOX OFFICE ... CJ 4DPLEX, the world's leading producer of premium film formats and cinema technologies, today announced record first-half domestic box office... ... ### CJ 4DPLEX ANNOUNCES SONY PICTURES' 'SPIDER-MAN: BRAND NEW DAY' SHOT FOR SCREENX ... CJ 4DPLEX, the world's leading producer of premium cinema formats and immersive theater experiences, announced today that Sony Pictures' highly..."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"CineNow Secures Majority Backing for $150M Fund, Targets $720M in Film-IP Monetisation - Entrepreneur Middle East - Entrepreneur Middle East",mena.entrepreneur.com (Entrepreneur Middle East Staff),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mena.entrepreneur.com/business-news/cinenow-secures-majority-backing-for-150m-fund-targets-720m-in-film-ip-monetisation,"CineNow Secures Majority Backing for $150M Fund, Targets $720M in Film-IP Monetisation - Entrepreneur Middle East - Entrepreneur Middle East ... # CineNow Secures Majority Backing for $150M Fund, Targets $720M in Film-IP Monetisation The BVI-incorporated vehicle is building a $150 million fund structured to generate up to $720 million in film-IP monetisation, converting Indian film IP into a tokenized, rights-based asset class from its UAE regional base, with plans to expand into Arabic content, aviation and real estate. By Entrepreneur Middle East Staff | Aug 03, 2026 Add Entrepreneur ... You're reading Entrepreneur Middle East, an international franchise of Entrepreneur Media. CineNow Limited, a film-tech investment vehicle, has secured majority backing, over 60% for its $150 million fund from a mix of family offices and ultra-high-net-worth individuals reflecting early institutional confidence in a category historically financed through fragmented, relationship-driven capital rather than structured investments. The model is designed to transform Indian cinema intellectual property into a formally investable, rights-backed and tokenisation-ready alternative asset for global capital. ... Building on this momentum, the vehicle is targeting up to $720 million in slate monetisation and more than $1 billion in long-term film-IP value, structured through its $150 million fund with built-in capital recycling and cost efficiencies. CineNow is coordinating its next phase with UAE positioned as its headquarters for operations, investor relations and portfolio administration. ... India’s film industry offers the scale to support this model: sector revenues reached approximately $2.1 billion in 2025 across more than 1,900 releases, with domestic box office at a record $1.4 billion. Regional-language cinema comprising Telugu, Tamil, Malayalam and Kannada accounted for 44% of that box office, while 216 million paid video subscriptions across 143 million households point to continued growth in digital, satellite and franchise revenue streams alongside theatrical release. ... “Film intellectual property is one of the world’s most valuable yet undercapitalised asset classes,” said Rohit Dalmia, Chairman and Managing Director of CineNow. “Our vision is to institutionalise it by bringing together governance, technology and global capital within a transparent investment framework. Our ambition is to position the UAE as the global gateway for rights-backed entertainment investments, connecting international capital with one of the world’s fastest-growing creative economies while laying the foundation for the future tokenisation of real-world intellectual property assets.” ... CineNow’s decision to establish the UAE as its regional operating headquarters reflects the country’s position at the intersection of global capital, technology and the creative economy. The UAE offers a sophisticated legal and commercial environment for intellectual-property ownership, cross-border investment and emerging tokenisation models, supported by deep pools of institutional, family-office and private capital. Its connectivity between Western financial markets and Asian content industries makes it a natural economic and cultural corridor for CineNow. ... The relationship is designed to create reciprocal value for the UAE. CineNow intends to register and administer film intellectual property through the UAE, execute regional contracting and capital flows locally, and require participating producers to establish UAE-based entities, contributing to long-term economic substance, professional-services activity and employment. The vehicle also plans to host more than 30 film premieres, industry events and talent-led engagements in the country, strengthening the UAE’s positioning as a destination for entertainment, tourism and global media visibility. Selected productions may also be encouraged to film in the UAE, where suitable locations, production infrastructure and rebate programmes can further support local expenditure and international exposure. ... Through this model, the UAE becomes more than an administrative base. It becomes the legal, financial, technological and commercial gateway connecting international investment with Indian and subsequently, Arabic cinematic intellectual property. ... With about 60% committed towards its $150 million current target, CineNow is now focused on building awareness among the wider global investor community as it works towards closing the remaining capital. The company says its priority at this stage is establishing the category positioning film IP as a credible, structured alternative asset in the UAE. ... Building on the framework developed for film IP, the company plans to extend the same model to arabic content, aviation and real estate in the coming months, creating a diversified suite of tokenized investment opportunities governed by the same compliance and liquidity standards. The goal is to connect global capital with high-growth markets through structured, technology-driven investment vehicles with Indian cinema as the proof of concept. ... CineNow Limited, a film-tech investment vehicle, has secured majority backing, over 60% for its $150 million fund from a mix of family offices and ultra-high-net-worth individuals reflecting early institutional confidence in a category historically financed through fragmented, relationship-driven capital rather than structured investments. The model is designed to transform Indian cinema intellectual property into a formally investable, rights-backed and tokenisation-ready alternative asset for global capital. ... Building on this momentum, the vehicle is targeting up to $720 million in slate monetisation and more than $1 billion in long-term film-IP value, structured through its $150 million fund with built-in capital recycling and cost efficiencies. CineNow is coordinating its next phase with UAE positioned as its headquarters for operations, investor relations and portfolio administration."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"A Brand New Record: Cinemark Achieves Biggest Domestic Weekend Box Office of All Time as Spider-Man: Brand New Day Delivers the Company’s Highest Grossing Single-Title, Three-Day Domestic Opening | Morningstar",www.morningstar.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.morningstar.com/news/business-wire/20260803895234/a-brand-new-record-cinemark-achieves-biggest-domestic-weekend-box-office-of-all-time-as-spider-man-brand-new-day-delivers-the-companys-highest-grossing-single-title-three-day-domestic-opening,"A Brand New Record: Cinemark Achieves Biggest Domestic Weekend Box Office of All Time as Spider-Man: Brand New Day Delivers the Company’s Highest Grossing Single-Title, Three-Day Domestic Opening | Morningstar ... # A Brand New Record: Cinemark Achieves Biggest Domestic Weekend Box Office of All Time as Spider-Man: Brand New Day Delivers the Company’s Highest Grossing Single-Title, Three-Day Domestic Opening Provided by Business Wire Aug 3, 2026, 12:30:00 PM ... A Brand New Record: Cinemark Achieves Biggest Domestic Weekend Box Office of All Time as Spider-Man: Brand New Day Delivers the Company’s Highest Grossing Single-Title, Three-Day Domestic Opening Cinemark also achieved all-time records across premium formats, with the best-ever weekend for Cinemark XD, ScreenX panoramic screens and D-BOX motion seats Demand for Cinemark’s food, beverage and merchandise offerings reached new heights, driving a record food and beverage revenue weekend Cinemark Holdings, Inc. (NYSE: CNK), one of the largest and most influential theatrical exhibition companies in the world, today announced that July 31 through August 2 was the biggest domestic weekend box office of all time for the company, propelled by the sensational opening of Spider-Man: Brand New Day, with additional contribution from The Odyssey’s strong holdover performance. Additionally, the web-slinging success of Spider-Man: Brand New Day delivered Cinemark’s best-ever domestic box office for a three-day opening weekend, surpassing the previous record set by Avengers: Endgame. In addition to the all-time box office highs, Cinemark’s continued investments in premium entertainment experiences with its expansive portfolio of enhanced viewing options drove the best-ever three-day U.S. weekend results for Cinemark XD, the world’s No. 1 exhibitor-branded premium large format, ScreenX 270-degree panoramic screens and D-BOX motion seats. As moviegoers swung into theaters for Spider-Man's latest adventure, they also indulged in food, beverage and merchandise, delivering Cinemark’s highest weekend food and beverage revenue of all time. “Cinemark’s outsized performance for Spider-Man: Brand New Day across our entire global circuit once again underscores how great films in immersive, shared theatrical settings have the ability to create must-see cultural events on a heroic scale – especially at Cinemark,” said Sean Gamble, President and CEO of Cinemark. “Hats off to our global team for making such a significant impact in enabling these special moments for our guests, and congratulations to our partners at Sony and Marvel on this exceptional weekend.” Coming Soon to the Big Screen There is a diverse, compelling slate ready to excite moviegoers through the rest of the year, including Practical Magic 2 (September 11), Resident Evil (September 18), Forgotten Island (September 25), Heart of the Beast (September 25), Verity (October 2), Digger (October 2), The Cat in the Hat (November 6), The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping (November 20), Hexed (November 25), Dune: Part Three (December 18), Avengers: Doomsday (December 18) and Jumanji: Open World (December 25). The Cinemark Experience Cinemark’s commitment to delivering a preeminent out-of-home entertainment experience comes to fruition through continual investment in its theaters and customer journey. - Fan-favorite Luxury Lounger recliners, with approximately 72 percent of the domestic circuit reclined. ... - Cinemark XD, the number one private-label premium large format in the world with over 300 auditoriums across the U.S. and Latin America, representing 13 percent of global box office in 2025 on 5 percent of screens. - Largest footprint of D-BOX motion seats with over 650 auditoriums. ... - Everyone’s favorite mouth-watering movie theater concessions with free refills on large drinks and XL popcorn, in addition to robust food and beverage offerings, with 80 percent of U.S. theaters offering restaurant-quality menu items and 60 percent offering beer, wine and alcohol. Guests can skip the line and order their cinema snacks ahead of time on the Cinemark app. ... - Must-have movie merchandise in theaters as well as online at shop.cinemark.com. - Superior sight and sound technology delivered by top-of-the-line multi-channel surround sound and Barco digital and laser projectors managed by an industry-leading technology team that delivers a 99.97 percent uptime across thousands of showtimes every day. This means moviegoers can count on Cinemark for a smooth, uninterrupted presentation. ... - Guest service scores that consistently reach satisfaction ratings from approximately 95 percent of domestic guests surveyed. ... - Cinemark Movie Club, the industry-leading movie theater subscription program with more than 1.5 million members in addition to Movie Rewards free loyalty program with outstanding member rewards. - Steeply discounted movie tickets at Cinemark theaters on Discount Tuesday, with Movie Rewards members saving even more. ... - National partnerships with UberEats, Door Dash, Grubhub and 7NOW to satisfy those movie theater concessions cravings at home. For full details about the Cinemark moviegoing experience, visit Cinemark.com or download the Cinemark app. Click HERE for general Cinemark images and b-roll. About Cinemark Holdings, Inc. Cinemark Holdings, Inc. (NYSE: CNK) provides extraordinary out-of-home entertainment experiences as one of the largest and most influential theatrical exhibition companies in the world. Based in Plano, Texas, Cinemark makes every day cinematic for moviegoers across nearly 500 theaters and more than 5,500 screens, operating in 42 states in the U.S. (301 theaters; 4,219 screens) and 13 South and Central American countries (194 theaters; 1,401 screens). Cinemark offers guests superior sight and sound technology, including Barco laser projection and Cinemark XD, the world’s No. 1 exhibitor-branded premium large format; industry-leading penetration of upscale amenities such as expanded food and beverage offerings, Luxury Lounger recliners and D-BOX motion seats; top-notch guest service; and award-winning loyalty programs such as Cinemark Movie Club. All of this creates an immersive environment for a shared, entertaining escape, underscoring that there is no place more cinematic than Cinemark. For more information, visit https://ir.cinemark.com. Cinemark Contacts: Media: Julia McCartha pr@cinemark.com Investors: Chanda Brashears investors@cinemark.com"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,CJ 4DPLEX's SCREENX and 4DX Deliver Record-Breaking $31 Million Global Opening for Sony Pictures' Spider-Man: Brand New Day,www.prnewswire.com (CJ 4DPLEX),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/in/news-releases/cj-4dplexs-screenx-and-4dx-deliver-record-breaking-31-million-global-opening-for-sony-pictures-spider-man-brand-new-day-302841426.html,"BURBANK, Calif., Aug. 3, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- CJ 4DPLEX, the world's leading entertainment technology and content company specializing in premium film formats, cinematic production, visual effects and immersive experiences, today announced that Sony Pictures' Spider-Man: Brand New Day achieved a record-breaking global opening of more than $31 million across SCREENX and 4DX combined, marking the biggest opening weekend in CJ 4DPLEX history. ... Domestically, both SCREENX and 4DX set new opening weekend records. SCREENX shattered its previous all-time high, grossing $7 million, 2.6 times its previous opening weekend record. 4DX also delivered its biggest opening weekend ever, generating $5.2 million from 77 locations while achieving an industry-leading per-screen average of $68,000, the highest among all premium formats. Cineplex Laval was the top-performing domestic SCREENX location, grossing $315,000 while reaching 91% occupancy. Regal Times Square 4DX, the world's largest 4DX auditorium, led all domestic 4DX locations with an impressive $200,000 gross and 94% occupancy. ... ""Spider-Man: Brand New Day delivered an unprecedented domestic debut and demonstrated that audiences continue to seek out premium theatrical experiences that simply can't be replicated at home,"" said Don Savant, CEO & President, CJ 4DPLEX Americas. ""We are deeply grateful to Sony Pictures, Marvel Studios, Director Destin Daniel Cretton, and our exhibition partners for allowing SCREENX and 4DX to play a small role in this extraordinary success. Congratulations to the entire Sony Pictures team on a remarkable achievement."" ... Internationally, Spider-Man: Brand New Day generated $19 million across SCREENX and 4DX, with standout performances in the United Kingdom, India, Australia, Mexico, France, Germany, Taiwan, Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, and Thailand, reflecting the growing global demand for CJ 4DPLEX's premium theatrical experiences. ... ""The global launch of Spider-Man: Brand New Day represents a defining moment for CJ 4DPLEX,"" said Jun Bang, CEO, CJ 4DPLEX. ""In addition to delivering the biggest opening weekend in our company's history, we're proud that SCREENX set new records in 34 countries and 4DX established new records in 19 countries, underscoring the extraordinary global momentum behind our premium formats. These historic results reflect the strength of our partnerships with Sony Pictures and exhibitors worldwide, as well as audiences' growing appetite for immersive theatrical experiences that continue to elevate the cinema experience."" ... Brand New Day ... ""Shot for ... Spider-Man: Brand New Day is now playing in SCREENX and 4DX theaters worldwide. ... About CJ 4DPLEXCJ 4DPLEX is a proud subsidiary of CJ Group, Korea's leading lifestyle and culture company. Headquartered in Sangam, Seoul, CJ 4DPLEX develops and operates the world's leading premium cinema technologies, partnering with major exhibitors across the Americas, Europe, Asia and the Middle East to deliver SCREENX, 4DX and ULTRA 4DX experiences. Through continuous innovation, the company is committed to expanding immersive storytelling and creating new ways for audiences around the world to experience cinema. ... ### CJ 4DPLEX ANNOUNCES SONY PICTURES' 'SPIDER-MAN: BRAND NEW DAY' SHOT FOR SCREENX ... CJ 4DPLEX, the world's leading producer of premium cinema formats and immersive theater experiences, announced today that Sony Pictures' highly... ... ### CJ 4DPLEX and AMC Theatres Launch First Four Premium SCREENX and 4DX Locations in the United States ... CJ 4DPLEX, the world's leading producer of premium cinema formats and immersive theater technologies, and AMC Theatres (NYSE:AMC), the largest..."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Excel Entertainment Launches Excel Music with Universal Music Group,thenewsmill.com,2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thenewsmill.com/2026/08/excel-entertainment-launches-excel-music-with-universal-music-group-partnership/,"Excel Entertainment Launches Excel Music with Universal Music Group ... # Excel Entertainment launches Excel Music with Universal Music Group partnership ... Excel Entertainment, founded by filmmakers Ritesh Sidhwani and Farhan Akhtar, has launched Excel Music, a new music label dedicated to original film soundtracks and scores. Universal Music Group has joined as a strategic shareholder and will serve as the label’s marketing and distribution partner. ... The first release from Excel Music will be the soundtrack album for ‘Mirzapur: The Movie’, scheduled for theatrical release on September 4, 2026. The album’s opening track will feature Haryanvi singer Dhanda, marking his Bollywood debut, with the song set to release later this week. ... Over the past two decades, Excel Entertainment has produced numerous acclaimed films including Dil Chahta Hai, Lakshya, Rock On!!, Karthik Calling Karthik, Zindagi Na Milegi Dobara, Dil Dhadakne Do, Baar Baar Dekho, Raees, and Gully Boy. The production house stated that Excel Music will release music not only from its own films but also collaborate with filmmakers and production companies across India. ... Sanujeet Bhujabal, Managing Director, India & South Asia, Universal Music Group, expressed enthusiasm for the partnership, stating, “Excel Entertainment has built a strong place in Hindi cinema over the years, and the company is looking forward to working together on the new label.” ... With Excel Music, Excel Entertainment is expanding its scope beyond film production into the music industry, beginning with the soundtrack of ‘Mirzapur: The Movie’."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Tandem PV acquires transparent coating tech firm nexTC to advance perovskite manufacturing - pv magazine USA,pv-magazine-usa.com (Ben Zientara),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/08/03/tandem-pv-acquires-transparent-coating-tech-firm-nextc-to-advance-perovskite-manufacturing/,"Tandem PV acquires transparent coating tech firm nexTC to advance perovskite manufacturing - pv magazine USA ... # Tandem PV acquires transparent coating tech firm nexTC to advance perovskite manufacturing ... Tandem PV has acquired Oregon startup nexTC, bringing the latter’s firm’s advanced thin-film metal oxide coating processes in-house and allowing the manufacturer greater control over a critical step as it ramps up its perovskite-silicon demonstration line. ... California-based Tandem PV has announced the acquisition of nexTC Corporation, a developer of advanced thin-film metal oxide coating processes based in Corvallis, Oregon. ... The acquisition will see nexTC founder and CEO Cory Perkins, Ph.D. joining TandemPV as it integrates the nexTC technology into its 40 MW commercial demonstration production line, on which it is producing large-format tandem solar panels for customer validation and market trials. ... “We’ve worked with Cory for years and know firsthand the value of his expertise in oxide thin films, which are critical to building durable, high-performing perovskite modules,” said Tandem PV CEO Scott Wharton in a statement. “Bringing Cory’s expertise and nexTC’s technology into Tandem gives us greater control over a core part of the manufacturing process and allows us to optimize it directly on our production line as we scale.” ... The nexTC acquisition represents another step in Tandem PV’s efforts to commercialize tandem solar technology, which combines a perovskite-bearing top glass layer over a traditional silicon solar module bottom layer. ... To date, the company says it has raised $100 million in capital from investors including Eclipse, Constellation Energy and the U.S. Department of Energy. The company also recently expanded its leadership team by adding former U.S. Energy Secretary Jennifer Granholm to its board of directors."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Nexus G1 Adds LiDAR Sensor-Fusion Autofocus That Works in Total Darkness,"www.techtimes.com (James Whitaker Published: Aug 03 2026, 10:36 AM EDT)",2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.techtimes.com/articles/322821/20260803/nexus-g1-adds-lidar-sensor-fusion-autofocus-that-works-total-darkness.htm,"Australian cinema camera startup Nexus has published its eleventh project update for the long-awaited G1, unveiling CINAF — a sensor-fusion autofocus system that fuses five distinct data streams to focus any lens, electronic or manual, including in total darkness — and confirming that its interchangeable U-Mount system will now ship as standard equipment with every unit. Shipping dates are still pending a future announcement, but the company says final integration testing is progressing and the next update will include confirmed delivery timelines alongside a live demonstration of the finished camera. ... The camera has missed two successive shipping targets — originally planned for 2024, then pushed to Q3 2025, then Q1 2026 — and Update #11 arrives after a gap of roughly eight months since the previous communication. In the update, the company acknowledges the delays directly: the team has been working seven days a week to complete production of a camera that comprises nearly 200 unique custom parts requiring more than 20 distinct manufacturing techniques. ... Both major cinema technology outlets that covered the announcement were careful to separate the architectural claim from verified field performance. RedShark News's Andy Stout noted that CINAF's real-world performance remains to be proven — ""the proof of such puddings is always in the eating"" — appropriate caution given that CINAF has not yet been independently tested. CineD similarly noted it looks forward to seeing how the system performs under real-world conditions. ... What RedShark's assessment does note is that Nexus's track record through the development process — the sustained series of updates, the concrete engineering disclosures, and the willingness to acknowledge delays and explain ... technical reasons behind them — ... with the crowdfunding hardware projects that generate deposits and then disappear. ... The second major announcement in Update #11 is the U-Mount inclusion. Previously planned as a paid optional accessory, the Nexus U-Mount interchangeable lens mount system will now ship standard with every G1 at no additional cost. ... U-Mount is Nexus's more capable successor to its original AutoLock lens mount system. It uses swappable mount modules — covering EF, E, MFT, L, PL, and other lens ecosystems — with a one-click installation mechanism, automatic positive locking, and a push-button release that requires no tools. In combination with CINAF's universal autofocus, this makes the G1 a notably flexible platform: a filmmaker can use modern Sony G Master glass with full electronic autofocus in one configuration, swap to a vintage Leica R prime with LiDAR-driven FIZ control in the next, and switch to a PL-mount cinema lens for a third setup, all on the same body and with the same autofocus system handling focus in each case. ... Production components are currently moving through manufacturing, finishing, and validation stages. Nexus says hardware and software are converging toward final integration validation, and the next project update will announce confirmed shipping dates alongside a real-world demonstration of the finished camera — including CINAF and the electronic ND system — in actual use. ... The G1 remains available for preorder with a 10% deposit. Preorder customers receive the Founders Edition at $2,980, a $320 discount from the standard retail price of $3,300. The deposit is credited toward the final purchase price. All Founders Edition units include custom markings and Lightning Strike carbon fiber side panels. The camera will be manufactured and assembled in Australia. Visit the Nexus G1 preorder page for full pricing and availability details. ... For a small startup, the G1's development trajectory has been unusual: multiple missed deadlines, yes, but accompanied by concrete engineering disclosures and repeated additions to the spec sheet beyond what was originally promised. CINAF, NexusOS, the electronic ND system, and now U-Mount as standard equipment are all additions that post-date the original 2024 announcement. The next update — with its promised shipping date and live demonstration — will be the one that finally resolves whether that trajectory ends in delivery. ... The main financial risk is loss of the 10% deposit (approximately $298 at the Founders Edition price) if the company fails to deliver. Nexus is not a crowdfunding campaign — it accepts deposits rather than full payment — and its development track record over two-plus years has been characterized by regular engineering disclosures, concrete updates, and additions to the specification sheet. RedShark News specifically noted the company's behavior compares favorably with hardware crowdfunding projects that generate deposits and then go silent. That said, no independent party has tested the finished camera, shipping dates remain unannounced, and preorder customers are making a bet on a still-undelivered product."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,HYOSUNG TNC Posts 'Strong Earnings'; Shares Rise Over 4% on Bullish Outlook for Spandex Market [Featured Stock] - EDAILY,en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202608035151/,"Posts 'Strong Earnings'; Shares Rise Over 4 ... on Bullish Outlook for Spandex Market [Featured Stock] - EDAILY ... ## HYOSUNG TNC Posts 'Strong Earnings'; Shares Rise Over 4% on Bullish Outlook for Spandex Market [Featured Stock] ... [Edaily Reporter Shin Ha-yeon ] HYOSUNG TNC(298020)is trading up more than 4% in early trading on the back of a strong spandex market and prospects for improved earnings.According to MP Doctor on the 3rd, as of 9:10 a.m., HYOSUNG TNC is trading at 322,000 won, up 4.55% from the previous trading day. A panoramic view of HYOSUNG TNC’s spandex plant in India. (Photo = Yonhap News) This is believed to be driven by investment sentiment spurred by securities analysts’ forecasts that a robust supply-demand environment will persist through next year, as spandex prices and spreads continue to strengthen.NH INVESTMENT & SECURITIES maintained its “Buy” rating on HYOSUNG TNC today and raised its target price by 9.3% from 430,000 won to 470,000 won.Choi Young-gwang, an analyst at NH INVESTMENT & SECURITIES, stated, “We have raised our 2027 operating profit forecast by 12.3% from the previous estimate to reflect stronger-than-expected spandex prices, spreads, and overall market conditions,” adding, “We expect the robust supply-demand balance for spandex to continue into 2027.”HYOSUNG TNC’s second-quarter operating profit reached 188.8 billion won, an 118.9% increase from the previous quarter, exceeding market expectations. Operating profit in the textiles division rose 124.5% quarter-over-quarter to 165.2 billion won, while operating profit in the trade and other divisions also increased by 87.3% to 23.6 billion won.Analyst Choi predicted, “With no planned spandex capacity expansions in 2026 and considering the expected increase in demand in 2027, utilization rates will rise, leading to a continued robust supply-demand balance.” He added, “Since inventories at Chonbang fabric manufacturers are at historic lows, the impact of the off-season in the second half of the year is expected to be milder than in previous years.”"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Spider-Man: Brand New Day tops Nigerian preview charts with N120.4m – Rifnote,www.rifnote.ng,2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.rifnote.ng/spider-man-brand-new-day-tops-nigerian-preview-charts-with-n120-4m/,"Spider-Man: Brand New Day tops Nigerian preview charts with N120.4m – Rifnote ... Spider-Man: Brand New Day has set a new Nigerian box office record with N120.4 million in preview screenings, ahead of a projected N500 million opening five-day run. ... Spider-Man: Brand New Day Sets N120.4m Preview Record in Nigeria ... Spidey swings past the competition. Per Nairametrics, data from Film Intelligence shows the Marvel-Sony blockbuster shattered Nigeria’s previous preview record, reflecting Hollywood franchise films’ growing commercial pull in the country. ... Despite the record previews, The Odyssey remained the week’s top earner, adding N63.6 million to reach N423.8 million after two weeks. Analysts expect Spider-Man to overtake it once full weekend numbers arrive. ... Elsewhere, Nollywood’s Call of My Life hit N826.2 million, retaining its spot as 2026’s top Nigerian film. Internationally, Spider-Man: Brand New Day earned a record $72 million in US previews, surpassing Avengers: Endgame, with a projected $260-280 million opening weekend."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,KDX and NXT Prepare for August 13 Fractional Investment Exchange License Deadline in South Korea | Gate News,www.gate.com,2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gate.com/news/detail/kdx-and-nxt-prepare-for-august-13-fractional-investment-exchange-license-23067147,"KDX and NXT Prepare for August 13 Fractional Investment Exchange License Deadline in South Korea | Gate News ... - KDX and NXT must submit formal licensing applications to South Korean financial authorities by August 13 deadline. - South Korean regulators require fractional investment exchanges to maintain 6 billion won minimum capital and eight IT specialists. - Shinhan Investment Securities and MusicCow plan to create a 40 billion won music intellectual property fractional investment fund. ... KDX and NXT, two South Korean consortiums operating fractional investment over-the-counter exchanges, are preparing formal licensing applications with a deadline of August 13, approximately two weeks away as of July 30. Both consortiums received preliminary approval from financial authorities in February and must submit capital approval and formal license applications within six months. South Korean financial regulators require a minimum capital of 6 billion won and staffing of at least one trading execution specialist and eight IT specialists for these exchanges. ... KDX and NXT consortiums received preliminary approval for fractional investment OTC brokerage operations from South Korean financial authorities in February. Both must apply for capital approval and formal licensing within six months, with the formal license application deadline set for August 13. The Financial Services Commission established minimum requirements of 6 billion won in capital and staffing of one trading execution specialist and eight IT specialists. ... KDX established its legal entity in mid-April. The consortium appointed a CEO and continued staff expansion, with approximately 30 employees currently working at the company. KDX received the highest evaluation in the capital adequacy category during the preliminary approval review. The consortium is focusing on IT infrastructure preparation while continuing personnel expansion. ... as NexChange ... NXT applied for capital approval under the name ""NexChange"" in May but has not completed corporate establishment. The consortium is accelerating related procedures after allegations of technology theft raised by LucentBlock were concluded with no charges. NXT plans to complete corporate establishment and staff hiring while immediately submitting its formal license application given the approaching deadline. The consortium is currently hiring approximately 10 people and accelerating physical and human resource preparations. ... Shinhan Investment Securities and MusicCow, both shareholders with stakes exceeding 5% in the NXT consortium, decided to pursue creating a 40 billion won fund to issue fractional investment products using music intellectual property. MusicCow pioneered South Korea's fractional investment era by launching music copyright fractional investment services in 2017. Shinhan Investment Securities is expanding fractional investment account management platforms to four locations with TogetherArt, a participant in the NXT consortium, to preemptively improve investor accessibility and infrastructure convenience. KDX's shareholder composition includes multiple fintech companies such as CasaKorea, which are preparing competitive products for the exchange launch. One financial investment industry official stated that exchanges engage in activities to attract listed companies centered on the KOSDAQ market, and fractional investment OTC exchanges cannot avoid conducting attraction activities to secure competitive products given their exchange role. ... The formal license application deadline for both KDX and NXT consortiums is August 13, approximately two weeks away as of July 30. Both consortiums received preliminary approval in February and must submit capital approval and formal licensing within six months. ... The Financial Services Commission requires a minimum capital of 6 billion won and staffing of at least one trading execution specialist and eight IT specialists for fractional investment OTC exchanges. ... Shinhan Investment Securities and MusicCow, both shareholders with stakes exceeding 5% in the NXT consortium, decided to pursue creating a 40 billion won fund to issue fractional investment products using music intellectual property. ... 07-3 ... 01:30KDX and NXT Race to Secure Formal Approval for Fractional Investment Exchanges by August 13 Deadline"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,On the ‘Spider-Man’ Set: CJ 4DPLEX Launches Immersive ‘Shot for SCREENX’ Initiative,newsroom.cj.net,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://newsroom.cj.net/shot-for-screenx-spider-man-4dplex,"#### For 17 years, CJ 4DPLEX has been redefining what it means to experience cinema — building formats, deepening studio partnerships and expanding its global footprint, one film at a time. The company’s latest initiative to bring immersive cinema to viewers, Shot for SCREENX, debuts with “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” ... What began as a bold experiment in Seoul has since grown into a global network of 4DX and SCREENX locations spanning more than 1,260 screens across 76 countries — generating 497 million USD in combined global box office in 2025 alone, a 32% increase year over year. ... “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” is the first title to carry the Shot for SCREENX designation. Under the Shot for SCREENX model, CJ 4DPLEX works with directors from the production stage — capturing footage conceived and designed specifically for SCREENX’s 270-degree panoramic environment, shaping what audiences will experience on the side walls of the auditorium. Building on CJ 4DPLEX’s established SCREENX capabilities, Shot for SCREENX represents a new collaborative possibility — one in which global studios and filmmakers can work with CJ 4DPLEX from the production stage to craft a SCREENX experience tailored to their creative vision. ... “Spider-Man: Brand New Day,” opening July 31 in SCREENX theaters worldwide, will serve as the first major showcase of what Shot for SCREENX can deliver at full scale. ... Seventeen years ago, CJ 4DPLEX set out to expand the boundaries of what audiences could experience inside a theater. With Shot for SCREENX, that pursuit takes on a new dimension — one that begins not in the auditorium, but on set, in collaboration with the filmmakers who bring stories to life. As CJ 4DPLEX continues to grow its global network of 4DX and SCREENX locations, Shot for SCREENX stands as part of CJ 4DPLEX’s ongoing exploration of what becomes possible when immersive cinema technology and creative vision come together. ... - CJ ENM Hosts a Semi-Final Round of Judging for the 2026 International Emmy® Awards for the Second Consecutive Year 2026.08.06 - CJ ENM Expands Strategic Partnership with Prime Video India, Bringing Over 100 Korean Titles to Indian Audiences 2026.08.05 - CJ ENM Earns 12 Nominations Across Seven Categories at the ContentAsia Awards 2026 2026.08.05 ... Shot for SCREENX” poster for “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” At a Glance A mainstay of Korea’s dining culture — chimaek — the popular pairing of fried chicken and beer — has become one of the country’s most recognizable food exports. The crisp texture and sauce-coated finish that define Korean fried chicken have long been difficult to reproduce in frozen products. CJ Foods says its proprietary sauce-coating technology helped overcome this challenge. Before launching as an independent brand in June 2026, Sobaba sold more than 25 million bags and expanded distribution across the United States, Japan and Europe. CJ Foods plans to grow Sobaba into a global chicken brand spanning retail, restaurants and delivery channels. “CJ 4DPLEX and their team came to the set of ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ to shoot footage that you will experience specifically for SCREENX auditoriums,” said director Destin Daniel Cretton. “This is something truly unique.” On the set of “Spider-Man: Brand New Day,” CJ 4DPLEX rolled cameras alongside the production crew, capturing footage designed specifically for SCREENX theaters. It was, in every sense, something new. 4DX enables viewers to immerse themselves in the film through augmented physical special effects. From Sensation to Format: How 4DX and SCREENX Were Born (2009-2012) Since its founding, CJ 4DPLEX has been driven by a single pursuit: expanding the boundaries of immersive experience that are only possible inside a theater.In 2009, CJ 4DPLEX introduced 4DX at CGV Sangam in Seoul — a thrilling cinema experience in which seats moved, wind blew and water sprayed in sync with the action on screen. The idea was simple but radical: What if the theater itself became part of the story? While the broader industry was skeptical, CJ 4DPLEX pushed forward with a clear conviction — that the cinema experience could offer something no living room ever could. Three years later, in 2012, that conviction took another shape. CJ 4DPLEX developed SCREENX — the world’s first multi-projection cinema format and its most immersive platform — extending scenes beyond the main screen and onto the side walls of the theater to place audiences at the heart of the movie through a 270-degree panoramic viewing environment. What began as a bold experiment in Seoul has since grown into a global network of 4DX and SCREENX locations spanning more than 1,260 screens across 76 countries — generating 497 million USD in combined global box office in 2025 alone, a 32% increase year over year. A snapshot of CJ 4DPLEX’s global footprint and growth. Growing Into a Collaborator: Studio Partnerships (2012-2024) During this period, 4DX continued to grow its global footprint, while CJ 4DPLEX deepened its creative collaboration with studios through SCREENX — learning how to bring each director’s vision to life within the 270-degree panoramic environment. Building industry recognition for an entirely new cinema format took time, but each collaboration demonstrated the format’s creative potential. The turning point came with “Top Gun: Maverick,” released in 2022. During production, director Joseph Kosinski installed six cameras inside the fighter jet cockpits to capture the raw aerial action. Working closely with Kosinski and Paramount Pictures, CJ 4DPLEX incorporated side camera footage from the film’s six-camera cockpit array into the SCREENX version, filling both wings of the format with real photography.. The result was 58 minutes of exclusive SCREENX imagery — the most ever produced for a single film at the time. The collaboration was one of many that continued to deepen the creative possibilities of SCREENX — and the relationship between CJ 4DPLEX and the filmmakers who brought their visions to the format. SCREENX is the world’s first multi-projection platform, providing viewers with a triple-screen viewing experience. Stepping Onto the Set: The Launch of Shot for SCREENX (2025-2026) “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” is the first title to carry the Shot for SCREENX designation. Under the Shot for SCREENX model, CJ 4DPLEX works with directors from the production stage — capturing footage conceived and designed specifically for SCREENX’s 270-degree panoramic environment, shaping what audiences will experience on the side walls of the auditorium. Building on CJ 4DPLEX’s established SCREENX capabilities, Shot for SCREENX represents a new collaborative possibility — one in which global studios and filmmakers can work with CJ 4DPLEX from the production stage to craft a SCREENX experience tailored to their creative vision. “Shot for SCREENX represents an exciting evolution for our format,” said Jun Bang, CEO of CJ 4DPLEX. “Our goal is to create a more encompassing experience that brings audiences closer to the story, the action and the world of Spider-Man.” “Spider-Man: Brand New Day,” opening July 31 in SCREENX theaters worldwide, will serve as the first major showcase of what Shot for SCREENX can deliver at full scale. CJ 4DPLEX has innovated cinema technology since 2009, continuously bringing new experiences to theatergoers globally. Seventeen years ago, CJ 4DPLEX set out to expand the boundaries of what audiences could experience inside a theater. With Shot for SCREENX, that pursuit takes on a new dimension — one that begins not in the auditorium, but on set, in collaboration with the filmmakers who bring stories to life. As CJ 4DPLEX continues to grow its global network of 4DX and SCREENX locations, Shot for SCREENX stands as part of CJ 4DPLEX’s ongoing exploration of what becomes possible when immersive"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Influence Media Partners to Acquire Anthem Publishing for $600 Million,variety.com (Jem Aswad),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://variety.com/2026/music/news/influence-media-partners-acquire-anthem-600-million-1236824616/,"Influence Media Partners to Acquire Anthem Publishing for $600 Million Influence Media Partners to Acquire Anthem Publishing for $600 Million ... Influence Media Partners, in collaboration with funds and accounts managed by affiliates of BlackRock, has signed an agreement to acquire substantially all of the assets of Anthem Entertainment: its music publishing catalogs, film & TV publishing assets and its portfolio of master recordings, for a purchase price of $600 million-plus. ... The catalogs include more than 24,000 released songs and 60,000+ additional unexploited works, including shares in such such as Britney Spears’ “Oops!… I Did It Again”; Justin Timberlake’s “SexyBack”; Timbaland’s “The Way I Are”; Cody Johnson’s “Til You Can’t”; Rush’s “Tom Sawyer”; OneRepublic’s “Counting Stars”; and others from songwriters Jordan Davis, Shane Profitt, and Chris Janson. The film & TV catalog contains soundtracks from iconic movies and television shows such as the “Spider-Man” franchise, the “Men in Black” franchise, and Lego Ninjago. The transaction is subject to customary closing conditions and is expected to close in Q4 2026. ... “This acquisition marks a major milestone for Influence Media and reflects the momentum we’ve built as a platform. Anthem’s catalog extends far beyond hit songs – it’s music that has become woven into iconic moments, films, and shows that audiences around the world know and love,” said Lylette Pizarro McLean, Influence Media Founder & Co-Managing Partner. “We’re proud to welcome these works into the Influence portfolio as we continue our next chapter of growth with the support of BlackRock, and look forward to collaborating with our industry-leading partners to create new opportunities and drive exposure for the works and the artists behind them.” Influence Media Partners’ portfolio includes DJ Khaled, Future, and Enrique Iglesias. ... Paul Braude, CIO of Direct Private Opportunities Group at BlackRock, said: “Anthem’s catalog exemplifies the high-quality, scaled intellectual property assets we seek within Direct Private Opportunities at BlackRock. Influence Media has built a differentiated platform with deep industry expertise and strong talent relationships, and we are pleased to broaden our partnership through this transaction.” ... Jason Klein, CEO of Anthem Entertainment Inc., said: “Over two decades, Anthem has built a rich and diverse catalog of songs, recordings, and film and television music. It has been a privilege to serve as custodian of this extraordinary music over the past three years, and I am proud of the dedication and integrity my team has brought to realizing its value.” ... Truist led the debt financing raise to support the transaction and served as financial advisor to Influence. Influence was advised by Alter, Kendrick & Baron; McDermott Will & Schulte; and McCarthy Tétrault. BlackRock was advised by Clifford Chance and Stikeman Elliott. Goldman Sachs served as exclusive financial advisor to Anthem, and Osler, Hoskin & Harcourt served as Anthem’s legal counsel."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,The sector is heating up! Multiple listed companies are intensively investing in PEEK projects. - ChemNet,news.chemnet.com,2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://news.chemnet.com/news-8124.html,"Following the announcement by domestic PEEK leader Zhongyan Shares that it would invest 100 million yuan to establish a subsidiary, Zhongyan Tuopu, to advance the implementation of an integrated project with an annual output of 10,000 tons of polyether ether ketone (PEEK) polymer materials and 2,000 tons of raw materials, three other domestic companies have recently seen significant progress in their PEEK-related projects, and the industry expansion boom continues to heat up. ... On July 27, DFBP (4,4'-difluorobenzophenone) leader Xinhan New Materials replied to the second round of inquiry from the Shenzhen Stock Exchange regarding its private placement and simultaneously disclosed the revised prospectus for the 2026 fixed-raise. The company's non-public issuance is expected to raise a total of no more than 1 billion yuan. The funds will be invested in three major projects, focusing on building an integrated system of ""core raw materials—resins—composite materials"" for specialty engineering plastics. ... Among the fundraising sectors, the annual output of 8,100 tons of high-performance resins and composite materials supporting project plans to form a capacity of 3,000 tons of PAEK resins and 5,100 tons of thermoplastic composite materials. The products cover modified materials such as PAEK, polyetherimide, polyphenylene sulfide, and PTFE. The project is scheduled to start in 2026 with a construction period of 36 months and will be completed and put into operation in 2029. ... The annual output of 5,000 tons of monomers project is an expansion of the existing main business, with the goal of adding 5,000 tons of DFBP capacity. DFBP is a key upstream raw material for synthesizing PEEK and directly affects the quality of the resin. This project can stabilize the supply of PEEK raw materials and strengthen cost competitiveness. In addition, the company is simultaneously building a high-performance composite material innovation center to improve R&D and testing support. ... Xinhan New Materials analyzes that the specialty engineering plastics industry continues to receive policy support, and downstream demand is steadily expanding. Although new supply in the industry continues to be released, overall supply and demand remain tight, and the new capacity after the completion of the new projects has room for market absorption. ... On July 27, the Tai'an Ecological Environment Bureau accepted the environmental impact assessment documents for Shandong Xiangyue New Materials' specialty engineering plastic polyether ether ketone polymer and supporting raw materials project. ... Shandong Xiangyue New Materials was established in July 2025 and is 80% held by Shandong Zhuotai Grease. Zhuotai Grease, which mainly deals with waste mineral oil recovery and lubricating oil processing, has officially crossed the border into the PEEK new materials track through its subsidiary. ... The total project investment is 184.486 million yuan, constructed in two phases, located within the Zhuotai Grease factory area in Ningyang Chemical Industrial Park. ... The first phase investment is 119.486 million yuan, building DFBP, polyaluminum chloride, and PEEK resin production lines. After completion, it will produce 1,000 tons of DFBP, 500 tons of PEEK resin annually, and co-produce 6,000 tons of polyaluminum chloride; ... The second phase adds a PEEK resin production line, forming another 500 tons of PEEK capacity. ... After the full completion of the project, the simultaneous production of PEEK and its core raw materials will be realized, further expanding the domestic supply map of PEEK and DFBP. ... Baihua Group Acquires Project Land, Promoting the Implementation of the Annual 1,000-Ton PEEK Project ... On July 21, organic pigment listed company Baihua Group secured the Hang Qiantang Gong Chu [2026] No. 12 plot, with a land area of 29.499 mu. The plot will be used to build the PEEK material project. This plot is integrated with the 132.067 mu of land previously acquired by the company, forming a total land scale of approximately 162 mu, for the coordinated layout of high-performance organic pigments, electronic chemicals, and high-end new material industries. ... As early as January 30 this year, Baihua Group announced a plan to invest no more than 100 million yuan to build an annual output of 1,000 tons of PEEK material project, located in the Linjiang High-tech Park, Qiantang District, Hangzhou. The project is implemented in two phases. The first phase has an investment cap of 50 million yuan (including land purchase) and a construction period of 12 months. After completion, it will form a capacity of 200 tons of PEEK; the second phase capacity will be launched based on market conditions. ... Currently, the company has formed a professional PEEK technical team and laid out the PEEK track to seize opportunities in high-end material demand in the fields of aerospace, medical, new energy, electronics and electrical, and industrial manufacturing, achieving an extension from traditional pigments to the high-performance engineering plastics field."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Confirmed: Influence Media Partners to acquire Anthem Entertainment catalogs for over USD $600M - Music Business Worldwide,www.musicbusinessworldwide.com (Murray Stassen),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/influence-media-partners-to-acquire-anthem-entertainment-catalogs-for-over-usd-600m/,"Confirmed: Influence Media Partners to acquire Anthem Entertainment catalogs for over USD $600M - Music Business Worldwide ... Influence Media Partners has signed an agreement to acquire substantially all of the assets of Anthem Entertainment for a purchase price of over $600 million. ... The deal was struck in collaboration with funds and accounts managed by affiliates of BlackRock, and covers Anthem‘s music publishing catalogs, its film and TV publishing assets, and its portfolio of master recordings. ... The transaction is subject to customary closing conditions and is expected to close in Q4 2026. ... Anthem‘s film and TV catalog contains soundtracks from franchises including Spider-Man, Men in Black and LEGO Ninjago. ... MBW reported in June, citing Billboard, that Influence Media had emerged as the winning bidder for Anthem‘s music assets, with the outlet putting the firm’s offer at a little over $650 million. ... It was the third time in a decade that the assets had been offered for sale, and the first to yield a buyer, after auctions in 2017 and 2022 fell short. ... Anthem’s controlling shareholder, the Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan, is set to exit through the sale, MBW reported. ... “This acquisition marks a major milestone for Influence Media and reflects the momentum we’ve built as a platform,” said Lylette Pizarro McLean, Influence Media Founder and Co-Managing Partner. ... “Anthem‘s catalog extends far beyond hit songs – it’s music that has become woven into iconic moments, films, and shows that audiences around the world know and love. ... “We’re proud to welcome these works into the Influence portfolio as we continue our next chapter of growth with the support of BlackRock, and look forward to collaborating with our industry-leading partners to create new opportunities and drive exposure for the works and the artists behind them.” ... “Anthem’s catalog exemplifies the high-quality, scaled intellectual property assets we seek within Direct Private Opportunities at BlackRock,” said Paul Braude, CIO of Direct Private Opportunities Group at BlackRock. ... “Influence Media has built a differentiated platform with deep industry expertise and strong talent relationships, and we are pleased to broaden our partnership through this transaction. We believe renowned entertainment assets with enduring cultural relevance can deliver long-term value for our investors.” ... “Over two decades, Anthem has built a rich and diverse catalog of songs, recordings, and film and television music,” said Jason Klein, CEO of Anthem Entertainment. ... “It has been a privilege to serve as custodian of this extraordinary music over the past three years, and I am proud of the dedication and integrity my team has brought to realizing its value. As we complete this sale, I am pleased to see our catalog and talented songwriters enter their next era supported by a creator-led independent with the vision and resources to unlock new opportunities and elevate them further.” ... Truist led the debt financing for the transaction and served as financial advisor to Influence Media. ... Goldman Sachs served as exclusive financial advisor to Anthem. ... Influence Media Partners is a New York-based music and entertainment company founded in 2019 and led by Founder and Co-Managing Partner Lylette Pizarro McLean. ... The company formed a $750 million fund with BlackRock Alternative Investors and Warner Music Group in 2022 to invest in music copyrights, as previously reported by MBW. ... It has since acquired catalogs from artists including Future, Enrique Iglesias and Blake Shelton, and in 2024 launched a frontline label and publisher called SLANG. ... In 2025, Influence acquired the catalog of DJ Khaled and launched two joint ventures with the artist. ... Anthem Entertainment is a Canada-based music rights company that holds recorded masters and publishing royalties from artists including Rush and Timbaland. ... The company was previously known as ole Media Management before rebranding as Anthem Entertainment. ... In 2024, Anthem sold its production music division to licensing company Slipstream, in a deal covering roughly 650,000 tracks.Music Business Worldwide"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Two Charter Next Generation Leaders Named 2026 Women Breaking the Mold Honorees,"www.prnewswire.com (Charter Next Generation, Inc.)",2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/two-charter-next-generation-leaders-named-2026-women-breaking-the-mold-honorees-302836655.html,"CHICAGO, July 28, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Charter Next Generation (CNG), a North American leader in specialty films and material science solutions, today announced that Beth Miller, Operations Manager, and Jamie Justice, Corporate Training Manager, have been named to Plastics News' 2026 class of Women Breaking the Mold. The annual program celebrates women across the industry whose leadership, innovation, and mentorship are helping shape the future of manufacturing. ... The recognition continues a growing legacy of CNG leaders being recognized through the Women Breaking the Mold program. Following three CNG honorees in 2025, this year's recognition further reflects CNG's commitment to empowering every employee-owner to lead, contribute ideas, and help share in the company's success. The announcement also comes during a milestone year for CNG's employee-owner culture as the company also earned Great Place To Work® Certification™ in 2026. ... Charter Next Generation (CNG) is a recognized leader in sustainable material science solutions in North America, delivering high-performance specialty films and advanced materials for flexible packaging and other critical applications across the food, consumer goods, industrial, and healthcare markets. With 18 facilities across the U.S. and more than 2,600 employee-owners, we bring together manufacturing excellence and innovation to help address global challenges—from reducing waste and preserving food to advancing equity and promoting climate resilience. As a company with broad-based employee ownership and a proud partner of Ownership Works™, we're committed to creating long-term, sustainable value through shared success. Visit cnginc.com, follow us on LinkedIn, or contact [email protected]. ... ### Charter Next Generation Appoints Mark Howell as Executive Vice President of Sales to Accelerate Commercial Strategy and Growth ... Charter Next Generation (CNG), a leading material science company specializing in specialty films and sustainable solutions, today announced the... ... ### Charter Next Generation Joins the US Flexible Film Initiative to Accelerate Scalable Recycling Solutions ... Charter Next Generation (CNG), a leading provider of sustainable material science solutions, announced today it has joined the US Flexible Film..."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Champion Breweries' revenue more than doubles after Bullet acquisition - Businessday NG,businessday.ng (Chinwe Michael),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://businessday.ng/companies/article/champion-breweries-revenue-more-than-doubles-after-bullet-acquisition/,"Champion Breweries' revenue more than doubles after Bullet acquisition - Businessday NG ... # Champion Breweries’ revenue more than doubles after Bullet acquisition ... Champion Breweries Plc has delivered the strongest financial performance in its 52-year history, with first-half revenue more than doubling after the brewer’s acquisition of the Bullet energy drink and ready-to-drink (RTD) alcoholic beverage portfolio transformed it from a regional Nigerian brewer into a pan-African beverage company with euro-denominated earnings. ... The Uyo-based brewer reported group revenue of N35.73 billion for the six months ended June 30, 2026, representing a 124.2 percent increase from N15.93 billion recorded in the corresponding period of 2025. Profit after tax rose by 15.6 percent to N2.65 billion from N2.29 billion a year earlier, according to the company’s unaudited half-year financial statements. ... The results are the first to fully reflect Champion Breweries’ consolidation of EnjoyBev B.V., the Netherlands-based holding company for the Bullet beverage portfolio, following the completion of its acquisition on February 26, 2026. ... The transaction marks one of the most ambitious overseas acquisitions undertaken by a Nigerian consumer goods company in recent years, giving Champion control of a portfolio distributed across 14 African markets while introducing hard-currency earnings into a business previously dependent almost entirely on the Nigerian market. ... Total assets expanded by 58.6 percent to N130.57 billion from N82.34 billion at the end of December 2025, while shareholders’ equity surged by an extraordinary 428 percent to ₦69.08 billion from N13.08 billion. ... The brewer successfully raised approximately N60 billion through a N15.9 billion rights issue and a N42 billion public offer, allowing it to finance the acquisition while simultaneously strengthening its balance sheet. ... As a result, total liabilities declined to N61.49 billion from N69.26 billion despite the sharp increase in assets, underscoring the company’s decision to pursue expansion without materially increasing financial leverage. ... The capital raising exercise also resolved a long-standing regulatory issue. ... Champion’s free float increased to 25.72 percent, valued at about N39.9 billion, from 16.96 percent previously, enabling the company to regain compliance with the Nigerian Exchange’s minimum listing requirements after previously being flagged for falling below the required threshold. ... Beyond the acquisition-driven jump in revenue, the brewer’s underlying operating performance also strengthened considerably. ... Gross profit increased by 59.3 percent to N13.14 billion, while operating profit rose by 59.9 percent to N6.17 billion. ... Net cash generated from operating activities climbed 286.7 percent to N8.45 billion compared with N2.19 billion recorded during the same period last year, indicating that earnings growth translated into stronger cash flows rather than remaining purely accounting gains. ... Quarterly performance showed an even faster pace of growth. Second-quarter revenue rose 186.8 percent year-on-year to N21.37 billion, while quarterly profit after tax increased 35.4 percent to N1.76 billion, reflecting almost three full months of contribution from the newly acquired Bullet business. ... most strategically significant development ... change in Champion’s earnings profile ... With EnjoyBev generating revenue from European production and pan-African distribution, Champion now derives part of its income in euros, reducing its exposure to the naira depreciation that has significantly eroded earnings across much of Nigeria’s consumer goods sector over the past three years. ... The benefits were already visible in the half-year accounts. The group recorded a N1.38 billion foreign currency translation gain within other comprehensive income alongside a N182 million net foreign exchange gain under finance income, highlighting how foreign currency exposure has become an earnings advantage rather than a liability. ... The acquisition structure also allows Champion to retain strategic control while preserving operational continuity. ... Champion owns 80 percent of EnjoyBev B.V., while Belgian company Vinar N.V., the long-standing manufacturing partner behind the Bullet brand, retains the remaining 20 percent stake. ... The group recognised N3.49 billion in goodwill arising from the acquisition and disclosed that no impairment indicators had been identified as of June 30. ... Finance costs rose sharply to N3.90 billion from N403.7 million in the corresponding period of last year, reflecting interest expenses associated with acquisition financing. ... Consequently, the standalone parent company reported an after-tax loss of N943.5 million compared with a N2.29 billion profit in the first half of 2025. ... Basic earnings per share declined to 16 kobo from 26 kobo after the company’s outstanding shares increased by 26.5 percent following the rights issue and public offer, diluting per-share earnings even as total profit increased. ... Management indicated that the second half of the year is expected to reflect the acquisition’s earnings potential more fully, as it will include six months of complete operational contribution from EnjoyBev. ... The brewer’s strategy also reflects a broader shift among Nigerian consumer goods manufacturers seeking geographic diversification and foreign currency earnings to reduce dependence on domestic demand, where consumers continue to struggle with elevated inflation, declining purchasing power, rising electricity tariffs, and higher logistics costs following the removal of petrol subsidies. ... By acquiring an established international beverage portfolio instead of relying solely on organic expansion, Champion has positioned itself among a small group of Nigerian listed consumer companies generating meaningful offshore revenue. ... Champion Breweries closed at N13.70 per share on June 30, 2026, giving the company a market capitalisation of approximately N155.1 billion based on its enlarged share capital of 11.32 billion shares. ... The stock has traded as high as N21.49 during the past 52 weeks, reflecting investor optimism surrounding the Bullet acquisition. ... EnjoyCorp Limited, which acquired a controlling interest in Champion Breweries in 2024, remains the company’s largest shareholder with a 64.08 percent stake, while Akwa Ibom Investment Corporation holds 10.15 percent"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,CHA Biotech Wins AX One-Stop Voucher to Automate Regulatory Documentation - Seoul Economic Daily,en.sedaily.com (Tae-heui Han),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/07/27/cha-biotech-wins-ax-one-stop-voucher-to-automate-regulatory,"CHA Biotech Wins AX One-Stop Voucher to Automate Regulatory Documentation - Seoul Economic Daily ... CHA Biotech has been selected for the ""AX (AI Transformation) One-Stop Voucher"" support program organized by the Ministry of Science and ICT (MSIT). The company plans to use the government funding to build a system that automates the drafting and verification of regulatory documents for cell therapies. ... CHA Biotech announced on the 27th that it will build ""AI-based application software (AI-SaaS)"" to accelerate the commercialization of cell therapies using generative artificial intelligence (AI) through the AX One-Stop Voucher support program. The AX One-Stop Voucher is a program that provides integrated support in the form of vouchers for AI solutions, cloud computing, and data utilization, based on the planning of demand companies, to promote the AI transformation of domestic firms. A total of 2.6 billion won in government funding will be invested in this project. ... CHA Biotech plans to pursue the project by forming a consortium with Naver Cloud, Persona AI, and MedAI Plus. The consortium plans to reduce delays in document and data processing across the entire cycle from cell therapy research and development to production. Naver Cloud will provide high-performance cloud infrastructure, Persona AI will handle AI solution development and SaaS platform construction, and MedAI Plus will be responsible for data structuring and quality verification. ... Based on this, CHA Biotech intends to automate the drafting and review procedures for regulatory documents related to chemistry, manufacturing, and controls (CMC). The company plans to improve work efficiency by consolidating documents scattered across multiple storage locations and reducing document work that has relied on manpower. Specifically, it aims to ▲improve the efficiency of document search, drafting, and review tasks ▲enhance the quality of regulatory response ▲secure global-level competitiveness in bio-regulatory response and ▲shorten the timeline for new drug development and licensing. ... ""We plan to structure scattered document data and build an automation system that spans from generating drafts of regulatory response documents to verification,"" said Yoon Seok-hwan, executive director of CHA Biotech's AI team. ""We will demonstrate AI transformation in the field of cell therapy CMC regulatory documents, which require a high level of precision, and create a best practice that accelerates the spread of AX."""
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com,2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/master-chains-n-jewels-files-ipo-papers-with-sebi-eyes-rs-400-cr-via-fresh-issue/articleshow/132657726.cms,"Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue - The Economic Times ... Business News› Markets› IPOs/FPOs›Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue ... # Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue ... Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue ... By PTILast Updated: Jul 2 ... , 2026, 0 ... :12:0 ... Master Chains N Jewels Ltd has filed preliminary papers for an initial public offering. The proposed IPO includes a fresh issue of equity shares worth Rs 400 crore. It also features an Offer for Sale of nearly 59.06 lakh equity shares. Proceeds will fund working capital needs and general corporate purposes. The company designs, manufactures, and distributes a wide range of gold jewellery. ... Organised gold jewellery manufacturer and wholesale distributor Master Chains N Jewels Ltd has filed preliminary papers with capital markets regulator Sebi to raise funds through an initial public offering (IPO).The proposed IPO comprises a fresh issue of equity shares worth up to Rs 400 crore and an Offer for Sale (OFS) of up to 59.06 lakh equity shares by promoter Taruna Madan Kothari, according to the draft red herring prospectus (DRHP) filed on Saturday. ... The proceeds from the fresh issue will be utilised towards funding the company's working capital requirements and for general corporate purposes.Master Chains N Jewels is engaged in the designing, manufacturing, job-work services and sale of a wide range of gold jewellery, including lightweight jewellery. ... It caters to customers across India through its wholesale distribution network and manufacturing capabilities. ... As of June 30, 2026, the company had a design database of around 80,666 jewellery designs. ... It operates two manufacturing units at Kala Chowki in Mumbai with an aggregate area of about 6,870 square feet and an installed manufacturing capacity of nearly 4,972.90 kilograms per annum as of March 2026. Systematix Corporate Services is the sole book-running lead manager to the issue, while Bigshare Services is the registrar to the offer."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue, ETRetail",retail.economictimes.indiatimes.com (www.ETRetail.com),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://retail.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/apparel-fashion/jewellery/master-chains-n-jewels-files-ipo-papers-with-sebi-eyes-rs-400-cr-via-fresh-issue/132656414,"Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue, ETRetail ... # Master Chains N Jewels files IPO papers with Sebi; eyes Rs 400 cr via fresh issue ... Master Chains N Jewels Ltd has filed preliminary papers for an initial public offering. The proposed IPO includes a fresh issue of equity shares and an offer for sale. Proceeds from the fresh issue will fund working capital and general corporate needs. The company designs, manufactures, and distributes a wide range of gold jewellery across India. Master Chains N Jewels operates two manufacturing units in Mumbai with significant annual capacity. ... Indian Gas Exchange Ltd (IGX), an associate company of Indian Energy Exchange Ltd (IEX), filed for an initial public offering (IPO).Organised gold jewellery manufacturer and wholesale distributor Master Chains N Jewels Ltd has filed preliminary papers with capital markets regulator Sebi to raise funds through an initial public offering (IPO).The proposed IPO comprises a fresh issue of equity shares worth up to Rs 400 crore and an Offer for Sale (OFS) of up to 59.06 lakh equity shares by promoter Taruna Madan Kothari, according to the draft red herring prospectus (DRHP) filed on Saturday.The proceeds from the fresh issue will be utilised towards funding the company's working capital requirements and for general corporate purposes. ... Master Chains N Jewels is engaged in the designing, manufacturing, job-work services and sale of a wide range of gold jewellery, including lightweight jewellery.It caters to customers across India through its wholesale distribution network and manufacturing capabilities.As of June 30, 2026, the company had a design database of around 80,666 jewellery designs.It operates two manufacturing units at Kala Chowki in Mumbai with an aggregate area of about 6,870 square feet and an installed manufacturing capacity of nearly 4,972.90 kilograms per annum as of March 2026.Systematix Corporate Services is the sole book-running lead manager to the issue, while Bigshare Services is the registrar to the offer."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Huaqin's growing stake in Nexchip shows ODMs reaching upstream into chipmaking,apps.digitimes.com (Jingyue Hsiao),2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://apps.digitimes.com/news/a20260723VL206/nexchip-huaqin-design-capacity.html,"Huaqin's growing stake in Nexchip shows ODMs reaching upstream into chipmaking ... # Huaqin's growing stake in Nexchip shows ODMs reaching upstream into chipmaking ... Jingyue Hsiao , DIGITIMES, Taipei Jul 25, 2026, 10:49 0 Credit: AFP Huaqin Technology, the world's largest consumer-electronics original design manufacturer, has again increased its stake in Chinese foundry Nexchip Semiconductor, underscoring how contract manufacturers increasingly view direct ownership of chip capacity as..."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Primis AI Becomes ChipNexus and Launches NEX for Agentic Chip-Design Automation - Semiconductor Digest,www.semiconductor-digest.com (Shannon Davis),2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.semiconductor-digest.com/primis-ai-becomes-chipnexus-and-launches-nex-for-agentic-chip-design-automation-2/,"Primis AI Becomes ChipNexus and Launches NEX for Agentic Chip-Design Automation - Semiconductor Digest ... Primis AI Becomes ChipNexus and Launches NEX for Agentic Chip-Design Automation ... Primis AI today announced that it has become ChipNexus and launched NEX, an agentic AI platform for semiconductor and hardware design. The new identity reflects the company’s evolution in response to a changing market: hardware teams increasingly need AI systems that can work across complex engineering workflows, not simply generate code or answer questions. ChipNexus developed NEX to address that shift. ... NEX helps hardware teams plan and execute multi-step engineering workflows across digital, analog, and physical design. It can generate and refactor RTL, analyze schematics, configure and run digital and analog simulations, investigate verification failures, and orchestrate synthesis and physical-design tools. NEX interprets outputs ranging from logs and waveforms to timing, power, and layout reports, using the results to guide subsequent actions toward defined engineering objectives. NEX connects with existing EDA environments, source code repositories, automation scripts, and CI/CD infrastructure, allowing teams to apply AI across their current toolchain rather than replace it. Engineers ... interactively through a lightweight command-line interface, ... bounded multi-step workflows, or ... projects, culminating in ... the most demanding project ... Alongside the rebrand and product launch, ChipNexus closed a seed funding round led by Cambium Capital. The company plans to use the funding to accelerate NEX’s agent capabilities and grow enterprise adoption. ... NEX is available now and includes out-of-the-box access to supported Google Gemini models. Enterprise customers can instead connect NEX to supported AI models using their own provider credentials. Private-cloud and on-premises deployment options are also available for organizations with additional security, privacy, or data-residency requirements."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"SRF Q1 Results: Profit jumps 76%, board approves ₹250 crore capex; shares fall 3% - CNBC TV18",www.cnbctv18.com,2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/srf-q1-results-profit-jumps-76-pc-board-approves-rs-250-crore-capex-shares-fall-dividend-19951461.htm,"SRF Q1 Results: Profit jumps 76%, board approves ₹250 crore capex; shares fall 3% - CNBC TV18 ... # SRF Q1 Results: Profit jumps 76%, board approves ₹250 crore capex; shares fall 3% ... ## The Performance Films & Foil business continued to be the standout performer, with segment revenue rising to ₹2,016.7 crore from ₹1,418.2 crore a year ago. Segment profit more than doubled to ₹349.7 crore from ₹140.2 crore. ... The board also approved a ₹250 crore capital expenditure to set up a 25,000 MTPA BOPET Thick Film Line, which is expected to be commissioned within 24 months. The company said the specialised BOPET thick film caters to industrial and electronics applications and should help reduce earnings cyclicality due to limited domestic capacity and differentiated demand. The project will be funded through a mix of debt and internal accruals. SRF stock movement Despite the earnings beat across key metrics, investors remained cautious. Following the results announcement, shares of the company were trading at the day's lows at ₹2,846.90, down 3.3%. The stock has fallen more than 9% over the last 12 months."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"Film Finances, Media Guarantors To Merge Creating Completion Bond Giant",deadline.com (Jill Goldsmith),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://deadline.com/2026/07/film-finances-media-guarantors-merger-completion-bonds-1236998898/,"Film Finances, Media Guarantors To Merge Creating Completion Bond Giant ... EXCLUSIVE: Film Finances, part of the STX Entertainment family, and Media Guarantors are merging, creating a leading global completion bond firm for independent film, a unique space with only a few key players. ... Specifically, STX Entertainment sister company Film Services International, the parent of Film Finances, is acquiring Media Guarantors from insurance brokerage CAC Group for an undisclosed price. ... Media Guarantors founder and chief executive Fred Milstein will be CEO of the combined bond company. Film Finances EVP Steve Berman will become president. ... Film Finances President Greg Trattner will assume the role of Executive Chairman, expanding his responsibilities across the broader family of companies held by Film Services International, under group CEO Peter Coleman. ... CAC acquired Media Guarantors in 2024, its first acquisition in the entertainment space. The sale follows CAC’s own merger earlier this year to rival insurance broker Baldwin Group. ... Completion bonds are contracts where the bond firm guarantees that a film will be completed on time and on budget, protecting investors, banks, sales agents and distributors. If there are problems, the firm is on the hook for overages or other costs. Bonds mitigate risk so it can be harder to get financing without one. Many indie productions use them. ... “The expanded platform strengthens the completion bond market that independent finance relies on, while accelerating investment in data-driven risk assessment that shortens the path from green light to bond and gives financiers earlier certainty,” Coleman said. Combined with the group’s other assets, he added, it creates a “preeminent partner for independent producers, financiers, and distributors, and marks the latest step in building a true one-stop shop for production, spanning financing, physical production, and post-production.” ... Film Services International, now wholly owned by large financial and insurance platform A-CAP, acquired Film Finances and its related companies— including Pivotal Post, EPS-Cineworks Digital Studios, Buff Dubbs + DAMsmart, Silver Trak Digital and LiquidLight — in the fall of 2024. The sale was part of a prepackaged bankruptcy enabling Film Finances to detach from its legally and financially challenged private equity owner at the time, 777 Partners. ... FFI joined STX in January when the production company relaunched— also under deep pocketed A-CAP — after years of false starts with a string of owners. That deal saw STX founder and chairman Robert Simonds and chief executive Noah Fogelson exit. ... “STX has been quiet for a few years. But it still has a brand and it still has IP that is valuable,” Coleman had noted back when A-CAP came in with plans to recapitalize the company. ... Romcom Happy Hours by and starring Katie Holmes with Joshua Jackson premiered at the 2026 Tribeca Festival. Coleman said the company is in development on a handful of projects with announcements coming over the next couple of months."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,What Merging Two Completion Bond Guarantors Means for Indie Films,www.indiewire.com (Brian Welk),2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.indiewire.com/news/business/what-merging-completion-bond-guarandots-means-indie-films-1235206476/,"Leading completion bond guarantors Film Finances and Media Guarantors are combining under the STX Entertainment family of companies. By Brian Welk ... Completion bonds are a little-discussed but essential part of the independent film financing process, the insurance by which indie films ensure that a film will be completed on time and on budget. You don’t really hear about them unless you need it. Today, though, two of the largest guarantors of such completion bonds are merging in a move that could have a big impact on the indie film space. ... Film Finances International (FFI), the parent company of completion bond provider Film Finances, is acquiring Media Guarantors Insurance Solutions (MGIS) to create a completion guarantor giant. The combined company is part of STX Entertainment and the Film Services International family of companies, and the merger helps Film Services become not just a studio but also a service provider. It can add an insurance component to complement its indie flywheel — which already includes financing, physical production, and post-production. The combination is being presented as a one-stop shop for the indie film market, something that can give studio-quality support and risk assurance across multiple territories, including the U.S., UK, Australia, Canada, and Europe, while also speeding up the investment in data-driven risk assessment tools, which can make it quicker for indie producers to obtain a bond and give financiers more certainty earlier. ... Fred Milstein, president and CEO of Media Guarantors, will now serve as CEO of the combined bond company. Steve Berman will become president, and Greg Trattner will assume the role of executive chairman, all under group CEO Coleman. Film Finances has been around for decades and has a large history of experience and knowledge, while Media Guarantors has become very hands-on with filmmakers and entrepreneurial, and the idea is that those two strengths will complement each other moving forward. ... The concern is what taking a guarantor out of the space means for indies who might now have to work with just a single company to get their film bonded. We know how consolidation has impacted and threatens to impact the rest of the industry. But in this case, the bond market is still a very niche space. A majority of films don’t bond if they can avoid it. And the broader challenges facing the indie film market mean that some smaller mom-and-pop vendors are struggling, and there isn’t necessarily a single entity with the breadth of knowledge to help indie producers across the board. ... A merger like this creates a healthier vendor that can be a full-service company. Film Services sees this as an opportunity to attract indie projects even if they don’t need a bond, namely because guarantors have the skills necessary to look at scripts and schedules and help identify anything that can go wrong. Through its post-production arms, Pivotal Post and SilverTrak, Film Services can also help at the finishing stage. It’s one of the leading renters of Avid tools, and STX is the studio-facing side of the operation, now building out a new slate from the old STX library. Case in point: the Katie Holmes-directed “Happy Hours,” which premiered at this year’s Tribeca Film Festival, was one film for which Film Services used all its resources to finance, bond, produce, and support post-production. The film is now working through distribution. Film Services believes that would not have been possible without the combined resources of the entire set of brands and services, and other indies will now have an avenue to do the same. ... Deadline first reported the news of the merger."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Global SIs drive NexFlex bidding as AI boom lifts FCCL demand in Korea - CHOSUNBIZ,biz.chosun.com,2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://biz.chosun.com/en/en-finance/2026/07/15/RBVXRBQYIZEA3IRLF4VAXDYXKE/,"Global SIs drive NexFlex bidding as AI boom lifts FCCL demand in Korea - CHOSUNBIZ ... # Global SIs drive NexFlex bidding as AI boom lifts FCCL demand in Korea ... With MBK Partners pushing to sell NexFlex, a maker of flexible copper-clad laminate (FCCL), two global materials corporations have recently jumped into the competition and begun due diligence, according to assessments. Following Taekwang Industrial, two more overseas corporations have joined the race, reshaping the deal into a contest among strategic investors (SI). ... According to the investment banking (IB) industry on the 15th, multiple SIs and financial investors (FIs) are proceeding with steps such as submitting letters of commitment (LOC) and conducting due diligence to acquire control of NexFlex. Some potential buyers are also moving to form alliances with one another. The sell-side advisor is Deutsche Bank. ... Industry sources said the hoped-for sale price for NexFlex is reported to be more than 900 billion won. The company's EBITDA last year was 85.1 billion won, and this year it is widely expected to exceed 100 billion won. ... There are believed to be at least three SIs currently interested in and pursuing an acquisition of NexFlex. In Korea, Taekwang Industrial is pushing to team up with an FI to join the bidding, and two global materials corporations have also joined and are conducting due diligence. In addition, a Chinese corporation is said to have pursued an acquisition until recently. ... Among FIs, Busan Equity Partners (EP) and the growth institutional sector of STIC Investments have joined the fray. In the case of STIC Investments, it is looking for another FI or SI to team up with for a joint acquisition. Separately, Affirma Capital is known to have recently completed even on-site due diligence. ... FCCL is a key material for flexible printed circuit boards (FPCB). Demand used to center on the smartphone market, but as applications expand to artificial intelligence (AI) smartphones, AI data centers, and Extended Reality (XR) devices, assessments say FCCL's strategic value is also rising. ... The market expects NexFlex to also benefit from these industry shifts. As high-performance graphics processing units (GPUs), AI servers, and high-density packaging technologies spread, demand will inevitably grow for high-spec FCCL suited for high-speed signal transmission and miniaturization. ... There are also increasing new demand sources. NexFlex is said to have recently begun supplying FCCL samples for Tesla's Humanoid Robot project. Although it is still in the early stage, if it leads to mass production, observers say it could become a new growth driver. ... An IB industry official said, ""While FIs often value corporations based on current performance, SIs frequently price in mid- to long-term market dominance and business synergies as well,"" adding, ""As SIs have successively jumped into the NexFlex bidding, the key question is how their participation will affect the company's valuation."""
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"Latecomers Join Nexplex Acquisition Race, Reshaping SI-FI Consortiums - Seoul Economic Daily",en.sedaily.com (Lee Deok-Yeon),2026-07-15T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-15 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/news/2026/07/15/latecomers-join-nexplex-acquisition-race-reshaping-si-fi,"Latecomers Join Nexplex Acquisition Race, Reshaping SI-FI Consortiums - Seoul Economic Daily ... The acquisition race for Nexplex, Korea's top maker of flexible copper clad laminate (FCCL), has entered a reshaping phase with the entry of a new group of bidders. The seller had originally selected around three financial investors (FIs) as preferred bidders on the shortlist, but as some dropped out and new strategic investors (SIs) emerged, consortiums are being newly formed. The FCCL produced by Nexplex is ultimately supplied to Samsung Electronics and Apple. ... According to the investment banking (IB) industry on the 15th, the group of Nexplex bidders, which originally consisted of STIC Investments-Armstrong Capital (Apalma Capital), Bain Capital, and Busan Equity Partners (Busan EP), is diversifying with the entry of multiple strategic investors. Taekwang Industrial is reviewing the acquisition of Nexplex and is in discussions with STIC Investments and others to form a consortium, while another strategic investor has emerged and is conducting due diligence. Global PEF manager Bain Capital has withdrawn from the race, and Armstrong Capital is weighing whether to continue with the deal. ... ""Originally, the STIC Investments-Armstrong consortium, Bain Capital, and Busan EP made the shortlist, but with Taekwang Industrial and another strategic investor emerging, there has been a change in the group of bidders,"" an IB industry official said. ""With Bain Capital out, the strategic investors are taking the lead and looking for partners to form consortiums together."" ... Nexplex traces its origins to SK Innovation's FCCL business division, and after passing through Korea's large PEF manager Skylake Equity Partners, MBK became its largest shareholder. It produces FCCL, a key material for flexible printed circuit boards (FPCB), a major component of information technology (IT) devices such as smartphones, and has long maintained the top market share. The FCCL produced by Nexplex is ultimately supplied to Samsung Electronics and Apple. Its performance is soaring, posting operating profit of 75 billion won last year, an 82.8% surge from 2024. ... With the entry of new strategic investors, the corporate valuation is rising. The IB industry had originally estimated the deal size at around 800 billion won based on a 100% stake acquisition, but some bidders are considering a higher price. MBK and sale manager Deutsche Bank are receiving binding offers from each bidder after due diligence is completed. ... MBK acquired a 100% stake in Nexplex from Skylake for about 530 billion won in 2023. Should the acquisition competition continue under the current structure, projections suggest that the exit performance for the fifth fund used in the Nexplex acquisition will become visible. MBK's fifth fund's main portfolio includes Nexplex as well as Osstem Implant, Medit, and Geoyoung."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Nexchip raises $880m on HKSE | Electronics Weekly,www.electronicsweekly.com (David Manners),2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.electronicsweekly.com/news/business/nexchip-raises-880m-on-hkse-2026-07/,"Nexchip raises $880m on HKSE ⋆ Electronics Weekly ... # Nexchip raises $880m on HKSE by David Manners 14th July 2026 11 year-old Nexchip, the world’s No.8 foundry, has raised $880 million on the Hong Kong stock exchange. ... Powerchip of Taiwan invested in Nexchip’s founding in 2015 and former Powerchip CEO Tsai Kuo-chih is Nexchip’s chairman. ... Tsai said the company would increase R&D and production capacity, while speeding up its global expansion. The company is currently developing a 22nm process and building a $5.1 billion fab in Hefei to expand its 40nm and 28nm production capacity to 55k wpm by 2028. ... nm, 110nm and 150 ... processes for DDICs, PMICs, and CIS ... Nexchip listed on the Shanghai STAR market in 2023. The Hong Kong listing was aimed at international investors and enables the company to raise Hong Kong dollars. ... Nexchip’s annual capacity is currently 1.67 million 300mm wafer equivalents in 2025, up 74% from 2023."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,"MBK Partners delays NexFlex sale bid deadline, denies link to Homeplus troubles - KED Global",www.kedglobal.com (KED Global),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.kedglobal.com/mergers-acquisitions/newsView/ked202607130007,"MBK Partners delays NexFlex sale bid deadline, denies link to Homeplus troubles - KED Global # MBK Partners delays NexFlex sale bid deadline, denies link to Homeplus troubles ... ## The private equity firm is seeking to exit the FCCL maker at an enterprise value of more than $544 million, about 9 to 10 times EBITDA ... Private equity firm (PEF) MBK Partners Inc. has postponed the main bid deadline for the sale of NexFlex Co., a South Korean maker of flexible copper-clad laminate (FCCL) used in smartphones, prompting market speculation that the delay is tied to turmoil at portfolio company Homeplus Co. ... ## MBK’s investment in Homeplus shaping up as one of the most costly deals in its history ... MBK Partners' office in Seoul MBK Partners Inc.'s investment in Homeplus Co., once envisioned as a landmark buyout that would cement the firm's status as Northeast Asia's largest private equity manager, is increasingly shaping up to be one of the most costly deals in its history.While the firm ... ## MBK’s buyout stint in Korea falters as $5.7 bn Homeplus revamp teeters on brink of collapse ... Image by In-Soo Nam &middot; Gemini (Nano Banana) More than a decade after paying an enterprise value of about 7.8 trillion won ($5.7 billion) for South Korea's No. 2 hypermarket chain, private equity firm (PEF) MBK Partners Inc. is poised to see one of Asia's most celebrated leveraged buyouts ... ## Affirma Capital joins race for MBK-owned FCCL maker NexFlex ... A roll of flexible copper-clad laminate Affirma Capital, a Singapore-based private equity firm, has entered the bidding for NexFlex Co., South Korea’s largest producer of flexible copper‑clad laminate (FCCL) and wholly owned by MBK Partners, according to people familiar with the process o ... ## MBK to acquire Korea’s top FCCL maker NexFlex for $407 mn ... FCCL manufacturing process (Courtesy of NexFlex) MBK Partners agreed to buy NexFlex Co., South Korea’s top flexible copper-clad laminates (FCCL) producer, as the leading Northeast Asian private equity firm saw high growth potential in the industry, given the strong consumption of smartpho"
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Innox Advanced Materials Advances Domestic Build-up Film Development < Supply Chain < 기사본문 - The Elec Inc.,www.thelec.net (Selye Moon),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thelec.net/news/articleView.html?idxno=12036,"nox Advanced Materials Advances ... Innox Advanced Materials is conducting sample evaluations of build-up film (BF) for semiconductor package substrates with multiple domestic and overseas customers, expanding its materials business from smartphone rigid-flex printed circuit boards (R-FPCBs) into semiconductor packaging. The company is the second South Korean supplier, after Hanwha e-ssential, to reach the build-up film sample stage. ... According to industry sources on July 7, Innox Advanced Materials has supplied build-up film samples to package substrate manufacturers and outsourced semiconductor assembly and test (OSAT) companies in South Korea and overseas. The identities of the customers and shipment volumes were not disclosed. The company expects the new business to generate synergies with its existing printed circuit board (PCB) materials operations. ... The company is currently tailoring material properties to individual customer requirements while conducting qualification testing. It is also discussing commercial production with some customers before the end of this year. Once substrate manufacturers complete qualification, surface mount technology (SMT) providers, electronics manufacturing services (EMS) companies and end customers must also approve the material before mass production begins. Full-scale commercialization is expected to start next year. ... Innox Advanced Materials plans to enter the semiconductor market through its circuit board materials business, branded SMARTFLEX, by commercializing build-up film. The move will expand its customer base beyond smartphone materials into semiconductor substrate manufacturers. The company aims to increase revenue from its circuit board business by more than 50% within the next five years, generating more than 50 billion won in additional annual sales. The business is also expected to account for a gradually larger share of total revenue, up from roughly 25% currently. ... The company's existing circuit board materials business has been heavily influenced by smartphone demand. Revenue from the segment fell to 25.1 billion won in the first quarter, down more than 20% from 31.8 billion won a year earlier and 32.4 billion won in the previous quarter. The decline reflected reduced adoption of digitizers for S Pens by a domestic customer and lower tablet and notebook shipments as rising memory prices weighed on demand. ... Innox Advanced Materials is initially targeting the mainstream flip chip-ball grid array (FC-BGA) market to accelerate commercialization of its build-up film. FC-BGA substrates for AI servers, which incorporate graphics processing units (GPUs) and application-specific integrated circuits (ASICs), require industry-leading material properties, including ultra-low dielectric constants, low coefficients of thermal expansion (CTE) and high heat resistance. By comparison, FC-BGA products used in automotive, PC and telecommunications applications have less demanding specifications. The company's strategy is to secure customer qualifications in mainstream applications before expanding into high-end AI server products. ... The build-up film has been under development for several years based on the company's existing bonding sheet technology for R-FPCBs. Bonding sheets serve as adhesive and interlayer insulating materials when laminating flexible copper clad laminates (FCCLs), giving them functions similar to build-up film. Semiconductor package substrates, however, require significantly higher levels of insulation and reliability than FPCBs. Innox Advanced Materials developed a resin for semiconductor package substrates by reformulating its existing materials to achieve low dielectric and high insulation characteristics. ... Build-up film is a key insulating material placed between circuit layers in semiconductor package substrates and is essential for fabricating the fine circuitry required in FC-BGA packages designed for high-speed data processing. Ajinomoto's ABF (Ajinomoto Build-up Film) remains the de facto industry standard, accounting for roughly 98% of the global market. Ajinomoto's electronic materials business generated approximately 1 trillion won in revenue last year. ... Other South Korean companies pursuing domestically developed build-up film include Hanwha e-ssential, HNS Hi-Tech, Dongjin Semichem and LG Chem. Hanwha e-ssential produced pilot samples in 2023 and has been conducting reliability testing with domestic and overseas customers. HNS Hi-Tech plans to begin supplying customer samples in the second half of this year and aims to start mass production in 2028. Dongjin Semichem and LG Chem have not disclosed detailed development schedules."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Nazdar acquires screen & flexographic analog ink business from FUJIFILM,graphics-pro.com,2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://graphics-pro.com/news/nazdar-screen-flexographic-fujifilm/,"Nazdar acquires screen & flexographic analog ink business from FUJIFILM ... Nazdar, a manufacturer and distributor of screen printing, wide format digital & flexographic inks, announced that the company has acquired FUJIFILM’s U.S., Canada, and Latin America screen and flexographic ink business — through a sale and licensing arrangement. Transition activities began on June 24, with transition targeted for completion by July 13. ... “Nazdar has been a valued, longtime partner of the Business Innovation Division,” said Tommy Katagiri, division president, FUJIFILM North America Corporation, Business Innovation Division. “Its acquisition of this ink business is a natural next step for both organizations to meet our mutual business goals. It allows Nazdar to continue to advance its ink business and supports Fujifilm’s focus on other priorities under the business innovation/printing umbrella.” ... Nazdar confirms that all core product attributes will remain consistent following the acquisition. Product formulations, specifications, and manufacturing locations will not change, and current SDS/TDS documentation will continue to be fully supported. This ensures a seamless transition with no disruption to product performance, supply, or quality. ... “Bringing these FUJIFILM product lines into Nazdar represents a strategic investment in the markets and customers that matter most to our future,” said Richard Bowles, CEO at Nazdar. “We’re expanding our capabilities, deepening our expertise, and positioning ourselves to deliver industry‑leading solutions for many years to come.” ... According to Nazdar, screen and narrow web have been core parts of its business for decades. As the company continues to invest in its manufacturing capabilities, this acquisition is said to reflect a deliberate expansion and opportunity for long‑term growth. The company stated that this expertise will support FUJIFILM’s customers with high‑quality, future‑ready products. ... In addition, Nazdar stated that customers will gain the benefits of its expanded resources, including dedicated screen and narrow web technical support, focused R&D and regulatory expertise, and long‑term investment in innovation and market leadership."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,Yulchon Chemical's New Poseung Plant Begins Battery Pouch Film Production < Battery < 기사본문 - The Elec Inc.,www.thelec.net (EunGyu Kim),2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.thelec.net/news/articleView.html?idxno=11930,"Yulchon Chemical has begun mass production of battery pouch film at its new Poseung plant in Gyeonggi Province, about one year after the facility entered trial operation in April last year. ... According to industry sources on July 3, Yulchon Chemical received 4M approval from LG Energy Solution for the Poseung plant's pouch film production line in late April. A 4M approval is the customer's final qualification process conducted whenever there are changes to the four key elements of a production system: Man, Machine, Material, and Method. ... Over the past year, Yulchon Chemical adjusted the Poseung plant's production equipment to meet LG Energy Solution's quality standards. The company's pouch film serves as the outer packaging material that encloses the internal components of battery cells. ... Yulchon Chemical will exclusively supply 183-micrometer (μm) high-formability pouch film to LG Energy Solution. The film will be used in the battery maker's second-generation energy storage system (ESS) pouch cells, known as JF2. ... As LG Energy Solution expands production of ESS pouch batteries this year at its facilities in Holland, Michigan, Ultium Cells Tennessee, the Honda joint venture in Ohio, NextStar Energy in Canada, and Wrocław, Poland, demand for Yulchon Chemical's pouch film has also increased. ... To meet rising demand, Yulchon Chemical plans to double the annual production capacity of its Poseung plant from 40 million square meters to 80 million square meters. The company aims to begin mass production on the new production line next year. Combined with its Ansan plant, which has annual capacity of 30 million square meters, Yulchon Chemical's total pouch film production capacity will reach 110 million square meters. ... The existing Ansan plant has generated annual revenue of 70 billion won to 80 billion won, and the company expects sales to increase further as the Poseung plant ramps up production. Yulchon Chemical projects that revenue from its electronic materials business, centered on pouch film, will grow at a compound annual growth rate of 50% between 2025 and 2028. ... Following the second-generation JF2 platform, LG Energy Solution plans to introduce its third-generation JF3 pouch batteries in 2027 and fourth-generation JF4 products after 2029. LG Energy Solution was Yulchon Chemical's largest customer for electronic materials last year, accounting for 19.6% of total revenue. ... Revenue from Yulchon Chemical's electronic materials business increased from 91.2 billion won in 2023 to 131.1 billion won in 2024 and 165.8 billion won in 2025. The segment's share of total revenue also rose from 22% in 2023 to 34.2% last year. ... Yulchon Chemical has localized battery pouch film production in a market traditionally dominated by Japanese suppliers, expanding its business beyond food packaging materials into battery materials. In addition to LG Energy Solution, the company is conducting sample evaluations of its battery pouch film with multiple other customers."
CHARTER NEX FILMS,,,,Exa,NEXE Innovations Provides Update on Partner Transition to,www.globenewswire.com (NEXE Innovations),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/06/22/3315658/0/en/NEXE-Innovations-Provides-Update-on-Partner-Transition-to-BPI-Certified-Compostable-Pods.html,"# NEXE Innovations Provides Update on Partner Transition to BPI-Certified Compostable Pods ... ## New U.S. nationwide account and two additional brand transitions reflect continued adoption in NEXE's compostable platform ... WINDSOR, Ontario, June 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- NEXE Innovations Inc. (“NEXE”, ""our"" or the “Company"") (TSX.V: NEXE) (Frankfurt: NX5) (OTC: NEXNF), a compostable and innovative materials company, today provided an update on the progress of its partner's planned transition to NEXE’s BPI-certified compostable coffee pod platform, first announced on March 25, 2026. Since that announcement, the Company and its commercial partner have advanced the transition across multiple business lines, with approximately 300,000 pods delivered as of early May 2026, two additional brands giving initial purchase orders, and a growing pipeline of OCS, retail, and ecommerce opportunities which management believes supports the potential scalability and commercial adoption of the NEXE platform. ... The North American distributor reports that it has had a positive experience with NEXE’s BPI-certified compostable coffee pod, compostable technology platform, and operations. With 1.5M pods shipped to date, the partner’s confidence in NEXE’s ability to scale is reflected in current ordering activity: repeat order volumes are trending higher, brand transitions are accelerating, and end-market feedback is positive. The distributor has placed additional purchase orders with NEXE, which NEXE expects to deliver in the next couple months. The partner anticipates commencing larger volume transitions ahead of the fall and winter season. ... The partner has advised NEXE that it also recently secured a nationwide partnership with a nationally recognized U.S. veterans’ nonprofit, which it has reported will be transitioning to NEXE’s BPI-certified compostable pods across its offices and events. Management believes this partnership supports further validation of NEXE’s sustainability credentials and product performance. In management's experience, accounts of this profile require consistent product performance and certified environmental credentials, and their adoption of the compostable pod platform is expected to open the door to similar opportunities across other nonprofit, government, and corporate channels. ... In parallel, the partner tells NEXE that it is investing in ecommerce and marketing initiatives designed to increase consumer awareness of its brands and support the transition to BPI-certified compostable pods. As part of this effort, the partner has launched a targeted Amazon promotion, with a $5-off offer planned for Amazon Prime Day (June 23–26) seeking to encourage trial and increase consumer engagement improve product rankings, and capture peak consumer traffic. Participating products span the Hurricane Coffee & Tea and Yummy Coffee brand lines. ... Management is also in the process of transitioning two more brands – one from a Canadian based coffee brand and the second from a U.S. based coffee company and café. The expected volumes from these two brands are approximately 1.5M pods annually and are part of the previous guidance provided of 10 million to 15 million annual pod volume run-rate. ... About NEXE Innovations Inc.NEXE Innovations is focused on providing innovative compostable material solutions and packaging to the B2B segment to help businesses achieve their sustainability goals. NEXE Innovations has developed a proprietary and patented compostable material that can withstand heat, pressure, and water. Our flagship product, the NEXE Pod, a BPI-certified compostable coffee pod, showcases our material's durability and is an ideal substitute for plastic. The NEXE pod is compatible with major coffee brewing machines and is manufactured at NEXE's vertically integrated facility based in North America. Discover our innovative approach to sustainability at www.nexeinnovations.com and join our journey on social media@nexeinnovations. #compostablecoffeepods #sustainability #greentech ... Release SummaryNEXE (TSXV: NEXE) large scale partner transition on track, progress across multiple fronts reflect continued adoption of NEXE's BPI-certified coffee pod. ... April 29, 2026 19:32 ET | Source: NEXE Innovations ... NEXE Innovations Reports Q3 2026 Results and Business Update ... NEXE Q3 2026: Key partner validates platform; volumes scaling to 10–15M pods with improving margins"
