50 RT for standard applications and 600 to over 1,500 RT for data centers. It also supports a maximum leaving chilled water temperature of up to 35°C, enabling seamless integration with waterside economizer and free cooling systems. In mission-critical environments, fast recovery is essential. The HSWE can restart within 25 seconds after power restoration and achieve full load within two minutes, drastically reducing the risk of server overheating and business interruption. ... the HSWE is equipped with the advanced AdaptiView™ controller, which integrates multiple patented control logics including adaptive control, feedforward control, and variable primary flow compensation. It also marks the successful application of adaptive refrigerant flow control on a centrifugal platform. Together, these capabilities enable precise chilled-water temperature control and stable output under changing loads and variable-flow conditions, supporting the sophisticated energy-saving strategies used in today's high-performance buildings and data centers. ... About Trane TechnologiesTrane Technologies is a global climate innovator. Through our strategic brands Trane® and Thermo King®, and our portfolio of environmentally responsible products and services, we bring efficient and sustainable climate solutions to buildings, homes and transportation. For more on Trane Technologies, visit tranetechnologies.com. ... ### Trane Launches HSAG Air-Cooled Magnetic Bearing Chiller to Drive Asia Pacific Data Center Growth ... Trane® – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator, has announced the launch of the HSAG, a revolutionary air-cooled magnetic... ... ### Trane Launches Advanced CDU to Enhance Liquid Cooling Efficiency in Asia-Pacific Data Centers ... Trane®— by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator – has announced the launch of its new DCDA series, the first locally developed..."
TRANE,,,,Exa,Trane Introduces HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller for Data Center Cooling in Asia Pacific – DW24 News,dw24news.com,2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://dw24news.com/trane-hswe-magnetic-bearing-chiller-asia-pacific/,"Trane Introduces HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller for Data Center Cooling in Asia Pacific – DW24 News ... Trane has launched the HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller to enhance data center cooling across Asia Pacific. The innovative HVAC solution improves energy efficiency, reliability, and sustainability. ... Trane, a global leader in HVAC systems, has launched its latest innovation—the HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller—aimed at revolutionizing data center cooling across the Asia Pacific region. This new system promises enhanced energy efficiency and reliability, addressing the increasing demand for sustainable cooling solutions in one of the world’s fastest-growing markets. ... The HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller stands out for its cutting-edge magnetic bearing technology, which reduces friction and mechanical wear, resulting in lower maintenance costs and improved operational lifespan. Designed specifically to meet the rigorous needs of data centers, the chiller provides precise temperature control essential for optimal server performance and uptime. ... Asia Pacific’s data center market has witnessed exponential growth due to rapid digital transformation and the expansion of cloud services. This surge in demand has intensified the need for advanced cooling systems that can handle high heat loads while minimizing environmental impact. Trane’s new chiller addresses these challenges by utilizing eco-friendly refrigerants and adopting energy-saving features aligned with global sustainability goals. ... “Our commitment is to drive innovation that supports the evolving infrastructure needs of data centers,” said a Trane representative. “The HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller is engineered to deliver unmatched efficiency and reliability, ensuring that our clients in Asia Pacific can maintain their critical operations with confidence.” ... The introduction of this technology also aligns with regional regulations aimed at reducing carbon footprints and promoting green building standards. As data centers consume significant amounts of energy for cooling, adopting advanced chillers like the HSWE Magnetic Bearing model is a strategic move to reduce operational expenses and environmental impact simultaneously. ... Industry analysts predict that the adoption of magnetic bearing chillers will accelerate as data centers seek solutions that balance performance with sustainability. Trane’s leadership in this domain positions it as a key player supporting the region’s digital infrastructure growth. ... This product launch marks a significant milestone in Trane’s ongoing efforts to integrate innovation with environmental responsibility, providing data center operators across Asia Pacific with tools necessary for future-ready cooling solutions."
TRANE,,,,Exa,Trane Launches HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller to Advance Data Center Cooling Across Asia Pacific - Siam News Network,www.siamnewsnetwork.net,2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.siamnewsnetwork.net/pr-news/trane-launches-hswe-magnetic-bearing-chiller-to-advance-data-center-cooling-across-asia-pacific/,"Trane Launches HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller to Advance Data Center Cooling Across Asia Pacific - Siam News Network ... # Trane Launches HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller to Advance Data Center Cooling Across Asia Pacific ... SHANGHAI, July 2, 2026 /PRNewswire/ — Trane – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator, announced the launch of the HSWE magnetic bearing centrifugal chiller, developed specifically for the Asia Pacific market. Designed to tackle the most demanding cooling applications, especially data centers, the HSWE combines ultra-high efficiency, reliable performance and intelligent controls, further strengthening Trane’s premium chiller portfolio across the region. ... ""The launch of the HSWE marks an important milestone for Trane Technologies in Asia Pacific, highlighting our advanced, ground-up innovation in the region,"" said Bruce Zhongping Gu, Vice President, Engineering and Technology, Trane Technologies Asia Pacific. ""As a regionally developed water-cooled magnetic bearing technology platform, the HSWE was created specifically to address the evolving needs of customers in Asia Pacific, including the extreme performance demands of modern data centers."" ... Powered by advanced compressor technology and an innovative heat exchanger design, the HSWE achieves a full-load COP of up to 7.3 under China’s GB standard and an AHRI IPLV of up to 12.3. With electricity estimated to account for approximately 88.5% of a chiller’s total lifecycle cost, its high efficiency can translate into substantial operational savings for building owners and operators. ... The unit is also designed with readiness for next-generation HFO refrigerants, helping customers in Asia Pacific prepare for evolving sustainability and regulatory requirements. Beyond energy performance, its ultra-quiet operation, with noise levels as low as 73 dB(A), also makes it ideal for noise-sensitive environments such as hospitals and commercial buildings. ... To support the demanding, year-round operating requirements of data centers, the HSWE offers a cooling capacity range of 500 -1,250 RT for standard applications and 600 to over 1,500 RT for data centers. It also supports a maximum leaving chilled water temperature of up to 35°C, enabling seamless integration with waterside economizer and free cooling systems. In mission-critical environments, fast recovery is essential. The HSWE can restart within 25 seconds after power restoration and achieve full load within two minutes, drastically reducing the risk of server overheating and business interruption. ... In addition, the HSWE is equipped with the advanced AdaptiView™ controller, which integrates multiple patented control logics including adaptive control, feedforward control, and variable primary flow compensation. It also marks the successful application of adaptive refrigerant flow control on a centrifugal platform. Together, these capabilities enable precise chilled-water temperature control and stable output under changing loads and variable-flow conditions, supporting the sophisticated energy-saving strategies used in today’s high-performance buildings and data centers. ... Trane® – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator – creates comfortable, energy efficient indoor environments for commercial and residential applications. For more information, please visit trane.com. ... About Trane TechnologiesTrane Technologies is a global climate innovator. Through our strategic brands Trane® and Thermo King®, and our portfolio of environmentally responsible products and services, we bring efficient and sustainable climate solutions to buildings, homes and transportation. For more on Trane Technologies, visit tranetechnologies.com. ... Trane Launches HSWE Magnetic Bearing Chiller to Advance Data Center Cooling Across Asia Pacific"
TRANE,,,,Exa,Trane Cloud Adds Cell Modem Connectivity | Trane Commercial HVAC,www.trane.com,2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.trane.com/commercial/north-america/us/en/about-us/newsroom/press-releases/introducing-cell-modem.html,"Trane Cloud Adds Cell Modem Connectivity | Trane Commercial HVAC ... # Trane Launches New Connectivity Solution to Elevate Customer Experience and Expand Digital Capabilities ... to Trane ... DAVIDSON, N.C., June 30, 2026 – Trane® – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator, is introducing a new connectivity solution that helps customers modernize building operations through secure, simplified access to equipment data and connected services. Purpose-built for speed, simplicity and security, the Trane® Cell Modem provides a seamless path for customers to connect their equipment to Trane Cloud– unlocking real-time insights, analytics and digital services that help enable smarter, more efficient facilities. ... For many building owners and operators, the complexity, cost and security considerations of connecting equipment to IT networks have been major barriers to modernization – particularly for legacy equipment not originally designed for digital connectivity. As a new connectivity gateway, the solution helps address those challenges with a streamlined, secure path to accelerate digital transformation across their portfolios, delivering broader visibility, faster decision-making and stronger operational performance. ... The solution uses cellular connectivity to connect installed Trane commercial equipment to Trane Cloud instead of relying on a building’s local Wi‑Fi or IT network. Designed for quick deployment and simplified installation, it provides a scalable, secure and affordable way to extend digital access across more equipment already in the field. ... “Early customer interest reinforces that connected equipment is a critical first step in modernizing building operations,” said Brian Fox, Director of Digital Sales, Commercial HVAC Americas, Trane Technologies. “This new offering helps customers take that step with simple, secure connectivity to Trane Cloud, where they can access the insights, analytics and expertise needed to optimize performance, improve reliability and operate more sustainably.” ... Through Trane Cloud, building owners, operators, and facility teams gain a connected view of equipment performance across sites and portfolios, enabling organizations to better manage energy use, help reduce downtime and enhance reliability. By combining Trane’s deep expertise in building systems with proven telematics capabilities, customers gain a simple, scalable and secure path to digital transformation – unlocking the full value of Trane Cloud, supporting circularity by extending the useful life of installed equipment and enabling smarter, data-driven building performance. ... Importantly, the solution also strengthens how Trane delivers service. Live data helps Trane experts continuously optimize offerings, while technicians can log in remotely to triage issues faster, diagnose performance trends and pair data-driven insights with the expertise of Trane’s best-in-class service teams. This combination of intelligent analytics and human expertise allows customers to resolve issues more quickly and improve performance across the equipment lifecycle. ... About Trane Technologies Trane Technologies is a global climate innovator. Through our strategic brands Trane® and Thermo King®, and our portfolio of environmentally responsible products and services, we bring efficient and sustainable climate solutions to buildings, homes and transportation. For more on Trane Technologies, visit tranetechnologies.com. ... Trane® – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator – creates comfortable, energy efficient indoor environments for commercial and residential applications. For more information, please visit trane.com."
TRANE,,,,Exa,Trane Named David Weekley Homes’ 2026 National Preferred Partner Award | Supply House Times,www.supplyht.com (Supply House Times Editorial Staff),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.supplyht.com/articles/107271-trane-named-david-weekley-homes-2026-national-preferred-partner-award,"Trane Named David Weekley Homes’ 2026 National Preferred Partner Award | Supply House Times ... ## This is ... consecutive year that the company has received ... Trane – by Trane Technologies has been named a 2026 National Preferred Partner by David Weekley Homes, one of the nation’s largest privately-held home builders. ... Trane is one of 13 companies to receive the National Preferred Partner designation, which recognizes field and manufacturing partners that consistently operate at ""world-class levels"" and earn top scores in David Weekley Homes’ National Preferred Partner Survey. This marks the 15th time Trane has received the award. ... “Being recognized for the 15th time by David Weekley Homes reflects the strength of our long-standing collaboration and our shared commitment to delivering exceptional homeowner experiences,” said Mark Majocha, President, Residential HVAC, Trane Technologies. “We’re proud to support builders with a broad portfolio of innovative, energy-efficient and reliable HVAC solutions designed to meet a wide range of homeowner needs while bringing lasting comfort to communities across the country.” ... “Throughout our 50 years as a company, David Weekley Homes has set a high bar for our National Preferred Partners. Trane consistently exceeds those standards and strengthens that legacy with their outstanding quality and service,” said John Schiegg, Vice President of Purchasing and Supply Chain Services for David Weekley Homes. ... “It’s an honor to continue earning recognition from David Weekley Homes as a trusted National Preferred Partner,” said Andy Stallworth, manager for strategic relationships for Trane’s residential HVAC business. “This award reflects our team’s dedication to delivering responsive service, trusted expertise and high-quality HVAC solutions that help our builder partners succeed.” ... # Trane receives David Weekley Homes’ 2025 National Preferred Partner Award for delivering exceptional products and service ... https://www.supplyht.com/articles/106644-trane-receives-david-weekley-homes-2025-national-preferred-partner-award-for-delivering-exceptional-products-and-service See More ... # Rheem named David Weekley Homes' National Preferred Partner for excellence in products and service ... # Moen named National Preferred Partner by David Weekley Homes for 13th consecutive year"
TRANE,,,,Exa,Trane Receives David Weekley Trusted Partner Award for 15th Year in a Row - Trane®,www.trane.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.trane.com/residential/en/resources/blog/press-releases/trane-named-david-weekley-homes-2026-national-preferred-partner-award-for-15th-consecutive-year/,"Trane Receives David Weekley Trusted Partner Award for 15th Year in a Row - Trane® # Trane Named David Weekley Homes’ 2026 National Preferred Partner Award for 15th Consecutive Year ... Published: June 24, 2026 ... Davidson, N.C., June 23, 2026 – Trane® – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator, has been named a 2026 National Preferred Partner by David Weekley Homes, one of the nation’s largest privately-held home builders. ... Trane is one of 13 companies to receive the National Preferred Partner designation, which recognizes field and manufacturing partners that consistently operate at world-class levels and earn top scores in David Weekley Homes’ National Preferred Partner Survey. This marks the 15 th time Trane has received the award. ... “Being recognized for the 15 th time by David Weekley Homes reflects the strength of our long-standing collaboration and our shared commitment to delivering exceptional homeowner experiences,” said Mark Majocha, President, Residential HVAC, Trane Technologies. “We’re proud to support builders with a broad portfolio of innovative, energy-efficient and reliable HVAC solutions designed to meet a wide range of homeowner needs while bringing lasting comfort to communities across the country.” ... our 50 years as a company, David Weekley Homes has set a high ... standards and strengthens that legacy with their outstanding quality ... service,” said John Schiegg, Vice President of Purchasing and Supply Chain Services ... “It’s an honor to continue earning recognition from David Weekley Homes as a trusted National Preferred Partner,” said Andy Stallworth, manager for strategic relationships for Trane’s residential HVAC business. “This award reflects our team’s dedication to delivering responsive service, trusted expertise and high-quality HVAC solutions that help our builder partners succeed.” ... Trane – by Trane Technologies (NYSE: TT), a global climate innovator – creates comfortable, energy-efficient indoor environments for commercial and residential applications. For more information, please visit www.trane.com or www.tranetechnologies.com. ... Trane Technologies is a global climate innovator. Through our strategic brands Trane® and Thermo King®, and our portfolio of environmentally responsible products and services, we bring efficient and sustainable climate solutions to buildings, homes and transportation. For more on Trane Technologies, visit tranetechnologies.com. ... David Weekley Homes, founded in 1976, operates in 19 markets across the United States and is headquartered in Houston. David Weekley Homes was the first builder in the United States to be awarded the Triple Crown of American Home Building, an honor which includes “America’s Best Builder,” “National Housing Quality Award” and “National Builder of the Year.” Weekley Homes has been recognized 20 times by Great Place to Work® and Fortune magazine as one of the 100 Best Companies to Work For. Since inception, David Weekley Homes has closed more than 130,000 homes. For more information about David Weekley Homes, visit the company’s website at https://www.davidweekleyhomes.com."
