SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"SEERS: ""We Will Maintain Our Market Leadership Through Platform Competitiveness, Not Price Competition"" - EDAILY",en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202608065291/,"SEERS: ""We Will Maintain Our Market Leadership Through Platform Competitiveness, Not Price Competition"" - EDAILY ... ## SEERS: ""We Will Maintain Our Market Leadership Through Platform Competitiveness, Not Price Competition"" ... NA EUN-KYUNG 2026-08-06 10:38:02 [Edaily Reporter NA EUN-KYUNG ] Medical artificial intelligence (AI) company SEERS TECHNOLOGY(458870)stated on the 6th, in response to concerns recently raised in some quarters about intensifying price competition in the patient monitoring market, that “we are maintaining our market leadership based on platform competitiveness, not price.” SEERS explained, “To date, there has been no decrease in orders or damage to revenue due to price competition,” adding, “Hospitals select vendors by comprehensively evaluating implementation experience, platform operational capabilities, and after-sales support systems, rather than simply choosing the lowest price.” The company also emphasized that its AI inpatient monitoring platform, “thynC™,” is not merely a medical device but a platform business that includes integration with hospital electronic medical records (EMR), AI analysis, operational processes, and customer support (CX). Ciers explained that, based on its extensive experience in deploying and operating systems at the largest number of medical institutions in Korea, it has secured numerous cases where it was selected as the final contractor even amid recent instances of price competition. Furthermore, the company stated that the real-world clinical data and customer feedback (VOC) accumulated as the number of partner medical institutions increases are key competitive advantages that enhance AI performance and service quality. It also added that it is securing cost competitiveness through proactive procurement and direct production of core components, while strengthening its market competitiveness based on economies of scale resulting from expanded operations. SEERS officials stated, “We are maintaining our number one position in the domestic market based on platform competitiveness, not price competition,” adding, “We will continue to expand our competitive advantage based on our accumulated operational experience and economies of scale.” Economy Corporation"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,ZEISS invests in SeeTrue Technologies to advance eye-tracking solutions - European Business,www.european-biz.com (Marie Weil),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.european-biz.com/industries/industrial/zeiss-invests-in-seetrue-technologies-to-advance-eye-tracking-solutions/,"ZEISS invests in SeeTrue Technologies to advance eye-tracking solutions - European Business ... # ZEISS invests in SeeTrue Technologies to advance eye-tracking solutions ... ZEISS Ventures led a EUR 2.2 million investment round in SeeTrue Technologies, a Finnish deep-tech company developing miniaturized eye-tracking technology. The investment will accelerate the commercialization of SeeTrue’s ultra-low-power eye-sensing architecture, which is designed to address important challenges in next-generation interfaces for smart optical systems and eyewear. ... SeeTrue’s proprietary architecture combines miniaturized sensing hardware with optimized embedded processing to enable scalable eye-sensing capabilities with low power consumption and a small hardware footprint. The technology supports gaze-based interaction and attention-aware computing for applications across healthcare-related, industrial, and smart eyewear contexts. ... “SeeTrue has developed a differentiated approach to eye tracking. We believe the team is well positioned to address important challenges across vision-based applications and enable more efficient ways of human-machine interaction,” states Prof. Dr. Boris Hofmann, Head of ZEISS Ventures. ... “We are working to make eye tracking more compact and suitable for the future of optical and wearable technology. ZEISS’ expertise in optical system design and vision-based technologies provides a valuable perspective as we continue to develop and commercialize our eye-sensing platform,” says Roman Bednarik, CEO and co-founder of SeeTrue Technologies. ... The investment round further includes participation from Superhero Capital and North Karelia Growth Fund (NKGF), managed by Redstone Nordics, among other investors. With this investment, ZEISS Ventures underlines its interest in supporting technologies that enable the next generation of smart optical systems and wearable devices."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SEERS Enhances 'Think' Operating System… Raises Barriers to Entry for the Platform - EDAILY,en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202608055228/,"SEERS Enhances 'Think' Operating System… Raises Barriers to Entry for the Platform - EDAILY ... ## SEERS Enhances 'Think' Operating System… Raises Barriers to Entry for the Platform ... Specializing in CX and Operational Systems Based on Experience Managing 220 Medical Institutions and 20,000 Hospital Beds Accumulation of Operational Data → AI Advancement: A Virtuous Cycle… Strengthening Platform Competitiveness ... (Photo courtesy of SEERS) [Edaily Reporter SONG YOUNG-DOO ] SEERS TECHNOLOGY(458870), a wearable AI diagnostic monitoring company, announced on the 5th that it has reorganized its operational structure into a business division system and enhanced the operational framework of its “thynC Connected Hub” in line with the expansion of its “thynC™” AI inpatient monitoring platform business.This reorganization is a measure aimed at enhancing the platform’s operational competitiveness rather than simply expanding the organization. Based on the field experience accumulated through its current operations at approximately 220 medical institutions nationwide—covering about 20,000 hospital beds—SEERS’ strategy is to further widen the gap with competitors by enhancing customer experience (CX) and operational efficiency.The company expanded its existing operations organization into a business division structure and separated the Operations Team from the Infrastructure Team. The Operations Team is dedicated to hospital operations and customer experience (CX), strengthening engagement with medical institutions, while the Infrastructure Team is responsible for hardware and AI software operations, as well as the procurement of key materials and cost management, thereby enhancing supply chain stability and price competitiveness.A dedicated hospital CX (Customer Experience) organization has also been newly established. By building a hybrid support system that combines an AI-based customer support system with specialized consultants, the company plans to respond swiftly to hospital inquiries and VOC (Voice of Customer) and incorporate accumulated customer feedback into product and service improvements.SEERS emphasized that the competitiveness of its AI healthcare platform lies not simply in increasing the number of hospitals, but in the data and know-how accumulated during operations. The company explained that as the number of hospitals grows, installation experience, operational standards, incident response history, and customer requirements are accumulated, creating a virtuous cycle that leads to the advancement of AI services and product improvements.In particular, given that the total number of hospital beds in South Korea is approximately 700,000, the company believes that its current scale of 20,000 beds is merely the beginning. It expects that if the number of operational beds expands to 50,000 or 100,000 in the future, the accumulated operational data and customer experience itself will become platform assets that competitors will find difficult to match in the short term.Jeong Hoon, Director of Think’s Business Division, stated, “The core competitive advantage of an AI healthcare platform lies in continuously incorporating the operational data and customer experiences accumulated in clinical settings into the improvement of AI services and products.” He added, “Based on the accumulated operational data, we will enhance service quality and operational efficiency to continuously strengthen the competitiveness of the Think platform.”"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,ZEISS Invests in SeeTrue Eye-Tracking Technology,www.zeiss.com,2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/newsroom/press-releases/2026/eye-tracking-seetrue.html,"ZEISS Invests in SeeTrue Eye-Tracking Technology ... Oberkochen, Germany | 5 August 2026 | ZEISS Group ... ZEISS Ventures led a EUR 2.2 million investment round in SeeTrue Technologies, a Finnish deep-tech company developing miniaturized eye-tracking technology. The investment will accelerate the commercialization of SeeTrue’s ultra-low-power eye-sensing architecture, which is designed to address important challenges in next-generation interfaces for smart optical systems and eyewear. ... SeeTrue's proprietary architecture combines miniaturized sensing hardware with optimized embedded processing to enable scalable eye-sensing capabilities with low power consumption and a small hardware footprint. The technology supports gaze-based interaction and attention-aware computing for applications across healthcare-related, industrial, and smart eyewear contexts. ... “SeeTrue has developed a differentiated approach to eye ... . We believe the team is ... positioned to address important challenges across vision-based applications and enable more efficient ways of human-machine interaction,” states ... Hofmann, Head ... “We are working to make eye tracking more compact and suitable for the future of optical and wearable technology. ZEISS’ expertise in optical system design and vision-based technologies provides a valuable perspective as we continue to develop and commercialize our eye-sensing platform,” says Roman Bednarik, CEO and co-founder of SeeTrue Technologies. ... The investment round further includes participation from Superhero Capital and North Karelia Growth Fund (NKGF), managed by Redstone Nordics, among other investors. With this investment, ZEISS Ventures underlines its interest in supporting technologies that enable the next generation of smart optical systems and wearable devices. ... is an internationally leading technology enterprise operating in the fields of optics and optoelectronics ... In the previous fiscal year, the ... ISS Group generated annual revenue totaling almost 12 billion euros in its four segments Semiconductor Manufacturing Technology, Industrial Quality & Research ... Medical Technology, and Consumer Markets (September ... 0, 2025 ... With a portfolio aligned with future growth areas like digitalization, healthcare, and Smart Production and a strong brand, ZEISS is shaping the future of technology and constantly advancing the world of optics and related fields with its solutions. The company's significant, sustainable investments in research and development lay the foundation for the success and continued expansion of ZEISS' technology and market leadership. ZEISS invests 14 percent of its revenue in research and development – this high level of expenditure has a long tradition at ZEISS and is also an investment in the future. ... With over 47,400 employees, ZEISS is active globally in around 50 countries with more than 60 sales and service locations, around 40 research and development facilities, and 30 production facilities worldwide (March 31, 2026). Founded in 1846 in Jena, the company is headquartered in Oberkochen, Germany. The Carl Zeiss Foundation, one of the largest foundations in Germany committed to the promotion of science, is the sole owner of the holding company, Carl Zeiss AG. ... ZEISS Ventures, the corporate venture capital arm of the ZEISS Group, invests in and partners with deep-tech start-ups that have the potential to shape future technologies, markets, and business models beyond ZEISS’ core business. In addition to providing capital, ZEISS Ventures supports portfolio companies with access to ZEISS’ technological and industry expertise, as well as its global network, helping accelerate the development and commercialization of innovative solutions. ... SeeTrue Technologies Oy, founded in 2018, is a Finnish deep-tech company based in Joensuu, Finland, developing ultra-miniature eye-tracking technology for medical optical systems, vision care, and smart wearables. Built on decades of elite research in photonics, embedded systems, and human-computer interaction, SeeTrue delivers the bio-adaptive sensing layer for the future of spatial computing."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,S-Tech System Builds AI-Based On-Site Management System for Facility Operations - Seoul Economic Daily,en.sedaily.com (Park U-In),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/08/05/s-tech-system-builds-ai-based-on-site-management-system-for,"S-Tech System Builds AI-Based On-Site Management System for Facility Operations - Seoul Economic Daily ... STech System will pilot its in-house developed on-site operations management platform ""S-Agent"" at select worksites to systematically accumulate and manage field operations experience. Photo courtesy of STech System ... S-Tech System, a company specializing in comprehensive safety solutions, is building a management system that standardizes its facility management operational know-how on a data-driven basis. ... S-Tech System said on the 4th that it has piloted ""S-Agent,"" a proprietary on-site operations management platform, at select business sites to systematically accumulate and manage field operation experience. ... The Facility Management (FM) industry relies heavily on the experience and skill of on-site managers, which poses a challenge in that service quality can vary when managers are replaced or when operations expand to new sites. As a result, demand from client companies for standardized operating systems and objective quality management is also growing. ... Based on operational know-how accumulated across various business sites, S-Tech System has been advancing an operating system that integrates the management of work plans, execution results, quality evaluations, and complaint handling. Through this, the company plans to reduce operational variance among managers and maintain consistent service quality even when expanding to new sites. ... S-Agent, currently under pilot operation, integrates the management of real-time work status, quality evaluations, and complaint handling records. The company plans to expand the scope of application to the security and facility management fields in the second half of this year. ... Going forward, the company will also introduce AI-based complaint analysis functions. It plans to automatically classify received complaints by type and analyze their frequency and trends to identify recurring complaints early, while also using the data to improve on-site operational efficiency, such as adjusting cleaning cycles, conducting facility inspections, improving patrol routes, and managing vulnerable areas. ... ""Through advancing our operating system, we expect to convert field experience into standardized organizational assets and data, improve operational efficiency, and reduce the management burden that comes with expanding business sites,"" an S-Tech System official said. ""We will strengthen customer satisfaction and long-term contract competitiveness by enhancing the consistency of service quality and continuity of operations."""
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seer Robotics clears HKEX hearing,kr-asia.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://kr-asia.com/pulses/162613,"Seer Robotics clears HKEX hearing ... # Seer Robotics clears HKEX hearing ... Seer Robotics cleared its Hong Kong IPO hearing on June 7. Despite leading the global robot controller market by 2025 sales volume, the company posted a cumulative loss of RMB 137 million from 2023–2025. Its filings also point to risks from a low-price strategy, shrinking controller margins, and cash flow pressure."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Searcher upgrades seismic intelligence app with real-time global survey tracking,worldoil.com,2026-08-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://worldoil.com/news/2026/8/2/searcher-upgrades-seismic-intelligence-app-with-real-time-global-survey-tracking/,"Searcher upgrades seismic intelligence app with real-time global survey tracking ... # Searcher upgrades seismic intelligence app with real-time global survey tracking August 02, 2026 (WO) — Searcher has launched an upgraded version of its Searcher Live mobile application, giving oil and gas professionals real-time visibility into global seismic survey activity, vessel movements and exploration programs. Powered by the company's SeisIntel™ platform, the updated application enables geoscientists, exploration teams and business development professionals to monitor active seismic campaigns, track survey vessels and identify operators involved in exploration projects worldwide. ... Searcher said the upgraded app provides streamlined access to operational data and exploration intelligence through an enhanced mobile interface, allowing users to follow activity across key offshore and onshore basins as it develops. ... ""The upgraded Searcher Live gives users a quick and intuitive way to stay connected to global seismic exploration activity,"" said Alan Hopping, managing director of Searcher. ""Access to timely, reliable intelligence is increasingly important in today's exploration environment."" ... The Searcher Live application is integrated with the company's SeisIntel platform, which combines real-time operational data with seismic survey information, company intelligence and industry analysis to support exploration planning and business development. ... Searcher said the relaunch reflects its continued investment in digital tools designed to improve access to exploration data and market intelligence for the upstream sector."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,ezCaretech signs $6.9 million next-generation HIS deal with Saudi healthcare group Care Med < Device/ICT < Article - KBR,www.koreabiomed.com (Kim Ji-hye jkim404@docdocdoc.co.kr See Other Articles),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.koreabiomed.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=32612,"ezCaretech signs $6.9 million next-generation HIS deal with Saudi ... Med < Device/ICT < ... Digital healthcare company ezCaretech said Thursday it signed a contract worth about 10 billion won ($6.96 million) with Saudi Arabia's National Medical Care (Care Med) to deploy its next-generation hospital information system, “BESTCare 2.0.” ... The agreement marks a strategic milestone for ezCaretech, expanding its Middle East business beyond the public healthcare sector into major private hospital networks. Previously, the company focused on public-sector customers, including the Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs (MNG-HA) and medical centers under Saudi Arabia's Royal Commission. ... By securing one of Saudi Arabia's ... private hospital chains as a client, ezCaretech has established references in both ... public and private healthcare sectors, ... its expansion into ... Care Med, listed on the Saudi Stock Exchange (Tadawul), operates multiple general hospitals and specialty medical facilities across Riyadh and other major regions. Under the agreement, ezCaretech will initially implement BESTCare 2.0 at four hospitals with a combined capacity of about 1,300 beds, followed by deployment at two affiliated clinics under a ""4+2"" project structure. ... As Care Med plans to continue expanding its hospital network, the project is expected to create opportunities for further system rollouts and foster a long-term strategic partnership. Following implementation, ezCaretech also anticipates recurring revenue from maintenance and operational service contracts, supporting long-term overseas revenue growth and improved cash flow. ... The company said it has spent the past year restructuring its overseas business strategy and significantly strengthening its marketing efforts in the Middle East to prepare for the contract win. ... At the Global Health Exhibition (GHE) held in Riyadh last October, ezCaretech organized the ""Team BESTCare Korea"" consortium, which drew strong interest from the local market. It also strengthened its regional presence by signing a memorandum of understanding with LEAN, a Saudi state-owned company that plays a central role in the country's digital healthcare ecosystem. ... This year, ezCaretech plans to expand the Team BESTCare Korea initiative further to reinforce brand recognition and deepen market penetration across the Middle East. ... The company's Middle East revenue nearly doubled last year, driven by existing customers. The Care Med contract shows that its overseas business has moved beyond relying solely on existing clients and is successfully generating new demand from the private healthcare sector. ... Amid Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030 initiative to expand private-sector participation in healthcare, ezCaretech plans to use the Care Med project as a reference to capture growing demand for digital transformation. The company added that it has already secured multiple promising sales leads across the region, raising expectations for additional contracts. ... ""This contract is the result of more than a year of carefully planned and executed strategies tailored to the Middle East market,"" ezCaretech CEO Hong Woo-sun said. ... ""We have successfully extended the technological capabilities proven in Saudi Arabia's public healthcare sector into the private market. Going forward, we will further strengthen the Team BESTCare Korea collaboration with leading Korean digital healthcare companies and serve as a catalyst for the broader expansion of Korea's healthcare industry into the Middle East,"" he added."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Esstee Exports bets on IoT platform Texplus to boost textile factory efficiency by up to 20% - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (Neha Dewan),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/small-biz/sme-sector/esstee-exports-bets-on-iot-platform-texplus-to-boost-textile-factory-efficiency-by-up-to-20/articleshow/132764883.cms,"Esstee Exports bets on IoT platform Texplus to boost textile factory efficiency by up to 20% - The Economic Times # Esstee Exports bets on IoT platform Texplus to boost textile factory efficiency by up to 20% Esstee Exports bets on IoT platform Texplus to boost textile factory efficiency by up to 20% ... Last Updated: Jul ... Designed specifically for the apparel manufacturing sector, Texplus offers a digital platform that connects every stage of the manufacturing process through real-time monitoring, QR-code traceability, production analytics, workflow automation and AI-powered decision support. ... Tiruppur-based Esstee Exports has devised Texplus Technologies, an advanced IoT-enabled solution for exporters to track real-time production updates. In a bid to make the garment manufacturing operations more efficient, faster, and seamless, Tiruppur-based Esstee Exports has developed an advanced IoT-enabled solution, Texplus, to enable exporters to track real-time production updates. The solution, available through Esstee’s subsidiary Texplus Technologies, can be accessed through its device. The company claims that its device can boost factory efficiency by around 15-20%. Esstee Exports has already sold 2,000 devices to five textile companies even before its official rollout in September. Designed specifically for the apparel manufacturing sector, Texplus offers a digital platform that connects every stage of the manufacturing process through real-time monitoring, QR-code traceability, production analytics, workflow automation and AI-powered decision support. ... Thirukkumaran Natarajan, Chairman, Esstee Exports, says that digitisation and automation are the need of the hour for the textile industry. “We are already facing a labour shortage, and we need solutions that can help overcome this challenge,” he says. ... Natarajan says that the government has set a target of reaching $40 billion in apparel exports from the current $16 billion; this can only be achieved with operational efficiency. “Such solutions will play an important role in achieving these objectives.” ### Live Events ... While the device (hardware) costs around Rs 17,000, the software is priced approximately between Rs 3 lakh and Rs 10 lakh, depending on the number of machines. Texplus Technologies has invested around Rs 2 crore in R&D to develop the hardware and software for this solution. ... Natarajan says that India has a huge opportunity which it needs to capitalise on with the FTA agreements that are coming up. “We are already seeing strong interest from buyers in the UK and Europe. They are de-risking their sourcing away from other countries and increasingly looking at India because we are politically stable, have abundant raw material resources, and are a major manufacturing destination. To fully capitalise on this opportunity, however, we need to improve productivity. That is one of India's biggest challenges today. Among textile manufacturing nations, India ranks among the lowest in terms of productivity,” he says. Tiruppur-based Sahana Clothing Private Limited, which manufacturers 40 million garments annually, has ordered 500 devices from Texplus Technologies. “It has been very useful for us. In any other device, we have to manually make the count of the pieces, but here it is all done automatically. We have 2,000 machines, and I took the initial lot to try. The results have been good, and we would like to purchase more for the rest of our machines too,” says S. Manikandan, Industrial Engineering Manager, Sahana Clothing Private Limited. ... Manikandan says that their efficiency has increased by 10% after using this IoT solution from Texplus. “It tracks all relevant cycle data, such as time study, needle study, skill mapping, and wash study through AI. Prior to this, there was no such clear data, and we had to be completely reliant on supervisors for their input,” he adds. The exporter states that countries such as Vietnam and China use the hanger system for garments in manufacturing, which is far more expensive. An automated garment hanger system—an overhead conveyor network moving clothing parts between production stations—boosts factory efficiency by 20-30%. Himani Gulati, Director of MEX Exhibitions, a specialty trade fair and B2B exhibition platform which is also organising the upcoming textile fair Gartex Textile Expo 2026, says that AI and automation are no longer conversations about the future; they are becoming part of how competitive textile businesses operate today. “Across global markets, we are seeing manufacturers use these technologies to improve everything from quality inspection and production planning to predictive maintenance and supply chain visibility. I strongly believe India is certainly moving in that direction. Many companies have already begun investing in automation and digital manufacturing, and it is encouraging to see even MSMEs recognising that technology is becoming a business necessity rather than a choice,” she says. Going forward, Esstee Exports plans to offer complete end-to-end tracking—from fabric production all the way to dispatch—with this solution. “Indian exporters are termed the lowest in efficiency standards. We want to change that image. We want India to become one of the best-performing manufacturing destinations in terms of productivity,” Natarajan says."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SEERS Begins Full-Scale Preparations to Supply Initial Shipment to the UAE… Accelerates Expansion into the Middle East with Participation in August’s IFM - EDAILY,en.edaily.co.kr (edaily),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202607285462/,"SEERS Begins Full-Scale Preparations to Supply Initial Shipment to the UAE… Accelerates Expansion into the Middle East with Participation in August’s IFM - EDAILY ... ## SEERS Begins Full-Scale Preparations to Supply Initial Shipment to the UAE… Accelerates Expansion into the Middle East with Participation in August’s IFM ... Preparations for Production and Delivery of Initial Shipment on Track Following UAE Supply Contract Participation in IFM, the Middle East’s Largest Digital Healthcare Event, in August Marks the Start of Full-Scale Expansion into the GCC Market ... (Photo: SEERS) [Edaily Reporter SONG YOUNG-DOO ] SEERS TECHNOLOGY(458870), a wearable AI diagnostic monitoring company, announced on the 28th that it is proceeding as planned with the production and supply of the initial batch of mobiCARE™ under a supply contract with the United Arab Emirates (UAE), and will accelerate its expansion into the Middle East market by participating in the “IFM 2026 (International Family Medicine Conference & Exhibition)” to be held in Dubai this August.SEERS’ Middle East business gained momentum last February with the signing of a strategic memorandum of understanding (MOU) with PureHealth, the UAE’s largest healthcare group. Although concerns about potential delays arose due to geopolitical uncertainties in the region, the company has continued to advance its business as scheduled through ongoing collaboration with local medical institutions and partners.As a result, the company entered the commercialization phase in May by signing a supply contract worth approximately 22 billion won with One Health, a digital healthcare company affiliated with PureHealth. Currently, the company is preparing to produce and supply the initial batch for the UAE market and is sequentially advancing follow-up projects—such as outpatient care and health screening services—in collaboration with local partners.The company also plans to expand its reach into the Middle Eastern hospital market—comprising approximately 800,000 hospital beds—with a focus on the UAE and other GCC (Gulf Cooperation Council) countries, in line with growing demand for smart hospital infrastructure, through its AI inpatient monitoring platform, “thynC™.”To expand its business in the Middle East, SEERS will participate as a Gold Sponsor in IFM 2026, taking place at the Dubai World Trade Centre from August 25 to 27. IFM is the Middle East’s largest academic event for primary care and digital healthcare, featuring participation from the UAE Ministry of Health and the Dubai Health Authority, among others. It attracts a large number of attendees, including medical institutions from major GCC countries such as Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, and Oman, as well as global healthcare companies and medical professionals.At this event, the company plans to showcase Mobicare and Think, with a strategy to expand cooperation with medical institutions and partners in GCC countries based on the operational track record it has established in the UAE. The company intends to treat the UAE not as a single market but as a strategic hub for entering the Middle East, with plans to expand its business in phases.A company official stated, “Our UAE operations are proceeding as planned, and we are currently moving forward without a hitch with the production and supply of the initial batch.” The official added, “We will use our participation in IFM 2026 as an opportunity to expand our network in the Middle East market and ensure the stable growth of our core businesses—Think in the domestic market and Mobicare overseas.”"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seer Stockholders Vote to Re-Elect All Seven of Seer's Director Nominees at 2026 Annual Meeting | INN,investingnews.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://investingnews.com/seer-stockholders-vote-to-re-elect-all-seven-of-seer-s-director-nominees-at-2026-annual-meeting/,"# Seer Stockholders Vote to Re-Elect All Seven of Seer's Director Nominees at 2026 Annual Meeting ... SEER, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER) ("" SEER"") today announced that, based on the preliminary voting results from SEER's 2026 Annual Meeting of Stockholders (the ""Annual Meeting""), SEER stockholders have voted to re-elect all seven of SEER's director nominees Omid Farokhzad, M.D.; Meeta Gulyani; Robert Langer, Sc.D.; Terrance McGuire; Dipchand (Deep) Nishar; Isaac Ro; and Nicolas Roelofs, Ph.D. to SEER's Board of Directors (the ""Board""). ... We thank our stockholders for their support and engagement over the last several months. This outcome reflects confidence in Seer's highly qualified, purpose-built Board and our directors' commitment to advancing the best interests of all stockholders. We remain focused on disciplined execution of our strategy that includes expanding utilization of our growing installed base, securing additional population-scale cohort and biobank studies, advancing our innovation pipeline and scaling platform commercialization with continued cost discipline. The business is building momentum, and we remain confident in Seer's ability to drive value creation over the long-term. ... Seer expects ... the final certified voting results ... Exchange Commission. ... About Seer, Inc. SEER, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER) sets the standard in deep, unbiased proteomics, delivering insights with a scale, speed, precision and reproducibility previously unattainable. SEER's Proteograph® Product Suite integrates proprietary engineered nanoparticles, streamlined automation instrumentation, optimized consumables and advanced analytical software to overcome the limitations of traditional proteomic methods. SEER's products are for research use only and are not intended for diagnostic procedures. For more information, visit www.seer.bio. ... ## Completion of $5.4M Placement ... Completion of $5.4M Placement ... ## Completion of $5.4M Placement ... ## Quarterly Activities & Cshflow Report"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Seekr and OneValley Partner to Empower Startups and SMBs with Explainable, Defensible AI",www.prnewswire.com (Seekr Technologies),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/seekr-and-onevalley-partner-to-empower-startups-and-smbs-with-explainable-defensible-ai-302835835.html,"RESTON, Va., July 28, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Seekr, the leader in explainable, defensible AI, today announced a strategic partnership with a global innovation platform supporting 10,000+ founders, startups, and small businesses. Under the agreement, OneValley will serve as a Value-Added Reseller (VAR) and managed services partner for Seekr's AI platform, making enterprise-grade AI accessible to the companies that need it most and can least afford to get it wrong. ... We are entering a time when only explainable and trusted AI will be given access to critical systems, data and operations. Current regulations like the Securities and Exchange Commission's (SEC) disclosure requirements look exactly the same for a publicly disclosed 20-person fintech as it does to a Fortune 500 bank – both must answer to the same regulators. And what meets requirements today, might not tomorrow as they try to keep pace with the latest threats shaped by AI innovations, shifting state AI mandates, ongoing federal preemption debates, and changing sector guidance. ... The reality is, most 20-person companies do not have the dedicated legal resources to track these changes. While large enterprises can dedicate fully staffed engineering teams and sizable compliance budgets to AI deployment, startups and small businesses usually can't. This puts smaller-sized businesses in the worst position – forcing them to choose between the risk of opaque, off-the-shelf models, the cost of building their own, or the tools needed to ensure safe AI deployment. Seekr and OneValley's partnership removes those barriers and equals the playing field for all companies looking to deploy trusted AI, no matter the size. ... By combining Seekr's explainable AI platform – including a no-code environment with a library of pre-built, industry-tailored AI solutions – with OneValley's global distribution and implementation capabilities, the two companies are giving startups and SMBs AI that is: ... OneValley brings the implementation layer: onboarding, integration, training, and ongoing support delivered through its network of accelerators, incubators, founder communities, innovation centers, and small business networks. Startups and SMBs can adopt explainable, cost-effective AI without building an AI stack from scratch. ... The partnership is designed to support companies dealing with highly sensitive data, such as financial services, government, supply chain, and other highly regulated industries, with plans to expand in the future. This first set of sectors faces the highest costs and consequences from unexplainable AI decisions. And as these companies move from utilizing AI as just an assistant to autonomous AI that takes action – approving, filing, and transacting – that cost only climbs along with the risk of tokenmaxxing or breakaway AI spending. ... ""A 20-person fintech selling into a Fortune 500 bank inherits that bank's compliance requirements, including everything from vendor risk reviews to model documentation, and even audit rights,"" said Nikhil Sinha, CEO of OneValley. ""But, they lack the resources to sufficiently and consistently meet those standards. Partnering with OneValley and Seekr creates equitable access to defensible, explainable AI directly into founders' hands, no matter their size, ensuring the next generation of regulated-industry companies can compete without compromising on the standards their customers demand."" ... ""Explainability isn't a feature we bolted on to win enterprise and government contracts. It's the architecture Seekr was built on, and it's what makes AI defensible in any environment where the cost of being wrong is real,"" said Rob Clark, President of Seekr. ""Through OneValley, that architecture is now in reach for the founders and operators who'll define the next wave of critical industries. The rules they have to follow are the same ones the Fortune 500 follows. The AI we're giving them is built for it."" ... Seekr is the leader in explainable, defensible AI built for critical decisions in environments that demand accuracy and accountability. Seekr's technology and products help enterprises and government agencies deploy domain-specific large language models (LLMs), vision language models (VLMs) that understand the physical world, and AI agents trained on their own data – across any infrastructure, including sovereign deployments. Backed by robust verification and validation tools that surface the provenance and intent behind every model decision, Seekr delivers AI that organizations can audit and defend across all modalities. Learn more at seekr.com. ... OneValley is a global innovation platform connecting entrepreneur communities, startups, and investors. Through its flagship platform, Passport, OneValley engages members worldwide with access to programs, perks, and ecosystem partners. By working across these networks, OneValley enables organizations to reach and connect with relevant startups, scaleups, and investors, and introduces vetted solutions aligned to their needs. ... ### Anderson Merchandisers Selects Seekr to Bring Edge AI to the Last 100 Feet of Retail Across the US ... Anderson Merchandisers, the nation's leading in-store retail services provider, today named Seekr as its enterprise AI partner — starting with the... ... ### Seekr Achieves CMMC Level 2 Certification for Trusted AI Deployment, Setting the Standard for Operational AI in Government ... As national security agencies accelerate the deployment of operational AI, Seekr today announced it has achieved Cybersecurity Maturity Model..."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,AVANTE’S MAJORITY-OWNED SUBSIDIARY NSSG LAUNCHES TESEUM: AN,www.globenewswire.com (Avante Corp.),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/28/3334805/36577/en/AVANTE-S-MAJORITY-OWNED-SUBSIDIARY-NSSG-LAUNCHES-TESEUM-AN-AI-POWERED-PLATFORM-REDEFINING-ENTERPRISE-RISK-MANAGEMENT.html,"- NSSG, Avante's majority-owned international risk-management subsidiary, has launched TESEUM, a fully modular, AI-powered intelligence platform helping organizations detect, understand, and anticipate risk across security, cyber, compliance, and geopolitical domains. ... - The platform unifies location intelligence, travel risk, cyber risk, third-party due diligence, and predictive modelling into a single operational environment — replacing fragmented tools with one integrated intelligence ecosystem. ... - Since Avante acquired a majority interest in NSSG in 2023, the business has become a core contributor to Avante's international growth strategy. NSSG delivered 67% revenue growth in Fiscal 2026, including 97% growth in its Consulting division, and a 52% gross profit margin, underscoring the scalability and high-margin profile of Avante's international risk-management platform. ... TORONTO, Ontario, July 28, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Avante Corp. (TSX.V: XX) (OTC: ALXXF) (“Avante” or the “Company”), a global provider of technology-enabled security solutions and services, is pleased to announce that its majority-owned subsidiary, North Star Support Group (“NSSG”), has launched TESEUM, an AI-powered intelligence platform for integrated and predictive risk management. Developed as a modular and multi-layered operational intelligence environment, TESEUM integrates AI-driven analysis, real-time monitoring, and expert intelligence support into a single environment, enabling organizations to transform fragmented information into operational clarity, informed decision-making, and forward-looking risk intelligence. ... Today, organizations operate in an environment where geopolitical instability, cyber threats, supply chain disruption, regulatory change, sanctions, third-party exposure and operational risks evolve simultaneously. While information has never been more abundant, identifying what truly matters—and what is likely to matter next—has become increasingly difficult. Traditional monitoring tools no longer provide sufficient situational awareness. TESEUM was developed to bridge this gap by combining multiple intelligence disciplines into a unified platform. ... Emmanuel Mounouchos, CEO, Chairman, and Founder of Avante, commented, “TESEUM is a significant step forward for NSSG and for Avante's broader technology ecosystem, combining AI-powered intelligence with the deep expertise NSSG has built over two decades. We've been extremely pleased with NSSG's performance since joining Avante, reporting 67% revenue growth the most recent fiscal year speaks to the strength of the team and the value of integrating NSSG's global reach with our technology platform. TESEUM is the next stage of that growth story. ... Since Avante acquired a majority interest in NSSG in 2023, the business has become a core contributor to Avante's international growth strategy. NSSG delivered 67% revenue growth in Fiscal 2026 compared to Fiscal 2025, including 97% growth in its Consulting division, alongside a gross profit margin of 52%, reflecting the high-margin, scalable nature of its specialized risk-management services. With offices and representation across Europe, the Middle East, North America, and Africa, NSSG continues to serve a broad base of multinational clients, including Fortune 500 companies operating in complex and high-risk jurisdictions. ... Alessandro Martello, CEO and Founder of NSSG, added, “Our partnership with Avante has been transformative for NSSG, giving us access to the technology, resources, and platform needed to compete for larger and more complex mandates on a global scale. TESEUM reflects what that partnership makes possible — pairing AI-driven intelligence with the judgment of our analysts so clients can act on what matters, not just what's loud. We're proud of the growth we've delivered together, and we're even more excited about what's ahead.” ... Avante Corp. is a Toronto-based leading provider of security personnel and technology-enabled security solutions for residential and commercial clients. Avante's mission is to deliver an elevated level of security globally, with a white-glove approach for high-net-worth families and corporations alike, through advanced solutions and methods for detecting conditions requiring immediate response. The company has developed a diversified security platform that leverages cutting-edge technology to deliver superior security services. With an experienced team and a proven track record of solid growth, Avante is taking steps to build a broad portfolio of security businesses and solutions for its customers through organic growth complemented by strategic acquisitions. Avante acquires, manages, and develops industry-leading companies that provide specialized, mission-critical solutions to address the security risks faced by its clients. Avante is listed on the TSX Venture Exchange under the ticker “XX”. For more information, please visit www.avantecorp.ca and consider joining our investor email list. ... NSSG is a globally recognized risk-management company delivering strategic, intelligence-led advisory and operational support to organizations operating in complex and high-risk environments worldwide. With more than two decades of proven expertise, NSSG supports clients across Technology & Infrastructure, Government & Defence, Luxury Retail & Manufacturing, Financial Services & Critical Infrastructure, Gaming, Non-profits, and other sectors. Avante Corp. holds a majority ownership interest in NSSG, acquired in 2023. For more information, visit www.nssg.global. ... AVANTE ANNOUNCES FISCAL 2026 FINANCIAL RESULTS WITH 24% INCREASE IN RECURRING MONTHLY REVENUE AND 30% ADJUSTED EBITDA GROWTH ... Avante achieved 10.3% year-over-year revenue growth in fiscal 2026, reaching $37.2 million, with Recurring Monthly Revenue improving by 24.4%.The Company achieved Adjusted EBITDA of $2.3 million in... ... Avante Announces Timing of Fourth Quarter and Year-End Fiscal 2026 Investor Webinar ... Investor Webinar scheduled for Monday, July 27, 2026, at 11:00 am ET (8:00 am PT) TORONTO, Ontario, July 20, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Avante Corp. (TSX.V: XX) (OTC: ALXXF) (“Avante” or the..."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Data Center Surges In Global Coverage - Light Mask,lightmask.net (Light Mask Team),2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://lightmask.net/trending/data-center-surges-in-global-coverage/,"Data center mentions worldwide have increased sharply, with GDELT reporting 26 mentions in recent weeks, indicating growing global interest and expansion. ... Recent reports show a sharp increase in global coverage of data centers, with mentions rising from baseline levels. This indicates heightened interest and expansion in the sector, though specific drivers remain unclear. ... Global coverage of data centers has surged significantly in recent weeks, with the GDELT database recording 26 mentions—an increase of 21 times the baseline level. This spike indicates heightened attention from media and industry sources, highlighting the sector’s expanding importance worldwide. ... The GDELT (Global Database of Events, Language, and Tone) monitoring system reported 26 mentions of data centers within a recent time window, compared to a baseline of around 1 mention. This represents a substantial surge in media and online coverage, suggesting increased interest or activity in the sector. ... While the specific reasons for this surge are not yet fully clarified, analysts suggest that factors such as new data center projects, investments in cloud infrastructure, or geopolitical developments could be contributing. Industry experts note that this rise in coverage aligns with broader trends of digital transformation and cloud adoption. ... Officials from major data center companies and industry associations have not yet issued detailed statements regarding the coverage increase, and it remains to be seen whether this is driven by new developments or media attention cycles. ... The surge in global coverage underscores the growing strategic importance of data centers in the digital economy, cloud computing, and data security. Increased media attention can influence investor interest, policy discussions, and public perception, potentially accelerating sector growth or prompting regulatory scrutiny. ... For businesses and governments, heightened awareness may translate into more investment and infrastructure development, but also raises questions about environmental impact and data sovereignty. The sector’s visibility could shape future policies and industry standards. ... Over the past few years, the data center industry has experienced rapid growth driven by the expansion of cloud services, 5G deployment, and digital transformation initiatives. The GDELT database has historically shown low levels of media mentions, so the recent spike indicates a notable shift. ... In particular, recent announcements of new data center projects in key markets, geopolitical tensions affecting supply chains, and increased investments from tech giants have likely contributed to this surge. Industry analysts note that media coverage often correlates with sector expansion, regulatory developments, or major technological breakthroughs. ... However, it remains unclear whether this increase in mentions reflects actual growth and activity or is influenced by media cycles and reporting trends. ... It is not yet clear what specific factors are driving the surge in mentions. While industry activity and new projects are possible causes, there is no confirmed data linking the coverage spike to particular developments or investments. Further analysis is needed to determine whether this is a temporary media cycle or reflects sustained sector growth. ... Industry analysts and market observers will track upcoming project announcements, investment flows, and policy developments to assess whether the coverage surge indicates a genuine expansion trend. Media monitoring and sector reports over the coming months will clarify if this is a transient spike or a sign of longer-term growth. ... The increase suggests heightened interest and possibly expanding investment in data infrastructure, though the actual growth impact remains to be confirmed through sector data. ... It is not yet clear which regions or companies are most involved; further analysis of media sources is required to identify key players. ... ### Could this coverage increase lead to regulatory changes? ... Potentially, as greater visibility might prompt policymakers to consider new regulations related to data security, privacy, and environmental impact, but no such changes have been confirmed yet. ... While possible, there is no direct evidence linking the coverage spike to specific technological breakthroughs or innovations at this stage."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Tecnotree Secures $8.8 Million LATAM Digital Transformation Deals | Martech Edge | Best News on Marketing and Technology,martechedge.com,2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,,https://martechedge.com/news/tecnotree-secures-88-million-latam-digital-transformation-deals,"Tecnotree Secures $8.8 Million LATAM Digital Transformation Deals | Martech Edge | Best News on Marketing and Technology ... # Tecnotree Secures $8.8 Million LATAM Digital Transformation Deals # Tecnotree Secures $8.8 Million LATAM Digital Transformation Deals Business Wire Published on : Jul 28, 2026 Tecnotree has expanded its footprint in Latin America after securing new digital transformation contracts valued at $8.8 million, highlighting continued demand for AI-powered telecom modernization platforms across the region. The agreements will see the company deploy its AI-native Digital Business Support Systems (BSS) and digital commerce technologies to help communications service providers streamline operations, improve customer engagement, and accelerate digital service innovation. ... Tecnotree has announced a series of new digital transformation contracts across Latin America worth a combined $8.8 million, strengthening the company's position in one of the world's fastest-evolving telecommunications markets. The agreements reinforce growing investment among communications service providers (CSPs) in AI-powered business platforms designed to modernize customer experiences, automate operations, and unlock new revenue opportunities. ... The contracts will involve the deployment of Tecnotree's AI-native Digital Business Support Systems (BSS) platform alongside its enterprise-focused B2B Marketplace solution. Together, the technologies are intended to provide telecom operators with a unified digital foundation for managing customer engagement, digital commerce, partner ecosystems, and monetization strategies. ... The Latin American telecommunications market has become an increasingly attractive destination for digital transformation investments. Mobile connectivity continues to expand across the region, while enterprises and consumers are accelerating adoption of digital services, cloud applications, fintech solutions, and AI-powered customer experiences. These shifts are creating demand for more flexible and scalable digital infrastructure capable of supporting evolving business models. ... Tecnotree's recent contract wins also reflect growing adoption of AI across customer engagement and revenue management functions. AI-powered marketing, predictive analytics, and experience management solutions help operators analyze customer behavior, personalize offers, and optimize service delivery. For enterprise marketers, these technologies create opportunities ... improve customer acquisition, increase lifetime value, and deliver more relevant digital experiences at scale. ... The competitive landscape for telecom digital transformation includes major technology providers such as Amdocs, Netcracker Technology, Nokia, and Ericsson, all of which are expanding investments in cloud-native BSS, AI-driven automation, and digital commerce solutions. Tecnotree's focus on AI-native architecture and integrated digital business platforms positions it within a rapidly growing segment of the telecom software market. ... As communications service providers continue modernizing legacy infrastructure, investments in AI-powered digital platforms are expected to remain a strategic priority. Tecnotree's latest Latin American contracts suggest that telecom operators are increasingly seeking unified technology ecosystems capable of supporting growth, innovation, and long-term digital transformation. ... Telecommunications providers are accelerating investments in AI-native BSS platforms, digital commerce ecosystems, and customer experience technologies. Gartner and IDC research indicate that telecom operators are prioritizing automation, AI-powered analytics, and cloud-native infrastructure to improve operational efficiency and support new revenue models. Latin America remains a key growth market as operators modernize legacy systems and expand digital service offerings. ... Tecnotree's latest contract wins strengthen its presence in a rapidly evolving telecom technology market. As communications providers pursue AI-driven transformation strategies, demand for integrated digital business platforms that combine monetization, customer engagement, marketplace capabilities, and analytics is expected to increase. The company's growing LATAM footprint positions it to capitalize on this ongoing shift toward intelligent telecom operations."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Issues Positive Profit Alert with Significant Revenue and Gross Profit Growth for H1 2026 – Minichart,www.minichart.com.sg,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.minichart.com.sg/2026/07/24/shanghai-seer-intelligent-technology-issues-positive-profit-alert-with-significant-revenue-and-gross-profit-growth-for-h1-2026/,"Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Issues Positive Profit Alert with Significant Revenue and Gross Profit Growth for H1 2026 – Minichart ... # Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Issues Positive Profit Alert with Significant Revenue and Gross Profit Growth for H1 2026 ... Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. Issues Positive Profit Alert for H1 2026 ... # Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. Issues Positive Profit Alert for H1 2026 ... Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. (Stock Code: 06106) has issued a positive profit alert regarding its financial performance for the six months ended June 30, 2026. This announcement is made in compliance with the disclosure requirements of The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited. ... - Substantial Revenue Growth: The Group expects to record unaudited revenue of at least RMB252.6 million for the reporting period, representing an increase of at least 60% compared to the same period in 2025. - Higher Gross Profit: Gross profit is anticipated to be at least RMB118.3 million, a rise of at least 65% over the prior year. ... - Reduced Net Loss: The company forecasts a net loss (unaudited) of no more than RMB40.5 million, which is an improvement of at least 20% compared to the corresponding period in 2025. - Significant Reduction in Adjusted Net Loss: Adjusted net loss (unaudited) is expected to be no greater than RMB13.2 million, a reduction of at least 40% year-on-year. ... - Growth Drivers: The positive performance is mainly attributed to increased revenue from intelligent robots and “robot brains”, as well as exponential growth in overseas revenue streams. - Operational Efficiency: Improved operational efficiency and stricter expense control have contributed to increased gross profit and reduced losses. ... - The significant increases in both revenue and gross profit, coupled with the sharp reduction in both net loss and adjusted net loss, indicate a strong recovery and growth trajectory for the company. - The exponential growth in overseas revenue suggests successful international expansion, which may signal further potential upside and diversification of revenue streams. - Effective cost management and operational improvements are beginning to materialize, potentially setting the stage for future profitability. ... - Shareholders and investors should note: The above figures are based on unaudited management accounts and are subject to change upon finalization. The official interim results announcement is expected by the end of August 2026. ... - This positive profit alert is considered price-sensitive information and may have a material impact on the share price. ... The detailed financial results for the six months ended June 30, 2026, will be published by the end of August 2026. Shareholders and potential investors are advised to exercise caution when trading in the company’s shares until the formal results are announced. ... 上海仙工智能科技股份有限公司 ... 2026 ... 上海仙工智能科技股份有限公司（股份代號：06106） 發佈有關截至2026年6月30日止六個月之財務表現的正面盈利預告，並依據香港聯合交易所有限公司之披露規定作出本公告。 ... - 收入大幅增長： 預期於報告期內錄得未經審核收入至少為人民幣2.526億元，按年增長至少60%。 - 毛利大升： 預期毛利至少為人民幣1.183億元，按年增長至少65%。 ... - 淨虧損收窄： 預計錄得未經審核淨虧損不多於人民幣4,050萬元，按年減少至少20%。 - 經調整淨虧損大幅減少： 經調整淨虧損（未經審核）預期不多於人民幣1,320萬元，按年減少至少40%。 ... - 增長動力： 主因智能機器人及機器人大腦收入增長，以及海外收入爆發式增長所帶動。 - 營運效率提升： 營運效率提升及有效控制費用，有助帶動毛利上升及虧損收窄。 ... - 收入及毛利大幅增加，淨虧損及經調整淨虧損顯著收窄，反映公司復甦及增長勢頭強勁。 - 海外收入爆發式增長，顯示國際業務擴展卓有成效，未來有望帶來更多增長空間及收入多元化。 - 營運成本管理及效率改善初見成效，為未來轉虧為盈鋪路。 - 股東及投資者注意： 以上數據基於未經審核管理賬目，最終數字有待公佈中期業績時確認。預期2026年8月底前發佈正式中期業績公告。 ... - 由於本正面盈利預告屬價格敏感信息，或會對公司股價產生重大影響。 ... 有關截至2026年6月30日止六個月之詳細財務資料，將