SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Electric Bidet Seats Market to Reach USD 394.2 Million by 2032 (9.2% CAGR) – Big News,www.bignews.uk,2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bignews.uk/business/electric-bidet-seats-market-to-reach-usd-394-2-million-by-2032-9-2-cagr,"As PW Consulting’s Senior Strategic Advisor and Lead Industry Analyst, I present a focused preview of our latest market study on electric bidet seats. The market is entering a decisive growth phase: our base year is 2025, the forecast window runs from 2026–2032, and the industry is projected to expand at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 9.2% through the forecast period. By the end of the horizon the market is expected to approach the high hundreds of millions (USD), demonstrating clear runway for product innovation, channel expansion, and institutional adoption. This briefing highlights the strategic implications for corporations planning investments, partnerships, or go-to-market moves in 2026—while intentionally withholding granular segment tables to preserve the “preview” purpose and to encourage access to the full report for transaction‑level detail. Electric Bidet Seats Market ... Regulatory and reimbursement tailwinds: Recent policy moves—most notably Medicaid waiver programs increasingly recognizing electric bidet seats as durable medical equipment—create a runway into healthcare procurement channels (notably long‑term care and assisted living). Early institutional adopters report reductions in infection rates, driving evidence-based procurement decisions. Electric Bidet Seats Market ... Growth profile: The market posted steady expansion through the 2020–2025 period and is forecast to continue expanding at ~9.2% annually over 2026–2032. That pace implies meaningful scale opportunities for players that can execute on product differentiation, cost control, and distribution reach by 2026. ... Regulatory compliance and product positioning: GFCI outlet requirements and hygiene performance standards (e.g., UV/nozzle sterilization) are now market norms. Compliance is table stakes; differentiation will depend on user experience, integrated services (warranty, subscription maintenance), and demonstrable clinical outcomes for institutional buyers. ... TOTO Ltd. — With its flagship Washlet platform, TOTO continues to set feature benchmarks (instant heating, self‑cleaning nozzles, app control). For strategic planners, TOTO’s playbook emphasizes premium product engineering, global brand leverage, and deep channel partnerships—particularly in regions where its name carries strong consumer trust. ... Kohler Co. — The January 2026 launch of the PureWash E930 with dual-wand, app connectivity, and voice control underscores Kohler’s strategy to blend design-led premium positioning with smart-home integration. Expect Kohler to push through both retail and specification channels (high-end residential and boutique commercial projects). ... features and institutional-ready specs (e ... g., UV sterilization, robust sterilizable nozzles ... Bio Bidet appeals to buyers who prioritize infection-control outcomes ... footprint in institutional and residential segments makes ... credible partner for bundled ... Brondell Inc. — Recent distribution expansions indicate a channel-driven growth strategy. By broadening retailer availability and offering a range of Swash models, Brondell is pursuing volume growth through mainstream shelf presence and competitive product breadth. ... illustrate two viable ... : value-driven ... and D2 ... sustainability/pop-culture positioning ... Alpha Bidet’s ... New product introductions and refreshed model lineups (early 2026) indicate that incumbents are accelerating product roadmaps to capture share among smart-home consumers and commercial specifiers alike. ... Distribution expansions suggest retailers and online marketplaces see sufficient demand elasticity to justify broader assortments—this will intensify pricing competition but also help normalize install costs through bundled promotions with plumbing and renovation services. ... Policy/coverage updates that explicitly recognize bidet seats as necessary medical equipment for certain populations can catalyze institutional procurement contracts and third-party reimbursement pathways—an attractive growth lever for vendors that can demonstrate clinical evidence and compliance. ... impact assessments, with a prioritized checklist for product compliance and clinical evidence generation. ... Actionable M&A and partnership screening criteria for bolt-on acquisitions, OEM relationships, and white‑label opportunities. ... Prioritize platform modularity: Design product platforms that ... commercial, and clinical settings without wholesale re-engineering— ... common back‑ ... Invest in compliance and clinical evidence: Vendors that can demonstrate reduced infection rates, validated safety compliance (GFCI and sterilization standards), and cost-savings in care settings will unlock institutional contracts and reimbursement channels. ... Manage cost-to-serve aggressively: Material sourcing strategies, installation partnerships, and bundled service offers (installation + extended warranty) will be decisive in protecting margins as competition intensifies. ... Choose channel strategy by cohort: Premium brands should double down on specification channels and design partnerships; value brands should expand big-box and e-commerce presence; D2C players should prioritize subscription and recurring-revenue services for aftermarket filters/wash cycles. ... Explore partnerships with healthcare integrators and O&P providers: Integration into durable medical equipment catalogs and hospital procurement frameworks requires both product certification and care pathway alignment. ... Fragmented standards: Divergent regional safety and hygiene regulations could raise compliance costs for global players. ... The electric bidet seat market in 2026 represents a compelling blend of growth and strategic complexity. With a clear CAGR trajectory and visible institutional adoption pathways, firms that act now to align product architectures, compliance programs, and go-to-market channels will secure advantaged positions for the rest of the decade. Our study provides the operational playbooks, financial models, and competitive maps to inform M&A diligence, product roadmaps, and channel investments."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Shanghai Seer Intelligent's IPO Stabilization Period Ends | MarketScreener Hong Kong,hk.marketscreener.com (MT Newswires),2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hk.marketscreener.com/news/shanghai-seer-intelligent-s-ipo-stabilization-period-ends-ce7f51dade81f32d,"Stabilization Period Ends | Market ... creener Hong Kong ... | 07-24 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Expects to Narrow H1 Loss | MT | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-23 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. Provides Group Earnings Guidance for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2026 | CI | ... # Shanghai Seer Intelligent's IPO Stabilization Period Ends ... ### Latest news about Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. ... | 07-24 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Expects to Narrow H1 Loss | MT | | --- | --- | --- | | 07-23 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. Provides Group Earnings Guidance for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2026 | CI | | 07-20 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent's IPO Stabilization Period Ends | MT | | 06-24 | Hong Kong Stocks Rebound; Seer Intelligent Technology, Micot Pharma Shine on Debut | MT | | 06-24 | Seer Intelligent Technology Opens Flat in Hong Kong Debut | MT | | 06-24 | Seer Tech Nets HK$995 Million from Hong Kong IPO Ahead of Debut | MT | | 06-24 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. has completed an IPO in the amount of HKD 1.066526 billion. | CI | | 06-15 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. Reports Earnings Results for the Full Year Ended December 31, 2025 | CI | | 06-15 | Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. announced that it has received HKD 462 million in funding from ACCF Capital Management PTE.LTD, Zhuhai Hillhouse Equity Investment Management Co., Ltd., Yuanbao Family Office Limited and other investors | CI | | 05-28 | SEER Robotics Launches AI Delivery Robot P300 | CI | | 05-27 | SEER Robotics Officially Launches Embodied Wheeled Humanoid Robot Base C1-D | CI | | 05-18 | SEER Robotics Participates as Strategic Partner in Hong Kong Embodied Intelligence Initiative, Accelerating Commercialization of Research Innovation | CI | | 04-24 | SEER Robotics Debuts at FAIR Plus 2026, Driving Embodied Intelligence Evolution with Robot Brain | CI | ... Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co Ltd is a China-based company principally engaged in the intelligent robotics business. The Company's main businesses include research, development and sales of robots, controllers, software, and accessories, with robot control systems as its core business, enabling one-stop development, acquisition and use of intelligent robots across real-world scenarios. The Company's products are primarily used in industries such as computers, communications and consumer electronics (3C), automotive, automation equipment, new energy, semiconductors, construction machinery and biopharmaceuticals. The Company mainly operates its businesses in the domestic and overseas markets. ... Industrial Machinery & Equipment"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SEIIM Secures Investment from CNT Tech to Expand AI-Driven Industrial Safety Platform - WOWTALE,en.wowtale.net,2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.wowtale.net/2026/07/14/234465/,"SEIIM Secures Investment from CNT Tech to Expand AI-Driven Industrial Safety Platform - WOWTALE ... # SEIIM Secures Investment from CNT Tech to Expand AI-Driven Industrial Safety Platform ... SEIIM, a Korean AI SaaS company specializing in industrial safety, has secured an investment from CNT Tech. CNT Tech is supporting SEIIM’s business model development and investment readiness through its Smart Construction Startup Accelerating and Open Innovation program. ... Founded in 2021, SEIIM develops and operates safety management ERP software designed to help companies comply with Korea’s Serious Accidents Punishment Act, along with AI tools that generate safety documentation and training content. Its core offerings include the AI safety assistant SAFE BUDDY, the AI safety and health education system SAFE EDU, and an integrated safety dashboard for smart construction sites. ... SAFE BUDDY digitizes and standardizes routine safety management tasks — including risk assessments, safety budget management, safety inspections, safety education, meeting minutes, e-signatures, worker safety proposals, and semiannual compliance checks — and supplies more than 60 mandatory safety document templates tailored to different industries and company sizes, kept current with the latest regulations. The platform runs on a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) system trained on industrial safety laws, manuals, and client-specific guidelines, letting its AI assistant automatically draft and recommend safety documents based on each client’s on-site conditions. ... SEIIM counts Hyundai Engineering & Construction, DL E&C, RSquare Design, Shinil, the Korea Institute of Water Resources Survey and Technology, and CHM among its clients, giving it early traction in construction and manufacturing site management, safety upkeep for large buildings, and public-sector safety management. Its multiyear collaboration with Hyundai Engineering & Construction — built around proof-of-concept testing and field validation — has been cited as a model case of cooperation between a large corporation and a startup. ... In 2025, SEIIM earned Grade 1 GS certification for SAFE BUDDY, won top honors at the 2025 Smart Construction EXPO startup competition, and received a commendation from the Korea Construction Safety Society presented by a member of the National Assembly. In 2026, the company was selected for the K-StartHub (SVC) resident program and for the Seoul-region R&D track of the Steppingstone Startup Growth Technology Development Program, as it continues to refine its products and expand into new markets. ... With the new investment, SEIIM plans to expand on-site adoption of SAFE BUDDY and SAFE EDU and enhance features such as automated AI document drafting. The company hopes its solutions will help small and midsize workplaces in Korea and abroad build smart safety management systems, freeing safety and health officers from office paperwork so they can spend more time ensuring proper on-site safety management. ... Hwasung Jeon, CEO of CNT Tech, said SEIIM is a team with the execution capability to connect safety documentation, training, inspections, e-signatures, and evidence management into a single AI-powered workflow. He added that the company has significant potential to meaningfully improve safety management in high-risk sectors such as construction, manufacturing, and facilities management, well beyond mere compliance with the Serious Accidents Punishment Act."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Serstech receives 12.6 MSEK order from South Korea,www.globenewswire.com (SERSTECH AB),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/13/3326041/0/en/Serstech-receives-12-6-MSEK-order-from-South-Korea.html,"Serstech receives 12.6 MSEK order from South Korea ... # Serstech receives 12.6 MSEK order from South Korea ... 2026 06:45 ET | Source: Serstech Follow Serstech ... Serstech has today received an order from its South Korean partner Young Jin Solutec Co. Ltd with a total value of 12.6 MSEK. The order consists of instruments and software and will be delivered and invoiced during the third quarter of 2026. ... This is information that Serstech AB (publ.) is obliged to make public pursuant to the EU Market Abuse Regulation. The information was submitted for publication, through the agency of the contact person set ... above at ... 2:45 CET on July 13, ... 026. ... Serstech delivers solutions for chemical identification and has customers around the world, mainly in the safety and security industry. Typical customers are customs, police authorities, security organizations and first responders. The solutions and technology are however not limited to security applications and potentially any industry using chemicals of some kind could be addressed by Serstech’s solution. Serstech’s head office is in Sweden and all production is done in Sweden. ... Serstech is traded at Nasdaq First North Growth Market and more information about the company can be found at www.serstech.com ... Company ProfileSerstechIndustry: SoftwareWebsite: ... July 15, 2026 02:45 ET | Source: Serstech ... Second Quarter Report 2026 ... SERSTECH GROUP, 1 APRIL – 30 JUNE 2026 Net sales amounted to KSEK 9 658 (4 563)EBITDA amounted to KSEK -2 426 (-9 041)EBIT amounted to KSEK -5 275 (-11 158)Cash flow from operating activities... ... April 28, 2026 09:15 ET | Source: Serstech ... Kommuniké från årsstämma i Serstech AB (publ) ... Idag, tisdagen den 28 april 2026, hölls årsstämma i Serstech AB (publ). Följande huvudsakliga beslut fattades. Stämman beslutade att fastställa resultat- och balansräkningen samt koncernresultat- och..."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"CloudSEK, Tech Mahindra Deliver Regulation-Ready Cybersecurity",www.techmahindra.com,2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.techmahindra.com/insights/press-releases/cloudsek-techm-announce-partnership-enable-predictive-regulation-ready/,"# CloudSEK and Tech Mahindra Announce Partnership to Enable Predictive, Regulation-Ready Cybersecurity at Scale ... CloudSEK, an AI-native predictive cyber intelligence company, today announced a partnership with Tech Mahindra(NSE: TECHM), a leading global provider of technology consulting and digital solutions to enterprises across industries. ... The partnership will deliver AI-driven threat intelligence, attack surface monitoring, AI attack surface monitoring, and digital risk protection solutions globally. ... Evolving cybersecurity regulations are driving enterprises to strengthen risk visibility, accelerate incident response, and enhance compliance readiness. Frameworks such as NIS2 and DORA in Europe, CERT-In mandates, CIRCIA and SEC cyber-disclosure rules in the US, DPDP Act in India, and similar regulatory and national cybersecurity initiatives across the Middle East are increasing expectations around continuous monitoring, third-party risk oversight, and timely breach detection and reporting. ... By combining CloudSEK’s AI-native predictive cyber intelligence platform with Tech Mahindra’s global cybersecurity services capabilities, the partnership offers a faster and more operationally scalable approach to regulatory compliance. CloudSEK’s ability to continuously monitor external and AI-driven attack surfaces, correlate threats, and identify real attack paths enables early risk detection and prioritization. Integrated with Tech Mahindra’s advisory, implementation, and managed security services, this enables enterprises to accelerate compliance execution, reduce response timelines, and operationalize regulatory requirements more efficiently across complex and dynamic digital environments. ... “This partnership strengthens our global expansion by bringing our AI-native predictive cyber intelligence platform to a much wider enterprise base. Organizations today are not struggling with a lack of alerts; they are struggling to understand how attackers will actually get in. With Tech Mahindra, we can deliver this capability at a global scale,” said Rahul Sasi, Co-founder and CEO, CloudSEK. ... Saket Singh, Business Head, Cloud, Infrastructure, Network & Security Services, Tech Mahindra, said, ""Enterprises can no longer rely on reactive security models in the face of accelerating cyber risks and tightening regulatory mandates. Our partnership with CloudSEK reflects a deliberate strategy to bring best-in-class, AI-native predictive cyber intelligence into our cybersecurity portfolio. CloudSEK’s strong market validation and its backing from a globally established investment ecosystem further reinforce its credibility as a trusted and innovative cybersecurity provider. Combined with Tech Mahindra’s global consulting, integration, and managed services strengths, this partnership enables us to deliver faster, more precise, and operationally scalable security outcomes for enterprises globally.” ... The partnership is focused on enabling telco and large enterprise customers across India, the Middle East, and Europe to respond to rapidly tightening cybersecurity regulations that demand immediate action. By combining CloudSEK’s AI-driven predictive threat intelligence with Tech Mahindra’s global delivery and managed security capabilities, the collaboration provides a scalable, real-time solution to help enterprises act now reducing compliance risk, improving response speed, and strengthening resilience across critical digital infrastructures. ... Tech Mahindra (NSE: TECHM) offers technology consulting and digital solutions to global enterprises across industries, enabling transformative scale at unparalleled speed. With 147,000+ professionals across 90+ countries helping 1100+ clients, Tech Mahindra provides a full spectrum of services including consulting, information technology, enterprise applications, business process services, engineering services, network services, customer experience & design, AI & analytics, and cloud & infrastructure services. It is the first Indian company in the world to have been awarded the Sustainable Markets Initiative’s Terra Carta Seal, which recognizes global companies that are actively leading the charge to create a climate and nature-positive future. Tech Mahindra is part of the Mahindra Group, founded in 1945, one of the largest and most admired multinational federation of companies."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"TechSee Launches Value Meter, Giving Enterprises a Real-Time View of AI Business Impact",www.prnewswire.com (TechSee),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/techsee-launches-value-meter-giving-enterprises-a-real-time-view-of-ai-business-impact-302820639.html,"TechSee Launches Value Meter, Giving Enterprises a Real-Time View of AI Business Impact Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... NEW YORK, July 8, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- TechSee, the leader in Visual AI for customer service, today announced the launch of Value Meter, a strategic analytics dashboard that turns raw service operations data into a real-time, executive-ready view of business impact. Value Meter addresses one of the most pressing challenges in enterprise AI today: organizations are investing heavily in AI but cannot attribute investment to economic impact. ... 83% of organizations do not track investment versus benefit for their AI tools, while 42% of companies have scrapped most of their AI initiatives for lack of returns. Most organizations still measure AI adoption instead of AI outcomes - and this gap leads to underperforming AI investments. Dashboards report users, sessions, and licenses, but executives need to understand business impact: fewer truck rolls, faster resolution, lower costs, higher customer satisfaction, and stronger retention. ... Value Meter closes that gap. It aggregates impact across TechSee's full product footprint, including Sophie Live, Sophie Assist and Connectivity Guru, into one account-level view, and it measures the outcomes that matter to the business rather than activity counts. Every metric tells a four-layer story: the absolute value, the trend versus the previous period, a benchmark against industry peers, and the potential still on the table if the account reached top-quartile efficiency. That final layer reframes the conversation from what a customer has saved to what they could still capture.""TechSee was built on a simple belief: you can't fix what you can't see,"" said Eitan Cohen, CEO of TechSee. ""We first applied that principle to customer service by making issues inside the home visible. With Value Meter, we're applying the same idea to AI itself. For the first time, organizations can see, in real time, the business impact their AI investments are creating. This is crucial for organizations looking to accelerate their AI investments where they matter most."" ... The outcomes Value Meter surfaces are drawn from results TechSee already delivers in the field, including self-service and self-install containment of 80 to 90% across telecom deployments, first-dispatch failure rates falling from 25 to 40% into the single digits, and truck-roll reductions of up to 75%. These results are no longer assembled by hand for a periodic review, but they are visible on demand, to every stakeholder from contact center manager to CXO. ... About TechSee TechSee is the leading Visual AI-powered platform harnessing vision to transform customer service. By enabling businesses to see the problem and solve it effectively, TechSee eliminates friction, reduces costs, and enhances customer satisfaction. Trusted by Fortune 500 companies and industry leaders in telecom, home security, and smart home, our platform delivers seamless, intelligent service experiences at scale. For more information, visit: www.techsee.com. ... ### MEO and TechSee Win ""Technology of the Year"" at 2026 Excellence in Customer Service Awards for Visual AI Innovation ... MEO, part of the Altice Group and one of Portugal's leading telecommunications providers and TechSee, have been named the Overall Winner in the... ... ### TechSee Named to Fast Company's Annual List of the World's Most Innovative Companies of 2026 ... TechSee is proud to have been named to Fast Company's prestigious list of the World's Most Innovative Companies of 2026. This year's list highlights..."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SeeTrue's AI Screening Automation Software Achieves TSA Certification and is installed for 2026 FIFA World Cup Security Operations,www.prnewswire.com (SeeTrue),2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/seetrues-ai-screening-automation-software-achieves-tsa-certification-and-is-installed-for-2026-fifa-world-cup-security-operations-302819232.html,"is installed for 2 ... 6 FIFA World Cup Security Operations Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... NEW YORK, July 7, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- SeeTrue AI, a global leader in AI-powered security screening, today announced two major milestones: its prohibited item detection software is the first AI solution to receive TSA Certification for use with the Analogic ConneCT computed tomography (CT) scanner, and SeeTrue's AI screening software is now installed at multiple U.S. airports serving 2026 FIFA World Cup host cities. ... TSA Certification for Prohibited Items DetectionSeeTrue's prohibited item detection software meets the rigorous requirements of the Transportation Security Administration 's detection standard. SeeTrue's software integrates directly with existing CT carry-on screening systems at an airport, automatically detecting prohibited items and presenting results to the scanner's operator interface. The solution allows for rapid integration and operational readiness within hours, accelerating checkpoint throughput without adding staffing burden a critical capability during sustained peak passenger volumes. ... This certification adds to SeeTrue's existing ECAC APIDS Approval for both the Analogic ConneCT and Rapiscan 920CT platforms, giving SeeTrue the broadest regulatory coverage across U.S. and European aviation environments. ... Installation for 2026 FIFA World CupSeeTrue's AI-powered screening software was first installed at TSA PreCheck© lanes at Indianapolis International Airport during the Indianapolis 500 and the installation was expanded to several TSA PreCheck© lanes at additional airports for FIFA World Cup host cities ahead of the tournament's June 11 kickoff. ... Industry Leadership and Commitment""We are proud to meet the TSA Certification standard and to support U.S. airports with a certified, production-grade AI detection solution,"" said Assaf Frenkel, Co-Founder and CEO of SeeTrue. ""The World Cup brings an extraordinary security challenge: millions of passengers, multiple cities, and sustained peak demand. Our prohibited item detection technology is built precisely for these environments, high volume, time-critical, zero margin for error."" ... About SeeTrueSeeTrue is an Artificial Intelligence (AI) software company and a global leader in prohibited items and threat detection technology, delivering secure, fast, and efficient security screening. SeeTrue's AI solutions integrate seamlessly with X-ray and CT scanners across airports, seaports, urban security checkpoints, customs, and shipment facilities worldwide, improving throughput and operational efficiency. SeeTrue's automated screening software is TSA Certified and ECAC APIDS Approved, enabling regulation-approved detection for advanced aviation security operations. SeeTrue operates from New York, Tel Aviv, London, and Amsterdam. For more information, visit www.seetrue.ai. ... ### SeeTrue AI screening solution becomes the first and only to receive ECAC certification for Automated Prohibited Items Detection (APIDS) ... SeeTrue AI, a global leader in AI-powered security screening, is proud to announce that its SeeTrue Automated Prohibited Items Detection Software..."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Seer Files Investor Presentation Highlighting Strong Momentum, Commercial Opportunity and Significant Long-Term Value Creation Potential | INN",investingnews.com,2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://investingnews.com/seer-files-investor-presentation-highlighting-strong-momentum-commercial-opportunity-and-significant-long-term-value-creation-potential/,"Presentation Highlighting Strong ... # Seer Files Investor Presentation Highlighting Strong Momentum, Commercial Opportunity and Significant Long-Term Value Creation Potential ... July 06, 2026 ... Seer is Delivering Clear Progress Against its Strategic Plan and Maintaining Focus on Cost Discipline, Governance Rigor and Product Innovation ... Highly Qualified, Independent and Accountable Board Has Taken Decisive Action to Advance Stockholders' Best Interests ... SEER, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER) ("" SEER"" or the ""Company"") today filed an investor presentation with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission in connection with its upcoming Annual Meeting of Stockholders (the ""Annual Meeting"") to be held on July 28, 2026. Stockholders as of May 29, 2026 will be entitled to vote at the Annual Meeting. ... Seer has pioneered a new market for deep, unbiased proteomics and is now uniquely positioned to power the next era of AI-driven precision medicine. ... - Category-leading technology capable of delivering significantly more data to train foundation models and reveal deeper insights than other proteomic platforms - Landmark population-scale studies and strategic collaborations are already underway, marking an acceleration point in Seer's commercial opportunity - Robust innovation pipeline, including next-generation detector, has potential to meaningfully expand the end market for proteomics beyond mass spectrometry users - Substantial and fast-growing proteomics market could reach $23 billion total addressable market opportunity by 20341 ... Seer is delivering demonstrable progress against the goals outlined at its IPO despite a sector-wide downturn, and the Company's commercial inflection point is now approaching. ... - Focus on cost discipline has led to meaningful reductions in SG&A and R&D expenses each year since 2023 and 36% decrease in annual cash burn2 since 2022 - Installed base has grown at a 62% CAGR since 2021,3 supported by partnerships with every major mass spectrometry platform - Cumulative publications doubled over the last year for a total of 84 peer-reviewed publications since 2022,4 underscoring scientific community's confidence in the platform - Product launches since 2021 have already increased platform throughput by ~10x, with additional launches on the horizon - With over 235 patent applications and issued patents, Seer is the leader in the category it created, and as industry validation continues to grow, the Company is ready to scale ... Seer's highly qualified, independent Board is actively engaged and accountable to advancing stockholders' best interests. ... Board has a clear track record of returning capital and protecting stockholder interests, including: ... - Authorizing $50 million in total share repurchases, with $25.5 million remaining in the program;7 - Overseeing ~75% decrease in stock-based compensation since 2023 to annualized run rate of $8.5M in 2026; - Maintaining cash position of ~$220 million with no debt, providing ample runway to fund platform commercialization; and - Adopting a tax benefit preservation plan to ensure $262.4 million of federal net operating loss carryforwards remain available to benefit stockholders long term8 ... Bradley Radoff and Michael Torok are running a self-interested campaign to force an early sale of the Company and strip it of its own cash. ... - Campaign lacks actionable ideas for value creation - Radoff and Torok lack credibility as potential buyers, providing no evidence of committed financing or indicating any desire to put their own capital at risk - The Board carefully reviewed, discussed and unanimously rejected all of Radoff and Torok's proposals in consultation with its independent financial and legal advisors ... Radoff and Torok are seeking to replace highly qualified members of Seer's Board with nominees who bring no relevant expertise or experience. ... - Proposed nominees bring no proteomics, life sciences instrumentation or operating expertise – only M&A experience - Long-standing ties to Radoff raise concerns about independence - Radoff and Torok declined to make nominees available for interviews, despite offers from the Board - Replacing existing directors with proposed nominees would remove invaluable expertise from Seer's boardroom at a critical time in the Company's growth trajectory ... The Board unanimously recommends that stockholders vote today using the BLUE proxy card ""FOR"" the election of each of Seer's seven highly qualified director nominees: Omid Farokhzad, M.D., Meeta Gulyani, Robert Langer, Sc.D., Terrance McGuire, Dipchand (Deep) Nishar, Isaac Ro and Nicolas Roelofs, Ph.D. ... SEER, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER) sets the standard in deep, unbiased proteomics, delivering insights with a scale, speed, precision and reproducibility previously unattainable. SEER's Proteograph® Product Suite integrates proprietary engineered nanoparticles, streamlined automation instrumentation, optimized consumables and advanced analytical software to overcome the limitations of traditional proteomic methods. Seer's products are for research use only and are not intended for diagnostic procedures. For more information, visit www.seer.bio. ... time to time. ... statements to reflect events ... the date on which they were made."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seer Shares Jump 30% After Investor Presentation Highlights Growth and Cost Cuts,tradevae.com,2026-07-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://tradevae.com/news/stock-markets/seer-shares-jump-30-after-investor-presentation-highlights-growth-and-cost-cuts/,"Seer Shares Jump 30% After Investor Presentation Highlights Growth and Cost Cuts ... Seer, Inc. (NASDAQ:SEER) saw its stock surge 30% on Monday after filing an investor presentation with the SEC that outlined commercial progress, market opportunity, and recent cost reductions. The filing, made ahead of the company's July 28, 2026 annual meeting, also came amid an active proxy contest. ... - Seer filed an investor presentation with the SEC ahead of its July 28, 2026 Annual Meeting; stockholders of record on May 29, 2026 are eligible to vote. - The company projects a $23 billion proteomics total addressable market by 2034 and reported a 62% CAGR in its installed base since 2021, supported by partnerships with major mass spectrometry platforms. ... - Seer highlighted cost discipline - a 36% reduction in annual cash burn since 2022, year-over-year cuts in SG&A and R&D since 2023, roughly $220 million in cash with no debt, and $25.5 million remaining of a $50 million share repurchase authorization. ... Quick summary - Seer, the Redwood City, California-based proteomics company, reported a set of commercial and financial updates in an investor presentation filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. The filing, timed ahead of Seer’s Annual Meeting of Stockholders scheduled for July 28, 2026, triggered a 30% rise in the company’s share price on Monday. ... The presentation, which applies to stockholders of record as of May 29, 2026 who will be eligible to vote at the meeting, summarized Seer’s view of the commercial opportunity and recent operational performance. In it, the company reiterated its projection that the proteomics market could become a $23 billion total addressable market by 2034, and it highlighted customer traction in its installed base. ... Seer reported that its installed base has expanded at a 62% compound annual growth rate since 2021. The company attributed that expansion in part to partnerships with major mass spectrometry platforms that support its commercial footprint. ... Financial and operational discipline were also focal points of the presentation. Seer said it has cut annual cash burn by 36% since 2022 and has achieved meaningful year-over-year reductions in selling, general and administrative expenses and research and development spending each year since 2023. The company noted that cumulative peer-reviewed publications referencing its work doubled over the last year, totaling 84 since 2022. ... On the balance sheet, Seer reported approximately $220 million in cash and stated it carries no debt. The board has approved up to $50 million in share repurchases under a buyback program, with $25.5 million still available under that authorization. ... Stock-based compensation has been reduced substantially, with the company reporting an approximate 75% decline since 2023. Seer said stock-based compensation had been reduced to an annualized run rate of $8.5 million in 2026. ... The timing of the presentation coincides with an ongoing proxy contest. Seer’s board urged stockholders to support its slate of seven director nominees by voting on the company’s blue proxy card. The board also stated that it has rejected proposals put forward by Bradley Radoff and Michael Torok, who are attempting to replace members of the board. ... Investors will consider the presentation and governance developments ahead of the July 28 meeting. The company’s statements and the outstanding proxy challenge were both presented in the SEC filing made public in advance of the vote. ... - Ongoing proxy contest that could create governance uncertainty - the board is urging votes for its seven nominees and has rejected proposals from Bradley Radoff and Michael Torok. - Only $25.5 million remains available under the $50 million share repurchase authorization, which limits further buyback activity under the current program. - Market projections such as the company’s $23 billion proteomics total addressable market by 2034 are forward-looking and form a basis for investment decisions presented in the filing."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI,www.brazilbusinessinsights.com,2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.brazilbusinessinsights.com/news/moomoo-engine-launch-futu-xp-nubank-brazil,"Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil · BBI ... # Exclusive: Moomoo to Launch Unified 'Moomoo Engine' Toolkit in Brazil ... Moomoo is launching 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified trading toolkit designed to capture active retail and professional traders in Brazil, challenging incumbents. ... - ▸ Global user base: Over 22 million users - ▸ Launch date: July 2, 2026 - ▸ Target market: Active retail & pro traders - ▸ Primary region: Brazil expansion ... The Bottom Line: - Moomoo, the digital brokerage subsidiary of Futu Holdings ($FUTU), is set to launch 'Moomoo Engine,' a unified suite of advanced trading tools designed to consolidate market analysis, charting, and execution. - The rollout represents a strategic push to capture high-value retail and professional traders in emerging markets, particularly Brazil, where digital brokerage competition is intensifying. - While the launch enhances $FUTU's technological moat, it poses direct competitive pressure on local incumbents such as XP Inc. ($XP) and Nubank ($NU). Strategic Expansion in Latin America: Futu Holdings ($FUTU), through its international trading platform Moomoo, is accelerating its expansion into Latin America with the exclusive announcement of 'Moomoo Engine.' This unified toolkit is designed to streamline the trading lifecycle for retail and professional investors. By integrating advanced charting, real-time data analytics, and algorithmic execution into a single, cohesive interface, Moomoo aims to address the fragmentation that has historically plagued active traders in emerging markets. The Brazilian market, characterized by a highly sophisticated retail investor base and a rapidly growing interest in global equities, serves as the primary launchpad for this technological deployment. Technological Disruption and the 'Moomoo Engine': The 'Moomoo Engine' represents a significant upgrade to the platform's existing infrastructure. Historically, active traders in Brazil have had to rely on multiple third-party platforms for technical analysis, order routing, and portfolio tracking. This fragmentation often leads to latency issues, higher subscription costs, and execution inefficiencies. Moomoo's unified toolkit addresses these pain points by offering proprietary, low-latency charting algorithms and institutional-grade data feeds directly within the trading application. This integration is expected to lower the barrier to entry for advanced trading strategies, enabling retail investors to execute complex multi-leg options strategies and automated technical trades with greater precision. Competitive Dynamics in the Brazilian Brokerage Sector: The introduction of the 'Moomoo Engine' comes at a time of intense competition within the Brazilian financial services sector. Incumbents like XP Inc. ($XP) and BTG Pactual have traditionally dominated the affluent and active trader segments through extensive advisory networks and proprietary platforms. Concurrently, digital-first platforms like Nubank ($NU) and Inter have successfully democratized access to basic investment products for the mass market. Moomoo's strategy bypasses the traditional advisory model, focusing instead on self-directed, tech-savvy traders who prioritize execution speed, analytical depth, and low transaction costs. By offering institutional-grade tools without the premium price tag, Moomoo is positioning itself to capture market share from both high-end incumbents and mass-market digital banks looking to upsell their user bases. Regulatory and Operational Considerations: Operating a foreign-backed digital brokerage in Brazil requires navigating a complex regulatory framework overseen by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Brazil (CVM) and the Central Bank of Brazil (BCB). Moomoo's expansion strategy relies heavily on seamless integration with local clearing systems and compliance with strict foreign exchange (FX) regulations. For Brazilian investors trading international assets, tax compliance—specifically the calculation of capital gains and the monthly 'Carnê-Leão' tax filing—has historically been a major friction point. To gain widespread adoption, the 'Moomoo Engine' must integrate localized tax reporting tools that simplify these compliance obligations for domestic users. Furthermore, fluctuations in the USD/BRL exchange rate remain a critical variable, as currency volatility can significantly impact the net returns of Brazilian investors trading on US exchanges through the platform. Implications for Futu Holdings ($FUTU): For Futu Holdings ($FUTU), the successful rollout of the 'Moomoo Engine' in Brazil is vital for its broader international diversification strategy. Facing mature markets and regulatory headwinds in mainland China and Hong Kong, Futu has increasingly looked to Southeast Asia and Latin America to drive its next phase of growth. Brazil represents one of the largest retail investment markets in the developing world, making it a high-stakes testing ground for Moomoo's global scalability. If the 'Moomoo Engine' succeeds in capturing a meaningful share of Brazil's active trading volume, it could serve as a blueprint for further expansion into other Latin American markets, such as Mexico and Colombia, thereby bolstering Futu's long-term revenue growth and reducing its geographic concentration risk. ... Market Impact: The launch of the 'Moomoo Engine' has distinct implications for the key players in the digital brokerage space: - Futu Holdings ($FUTU): Bullish. The successful deployment of advanced trading tools in Brazil accelerates Futu's international diversification, reducing its reliance on Asian markets and opening a high-margin revenue stream from active Latin American traders. - XP Inc. ($XP): Bearish. XP faces direct technological competition in its high-value active trader segment. While its advisory network remains a strong moat, Moomoo's low-cost, high-tech offering could pressure XP's commission margins and active client retention. - Nu Holdings ($NU): Neutral. Nubank's primary investment audience consists of mass-market retail investors rather than sophisticated active traders. However, as Nubank seeks to upsell its client base into more complex financial products, Moomoo's advanced platform represents a long-term competitive hurdle. ... > analyst consensus: Bullish on Futu Holdings ($FUTU) international expansion; bearish on XP Inc. ($XP) active trader retention; neutral on Nu Holdings ($NU). > asset_class: Equities"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seer wins EPO patent ruling and secures ITC probe into Nanomics | The Biotech Times,biotech.disruptsmedia.com,2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://biotech.disruptsmedia.com/proteomics/seer-wins-epo-patent-ruling-and-secures-itc-probe-nanomics,"Seer wins EPO patent ruling and secures ITC probe into Nanomics | The Biotech Times ... Seer, Inc. has secured two intellectual property victories within days of each other, strengthening its legal grip on the nanoparticle-based protein enrichment technology that underpins its Proteograph Product Suite. ... On 25 June 2026, the European Patent Office concluded proceedings on EP4056263, an opposition lodged by an unnamed party that sought to revoke the patent entirely. The EPO ruled that the patent will be maintained, preserving claims broadly covering particle-based enrichment for proteomics applications. A written decision is expected within approximately two months. The patent is owned by The Brigham and Women's Hospital, which holds it under an exclusive licence arrangement with Seer. ... Four days later, on 29 June, the US International Trade Commission formally instituted an investigation into Nanomics Biotechnology Co., Ltd., a move that followed a complaint Seer originally filed on 28 May 2026 and supplemented on 12 June. The ITC proceeded despite Nanomics having requested on 10 June that the Commission decline to open the case. Seer is seeking a limited exclusion order that would bar the import and sale of Nanomics' Proteonano kits and workstations in the United States. Brigham and Women's Hospital has joined the ITC action as co-complainant. ... The ITC investigation runs in parallel with a federal district court patent infringement suit Seer filed against Nanomics on 12 May 2026. ... Omid Farokhzad, chair and chief executive of Seer, said the outcomes send a clear signal. ""We pioneered this field and built the foundational intellectual property that underpins it,"" he said. ""These actions underscore the strength of our IP portfolio and make clear that we will vigorously defend our innovations and protect the technology our customers depend on."" ... The two rulings follow an earlier win for Seer in March 2026, when the US Patent Trial and Appeal Board issued a final written decision in an inter partes review upholding key claims of US Patent No. 11,435,360. Across its full estate, Seer holds more than 250 patent applications and issued patents, including 84 granted patents worldwide, a substantial portion of which protect the Proteograph platform. ... The proteomics instrumentation market has grown markedly more competitive as the field moves from niche academic research tool toward large-scale clinical and translational studies. Seer's Proteograph approach, which uses engineered nanoparticles to enrich low-abundance proteins and dramatically expand the detectable proteome, competes with mass spectrometry-centric workflows from established players as well as a growing number of newer entrants developing their own sample-preparation technologies. ... IP position is consequently becoming a differentiating factor in the sector, not merely a defensive exercise. Investors in proteomics platforms have increasingly scrutinised patent estates since several high-profile disputes in adjacent omics fields demonstrated that foundational technology patents can shape commercial access to entire market segments. The ITC route, which Seer is pursuing alongside the federal court case, is notable because an exclusion order, if granted, operates at the border and can be more immediately disruptive to a competitor's commercial operations than a district court injunction alone. ... The next milestones to watch are the EPO's written decision in roughly two months, the early procedural schedule in the ITC investigation, and any development in the parallel federal case. Investors will also look for Seer to disclose whether additional parties are in its sights or whether the current actions against Nanomics represent the full scope of its enforcement programme."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seer Prevails in European Patent Opposition as U.S. ITC,"www.globenewswire.com (Seer, Inc.)",2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/01/3320503/0/en/Seer-Prevails-in-European-Patent-Opposition-as-U-S-ITC-Opens-Investigation-into-Nanomics.html,"Prevails in European Patent ... # Seer Prevails in European Patent Opposition as U.S. ITC Opens Investigation into Nanomics ... IP withstands challenges in both ... REDWOOD CITY, Calif., July 01, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Seer, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER), a pioneer and trusted partner for deep, unbiased proteomic insights, today announced two significant developments that reinforce the strength of the intellectual property portfolio protecting its proprietary nanoparticle protein enrichment technology. These milestones underscore Seer's leadership in proteomics, validate the innovation behind its differentiated platform, and reflect the company's continued commitment to protecting the technologies that are advancing the future of proteomics. On June 25, 2026, the European Patent Office (EPO) concluded that European Patent No. EP4056263 will be maintained on the basis of claims covering particle-based enrichment for proteomics, and on June 29, 2026, the U.S. International Trade Commission (ITC) instituted an investigation into the importation by Nanomics Biotechnology Co., Ltd. of products that Seer alleges infringe five of its U.S. patents. ... The EPO outcome followed an opposition that sought revocation of EP4056263 by an unnamed opponent. After the proceedings, the EPO determined that the patent would be maintained, with claims broadly covering the particle-based approach at the core of Seer's proteomics technology. A written decision is expected in approximately two months. EP4056263 is owned by The Brigham and Women's Hospital and exclusively licensed to Seer. ... The ITC investigation stems from a complaint Seer filed on May 28, 2026, supplemented on June 12, 2026, and parallels a patent infringement suit Seer filed in U.S. federal district court on May 12, 2026. The Commission instituted the investigation notwithstanding Nanomics' June 10, 2026, request that it decline to do so. The investigation concerns Nanomics' Proteonano kits and workstations, and Seer is seeking a limited exclusion order to bar the importation and sale of those products in the United States. The Brigham and Women's Hospital has joined the ITC action as a co-complainant. ... These decisions add to a growing record of validation for Seer's patent estate. On March 23, 2026, the U.S. Patent Trial and Appeal Board issued a Final Written Decision in an inter partes review upholding key claims of U.S. Patent No 11.435,360. Seer holds a portfolio of more than 250 patent applications and issued patents, including 84 issued patents worldwide, a substantial portion of which protect the IP integral to Seer's Proteograph® Product Suite. ... “We pioneered this field and built the foundational intellectual property that underpins it. The European Patent Office has upheld a key patent covering our particle-based enrichment technology, and the U.S. International Trade Commission has instituted an investigation into Nanomics despite the company’s opposition,” said Omid Farokhzad, Chair and Chief Executive Officer of Seer. “These actions underscore the strength of our IP portfolio and make clear that we will vigorously defend our innovations and protect the technology our customers depend on.” ... Seer, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER) sets the standard in deep, unbiased proteomics, delivering insights with scale, speed, precision, and reproducibility previously unattainable. Seer’s Proteograph ® Product Suite integrates proprietary engineered nanoparticles, streamlined automation instrumentation, optimized consumables, and advanced analytical software to overcome the throughput and complexity limitations of traditional proteomic methods. Seer’s products are for research use only and are not intended for diagnostic procedures. For more information, visit www.seer.bio. ... August 03, 2026 16:15 ET | Source: Seer, Inc. ... Seer to Participate in the Canaccord Genuity 46th Annual Growth Conference ... REDWOOD CITY, Calif., Aug. 03, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Seer, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER), the pioneer and trusted partner for deep, unbiased proteomic insights, today announced that the company will be... ... August 03, 2026 16:05 ET | Source: Seer, Inc. ... Seer to Report Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results on August 11, 2026 ... REDWOOD CITY, Calif., Aug. 03, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Seer, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER), the pioneer and trusted partner for deep, unbiased proteomic insights, today announced that it will report..."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"DLA Piper advises on HKD1.067 billion Hong Kong IPO and H share listing of Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd.",legaldesire.com (Cynthia Lydia Marbaniang),2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://legaldesire.com/dla-piper-advises-on-hkd1-067-billion-hong-kong-ipo-and-h-share-listing-of-shanghai-seer-intelligent-technology-co-ltd/,"DLA Piper advises on HKD1.067 billion Hong Kong IPO and H share listing of Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. ... # DLA Piper advises on HKD1.067 billion Hong Kong IPO and H share listing of Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. ... Global law firm DLA Piper advised the sole sponsor, China International Capital Corporation Hong Kong Securities Limited, on the IPO and Hong Kong listing of Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. (上海仙工智能科技股份有限公司) (Stock Code: 06106) on the Main Board of The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited. ... The company’s H shares commenced trading on 24 June 2026, and the IPO was conducted under Chapter 18C, the specialist technology company regime. ... Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. (SEER Robotics) is an intelligent robotics company based on robotic control systems. Built on SEER Robotics’ industry-leading position and technology in what SEER calls the “robot brain” – the robotic control system – the Company is the world’s first open platform for intelligent robots, connecting supply chain resources and enabling one-stop development, acquisition and use of intelligent robots at scale across real-world scenarios, according to China International Capital Corporation (CIC). The Company ranked first globally in terms of robotic controller sales volume in both 2023, 2024 and 2025, according to the same source. ... The offering raised total gross proceeds of approximately HKD1.067 billion (approximately USD136 million). The proceeds will be used to support ongoing research and development, enhance the company’s product portfolio and technological capabilities, and accelerate commercialisation and market expansion in both domestic and international markets. ... George Wu commented: “This transaction highlights continued investor confidence in high-growth robotics and advanced manufacturing businesses, and reinforces Hong Kong’s position as a leading international capital markets hub for innovative companies.”"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seerist launches rebuilt risk intelligence platform with automation focus | Noah Intelligence,noah-news.com,2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://noah-news.com/seerist-launches-rebuilt-risk-intelligence-platform-with-automation-focus/,"Seerist launches rebuilt risk intelligence platform with automation focus | Noah Intelligence ... # Seerist launches rebuilt risk intelligence platform with automation focus ... Seerist has unveiled a major overhaul of its risk intelligence platform, enhancing signal integration, natural-language search, and automation prospects, positioning itself for broader enterprise and government... ... Seerist has unveiled a major overhaul of its risk intelligence platform, enhancing signal integration, natural-language search, and automation prospects, positioning itself for broader enterprise and government use. ... Seerist has unveiled what it describes as a rebuilt version of its intelligence platform, saying the overhaul is intended to make it easier for users to find, analyse and act on risk information while also laying groundwork for more automated features in future. The company said the changes reflect a long-term effort to adapt the product to how intelligence teams work, rather than simply adding surface-level functions. ... At the centre of the update is a set of changes Seerist says will bring together a wider range of signals in one place, including strategic analysis, tactical developments, AI-based event detection, human-verified alerts and analytics. The firm said the redesigned system also adds more natural-language search, more advanced query tools and faster report creation, while aiming to reduce the friction that can come from moving between different parts of a workflow. ... Seerist has also been positioning itself more broadly as an intelligence provider for corporations, governments and other organisations dealing with operational risk. Its website says the platform is used by more than 400 clients, including a quarter of the Fortune 100, and that its offer combines automated monitoring with expert analysis. That positioning appears consistent with earlier product moves, including the launch of its risk intelligence business in 2022 after combining the Control Risks CORE platform with Geospark Analytics’ Hyperion technology. ... The latest announcement also comes after Seerist and Janes said in March that they were working together on a defence and intelligence workflow that would pair real-time alerts with validated military data. In Seerist’s broader platform messaging, features such as AskAnna, Verified Events and mobile access are presented as part of a system designed to give users a single operating environment for situational awareness. The company says the refreshed platform is intended to support that strategy, while also creating a base for deeper workflow automation and agentic capabilities."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Seerist Unveils Next-Generation Platform, Building the Foundation for the Future of Risk Intelligence",www.prweb.com (Seerist),2026-06-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prweb.com/releases/seerist-unveils-next-generation-platform-building-the-foundation-for-the-future-of-risk-intelligence-302809684.html,"Seerist Unveils Next-Generation Platform, Building the Foundation for the Future of Risk Intelligence Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... RESTON, Va., June 30, 2026 /PRNewswire-PRWeb/ -- Seerist, the AI-enabled risk and threat intelligence platform, announced a major evolution of its platform, introducing a new AI-native foundation designed to help intelligence, security, and risk professionals access critical insights faster, work more efficiently, and make better-informed decisions. ... Built from years of customer feedback, research, and development, ... transformation extends beyond ... features to fundamentally ... ""This release represents years of investment in understanding how intelligence teams work and where they're headed,"" said Tim Roots, Chief Product Officer at Seerist. ""We've reengineered the platform to make intelligence easier to discover, analyze, and operationalize today while creating a foundation that allows us to deliver even greater value through agentic capabilities and deeper operational workflows."" ... analytics. New capabilities ... inputs, advanced ... streamlined report generation. ... Integrated Intelligence connects tactical developments with strategic analysis to provide a richer common operational picture. Enhanced location overviews, powered by Seerist's partnership with Control Risks, bring together real-time events, historical risk trends, and expert analysis in a unified view. ... While many of the platform's most significant advancements occur behind ... scenes, they establish ... foundation for Seerist's long-term vision: to be the trusted ... for intelligence. ... Seerist, Inc. enables global corporations, governments, and organizations to navigate a volatile and uncertain world by preparing them for potential events that could disrupt operations. Trusted by more than 500 customers, including over 20% of the Fortune 500 and over 50 government agencies, Seerist combines cutting-edge artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML)—parsing millions of data points—with expert human analysis built on decades of insight. With 10 global offices and a strategic partnership with Control Risks, Seerist delivers the foresight and clarity needed to make rapid, strategic, and reliable decisions when it matters most. To learn more, visit www.seerist.com"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Seers Wins US FDA Clearance for mobiCARE, Expands Arrhythmia Diagnosis Globally - Seoul Economic Daily",en.sedaily.com (Tae-heui Han),2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/06/29/seers-wins-us-fda-clearance-for-mobicare-expands-arrhythmia,"Seers Wins US FDA Clearance for mobiCARE, Expands Arrhythmia Diagnosis Globally - Seoul Economic Daily ... Seers (458870) announced Monday that its wearable electrocardiogram (ECG) testing device ""mobiCARE"" has received 510(k) clearance from the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The company completed its final FDA 510(k) document submission in May. ... The United States is one of the world's largest arrhythmia diagnosis markets, with more than approximately 14 million arrhythmia diagnostic tests conducted annually. Medicare-based ECG testing reimbursement is known to be about $250 per case, roughly five times Korea's insurance reimbursement rate. Demand for wearable-based long-term ECG monitoring is also expanding amid an aging population and rising cardiovascular disease. ... With this FDA clearance, Seers plans to accelerate its push for medical concierge-based ECG testing services in the United States. The company is pursuing a strategy to enter the Medicare public insurance reimbursement market after conducting outpatient proof-of-concept (PoC) trials in cooperation with local medical institutions. ... Seers expects the FDA clearance to have a positive impact not only on US market entry but also on its global business expansion. The company plans to use it as an important reference in product approval and business negotiation processes in overseas countries such as the Middle East and Asia. ... ""This FDA clearance has laid the foundation to verify in the US market our AI ECG analysis platform, whose business viability we have already proven domestically,"" Seers CEO Lee Young-shin said. ""We plan to push forward with US outpatient trials and entry into the Medicare market without setbacks, and based on this, gradually expand our global business."""
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,XiaoZhi Weekly News | Seer Robotics Officially Lists on HKEX; Galaxy General's Galbot S1 Joins CATL Workforce | Gasgoo,autonews.gasgoo.com,2026-06-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://autonews.gasgoo.com/articles/icv/xiaozhi-weekly-news-seer-robotics-officially-lists-on-hkex-galaxy-generals-galbot-s1-joins-catl-workforce-2071589351476473857,"Seer Robotics makes HKEX debut, becoming the first ""robot brain"" stock on the market ... Seer Robotics (06106.HK) officially listed on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange’s main board on June 24, marking the debut of the market’s first ""robot brain"" stock. ... The company offered 10,497,300 shares globally in its IPO (excluding the over-allotment option). After the clawback mechanism was triggered, the public offering accounted for 2,099,500 shares, while international placement covered 8,397,800 shares. Priced at 101.6 Hong Kong dollars per share, the issuance raised 1.067 billion Hong Kong dollars, giving the company a market capitalization of 11.227 billion Hong Kong dollars. ... On its debut, Seer Robotics surged more than 30% at the open—a clear sign of strong market appetite. ... The offering drew extraordinary attention during the subscription phase. Eight cornerstone investors committed 462 million Hong Kong dollars in total, representing 43.34% of the deal. Hillhouse’s HHLRA led the group as the cornerstone investor with 118 million Hong Kong dollars, joined by prominent institutions including Yuanbao, 3W, GF Fund Management, and Ruihua Investment. ... Founded in 2020, Seer Robotics has cemented a formidable market position in just a few years, anchored by its core product: the ""robot brain,"" or robot controller. ... According to CIC data, Seer Robotics held the top spot globally for robot controller sales for three consecutive years from 2023 to 2025, boosting its global market share to 25%. In China, its controller market share reached as high as 45.2%. On the financial side, revenue climbed from 2.49 billion yuan in 2023 to 4.42 billion yuan in 2025, representing a compound annual growth rate of 33.2%. ... Yet Seer Robotics’ true moat is ... data flywheel."" ... Over the past few years, the company has pursued a strategy centered on real-world machine data. By deploying robots at scale and applying them in actual scenarios, Seer has continuously accumulated data assets across diverse scenarios, tasks, and robot form factors. Today, robots powered by Seer’s ""brain"" are deployed in over 1,000 factories across more than 20 industries. ... Large-scale deployment has fostered strong customer stickiness, driven by a massive base of benchmark clients and high repeat purchase rates. This has allowed Seer to construct a data flywheel system: deployment, data feedback, closed-loop training, model iteration, and expanded deployment. ... These data assets—refined in real production environments across scenarios, tasks, and robot types—have created a scaled data moat that latecomers will find difficult ... Galaxy General's Galbot S1 joins the workforce at CATL ... Gasgoo has learned that CATL recently signed a global strategic partnership agreement with Galaxy General. The two companies will focus on upgrading smart production lines, promoting the expansion and application of embodied intelligence robots in global markets, and jointly establishing service standards for the embodied intelligence aftermarket. ... At the center of this collaboration is Galaxy General’s heavy-duty humanoid robot, the Galbot S1. Notably, it is the world’s first embodied intelligence robot in regular operation to be powered by a CATL battery. ... The Galbot S1 has officially joined CATL’s smart production lines, handling long-range autonomous tasks in module and battery pack assembly. It is directly replacing human labor in high-intensity processes such as material handling and sorting. ... Since completing acceptance testing at CATL’s Ningde HX base in March, the Galbot S1 has been operating 7x24 hours on the company’s mass production lines for over three months, ensuring round-the-clock uninterrupted operations. ... Building on this, Galaxy General and CATL are deepening their collaboration on tackling complex scenarios, including loading and unloading, cell sorting, screw ... harness assembly. ... Meanwhile, CATL’s ""Ningjia Service"" is expanding its established service ecosystem—which covers battery testing, maintenance, and recycling. Its scope will extend beyond ""power batteries"" and ""energy storage systems"" to include ""embodied intelligence robots."" Together, the partners aim to establish the world’s first aftermarket service standard for embodied intelligence. ... Through this partnership, Ningjia Service will leverage Galaxy General’s highly reliable products and technical expertise to upgrade its global network of over 1,300 service stations into an embodied intelligence robot service network, achieving ""multi-function capability at a single station."" ... Notably, CATL had already deployed the humanoid robot ... Xiao Mo"" from Qianxun Intelligent at its Zhongzhou ... battery pack production line by the end of 2025. ... Intelligent is part of CATL’s ecosystem."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SEER Robotics Marks Hong Kong Listing and Showcases Embodied Intelligence Robotics at Global Industry Events,www.digitaljournal.com,2026-06-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.digitaljournal.com/pr/news/newsfile/seer-robotics-marks-hong-kong-133435615.html,"Shanghai, China--(Newsfile Corp. - June 26, 2026) - SEER Robotics (Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd.) today announced that it completed its Hong Kong listing on June 24, 2026, and presented its embodied intelligent robotics portfolio at AUTOMATE 2026 in Chicago and CeMAT Australia 2026 in Melbourne. ... The exhibitions featured SEER Robotics' Robot Brain-enabled automation platforms, robot controllers, autonomous mobile robots (AMRs), intelligent forklifts, humanoid robots, and related solutions for manufacturing and logistics environments. ... Together, these technologies reflect SEER Robotics' Robot Brain + Open Platform approach to coordinating heterogeneous robots through a unified software architecture. The company presented how its systems can support material handling, storage, delivery, fleet dispatching, and autonomous inspection workflows across industrial sites. ... At AUTOMATE 2026, SEER Robotics showcased closed-loop smart logistics applications for North American manufacturing and warehousing environments. The demonstrations included reach trucks for narrow-aisle, high-bay warehousing and pallet trucks designed for US-standard closed pallets, along with coordinated workflows for material movement and workstation delivery. ... At CeMAT Australia 2026 in Melbourne, SEER Robotics presented automation solutions for warehouses seeking to improve operational efficiency without broad infrastructure reconstruction. Demonstrations at the booth included coordinated reach truck and lifting robot workflows covering high-bay storage, material handling, and workstation delivery. ... The company's Hong Kong listing marks a corporate milestone for SEER Robotics as it continues to support customers in manufacturing and logistics markets worldwide. ... Following the listing, SEER Robotics said it will continue to invest in Robot Brain technologies, Open Platform development, and international customer support for industrial automation applications. ... SEER Robotics (Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd.), founded in 2020, is a globally leading platform-based embodied intelligent robotics company. The company was listed on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on June 24, 2026. It is ranked No.1 in global intelligent robot controller shipments for three consecutive years, and offers one of the most comprehensive robot portfolios in the industry, spanning controllers, autonomous mobile robots (AMRs), and embodied intelligent robots."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seerist and DataExpert Partner to Deliver Forward-Looking Risk Intelligence and Enhanced Situational Awareness,www.prweb.com (Seerist),2026-06-25T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prweb.com/releases/seerist-and-dataexpert-partner-to-deliver-forward-looking-risk-intelligence-and-enhanced-situational-awareness-302810253.html,"Seerist has partnered with DataExpert to bring AI-powered, decision-ready risk intelligence to government, law enforcement, and enterprise organizations, helping them transform complex data into actionable insights for more proactive and informed decision-making. ... RESTON, Va., June 25, 2026 /PRNewswire-PRWeb/ -- Seerist, the AI-powered risk intelligence platform trusted by security and intelligence teams around the world, announced a new partnership with DataExpert, a trusted provider of solutions in OSINT, digital forensics, data analytics, and cybersecurity. Through this collaboration, DataExpert will integrate Seerist's AI-driven risk intelligence capabilities into its portfolio, enabling customers to move beyond traditional data collection and analysis toward more proactive, risk-informed decision-making. ... Seerist combines advanced artificial intelligence with expert human analysis to provide organizations with real-time intelligence and insights that help identify emerging threats and evolving global risks. By incorporating Seerist's platform into its offering, DataExpert will empower customers across government, law enforcement, and enterprise sectors with forward-looking intelligence that enhances situational awareness and supports faster, more confident decision-making. ... ""Organizations today need more than raw data — they need context, clarity, and the ability to anticipate what's next,"" said Barry Saadatmand, Chief Revenue Officer at Seerist. ""Partnering with DataExpert expands access to Seerist's decision ready risk intelligence capabilities and helps organizations better understand how evolving global risks can impact their assets, people, and operations."" ... Through the partnership, customers will gain access to localized risk intelligence and insights that help identify where risks are emerging, how they are evolving, and the potential operational impact. Seerist's platform transforms large volumes of global data into actionable intelligence, enabling security and operational teams to respond proactively rather than reactively. ... ""While DataExpert supports organizations in collecting and analyzing data, Seerist's platform adds a critical layer. By combining artificial intelligence with human expertise, it translates data into actionable, localized risk insights. This provides forward-looking intelligence that enhances situational awareness and enables organizations to respond more proactively, with a clearer understanding of how risks may impact their operations — whether in law enforcement or enterprise environments,"" said Gino Flem, Managing Director of DataExpert BV. ... The addition of Seerist strengthens DataExpert's offering across its core domains, including OSINT, digital forensics, data analytics, and cybersecurity. Customers will benefit from enhanced situational awareness, improved risk assessment, and more proactive response capabilities powered by Seerist's risk intelligence platform. ... By expanding access to location-based risk intelligence, the partnership reinforces both companies' commitment to helping organizations transform complex data into actionable insights that support operational resilience and informed decision-making. ... To mark the partnership, Seerist and DataExpert will host a joint webinar on July 9, 2026, benefitting European Government Organisations. More information and registration: https://dataexpert.eu/events-webinars?mc_cid=e3ff08ae0a&mc_eid=UNIQID. ... Seerist, Inc. enables global corporations, governments, and organizations to navigate a volatile and uncertain world by preparing them for potential events that could disrupt operations. Trusted by more than 500 customers, including over 20% of the Fortune 500 and over 50 government agencies, Seerist combines cutting-edge artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML)—parsing millions of data points—with expert human analysis built on decades of insight. With 10 global offices and a strategic partnership with Control Risks, Seerist delivers the foresight and clarity needed to make rapid, strategic, and reliable decisions when it matters most. To learn more, visit www.seerist.com ... DataExpert is a trusted partner in data-driven investigations and intelligence solutions, specializing in OSINT, digital forensics, data analytics, and cybersecurity. The company supports government, law enforcement, and enterprise organizations in transforming complex data into actionable intelligence that improves operational effectiveness and decision-making. www.dataexpert.eu"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"'Robot brain' maker SEER lists in Hong Kong, pares early gains - The Yangtzeer",yangtzeer.com (Yangtzeer observers),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://yangtzeer.com/news/deals/robot-brain-seer-lists-hk/,"'Robot brain' maker SEER lists in Hong Kong, pares early gains - The Yangtzeer ... SEER (仙工智能), a Chinese robotics software and controller maker known as the industry’s “ robot brain” supplier, debuted on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on June 24, becoming the first company in the segment to go public as a specialist technology listing. ... The stock opened flat at HK$101.6 ($13), surged as much as 38% to HK$140.5 during trading, and later gave up much of those gains to close at HK$116.9, up 15.1% from its offer price. ... The company ended its first trading day with a market cap of about HK$12.9 billion. ... Founded in 2020, SEER specializes in robot control systems, which serve as the central control layer for autonomous mobile robots and other industrial machines. ... According to China Insights Consultancy, the company ranked first globally and in China by robot controller sales volume in 2025, with market shares of 24.8% and 45.2%, respectively. ... The IPO was conducted under Hong Kong’s Chapter 18C regime for specialist technology companies. Shares were priced at HK$101.6 each, while the retail tranche was oversubscribed by 5,934.6 times. ... Eight cornerstone investors led by HHLR, the investment arm of Hillhouse, subscribed a combined HK$462 million worth of shares. ... Despite its market-leading position in robot controllers, profitability remains elusive. ... Revenue rose from 249 million yuan ($36.67) in 2023 to 442 million yuan in 2025, representing a compound annual growth rate of 33.2%. ... Net losses, however, stood at 47.7 million yuan, 42.3 million yuan and 47.1 million yuan over the same period, totaling nearly 137 million yuan. The company expects to remain loss-making through the end of 2026. ... Cash flow has also come under pressure. Net cash used in operating activities reached 27.8 million yuan in 2025, while trade receivables more than tripled from 53.7 million yuan in 2023 to 169.6 million yuan in 2025. ... The average collection period stretched to 111 days, highlighting growing working-capital demands from customers. ... SEER’s business mix has also shifted in ways that could weigh on margins. Robot controllers, its highest-margin product with a gross margin of 79.8%, accounted for 19.3% of revenue in 2025, down from 26.5% two years earlier. ... Meanwhile, lower-margin robot hardware products, which carry a gross margin of 38.4%, expanded to 67.9% of total revenue. ... That transition has coincided with a sharp decline in controller pricing. The average selling price of the company’s controllers fell from 25,900 yuan in 2023 to 10,700 yuan in 2025, a drop of nearly 60%. ... With its core high-margin business shrinking as lower-margin hardware drives growth, investors are now focused on whether SEER can convert its technology leadership into a sustainable profit model."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SEER Robotics Raises 7M in Hong Kong IPO Debut,theroboticsmedia.com (The Robotics Media),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://theroboticsmedia.com/article/seer-robotics-hong-kong-ipo-137-million-robot-brain-listing,"SEER Robotics Raises 7M in Hong Kong IPO Debut ... # SEER Robotics Raises $137M in Hong Kong's First 'Robot Brain' IPO ... Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology (SEER Robotics) debuted on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange, raising about $137 million to fund embodied-AI navigation and global expansion of its robot controllers and AMRs. ... SEER Robotics, the Shanghai-based maker of robot controllers and autonomous mobile robots formally known as Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology, made its trading debut on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on June 24, 2026, raising roughly HK$1.07 billion (about US$137 million) in what the company billed as the first ""robot brain"" IPO. ... The company floated about 10.5 million H-shares at a fixed price of HK$101.60 each under the stock code 06106.HK, with China International Capital Corporation (CICC) acting as sole overall coordinator. Proceeds are earmarked for proprietary embodied-AI navigation algorithms, industrial logistics software infrastructure, and the expansion of SEER's international service networks. ... Founded in 2020 by Zhao Yue, SEER Robotics has ranked No. 1 in global intelligent robot controller shipments for three consecutive years. Its portfolio spans motion-control ""robot brain"" controllers, autonomous forklifts, lifting robots and fleet-management software under the slogan ""All Robots. One Platform."" The company reported 2025 revenue of 442 million yuan ($61.5 million), up 30.2% year on year, though its net loss widened 11.2% to 47.1 million yuan — a profitability gap common among scaling robotics firms. ... SEER's debut adds to a busy stretch for robotics public markets, particularly in China. It follows Unitree's STAR Market IPO approval and growing demand for warehouse autonomy seen in deployments like the Rainbow Robotics RB-Y1 Coupang pilot and orchestration platforms such as Roboteon's software shown at Automate 2026. Investor appetite for AMR firms is being tested as several Chinese players line up Hong Kong listings."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Fangda Advises SEER TECH on Its Hong Kong 18C Listing as the “First Robot Brain Stock” | Law.asia,law.asia (Website team 06),2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://law.asia/press-release/seer-tech-first-robot-brain-stock-hong-kong-listing/,"- On 24 June 2026, Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. (“ SEER TECH” (stock code: 06106.HK) , a technology company listed under Chapter 18C of the Hong Kong Listing Rules as a Specialist Technology Company, successfully completed its initial public offering (IPO) and was listed on the Main Board of The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited, becoming the “ first robot brain stock”. SEER TECH priced its global offering at HKD 101.6 per share, raising total proceeds of over HKD 1 billion. ... - SEER TECH is an intelligent robotics company with robot control systems, often described as “robot brains”, at the core of its research and development. Leveraging its self-developed SRC series controllers, the company enables the autonomous operation of intelligent robot bodies through a layered technology architecture that integrates vision-language-action (VLA), reinforcement learning, end-to-end navigation, and simultaneous localization and mapping (SLAM). Its controllers are compatible with more than 400 types of components, allowing customers to flexibly build their own robots in a modular, building-block-like manner and providing truly one-stop intelligent robotics solutions. In 2025, SEER TECH ranked first globally and in China by sales volume of robot controllers, establishing a leading position in the market. ... , the sole sponsor and overall coordinator, CMBI, the overall coordinator, and other underwriters in ... Fangda’ ... work covered legal due diligence, CSRC filing, assistance with regulatory communications and responses to regulatory enquiries. ... - We provided one-stop, high-quality professional legal services for the transaction and supported SEER TECH in successfully completing its Hong Kong listing. The Fangda team advising on SEER TECH’s Hong Kong listing was led by partners Aaron CHEN, Jane CHEN and QIU Tianyuan. Key team members included ZHANG Chao and Lisa BU. ... - We extend our sincere congratulations to SEER TECH on its successful listing on The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong, and also thank WANG Yusong and other colleagues for their contributions to SEER TECH’s Pre-IPO private equity financing."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SEER Robotics Announces HK$1.07 Billion IPO // Cooley // Global Law Firm,www.cooley.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.cooley.com/news/coverage/2026/2026-06-24-seer-robotics-announces-hk$1-07-billion-ipo,"SEER Robotics Announces HK$1.07 Billion IPO // Cooley // Global Law Firm ... # SEER Robotics Announces HK$1.07 Billion IPO ... Beijing – June 24, 2026 – Cooley advised Shanghai Seer Intelligence Technology (SEER Robotics), a globally leading platform-based embodied intelligent robotics company, on its HK$1.07 billion initial public offering(IPO). Seer Robotics offered 10,497,300 H shares (subject to over-allotment option) priced at HK$101.60 per share. The company’s shares began trading on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on June 24, 2026, under stock code 06106. ... CICC acted as the sole sponsor, sponsor-overall coordinator, overall coordinators, joint global coordinators, joint bookrunners and joint lead managers for the offering. CMBI acted as overall coordinators, joint global coordinators, joint bookrunners and joint lead managers. Soochow Securities (Hong Kong) acted as joint global coordinator, joint bookrunner and joint lead manager. BOCI, FUTU Securities International, Tiger Brokers, Zheshang International and ABCI acted as joint bookrunners and joint lead managers. ... Lawyers Ethan Jin, Yilin Xu, Mengchao Wu and Dichun Duan led the Cooley team advising SEER Robotics."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Farseer expands to UK & North America with AI Analyst,itbrief.co.uk (Karen Joy Bacudo),2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://itbrief.co.uk/story/farseer-expands-to-uk-north-america-with-ai-analyst,"Farseer expands to UK & North America with AI Analyst ... # Farseer expands to UK & North America with AI Analyst ... Farseer has expanded into the UK and North America and launched a finance tool called AI Analyst, extending the European company into two large markets for finance software. ... AI Analyst is already in use with customers, including TT Hotels and EuroTeleSites. Farseer describes it as a conversational tool that lets finance teams query live financial models in plain language while keeping calculations within its existing governed model. ... under pressure to ... their planning, reporting, and forecasting systems ... maintaining confidence in ... figures used by executives, auditors, and boards ... does not generate financial numbers on its own. ... , it relies on ... 's model, called Rama, to perform calculations. ... The launch follows Farseer's USD $7.2 million Series A funding round. Its reporting has also received certification from the International Business Communication Standards, which aligns with ISO 24896. ... The expansion gives Farseer a local presence in the UK through implementation consultants Maksim Grigorjev, Rajvinder Dhesi and Velislav Asenov. The new footprint is intended to support finance teams adopting its software in the region. ... North America is the second part of the international push as Farseer looks to broaden its reach beyond its European base. It sees both markets as important destinations for finance and business software suppliers. ... Its broader platform is designed to support forecasting cycles, the loading and reconciliation of actuals from ERP and CRM systems, and the assignment of tasks and deadlines. Farseer says this can reduce the time needed for financial planning and cut manual finance work. ... AI Analyst is designed to work inside tools already used by finance teams, including Slack, Microsoft Teams and WhatsApp. It supports analysis across performance and positioning, price-volume-mix, trend and seasonality, multi-dimensional profitability, and variance across actuals, budgets, forecasts and plans. ... ""Farseer has taken a different approach. The governed model does the maths, the AI does the reasoning, and every answer points back to the definitions finance teams have already agreed. We're excited to expand into the UK and North America, where finance leaders need AI solutions they can defend to a CFO, an auditor and a board,"" said Trbara. ... Farseer said its reporting certification places it among a small number of financial reporting platforms that meet the standard."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seer and Korea University Present Preliminary Data at ASMS 2026 Demonstrating Potential of AI-Driven Plasma Proteomics for Multi-Cancer Screening | INN,investingnews.com,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://investingnews.com/seer-and-korea-university-present-preliminary-data-at-asms-2026-demonstrating-potential-of-ai-driven-plasma-proteomics-for-multi-cancer-screening/,"# Seer and Korea University Present Preliminary Data at ASMS 2026 Demonstrating Potential of AI-Driven Plasma Proteomics for Multi-Cancer Screening ... June 22, 20 ... SEER, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER), a leader in deep, unbiased proteomics, today announced preliminary data presented at the 2026 American Society for Mass Spectrometry (ASMS) Annual Conference demonstrating the potential of the Proteograph® Product Suite to enable AI-driven approaches for multi-cancer screening. The findings were presented by Sang-Won Lee, Ph.D., Professor at Korea University and Chief Executive Officer of TargetX, and Jaewoo Kang, Ph.D., Professor at Korea University and Chief Executive Officer of AIGEN Sciences, during the SEER Breakfast Symposium on June 1 in San Diego. ... ""By incorporating the Proteograph platform into our plasma proteomics workflow, we are able to profile the plasma proteome at remarkable depth and scale across thousands of patient samples with the reproducibility required for large-scale clinical research,"" said Dr. Lee. ""Equally important, the quality and consistency of the data enable us to explore new computational approaches that extend beyond conventional identification-based analyses. By combining deep proteomic datasets generated using the Proteograph and Orbitrap Astral mass spectrometer combined with our ID-Free AI framework, we can learn directly from a substantially larger portion of the underlying data and uncover biological patterns that may otherwise remain inaccessible."" ... ""The Proteograph platform significantly expands the breadth and depth of proteomic information captured from plasma samples,"" said Dr. Kang. ""Applying self-supervised AI models directly to these rich datasets allows us to extract biological signal beyond what traditional workflows can utilize. This creates an opportunity to investigate whether previously untapped information can contribute to future multi-cancer screening approaches."" ... ""The convergence of AI and large-scale biology will require datasets of unprecedented depth, quality, and scale,"" said Omid Farokhzad, Chair and Chief Executive Officer of Seer. ""The work presented by Drs. Lee and Kang exemplifies the type of transformative science the Proteograph platform was designed to enable. Their early findings provide an exciting glimpse into how deep proteomic datasets, analyzed with advanced AI methods, may help unlock new approaches to disease detection and biological discovery. We are proud to support this pioneering research and the scientific community's efforts to push the boundaries of what is possible."" ... At ASMS, Drs. Lee and Kang presented results from an ongoing collaboration between Seer and Korea University focused on generating one of the largest deep, unbiased plasma proteomics datasets assembled to date. The analysis included more than 5,500 plasma samples spanning ten major cancer types and healthy controls. ... The researchers reported deep and highly reproducible plasma proteome coverage at population scale, averaging more than 14,000 protein groups per sample, while enabling the construction of a comprehensive cohort-derived proteomic reference resource. They also described an emerging ID-Free AI framework designed to leverage the substantial portion of mass spectrometry data that remains uncharacterized by conventional identification-based workflows. Together, these efforts establish a foundation for evaluating whether additional biological information contained within complex proteomic datasets can improve future multi-cancer screening strategies. ... The findings represent an early milestone in an ongoing collaboration between Seer and Korea University that is expected to analyze more than 20,000 clinical plasma samples across ten of Korea's highest-incidence cancer types. ... SEER, Inc. (Nasdaq: SEER) sets the standard in deep, unbiased proteomics, delivering insights with scale, speed, precision, and reproducibility previously unattainable by other proteomic methods. SEER's Proteograph Product Suite integrates proprietary engineered nanoparticles, automation instrumentation, optimized consumables, and advanced analytical software. SEER's products are for research use only and are not intended for diagnostic procedures. For more information, visit www. SEER.bio. ... This communication contains ""forward-looking statements"" within the meaning of the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995, as amended. Such forward-looking statements are based on Seer's beliefs and assumptions and on information available to Seer as of the date of this press release. Forward-looking statements may involve known and unknown risks, uncertainties, and other factors that may cause Seer's actual results, performance, or achievements to be materially different from those expressed or implied by the forward-looking statements. These statements include, but are not limited to, statements regarding the potential of the Proteograph platform to enable AI-driven multi-cancer screening and statements regarding Seer's plans, strategies, expectations, strategic opportunities, research and development initiatives, and prospects. These risks are described more fully in Seer's filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission and other documents that Seer subsequently files with the Securities and Exchange Commission from time to time. Except to the extent required by law, Seer undertakes no obligation to update such statements to reflect events that occur or circumstances that exist after the date on which they were made."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Seers Surpasses 200 Adopting Hospitals for ‘thynC,’ Upgrading Operations for Rapid Scaling",hi.kormedi.com,2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hi.kormedi.com/en-us/articles/2825279,"Seers Surpasses 200 Adopting Hospitals for ‘thynC,’ Upgrading Operations for Rapid Scaling ... # Seers Surpasses 200 Adopting Hospitals for ‘thynC,’ Upgrading Operations for Rapid Scaling ... ## Healthcare AI monitoring firm appoints Director Jeong Hoon, a Daiichi Sankyo Korea veteran, to refine enterprise strategy and customer experience ... Seers, a leading wearable artificial intelligence (AI) diagnostic monitoring company, is sharpening its commercial strategy by recruiting a veteran executive from a global pharmaceutical firm. The company announced on June 16 that it has appointed Director Jeong Hoon, formerly of Daiichi Sankyo Korea, to lead initiatives aimed at elevating customer experience and operational quality. ... As its flagship AI inpatient monitoring platform, thynC, enters a rapid market expansion phase, Seers is refining its enterprise strategy. The updated approach shifts focus from merely securing new deployments to systematically managing operational quality and custom clinical experiences across individual medical institutions. This strategic shift follows record-breaking first-quarter financial results, with Seers reporting 32.5 billion won in revenue and 13.9 billion won in operating profit. Concurrently, the number of medical institutions adopting the thynC platform has officially surpassed 200. ... Against this backdrop of rapid commercial growth, Seers aims to continuously optimize its client onboarding and interface management through the recruitment of Jeong, who brings an intimate understanding of clinical environments alongside a broad hospital network. The high-profile appointment underscores the strategic emphasis the company places on fortifying thynC's real-world operational capabilities. ... The thynC platform is rapidly evolving into a comprehensive medical AI ecosystem. Moving far beyond basic vital-sign monitoring, it now integrates advanced features such as real-time AI anomaly detection, clinical early warning scores (EWS), and automated fall detection. By expanding its operational footprint into South Korea's premier tertiary general medical centers, including the nation's prominent ""Big 5"" hospitals, the platform continues to solidify its leadership position in the domestic inpatient monitoring market. ... ""For thynC to solidify its role as essential medical AI infrastructure rather than just a newly adopted piece of technology, it must function as a platform that clinical teams trust and rely on daily,"" Jeong noted. ""Through the strategic rollout of the 'thynC Connected Hub,' which systematically monitors operational quality and clinical feedback across individual institutions, we intend to forge enduring, high-value partnerships with our adopting hospitals."""
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SeerBit Integrates with Xero to Streamline Invoice Payments Across Africa - Tech In Africa,www.techinafrica.com (Grace Ashiru),2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-17 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.techinafrica.com/seerbit-integrates-with-xero-to-streamline-invoice-payments-across-africa/,"# SeerBit Integrates with Xero to Streamline Invoice Payments Across Africa ... by Grace Ashiru June 17, 2026, 7:36 am 152 Views SeerBit, a leading Pan-African payments company has integrated with Xero, a global small business platform to simplify how businesses across Africa get paid from invoices. ... Through the integration, businesses using SeerBit and Xero on the continent can now embed a “Pay Now” option directly into invoices, allowing customers to complete payments instantly using local and international methods, including cards, bank transfers and mobile money. ... The integration also supports multi-currency transactions, enabling businesses to invoice and receive payments across different markets with fewer barriers related to conversion and settlement. ... Omoniyi Kolade, CEO at SeerBit, said: “Our focus has always been on making it easier for businesses across Africa to move money without friction. We see a future where payments are not a separate step, but embedded into every part of how businesses operate. Integrating with platforms like Xero is a natural step in that journey, allowing us to bring payments directly into the tools businesses already rely on and move closer to a fully connected workflow between invoicing and settlement.”"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"SEER Robotics Passes HKEX Listing Hearing, Ranking First Globally in Robot Controller Sales | NewTimeSpace",www.newtimespace.com,2026-06-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newtimespace.com/en/ipo/1411959.html,"SEER Robotics Passes HKEX Listing Hearing, Ranking First Globally in Robot Controller Sales | NewTimeSpace ... SEER Robotics Passes HKEX Listing Hearing, Ranking First Globally in Robot Controller Sales ... NewTimeSpace News: Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. passed the Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing (HKEX) listing hearing on June 7, 2026, with China International Capital Corporation (CICC) acting as the sole sponsor. The company is an intelligent robot firm focused on self-developed robot control systems. According to CIC Consulting, it ranked first globally and in China in robot controller sales volume in 2025, with market shares of 24.8% and 45.2% respectively. ... NewTimeSpace News: Shanghai Seer Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd. passed the HKEX Main Board listing hearing onJune 7, 2026, with CICC as the sole sponsor. ... As an intelligent robot company core to self-developed robot control systems—dubbed the ""robot brain""—SEER Robotics develops and sells robots, controllers, software and accessories. It deliversone-stop intelligent robot solutionscovering development, deployment and operation for real-world scenarios, underpinned by the market position and leading technology of its robot control systems. ... Per CIC Consulting data on industrial intelligent robot companies:By 2025 revenue: Ranked7th globally and 3rd in China, with 1.1% and 2.5% market shares respectively.By the number of industrial intelligent robots equipped with its controllers: Ranked2nd globally and 2nd in China, with 7.7% and 14.6% market shares respectively.By 2025 robot controller sales volume: Ranked1st globally and 1st in China, with 24.8% and 45.2% market shares respectively. ... - Seer Robotics (06106.HK): Grey Market Down 11.42% at HK$90 - Seer Robotics (06106.HK) Launches IPO: Offer Price at HK$101.60, Entry Fee Around HK$5,131 per Lot"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seerist Recognized in Frost & Sullivan's 2026 Frost Radar™ for Risk Intelligence Solutions,www.prweb.com (Seerist),2026-06-02T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-02 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prweb.com/releases/seerist-recognized-in-frost--sullivans-2026-frost-radar-for-risk-intelligence-solutions-302788659.html,"RESTON, Va., June 2, 2026 /PRNewswire-PRWeb/ -- Seerist, the leading AI-enabled risk and threat intelligence platform, announced it has been recognized in the Frost Radar™: Risk Intelligence Solutions, 2026 report by Frost & Sullivan. The report highlights Seerist as a key innovator in the rapidly evolving risk intelligence market, citing the company's decision-centric intelligence model, AI-driven capabilities, and ability to transform complex global risk data into actionable insights for organizations operating in increasingly volatile environments. ... According to Frost & Sullivan, ""Seerist is redefining how organizations improve their risk posture from simple exposure awareness to remediation."" The analyst firm recognized Seerist for its ability to fuse ""real-time events, historical context, verified analyst insight, and foresight into a single, API-first platform."" ... ""Organizations today are overwhelmed with fragmented risk signals and disconnected intelligence feeds,"" said Alex Berry, CEO of Seerist. ""This recognition from Frost & Sullivan validates our mission to help organizations move beyond reactive monitoring toward faster, more confident decision-making powered by AI, trusted intelligence, and human expertise."" ... Frost & Sullivan specifically highlighted Seerist's unique four-pillar intelligence architecture — Events, Contextualization, Exposure, and Foresight — which combines real-time event detection with historical analysis, analyst validation, and predictive intelligence. The report noted that Seerist's platform helps organizations transform ""the overwhelming volume of threat signals into defensible, timely risk insights and decision-making."" ... The report also recognized Seerist's recently launched AskAnna capability as ""one of the company's most groundbreaking capabilities."" AskAnna uses Seerist's proprietary AI models combined with expert analysis from Control Risks' global analyst team to deliver concise, fully sourced intelligence insights that explain the ""why"" behind emerging risks and geopolitical developments. ... Frost & Sullivan also recognized Seerist's accelerating enterprise growth across industries including financial services, energy, technology, and industrial sectors, citing increasing demand for proactive geopolitical, operational, and supply chain risk intelligence. ... Frost & Sullivan projects the global risk intelligence market will grow from $58.84 billion in 2025 to $170.14 billion by 2030, driven by increasing demand for integrated intelligence platforms that unify physical, cyber, and operational risk visibility. ... Seerist, Inc. enables global corporations, governments, and organizations to navigate a volatile and uncertain world by preparing them for potential events that could disrupt operations. Trusted by more than 500 customers, including 25% of the Fortune 100, 15% of the Global 2000, and over 50 government agencies, Seerist combines cutting-edge artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML)—parsing millions of data points—with expert human analysis built on decades of insight. With 10 global offices and a strategic partnership with Control Risks, Seerist delivers the foresight and clarity needed to make rapid, strategic, and reliable decisions when it matters most. To learn more, visit www.seerist.com"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,BTCPresswire Expands Structured Financial Media Access to Support Advisor and Investment-Focused StreetInsider Announcements - Dutable,dutable.com (Mike),2026-05-26T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,,https://dutable.com/btcpresswire-expands-structured-financial-media-access-to-support-advisor-and-investment-focused-streetinsider-announcements/,"BTCPresswire Expands Structured Financial Media Access to Support Advisor and Investment-Focused StreetInsider Announcements - Dutable ... BTCPresswire today announced continued advancement of its financial distribution infrastructure, reinforcing how cryptocurrency, blockchain, fintech, and broader financial service providers coordinate structured investor-facing announcements. As digital asset enterprises increasingly intersect with traditional finance, BTCPresswire is strengthening its operational standards to support disciplined formatting, sector-aligned disclosure sequencing, and predictable financial readership visibility within recognized market environments. ... The growing relevance of a structured Financial advisor press release on StreetInsider reflects expanding collaboration between blockchain platforms and traditional financial advisory firms. BTCPresswire recognizes that advisor-focused announcements must prioritize factual clarity, regulatory sensitivity, and capital markets readability. ... As blockchain-based investment products gain visibility, structured Investment news distribution StreetInsider becomes increasingly important. BTCPresswire supports digital asset enterprises and fintech companies preparing announcements related to funding rounds, asset tokenization, capital raises, portfolio expansions, and investment vehicle launches. ... Through disciplined documentation workflows, BTCPresswire ensures that investment-related updates are sequenced around measurable milestones and professional presentation standards. The emphasis remains on clarity and compliance-conscious structuring rather than promotional positioning. ... The relevance of a properly formatted Business loans announcement on StreetInsider has grown as blockchain and fintech platforms expand into lending, credit markets, and decentralized finance solutions. BTCPresswire assists organizations in presenting financing developments with clarity and operational transparency. ... Whether announcing lending facility launches, credit product integrations, institutional financing agreements, or capital deployment strategies, BTCPresswire structures disclosures around verifiable data and disciplined sequencing. ... BTCPresswire operates exclusively within cryptocurrency, blockchain, Web3, and related fintech communications. This specialization enables BTCPresswire to anticipate disclosure categories typical of decentralized finance platforms, asset tokenization providers, NFT infrastructure companies, venture-backed startups, staking networks, and analytics firms. ... Because BTCPresswire works within this focused domain, it understands how to structure announcements involving validator expansions, cross-chain integrations, liquidity programs, governance reforms, regulatory updates, and strategic financing agreements. BTCPresswire applies consistent formatting logic to maintain investor-facing readability. ... BTCPresswire clearly communicates that it functions as a paid press release distribution platform rather than an independent editorial outlet. Content disseminated through BTCPresswire is supplied by clients for informational and promotional visibility across financial and crypto-focused readership networks. ... BTCPresswire continues investing in its financial media coordination framework as blockchain adoption expands across advisory, investment, and lending markets. Institutional scrutiny, regulatory oversight, and capital market integration are shaping how digital asset enterprises approach structured communication. ... Through enhanced coordination capabilities and sector expertise, BTCPresswire strengthens predictable financial visibility for cryptocurrency and fintech organizations. BTCPresswire remains committed to disciplined workflows, transparent service positioning, and consistent formatting standards. ... By reinforcing its advisor- and investment-focused distribution infrastructure, BTCPresswire strengthens its role as a specialized provider supporting sustainable investor engagement within evolving global capital markets."
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,SeerBit Technologies partners IIAN to enhance audit work in Nigeria - Businessday NG,businessday.ng (BusinessDay),2026-05-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://businessday.ng/life/article/seerbit-technologies-partners-iian-to-enhance-audit-work-in-nigeria/,"SeerBit Technologies partners IIAN to enhance audit work in Nigeria - Businessday NG ... # SeerBit Technologies partners IIAN to enhance audit work in Nigeria Ngozi Okpalakunne May 24, 2026 ... SeerBit, one of the leading financial technology companies that provides secure payment gateways for both online and offline businesses, has collaborated with the Institute of Internal Auditors Nigeria (IIAN) to provide practitioners with technology solutions to everyday problems that internal auditors face in carrying out their duties. The event, which held in Lagos, was put together as part of yearly global awareness campaign for internal auditors and it involved the company showcasing all their latest Apps, POS and In-Store Payment Systems it has developed for easy payment, to keep internal auditors abreast of new technologically innovative solutions. In ... “So, this event was meant to ... , how our new ... , including all ... from the standpoint control, standpoint visibility ... According to him, at Se ... Bit, they don’t just make payments, they carry out their business ... technology which has given an edge ... “We have seen the complexities of different systems, that causes fragmentation in the system which affects audit firms. What we have done as a technology company, is to bring all those factors together to create flexibility for auditors so that after all the transactions have been done whether quarterly or yearly, auditors will be able to shorten their audit cycle, bridge the gap in their auditing work as well as ensure that businesses take faster decisions because they’re sure that their investment is secured,” he added. ... Oyelade while emphasising that business is based ... trust, listed the advantages of their Apps as real- time payment confirmation, automated reconciliation and reporting, faster collection ... Others are, improved financial visibility, reduced manual processing and unified payment experience across channels amongst others. Senior Product Manager of the company, Babajide Shoyebo explained the innovations they have introduced in POS and In-Store Payments which Provides hardware and software solutions to facilitate seamless transactions at physical store locations. He explained that their payment gateway, allows businesses to accept multiple payment methods including cards and bank transfers directly on their websites or apps. ... In her remarks, ... Chief Executive Officer of the Institute, Don Umeha, expressed happiness that the collaboration with SeerBit Technologies on ways to enhance payment systems in the country was a success, noting that the company has brought out some innovations that would enhance payment systems which will give rise to automatic account reconciliation. “Reconciliation of account has been a problem in this country especially where there are several thousands of transactions that happen in a business organisation. So, real time reconciliation is what’s happening and they have an app that can be used to ensure that such objectives are met, that will give room to transparent transactions at any point in time and also bring trust in business.”"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Samsung Fire, SEERS plan wearable-based health monitoring service < Device/ICT < Article - KBR",www.koreabiomed.com (Kim Ji-hye jkim404@docdocdoc.co.kr See Other Articles),2026-05-20T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-20 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.koreabiomed.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=31729,"Samsung Fire, SEERS plan wearable-based health monitoring service < Device/ICT < Article - KBR ... Samsung Fire, SEERS plan wearable-based health monitoring service ... Samsung Fire & Marine Insurance is bringing SEERS’ wearable monitoring technology into its healthcare business, giving the insurer a new source of biometric data for services that could follow customers after treatment and into daily life. ... The agreement centers on SEERS’ digital biomarker technology, which analyzes physiological data such as heart rate collected through wearable devices. The companies plan to use that data to build health management services that extend monitoring beyond hospital treatment. ... For Samsung Fire, the deal pushes its healthcare business further from simple wellness apps and closer to continuous monitoring. The company said the service could support disease prevention, recovery management and a customer’s return to daily life after illness or injury. ... Lee Hai-sung, head of Samsung Fire’s healthcare business team, called the agreement “the beginning of a new cooperation model” between insurance and digital healthcare, saying the company would work as a health partner that manages risks before they worsen and supports customers through recovery. ... Samsung Fire already runs digital health services including Anyfit Plus and Sugarfit, which provide health management and disease-risk prediction. The insurer has also worked with other healthcare partners in areas such as blood glucose management and AI-based services. ... A Samsung Fire spokesperson told Korea Biomedical Review that the insurer chose SEERS because its technology has been adopted by major hospitals in Korea and used by about 1,000 medical institutions. ... The spokesperson also said SEERS has the largest market share in its field, making it the most suitable partner for the project. ... For SEERS, the deal gives its hospital monitoring technology a path into post-discharge care. ... Lee Young-shin, CEO of SEERS, said the partnership would test whether that hospital experience can be turned into an insurer-linked care model. ... “This partnership marks the starting point for building an integrated model that connects post-discharge patient management and prognosis prediction, based on the data analysis capabilities and operational experience we have accumulated through in-hospital patient monitoring,” Lee said. ... - Korea’s SEERS signs $14.7 mil. UAE deal to supply AI heart-monitoring wearables - SEERS shows AI ward monitoring in use at Dongtan City Hospital - Seers Technology to rebrand as SEERS, signaling global digital healthcare push - Seers Technology unveils 200% bonus issue, says UAE digital health rollout remains on track - Daewoong targets 100,000 beds, ₩300 bil. in digital health push with AI monitoring platform - After years of losses, Korea’s medical AI sector edges toward profitability - Daewoong joins SEERS, TR to develop bedside pulmonary testing smart ward solution - SEERS wins FDA clearance for mobiCARE wearable heart monitor"
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,"Ceragem AI Unit Seers Posts Record Quarterly Earnings, Revenue Jumps 700% - Seoul Economic Daily",en.sedaily.com (Park Hyo-Jeong),2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/05/12/ceragem-ai-unit-seers-posts-record-quarterly-earnings,"Ceragem AI Unit Seers Posts Record Quarterly Earnings, Revenue Jumps 700% - Seoul Economic Daily ... Seers (458870.KQ) posted its largest quarterly earnings since its founding, the company said in a regulatory filing Wednesday. ... Seers reported first-quarter revenue of 32.5 billion won and operating profit of 13.9 billion won on a consolidated basis. Revenue surged 700 percent from a year earlier, while operating profit swung to positive territory. The first-quarter operating profit alone surpassed about 85 percent of last year's full-year operating profit of 16.3 billion won. The operating margin stood at 42.6 percent, marking the third consecutive quarter above 40 percent. ... Thinq, an artificial intelligence-based inpatient monitoring platform, drove overall performance with 31.2 billion won in revenue. The figure represents about 70 percent of Thinq's full-year 2024 revenue of 44.6 billion won. Thinq has been installed in more than 17,000 cumulative hospital beds, primarily at major hospitals nationwide. ... ""As the No. 1 player in Korea's AI hospital bed platform market, we are rapidly expanding our multi-ward operational experience at large hospitals and references based on electronic medical record (EMR) integration, strengthening our market dominance,"" a Seers official said. ""Existing and new orders will be reflected from the second quarter, and the high-growth trend will continue."" ... Seers believes its platform-based leverage effect is materializing in terms of profitability. Despite external cost pressures in the first quarter, including rising prices for server memory chips, the company maintained high profitability based on its in-house development and production system for AI wearable devices and fixed wireless gateways, along with operational efficiency. ... The company is also accelerating its overseas expansion, signing a three-year supply contract for its wearable electrocardiogram analysis solution Mobicare with One Health, an affiliate of PureHealth, the largest healthcare group in the United Arab Emirates (UAE). In the United States, the company is in the final stages of the approval process with the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for Mobicare. ... ""These results demonstrate that our Thinq-centered AI hospital bed monitoring business has entered a full-fledged growth trajectory,"" said Lee Young-shin, CEO of Seers. ""Along with expanding the domestic bed platform, we will fully launch our global business in the UAE and the United States centered on Mobicare, growing into an AI healthcare platform company."""
SEERTECH SOLUTIONS,,,,Exa,Seers reports record-breaking quarterly growth driven by AI inpatient platform expansion and overseas ambitions | Noah Intelligence,noah-news.com,2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z,2026-05-12 00:00:00+00:00,,https://noah-news.com/seers-reports-record-breaking-quarterly-growth-driven-by-ai-inpatient-platform-e/,"Seers reports record-breaking quarterly growth driven by AI inpatient platform expansion and overseas ambitions | Noah Intelligence ... # Seers reports record-breaking quarterly growth driven by AI inpatient platform expansion and overseas ambitions ... Seers achieves its strongest quarterly performance amid soaring sales of its AI-based inpatient monitoring system, thynC, with significant growth expected in domestic hospital bed installations and international markets... ... Seers achieves its strongest quarterly performance amid soaring sales of its AI-based inpatient monitoring system, thynC, with significant growth expected in domestic hospital bed installations and international markets including the UAE and US. ... Seers said on Tuesday that it posted its strongest quarterly performance since founding, as first-quarter consolidated sales reached 32.5 billion won and operating profit came in at 13.9 billion won. The company’s operating margin was 42.6%, extending a run of profitability that has now lasted three quarters, while first-quarter operating profit alone amounted to about 85% of last year’s full-year operating profit. ... Much of the growth came from thynC, its AI-based inpatient monitoring platform, which generated 31.2 billion won in sales in the quarter. According to the company, that figure was roughly 70% of thynC’s full-year revenue in 2024. Seers said the system has now been installed in more than 17,000 hospital beds nationwide, with uptake accelerating at major hospitals in the Seoul metropolitan area and other large institutions. ... The company is increasingly presenting itself as a platform business rather than a hardware supplier. Analysts and industry coverage in Korea note that thynC is still used in only about 2% of the country’s roughly 700,000 hospital beds, leaving considerable room for expansion if adoption continues at current hospitals and spreads to new sites. Seers has also been building references through multi-ward deployments and electronic medical record integration, which it sees as key to reinforcing its position in the domestic market. ... Seers said the second quarter should bring further momentum as Korean hospitals enter their busiest seasonal period. It expects additional bed installations and new orders to be recognised progressively, including about 3,000 beds already won through distributor Daewoong Pharmaceutical but not yet installed. The company’s gross profitability has also held up despite higher server memory chip costs, helped by in-house development and production of its AI wearables and fixed wireless gateways. ... Overseas expansion is becoming a more important part of the story. The company’s wearable ECG analysis product, mobiCARE, is expected to support growth abroad after Seers signed a three-year supply deal worth at least 22 billion won with ONE HEALTH, a unit of Abu Dhabi-based PureHealth. Seers also plans to begin a proof-of-concept project for thynC at leading hospitals in the United Arab Emirates, while work towards US regulatory clearance for mobiCARE is nearing completion, according to the company."
