NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,NIMS launches local-flavoured snack range to boost global presence - Sinar Daily,www.sinardaily.my (SD Reporter),2026-08-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.sinardaily.my/article/739568/focus/money/nims-launches-local-flavoured-snack-range-to-boost-global-presence,"NIMS launches local-flavoured snack range to boost global presence - Sinar Daily ... # NIMS launches local-flavoured snack range to boost global presence ... The new product line features Teh Tarik Crunch, Sirap Bandung Laici Crunch, and Onde Onde Crunch, combining iconic local ... and dessert tastes with crispy cereal in modern snack packaging. ... SHAH ALAM - Iconic Malaysian flavours such as teh tarik, sirap bandung, and onde-onde have been translated into three new variations of NIMS Chocotub® - Taste of Malaysia, as an effort to showcase the diversity of local culinary heritage to consumers both domestically and internationally. ... NIMS Adelicious Sdn Bhd chief executive officer Tengku Norhanim Tengku Othman said that the three variations, namely Teh Tarik Crunch, Sirap Bandung Laici Crunch and Onde Onde Crunch, combine flavour elements synonymous with Malaysian society in the form of modern snacks. ... ""Through NIMS Chocotub® - Taste of Malaysia, we want to bring the unique flavours of Malaysia to global consumers. Each flavour elevates the culture and nostalgia that are close to the hearts of the people, while also showcasing the potential of local products to compete on the international stage. ... Tengku Norhanim said this at the launch event of NIMS Chocotub® - Taste of Malaysia, which was also attended by Malaysia External Trade Development Corporation (MATRADE) deputy chief executive officer (Entrepreneur Development) Mansor Shah Wahid, at the Ideal Convention Centre (IDCC) here today. ... ""We want this product to connect culture, nostalgia and user experience, while also strengthening the position of local brands in the global market. We hope that when the world enjoys this product, they will recognise and feel the uniqueness of Malaysia through every product we create,"" she said. ... Meanwhile, Tengku Norhanim said the introduction of the new product is also aligned with the NIMS Buy & Win Campaign 2026, which runs from Aug 8 to Nov 8. ... In the meantime, Mansor Shah said that agencies and ministries are always ready to assist local entrepreneurs with the potential to expand internationally because success in penetrating foreign markets can have a positive impact on the country's economy, including creating job opportunities. ... ""NIMS made its debut at the Malaysia International Halal Showcase (MIHAS) as early as 2023, just four years after its establishment. It is a proud achievement because Malaysian companies are able to compete in terms of innovation, quality and determination, and the world has responded positively. ... ""After South Africa and Kenya last year, NIMS will join another MATRADE export acceleration programme to Cambodia, which is one of the world's rapidly growing markets with a 46 per cent increase,"" he added. - BERNAMA"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"Plastics industry seeks policy push, eyes RS 1.4-l-cr exports",www.bizzbuzz.news (Bizz Buzz),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.bizzbuzz.news/industry/plastics-industry-seeks-policy-push-eyes-rs-14-l-cr-exports-1400228,"By Bizz Buzz 8 Aug 2026 12:10 AM IST Hyderabad: Plastics industry in India is poised to cross Rs 1.4 lakh crore in exports this year and sustain an annual growth of 6-9 per cent through 2031, but achieving its full potential will require greater investments in infrastructure, technology, skills and sustainability, industry leaders said at HIPLEX 2026 on Friday. ... Speaking at the international plastics exhibition, Dr Raju Desai, President of Plastindia Foundation, said the industry has grown into a Rs 4.5 lakh crore sector employing nearly 55 lakh people. He said India has emerged as one of the world’s leading plastic recyclers, with nearly 60 per cent of consumed plastics being recycled. ... Highlighting the sector’s role in India’s manufacturing ambitions, he said initiatives such as Make in India, Digital India and Skill India have strengthened the ecosystem by encouraging investments, technology adoption and workforce development. He added that the plastics industry would play a pivotal role in helping India achieve its goal of becoming a $7-trillion economy and realise the Viksit Bharat vision. ... Arvind Mehta, Chairman of the Governing Council of the All India Plastics Manufacturers' Association (AIPMA), said the industry must focus on four strategic priorities, including exports, technology adoption, skill development and sustainability. He said India has significant untapped potential to expand exports of plastic products and strengthen its position as a global manufacturing hub. ... Seeking policy support, Anil Reddy Vennam, Senior Vice President of AIPMA, urged the Telangana and Andhra Pradesh governments to establish a dedicated Plastics Park with world-class infrastructure to help MSMEs set up manufacturing units. He also sought the allocation of 250 acres for a Recycling Cluster equipped with a Common Effluent Treatment Plant. Anil Reddy called for greater investments in infrastructure, water management, packaging and medical plastics, with the objective of increasing plastic consumption in Telangana and Andhra Pradesh to two million tonnes by 2030 and raising their combined share in the national market to more than 8 per cent. ... He also said HIPLEX 2026 has been provided with a dedicated 2 MW power supply, enabling exhibitors to conduct live demonstrations of advanced processing machinery, recycling systems, bio-polymers and next-generation polymer technologies. Narendra Baldwa, President of the Telangana and Andhra Plastics Manufacturers Association (TAAPMA), said the 55-year-old association, representing more than 1,000 members, has consistently promoted technology, innovation and sustainability across the plastics industry. ... Pointing to India’s significant growth potential, Jayadev said the country's per capita plastic consumption is only 7 kg, compared with 24 kg in China. Spread across seven exhibition halls covering over 26,000 sq m, HIPLEX 2026 has brought together 550 exhibitors, including around 40 companies from China. A major attraction is the Recycling Pavilion, showcasing how discarded plastics are transformed into roads, railway sleepers, furniture, construction materials and garments."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Plastics manufacturing: Telangana eyes leadership,hyderabadnewshunt.com (HNH Web Desk),2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://hyderabadnewshunt.com/telangana-plastics-manufacturing-hub-hiplex-2026/,"# Telangana aims to emerge as plastics manufacturing hub: Sridhar Babu ... By HNH Web Desk On Aug 7, 2026 Hyderabad: Industries and Commerce Minister D. Sridhar Babu on Friday said Telangana aimed to become a national leader in Plastics manufacturing. He described the sector as a key driver of India’s economic growth. ... Inaugurating HIPLEX 2026 at the HITEX Exhibition Centre, the Minister invited industry stakeholders to partner with the government. Moreover, he urged them to accelerate investment, innovation and sustainable manufacturing in the State. ... Sridhar Babu said the plastics and polymers sector provides direct employment to nearly 50 lakh people. It also supports indirect employment for more than one crore people nationwide. Meanwhile, nearly two lakh families in Telangana depend on the industry for their livelihoods. ... The Minister assured industry representatives of the government’s support for policy reforms. In addition, he said Telangana planned to replicate its success in IT, electronics, pharmaceuticals, GCCs, defence and aerospace in the plastics and polymers sector. ... According to Plastindia Foundation president Raju Desai, India’s plastics industry had grown into a ₹4.5 lakh crore sector. The industry was expanding at 6–9 per cent annually. Exports are expected to cross ₹1.4 lakh crore this year, he said. India also recycles nearly 60 per cent of the plastics it consumes. ... AIPMA Chairman Arvind Mehta called for greater focus on exports, technology adoption, skill development and sustainability. Finally, AIPMA Senior Vice President Anil Reddy Vennam urged Telangana and Andhra Pradesh to establish a dedicated Plastics Park and a 250-acre recycling cluster with a Common Effluent Treatment Plant."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Pregis Acquires MP Global Packaging Cold Chain and Thermal Packaging Business | Packaging Strategies,www.packagingstrategies.com (Packaging Strategies Editorial Team),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packagingstrategies.com/articles/106601-pregis-acquires-mp-global-packaging-cold-chain-and-thermal-packaging-business,"Pregis Acquires MP Global Packaging Cold Chain and Thermal Packaging Business | Packaging Strategies ... # Pregis Acquires MP Global Packaging Cold Chain and Thermal Packaging Business ... Pregis, a global supplier of protective packaging, mailing and bagging solutions and flexible packaging, has acquired MP Global Packaging, a division of MP Global Products. “The acquisition complements the Pregis fiber-based packaging portfolio and supports continued investment in sustainable material innovation and temperature-sensitive shipping solutions,” Pregis notes. ... The acquired business operates two manufacturing facilities — in New Albany, Indiana, and Norfolk, Nebraska — and employs approximately 110 people. It produces paper-based thermal packaging used to protect temperature-sensitive shipments, enabling curbside recycling where collection systems exist. Pregis says it will continue to serve existing customers of the business while investing in scaling the technology. ### Strengthening a Fiber-Based Cold Chain Platform ... Pregis says the acquisition strengthens the company’s position in the growing cold chain market and complements the paper-based cold chain solutions Pregis has been developing. The acquired technology creates packaging that provides thermal insulating properties made from macerated cardboard. Pregis views this capability as a strategic avenue for fiber-based cold chain solutions. ... “This approach mirrors the successful expansion of Pregis EverTec® paper mailer technology, which was acquired in 2020 and scaled into a business producing more than one billion mailers annually across five dedicated manufacturing facilities,” Pregis said in a statement. “Pregis will apply the same investment-led, growth-oriented approach to scale its cold chain platform.” ... “At Pregis, our Purpose and 2K30 commitment challenges us to deliver packaging solutions that create value for our customers while advancing a more sustainable future,” said Kevin Baudhuin, Chairman and CEO of Pregis. “Sustainable, fiber-based materials are an increasingly important part of our portfolio, and cold chain packaging is a natural extension of that strategy. This acquisition brings proven technology, deep expertise, and an experienced team that will help accelerate our ability to scale paper-based thermal solutions and support customers in achieving their own sustainability goals.” ... Reid Borgman, who led the MP Global Packaging division and joins Pregis to continue leading the operation as VP & GM of Cold Chain, said, “Becoming part of Pregis brings more resources and reach to the customers we serve and our employees. Together, we can advance innovation in fiber-based cold chain and expand our portfolio of solutions that deliver the performance, protection and sustainability the market relies on.” ... The business will continue to operate from its current facilities, and Pregis says it will work closely with employees, customers and suppliers throughout the transition."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"Franchise ""Nolbu"" Files for Rehabilitation Amid Soaring Operating Losses - The Asia Business Daily",www.asiae.co.kr (Choi Taewon),2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-06 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2026080618552637959,"Franchise ""Nolbu"" Files for Rehabilitation Amid Soaring Operating Losses - The Asia Business Daily # Franchise ""Nolbu"" Files for Rehabilitation Amid Soaring Operating Losses ... Taewon ... Published 06 Aug.2026 18:55(KST) ## Representative Examination Hearing Scheduled for August 11 ... Nolbu, a franchise restaurant company, has filed for rehabilitation with the court. According to the legal community on August 6, the 15th Division for Rehabilitation of the Seoul Bankruptcy Court (Presiding Judge Kim Yunseon) issued a comprehensive stay order to Nolbu, which had applied for rehabilitation, on August 4. A comprehensive stay order is a measure that freezes all claims until the court decides whether to commence rehabilitation proceedings. ... representative examination hearing is ... Nolbu began in 1987 as a bossam restaurant in Sillim-dong, Gwanak-gu, Seoul. In the 1990s and 2000s, bossam and budae-jjigae were popularized as franchise menu offerings. At one point, the company expanded to operate around 1,000 stores nationwide. ... The sharp increase in operating losses appears to be the main driver behind the application for rehabilitation. According to the electronic disclosure system of the Financial Supervisory Service, last year’s operating loss was approximately KRW 8.69 billion, about 14.8 times greater than in the previous year. ... Revenue also decreased by 16.1% year-on-year to KRW 63.85 billion. Net loss for the period was about KRW 13.93 billion, which is roughly nine times higher than the previous year. Accumulated deficit reached KRW 95.92 billion, up 17.0%. As of the end of last year, the capital impairment ratio was about 82.2%, indicating the company remained in a state of partial capital erosion. ... Meanwhile, since 2024, Nolbu's CEO has been Kim Yongwi, who previously served as the exclusive photographer for former President Yoon Suk-yeol and as the chief of the presidential office media team. The largest shareholder is NB Holdings."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"Oben Group, Think Plastic Brazil member, strengthens presence in Brazil with investment in new BOPP film line - Think Plastic Brazil",thinkplasticbrazil.com (Vinicius),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://thinkplasticbrazil.com/en/oben-group-think-plastic-brazil-member-strengthens-presence-in-brazil-with-investment-in-new-bopp-film-line/,"Oben Group, Think Plastic Brazil member, strengthens presence in Brazil with investment in new BOPP film line - Think Plastic Brazil ... # Oben Group, Think Plastic Brazil member, strengthens presence in Brazil with investment in new BOPP film line - August 5, 2026 New investment reinforces the company’s expansion strategy in the Americas and consolidates its presence in the Brazilian BOPP film market. Oben Group, a global leader in high-performance packaging solutions, announces the signing of an agreement to acquire a new state-of-the-art 12-meter-wide BOPP (Biaxially Oriented Polypropylene) film production line, considered one of the most productive and efficient in the world, destined for the Brazilian market. Oben Group is a member of Think Plastic Brazil, a portfolio of solutions for the converted plastics products sector in the internationalization process for target markets, carried out through a partnership between ApexBrasil (Brazilian Trade and Investment Promotion Agency) and the INP (Brazilian Plastic Institute). ... Following the successful integration of Terphane and Vitopel do Brasil into Oben Group’s operations over the past two years, this new investment responds to the growing need to expand large-scale manufacturing capacity for the Brazilian market. With an annual production capacity of approximately 94,000 metric tons, the new line will significantly expand the company’s manufacturing platform, further strengthening service, flexibility, and supply reliability for customers in Brazil and the Southern Cone. ... The new investment reinforces the company’s long-term commitment to innovation, operational excellence, and strategic growth in the Americas. Equipped with state-of-the-art technology, the new line will increase production efficiency and support the growing demand for high-quality flexible packaging solutions in the region. “Oben Group demonstrates, once again, its capacity to invest in innovation and technology to drive the evolution of the packaging sector. It is a movement that strengthens the entire industry,” states Carlos Moreira, Executive Director of the INP and CPO at Think Plastic Brazil. The new line destined for the Brazilian market is part of Oben Group’s global expansion plan, following the announcement made in February 2025 regarding the acquisition of another 12-meter BOPP line for Mexico. Together, these investments reinforce the company’s position among industry leaders, with advanced large-scale manufacturing capabilities. About Oben Group ... Think Plastic Brazil started its activities with 38 companies and, over the last 20 years, has expanded its participation to more than 250 companies. During this period, the Portfolio promoted 4,773 participations of companies in the industry in 240 projects specifically for Trade Promotion, resulting in 64,366 meetings. The economic impact was significant, with more than US$1.247 billion in business generated and a total investment of US$12.338 million, achieving an impressive ROI of US$101.04 for every dollar invested. ... INP arises amid ... process of globalization and the need to make the plastic market more competitive internationally ... Its strength and representativeness are the results of the union of the Brazilian Processed Plastic and Recycling Industry (ABIPLAST), the ... Association of the Chemical Industry (ABIQUIM), ... the Union of Synthetic Resin Industries in the State of ... As a sectoral technological body, the ... P’s is to be the focal point for the entire plastics production chain in ... To this end, ... body maintains an extensive workforce qualification program, promotes access to ... most modern technologies, especially for small and medium-sized ... , and develops Technical Standards so that products with better quality be manufactured. ... The Brazilian Trade and Investment Promotion Agency (ApexBrasil) works to promote Brazilian products and services abroad and attract foreign investments to strategic sectors of the Brazilian economy. In order to achieve its goals, ApexBrasil carries out several trade promotion initiativesaimed at promoting Brazilian products and services abroad, such as prospective and trade missions, business rounds, support to the participation of Brazilian companies in major international fairs, visits of foreign buyers and opinion makers to learn about the Brazilian productive structure, among other business platforms that also aim at strengthening the Brazil brand. The Agency also acts in a coordinated way with public and private players to attract foreign direct investment (FDI) to Brazil with a focus on strategic sectors for the development of the competitiveness of Brazilian companies and the country."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,NUBURU Receives Italian Regulatory Clearance for Majority Acquisition of Tekne | citybiz,www.citybiz.co (Paul Bluemner),2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.citybiz.co/article/884747/nuburu-receives-italian-regulatory-clearance-for-majority-acquisition-of-tekne/,"NUBURU Receives Italian Regulatory Clearance for Majority Acquisition of Tekne | citybiz ... # NUBURU Receives Italian Regulatory Clearance for Majority Acquisition of Tekne August 5, 2026 NUBURU has received authorization from the Italian government to acquire a 70% controlling interest in defense engineering company Tekne S.p.A., clearing the principal regulatory hurdle for a transaction that would significantly expand the company’s defense and security platform in Europe. ... The approval was granted under Italy’s Golden Power framework, which allows the government to review acquisitions involving businesses operating in strategically important sectors such as defense and national security. The authorization follows a binding share purchase and investment agreement signed on May 26, 2026, and a subsequent regulatory review initiated through a Golden Power notification submitted on June 5. ... The transaction is expected to close within 30 calendar days following satisfaction of the Golden Power condition, subject to the remaining corporate approvals, financing, governance actions and other closing requirements outlined in the agreement. Upon completion, NUBURU expects to own 70% of Tekne and, subject to a final U.S. GAAP accounting assessment, consolidate the Italian company’s financial results. ... The acquisition represents a strategic shift for NUBURU as it builds an integrated defense and security platform centered on dual-use technologies. The company said Tekne will serve as the industrial foundation of its Italy-based operations, adding established engineering, manufacturing and systems integration capabilities across defense mobility, electronic warfare, cyber-electromagnetic activities (CEMA), tactical communications and counter-unmanned aerial systems. ... NUBURU Executive Chairman and Co-Chief Executive Officer Alessandro Zamboni said the government approval marks the company’s transition from regulatory review to transaction execution. He noted that NUBURU has raised acquisition financing, reduced outstanding debt obligations and continued supporting Tekne’s working capital while preparing for the integration process. ... Following the acquisition, NUBURU plans to preserve and expand Tekne’s Italian manufacturing footprint while investing in strategic technologies, production capabilities and workforce development. The company also intends to support existing customer programs, strengthen governance and compliance systems, and pursue growth opportunities across Italian, European Union and NATO defense markets in accordance with applicable procurement, export control and national security regulations. ... The investment agreement values Tekne at a fixed euro-denominated pre-money valuation equivalent to approximately $59.7 million based on the referenced exchange rate. The transaction includes a capital increase equivalent to approximately $34.1 million for a 57.1% ownership interest, NUBURU’s existing 2.9% stake, and an additional cash purchase equivalent to approximately $6 million from existing shareholders to bring total ownership to 70%. The agreement also includes a performance-based earn-out tied to future revenue, subject to specified limits and terms. ... As of July 30, 2026, NUBURU had advanced approximately $23.7 million in shareholder loans to Tekne, with portions expected to be converted into equity at closing under the transaction structure. The company said it recently completed a $38 million public offering and used part of the proceeds to retire approximately $16.75 million of principal debt obligations, with remaining funds intended to support the Tekne acquisition and related working capital requirements. ... The acquisition positions NUBURU to expand from its technology platform into a larger operational defense business with established manufacturing capacity, customer relationships and active production programs. The company believes the transaction will significantly increase its industrial scale while providing a foundation for future growth across European defense and security markets."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Mutares launches former Sabic engineering thermoplastics business as NexPoint - Plastics News,www.plasticsnews.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.plasticsnews.com/suppliers/materials/sp-mutares-sabic-engineering-thermoplastics-business-acquisition-launch-nexpoint/,"Mutares launches former Sabic engineering thermoplastics business as NexPoint - Plastics News ... # Mutares launches former Sabic engineering thermoplastics business as NexPoint ... Sabic's manufacturing site in Cartagena, Spain is one of the acquired business units. (Sabic) ... 04, 2026 04:12 AM EDT"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Mutares (FRA: MUX) completes largest-ever acquisition - Edison Group,www.edisongroup.com,2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.edisongroup.com/spark/mutares-fra-mux-completes-largest-ever-acquisition/DE000A2NB650/,"Mutares (FRA: MUX) completes largest-ever acquisition - Edison Group 4 August 2026 ... Mutares (FRA: MUX) completes largest-ever acquisition Published by Liam O’Byrne Mutares has completed the acquisition of SABIC’s regional Engineering Thermoplastics (ETP) business in the Americas and Europe at an enterprise value of $450m. The deal is the largest transaction in Mutares’ history and anchors its new Chemicals & Materials segment. The acquired business will operate as NexPoint Materials. SABIC has also disclosed an earnout linked to the business’s free cash flow over the next four years and any subsequent sale. ... NexPoint Materials operates eight production facilities across the Americas and Europe, employs c 2,800 people and generates annual revenue of c $2.5bn. Its products include polycarbonate (PC), acrylonitrile butadiene styrene (ABS) and polybutylene terephthalate (PBT) resins and compounds. Mutares describes it as the world’s second-largest PC producer, the leading US ABS producer and the sole US PBT producer. Its end markets include automotive, building and construction, consumer products and electronics. ... The acquisition provides Mutares with an upstream-integrated core platform, broad technical capabilities and an established innovation pipeline through which it can expand its Chemicals & Materials segment. It also materially increases Mutares’ US exposure, with the Americas accounting for 66% of the acquired business’s revenue."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"[더벨]FSN 자회사 부스터즈 '기픈', 와디즈 펀딩 성료 - 머니투데이",www.mt.co.kr (김인규 기자),2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.mt.co.kr/stock/2026/08/05/2026080508389663229,"코스닥 상장사 FSN의 자회사 부스터즈는 스킨 롱제비티 브랜드 ‘기픈(GIPPEUN)’이 와디즈 펀딩을 마무리하고 이를 기반으로 국내 주요 커머스 채널과 북미 아마존 진출을 추진한다고 5일 밝혔다. ... 기픈은 이번 와디즈 펀딩에서 목표 금액을 초과 달성하며 누적 펀딩액 1억원 이상을 기록했다. 여기에 총 1480명의 참여 서포터를 확보해 초기 고객 기반을 마련하고 향후 브랜드 운영에 활용할 후기와 소비자 데이터를 축적했다. ... 부스터즈는 이번 와디즈 펀딩을 브랜드 검증과 초기 충성 고객 확보의 과정으로 삼을 예정이다. 체험단 운영부터 실제 구매, 후기 축적에 이르기까지 단계별 소비자 검증을 거쳤고 이를 통해 확보한 고객 데이터와 피드백을 향후 제품 개선과 마케팅 전략 수립에 반영할 계획이다. ... 부스터즈는 와디즈 펀딩을 통해 확인한 시장 반응을 기반으로 8월 중 본격적인 유통망 확장에 나선다. 네이버 스마트스토어를 비롯한 국내 주요 커머스 채널 입점을 추진함과 동시에 북미에서는 아마존(Amazon) 공식 론칭을 준비하고 있다. 여기에 자사몰을 기반으로 한 프리 론칭을 통해 브랜드 메시지와 소비자 반응을 사전 검증하고 이를 실제 판매 전략에 적용한다는 방침이다. ... 부스터즈 관계자는 ""와디즈 펀딩은 초기 고객 확보를 넘어 기픈의 브랜드 콘셉트와 제품 경쟁력에 대한 소비자들의 긍정적인 시장 반응을 확인한 계기가 됐다""며 ""이번 펀딩을 통해 확보한 고객 데이터와 리뷰 자산을 기반으로 국내 주요 커머스 채널과 북미 아마존까지 사업을 빠르게 확대해 나갈 것""이라고 말했다. ... 이어 ""기픈을 시작으로 차별화된 기술 기반 K-뷰티 브랜드를 지속적으로 육성하며 글로벌 시장에서 경쟁력을 갖춘 브랜드 포트폴리오를 확대해 나갈 계획""이라고 밝혔다."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"Minister Bahati Inspects Najjera Industrial Hub, Commits to Strengthening Support for Local Manufacturers - Uganda Broadcasting Corporation",ubc.go.ug (Uganda Broadcasting Corporation),2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z,2026-08-03 00:00:00+00:00,,https://ubc.go.ug/2026/08/03/minister-bahati-inspects-najjera-industrial-hub-commits-to-strengthening-support-for-local-manufacturers/,"ati Inspects Najjera Industrial Hub, Commits to Strengthening Support for Local Manufacturers ... The State Minister for Industry, Hon. David Bahati has conducted an oversight visit to Najjera Business Hub in the suburbs of Kampala as part of his ongoing routine monitoring of the industrial sector. ... The visit was aimed at evaluating operational efficiency, monitoring production processes, and gaining firsthand insight into the challenges faced by manufacturers, and identifying strategic areas where the government of Uganda can provide targeted support to strengthen productivity and value addition. ... Speaking after touring the business hub, Hon. Bahati commended the investors at the hub for their commitment to value addition, job creation, and supporting the Buy Uganda Build Uganda initiative. “This hub not only adds value to our raw materials but employs over 200 Ugandans and continues to strengthen Uganda export potential,” said Bahati. ... The minister reiterated ... government’s commitment to supporting value ... , especially in cocoa, coffee ... Najjera business hub is home to a number of manufacturing facilities, including ADMA International, Nova Plastic Packaging Ltd, and SAMCO plastics that produce a wide range of products, including plastics, packaging materials, high-end liquid soaps, and animal feeds, among other and other value-added products. ... Speaking on behalf of the investors at Najjera business hub, Laban Musinguzi raised some of the challenges affecting their operations, including the high production costs, access to markets, poor infrastructure, among others that affect their competitiveness. ... Minister Bahati assured the manufacturers of Government’s commitment to working closely with the private sector to address these challenges and ensure that industries have the support they need to expand, increase productivity, and add value to locally available raw materials. ... The factory engagement underscores government commitment to maintaining close collaboration with industrial players, ensuring a conducive business environment, and fostering sustainable growth within Uganda’s industrial value chain. ... The routine visits to industries are designed to assess the performance of industries, identify policy and operational bottlenecks, and strengthen collaboration between government and manufacturers. Such engagements provide valuable feedback that informs interventions aimed at promoting industrialization, boosting value addition, creating jobs, and advancing Uganda’s vision of a resilient and competitive manufacturing sector."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Arburg to acquire Dutch moulding machine maker Stork IMM,www.packaging-gateway.com (Vidhya Edwards Munnangi),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.packaging-gateway.com/news/arburg-to-acquire-stork-imm/,"Arburg to acquire Dutch moulding machine maker Stork IMM ... Arburg is set to acquire Netherlands-based Stork Plastics Machinery (Stork IMM) from Stibbe Participaties, which links two companies in the plastic injection moulding machine sector. ... The acquisition is expected to close in two months, with the financial terms remaining undisclosed. ... Stork IMM CEO Eric Pans added: “The acquisition by Arburg will help to strengthen and expand Stork’s business activities, among other things through international sales and service capacities, a broader product range, synergies in purchasing and supply chain, as well as further professionalisation of processes.” ... German family-owned company Arburg is among the leading global producers of injection moulding machines. The wider Arburg group also includes AMKmotion, which makes electric drive systems. ... systems and turnkey systems tailored ... digital products and services ... Arburg’s machines are used to make plastic products for sectors, including construction and equipment engineering, electronics, leisure, medicine, mobility, and packaging. ... Based in Lossburg, Germany, the company also has its own operations at 37 sites in 27 countries and, together with trading partners, has a presence in more than 100 countries. ... Arburg CEO Volker Nilles said: “With this acquisition, two strong brands that have been well known on the market for many decades are now coming together: a clear win-win situation for everyone, and especially for customers.”"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Minister Bahati Commends Najjera Business Hub During Industry Inspection - Ugnews Line,www.ugnewsline.com (J Andrew),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ugnewsline.com/minister-bahati-commends-najjera-business-hub-during-industry-inspection/,"Business Hub During ... Minister Bahati Commends Najjera Business Hub During Industry Inspection ... engagements also provide valuable feedback that informs interventions aimed at promoting industrialisation ... expanding value addition ... by J Andrew July 31, 2026 The State Minister for Industry, Hon. David Bahati, has conducted an oversight visit to Najjera Business Hub on the outskirts of Kampala as part of the government’s routine monitoring of Uganda’s industrial sector. The visit was aimed at assessing operational efficiency, reviewing production processes, understanding the challenges faced by manufacturers, and identifying strategic areas where the government can provide targeted support to boost productivity and value addition. ... After touring the hub, Hon. Bahati praised the investors for their commitment to value addition, job creation, and advancing the Buy Uganda, Build Uganda (BUBU) initiative. ... “This hub not only adds value to our raw materials but also employs more than 200 Ugandans and continues to strengthen Uganda’s export potential,” Bahati said. ... He reaffirmed the government’s commitment to supporting value chains, particularly in cocoa, coffee, and other locally available raw materials, as part of efforts to accelerate industrial growth and economic prosperity. ... Najjera Business Hub hosts several manufacturing companies, including ADMA International, Nova Plastic Packaging Ltd, and SAMCO Plastics. The firms produce a wide range of products, including plastic goods, packaging materials, premium liquid soaps, animal feeds, and other value-added products. ... Speaking on behalf of the investors, Laban Musinguzi highlighted several challenges affecting their operations, including high production costs, limited market access, and inadequate infrastructure, which continue to undermine their competitiveness. In response, Minister Bahati assured manufacturers of the government’s commitment to working closely with the private sector to address these challenges and create an enabling environment for industries to expand, increase productivity, and enhance value addition. ... The visit underscores the government’s commitment to strengthening collaboration with manufacturers, improving the business environment, and promoting sustainable growth across Uganda’s industrial sector. ... Routine industry inspections are intended to evaluate the performance of manufacturing enterprises, identify policy and operational bottlenecks, and strengthen partnerships between government and the private sector."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Wipro expands PH portfolio with S Brands acquisition,newsbytes.ph (Jinji Quiambao),2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-31 00:00:00+00:00,,https://newsbytes.ph/2026/07/31/wipro-expands-ph-portfolio-with-s-brands-acquisition/,"Wipro expands PH portfolio with S Brands acquisition ... # Wipro expands PH portfolio with S Brands acquisition ... Wipro Consumer Care International (WCCI) has acquired 100% of Philippine personal care company S Brands Consumer Care Inc., adding brands such as KERATINplus, AlcoPlus, DeoPlus, and Fiona Cologne to its portfolio. ... The deal marks Wipro’s second acquisition in the Philippines after it bought Splash Corporation in 2019. Splash owns personal care brands including SkinWhite, Maxi-Peel, and Vitress. ... S Brands’ portfolio includes hair treatment brand KERATINplus, hygiene brand AlcoPlus, and fragrance and deodorant products sold under DeoPlus and Fiona Cologne. Wipro said the acquisition would support plans to bring some of these brands to markets outside the Philippines. ... “This acquisition is an important milestone in our journey to become one of Asia’s leading personal care companies. It reinforces our long-term commitment to the Philippines and our focus on investing in high-growth emerging markets,” Wipro Consumer Care International president and chief operating officer Nagender Arya said. ... WCCI, the international consumer care arm of Wipro Enterprises, reported annual global revenue of more than $1.2 billion. It operates in over 18 countries and markets more than 37 brands across over 60 countries. ... The company is targeting growth in the Philippine hair care, skin care, fragrance, and hygiene segments. It described the country as Southeast Asia’s fourth-largest personal care market. ... “S Brands is growing and we’re ready to reach more people in more markets. Wipro has the track record and global reach to help make that happen. Together, we can enhance our offerings and give back to communities, a value shared by both companies,” S Brands founder and president Dick Sy Ong said."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Plastic Packaging’s Oshakati branch to improve service - New Era,neweralive.na (Pricilla Mukokobi),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://neweralive.na/plastic-packagings-oshakati-branch-to-improve-service/,"Plastic Packaging’s Oshakati branch to improve service - New Era ... Businesses and consumers in northern Namibia are expected to benefit from faster access to packaging products following the opening of Plastic Packaging Namibia’s new branch in Oshakati. ... The company officially inaugurated the branch on Friday, saying the investment will improve product availability, reduce delivery times and strengthen support for businesses across the region. ... consists of a ... 2 100- ... metre warehouse, ... It will serve as a regional distribution centre for customers in central and north-western Namibia. ... Plastic Packaging Namibia managing director Nico du Plessis said the branch was opened in response to growing demand in northern Namibia. ... “The Oshakati branch is an important investment that strengthens our ability to serve customers across northern Namibia. By increasing our stockholding capacity and improving our logistics, we will provide faster deliveries, better product availability and improved customer service,” he said. ... “Customers will now have easier access to a full range of packaging products through our retail outlet, while businesses will benefit from quicker deliveries and improved logistical support,” Du Plessis said. ... The company said the Oshakati branch will help meet the growing demand for packaging solutions while bringing services closer to customers. ... , Immigration, Safety and Security Minister ... said private sector investment plays a key role in developing regional economies. ... Oshakati mayor Leonard Hango welcomed the investment, saying it reflects growing confidence in the town as a business hub for northern Namibia. ... Plastic Packaging Namibia chairman Frank Fredericks said the company remains committed to expanding its services across the country. ... “This branch represents another important step in strengthening our national footprint. We will continue investing in infrastructure, technology and our people to ensure customers receive world-class products and services wherever they are in Namibia,” he said. ... Plastic Packaging Namibia is one of the country’s leading manufacturers and suppliers of packaging products. he company said the Oshakati branch forms part of its long-term strategy to improve service delivery while supporting Namibia’s economic and industrial growth."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Exim Banca Romaneasca Supports TeraPlast’s Expansion in Europe: €14.7 Million for Investments in Hungary and Spain - Lovitura de Presa,lovitura.ro (Ioana Pop),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://lovitura.ro/2026/07/30/exim-banca-romaneasca-supports-teraplasts-expansion-in-europe-e14-7-million-for-investments-in-hungary-and-spain/,"Exim Banca Romaneasca Supports TeraPlast’s Expansion in Europe: €14.7 Million for Investments in Hungary and Spain - Lovitura de Presa ... Romaneasca Supports Tera ... ast’s ... Bucharest, 29 July 2026 – Exim Banca Romaneasca has supported the European expansion of TeraPlast Group, the largest polymer processor in Southeast Europe, by financing the group’s acquisitions of production facilities in Hungary and Spain. ... The total financing provided by the bank amounts to €14.7 million and coveres, among other things, the acquisition of Wavin Hungary’s PVC and polyethylene pipe production assets (completed in 2025), as well as the acquisition of a polyethylene pipe manufacturing plant in Spain, previously part of the MASA division of the Aliaxis Group, a transaction finalized earlier this month. ... Through this financing agreement, Exim Banca Romaneasca contributes to strengthening the international presence of one of Romania’s most important industrial groups with majority Romanian ownership. ... “Romania needs an increasing number of companies owned by Romanian capital that can prove their competitiveness on international markets, as TeraPlast Group is doing today. As a Romanian bank, Exim Banca Romaneasca understands the challenges and opportunities faced by local companies and has extensive experience with successful partnerships that prove how performance is achieved when entrepreneurs benefit from tailored financial solutions offered by a partner that supports their growth objectives. Supporting the internationalization of Romanian companies remains a strategic priority for us, and we will continue to work together with those that choose to expand beyond the country’s borders,” said Traian Halalai, Executive President of Exim Banca Romaneasca, during the inauguration of TeraPlast’s new production facility in Spain. ... Spain becomes the fifth foreign market in which TeraPlast Group operates, following its expansion into Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia. ... The production facility, located in Okondo in northern Spain and inaugurated at the end of last week, has an annual production capacity of 16,000 tonnes. The plant serves a solid customer base in Spain, France, and Germany, and generated €29.4 million in revenue in 2025. ... “After Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia, TeraPlast is now producing in Spain. We have added another marker of Romanian industry on the map of Western Europe, demonstrating that Romanians can invest, build industry, and generate profit in Western European markets. Moreover, throughout this process we were supported by a 100% Romanian bank, Exim Banca Romaneasca, a trusted partner in our expansion plans. Together, we are proving that through courage and vision, Romanians can have a strong voice at the European level,” said Alexandru Stânean, CEO of TeraPlast Group. ... The Spanish plastic pipes market is the seventh largest in Europe, offering significant growth potential. Through this transaction, TeraPlast strengthens its position as a major regional player and takes a significant step toward becoming a European supplier with an extensive international presence. ... TeraPlast Group is the largest polymer processor in Southeast Europe. The Group includes TeraPlast (Romania, Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Spain), TeraGlass (Romania), TeraPlast Recycling (Romania), TeraBio Pack (Romania), Pro-Moulding (Romania and Hungary), Optiplast (Croatia), and Aquatica Experience Group (Romania). The Group’s parent company, TeraPlast SA, has been listed on the Bucharest Stock Exchange since July 2, 2008, under the ticker symbol TRP."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Manila Bulletin - nubia expands the NEOverse with new product ecosystem,mb.com.ph (Manila Bulletin Newsroom),2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mb.com.ph/2026/07/30/nubia-expands-the-neoverse-with-new-product-ecosystem,"Manila Bulletin - nubia expands the NEOverse with new product ecosystem ... # nubia expands the NEOverse with new product ecosystem ... Published Jul 30, 2026 10:08 am ... The NEOVerse is expanding. As part of its #NEOVerseMaxOut: Max Out Your World campaign, nubia is taking the next step in building a smarter, more connected ecosystem in the Philippines with the launch of its first-ever lineup of mobile accessories. ... Designed to complement today's gaming, entertainment, and always-on lifestyles, the nubia LiveBuds 3 Pro, nubia LiveFlip, and nubia 80W Three-Port GaN Quick Charger make it easier for users to game, work, stream, and stay powered throughout the day. Together with the expanded nubia Neo 5 Series, the new accessories reinforce nubia's commitment to delivering an ecosystem of intelligent devices and experiences that seamlessly work together. ... The launch forms part of nubia's #NEOVerseMaxOut: Max Out Your World campaign, which officially launches on July 29 and invites users to unlock bigger possibilities through a growing ecosystem of products, partnerships, and experiences. ... More than a smartphone campaign, #NEOVerseMaxOut represents nubia's vision of empowering users to maximize every moment—whether gaming, streaming, creating content, or staying productive on the go. Following the introduction of the nubia Neo 5 Max and nubia Neo 5 GT Special Edition, nubia now completes the experience with its first-ever ecosystem accessories in the Philippines, bringing greater convenience, intelligent connectivity, and all-day performance to Filipino consumers. ... The expansion of the NEOVerse goes beyond hardware. Customers can also look forward to exciting ecosystem partnerships and community-driven experiences, including FREE three-month VIU subscriptions with participating Neo 5 Series smartphone purchases during the campaign period. nubia will also introduce its upcoming partnership with Cotti Coffee, featuring exclusive coffee voucher bundles and social media activations, as well as the highly anticipated nubia Social Run initiative, bringing the brand's gaming and lifestyle ecosystem closer to its growing community of Filipino users. ... Together, these launches and collaborations showcase nubia's commitment to building a lifestyle ecosystem that seamlessly integrates gaming, entertainment, productivity, and everyday experiences. ... Together, the nubia LiveBuds 3 Pro, nubia LiveFlip, and nubia 80W Three-Port GaN Quick Charger reinforce nubia's vision of delivering a connected ecosystem that extends beyond smartphones. By combining intelligent audio, reliable power solutions, and seamless compatibility, the accessories empower users to stay productive, entertained, and connected wherever life takes them. ... As the NEOVerse continues to expand, nubia remains committed to bringing innovative technologies, meaningful partnerships, and immersive experiences to Filipino consumers. Through the #NEOVerseMaxOut: Max Out Your World campaign, the brand is creating a smarter and more connected ecosystem that empowers users to maximize every experience—from gaming and entertainment to work, lifestyle, and everyday life. ... The nubia LiveBuds 3 Pro will be available in White with a launch price of P1,999. ... The nubia LiveFlip will be available in White and Dark Blue with a launch price of P1,999. ... The nubia 80W Three-Port GaN Quick Charger will be available at a launch price of P1,199."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Exim Banca Romaneasca Supports TeraPlast’s Expansion in Europe: €14.7 Million for Investments in Hungary and Spain - Exim - Banca Romaneasca,www.eximbank.ro (Miruna Lebedencu),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.eximbank.ro/en/2026/07/29/exim-banca-romaneasca-supports-teraplasts-expansion-in-europe-e14-7-million-for-investments-in-hungary-and-spain/,"Exim Banca Romaneasca has supported the European expansion of TeraPlast Group, the largest polymer processor in Southeast Europe, by financing the company’s acquisitions of production facilities in Hungary and Spain. ... The total financing provided by the bank amounts to €14.7 million and coveres, among other things, the acquisition of Wavin Hungary’s PVC and polyethylene pipe production assets (completed in 2025), as well as the acquisition of a polyethylene pipe manufacturing plant in Spain, previously part of the MASA division of the Aliaxis Group, a transaction finalized earlier this month. ... Through this financing agreement, Exim Banca Romaneasca contributes to strengthening the international presence of one of Romania’s most important industrial groups with majority Romanian ownership. ... “Romania needs an increasing number of companies owned by Romanian capital that can prove their competitiveness on international markets, as TeraPlast Group is doing today. As a Romanian bank, Exim Banca Romaneasca understands the challenges and opportunities faced by local companies and has extensive experience with successful partnerships that prove how performance is achieved when entrepreneurs benefit from tailored financial solutions offered by a partner that supports their growth objectives. Supporting the internationalization of Romanian companies remains a strategic priority for us, and we will continue to work together with those that choose to expand beyond the country’s borders,” said Traian Halalai, Executive President of Exim Banca Romaneasca, during the inauguration of TeraPlast’s new production facility in Spain. ... Spain becomes the fifth foreign market in which TeraPlast Group operates, following its expansion into Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia. ... The production facility, located in Okondo in northern Spain and inaugurated at the end of last week, has an annual production capacity of 16,000 tonnes. The plant serves a solid customer base in Spain, France, and Germany, and generated €29.4 million in revenue in 2025. ... “After Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia, TeraPlast is now producing in Spain. We have added another marker of Romanian industry on the map of Western Europe, demonstrating that Romanians can invest, build industry, and generate profit in Western European markets. Moreover, throughout this process we were supported by a 100% Romanian bank, Exim Banca Romaneasca, a trusted partner in our expansion plans. Together, we are proving that through courage and vision, Romanians can have a strong voice at the European level,” said Alexandru Stânean, CEO of TeraPlast Group. ... The Spanish plastic pipes market is the seventh largest in Europe, offering significant growth potential. Through this transaction, TeraPlast strengthens its position as a major regional player and takes a significant step toward becoming a European supplier with an extensive international presence. ... TeraPlast Group is the largest polymer processor in Southeast Europe. The Group includes TeraPlast (Romania, Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Spain), TeraGlass (Romania), TeraPlast Recycling (Romania), TeraBio Pack (Romania), Pro-Moulding (Romania and Hungary), Optiplast (Croatia), and Aquatica Experience Group (Romania). The Group’s parent company, TeraPlast SA, has been listed on the Bucharest Stock Exchange since July 2, 2008, under the ticker symbol TRP"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Kritis Plastics seeks to acquire Moroccan Naturplas Industrial. - en.mcg24.com,en.mcg24.com,2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://en.mcg24.com/kritis-plastics-seeks-to-acquire-moroccan-naturplas-industrial/,"Kritis Plastics seeks to acquire Moroccan Naturplas Industrial. - en.mcg24.com ... ## Greek Company Plastika Kritis SA Expands Into the Moroccan Market ... Plastika Kritis SA, a Greek company, is continuing its international expansion by focusing on the Moroccan market. The firm has announced its plans to acquire 100% of the shares of Naturplas Industrial SARL, a Moroccan-based company specializing in the production of plastic solutions for the agricultural sector. ... This operation, which remains subject to approval from the Competition Authority, marks a new milestone in the development of the plasticulture market in the Kingdom. ... The project involves the purchase of 100% of Naturplas Industrial’s shares as well as all voting rights associated with the company. Once validated by the relevant authorities, this acquisition will allow Plastika Kritis to gain full control over the Moroccan enterprise. ... This move is part of the Greek group’s expansion strategy, which is already present in several international markets in the field of agricultural plastic films. ... Based in Heraklion, Crete, Plastika Kritis SA is renowned for manufacturing and marketing plastic films designed for agricultural use. Its catalog includes mulch films, covers for greenhouses and agricultural tunnels, silage films, and biodegradable solutions that meet new environmental standards. ... Naturplas Industrial, headquartered in Tangier with a production facility in Tétouan, offers a wide range of products for agricultural enterprises. The company produces greenhouse films, mulch films, irrigation sleeves, silage tarps, and insect protection nets. ... Through this operation, the Greek group is strengthening its position in the plasticulture market, a sector encompassing all plastic products used in agricultural activities to boost yields, optimize irrigation, and protect crops. ... If it receives the green light from the Competition Authority, this acquisition could enhance the industrial capabilities of the sector and support the development of innovative agricultural solutions in Morocco."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Plastic Packaging goes north - Namibian Sun,www.namibiansun.com (Augetto Graig),2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.namibiansun.com/mw-main/plastic-packaging-goes-north-NMH014428-3015-17918,"Plastic Packaging goes north - Namibian Sun Frank Fredericks, chairman of Plastic Packaging Namibia, is all smiles with the minister of home affairs, immigration, safety and security, Lucia Iipumbu.Photo Plastic Packaging Namibia Plastic Packaging promises that the new ... akati branch will improve ... Plastic Packaging Namibia ... availability is one of the reasons why ... a new branch in Oshakati ... Plastic Packaging Namibia has expanded its national distribution network with the opening of a new branch in Oshakati, a move aimed at improving product availability and delivery times across northern Namibia. ... The facility, officially inaugurated on 24 July, is located in the Oshakati Industrial Area along Oshikango Road. It comprises approximately 2,100 square metres of warehouse, retail and office space and has been developed as a regional distribution centre serving central and north-western Namibia. ... Marking what the company described as a significant milestone in its continued expansion, the new facility reinforces its commitment to customers in northern Namibia. ... According to the company, ""The investment reflects Plastic Packaging Namibia's confidence in the region's economic growth and its long-term commitment to supporting businesses and communities across northern Namibia."" ... Plastic Packaging Namibia said the Oshakati branch will increase stockholding capacity and improve logistics, enabling faster deliveries, improved product availability and enhanced customer service across the region. ... The facility also includes a dedicated retail outlet, providing customers with access to a comprehensive range of packaging products. ... Oshakati mayor Leonard Hango delivered the welcoming address, while Plastic Packaging Namibia managing director Nico du Plessis presented an overview of the company's operations and expansion strategy. ... Delivering the keynote address, home affairs, immigration, safety and security minister Lucia Iipumbu highlighted the role of private sector investment in regional development, job creation and industrialisation. ... Iipumbu was introduced by Oshana governor Hofni Iipinge, while Plastic Packaging Namibia chairman Frank Fredericks delivered the vote of thanks and outlined the company's strategic outlook. ... Plastic Packaging Namibia said the Oshakati branch would provide ""improved service levels through increased local stock availability, faster and more efficient product distribution, convenient over-the-counter purchasing through the retail outlet, increased capacity to meet the growing demand for quality packaging solutions, and enhanced logistical support for customers across the region."" ... The company said the new branch represents another step in its expansion strategy, ""while contributing to Namibia's economic growth and industrial development."" ... Plastic Packaging Namibia added that it would continue investing in infrastructure, technology and people to ensure customers receive ""world-class products and service throughout the country."""
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Press release from the Competition Council regarding the economic concentration project concerning the exclusive takeover by the company “Plastika Kritis SA” of the company “Naturplas Industrial SARL” - Conseil de la concurrence du Maroc,conseil-concurrence.ma (Youssef OTMANE),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://conseil-concurrence.ma/en/press-release-from-the-competition-council-regarding-the-economic-concentration-project-concerning-the-exclusive-takeover-by-the-company-plastika-kritis-sa-of-the-company-na/,"Press release from the Competition Council regarding the economic concentration project concerning the exclusive takeover by the company “Plastika Kritis SA” of the company “Naturplas Industrial SARL” - Conseil de la concurrence du Maroc ... # Press release from the Competition Council regarding the economic concentration project concerning the exclusive takeover by the company “Plastika Kritis SA” of the company “Naturplas Industrial SARL” ... - The acquirer: the company “Plastika Kritis SA”; - The target: the company “Naturplas Industrial SARL”. ... - Exclusive takeover. ... - Manufacture of plastic products for agricultural use “plasticulture”. ... The Competition Council received notification of an economic concentration project concerning the exclusive takeover by the company “Plastika Kritis SA” of the company “Naturplas Industrial SARL”, through the acquisition of 100% of its share capital and related voting rights. ... “Plastika Kritis SA” is a Greek anonymous company, registered under number GRS326003019, with its head office located in the Industrial Zone of Cranea, Heraklion, Crete, Greece. The company is active in the manufacture and distribution of plastic films for agricultural use, including mulch films, greenhouse and tunnel films, silage sheets, and biodegradable films. ... “Naturplas Industrial SARL” is a Moroccan limited liability company with its head office at Place Almadina, Jabal Tarik Street, Dar Al Farah 2 Residence, 5th floor, apartment No. 96, in Tanger, registered with the Tanger Trade Register under number 165363. It is engaged in the manufacture of films and plastic products for agricultural use, including mulch films, greenhouse and tunnel films, irrigation sleeves, silage films, and anti-insect nets, from its production unit located in Tetouan. ... Done in Rabat, July 27, 2026"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Le grec Plastika Kritis prépare son entrée dans la plasticulture marocaine - Le Nouvelliste Maroc,www.lenouvelliste.ma (Rédaction),2026-07-27T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-27 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.lenouvelliste.ma/le-grec-plastika-kritis-prepare-son-entree-dans-la-plasticulture-marocaine/,"Le grec Plastika Kritis prépare son entrée dans la plasticulture marocaine - Le Nouvelliste Maroc ... # Le grec Plastika Kritis prépare son entrée dans la plasticulture marocaine ... Le grec Plastika Kritis prépare son entrée dans la plasticulture marocaine ... Le groupe grec Plastika Kritis SA projette de prendre le contrôle intégral de Naturplas Industrial SARL, une société marocaine spécialisée dans les solutions plastiques destinées au secteur agricole. ... L’opération prévoit l’acquisition de 100 % du capital social de Naturplas Industrial ainsi que de l’ensemble des droits de vote qui y sont attachés. Elle reste soumise à l’examen de l’autorité de la concurrence. ... Plastika Kritis est implantée à Héraklion, en Crète. L’entreprise fabrique et commercialise plusieurs catégories de films plastiques à usage agricole, notamment pour le paillage, les serres, les tunnels et l’ensilage. Son offre comprend également des films biodégradables. ... Naturplas Industrial, dont le siège social est établi à Tanger, dispose d’une unité de production à Tétouan. La société produit notamment des films de paillage, des films pour serres et tunnels, des gaines d’irrigation, des bâches d’ensilage et des filets anti-insectes. ... Ce projet de concentration concerne ainsi le marché de la plasticulture, qui regroupe les produits plastiques utilisés dans les activités agricoles."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Romanian manufacturer TeraPlast inaugurates polyethylene pipe factory in Spain | Romania Insider,www.romania-insider.com,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.romania-insider.com/teraplast-inaugurates-spain-factory-july-2026,"Romanian building materials manufacturer TeraPlast Group inaugurated its TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene pipe factory in Spain, strengthening its expansion into Western European markets. The facility, located near Bilbao, is expected to serve customers across Spain, France, and North Africa. ... The factory, inaugurated on July 23, is located in Okondo, in Spain's Álava province, about 20 kilometers from Bilbao. It has an annual production capacity of 16,000 tonnes and employs 79 people. ... The opening follows TeraPlast's acquisition of the facility and forms part of the group's international expansion strategy after earlier investments in the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia. ... “Romanian industry can compete and thrive at European level, and we demonstrate it through actions, not idealistic speeches. Following our expansion into the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria and Croatia, our entry into the Spanish market marks another important step in our international growth strategy,” said Dorel Goia, chairman of the TeraPlast Board of Directors. ... The company plans to invest EUR 4 million in the Spanish factory over the next three years to increase production by 60% and achieve an EBITDA margin of more than 10%. ... “The expanded production capacity will serve the markets of Spain, France, and North Africa. This will enable us to reduce leverage while generating returns on our investment for the benefit of the group's shareholders,"" Goia added. ... According to the company, the factory has an established customer base in Spain, France, and Germany and will serve as a regional hub for the group's operations in Western Europe. ... TeraPlast Group is the largest polymer processor in Southeastern Europe and operates production facilities in Romania, the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria, Croatia, and Spain. Its parent company, TeraPlast SA, is listed on the Bucharest Stock Exchange under the symbol TRP. ... Romanian building materials manufacturer TeraPlast Group inaugurated its TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene pipe factory in Spain, strengthening its expansion into Western European markets. The facility, located near Bilbao, is expected to serve customers across Spain, France, and North Africa. ... The factory, inaugurated on July 23, is located in Okondo, in Spain's Álava province, about 20 kilometers from Bilbao. It has an annual production capacity of 16,000 tonnes and employs 79 people. ... The opening follows TeraPlast's acquisition of the facility and forms part of the group's international expansion strategy after earlier investments in the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia. ... “Romanian industry can compete and thrive at European level, and we demonstrate it through actions, not idealistic speeches. Following our expansion into the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria and Croatia, our entry into the Spanish market marks another important step in our international growth strategy,” said Dorel Goia, chairman of the TeraPlast Board of Directors. ... The company plans to invest EUR 4 million in the Spanish factory over the next three years to increase production by 60% and achieve an EBITDA margin of more than 10%. ... “The expanded production capacity will serve the markets of Spain, France, and North Africa. This will enable us to reduce leverage while generating returns on our investment for the benefit of the group's shareholders,"" Goia added. ... According to the company, the factory has an established customer base in Spain, France, and Germany and will serve as a regional hub for the group's operations in Western Europe. ... TeraPlast Group is the largest polymer processor in Southeastern Europe and operates production facilities in Romania, the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria, Croatia, and Spain. Its parent company, TeraPlast SA, is listed on the Bucharest Stock Exchange under the symbol TRP. ... Romanian building materials manufacturer TeraPlast Group inaugurated its TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene pipe factory in Spain, strengthening its expansion into Western European markets. The facility, located near Bilbao, is expected to serve customers across Spain, France, and North Africa. ... The factory, inaugurated on July 23, is located in Okondo, in Spain's Álava province, about 20 kilometers from Bilbao. It has an annual production capacity of 16,000 tonnes and employs 79 people. ... The opening follows TeraPlast's acquisition of the facility and forms part of the group's international expansion strategy after earlier investments in the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria, and Croatia. ... “Romanian industry can compete and thrive at European level, and we demonstrate it through actions, not idealistic speeches. Following our expansion into the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria and Croatia, our entry into the Spanish market marks another important step in our international growth strategy,” said Dorel Goia, chairman of the TeraPlast Board of Directors. ... The company plans to invest EUR 4 million in the Spanish factory over the next three years to increase production by 60% and achieve an EBITDA margin of more than 10%. ... “The expanded production capacity will serve the markets of Spain, France, and North Africa. This will enable us to reduce leverage while generating returns on our investment for the benefit of the group's shareholders,"" Goia added. ... According to the company, the factory has an established customer base in Spain, France, and Germany and will serve as a regional hub for the group's operations in Western Europe. ... TeraPlast Group is the largest polymer processor in Southeastern Europe and operates production facilities in Romania, the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria, Croatia, and Spain. Its parent company, TeraPlast SA, is listed on the Bucharest Stock Exchange under the symbol TRP."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,TeraPlast Group inaugurated the TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene factory in Spain | KomuniK Europe,komunik.eu,2026-07-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://komunik.eu/teraplast-group-inaugurated-the-teraplast-iberia-polyethylene-factory-in-spain/,"TeraPlast Group inaugurated the TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene factory in Spain | KomuniK Europe ... # TeraPlast Group inaugurated the TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene factory in Spain ... TeraPlast Group inaugurated its TeraPlast Iberia polyethylene pipe factory in Spain, a firm and important step in its development strategy aiming the European markets. Thanks to the plant's strategic location, the Group will be ideally positioned to serve customers across Western Europe and North Africa. ... The inauguration ceremony was attended by representatives of TeraPlast Group management, alongside Her Majesty Margareta Custodian of the Romanian Crown, His Royal Highness Prince Radu of Romania, Her Excellency Raluca Mihăilă, Chargé d'Affaires a.i. at the Romanian Embassy in the Kingdom of Spain, Mrs. Bianca Gavriliță, General Consul of Romania in Bilbao, Mr. Bogdan-Gruia Ivan, Member of the Romanian Parliament, Mr. Emil Boc, Mayor of Cluj-Napoca, Mr. Gabriel Lazany, Mayor of Bistrița, as well as Spanish public officials, respectively Mrs. Saray Zárate Fernández de Landa, Provincial Deputy of Development and Innovation of Álava, Mr. Andoitz Korta Zearreta, Deputy Advisor for Industrial Promotion of the Basque Government Council and Mr. Jon Escuza del Campo, Mayor of Okondo, where the TeraPlast Iberia factory is located. Their presence highlighted the strong institutional support for Romanian investment, the importance of industrial development within the European Union Single Market, and the continued strengthening of bilateral relations between Romania and Spain. ... ”Romanian industry can compete and thrive at European level, and we demonstrate it through actions, not idealistic speeches. Following our expansion into the Republic of Moldova, Hungary, Austria and Croatia, our entry into the Spanish market marks another important step in our international growth strategy, once again proving that we do not waste time but move forward with vision, determination and confidence across Europe. ... Now that the acquisition has been completed, we are launching the integration and consolidation process. Through investments of EUR 4 million, we aim to increase production by 60% over the next three years and achieve an EBITDA margin of more than 10%. The expanded production capacity will serve the markets of Spain, France and North Africa. This will enable us to reduce leverage while generating returns on our investment for the benefit of the Group's shareholders.” stated Mr. Dorel Goia, Chairman of the TeraPlast Board of Directors. ... The TeraPlast Iberia factory is located in Okondo, in the province of Álava, Northern Spain, approximately 20 kilometers from Bilbao, and has an annual production capacity of 16.000 tonnes. With a team of 79 employees and a solid customer base in Spain, France and Germany, the factory will serve as a strategic hub for the expansion of TeraPlast's operations in Western Europe and further strengthen the Group's international presence."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Family wins grand prize in nubia PH campaign - NewsCentral,newscentralmedia.com (Myke Soon),2026-07-23T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,,https://newscentralmedia.com/family-wins-grand-prize-in-nubia-ph-campaign/,"# Family wins grand prize in nubia PH campaign ... NUBIA Philippines concluded its four-month #EnterTheNEOverse campaign with the turnover of its grand prize — a Geely GX3 Pro car and a nubia Neo 5 GT smartphone — to a Filipino family whose entry started with an ordinary upgrade. ... The winning entry belonged to Clark Adel Marquez, drawn from a nubia Neo 5 Series unit his father, Adel Era Marquez, had purchased. What began as a routine phone upgrade turned into a genuine family milestone, with the Marquez family going home with both prizes at the official turnover — the kind of story that makes a raffle promo feel a little more human than the usual giveaway headline. ... The campaign leaned hard into the local gaming scene from the start. Alongside its March launch at SM Megamall with ambassadors ONIC Philippines and actress Sanya Lopez, nubia ran the Clash of Sonics Community Tournament with UNISOC and ONIC Philippines, giving grassroots mobile esports teams a genuine stage rather than just a marketing tie-in. ... Champion team Totch ODK Heroes took home five nubia Neo 5 5G units, followed by months of TikTok activations, creator collaborations, and livestreams that kept the campaign visible well past launch day. ... The end of nubia PH’s campaign does not mean it is totally over. The company is getting ready for its next chapter, #NEOverseMaxOut, as it launches this August with two new devices — the nubia Neo 5 Max and Neo 5 GT Special Edition — aimed at expanding the NEOverse beyond gaming into everyday lifestyle use: entertainment, creativity, and productivity alike."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,nubia PH Awards Geely Car in #EnterTheNEOverse; Teases Neo 5 Max,www.teknogadyet.com (Staff ni Anjie),2026-07-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.teknogadyet.com/2026/07/nubia-neo-5-max-philippines.html,"# nubia PH Concludes #EnterTheNEOverse Campaign with Geely Car Turnover; Teases August Expansion ... nubia Philippines has officially wrapped up its multi-month #EnterTheNEOverse campaign, holding a ceremonial grand prize handover for its nationwide ""Your Next Phone Could Be Your Next Ride"" raffle promotion. Grand raffle winner Clark Adel Marquez officially took home a brand-new Geely GX3 Pro crossover alongside a nubia Neo 5 GT smartphone. ... The campaign finale marks the conclusion of a four-month integrated rollout that combined immersive hardware launch zones, grassroots mobile esports tournaments, and strategic brand partnerships. During the turnover event, the brand also dropped teasers for its next evolution: the upcoming #NEOverseMaxOut launch scheduled for August 2026. ... Editor’s Note: This article provides a comprehensive overview of nubia Philippines' campaign finale and upcoming August product teasers. All details reflect official brand announcements updated for July 2026. ... The highlight of the #EnterTheNEOverse campaign was the ceremonial turnover of the grand raffle prize—a brand-new Geely GX3 Pro crossover vehicle. The winning raffle entry belonged to Clark Adel Marquez, whose entry was generated when his father, Adel Era Marquez, purchased a qualifying nubia Neo 5 Series handset. ... In addition to driving home the crossover vehicle, the Marquez family also received a new nubia Neo 5 GT smartphone to complete their grand prize package. ... Beyond promotional giveaways, nubia Philippines actively expanded its local footprint through community-level mobile gaming initiatives. Partnering with chipset maker UNISOC and esports powerhouses ONIC Philippines, the brand hosted the Clash of Sonics Community Tournament. ... Grassroots gaming team Totch ODK Heroes emerged as the tournament champions, winning five nubia Neo 5 5G smartphones. Powered by the UNISOC T9300 octa-core processor, the devices were awarded during the live 6.6 NEOverse Hypermode broadcast, demonstrating nubia's commitment to supporting rising esports talent across the country. ... ## 3. Coming in August: #NEOverseMaxOut Product Expansion ... While the initial #EnterTheNEOverse campaign focused heavily on mobile gaming performance, nubia Philippines announced that the brand is expanding into a broader lifestyle ecosystem. ... Starting August 1, 2026, the brand will launch its next campaign phase—#NEOverseMaxOut: Max Out Your World. The upcoming rollout will introduce two new key hardware additions: ... - nubia Neo 5 Max: Engineered to provide a larger, immersive entertainment screen and extended battery life for content consumption. - nubia Neo 5 GT Special Edition: Featuring enhanced aesthetic styling, high-performance thermal cooling, and gaming optimizations. ... > Teknogadyet Insider Note: These new additions aim to expand nubia's lineup past dedicated gaming hardware into productivity, digital content creation, and everyday entertainment setups. ... ## Teknogadyet Verdict: nubia's Growing Impact in the PH Market ... By pairing accessible UNISOC-powered gaming smartphones with major brand partnerships like Geely Philippines and ONIC PH, nubia has built strong momentum among young Filipino mobile gamers. As the brand prepares to launch the Neo 5 Max and Neo 5 GT Special Edition this August, tech buyers have plenty of competitive options to look forward to in the budget-to-mid-range smartphone category. ... Filipino mobile gamers and consumers can track upcoming product rollouts, livestreams, and campaign updates by following nubia Philippines on Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, and YouTube. ... and Geely Motor Philippines"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Boot family welcomes Foreman Capital as new shareholder of the Royal NNZ Group | the Royal NNZ Group bv,www.nnz.com,2026-07-21T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.nnz.com/media/boot-family-welcomes-foreman-capital-as-new-shareholder-of-the-royal-nnz-group/,"Boot family welcomes Foreman Capital as new shareholder of the Royal NNZ Group | the Royal NNZ Group bv ... BOOT FAMILY WELCOMES FOREMAN CAPITAL AS NEW SHAREHOLDER OF THE ... After more than 104 years of family ownership, the Boot family has decided to welcome a new shareholder to The Royal NNZ Group. Following a carefully managed strategic process, Foreman Capital has been selected as the partner to support the next phase in the development of the international packaging company. The Boot family will remain actively involved in the business and considers Foreman Capital the ideal partner to support the company’s continuity, growth and ongoing professionalization. ... The investment by Foreman Capital marks the beginning of a new chapter in the company’s history. It provides the financial strength to support and accelerate the strong growth achieved in recent years. The additional investment will enable NNZ to further strengthen its inventory position, logistics capabilities, digital transformation, artificial intelligence initiatives, commercial development and international expansion. ... Behind that success are the people of NNZ. Over the past year, I have seen first-hand how their knowledge, entrepreneurial mindset and dedication make a real difference for our customers every day. To further strengthen that position, we will continue investing in expertise, sustainability, innovation and technology. ... With Foreman Capital, we are gaining not only additional investment capacity, but also a partner with extensive experience in commercial growth, digital transformation and artificial intelligence. This will enable us to further enhance our services and accelerate the realization of our international ambitions. ... “The Royal NNZ Group is an exceptional company with a rich heritage, a strong international market position and a unique corporate culture. We have great respect for everything the Boot family has built over more than a century. ... We look forward to working alongside the family, the management team and all employees to support the company’s continued growth. Our role is to actively support management in delivering the next phase of growth while preserving the unique character, entrepreneurial spirit and culture that define NNZ.” ... About The Royal NNZ Group The Royal NNZ Group is an international supplier of packaging solutions for the agriculture, food and industrial sectors. Originating in Groningen, the Netherlands, the company has developed into an internationally operating organisation that supports customers with innovative, sustainable and high-quality packaging solutions throughout the supply chain. ... About Foreman Capital Foreman Capital is an independent investment firm that invests in successful mid-sized companies from its offices in Amsterdam and Copenhagen. The firm partners with entrepreneurs and management teams to create sustainable long-term value through investment in growth, international expansion, digital transformation and operational improvement, while respecting the culture, identity and heritage of the businesses in which it invests."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Unica Plastics Backs South African Venues With Locally Moulded Seating - Main News,mainnews.co.za,2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://mainnews.co.za/business/unica-plastics-backs-south-african-venues-with-locally-moulded-seating/,"Unica Plastics Backs South African Venues With Locally Mould ... - Main News ... # Unica Plastics Backs South African Venues With Locally Moulded Seating ... July 16, 2026 ... The Pretoria manufacturer heads into the mid-2026 events season with a full range of injection-moulded chairs, desks and homeware built for South African conditions. ... As South Africa works through the cooler months of 2026, the steady flow of weddings, conferences, school events and community gatherings keeps demand high for seating that is easy to move, simple to store and built to last. Unica Plastics, a Pretoria-based manufacturer of injection-moulded plastic products, is meeting that demand with a locally made range of chairs, desks and homeware designed for the way South Africans actually use them. ... Operating from its premises in Pretoria West, Unica Plastics has been manufacturing injection-moulded plastic goods since 1998. Over that time the company has grown a catalogue that runs from event seating through to school furniture, stadium seating and everyday household items. Everything is made locally, which shortens supply lines for South African buyers and supports orders that reach cross-border markets in the wider region. ... For buyers who want a straightforward, robust seat, Unica Plastics also lists a wide selection of plastic chairs for sale across its catalogue. The Rocky Chair sits alongside long-standing lines such as the Party Chair, The Best Chair, the Econo Shell Chair and the Lawn Chair, together with the Revo Stool for casual and hospitality settings. The Party Chair has been part of the range since the company started in 1998, and it remains a familiar sight at functions and public events across the country. ... The company’s work is not limited to social occasions. Its Greenfield Stadium Seat is aimed at sports grounds and public venues that need durable fixed seating able to cope with the outdoors and heavy footfall. On the education side, Unica Plastics introduced its Desk in a Box in 2017, a school desk designed to be practical to transport and put together, which speaks to a market where classrooms often need affordable, hard-wearing furniture that can be moved and maintained without fuss. ... Beyond seating and desks, the range extends into homeware and utility products. Unica Plastics manufactures laundry baskets, basins and buckets for everyday household use, along with a 240 litre wheelie bin for waste handling. Keeping such a broad mix of products under one roof reflects the company’s core capability, which is injection moulding at scale, applied to whatever form a durable plastic product needs to take. ... That breadth carries weight in the current market. Buyers across events, hospitality, education and local government tend to look closely at value and longevity, and locally manufactured goods offer a practical answer to both. Sourcing chairs, desks and bins from a South African maker keeps lead times manageable and makes it easier to reorder matching stock as needs grow. It also means the products are shaped around local conditions and local use rather than imported to a generic specification. ... Unica Plastics describes itself as ... products, and its approach rests ... combining quality raw material with experienced technical teams and quality assurance across the production process. ... that will be stacked, knocked and stored for years, ... is what separates a product that ... up from one that does not. ... As the mid-year event calendar fills out and organisations plan ahead for the spring and summer functions to follow, the appeal of a single local supplier able to cover formal event seating, everyday chairs, school desks, stadium seating and household basics is clear. Unica Plastics continues to serve that need from its Pretoria base, supplying both the South African market and cross-border customers who want moulded plastic products made to last. ... Unica Plastics is a South African manufacturer of injection-moulded plastic products based in Pretoria West, Gauteng. In operation since 1998, the company produces a range that includes event and stadium seating, the Tiffany chair, the Party Chair, the Rocky Chair and other plastic chairs, the Desk in a Box school desk, a 240 litre wheelie bin and homeware such as laundry baskets, basins and buckets. Its products are made locally for both the South African and cross-border markets."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Contract manufacturer Naturis Cosmetics raises Rs 100 crore led by Sharrp Ventures - The Economic Times,economictimes.indiatimes.com (ET),2026-07-16T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/funding/contract-manufacturer-naturis-cosmetics-raises-rs-100-crore-led-by-sharrp-ventures/articleshow/132434937.cms,"Contract manufacturer Naturis Cosmetics raises Rs 100 crore led by Sharrp Ventures - The Economic Times ... # Contract manufacturer Naturis Cosmetics raises Rs 100 crore led by Sharrp Ventures ... Naturis Cosmetics said it will use the fresh capital to expand its footprint by setting up a manufacturing facility in Vapi, an experience centre in the Delhi-NCR region and a research and development centre in Mumbai. It also plans to strengthen its team across functions. ... Naturis Cosmetics, which manufactures products for beauty and personal care brands such as Pilgrim, Plum, Nykaa's Kay Beauty, and Innovist's Bare Anatomy, has raised Rs 100 crore in its maiden funding round led by Sharrp Ventures. Mirabilis Investment Trust, the family office of Infosys cofounder K Dinesh, Anicut Capital, and Surat-based asset management firm Niveshaay also participated in the round.ET had reported on June 24 that Naturis was in talks to raise its first institutional funding.According to people aware of the matter, the round values Naturis at around Rs 350-400 crore. The Mumbai-based company, which is profitable, generated an estimated Rs 250-300 crore in revenues in the last fiscal year. ... In a statement, Naturis said it will use the fresh capital to expand its footprint by setting up a manufacturing facility in Vapi, an experience centre in the Delhi-NCR region, and a research and development centre in Mumbai. It also plans to strengthen its team across functions.Besides, Naturis, which also counts pharma companies such as Glenmark among its clients, is looking to diversify into newer product categories, including men's grooming, body care, colour cosmetics, fragrances, and exports, while strengthening its over-the-counter (OTC) pharmaceutical capabilities.The funding comes amid growing investor interest in India's booming beauty and personal care sector, extending beyond consumer-facing brands to the manufacturing ecosystem that supports them. Contract manufacturers, many of which are family-owned or bootstrapped, are increasingly attracting institutional capital. ... In April, JM Financial's private equity arm invested Rs 150 crore in NG Electro Products, which manufactures gels, creams, and other personal care items for D2C startups as well as established fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG) companies.""Our long-term vision is to build India's leading ODM (original design manufacturer) platform in the beauty and personal care space. With the strategic expertise of our investors and partners, we are well-positioned to accelerate our growth, strengthen our R&D capabilities, expand our manufacturing footprint, and help build the next generation of brands from India,"" Rahul Tandon, cofounder and CEO of Naturis, said in a statement.According to market intelligence firm 1Lattice, India's online beauty and personal care market is expected to grow to $13 billion by FY30 from $6 billion in FY25, driven by rising affluence, greater awareness, and wider access."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Nips by Nippies Enters Next Phase of Growth with National Retail Expansion,www.prnewswire.com (Nips by Nippies),2026-07-13T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/nips-by-nippies-enters-next-phase-of-growth-with-national-retail-expansion-302823038.html,"Nips by Nippies Enters Next Phase of Growth with National Retail Expansion Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation ... NEW YORK , July 13, 2026 /PRNewswire/ - Nips by Nippies, the modern everyday essentials line from Nippies, is entering its next phase of growth through new retail partnerships. Building on the success of the broader Nippies brand across Amazon, direct-to-consumer and specialty retail, Nips by Nippies is expanding beyond its existing presence at CVS, bringing its collection to even more shoppers nationwide. ... As women continue to prioritize comfort, versatility and confidence in the way they dress, Nips by Nippies is meeting them where they already shop. Expanded distribution across leading national retailers makes the collection easier to discover and incorporate into everyday routines. ... ""Consumer demand continues to validate our vision for the brand and the opportunity within this evolving category,"" said Dave Johnson, Chief Executive Officer. ""As more consumers discover Nips by Nippies, we're focused on ensuring our products are available wherever women shop. This next phase of growth allows us to introduce the brand to new audiences while building on the strong retail momentum we've created through innovation and trusted retail partnerships."" ... The expansion marks a significant milestone in the brand's evolution, representing Nips by Nippies' first national mass retail expansion beyond the drug channel. By broadening its presence across multiple retail formats, the brand is strengthening its omnichannel strategy while reinforcing its position as a destination for modern everyday essentials. As the company continues to invest in product innovation and national distribution, this expanded footprint supports its long-term growth ambitions. ... As part of its continued retail expansion, Nips by Nippies will launch with additional national retail partners throughout 2026, further strengthening its omnichannel presence. Beginning July 5, 2026, the brand will be available nationwide at Target with 10 SKUs in stores and online, introducing the collection to a trend-conscious customer who closely aligns with the brand's growing community."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"GIZ, Borno company to create green jobs, mitigate climate change - Businessday NG",businessday.ng (Olatunji Omirin),2026-07-08T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-08 00:00:00+00:00,,https://businessday.ng/news/article/giz-borno-company-to-create-green-jobs-mitigate-climate-change/,", mitigate climate change - Business ... # GIZ, Borno company to create green jobs, mitigate climate change Olatunji Omirin July 8, 2026 ... The Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) and Borno Plastic Industries Limited (BOPLAS), in partnership with Tatabe Global Services Limited, have rolled out measures to create employment opportunities from the waste menace to green jobs as part of efforts to combat climate change, poverty, and restiveness among youth and women in the state. The initiative aims to promote inclusive plastic recycling as a pathway to environmental sustainability, climate resilience, and economic empowerment in Borno State. Aliyu Usman, the Director-General of the Borno State Great Green Wall, spoke during an inception meeting for the POPLAS -GIZ Supporting Sustainable Social Protection, Participation and Economic Resilience in Northeast Nigeria (SEPIN SUSI) held in Maiduguri. According to him, it underscores the need to address the growing environmental and socio-economic challenges associated with plastic waste accumulation in Maiduguri, where rapid urbanisation, inadequate waste management systems, and indiscriminate plastic disposal contribute to flooding, pollution, public health risks, and greenhouse gas emissions. ... “This initiative will help the Borno State Government, with the support of GIZ, recognise the untapped economic value of recyclable plastic waste and seek to transform it into a source of sustainable livelihoods for vulnerable communities. ... “The initiative is expected to create inclusive green jobs, strengthen household incomes, improve environmental sanitation, reduce plastic pollution, and promote climate-smart community practices. It will also strengthen private sector participation in local development, encourage the adoption of circular economy principles, and demonstrate how market-based partnerships can deliver sustainable environmental and economic outcomes in fragile and conflict-affected settings, “Usman Also, Falmata Umara Lawan, the Director of Women and Gender at the State Ministry of Women Affairs, opined that there is a need for greater enlightenment and training to enable women to understand the concept of waste value addition, citing knowledge gaps among youths and women in the state. “The project would address unemployment and joblessness among our teeming youths. It is a strategic and timely response to address challenges, but we need more information and training to enable women to understand the business. That’s the only area we are appealing to the GIZ and its partners to ensure they are well-trained on this,” she disclosed. On his part, Papka Wabbas, BOPLAS Industries Limited, said it will establish a structured, market-driven plastic recycling system that empowers members of Ward Development Support Committees (WDSCs), women and youth cooperatives, and other community groups to collect, sort, aggregate, and sell recyclable plastics through designated community collection centres. ... “BOPLAS will provide technical training, transparent market information, guaranteed off-take arrangements, and access to established recycling markets. “As a pilot model, the partnership will generate evidence and lessons to inform the expansion of inclusive recycling systems across Borno State and beyond, while contributing to the state’s environmental protection agenda and broader efforts to build resilient communities through sustainable economic opportunities.”He said. The initiative was launched by the Supporting Sustainable Social Protection, Participation and Economic Resilience in Northeast Nigeria (SEPIN SUSI) Programme, commissioned by the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ), co-funded by the European Union (EU), and implemented by Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) GmbH."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,From lily bulbs to international packaging lines,www.freshplaza.com,2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.freshplaza.com/north-america/article/9854364/from-lily-bulbs-to-international-packaging-lines/,"Anyone familiar with Niverplast, based in Rijssen, the Netherlands, might first picture its bright yellow clogs, an iconic Volkswagen bus, and the lively atmosphere the company brings to trade shows. Behind that image, however, lies a more understated story spanning four decades: listening closely to customers, identifying what could be improved, and then getting to work. ... Some companies start with an elaborate business plan. Niverplast started with a much simpler question, one that came not from the fresh produce sector or the food industry, but from flower bulb growers. Forty years on, the company develops and builds complete bag-in-box packaging machines, packaging lines, and premade EasyOpen bags for customers around the world. That journey began with a practical request from the bulb sector, one that would lay the foundation for four decades of innovation. ... From bag to machine Niverplast was founded in Rijssen in 1986. Operating from a facility on Schoolstraat, the company produced plastic bags for a range of applications. One of these was designed for the flower bulb sector and would later develop into the now well-known EasyOpen bag. ... In 1996, the first automatic bag-in-box machine was developed and installed at De Jong Lelies. The installation ran successfully from its first start-up and quickly proved its value in daily operations. That original machine now holds a prominent place in Niverplast's Experience Center, while De Jong Lelies has since moved on to a newer generation of machines. ... It didn't stop at a single installation. Other bulb growers faced similar challenges and soon recognized the benefits of automated bag placement. Over the following years, Niverplast supplied dozens of machines to companies across the sector, and many of those installations remain in operation today. ... The company decided to focus entirely on developing packaging machines and premade EasyOpen bags. Bag production was outsourced to specialized partners, while knowledge, development, and innovation around the bag itself remained firmly within Niverplast. This allowed the company to concentrate on smart combinations of bag, machine, and production process. ... What began as a single machine for one bulb grower has grown into a complete portfolio of bag-in-box solutions. Niverplast now supplies complete packaging lines worldwide, covering everything from automatic box erecting and premade bag placement to filling, sealing, palletizing, and every step in between. ... The fresh produce sector is also changing Although the first machine was developed for the flower bulb sector, the challenges faced by other industries are strikingly familiar. Whether the product is leafy greens, carrots, onions, or soft fruit, the core challenge tends to be the same: packaging as efficiently as possible without compromising on quality, food safety, or capacity. ... According to Niverplast, a successful automation solution begins not with the machine, but with the production process itself. Based on required capacity, available space, product characteristics, and future plans, a packaging line is designed to fit daily operational needs. ... Premade EasyOpen bags remain an important part of that offering. While Niverplast no longer produces the bags itself, it continues to develop them further together with specialized partners, focusing on reliability, ease of use, reduced downtime, and lower material use compared with many traditional alternatives. ... Practice as the starting point Forty years on, Niverplast still begins the same way: with a question rooted in practical experience. The difference now is that those questions no longer come solely from the bulb sector, but from customers around the world."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,Romania's TeraPlast completes acquisition of Spain plant | Romania Investments News | SeeNews,seenews.com,2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://seenews.com/news/romanias-teraplast-completes-acquisition-of-spain-plant-1297397,"Plast completes ... of Spain plant | Romania Investments ... # Romania's TeraPlast completes acquisition of Spain plant ... July 1 (SeeNews) - Romanian construction materials producer TeraPlast Group said on Wednesday that it has completed the acquisition of the MASA polyethylene pipe manufacturing facility in Spain from Belgian peer Aliaxis. ... ###### Romania's TeraPlast inaugurates pipe plant in Spain ... ###### Bucharest stocks fall further, TeraPlast leads blue-chip decliners ... ###### Romania's Teraplast enters Spain through plant acquisition ... ###### Romania's TeraPlast swings to net loss in Q1"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"nubia launches LiveBuds 3 Pro, LiveFlip, and 80W GaN charger in PH—price starts at PHP 1,199","www.gizguide.com (Peter Jan ""PJ"" R. Icogo)",2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z,2026-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.gizguide.com/2026/07/nubia-new-ecosystem-devices-ph.html,"nubia launches LiveBuds 3 Pro, LiveFlip, and 80W GaN charger in PH—price starts at PHP 1,199 ... nubia today introduced its first ecosystem accessories in the Philippines #NEOVerseMaxOut: Max Out Your World campaign. ... | nubia LiveBuds 3 Pro, LiveFlip, and 80W GaN charger now in PH | ... Products include the nubia LiveBuds 3 Pro, nubia LiveFlip, and nubia 80W Three‑Port GaN Quick Charger. ... According to the company, these accessories complement the expanded nubia Neo 5 Series, reinforcing nubia’s vision of a connected ecosystem for gaming, entertainment, productivity, and everyday use. ... ia 80W Three‑Port GaN Quick Charger - PHP 1,199 ... - PHP ... The new devices are now official in the Philippines. ... nubia is rolling out ecosystem partnerships like a FREE 3‑month VIU subscription with Neo 5 Series purchases, Cotti Coffee vouchers and social activations, and the nubia Social Run community initiative."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,New Tampon Line: Premium Care Expansion | AIMISIN,www.newclears.com,2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.newclears.com/news/new-tampon-production-line-launched-expanding-premium-feminine-care-capacity-aimisin/,"New Tampon Line: Premium Care Expansion | AIMISIN ... # New Tampon Production Line Launched: Expanding Premium Feminine Care Capacity | AIMISIN 2026-06-24 To meet the fast-growing global demand for high-quality, safe, and eco-friendly feminine hygiene products, our company has officially put a new professional tampon production line into operation. This capacity expansion marks a key strategic upgrade in our feminine care product portfolio, enabling us to deliver more standardized, comfortable, and trustworthy menstrual care solutions for global distributors, retailers, and brand partners. With upgraded automated production equipment and optimized manufacturing workflows, the new line greatly improves production efficiency, product consistency, and product safety standards, laying a solid foundation for large-scale order fulfillment and high-end customized cooperation. As a professional FDA certificated tampon manufacturer, we have always adhered to strict international health and safety standards throughout product research and development, production, and quality inspection. All products produced by the new production line fully comply with FDA regulatory requirements, with rigorous testing implemented for raw material safety, production hygiene, finished product sterilization, and physical performance. Every batch of tampons undergoes systematic quality screening to eliminate potential safety risks such as harmful residues and unqualified materials. This strict compliance system ensures that our feminine care products can stably serve global mainstream markets and meet the stringent access standards of North America, Europe, and other regions. ... Equipped with advanced flexible production systems, the new line focuses on upgrading high-end feminine care products, especially the development and mass production of organic tampon for feminine daily care. Different from ordinary synthetic material tampons, our organic series adopts pure natural organic cotton as the core raw material, free of fluorescent agents, fragrances, chlorine bleaching, and synthetic additives. The ultra-soft and breathable material effectively reduces skin friction and sensitivity, bringing gentler and more comfortable protection for women with sensitive skin. The launch of the new production line solves the capacity bottleneck of organic tampon mass production, enabling stable and continuous supply of high-quality organic feminine care products for global users. ... The completion of the new production line also comprehensively strengthens our service capability for tampon wholesale business. In the past, high-end organic tampon products were restricted by production capacity, making it difficult to meet the growing bulk order demands of cross-border distributors, supermarket chains, and maternal and child stores. The newly launched automated line achieves high-speed, standardized, and large-scale production, greatly shortening order delivery cycles while maintaining stable product quality. Whether customers need conventional standard tampons or customized organic tampons with exclusive packaging and specifications, we can efficiently complete bulk production and timely delivery. ... In addition to capacity improvement, this expansion further enriches our product matrix and market competitiveness. We can now provide diversified product combinations covering daily conventional tampons, high-absorption night-use tampons, and pure organic skin-friendly tampons, fully meeting the differentiated needs of different age groups, usage scenarios, and market positioning. Meanwhile, we continue to support OEM and ODM customized services, helping global partners create personalized feminine hygiene product lines and quickly occupy the high-end feminine care market. Looking ahead, we will continue to invest in production technology upgrading and product innovation, always focusing on women’s healthy and dignified care. By virtue of standardized FDA certification, reliable large-scale production capacity, and professional wholesale and customized service systems, we will further expand global market layout, provide more cost-effective and high-quality feminine hygiene products for global partners and end users, and consolidate our position as a trustworthy supplier in the global feminine care industry."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,"Kejar Kenaikan Laba, Emiten Aguan (PDPP) Ekspansi ke Bisnis Daur Ulang Plastik",market.bisnis.com (Ibad Durrohman),2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://market.bisnis.com/read/20260622/192/1982452/kejar-kenaikan-laba-emiten-aguan-pdpp-ekspansi-ke-bisnis-daur-ulang-plastik,"Primadaya Plastisindo (PDPP) berencana memperluas bisnis dengan menambah usaha daur ulang plastik melalui KBLI 38302 untuk perkuat posisi di industri plastik. Ibad Durrohman - Bisnis.com Senin, 22 Juni 2026 | 17:14 Perbesar Emiten terafiliasi konglomerat Sugianto Kusuma atau Aguan, PT Primadaya Plastisindo Tbk. (PDPP) berencana memperluas lini bisnisnya dengan menambah kegiatan usaha baru di bidang pemulihan material barang plastik. Istimewa ... Bisnis.com, JAKARTA — Emiten terafiliasi Sugianto Kusuma atau Aguan, PT Primadaya Plastisindo Tbk. (PDPP) berencana memperluas lini bisnisnya dengan menambah kegiatan usaha baru di bidang pemulihan material barang plastik melalui KBLI 38302, yang mencakup aktivitas pengolahan dan daur ulang limbah plastik menjadi bahan baku industri. ... Direktur Utama PDPP Kennie Angesty menyampaikan bahwa penambahan kegiatan usaha tersebut merupakan bagian dari strategi pengembangan bisnis perseroan untuk memperkuat posisi di industri plastik sekaligus menangkap peluang dari meningkatnya permintaan material daur ulang di pasar domestik maupun global. ... “Penambahan kegiatan usaha berupa KBLI 38302 merupakan bagian dari strategi pengembangan kegiatan usaha perseroan untuk memperkuat posisi perseroan di industri plastik serta mendukung kegiatan usaha yang berkelanjutan,” kata Kennie dalam keterbukaan informasi, Senin (22/6/2026). ... Kennie menjelaskan bahwa rencana penambahan kegiatan usaha tersebut akan terlebih dahulu dimintakan persetujuan pemegang saham melalui Rapat Umum Pemegang Saham (RUPS) yang dijadwalkan pada 24 Juni 2026, sesuai ketentuan dalam Peraturan Otoritas Jasa Keuangan (POJK) 17/2020. ... Penambahan kegiatan usaha ini dilakukan melalui KBLI 38302-Pemulihan Material Barang Plastik, yang mencakup aktivitas pengolahan limbah plastik menjadi material dasar seperti serpihan plastik (flakes) dan bijih plastik (pellets) yang dapat digunakan kembali oleh industri hilir. ... Dalam rencana pengembangan tersebut, PDPP akan fokus pada pengolahan material plastik seperti Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET) dan Polycarbonate (PC), dengan potensi pengembangan ke jenis material lainnya sesuai kebutuhan pasar dan perkembangan industri. ... Kennie menilai langkah ini sejalan dengan tren global industri plastik yang semakin mengarah pada penerapan prinsip ekonomi sirkular, seiring meningkatnya permintaan material daur ulang dari industri kemasan dan manufaktur. ... embangan industri plastik, baik di ... maupun secara global ... menunjukkan peningkatan perhatian terhadap pengelolaan limbah plastik, pemanfaatan material daur ulang, serta penerapan prinsip ekonomi ... irkular dan keberlan ... utan,” tambah Kennie. PDPP juga menyebut bahwa permintaan terhadap material ... daur ulang terus meningkat, ... itmen pelaku industri dalam menerapkan prinsip Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG ... Untuk mendukung pengembangan usaha baru tersebut, PDPP telah menyiapkan kapasitas operasional berupa enam fasilitas pabrik dengan total luas sekitar 8 hektare serta sekitar 35 mesin produksi yang sudah digunakan dalam kegiatan usaha utama. ... kegiatan pemulihan ... Adapun kebutuhan investasi untuk pengembangan kegiatan usaha tersebut diperkirakan mencapai sekitar Rp7,5 miliar yang akan dilakukan secara bertahap hingga 2028 dan seluruhnya berasal dari dana internal perseroan. ... Berdasarkan hasil studi kelayakan, penambahan kegiatan usaha ini diproyeksikan memberikan dampak positif terhadap kinerja keuangan PDPP, dengan Net Present Value (NPV) sebesar Rp18,46 miliar serta indikator kelayakan investasi yang dinilai kuat. ... Dari sisi proyeksi keuangan, penambahan bisnis ini juga diharapkan meningkatkan pendapatan dan profitabilitas perseroan seiring dengan bertambahnya sumber pendapatan baru dari lini usaha pemulihan material plastik. ... Perseroan menegaskan bahwa seluruh rencana tersebut masih menunggu persetujuan RUPS, sebelum kemudian dilanjutkan dengan pemenuhan perizinan usaha melalui sistem Online Single Submission (OSS) serta penyesuaian Nomor Induk Berusaha (NIB)."
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,NuCel mobile service reaches 1 million customers,valorinternational.globo.com,2026-06-22T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-22 00:00:00+00:00,,https://valorinternational.globo.com/business/news/2026/06/22/nucel-mobile-service-reaches-1-million-customers.ghtml,"NuCel mobile service reaches 1 million customers ... # NuCel mobile service reaches 1 million customers ... ## Partnership between Nubank and Claro hit milestone after 17 months of operations ... NuCel, the mobile virtual network operator (MVNO) launched by Nubank in partnership with Claro in January 2025, has reached 1 million customers after 17 months of operations. The milestone was achieved in a segment that totaled 9.84 million mobile accesses in the first quarter of 2026, according to Brazil’s telecommunications regulator Anatel. MVNOs operate in a market dominated by Vivo, Claro, and TIM, which account for about 94% of the country’s 271.3 million mobile connections. ... In an interview with Valor, Livia Chanes, chief executive of Nubank in Brazil, and Rodrigo Marques, chief executive of Claro, attributed the result to the integration model adopted by the two companies. According to the executives, their teams have worked jointly from product development through commercial operations. ... “NuCel was born from our desire to expand our product offering and increase our relevance in our customers’ daily lives. We chose mobile services because it is a product that 100% of our customers use,” said Chanes. According to the executive, the strategy was to bring attributes from financial services, such as transparency and simplicity, into the telecommunications industry. ... For Marques, previous MVNO experiences in Brazil ran into difficulties because of both limited service offerings and insufficient integration between partners. “For it to work, it had to be a partnership where we understand that the product is ours as well. It’s not simply a matter of delivering a service to Nubank.” ... Claro provides network infrastructure and operational expertise, while Nubank is responsible for digital distribution and customer experience through its app. For the telecom operator, the partnership expands the reach of its 5G network through a brand with a strong presence in digital channels. “Nubank was born in the digital environment and is recognized for its relationship with customers. For us, it is a way to incorporate new knowledge and learn from that culture,” said Marques. ... The operator offers benefits integrated with Nubank’s financial services. In addition, use of the bank’s app and WhatsApp does not count against customers’ data allowances. ... Marques said the operator aims to differentiate itself through integration with Nubank’s other products rather than through an aggressive pricing strategy. “We are not in the market to compete solely on price, but on a different quality and value proposition,” he said. According to the executive, part of the market initially expected the company’s entry to trigger a price war, a scenario that has not materialized. ... The expansion of the user base coincided with several adjustments to the service offering. After launch, NuCel stopped operating exclusively with eSIMs and began offering physical SIM cards, broadening the service’s reach. In May 2026, the service was also opened to customers aged 16 to 18, allowing them access to both connectivity services and Nubank’s financial products. ... Chanes said the strategy was to prioritize consolidating the service before accelerating user growth. “We started with a smaller base, testing hypotheses to ensure everything worked well,” she said. ... The executive did not disclose projections for revenue or customer numbers over the next 12 months but said the operator would continue to be a growth avenue for the company. “We always want more. This is the first step in a journey.” ... Despite the growth in its customer base, Nubank and Claro have not disclosed data on revenue, profitability, or the amount invested in the venture. Chanes said, however, that customer satisfaction indicators are above the telecommunications industry’s average. According to the executive, the company’s Net Promoter Score (NPS), a metric that measures consumers’ willingness to recommend a brand, exceeds the industry average. ... Asked about the possibility of extending the model to Nubank’s operations in Mexico and Colombia, Chanes said there are no plans for international expansion in the short term. “We are focused on ensuring that the product works very well in Brazil. As operations scale, we can keep this conversation open in the future.” ... The agreement between the two companies provides for exclusivity under a long-term partnership model. For Marques, the model depends on a level of integration that goes beyond the traditional relationship between infrastructure provider and customer. “It’s difficult to imagine an MVNO where you can keep switching networks. It’s a joint effort to solve problems and innovate.”"
NUBIZ PLASTIC,,,,Exa,ERW steel pipe and steel tubular pole specialist company Anubhav Plast Ltd launches Rs. 24 crore IPO - Ek Aaina Bharat,www.ekaainabharat.com (Ek Aaina Bharat),2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z,2026-06-19 00:00:00+00:00,,https://www.ekaainabharat.com/en/business/erw-steel-pipe-and-steel-tubular-pole-specialist-company-anubhav-plast-ltd-launches-rs-24-crore-ipo,"ERW steel pipe and steel tubular pole specialist company Anubhav Plast Ltd launches Rs. 24 crore IPO - Ek Aaina Bharat ... # ERW steel pipe and steel tubular pole specialist company Anubhav Plast Ltd launches Rs. 24 crore IPO ... ## The company’s IPO will open on June 19 and close on June 23, 2026 New Delhi [India], June 19: Kanpur-based ‘Anubhav Plast Limited’ of Uttar Pradesh is a specialist company engaged in the manufacturing of ERW steel pipes and steel tubular po... ... W steel pipe and steel tubular pole specialist company Anubhav Plast Ltd launches Rs. 24 crore IPO” ... ERW steel pipe and steel tubular pole specialist company Anubhav Plast Ltd launches Rs. 24 crore IPO ... The company’s IPO will open on June 19 and close on June 23, 2026 ... New Delhi [India], June 19: Kanpur-based ‘Anubhav Plast Limited’ of Uttar Pradesh is a specialist company engaged in the manufacturing of ERW steel pipes and steel tubular poles. The company is bringing an IPO of Rs. 24 crore on the BSE SME platform for setting up a new manufacturing facility for the production of crash barriers and solar panel structures within the existing manufacturing premises, meeting working capital requirements, and general corporate purposes. The team of Business Remedies has obtained information regarding the company’s business activities from the company’s prospectus. ... Information Regarding the IPO: The The IPO of ‘Anubhav Plast Limited’ will open on June 19 and close on June 23, 2026, on the BSE SME platform. Price band for the public issue is Rs. 77-80 per share. The company will issue 30,00,000 equity shares of face value Rs. 10 each. The IPO is being managed by Capital Square Advisors Private Limited. ... Business Activities: Anubhav Plast Limited was incorporated in January 1987. The company is engaged in the manufacturing of Electric Resistance Welding (ERW) steel pipes and tubes, which are available in round and square hollow sections. The company also manufactures swaged steel tubular poles. The company’s product portfolio, comprising ERW steel pipes and steel tubular poles, serves various sectors including electric transmission and distribution, street lighting, telecom infrastructure, construction, irrigation, water supply, general engineering, and fabrication. The company markets its products under the “Anubhav” brand. The company operates two manufacturing units in Kanpur Dehat, Uttar Pradesh, and has established a strong presence in government tender-based projects across several Indian states. The company’s ERW products are manufactured in accordance with IS:2713, IS:9295, IS:1239, IS:4270, IS:1161, IS:4923, and IS:3589 standards and are widely accepted by customers for their quality, reliability, and durability. Currently, the company has an installed capacity of 7,500 metric tonnes per month and 90,000 metric tonnes per year for ERW steel pipes and tubes, and 12,500 units per month and 1,50,000 units per year for swaged steel tubular poles, based on a single-shift operation. ... At present, the company’s product portfolio includes more than 80 standard sizes of steel tubular poles ranging from 410SP-1 to 410SP-80 as per IS:2713. The company manufactures round pipes ranging from 1.5 inches to 8 inches and 100 x 100 mm square hollow sections. The 100 x 100 mm swaged high-strength sections are used for structural support. The company is also manufacturing other pipes and tubes of various diameters and thicknesses in accordance with IS:3589, IS:4270 and IS:9295. The company is expanding its product range to include round pipes up to 10 inches and square pipes up to 200×200 mm. The company supplies products according to customer specifications, including galvanization. Galvanization is a process that enhances corrosion resistance and increases the service life of steel structures, especially in outdoor and high-moisture environments. ... Financial Performance: In Financial Year 2023, the company earned operating revenue of Rs. 8,713.69 lakh and profit after tax of Rs. 74.36 lakh. In Financial Year 2024, the company earned operating revenue of Rs. 8,732.69 lakh and profit after tax of Rs. 207.99 lakh. In Financial Year 2025, the company earned operating revenue of Rs. 9,816.74 lakh and profit after tax of Rs. 599.68 lakh. For the period ended December 31, 2025, in Financial Year 2026, the company earned operating revenue of Rs. 8,048.88 lakh and profit after tax of Rs. 529.57 lakh. For the period ended December 31, 2025, in Financial Year 2026, the company earned a profit after tax margin of approximately 6.58 percent. ... | IPO Highlights- Anubhav Plast Limited | | | --- | --- | | IPO Opens on | June 19, 2026 | | IPO Closes on | June 23, 2026 | | Issue Price Band | Rs. 77-80 Per Share | | Issue Size | 30,00,000 shares – up to Rs. 24 crore (At upper price band) | | Listing on | BSE SME Platform |"
